ARCHIVE_LOADED(1,[{"n":50073,"r":"BLECOURTNB0078","p":"Bergeijk","v":"N.-Br.","y":1892,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Kabouters (gnomes) do all kinds of work on a farm in the evening or at night, invisibly and silently. The curious who try to spy on them are threatened with having their eyes put out. In the morning, however, the work is no further along than when it began. While ploughing, a farmer is given a pancake by a kabouter (gnome), who asks him to report when he gets home that Kyrië is dead.","i":"P.N.P.","o":"2.32. De pannekoek van een Kaboutermanneke\nTe Hoog-Casteren, een gehucht van Hoogeloon, staat nog een gewoon landbouwershuis, waarin de Kaboutermannekens uit den Witvrouwsberg, ook Kabouterberg geheeten en in het Koebosch gelegen, bepaaldelijk des avonds of in den nacht, verschillende bezigheden kwamen verrichten. Deze waren gemeenlijk dezelfde als die de bewoners van dat huis dien dag gedaan hadden of die zij 's anderendaags moesten doen. Als de Kaboutermannekens des avonds, bij voorbeeld na 10 ure, reeds aan het werk waren, zonder dat de bewoners ter rust lagen, dan klopten zij op deur of venster, om den huisgenooten te beteekenen dat zij naar bed moesten gaan, dewijl zij - de Kaboutermannekens - verlangden binnen te komen om met het werk te beginnen. De bewoners hoorden hen gedurig druk arbeiden, als: bakken, boteren, den vloer of huisraad schuren, de spijzen bereiden, enz.; in de schuur: dorschen, wannen, enz. Nooit zagen zij echter deze ieverige nachtwerkers; ook verrichtten deze sprakeloos hunnen arbeid, tenware iemand hen door een sleutelgat, eene spleet der schuur- of staldeur of anderszins wilde bespieden; want dan hoorde de nieuwsgierige de onmiddellijke bedreiging hem de oogen uit te steken. Het verwonderlijkste was evenwel dat de huisbewoners des morgens van den arbeid der Kaboutermannekens niets gevorderd vonden; alles was nog als te voren.\nOp zekeren voormiddag wa"},{"n":35068,"r":"BOEKV187","p":"Koog aan de Zaan","v":"N.-H.","y":1899,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"When an old maidservant sits sewing in the evening, she often hears hammering and sawing in the shipyard. When she goes to look, she never sees a light burning. She then predicts that the nachtwerkertjes (little night workers) will bring a lot of work again. Indeed, within a few days it becomes so busy that the carpenters have to work through the night.","i":"C.B.","o":"Kaboutermannetjes. A.\n\nBij ons ouderlijk huis stond een molenmakerswerf. Mij is dikwijls verteld, dat een meid van grootmoeder, 's avonds als ze zat te naaien, vaak druk hoorde timmeren en werken op de werf. Als ze ging kijken zag ze niemand; zelfs brandde er geen licht. Dan zei ze: \"De nachtwerkertjes zijn weer aan den gang; nou zullen ze het wel gauw druk krijgen.\" En werkelijk kwam er dan binnen enkele dagen werk aan den winkel, zoodat men 's nachts moest overwerken."},{"n":8748,"r":"CBAK0145","p":"Koog aan de Zaan","v":"N.-H.","y":1899,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"A maid hears knocking and working on the premises in the evening, though nothing can be seen. Her prediction that it will get busy comes true.","i":"C.B.","o":"Bij mijn ouderlijke huis stond een molentimmerwerf. Een meid van mijn grootvader hoorde vaak 's avonds, als ze zat te naaien, druk kloppen en werken in de werf. Als ze dan ging kijken, zag ze niemand; zelfs geen licht branden.\nDan zei ze: \"De nachtwerkertjes zijn weer aan den gang. Nu zullen ze het wel gauw druk krijgen.\"\nWerkelijk kwam er dan binnen eenige dagen werk aan de winkel, zoodat men 's nachts moest overwerken."},{"n":12807,"r":"SWATER30","p":"Koog aan de Zaan","v":"N.-H.","y":1899,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Nachtwerkertjes (little night workers) cannot be seen but can be heard. When a storm is coming they are very busy, which is taken as an omen of the large amount of work in store for carpenters. When an old maidservant sits sewing in the evening, she often hears hammering and sawing in the shipyard. When she goes to look, she never sees a light burning. She then predicts that the nachtwerkertjes will bring a lot of work again. Indeed, within a few days it becomes so busy that the carpenters have to work through the night.","i":"C.B.","o":"NACHTWERKERTJES\nIn de Zaanstreek sprak men vroeger veel over de nachtwerkertjes, die men wel hoorde maar nooit zag. Als er storm op til was waren deze nachtwerkertjes druk in de weer. Dat werd als het voorteken beschouwd van het vele werk dat voor de timmerlui op handen was, omdat er door de harde wind veel schade aan de tientallen molens langs de Zaan zou worden toegebracht. De ouders van Cornelis Bakker woonden in het midden van de vorige eeuw in Koog aan de Zaan, naast een molenmakerswerf. Als 's avonds de oude dienstbode van Cornelis' grootmoeder zat te naaien, hoorde ze vaak druk timmeren en zagen op de werf. Als ze dan ging kijken zag ze niemand en er brandde ook geen licht. \"De nachtwerkertjes zijn weer aan de gang en nou zullen ze op de werf wel gauw handen te kort komen\" zei ze dan. En werkelijk, binnen enkele dagen was het zo druk op de werf dat men 's nachts moest overwerken."},{"n":9349,"r":"CBAK0490","p":"Ransdorp","v":"N.-H.","y":1911,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Skippers sleeping out at sea often hear a sound as if someone is working on the ship. They hurry home, because it is a sign that the ship will have to go onto the slipway.","i":"C.B.","o":"Als een Volendammer 's nachts leit te slapen in volle zee, dan hoort hij vaak een geluid alsof men aan zijn schip te timmeren en te breeuwen is. Dan haast hij zich om thuis te komen, want dan is dat een bewijs dat zijn schip noodig op de helling moet.\n(J. Vet)","l":"Waterlands"},{"n":9378,"r":"CBAK0517","p":"Koog aan de Zaan","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In the run-up to a storm the nachtwerkertjes (little night workers) can be heard, signalling that a lot of work is coming for carpenters on mills damaged by the wind.","i":"C.B.","o":"Nachtwerkertjes. Die hoorde men aan de Zaan, 's nachts als er storm in aantocht was. Zij waren voorboden van het vele werk, dat voor de timmerlieden op handen was, als door den harden wind schade werd toegebracht aan de vele molens, die er in mijn jeugd nog stonden.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.89)"},{"n":42315,"r":"LAAN013","p":"Lellens","v":"Gr.","y":1930,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Work spirits are invisible but can be heard, and their work at night comes to nothing. They come mainly to farmers who set everything ready in the evening for the next day.","i":"E.F.","o":"Waarkgaisten\nWaarkgaisten kìn je nooit zain, mor heuren kìn je ze zoveuls te beter. 't Is aal gehaaimzinneghaid wat ter bie is. Zo gaauw as 't goud duuster is, moaken ze lewaai, zo haard binnen ze aan 't aarbaiden. In timmerwinkel timmern en klòppen ze; in de smederij haauwen ze op 't ambòld, trekken aan de bloasbaalk òf besloagen peerden, van 's oavends òf aan, hail nacht deur. Slim is 't ook voak op meulens: ie heuren ze draaien. Mor 't allerslimste is 't op ainege boerenploatsen, benoam dij wat ainzoam op roemte stoan.\nAs ie 's mörns wakker wòrden, is 't niks wieder komen; ze aarbaiden haard genog, en ze kriegen tòch nooit gain slag doan.\nHail slim was 't aleer joaren op Klaaine Nes tussen Hòlwier en Baairm. Kaarnmeulen luip; 't dörsblòk gong in 't rond; gain peerd ter veur; de waaier draaide lusteg op; de haile schuur in voile bedrieveghaid. En weer, as ie der 's mörgens kwammen, was ter niks oet 't stro zet.\nMor de schudeuren stonden lös, ja soms wiedwoagen open. En de peerden stonden nat van swait op staal.\n\nAs 't koornmeten doan was, mos 't haalf mud ondersteboven en de schop aan zied legd wòrden; aans begunden 's nachts de waarkgaisten.\nDe smid legde zien schootsvel 's oavends over 't ambòld.\nDe waarkgaisten komen aaltied bie boeren dij verbraand op 't waark binnen en dij 's oavends ales kloar leggen veur aander dag.\nZo is 't gebeurd in Gareweer bie Tjamsweer aan aander","l":"Gronings"},{"n":21925,"r":"CJ030003","p":"Gersloot","v":"Fr.","y":1951,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"A bewitched butter churn must be secured, otherwise it keeps rattling all night. A spinning wheel and carpentry tools must also be carefully put away for the same reason.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De tsjerne moast op 'e joun fêstset wurde, oars tsjerne it de hiele nacht troch. Ek it spinnewiel. Ek it ark fan 'e timmerman moast opburgen wurde.\nFaek wie de molke bitsjoend, dan woe 't net bûterje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":13246,"r":"LYST032","p":"Briltil","v":"Gr.","y":1953,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Work spirits are spirits that at night finish the work that was not completed during the day. When a farmer stops threshing halfway, he hears knocking and threshing at night. Unfortunately the work is not done the next day; it is just as it was the day before.","i":"R.H.","o":"Werkgeesten\nDit zijn geesten die 's nachts het werk voortzetten waar de mensen niet klaar mee zijn gekomen. Een boer die aan het dorsen was (met de hand natuurlijk) en hij laat alles 's nachts liggen, dan hoorde men des nachts geklop en gedors. (De volgende dag was het werk niet gedaan hoor.)"},{"n":15526,"r":"CJ002316","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1954,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Father comes home at night and clearly hears sounds as if people are at work. Yet everyone is still in bed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit kom op in nacht thús, doe hearde er skoan dat se allegear oan it braekjen wienen. Teake syn slach koe hy der skoan út. En dochs leinen wy allegearre op bêd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23642,"r":"CJ040504","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1954,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"If a woman did not take the thread off the spinning wheel, it went on spinning at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Beppe spoun, mar as hja de snare net fan it spinwiel ôf die, dan spoun it yn 'e nacht troch.\nIt spinwiele woarde dus útspand.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":43462,"r":"AMPT000502","p":"Hasselt","v":"Ov.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At night the churning mill turns, without any horse or person to be seen.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"M'n eigen moeder vertelde me dat het spookte in het achterhuis. Daar stond een karnmolen, die getrokken werd door een paard. Wanneer ze 's nachts wakker werd gebeurde het vaak dat de karn liep zonder dat er een paard stond of iemand bij was."},{"n":50607,"r":"KOOIJMAN0064","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"If someone was a hard worker, people said: \"He is driven by the work spirit.\"","i":"H.K.","o":"Als je een werks mens had, dan zeiden ze: \"Die wordt aangedreven door de werkgeest\"."},{"n":50903,"r":"KOOIJMAN0204","p":"Benschop","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In the evening the work spirits are at work; they can be heard above the ditches, but also in the distance when it thunders.","i":"H.K.","o":"De werkgeest kon je 's avonds horen, boven de sloten. Ze noemden dat ook wel het groei. In de tijd dat de kikkers kwaken. Ik heb ook wel eens in Benschop horen zeggen dat als het rommelde in de verte, dat de werkgeest was. \"Hoor de werkgeest eens\", zeiden ze dan."},{"n":129836,"r":"WOUDA002302","p":"Workum","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"People who let kabouters (gnomes) work for them are frowned upon for it.","i":"E.W.","o":"Kabouterforhalen hearre by de bern thús, mar yn myn jonge jierren leaude men: sommige minsken lieten har bitsjinje troch de kabouters. Se dienen neat, brûkten wol gjin drank, mar waerden troch de minsken, de maetskippij, skoudere.","l":"Fries"},{"n":125791,"r":"KOOIJMAN1599","p":"Rijswijk","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"The little kabouters (gnomes) come to do the work at night, so set out the food for them.","i":"H.K.","o":"De kabouterkes komme 's nachts 't werk doen, zet 't ete maar klaar."},{"n":12493,"r":"CJ001815","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Residents hear hammering in their old house. Later it is demolished and a new house is built on the spot. So the hammering was a prediction.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By de Feanster Nije Wei stiet in hûs, dêr't earder in âld hûs stien hat. Doe wenne Harm Wever der noch yn. Op in nacht gong it dêr op in smiten en dwaen mei balken en spanten en ek op in timmerjen. Heit en mem leinen op bêd. Sy wennen der njonken.\nSy hearden it beide dúdlik. \"Dêr komt in nij hûs\", seinen se. En dat is ek gebeurd, mar even neitiid. It âlde hûs woarde ôfbrutsen. De spanten woarden delsmiten, en heitendy hearden krekt deselde lûden as doe yn dy nacht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12494,"r":"CJ001816","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"The narrator and his wife hear hammering at night. This is a prediction. A new house is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Om 1940 hinne hearden ik en Sjouk (syn wiif) yn 'e Harkema dúdlik guon timmerjen yn 'e nacht. Ik sei: \"Hjir komt in nij hûs.\" Wy hienen dúdlik de lûden heard fan it bikappen fan 'e stien. It hûs kom der ek, ridlik gau dêrnei. It wienen deselde lûden, dy't wy earder heard hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12498,"r":"CJ001820","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Grandmother predicts that a house will burn down. She had seen it burning at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us âlde beppe wenne op 't Ketling, ûnder Surhústerfean. Op in moarn sei se: \"Binnen 14 dagen brânt dat en dat hûs op. Ik ha 't fannacht brânnen sjoen.\"\nBinnen twa wiken tiid wie 't hûs in jiskebult.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12499,"r":"CJ001821","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"The narrator predicted that a house would later burn down. He had seen it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw ris fan to foaren in hûs yn 'e brân sjoen. It brânde hiel bot. De flammen fleagen yn 'e hichte. In pear dagen letter is 't opbrând. 't Wie hjir oan dizze wei. Teije Mozes wenne der yn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15595,"r":"CJ002407","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At night, from the meadow, father hears a lot of hammering at a house. A week later there was a new loft.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear kom heit thús, let op 'e joun. Doe sei er: \"Och, och hwat gong it dêr op 'e âld pleats (dêr't nou Gjalt van der Ley wennet) op in spikerjen en in slaen. Ik koe 't fan 'e wei ôf skoan hearre.\nIn wike letter krigen se dêr in nije koesouder.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16821,"r":"CJ006208","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"A man builds a new shed but does not finish it. At night he hears very clearly that beams are being thrown about. Later, when the shed is finished, the sound comes exactly as close.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jan Goaitsens Nicolaï boude in nij hok. Dat wie noch net ôfdien. Doe hearden se dúdlik yn 'e nacht dat der mei dikke balken smiten woarde, nei ûnderen ta. Dit kom krekt sa nei letter, doe't it hok ôfmakke woarde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16883,"r":"CJ006609","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Hammering was very often heard in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Timmerjen hearden se hiel faek fan to foaren. Dan sei de iene tsjin 'e oare: \"Mast ris hearre, sa giet it dêr op in timmerjen.\" Dat is op forskeidene plakken gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17006,"r":"CJ007604","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"The sound of hammering at night always points to the building of new houses, sheds or gates.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wol hûndert kear ha'k timmerjen heard yn 'e nacht op ûnderskate plakken. Dat tsjutte altyd op nije huzen of hokken of hekken of sa. 't Kaem altyd nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17008,"r":"CJ007606","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"The sound of hammering points to a house that will later stand on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear wie 'k mei noch ien by de Swadde. \n\"Hark, sa timmerje se dêr\", sei myn maet. Ik hearde it ek dúdlik. Mar der wie dêrom neat to sjen. \nEfkes letter kaem dêr in hûs to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17059,"r":"CJ007916","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"On a farm in Oudega, churning went on at night when everyone had gone to bed. When they came to look, nothing was wrong, but as soon as they were back in bed, the churning started again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Aldegea stiet in pleats, dêr wennet nou Lou Oosterhof. Dêr waerd nachts tsjerne, as alles op bêd lei. Mar as se der by kamen wie der neat to rêdden. Mar se leinen noch mar krekt wer op bêd of it bigong wer opnij to tsjernjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17060,"r":"CJ007917","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"When the narrator was a boy, they always fetched old tree stumps from the Oude Venen for firewood. They were chopped on a block behind the house. At night the narrator always heard chopping on that block, but the others did not hear it. His mother kept a box of matches on the corner of the table. He also always heard someone strike a match, but they never caught fire. There was never anything to be seen either. Their house was built from the stone of an old house in Wartena that was called the Spookhuis (Haunted House) because it was haunted at night. His wife thought that some of the haunting had passed to their house through the stone.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik noch in jonge wie hellen wy altyd âlde stobben en sok spul út 'e Alde Feanen om dy op to stoken, hwant wy hienen 't froeger o sa krap. Achter hûs hienen wy in blok stean, dêr woarden dy stobben op kapt.\nMar nachts, dan hearde ik altyd it kappen op dat blok. It fremde wie, de oaren hearden it net, ik allinne. Heit en dy woenen it net leauwe en laken my út, mar ik spriek de wierheit.\nUs mem hie altyd op 'e hoeke fan 'e tafel in doaske mei lúsjefers lizzen. Ik hearde elke nacht dat ien mei in lúsjefers op it doaske striek, mar de lúsjefers kom net yn 'e brân. Ik bin der wol om út bêd kom, hwant bang wie ik net, mar der wie noait hwat to sjen. En doch hearde ik it dúdlik.\nUs húske wie boud fan 'e stien fan in âld hûs út Warten, en dat neamden se dêr it Spoekhûs, omdat it dêr nachts altyd yn spoeke. Myn wiif wol wol ha, dat der hwat fan dy spûkerij op ús hûs oergien wie troch dy stien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17089,"r":"CJ008101","p":"Sweagerbosk","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Before the house next to the narrator's was built, distinct hammering and knocking on stones was once heard on that spot without anything to be seen. Later a house was built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir njonken my stie froeger net in hûs. Doe hawwe âlde minsken dêr us op in kear tige dúdlik timmerjen en stienklopjen heard, sûnder dat der hwat to sjen wie. Doe kom der letter in hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17107,"r":"CJ008204","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"From the knocking of stones and hammering at a spot, it was heard in advance that a house would be built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It hûs dêr't heit en dy yn wenne ha, ûnder Garyp is der nou net mear. Doe't se der noch net mei oan 't bouwen wienen, ha se it timmerjen en stienklopjen dêr al heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17110,"r":"CJ008302","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"The narrator often heard hammering at night in Garijp. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Garyp yn 'e Westerein gong it yn 'e nacht faek op in timmerjen. Dan woarde ik wekker en hearde der nei. Dat wie foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17343,"r":"CJ008806","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At the narrator's home, the thread must always be slackened after weaving mats. If the thread stays taut, you hear the weaving go on all night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As wy oan 't matteweven wienen en wy hâldden op, dan moesten wy de tried altyd slap sette. As wy de tried spand lieten, dan gong it de hiele nacht troch op in matteweven. Dan wie 't hyltyd mar tyng- tyng- tyng-","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17344,"r":"CJ008807","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In the flax factory in Middelstum, flax is broken by machine. The narrator has sometimes heard the breaking continue there at night.\nThe churn must be dismantled before night, otherwise the churning goes on at night. Then you hear the same motion all night long.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Winterdeis haw ik wol yn Middelstum op it flaeksfabryk arbeide. Dêr braekten wy dan mei de mesjine. Dêr gong it nachts ek wol ris op in braekjen, ik ha 't sels wolris heard.\nDe tsjerne moast foar de nacht ek útklaeid wurde, oars tsjerne it troch yn 'e nacht, dan hâldden jy de hiele nacht deselde biweging.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17377,"r":"CJ009003","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"The narrator and his wife often hear hammering at night opposite their house. They sometimes go to look, but there is nothing to be seen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy hearden beide yn 't bigjin fan ús trouwen faek timmerjen yn 'e nacht, hjir skeanoer. \"Hwa mei dêr nou noch timmerje yn 'e nacht?\", seinen wy dan.\nIk ha der wolris ôf west, om der nei to sjen, mar der wie neat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20374,"r":"CJ018703","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"When breaking flax, the farmers always tipped the bin onto its side after work. They did this to prevent the work spirits from resuming the work at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger gong it by ús jouns faek op in braekjen. Mar heit soarge der altyd foar dat de bûke op 'e side smiten woarde, as er ophâldde mei braekjen. Dy mocht fral net yn 't wurk stean bliuwe, oars gong 't de hiele nacht op in braekjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":41562,"r":"OIRSCHOT072","p":"Moergestel","v":"N.-Br.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"The kabouters (gnomes) came to work at night. When people returned to the work during the day, all the work was done. The kabouters had done it.","i":"L.H.","o":"Kabouters\n\nDe kabouters dinne 't werruk snaags. As de miense dan terug kwaome was 't werruk gedaon. Da ha'n dan de kabouters gedaon. Ik heb er wel us oat over heure vertelle, mar zoveul he'k 't toch niet van geheurd.","l":"Noord-Brabants"},{"n":20102,"r":"CJ016901","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"A farmhand often hears work spirits doing 'preparatory work' at night. The spirits are not visible.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik yn Kloosterburen by de boer wenne, wie dêr nachts faek 'voorbereiding'. Dan koe 'k net sliepe. Dan gong de tsjerne sa'n hiele nacht troch, wylst der net ien by wie. Hwant oeral is nachts 'voorbereiding' fan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20219,"r":"CJ017906","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"A man hears hammering in the evening at a place where a house was later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde faker as iens dat ik jouns let oer Eastemar nei Skûlenburch roan en dan in timmerjen hearde op it plak dêr't nou de dokter wennet, op it Heechsân.\nFuort neitiid woarde dêr it 'Hooghof' delset fan Rypke Atsma. Dat timmerjen hat foartsjirmerije west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20221,"r":"CJ017908","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Hammering is heard at night where a house is later put up.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Sumar hjir njonken, hearde ik yn 'e nacht faek timmerjen. Dat is noch mar in skoftsje lyn. Fuort dêrnei ha se dat nije hûs der delset. It wie foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20544,"r":"CJ019812","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"On a farmstead nothing is ever where it belongs: everything is moved and found again in the strangest places. This is probably the work of work spirits. The exorcist scatters some substance around and predicts that something is about to happen soon. Shortly afterwards the whole farmstead burns down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Sweagerbosk stie in boerespultsje. It gong der dêr altyd bot oan wei. De dingen rekken dêr samar fansels fan 't plak en men seach noait ien dy't it die. Se ha wol sein dat it it wurk fan wurkgeasten wie. De frou har earizer lei soms yn 'e groppe achter de kij ynpleats fan yn 'e kast. Alles kaem dêr op rare plakken tolânne. Doe binne se nei Jonge Jan tagong, de duvelbanner fan 't Wytfean. Dy is kom. Doe't er noch net oan har ta wie, sei er:\n\"Dêr wenje jim.\"\nHy bistruide de boel mei it iene en oar en sei:\n\"Nou sil hjir yn 't koart wol hwat gebeure.\"\nIn skoftsje letter is 't spul ôfbrând. De frou dy't dêr wenne hat, hat ús faek forteld, hoe't it dêr wol oanwei gong wie. Alles lei altyd oeral.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20545,"r":"CJ019813","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In the loft of a house, the lady of the house and her daughters often hear a terrible noise. One time bundles of brushwood come down from the loft for no reason; another time shoes and slippers are thrown. It is probably the work of work spirits.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ringer syn mem wenne yn Muntsjesyl, achter Kollum. Dy fortelde, tichte by har stie in hûs, dêr wenne in frou yn mei dochters. Dêr gong it der soms alderheislikst oan wei. Sy hienen dêr takkebosken op 'e souder, dy woarden soms samar yn 't achterhûs smiten. Soms woarde der ek mei toffels en skuon omsmiten. Mar sy woarden noait ien gewaer. It wiene wurkgeasten, dy't dat dienen.\nHja rekken der oan wend, seinen se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20803,"r":"CJ021404","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"A married couple could still hear the circular saw in a carpenter's workshop at night. But there was nothing to be seen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy leinen us op in kear by de âld skoalle to Waskemear. Myn man wie net thús. 't Woarde bêdtiid en ik seach út of hy der hast oankaem. Wylst ik bûten op 'e wâl stie, hearde ik yn 'e timmerwinkel hwat. 't Wienen de sirkelsagen dy't dêr gongen. Ik gong oer de brêge hinne, hwant ik woe 't better wite. Hoe koe dat nou, dat se by nacht noch oan 't wurk wienen en dan sûnder ljocht der by. 'k Seach by de timmerwinkel troch de glêzen, mar ik koe neat gewaer wurde. 'k Seach neat, mar 'k hearde de mesine gean.\n't Wie sahwat healwei tolven en ljochtmoanne waer.\n'k Ha dêr sahwat tsien minuten stien, doe kaem myn man der oan.\n\"Moast hjir us even komme,\" sei 'k, \"dêr binne se noch oan 't wurk.\"\nWy hearden 't allebeide. Der wienen gjin ljochten op. 't Wie de timmersaek fan Germ en Douwe Offringa.\nDe oare deis fregen wy: \"Binne jimme sa let noch oan 't saegjen?\"\n\"Né,\" seinen se, \"mar hwat jimme bidoele, dat gebeurt hjir nachts wol faker.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21184,"r":"CJ024704","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"A farmer often heard the sound of threshing coming from the barn at night. That was witchcraft, for the next day they really did thresh.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn omke wie boer op 'e Tike. Faker as ien kear is 't gebeurd, dat it dêr yn 'e nacht op in terskjen gong yn 'e skuorre. Dat wie foartsjirmerije, hwant de oare deis tursken se echt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21420,"r":"CJ026620","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"It sometimes happened that the churning mills kept working on their own at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde hjir wol gau us dat de tsjernmounen samar út harsels nachts troch werkten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21421,"r":"CJ026621","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In the old days the threads in the mat-weaving workshops were loosened in the evening. Otherwise the weaving would go on by itself at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wienen froeger matteweverijen. Jouns woarde der altyd ophâlden mei matteweven. Dan woarde it stel losmakke. De spanning woarde fan 'e triedden ôfnaem, oars weve it nachts troch, nei't se seinen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21895,"r":"CJ029207","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In a haunted barn all kinds of noises can be heard at night, as if work is being done: it is work spirits.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Zuurdijk by Leens wie èk in skuorre dêr't it yn spûke. As wy dêr nachts leinen, dan bigong alles dêr to skodzjen en dan bigong de tsjernmoune út himsels to draeijen. Guon fan 'e arbeiders sprongen dan wol op 'e tsjernmoune. Mar dan koenen se der noait wer ôfkomme, hwant hy draeide troch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21997,"r":"CJ031203","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Two brothers who have been visiting their girlfriends each separately hear activity in the attic at night: it is probably work spirits.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn swager Albert hie us op in snein-to-joun nei de faem west. Hy kaem thús yn 'e nacht.\nHy slepte yn 't bûthús.\nDoe't er op 't bêd soe, wie 't krekt as kladdere der ien by 't bêd op en sa gong it by de souder op. En doe wie 't ien stik gewelt op 'e souder.\nMar doe't Albert der hinne gong mei ljocht, wie der neat to sjen.\nIn pear ûren letter kaem Albert syn broer thús. Dy hie ek nei de faem west. Doe't er goed en wol lei - èk yn 't bûthús -, hearde er klear dat se oan 't pompen wienen, flak by him.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":46236,"r":"WEV017303","p":"Overschild","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of building is knocking with nothing to be seen, hearing work spirits, a moving post in a barn.","i":"F.W.","o":"Waarkgeestn.\nDei hebben wie hier zulf had bie hoes. t Was in 1959. \nIn dat joar hebben wie ain kapschuur zet. In de oorlogsjoarn wozzen wie al, dat er n keer timmerd worn zol. Want wie hebben geklop heurd op boetn; t gong “boem-boem-boem”. Ik heb dat heurd en mien oln ook. Wie gungen kiekn, of er misschain wat te zain was, moar niks heur. \nMit waarkgeestn is t zo: as ie ze heurn veur 12 uur s nachts, den wordt er binnenkört bouwd. Noa 12 uur zel t langer duurn.\nWie harn in de oorlogsjoarn wel n klain schuurtje. Ain van onze knechtn zag in dat schuurtje n poale zo moar op en doale goan. \nVolgens hom betaiknde dat ook, dat er wat gebeurn zol loater.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":22274,"r":"CJ034307","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Children are advised not to leave a book lying open in the evening before going to bed. After all, the book could then be read at night by 'the wrong folk'.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy mochten thús noait in boek iepen lizze litte foardat wy op bêd gongen, hwant oars woarde der yn 'e nacht yn lêzen troch forkeard folk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22275,"r":"CJ034308","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Children are advised not to leave a knife on the table at night, so that the night spirits do not cut themselves.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy mochten ek net in mes nachts op 'e tafel lizze litte, hwant oars snijden oaren der mei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22276,"r":"CJ034309","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Clogs must be placed upside down at night, so that others do not run off in them.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De klompen moesten fóár de nacht by ús altyd omkeard wurde, oars roannen oaren der yn om.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22277,"r":"CJ034310","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In the evening before going to bed you must tie a bit of flax around the flax brake, so that the work spirits do not do it at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der moest jouns in strike flaeks om 'e brake boun wurde, foardat de lju op bêd gongen, oars woarde der yn 'e nacht troch brake.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22278,"r":"CJ034311","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At night you must fix the spinning wheel in place, so that the work spirits do not set to work with it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It spinwiele woarde fêstset oars woarde der yn 'e nacht troch spoan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22313,"r":"CJ034505","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In a haunted house with four pear trees in front of it, spirits dance in the attic at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 'e Feanster feart, flak by de Harkema stie in hûs mei fjouwer parrebeammen. 't Wie in arbeidershûs.\nIt hûs is der wei, miskien dat dy parrebeammen der noch stean. Dêr dânsen nachts guon op 'e souder om, dan dreunde it der oer.\nDe minsken wennen dêr noait langer as in jier. Langer koenen se it net úthâlde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22335,"r":"CJ034527","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"You must fix the butter churn and the flax brake in place at night, to prevent work spirits from setting to work with them.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde wol dat de minsken nachts de tsjerne gean hearden. Dy stie foar yn 'e skuorre. Hy moest jouns ôfsluten wurde, oars tsjerne er troch.\nSa wie 't ek mei de brake. Dêr moest foar de nacht flaeks omhinne boun wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23058,"r":"CJ037602","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"A married couple always heard the beating of the flax at night beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en mem gongen der froeger om twa ûre yn 'e nacht al út. Dan moest it flaechs buike wurde. In ûre fan tofoaren hienen se dan op bêd it slaen al heard. Se binne der faek wekker fan woarn. Sy wennen doe oan 'e Godloaze Singel yn 'e Broek yn in âld húske mei houten gevel en houten skoarstien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23072,"r":"CJ037616","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In the old days people often heard the flax brake at work. If they tied a handful of flax around it in the evening, they were not troubled at all.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger hearden se nachts faek, dat de brake gong.\nAs se der in hanfol flaechs omhinne bounen, foardat se op bêd gongen, dan hienen se der gjin hinder fan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23151,"r":"CJ038401","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"One night a man already heard the sound of the next day's churning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit wie yn syn jonge jierren boerefeint by âlde Bonne Algra yn Sumar.\nIt gebeurde wol us dat er fan 'e faem kom op mandei-to-moarn. Hy wie dan noch lang net thús, dan hearde er ûnderweis al dat se by Bonne Algra oan it terskjen wienen. Ien slach fan it terskjen hearde hy boppe alles út. Dat wie de slach fan Jean-om. De oare slach wie lichter.\nDeselde moarns, mar folle letter bigong it terskjen, dêr't hy de lûden al fan yn 'e nacht heard hie.\nEk hearde er soms, as er fan 'e faem kom, dat de tsjernmoune gong. Dy rekke pas de oerdeis oan 'e gong.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23606,"r":"CJ040303","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Two little sisters sometimes heard the sounds of the next day's work in the shop at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn pake en dy oan memme kant wienen Bosgra's. Hja hienen kwekerije en siedhandel. Dat sied waerd altyd waegen op skealjes en yn pûden oerdien.\nDan gongen de reizgers der mei op stap dy't it ûnderweis forkochten.\nLammert Kromkamp moest it sied altyd wage.\nMem en har suster wienen doe noch bern, mar dy hearden faek fantofoaren hwat der gebeure soe.\nMem sei: \"O, o, hwat wie 't fannacht wer drok.\nLammert wie wer sa oan 't slepen en de skealjes en de gewichten gongen al mar.\"\nPake sei: \"Nou, dan komt der wer wurk oan 'e winkel. Dêr haw ik it leaver om.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23608,"r":"CJ040305","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Before a new stable was built for some people, they already heard the hammering.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha hjir yndertiid in nij bûthús krigen. Fan tofoaren doe ha wy en ús folk it wol timmerjen heard by nacht. Wy ha der wol binaud fan west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23699,"r":"CJ041101","p":"Peize","v":"Dr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"If a handful of flax was left under the flax brake after work, the brake could be heard going all night long.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir waerd froeger in hiele bulte braekt troch de earme minsken. Liet men in hânfol flaechs ûnder 'e brake sitte, dan hearde men yn 'e nacht de brake gean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23735,"r":"CJ041312","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"If you do not take the reed off the mat loom before nightfall, the weaving goes on during the night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As jy de kaem fan 't mattestel net der út dogge foar de nacht, dan wurdt der yn 'e nacht trochweefd, wurdt der sein. (Se weefden froeger matten yn Houtigehage en Boelensloane)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24204,"r":"CJ044901","p":"Harlingen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"A boatman's family sometimes heard knocking in the ship at night. They believed it was the work spirits.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Toen wij in 't Hoornse diep lagen met het schip hoorde het 's avonds precies alsof ze aan 't kloppen waren in 't schip. Moeke sei dat waren werkgeesten die bij ons in 't schip bezig waren."},{"n":24243,"r":"CJ045118","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At a haunted spot the rattling roll of wagons can be heard at night. When two mates go to take a look, there is nothing to be seen. It is a foreshadowing of work that will be done in the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw ris nei Ulrum ta west to flaechsteppen mei de keppel. Wy moesten dêr yn in skuorre sliepe. De keppelbaes warskôge ús en sei, it spûke dêr yn dy skuorre. Der stienen weinen op 'e telle dy bigongen alle nachten to ratteljen, sei er.\nIk en in maet fan my wienen net bang. Wy seinen wy sille fannacht wekker bliuwe en as dy weinen dan bigjinne, geane wy der hinne om to sjen.\nDoe't dan dy weinen wer oan 't ratteljen en oan 't roljen wienen, gongen wy der op ôf. Mar doe wie der neat, alles wie stil. Doe't wy ús wer deljown hienen bigong it wer.\n't Wie foartjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24565,"r":"CJ047508","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In a certain village many mats used to be woven. At night weaving sounds could sometimes already be heard in that village: an omen. The sound of the flax brake, the churn or the flail could sometimes be heard at night as well.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger woarde der yn 'e Houtigehage in protte matte-weefd. \nAs it nacht wie, dan hearden se de slaggers wol, dêr't se matten mei weefden. Dat wie tsjirmerij. It bitsjutte safolle as dat der de oare deis wer weefd wurde soe.\nSoms ek brake it yn 'e nacht troch. Dat wie ek tsjirmerije.\nIt tsjerne ek wolris troch yn 'e nacht.\nEn soms gong de flaeije yn 'e nacht. Dan soe der de oare deis tursken wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24938,"r":"CJ050708","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"If tools and implements are not properly put away at a certain farm, the work spirits set to work with them at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Grinzer Pein tsjinne in faem by de boer. Terpstra hiet dy boer. Dêr op dy plaets moest jouns alles sekuer opburgen wurde. Dienen se dat net, dan gong it dêr bot oan wei yn 'e nacht. De wein moest opburgen wurde yn 't weinhok. Lieten se him op 'e telle stean, dan rolle er nachts al mar hinne en wer. En de flaeijen sloegen yn 'e nacht en al sokke dingen mear. 't Wienen werkgeesten dy't dan warber wienen.\nDe faem woe dêr net langer bliuwe en hat de tsjinst opsein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25621,"r":"CJ055804","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At a farmer's place people heard the churning mill all night long.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha us op 'e Grinzer klaei by de boer west, doe gong dêr yn 'e nacht hyltyd de tsjernmoune.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26293,"r":"CJ060509","p":"Earnewâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"One night a few men are fishing on the Foxholstermeer and hear someone brewing. But there is nothing to be seen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In âld man út Grinslân fortelde my, op 'e Foxholster Mar wienen syn heit en syn omke yn 'e nacht oan 't fiskjen. Doe hearden se dúdlik dat der guon oan 't broujen wienen. Hja der hinne to sjen, mar it wie sa net. Der wie neat. Even letter gong it wèr op in broujen. Hwat dat west hat ha se noait bigrepen hawn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25322,"r":"CJ053201","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At a certain place a new church is busily being built during the day. A man also hears all kinds of noises at night, as if work is being done.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik kom ris yn 'e nacht Houtigehage del. 't Wie oeral donker. Se wienen oerdeis mei in nij tsjerkje oan 't bouwen. Dan gong it drok op in timmerjen. Mar ik hearde dêr dy nachts klear dat se mei balken en planken oan 't smiten wienen. It bounze der oer.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25561,"r":"CJ055313","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"When people do not finish their work in the evening, they sometimes place a doll or a little animal beside it. Then at night they hear the work being done.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik kin wol minsken, as dy it wurk jouns net dien krigen, dan setten se der in popke by del, ek wolris in beestje.\nDan hearden se nachts wol hoe't der wurke woarde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25694,"r":"CJ056227","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At night a bunch of flax must be tied around the flax brake, otherwise the work spirits keep working through the night. And that is the devil's work. The threshing must also be cleared away, otherwise threshing goes on all night. And the cups must be stacked before going to bed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wurkgeesten binne nachts warber. Mar men mat dat forhinderje, hwant it is duvelswurk. Dêrom mat men foar de nacht om 'e brake altyd in boskje flaeks hinne bine, hwant oars braekt it nachts.\nMei 't terskjen mat de tersk jouns òf hielendal ôf wêze, of men mat de tersk yn 'e bân lizze. Die men dat net, dat wie bislist net fortroud, hwant dan woarde der de hiele nacht troch tursken.\nDe kopkes moesten foar it nei-bêd-gean ynelkoar set wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25823,"r":"CJ057201","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"A vessel with wooden hatches was always haunted at night. The work spirits then made everything flap. But there was never anything to be seen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Frjentsjer lei in fartúch mei houten lûken der foar. 't Wie dêr net plús. Der wienen nachts altiten werkgeesten dwaende. Dan gong it op in flapperjen, dan wie 't rounom lawaei. Wy ha 't wol faek heard. Mar wy ha noait hwat sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25962,"r":"CJ058023","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At the farmer's the churning sometimes started at night. That meant there would be churning again the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e klaei gebeurde 't wol dat nachts by de boer de tsjerne gong. Dat wie foartjirmerij. De oare deis woarde der wer tsjerne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25991,"r":"CJ058208","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"People sometimes heard the flax brake going at night. That meant flax would be broken again the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By ús heit en mem op 'e Skieding hearden se nachts faek de brake gean. Dan stompte mem heit oan op bêd en sei: \"Jan, hearst de brake wol?\" It wie foartjirmerije.\nDan gong it de oare deis wer op in braekjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26017,"r":"CJ058313","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In the old days farmhands slept in the hay in the barn. At night the work spirits came and stuck pitchforks into the hay.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doar was in man die heette fan Piter, die warkte feul op 'e Groninger klei. Myn mem dy warkte doar ook eens met hem bij deselfde boer. Piter sloapte doar in de schuur in 't hooi. Moar doar waren warkgeesten. Midden in de nacht kwoamen doar fan dy geesten en die stoken met forken in 't hooi, \"roerend bij mij langs\", sei Piter. Hy is fan binaudens noar onderen flogen.\nSe woaren doar toen oan 't flasteppen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26049,"r":"CJ058513","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"When people heard flax being broken at night, they knew it would really happen the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As wy nachts hearden dat it op in flaechsbraken gong, koe men der mar fan op oan dat it de oare deis gebeurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26363,"r":"CJ061016","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"After the flax breaking, the beater of the flax brake is fixed in place, otherwise it goes on all night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As wy jouns braekt hienen en wy soenen op bêd, dan setten wy earst de klapper fan 'e brake fêst. Oars hearden wy de hiele nacht de brake gean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26839,"r":"CJ061301","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"If you step out of your slippers when going to bed, the work spirits get into them. If you place them with the heels against the bed, you will not be troubled by nightmares.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger seinen se altyd: as jo sa út 'e toffels stappe en jo gean op bêd, dan komme der werkgeesten en dy stappe yn jou toffels om.\nDan bigjint it spinnewiel to draeijen en al soksoarte dingen mear. Né, de toffels moesten mei de hakken tsjin 't bedsket oan stean, dan krige men ek gjin lêst fan 'e nachtmerjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26840,"r":"CJ061302","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At night you must tie some grass around it, otherwise it turns to flax breaking at night. The churn must be fixed in place, otherwise it starts churning, and the spinning wheel turns. You must stack the cups and little pans, otherwise they will be standing in the cupboard the next morning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foar de nacht moest men in eintsje flaechs om 'e brake hinne wuolje, oars gong it yn 'e nacht op in braekjen.\nDe tsjerne moest fêstset wurde, oars gong it op in tsjernjen. It spinwiele krektsa.\nDe kopkes en pantsjes moesten yn elkoar set wurde, oars stienen se de oare moarns yn 'e kast.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26841,"r":"CJ061303","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"When it thunders and the weather turns bad, the boys must all smoke with hay in their pipes. During thunder the stove is lit, the copperware is done and the mirror is turned around or covered with a cloth.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As it tongere en it woarde swier waer, dan moesten de jonges allegearre smoke mei hea yn 'e pipe.\nMei tonger woarde de kachel oanset. It koperwurk woarde bidutsen en de spegel woarde omkeard of der woarde in doek oer hinne dien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26850,"r":"CJ061401","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Someone lives in a wood in Harkema, and one evening he suddenly hears oats being threshed in the attic, but there is nothing to be seen. In spring he decides to thresh a bit of oats in the attic, and after that the threshing sound disappears.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wenne yn 'e Harkema yn 'e Bosk. Ik lei jouns krekt op bêd, dan bigoun it to terskjen fan jewelste op 'e souder. Ik hie dêr hwat hjouwer. Ik gong der ôf om to sjen, mar der wie neat to rêdden. Ik roan om 't hiele hûs hinne, oeral seach ik: neat to sjen.\n't Woarde Maitiid. Ik tocht: ik sil dat stikje hjouwer op 'e souder ôfslaen. Doe't ik dat dien hie, ha 'k it noait wer terskjen heard by ús yn 'e hûs, doe wienen de lûden fuort.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26851,"r":"CJ061402","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At another person's place in Harkema flax is always broken with the flax brake at night, and at yet another's the churning goes on all night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By oare lju yn 'e Harkema woarde nachts altyd braekt. Dat gong altyd troch. By ús net, hwant ik haw noait braekt.\nIk haw ek wol in hûs kend, der gong de tsjerne altyd de hiele nacht troch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27202,"r":"CJ064108","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In Bilt, labourers broke a heap of flax with the flax brake, which is fastened in the evening, otherwise it goes on braking all night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha yn 't Bilt wenne. Dêr woarde in soad brake troch de arbeiders. Jouns foardat men op bêd gong woarde de brake fêst set, oars braekten se de hiele nacht troch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27216,"r":"CJ064204","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"My uncle went to the Groningen clay country to mow with the scythe for a farmer. An old man there has already made up his bed in a clean, empty liquid-manure tank. Nobody wants to sleep in it because a dead man once lay in it. At night you are shaken back and forth in it, and the machines do not stop during the night. That night, however, the old man is not shaken back and forth, but the machines are constantly moving and do not stay in the same place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In omke fan my hat ris nei de Grinzer klaei ta west to sichtsjen, by in boer. Dêr wie ek in âld man, dy hie syn bêd klear makke yn in skjinne lege jarrebak.\nDêr woe oars net ien yn sliepe, hwant der hie ris in deade man yn dy bak lein. Sûnt woarden de minsken dy't dêr yn leinen nachts altyd hinne en wer set yn 'e skuorre.\nDe masinen stienen de hiele nacht net stil. Dy gongen de hiele nacht hinne en wer.\nDy âld man wie dy nachts net hinne en wer set woarn. Mar de masinen wienen de hiele nacht yn biweging en dy bleauwen net op itselde plak, sei er. Dat hied er sels sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27258,"r":"CJ064331","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In Groningen there are haunted barns where wagons drive back and forth across the floor in the middle of the night. This means they will be used the next day. You also hear peat-cutting and flax-braking. All of this is foretelling.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Grinslân hienen se spoekskuorren, mar ik ha noait yn sa'n ien west. Wol ha 'k it meimakke, dat de weinen dêr midden yn 'e nacht op 'e telle hinne en wer rieden. Dat bitsjutte, dat se de oare deis wer brûkt wurde soenen.\nIk ha 't ek wol heard dat der midden yn 'e nacht tursken woarde en ek wol dat se oan 't braken wienen yn 'e nacht. Dat wie allegear foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27270,"r":"CJ064410","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"It sometimes happens that at night the butter churn starts turning by itself, and sometimes the winnowing machine too. This is an omen of what will be done the following day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde by de boeren wol gauris dat yn 'e nacht samar fansels de tsjerne bigong to draeijen en ek de winen draeiden soms samar yn 'e nacht. (de winen dêr moest it sied troch skifte wurde) Dit wie foartsjirmerij. De oare deis soe 't dan wer op in tsjernjen en wynjen gean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27282,"r":"CJ064501","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At night people often hear flax being worked. The next day flax is then braked.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger gebeurde it faek, dat wy yn 'e nacht it boekjen fan it flaechs hearden. Dat wie altyd tjirmerije. Dan koe men der mar fêst fan op oan, dat it de oare deis wer op in braekjen gong.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27324,"r":"CJ064908","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"The churn had to be fastened after work, otherwise churning went on all night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De karn moest fastset worden, anders werd der in de nacht doorgekarnd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27447,"r":"CJ065703","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In the old days it sometimes happened that the churn kept working at night. That was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik jong wie gebeurde it wol dat de tsjerne nachts gong; dat gebeurde mei in rad dêr't de pols mei yn 'e tsjerne gong. Dat neame se in wige.\nDeis hienen se it hynder der foar. Mar nachts gong it mei de wige. 't Wie foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27683,"r":"CJ068302","p":"Noordwijk","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Paulus Paulusma murdered a certain Berghuis.\nPaulus Paulusma sometimes heard hammering at night. He always said that another coffin would have to be made. And that was always the case.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Sumar wenne Paulus Paulusma. Dy hat in moard dien. Hy hat in sekere Berghuis fan Strobos formoarde.\nDêr wenne ek in stelmakker. Paulus hearde dêr soms nachts getimmer. Dan sei er: \"Der sil moarn ek wer in lykkiste timmere wurde.\" It kom altyd nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27722,"r":"CJ068519","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In the old days it sometimes happened that the churn kept going at night. That meant there would be churning again the next day. This also happened with the flax brake, but people could prevent it by putting flax around the brake. And sometimes threshing was heard at night. That too was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde yn 'e Harkema wol faek dat de tsjerne yn 'e nacht troch gong. Dat wie foartsjirmerije. Dan tsjernen se de oare deis wer. Ik ha wol guon kend dy't altyd in toppe flaechs om 'e brake hinne dienen as se ophâldden mei braekjen, oars gong it yn 'e nacht op in braekjen.\nDer woarde nachts ek faek tursken. Dat wie ek foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27814,"r":"CJ069401","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"People sometimes heard banging from the boathouse where the lifeboat was kept. This was seen as an omen: the boat would soon have to go out again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger hienen se hjir in reddingsboat. Dy lei yn in boathûs. Sa nou en dan wie der in bouns yn dat boathûs. Guon hearden dat. Dan seinen se: \"'t Spookt ek wer yn 'e reddingboat. De boat moat der yn 't koart wer op út.\" It woarde as foartsjirmerij biskôge.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27861,"r":"CJ069813","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"It sometimes happened that the churning mill was running at night. Then the work spirits were at work.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde wol faek dat 'e tsjernmoune gong yn 'e nacht. Dat wie it wurk fan 'e wurkgeasten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27878,"r":"CJ070006","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In some places, flax-braking or threshing used to be heard at night. That was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op guon plakken woarde nachts brake. En ik haw ek wolris heard dat der nachts ergens tursken woarde. 't Wie foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27941,"r":"CJ070601","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"People sometimes heard the gnomes spinning at the spinning wheel at night. At the carpenter's, hammering was sometimes heard at night. That meant another coffin had to be made the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Gebeurde wol dat minsken yn 'e nacht it spinnewiel hearden. Dan waerd der spoun. Dat wie 't wurk fan 'e kabouters, waerd der sein.\nBy de timmerman gebeurde 't wol dat se dêr yn 'e nacht timmerjen hearden. Dan seinen sei: \"Der sil ek gau wer ien stjerre, hwant by de timmerman wienen se al mei de lykkiste oan 'e gong.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28077,"r":"CJ071701","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"A family sometimes heard at night in their house flax being carried up to the attic, and a little later the sound of braking.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr't nou de Betonwei is yn 'e Harkema, dêr ha wy froeger wenne, tsjin it hûs oer dêr't Ate Stoarm wennet. Soms hearden wy dat der by ús yn 'e nacht flaechs nei de souder droegen woarde. Dan gong 't even letter wer op in braekjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28094,"r":"CJ071801","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"People sometimes heard the oars of the lifeboat moving at night. That meant it would soon go out again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der stiet hjir in garage yn Moddergat. Froeger wie dêr de reddingboat yn. De minsken hearden nachts, as de boat der yn stie, dat se mei de rimen omsmieten.\nDat bitsjutte dat de boat der mei gauwens wer op út farre soe. It is nou in garage.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28109,"r":"CJ071816","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"It sometimes happened that the churning mill was running at night. People did not know what it was.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Gebeurde wol dat de tsjernmoune gong yn 'e nacht.\n\"Hwat dat wer is, dat witte wy net\", seinen wy dan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28163,"r":"CJ072110","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Tools always had to be put away in the evening, otherwise the work spirits would set to work with them at night. Then there would be threshing, chopping, flax-braking, churning, and so on.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Soms gong de tsjernmoune nachts. Dy moesten se earst altyd út it wurk sette.\nDe wine gong nachts ek wol om deselde reden.\nDe brake gong nachts ek, as se him net fêstsetten mei in boskje flaechs der om hinne.\nDer woarde nachts ek tursken as se de flaeijen samar op 't sied yn 'e skuorre lizze lieten. De flaeijen moesten ophong wurde. De bile moest foaral net yn 't blok stean bliuwe, hwant dan woarde der de hiele nacht troch kapt.\nDe spinwiele moest ek út it wurk wei, oars spinde it de hiele nacht troch.\nFoar sokke dingen warskôgen heit en mem altyd. Dan wienen nachts de nachtgeasten warber.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28393,"r":"CJ074227","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"People sometimes heard the churn going at night, or the beating of the flail.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha faek heard dat de tsjerne yn 'e nacht troch gong - dat dat sein woarde, en ek dat se yn 'e nacht de kloppen fan 'e flaljes hearden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28450,"r":"CJ074722","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Sometimes people heard the churning mill working at night. They heard the horse going round. That was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Falom, op 'e Breedte gebeurde 't faek, dat de tsjernmoune yn 'e nacht gong. Hja hearden it hynder klear yn 'e rounte gean. Dat wie foartjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28509,"r":"CJ075614","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"It sometimes happens that the butter churn or the flax brake runs at night. It is an omen of what will happen the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde froeger faek dat de tsjerne yn 'e nacht gong, of de brake of dat der tursken woarde yn 'e nacht. Dat wie foartjirmerij. De oaredeis gebeurde it yn werklikheit.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28623,"r":"CJ076707","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"On a farm in Veenwouderwal, churning and threshing are often heard at night without anything being seen. Sometimes flax-braking is heard too.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Feanwâldsterwâl stie in boerespul, dêr gong nachts altyd de tsjernmoune. Wy ha 't faek heard. En dochs wie 't sa net as men der hinne gong to sjen.\nEk it terskjen yn 'e nacht waerd gauris heard.\nUs heit braekte ek. Ik wie in jonkje fan in jier of acht, dan sei mem soms midden yn 'e nacht, as se op bêd leinen, tsjin heit: \"Mast ris hearre Tsjipke, de brake giet èk noch.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28624,"r":"CJ076708","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"You must put the spinning wheel away before night, otherwise it will go on spinning all night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Spinwiele mat men foar de nacht net yn 't wurk stean litte, oars wurdt der yn 'e nacht trochspoun.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":41735,"r":"OIRSCHOT003114","p":"Haaren","v":"N.-Br.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Gnomes help with work; they disappear when they are seen.","i":"A.v.O.","o":"Kabouterhulp\nVruuger hadde ok kabouters die ok kwaome helluppe, mee de vlegel dorse. Mar as de kabouters kwaome moeste d'r ut blijve, want as ze oe zaoge waore ze inins vertrokke. Da mogge ze nie zien dage ze zaag, Da waore kleine mennekus.","l":"Brabants"},{"n":29362,"r":"CJ080716","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At night labourers already heard the flax-braking of the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By it flaechsbraekjen moest it flaechs bûke wurde.\nIt gebeurde faek dat wy dat bûkjen de nachts fan tofoaren al hearden. Dat wie foartjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29396,"r":"CJ081015","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In some places people heard the churn going at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha wol plakken kend, dêr hearden se nachts altyd de tsjerne gean. Dat wie yn Boelensloane.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32955,"r":"CJ085008","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At one house, when people were going to brake flax, they heard the sound of braking beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By ús heit en dy hearden se earen, as se braekje soenen, fan tofoaren de lûden fan 'e brake al.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34443,"r":"CJ086601","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"A carpenter sometimes heard a coffin being made at night. A few days later he always really had to make a coffin.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn 'e Rotfalle hat earen in timmerman wenne. Se ha my wolris forteld, dat dy timmerman soms yn 'e nacht biweging yn 't hout hearde. Dat wie krekt itselde lûd as hwannear't er in deakiste timmere.\n't Soe noait misse as dan waerd der mei gauwens wer in kiste troch him makke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33195,"r":"CJ087718","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At a farm people heard at night the milk churns being put on the wagon. In reality that only happened during the day. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op Japik Mulders plaets op it Wytfean woarden midden yn 'e nacht de bussen samar op 'e wein set en rieden se fuort to melken. Yn werklikheit gebeurde dat earst yn 'e moarn. Mar de minsken dy't dêr wennen hearden it dúdlik.\nDat wie in gefal fan foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34635,"r":"CJ094201","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"One day a brother of our father passes through the Suameer. At one spot he hears hammering, but sees nothing. Later a farmhouse is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In broer fan ús heit kom us op in jountiid let noch troch Sumar. Doe't er dêr de Lânsbuorren lâns roan, hearde er dêr op in plak timmerjen. Hy sjen en sjen, mar der wie neat to rêdden.\nLetter woarde der op dat plak in plaets delset.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33715,"r":"CJ093601","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At a carpenter's, hammering could always be heard a few nights before someone died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn pake wie timmerman yn 'e Rottefalle. Bloembergen hiet er. It gebeurde faek dat er in deakiste meitsje moest. Dan wie 't wolris dat er in nacht of trije fan tofoaren it getimmer oan dy kiste al hearde. Dan libbe deselde noch dy't der yn to lizzen kom. Dat kom altyd nei.\nEk oare lju ha dyselde lûden wol by myn pake heard yn 'e nacht. Dan seinen se: \"Der sil gau wer ien stjerre. Wy ha de timmerman al oan syn kiste timmerjen heard.\"\nPake rûkte it soms èk fan tofoaren. Hwant oan in deakiste siet altyd in aparte reuk. Dat wie de reuk fan it swartsel, dat se op it hout fan 'e kiste smarden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33743,"r":"CJ0940b01","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In the old days the flax brake had to be tied down with rope at night, otherwise the braking would go on.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men moest de brake fêstbine foar de nacht, mei in tou deromhinne, hwant oars woarde der yn 'e nacht braekt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33786,"r":"CJ094306","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"After work the farmers had to put their tools away, otherwise the work spirits would set to work with them at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As se by de boeren oan 't terskjen wienen, moasten der maetregels nom wurde foar de nacht. As de skeaven klear leinen om tursken to wurden, en hja lieten se sa lizze foar de nacht dan bigoun it yn 'e nacht fansels to terskjen. Dat wie it wurk fan 'e wurkgeesten. In lech moest earst hielendal ôfmakke wêze. Earder hâldde it folk net op. (Sa wie 't gebrûk yn 'e Rottefalle).","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33787,"r":"CJ094307","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Equipment such as the churning mill, the spinning wheel and the flax brake had to be put away at night, otherwise the work spirits would set to work with it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In tsjernmoune lieten se jouns net yn 't wurk stean, hwant dan bigoun er de nachts út himsels to draeijen (wurkgeesten). Hy moest dus foar de nacht út it wurk nom wurde. Ek it spinnewiel moest foar de nacht út it wurk wei, oars waerd der yn 'e nacht spoun.\nEk de brake mocht net yn 't wurk stean bliuwe, oars woarde der yn 'e nacht braekt.\nIt wie ek sa mei 't breidzjen. Dat moest yn elkoar rolle wurde, oars woarde der nachts breide.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36055,"r":"CJ096201","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Before the Christian school in Boelensloane was built, some people already heard sounds of hammering in the evening while there was still nothing to be seen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foardat de Kristlike Skoalle yn Boelensloane der wie hawwe guon dêr in kear of hwat timmerjen heard, krekt as woarde der in hûs boud. Se hearden it by jountiid.\nBoele Koekoek en de meester wienen der ek by. As se der hinne gongen to sjen wie der neat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12976,"r":"YPFOE127c","p":"Nieuwe Bildtzijl","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"When the skippers go ashore, they hear at night hammering on the wooden ships. It sounds as if a number of men are at work, but when the skippers go to look, there is nothing to be seen. When the skippers are in bed, the sound starts again. It also happens that when workmen arrive in the peat bog, at night they hear full wheelbarrows going over the planks, and then hear a load of sand being dumped.","i":"Y.P.","o":"Foartsjirmerij by ambachtslju\nAs de skippers oan 'e helling leinen, dan koe it barre, dat se nachts de breauhammers slaan hearden. Dat wie yn 'e tiid fan 'e houtene skûten. Der waard breaud en dan waard der mar bot op timmere. Se hearden soms tige dúdlik, dat der in man of wat oan 't wurk wienen, mar as se der hinne gyngen, dan wie der neat en alles wie stil. Lykwols, as se har wer deljoegen, dan wie 't der daadlik op 'e nij.\nIk ha sels ek wol ris sokssawat heard. Dan wienen wy yn it fean oankommen. En de jûns of de nachts foardat wy begûnen te laden, dan hearden wy it: de kroaden rieden oer de planken en, boem! dêr gyng in kroadfol yn 't rom. Dat gyng: plof! Mar der wie neat.","l":"Fries"},{"n":36106,"r":"CJ096502","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In the old days, when the barn was full of grain in autumn, we sometimes heard the sound of threshing in the evening, though it only really happened much later. We then heard the \"foresound\" of the threshing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger, as wy by uzes thús de skuorre fol sied hienen by 't hjerst, gebeurde 't wol dat wy jouns dêr terskjen hearden. Mar it echte terskjen gebeurde pas letter. Wy hienen dan de foarklank der fan heard. Wy wennen doe yn Drachten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36237,"r":"CJ097501","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"One evening two men heard sounds of building work coming from a house. But nobody was working there. Later that house was demolished, and a new house was indeed built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit roan mei noch in man op in joun tusken Oerterp en de Lange Wyk by Drachten. 't Wie donker. Hja kommen by in hûs, dêr gong it bot op in timmerjen en saegjen.\nHja tochten: hoe kin dit sa let op 'e joun - En hja dêrhinne to sjen. Mar dêr wie net in minske warber en der wienen ek gjin lûden mear.\nOp 't lêst gongen se fuort. Se seinen: Dit is foartjirmerij.\nLetter is dat hûs dêr ôfbrutsen, en der kom in nij foar yn it plak.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36321,"r":"CJ097801","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"A woman from Westerein heard hammering in places where building would later take place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wenne in frou yn 'e Westerein, dy hearde 't op ûnderskate plakken timmerjen. Yn werklikheid gebeurde dat net. It minske sei: De Westerein wurdt o sa great en rekket rounom bikend. It wurdt in stêd gelyk. Mar it sil net dien reitsje.\nIt wie Gjerte Rinskje har mem dy't dat timmerjen allegear hearde. It minske hat gelyk krige.\nSe sizze wol: Der falt noch gjin blêd fan 'e beam of dêr is foartsjirmerije fan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36342,"r":"CJ097901","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"In the old days people often heard hammering where houses would later be built, and saw houses burning before it happened.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie hjir froeger allegear foartsjirmerij. Oeral hearden se fan to foaren timmerjen op plakken dêr't letter huzen kamen to stean en it gebeurde ek wol dat se seinen: dat of dat hûs mat nochris opbarne. Wy ha 't al barnen sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36516,"r":"CJ098805","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"The narrator's grandfather was a carpenter. One night he heard hammering nearby. Some time later a house was built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie in âlde pake, dy wenne yn Sweagerbosk. Hy wie timmerman. Hy sei op in moarn: \"Der hat fannacht sa'n getimmer west, hjir flak by yn 'e buert, der sil grif wer hwat gebeure.\"\nIn skoft letter waerd der njonken him in hûs boud.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36639,"r":"CJ099309","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Sometimes churning was done in the middle of the night without anyone being there. That was an omen and meant that churning would be done the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde wolris dat de tsjerne midden yn 'e nacht gong, sûnder dat der ien by wie. Dat wie foartsjirmerije. It bitsjutte dat er de oare deis wer draeije soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36802,"r":"CJ100401","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"My mate and I went along with a small group to Texel. We slept in the hay at a farmer's, in a spot that had not yet been boarded up. In the middle of the night we clearly heard the sounds of carpentry.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik en myn maet wienen mei de keppel op it eilân Texel.\nDoe't it wurk dêr biret wie bleauwen wy dêr togearre noch in skoftsje by in boer yn 'e bollen. Wy sliepten neist elkoar yn in nije pleats, dy't noch net ôftimmere wie, op hwat hea.\nYn 'e nacht woarden myn maet en ik beide wekker.\nIk sei tsjin myn maet: \"Hearst it wol?\"\n\"Jawol\", sei er.\nWy hearden dúdlik timmerjen, flakby. It gong oan ien stik troch.\nDe oare deis gong it wer drok op in timmerjen oan 'e pleats.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37195,"r":"CJ103102","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"A mate and I slept in a farmer's barn. Every night we heard the sound of the dung cart spreading manure, but in reality that only happened during the day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw yn 't wurk west yn Wikel by in boer, in sekere Atsma. Ik hie in maet by my en wy sliepten togearre yn 't bêdsté yn 't bûthús.\nDoe sei de boer tsjin ús: \"Hearre jim wolris hwat nachts? Us foarige feint woe hjir net langer bliuwe hwant der wienen nachts altiten lûden yn 't bûthús. Mar ik ha jim dêr net oer heard.\"\nDoe sei myn maet: \"Fannacht haw ik in skoft wekker lein. Ik hearde klear dat se de dongkroade ta 't bûthús yn rieden en dat se de skeppe op 'e kroade smieten en dat se de dong yn 'e kroade skepten.\"\nDy lûden wienen dêr alle nachten. Mar wy ha noait hwat sjoen. It wie foartjirmerij, hwant hwat wy hearden gebeurde de oare moarns yn werklikheit.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37396,"r":"CJ104104","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"At the time the Reformed church was being built, Romke once walked past it in the dark. He heard the sounds of carpentry but saw nothing. He called out and was answered that the church had to be finished.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De grifformearde tsjerke fan Stiensgea wurdt faek de pypketsjerke neamd omdat der in pypke ûnder 'e wei troch rint.\n't Wie yn 'e tiid dat se dêr mei oan 't bouwen wienen.\nOp in joun hiel let, - 't wie hiel tsjuster - doe kaem Romke Laanstra dêr lâns. Doe hearde er dêr timmerjen. En dochs wie 't tsjuster. Dat moest de duvel wêze, dat koe net oars.\nRomke sei: \"Dû bist ek noch let oan 'e gong.\"\nDoe kom der in antwurd út 'e tsjerke wei: \"Ik wol 't klear ha.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31061,"r":"CJ115127","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"If in the evening you do not put away the work you were busy with during the day, it will be worked on at night by the wrong hands.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jouns foardat men op bêd giet moat men it breidzjen oprolje, oars wurdt der yn 'e nacht fierder breide en komt it forkeard. Ek it théguod mat men yn elkoar sette, it spinwiele út it wurk sette, de brake oan kant en al sa mear. Hwant dêr reitsje oars yn 'e nacht kweade hannen oer gear.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31111,"r":"CJ115506","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0061","d":"Gnomes sometimes do people's work at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De ierdmantsjes dogge soms foar de minsken it wurk yn 'e nacht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":50057,"r":"BLECOURTNB0063","p":"Bergeijk","v":"N.-Br.","y":1837,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul sees a funeral procession in the evening. His prediction that his sick wife will die within three days comes true.","i":"P.N.P.","o":"2.17. Een man met den helm geboren\nDaniël van Poppel, geboren te Rotterdam, doch den meesten tijd van zijn lang leven te Luiksgestel gewoond hebbende, was met den helm ter wereld gekomen, zooals zijne zonen en andere lieden mij dikwijls verklaard hebben.\nToen hij reeds den ouderdom van 80 jaar bereikt had, ging hij op éénen dag van Luiksgestel naar 's Bosch, om eene dochter te bezoeken die daar woonde: hij toefde bij haar eenigen tijd en stierf er. Deze man had een sterk gestel en een onbevreesd karakter, daar- enboven een voorgevoel van vele toekomende dingen, en dewijl hij met den helm (d.i. een vliesje aan één of beide oogen) geboren was, ontmoette hij vele nachfverschijnselen van allerlei soort. Hij heeft in zijne woonplaats Luiksgestel o.a. het beroep van verkensslachter uitgeoefend en toen hij, in 1837, op zekeren avond door de Hasseltsche straat huiswaarts ging, zag hij aldaar eenen rouw of eene lijkstatie. Thuis gekomen, vertelde hij aan zijne kinderen dat zijne vrouw, die reeds lang ziek was, nu geene drie dagen meer zou leven, omdat hij eenen rouw gezien had. Zijne vrouw stierf inderdaad binnen de drie dagen."},{"n":50010,"r":"BLECOURTNB0016","p":"Veldhoven","v":"N.-Br.","y":1889,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing a funeral procession between twelve and one at night; a few days later the neighbour is buried in the same way.","i":"J.C.","o":"1.16. Een rouw\nEen inwoner van Netersel zag des nachts tusschen twaalf en één uur een rouwstoet langzaam en plechtstatig op den openbaren weg voortschrijden. Voorop gingen de vier dragers met de lijkbaar; achter hen aan stapten twaalf mannen, in rouwmantels gehuld, met omfloersten hoed, en veertien vrouwen, in falies gewikkeld, zwijgend voort. Hij had dikwijls hooren zeggen, dat de verschijning van een rouw een zeker voorteeken was van een sterfgeval in de buurt; en inderdaad vijf dagen later werd zijn buurman ten grave gedragen, gevolgd door evenveel mannen en vrouwen, als hij in het nachtelijk uur had zien voorbijtrekken. N.B. Dergelijke verhalen heb ik hier in de omstreken meer gehoord en iemand verzekerde mij in allen ernst, dat hij zelf in den nacht een rouw had zien voorbijtrekken en dat eenige dagen naderhand in zijne buurt een lijk boven de aarde stond."},{"n":50282,"r":"BLECOURTNB0173","p":"Helmond","v":"N.-Br.","y":1891,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"On the third night before someone dies, a funeral procession goes about. Someone who passes a medlar thicket that night gets a hard blow from an invisible hand, from the mispelman (medlar man).","i":"A.H.S.","o":"In den derden nacht vóór er op het gehucht De-n-Oliemolen onder Helmond iemand stierf, trok daar ter plaatse een geheimzinnige lijkstoet rond. Als iemand in zoo'n nacht over de-n-Olie-molen ging en zekeren mispelbos, die langs den weg stond, passeerde, ontving hij van een onzichtbare hand een harden klap om de ooren. De geest, die den slag toebracht, noemde men de-n-mispelman."},{"n":50034,"r":"BLECOURTNB0040","p":"Veldhoven","v":"N.-Br.","y":1892,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"At midnight a man gets a box on the ear because he is in the way of a funeral procession that must pass.","i":"J.C.","o":"1.40. Avonturen van een vrijer \nZeker jonge boer uit H. had kennis met een meisje uit het naburige L. Van tijd tot tijd bracht de minnaar een avondbezoek aan zijne Dulcinea. Vooral des winters, wanneer er werd gekaartspeeld, werden zulke bezoeken wel eens gerekt tot de klok haar grootste aantal slagen had doen hooren en het spookuur was aangebroken. Verschillende onaangename ontmoetingen waren het gevolg. Zoo werd bedoelden persoon op zekeren nacht een ferme oorveeg toegediend, omdat hij in den weg liep, dien, naar het scheen, een lijkstoet moest passeeren, welken hij in het donker duidelijk genoeg zag voorbijtrekken."},{"n":50055,"r":"BLECOURTNB0061","p":"Bergeijk","v":"N.-Br.","y":1892,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One night a man sees a line of men in black going to the churchyard, but when he waits for them they do not come. Many people see a funeral procession, but it is thought that only people born with a caul can.","i":"P.N.P.","o":"2.15. De rouw of de lijkstatie\nEens zag Amold van der Meyden te Bergeik, in zekeren nacht aan den schutsboom in 't Eikereind, eenige achtereengaande manspersonen, elk met een zwarten rouwmantel omhangen, door de straat gaan en den weg naar het kerkhof volgen.\nNu liep hij spoedig langs het pad, dat bij den schutsboom begint en bij de kerk uitkomt, om de lijkstatie vooruit te zijn, want hij dacht ze zeker daar weder te zien, hetgeen tot zijne verwondering niet gebeurde.\nGroot is het getal van degenen, die in verschillende dorpen en plaatsen zulk eenen rouw, altijd zonder lijk of doodskist, ontmoet hebben. Doch geene andere dan 'die met den helm geboren zijn,' meenen sommige lieden, zien zulk eene vertooning."},{"n":8635,"r":"CBAK0038","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1899,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People born with a caul are more likely to see a funeral procession, and they warn others to step aside for it. They do not step aside themselves.","i":"C.B.","o":"De met een helm geborenen zien (in hun verbeelding?) een lijkstatie aankomen. Daarvoor vorderen ze eerbied en manen dan de lui aan om op zijde te gaan voor de stoet, terwijl ze zelf geen haarbreed uitwijken. Ze zien de lijkstoet een dag voor iemand sterft. Grietje Holleman bijvoorbeeld liep dan in de buurt van het huis en zeide tegen groot en klein: \"Opzij, daar komt de lijkstoet.\"\nHetzelfde deed een andere vrouw, maar alleen tegen kinderen die ze dan geducht kneep."},{"n":8758,"r":"CBAK0149","p":"Uitdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1900,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman assisting at a birth is obliged to bury or burn the caul immediately, otherwise both the newborn and whoever owns the caul can foretell things. Sailors like to own a caul so they can foresee the weather, and pay a lot for one, which encourages theft of cauls. Examples of voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of death.","i":"C.B.","o":"Van de week vertelde een Uitdammer mij, dat de zaak van met een helm geboren te worden zoo in elkaar zit. Het is de plicht van degene die assisteeren bij de partus de helm dadelijk te begraven of te verbranden, dan heeft het kind later geen last van die rarigheid (getuige Jan Boot te Uitdam, die ook met een helm is geboren en die geheel normaal is. Dit komt omdat de moeder van mijn zegsman de helm dadelijk begraven heeft). Doet men dit niet, dan heeft zoowel de met een helm geborene, als de bezitter van de helm later een voorspellende geest (getuige bijvoorbeeld iemand uit Durgerdam die vooraf storm, hoogwater etcetera voorspelt). Vandaar dat zeelui erg op het bezit van een helm zijn gesteld en er hooge prijzen voor besteden, wat hen die bij de partus assisteeren dan ook tot diefstal verlokt (zie mijn verhaal van G. Holleman). Mijn zegsman is niet bijgeloovig, doch dit gelooft hij vast (sic). Even als dat men voorboden krijgt van den dood van familieleden. Zijn broer zag bijvoorbeeld vóór het sterven van een anderen broer, toen hij voorbij de kerk ging, een lijkstatie over zijn hoofd gaan. Ook hadden de andere familieleden slagen op de deur etcetera gehoord."},{"n":8802,"r":"CBAK0187","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A farmer was born with a caul and has second sight. As he comes back from the fields with his farmhand, the farmer sees a funeral procession approaching. The farmer urges the farmhand, who is carrying milk on a yoke, to step aside. Because the farmhand sees nothing coming, he does not step aside. Then the farmhand is knocked over, and the farmer has to explain that the farmhand ran into a funeral procession.","i":"C.B.","o":"Zoo het de ouwe me dikwijls verteld dat er op Durgerdam een boer was die met een helm was geboren. Die boer kwam op een goeie morgen met de knecht oit het land. De knecht jukte een gang melk.\n\"Gaan op zaai, maat,\" zaai de boer.\nDe knecht keek vreemd op; de weg was breed en er kwam niks an.\n\"Gaan op zaai, maat,\" zei die nag er es, maar de knecht liep door.\nOpiens wordt ie me deer met emmers en al op de grond egooid.\n\"Wat is dat nou?\" kermt ie.\n\"Ja, ik hew et je wel ezaaid,\" zaai de boer: \"Der kwam een begrafenisstoet an, en die is teuge je op eloope.\""},{"n":8808,"r":"CBAK0192","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A girl with second sight, while growing more and more anxious, sees a funeral procession approaching. When she has calmed down, she says the procession has passed, but that there will soon be a death at the place where she is, which indeed happens.","i":"C.B.","o":"In de Beets was ook een meisje dat voorgevoelens had. Eens was ze weer zeer benauwd en vroeg aan een ander meisje om met haar te gaan wandelen.\nToen ze bij het laatste huisje gekomen waren, vroeg ze aan haar gezellin: \"Zie je niets?\"\n\"Neen.\"\n\"Nou, daar komt een lijkstoet aan.\"\nZij werd al benauwder.\nTen slotte bedaarde zij en zei: \"Nu is hij voorbij; nu zal er wel spoedig hier iemand sterven.\"\nDen volgenden dag was er werkelijk een sterfgeval."},{"n":8813,"r":"CBAK0197","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who sees a funeral procession approaching warns a man coming towards him to step aside. Because the other man does not step aside, the first man is struck on the cheek.","i":"C.B.","o":"Een jood uit Hoorn kwam den overgrootvader van mijn zegsman tegen. Ze kenden elkaar, maar meer ook niet.\n\"Ga op sij, ga op sij,\" riep de jood.\nDe ander week geen haarbreed van den weg af.\n\"O waai, o waai, wat wor ik op mijn wang geslagen,\" kermde de jood.\nEr was niets in de buurt. De jood had een lijkstatie zien aankomen, had, doordien de ander niet uitweek, zelf niet kunnen uitwijken, en nu een stoot tegen zijn wang gekregen."},{"n":8819,"r":"CBAK0200","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Someone born with a caul tells another person to step aside. He does not, and then he trips over a funeral procession. The next day someone dies at that place.","i":"C.B.","o":"De broer van N. Kleerenbezem liep met een Zuiderwouder die met een helm geboren was.\n\"Ga opzij,\" zei deze.\nDie broer deed het niet omdat de weg breed was. Hij struikelde. Hij was natuurlijk weer over een begrafenisstoet gestruikeld. Den volgenden dag was daar ter plaatse iemand gestorven."},{"n":9428,"r":"CBAK0567","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man with second sight sees a funeral procession before a death. He warns his farmhand to step aside, but because the farmhand sees nothing, he stays where he is and is thrown to the ground.","i":"C.B.","o":"N.N., een Durgerdammer zag, vóór er een sterfgeval in dit gehucht plaats greep, een lijkstatie aankomen. Eens waarschuwde hij zijn knecht daarvoor en beval hem op zij te gaan, om den stoet te laten passeren. Daar deze evenwel niets zag, bleef hij staan, waar hij stond. Een poos later werd hij met juk en emmers met melk, tegen den grond gegooid.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.268.)"},{"n":9429,"r":"CBAK0568","p":"Ransdorp","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who can see a funeral procession coming in advance calls on people to step aside. Nobody responds, so he cannot get out of the way himself either, and is struck on the cheek by a carrying pole.","i":"C.B.","o":"N.N., een jood uit Hoorn, kon ook lijkstaties zien aankomen, vóór iemand van zijn kennissen zou sterven. Eens stond hij te midden van een groep menschen, toen hij weer zoo'n begrafenisstoet zag aankomen.\n\"Ga op zij, ga op zij,\" riep hij, maar niemand voldeed aan zijn verzoek, omdat niemand er het noodzakelijke van inzag. Even later liep N.N. kermende weg, terwijl hij zijn hand aan zijn wang hield. Omdat niemand op zij was gegaan, had hij zelf ook niet uit kunnen wijken en had een draagstok van de burrie tegen zijn wang gestooten.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.268-269.)"},{"n":9450,"r":"CBAK0589","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman sees funeral processions; she does not step aside for them herself, but urges others to do so.","i":"C.B.","o":"Zij zag lijkstaties aankomen, vermaande ieder om op zij te gaan, maar week zelf geen haar breed uit.\n(N.B. Behalve het gesprek met haar, heb ik geen van die dingen persoonlijk met haar beleefd, en is alles mij door anderen meegedeeld.)\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.273)"},{"n":42732,"r":"KEMP102","p":"Broek","v":"L.","y":1925,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The carriage in which a young lady was riding to Maastricht one evening suddenly stopped because the horse would not go on. The young lady saw a funeral procession pass by. She told the coachman. He had seen nothing, but knew that this was a bad sign for the lady. And so it was: three days later the young lady's sister suddenly died.","i":"I.S.","o":"DE LIJKSTOET.\n\nEen jonge dame, die 's avonds laat met haar rijtuig van Maastricht naar Wijk werd gereden, voelde in de Maastrichter Brugstraat opeens het rijtuig stilstaan. Zij hoorde den koetsier het witte paard aanzetten, maar het dier wilde niet meer vooruit. Toen zij den koetsier wilde vragen, wat er gaande was, zag zij, door het raampje, een begrafenisstoet naderen. De lantaarns aan den lijkwagen brandden en een lange rij rouwkoetsen volgde. Nadat de stoet voorbij was, vroeg zij den koetsier, of hij iets had gezien. Hij antwoordde ontkennend, maar had aan het paard gemerkt, dat het iets bijzonders zag. De jongedame vertelde nu, wat zij gezien had.\n,,Dat is een slechte tijding, juffrouw\", meende de koetsier, \"dat is een doodsbericht,\"\nZoo was het; drie dagen na dit gezicht overleed de zuster van de jonge dame plotseling."},{"n":42324,"r":"LAAN016a","p":"Lellens","v":"Gr.","y":1930,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"An innkeeper sees a funeral procession pass by. Shortly afterwards the plague breaks out.","i":"E.F.","o":"Begraftenis bie nacht\n\nIn de vorige overlevering gebeurde het, dat iemand zijn eigen begrafenis vooruit ziet. Gewoonlik ziet men in een veurloop geschieden, wat anderen overkomt; dat kan ieder treffen die zich op de weg bevindt.\n\nDer was es in Pènne 'n kastelaain, dij kwoad zain kon. Op 'n oavend, dat 't duuster was, zag e 'n woagen aankomen, hail langsoam, voutje veur voutje, net of 't 'n liekwoagen was. Mor dat kon tòch nait, van der luipen twij manlu veur, elk mit 'n schienvat. En 'n begraftenis bie nacht, dat kon nooit woar wezen.\nDer was ook gain ain dood in de haile omtrek. Mor tòch, de swaarde peerden veur de woagen, de kist op de woagen mit 'n swaart klaid ter over, de vòlgers der achter, twij aan twij, ales net zo as de òlle plecht was.\nDou wos e 't: 't was 'n veurloop; 't kwam aaltied oet aan nou tou. Mor dit kon nooit gebeuren, en aan gain mìnsk het e der ooit wat van zegd as aan zien òl Moeke.\nDou is 't gebeurd dat ter pest kwam. Dij dood was, mos vot weg, al was 't ook midden in de nacht. Zo kwam 't toch oet; veurlopen komen aaltied oet; aans wazzen 't ja gain eerliekse veurlopen.\n(Zie Josef Cohen, II, 166)."},{"n":42327,"r":"LAAN016b","p":"Lellens","v":"Gr.","y":1930,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Someone sees a funeral procession pass by. He also sees himself walking behind it. Later his brother dies. When a funeral procession comes by, you must always stay at the side of the road.","i":"E.F.","o":"'n Aander aarbaider zit 's Zundagssnommiddoags veur 't glas. Laanksoam zugt e op de weg 'n liekstoatsie aankomen. As e toukikt, zugt e dat e der zulf ook achter löpt. Vot ter noa was de haile begraftenis weg, mit vòlgers en aal.\nVattien doagen loater hebben ze zien bruier begroaven: zo zond en zo dood!\nAs joe 't ooit gebeurt, mòie aan kaant van weg blieven; veurlopen hòlden aaltied 't midden van 't pad.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":34865,"r":"ABOEK007","p":"Zwolle","v":"Ov.","y":1932,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If a child is born with a caul, the parents must burn the caul as soon as possible. If they do not, the child will be unhappy. Someone who owns such a caul is glad of it in wartime, because the caul makes its owner invulnerable and bulletproof. People born with a caul can see a funeral procession coming in advance. They must then go to the churchyard on the evening before the funeral to bring the corpse there ahead of time. One day a farmhand born with a caul goes to watch a funeral procession. A younger farmhand wants to come and watch, but the older one warns him he will not see anything anyway. When the younger farmhand complains that he indeed sees nothing, he gets a blow to the head. From that moment the young farmhand has the caul and the older one is free of it.","i":"B.J.S.","o":"De Helm\nIe èm miskien wel is '(h)eurd van iene, die met d'(h)elm op geboo(r)n is. Wat of dàt is? 'k Zal 't oe ve'tell'n. \nDe 'elm is een vluus, dàt sommige kinde(r)s bi-j de geboo(r)te an 't 'eufd eb'm zitt'n, ma(r) dàt (h)ebt ze mar (h)eel zeld'n. Dàt vluus mut ve'braand wön'n en doet ze dàt niet, dan is zo'n kind veur zien lèèv'n ongelukkug, al wit'e zelf niet, dàt (h)i-j met d'(h)elm op geboo(r)'n is. De vroedvrouwe of de dokter naam'm dàt vluus wel is stiekum vut, ma(r) 't mog beslist niet. Zo'n 'elm köj duu(r) ve'koop'n, d'r is wel is vief'onde(r)d tut duuz'nd gul(d)'n veur egéév'm. Want ie mun weet'n, dàt, aj zo'n 'elm in oe bezit 'eb'm, dan bi-j dao(r) gelukkug mee, want in d'oo(r)log bi-j dan kogelvri-j, of onkwetsbaar. Dit is wel vàke gebeu(r)d. Zokke mèèns'n, die met 'n 'èlm op geboo(r)n bin'n kön'n d'r 's nachts zoo uutmun'n. As t'r now beveu(r)beeld mà(rg)'n iene begrààv'm zal wön'n, dan mut zo'n pe(r)soon d'r vanaomt, dus de nacht veu(r) de begrààf'nisse iniens uut umme 't liek vut te breng'(n) nao 't kark'of. Ok gebeu(r)t 't wel, dàt ze in 't (h)olle van de nacht een liekstaosie tèèg'nkom'm. Zie zien dan (h)oevölle wààg'ns d'r achter de doodwààg'n ankom'm, enz. Wi-j èb'm vàke iemand uut de buu(r)te bi-j oons '(h)ad, die ok zokke liekstaosies zag en dan zèèg e tèèg'n mien vàder: \"Ik bin vannacht nog op Bargklooster ewest.\" Ma(r) (h)i-j zèèg'n nooit, wat of 'e dao(r","l":"Gelders"},{"n":46737,"r":"SINBRABSAG090","p":"Bladel","v":"N.-Br.","y":1933,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One night a resident of Netersel saw a funeral procession pass by. Five days later his neighbour was buried, followed by as many men and women as he had seen that night.","i":"I.S.","o":"No. 90. Een inwoner van Netersel (onder Bladel) zag 's nachts tusschen twaalf en één, langzaam en plechtig, een rouw, langs den weg, voorbijtrekken. Voorop gingen de vier dragers met de lijkbaar, achter hen stapten twaalf mannen, met rouwmantels om, en omfloersten hoed, en viertien vrouwen, in falies gewikkeld. Vijf dagen later werd zijn buurman begraven, gevolgd door evenveel mannen en vrouwen, als hij 's nachts had zien voorbijtrekken. 1)"},{"n":46738,"r":"SINBRABSAG091","p":"Rijsbergen","v":"N.-Br.","y":1933,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Adriaan Kr. from Rijsbergen once saw a funeral procession pass. This turned out to be a bad omen, for less than a month later his mother was buried.","i":"I.S.","o":"No. 91. Adriaan Kr. had in zijn jonge jaren ook eens zoo'n ontmoeting. Mannen in rouwmantels liepen achter elkaar, langs een oud karrespoor, dat recht op de kerk van Rijsbergen aanhield. 't Bleek een kwaad voorteeken te zijn, want geen maand later werd zijn moetje Dien begraven. 2)"},{"n":46740,"r":"SINBRABSAG093","p":"Heeze","v":"N.-Br.","y":1933,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"It is advisable to avoid a nighttime funeral procession, otherwise you risk getting a box on the ear.","i":"I.S.","o":"No. 93. Het is geraden om een nachtelijke rouw te ontwijken. Een jongen uit Heeze, die zoo'n stoet zag aankomen en toch op den weg bleef loopen, kreeg een fiksche oorveeg, die hem nog lang heugde. 1)"},{"n":13643,"r":"LYST298","p":"Achthuizen","v":"Z.-H.","y":1937,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A beelwitter (seer of phantom funerals) is someone who, on the track of a road at exactly midnight, sees the funeral procession pass of someone who has already died but has not yet been buried. \"Beelwitten\" also means wandering about at night, or haunting.","i":"J.A.J.","o":"Beelwitten\nEen beelwitter was een mensch die in staat was te middernacht, precies op het spoor van een weg, een lijkstoet te zien passeren, ik meen van diegenen die wel dood, maar nog niet begraven waren; dus van diegenen die boven aarde stonden. In uitgebreide zin betekent beeldwitten: des nachts op zeer ongelegen uren rondlopen, en in het algemeen ook rondspoken."},{"n":15732,"r":"CJ002909","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Sytske Koster sees in Eastermar [Oostermeer], in broad daylight, the funeral procession of a woman who died in childbed. Shortly afterwards two more women die in childbed, but neither funeral procession resembles the one Sytske saw. Twenty years later his sister-in-law or daughter-in-law dies. She had exactly the same funeral procession as the one Sytske had seen pass by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e foarige ieu wenne Sytse Koster yn 'e Hamsterheide. Hy wie arbeider by Wilco Buning yn Eastemar. Hy wie us oan 'e Boskwei oan 't wurk. Doe seach er in lykstaesje. It wie ljochtskyndei. De kiste stie op 'e wein en der lei in wyt kleed oer de kiste hinne. It wie dus in kreamfrou. De lykstaesje roan him foarby.\nKoart dêrnei forstoar der in kreamfrou to Eastemar. Mar dy lykstaesje seach der hiel oars út. Dy wie it net. Letter stoar der wer in kreamfrou. En noch letter forstoar in trêdde kreamfrou, mar Sytse Koster hie in oare lykstaesje sjoen.\n20 jier letter forstoar syn snoars yn 'e kream. Dy wie it. Alles wie krekt sa't hy it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20069,"r":"CJ016704","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Every night a woman sees a funeral procession pass. Someone of about seventeen lies in the coffin. The woman can no longer bear it and moves away. Shortly afterwards the new occupants lose their seventeen-year-old son. The previous occupant had foreseen his death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie in minske, dat seach alle nachten in lykstaesje. 't Wie ien fan sa'n sawntjin jier dy't yn 'e kiste lei. Sy woe der net langer wenjen bliuwe en sy forhuzen nei in oar plak.\nDoe kommen der oare minsken yn it hûs. Dy lju hienen in jonge fan sawntsjin. Dy jonge rekke siik en in healjier letter stoar hy.\nDat hie de foarige biwenster sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20081,"r":"CJ016716","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Towards the end of the night a baker sees a woman pass his bakery. Because he does not trust it, he follows her. She turns out to be a well-known woman born with a caul who always has to go out at night to see something. She tells the baker she sees a funeral procession passing. Some time later someone really does die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde yn 'e foarige ieu to Eastemar, dat Popke bakker yn 'e neinacht in minske by de bakkerije lâns gean seach. Hy tochte, dy koe wol us net folle goeds yn 't sin ha. It koe wol us om syn takkebosken to dwaen wêze.\nDat hy slûpte har stil achternei. It minske gong de kant nei de Koemarke út en bleau stean op 'e earste trime fan 'e hekke.\n\"Hwat mat dat dêr?\" sei Popke foars, mar doe seach er dat it Frytsen wie, dy't mei de helm geboaren wie. Frytsen sei: \"Der komt in lyk út 'e Skytsleat op yn in deafet. Ik wyt net hwa't it is.\"\nDe bakker seach neat, mar in deimennich letter stoar der ien op it Wytfean. It Wytfean stie doe blank, lyk as dat yn 't foarige by 't winter wol faker it gefal wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24613,"r":"CJ048102","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1951,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two children see a funeral. It is a premonition: shortly afterwards their mother dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn suster en ik wienen bern fan sa'n sechtsjin jier. Wy gongen nei in winkeltsje to boadskipjen, by de wâl lâns. 't Wie op 'e joun.\nDoe seagen wy in bigraffenis. Wy seinen der thús neat fan. Koart dêrnei woarde muoike dêr wei droegen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":13405,"r":"LYST154","p":"Stedum","v":"Gr.","y":1957,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman sees a hearse with a white horse. Other people can walk right through a hearse, which then suddenly disappears again.","i":"J.F.G.","o":"Bij overlevering had een vrouw een begrafenis met een wit paard voor de koets gezien. Tevoren had de betreffende boer gewenscht te worden begraven met een wit paard voor de lijkwagen. Verder, ook bij overlevering, was een lijkkoets gezien, waarbij men langs de disselboom opliep, door de wagen heen en er achter weer uitkwam. Het heele tafereel was daarna plotseling weer verdwenen."},{"n":23676,"r":"CJ040911","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1960,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One evening two women saw a funeral procession pass by. A few days later a man died and the funeral procession passed by in reality.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is us gebeurd dat der twa froulju op in joune molke helje soenen by Bearn Tabak wei. Bearn Tabak hie in bytsje buorkerije. Underweis nei hûs ta seagen dy beide froulju in lykstaesje.\nDy passearde har. In pear dagen letter woarde de bigraffenis hâlden fan de man dy't stoarn wie.\nDe beide froulju hienen deselde lykstaesje al sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":43259,"r":"AMPT000308","p":"Hasselt","v":"Ov.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul foresees funerals and is a counterfeiter.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"Jan de Karreman was met de helm geboren. Hij zag begrafenissen van te voren. De mensen geloofden er aan. De dochter heeft het zelf verteld. Dat moet nu (1962), 73 jaar geleden zijn. Jan de Karreman is nog veroordeeld, hij maakte vals geld."},{"n":43278,"r":"AMPT000501","p":"Hasselt","v":"Ov.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Some people can 'see evil': they see in advance a farm wagon carrying a coffin, and a few days later there is a funeral.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"Sommige mensen waren behept met \"kwoad zien\". Soms stonden ze met de handen boven de ogen te kijken en dan zagen ze in de verte een boerenwagen aankomen met een lijk. En inderdaad was er dan na een of twee dagen een begrafenis en werd er iemand zo als dat vroeger de gewoonte was op een boerenwagen aangebracht om begraven te worden. Als iemand in het dorp aangewezen was als een man die kwoad kon zien, dan ging dat als een lopend vuurtje door het dorp en iedereen lette op of hij de man iets bijzonders zag doen. Deed hij dan eens iets dat uit de toon viel, dan wist binnen zeer korte tijd dat iedereen."},{"n":43523,"r":"AMPT000607","p":"Hasselt","v":"Ov.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees funeral processions and foresees deaths.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"Een man, ze noemden hem Karreman omdat hij de vuilnis reed voor de gemeente, kon veuruut zien. Van tevoren zei hij: \"Ik heb een liekstatie gezien\" en dan stierf er al gauw ene.","l":"Overijssels"},{"n":69432,"r":"ENGELS000721","p":"Hout-Blerick","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing a funeral procession in advance; from the mourners you can tell who the dead person is.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Spookbegrafenis:\nEr werd hier van een vrouw verteld, die 1 week vantevoren iemands dood kon voorspellen. Ze vertelde, dat ze in een droomgezicht een lijkstoet zag, en aan de volgers kon uitmaken, wie er in de kist moest liggen."},{"n":210487,"r":"ENGELS001303","p":"Beringe","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A death foreseen, with the make-up of the funeral procession seen in advance.","i":"E.G.G.","o":"Spookbegrafenis:\nIk hoorde vroeger van een vrouw, die in een droomgezicht een lijkstoet zag voorbijtrekken. Ze kon alle mensen, die in de stoet meeliepen, herkennen, en uit de volgorde der nabestaanden opmaken, wie er in de kist moest liggen. Ze kon voorspellen, wie er binnenkort ging sterven.\n\nVerslag 58, Omzetting in Heldens dialect van de verhalen van Johanna Janssen, Helden-Beringe; weergegeven in rapport no. L291-13 van 15-12-62. Helden, 5-2-1970. \nIch huurde vreuger ens van ’n vrouw, die s’jnaochs in euren druim èns ’n begrèèfenis vörbei zaag trèkke. Ze koos allemann’ dèè aochter “de liek” gong duudelik kènnen, en oet te volgorde van loupen opmake, wèèm d’r begrave woordt. Zoeë vertelde ze dét s’angerendaags, en vörsjpélden dao mèt, wèèm d’r bènnekort sjtorf"},{"n":210536,"r":"ENGELS001710","p":"Grashoek","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman sees a funeral procession in advance, with someone arriving late. At the later funeral she herself is late.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Spookbegrafenis:\nMijn grootmoeder van moeders kant woonde omstreeks 1850 als meid op een boerderij aan Egchel. Op een keer ging ze ’s avonds water putten in de maneschijn. Ze zag een begrafenisstoet voorbij trekken. Er kwam nog een vrouw achterna gelopen, die te laat was, en nog bezig, haar “luusjterse sjollek” vast te knopen. Het kwam haar later bij, dat ze zelf deze laatkomster moest zijn geweest. Een tijdje later, toen ze naar een begrafenis moest, kwam ze te laat, en was lopend nog bezig, haar schort vast te knopen. De gelijkenis met het voorteken viel haar nu op.\n\nMien groeëtmooder van mooders kankt wonden öm ongevieër 1850 as maagd bei ennen boor an Eègchel. Wie ze enne kieër s’aoves in de maonesjjien water gong pötte, zaag ze’n begrèfenis vörbei trèkke. Dao kwaam nag ’n vrouw aochterop gelaupen, die te laat kwaam. Ze waas nach drök bezig mèt ’t vaostknuipe van eure luusjterse sjóllek. ’t Kwaam later bei eur op, tét ze zelf die laatkömster waas geweest. Det veel eur in, wie ze ’n wielke later örges nao ’n begrèfenis mos, woe ze te laat kwaam, en ongerweegs bewèrkt waas met euren eige luusjterse sjóllek."},{"n":209483,"r":"HOL000109","p":"Ingen","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"On seeing a funeral procession, stand at the side to avoid being pushed aside.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen werden van de weg gezet, als er een \"lijkstatie\" passeerde. De \"aauwe Gurt Bouw\" is dat overkomen bij de Commanderie (naam boerderij vlak bij het dorp). Han Briene is op de \"Zeuve Maarrege\" langs het pad gezet. Zag men een \"lijkstatie\" komen, dan deed men verstandig aan de kant van de weg te gaan staan, uit eigen beweging."},{"n":209520,"r":"HOL000309","p":"Ingen","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Heard about funeral processions for which one must step aside.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Kwint wel van \"lijkstaties\", die 's avonds langs de weg gingen, gehoord, heeft er echter nooit een gezien. Passeerde er een \"lijkstatie\", dan moest men niet in het wagenspoor blijven lopen. Men moest aan de kant gaan staan, anders werd men in de sloot gegooid."},{"n":209521,"r":"HOL000310","p":"Ingen","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A person born with a caul foresees deaths, sees funeral processions and who is being buried; the caul-born person must open a gate at night for a funeral procession; the caul-born person prevents a sick person from dying.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"\"Den aauwen Gart Jan de Kat\" (de Kat was zijn bijnaam) (Ik heb deze persoon, een doortrapt kippenhandelaar enz. goed gekend) zei eens tegen Kwint: \"Aorie, gao nie baauwe, want oew vrouw staarft\" (een huis bouwen). En zie, het gebeurde kort daarop. \nGart Jan zei het ook van zijn eigen vrouw. G.J. zag de lijkstoeten trekken en wist ook, wie er begraven werd. Hij was met de helm geboren\nHent van Orsel (over deze persoon spraken vorige zegslieden ook) werd 's nachts geklopt. Hij moest dan naar buiten om de \"hekkes\" open te doen.\nZolang Gart Jan de Kat bij een ziek mens stond, ging deze niet dood."},{"n":209546,"r":"HOL000412","p":"Ingen","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man and a woman were pushed into the ditch by a passing funeral procession.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Moeder van Eck vertelde hoe zij eens op 26 april, de verjaardag van haar moeder, blij, langs de \"Varse Straot\" naar huis liep. Ze had een fles jenever gehaald bij Roelofsen en had van vrouw Roelofsen een half pond koekjes gekregen voor haar jarige moeder. Opeens stond zij in de sloot (in de sloten bij ons staat in de regel niet veel water), de fles was stuk en alle jenever ging verloren een groot verlies in die tijd, ook de koekjes waren weg. Ook haar zilveren halsketting was verdwenen. Dezelfde avond was Willem van Ledden ook in de sloot gezet. En wat bleek de volgende morgen: Willem van de Waal was gestorven. Zijn \"lijkstatie\" was dus voorbij getrokken, want als er een lijkstatie passeerde, moest men van de weg af en daarom moest men ’s avonds nooit midden op de weg lopen."},{"n":209580,"r":"HOL000513","p":"Ommeren","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Being pushed into the ditch when an invisible funeral procession passes.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Hent van Arkel kwam van Lienden. Hij werd in de \"Meulestraot\", die van Lienden naar Ommeren en Ingen loopt, in de sloot gezet. Ook de broer van Van Ommeren is dit overkomen. Zowel de een als de ander zag niets, maar het stond voor hen vast, dat er een \"lijkstatie\" was gepasseerd."},{"n":209616,"r":"HOL000608","p":"Ommeren","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Being pushed aside by a funeral procession; people born with a caul see funeral processions and can predict who will die; the caul must be buried; midwives sell cauls.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Het gebeurde soms op een donkere avond, dat men van de weg afgezet werd in de sloot. Er ging dan een \"lijkstatie\" voorbij. Niet ieder kon die zien gaan. Zij, die met de helm geboren waren, konden dit wel. Ook konden deze voorspellen, wie er sterven zou. \"Niltje van Strienen\" is dit (met de helm geboren). De helm moet begraven worden. Vroedvrouwen hebben deze helm wel eens verkocht, maar dat mag niet."},{"n":209635,"r":"HOL000708","p":"Ommeren","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Being pushed aside by a funeral procession; who can see a funeral procession.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Hent van Arkelen is eens bij de nieuwe school (in Ommeren) in de sloot gezet. Hij meende, dat er toen een \"lijkstatie\" was voorbij gegaan. Zo’n lijkstatie kon niet iedereen zien, alleen mensen, die met de helm geboren waren, konden dit. Wilde men een lijkstatie zien, dan moest men bij zijn kameraad over de linkerschouder kijken (verhaal Septer) \nJuffrouw Van Hemert had ook wel gehoord van mensen, die van de weg waren getrokken en in de sloot gezet. \nPaarden kon men soms niet in het spoor houden. Zij zagen dan \"wat.\""},{"n":209659,"r":"HOL000807","p":"Lienden","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Being pushed aside by a funeral procession when walking in the middle of the road.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Het overkwam sommige mensen op donkere avonden, dat zij, als zij midden op de weg liepen, \"op zij gezet werden\", soms in een sloot terecht kwamen. Er passeerde dan een \"lijkstatie\" (bespannen boerenwagen waarop lijkkist en enige mensen twee aan twee achter de wagen) Krelis van Doorn zag hem komen; hij duwde dan de mensen met wie hij liep op zij (Krelis van Doorn was een stil, in zich zelf gekeerd mannetje. Hij was astmalijder) Er werd dan ook aangeraden om aan het natte pak te ontkomen, 's avonds niet in het wagenspoor te lopen."},{"n":209691,"r":"HOL000910","p":"Lienden","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Being pushed aside by a ghostly funeral, an omen of a coming funeral.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"'t Kwam voor, dat mensen op donkere avonden van de weg werden getrokken. Ze kwamen dan soms in de sloot terecht of werden over de heg gezet. Er was dan een spookbegrafenis voorbij gegaan en dit was een voorteken voor de begrafenis, die daar spoedig zou passeren."},{"n":209714,"r":"HOL001007","p":"Opheusden","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Being pushed aside by a funeral procession; voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Het gebeurde in de donkere avond, dat mensen aan de kant van de weg werden gezet. Er passeerde dan een lijkstatie. Iemand, die bij Olleke (Aaltje) voorbijkwam, zei: \"Gao op zij\" \"Wa ziede\" zei een ander. De eerste zag een begrafenisstoet passeren. Er werd gevraagd, of het een grote of kleine was. \"Gin kleintje, mar ok gin grote\" was het antwoord. Nog geen veertien dagen later was het \"dernje\" van Olleke (12 jaar oud) gestorven."},{"n":130749,"r":"KEUNING000208","p":"Feanwâldsterwâl","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul gets up at night to see a funeral; not long afterwards someone is buried.","i":"S.K.","o":"Metske smid wier mei de helm geboren. Hy gyng der faek nachts ôf om nei in bigraffenis to sjen. Gau derop waerd er dan ek ien bigroeven.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130752,"r":"KEUNING000301","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People never walk in the middle of the road because of funeral processions, because of the danger of, for example, having to walk over the hearse or being picked up and thrown into a ditch.","i":"S.K.","o":"It wier by de Oare Hoek. Yn 'e nacht. Der wie in lykstaesje. De minsken rounen doedestiids altyd oan 'e kant fan de wei, nea yn 'e midden. Bynammen nachts net. Hwant in lykstaesje gyng midden op 'e wei.\nEn dr wie sa 'n bigraffenis. Der kaem ien oan. Dy soe dwers oer. En dy gyng samar oer 'e lykwein hinne. De iene kant der by op, de oare kant der by del.\nSa is it ek foarfallen efkes fjidder dan Janke Fokke. Dêr waerd in man, dy 't Geart hiette, midden yn 'e nacht opnommen en yn 'e sleat smiten. Dat kaem troch de lykstaesje. In pear dagen letter stoar Geart.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130781,"r":"KEUNING000701","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man often sees a funeral procession at night; a few days later there is a funeral.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ik ha wol es heard, dat Bontsje Keke faek nachts in lykstaesje seach. In pear dagen letter waerd er dan fêst ien to hôf brocht.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130801,"r":"KEUNING000910","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A docile horse turns around and will not go on. The cause is said to be a passing funeral procession. A week later someone dies whose funeral goes along the same route.","i":"S.K.","o":"Wytse hie lân yn 'e Finnen. Op in kear helle hy dêr wetter wei. Hy hie in tige mak hynder foar de wein. Der sieten ek in stik ôf hwat bern op 'e wein. Se wierne krekt wer op 'e dyk, dêr by de weinmakker, dêr swaeit ynienen it hynder om en fljocht yn 'e hage.\nWytse seit: \"Hwat mankeart dy.\" Mar it hynder woe net fjirder. Wytse kriget him by de kop. De bern naeije út.\nAs Wytse thús komt, fortelt hy, hwat er bard wie.\nIk sei: \"Wie der neat?\"\n\"Ne, seit hy.\nIk wer: \"Dou ljeauwst it noait. Mar der wier in lykstaesje.\"\nDeselde wike stoar der in frou. De bigraffenis moast dat selde paed ek lâns.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130831,"r":"KEUNING001307","p":"Kûkherne","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Stepping aside for a funeral procession at night, and someone will surely die.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ja, foar in lykstaesje koe min nachts mar oan 'e kant gean. En dan stoar der ek fêst ien.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130857,"r":"KEUNING001607","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Walking at the side of the road at night so as not to be pushed aside by a funeral procession.","i":"S.K.","o":"lykstaesje\nAs min nachts de wei lâns roun, moast min altyd oan 'e kant fan 'e wei rinne. Oars waerd min der ôfsmiten, as der in lykstaesje lâns kaem.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130866,"r":"KEUNING001705","p":"Driezum","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul warns people to step aside for a funeral procession he sees. Seeing a funeral procession is also an omen of a funeral shortly afterwards.","i":"S.K.","o":"mei de helm berne\nJa, hjir wier ek ien, dy 't mei de helm berne wier. It barde faek, as hy mei ien of mear nachts de wei lâns roun, dat hy sei: \"Gean effen oan de kant, der komt in lykstaesje oan.\" Dan wier der ek gau in bigraffenis.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130883,"r":"KEUNING001902","p":"Westergeast","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A few days before someone dies, a man born with a caul sees a funeral procession on a wall.","i":"S.K.","o":"A. wier mei de helm op berne. In pear dagen foar dat der ien forstoar, seach hja altyd in lykstaesje op 'e muorre.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130913,"r":"KEUNING002307","p":"Suwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul sees the funeral procession of his own funeral.","i":"S.K.","o":"Omke seach ek in kear op in nacht, doe hy noch ûnderweis wier, in lykstaesje. Foar de lykwein rounen twa hynders. Omke seach wol fan hwa dy wierne. Ek koe hy alle minsken, dy efter de lykwein rounen, op ien nei. Dat wier hy sels.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130963,"r":"KEUNING003013","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A warning to keep a path clear in the middle of the barn at night. Someone who sleeps there is picked up and thrown down further on.","i":"S.K.","o":"Heit en dy ha ris yn Grinslân arbeide. Hja slepten yn in skuorre. De earste joun waerd der sein, dat yn it midden in paed rom bliuwe moast, hwant der kaem nachts wol ris hwat lâns. Ien fan ús hie der de gek mei en gyng yn it paed lizzen. Mar wylst hy slepe, waerd hy opnaem en in ein fjirder delgoaid.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130992,"r":"KEUNING003307","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A few days before his wife's death, a man sees a funeral procession coming from the farmyard.","i":"S.K.","o":"In broer fan my hat in pear jier lyn syn frou forlern. In pear dagen foar har forstjerren seach myn broer in lykstaesje fan it hiem kommen. De minsken hiene greate kleden om. Dy sleepten troch de hage.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131003,"r":"KEUNING003406","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A warning not to walk in the middle of the road, so as not to have to walk over a funeral procession.","i":"S.K.","o":"Us âlde ljue warskouwen ús altyd, net midden op de wei to rinnen. As der dan in lykstaesje kaem, soen wy der boppen oer hinne moatte.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131016,"r":"KEUNING003604","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"At night someone in the street is picked up and lifted over a hearse.","i":"S.K.","o":"Wy hawwe ien kend, die wier op in nacht op 'e wei. Hy waerd opnaem en samar boppe oer in lykwein hinne tild.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131036,"r":"KEUNING003802","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing a funeral procession; a man's prediction that it concerns his daughter comes true.","i":"S.K.","o":"Wy moasten faek foar mem nei B.D. om môlke. Op in kear stiene wy wer by har by de doar. Doe sei hja: \"Pasop, dêr komt in lykstaesje oan.\" En it wie ek sa. Mem wie der ek by en dy seach him ek. Sy fortelde dat oan in man. Dy sei: \"Dan sil dat ús D. wol wêze.\" Dat wie syn dochter. D. Tabak neamden se har altyd, hwant sy hie altyd in prúmke tabak tusken de kiezzen. En it kaem ek ut. In dei of hwat letter waerd D, bigroeven.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131050,"r":"KEUNING003908","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who has seen a funeral procession at night predicts it will be a large funeral, and this comes true.","i":"S.K.","o":"S. moast er nachts wol ris ôf. Dan seach hy in lykstaesje.\"Der komt mei koarten ek ien op it hôf,\" sei hy dan. In kear sei hy ek noch: \"Hwa it is wyt ik net, mar it wurdt in greate bigraffenis.\" En it waerd in greate bigraffenis.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131063,"r":"KEUNING004002","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Mother advises walking at the side of the road; she sees a funeral procession the evening before someone dies.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ús mem sei altyd tsjin ús, dat wy oan de kant fan de wei rinne moasten. As der ien wei rekke seach hja de jouns foartyd altyd in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131077,"r":"KEUNING004102","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the evening, men in the street are flung aside by something.","i":"S.K.","o":"Twa mannen rounen op in lette joun de wei lâns. Yn ienen leinen se beide oan de kant fan de dyk. Hja waerden smiten, mar troch hwa, wisten se net.\n\"Litstou dy smite?\" sei de iene.\n\"Né hjer. Mar hwer bistou?\"\nEn doe wie it wer oer.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131081,"r":"KEUNING004106","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman gets up at night to see a funeral procession; her husband notices nothing.","i":"S.K.","o":"In frommis hjirre gong nachts faek fan it bêd. Dan seach hja wer in lykstaesje. Dan lei hja in skieppebloat by har man op bêd. \nDan sliepte hy rêstich troch.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131086,"r":"KEUNING004203","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession; very soon afterwards someone dies. The funeral goes as he saw it.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ja, in lykstaesje ha ik sels al ris sjoen. Ik wie doe om branhout west. Ik seach in man of sâwn mei in lykkiste. Dêr siet in lyk yn. En ynienen wie ek alles wer fuort. Thús hearde ik, dat P. stoarn wie. En op de bigraffenis rounen ek mar sâwn man mei.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131088,"r":"KEUNING004205","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man tells a woman that her husband will come home dead, because he has seen his funeral procession. The funeral goes as foretold.","i":"S.K.","o":"In man en in frou stienen meielkoar to praten. De frou sei: \"Ik moat de boel noch netsjes oprêdde. Myn man komt joun thús.\"\nDe man sei: \n\"Hy komt al thús, mar dea. Ik ha syn lykstaesje sjoen. En by de bigraffenis sil it hynder foar de lykwein ûnderweis by de dobbe stean bliuwe.\" It kaem presies sa út.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131122,"r":"KEUNING004603","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Warning to step aside for a funeral procession.","i":"S.K.","o":"It is wier bard. In man roun de Dwarsfeart lâns. Der wie noch ien by him. It wie yn de lette joun. Ynienen sei de earstneamde: \"Jo moatte efkes wachtsje. Gean efkes oan de kant. Der komt in lykstaesje oan.\"\nDe man die it, mar hy hat neat sjoen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131136,"r":"KEUNING004805","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man has to get up at night to see a funeral, the course of which he can later describe. He warns not to walk in the middle of the road at night between twelve and one, because then you can be pushed aside.","i":"S.K.","o":"Der wie hjir in man, dy waerd der nachts faek utkloppe. Dan seach hy in bigraffenis. En hy koe letter krekt sizze, hoe 'n hynder der foar de lykwein roun, hoefolle manljue en hoefolle frouljue der mei rounen en sa mear.\n\nHy sei ek altyd, dat min noait nachts tusken toalf en ien ûre midden op 'e wei rinne moast. It wie him al ris oerkaem, dat hy it al die, en doe waerd hy samar oan 'e kant smiten.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131172,"r":"KEUNING005404","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man often has to get up to see a funeral procession. The unknown person he once sees turns out to be himself.","i":"S.K.","o":"Der wie by ús ek ien, dy moast faek fan it bêd ôf. Dan seach hy in lykstaesje op de wei. Ienkear wie der ien by, dy koe hy net. Mar doe wier de bigraffenis wie, kaem it út. Dat wie hy sels.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131194,"r":"KEUNING005705","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Unexplained throwing of stones at night. Getting up at night to see a funeral. A case in which the unknown person in the funeral procession is the one who saw the procession beforehand.","i":"S.K.","o":"Mar dochs barden der in bulte dingen dy net to forklearjen wienen.\nSa wie der in man, dy kaem der nachts faek ôf, hwant der waerden altyd stiennen by harren yn de kakstoel goaid.\nIn omke fan ús moast der nachts ek faek ôf, hwant dan seach hy in bigraffenis. It is ienkear west, doe telde hy hoefolle der efter rounen. It wiernen achtjen. Sâwntjen koe der thúsbringe, mar ien net. Doe 't hy in pear dagen letter sels op bigraffenis moast, kaem út hwa dit wie. Sâwntjen wienen de selden, dy hy dy nachts sjoen hie en de achtjende wie hy sels.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131221,"r":"KEUNING006007","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Warning not to walk in the middle of the road at night.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ja, dat is ek sa. Wy mochten nachts ek nea midden op de wei rinne. En nou mei it oerdei ek al net mear.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131241,"r":"KEUNING006302","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman was said to be able to work magic and saw a ship with a coffin at night.","i":"S.K.","o":"Fan M.A. waerd ek sein, dat hja tsjoene koe. Ek moat hja yn 'e nacht wol ris sjoen ha, dat der in skou mei in lykkiste der yn oan driuwen kaem.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131253,"r":"KEUNING006408","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A few nights before a death, a woman has to get up and go outside to see a funeral procession.","i":"S.K.","o":"Alde A. hat faek sein, dat hja bliid wie, dat hja net oan 'e wei wenne. As der ien stoar en de bigraffenis (lykstaesje) moast by har foar it hûs lâns, dan seach hja dy in pear nachten foar de tiid al rinnen. Hja seach ek, dy roun hjir en dy dêr. Mar hja moast ek fan bêd ôf. En nei bûten. As se in bern droech, (bifalle moast) dan hoefde hja net nei bûten, mar hja moast wol nei it raem om troch it finster to sjen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131309,"r":"KEUNING007014","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A vision that a funeral procession drives along a path where no hearse can go comes true.","i":"S.K.","o":"It wie yn Harkema. Der stienen guon efter it hûs to praten. Doe kaem der ien by harren en sei:\n\"Der komt in lykstaesje it Skeanpaed del. Der binne twa by mei heg huodden, dan noch fiif manljue en fiif frouljue.\"\n\"Dat kin net, sei ien fan harren, der kin noait in lykwein it Skeanpaed del.\"\nIn skoft letter stoar ús buorman. Pake en K. moasten tafeltsjinje. De dominé, dy mei in âlderling, beide mei in hege hoed, de foargong hie wie in fremden ien. Hy is letter ek ôfset. Doe 't se by it Skeanpaed kamen, sei hy:\n\"Wij gaan hier maar langs. De wagen kan de weg wel houden\".\nEn hwat dominé sei barde.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131340,"r":"KEUNING007403","p":"Paesens","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Having to get up at night to see a funeral procession.","i":"S.K.","o":"Hjir wie ek ien, dy seach nachts lykstaesjes. Dan moast hja der út.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131368,"r":"KEUNING007902","p":"Grou","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing a funeral procession is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death. Warning to walk at the side of the road, or else be pushed aside by the funeral procession.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ien út memme femylje seach nachts ek faek in lykstaesje. En dan kaem der ek grif ien op it hôf. Wy moasten ek altyd oan de kant fan de wei rinne. Oars waerden wy, as der in lykstaesje kaem, oan 'e kant smiten.","l":"Fries"},{"n":50620,"r":"KOOIJMAN0078","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If you went along the horse path, you were pushed aside.","i":"H.K."},{"n":50858,"r":"KOOIJMAN0158","p":"IJsselstein","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"At night one can be pushed aside by a funeral procession, though the procession itself is not visible.","i":"H.K.","o":"Ik heb het moeder vaak horen vertellen. Ze kwam uit Lopik. \"Als er een van dat soort begraven wier, dan beurde dat 's nachts. Wie de stoet tegenkwam, werd op zij gedrukt\". Maar je zag niks."},{"n":50954,"r":"KOOIJMAN0254","p":"Ammerstol","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The narrator is warned by his wife's grandmother about a certain stretch of dike. Blinde belies (a funeral procession) were said to appear there, and they could carry people over great distances.","i":"H.K.","o":"M'n vrouws opoe, die was erg bijgelovig. Ik was op een avond bij m'n meisje geweest, wat nou m'n vrouw is. Ik 's avonds naar huis toe. Nou hebbie daar zo'n kaal stuk dijk. En daar liepen volgens de verhalen de blinde belies. ,Jongen, zal je voorzichtig zijn? Want je weet niet, waar je neergezet wordt\". Want ze geloofden vast, dat die blinde beliesje helegaar in Jaarsveld of in een andere provincie konden neerzetten. Die blinde belie was een soort lijkstoet. Die kwam de dijk uit. Alles moest d'r voor op zij."},{"n":50955,"r":"KOOIJMAN0255","p":"Ammerstol","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man is on his way home when he sees a funeral procession coming towards him. He neatly moves to the side, and when the procession has passed he cycles on.","i":"H.K.","o":"Een kennis van me had verkering met een meissie in de Vlist. Die kennis kwam uit Langerak. Op 'n keer komt ie midden in de nacht van z'n meissie vandaan, helegaar alleen. Hij fietst de Franse Kaai op*. Daar ziet ie in de verte een lijkstoet aankomen over de Franse Kaai. 't Was helderlichte maan. Hij stapt af, gaat bezije z'n fiets staan. De hele stoet komt voorbij. Niemand die iets zei. In 't holst van de nacht. Maar d'r gebeurde 'm niks, omdat ie aan de kant sting. Hij stapt op z'n fiets en ree weer deur.\n\n*verbindingsweg tussen de West Vlisterdijk en de Bovenbergse Weg te Bergambacht"},{"n":42831,"r":"WEV000402","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man with the evil eye has to get up at midnight. He then sees a funeral procession and sometimes a bridal carriage.","i":"F.W.","o":"In Hanetange onder Ter-Apel leefde Meijer. Deze had het \"kwade gezicht\" of het \"kwade oog.\"\n Grif elke nacht om 12 uur moest hij het bed uit. Hij ging dan midden op straat staan. En dan zag hij de dingen, die gebeuren moesten.\n Dat was soms een begrafenis.\nHij herkende de mensen. Hij zag de kleur van het paard. \nSoms zag hij een bruiloft-koets. \nAltijd kwam het uit, wat hij had gezien."},{"n":42971,"r":"WEV000702","p":"Onstwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man tells the minister he has seen a hearse coming from a farm where bachelors live, and how a woman and a child fell out of the coffin. The minister tells him to keep quiet. Later the new maid becomes pregnant, dies with her child, and both are taken to her village in one coffin.","i":"F.W.","o":"Voorloop.\n\nVerteller: De heer Brakke.\n\nDDit verhaal heb ik van de dominee zelf, en die liegt er niet om.\nDominee kreeg eens een boerenknecht op bezoek. De jong was bleek van schrik. Onderweg had hij een lijkwagen gezien. Die kwam een laan af van een boerderij.\nPlotseling sloegen de paarden op hol.\nDe wagen kantelde en uit de kist vielen twee mensen, een vrouw en een kind.\nHet vreemde was, dat er in die boerderij een paar oude vrijgezellen woonden. \nDe dominee zei tegen de knecht, dat hij er maar over zwijgen moest.\nEn wat gebeurt er?\nBij de vrijgezellen komt een nieuw dienstmeisje. Over verloop van tijd verwacht deze een baby.\nDoch beiden sterven.\nDe familie van het meisje wenste ze begraven te zien in haar geboortedorp.\nZo gebeurde het toch, dat ze in één kist van de boerderij werden gebracht."},{"n":43098,"r":"WEV001001","p":"Roswinkel","v":"Dr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A family puts a separate window in the house, so that the man who has to get up at night because he sees a funeral procession can stay inside.","i":"F.W.","o":"Verteller: de heer A. Veltrup te Roswinkel\n\nKijk eens, vroeger was er veel bijgeloof.\nIn mijn jeugd zagen de mensen meer dan nu.\nMaar gooi niet alles weg.\nWat waar is, is waar.\nEn dingen, die ik zelf heb meegemaakt, moeten geloofd worden.\nDaar heb je veurloop. Dit bestaat.\nHier vlak bij ons woonde vroeger een man, die er 's nachts uit moest, omdat hij een begrafenis zag voorbijtrekken.\nDe familie vond dit tenslotte zo lastig, dat ze een apart raam in het huis hebben laten zetten.\nDan kon hij 's nachts rustig binnen blijven en hoefde hij dus geen kou te lijden buiten."},{"n":43205,"r":"WEV001202","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees in advance a hearse drawn by a white horse and a blaze-faced horse. After buying a blaze-faced horse to go with his white one, he remembers what he saw. He cannot sell the blaze-faced horse. When his daughter dies, she is carried away in a hearse drawn by the white horse and the blaze-faced one. Three days later a buyer for the blaze-faced horse turns up.","i":"F.W.","o":"Schoenmaker vertelt over voorloop.\n\nMijn grootvader, oale Steffen, heeft veel gezien en beleefd. Hij zei altijd: \"As 't wat zugst, moust 't er nich tegen in goan; d'r is niks aon te verandern.\"\n\nOp een avond komt hij thuis.\nAls hij de deur open doet, ziet hij op de deel een lijkwagen staan met twee paarden er voor. Een wit en een bles.\nOver verloop van tijd koopt hij in Zuidbroek een bruine bles. Een wit paard had hij al. Nu denkt hij terug aan 't gezicht, dat hij heeft gehad.\nOm aan een naderend onheil te ontkomen, doet hij alle moeite, de bruine bles te verkopen. Het lukt evenwel niet.\nLater sterft een dochtertje.\nHet kind wordt weggebracht in een lijkwagen, getrokken door de witte en de bles.\nDrie dagen later komt er een koper."},{"n":43091,"r":"WEV001301","p":"Gasselternijveen","v":"Dr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees funeral processions; others see lights where roads are later built.","i":"F.W.","o":"In mijn woonplaats alhier heb ik geen bijzondere dingen te vermelden, hoewel ik hier al 68 jaar woon.\nWel weet ik van iemand uit Beilen, die vooruit zien kon.\nHet was een klein \"kereltien\" met een dophoed op. Hij woonde in een praam. Soms ging hij 's nachts de weg op, waar hij lijkstaties zag. Zo eens een, waarbij hij voor de wagen een wit en een zwart paard zag. Het kwam later uit ook. \nOok zagen sommige mensen in Drente lichtjes, waar later wegen kwamen."},{"n":43222,"r":"WEV001404","p":"Mussel","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"On the road one man warns the other to step aside. The other sees nothing and falls to the ground, because the hearse has driven over him.","i":"F.W.","o":"Het volgende heb ik zelf niet meegemaakt.\nMijn kameraden hebben 't mij verteld.\nZe lopen op de weg bij avond.\n\"Ga opzij\", zegt de een tegen de ander.\n\"Waarom?\"\n\"Er komt wat aan.\"\n\"'k Zie niks.\" \nEven later valt hij op de grond.\n\"Kijk,\" zegt de eerste, \"de lijkwagen is over je heen gegaan.\""},{"n":43313,"r":"WEV001603","p":"Alteveer","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession in which one of the horses is unknown to him. At the funeral it turns out that one of the farmers has bought a different horse.","i":"F.W.","o":"Een andere kennis van me zag soms lijkstaties.\nMaar één keer wist hij er geen weg mee.\nHij had weer een boerenwagen gezien met de kist erop. Je weet, vroeger bestonden er nog geen lijkwagens, maar de gestorvene werd weggebracht op een gewone boerenwagen. Het voertuig werd getrokken door geschikte paarden uit de buurt.\nDie éne keer zag hij echter een paard, zoals er in de hele omgeving niet te vinden was.\nToch vergiste hij zich niet.\nWant toen de bewuste persoon begraven werd, die hij had gezien, had een der boeren intussen een paard gekocht.\nEn dit dier had de kleur, door mijn kennis gezien."},{"n":45320,"r":"WEV002202","p":"Sellingen","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man has to go outside at night to watch a hearse pass, even when the door is locked and barricaded.","i":"F.W.","o":"In de Maten heb ik toch iemand gekend, die ’s nachts bij de weg liep. Hij moest zijn bed uit om een lijkwagen te zien voorbijtrekken. De familie vond dat nogal vervelend. \nDaarom maakten ze een raampje in zijn slaapkamer. Dan kon hij dus binnen blijven. Dit hielp echter niet. Hij bleef naar buiten gaan. Toen hebben ze eens de deur stevig gegrendeld. Ook dat had geen succes. Daarop is de deur nog vaster gebonden en een regenton werd er voor gezet. \nDat hielp. De man kon er niet uit, maar hij had zijn handen helemaal stukgekrabd. Hij heeft toen ook gezegd: “Dou dat nou nooit weer; ik mout d’r oet.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45321,"r":"WEV002203","p":"Sellingen","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A mother warns her son to get out of the wheel track. He suddenly walks up onto the front of a hearse and falls off the back.","i":"F.W.","o":"Hier vlak over de grens liep een vrouw met haar zoontje. Deze liep door een wagenspoor. De vrouw zei: “Jonge, kom maal heer, doe vaalst dom m’t.”\nEn kijk, de jongen loopt plotseling voor bij een lijkwagen op en valt er achter weer af.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45345,"r":"WEV002406","p":"Stadskanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man can see funeral processions and sometimes walks across the churchyard at night ahead of a hearse of a future funeral.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wat ik gelukkig niet zien kon, waren de lijkstaties, wat anderen wel konden. Zo bijv. R. te Horsten, die soms voor een lijkkoets uit ’s nachts over het kerkhof liep van een toekomstige begrafenis.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":129842,"r":"WOUDA023008","p":"Workum","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man has seen a funeral procession at a house with a sick child, but sees a large coffin. A week later the child's father dies.","i":"E.W.","o":"In âlde muoike fan my hie in greate hûshâlding. Se wenne yn 'e Hommerts. Der kaem ris in bidler by de doar. Se joech him hwat en hy sei tsjin 't minske: “Hjir kaem my in bigraffenis tsjin op 'e reed.” Tafallich wie it jongste bern slim siik, ja dea min. Doe sei myn muoike: “Och, och, dat earme lytse bern; it is al sa siik.” Doe sei dy by de doar stie: “Né, it wie in grutte kiste.”In wike letter waerd har man útdroegen! Myn heit hat it my forteld; dy wenne dêr doe; it wie om 1880 hinne.","l":"Fries"},{"n":209748,"r":"HOL001106","p":"Eck en Wiel","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing a funeral procession; being pushed aside when walking in the middle of the road.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Sommige mensen meenden, dat zij 's avonds wel eens een \"lijkstaosie\" hadden zien gaan langs de weg. Dit was een voorteken van een begrafenisstoet, die daar weldra zou passeren. Mensen, die bij hen waren, zagen deze niet. Het was niet gewenst 's avonds in het spoor van de karren en wagens midden op de weg te lopen, want naderde zo 'n spookbegrafenis, dan werd men aan de kant van de weg gezet en ook wel in de sloot."},{"n":209794,"r":"HOL001307","p":"Eck en Wiel","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing a phantom funeral procession is an omen of a real funeral procession.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Als er in een donkere avond een lijkstatie moest passeren, werd een voetganger eenvoudig in de sloot gezet. Zag men een lijkstatie dan wist men, dat er binnen korte tijd werkelijk een begrafenisstoet zou trekken."},{"n":209823,"r":"HOL001407","p":"Kesteren","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing funeral processions; being pushed aside when walking in the middle of the road.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Vroeger wel verhalen in omloop over \"lijkstaties\", die men op donkere avonden had zien trekken. Zag men deze aankomen, dan mocht men niet midden op de weg blijven lopen. Deed men dit toch dan werd men aan de kant gezet."},{"n":209846,"r":"HOL001505","p":"Kapel-Avezaath","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Being pushed aside by a funeral procession; the funeral procession is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death; a waterkijker (water-gazer, a healer who diagnoses by looking at urine) foresees a death and the course of the funeral.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen werden soms 's avonds van de weg getrokken. Er was dan een lijkstatie voorbij gegaan, veronderstelde men. Men moest daarom 's avonds nooit in het rechterwagenspoor lopen. De moeder van Van Zijtveld, afkomstig uit Drumpt, had hierover herhaaldelijk het volgende verteld. Zij woonde toen in de Roskam (herberg) in Drumpt. In het gezin, waartoe zij behoorde heerste \"vliegende tering\". De buurvrouw was in de nacht na de begrafenis van één van de zoons uit de Roskam even buiten. Zij zag voor de deur van de Roskam een lijkstatie staan. In die nacht stierf een dochter uit de Roskam.\nDe oudste zoon van Aart van Kuilenburg, Ooijke was ernstig ziek. Zijn tweede moeder ging naar een z.g. waterkijker in Rotterdam. Deze had gezegd, dat de jongen zou sterven en dat men er voor moest zorgen dat een kind, dat altijd op zijn bed speelde, dat voortaan niet meer deed. Hij zag een oude man (ouderling v.d. kerk) bij het bed zitten, zag de begrafenis, waaraan een aantal lange mannen (de Boudewijnen, die lang waren) deelnamen, zag de boerenwagen, waarop de kist werd vervoerd."},{"n":209875,"r":"HOL001610","p":"Opheusden","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing funeral processions in the evening; being pushed aside; warning not to walk in the middle of the road.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Verschillende mensen zagen 's avonds lijkstaties trekken. Ze herkenden vaak de wagen, de paarden, de kleren van de volgers. Een boerenknecht die twee paarden bij zich had, werd eens met paarden en al van de weg gezet, over de sloot. Sommige mensen zagen die lijkstaties midden op den dag. Gebeurde dit, dan volgde heel spoedig een sterfgeval, zag men de lijkstatie 's avonds dan kon het nog wel enige tijd duren, eer het plaats had. \nMevr. Schaap vertelde, hoe zij, toen zij nog een meisje was, als zij 's avonds uit moest door de ouders gewaarschuwd werd niet in het wagenspoor of midden op de weg te lopen."},{"n":209921,"r":"HOL001717","p":"Kesteren","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman sees funeral processions and who will die; she has to open the churchyard gates at night.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Janje Piet Geitenbeek (een andere vrouw dan de hiervoor genoemde) zag lijkstaties trekken en wist ook waar ze vandaan kwamen (wie er dus weldra zou sterven). Zij moest 's nachts de hekken van het kerkhof open gaan zetten"},{"n":209923,"r":"HOL001719","p":"Kesteren","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Warning not to walk in a wagon rut in the evening because of funeral processions.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mevrouw V.d. Brenk (uit Ochten) vroeger wel horen zeggen, dat men 's avonds niet in het wagenspoor mocht lopen vanwege de lijkstaties, die konden trekken."},{"n":209947,"r":"HOL001808","p":"Lienden","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Pushed aside by a funeral procession, an omen of a coming funeral.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"In de donkere avond gebeurde het, dat mensen plotseling \"in de sloot werden gezet\" Er passeerde dan een \"lijkstatie\". Deze was een voorteken van een begrafenisstoet, die langs die weg binnen korte tijd zou trekken."},{"n":209971,"r":"HOL001907","p":"Maurik","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul sees the funeral procession in advance when someone dies.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Hent de Vries zag, als er iemand zou overlijden, 3 dagen van tevoren een lijkstatie. Niltje zijn vrouw vertelde dat. Hij zelf sprak er nooit over. Hij was met den helm geboren"},{"n":209999,"r":"HOL002010","p":"Maurik","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Warning not to walk in a wagon rut in the evening.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Men moest 's avonds niet in het wagenspoor lopen, want dan kon men dat beleven."},{"n":210026,"r":"HOL002108","p":"Maurik","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing funeral processions; being pushed aside by a funeral procession when walking in the middle of the road.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Hent de Droetel (scheldnaam) zag \"lijkstaosies.\" Hij zag de boerenwagen met de paarden er voor, de mensen, die er achter liepen. Hij kon zeggen, wie het waren. Voor die \"lijkstaosies\" werd men \"van de weg\" gezet. Het was daarom beter niet midden op de weg te lopen. Kinderen werd ingeprent dit niet te doen."},{"n":210067,"r":"HOL002210","p":"Ochten","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Pushed aside by a funeral procession; advice not to walk in the middle of the road.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"\"Moeke\", zo vertelde mevr. Keuken \"was eens op een avond van de weg gezet\". De vrouw van Bloemendaal was die avond gestorven. Er werd verondersteld, dat er een \"lijkstatie\" was gepasseerd. \nEen kameraad van Keuken zag vaak een lijkstoet in de donkere avond. Hij zag van welke kant die kwam. Men werd daarom gewaarschuwd 's avonds niet midden op de weg te lopen, omdat men dan de risico liep er afgezet te worden."},{"n":210074,"r":"HOL002217","p":"Ochten","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman sees funeral processions and, long beforehand, sees blood at a place where fighting takes place in the war.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Dientje den Hartog (zij hield een winkeltje) zag vaak lijkstaties. Zij zag het bloed aflopen van de Grebbeberg (in mei '40 zijn de Duitsers op de Grebbeberg door de Hollandse linie gebroken) (Lang voor '40 moet Dientje, dat al verteld hebben, de fam. Keuken had dit verhaal al gehoord toen zij nog kinderen waren)"},{"n":131433,"r":"KEUNING008705","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing a coffin, funeral wreath or funeral procession at night; foreseeing a death.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ik ha it nachts ek faek, dat ik in glimke sjoch fan in deakiste. Of fan in lykkrânse. Of fan minsken, dy mei rinne mei in begraffenis. Ik wyt ek faek fier foarút as der ien stjerre sil. Fan myn man wist ik it ek. Dêrtroch wie ik der hiel kalm ûnder.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131440,"r":"KEUNING008805","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A joke about seeing a funeral procession that shows fear of funeral processions.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ja, dy lykstaesjes ha se it hjir ek wol oer hâwn. In skarlún hat der hjir ris in grap mei hâwn. Hy frege in oare jongfeint, ôf hy efkes mei nei it Wytfean woe. Dat gong oan. Doe se by it dykje nei it Wytfean kamen, sei de skarlún: \"Hjir komt wol ris in lykstaesje lâns. Eltsenien sjocht se net, mar ik wol. Ik nim dan altyd de pet efkes fan 'e holle. Dat moast dû ek dwaen.\"\nHja rounen efter mekoar, mar doe hy de pet fan 'e holle krige, naeide syn maet út, sa hurd hy koe. Sa bang wienen yn dy tiid in bulte foar sok spul.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131492,"r":"KEUNING009601","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession and then has to go to the house where someone will die.","i":"S.K.","o":"Wy holpen as jonges faek by it flaeksoandragen. Der arbeide ek in man, dy faek lykstaesjes seach. Op in kear gong hy midden op 'e dei by it wurk wei. Hy seach wer in lykstaesje en moast nou nei it hûs ta, hwer ien stjerre soe. Efkes letter kaem hy wer.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131540,"r":"KEUNING010507","p":"Eanjum","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing a funeral procession at night; the later funeral of a relative goes as seen in the procession.","i":"S.K.","o":"In omke fan my seach op in nacht ris in lykstaesje. Hy seach de lykwein mei de kiste, dêr efter de dominé en in âld man, dan trije jongeljue, alle fiif mei hege huodden op en dan noch hwat manljue en frouljue. Oardeheal jier letter stoar in omke fan dy omke. En de bigraffenis wie krekt sa as omke dy sjoen hie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131563,"r":"KEUNING011004","p":"Nijewier","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Warning about funeral processions, fear of walking in the middle of the road, the feeling of walking over something.","i":"S.K.","o":"As wy sneintejouns út 'e herberch kamen, barde it faek, dat myn broer ynienen saei: \"Ho, bliuw stean.\" En efkes letter: \"Nou mar wer fierder.\"\nDan wie der in lykstaesje. Ik trille faek noch, as wy al thús wienen. Wy doarden ek nea op it spoar (midden op it paed) to rinnen. It is ek wol ris krekt west ôf stapte ik earne oer hinne.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131570,"r":"KEUNING011101","p":"Wetzens","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman sees funeral processions and a prediction of misfortune comes true.","i":"S.K.","o":"De húshâldster fan myn omke seach soms yn 'e nacht in lykstaesje. Ek hat sy in kear sein, dat der in ûngelok barre soe. En dat kaem ek út. It wie yn de môlkfabryk.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131596,"r":"KEUNING011603","p":"Ternaard","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Warning to walk on the right side, or else risk meeting a funeral procession.","i":"S.K.","o":"Wy waerden altyd warskouwe troch ús âlden oan de goede kant fan de wei to rinnen. Oars koenen wy lêst fan in lykstaesje krije.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131679,"r":"KEUNING013005","p":"Blije","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Warning to walk on the right; walking on the left or in the middle risks being picked up and lifted over the funeral procession.","i":"S.K.","o":"De bern waerden hjir altyd warskouwe, dat sy oan de rjochterkant fan 'e dyk rinne moasten. Rounen sy by joun oan de linkerkant ôf yn 'e midden, dan koenen hja opnaem wurde en fan foaren nei efteren oer in lykstaesje hinne tild wurde.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131697,"r":"KEUNING013305","p":"Hegebeintum","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The seer of a funeral procession predicts who the dead person is, and this comes true.","i":"S.K.","o":"In âld man stie, mei de hân boppen de eagen, yn de fjirte to dikerjen. In oare man seach him dêr stean en saei: \"Soa âlde, hwat sjochstou dêr wer?\"\nDe âlde andere: \"Dû hast de gek der mei, mar astou wytste, hwat ik sjoch, lakest net mear.\"\n\"En hwat is dat dan?\"\n\"Ik sjoch in lyksteasje. En it lyk, dat bistû.\"\nIt moat ek útkaem wêze.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131718,"r":"KEUNING013704","p":"Gytsjerk","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"At night funeral processions are often seen with a black figure in front. Someone who has done wrong is pushed aside.","i":"S.K.","o":"Nachts seach min faek in lykstaesje op 'e wei. Dêr roun in gestalte yn it swart foarop. En it wie ek samar wer wei. Kaem ien, dy hwat op syn kerfstok hie, sa 'n lykstaesje tsjin, dan waerd hy oan de kant smiten.","l":"Fries"},{"n":72618,"r":"KOOIJMAN1128","p":"Hoenkoop","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Kees Stolwijk says that his wife's father used to live in Honkoop. Once when they were walking somewhere, her father suddenly said that someone had to step aside. They did not want to. He could see what was coming and the others could not.\n\nMrs Stolwijk says that her father called out that they had to step aside, because a funeral procession was coming.","i":"H.K.","o":"M'n vrouws vader woonde vroeger in Honkoop. Toen wazze ze op weg, ze liepe zo'n beetjie. ,Joh, gaat effe op zij\", zee m'n vrouws vader toen. Nee, daar wouwe ze niet an. ,Je zit temee zo van de dijk\". Toen ging het volk op zij. Want hij zag het wel, maar de andere niet.\n\n(Mevrouw Stolwijk)\n\"Op zij, op zij\" , zee m'n vader, \"d'r komt een begrafenisstoet\". Dat is in Hoenkoop gebeurd. Een hele lijkstoet. \"Lope jullie maar op zij\""},{"n":72694,"r":"KOOIJMAN1197","p":"Blokland","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul was walking on the dike when he was pushed aside by a funeral procession. That funeral procession was for a man who did not die until the following night.","i":"H.K.","o":"D'r was een man, die was met de helm gebore. Op een dag liep die op de dijk en toen werd ie op zij gezet door een begrafenisstoet. Hij kwam onder an de dijk terecht. Die begrafenisstoet was van een man, die pas de volgende nacht kwam te sterve."},{"n":72702,"r":"KOOIJMAN1203","p":"Blokland","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"There was once a man who was born with a caul. He could foresee funeral processions. Sometimes he would stand in front of someone, and if that person then looked back, he saw the funeral procession too.","i":"H.K.","o":"Met de helm gebore, ja, je had hier vroeger een man, die met de helm gebore was. Die man kon begrafenisstoete vooruitzien. 't Gebeurde wel, dat ie pal voor iemand ging staan. Dan keek die over de linkerschouder van zo'n man en as die man dan omkeek dan zag die ok de begrafenisstoet."},{"n":72828,"r":"KOOIJMAN1313","p":"Woudrichem","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman was born with a caul. When someone was dying, she would call out that a funeral procession was coming.","i":"H.K.","o":"Een vrouwke hier, da was met den helm geboren. As d'r iemand op sterven lag, dan liep ze door de straat: \"Ga opzij, want d'r komt een begrafenisstoet\" ."},{"n":72853,"r":"KOOIJMAN1334","p":"Giessen","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"There were people with second sight who could see a funeral procession coming.","i":"H.K.","o":"Je had van die mense, altijd als er iemand stierf in 't durp, dan door de deur kijke. Vooruit een begrafenisstoet gezien. M'n oom, die lag ziek en m'n vaoder die ging daor wake. En d'r was nog een man in Rijswijk die moest d'r altijd uit. Op een nacht werd d'r an 'm gevraagd: \"Waar vandaon komt 't lijk?\" En dat is uitgekomen.","l":"Noord-Brabants"},{"n":125550,"r":"KOOIJMAN1432","p":"Woudrichem","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"It was said of a woman that she was born with a caul. She had second sight and the children were afraid of her.","i":"H.K.","o":"Da was een vrouwke bij ons, die woonde vlak bij ons in de Schoolstraat. En die zeje ze dat ze met den helm gebore was. Ze zag vooruit een begrafenis. De kindere ware bang van da vrouwke.","l":"Noord-Brabants"},{"n":125775,"r":"KOOIJMAN1584","p":"Veen","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People born with a caul can see a death coming. They see a funeral procession beforehand.","i":"H.K.","o":"Met den helm gebore, ja, ik heb is een ouwe knecht gehad en die vertelde, as d'r in de buurt iemand op sterve lag, dan had je sommigte, die moeste daar naar toe. Dan kon die daags tevore de begrafenisstoet zien. As 't kind gebore was, moest 't vlies vernietigd worden."},{"n":127477,"r":"KOOIJMAN2209","p":"Hurwenen","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People met a funeral, but the person to be buried had yet to die. The people who saw this were pushed off the road.","i":"H.K.","o":"Da waren mensen dan kwamen ze een begrafenis tegen. Maar die begraven moest worden, die moest nog sterven. Die mensen die dat zagen werden van de weg afgezet."},{"n":207244,"r":"KUSTERS008008","p":"Heeze","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing a fireball; people being pushed aside.","i":"C.K.","o":"Soms is er 'n vuurbol gezien en in oude tijden zijn ooit mensen van de weg af getrokken."},{"n":207319,"r":"KUSTERS008603","p":"Lierop","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing a funeral procession is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"C.K.","o":"Er zijn mensen, die in de toekomst kunnen kijken. Als die aandrang komt, kan men ze niet tegenhouden; ze zijn gedwongen daaraan toe te geven. Zo 'n man ging onder het werk plotseling naar buiten. Binnenkomend vertelde hij, dat hij 'n begrafenisstoet had gezien: teken dat binnenkort iemand zou sterven. Inderdaad was in die buurt, kort daarop, 'n onvoorzien sterfgeval."},{"n":45398,"r":"WEV003102","p":"Musselkanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing a funeral procession and the dead returning.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ja, mien moeke woonde op de Hörsten bie mensen in de buurt, dai ook slim biegeleuvig wazzen.\nDe man laip asmits veur ’n liekwoagen over ’t kerkhof; hai zag dai woagen tenminste en dan möz hai mit.\nDe vrou zag gounend weer, dai al laank dood waren. In de Muzzel, woar onze buurvrou ook rooms was, zee ’t zölfde.\nRoomsen leven slim in de verbeeln, dat zuks kan.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45414,"r":"WEV003301","p":"Mussel","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Fear of dogs howling and birds screeching; seeing a funeral procession; fear of a spinner woman in a wood.","i":"F.W.","o":"In Onstwedde wazzen vrouger de maiste mensken biegeleuvig.\nVeur hondengehoel wassen de lu baange, want dan kwam d’r ’n dode. Vogelgeschatter hadden z’ ook ’n hekel aan.\nDan wazzen d’r gounend, dai liekwoagens zaggen en dan gungen ze mitlopen.\nIn ’t Metbroukerbos zat ’n wief te spinnen, doar dözzen de lu nich langs.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45512,"r":"WEV003402","p":"Zaadstukken","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Being able to see events in advance used to be common. A man sees funeral processions at night and then has to get up.","i":"F.W.","o":"Voorloop? Ja, dat zal ’t wel zijn. Och, ik heb veel mensen gekend, die van te voren branden zagen, huizenbouw, wegen, kanalen, spoorlijnen, auto’s en ga zo maar door. Dat was in mijn jeugd de gewoonste zaak van de wereld.\nDie mensen zijn meest gestorven. \nEen ken ik er nog; de heer S. te Veenhuizen bij Onstwedde.\nDe man is nu al oud en ik weet niet, of hij nog wat ziet. Vroeger was ’t een echte “spuikkieker.”\nGeregeld zag hij lijkwagens.\nVooral ’s avonds en ’s nachts. En dan stapte hij zijn bed uit, ging naar buiten en liep over de weg, waar binnenkort een lijkstatie zou passeren. \nZ’n vrouw zei wel eens: “Blief toch liggen.”\nMaar dan zei hij: “Dat kan ’k nich, ik mout d’r hen.”"},{"n":45515,"r":"WEV003502","p":"Jipsinghuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees funerals in advance, including who walks in the procession and what they wear.","i":"F.W.","o":"In Onstwedde was een man, die begrafenissen zag.\n’t Is eens gebeurd, dat er een stoet voor zijn huis langs trok en dat men tegen hem zei: ”Die en die is er ook achter.”\nToen moet hij gezegd hebben: “Maar die komt ook nog, en hij heeft klompen aan.” En ja, even later had men deze man ook in de stoet gezien.\n\nGeloof je ’t niet? Denk maar niet, dat de mensen er om logen.\nWeet je, nu lacht men overal om, vooral jonge mensen. Er zal vroeger bangmakerij geweest zijn, dat neemt niet weg, dat alles versleten moet worden voor bijgeloof."},{"n":43119,"r":"WEV005303","p":"Roswinkel","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man warns people to step aside for a hearse that cannot be seen.","i":"F.W.","o":"In Barnflair luip'n ander man mit zien kameroad op kloarlöchte dag over de weg. Inains zèg 'e tegen kameroad:“Kom even biezied, ik zai 'n liekwoagen aonkomen.” Zien kameroad zag niks, man gung wel aan de kaande.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43120,"r":"WEV005304","p":"Roswinkel","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The hearse a man sees turns out to be an omen of his own funeral.","i":"F.W.","o":"Dou ik bie Onstwedde woonde, heurde ik 'n verhoal over 'n M. in de Plaggenbörg (gem Vlagtwedde.). \n M. har de vrou in berre. Was 'n popke komen. \nDe goie man komp op 'n middag bie hoes, stapt de dele op en zug doar 'n liekwoagen stoan. Mit peerden d'r veur. Doadelk gèèt 'e noar zien vrou en vrag:“Hou ist d'r mit?” Netuurluk was 'e schrokken en har 'e docht dat zien vrou 't nich laank meer muik. Man nooit har hai aan zuk zölf docht. En toch zag 'e zien aigen begravvenis. 'n Zet loater kreeg 'e longentsteekn en binnen drai doage was 'e vot.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43281,"r":"WEV006002","p":"Smeerling","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession; the boys do step aside, but still get pushed.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wie luipn as kwoajong ais n moal deur Onstwedde. \nDou bejeegn wie A.H. en dai ruip; “Goat es eevn biezied.”\nWie zeden: “Veur die?”\n“Nee, nich veur mie, en ik zeg ook nich veur wel, man dr mout net aine langs; hai wordt wegbrocht.”\nWie luipen stil door, man kreegn wol n fikse opdonder.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43296,"r":"WEV006301","p":"Dikbroeken","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a funeral: seeing the course of a funeral beforehand.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurbode.\nIk kwam es n keer op n oavend bie huus en toun bin k schrokn. Vlak bie huus zag ik dudelk n liekwoagn stoan. t Volk ston aal op tegelpad. \nk Wur dr huverg van, mor k heb dr niks van zegd. \nMoar n poar weekn loater wur de buurman begroavn.\n Ik har mie wat verloat en zodounde kwam ik wat loat op begravvenis aan. De woagn ston al kloar en de mensen luipen net over t tegelpad.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43358,"r":"WEV006403","p":"Nieuw-Weerdinge","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman who sees funeral processions at night has to get up.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nVrouw Pr. zag nog meer; zij woonde in het Eksler moeras. \nVeurnoamelk waarn het liekstaties, woor ze met bezig was. \nEn dan gung ze dr s nachts uut. \nHeur man zee dan:“Blief toch lign.” \nMoar dat kon ze onmeugelk. Dan zol ze er last van kriegen, zee ze.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43579,"r":"WEV006905","p":"Vriescheloo","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man tells another, who sees nothing, to step aside because a funeral procession is coming. The other man can see the procession when he places a foot on the left foot of the one who can see it.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nOp n oavend luipn voader en Oabram bie de weg. Den zegt O. “Kom, jong, eevn biezied; kompt n liekstoatie aan.”\n“Ik zai niks.”\n“Moar t is wel zo, kom aan de kaande.”\nLiekwoagen gung dr langs; Oabram zag de peerden en t volk ook.\nEn nou komt t aigenoardige. Mien voar zag ja niks. Toun zee Oabram:“Zet dien vout nou es eevn op mien linkervout; den zugst t ook.” \nVoader het dat doan en beslist zag hai de woagen toun ook langs trekn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43586,"r":"WEV007003","p":"Drouwenermond","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A girl born with a caul sees a hearse on the threshing floor and hears the sound of clogs. A few days later her deceased grandfather is brought to that house.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nWie hebben joaren terugge een wicht kend, die mit de helm geboorn was en soms n liekwaogen zag. t Is gebeurd, dat ze op n oavend tegen heur zuster zeg:“Doar komp een liekwoagn aan; o, hij giet noar ons huus; nou is e al op de dele, ik heur de klompn van de kerels.” \nEnkele doagen loater is dr warklek een overleden opa in dat huus brocht.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43587,"r":"WEV007004","p":"Drouwenermond","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A carter pulls over for a funeral procession that someone else does not see.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien voar reed es n moal mit iemand mit van de Roldermaarkt op huus aan. \nMidden op t Rolderveld zeg de voerman:“Ik moet even aan de kaante, want doar komp een liekstoatie aan.” Hij bleef toen stoan, tot de stoet veurbie was. Mien voar had van t hele geval niks zien.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44136,"r":"WEV007602","p":"Gieten","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The narrator was born with a caul, so she knows many things in advance. Her caul was burned straight away, so she does not have to go out and look at night.\nShe sees lights at a place where a churchyard is later built.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mit helm geboorn.\nDat bin ik zulf.\nn Hoop dingn wait ik den ook veuruut. Ik zai asmis n liekwoagn, moar k wait gelukkig nait, wel begroavn wordt. Mien helm is doadelk verbrand. As dat nait gebeurt, den loop je de kans, da-je dr s nachts uut moutn. Wordt ook beweerd, dat zo n helm joe in de oorlog vrijwoart veur koegels; n seldoat wordt dus nait troffn.\nIk vertel joe dus dingn, dei [k] uut aign ervoarn wait.\nWie woonden destieds in Erica. Op n keer zeg ik tegn mien moeke: \"Kiek doar es in t veld, doar goan twei lichies achter mekoar aan.\"\nPas joarn loater is dr op dat stee n kerkhof aanlegd. En de eerste dei begroaven wur, was aine, dei in de typhus overleedn was en doorom noar t liekhuussie brocht wur. Doarbie druigen de manlu twei lampies, ie waitn wel, van dei störmlanteerns.\nToun ik de lichten veur t eerst zain har, was dr van n kerkhof nog hailemoal gain sproake.","l":"Drents"},{"n":210096,"r":"HOL002309","p":"Kapel-Avezaath","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A place where people are pushed aside by a funeral procession; do not walk in the middle of the road at night.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Sommige mensen vertelden, dat men in \"den donkeren avend\" van de weg kon worden gezet. In Zoelen bij \"de Schèlen hoek\" was het een gevaarlijke plaats; daar gebeurde het wel en men kwam dan in de Linge terecht.\nEnkele personen zagen daar een \"lijkstatie\" trekken. Het was lang niet zeker, dat hun metgezellen die op dat moment ook zagen. Om niet het risico te lopen in het water terecht te komen, moest men 's avonds nooit midden op de weg lopen."},{"n":210117,"r":"HOL002410","p":"Opheusden","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Advice not to walk in the middle of the road in the evening, or you may be pushed aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen werden soms 's avonds aan de kant van de weg gezet. Er passeerde dan een \"lijkstatie\" werd gezegd. Maar niet ieder zag deze. Daarom moest men 's avonds niet midden op de weg lopen."},{"n":210118,"r":"HOL002411","p":"Opheusden","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man has to open the churchyard gate at night, sees a funeral procession in advance and knows who has died.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"V.d. Bosch (de Rank bijnaam) zag ze wel. Deze V.d. Bosch was eens aan het \"appels keden\" (toezicht houden op appels) aan de \"ginne\" kant (dus ten noorden v.d. Rijn). V.d. B. ging 's avonds altijd naar huis terug (men bleef ook wel i.d. boomgaarden 's nachts), want het zou kunnen gebeuren dat deze man 's nachts de \"hekkes\" van het kerkhof zou moeten open gaan zetten. \nToevoeging bij punt 11. V.d. Bosch sprak niet veel over zijn buitengewone gave. Hij wist wel, wie er begraven werd, als hij een lijkstatie zag trekken."},{"n":210138,"r":"HOL002511","p":"Kapel-Avezaath","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People being pushed aside; avoiding being pushed aside by not walking in the wheel ruts.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Twee mensen liepen op een donkere avond eens langs een weg. Op een zeker ogenblik werden ze van de ene kant van de weg naar de andere kant gezet. \"Ze zage niks, hurde niks\". Men moest om dit niet te beleven zorgen, dat men niet in het wagenspoor liep."},{"n":210201,"r":"HOL002710","p":"Ochten","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Pushed aside by a passing funeral procession and put into a ditch; seeing funeral processions by day.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"V.d. Hatert had eens iemand naar huis gebracht, die stevig gedronken had. Ook hij zelf had zich niet onbetuigd gelaten, maar hij kon nog wel alleen lopen Op de terugweg, nadat hij zijn vriendendienst had verricht, werd hij van de weg gezet in een sloot, hoewel hij dit niet wilde. Hij kreeg flinke natte voeten en benen. Dit gebeurde, omdat er een lijkstatie was gepasseerd, was de uitleg. Wilde men een nat pak vermijden, dan moest men 's avonds niet midden op de weg lopen. \nEen meisje zag zelfs lijkstaties midden op den dag."},{"n":210232,"r":"HOL002805","p":"Varik","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Someone born with a caul is clairvoyant and sees funeral processions.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Iemand, die met de helm geboren is, ziet van tevoren de dingen, die gebeuren zullen. Hij ziet ook lijkstaties (begrafenisstoeten), maar van wie, kon men niet zeggen"},{"n":210289,"r":"HOL003110","p":"Dodewaard","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Stepping aside for a funeral procession; having to get up at night and seeing a funeral procession.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Sommige mensen vertelden, dat zij op een donkere avond een \"lijkstatie\" hadden zien trekken. Zij moesten er voor op zij.\nEen arbeider (naam genoemd) moest eens volgens Vink, 's nachts het bed uit en toen hij buiten kwam, zag hij een \"lijkstatie\" voorbij trekken."},{"n":44139,"r":"WEV007702","p":"Ommen","v":"Ov.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A doctor warns people to step aside because of an approaching funeral procession.","i":"F.W.","o":"Lijkstaties.\nEr was een dokter, die zijn tochten per boot maakte, want goede wegen waren er niet. De boot werd getrokken door een knecht. Soms gebeurde het dan, dat de dokter riep: “Even an de kant, jongen, want er komt een lijkstatie aan.”\nDit was ook inderdaad enige tijd later wel eens het geval."},{"n":130177,"r":"BIJLSMA000106","p":"Hemelum","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One must not look over the left shoulder of a man born with a caul, who can therefore see funerals in advance, for then one also gets the second sight.","i":"T.B.","o":"In man, dy't mei in helm berne wie en dus bigangels (bigraffenissen) foarút sjen koe, moast men net oer it lofter skouder sjen, dan waerd men ek sa.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130257,"r":"BIJLSMA001107","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Do not walk in the middle of the road in the evening, or you risk being pushed aside by a funeral procession.","i":"T.B.","o":"Jehannes Hooghiemstra fortelde my noch ek, dat der foarhinne sein waerd, dat men by joun net midden op 'e dyk (op it hynstepaed) rinne moast. Der koe jin dan in lykstaesje tsjinkomme, en men waerd dan oan 'e kant setten.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130263,"r":"BIJLSMA001301","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul has to get up at night and sees funerals.","i":"T.B.","o":"Roel Otter, klokskilder op 'e Jouwer (73), fortelde my fan Thys kûper, dy't op it Sân wenne en kûper wie op it bûterfabryk fan Brouwer, dêr't nou D.E.fabryk is. Dy Thys kûper wie mei in helm berne, moast der nachts út en seach bigraffenissen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130278,"r":"BIJLSMA001603","p":"Rottum","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul warns people to step aside for a funeral procession. A warning not to walk in the middle of the road in the evening.","i":"T.B.","o":"Pake roun ris op in joun it Rottumer tsjerkhôf foarby mei in oare man. De man sei ynienen: even oan ’e kant, Van der Wal!\nPake seach neat bysûnders en frege de man hwat der to rêdden wie. De man woe der earst net oer prate, mar doe't pake der him op oanstie, sei er: \"Hjir gie sapas in lykstaesje lâns mei twa hynders foar de lykkoets. Jo kinne dat net sjen, ik wol, ik bin mei in helm berne\".\nPake sei: en as ik nou net oan 'e kant gien wie -. Dan, sei de man -, dan wiene Jo op 'e dyk fallen. Hy sei: Jo moatte by joun nea op it hynstepaed rinne, dan kin Jo soks tsjinkomme.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130287,"r":"BIJLSMA001702","p":"Haskerhorne","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A person born with a caul can meet a funeral procession.","i":"T.B.","o":"By Boyl roun - lang forlyn - in man mei de heit fan mefrou De Jong in sânwei lâns. Doe't hja by in oare wei kamen, sei de man: nou gean ik dizze kant op en dan kom ik aensens wer by Jo dêr't dizze wei op de oare útkomt. Sa barde en in ein fierder kamen de beide manlju wer byelkoar.\nDe man sei tsjin heit: Jo ha neat sjoen, tink?\nNé, sei heit, hoe dat sa?\nDe man sei: as ik dat paed fan Jo gongen wie, dan hie it barre kinnen, dat my in bigraffenis tsjinkaem. Dat is wol folle sa. Dêrom gean ik dy oare wei lâns. Jo sjogge soks net, ikke wol. Ik bin mei in helm berne.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130294,"r":"BIJLSMA001806","p":"Sintjohannesga","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession coming and warns others to wait.","i":"T.B.","o":"Jozef de Vries hat ris by Hindrik de Groot west te joupraten. Doe't Hindrik him wer útliet, bleau Hindrik yn 'e doar stean en sei: \"even wachtsje, dêr komt in lykstaesje oan\".\nJozef seach der neat fan. Even letter sei Hindrik: \"Nou kinst wol fuortgean, nou is it foarby.\"","l":"Fries"},{"n":130335,"r":"BIJLSMA002404","p":"Warns","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman walking in the middle of the road in the evening is pushed aside when she meets a funeral procession.","i":"T.B.","o":"Minne Neel roun op in joun to Himmelum midden op 'e dyk, op it hynstepaed. Hja waerd opnomd en oan kant setten. Hja wie - sa sei men - in lykstaesje tsjin kommen, hja hie neat sjoen.\nSadwaende is it nuodlik om by joun midden op 'e dyk to rinnen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":49640,"r":"GENDT011","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the past there were various people who claimed to see omens. These were often omens of death, such as the funeral procession of someone who had not yet died, the call of an owl, magpies flying about or a howling dog. Fire and unexpected visitors could also be seen in omens.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Er ware vroeger verschillende minse, die zèjje da ze van te veure iets al gezien hadde. Zo zagen ze al dagen en wèke van te veure ’n liekstoatsie over de weg goan, woarmee ’n bekende begrave wier. En lotter gebeurdenet ok zo. Aandre zagen van te veure al ’n huus braande. En het braandde lotter ok af. Ze nuumde de namen erbé’j. Aj ’n uul duk bij een huus hört krijsen, kuje ien de buurt ’n doje verwachte. Vliegen er eksters um ’t huus, dan is er hetzelfde gevoar. Eksters um ’t huus kunnen ok betèkene: ge krieg onverwachs bezoek. As ’n hond jank, kum d’r ok ’n doje. De begraffenisstoet zal dan uut dezelfde richting komme, as den hond zien kop hil bij ’t janke.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":49641,"r":"GENDT012","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession at night that the person walking with him cannot see. He pulls this person aside so the procession does not pass over him.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Hendje Rikken kos zelfs ’s nachs zo’n begraffenis zien onkomme. Ik liep ’n keer soaves loat mit ’m over de stroat, midden over de weg. Ienens groop Hendje mien vas en zèj: “Jong, kom gaauw on de kant”. En ’n eindje wieër vroegtie: “Wit gé’j wurrum ik da deej? Ik zag ’n liekstoatsie onkomme. Aj nie opzied was gegoan, was de liekstoatsie over ou hèr gegoan”.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":49695,"r":"GENDT061","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman sees her husband's funeral procession before he has died.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Moeder het duk verteld: “Voader had klem ien de mond”. Dor kosse ze vroeger niks on doen. Hé’j is er on gesturve. Moeder had van teveure al gezien, da ze ’m uut ’t sterfhuus droege. En wie ’r bé’j de begraffenis was.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":49779,"r":"GENDT128","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Someone can see which of the people walking in a funeral procession will die soon.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Ien Doornenburg het iemes duk al van teveure gezien, welke minsen, die ien ’n begraffenisstoet meeliepe, heel gaauw zoue stèrve. En ze zegge, dat ’t altied uutgekomme is ok.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":50160,"r":"GENDT134","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People are pushed aside in the evening; often they have seen a funeral procession approaching and did not step aside quickly enough.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Ik heb verschillende kere heure vertelle, da vroeger de minse van de weg af wiere gezet, ien den bèrm of ien de sloot, of da ze over ’n heg of vrach wiere gebeurd. Mar ’t gebeurde altied soaves. Ok zage ze dan wel es ’n liekstoet onkomme. En as ge dan nie gaauw wied genoeg opzé’j gieng, wier ge van de weg af gedouwd, ’n graaf of ’n heg ien.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":50199,"r":"GENDT175","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man knows in advance who has drowned; he has already seen the funeral procession.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Ik was ’n joar of 18 en ik werkte opte twedde febriek [steenfabriek]. Nöl Tunnisse werkte opte erste febriek. We zate mèd’n pluugske aander minse wa te schofte. Opens hörde we wa bé’j de rivier tegenover de erste febriek. En d’r holde wa minse nor toe. Iemes van ons pluugske zèj: “D’r zal iemes mèd’t steenkrujje van de pril [plank] afgevalle zien”. ’n Aander vroeg on Hendrik Arends, de ploegboas, of ie ekkes woj gon kieke. Die zèj: “Da doe ik nie gern. En d’r is genoeg volk bé’j um te helpe, as ’t mot”. En toe zèj Kees Janse: “Dor ister zeker een verdronke. Da kan zien: Nöl Tunnisse of Wim van Hendje boas”. ’n Schipper, die bé’j ons ston, gieng kieke en toetie wer terugkwam, zeitie: “Kees het geliek. Nöl Tunnisse is verdronke”. “Ja”, zèj Kees, “ik het ’t ow toch vöraf gezeid. ’k Had de liekstoet al gezien”.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":50204,"r":"GENDT180","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Advice not to walk or cycle in the middle of the road, or you risk being pushed aside by a funeral procession.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Ze zèje vroeger duk: “Lop of fiets nooit midden opte weg, want dan wor je op zied gezet dor ’n verbörge liekwage”.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":44276,"r":"WEV008303","p":"Nieuw-Weerdinge","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man is picked up by something and thrown into the water.","i":"F.W.","o":"Zulf beleefde ik ook es wat geks. Ik luip in Vledderveen veur ’t schip. Inains lag ’k midden in ’t daip; ’k wör net zo van de wale ofsmeetn. Mien voader ruip: “Wat mekaiert die?”\nIk zee: “’k Wait 't zulf nait, moar ’t was net of mie aine oppakde en biezied smeet.”\n’k Heb niks zain, moar binnen ook mensn, dei zeggen, dat er den ’n liekstoatie langs komp.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44283,"r":"WEV008406","p":"Nieuw-Weerdinge","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A funeral procession makes a man fall; dislike of magpies.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik zel joe aigen belevenissen vertellen; alles is woar.\n\nMien voader moz mit zien kameroad op ’n nacht woakn bie ’n zaike. Ze luipen langs ’t knoal. Doar lig mien voar opains midden op ’t ies. Uutgleden?\nNee heur, ’t was net of hai van de weg trokn was. Hai zel wel ’n liekwoagen teegn komen wezen.\nMien mouder woarschouwde altied veur eeksters veur de roamen.\nNait dat ik d‘r aan leuf, moar toch heb ’k ’t nait op dei vogels.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44290,"r":"WEV008604","p":"Emmen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Some people see funeral processions in advance; it is not known whether people are recognised or whether one has to get up at night.","i":"F.W.","o":"Lijkstaties zagen sommige mensen ook van te voren.\nMaar ik heb nooit gehoord, dat men personen herkende of dat de “ziener” er ’s nachts voor opstond."},{"n":44539,"r":"WEV008903","p":"Jipsingboermussel","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who sees nothing after being warned to step aside for a hearse is picked up and set aside.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien schoonvoader kwam uut de Pekel (Nieuwe Pekela).\nHai vertelde mie op n keer:\n\"Mien kameroad en ik wazzen op noavend loat bie t pad; wie kwamn van t wicht en den bin je ja maistied nait zo vrou.\nToun zee Jan, dat ik eevn biezied goan mos; er kwam wat aan.\nIk zee, \"k zai niks\" en luip den ook deur, moar Jan ston aan t kaande van de weg te wachtn.\nMoar opains wur ik oppakt en biezied smeetn; moar wat zain, nee heur.\nIk vruig toun aan mien kameroad, wat of dr west was.\n\"Gung n liekwoagen langs\", zee hai, dou zagst hom nait, moar ik wel.\"","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44550,"r":"WEV009006","p":"Holte","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man walking on the higher part of the road is picked up and thrown down, because he has collided with a hearse.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nMien man luip n moal mit aine in de buurt van Selng (Sellingen).\nWazzen twai weegn; de aine lag wat hoger dan de ander; mien man luip op de hogere. t Was aal veen, mou je reekn. Opains wordt mien man dan oppakt en noar doale (omlaag) gooid; dou kwam e bie zien kameroad terechte.\nHou kwam dat? n Zetkng loater is door boovn liekwoagen langs goan, woor mien man dou al teegn aan botst is.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43144,"r":"WEV010302","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman sees a hearse at the neighbours' that suddenly vanishes. At a later death a hearse stands in the same spot.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien moeke hef hier op de Tange es n keer wat beleeft, wat wel vaker veurkomt, moar nait veile mensn mitmoakn. \nZe gait es op oavend noar de buurman en den stait dr inains wat noast heur. As ze goud toukikt is t n liekwoagen. Zai gript dr op, moar den is t ding gans en al vot.\n n Zet noa tied wordt dr bie buurman n tweiling geboorn; ain van de kinder staarft. As liek woagen veur komt, stait dei op dezulfde stee woor moeke hom van te veurn woarnomen har. De olle lu hebben mie dat allemoal zulf verteld en aan de woarhaid huiven ie nait te twiefeln.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43145,"r":"WEV010303","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A warning to a boy not to go along with someone who gets up at night, for example to see a funeral. The other will make him look over his right shoulder to pass on the gift and be rid of it himself.","i":"F.W.","o":"Dat veurzain komt veul meer veur. t Is hail nait zo mooi, as ie dat bie, joe hebben. Ik zel dr nog wat van verteln. \nMien pabbe hef dat ook zulf beleefd; laigen dee hai nait en doorom is t woar.\nMien voader den was lutje knecht bie de boer. Was vrouger ook ja altied n grode knecht. \nDizze den sluip in de snikke. Moar asmits mos hai dr s nachts uut, want den zag e wat: n begravvenis of n geval van verdrinkn; den was e mit gain middel in huus teholn. \nNou zee mien pabbe, dei wel wat neisgierig was: \"Wat dust dr altied uut, loat mie ais n keer mit goan.\" \nDat mog den wel.\nMoar de boer dei dat vernam zee: \"Jong, dou nou nait, hai let die over de rechter scholler kiekn en den kenst doe t en hai is dr of.\" \nVoader hef zok roaden loatn en is nooit nit west.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43165,"r":"WEV010510","p":"Barger-Oosterveld","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who does not step aside after a warning is pushed aside by another man. When he looks over the other's right shoulder, he sees a funeral procession.","i":"F.W.","o":"Kwoad zain. \nMien voader luip es n moal mit aine op duuster pad, tuskn 12 en 1 uur in de nacht. Dou zee de veurste teegn mien voar dai achter hum aan luip: \"Goa eevn bie zied, komp wat aan.\" Mien voar zee: \"Dat dou k nich, ik zai niks.\" \nZien kameroad hef hum dou bie de schammelakn greepm en aan de kaan- van de weg hen zet. \n\"Kiek es eevn over mien rechter scholler? zee de veurste. \nMien olle heer hef dat doan en wat zag hai dou? \nKwam n liekwoagn aan mit volk dr achter enaal. \nDit mout woar gebeurd weezn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43177,"r":"WEV010702","p":"Weende","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man is lifted up with his bicycle and slammed to the ground. He believes he probably ran into a funeral procession.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloopm.\nDoar ken ik joe hail wat stoaltjes van verteln, dei allemoal woar binnen.\n\nToun wie in Duutsland woonden, heb ik wat anders mitmoakt. \nIk ree op n fietse over n vlakke weg. \nInains goa k omhoog de lucht in. Nait zo 'n groot ende, moar k vuilde t toch dudelk. Toun sluig k ondersteboovn teegn de vlakte. Gelukkig op de weg, anderswas k in de sloot terechte komen en verzoopm. \nIs mie netuurlijk wat teegn komen; woarschienlijk n liekwoagn; doar mou k over komen weezn, anders ken k t nait verkloarn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43188,"r":"WEV010705","p":"Weende","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A horse that refuses to go on at the churchyard may be seeing a funeral procession.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloopm.\nDoar ken ik joe hail wat stoaltjes van verteln, dei allemoal woar binnen.\n\nToun ik in Vlagtwedde op de omnibus ree, gebeurde t wel es, dat ik s nachts mit dokter op stap mos. \nOp n nacht reden wie langs t kerkhof en door blif mie t peerd stokstief stoan. Ik huif dr op, moar dat huilp nait; t ding dee gain stap meer. Dokter zee toun teegn mie: \"Niet slaan Winkel, het dier ziet misschien iets, wat wij niet zien.\"\n t Daier zel door veur t kerkhof ook wel n begravvenis zain hebben. Toun t eevn stoan har, gung e rustig weer wieder.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43248,"r":"WEV010803","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A young woman meets women in black clothing and headscarves who have thrown her off the road.","i":"F.W.","o":"Loat et ais vieftien joar leden weezn, toun trof ik nog n vrou in Jipsinghoezn, dei mie vertelde dat ze onderweg zwaarde wiefjes teegn komen was mit zwaarde doukn um de kop. Zai hadden heur net zo van de weg ofsmeetn. t Was n betrekkelk jonk mens, moar heur ollers wazzen in heur tied slim biegeleuvig. \nZo kennen ie nou nog enkeln teegn komen, dei weerde hechtn aan vertelsels, woor de maistn nou om lachn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43020,"r":"WEV010804","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A warning not to walk in the middle of the road, or you risk being flung aside. Children never walk in the track of a hearse.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien moeke zee altied: \"Kinder, loop nooit midden op de weg; ie kennen moar watin de muide loopm, da-je biezied gooid worn.\"\nWie pazzen den wel op netuurlijk.\nSpoorn van n liekwoagn luipen wie veural nait deur. \nGeslachtn laank hef t biegeleuf hier in Westerwolde touhollen. \nOllers verteln t aan de kinder en dei weer aan heur jongen. \nDe leste vieftig joar is t oarig aan t verdwienen.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43433,"r":"WEV011003","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A week after a woman has watched a hearse drive by for several minutes, a real hearse passes there.","i":"F.W.","o":"Liekwoagens. \nMien vrouw (deze werd geboren te Emmercompascuum en haar moeder te Roswinkel; ze bevestigde het vertelsel: F.W.) fietsde es n moal op Laudermaarke. Den zug ze inains n liekwoagn veur zuk; twei peerden dr veur. Zai stapt of, want achter zo 'n liekwoagn aanfietsn dat is ja zo roar. \nIn werkelijkheid was dr niks aan de hand en zai zag et verschiensel ook moar n poar menuutn. \nAl n weke loater gung dr eevnwel n liekstoatie langs.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43644,"r":"WEV011512","p":"Wierum","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A scoffer is frightened by a phantom funeral procession he meets one evening.","i":"F.W.","o":"Een man in Wierum had overal de gek mee. \nIedere avond kwam hij van zijn werk thuis; heel vaak stomdronken. \nOm thuis te komen, moest hij door een smal steegje. \nOp een keer slingerde hij weer van de ene kant van de weg naar de andere. \nDaar kwam hij opeens een lijkstatietegen. \nVan schrik werd hij bont en blauw. \nThuis ging hij dadelijk met kleren en al aan naar bed. \nHet spotten is nadien wel wat minder geworden."},{"n":130372,"r":"BIJLSMA002608","p":"Vegelinsoord","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People born with a caul who have to get up at night and see a funeral procession; from the person missing from the procession they see who will die; the gift is passed on by looking over the left shoulder.","i":"T.B.","o":"Hinke Kaert wie ek mei in helm berne. Hja moast nachts fan it bêd en seach dan in lykstaesje. Oan 'e lju, dy’t efter de bier rounen, koe hja dan ôfliede hwa't der miste en dus stjerre soe.\nTo Stobbegat wenne ek in jongfaem, dy’t mei in helm berne wie.\nIn man yn 'e Haske, Lute Papjes, wie mei it selde lêst oanhelle. Dy't him oer it lofter skouder seach, koe it ek sjen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130379,"r":"BIJLSMA002705","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession in the churchyard, led by a white figure that beckons to him. A few weeks later his father dies, and when he lies in the coffin the man sees that his father was the figure in the churchyard.","i":"T.B.","o":"In jager fytste op in joun let fan 'e Gerdyk nei Luksterhoek. Doe't er op it Sweagemerhou (Langsweagen) wie, moast er ôfstappe. Hy wist net hoe of hwat, mar hy waerd der om sa mar to sizzen ta twongen. It wie by it tsjerkhôf, dêr't in gloppe yn 'e hage wie. Hy seach dêr in lykstaesje. Foarop gie in wite gedaente dy't wonk. Doe wie alles wer fuort en stapte de jager wer op 'e fyts.\nIn fjirtsjen dagen letter gie de gryp roun. De jager syn heit krige ek gryp en dêrnei longûntstekking; hy rekke der mei fuort. Doe't de âldman yn 'e kiste lei, seach de jager klear, dat syn heit de forskining op it tsjerkhôf wie. Op dy joun dat de jager de bigangel seach, en ek in goed wike dêrnei, wie de âldman noch soun en goed.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130432,"r":"BIJLSMA003603","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul can say in the evening that people must step aside for a funeral procession. A few days later someone dies, and the funeral goes as the man saw it.","i":"T.B.","o":"Lang forlyn wenne der yn 'e Keakelsteech op 'e Jouwer in man (Van der Zee), dy't mei in helm berne wie. Hy koe soms op in joun sizze: \"gean oan kant, dêr komt in lykstaesje oan\".\nIn pear dagen letter stoar der dan immen, en de bigraffenis wie, sa't Van der Zee it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130443,"r":"BIJLSMA003704","p":"Eesterga","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A person born with a caul sees his own funeral and dies a few days later.","i":"T.B.","o":"To Easthim wenne foar in goed tachtich jier in man dy wie mei in helm berne. Dy man seach op in kear syn eigen bigraffenis. Hy hearde ek de klokken lieden. In dei of hwat letter kaem er to forstjerren.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130459,"r":"BIJLSMA004205","p":"Sondel","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The funeral procession for a boy who has died is exactly like the funeral procession a woman met at night.","i":"T.B.","o":"Fan Aldegea H.O. nei Harich rint in wei, dy't de Bokkeleane hjit. Dêr is Bakker syn beppe op in nacht in lykstaesje tsjinkommen. \nDe oare wyks stoar der in jongkeardel yn 'e Wâlde (Kolderwolde). \nDe lykstaesje gie de Bokkeleane lâns, en it wie deselde dY't beppe sjoen hie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130521,"r":"BIJLSMA004906","p":"Langweer","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A warning to step aside for a funeral procession.","i":"T.B.","o":"Op 'e Wâldfinnen, tusken Boarnsweach en de Jouwer, rounen op in nacht ris twa mannen. Der wie doe noch gjin dyk. De iene sei tsjin de oare: \"Gean oan 'e kant, der komt in lykstaesje oan\".","l":"Fries"},{"n":130547,"r":"BIJLSMA005110","p":"Bantega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul sometimes gets up at night to see a funeral procession, and then knows who will die. Once he sees a funeral procession coming and warns someone not to stay in the middle of the road. The other does not step aside, and has to climb onto a farm wagon, walk over the coffin and then get off.","i":"T.B.","o":"Alde Roelof Schaap to Eastersé (Postma hat wol mei him arbeide) wie mei in helm berne. Nachts moast er soms fan 't bêd en seach dan in lykstaesje út in hûs kommen mei alle bysûnderheden, dy 't der om en ta hongen. Hy wist dan hwa 't der kaem to forstjerren, en it kaem ek stéfêst út.\nOp in kear roun er mei in oare man op 'e dyk, doe 't er ek in lykstaesje oankommen seach. Hy sei tsjin de oare, dy 't op it hynstepaed roun, dat er romte jaen moast. Mar de oare seach it net en gie ek net oan kant. In eintsje fierder sei de man: \"Ik fornaem wol hwat, ik moast earne opstappe en doe wer ôfstappe\".\n\"Ja\", sei Schaap, \"dou bist op de boerewein stapt, oer de deakiste hinneroun en doe wer fan de wein ôfstapt\".","l":"Fries"},{"n":130551,"r":"BIJLSMA005201","p":"Sint Nicolaasga","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul predicts a fire and a child's drowning, sees funeral processions and then knows who will die.","i":"T.B.","o":"Der wenne foar sa 'n sawntich jier to Wirdum in Aent Smoar. Hy wie mei in helm berne. Hy foarsei op in kear, dat der in pleats ôfbrânne soe en dat der in jonkje yn in sleat fordrinke soe. It kaem krekt út sa 't er it foarsein hie. \nEk seach er yn 'e nacht wolris in lykstaesje, en koe dan sizze hwa 't der weireitsje soe.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130557,"r":"BIJLSMA005301","p":"Sint Nicolaasga","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul has to get up at night to see a funeral procession. He goes to a quack healer on behalf of others.","i":"T.B.","o":"Der wenne foar jierren in Anne Snider - de man wie snider fan syn fak - to Jidskenhuzen. Hy reizge foar de doarpslju nei it Staphorster boerke. Anne Snider wie in tige leauwich man. Hy seach mear as oaren; hy wie mei in helm berne. Nahts moast er fan 't bêd en seach dan in lykstaesje. Troch ophingjen hat er himsels optlêst tokoart dien. Hy hie op in briefke skreaun: \"onbegrijpelijk, raadselachtig\".","l":"Fries"},{"n":130578,"r":"BIJLSMA005902","p":"Poppenwier","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul has to get up at night to see a funeral procession, which is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"T.B.","o":"By Schilstra syn heit wenne destiids in arbeider, Jehannes Fokma hjitte er, dy wie mei in helm berne. Nachts moast er fan 't bêd, en seach dan in lykstaesje. Dan kaem der ien to forstjerren.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130585,"r":"BIJLSMA006006","p":"Gauw","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession; a week later someone dies.","i":"T.B.","o":"Op in winterjoun hie in boerefeint to Gau ôfljochte. Hy seach optlêst noch even troch it bûthúsfinster nêst de doar. Hwat er sjoen hie, dêr bisaude er fan, en sa wyt as in doek kaem er yn 'e hûs. Hja seagen it wol oan him en fregen hwat der oan skeelde. Troch dat finster hied er efter op it hiem in lykstaesje sjoen. De oare wyks kaem der ien to fostjerren.","l":"Fries"},{"n":12252,"r":"CJ001004","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul sees a funeral procession; a few days later a woman dies.\nHe also dares to speak to the dead. A friend promises a dying man that he will see to it that a payment is made. He forgets, whereupon a ghost starts haunting the widow. After the debt is paid the ghost stays away.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Gerben Visser wenne op 'e Tike. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren. Op in joun hied er mei 't wiif to praten west. It gong froeger faek op in jounpraten. Se wienen ûnderweis nei hûs ta.\nMast even achter my gean, sei Gerben tsjin har. Is der hwat, Gerben?\nJa, sei er. Doe gong er in eintsje sydlings op in sânpaed.\nEven letter sei er: Kinst wol wer njonken my komme.\nHast hwat sjoen?\nJa, sei er. Der kom in slide lâns mei in lyk der yn. Dat wie ús nije slide.\nKobus de Vries fortelt fierder: De suster fan myn heit forstoar in pear dagen letter. It wie yn 'e winter en de wegen wienen tige glêd. Doe ha se de slide fan Gerben liend en dêr is se yn nei 't hôf ta brocht woarn.\n\nGerben doarst ek wol forstoarnen oan to sprekken, dy't weromkamen.\nAlbert Gjert hie gedoente mei Tseard kuorkemakker. Op in kear kom Albert by him. Hoe giet it mei dy, Tseard? \nNet bêst, jonge. Ik liz hjir nou al gâns in skoft. Ik krij der net in healjier mear by.\nHy krige gelyk. Binnen 't healjier rekke er hjir wei. Mar foar syn forstjerren sei er tsjin Albert:\nAs ik der aenst ôf kom to reitsjen, wolst der dan om tinke, dat ik noch in protsje rogge ha, dat noch bitelle wurde mat? Ik wol net mei skulden yn 't graef lizze. Soargestû der foar dat dat yn oarder komt?\nAlbert biloofde it.\nMar it hinge mei 't biteljen. It wie Albert syn doel wol it to dwaen, mar hy kom der net oan ta.\nMar Tseard syn wiif hie gjin rêst yn '","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12270,"r":"CJ001106","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man often has to get up at night to see something, usually funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tsjerke Lize wie heldersjende. Hja wenne oan 'e Mûzegroppewei en moest der hiel faek ôf nachts om hwat to sjen. Sy seach dan meast lykstaesjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12275,"r":"CJ001111","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A boy was worried for a long time after seeing a funeral procession, but it did not come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ien kear ha 'k yn 'e nacht in lykstaesje sjoen. Ik wie doe noch in jonge. Ik ha der lange tiid raer fan west. Mar it is by myn witen noait neikom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12330,"r":"CJ001420","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"There are funeral processions on the road at night. I have often enough heard the funeral clothes flapping.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wienen nachts faek lykstaesjes op 'e wei. Ik ha faek genôch de regenkleden wapperjen heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15597,"r":"CJ002409","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two men are walking along the road in the dark when one pulls the other aside and warns him of a funeral procession. It has passed by, but the other man has seen nothing go past. If the first had not pushed him away, he would have rolled over the hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear roan myn omke mei Martens Ale oer de Aldegeaster dyk. It wie tsjuster. Ale sei: \"Mast hjir even komme, Hindrik, der komt in lykstaesje oan.\"\nEven letter sei se: \"Nou kinst wol wer op 'e wei rinne, hy is foarby.\"\nOmke sei: \"Ik sjoch neat.\"\n\"Mar goed, dat ik der by wie\", sei se. \"Oars gongst der foar by op en der achter by del.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15723,"r":"CJ002820","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession pass by, with a white and a black horse in front of the hearse. He says that someone will therefore die soon, but nobody believes him: there is not even a farmer with a white and a black horse. Yet he soon dies himself, and there are a white and a black horse in front of the hearse after all: borrowed from a neighbour, because the water was too high for the family's own horses.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wenne to Aldegea in man, dy seach dat der ien yn 't koart stjerre soe. Hy seach de lykstaesje fan tofoaren, der roan in swart en in wyt hynder foar de wein.\nSyn famylje lake der om. Dat koe net, seinen se, der wie yn Aldegea net iens in wyt en in swart hynder by ien en deselde boer.\nMar de oare wyks stoar der in man. Wylst er dea op ierde stie woarde it wetter sa heech, dat sy koenen net fan 't hiem komme. De hyns fan 'e buorlju doarsten net troch 't wetter.\nDoe woarden de hyns fan 'e nijboer ynspand, dy't fan 't Amelân kom, en dêr krekt kom wie to wenjen. Dy hie in wyt en in swart hynder en dy beide dieren woarden foar de wein spand.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15895,"r":"CJ003905","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Teake Postma was born with a caul and can see future events. He sees the funeral of Lefferts Willemke in Bosk fourteen days in advance and sees exactly what the funeral procession will look like.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Teake Postma wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest alles sjen. Nachts gong hy der ôf en dan seach er lykstaesjes. Hy hat de hiele bigraffenis sjoen fan Lefferts Willemke yn 'e Bosk (yn 'e Harkema).\nFan to foaren hat er de hiele bigraffenis útskildere. Der roan in wyt hynder foar de boerewein. Hy fortelde hwa't de foargong hie, hoefolle man der achteroan roannen en hokker jas dy en dy oanhie.\nOp in joun wied er mei 't jongfolk op 'e wei. Doe sei er tsjin syn maten: Ik mat hjir even wei gean, ik sjoch in lykstaesje.\nDy bigraffenis fan Lefferts Willemke wie 14 dagen letter as doe't er it sjoen hie. It wite hynder wie fan Jetse Stoarm.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16131,"r":"CJ004616","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Boardzer Bruining (son of Thomas Klare, see: Kollumerzwaag) lives at Houtigehage and was born with a caul. One night he had to go out; he was woken. When he came home he was as white as buttermilk. He had seen a funeral procession. There was a puddle on the road and the horse stepped around it. That same week a funeral procession came by and the horse walked around the water.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining (soan fan Thomas Klare - sjoch Kollumersweach) wennet op 'e Houtigehage en is mei de helm geboaren. Op in nacht sei er tsjin syn wiif Duotsje:\n\"Ik mat der wer út, ik wurd kloppe.\"\nDoe't er wer thús kom, wied er sa wyt as sûpe. \"Ik haw in lykstaesje sjoen\", sei er. \"Der lei in plak wetter op 'e wei, dêr stapte it hynder om hinne.\"\nDeselde wyks noch kom der in lykstaesje en it hynder roan om it wetter hinne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16776,"r":"CJ006109","p":"Noardburgum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The narrator meets a funeral procession around midnight.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie in broer yn 'e Westerein wenjen. Dêr kom ik op in nacht sahwat om tolve ûre hinne wei op 'e fyts. Doe't ik omtrint by de Skilige Piip wie skaefde der in lykstaesje flak by my lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16828,"r":"CJ006215","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One evening a woman is suddenly knocked off the road. She had walked into a hearse and fallen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us buorfrou roan altyd midden op 'e wei lâns. Doe rekke se op in joun ynienen by de wei del. Sy wie by in lykwein oproan en doe foel se der by del.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16836,"r":"CJ006301","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One evening a woman is coming back from milking. Suddenly she is thrown into a ditch, milk and all. It had been a funeral procession that swept her off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn wiif soe om molke. 't Wie by 't winter, om in ûre of sawn hinne op 'e joun. Doe woardde se samar mei molke en al, doe't se werom kom, yn 'e sleat set. Samar fan 'e wei ôf, hjir flak by. As Janne Swaen har net holpen hie, wie se der net wer levend útkom. 't Hat in lykstaesje west, dy't har fan 'e wei ôfreage hat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16837,"r":"CJ006302","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"An old woman is pushed off a path. She ends up in a ditch. It was caused by a funeral procession. Some time later a real funeral procession went along the same path to the churchyard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek âlde Sytske, oan 'e oare kant it tsjerkhôf ha se sa oan kant set. Sytske kom ek yn 'e sleat tolânne. Dat wie ek in lykstaesje. In skoftsje letter is âlde Harte Jehanne stoarn. Dêr hat it fan west. Dy ha se lâns 't selde paed nei 't hôf ta brocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16851,"r":"CJ006413","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two people live in Twizelerheide. Their little daughter is ill. The man says to his wife: \"We won't keep our girl, there goes the funeral.\" On the path is a drake with 7 ducks. A week later is the child's funeral. The hearse in front and 7 people behind it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Twizelerheide wennen twa minsken, dy har famke wie siik. Doe sei op in kear de heit tsjin 't wiif: \"Wy hâlde ús famke net, sjoch, dêr giet de bigraffenis.\" Doe wie dêr op 't paedtsje in jerke mei 7 einen. In wike letter wie de bigraffenis fan 't famke. De lykwein gong foarop en sawn minsken der achteroan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16852,"r":"CJ006414","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Rapke Tuinstra and his brother-in-law Beam Reisma go out to catch moles. When they are near Gjert Oosterwoud in the Wylgen, Rapke says that Beam is pushing him into the ditch. Beam denies it. Splash. Rapke is in the ditch. According to Rapke he was cycling in the middle of the road. It was as if he was pulled into the canal along a line. He had collided with a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Rapke Tuinstra en syn swager Bearn Reitsma wennen yn 'e Wylgen. Sy soenen der togearre op út to mollefangen. It doel fan 'e reis wie Swolle. Sy wienen sahwat by Gjert Oosterwoud yn 'e Wylgen, doe sei Rapke: \"Bearn, dû twingst my yn 'e sleat.\"\n\"Welné,\" sei Bearn, \"ik bin in hiel ein achter dy, ik bin lang net oan dy ta.\"\nKlets, dêr lei Rapke yn 'e sleat.\nBearn sei: \"Hoe hiest dat? 'k Wie lang net oan dy ta.\" Doe sei Rapke: \"Ik fytste op 'e midden fan 'e wei. Doe wie 't krekt as gong it by in line lâns, dy't my yn 'e feart twong.\" 't Wie in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16869,"r":"CJ006517","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman goes with a friend to the singing evening of the Salvation Army. On the way home one ends up in the ditch and the other against the house. It is a funeral procession that pushed her aside. Shortly afterwards her mother dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't de frou fan Mekke Witteveen noch faem wie, gong se wol nei de heilsoldaten dy't op 't Bomkleaster preken. Dêr gongen se dan jouns sjongende wer wei. Op in kear wie dat ek wer sa it gefal. Hja hie in kammeraetske by har. Doe't se al tichte by har hûs wienen, woarden se samar útelkoar set. De iene kom yn 'e sleat tolânne, de oare tsjin 't hûs oan. It wie in lykstaesje, dy't harren oan kant set hie. Sy hienen neat sjoen, mar even letter forstoar har mem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16880,"r":"CJ006606","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man was walking on a road with some young people. Then he saw a funeral procession coming and could make out everything clearly. Later a real funeral procession came past at that same place. It was all the same, except there was one horse and cart fewer. But a little later they came along too and the procession was complete.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Gjert van der Wyk wie mei hwat jongfolk op 'e wei. Doe seach er in lykstaesje. Hy koe alles ûnderskiede, alle persoanen, hwat se om en oan hienen en al sa mear.\nLetter kom der op dat selde plak yn werklikheit in lykstaesje. It wie allegear krektengelyk. Gjert seach it. Mar hy sei, der is ien hynder en wein to min.\nMar even letter kom Buma der noch oan mei in hynder en wein. Doe wie 't foltallich.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17018,"r":"CJ007616","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The narrator is walking beside a man born with a caul. The man pulls him aside when a funeral procession passes. The narrator does not see the procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in nacht roan ik mei ien de Swadde del. Dyselde wie mei de helm geboaren. Gean even oan kant, sei er ynienen. En doe luts er my oan. Hy seach in lykstaesje foarbygean, mar ik seach neat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17045,"r":"CJ007902","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Ale van Marten in Oudega was born with a caul. She saw funerals in advance. Once she saw a funeral procession coming across the land, which was still water then. A while later a daughter of Hindrik de Vries died. Those people lived in the polder and had to cross the water, otherwise they could not reach the road. The body had to be taken by boat across the water to the churchyard. Ale had seen all of that in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Martens Ale to Aldegea wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy seach bigraffenissen fantofoaren ensa.\nOp in kear seach se in lykstaesje oer't lân kommen, doe't dat allegear noch wetter wie. \nIn skoftsje letter stoar in dochter fan Hindrik de Vries. Dy minsken wennen yn 'e polder en moesten oer 't wetter, oars koenen se net op 'e wei komme. It lyk moest mei de bok oer 't wetter nei 't tsjerkhôf ta.\nDat hie Ale allegear al fantofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17074,"r":"CJ008002","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The narrator's father had a cousin, Tseard de Wal. He was born with a caul. He knew everything in advance and saw beforehand that someone would die. When someone was ill, he could sometimes say: \"I've already seen him as a corpse.\" Then you could be sure that person would not recover.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit hie in neef, dat wie Tseard de Wal. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy wist alles foarút en seach al fan tofoaren as der ien stjerre soe. Wie der ien tige min, dan koed er soms sizze: \"Ik haw him al sjoen as lyk.\" Dan koe men der fan op oan dat dyselde it net helje soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17090,"r":"CJ008102","p":"Sweagerbosk","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man from Kollum wants to leave his girlfriend's in Zwagerbos towards morning. When he gets outside, he stands still for a while. Then he warns that a funeral procession will soon come past from a house further along. Someone in the procession will wear a hat with a white plume. And so it came to pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear kom der in feint by de faem wei. Hy hie de hiele nacht by har opsitten en 't wie in eintsje yn 'e moarn op. 't Wie mendei.\nHy soe fuort. Se stienen togearre bûten, doe sei er: \"Ik mat fuort noch net hjir wei. Ik sil dy aenst wol sizze hwerom.\" Hy bleau in skoftsje stean to sjen. Doe sei er: \"Nou is 't foarby. Nou matte jimme der ris om tinke, it duorret net sa lang mear, dan komt hjir in lykstaesje foarby út dàt hûs (hy wiisde it oan) En dan mat der ien ûnder wêze, dy hat in wite plûm op 'e hoed. 't Is krekt sa útkom. It gebeurde yn Sweagerbosk. De feint kom út Kollum.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17091,"r":"CJ008103","p":"Sweagerbosk","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The narrator's father always said you should not walk in the middle of the road but always at the side, because a funeral procession may come along the road and then you get pushed aside.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit sei altyd: Jimme matte noait midden op 'e wei rinne, mar altyd oan 'e kant lâns, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje op 'e wei wêze en dan wurde jim oan kant reard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17092,"r":"CJ008104","p":"Sweagerbosk","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man from Kollum was born with a caul. Once, when he is standing at the window with his father, he asks him to step aside. Later he explains that his child is going to die. He has seen people come in and set a coffin down in the room. A few days later the child has died, and the coffin is put down in the same spot where he had already seen it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy feint út Kollum wie mei de helm geboaren. Doe't er mei syn faem troude kommen se earst by syn heit yn Kollum yn to wenjen. Dêr krigen se in bern.\nOp in kear stienen hy en syn heit foar 't finster. Doe sei er tsjin syn heit: \"Wol heit dêr even wei gean?\" Doe't syn heit dat die, sei er even letter: \"Nou kin heit der wol wer stean gean.\"\nDoe joech er de forklearring. \"Wy hâlde ús berntsje net,\" sei er. Ik seach hjir guon lâns gean, dy droegen in kistke, dêrom sei 'k tsjin heit of heit dêr even wei gean woe. Doe brochten se it kistke hjir yn 'e keamer. Sjoch,\" sei er, \"dêr komt it to stean. Dêr ha se it delset.\nIt is krekt sa kom as hy it sjoen hie. In dei of hwat letter is it berntsje stoarn en it kistke setten se del op it plak, dat hy syn heit doe oanwiisd hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17094,"r":"CJ008106","p":"Sweagerbosk","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The narrator's father is chopping chicory with a few others. Suddenly one of them stops and stares fixedly at the road. Then he says he has seen two funeral processions coming one after the other, and that the dead are related to each other. Shortly afterwards a brother and a sister die in Zwagerbos. They are buried in the churchyard at Kollumerzwaag. The procession passes the spot where they were working.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde ek us dat Knjillis mei heit en noch in pear oaren oan 't sûkerij-dollen wiene yn Kollumersweach. Mar dat is al forskeidene jierren lyn. Doe hâldden se even tabak. Doe't dat sahwat dien wie en de oaren wer bigongen to dollen, bleau Knjillis stean en seach mar strak nei de hurde wei. Even letter bigong er ek to dollen. Doe wie der ien by 't ploechje, dy frege Knjillis: \"Wie der wer hwat to sjen, Knjillis?\" Hy sei dat op in spottende toan.\n\"Ja,\" sei Knjillis, \"mar dat wie net sa moai, hwat ik sjoen ha.\" Der kommen twa lykstaesjes fuort achter elkoar oan. En 't wie ek noch famylje fan elkoar.\"\nEven letter forstoaren der yn Sweagerbosk in broer en in suster, in Sije en in Grytsje. Dy kommen yn Kollumersweach op it hôf. Beide lykstaesjes kommen by it plak lâns, dêr't it ploechje folk sûkerij-dold hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17106,"r":"CJ008203","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The brother of a woman who has died had already seen the whole funeral beforehand. He was pushed aside when the funeral procession went past.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik noch faem wie, fortelde in bolkoerrinster fan Garyp by ús, dat der wie in frommes yn Garyp forstoarn en har broer hie fan to foaren de hiele bigraffenis sjoen. Hy waerd oan 'e kant set doe't de lykstaesje foarby gong.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17336,"r":"CJ008708","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One evening the narrator's wife sees a funeral procession approaching. She goes to put salt in the potatoes, but when she comes back the procession has vanished. Shortly afterwards a funeral notice arrives and an old housekeeper of hers is buried. She does not know whether it is the same funeral she had already seen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn wiif stie us op in joun foar 't glês to sjen. Doe seach se ynienen in lykstaesje oankommen. De lykwein foarop, mei in man mei in hege hoed der op, allegear minsken yn 't swart der achteroan. Hja hie de jirpels oer en tochte: ik gean even nei achteren om sâlt yn 'e jirpels to dwaen; as ik dan werom kom, binne se hjir sahwat oan ta, dan sjoch ik it better.\nMar doe't se weromkaem, wie der fan 'e hiele lykstaesje neat mear to sjen. Hja stie forsteld. Healwei seizen op 'e joun hie se tocht, wie ek al in nuvere tiid. Binnen de wike kaem der in roubrief en moast se op bigraffenis fan in âld minske, dat froeger húshâldster by harren west hie. Of dat nou deselde bigraffenis wie, wist hja net, omt hja de minsken net ûnderskiede koe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17339,"r":"CJ008802","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man always has to get up at night when a funeral procession is coming. He cannot help it. He has to see it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Anne Bekkema dy moast der nachts altyd ôf as der in lykstaesje lâns kom. Hy sei: \"Ik ha der in hekel oan, mar ik kin der neat oan dwaen. Ik mòat it sjen.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17340,"r":"CJ008803","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One evening the narrator is out with his father. Suddenly his father says they must stand beside the path for a moment. His father does not say he sees a funeral procession, but he does see it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in joun kaem ik mei ús heit by ús beppe wei. Doe sei heit: \"Toe jonge, gean dêr út dy spoaren wei. ('t Wienen doe noch sânpaden) Wy bliuwe even stean.\" Hy sei net: \"Ik sjoch in lykstaesje,\" mar dy hat er dêrom wol sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17386,"r":"CJ009012","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The narrator's cousin once goes from Surhuisterveen back to De Harkema along the road that funeral processions take to the churchyard. Three times he is pushed off the road. Finally he is thrown into a ditch. This was done by a funeral procession he was walking in the way of.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger waerden de forstoarnen út 'e Harkema nei Surhuzum ta op 't hôf brocht. De lykstaesje gong in reed del, dy't njonken in paed wie. Dat wie it Langpaed. \nOp in nacht hie in neef fan my nei de froulju west yn Surhuzum. Hy wie op 'e weromreis nei Harkema.\nHy roan op 'e reed. Doe woarde er samar op it paed set. Hy gong wer nei de reed. Mar wer waerd er op it paed set, oant trije kear ta. En doe woarde er yn 'e sleat reard. Dat hat in lykstaesje west dy't dêr lâns kaem en hy hat yn 't paed roan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17469,"r":"CJ009316","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"It is late and someone sees through the window a funeral procession on its way to the churchyard. But there is no deceased with it. That night old Gradus dies, and at his funeral everything looks exactly the same.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie yn in barak. It wie let. Ik seach troch 't finster, doe woarde ik in keppeltsje folk gewaer. 't Wie in bigangel. 't Wie bigraffenisfolk, mar der wie net in lyk by. Hja gongen nei 't âlde tsjerkhôf fan Hamsterheide. Dy nachts is âlde Gradus forstoarn. Doe't dy biierdige woarde wie de sitewaesje krekt sa.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17474,"r":"CJ009403","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A father is on his way home at night with some other people. In the distance they see a group of people approaching and they hide for fear of being robbed. A solemn procession passes. The last man wears a tailcoat and briefly looks at the father. The father thinks it was a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en dy hienen to flaechslûken west yn Pitersbierrum yn Grinslân. Yn 'e nacht, sahwat om twa ûre wienen se ûnderweis. Se roannen net hurd, hwant der roan in ploechje folk út 'e Harkema foar har, en dêr wienen se hwat binaud foar. Dêrom bleauwen se hwat achter. It paedtsje dêr't se lâns roannen, dêr wie in stikje rogge njonken.\nDoe seagen se dat der yn 'e fierte hwat oankaem. Se koenen net sjen hwat it wie, mar sy tochten dat it it ploechje fan 'e Harkema wie en dat dy it op har jild forsjoen hienen. Dêrom fluchten se allegear yn 'e rogge en sy hâldden har sa stil as in mûs.\nMar sy wienen dêrom wol op har iepenst en seagen goed út nei hwat der gebeurde. Heit hie de holle boppe de rogge. Doe kommen der wol in 30, 40 man oan. Dy roannen allegear plechtich en statich en net ien fan har dy't in wurd sei. De achterste hie in flipjaske oan, en dy hie even oan kant sjoen en heit oansjoen. Mar der waerd neat sein. \nHeit tocht, dat dat in lykstaesje west hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17479,"r":"CJ009408","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A young man is walking on the road at night and it is dead quiet. Suddenly there are people all around him. They run past him without saying anything. When someone is buried later, he realises he has seen the funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der kom us in feint by de froulju wei yn 'e Westerein. It wie stil op 'e wei en der wie neat to hearren of to sjen. Mar doe stied er samar ynienen midden yn 't folk. Dy minsken roannen him allegear stadich foarby, sûnder dat se ien wurd seinen. 't Wie midden yn 'e nacht.\nIn dei of hwat letter stoar der ien by Klaes Pink (= Kl. Lulofs). Dat waerd de bigraffenis dy't hy sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17493,"r":"CJ009501","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"There was an old man who often had to get out of bed at night to go and look at something. If he stayed in bed, he was more or less thrown out of it. He often went to the churchyard, and once he saw a funeral procession there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Kollumersweach by 't spoar wenne in âld man, dy moest der nachts faek út om hwat to sjen. Bleau er lizzen, dat joech neat. Dan waerd hy der út dreaun, ja smiten hast. Hy moest dan faek nei 't tsjerkhôf fan Kollumersweach ta. Dêr seach er dan in lykstaesje. Dy man wie Bontsje Knjillis.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17581,"r":"CJ010103","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman claimed to see all sorts of things. At night she often got out of bed and then she saw funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Achter de Poel op 'e Boelensloane wenne âlde Elske. Dy moest fan alles sjen. Nachts kom se faek út bêd wei en dan seach se lykstaesjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17682,"r":"CJ010801","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A boy is born with a caul and always foresees everything. Once, coming back from milking the cows, he sees a funeral procession. He is so frightened that he spills all the milk. His mother is very angry with him about the wasted milk. His father is not angry, because he sometimes sees omens himself.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik bin mei de helm geboaren. Ik moest altyd alles sjen. Dat fornaem ik it earst, doe wie 'k toalf jier âld. Op in jountiid moest ik molke helje fan 'e boer. It wie noch ljocht. Ik moest skean de fjilden oer. Ik hie in fjildskutte by my lyk as de soldaten brûke. Dêr kaem de molke yn. Op 'e weromreis wie 't skimerich. By de hoeke fan 'e Sânwei seach ik ynienen in boerewein foar my en dêr stie in deafet op. Allegear folk roan der achter oan, it wie in lykstaesje. \nIk tochte: \"hwat bitsjut dit.\" Mar dy staesje bleau mar fóár my. Ik waerd doe sa deabinaud, dat ik puozze mei de molke. Der bleau neat yn 'e fjildskutte oer. Tichteby stie in lyts winkeltsje, dêr wenne in âld wyfke yn, dêr wie snobbersguod to keap en ek wol apels. Dêr roan ik hinne. En ik hie dêr net wei gong, ja, ik hie der hjoed-de-dei nòch sitten, wie it net, dat heit my dêr op it lêst weihelle hat. Mem fûtere bot op my, omt de molke allegear wei wie, mar heit fûtere net. Doe't ik it forhael fortelde, sei er: \"Dy jonge krijt it net maklik yn 't leven.\" Hwant hy wist wol hwat it bitsjutte as men hwat sjen moest. Hy sels hie it soms ek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17698,"r":"CJ011001","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A boy tells his friend to step aside on the road. Later he says he saw a funeral procession go past.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer Sytse Taekema wie us op in joun mei in freon by Piters Jantsje oan 'e Gielewyk. Doe sei er tsjin syn kammeraed: \"Jow even hwat rûmte.\" Mear sei er net.\n\"Hwat bistû healwiis, hwerom matte wy oan 'e kant gean?\" sei syn kammeraet. Mar Sytse woe 't net sizze. Letter hat er it forteld. Der gong doe in lykstaesje foarby. De regenkleden fan 'e froulju seach er wapperjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17715,"r":"CJ011114","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman was running down the middle of the road. Then she thought: \"Goodness, this is heavy going.\" Then she ended up sitting on a hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In frou út 'e Harkema roan op 't midden fan 'e wei. Doe tocht se: \"Heden, hwat giet dat swier.\" Doe gong se by in lykwein op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17723,"r":"CJ011206","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"An old man boarded with a married couple. At night he often got out of bed because he had to see hearses. As he grew older, it cost him more and more effort. He was then flung over hedges and fences by the devil just to be in time for the hearses. He was never late. When he really could not go on, he asked the couple to pray for him. The husband knew something about praying, and so the old man was released.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ús mem yn 'e Westerein wenne, wie der in âld man by har yn 'e kost. Dy moest der nachts faek ôf. Dan moest er in lykstaesje sjen. \nHy wie al sa âld en sa minnichjes, dat hy koe hast net mear út bêd wei komme.\n\"O Klare, Klare,\" sei er dan, \"ik mat wer fuort.\" Dan stie er op syn skonken to triljen. Hy woarde dan oer hagen en oer hekken hinne smiten om mar op tiid by de lykstaesje to wêzen. Mar hy kaem noait to let.\nOp 't lêst koed er bislist net mear. Mar hy moèst, sa sieten se him achter. Neffens my wie dat de kweade, dy't him achter siet.\nDoe smeke er Fedde, dat wie mem har twadde man, as dy foar him bidde woe, dat hy der net mear achteroan hoefde. Hwant hy sei: \"Ik ha gjin duer en ik kìn net mear.\"\nFedde hie wol hwat forstân fan bidden en doe is dy âld man dan forlost. It wie de duvel, dy't him oer hagen en hekken hinne smiet.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18144,"r":"CJ011805","p":"Gerkesklooster","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A carter is on his way home with a wagon of coal when he bumps into something and goes off the road. It turns out to be a funeral procession, but the carter did not see it himself.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ien fan dy beide mannen, Ate, wie ek fuorman. Op in kear helle er twa weinfollen stienkoal fan Bûtenpost. Dy moest er nei 't fabryk op Blaufallaet tabringe. Underweis staette syn wein tsjin hwat oan en rekke alhiel oan 'e kant. It hynder wie tige skruten, dat seach dêr in lykstaesje, hysels seach it net.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18190,"r":"CJ012012","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Someone ran into a hearse at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir hat ien wenne, dy roan by nacht midden oer de wei. Doe kaem der in lykstaesje oan, mar hy seach it net. Hy is foar by de boerewein op roan, en achter der wer by del.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19334,"r":"CJ012408","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man was once cycling along a road when he was suddenly lifted up, bicycle and all, floated through the air and landed in the ditch. There was nobody to be seen, so he thought he had ridden into a hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha mei in man wurke op 'e flaeksfabryk yn Bedum. Dy man kaem fan Twizelerheide. Hy fortelde my, hy fytste us op in saterdeijoune nei hûs ta. Hy fytste midden op 'e wei en wie sahwat yn Twizelerheide by de âlde staetsskoalle, doe woarde er samar mei fyts en al optild, sa sweefde er troch de loft en waerd pardoes op 'e kop yn 'e sleat smiten. Der wie net ien op 'e wei en hy hie hielendal neat sjoen.\nMar hy wie der wis fan dat it in lykstaesje west hie, dy't er tsjinkaem wie en dêr't er mei fyts en al oerhinne rekke wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19384,"r":"CJ012702","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman who had been born with a caul called her neighbour's girl to come and look at a hearse. A few days later a farmer's little son died. Then they saw the same hearse in reality.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn frou komt fan Bûrum. Sy hienen dêr in âlde buorfrou, dy hiet fan Roelfke. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Op in joun, doe wie myn frou noch in famke, doe kloppe Roelfke by harren op it rút. \"Der komt in lykstaesje oan\", sei se. Doe gongen se nei bûten ta en doe seagen se de lykstaesje. In dei of hwat letter stoar der in jonkje fan in boer. Doe seagen se deselde lykstaesje yn werklikheit.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19453,"r":"CJ012919","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man is knocked off the road by a hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jehannes Koster wenne yn Kollum. Hy hie in kear nei syn famylje ta west yn Twizelerheide. Doe't er op 'e weromreis wie, doe wie 't al let op 'e joun. Doe woarde er samar ynienen oan kant reage. Doe stie dêr in lykstaesje. Hy woarde sa binaud, dat hy is weromgong nei de famylje yn Twizelerheide en dêr is er dy nachts bleaun. Hy doarst net nei hûs ta.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19464,"r":"CJ013006","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One evening a man is knocked off the road by a hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sibe van der Veen wie boade fan 'e bigraffenis yn Harkema. \"Op in joun,\" sei er, \"kom der in lykstaesje oan. Ik waerd oan kant set. Ik seach alles. Ik wist ek wol hwa't de deade wie. Doe't de lykstaesje foarby wie, koe 'k wer op 'e wei komme.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19513,"r":"CJ013121","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You should never walk in the middle of the road, because then a hearse can suddenly push you aside.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne. Dan kin men samar oan kant reage wurde. Hwant dan rinne je yn 'e wei. Der kin in lykstaesje wêze.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19545,"r":"CJ013405","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man often had to get out of bed at night. Outside he would see a hearse go by. He always counted the people walking behind it. But he never knew who had died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw in omke hawn, dy wenne op 'e heide. Nachts dan moest hy der faek ôf om hwat to sjen. Dan wie 't krekt as woarde er roppen. Dan gong er oan 'e kant fan 'e wei stean. Dan seach er in lykstaesje. Hy telde altiten de minsken, dy't achter it lyk oanroannen. Mar hy wist noait hwà't der stoarn wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19587,"r":"CJ013802","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One night a man was knocked off the road. A funeral procession had probably passed by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In omke fan my fortelde my, hy wie us in kear by de faem wei kom op in nacht. De Trije Roede wie doe noch in sânpaed. Hy hie midden op 'e wei roan. Doe wied er ynienen fan 'e wei ôfsmiten woarn en yn 'e berm torjochte kom. De skuon hienen him fan 'e fuotten west. It mat in lykstaesje west ha, dy't der doe passearde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19602,"r":"CJ013910","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man regularly had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Sweagerbosk (by de Westerein) hie ús mem (Thomas Klare) in âld man yn 'e kost. Dy wie tige krebintich. Mar wie der in lykstaesje yn 'e buert op komst, dan moest hy dy fan tofoaren sjen. Hy koe hast net mear út bêd komme, sa knoffelich wied er. Hy tûmele der út. Dat gebeurde samar midden yn 'e nacht. Hy woarde dreaun. Hy mòest it sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19629,"r":"CJ014203","p":"Feanwâldsterwâl","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Old Metske Smit was born with a caul. At night he often had to get up to watch funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Metske Smit wie mei de helm geboaren. Yn 'e nacht moast hy der ôf. Dan seach er lykstaesjes de wei passearen. 't Kaem letter altyd krekt sa nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19696,"r":"CJ014601","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A farmhand is born with a caul and often has visions of the future. He lives in a small cottage on the farmer's land. The farmer has two sons, and one of them has made a girl pregnant. The farmer wants nothing to do with it, and the son asks whether the mother-to-be may live with the farmhand in the cottage for the time being. The farmer's son soon backs out, and in the end the farmhand marries the girl because he has come to care for her a great deal. One day the farmhand sees, in the middle of a funeral procession, a coffin with a white sheet. It is a vision: his wife gives birth to a daughter but dies in childbed.\nAnother day he is woken at night because he has to take the eldest farmer's son to the doctor. On the way back he again sees a funeral procession, but now with a very grand coffin. He foresees that an important person will die and tells the farmer. Some time later the youngest son is killed riding a wild horse. The funeral procession is the same one that had already been seen. The farmer beats the farmhand to death. The farmhand's daughter, who has grown up considerably by now, tells the farmer he will pay for the murder of the farmhand. The farmer cuts himself on a plant and gets an infection. A little later he dies of fever.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ergens yn 'e Wâlden wenne in âld-feint. Dy wie arbeider by de boer. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren en moest alles sjen.\nDe boer dêr't er by wenne, hie twa soannen. Ien dêrfan woardde great mei de faem. Dy faem moest fan him bifalle. Sy mienden 't elkoar wol, mar de boer woe syn tastimming net jaen.\nDoe gong de soan mei syn faem nei dy arbeider ta. Dy wenne allinne yn 'e húske. Hy frege of syn faem dêr in skoft tahâlde mocht. Dêr hie de arbeider gjin biswier yn. \"Ik sil 't jo forgoedzje\", sei er tsjin 'e arbeider.\nDe faem krige dêr doe har thús. Sy knapte dêr alles moai op, dat it kom der skjin en kreas út to sjen.\nDe arbeider hie wite en swarte skiep. Fan 'e wolle spoun hja jern en hja breide trije lytse gespikkelde boarstrokjes foar it lyts dinkje dat se ha soe. \nDe boeresoan bleau stadichoan mear wei en doe sei de arbeider tsjin 'e faem: \"Dû koest hjir om my wol bliuwe.\" En noch in skoftsje letter frege er har to trouwen en hoewol hy nochal hwat âlder wie, joech se har tawurd. Hja trouden togearre.\nMar doe't se in skoftsje troud west hienen woarde de arbeider hiel stil. Hy hie in lykstaesje sjoen, dy kaem by syn hûs wei en der lei in wyt ruft oerhoeks oer de kiste hinne.\nOp it lêst siet er to gûlen. Mar doe't hja frege nei de reden woe er it net sizze.\nMei de bifalling kaem der in famke. Mar de mem oerlibbe it net. De arbeider hâldde it famke by him. It sei 'heit' tsjin him.\nOp","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20020,"r":"CJ016307","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A clairvoyant often foresees a death. He has to get out of bed at night and then sees funeral processions passing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Steffen Veenstra wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest der yn 'e nacht út. Dan seach er lykstaesjes. Hy wist altyd fan tofoaren as der wer ien stjerre soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20131,"r":"CJ017106","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"An old man has seen a funeral procession twice, but he stayed standing in the middle of the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e tiid dat wy jonges wienen wenne âlde Harm Slinger (Harm de Haan) yn Twizelerheide. Twa kear hat er in lykstaesje sjoen. Hy gong noait yn 't midden fan 'e wei lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20376,"r":"CJ018705","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Children are warned not to walk in the middle of the road because funeral processions may pass. The processions are a harbinger of a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy mochten noait midden op 'e wei rinne fanwege de lykstaesjes, dy't ús oanrame koenen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20672,"r":"CJ020714","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You must never walk in the middle of the road, but always at the side. A funeral procession might come along that you cannot see.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In minske mat altyd oan 'e kant fan 'e wei rinne, noait yn 'e midden, hwant dan kin der us in lykstaesje oankomme, dy't men net sjocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33019,"r":"CJ085803","p":"Harlingen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man once saw a funeral procession approaching in the dark. When he had passed it, he saw nothing more.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik kom ris fan Grins mei de fyts. Ik ried troch Visvliet, doe wie 't al donker. Doe kom der my in lykstaesje tsjin. Doe't ik foarby wie doe wie alles fuort.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":50184,"r":"GENDT158","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A boy sees a funeral procession two days before a drowned man is carried past the house at the same time.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Ik was nog jong. Wel gieng ik al nor schol. We zate op ’n zondagnomiddig, um ’n uur of vier, same bute optebank. Voader en moeder waren d’r ok bé’j. Ienens zag ik over den diek ’n liekstoet vurbé’j komme, mè mar inkele minse d’r bé’j. Ik zèj tege voader en moeder: “Kiek es, ’n begraffenis op zondag”. “Och jong, ge ziet gek”, zèje ze, want zé’j zage niks. Mar twee dage dornoa kwam er op dezelfde tied ongevèr wel ’n liek vurbé’j. D’r ware mar inkele mense bé’j en ok de pelisie. Ze brochte ’t liek weg van ’n vremde schipper, die ien de Woal was verdronke en opgevist.\nVgl. Bandopname III, verhaal 5.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":43880,"r":"WEV012309","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession in advance.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloopn.\nOal Fekke, hai leeft nait meer, was vrouger in Bennewol ook zo'n man dei hail wat veuruut zag. \nIk ree es n moal mit hum deur t dörp en toun zee e: \"Ik mout eevn van de fietse of te pisn bie de boom.\"\nd Oale stait bie de boom en den zugt hai wat aankomen. \nLiekwoagn mit de volgers dr achter. \nHai vertelt mie dat, moar zee gain noamen. \nIk har zo laank op hom wacht en niks zain. \nNoa nait al te laanke tied bleek, dat oal Fekke zok nait vergist har.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43922,"r":"WEV012702","p":"Sellingen","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A warning to step aside for a cart with a coffin is voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wieluipen ook es n moal mit oons beidend op boetn en dou zee ootje: “Wacht eevn kind, goa es biezied, door gèèt n woagn langs mit n kiste dr op.”\nEen dag dr op was dr n staarfgeval bie de buurn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44367,"r":"WEV013103","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman who is thrown aside knows that a hearse will pass. \nA man who meets a funeral procession asks who is being carried away, and his own name is given.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mouder is ook n moal biezied smeetn van de weg of. Zo zee ze. \nZai haar n stomp vuild en door lag ze op de grond. Zai kraabde weer overenne; moar ze wos toun al, dat er n liekwoagn langs komen zol. t Mou ook gebeurd weezn.\n\nIn Wijmeer mout op dezulfde menaier n man s nachts n liekstoatie teegn komen weezn. Hai vruig de koetsier, wel hai nou toch weg brengen mos. De liekmenner har toun de dag en de noam nuimd van dei man zulms.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43656,"r":"WEV013804","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A girl sees a dead person being carried out of a house and who walks in the procession. After a death in that house, the funeral procession is just as the girl saw it.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik wait ook nog van ngeval van t Haim (t Heem bij Ter Apel). \nDoor dainde n maid van n joar of zestien.\nOp n oavend gait ze eevn noer boetn en blift n haile zet vot. \nDe dochter van de boer wil doorom es kiekn, wat of de maid toch uut hangt. t Wicht stait stil te stoarn noar n huus door nait ver of.\n“Wat wolt doe door aal zo te stief te kiekn?”, vragt boerndochter, “zugst misschien wat?”\n“Joa”, zegt t wicht, “ik zai wat. Door bie M. wordt net n dode tou t huus uut droagn.”\n“Hou komst dr bie; is ja gain mens zaik.”\n“Toch is t zo; kiek. doe lopst dr achter en doar lopt dei en doar achter dei.” En zo nuimde dat wicht n hail riege op.\nWerklijk is in dat huus ain sturven. Bie de begravvenis hebben ze dr op let en toun luipen ze net zo as dat kind veurspeld har.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":16498,"r":"CJ005208","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A few men were coming back from Leeuwarden one night. Alle Putter (=Jager) was with them too. Near Bergumerheide he said: \"Men, step aside, or we'll stumble. There's a funeral procession coming.\" When the funeral procession had passed, they went back to walking in the middle of the road. He was the only one who had seen it. A week later there was a real funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In stik of hwat mannen kommen fan Ljouwert. Alle Putter (= Jager) wie der ek by. 't Wie by nacht. Tichte by Burgumerheide sei Alle: \"Mannen, oan kant, oars stroffelje wy. Der komt in lykstaesje oan.\" Doe't de lykstaesje foarby wie, sei er: Kom nou mar wer midden op 'e wei. Hy wie de iennige fan 'e mannen dy't it seach. In wike letter wie dêr in èchte lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16499,"r":"CJ005301","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In Zwagerbosch there lived a man who very often had to go out at night. Once he had to go out again. Fedde, the second husband of Thomas Klare, had died then. The man saw Fedde's funeral procession. Some people followed him. All the gates opened for him. So he had to see it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Sweagerbosk wenne in man dy moest der nachts hiel faek út. Op in kear moest hy der ek wer út. Doe wie de twadde man fan Thomas Klare forstoarn, dy hiet fan Fedde.\nFedde en Klare wennen doe yn Sweagerbosk. Tusken eigen hûs en sterfhûs seach de man de lykstaesje fan Fedde. Guon binne him achternei gong. Doe seagen se dat alle hekken foar him iepengongen. Hy mòest it dus sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16507,"r":"CJ005309","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In Kollumerzwaag there lived a labourer who had to see everything. At night he would go out and run through the gates. They opened for him by themselves. In no time he was at the place where he had to be, as if he flew. Then he saw the funeral procession. He always knew who was going to die, but he never said.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Kollumersweach wenne in arbeider, dy moest alles sjen. Nachts gong er wit hoe faek út it bêd en der op út. Dan roan er as in hazze en hy switte as in oandrager. Hy roan gewoan troch de hekken hinne. Dy gongen fansels foar him iepen. Yn in sucht wied er op it plak dêr't er wêze moest, krekt as fleach er. Dan seach er de lykstaesje. Hy wist altyd hwa't der stjerre soe. Mar hy sei it noait.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16508,"r":"CJ005310","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One night a man saw someone coming towards him on the Feansterheide. He said good evening but got no answer. Then he saw the funeral procession coming. The man had been its forerunner.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der roan in man yn 'e nacht op Feansterheide. Ynienen sjocht er ien oankommen.\n\"Joun\", sei de earste, mar de oare sei neat werom. De earste sei noch us fan \"joun\", mar wer krige er gjin antwurd.\nDoe seach er in lykstaesje oankommen.\nDy man hie dêr de foarboade fan west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18091,"r":"CJ011413","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Once a man and a woman were out walking when the woman (who had been born with a caul) said they had to get away from that spot. The man refused and held on to her. But suddenly she is sitting three metres further on, on the road. A hearse went past.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanmem wie mei de helm geboaren. Sy wennen yn Ten Post (Grinslân). Op in kear wie se mei skoanheit oan 't kuijerjen. Doe sei se ynienen tsjin him: \"Wy matte hjir wei, jonge.\"\nSkoanheit sei: \"Dû mei dyn fratsen altyd. Wy bliuwe hjir.\" En hy hâldde har fêst.\nMar fuort dêrnei siet se plat op 't gat op 'e wei, wol trije meter fierder.\n\"Wolst it nou wol leauwe?\" sei se tsjin skoanheit.\n\"Jawol\", sei er. Der passearde in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19771,"r":"CJ015102a","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man is born with a caul and is therefore clairvoyant. He foresees all funerals: he urges people to step aside because a funeral procession wants to pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wibe fan Paulus Klas wenne op 'e Tike. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. It gebeurde wol, dat er sei: \"Minsken, jimme matte oan kant gean, hwant der komt in lykstaesje oan. De tsjillen fan 'e wein komme aenst tsjin jimme oan.\" Dan gongen se oan kant. Mar hy wie de iennige dy't it seach. Hy seach alle bigraffenissen út 'e omkriten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19861,"r":"CJ015410","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A father warns his children never to walk in the middle of the road, because a funeral procession might pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit sei tsjin ús, wy moesten noait midden op 'e wei rinne fanwege de lykstaesjes, dy't wol us passeare koenen. Ik ha my dêr hast altyd oan hâlden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19879,"r":"CJ015509","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A boy passes a funeral procession and recognises all the people walking behind the coffin. The deceased also seems familiar to him. Later the man really dies. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer Marten hat us in kear in lykstaesje sjoen. It wie op in joun yn Twizelerheide. Hy gong by dy lykstaesje lâns. Alle minsken dy't achter it lyk oan roannen koed er wol. It wie in man dy't stoarn wie. In skoftsje letter is dy man werklik stoarn. Dat gebeurde sa'n sechstich jier lyn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19900,"r":"CJ015610","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul, a clairvoyant, often sees funeral processions passing at night. The man foresees deaths.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Broek wenne in man, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Soms moest er midden yn 'e nacht út bêd wei. Dan gong hy der út, soms yn 'e winterkjeld om nei lykstaesjes to sjen. Letter wie dy lykstaesje der dan faek werkelik.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19919,"r":"CJ015704","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman is out late in the evening and is pushed aside twice because a funeral procession wants to pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem gong us op in kear by jountiid tusken tsien en alven in reed del. It wie yn 'e Harkema, sahwat op it plak, dêr't nou de fabryk fan Spinder stiet. Doe woarde se twa kearen oan kant reage, trochdat der in lykstaesje lâns kom. Hja seach beide kearen dúdlik de lykwein mei de greate minsken en de bern der achteroan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19954,"r":"CJ015810","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A clairvoyant woman sometimes sees funeral processions passing at night. The woman foresees impending deaths.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hja seach de bigraffenissen foarút. Nachts moest se der faek ôf. Sa hat se ek us op in nacht foar de herberch fan Rienk de Poel stien. Doe passearde der har in lykstaesje.\nIn wike letter wie de èchte lykstaesje dêr.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20028,"r":"CJ016404","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"As a little girl, a woman once bumped into a hearse. It was a vision of an impending death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem wie noch in fanke, doe hie se om boadskippen west en wie op wei nei hûs ta. Doe hat se ûnderweis in lykstaesje sjoen, dêr't se tsjin oproun. Hja is der sa kjel fan woarn, dat sy kom sûnder boadskippen thús. De hynders kommen tsjin har oan. Dat hat foartsjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20029,"r":"CJ016405","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"At a haunted spot funeral processions can often be seen. Everyone must always step aside to let the procession pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 't Langpaed tusken Harkema en Surhuzum wie altyd in lykstaesje. It wie de lykwei foar de Harkema. It wie dêr lang net plús. Elkenien moest dêr foar de lykstaesje wike.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20048,"r":"CJ016508","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two brothers on their way home have to jump aside for a passing funeral procession. A few weeks later someone really dies and they see the same funeral procession. It was a vision of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Piter en Knjilles Alma fan 'e Harkema (twa bruorren) hienen us togearre to jounpraten west. Doe't se op stap nei hûs ta wienen, kom der in lykstaesje oan. Sy gongen beide oan 'e kant fan 'e wei stean. Doe passearde dy lykstaesje dêr.\nIn pear wiken letter kom de èchte lykstaesje dêr lâns. 't Wie presys deselde, seinen se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20089,"r":"CJ016802","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul often has to go out at night to see things. He often sees funeral processions pass. The Lord frees him of his second sight, because the boy finds it very hard to bear.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer Boardzer fan 'e Boelensloane is mei de helm geboaren. As jonge fan tolve jier moest er al hwat sjen. Nachts moest er der faek út. Dan gong er oan 'e kant fan 'e wei stean. Dan seach er in lykstaesje passearen. Dan wist er wol hwa't it wienen. Hy hat dat nou net mear. De Heare hat him der fan forlost. Hwant it is in straf as men soks hat. Mar der is in tiid fan bigjinnen en in tiid fan ophâlden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20094,"r":"CJ016807","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You often cannot see a funeral procession, but you can feel it pass. People are often simply pushed off the road, or driven to the side because the hearse has to get by. This is an omen, a harbinger of death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in lyk passeart, dat sjocht men lang altyd net. Mar men fielt it wòl oan jinsels. De minsken wurde dan oan kant reage. Dat is heit en mem ek us in kear oerkom. Soms mat men foar by de lykwein op en der achter wer by del. Fleden jier (1966) is 't noch gebeurd op 'e hege brêge yn Koatstertille. Doe siet ik yn 'e auto. Doe gong der hwat by ús lâns, dat moest èk oer de brêge. Mar ik koe 't net sjen. Wy moesten hwat oan kant. Sa'n tsien minuten ha wy dêr stien. Doe wie 't foarby. Dat hat ek in lykstaesje west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20144,"r":"CJ017203","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"An old woman tells a farmer that she has seen a funeral procession somewhere. The farmer says that is impossible, because the procession would drive into the water there. Later the farmer takes on a farmhand, whom he has to house in a boat by the water. One of the farmhand's children dies, and the funeral procession does pass just as the old woman saw it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Fan Akkrom nei de Jouwer moest men by Aldskou mei in pont oerset wurde. Op in kear kom dêr in âld frou by in boer om molke. \"Ik hie in rare moeting\", sei se. \"Der kom in lykkoets dwars troch 't lân hinne.\" En hja wiisde it plak oan.\n\"Dat bistiet net\", sei de boer. \"Dat kin ommers net, dat rint dêr dea. Dat giet dêr op it wetter yn.\"\nMar hja hâldde fol dat hja it sjoen hie.\nDe Maeijes dêroan krige de boer in fêste arbeider. Dêr wie doe gjin hûs foar to krijen, dat doe kom er yn in skipke to wenjen, dat yn in opfeartsje lei fan de Aldeskou.\nDe simmers kom dêr in berntsje to forstjerren yn dat skipke. Doe woarde dat bern mei de lykkoets ophelle, krekt itselde paed lâns as it âldminske it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20224,"r":"CJ017911","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two people step aside for a funeral procession; a short time later someone actually dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik en Wibe Weening hienen op in joun yn 'e Harkema oan 't kuijerjen west. Doe sei Wibe tsjin my: \"Mast even út 'e wei gean.\" Wy stienen in skoftsje oan 'e kant fan 'e wei. \"Nou kinne wy wol wer op 'e wei\", sei er. Hy hie in lykstaesje foarbygean sjoen. Mar ik seach neat. 't Wie Pytsje Alma har man, dêr't er de bigraffenis fan sjoen hie. Dy is koart dêrnei stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20248,"r":"CJ018009","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul always has to go out at night to see something. Once he sees a young girl being taken to the churchyard: he can see the whole funeral procession clearly. A week later the girl really dies. It was a vision of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bearn Dekker (= Boonstra) wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy moest wol gau us yn 'e nacht fan 't bêd. Dan moest er hwat sjen. Hy hat us op in nacht sjoen, dat der in jongfaem, dy't op 'e Harste ûnder Sumar forstoarn wie, nei 't hôf ta brocht woarde.\nHy seach it yn 'e nacht. De hiele bigraffenis, sa klear as by ljochtskyndei. In wike letter woarde dy faem nei 't hôf ta brocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20269,"r":"CJ018115","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Sometimes people are suddenly driven to the side of the road because an invisible funeral procession has to pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha wol minsken yn Burgumerheide kend, dy woarden oan kant set, doe't der in ûnsichtbere lykstaesje oan kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20286,"r":"CJ018201","p":"Burum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A father warns his children never to walk in the middle of the road because a funeral procession might pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Nooit midden op de weg loopn, want dan kan je bij een lijkstaasje oploopn, vertelde vader. Vader liep als nachtwacht.","l":"Fries"},{"n":20312,"r":"CJ018307","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Three labourers are on their way home when one of them urges the other two to step aside because a funeral procession wants to pass. Only he can actually see the procession, because he was born with a caul.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit hat us in kear mei twa man nei Grinslân ta west to werken. Op in joun soenen se mei har trijen wer nei hûs ta. Sy kommen fan Zoutkamp en roannen oer Muntsjesyl en woenen sa nei Burum ta. Doe kommen se by in sydwei. Doe sei de iene fan syn beide maten, dy't in hiel stik âlder wie: \"Even oan kant. Der komt in lykstaesje oan.\" Heit en dy oare gongen mei him oan kant stean. Mar heit seach neat. Mar dy âld man seach it wòl. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20345,"r":"CJ018601","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul sees a funeral procession pass at night. It is a vision of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Gjalt Wagenaar wie in soan fan Alle Tet. Hy wenne yn 'e Harkema en wie mei de helm geboaren. Op in kear yn 't holst fan 'e nacht seach er op 'e dwarsreed by Hindrik Holthuis yn 'e Harkema in lykstaesje.\nHy is oerside gien, doe gong de lykstaesje foarby.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20347,"r":"CJ018603","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man, Douwe, urges another man to step to the side because a funeral procession has to pass. Only Douwe can see the procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn wiif har pake wenne yn Doezum. Hy roan us op in kear mei Douwe-mei-ien-hantsje op 'e wei. Doe sei Douwe ynienen: \"Wy matte fan 'e wei of.\"\n\"Hwerom?\" frege pake.\n\"Dêr komt in lykstaesje oan\", sei Douwe.\nPake seach neat, mar sy gongen oan kant. De lykstaesje passearde har. De froulju binne mei har kleden deun by har fuotten lâns gong.\nDouwe koe alles ûnderskiede, de hynders en de wein en ek koed er guon fan 'e minsken. Mar pake hat neat sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20447,"r":"CJ019211","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul urges his companions to step aside for a passing funeral procession. The seer predicts that a man will be killed in an accident and how it will happen, and he sees the whole funeral pass before him in detail. Fourteen days later the man in question actually dies when he falls between two wagons. Everything happens exactly as the man with the caul foresaw.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Knjillis Veenstra wenne yn Sweagerbosk. Wy seinen altyd Bontsje Keke, ek wol âlde Keke. Heit en dy wienen us op in nacht om twa ûre byelkoar bûtendoar. Mei in stik of hwat oaren soenen se nei Grinslân ta nei de bou. Keke wie der ek by. Doe sei Keke ynienen: \"Gean achter my. Toe, fan 'e wei ôf, hwant der komt hwat oan.\" Heit en dy seinen: \"Der is ommers neat.\" Hwant sy seagen neat. Mar sy gongen dêrom al oan kant. It skeat heit yn 'e gedachte dat âlde Keke mei de helm geboaren wie. Hy seach altyd lykstaesjes ensa.\nEven letter sei Keke: \"Kom nou mar wer op 'e wei, hwant hja stean al om 't graef hinne.\"\n\"Hwa is dat, dy't yn 't graef komt\", frege heit.\nKeke sei: \"Hjir gebeurt in ûngelok. Binnen fjirtsjin dagen rekket Piter fan Bearn Aukes dea yn Burgum. Hy rekket tusken twa weinen en hy wurdt hjir bigroeven.\"\n't Gebeurde ek sa en hy is dêr op 't hôf kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20449,"r":"CJ019213","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A girl sees a funeral procession pass: all her relatives walk behind the coffin, but she herself is missing. She thinks it possible that she herself will soon die, or perhaps someone else.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik lei siik op bêd yn 'e hûs. Us Joukje siet mei in feint yn 'e keuken. 't Gebeurde oan 't Wyldpaed. Hja wie och sa stil, dat de feint dy frege: \"Hwat mankeart dy?\" Doe sei se: \"Ik sjoch in lykstaesje.\" Hja seach ús der achteroan, en harsels net. Doe tocht se net oars as sy soe sels deareitsje.\nDoe't se by my kom wie se sa stil.\n\"Hwat is der oan?\" sei 'k. \"Ik ha sa'n nuver gefoel\", sei se. En doe fortelde se it. Ik sei: \"'t Kin ek wol in oaren wêze, dy't weirekket.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20450,"r":"CJ019214","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One night a girl sees a funeral procession with a dead person pass. A little later a coffin is also placed in the kitchen. These are omens: shortly afterwards her little sister is killed in a traffic accident. The funeral takes place exactly as the girl saw it earlier.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hja hat it ek sjoen fan ús Jeltsje. Doe wie se sa raer gesteld. Doe't se dy nachts op bêd lei, seach se it leefolk en in lyk. Sy gong der ôf. Doe kommen se der oan en setten de kiste yn 'e keuken.\nDe oare moarns kom Jeltsje by har. \"Hoe is 't mei mem, leave\", frege se Joukje noch.\n\"Goed\", sei Joukje. Jeltsje gong deselde moarns nei Bútenpost en dêr rekke se dea troch in forkearsûngelok.\nAlles kom fierder krekt sa út as Joukje it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20451,"r":"CJ019215","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees the whole course of a funeral pass before him in detail. Shortly afterwards the person in question actually dies. The man often foresees things: they are visions of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit seach de dingen ek foarút. Fan ús Baeije hat er de hiele bigraffenis fan tofoaren sjoen. Hy hat it leefolk sjoen en hy hat ek sjoen, dat se har biklaeiden.\n\nBaeije","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20452,"r":"CJ019216","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A clairvoyant always has to go out at night to see things. Once he stands by the road in his underpants to watch a funeral procession pass. He had been driven out of bed with such irresistible force that he had no time even to pull on his trousers.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Keke stie op in nacht yn 'e ûnderbroek nei in lyk to sjen op 'e hoeke fan 't Wyldpaed, sa hurd moest er doe út bêd wei. Hy hie gjin tiid mear om 'e broek oan to dwaen, hwant dan kom er to let.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20582,"r":"CJ020204","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days children were not allowed to walk in the middle of the road because of the funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen as bern op it Hegelân to Jistrum. Wy mochten net midden op 'e wei rinne fanwege de lykstaesjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20613,"r":"CJ020411","p":"Tzummarum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two friends were once walking along the middle of the dyke. One man said they had to step aside because a funeral procession was coming past. The other man saw nothing. A few days later an old woman died, and she was carried over the dyke.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en in kammeraet fan him rounen ris op in kear op 'e buorren. Hja wienen midden op 'e dyk. Doe sei dy kammeraet tsjin ús heit: \"Kom gau oan kant.\"\n\"Hwat wolstû\", frege heit.\nMar hy helle heit nei de kant ta.\nIn skoftsje letter sei er: \"Kom hjir nou mar wer.\" En doe gyngen se wer nei de midden ta.\nHeit sei: \"Hwat wie der nou?\"\n\"In bigraffenis\", sei er. Heit hie neat sjoen.\nIn pear dagen letter stoar dêr in âld minske, dat de oare wyks op 't hôf kaem. Dat minske waerd dêr lâns droegen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20622,"r":"CJ020503","p":"Tzummarum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"An old woman once told a passer-by on the dyke that he had to step aside. She saw a funeral procession with rearing horses approaching. A few days later the carriage really came past.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Sint Anne wenne in âld-wyfke, dat wie ek mei de helm geboaren. Hja sei us in kear tsjin ien dy't midden op 'e dyk stie: \"Tinus, je motte an kant gaan, want der komt in roustoet an met twee swarte peerden. 't Ene peerd begint te stegeren, der komt aenst een wit peerd bij feur.\"\nIn dei of fjouwer letter gebeurde it. Der roannen earst twa swarte hynders foar de lykwein, mar 't iene kaem in wyt foar yn 't plak.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20685,"r":"CJ020806","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man often had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions.\nPeople walking in the middle of the road are sometimes suddenly set aside at the edge of the road. Then a funeral procession is passing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Rapke wenne to Koartwâld. Hy wie timmerman. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Nachts moest hy der faek ôf. Dan seach er lykstaesjes.\nIk ha wol gauris heard dat lju dy't midden op 'e wei roannen samar oan kant set woarden, sûnder dat se hwat seagen. Dan passearde der in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20710,"r":"CJ021106","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Three boys were strolling about when one of them suddenly jumped aside. He saw a black carriage drawn by two horses approaching. The others saw nothing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Trije jonges kuijeren sahwat omtrint Beneden-Haulerwyk.\nIen fan 'e trije is troud. Ien fan dy jonges sprong samar ynienen oerside. \"Hwerom dochstû dat?\" fregen de oaren.\n\"Der komt in swarte wein oan mei twa hynders der foar\", sei de jonge. De oaren seagen it net.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20714,"r":"CJ021110","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two men who were born with a caul saw funeral processions now and then.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wienen twa, dy't mei de helm geboaren wienen: Graanstra en âlde Merk. Sy seagen nou en dan lykstaesjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20728,"r":"CJ021208","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You must never walk in the middle of the road in the evening. For if you meet a funeral procession, you are pushed aside. It also happened that people walked right into the front of a hearse. Then they fell.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat jouns noait midden op 'e wei rinne.\nHwant komt men in lykstaesje tsjin, dan wurdt men oan kant reage. Ek gebeurde it wol, dat men foar by de lykwein oproan. Dat fornaem men oan 'e foarkant net, mar achter wòl. Dêr foel men der dan by del.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20802,"r":"CJ021403","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman who was born with a caul saw funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit hie in healsuster, dat wie Griet fan der Wyk, dy hat gekke Jouke hawn. Grietmoai wie mei de helm geboaren. Sy moast der nachts faek út. Dan waerd se skodde. Op in kear wie se mei ús heit en oaren achter Feanhuzen om dêr baelders to birêdden. Sy roannen meielkoarren oer de wei. Doe sei Grietmoai: \"Net midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant dêr komme se mei in lyk oan.\" Hja luts de oaren nei de kant fan 'e wei ta. De oaren seagen neat.\nEk wol, dan stie se yn 'e hûs to sjen. Soms wie 't achter hûs, soms foar hûs, dat se hwat seach.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20896,"r":"CJ021906","p":"Sweagerbosk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who was born with a caul often had to go out at night to see funeral processions. Once the weather was so bad that he wanted to stay in bed. But then a huge black dog with glowing eyes came, and the man got up quickly after all.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Knjillis Veenstra wenne by 't spoar. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy moest alles sjen. Op in nacht moest hy der wer ôf. Mar it wie sok min waer, dat hy seach der bot tsjin oan en hy bleau lizzen.\nMar doe kom der in beest as in greate grouwe swarte houn by syn bêd mei hiele greate gleone egen. Doe gong hy der ôf. Hy moest hiel bot rinne om op 'e Sweach to kommen. It wie sa'n waer, dat de koppen fan 'e beammen rekken de groun. Hy kom noch krekt op tiid om de lykstaesje to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20911,"r":"CJ022008","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"An old spinster often had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions. Once she refused to give way to something she saw coming, and she got a crack in her head. When she grew too old to get out of bed at night, she opened the curtains and saw everything through the window.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Sweagerbosk wenne in âld minske, dat wie âlde Buoi. Hja frijgeselle by ús beppe. Hja moest der nachts wit hoe faek ôf. Dan moest se nei bûten ta om in lykstaesje to sjen.\nDan gong se oan 'e kant fan 'e wei stean. En dan sei se letter dat se in wein sjoen hie mei sa'n en sa'n hynder der foar en safolle minsken der achter.\nOp in kear doe wie se op 'e wei. Doe kom der har hwat tomjitte. Hja tocht: \"Ik wyk net.\" Doe wie se stean bleaun. Mar doe hie se in barst yn 'e holle krigen, en dy barst is der altyd yn bleaun.\nSy wie by heit syn beppe yn 'e kost. Op 't lêst koe se der net mear út. Dan skoude se 't gerdyntsje oan kant en dan seach se alles.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20912,"r":"CJ022009","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Old Bontsje Knjillis foresaw all kinds of things. He often had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions. Once he did not want to get up, but then a big dog with glowing eyes came to him. Another time a farmhand died after coughing up blood for some time. Knjillis believed it was his fault, because he had once given the farmhand a severe beating.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Bontsje Knjillis (Veenstra?) moest ek alles sjen. Tije Sjoeke hat fjouwer berntsjes forlern: trije berntsjes tagelyk en ien in wike letter. Dy stoaren oan 'e blauwe mûzels. Knjillis hie 't allegear fan tofoaren al sjoen.\nHeit bargeslachte by 't hjerst by him.\nOp in nacht, doe moest er wer hwat sjen. Mar doe tocht er \"Ik bliuw lizzen.\" Hwant hy seach der bot tsjin oan yn 'e kjeld nei bûten ta. Doe wie hy der net út gong. Mar doe wie der in houn mei gleone egen by syn bêd kom. Hy mòest der út. Doe is er nei de Sweach ta roan. Dêr wie de lykstaesje.\nDy Knjillis wie in raren-ien. It wie in greate beul. Heit syn mem wie us by him op 't lân west to wjudden. Doe wie der krekt in feint stoarn, dy't se beide bêst koenen. Dy feint hie de lêste tiden hyltyd bloed opjown. Doe fortelde Knjillis oan ús beppe, dat hy hie dy feint de reis jown. Hy hie him sa bot houd en slein, dat hy hie noait wer goed west en wie der op 't lêst troch stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20915,"r":"CJ022011","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"An old woman who was born with a caul often saw funeral processions pass her house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn man Ringer kom wol mei syn handel yn klaeijng ensa by in âld minske, dat yn 'e Harkema wenne. Dat minske wie mei de helm geboaren. Soms stie se by de doar en dan seach se lykstaesjes. Ringer krige sa'n ôfskrik fan har forhalen, dat hy woarde suver bang foar har en hy kom der dêrom op 't lêst mar net mear.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21026,"r":"CJ023206","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Hinke Kaert was born with a caul. She had to go out at night to see funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hinke Kaert fan Nijebrêge wie mei de helm geboaren. Sy moest der nachts ôf om lykstaesjes to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21040,"r":"CJ023402","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man used to see funeral processions all the time. He would then step aside to let the procession pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Bakkefean wenne in man dat wie Menkema, dy seach froeger altyd lykstaesjes. Hy gong dan oan kant om sa'n lykstaesje passeare to litten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21065,"r":"CJ023901","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man always had to go out at night. Sometimes he did not even have time to dress properly. Once he did not want to get up and stayed in bed. But then a huge dog with eyes like saucers came and pulled him out of bed.\nThe man also saw his own daughter's funeral in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Knjillis moest alles sjen. Hy hat de bigraffenis fan syn eigen dochter fan tofoaren sjoen, dy't forsûpt is.\nAs Knjillis hwat sjen moest yn 'e nacht gong dat soms hiel hurd. Dan koed er de klean faek sa gau net oan krije. Soms rekke hy der út mei ien hoas oan en ien hoas út. Hwant hy moèst sjen. Soms moest er yn 'e nacht oer hekken hinne klauwe.\nOp in kear doe woed er net. Hy bleau lizzen.\nMar doe kom der in greate grouwe houn by him mei egen as thépantsjes. Dy hat him fan bêd ôfskuord.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21081,"r":"CJ023917","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A young man once saw a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":21143,"r":"CJ024415","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Never walk in the middle of the road, or you might walk into a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Rin noait midden op 'e wei! (Lykstaesje)\nYt neat fan in tsjoenster op, oars kriget men in pod yn 't liif.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21186,"r":"CJ024706","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man was born with a caul. In the daytime he always saw funeral processions. Then he had to step aside.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Beint Boonstra fan 'e Tike wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy seach oerdei altyd lykstaesjes. Dan moest er oan kant.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21391,"r":"CJ026506","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man was once pushed off the road. He had seen a funeral procession in which he knew all the people.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Roanes Pander is noch in bitreklik jonge man yn 'e Harkema. Hy is us in kear fan 'e wei ôfreage woarn. Doe hat er in lykstaesje sjoen, dêr't er alle minsken fan koe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21413,"r":"CJ026613","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days in Boelenslaan it happened quite often that people were pushed off the road by an invisible funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde froeger yn 'e Boelensloane noch al us dat in minske op 'e wei samar oan kant set woarde. Dan passearde der in lykstaesje, woarde der sein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21419,"r":"CJ026619","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who was born with a caul often saw funeral processions in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tiense Boomsma hat hjir wenne. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy seach lykstaesjes fan tofoaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21443,"r":"CJ026710","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A girl cycled very fast for a stretch because she saw a funeral procession coming and wanted to get round the corner first. The following week a funeral procession did indeed come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear doe hie ik nei tsjerke ta west, yn 'e Koaten. Ik wie op 'e fyts. Der fytste ek ien njonken my. Doe sei dyselde tsjin my: \"Hwat fytse jo hurd.\"\n\"Ja\", sei 'k.\nEven letter fytste ik wer gewoan.\nIk sei: \"Hjir komt fan 'e wike in lykstaesje lâns. Hjir stjert ien. Ik seach de lykstaesje oankommen. Ik woe earder de hoeke om wêze.\"\n't Kom krekt sa út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21455,"r":"CJ026805","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A farmhand often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. Once his mates put sacks of rye in front of his bed so that he could not get out. When they removed the sacks the next day, they found their friend more dead than alive. He had turned completely blue.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us pake moest der nachts altyd ôf om hwat to sjen.\nHy tsjinne by in boer. Doe seinen se op in kear: \"Wy sille him fannacht wol ha. Hy komt der net ôf.\"\nDoe setten se allegear sekken mei rogge foar syn bêd. Se seinen: \"Nou kin hy der net ôfkomme.\"\nEn dat wìe èk sa.\nDe oare moarns hellen se de sekken der wei. Mar doe't pake der ôf kom, doe wied er blau. Hy leefde noch al, mar 't hie net lang mear duorre of hy hie dea west. It wienen syn kammeraten dy't dy sekken dêr foar set hienen. Mar sy ha 't letter noait wer dien.\nHwant dy't hwat sjen mat, dy mat der ôf. Oars komt it net goed mei him. Pake hiet fan Sieds Leenstra. Hy seach altyd dingen, dy't net noflik wienen om to sjen, lyk as in ûngelok, in lykstaesje ensfh.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21474,"r":"CJ026910","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People were sometimes suddenly pushed off the road for no reason. Then a funeral procession would pass by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wenje wol minsken yn 'e Westerein, dy binne samar oan kant reage woarn op 'e wei. Dan kom der in lykstaesje oan. Ik ha 't sels noait meimakke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21540,"r":"CJ027004","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A group of labourers who always slept on the floor grew tired of a woman coming down from the loft every night. One evening they took the ladder away, but at night the woman stood wailing that she had to come down. She was born with a caul and had to get up at night to see funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Uthuzermeden wienen twa keppels by de boer to wjudden. Uthuzermeden leit yn 't noarden fan Grinslân. De iene keppel kom fan Twizelerheide, de oare fan 'e Harkema.\nDe keppel fan 'e Harkema slepte boven op in souder en dy fan Twizelerheide ûnder op 'e telle.\nAlle nachten moest der in frommes fan 'e Harkema ôf. Dan gong se by de leider del. Guon hienen dêr in hekel oan, hwant dy woarden der wekker fan. Dy seinen: \"Wy sille de leider der wei krije, hja komt der net wer ôf.\"\nDoe hearden se it minske midden yn 'e nacht kjirmjen: \"De leider! De leider! Ik mat nei ûnderen!\"\nDoe hie de keppelbaes gau de leider der wer delset.\nDe oare deis fregen se har \"Hwerom moasten jo der ôf?\" Hja sei: \"Hjir stjert binnenkoart ien. Dat moest ik sjen.\"\nIn wike letter stoar der ien.\nIt minske wie mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21541,"r":"CJ027005","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man told his companion to step aside. A funeral procession passed by which the other did not see.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Harkema roannen op in nacht twa mannen neist elkoar lâns. Doe sei de iene tsjin 'e oare: \"Kom hjir hwat hinne, de wei mat frij bliuwe.\"\n\"Hwerom?\" frege de oare, mar hy gong oan kant.\nDe oare woe neat sizze en bleau stean. Even letter fortelde er it. \"Der wie in lykstaesje op 'e wei. Dêrom moesten wy oan kant.\"\nMar syn maet hie neat sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21612,"r":"CJ027508","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who was born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir tichteby hat in man wenne, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest der nachts altyd út, dan woarde er roppen. Dan seach er in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21629,"r":"CJ027602","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A boy once pulled his brother off the road so that he nearly ended up in the ditch. Angrily he asked what that was for, but the other said he had nearly walked into a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer Wessel en ik wienen op in nacht oan 't murdejeijen. De Trije Roede wie doe noch sânwei. Dêr wie bosk oan. Dêr hâldden wy doe ta. Ynienen pakte Wessel my by 't skouder.\nIk roan midden op 'e wei. Dat die 'k altyd, mei opset sin. Hwant der kin us ien fan 'e sydkant komme dy't jin ûnforwacht in mep jaen wol.\nMar Wessel pakte my by de nekke en smiet my omtrint yn 'e sleat.\nIk sei: \"Hwat wolstû, godfordomme?\"\n\"Sjochstû dan neat?\" sei er. \"Dû wiest boven op in lykstaesje roan.\"\nMar ik wie lulk, hwant ik seach neat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21655,"r":"CJ027905","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Whoever does not see a funeral procession does not need to step aside.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":21656,"r":"CJ027906","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In a group of women, an old woman is pushed to the ground. This was done by a funeral procession. The other women had not seen the procession. The old woman explains that whoever does not see the procession does not have to step aside either. She did see it, but stepped aside too late.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der kom us in keppeltsje froulju fan 't wjudderslân. Dêr wie ek in âld minske by, dy roan hwat foaroer. Sy gongen in reed del en doe woarde dat âld minske samar ynienen oan kant treaun, sûnder dat ien fan 'e oaren har oanrekke. Sy kom ta fallen. \nDe oaren seinen: \"Hoe is 't nou?\" \n\"Och ja,\" sei 't âldwyfke, \"dêr wie in lykstaesje.\" \n\"Hea,\" seinen de oaren, \"wy ha neat sjoen.\" \n\"Né,\" sei se, \"mar ik seach jim wol by de Cykwein opgean en der wer by delgean. En ik seach jim ek by de hynders lâns gan. Ik seach it hwat ta let, dêrtroch woarde it oan kant treaun. Soks komt my oars noait oer. Dy 't it net sjocht, dy hoeft net oan kant ta goan.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21699,"r":"CJ028202","p":"Houten","v":"Utr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A clairvoyant urges people to step aside for a passing funeral procession. He often foresees funerals.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Job Smit zag alles. Hij wist het altijd wanneer er weer een begrafenis zou komen. Soms zei hij tegen de mensen: \"Denk er om, aan kant. Daar komt een lykstaasje aan.\" Dan zagen die mensen niks."},{"n":21833,"r":"CJ028807","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a hearse with a coffin. A little later the same hearse passes by: an old woman has died. It was a foreseeing vision.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Germ Visser hie op in joun mei 't wiif to jounpraten west. Underweis sei er: \"Even achter my lâns gean.\" Doe seach er syn eigen slide (it wie in nije slide dy't krekt yn 'e swarte tar siet). Dêr stie in deafet op.\nLetter kommen se om syn slide to lien. De slide moest foar syn glêzen lâns. Der wie in frommeske forstoarn. ('t Gebeurde op 'e Tike)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21945,"r":"CJ030601","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul often has visions of the future. Sometimes he has to get up at night to see funeral processions pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik as jonge yn Dútslân op 'e minen arbeide, wie dêr ek in sekere Tiense Boomsma. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy gong nachts fan bêd ôf. Dan seach er lykstaesjes","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21993,"r":"CJ031114","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul urges bystanders to step aside for a passing funeral procession. Since there is nothing to see, everyone stays put, laughing a little. Promptly one of them is struck by the horse and cart.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha twa jier lang forkearing hawn mei in feint, dy hiet fan Oene. Dy syn broer wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy seach altyd lykstaesjes.\nOp in kear wied er mei oar jongfolk op 'e wei.\n\"Even oan kant,\" sei er, \"der komt hwat oan.\"\nMar de oaren seagen neat en laken him út en sy bleauwen stean.\nDoe is ien fan har oer hynder en wein en alles hinne smiten. Hy kaem raer wer del.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22263,"r":"CJ034102","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man often has to get up at night to see funeral processions pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Minnertsgea hat in man wenne, dy gong der nachts op út om lykstaesjes to sjen. It kom altyd nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33014,"r":"CJ085702","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One night a man saw a funeral procession. At the new churchyard the people stopped.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear seach ik in lykstaesje. 't Wie yn 'e nacht. By 't nije tsjerkhôf bleauwen de minsken stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33219,"r":"CJ088001","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man always saw funeral processions in advance, and he would warn people about them. He also saw naked people. Those were the people who had been buried without grave clothes.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Joeke Spoekgûler wenne to Drachten op 'e Dwarsfeart. Dy seach oerdei de spoeken foarút. Dan warskôge er de minsken dat se op dy en dy ûre net midden op 'e wei rinne moesten.\nHy seach lykstaesjes.\nHy seach ek neakene minsken. Dat wienen guon dy't gjin deaklean oan krigen hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":50328,"r":"GENDT256","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Advice not to walk in the middle of the road in the evening because of the danger of being run over by a hearse.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Lop soaves nooit midden opte weg. Dan kuj dör ’n liekwage overreje worre.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":50356,"r":"GENDT266","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees funeral processions before deaths.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Kees Janse zag veul dingen al van teveure. Hé’j zèj ’s ’n keer tegen iemand: “Kom ’s op zij van ’t huus stoan”. De man gieng mee. En Kees zèj: “Zie gé’j da? Dor geet ’n liek hen en d’r is mar één wage achter en mar weinig volk”. Den aandre zag niks. Inkele dage lotter kwam er ’n ouwe moeder logere bé’j Hendrik Aarntzen. Ze stierf gaauwechtig. Ze zou ien Gendt begrave worre. Er was nie veul volk bé’j de begreffenis. En mar één wage. Kees had ’t dus wel goed gezien.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":130073,"r":"VERHGOEFF000705","p":"Apeldoorn","v":"Gld.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"After being warned about a funeral procession, a boy walks on, over horse and cart, falls and breaks his legs.","i":"L.V.","o":"De avondschool kwam uit en die jongens schreeuwen en doen, zoals jongens altijd doen en toen was er een, die zei: “Kijk uit, daar komt een lijkstoet” maar z’n vriend riep: “Ik zie niks!” en bleef doorlopen en toen liep die over het paard en de wagen heen en viel er aan de achterkant af: allebei z’n benen gebroken!"},{"n":131969,"r":"VODA_033_12","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Abraham foresaw a funeral. He saw people in white caps walking in front of a coffin.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"O en now, eh, wol je dea ander nog eben heb’n, van Oabram. \nOabram dea kon kwoad zain [voorbijrijdend verkeer] en dea komt ook wel ‘ns bee ons vrouger, doa… doa was ik nog maar zo’n jong, det wait ik ook nog. Hea, Oabram, dea zegt tegen mien voader: “Môs t’ es even mit noar boet’n goan.” Hea deugde niks. \n“Wat is ’r den?” Nja. \nHij had ’n stok bie zich. “Now môs te es over mien stok heen kiek’n en môs mie op de linkertuinen trappen. Doa kom’n ze aan met de witte mutsen op… voor de kist.”\n“Ja, eh, ik zain d’r niks van.” zeat e.\n“Maar nou môs te op die aander tuindet[?] letten, dan zeust ’t wel.”\nEn woar, hij had zain, kijk, doar waren ze d’r aan’kom’n, ’n halle troep van met die witte mutsen en zo wat, hè. Enne, zee kom’n dicht bie eur.\n“As je van de duvel bent, den eh… mag e wegblieben en anders dan ken e bie mie kom’n.”\nDat was ook weer gebeurd.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":130160,"r":"VOORDE000101","p":"Borne","v":"Ov.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A sick man sees a hearse at the neighbour's house and someone being carried inside. The others see nothing. Three days later a hearse carrying the body of the neighbour's dead son stops at the house at the same time, and the body is carried inside.","i":"G.J.t.V.","o":"Ne Vuurgeschichte.\n\nNen gòòn vrèend van miej, de man is net tachtig joar wödd’n, èen van dèe leu, woar iej op an könt, en zich nig met luug’ns ophoolt, vertöl miej wat non koemp en wat ‘m zölm was oawerkömm’n. Zien vaar har naa vol lèèfhebberiej vuur boerken, al hadd’n ze d’r nig alleen van hòow’n te ett’n. Meer dat boerken har e d’r zo biej doan. Hee heul völ van vee en zo har e d’r ook nog mangs ’n luk biej hoandeld, en ze hadd’n zölm ook nog groend had. Dan koff’n e in ’t vuurjoar ’n paar terugg’n en verkoff’n ze meesttied in ’t noajoar wier. Zo kèend’n heel völ boer’n en völ boer’n kèend’n hem. Zien lèefste was um Zundagsmirrags, noa de Vesper, noar nen boer hen kuier’n te goan, dan veuld’n hee zich good te pas. ’t Was ’n moal wier dèep in ’n hèerfst wes, dow zien vaar de koeze vuur ’t lechte har kreeg’n en ‘m har vroag’n: “Jong, goa’j met, dan goa’w nog eff’n noar den en den in Bèerghoezen”, ne boerschop oender Oldenzel. \nWiej wadd’n d’r ook vuur ’n wek of wat wes en dow was de oole boer nig al te bes op de deune, hèe lèe dow in ’t ber, hèe har ’t zo vaste zitt’n en ’t gömm’n zo op de böste. “Wiej wilt eef’n zeen hoe ’t non met ‘m is”, zèe mien vaar tieg’n miej. Wiej moss’n ook duur nen groot’n, deuster’n bos, woar ik vuur gin geeld van de weerld alleen duurhen was goan. ‘k Was ook nog meer zonnen bol van ne jong, van loa’k zegg’n ’n joar of elm, mu’j weet’n. Wiej wadd’n d","l":"Twents"},{"n":45708,"r":"WEV015401","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing a funeral procession; a man born with a caul sees in advance a funeral procession, a fire, ships on land where a canal is later dug, and lights where a road later runs.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien voader vertelde:\n Ik luip es n keer mit ain van mien bekenden deur Lo (= Vriescheloo) en toun zee e teegn mie: “Goa es eevn oet zied, door komen ze aan”.\n Ik vruig: “Wat komp dr aan?”\n “Kiek”, zeg e, zai binnen aal in t wit: aine, twei-e, drei-e, vare, vieve; zai loopt mooi op n riege achter nander aan.” \n“Moar wat zugst nou,” zee mien oal heer.\n “Ain begraffenis”; ik wait, wel dr achter loopn, moar dat zeg ik die nait.”\n Mien voader het niks zain, moar zien vrund wos et wel; dei liekstoatie is nait lang loater over de weg goan.\n Mien voar kon asmis ook wat zain; hai was mit de helm geboorn. \nBie de geboorte hebben mien oal lu dat ding in n flessie doan; toun mien voader overleedn is, gung de helm mit in de kiste. \nt Is hom overkomen, dat e n moal op hoes aan gung en toun zag e volk oet hoes komen. Hai vruig den ook aan de vrouw, wel of dr toch west wazzen. Moeke mos erkennen, dat dr gain mens over vlouer west was. “Singelier”, zee de olle man, ”k zag ze zo dudelk loopn.” \nn Zet loater is ain van mien bruiers overleden. Toun luip dus et volk tou t hoes oet. Voader was gain man, dei zokke dingen moar zo verzon; hai zag beslist veuruut. \nBrandende hoezen het e ook zain. Ie konnen dr op aan, dat zo’n hoes er werklijk nait laank meer ston in zo’n geval. \nVerder zag e riegn lichies. Hai zee voak: “Door komp nog es n weg.” Scheepn zag e voarn over t land en den wos hai, dat dr n","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46194,"r":"WEV016603","p":"Gieterveen","v":"Dr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A hearse heading to a house turns out to be an omen of a death in that house.","i":"F.W.","o":"Toun wie in Drouwenerveen woonden, zee mien oal heer opn keer: “Kiek nou toch ais, doar draait n liekwoagn noar ons Jan zien huus tou.” \nMien moetje gung gauw kiekn, moar zai zag niks. De oale heer ook nait meer, t was moar n moment, dat hai et zag. t Duurde nait laank, toun sturf door n nichte van mie in dat huus.","l":"Drents"},{"n":46222,"r":"WEV017001","p":"Stadskanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A couple who are pushed aside see nothing, but hear wagons passing and think of a hearse. A short time later a dead person is carried along that path to the churchyard.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien oal lu hebben mie vrij wat verteld over vrouger; spokerij en zowat, door geleufden ze nogal aan. In mien jonge joarn keb ik t zulf ook leufd, moar nou loater goud bekeekn komt t mie onwoarschienlek veur. De oale mensn twiefelden dr nait aan en ze vertel-ons den de volgende verhoaln:\nZai luipn n keer op t Alteveer over n zandpad en toun wurn ze allebaide biezied zet. Stonden aan t kaande van de weg. Was niks te zain, moar ze heurden wel woagens veurbie roln. Onmiddelk dochden ze aan ain begravveniswoagn. Zai hadden t nog goud ook; eevn loater is oal Bos overleden en dei wur over dat pad noar t kerkhof brocht.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46230,"r":"WEV017104","p":"Wedde","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The son of a man who is pushed aside in the street has a fatal accident at that very moment, and his body is brought home through that street.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik heb zulf ook es wat biezunders zain.\nk Zat zo in huus uut t roam te kiekn en zag dat ain van de overkaande net zo biezied zet wur. Hai strompelde nait, was eevnmin wind, zodat e gain stöt van de wind in de rogge kreeg. Hai kwam aan de kaande van de weg te stoan en toun luip e de weg weer op en gong wieder.\nWat gebeurde toun op datzulfde oognblik? Loater wur mie dat dudlk. \nIn Blijham kreeg n zeun van hom n oongeluk; hai kwam doorbie te dode en wur deur de stroade, woor ik inkeek noar huus brocht.\nDizze man is, as ie t goud bekiekn, ook van te veurn woarschouwd, dat er wat ophanden was.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46237,"r":"WEV017304","p":"Overschild","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman sees in advance that a hearse is drawn by a black horse and a white horse, which later comes true.","i":"F.W.","o":"Liekstoatie.\nMien grootmoe het wel zain, dat er ain begravvenis langs de weg gung. Ik heur het heur nog verteln: “Kinder, ik zai n liekwoagn; lopen n zwaart en n wit peerd veur.”\nLoater kwam dat ook oet; zai vertrokn mit twei zwaarte peerden veur de woagn; onderweg kon ain peerd t nait langer doun en den wur dr vroagd bie n boer, of e zien peerd eevn afstoan wol. Dat was ain widde west.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46271,"r":"WEV017602","p":"Muntendam","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Seeing funeral processions, with people in the procession, two horses, etc.","i":"F.W.","o":"Liekstoaties zaggen verschilnde mensn ook. n Boel volk, twei peerden en wat dr verder bieheurde. Ik denk nait, dat ze de personen, dei dr achter luipn, herkend hebben.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":130724,"r":"BIJLSMA008801","p":"Hommerts","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession at night in which the men wear black caps. A few days later there is the funeral of someone from a region where men wear black caps at funerals.","i":"T.B.","o":"To Hommerts wenne foar jierren Kobus Martens. Nei syn fak waerd er altyd Kobus snider neamd. Hy lies in soad, wist folle en wie tige from. Hy seach en bilibbe faek nuvere dingen dêr 't in oar gjin aen fan hie. Op in kear hie er in rare nacht hawn. Hy moast fan it bêd. Op 'e dyk seach er in lykstaesje oankommen, en dat wie allegear hwat oars as men wend wie. De manlju, dy 't efter de bier rounen, hienen allegear swarte petsjes op.\nIn pear dagen letter stoar dêr to Hommerts in boerefaem, dy 't út Gaesterlân fandinne kaem. Dêr hiene de manlju swarte petsjes op by in bigraffenis, krekt sa 't Kobus dat yn syn fisioen sjoen hie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":22113,"r":"CJ032501","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul wants to convince his friend of his gift of second sight and takes him out at night to see things. The seer urges his friend to step aside for a passing funeral procession. A week later a funeral really does pass by at the same spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mem har heit (myn pake) hie in maet, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest alles sjen. Hy gong der yn 'e nacht faek ôf.\nPake woe net leauwe dat syn maet dan hwat seach.\n\"Dan mast mar us mei\", sei syn maet. Sy praetten ôf, as hy der wer op in nacht út moest, soed er pake wekkermeitsje en meinimme.\nOp in kear gebeurde dat. Togearre roannen se in eintsje de wei út.\nDoe sei pake syn maet: \"Nou komt der in lykstaesje oan. Nou matte wy fan 'e wei ôf.\" Dat dienen se doe. Even letter sei pake syn maet: \"Nou kinne wy wol wer op 'e wei. De lykstaesje is foarby.\"\nPake hie neat sjoen.\nMar it kaem wòl út. De oare wyks wìe der in lykstaesje. Dy passearde krekt itselde plak dêr't pake en syn maet dy nachts stien hienen.\nDoe koe pake de lykstaesje sels sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22176,"r":"CJ033502","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A farmhand sees a funeral pass by at night. Three days later someone really does die and the same procession passes by. It was a foreseeing vision.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie in feint, dy wie by de boer. Hy sliepte yn 't bêdsté yn 'e stâl, achter de kij. Op in nacht doe seach er in bigraffenis de mjilgong lâns gean. Der wie hielendal net in siken yn 'e hûs, mar trije dagen letter is de boer syn soan forstoarn. Doe is de bigraffenis de mjilgong delgong. Dit hat ús pake forteld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22180,"r":"CJ033506","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral pass by in thick fog. It is a foreseeing vision: a few days later someone really does die and the same procession passes by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie op in joun letter en der hong in mist fan sa'n heale meter hichte oer de groun. Doe seach dyselde Anders de Haan fan Garyp in bigraffenis.\nSe roannen boven op 'e mist. In pear dagen letter wie der op itselde plak in bigraffenis.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22212,"r":"CJ033705","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who once stumbled over a corpse at night takes care not to run into a funeral procession a second time.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jan Kooistra fan 't Fean (hy komt fan 'e Harkema) past wol op dat er altyd by nacht oan 'e kant fan 'e wei rint, hwant oars kinne de lykstaesjes net passeare. Hy mat us oer in lyk hinne fallen wêze.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22222,"r":"CJ033806","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man claims to have seen a funeral procession at night. It may have been a foreseeing vision.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn neef Willem Peule (= W. Nicolai) biweart, dat er us op in nacht in lykstaesje sjoen hat. Hy soe nei syn heit en mem (Sjoerd en Gees). Mar hy doarst der net hinne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22232,"r":"CJ033902","p":"Ons Belang","v":"Utr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul often foresees deaths at night in passing funeral processions. At birth, the caul of a seer often has to be anxiously hidden from greedy doctors.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der hat in man by my wenne, dat wie Sytse Rapkes. Dy moest der nachts altyd ôf om nei bigraffenissen to sjen. De lykstaesje moest earst passeard wêze, earder gong er net wer op bêd. Hy wist hast altyd wol hwa't der stjerre soe, mar hy sei it net. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren.\nDer wienen wol dokters, dy knoeiden de helm wei, dy wienen der hyt op. Dêrtroch moesten dy stumpers it sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22233,"r":"CJ033903","p":"Ons Belang","v":"Utr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You should never walk in the middle of the road at night, because a funeral procession may pass. Only certain people who often have visions of the future see such a procession go by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne.\nMyn buorman dat wie Willem van Doezum, dy arbeide yn de Ham by syn swager Sytse, dy hie dêr in boeredochter troud.\nDoe kommen Sytse en Willem us togearre fan 't wurk. Sy wienen op 'e rydloane oan diz kant fan it Bouwekleaster.\nDoe hie Sytse Willem ynienen fan 'e wei ôflutsen nei de kant ta.\n\"Hwat ha wy nou?\" sei Willem.\n\"As ik dy net oan kant skoud hie, wiest by in lykstaesje oproan\", sei Sytse.\nMar Willem hie neat sjoen. Sytse wòl.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22251,"r":"CJ034002","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Some people are driven to the side of the road at night because a funeral procession wants to pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha wol minsken kend, dy't op 'e joun of yn 'e nacht oan kant reage woarden, as der in lykstaesje oankom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22256,"r":"CJ034007","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession at night and flees in fear.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Willem Peule (= Nicolai) ^ kom us thús fan 'e faem. 't Wie midden yn 'e nacht, en sa'n fjirtich jier lyn.\nDoe seach er in lykstaesje op 'e Singel. Hy is hurd útnaeid.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22257,"r":"CJ034008","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession pass at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Roanes Pander seach ek us op in nacht in lykstaesje. Doe stie er by Wierd Kooistra op 't hiem. Hy seach de lykstaesje foar him lâns gean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22266,"r":"CJ034202","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession pass and runs off in terror as fast as his legs can carry him.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn frou har omke Gjert v.d. Heide wie op in moandei-to-moarn ier fan 'e faem thús kom. Hy wie alhiel fan 'e wize. Hy sei, der wie him in lykstaesje foarby gong. Doe wied er sa binaud woarn, dat hy hie sa hurd roan, de soallen hienen ûnder 'e skuon wei west. 't Wie op 'e Trije Roede gebeurd (Boelensloane).","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22292,"r":"CJ034325","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman runs into a funeral procession and boldly climbs over the hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem hat us hwat bileefd mei in lykstaesje. Sy roan op in joun allinne midden op it paed. Sy wenne doe by de Nije Wei. Dêr is 't ek gebeurd. Sy wie boven oer de lykwein hinne stapt en der achter wer by del tûmele.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22304,"r":"CJ034409","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman sees a funeral procession pass and suspects a death is imminent. Shortly afterwards a boy dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ruerde Saek helle saterdeijouns altyd boadskippen op yn in âlde sek. Dy boadskippen forkocht se dan wer. Sy wenne yn 'e Smoarhoeke.\nOp in kear doe hie se wer boadskippen kocht. Doe't se op 'e Fûgelkamp wie, bleau se stean. 't Wie tichte by de keet fan Albert en Tet.\nDoe seach se in lykstaesje. De minsken dy't achter it lyk oanroannen, koe se wol.\nKrekt yn dy tiid wie Paulus (Alma) fan Albert en Tet tige siik. De jonge wie sechstjin jier. Ruerde Saek sei: \"Hjir gebeurt hwat by Albert en Tet yn 't koart.\"\nHja fortelde dat oan oare lju en sa kom Tet it ek to hearren. Doe hat Tet nei har ta west to freegjen hwat se sjoen hie. \"Is 't wol sa?\" frege Tet. \"Ja,\" sei se, \"ik liich net.\"\nEn 't is ek gebeurd. In skoftsje letter ha se Paulus útdroegen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22316,"r":"CJ034508","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A mother sees a funeral procession pass at a certain spot and runs away in fear.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem en dy soenen us in kear nei 't Fean ta. Dêr roannen se hinne. Sy hienen in lytse jonge by har. Doe seagen se ûnderweis in lykstaesje oan 'e oare kant de wei. Dat doogde lang net. Sy binne fuort werom gong.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22317,"r":"CJ034509","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You should never walk in the middle of the road at night, because a funeral procession may come up behind you.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In minske moat by joun of by nacht noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant dan kin er in rare reis meitsje. Dan rinne jy by in lykwein op en ploffe der achter wer by del.\nMen kin ek wol oan kant skoud wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22318,"r":"CJ034510","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman in labour sees a funeral procession pass. It is a foreseeing vision of her own death: the woman dies shortly afterwards in childbed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Harkema stie in hûske, dêr wenne froeger Jan Hamstra yn. Dy syn wiif dat moest yn 'e kream fan har earste bern.\nSy seach in lykstaesje. Der lei in wite doek achter oer de kiste hinne. Alle minsken dy't achter de kiste oan roannen, koe se wol. 't Wienen lju út har buorren. (buorreplicht!)\nHja is yn 'e kream stoarn. Sy hie har eigen lykstaesje sjoen. 't Wie doe noch boereplicht. De lju fan har buorren roannen der achteroan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22678,"r":"CJ034606","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You should never walk in the middle of the road, because you may be pushed aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der woarde ús al hiel jong leard, noait midden op 'e wei to rinnen. Hwant it koe gebeure dat der in lykstaesje oankom en dan woarde men oan kant set.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22735,"r":"CJ035205","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul has to get up at night to see things, such as funeral processions. A caul must not be destroyed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Pake hie in kammeraed, dat wie Marten. Dy wenne by de boer. Marten wie mei de helm geboaren. Nachts gong hy der ôf, dan moest er hwat sjen. Dat wienen yn de regel lykstaesjes.\nSa'n helm mei net fornietige wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22780,"r":"CJ035413","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You should never run in the middle of the road, because you might be pushed aside.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In minske mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant dan kin er us oan kant skoud wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22847,"r":"CJ036204","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man foresees deaths in passing funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us pake (heit syn heit) seach wol us lykstaesjes fan tofoaren. Hy wist altyd as der yn 'e omgeving in sterfgefal komme soe. In skoftsje letter kom dat ek altyd út. Hy wenne yn Bûtenpost en wie ôfkomstich fan Stiens.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22927,"r":"CJ036714","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man is suddenly pushed to the side for no reason. He suspects a funeral procession passed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn sweager fan 'e Boelensloane kuijere us in kear op in snein-to-joun tusken it jongfolk. Doe woarde hy samar oan kant set. Hy hie neat sjoen, mar nei alle gedachten hat dêr in lykstaesje west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22933,"r":"CJ036720","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man urges his companions to step aside for a passing funeral procession. Only he can see it. He foresees that his brother will die. It turns out exactly so.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining fan 'e Boelensloane soe us in kear nei Noord-Jerneel (de tsjerke). Dêr soenen lichtbeelden fortoand wurde. Syn skoanâlden wienen by him. Doe't se sahwat oan 't kafé fan Bouke Pultrum ta wienen, doe sei er:\n\"Jimme matte oan 'e kant en even wachtsje.\"\nSy gongen oan kant en bleauwen stean.\n\"Ha jo hwat sjoen?\" fregen se.\n\"Ja,\" sei er, \"der is in lykstaesje foarby gong en dat is fan myn broerke. It skúfgleske sil dêrby iepen gean en it gerdyn sil dêr trochwapperje.\" Sa is 't ek gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22935,"r":"CJ036722","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman warns her pregnant neighbour that she has seen a funeral procession pass made up only of men. The woman suspects that her neighbour will lose her unborn child. It turns out exactly so: the men carry the baby.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn wiif wie swier fan in bern. Doe kom de buorfrou by har en sei: \"Hark us, ik haw in lykstaesje sjoen, dêr wienen hast gjin froulju by, wòl manlju.\"\nMyn wiif hie fuort yn 'e gaten dat dit fan it bern wêze soe, dat se krije soe, mar sy woarde der net oars fan. Sy sei rêstich: \"As God it bileavet fan net, dan gebeurt it net.\"\nIt bern gong dea. De buorfrou hie 't wol goed sjoen.\nDe manlju droegen it berntsje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22969,"r":"CJ036920","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul is often forcibly driven out of bed at night to see funeral processions pass. A man born with a caul foresaw his own daughter's suicide.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei de helm geboaren is, dy mat der nachts faek út. Dan mat er lykstaesjes sjen. Der wenne sa'n man ûnder Kollumersweach, dy ha 'k wol kend. Dat wie Knjillis Veenstra. Dy seach geregeld lykstaesjes yn 'e nacht. Hy moest der soms hiele einen foar rinne, hiel Kollumersweach troch. Woed er lizzen bliuwe, dat joech him neat, hy woarde út bêd licht.\nHy hat ek de bigraffenis fan syn eigen dochter sjoen. Dy dochter hie forkearing mei in feint. Mar har âlden woenen it net lije. Doe hat dy dochter har fordronken yn in dobbe, flak by 't spoar.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22970,"r":"CJ036921","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You should never walk in the middle of the road at night, because you could take a nasty fall from a passing hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In minske mat nachts net midden op 'e wei rinne. Hwant dan kin 't gebeure dat er foar by in lykwein oprint en der achter by delfalt, en dan kin er in rare smeet meitsje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22993,"r":"CJ037020","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If you walk in the middle of the road at night, you are sometimes pushed to the side by an invisible funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As men yn 'e nacht midden op 'e wei rint, wurdt men soms oan kant treaun troch in lykstaesje, dy't passeare mat.\nSa'n lykstaesje sjogge jo net.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23059,"r":"CJ037603","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One night a man saw a funeral procession while in reality there was nothing there. A week later the funeral procession really came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Sipke Hil seach yn 'e nacht froulju yn greate redenskleden rinnen achter in lyk oan. Doomny Feitsma roan foarop, dat wie in oefener. 't Folk roan nei Ikkerwâld ta. 't Wie doe allegear noch sânwei.\nSahwat in wike letter wie de echte lykstaesje der.\nDer binne wol folle mear minsken yn Ikkerwâld west, dy't nachts lykstaesjes seagen, sûnder dat se mei de helm geboaren wienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23116,"r":"CJ038109","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who was born with a caul often had to get up at night. Then he saw funeral processions and knew who was going to die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Greate Taeke (= T. Wagenaar, byneamd Syngsang) wenne yn 'e Westerein fan Garyp. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Nachts moest hy der wolris ôf, om nei in lykstaesje to sjen, dy't dêr lâns kom. Hy wist dan wer hwa't der stjerre soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23135,"r":"CJ038306","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who was born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. Because of this he always knew in advance that a death was coming, but he did not know who would die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir op 'e Klontsjebuorren (nou Boskwei) hat in man wenne, dy wist altyd as der in deaden kom. It wie Douwe Stavasius. Nachts moest er der ôf. Dan koed er net langer op bêd wêze. Dan roan er op 'e wei om. Sy seinen, Douwe wie mei de helm geboaren. 't Kom altyd nei hwat er fortelde. Mar hy wist noait hwa't der stjerre soe. Hy sei 't wol dagen fan tofoaren dat der wer in begraffenis komme soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23345,"r":"CJ038405","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who was born with a caul often saw funeral processions in advance. Once he pulled his wife to the side because he saw a coffin being pulled along on a sledge. His wife saw nothing. Some time later someone died, and his coffin was pulled across the ice.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Tike hat ien west, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Nachts moest hy der wol us ôf, dan moest er hwat sjen. Dat wienen yn de regel lykstaesjes.\nAs er jouns mei syn frou to jounpraten gong dan seach er soms ek fan alles. Hy wenne sahwat by de skoalle. Op in joun soed er mei syn wiif to jounpraten. 't Wie yn 'e winter en der lei snie.\nDoe krige er har by de earm en treau har oan kant. Hy sei: \"Kom hjir even.\"\n\"Hwat is der nou wer?\" frege se.\n\"Der komt in slide oan,\" sei er, \"mei in kiste der op.\" Der roannen twa man achter, dy koed er beide. En sy gongen de kant nei de Leijen út.\nDer wie net ien dea, mar in skoftsje letter forstoar der ien. Doe gongen der twa mei in slide oer de Leijen, dy't biferzen wie om in kiste fan Eastemar to heljen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23346,"r":"CJ038406","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days children were warned never to walk in the middle of the road. An [invisible] funeral procession might come along and push them to the side.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en dy seinen altyd tsjin ús: \"Jimme matte noait midden op 'e wei rinne. Hwant dan kin der jimme in lykstaesje tomjitte komme en dan wurde jimme oan kant smiten.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23385,"r":"CJ038902","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Just before a funeral it sometimes happened that people were suddenly pushed off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in bigraffenis op til wie, dan woarden guon oan kant skoud, sûnder ûngelokken. Sieten jy op 'e fyts, dan woarde de fyts mei oan kant set. It gebeurde by nacht, mar ek wol by dei. As soks gebeurde seinen se: \"Nou komt der in bigraffenis\", en dat gebeurde ek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23407,"r":"CJ039008","p":"Siegerswoude","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man always saw funeral processions in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Wylp wenne ek in man dy koe lykstaesjes fan tofoaren sjen. Dy leefde yn 'e tiid doe't ik noch jong wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23519,"r":"CJ039802","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A young man once saw a funeral procession in front of a house. Not long afterwards a little daughter died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn man wie in jonge fan sa'n sawntsjin jier. Der wenne in âld minske yn 'e buert, dy hie twa dochters. Ien fan dy famkes wie ûngelokkich, it minske droech har altyd op 'e rêch.\nOp in nacht kom myn man dêr us lâns, doe seach er dêr in lykstaesje. In skoftsje letter stoar dat ûngelokkige bern.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23521,"r":"CJ039804","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who was born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Rapke Wijma fan Surhuzum wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest alles sjen, oan 'e lêste ûre fan syn libben ta. De lêste nacht noch, - doe koed er op syn fuotten net mear stean - is er út bêd weiklaud om hwat to sjen. Yn 'e gong is er yn elkoar sakke.\nHy makke soms hiele reizen yn 'e nacht, wolris oan Eastemar ta. Rounom gong er hinne. En 't kom altyd nei as er wer in lykstaesje sjoen hie. Hy mòest it sjen. Hy waerd dreaun.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23583,"r":"CJ040106","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One night a man was out on the road with his cow. Twice the cow suddenly ended up on the other side of the hedge for no reason. In this way the cow made sure the man got to see a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Pake fortelde, yn Houtigehage, by de Megielsreed, dêr wie in man, dy hie in koe forkocht; dy moest mei de boat mei. De nachts die er de koe oan 't tou en gong der mei op stap. Underweis moest er by in hage lâns. Dêr woarde dy koe samar opnom - ik hâldde him beet, sa fortelde er - en doe woarde dy koe oan 'e oare kant fan 'e hage wer delset. It tou siet dwars troch de hage hinne.\nDe man gong nei de oare kant ta. De koe trille as in rusk. Hy nom de koe wer mei op 't paed. Doe't er in eintsje fierder roan hie, woarde de koe wer opnom en dat gong wèr oer de hage hinne. Doe híj ek wer nei de oare kant ta.\nEn doe seach er hwat dêr to rêdden wie. Dêr hie in lykstaesje west, dy moèst er sjen. De koe hie him dêrhinne loadst. Dy hie makke dat hy 't seach.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23594,"r":"CJ040204","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man once saw a funeral procession in the night. A few days later one of the neighbours died and he saw the funeral procession in reality.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Harmen Bouwes Postma fan 'e Grinzer Pein dy hie in lykstaesje sjoen yn 'e nacht. Dy lykstaesje gong de wei lâns, in doomny foarop en 't folk der achteroan. Sy droegen it lyk de wei del. Doe wienen se by in hûs kom en dêr swaeiden se de reed op nei 't tsjerkhôf ta. Doe woarden se wei.\nIn dei of hwat letter stoar ien fan 'e buorren. Doe gongen de lju 't selde paedtsje del mei de bigraffenis ûnder deselde sitewaesjes lyk as hy it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23605,"r":"CJ040302","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People often knocked on a man's windows. He then had to go out to see funeral processions. Once he told the other man on a cart that he should lead the horse to the side because a funeral procession was coming. But the other man saw nothing and refused. Then they ended up in the ditch, cart and all.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wibe-fisker fan Sumar moest der nachts faek ôf. Dan woarde der by him op 'e ruten kloppe. Dan wist hy wol hoe let it wie. Dan moest er wer in lykstaesje sjen. Soms roan er hiele einen.\nOp in kear hied er mei noch ien nei Garyp ta west nei in forkeaping. Sy rieden togearre yn in wein en hienen tofolle drank hawn.\nUnderweis sei Wibe: oan kant, der komt in lykstaesje oan. Mar de oare man hie de leije yn 'e hân en woe net oan kant. \"Merakels\", sei er.\nDoe binne se mei reau en al oan kant set en yn 'e sleat tolânne kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23709,"r":"CJ041111","p":"Peize","v":"Dr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One should never walk in the middle of the road in the evening or at night. Sometimes you are suddenly pushed to the side when a funeral procession is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat jouns en nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne. Men wurdt soms samar oan kant set, as der in lykstaesje oankomt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23753,"r":"CJ041605","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People should never walk in the middle of the road, because they can suddenly be pushed to the side. A funeral procession might pass by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem sei altyd: in minske mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant hy kin oars samar oan kant set wurde. Der kin us in lykstaesje oankomme.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23770,"r":"CJ041905","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who was born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. He also saw his own child's funeral procession in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Knjillis Veenstra wenne by 't spoar. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy útfanhûze wol gauris by syn suster.\nDy hat wolris forteld, as hy kom, dan rûme hja bûten alles op, hwat mar yn 'e wei lizze koe. Hwant it gebeurde wit hoe faek dat hy der nachts op út gong, en dan koe 't wolris gebeure, ornearre se, dat er oer dingen yn 't tsjuster stroffelje soe.\nKnjillis hat de lykstaesje sjoen fan syn eigen bern.\nDy is doe fordronken.\n't Kom altyd nei, hwat hy fan tofoaren seach.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23780,"r":"CJ042004","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who was born with a caul saw a funeral procession pass by. The next day the funeral procession really passed by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek us in kear doe gong Piter Mook de Hegewei del mei syn dochter. Doe sei er: \"Wy matte oan kant, der komt hwat oan.\" Sy gongen oan kant. Der gong in lykstaesje foarby. De oare deis waerd dyselde bigroeven.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23807,"r":"CJ042108","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman who was born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. Because of this she always knew in advance who would die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hinke hat my forteld: \"Ik bin mei in helm geboaren. Hie 'k him mar net. Ik sil 't jo fortelle, ik ha der fannacht twa kear út west. Beide kearen ha 'k in lykstaesje sjoen. Hjir ien fan myn neiste buorren, dy hat der aenst west.\"\nEn hwat blykt? De oare moarns is de man wol dea. Sy sei, 't siet yn 'e helm.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23914,"r":"CJ042908","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man was once lifted over the ditch, bicycle and all. People thought funeral processions sometimes passed by at that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op it Langpaed (fan Harkema nei Surhuzum) woarde Jehannes Laanstra mei fyts en al oer de sleat set.\nIt Langpaed wie fan âlds in lykpaed. De lju woenen wol ha dat der doe in lykstaesje west hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23953,"r":"CJ043212","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A few men were once on the road with a horse and cart. Suddenly the horse got scared and jumped to the side. The men saw nothing. Someone came by and said that this happened more often. That man, like the horse, then saw a funeral procession pass by. If it was a white coach, all was well, then it was spiritual. If it was a black coach, then it meant death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen op 'e ein fan 'e Krúswei en hienen froeger in molkrit. Wy moesten de bussen nei dikke Marten bringe, dat wie de fierste. Mar dan moesten wy by Freark lâns. Dêr gongen wy fan 'e wein.\nDat gebeurde op in kear, doe woarde it hynder kjel. It sprong oan kant. Wy woarden kjel, mar Freark bleau bidaerd. Hy sei: \"Dat ha 'k wol faker bileefd. Salang as 't wyt is, is 't neat. As 't swart is, is 't minder.\"\n't Hynder hie in lykstaesje sjoen. Wíj seagen 't net, mar Freark wol. ('t Wie in wite lykstaesje - dat is geastlik - ; in swarten is fan 'e dood)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23955,"r":"CJ043214","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days people were warned never to walk in the middle of the road. A funeral procession might pass or even make you fall.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der is ús altyd leard: Noait midden op 'e wei rinne. Men kin samar oan kant skoud wurde as der in lykstaesje passeare mat. Slimmer nôch: men kin der fóár by oprinne en der achter by del knoffelje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24119,"r":"CJ044306","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who was born with a caul always has to see everything in advance. He sees that people will die, because he saw funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik bin mei de helm geboaren. Sy ha my by myn geboarte de helm net ûntnom. Sadwaende moest ik alles altyd sjen. Hoefolle minsken as ik net fantofoaren dea sjoen ha. Ik ha wol gauris minsken warskôge. It kom altyd nei. Ik seach de lykstaesjes tusken tolven en ienen yn 'e nacht.\nAlle nachten moest ik der dan ôf. En dan seach ik se passearen as 'k foar 't rút stie of op 'e wei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24123,"r":"CJ044310","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"At night a man often saw funerals as an omen of the coming day. He was then driven out of his bed and had to watch.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De bigraffenissen sjoch ik altyd by nacht. Dat is de foarboade fan 'e dei. Meastal stean 'k oan 'e kant yn 'e barm, en dan gean se foarby. Dat duorret mar even. Op syn langst duorret it dan noch trije dagen, dat se komme mei 't lyk.\nIk wurd net kloppe. Ik wurd twong om der út. Ik bliuw noait lizzen.\nIk bin nou sawn en tachtich. Ik gean der nou net mear út. Mei de âlde dei giet it fuort.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24135,"r":"CJ044401","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who was born with a caul often had to get up at night to see a funeral procession. A few days later someone really died.\nA midwife sometimes delivered children with a caul. That was a thin membrane. No strange eyes may look upon it. The caul must be removed in a particular way. The midwife would then secretly take it with her and burn it as soon as she was alone. Doctors are mad about such cauls.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wenne in man yn Ikkerwâld, dy moest yn 'e nacht faek fan bêd, dan moest er in lykstaesje sjen. As sa'n lykstaesje passeard wie, gong er wer op bêd. In dei of hwat letter stoar der dan ien dêr't hy fantofoaren de bigraffenis al fan sjoen hie.\nHy wie mei de helm geboaren, seinen se.\nUs beppe wie kreamheinster, dy hat wol us sa nou en dan ien in helm ôfdien. Dêr mochten gjin oare egen oer gean. 't Wie mar sa'n tin flueske. Beppe die de helm ornaris gau by 't jak yn en dan in skoftsje letter, as se allinne wie, die se him gau yn 't fjûr, dat gjin ien it seach.\nDokters binne hyt op sokke helmen, sizze se.\nMen mat wol oppasse hoe't men sa'n helm ôfdocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24179,"r":"CJ044517","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If you see a funeral procession coming, you must step aside. Otherwise you are thrown to the side. People who do not see the funeral processions are pushed aside too.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik sjoch in lykstaesje altyd fan fierrens al oankommen. Men mat dan beslist oan kant gean yn 'e barm. Dan geane se jo foarby. As men se gjin paed lit en men bliuwt midden op 'e wei, dan wurdt men oan kant smiten. Ek deselden dy't de lykstaesje net sjogge wurde dan oan kant reage.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24199,"r":"CJ044805","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man always saw funeral processions passing along the road that nobody else saw.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tichte by Fryske Peallen wenne in persoan, as jy dêrmei gongen, dan sei er ûnderweis: \"Even oan kant, der komt hwat oan, dat mat rûmte ha.\" Net ien dy't seach hwat it wie, mar hy sels wol. Dan gong er oan kant oant it passeard wie, dat wie dan in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24244,"r":"CJ045119","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A father warns his children never to walk in the middle of the road in the evening.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn heit sei altyd tsjin ús: As jim by jountiid fuortgean, rin net midden op 'e wei, mar altyd oan 'e kant.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24330,"r":"CJ045803","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man urges his companions to step aside for a passing funeral procession. A child is being buried. It is a premonition: shortly afterwards a little child really dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Taeke Postma, in broer fan myn mem/man, hat us hwat sjoen. Hy kuijere mei noch in stik of hwat fan syn maten nei de wei ta. Wy wennen doe oan 'e Boskreed. Doe sei er tsjin 'e oaren: \"Even oan kant. Der komt hwat oan. 't Is in lykstaesje.\"\n't Wie in lytsen-ien, fan in bern.\nGau dêrnei forlearen guon in bern. Taeke sei: \"Dat is 't net.\"\nIn skoftsje letter forlearen Jille en Sybrich in bern. Dat wie 't hwat er sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24331,"r":"CJ045804","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman is driven into the ditch by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem roan us midden op 'e wei. Sy hie 't molkammerke yn 'e hân, hwant sy soe om molke nei 't hûs dêr't nou Mekke v. D. wennet.\nMar ûnderweis woarde se samar yn 'e sleat set. Der hie in lykstaesje west. Mei 't lege ammerke kom mem werom. Sy sei tsjin heit: \"Nou hellestû mar molke op. Ik kom dêr net wer lâns.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24333,"r":"CJ045806","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man is driven into the ditch by a passing funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Djoede Rins woarde ek al us in kear yn 'e sleat set, doe't der in lykstaesje oan kaem. Dat gebeurde hjir ek oan 'e betonwei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24383,"r":"CJ046112","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul sees a funeral procession pass in windless weather. The people in the procession, mostly wrapped in rain clothes, can barely stay on their feet because of a violent storm. It is a premonition: when someone dies later, there is a violent storm as well.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie ien op 'e Loane dy hie fan tofoaren in lykstaesje sjoen. Mar dat wie hiel eigenaerdich, hwant it wie dy nachts blêdstil waer. Mar de minsken dy't by dy lykstaesje wienen hienen de huodden en petten fêsthâlden en de regenkleden fan 'e froulju waeiden en wapperen alle kanten út. Sy wienen der skjin forlegen mei.\nDy lykstaesje wie op 't tsjerkhôf fan 'e Loane taset.\nIn skoft letter forstoar der ien. Doe stie der in stoarm. It waeide dat it rikke en de froulju hienen hâlden en kearen mei har regenkleden. 't Wie krekt sa lyk as hy it dy nachts sjoen hie.\nDy man wie mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24424,"r":"CJ046312","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Never run in the middle of the road at night: a funeral procession may pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy woarden altyd warskôge: rin noait midden op 'e wei by joun of by nacht, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje passeare.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24425,"r":"CJ046313","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One hunter urges the other to step aside for a passing funeral procession. The one man foresees that a certain woman is going to die, and it turns out exactly so.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn man hat murdefanger west. Op in kear wie Piter de Graaf mei myn man to murdejeijen. Sy wienen yn 'e Kompenije op in âld reedtsje. Doe sei Piter tsjin myn man: \"Wolst even oan kant gean?\" \n\"Hwerom mat ik oan kant?\" sei myn man.\n\"Gean even oan kant,\" sei Piter, \"hwant der komt in lykstaesje oan.\"\n\"Och, rin hinne\", sei myn man. Mar hy wie even mei Piter oan kant stean gong, yn 'e wâl. 't Wie nacht. Even letter sei Piter: \"Kom der nou mar wer wei. Hast it ek sjoen?\"\n\"Né,\" sei myn man, \"ik ha neat sjoen.\"\n\"Sjochst dat hûs dêr wol?\" sei Piter.\n\"Ja\", sei myn man.\n\"Binnen fjirtsjin dagen is de frou wei dy't dêr yn wennet.\"\nIt is krekt sa útkom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24547,"r":"CJ047401","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"At a haunted spot, the stakes used to moor a ship to the ground are thrown onto the deck again and again. A funeral procession once had to pass the place where the ship lies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en dy wienen skipper. Op in nacht leinen wy mei 't skip op in plak by in stik lân, dêr't wy oars noait leinen. Heit hie de beide spitten yn 'e groun set en wy joegen ús del.\nYn 'e nacht woarden de spitten mei in great stik lawaei op it dek smiten.\nHeit der út om to sjen, mar der wie neat. Hy treau de spitten wer yn 'e groun en it skip lei wer fêst. Doe gong er wer op bêd.\nMar hy hie noch mar in kertier lein of dêr wie 't wer bouns, bouns! De beide spitten, dêr't de touwen oan sieten, hienen se wer op it dek smiten.\nDoe heit der wèr ôf. Mar der wie ek nou neat to sjen. Doe hat heit it skip in skipslingte forlein. Dêr hat er de spitten wer yn 'e groun set. Doe ha wy dy nachts gjin lêst wer hawn.\nMen woe wol ha dat dêr op it plak, dêr't wy earst leinen froeger in lykstaesje lâns moest. Dy krige dan kear fan 'e touwen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24551,"r":"CJ047405","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman urges a companion to step aside for a passing funeral procession. Only the one woman can see the procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem dy tsjinne by de boer en sy hie in kammeraetske, dat tsjinne by in oare boer. Jouns gongen se wol gauris togearre to kuijerjen. Op in kear, doe hienen se wer in eien kuijere, doe sei dy oare faem tsjin mem: \"Dû mast dêr wei komme, Afke, der komt in lykstaesje oan.\"\n't Wie al let op 'e joun.\nSy pakte mem by 't skouder beet en luts har oan 'e kant. Even letter sei se: \"Kom nou mar wer, 't is foarby. Wy kinne wol wer fuortgean.\"\nMem hat letter noait wer mei har kuijerje wold.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24596,"r":"CJ047801","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man urges a companion to step aside for a passing funeral procession with a hearse drawn by a white horse. It is an omen: a week later a dead person is taken to the churchyard. Because the black horse refused, a white horse was harnessed to the hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der roannen us twa man by nacht fan Drachten ôf de Hegebrechster loane del. Doe sei de iene tsjin 'e oare: \"Even oan kant. Der komt in lykstaesje oan.\" Doe seach er in lykwein mei in wyt hynder der foar. Doe't de lykstaesje foarby wie sei er tsjin 'e oare: \"Nou gean wy mar wer fierder.\"\nIn wike letter doe kom der in man fan 'e Dammen (ûnder Drachtster Kompenije) op 't hôf. It lyk woarde de Hegebrechsterloane del riden, it kom op it Noardertsjerkhôf to hôf. (to Drachten). It swarte hynder, dat se der earst foarspanden, hie wegere. Doe hienen se in wyt hynder foar de boerewein spand, út need.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24670,"r":"CJ049204","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A mother and son are driven out of bed at night to foresee deaths in passing funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tiense Boomsma sawol as syn mem dy seagen altyd lykstaesjes fan tofoaren. Dan moesten se der ôf. Sy gongen dan yn 'e nacht foar 't glês stean. Dan telden se de minsken dy't der achteroan roannen en sy seagen nei 't hûs dêr't se weikamen.\nDoe't it âld minske al bot siik wie en op bêd bliuwe moest, gong se der nòch ôf en dan bleau se hiele skoften foar 't glês stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24673,"r":"CJ049207","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man is driven to the side of the road at night by a passing funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Aelsen Booi fan Houtigehage wie in broer fan myn skoanheit. 't Wie yn 'e nacht en hy gong de wei lâns. Doe waerd er ynienen samar oan kant set. Hy koe net fierder komme. Dêr hat doe in lykstaesje west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24674,"r":"CJ049208","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Warning: never walk in the middle of the road at night.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":24696,"r":"CJ049303","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man suddenly sees a funeral procession. It is a premonition of an approaching death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Piter Claus fortelde my, hy wie ris yn syn jonge jierren nei de faem ta west nei 't Wytfean. Doe wie der him yn 'e Rottefalle in lykstaesje passeard.\nLetter seach er dyselde lykstaesje wer by dei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24697,"r":"CJ049304","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A poacher coming home at night sees a number of cats sitting by his door. He tries to shoot the cats. When his mortally ill wife dies, the nightly visits by the cats suddenly stop. When his second wife is expecting, he suddenly sees a funeral procession. He is very afraid his wife will die in childbed, but this fate befalls another woman.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn neef Wessel wenne yn it Wyldfjild. Hy fortelde my: Ik gong altyd in bulte to streupen. As ik nachts thús kom, wienen 't by ús allegearre katten om 'e doar.\nBaeije, myn wiif wie altyd siik. Dy tsjirme. As ik dan nachts dy katten allegear seach, koe 'k it net litte en sjit der op.\n\"Skeatstû noch?\" sei Baeije dan.\n\"Ja,\" sei 'k, \"ik woe de patroanen út it gewear ha.\"\nWessel wie in keardel as in beam mar op it lêst woarde er bang fan dy katten altyd om 'e doar.\nBaeije kom to forstjerren.\nWessel sei: \"'k Ha noait in kat wer sjoen.\"\nDoe is er wer troud mei Jel.\nHy fortelde: \"Jel wie op in kear wer yn forwachting. Ik kom thús, doe seach ik in lykstaesje. Der lei in wite doek oerhoeks oer de kiste hinne.\nIk seach de lykstaesje nei. Ik seach him de Loane yngean. Ik tocht: 'Och heden, dêr giet Jel èk noch nei de sânheuvel ta.' (As er dat fortelde roannen him de triennen by de wangen del)\nIn dei of hwat letter overleed Anne Betsje yn 'e kream.\nDoe wie 'k sa bliid, hwant ik tochte o heden, dêr giet Jel wer hinne.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24810,"r":"CJ049601","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Warning: never walk in the middle of the road, because of passing funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der waerd ús froeger altyd foarhâlden: rin noait midden op 'e strjitte, hwant dan kin 't gebeure dat jim tsjin in lykstaesje oanrinne en oan kant set wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24944,"r":"CJ050804","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You must never walk in the middle of the road at night, because a funeral procession may pass. A man was once driven into the ditch by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der waerd de minsken froeger altyd foarhâlden: Rin noait midden op 'e wei by nacht.\nAlde Hindrik de Vegt wenne by de Oerterper feart. Hy gong yn 'e nacht de Modderwyk lâns. Doe passearde dêr in lykstaesje. Hy woarde samar yn 'e brede wyk smiten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24947,"r":"CJ050807","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A midwife sometimes warns of passing funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Antsje Huizinga fan Burgum wie in bikende froedfrou. Dy hellen se faek yn 'e nacht op, as der in lytsen op komst wie. Dan sei se wolris, as de lju midden op 'e wei wienen: \"Ho, dêr net lâns, hjir mat in lykstaesje passeare.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25083,"r":"CJ051006","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A father warns his children never to walk in the middle of the road at night. After all, they might run into a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit woe noait lije, dat wy froeger by jountiid of by nacht midden op 'e wei roannen. Sels gong er ek altyd yn 'e berm lâns. Men koe ris tsjin in lykwein oprinne, wie syn sizzen altyd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25128,"r":"CJ051602","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If someone walks in the middle of the road, it may happen that he is seized by an invisible funeral procession and flung over the hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is wol gebeurd dat ien midden op 'e wei lâns roan sûnder dat er it lykfolk oankommen seach. Dan woarde sa'n ien oer de boerewein hinne smiten, dêr't it lyk op lei. Alles wie foar him ûnsichtber.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25132,"r":"CJ051606","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man often sees funeral processions pass during the day. They are premonitions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Liuwe de Haan fan 'e Westerein seach soms ek fan to foaren lykstaesjes by dei. Hy wennet oan 'e Verlengde Stationsstrjitte.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25167,"r":"CJ052002","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman and her little nephew see a funeral procession approaching. Shortly afterwards they are both flung into the ditch. It is a premonition: later a girl dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jille Pultrum - dy't froeger winkelman wie - syn (skoan?)mem hiet fan Antsje. Dat wie myn suster. Har man siet ûnskuldich yn 'e gefangenis. Ik moest dêr nachts by Antsje sliepe, hwant sy moest bifalle.\nDoe't it har oan kom, sei se tsjin my: \"Clare, wolst even myn mem helje?\" Dy wenne dêr in eintsje fandinne.\n\"Nim Jille dan mar even mei\", sei se tsjin my.\nIk rôp lytse Jille fan bêd. Wy gongen togearre op stap.\nMyn iene rôk hie 'k ûnder 'e earm. Jille hie 'k beet by de hân. 'k Sei: \"Leave, wy sille gau beppe helje.\"\nWy gongen 't paedtsje skean oer. Doe't wy in eintsje fan myn susters hûs ôf wienen, kom der in bigraffenis oan. Sa like it my tominsten ta. En sa hat it ek west. Hwant doe't wy noch in eintsje fierder wienen woarden ik en lytse Jille yn 'e sleat goaid. Wy hienen allebeide de lykstaesje sjoen. Ik liet fan kjellens de rôk lizze.\nDoe't wy in eintsje fierder wienen, sei 'k tsjin Jille: \"wy matte gau werom.\" Dat dienen wy. Ik taestte en doe foun ik de rôk. Doe wy togearre werom skean oer 't paedtsje.\nDoe't ik by ús thús wie fleach it my ynienen oan. Ik wie bang. Ik kletste op 'e doarren en sei: \"Mem, mem, gau mei. Us Antsje sa en sa.\"\nDoe't ús mem by myn suster Antsje kom, kom skoanmem dêr ek. Doe't mem har it forhael die fan 'e lykstaesje, sei se: \"'t Kin bêst sa gebeure. 't Kin bêst wêze dat it foartjirmerij is.\" \"Tichteby wenne in faem: Fintsje. Dy is in skoft letter st","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25218,"r":"CJ052315","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man has to step aside for a funeral procession. It is a premonition: a few days later someone dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn neef Wessel Gal wie in kear op 'e wei, doe moest er oerside, hwant der kom in lykstaesje oan.\nDe èchte lykstaesje wie pas in dei of hwat letter.\nHy hat ek fan to foaren sjoen dat se syn earste wiif biklaeiden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25234,"r":"CJ052415","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The narrator tells of two men who often saw funeral processions. You must never walk in the middle of the road, because an invisible funeral procession can drive you off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Douwe Stavasius fan Grinzer Pein seach lykstaesjes.\nBoardzer Bruining fan Boelensloane ek. Dy leeft noch.\nMen mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje oankomme, sûnder dat men it sjocht. Dan wurde jo fan 'e wei ôfsmiten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25261,"r":"CJ052608","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man, born with a caul, urges a companion to step aside for an approaching funeral procession. The companion ignores his warnings and keeps walking on the road. Promptly he is lifted up by a hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Surhuzum wenne Rapke Wijma. 't Wie famylje fan 'e bikende klokmakker fan Eastemar. Hy wie âld-feint. Ik gong jouns wolris mei him to kuijerjen. Op in joun doe wie 'k wer by him, doe sei er ynienen tsjin my: \"Nou mast fan 'e wei ôfkomme.\"\n\"Hwerom mat ik dat?\" sei 'k.\nHy sei: \"Der komt in lyk oan. 'k Sil dy moarn wol sizze hwa't it is.\"\nIk sei: \"Praetsjes.\" En ik gong net fan 'e wei ôf.\nMar doe gong 'k boven oer de lykwein hinne. Ik gong der fóár by op en der achter wer by del. 'k Stapte der samar by del, 'k foel hielendal net.\nRapke Wijma wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy hie harten yn 'e blinen foar de glêzen. Dan hoefde hy der net út, as der in lykstaesje passearde. Hy koe it troch dy harten sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25285,"r":"CJ052801","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man foresees that a hearse will have to take a detour because the road is flooded. The premonition comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn suster Harmke hat in great-dochter forlern, in fanke fan fjirtsjin à fyftsjin jier. Sy wennen yn 'e Westerein oan 't kanael. Harmke bigearde dat it bern soe op it tsjerkhôf yn Ikkerwâld biïerdige wurde.\nIt lyk kom op in boerewein, lyk as de gewoante wie.\nDe minsken kommen yn in lange wein, in Janplezier, mar it reinde sa bot, dat sy koenen net it gewoane paed del: dêr lei tofolle wetter.\nDoe moesten se in oar paed nimme en sa kommen se by Roel van Kammen foar de glêzen lâns.\nRoel sei: \"Dat wist ik wol, dat dy wein dêr net lâns gean soe. Ik ha de lykstaesje al in pear maend lyn by ús foar de doar lâns kommen sjoen.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25310,"r":"CJ053005","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A farm wagon is driven off the road. The horse seems to sense something. It was a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Ate Klazes ried mei de wein. 't Wie mar in gewoan boereweintsje. 't Hynder fornom dat der hwat wie, de man net. 't Hynder woe oan kant. Doe hearde er noch al in bouns oan 't achterste rad. De wein gong oerside. Der wie in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25360,"r":"CJ053330","p":"Ons Belang","v":"Utr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man becomes completely distraught when he is driven off the road by a funeral procession. He has to be escorted home and never dares to show himself at that spot again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Willem Peule (= Nicolai) hie ris by ús west to jounpraten. 't Wie al in moai eintsje yn 'e nacht op doe't er fuortgong. In skoft letter kom er werom, sa wyt as in deaden en alhiel oerstjûr.\nIk sei: \"Hwat skeelt dy, jonge.\"\nHy sei: \"Der kom my in lykstaesje foarby en ik woarde oerside set.\" Hy trille alhiel.\nMyn soan hat him doe nei hûs ta brocht. It gebeurde oan 'e Singel, dêr't nou Willem Weening wennet.\nLetter doarst er nachts net wer fuort.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25365,"r":"CJ053405","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"At night invisible funeral processions sometimes pass. A farmhand was once flung across the ditch by such an invisible funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Soms binne der lykstaesjes yn 'e nacht, dy sjocht men net.\nBy de Foarwei wenne Germ Pompomme, sa neamd omdat er stammere. Hy wie âldfeint en 't wie in goed mantsje. Op in joun soed er nei hûs ta, doe waerd er samar fan 'e wei ôf oer in sleat hinne smiten yn in oar syn lân. Dêr mat doe in lykstaesje west ha, dêr't er rûmte foar jaen matten hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25478,"r":"CJ054417","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Warning: at night always stay on the footpath and never go onto the road. After all, you may be driven aside or carried off by a passing funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat nachts der om tinke altyd op 't fuotpaed to bliuwen. Rin noait op 'e wei. Hwant der binne in bulte lykstaesjes. Jo wurde oan kant treaun of oer de lykwein hinne smiten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25877,"r":"CJ057511","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man always saw funeral processions in advance. Because of this he always knew in which house someone would die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining hie 't altyd oer lykstaesjes, dy't er fantofoaren seach. Hy wist altyd krekt yn hwat hûs as der ien stjerre soe. Mar dêr praet er nou net mear oer.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25881,"r":"CJ057515","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the past people always warned not to walk in the middle of the road because of funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mem sei altyd tsjin ús: Jouns oan 'e kant fan 'e wei rinne. Noait yn 'e midden! Fanwege lykstaesjes wie dat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32254,"r":"CJ1235B03","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People do not dare to ride on a certain cycle path at night, because funeral processions are said to pass there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By de Triemen is in fytspaed, dêr doarsten guon froeger by nacht nèt lâns, hwant dêr passearden altyd lykstaesjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":46291,"r":"WEV018003","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man has been pushed aside and believes something will happen at that spot, because he has seen a hearse.","i":"F.W.","o":"Biezied smeetn.\nOal Beernd kwam op n keer driefnat in hoes. \nHai har in sloot zeetn; was net zo van de weg ofgooid. \nNee, t kwam nait deur de wind, drank har e ook nt had. \nZol wel wat gebeurn op dei plekke, zo docht hai.\nJoa, was n liekwoagn langs goan, vertelde hai.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":25537,"r":"CJ055107","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. Some watched from the window, others had to walk a long way outside. Others were sometimes pushed off the road at night when a funeral procession came along.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon minsken binne wol oan kant set, as der in lykstaesje oankom. 't Gebeurde hast altyd by nacht.\nGuon seagen sa'n lykstaesje fan tofoaren. Dat wienen guon dy't mei de helm geboaren wienen. Sy moesten dan nachts út bêd wei. Sy woarden der útkloppe. Guon stienen dan foar 't finster to sjen. Mar oaren gongen bûtendoar en moesten soms hiele einen rinne om de lykstaesje to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25550,"r":"CJ055302","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man often got out of bed at night to see funeral processions. From the window he would see them float past.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tiense Boomsma fan 'e Houtigehage seach nachts altyd lykstaesjes. Sokken wienen der trouwens ek wol yn Boelensloane. Tiense is nou al fiif en fjirtich jier dea. Nachts gong hy út bêd wei. Dan gong er oan 't glês ta en dan die er 't gordyn iepen. Hy fortelde, dan kom der in lykstaesje oan, altyd út it westen wei, hjir oan ta, sei er - hy wenne oan 'e Skoallewyk - dan gong dy lykstaesje oer de wyk en dan oan 'e oare kant de wyk werom. It eigenaerdige wie dat de minsken en de lykwein samar oer de wyk hinne gongen. Se hoefden dan gjin groun ûnder har to hawwen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25602,"r":"CJ055611","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A young man on his way back was once pushed off the road several times by a hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Gerrit van der Heide wie myn omke. Gjert-om seinen wy tsjin him. Dy kom op in kear fan 'e faem. Dy wenne op 'e Trije Roede. Dy faem, dat waerd letter Frearkje-moai, dêr is er mei troud. De Trije Roede dat wie doe allegear noch sânwei.\nDoe't er in eintsje op stap wie, woarde er samar yn 't holst fan 'e nacht by in lykwein op smiten - doe der wer ôf, doe der wèr op en der wèr ôf.\nDoe't er thús kom wie hied er gjin soallen mear ûnder 'e skuon hawn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25615,"r":"CJ055624","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"It sometimes happened that horses refused to pull the wagon any further in the middle of the night. They were seeing a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Is wol gauris gebeurd, dat, as der ien mei hynder en wein ried by nacht, it hynder ynienen stean bleau. Dan woe 't mei gjin stok fierder. Dan seach it in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25633,"r":"CJ055910","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the past it sometimes happened that someone was suddenly pushed off the road by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde froeger wolris, dat ien samar oan kant stompt waerd, as der in lykstaesje passeare moest.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25672,"r":"CJ056205","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. They then knew that someone would die within a few days.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir ha guon wenne, dy wienen mei de helm geboaren. Dy koenen dan sizze binnen hoefolle dagen der wer in deaden yn Boarnburgum wêze koe. Sy seagen de lykstaesjes foarút. Nachts moesten sy der dan út.\nWie der ien dea, dan sei sa'n ien: \"Ik ha 't wol sjoen.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25754,"r":"CJ056717","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A married couple was on the way home one evening when the wife saw a funeral procession pass. The husband saw nothing. Some time later someone died, and the funeral procession really came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Frits Klunder wennet nou yn Bûtenpost (west). Mar earder wenne er op 'e Bulten yn 'e Harkema.\nOp in joun doe wienen hy en 't wiif to praten west nei har âlden, dy wennen yn 'e Bosk. Dêr wie doe in âld sânweike, der roannen se lâns. Doe kom der ûnderweis in lykstaesje oan. Hy passearde harren. Frits seach it net, mar syn wiif wol. Hy gong kantroerend by har lâns.\nMar in lyts skoftsje letter, doe stoar dêr ien. Doe gong de lykstaesje dêr lâns. Dat hie hja dus sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25761,"r":"CJ056802","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One evening a woman saw a funeral procession pass. She thought it was the funeral procession of an acquaintances' little child, who was not doing well. Later that child did indeed die, and the funeral procession really passed by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear hienen myn skoanmem en dy to jounpraten west yn 'e Bosk hjir yn 'e Harkema. Sy wienen noch mar in eintsje op stap, doe kommen se in lykstaesje tsjin. 't Wie let op 'e joun. Skoanmem sei: \"Dat kin wolris in bern fan Durk Jager wêze\", hwant dy wenne dêr, en dat bern wie noait net rjocht goed. Letter gong Durk Jager dêr wei to wenjen, doe sei mem: \"Ik ha mist west.\" Mar letter kom Durk Jager wer op itselde plak to wenjen, en doe stoar de jonge.\nDoe is dy lykstaesje dêr west, dy't skoanmem en dy sjoen hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25777,"r":"CJ056818","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If a funeral procession passes at night and people do not make way, they are pushed aside.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in lykstaesje nachts passearde, en de minsken joegen gjin rûmte dan woarden se oan kant set.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25892,"r":"CJ057604","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. Because of this he always knew in advance that someone would die. He also predicted that a major road would be built in a certain place. That came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Douwe Stavasius wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy wenne hjir yn 'e Pein. Stoar der ien, dan seach er dat fan tofoaren.\nHy hie in kwea âld wiif. As hy der nachts wer út west hie om nei in lykstaesje to sjen, dan sei se de oare deis: \"Douwe leit weer op 't nest, die is weer syk, dy het fannacht weer te spoekjen west.\"\nDouwe woarde der siik en ellindich fan. 't Wie in biswierlike húshâlding. Se wennen in een spitkeet en hadden twoalf kienders. Doar he se moar drie van overholdn.\nOp in kear wie olle Douwe yn 't branjefjild. Doe wie de greate forkearswei hjir noch net. Doe roan der noch in âld djipke troch de lannen.\nDoe sei Douwe: \"Dat old diepke wordt noch us uutgroavn, hwant der komt heel wat langs. Moar God, wat fliegen se hard!\"\nLetter is dêr de greate forkearswei komd en nou stouwe de auto's der lâns. Dy auto's hat hy doe al sjoen.\nSyn dochter Tietje Stavasius hat it ek, en syn heit hie it ek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25894,"r":"CJ057606","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man was once walking in the middle of the road when a funeral procession came along and he was flung off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is hier is gebeurd op in oavend, dat der in man over de weg liep. Die man liep gewoon midden op de weg. Toen kwam der in lykstaasje an en toen is-ie een heel eind smeten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25900,"r":"CJ057701","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two men were once walking along a sand road. One warned the other to step aside because a funeral procession was coming. But the other saw nothing and kept walking where he was. Then he was flung a long way.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in sânwei yn 'e Harkema roannen Klaes Postma en in kammeraet fan him. Dy't njonken him gong sei tsjin Klaes: \"Dû mast op side gean, der komt in lykstaesje oan.\"\nMar Klaes die it net. Doe is er in hiel ein fuortsodemitere woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25959,"r":"CJ058020","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People must never walk in the middle of the road at night. Otherwise they may be pushed off the road by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In minske mat op 'e joun en yn 'e nacht moait midden op 'e wei rinne. Alde Popke Albertsje hat it al ris dien.\nDoe kom der in lykstaesje oan en doe is sy smiten woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26069,"r":"CJ058613","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two men once came out of the pub and walked in the middle of the road. One warned the other to step aside because a funeral procession was coming. But the other saw nothing and kept walking where he was. Then he ended up in the ditch. He had walked into the hearse and been thrown off the back of it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wykstra fan Tolbert trof ik us in kear by Meint de Boer yn 'e kroech to Mearum. Wykstra fortelde:\nIk wie forline wike mei in maet op stap. 't Wie al let op 'e joun. Ik roan midden op 'e wei. Myn maet sei tsjin my: \"Kom dêr wei, Wykstra, hwant der komt in lykstaesje oan.\" Ik gong net fan 'e wei, mar roan troch.\nDêr liz ik - God help my - yn 'e sleat. 'k Wie dweiltrochwiet. Ik kom ta de sleat út. Doe sei myn maet: \"Ik ha dy warskôge. Dû bist foar ta de lykwein oproan en sy ha der dy achter ôfgoaid.\"\nDit gebeurde yn 'e buert fan Tolbert.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26114,"r":"CJ059006","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man was once pushed off the road by a funeral procession and ended up in the ditch.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bearn van der Woude kom op in saterdeijoune út 'e winkel wei. Hy wenne yn Driemunt, yn in âlde woanwein. Underweis woarde er samar fan 'e wei ôfslingere en oer in sleat hinne goaid.\nDêr hie in lykstaesje west. Hy hat it my sels forteld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26155,"r":"CJ059203","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two young men were once out on the road. One warned the other to step aside for a moment, because a funeral procession was coming. The other saw nothing. Not long afterwards someone died, and the funeral procession really did pass by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hindrik de Zwart wennet nou oan 'e Mûzegroppewei yn 'e Rotfalle. Hy en myn broer Germ kommen togearre de Mûzegroppewei ris delkuijerjen. 't Wie op in joun. Sy wienen sahwat ta oan it plak dêr't Sytse Batema formoarde is.\nDoe sei Hindrik tsjin Germ: \"Dû mast rûmte jaen. Even fan 't fytspaed ôf. Der komt in lykstaesje oan.\"\nSy stapten beide oer de groppe. 't Lyk gong harren foarby. Germ seach it net, mar Hindrik wol. Mar in lyts skoftsje dêrnei stoar der in man oan 'e Mûzegroppe.\nGerm en Hindrik wienen doe sa'n tritich jier âld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26172,"r":"CJ059401","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man had been born with a caul. At night he always saw funeral processions. Once, when he was out walking with someone, he said they had to move to the side because a funeral procession was coming. The other saw nothing, but did come home with soaking wet feet because they had been standing in the mud.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit kom fan Rotfalle. Dêr wenne in man, fortelde er, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy seach lykstaesjes yn 'e nacht.\nOp in nacht hied er in man by him hawn. Doe hied er sein: \"Mast hjir om tinke, as der aenst in lykstaesje komt, dan mast oan kant gean.\"\nDoe't it sa fier wie, sei er: \"Op side.\" Doe moest dy oare yn allegear drek en brabze stean gean. Hy wie mei kletstrochwiete fuotten thúskom en hie neat sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26208,"r":"CJ059618","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If you walk in the middle of the road, you may be pushed to the side by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Rinne jo midden op 'e wei dan kin 't gebeure dat jo troch in lykstaesje oan kant skoud wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26229,"r":"CJ060010","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A mother-in-law is once near a state school and sees two naked children. She is thrown aside, and the children, who were not given burial clothes, cannot find the others and have to pass by. The woman makes way for them.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanmem wie us yn 'e buert fan 'e staetsskoalle. 't Wie op in joun. Doe seach se twa neakene berntsjes. Doe woarde se in hiel ein oan kant smiten. Dy berntsjes koenen de rêst net fine. Dy moesten dêr lâns. Myn skoanmem moest rûmte jaen. Dy berntsjes hienen gjin leedguod meikrige.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26312,"r":"CJ060806","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If you walk in the middle of the road, you can be put aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As bern al seinen se tsjin ús: \"Noait midden op 'e wei rinne.\" Dat wie fanwege de lykstaesjes. Men koe us oan kant set wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26313,"r":"CJ060807","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man's brother is clairvoyant and grabs hold of the man between Hûs ter Noord and Kollumersweach, then lets him go again later. The man saw nothing apart from a small milestone. Hindrik, however, saw the ghost of a child passing by, and that is why he stepped aside.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw kunde hawn oan in Roomse man, dy sijn broer koe alles sjen. Hy en syn broer roannen us togearre tusken Hûs ter Noord en Kollumersweach. Doe hie syn broer him beet krigen en sein: \"Mast hjir even komme.\" \nEven letter sei er: \"Nou kinst dêr wol wer hinne gean. Hast neat sjoen?\" \"Né,\" sei myn kammeraet, \"allinne mar in mylpealtsje. Wie der dan hwat?\" \"Ja,\" sei Hindrik - sa hiet er - \"dêr wie in bern. Dat bern moesten wy rûmte jaen.\" 't Wie de geast fan in bern.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26315,"r":"CJ060809","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Someone was once suddenly lifted up, cart and all, and thrown into a ditch. He never saw anything. According to Hindrik, the man had been in the way of a ghost that had to pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn dy buert hat us ien mei de skoukarre west. Doe waerd er samar ynienen opnaem en yn 'e sleat smiten. Hy hie noait hwat sjoen. Hy fortelde 't Hindrik. Dy sei: \"Dû hast dêr ien yn 'e wei roun. In geast hat dêr lâns matten.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26856,"r":"CJ061407","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Durk lives by the Boskreed in Harkema. One night a brother of my father, Aen Klokje, sees from that house a funeral procession pass by for a boy who has died. Durk dies soon after this incident and the funeral really takes place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Durk hat by de Boskreed wenne yn 'e Harkema yn in forlofsaek. De broer fan myn heit, Aen Klokje (= Aen Alma) hat foar eigen egen sjoen dat der op in nacht út dat hûs in bigraffenis weikom. Hy hat it my sels forteld. 't Wie fan in jonge, dy wie dêr stoarn. 't Kom krekt sa nei. Durk syn jonge stoar al gau dêrnei en doe hâldden se de bigraffenis dy't myn omke sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26857,"r":"CJ061408","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Klaes Kooistra is walking with other people on the road to Harkema when he urges them to move aside, because the hearse is coming. He is the only one who sees it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Klaes Kooistra yn 'e Harkema stapte mei in ploechje oar jongfolk út 'e Harkema de wei del. Doe sei er ynienen: \"Even oan kant, der komt hwat oan.\" Doe kom der in lykstaesje foarby. Klaes wie de iennige dy't it seach.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26896,"r":"CJ061707","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Bearn van der Woude sometimes sees funeral processions in advance.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":26953,"r":"CJ062105","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Jehannes Koster always cycles to the oil mill where he works. Once he is very late, because he saw a funeral procession coming and stood behind a tree. First he sees four black dogs, followed by people in black. It was a phantom funeral.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw op 'e oaljemoune wurke, dêr hienen se èk in jonge. Dat wie Jehannes Koster. Hy wie koeksnijer, hy snijde de lynkoeken. Hy kom altyd op 'e fyts fan Feankleaster, dan ried er de âld sânwei del. Op in moarn kom er in healûre to let.\nIk sei: \"Hast ûngemakken hawn?\"\n Doe sei er: \"Der kom my in lykstaesje foarby op 'e sânwei. Doe bin 'k achter in beam stean gong.\"\nIk sei: \"Hoe siet dat?\"\nHy sei: \"Der wienen earst fjouwer swarte hounen. Op elke kant fan 'e wei roannen twa. Doe kom de lykstaesje.\nDer wienen manlju by, allegear yn 't swart mei hege huodden op. Ik ha dêr krektsalang stien oant alles foarby wie.\"\nIt wie in skynbigraffenis. It eigenaerdige wie, dat dêr noait in lykstaesje lâns kom op dy sânwei, hwant dêr wennet net in minske oan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26986,"r":"CJ062412","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Mâlle Hindrik, Hiltsje's father, can do ventriloquism, fix people to the ground, see funeral processions, and make rhymes.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"(Hiltsje har heit neamden se 'Mâlle Hindrik'. Hy koe bûksprekke en de minsken steanlitte en hy seach lykstaesjes en hy makke forskate rymstikken en rymkes.)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26993,"r":"CJ062605","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"At night you must always walk at the side of the road and never in the middle, because hearses drive past then, and otherwise you will be thrown off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It koe gebeure dat der nachts lykstaesjes ûnderweis wienen. Dan woarden de minsken dy't se passearden samar fan 'e wei ôfgoaid. Men mat altyd oan 'e kant rinne, noait op 't midden fan 'e wei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27008,"r":"CJ062812","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Some people see funeral processions in advance, and people have sometimes been put aside at night when a funeral procession was coming, or been lifted over it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wennen froeger guon, dy seagen fantofoaren lykstaesjes. Der binne hjir nòch wol guon dy't dat sjogge.\nHjir binne wol guon yn 'e nacht oerside set woarn, as der in lykstaesje oankom en ek wol binne se oer de lykwein hinne tild.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27067,"r":"CJ063403","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman from Haulerwyk tells her son never to walk in the middle of the road in the dark, because a little hearse might come along.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In frou fan Haulerwyk sei tsjin har soan: \"As 't donker is, mast noait midden op 'e wei lâns gean, omdat der in lykstaesje oan komme kin.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27112,"r":"CJ063618","p":"Soesterberg","v":"Utr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"My uncle once tells that he was pushed to the side by a funeral procession. He was born with a caul and sees and knows everything, and at night he gets out of bed to see funeral processions. When he predicts a death, it comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mijn oom - een broer van mijn moeder - was bij mijn moeder in de kost. Die kwam eens op een avond thuis, toen vertelde hij dat hij door een lijkstoet op zijde gezet was.\nMijn oom was met de helm geboren. Hij zag alles en hij wist alles. 's Nachts ging hij uit bed om lijkstaatsies te zien.\nHij zei wel eens: die en die gaat er dood. Dan kwam dat uit."},{"n":27155,"r":"CJ063822","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If you walk in the middle of the road, you can be flung aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Noait midden op 'e wei rinne jouns. Genôch yn 'e Pein, dy't troch in lykstaesje oan kant rêge woarden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27169,"r":"CJ063909","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If you walk in the middle of the road at night, you can be flung aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Rinne jo yn 'e nacht midden op 'e wei, dan kinne jo oan kant reage wurde troch in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27205,"r":"CJ064111","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"From an early age people are warned never to walk in the middle of the road in the evening or at night, because a funeral procession might come. On the Summareweg someone was thrown aside in this way.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der woarde ús al jong werskôge: \"Rin noait midden op 'e wei by joun of by nacht.\" Hwant dan kin men tsjin in lykstaesje oanrinne. Op 'e Sumarrewei is ris ien oan kant reage woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27245,"r":"CJ064318","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You must never walk in the middle of the road at night, because if a funeral procession comes, you will be thrown aside. This once happened in Harkema.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In minske mat nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne. As der in lykstaesje oankomt, wurde jo oan kant reard. Jo matte rûmte jaen. Hjir yn 'e Harkema is dat gauris gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27284,"r":"CJ064503","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Roanes Pander is a farmhand for Wierd's daughter and later marries her. Once, on his way home, he sees a hearse and goes back to Wierd. He is afraid.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer Wierd hie in dochter, dy hie in feint, dat wie Roanes Pander. Hja is letter mei him troud.\nOp in nacht kom er by har wei, hy soe wer nei hûs ta, doe trof er in lykstaesje. Hy woarde sa binaud, dat hy gong werom nei Wierd en dy ta. Hy wie alhiel fan 'e wize.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27285,"r":"CJ064504","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"As Klaes and Simen are walking on the Reitsmaweg, Klaes says they must move aside to give the funeral procession room. Simen, however, does not see it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De Reitsma-wei, dat wie froeger in sânpaed mei diken.\nMyn broer Klaes en Simen (dat wie syn maet) roannen dêr us op in joun lâns. Doe sei Klaes tsjin Simen: \"Oan kant, jonge, rûmte jaen.\" Doe passearde der in lykstaesje.\nKlaes seach it, mar Simen seach it net.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27352,"r":"CJ065109","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two men were out on the road one night. Suddenly one stepped aside. The other fell. He had been knocked down by a hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Piter Scheper fan Luchtenveld en nòch in man roannen us togearre op in nacht oer de wei. Ynienen gong Piter oan kant.\nMar de oare man makke in nuvere gisel.\nDoe't dat gebeurd wie, sei Piter tsjin him: \"Wytst wol hwerst nou by opkom biste?\"\n\"Né\", sei de man.\n\"Dû bist fóár by de lykwein opkom en achter bist der by delknoffele.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27374,"r":"CJ065202","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman sometimes saw funeral processions in the evening. Then she would stand at the side of the road. For if she stayed in the middle, she would be thrown off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem fortelde, hja seach wolris in lykstaesje jouns. Dan gong se oan 'e kant stean om der nei to sjen. Bleau se midden op 'e wei stean, sei se, dan soe se oan kant smiten wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38668,"r":"CJ066202","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Some people see a funeral procession at night; it is a portent of a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon seagen jouns, as se op in paed wienen, in bigraffenisstoet.\nLetter kom dr dan in bigraffenis.","l":"Fries"},{"n":38669,"r":"CJ066203","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You should not walk in the middle of the road, because of a funeral procession that may pass by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In minske mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne fanwege de lykstaesjes.","l":"Fries"},{"n":27490,"r":"CJ066402","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man warned people not to walk in the middle of the road at night, because they might run into a funeral procession. When a dog howls eerily, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Lubbe van Duinen fan 'e Grinzer Pein sei: \"Rin nachts noait midden op 'e wei, hwant dan kinne jo tsjin in lykstaesje oprinne.\"\nIk wyt ek noch dat er ris sei: \"Der hat ek wer in houn sa spûkgûld. Der komt wer in sterfgefal.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38662,"r":"CJ066503","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Someone is born with a caul and can see funeral processions passing. You must not walk in the middle of the road, otherwise you will be flung aside by the funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jan de Wylde wenne yn 'e Rottefalle. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy seach lykstaesjes fan tofoaren.\nSe seinen altyd: noait midden op 'e wei rinne by joun. Jy kinne oars ris troch in lykstaesje oan kant reage wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27523,"r":"CJ066612","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One should not walk in the middle of the road in the evening or at night, or one may be put aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Rin noait midden op 'e wei by joun of by nacht, oars kin men troch in lykstaesje oan kant reage wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27560,"r":"CJ066912","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A boy always had to fetch milk. He was warned not to walk in the wheel ruts on the way, because he might be put aside by a funeral procession. He also had to watch out not to meet the devil.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't wy út Jistrum wei forhuzen, kommen wy oan 'e Burgumer Achterwei to wenjen. Jetse Leegsma wenne dêr ek, dêr moest ik de molke altyd weihelje. Ik moest dan in sânpaed del.\n\"Tink der om,\" sei Jetse tsjin my, \"ik haw in klap hawn fan 'e duvel mei de moalpûde. Tink dêr om,\" sei er, \"noait yn 'e weinspoaren rinne, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje oankomme dyst' net sjochste en dan kinst samar oan kant set wurde.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27576,"r":"CJ067109","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the past people were always warned not to walk in the middle of the road because of the funeral processions that had to pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der waerd froeger altyd sein: Net midden op 'e wei rinne fanwege lykstaesjes dy passeare matte.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27580,"r":"CJ067201","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A married couple were driving their dog cart. A funeral procession passed without their seeing it. They were put aside, cart and all.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Thomas en Clare rieden mei de hounekarre. Doe passearde der in lykstaesje, dy't se net seagen. Sy woarden mei karre en al yn 'e berm set. Doe't de lykstaesje foarby wie koenen se wer fierder.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27648,"r":"CJ067907","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the past people were warned never to walk in the middle of the road, because a funeral procession might come by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der woarde froeger altyd tsjin ús sein: \"Rin noait midden op 'e wei, hwant der kin ris in lykstaesje oankomme.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27682,"r":"CJ068301","p":"Noordwijk","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man was once put aside by a funeral procession. He ended up in the ditch.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Klontjebuurt (dat is oan 'e Boskwei) yn de Pein spoeke it froeger altyd.\nTite Frankes is dêr in kear oan kant set woarn, doe't dêr in lykstaesje lâns kom. Hy wie yn 'e sleat torjochte kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27704,"r":"CJ068501","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man once did not see a funeral procession coming and was thrown to the ground.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Eastemar wenne Durk Boadskip (= D. Brodze = D. v.d. Veen). Dy wie op in joun op 'e Swarte Wei. Doe gebeurde it dat der in lykstaesje oankom sûnder dat er it seach. Doe rekke Durk foar by de lykwein op en achter der wer by del.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27724,"r":"CJ068521","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Someone sometimes had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions. In the past people were warned not to walk in the middle of the road because of the funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw yn 'e Harkema wol ien kend, dy seach lykstaesjes yn 'e nacht. Dan moest hy der út en der hinne om se to sjen.\nWy woarden froeger warskôge: rin noait midden op 'e wei fanwege de lykstaesjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27785,"r":"CJ069104","p":"Franeker","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If a funeral procession comes along at night, you had best turn your back to it. There are things you are better off not seeing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der nachts in lykstaesje oankom, dan wie 't geraden en kear sa'n lykstaesje de rêch ta. Der binne dingen dy kinne jo mar better net sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27818,"r":"CJ069405","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two brothers were walking home along the dike one evening when suddenly they were both flung off the dike. A funeral procession was passing. A few days later their mother died and the funeral procession really did pass by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Njonken ús wennen in man en in frou. Dy hienen twa soannen. Op in joun let wienen se ûnderweis nei hûs ta. Hja roannen op 'e dyk lâns, hwant beneden wie de wei smoarch. 't Wie slim modderich. Doe woarden se ynienen allebeide by de dyk delsmiten.\nIn pear dagen letter forstoar dy jonges har mem. Omdat it paed sa smoarch wie, gongen se mei 't lyk op 'e dyk.\nDe gewoante wie oars altyd, dat se oer 't paed gongen mei 't lyk. It hie in lykstaesje west dêr't de soannen troch fan 'e dyk reage wienen. Deselde lykstaesje - dy fan har mem - wie der nou.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27829,"r":"CJ069416","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A group of women were once on their way back home. At the bend in the road they saw a funeral procession, and then they did not dare go on. They turned back.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In stik of hwat fammen fan Wierum hienen nei Moddergat op bisite west, nei kunde. Yn 'e bocht by de Blauwe Daem spoke it altyd. Doe't de froulju de jouns werom kamen seagen se dêr in lykstaesje. Doe setten se werom op Moddergat ta. Sy doarsten dêr net foarby.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27849,"r":"CJ069801","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman was out on the road one night when she suddenly ended up off the road in the ditch. A funeral procession had passed that she had not seen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In nicht fan myn mem wie op in joun let noch op in paed.\nSy wie sahwat oan it skoallehûs to Moddergat ta, doe woarde se samar ynienen fan 'e wei ôfnaem en yn 'e sleat set. Der hie in lykstaesje west, dy't hja net fornaem hie.\nMem sei altyd: \"Rin by nacht noait midden op 'e wei, gean altyd oan 'e kant lâns.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27896,"r":"CJ070110","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two men were once pushed off the road by a funeral procession one night. One of them ended up in the ditch and drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Boelensloane mat it gebeurd wêze dat der twa man wienen dy't op in nacht in lykstaesje troffen wylst se midden op 'e wei roannen. Se woarden oan kant slingere. De iene kom yn 'e sleat tolânne en is fordronken. De oare hie de kleden wapperjen sjoen. - Mem hat it wol forteld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27998,"r":"CJ071007","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the past people warned against walking in the middle of the road at night. You could be knocked down by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Se seinen froeger algemien: noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant der kin ris in lykstaesje oankomme dy't men net sjocht. Dan wurde jo samar oan kant reage.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28082,"r":"CJ071706","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. She was forced to do so.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Janke moest der nachts altyd út as der in lykstaesje to sjen wie. Dan wie 't net to kearen. Sy woarde twongen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28088,"r":"CJ071712","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A group of men were out on the road one night when one of them warned that they had to move aside. He saw a funeral procession coming. The others saw nothing. He listed everyone he saw walking in the procession. Shortly afterwards someone died, and a week later the procession really walked there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie yn 'e Harkema op in joune, moai let, tsjin 'e nacht oan. Ik wie by in ploechje jongfolk, dêr wie Taeke Postma ek by. Wy wienen op 'e Boskreed, dy't nou forhurde is.\nDoe sei Taeke ynienen: \"Even oan kant, jonges, der komt in lykstaesje oan.\" Wy gongen allegear oan kant wylst dy lykstaesje passearde, mar net ien fan ús, bihalve Taeke, dy't hwat seach.\nTaeke neamde se allegear op dy't der by wienen.\nIn wike dêrnei passearde dêr it lyk fan Durke Willemke, dy wie fuort dêrnei dearekke. Dat wie de lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28089,"r":"CJ071713","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two men were once coming back from a polecat hunt. Suddenly one of them was pushed off his bicycle and ended up in the ditch. A funeral procession was probably passing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear wie 'k mei myn maet to murdzjen. Wy wienen op 'e weromreis, op 'e Bopperein fan it Wytfean. Wy rieden op 'e fyts de bocht om, even foarby Jonge Jan. Ik hie de binnenbocht en fornom neat. Mar myn maet, dy't de bûtenbocht hie, woarde samar fan 'e wei nom. Hy woarde oan kant set, op 'e harsens yn 'e sleat. Letter doarst er dêr noait wer lâns by joun of by nacht. Myn maet wenne, krekt as ik, yn 'e Harkema.\nDer kaem my neat oer. Ik ha se net yn 'e wei roun. (W. v.d. Bos vermoedt, dat er een begrafenisstoet moet zijn geweest, die ze geen van beiden gezien hadden A.A.J.)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28115,"r":"CJ071822","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two men were once on the road when one warned the other to step aside. A funeral procession was coming. Not long after, a girl living on that road died, and the funeral procession really did pass by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit sei, hy kom ris in kear fan Nes op in joun. Der wie in oare man by him, dy moast nei Wierum ta. Doe hie dy man ynienen tsjin heit sein: \"Jo moatte oan kant gean.\"\nHeit gong oan kant. Even letter sei er: \"'t Is foarby, kom mar wer op 'e wei.\"\nDy man woe net sizze hwa't it wie dy't stoarn wie.\nOp in pleats tichte by it plak dêr't se oan kant gien wienen stoar even letter in dochter. Doe kaem dêr in lykstaesje lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28203,"r":"CJ072710","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days people were warned not to walk in the middle of the road at night. Otherwise they could be pushed aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der woarde froeger altyd sein: Rin by nacht noait midden op 'e wei. Der kin wolris in lykstaesje oankomme, dy't dy oan kant reaget.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28223,"r":"CJ072905","p":"Kornhorn","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days people were warned not to walk in the middle of the road. Otherwise the old fellow would grab them. Then you were thrown from one place to another. It could also happen that you were pushed aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Se seiden froeger teugen ons, wij moesten noait midden op de weg loopn. De olle fent was dan op de weg en dan pakte die je. Je werd dan fan 't ene plak noar 't andere goaid.\nGerrit Bosje is 't overkoomn. Die liep van Noordwyk noar Marum. Doar pakte de olle fent 'm. Moar Gerrit Bosje was in roaren, dy was foak dronken.\nAs je midden op de weg liep kon 't ook gebeuren dat der een lijkstaasje oan kwam. Dan werd je oan kant gezet. \nMijn volk zei, dat was een domineeszoon in Noordwijk eens overkomen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28290,"r":"CJ073312","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A boy once could not get out past his gate, because lots of men in black were walking by. It was probably a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't myn âldste soan Wopke op in joun ta 't hûs út gong, woarde er by de homeije keard. 't Wienen allegear swarte keardels, sei er, hy koe der net troch. Hy soe fuort, mar doe is er wer ta de hûs yn gong.\nNei alle gedachten hat dat in lykstaesje west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28313,"r":"CJ073702","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One night a man saw a funeral procession go by. A week later someone really was buried.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining seach op in kear in lykstaesje midden yn 'e nacht fan 'e kapper (oan 'e Spekloane) ôf oan Hindrik de Haan ta (oan 'e Houtigehaechsterwei). In wike letter wie dêr in èchte bigraffenis.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28322,"r":"CJ073803","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One night a man could not walk on because a funeral procession was passing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Kij de Vries fan 'e Boelensloane wie us op in snein nei syn faem Anne ta west, dy wenne yn Beets. Let yn 'e nacht kom er werom. Doe't er yn 'e Rottefalle wie, woarde er dêr in lykstaesje gewaer. Sy hâldden him dêr beet, mar hy koe net sjen hwa. Hy koe foar - noch achterút.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28331,"r":"CJ073907","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A boy was once on his way to his girlfriend when he was pushed aside by a funeral procession. Later his girlfriend's grandmother died; he lived in her house. It was her funeral procession he had seen pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In broer fan my soe ris op in kear nei de faem ta. Dy wenne yn 'e Bûtenpostumer mieden. Doe't er by 't brechje kom, dêr't er oer moest, flak by 't hûs dêr't syn faem wenne, wie dêr in lykstaesje. Myn broer woarde oan kant set, hwant dy lykstaesje moest by him lâns.\nIn pear wiken letter stoar de beppe fan syn faem, dy't by har ynwenne. Dêr hie myn broer de lykstaesje fan sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28355,"r":"CJ074113","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two men in a carriage once did not see a funeral procession coming. The horse did, and kept trying to go to the side. Then they were suddenly driven onto the verge and off the dike.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hindrik de Groot fan Nijskoat reizge om 'e fjirtsjin dagen nei de froulju ta. Op in joun soed er wer nei de faem ta.\nUnderweis kom der him in boer achterop, dy siet yn 'e tilbry. Dy boer sei: \"Wolle jo ek mei ride?\"\nDoe wie dêr in lykstaesje oankom. Síj hienen 't net sjoen, mar 't hynder wòl. Dat woe mar oan kant. Ynynen skeaten se mei 't hynder yn 'e barm en rekken se fan 'e dyk ôf.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28387,"r":"CJ074221","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman was once pushed off the road by a funeral procession. There was a rather sick boy, but she made sure he got better.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde frou Reitsma fortelde ek noch, op in kear wie se op 'e fyts nei har dochter ta, dy't yn Rinsumageast wennet.\nDoe't se dêr oankaem hie se sein: \"Nou ha 'k ûnderweis in lykstaesje sjoen. Ik woarde fan 'e wei ôfdrukt.\"\nHja fortelde oan har skoandochter Roas: in eintsje fan har ôf wenne in jonge, dy wie hiel bot siik. De minsken seinen, hy koe net wer opknappe.\nMar hy is àl wer better woarn. Dat hie har wurk west.\nHja hie dy jonge it leven ret. (Hja fortelde der net by, hoe)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28436,"r":"CJ074708","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One evening two men were pushed off the road. They had seen nothing, but a funeral procession had probably passed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tusken de Falom en de Breedte roannen us in kear twa feinten. It wienen Wiberen van der Weide en Sjoerd Visser. Sy kommen fan Moarmwâld en de Broek. 't Wie op in joun. Sy woarden samar ûnforwacht fan 'e wei ôfset en kommen yn 'e berm to stean. Der mat in lykstaesje west ha, mar sy hienen neat sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28482,"r":"CJ075312","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"An uncle of mine is walking through Terwispel with a mate when he suddenly says they must step aside, because a funeral procession is coming. His mate, however, stays in the middle of the path and is then lifted up and set down further on.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In omke fan myn frou wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy roan ris op in joun troch Terwispel, doe hied er ergens hinne west. Hy hie in maet by him.\nDoe sei er ynienen tsjin syn maet: \"Mast even oan kant, dêr komt in lykstaesje oan.\"\nMar syn maet woe net oan kant, dy bleau midden op it paed.\nDoe is er opnom woarn en in hiel ein fierder wel delset.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28497,"r":"CJ075602","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"At night in the woods at Harkema, Praamsma sees a funeral procession and becomes frightened. A little later old Melle Dieuwke in Bosk dies. He had seen this in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde ris op in kear yn 'e nacht, doe kom in sekere Praamsma by de faem wei. Hy kom troch de Bosk yn 'e Harkema.\nDoe krige er dêr in lykstaesje to sjen. Hy wie sa binaud woarn, dat, doe't er letter thús kom, wied er by syn mem op bêd sprong.\nEven letter kom âlde Melle Dieuwke yn 'e Bosk to forstjerren. Dêr hie hy de lykstaesje fan sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28499,"r":"CJ075604","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"On the Rijkslaan a group of young people is simply pushed aside and a funeral procession passes. People also sometimes stumble when one comes by, or are set on the front of the hearse and thrown off again at the back.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Ryksloane (= betonwei) fan 'e Harkema wie ris in keppeltsje jongfolk op in joun. Dy woarden allegear samar oerside set.\nDoe kom der in lykstaesje lâns. Guon seagen hwa't der by wienen, dy koenen de minsken fan dy lykstaesje.\n't Is ek wol gebeurd dat se stroffelen as der in lykstaesje passearde.\n't Is hjir yn 'e Harkema ek in kear gebeurd, dat in man by nacht samar foar op in lykwein set woarde en der achter wer by delsmiten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28596,"r":"CJ076501","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One evening, as father walks along a narrow path on his way to the shop in Smoorhoek, he suddenly sees a coffin in front of him, but he cannot see who is in it and the coffin quickly disappears. On the way back there is nothing to be seen. Two weeks later a dead person's coffin stands in the same spot. The hearse cannot get along the narrow path, so they carry the coffin. At the very spot where father saw the coffin earlier, they now stop to rest. It was a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It sil sa'n lytse tachtich jier lyn wêze, doe wie heit noch mar krekt troud. Doe moest er op in joun nei in winkeltsje ta yn 'e Smoarhoeke hjir, in smel paedtsje lâns.\nDoe seach er ynienen in kiste foar him. Hy wie net bang en tocht: ik wol wite hwa't dêr yn leit.\nHy bûgde him foaroer om to sjen, doe wie dy kiste samar ynienen fuort. Heit roan fierder, nei de winkel. Doe't er werom kom, itselde plak lâns, wie dêr neat.\nIn fjirtsjin dagen letter moest de kiste op itselde plak stean dêr't heit him sjoen hie. Der wie ien stoarn; it paedtsje wie sa smel, dat der koe net in lykwein lâns. Doe sjouden se de kiste mei 't lyk der yn. Underweis rêstten se even; - sy wienen warch - en doe setten se de kiste even del, krekt op it plak, dêr't heit it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28603,"r":"CJ076508","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Van der Wal is walking along the Turflaan at night when a funeral procession comes and he is pushed aside. Afterwards he tells everyone never again to walk in the middle of the road in the evening.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Turfloane tusken Readskuorre en Stiensgea roan ris in sekere Van der Wal. 't Wie yn 'e nacht. Doe kom der in lykstaesje oan en hy woarde oan kant set. Hy kom yn 'e barm torjochte. Letter sei er tsjin ús: \"Jimme matte noait midden op 'e wei rinne by jountiid.\" (Dat hie hy àl dien)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28701,"r":"CJ078101","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman often sees a small funeral procession and is then lifted up and set aside. She herself has lost two husbands and five children as well.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw in frou kend, dy seach wit hoe faek in lykstaesje. Dan woarde se optild en oan kant set. Hja libbet noch en wennet yn 'e Westerein. Hja hat twa kear de man forlern en noch fiif bern.","l":""},{"n":28760,"r":"CJ078701","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People go to work on the Groningen clay and walk home along the railway, among them mother-in-law, who sees two men in black walking. She does not see her nephew Piter. Finally she sees the men turn into a funeral procession. She quickly runs away.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Se gongen froeger hjirwei in bulte nei de Grinzer klaei ta to arbeidzjen. Op in kear hie skoanmem ek mei west dêr hinne. Sy kommen op in joun let werom. 't Wie in hiel ein rinnen. Sy roannen op 't spoar, dat wie 't koartste.\nDat gong rjocht op 'e Westerein oan.\nDoe't se omtrint oan 'e Westerein ta wienen, doe seach skoanmem twa mannen yn 't swart rinnen, mei hiele greate swarte hege huodden op. Sy wienen sels sahwat mei har seizen en sy seagen dy beide mannen allegear, op ien nei.\nDat wie Piter, in neef fan skoanmem. Dy seach neat, sei er.\nDoe sei skoanmem: \"O heare, nou ha se ús sakrekt krige, en nou krije se ús wer. (hja hienen in skoftsje lyn boete krigen, omdat se op 't spoar roannen. Dat mocht net, mem seach dy twa mannen foar plysjes oan) Sy wie binaud, hwant boete mocht har net barre.\nSy gongen by de neiste reed fan 't spoar ôf. Doe koenen se by 't spoar lâns rinne, net op it spoar. De beide mannen hâldden se hyltyd yn 't sicht. Dy mannen biweegden har op it grint en dat kraste en knerpte altyd tige as dêr ien oer roan, mar dy mannen koene se net stappen hearre.\nSy sweefden. Hja hâldden it eech der op. Op 't lêst wie 't in hiele lykstaesje woarn. De regenkleden hienen de froulju mei gewelt om 'e holle wappere, dat hie skoan to hearren west.\nSkoanmem en dy binne fan binaudens útnaeid, hwant it wie midden yn 'e nacht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28797,"r":"CJ079002","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Taeke Postma was born with a caul and dies young. One night a funeral procession passes him and he steps aside. The next day he predicts a death. It comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Taeke Postma is jong stoarn. Hy wenne èk yn 'e Bosk. Hy wie mei in helm geboaren. Op in nacht, doe kom der him in bigraffenisstoet tomjitte. Doe gong er gau oerside. Hy sei de oare moarns: \"Hjir stjert yn 't koart ien, ik ha de bigraffenis sjoen.\" Dat is doe sekuer nei kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28824,"r":"CJ079112","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Teake was born with a caul and also saw Martens Wip's funeral procession in advance when it came towards him one evening. He can only say how many people there are, but not who.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer Teake, dy't mei de helm geboaren wie, hat ek de lykstaesje sjoen fan âlde Martens Wip. Dy lykstaesje kom him op in joun tomjitte. Hy koe krekt sizze hoefolle minsken der achter de kiste oan roannen. Hokker minsken wist er net.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28837,"r":"CJ079209","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"When people walk past the churchyard in the evening, it sometimes happens that they are pushed aside because a funeral procession has to pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is hjir gebeurd dat der op in joun by tsjuster guon lâns it tsjerkhôf gongen. Dy woarden fan 'e iene kant nei de oare smiten. Dat kom fanwege in lykstaesje. Dêr moesten se rûmte foar jaen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29341,"r":"CJ080616","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Near a churchyard people sometimes ended up in the water. Then they had not seen that a funeral procession was passing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 'e betonwei yn 'e Harkema ha jy it âld tsjerkhôf. It earme-tsjerkhôf wurdt it neamd. Dêr wurdt al lang net mear bigroeven. Foar 't tsjerkhôf oer stie froeger in pleatske.\nDêr hat Taeke v.d. Veen op wenne. Soms koenen se dêr net mei de wein troch de hekken komme. Se waerden dêr dan samar weismiten yn 'e tsjerkhôfsleat. Dat gebeurde dan yn 'e nacht. Dat trof dan krekt sa dat der in lykstaesje lâns kaem, dy't se net seagen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29361,"r":"CJ080715","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days people warned never to walk in the middle of the road at night. Otherwise you could run into a funeral procession.\nA woman was often outside at night. She was born with a caul.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy mochten froeger noait midden op 'e wei rinne. Alde frou Wobbes (Janke Hollander) sei: Dy't jouns midden op 'e wei rint hat de kâns dat er foar by de lykwein op rint en der achter wer by del falt.\nJanke wie nachts altyd op 'e lappen. As wy fan in feestje werom kommen yn 't holst fan 'e nacht, siet hja altyd as in roungear protsje by de hage. 't Wie ús buorfrou. Sy wie mei de helm geboaren, seinen se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29364,"r":"CJ080802","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days people were sometimes pushed off the road. Then there was a funeral they did not see.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Soms waerden der yn 'e Harkema minsken fan 'e wei ôflutsen. Dan wie der in bigraffenis dy't se net seagen. It is ris gebeurd mei ien op it plak dêr't âlde Hindrik Pitstra wennet.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29383,"r":"CJ081002","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two men were once coming from the market when the dogs would no longer pull the cart. The men quickly moved aside, and the cart was simply thrown off the road. A funeral procession was passing without them seeing it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Twa man fan 'e Boelensloane hienen mei de karre mei hinnen nei Ljouwert ta west. Dy hinnen hienen se op 'e merk to jilde makke - 't wie op in freed - en se hienen der wer smoar foar kocht. Dat kochten se op 'e merk. De oare deis - saterdei - soenen se it togearre útsutelje.\nDoe't de beiden ûnderweis wienen fornommen se dat der hwat oan komme moest, hwant de hountsjes, dy't foar de karre roannen, doarsten ynienen net fierder. De iene sei tsjin 'e oare: - Der is hwat - Mar sy koenen neat sjen. Sy wienen gau oan kant gong, mar de karre lieten se stean. Doe wie de karre sa mar fan 'e wei smiten woarn. Der wie in lykstaesje passeard, dy't se net sjoen hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29385,"r":"CJ081004","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days people were warned never to walk in the middle of the road at night, because they might be pushed aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der woarde ús as bern al yndruid: tink der om, rin nachts noait op 't midden fan in paed, mar altyd op 'e kant.\nHwant oars kinne jim oan kant reage wurde troch in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29413,"r":"CJ081303","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days people warned not to walk in the middle of the road at night. For if a funeral procession happened to pass, you were pushed off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Skoanmem sei: \"By joun matte jimme noait midden op 'e wei rinne.\" Hja wie sels al ris fan 'e wei ôfset en doe wie se yn 'e sleat tolânne kom. Doe hie der in lykstaesje passeard, dy't se net sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32643,"r":"CJ082105","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman often has to get up at night to foresee deaths in passing funeral processions. If the caul of someone born with a caul is burned straight away, that person is not troubled by visions of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Jan Doedel (= Mulder) syn frou wenne yn Nyegea. Dy moest der nachts ek altyd ôf om lykstaesjes to sjen. Dy wist altyd fan tofoaren as der ien stjerre soe.\nAs se de helm fuort opbrânne hoeve se it net to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32649,"r":"CJ082111","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You should never walk in the middle of the road at night, because you can be driven to the side by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In minske mat nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne.\nOp 'e Hearrewei is 't ris in kear gebeurd, dat dêr in rydtúch samar oan kant set woarde. Dat moest rúmte jaen foar in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32664,"r":"CJ082305","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man urges a man on a wagon to make way for a funeral procession. But the man on the wagon cannot see the procession. It is a vision foreshadowing a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn frou har pake ried ris op 'e bargewein nei Ljouwert ta yn 'e iere moarn. 't Wie op in freed en 't wie noch tsjuster. Doe frege der ûnderweis ien oft er mei ride mocht en dy kom njonken him to sitten op 'e wein.\nDoe't se in eintsje riden hienen sei dyselde: \"Wy matte even oan kant gean, hwant der komt in lykstaesje oan.\" Pake wie oan kant gien, mar hy hie neat sjoen.\nDat is nou wol 140 jier lyn doe't dat gebeurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32665,"r":"CJ082306","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days people warned never to walk in the middle of the road. If you did, you could be struck by a passing funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger seinen se: \"Tink der om, rin noait midden oer 't paed, hwant dan kin 't wolris gebeure datst tsjin in lykstaesje oanrinste.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32726,"r":"CJ083002","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman sees a funeral pass by very clearly. She knows the people walking in the procession. It is a vision of the future: shortly afterwards someone dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Skoanmem wenne yn 'e buert fan Beerta yn Grinslân. Op in joun seach hja dúdlik in bigraffenis. Hja koe de minsken, dy't achter it lyk oanroannen. In dei of hwat letter wie de èchte bigraffenis der. It kloppe allegear krekt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32710,"r":"CJ082906","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A person born with a caul often foresees deaths in passing funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Meine Boetes fan Stiensgea wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy seach faek lykstaesjes fan minsken dy't letter pas stoaren.\nIk wyt noch dat er op in moarn bitiid wer ris in lykstaesje seach op 'e wei. Dat hat er doe forteld. In dei of hwat letter koe elkenien dyselde stoet sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32773,"r":"CJ083402","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If you walk in the middle of the road in the evening, you can be driven aside by a passing funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy mochten fan ús âlden jouns noait midden op 'e wei lâns rinne. Dat dienen wy ek noait, hwant dan koe 't samar gebeure dat wy tsjin in lykstaesje oprounen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32774,"r":"CJ083403","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A person born with a caul keeps foreseeing deaths in passing funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Iense Boomsma wenne hjir op 'e Boelensloane. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren, seinen se. Hy moest alle lykstaesjes sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32787,"r":"CJ083503","p":"Dokkum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"An old woman urges someone else to make way for a funeral procession. It is a vision of the future: a few days later a real funeral passes.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger woonde hier in oude frou, dy sei us tegen een: \"Dû moest aan de kant gaan, der komt een lykstaasje an.\"\nIn pear dagen letter gong dêr echt in lykstaesje lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32819,"r":"CJ084101","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman predicts that things will go badly for the narrator's brother because she has seen a funeral procession pass his house. The prediction comes true: the brother dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Janke Koaning (= Kootstra) wie ús buorfrou. Op in kear sei se tsjin mem - doe wennen wy noch yn 'e Harkema -:\n\"It komt net goed mei jimme Minne (Minne wie myn broer), hwant ik haw in lykstaesje by jimme sjoen.\"\nHja krige gelyk, ús Minne kom to forstjerren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32820,"r":"CJ084102","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman born with a caul often has to get up at night to foresee deaths in passing funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't wy letter yn 'e Houtigehage wennen kom âlde Janke sa nou en dan wol ris út 'e Harkema by ús. Sa hâldden wy omgong mei inoar. As se dan by ús útfanhûze moest se der nachts wolris ôf. Dan moest se hwat sjen, hwant sy wie mei de helm geboaren. Op in kear, doe seach se by ús op it hiem in lykstaesje. Wy wienen doe noch bern. Mar de èchte lykstaesje hat der oan diz tiid ta noch net west by myn witen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32916,"r":"CJ084804","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man once saw a funeral. He named all the people he saw walking behind the coffin, but he could not say who lay in the coffin. Two weeks later he himself was dead; he had seen his own funeral.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn beppe fortelde, dat der hie in man yn Sumar wenne dy seach in bigraffenis. Dat hat west yn 1897. Hy neamde mar op en hy neamde mar op dy't achter it lyk oanroannen, hy koe se allegear by namme. Mar hy wist net hwa't der yn 'e kiste lei. In fjirtsjin dagen letter hied er sels dea west. 't Wie syn eigen bigraffenis, dy't er sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33034,"r":"CJ086101","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman once saw a funeral pass by. A week later the funeral really took place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde tante Dike, dat wie de frou fan Jan Mulder, dy seach op in nacht yn Nyegea in bigraffenis foarbygean. In wike letter wie dy bigraffenis dêr.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33060,"r":"CJ086403","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man told his sons he had seen a funeral procession and that he feared their mother would die soon. Not long after, he himself died; it was his own funeral procession he had seen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear wie heit mei myn beide bruorren oan 't wurk yn Surhústerfean. Myn broer Jehannes wie der èk by. Dy is nou 80 en wennet yn Drachten, de oare leeft net mear.\nDer kom in nij tsjerkhôf op 't Fean, se wienen mei in sleat oan 't slatten. De modder woarde op 't tsjerkhôf brocht.\n\"Hwa't der ris yn dit kroadfol komt?\" sa redenearren se.\nDoe sei heit op in stuit: \"Ik ha fannacht droomd.\"\n\"Ja?\" seinen myn bruorren.\n\"Ja\", sei heit, en hy suchte. \"Ik bin bang dat wy jimme mem misse matte. Ik ha fannacht in lykstaesje sjoen by ús op it hiem.\"\nFuort letter wie heit sels dea (op 'e Poffert). Hy hie syn eigen lykstaesje sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33073,"r":"CJ086501","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One night a man saw a funeral procession approaching, but he kept walking in the middle of the road. Then he was driven aside and ended up on the verge.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn swager wie in ûnforskillich man. Hy wenne yn 'e Westerein. Doe seach er op in nacht in lykstaesje oankommen. Mei opset bleau er midden op 'e wei rinnen. Dêr wie him leard: rin yn 'e nacht noait midden op 'e wei. Mar hy gong net oan kant. Doe woarde hy oan kant treaun. Yn 'e berm kom er tolanne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34446,"r":"CJ086604","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man was born with a caul. He often saw funeral processions. A few days later there was always a funeral.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Boardzer Bruining (_) fan 'e Boelensloane seach lykstaesjes en dan duorre it mar even, dan wie der yn werkelikheit in bigraffenis. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33135,"r":"CJ087310","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. Because of this he always knew when another funeral was coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wenne in man yn 'e Westerein, dy moest der nachts faek út. Dan woarde er kloppe, sei er, dan wie der in lykstaesje ergens to sjen. Sa'n lykstaesje moest hy sjen. Hy koe altyd foarút sizze hwer't in bigraffenis kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33158,"r":"CJ087504","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man always saw funeral processions. He would always say whom he had not seen among them. That person was always dead a few days later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Rottefalle wenne in man, dy seach altyd de lykstaesjes. Dan sei er: Dêr en dêr ha 'k it sjoen, mar dy of dy wie der net by. Dan wie 't altyd dyselde dy't der net by wie, dy't stoarn wie (stjerre soe).","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33171,"r":"CJ087604","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman once saw a funeral procession at a house. Not long after, a little boy died in that house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By 't selde hûs hat ús mem ris op in kear in lykstaesje sjoen. Hja stie op 'e reed op in simmerjoun. 't Wie noch ljochtskyndei. Doe seach se de bigraffenisminsken bûtendoar op it hiem fan har hûs. Hja koe net ûnderskiede hwa't it wienen, dêrfoar wie se der to fier ôf.\nIn skoft letter stoar it jonkje. Doe wie dêr de bigraffenis dy't hja sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33203,"r":"CJ087803","p":"Dokkum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman was born with a caul. At night she often had to get up to see funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Ritske Vellinga fan Ikkerwâld wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy seach altyd lykstaesjes fan tofoaren. Der wienen trouwens wol mear dy't wolris in bigraffenis fan tofoaren seagen. Mar Ritske seach se altyd, dy moest se sjen. Nachts moest hy der foar út bêd wei. Dan seach er al de gesichten fan 'e minsken dy't achter 't lyk oan roannen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33266,"r":"CJ088217","p":"Schagerbrug","v":"N.-H.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"At night one should not walk in the wheel ruts of the road, or else one might run into a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Wienen hjir op Sumarreheide froeger allegear sânpaden mei weinspoaren. By nacht mochten wy noait yn sa'n weinspoar lâns rinne. Oars koenen jy tsjin in lykstaesje oanrinne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33286,"r":"CJ088404","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One night a young man was pushed to the side by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw in kammeraet, dy hyt fan Fokke. Dy wennet hjir ek yn 'e Harkema. Dy syn suster hie forkearing. Dy har feint kom op in nacht by harren wei. Hy moest earst in eintsje sânpaed del. Mei't er op 'e wei fytse soe, komt er werom, hwant hy hie dúdlik in bigraffenis sjoen. Dat wie op Homeare. Dy feint woarde troch dy lykstaesje tobekdrukt. Hy koe der bislist net lâns. Fokke hat it my wol faek forteld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33289,"r":"CJ088407","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Older people in Harkema still do not walk in the middle of the road, because they fear they might otherwise run into a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De âlden fan 'e Harkema rinne hjoed-de-dei noch altyd net midden op 'e wei omdat se fêst miene dat se dan de kâns ha tsjin in lykstaesje op to rinnen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33300,"r":"CJ088418","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man was once driven to the side of the road by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Sibe van der Veen fan 'e Harkema is ris op in kear tsjin in lykstaesje oanroan. Doe woarde hy oan kant set.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34638,"r":"CJ094204","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In Oostermeer a man tells another, who was born with a caul, that he must step aside because a funeral procession is coming. And Willem Mulder's grandmother was also born with a caul, and she has to see everything.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wienen yn Eastemar ris twa man op in joune let noch op in paed. De iene sei tsjin 'e oare: \"Dû mast fan 'e wei gean, der komt in lykstaesje oan.\"\nDyselde wie mei de helm geboaren.\nWillem Mulder syn beppe, âlde Frytsen, wie ek mei de helm geboaren, dy moest alles sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12970,"r":"YPFOE125f","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A grandfather and grandmother see a funeral procession with five men, three women and two people wearing top hats. Grandmother says the procession is crossing the road diagonally. Grandfather does not believe it, but a year later they see exactly the same procession crossing the road diagonally.","i":"Y.P.","o":"Lykstaasjes\nMyn pake en beppe, âlde Alle Bijma en Fokje, wennen yn 'e Harkema. Op in kear stienen se efter 't hûs te praten mei Kees Arjens. Ynienen sei beppe: 'Sjoch, dêr komt in Iykstaasje oan! Sjoch, twa mei hege huodden op—fiif manlju en trije froulju'. Se wienen al oan 't Skeanpaad ta, doe sei se: 'Hea, dêr gean se skeanoer!' 'Dat kin net', sei pake. Mar Kees Arjens ornearre: 'Och, dat wit men net, Alle'.\nMar in jier letter dêr stoar har buorman. In dominy fan 't Surhústerfean hie de foargong, dy hie 't wol wat yn 'e holle en ús pake en Kees Arjens moasten tafeltsjinje. Doe wienen se oan 't Skeanpaad ta en doe sei dominy: 'Laat het lijk de weg maar om passeren, wij lope schuins over'. Doe sei Kees Arjens tsjin ús âlde pake: 'Sjochst no wol, Alle! Dêr giet it hinne'. It kaam krekt sa nei as beppe it sein hie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":12971,"r":"YPFOE125g","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A clairvoyant woman is home alone because her husband is travelling. Two men with moustaches come in carrying a small coffin. They put the coffin on the table and then under the clock. Both men suddenly vanish, and so does the coffin. The woman predicts that their little daughter will not live much longer. A few years later the girl does indeed die.","i":"Y.P.","o":"Lykstaasjes\nDyselde beppe hat it hân, doe wie pake fuort en doe hearde se de doar en dêr kamen twa mannen yn mei dikke snorren en dy hienen in deafetsje by harren— beppe sei net fan kistje, mar fan deafetsje. Dat setten se op in ein fan 'e tafel del, mar dêr krigen se it ek wer wei en setten it ûnder de klok. En dy beide mannen wienen sa mar wer fuort. Se soe nei 't deakistje ta, mar dat wie ek fuort.\nSe hienen in famke. Doe't pake wer thús wie, sei se: 'Alle, wy meitsje mar gjin klean klear, want wy behâlde dit famke net'. En in jier letter ferlearen se it famke. In wipke, sei se.","l":"Fries"},{"n":34498,"r":"CJ090712","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days people were warned not to walk in the middle of the road, or they might be driven aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy mochten froeger noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant dan koenen wy samar oan kant reage wurde troch in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33522,"r":"CJ090906","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One evening a married couple saw a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in joun soenen heit en mem to praten nei 'de laatste Stuver'. Heit hie de hountsjes meinom. Dat die er altyd as er jouns to praten gong. Hwant der koe ris in murd wêze ûnderweis. (Hy die neat leaver as murdejeije.) Doe gebeurde it dat de beide hountsjes mei de sturt tusken de poaten by heit kamen. Heit en mem tochten: hwat sil dit bitsjutte.\nDoe seagen se in boerewein. Mei in kiste der op en in man of acht yn 't swart der achteroan. Ek ien foar. Dy droech in lange sluijer. 't Wie in lykstaesje yn 'e nacht.\nDe hountsjes hienen dat it earst fornaem. 't Wie op in lykpaed by 'de laatste Stuver'. Dat paed hyt noch it lykpaed. \"Mast my mar beethâlde,\" sei heit tsjin mem, \"der komt dy neat fan oer.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33523,"r":"CJ090907","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One should never walk in the middle of the road at night, or else one may be driven to the side by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant dan kin men wolris oan kant reage wurde troch in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33525,"r":"CJ090909","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One night two men saw a funeral procession pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear wie heit mei noch ien yn 'e nacht oan 't murdejeijen tichte by 't tsjerkje fan Lytsewâld. Dy't by heit wie wie in Veenstra. Heit en hy gongen troch 't fjild mei de hountsjes. Doe seagen se dat der in lykstaesje fan 'e Goudberg kom. Dy passearre har en gong nei 't tsjerkje fan Lytsewâld. Se gongen oer de Stuver.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33576,"r":"CJ091216","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One should not walk in the middle of the road at night, or one may run into a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In minske mat nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne, dan kin er wolris by in lykwein oprinne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33621,"r":"CJ091703","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman was thrown off a path three times in a row. She understood that a funeral procession she could not see was passing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us beppe dy't yn 'e Harkema wenne gong jouns altyd itselde paedtsje del om molke to heljen.\nOp in joun gong se dêr wer lâns. Mar doe woarde se ynienen samar fan 't paedtsje ôfset. En sy seach neat. In skoftsje letter gong se wer it paedtsje del. Mar doe woarde se nochris wer oan kant set, sûnder dat se hwat seach. Foar de trêdde kear gong se oer 't paedtsje. Mar doe woarde se der ôfsmiten. 't Ammerke stoude in ein fuort. Doe tocht se: \"Nou gean 'k der net wer lâns.\" Hja hie wol yn 'e gaten dat der in lykstaesje passearde. Mar sy hat him noait sjoen. 't Gebeurde op 'e Bulten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34517,"r":"CJ091905","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One evening a man was driven off the narrow road into the little ditch three times. Later it turned out that the woman in the nearby shack had died. The next day she was taken away in a coffin. The man had probably been pushed off the road by her funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir dwarsoer hat in hutte stien, dat wie net mear as in foech keet. Dêr wenne in âld minske yn. Dat âld-minske kom to forstjerren. Dêr koe net in wein op 't hiem komme, hwant der roan allinne mar in smel fuotpaedtsje nei de dwarsreed ta. Doe moest de kiste fan 'e hoeke nei dy keet ta droegen wurde.\nUs buorman passearde de jouns fan tofoaren, doe wie 't minske dus al dea, mar sy lei noch yn 't bedsté.\nDoe woarde er oan trije kear ta yn 'e sleat set. Doe't it de earste kear gebeurde, sei er: \"Heden, heden, hwat is dit raer. Hwerom wurd ik yn 'e sleat set?\" Hwant hy hie neat sjoen.\nDe oare moarns fortelde er it ús folk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33675,"r":"CJ092607","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days some people saw funeral processions in advance. If one did not step aside quickly, one was flung off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wienen guon dy seagen soms lykstaesjes foarút. Sy moesten sjen dat se oan kant kommen, oars woarden se fan 'e wei ôf smiten. Ik haw ien kend, dat wie in sekere Sytse Jager út 'e Harkema, dy wie op in nacht to murdejeijen, doe kom der in lykstaesje oan, Sytse woarde opnom en samar oer 't lyk hinne smiten. Hy hat it my sels forteld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33677,"r":"CJ092609","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"At night one should not walk in the middle of the road; one must make room for the funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat noait midden op 'e wei lâns rinne by nacht. Dat wurdt nòch altyd sein. Men mat rûmte jaen oan 'e lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34546,"r":"CJ092804","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man had seen a coffin and so knew that someone in his household would soon die. Not long afterwards an old lady who lodged with them died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie yn 'e tiid, doe wie ús mem yn forwachting fan my. Doe krigen se op in kear praters, dat wienen Jan de Haan en syn frou. Dy lju hienen in greate húshâlding en Jan syn mem wenne by harren yn. Dat wie in âld minske. It wie âlde Iebeltsje. Dat âld minske woe by mem en dy wenje. Doe nom heit har mei hjirhinne.\n't Ald-minske wie smoarch en sy siet ûnder 't ûngemak. Mem moest har hielendal reinigje. Doe't dat gebeurd wie gûlde se fan blidens.\nMar doe woarde dat âld-minske siik en bêdlegerich. Mem hie 't der drok mei. Doe sei mem tsjin heit: \"Dû hast my hwat op 'e hals helle mei dat âld-minske hjir hinne to bringen.\"\n\"Och fanke,\" sei heit, \"'t is in gelok datst har hjir hast, hwant hja stjert direkt. It is al in skoft lyn dat ik har kiste sjoen ha; in greate kiste.\"\n\"Hwerom hast dat net earder sein?\" sei mem.\n\"Ja fanke,\" sei heit, \"dat doarst ik eins net dwaen om dy. Dû bist yn forwachting en ik wie bang datste tinke soest dat de poppe dystû draechste dea gean soe. Dêrom hâldde ik my stil.\"\nAlde Iebeltsje is ridlik-gau dêrnei stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33704,"r":"CJ093009","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People were sometimes suddenly put to the side of the road. Then a funeral procession was passing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde wol dat lju yn 'e nacht samar oan kant set woarden. Dan passearde der in lykstaesje, waerd der sein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34557,"r":"CJ093202","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A maid once saw a funeral procession pass by. She saw the cloth over the coffin blow up. A week later someone died. Then she saw the same funeral procession really pass by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde ris in kear dat in jongfaem de Lange Reed delgong om molke to heljen. Hja hat it my sels forteld. \"O heden,\" sei se, \"doe trof ik dêr in wein mei in kiste der op. In eintsje fierder waeide it kleed yn 'e hichte. En wer in eintsje fierder stie deselde wein stil.\"\nDêr stoar in wike letter in âld frou. It is doe presys sa gebeurd lyk as dy faem it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34562,"r":"CJ093207","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman had seen a funeral procession at a house. A week later the man of the house died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By ús woarde it hûs fortimmere. Wy hienen in greate húshâlding, der wienen 9 bern en mem forwachte it tsiende. Doe kom der in frou by ús op bisite. 't Wie âlde Auke Tryn. Dy biseach alles fan de fortimmerderije.\nDoe't se thúskom, sei se tsjin har man: \"Och och, 't wie dêr allegear folk yn 'e hûs/yn 't achterhûs en om 'e doar. Sil ik dy ris hwat sizze?\nHet huis groot,\nmaar/en de man dood.\"\nHja hie dêr by uzes in lykstaesje sjoen.\nHeit forûngelokke in wike letter.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34572,"r":"CJ093217","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man was suddenly thrown over a hedge for no reason. He had been pushed aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in lykstaesje oankom waerd ien samar oan kant set. It is Sake Bottema oerkaem. Op it plak, dêr't nou de bioscoop stiet - (dêr krekt achter) waerd er samar oer de hage hinne smiten. Dat hiet dêr doe de Jordaen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33718,"r":"CJ093604","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People born with a caul saw funeral processions pass in advance. Others did not see these processions and were quite often pushed off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon dy't mei de helm geboaren wienen, dy seagen de lykstaesjes fan tofoaren. Sokken woarden noait oan kant skoud. Der wienen ek guon dy seagen de lykstaesjes net oankommen. Dy doarsten jouns de wei net del, sa bang wienen se dat se oan kant set wurde soenen. Boardzer Bruining wie mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33720,"r":"CJ093606","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days people warned not to walk in the middle of the road at night because of the funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der woarde froeger altyd sein: Noait midden op 'e wei rinne by nacht. Dat wie fanwege de lykstaesjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33754,"r":"CJ094009","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One should never walk in the middle of the road at night, or else one may be put to the side.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In minske mat nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant dan kin 't gebeure dat er oan kant set wurdt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33810,"r":"CJ094405","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"It sometimes happened that people on foot or on horseback could not go any further at night. Then a funeral procession came by. Once it had passed, they could continue.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mear as ien kear is 't gebeurd dat guon rinnende of mei hynder en wein nachts ûnderweis wienen en ynienen net fierder koenen. Dan woarden se keard. Se moesten dan rûmte jaen foar in lykstaesje, dy't foarby moest. Wie dy passeard, dan koenen se sels ek wer fierder. Dat haw ik faek heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":35916,"r":"CJ094907","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man has to make way for a funeral procession and ends up in the ditch.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In omke fan 'e frou wenne yn 'e Wylgen. Op in joune let kom er fan Drachten werom. Hy soe nei de Wylgen ta en wie sahwat by Teade Hoekje. Doe kom dêr in lykstaesje oan. De lykwein koed er allinne mar sjen. Mar hy woarde troch de lykstaesje oan kant set en yn 'e sleat reage.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36045,"r":"CJ096102","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the east of Grinzer Pein a man was riding a bicycle in the middle of the night. Suddenly he was picked up and flung aside. He saw nothing, but later he was told that a funeral procession had passed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie in man dy ried yn 'e nacht tusken tolven en ienen op 'e fyts yn 't oasten fan Grinzer Pein. Hy ried midden op 'e wei en wie alhiel allinne. Doe woarde er samar ynienen mei fyts en al oan kant smiten. Hy hat noait hwat sjoen, mar der woarde doe forteld dat der in lykstaesje passearde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36046,"r":"CJ096103","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In Drachtster Compagnie there lived a man who often ran over the planks across the ditches at night to see a funeral procession. He could then predict who would be the next to die. It always came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Drachtster Kompenije wienen 't froeger allegear bartsjes. Dêr wenne yn dy tiid in man, dy moast der nachts wit hoe faek ôf, dan moast er lykstaesjes sjen. Dan roan er de feart del oer al dy bartsjes hinne. As er it dan sjoen hie gong er wer op hûs ta. Hy wist altyd krekt hwa't der stjerre soe. 't Kom grif út. Even letter stoar deselde dan, dêr't hy de bigraffenisstoet fan sjoen hie. Wy wennen doe ek yn 'e Kompenije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36047,"r":"CJ096104","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Boardzer Bruining was born with a caul. He also always saw funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining fan Houtigehage wie mei de helm geboaren, dat wie algemien bikend. Dy seach ek altyd lykstaesjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36057,"r":"CJ096203","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Boardzer Bruining always had to watch funeral processions. Others had to get out of bed at night for them and sometimes ran long distances to see them.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining moest lykstaesjes sjen. Mar der wienen ek wol oaren dy't der nachts om út bêd moesten. Dan roannen se soms wit hoe fier.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":207263,"r":"VODA_038_11","p":"Lievelde","v":"Gld.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Own funeral seen.\nTwo brothers, Jan and Drieks, are walking home together. Suddenly Jan hears church bells begin to ring. Then he sees a procession approaching. Drieks hears and sees nothing. Later a new church is built on that spot. Jan is the first to be buried there. Years earlier he had seen his own funeral procession.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"- En dan.. dan is d’r ook nog een verhaal over de karke van Mariënvelde.\n- Ja, dat is mien vader die is vroeger, ging daen struëp, en toen ging e met zien breur [er wordt een lucifer gepakt en aangestoken], n’hoes van ’t struëp, en doe komt ze daor op Ballasbulte, weg trouwens, en toen zeg zien breur Jan, die zeg: “Zie, Drieks, daor begint ’t te loe’en.”\n“Ach, i-j ziet ‘n kuken, met oe loe’en.”\nToen zeg e: “Ja, heurt dan maor.”\nOw. Maar Drieks daen kan ’t niet heuren. Maar Jan wal. En as Drieks noe zeg: “Allee Jan, gaot noe mit. En gaot noe niet mit.” Maar eh.. Jan was blieven staon en Drieks ook.\nEn inlikke toe.. toen zeg e: “Zie, maor zie det dan toch niet, dao kump vanachter ‘t.. de processie aan.”\n“Och, ik zeen niks.”\nJao. En die processie die geet langzaam veuroet en langzaam veuroet en die höld stille achter op Ballasbulte. En inlikke, […?], toen kump de processie weer op […?] an, maar toen geet ze oet mekaar. En toen ze zowat op ’n diek zoe’n doe is ’t weg.\nMien vader ook nooit over prakkeseerd. En wat is ’t geval? Jaor of wat later, veertig jaor later, doe kump d’r dao ’n nieë kerke te staon [gerinkel van glazen op de achtergrond] en laot now zien breur Jan het eerste begraven dao worden. En toen, daen begrafenis is mien vader mit’ewès en toen zeg e: “Ooo, ôzze Jan dae haet zien eigen liek gezeen, zien eigen processie.” En dat is werkelijk gebeurd.\n- […?], zeg.\n- Is wer","l":"Gelders; Nedersaksisch"},{"n":12965,"r":"YPFOE125a","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman says she saw a hearse drawn by two horses. She knows which farm the dead person comes from. She also says that one of the horses is not the farmer's own horse. A year later this comes true exactly. The farmer's wife dies, and one of the horses pulling the hearse is borrowed, because the farmer's horse has broken its leg.","i":"Y.P.","o":"Lykstaasjes\nUs mem stie as Iyts fanke op 'e buorren te Warten by in frou te praten. 'Ik ha 't hiel nuver sjoen', sei se. Dat wie in Iykstaasje en dy en dy, Iju dy't se koenen, rûnen der yn mei. Se koenen der út opmeitsje, op hokfoar pleats der dan in stjergefal komme soe. It wie in boer ûnder Wergea. Mar it frjemde wie, der rûn ien hynder fan'e boer foar de wein, mar it oare hynder koenen se net te plak bringe. Doe sei ús mem: 'Sa'n hynder hat de boer net'. En dat wie ek sa.\nIn goed healjier letter kaam it nei. De boerinne ferstoar. Doe wie it oan 'e begraffenis ta en in hynder fan 'e boer briek in poat. Wêr't se dat oare hynder wei hienen, wit ik net. Mar alles kaam krekt sa ut, as dy frou it in healjier tefoaren ús mem ferteld hie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":12968,"r":"YPFOE125d","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Our great-uncle is clairvoyant. One day he is mowing grass with some men. He tells the men to look up for a moment because a funeral procession is passing along the road. He says one of his men is in it, and that man's brother-in-law too. A few days later it comes true. When the great-uncle eats his break at his sister's, all the clogs have to be put aside. He wants to be able to get outside easily if another funeral procession comes along the road. He lost two of his daughters, and both times he had already foretold it.","i":"Y.P.","o":"Lykstaasjes\nIn âldomke fan my, Knilles Veenstra, sjoech ek foar. Se wienen oan 't greiddollen en doe sei er tsjin ien fan 'e oare mannen: 'Wy moatte even opsjen, want der giet in Iyk de wei del en dêr bistû ek by, en dyn sweager is der ek by. En it kaam ek sa út, in pear dagen letter wie dat al sa.\nDizze âldomke hat ek in skoftsje by myn beppe, dat wie syn suster, hjir yn 'e Westerein yn 'e hûs west. Der wennen ek in pear beppesizzers by har, dan sei omke tsjin 'e bern`: 'Jim moatte jûns de klompen al in bytsje oan 'e kant sette, want ik bin in âld man en ik moat der faak hastich troch. Ik móát hastich. Mei in pear dagen giet hjir in Iyk de wei del en dat móát ik foartiid sjen'. Dan moast er oan it hekje ta, hy waard fan 't bêd ôfdreann. En oft der in hek of in stek wie, likefolle mei hok skerp stikeltrie, hy moast rjocht troch. Letter doe't er in hiel âld man wie, doe koe er sa goed net mear, mar hy moast it sjen.\nTwa fan syn dochters hat er ferlern. Doe hie er de kisten foartiid al oer de flier stean sjoen. Hy wist, dat se stjerre soenen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":12969,"r":"YPFOE125e","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man was born with a caul and is therefore clairvoyant. When he sees a funeral procession pass, he always has to go and look. Even in the middle of the night he gets up for it, otherwise he gets no more rest.","i":"Y.P.","o":"Lykstaasjes\nDer ha guon west, dy wienen mei de helm berne, seinen se dan, en dy moasten alles foarsjen. Sa'n man hat hjir ek yn 'e Harkema wenne. Ik ha him wol kend. As er op bêd lei, dan moast hy der ôf en nei it plak ta dêr't dy Iykstaasje lâns kaam, want dy moast er sjen. Dan seach er de hiele Iykstaasje. Us mem frege him wol ris: 'Kinne jo dan net thúsbliuwe? Dat is doch neat gjin moais—yn 'e nacht fan 't bêd en dêrhinne en sjoch soks'. 'Nee', sei er, 'ûnmooglik! Dan ha 'k gjin rêst mear'.","l":"Fries"},{"n":36092,"r":"CJ096313","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Father always warned us not to run onto the road at night. If a funeral procession comes, you get flung aside.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en dy warskôgen ús altyd: \"Tink der om, rin nachts noait midden op 'e wei. Der kin ris in lykwein oankomme en dan wurde jim oan kant smiten.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36141,"r":"CJ096709","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Running across the road at night is dangerous, because you can be thrown over a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is ús altyd foarhâlden woarn noait midden op 'e wei to rinnen by nacht. In minske kin dan oer in lykstaesje hinne smiten wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36168,"r":"CJ097002","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If you run across the road at night, you can be pushed aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant dan kin men oan kant set wurde troch in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36184,"r":"CJ097103","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man went outside at night to see funeral processions. He could predict who would die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wenne ek in man dy gong der nachts op út om lykstaesjes to sjen. Hy woarde dan dreaun. Hy wist fan tofoaren hwa't der stjerre soe. Sa'n frou wenne hjir ek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36185,"r":"CJ097104","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If you run down the middle of the road at night, a funeral procession may come. You are then pushed aside or flung away.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Net midden op 'e wei rinne, yn 'e nacht. Hwant dêr kin ris in lykstaesje oan komme. Dan wurdt men oan kant set of in meter of hwat fuortsmiten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36265,"r":"CJ097528","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A clairvoyant man can see funeral processions pass by at night. If someone is running on the road when such a funeral procession passes, that person can be pushed aside.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha ús heit en dy faek praten heard oer minsken dy't mei de helm geboaren wienen. Dy gongen der nachts ôf. Dan seagen se lykstaesjes. Dan fortelden se de oare deis: der roannen sàfolle manlju achter en sàfolle froulju.\nSoms seinen se tsjin ien: even oan kant gean, hwant dêr komt in lykstaesje oan. Mar de oare seach dan neat. Nachts moest in minske net midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant dan koed er samar oan kant set wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36282,"r":"CJ097611","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The narrator's father-in-law once met a funeral procession at night. He was pushed off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanheit is ris by nacht in lykstaesje tsjinkom. Hy woarde fan 'e wei ôfset en moest yn 'e berm lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36343,"r":"CJ097902","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Knillis Veenstra could predict deaths and often saw funeral processions travelling along the road. Whenever a funeral procession came, Knillis had to go to it. He could no longer stay at home and ended up in a poorhouse in Kollumerzwaag.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie in âldomke, dat wie in broer fan myn beppe. It wie Knillis Veenstra en hy wenne yn Twizelerheide, flak by 't spoar. Keke-om seinen se. De lju seinen ek wol: âlde Keke.\nKeke-om wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy seach geregeld bigraffenissen fan tofoaren. Sa hat er de dea ek fan syn dochter sjoen, dy't har fordronken hat. Hy seach dagen fan tofoaren de kiste al op 'e flier stean.\nSoms gebeurde it dat er mei guon op stap wie. Dan sei er: Even oan kant gean. Der giet in lykstaesje de wei del.\nIn âld man hat my ris forteld, dat er sa ek ris mei Keke-om ûnderweis wie. De âld man syn sweager wie der ek by. Doe hie Keke-om èk sein: Even oan kant gean. Der is in lykstaesje. Doe't dy passeard wie hied er tsjin dy âld man en dy sweager sein: Jim wienen der beide by.\nDe oare wyks stoar der in famyljelid fan dy beiden. Doe roannen se beide achter 't lyk oan. Keke-om hie 't goed sjoen. Letter hat Keke-om hjir yn dit hûs by myn beppe ynwenne. Heit en syn bruorren wienen op in kear it fjild yn mei handel. De bern hienen de klompen by de achterdoar delset. Doe sei er: \"De klompen net sa bot yn 't paed sette bern, hwant ik mat der wolris út en dan kin 'k hast sa hurd net mei al dy klompen.\" Dat gebeurde dyselde nachts. Hy sei: \"Der giet wer in lykstaesje de wei del. Der komt wer ien op 't hôf.\"\nDan sette er mei tûzen hasten ôf. Hy mòest nei dat plak ta. Hy hat wol nachten hawn dat er oer hekke","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36344,"r":"CJ097903","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If you went out on the road at night, you could be pushed aside by a funeral procession. That sometimes happened in Westerein.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy woarden altyd warskôge: Rin noait midden op it paed by nacht. Dû kinst troch in lykstaesje oan kant set wurde. Guon fan 'e Westerein is dat wol oerkom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36365,"r":"CJ098005","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"During the war the narrator's wife once walked to Kollum in the evening. On the way she had to stand on the verge because a funeral procession was passing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn frou kom ris op in joune let noch by de boer wei yn Aldwâld. Sy moest nei Kollum ta. 't Wie yn 'e oarloch. Underweis kom der har in bigraffenis tsjin. Hja wie needsake om yn 'e berm to gean. Hja hat dêr sa lang yn 'e berm stien oant de bigraffenis foarby wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36480,"r":"CJ098609","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The narrator's little sister was clairvoyant. She saw funeral processions travelling along the road. She also saw her grandfather's funeral pass by. She often got out of bed at night to see the funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn suster wie mei de helm geboaren. Hja wie noch mar in famke, doe opponearre him dat al. Op in kear boarten wy mei elkoarren op 'e dyk. Doe treau hja ús dêr allegear ien foar ien wei, hwant der kaem in lykstaesje oan, sei se. \"Hja binne nou oan Wigerom ta\", sei se. \"Dy giet út 'e staesje wei, dy giet yn 'e hûs.\" Wy moesten allegear oan kant stean gean.\nKrekt seis wiken letter is myn pake overleden. Se moesten Wiger-om syn hûs foarby. Doe is Wigerom út 'e staesje weigong. Hja seach it by dei. Letter is myn suster skoaljuffer woarn.\nHja is al in skoft dea. Ik wit noch dat se sei: \"Mem, hwat ha 'k nou hwat raers sjoen. Se ha pake bigroeven.\"\nHja hat folle faker lykstaesjes sjoen. Hja moest nachts faek út it bêd wei om to sjen. Dan waerd der kloppe. Dan mòest se der út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36491,"r":"CJ098704","p":"Noardburgum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Schoolteacher Foekje v.d. Bos had to get up at night to see funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir hat in skoaljuffer wenne, dat wie Foekje v.d. Bos. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy gong der yn 'e nacht op út om lykstaesjes to sjen. Hja mòest it dwaen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36496,"r":"CJ098709","p":"Noardburgum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Children were not allowed to walk on the path at night. You could then be pushed aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As bern waerden wy altyd warskôge: \"tink der om, rin by nacht noait midden oer 't paed. Dan kin jim wolris in rare reis meitsje, as jim oan kant reage wurde troch in lykstaesje.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36531,"r":"CJ098820","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Shortly before her death, a young woman from Westerein saw a funeral procession. The names of all the people walking in it were called out, but her own name was not among them.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wenne in jonge frou yn 'e Westerein, dy wie in bytsje heal. Har mem kaem by har op bisite. Doe sei se tsjin har mem:\n\"Mem, nou ha 'k hwat sjoen. Ik haw in lykstaesje sjoen by my yn 'e hûs.\" En hja neamde de nammen fan alle persoanen dy't dêr by wienen. Hja sei: \"Ik wie der net by.\"\nFuort dêrnei is dy jonge frou stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36532,"r":"CJ098821","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A couple who bought a house in Westerein sold it again after they had seen a funeral procession. The woman's sister then went to live in the house and died shortly afterwards.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Westerein wennen twa jonge minsken, dy kochten hjir in hûs en dêr kamen se yn to wenjen. Hja hienen der noch mar even yn wenne, doe seagen se dêr allebeide yn 'e nacht in lykstaesje. Doe ha se 't hûs wer forkocht.\nDoe kom dêr in suster fan 'e frou yn to wenjen, dy har man kocht it. Dy suster stoar yn dat hûs, doe wenne se der noch mar even yn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36554,"r":"CJ098843","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You should never walk in the middle of the path at night, because a funeral procession may come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Rin noait op 't midden fan in paed by nacht. Bliuw altyd oan kant. Dêr koe ris in lykstaesje oankomme, dy't men net sjocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36561,"r":"CJ098904","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Auke [de Vries] saw a funeral procession come out of old Tryn's house. Tryn died about a year later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ymke syn broer Auke fortelde ris: Ik bileefde justerjoune hwat. Ik stie bûtendoar. Ik seach de wei del, doe waerd ik in lykstaesje gewaer. 't Kaem út 'e hûs fan âlde Tryn wei. Alde Tryn is ± in jier letter forstoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36577,"r":"CJ098920","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Bontsje Keke said that at night people were sometimes pushed aside when a funeral procession came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Keke fortelde, dat der yn 'e nacht wolris minsken oan kant reage waerden as der in lykstaesje oan kaem. Hy hie wolris guon warskôge.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36620,"r":"CJ099216","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Some clairvoyant people saw funeral processions at night. They would then warn others to step aside. Sometimes people were held back and could not go any further.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon dy't mei de helm geboaren binne sjogge lykstaesjes by nacht. Se warskôgje oaren oan kant to gean, as der ien oankomt.\nSoms wurde de minsken keard, dan kinne se net fierder.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36657,"r":"CJ099412","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Sometimes someone was pushed aside by a funeral procession that he could not see.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw wol gauris heard dat der ien oan kant reage waerd troch in lykstaesje dy't se net seagen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36871,"r":"CJ100816","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If you see a funeral procession, you must always step aside. That is why we were never allowed to walk in the middle of the road in the evening or at night when we were young. A person born with a caul always has to get up at night to see funeral processions, whether he wants to or not. Bontsje Keke sometimes had to go to the churchyard or some other place. He often had hardly any clothes on, so hastily did he have to get out of bed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ien dy't op jountiid in lykstaesje sjocht mat der om tinke dat er oan kant giet. Ek as er neat sjocht. Der waerd ús altyd foarhâlden: by jountiid en by nacht noait midden op 'e wei rinne.\nBontsje Keke wie mei de helm geboaren. As der in lykstaesje wie ergens en hy woe graech lizzen bliuwe, dan joech him dat neat. Dan moest er der út, nei 't tsjerkhôf of nei in oar plak. Dan hied er soms hast gjin klean oan, sa hastich wie hy der út rekke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36913,"r":"CJ101214","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"We were always warned not to walk in the middle of the road at night. People told of those who ran ahead of a hearse in the middle of the road, tripped and were run over.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger hearde ik faek forhalen fan minsken dy't by nacht midden op 'e wei roannen. Dy wienen foar by de lykwein opflein en der achter wer by del knoffele. Wy waerden altyd warskôge: Tink der om, rin by nacht noait midden op 'e wei. Ik rin nòch altyd oan kant.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36951,"r":"CJ101402","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Mother could see funerals in advance. So it was with our old neighbour, whose funeral procession she had already seen two weeks earlier.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem seach ris in kear in bigraffenis fan tofoaren.\nNjonken ús wenne in âld man, Klaas Mulder. Mem seach de lykstaesje op in âld reed. Dêr kaem oars noait hwat lâns. Sa'n fjirtsjin dagen letter stoar ús âld buorman en waerd er lâns dy âld reed nei 't tsjerkhôf ta brocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36985,"r":"CJ101523","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"We were never allowed to run in the middle of the road, because then you might be pushed aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy mochten froeger noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant dan koenen wy wolris oan kant set wurde troch in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37088,"r":"CJ101903","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Sytse Wijma often had to get out of bed at night to watch funeral processions. He saw them best in the middle of the road. It always meant that someone would die soon.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wenne in man yn Surhuzum, dat wie Sytse Wijma. Dy koe samar midden yn 'e nacht út bêd wei gean, dan moest er in lykstaesje sjen. Dan roan er altyd midden op 'e wei, mei in sage ûnder 'e earm. Midden op 'e wei koe er it better sjen. Hy roan soms hiele einen yn 'e nacht.\nHy fielde 't oan. 't Kaem altyd út. As hy in lykstaesje sjoen hie duorre 't altyd mar even dan stoar der ien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37102,"r":"CJ102104","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Some people had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions. You should never run in the middle of the road at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Harkema en yn Stiensgea ha 'k wol guon kend dy't nachts fan bêd moesten om lykstaesjes to sjen.\nMen moest nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37104,"r":"CJ102106","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A carpenter who sometimes said the grace backwards and was not afraid of the devil had to walk home one evening. A dog kept running along with him. When he wanted to cross a plank, the dog blocked his way. The man put down his toolbox and shouted that he was not afraid, but then he was lifted up and flung away. He landed on his knees on the plank and was lame for the rest of his life.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wenne in sekere Ruerd van der Veen yn 'e Harkema, dat wie in timmerman. It wie in raer feint. Hy hie oan 't timmerjen west op 't Bomkleaster en dêr hie er it mâl opsein. Hy joech neat om 'e duvel en al sokke dingen mear.\nDy jouns moest er nei hûs ta. Hy wie in moai eintsje yn 'e lannen dêr't it paed troch roun nei Harkema ta, doe kom der in houn oan, dy't iderkear njonken him lâns roun. Dy houn woe Ruerd dêr wei ha.\nDoe moest er oer in planke oer in sleat. Doe gong dy houn midden op 'e planke sitten.\n\"Nou sil 'k it dy sizze,\" sei Ruerd tsjin 'e houn, \"dû der wei. As wiest de duvel ek, ik bin net bang foar dy.\" Hy sette de bak mei timmerridskip, dy't er oer 't skouder hie, del. Mar doe waerd er grypt en smiten. Hy kaem krekt mei de knibbel op 'e planke dêr't er oer moest. Hy koe net mear goed rinne.\nKreupel kaem er thús.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37119,"r":"CJ102302","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Father sometimes saw funeral processions. Later a real funeral would follow.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit hat wolris fan tofoaren lykstaesjes sjoen. Letter wie dêr dan de echte bigraffenis. 't Wie oan 'e Noarderdwarsfeart dêr't er dy lykstaesjes seach.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37144,"r":"CJ102505","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Someone was walking in the middle of the road in the evening. His mate suddenly said they had to walk on the verge. At that moment, he said, a funeral procession was passing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Noait midden op 'e wei rinne by joun, seinen de minsken froeger altyd. Ien fan 'e Dwarsfeart roun ris mei syn maet midden op it paed.\nDoe sei syn maet: \"Even oan kant, even yn 'e berm.\"\nIt duorre even, doe sei er: \"Gean nou mar wer op it paed. Der gong ús nyskes in lykstaesje foarby; dy is ús nou al passeard.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37242,"r":"CJ103314","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"At night you should not walk in the middle of the road, because then you can be pushed aside by a phantom funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Nachts mat men noait midden op 'e wei rinne hwant men kin oan kant set wurde troch in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37328,"r":"CJ103914","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man saw phantom funeral processions, and not long afterwards there were real funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Piter Terpstra fan Droegeham seach lykstaesjes fan tofoaren. Even letter hienen jy dan de èchte lykstaesje op it paed.\nDat kloppe altyd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37333,"r":"CJ104002","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One evening we had to move to the side because father-in-law saw a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanheit wenne by 't Wyldpaed oan 't Heideloantsje.\nOp in joune wie 'k der by him. Doe moesten wy oan kant, der kaem in lykstaesje oan. Skoanheit seach him wol, ik net.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37573,"r":"CJ105502","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man was born with a caul and foresaw funeral processions. Once he again saw a phantom funeral procession in which, along the way, one of the traces of the harness of the horses before the hearse broke. He told others about it.\nA few days later a well-known person from De Pein died. When he was taken to the churchyard, the traces of one of the horses broke.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn de Pein hat in man wenne, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy man seach lykstaesjes foarút.\nOp in kear doe seach er wer in lykstaesje. Underweis gong ien fan 'e stringen fan 'e beide hynders dy't foar de wein rounen, stikken. Dat seach er en dat fortelde er oan 'e minsken.\nIn dei of hwat letter forstoar der in bikend persoan yn De Pein. Doe't dy nei 't hôf ta brocht waerd, doe brutsen de stringen fan it iene hynder.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37576,"r":"CJ105505","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days people always said never to walk in the middle of the road at night, because then you might run into a phantom funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der waerd ús froeger altyd foarhâlden noait by nacht midden op 'e wei to rinnen, hwant dan koe 't gebeure dat men tsjin in lykstaesje oproun.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37608,"r":"CJ105604","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"An old woman sometimes saw funeral processions when she got out of bed at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Frytsen wenne yn Eastemar yn 'e foarige ieu. Dat minske gong nachts soms út bêd, dan seach se lykstaesjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":131998,"r":"VODA_036_16","p":"Soest","v":"Utr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man is pushed off the road and into the water when a funeral procession passes by.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Het gaat over over het van de weg af zetten. Dat was ook een heel bekend verhaal. Ennuhm, da’s een verhaal uit, uh, van Wilfred Houtveen uit Hoogland. ’t Is Henk Vonk overkommen. Die werd van de weg af gezet. Hij liep midden op de weg, want daar was secuurder. Meer opeens wierd Henk met zijn twaalf ponds roggebreed onder z’n arm, in ’t waoter gezet. ’t Gebeurde bie de farmerie. Er moest een lijkstoet voorbie. Deze verhalen die komen praktisch overal voor en worden ook door allerlei oudere mensen worden die, worden die verteld."},{"n":207294,"r":"VODA_038_16","p":"Rekken","v":"Gld.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A maid saw things before they happened. She foresaw the death of a farmhand. The lady of the house did not believe her, because the farmhand was as fit as a fiddle. But the farmhand fell from the hay wagon and died.\nThe maid had also seen that the master's white horse would pull the hearse. The lady of the house asked her husband to harness the brown horse, to show the maid that not everything she saw happened exactly so. But the brown horse was so restless in front of the hearse that in the end they had to use the white horse after all. So everything the maid had seen came true exactly.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Ja, eh, triestige dingen wist ze ook wel.. grootmoeder ook wel van te vertellen. Iën van de meiden die was.. helderziende.. en eh.. dan was ze heel triestig, had ze zeene had wie d’r dood zou gaon of wie ’t k.. d.. d’r is ‘ne arbeider is van de heuiwagen of’evallen. Ehm.. Beppe die probeerd’n eur dat oet ’t heuf te proat’n. Die zei, doet ze ‘r aan de karne v..vônd grienen: “Janne, wat heb i-j toch?”\n“O, eh.. vrouwe, eh.. Hendrik daen gied dood.”\n“Ach, wat word j’ toch moe, […?] zo gezond as ‘ne vis.”\nMaar Hendrik viel van de heuiwagen en hie was dood.\n“Ja, vrouwe,” had ze zegd, “gebeurd toch, want eh.. ik heb ‘m zien veur’n. Ik zeen.. zien dat ze met hem veur’n. En eh… oeze witte peerd was d’r vuur, daor, jao, bie dat hekke.”\nDoe te doe dood was, toe zeg de vrouwe tegen eur man: “Och noe.. ’t is naar genoeg at dat zo gaon is, maar now waal kan je me een plezeer deed’n, doet ‘r now ’t broene peerd vuur. Anders meent die arme deerne at alles zo oet môt kom’n.”\nEn dat dee de baas. Maar ’t broene peerd det maken zo’n spektakele veur de liekwagen dat ze ‘m van armoed weer of moesten span’n en wit’n d’r veur deden [fluit op de achtergrond]. Dus op dat.. toen ze bee det punt war’n waor ’t zee ‘t ezeen had, toen was dat witte peerd vuur.","l":"Gelders; Nedersaksisch"},{"n":210366,"r":"VODA_045_02","p":"Barger-Compascuum","v":"Dr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You should not walk in the middle of the road at night, because you could collide with a hearse. That happened to Berend when he was on his way home drunk. He injured his leg and suffered from it for the rest of his life. No one could heal his leg.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Dat biegeloof, ja, dat zat hier ook. Ja, jong, dat was de dood eigenlijk met die spokerij. As je midden over de weg leupen dan ko-je zo tegen ’n liekwagen aan botsen [gekraak].. tenminste as ’t duuster was. En dan waren die nog niet jórig. \nIk ken d’r eine dae met zo’n liekwagen te doon had ehad. En he had d’r altied een slim bein van overhold’n. Dat was.. dat is zo bin: Berend had dae dag de haile dag al wat last had van liefzeer en zo tegen de aobend was ie es eben naor ’n kroegie gaon om ’n borrel te drinken. D’r had natuurlijk veel meer zitten en daor heeft Berend nog gemieterd an de zoep kom’n. Daor is nog oet vortkomen dat hij de haile boel daor kort en klein slagen had, maar dat was zien schuld ook niet; hij had of en too zo’n aanval van delirium en daor komt zulks natuurlijk al es oet voort, dat wisten ze ook wel. \nMaar door is hij met zien grille kop in hoes gaon en is midden over de weg lopen, door ’t wagenspeur, en door is hij natuurlijk tègen ’n liekwagen oplopen. \nZien bein was kepot en d’r was geen ein dae daor wat aan doon kan. En ‘t bleef kepot en he had d’r lebenslang met pinkt.","l":"Nedersaksisch; Drents"},{"n":12967,"r":"YPFOE125c","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A clairvoyant woman tells a man that they will soon be at the same funeral together. She will nod to him when he is standing in front of a gap in a hedge. The man does not believe it, but when his father dies he begins to believe it. He wants to make sure she is not proved right, and so means to avoid standing in front of the gap in the hedge. At the funeral the bearers want to change positions, and before he knows it the man is standing in front of the gap in the hedge. On the other side the clairvoyant woman nods to him.","i":"Y.P.","o":"Lykstaasjes\nOp Sumarreheide wenne in frou, Antsje, dy seach foar. Doe wie der in jongkeardel, dy sei: 'No Antsje, is der ek wat nijs op 'e buert?' Se sei: 'Ja, der komt nijs. Dû en ik komme op 'e selde begraffenis. En moatst hjir mar om tinke—ast foar it gat fan 'e hage stieste, dan sil ik dy wol even taknikke'. No, doe waard er al in bytsje kjel. En it wie de oare wyks, syn heit waard raar, krige in beroerte en rekke desélde deis wei. Hy tocht, Antsje komt fêst op 'e begraffenis, want dy wenne tichteby, mar se sil noait gelyk krije—ik sil soargje, dat ik net foar it gat fan 'e hage kom te stean. Mar doe't it begraffenisfolk allegear bûtendoar wie, feroaren se de opstelling. De dragers seinen: 'Dit mar út en dat mar út', en ear't hy der erch yn hie, stie er foar it gat fan 'e hage. Hy seach krekt foar him út en dêr stie Antsje en hja knikte him ta. Antsje hat wol folle mear foarsjoen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":38215,"r":"CJ108501","p":"Feanwâldsterwâl","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A week before a man hangs himself, his son is flung aside at that spot by a phantom funeral procession that has to pass by. The narrator's mother warns never to walk in the middle of the road in the evening.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De Westereindersingel giet nei Kûkherne ta. Dy giet it lân troch by de Westereinder brêge. De Tolheksingel hyt dat stik lân. Winterdeis is it wetter dêr tige heech.\nDe reed allinne is aerdich heech.\nIn man hat him der by winterdei ophong, doe't it wetter sa heech wie. Se ha it lyk yn 'e kiste mei in pream dêr wei brocht.\nIn wike fan tofoaren kaem de soan dêr lâns. Dy is dêr by de hege dyk samar ynienen oan kant smiten woarn.\nDoe moest de lykstaesje dêr lâns.\nIn wike letter wie dêr de lykstaesje fan syn eigen heit.\nUs mem sei altyd: tink der om, noait midden op 'e wei rinne by jountiid.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38288,"r":"CJ108738","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A week before his mother's death, a son saw the procession with her coffin pass by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As fanke tsjinne ik by in boer. Dat wie Floris Koning. Hy wenne oan 'e Heidstreek, op 'e Swette. Doe't ik dêr in skoftsje west hie, stoar de boer syn frou.\nDoe sei de soan tsjin my: \"Ik ha 't fleden wike allegear fan tofoaren sjoen. Se binne my foarbygien mei ús mem yn 'e kiste.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38339,"r":"CJ108928","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Do not walk in the middle of the road at night; there is a chance of being pushed aside by a phantom funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By nacht mat men noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant men kin dan oan kant reage wurde troch in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38357,"r":"CJ109018","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One evening a boy sees a group of people standing in the distance, which grows larger the closer he gets to the house. A few weeks later the neighbour woman dies. The boy has seen her funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In neef fan my yn 'e Westerein wie noch mar sa'n foech jonge. Op in joun moest er foar syn mem om turf. It wie al hwat tsjuster en de jonge wie bang. Doe't er by it hûs kaem, dêr't de winkel wie, stie dêr in kloftsje minsken. Hy tocht: gelokkich, dêr kin ik aenst moai mei oprinne, dan hoef ik net allinne to gean.\nMar hwat tichter hy by it hûs kaem, hwat mear minsken dêr wienen. Doe't er tichterby kaem, sweefden al dy minsken.\nFjouwer wiken letter kaem de âlde buorfrou fan dat hûs to forstjerren. It wie har lykstaesje dy't de neef fan my dy jouns sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38358,"r":"CJ109019","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A neighbour was flung into the canal by a phantom funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie in buorman hjir yn 'e Westerein, dy is ris troch in lykstaesje yn 'e feart smiten woarn, fan 'e wei ôf. Hy wie op 'e fyts en woarde oan kant reage. Hy seach neat. 't Gebeurde by de grifformearde tsjerke yn 'e Westerein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38387,"r":"CJ109201","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man has to get up at night to see funerals, usually in a churchyard. He also knows who is going to die, and he sees in advance that his two daughters will drown. The story goes that gates open by themselves for him. Everything he experiences is a punishment for all the evil he has done. When he goes out he must not look back, otherwise he is bitten by the dogs, henchmen of the devil, that drive him on.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Keke wie it fremdste mantsje fan 'e Westerein.\nIk en myn broer hienen moalhandel. Wy brochten wol mais en koarnmoal en sa by him en dan die hy ús de forhalen.\nHy fortelde altyd oer syn bilevenissen by nacht.\nHy wenne by 't spoar. Elkenien koe him.\nKeke moest nachts wit hoe faek út bêd wei. Dan moest er in bigraffenis sjen. Meastal wie dat op it tsjerkhôf en dat wie wit hoe fier rinnen. Ik ha wolris tsjin him sein: jo moesten hwat tichter by it tsjerkhôf wenje, man, dan hienen jo 't folle makliker. Soms moest hy der trije nachten yn ien wike hinne. Dan wist er altyd to sizzen hwa't der stjerre soe. Hy telde de manlju en de froulju dy't achter 't lyk oan roannen en 't kom altiten krekt út.\nHy hat wol prebearre lizzen to bliuwen, as it wer sa fier wie. Mar 't joech him neat, hy moest der út. Hy waerd jage en dreaun. Se sieten altyd achter him oan.\nSoms tocht er: ik bliuw dochs lizzen. It joech neat. En dan moest er hiel hurd. Dan gong er soms skean de lânnen troch om mar op tiid to kommen. De hekken gongen fansels foar him iepen, seinen se. Wol in biwiis, dat er it sjen moèst.\nKeke mat froeger hiel hwat op syn kerfstok hawn ha. Syn eigen suster fortelde dat der gjin greater stjonkert wie as Keke. It wie in echte minnen-ien. Hy hat hiel hwat bileefd.\nOer 't algemien seinen se dat dit de straf wie foar alle kwea dat er útheefd hie. Dêrom moest er alles sjen.\nTwa dochters fan","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38388,"r":"CJ109202","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"The narrator's father was pushed aside at night by a phantom funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is sa'n tachtich jier lyn, wy wienen noch fan dy bern. Doe wienen der noch sânloanen yn 'e Westerein en hjir en dêr stie in húske. Wy wennen oan in donkere loane.\nUs heit fortelde, hy wie ris op in nacht dy loane lâns kaem, doe wie er oan kant skoud woarn. In hiel ein, sûnder dat er hwat seach. Dêr hat in lykstaesje west dy't dêr lâns kaem, mar heit koe der net by komme. In skoftsje waerd er sa oan kant skoud, doe wie 't oer.\nDoe wie de lykstaesje foarby.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38406,"r":"CJ109220","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Someone tells his companion to step aside because a phantom funeral procession is coming. He also sees the number of people walking in it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie in omke, dy is jong stoarn. Op in nacht wied er mei in maet oan 't murdejeijen. Doe sei dy kammeraet ynienen tsjin him: \"Dû mast even oan kant gean, dêr komt in lykstaesje oan.\" Doe gongen se oan kant stean. Even letter sei de kammeraet: \"Nou is 't foarby. Nou kinne wy wol wer op 't paed.\"\n\"Hast it ek sjoen\", frege er myn omke.\n\"Né,\" sei omke, \"ik seach neat.\"\nMar hy koe krekt sizze, hoefolle manlju en hoefolle froulju der achteroan roannen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38440,"r":"CJ109324","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul warns people to step aside because of a phantom funeral procession. A few days later there is a real funeral procession. Johannes Meerstra is also said to have been born with a caul.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Metske-smit wie op in jountiid mei oare minsken op 'e wei. Doe sei er: \"Jimme matte even oan kant gean, hwant der komt in lykstaesje oan.\"\nIn dei of hwat letter wie dêr in èchte lykstaesje. 't Gebeurde op 'e Wâl. Metske wie mei helm geboaren.\nHja seinen, dat Jehannes Meerstra ek mei de helm geboaren wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38441,"r":"CJ109325","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"To avoid an invisible phantom funeral procession, you should not walk in the middle of the street at night. A funeral procession never moves aside; it must be given room.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat by nacht net midden op in paed rinne, hwant der kin ris in lykstaesje wêze dy't men net sjocht. En in lykstaesje giet noait oan kant, dy mat men rûmte jaen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38462,"r":"CJ109404","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Do not walk in the middle of the road at night, so as not to be pushed aside.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne, oars kin men oan kant set wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38474,"r":"CJ109416","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man who meets a phantom funeral procession at night gets no answer to his greeting.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Westerein wenne ien, dy trof yn 'e nacht in lykstaesje.\nHy hie 'joun' sein, mar hy krige gjin antwurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38570,"r":"CJ109825","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Do not walk in the middle of the road at night, because then you can be pushed aside.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By nacht mat in minske noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant dan kin er wolris oan kant reage wurde. Us heit hat wol guon neamd, dy't dat oerkomd is.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38629,"r":"CJ110007","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"After midnight do not walk in the middle of the road, because if a phantom funeral procession passes you can be pushed away.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne nei tolve ûre yn 'e nacht. Dan kin men fan 'e wei ôfsmiten wurde, as der in lykstaesje passeart.\nHjir yn 'e heide is sa alris ien oan kant reage.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29484,"r":"CJ110202","p":"De Wilgen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You must never run in the middle of the road at night, because you may run into an invisible funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat yn 'e nacht noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant dan kin men tsjin in lykstaesje oanrinne, dy't men net sjocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29519,"r":"CJ110417","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Warning: you must never walk in the middle of the road at night, because you may be struck by a passing funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der waerd altyd sein: Rin yn 'e nacht noait midden op 'e wei, hwant as der in lykstaesje oankomt kinst in rare gisel meitsje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29521,"r":"CJ110419","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"It sometimes happens that someone urges another person to step aside for a passing funeral procession. The other, however, cannot see the procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde hiel faek dat as guon ûnderweis wienen, der ien sei: \"Even oan kant gean, der komt in lykstaesje oan.\"\nDan seagen de oaren dy lykstaesje net.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29555,"r":"CJ110502","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"From the appearance of a hearse in the farmyard, a mother foresees the death of her daughter. She also hears the coffin bump against the door and the window.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us Gjetsje is stoarn oan 'e Spaense gryp yn novimber 1918. Us mem hat alles in wike of seis fan tofoaren sjoen.\nMem sei doe: \"Hwat mat dy lykwein hjir op 't hiem?\"\nDer wie doe hielendal net in lykwein.\nHja hearde de wein draeijen en piipjen. De kiste stompte tsjin 'e doar oan en kraste tsjin 't kezyn.\nLetter is 't krekt sa gebeurd. De kiste stompte tsjin 'e doar.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29556,"r":"CJ110503","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"If you walk in the middle of the road at night, you may be driven aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Rin noait by nacht midden op 'e wei, seinen se froeger altyd, hwant jo kinne dan oan kant set wurde troch in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29558,"r":"CJ110505","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man is often driven out of bed at night to see funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Keke moest der nachts altyd út. Dan wie 't krekt as sieten se him achter. Dan moest er in lykstaesje sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29582,"r":"CJ110613","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession at night. He recognises everyone walking in it. It is a premonition: shortly afterwards his neighbour dies. He had also noticed that she was missing from the procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Gerke Veenstra wenne yn 'e Rottefalle. Hy wie fékoopman.\nOp in nacht seach er in lykstaesje dy't nei 't tsjerkhôf ta gong. Hy moest dêr doe lâns mei fé. Hy koe alle minsken herkenne, dy't achter it lyk oanroannen.\nAl syn buorlju wienen der by. Mar der ûntbriek ien, dy miste hy.\nTrije dagen letter overleed syn buorfrou. Dat wie deselde dy't er net sjoen hie; dy lei yn 'e kiste.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29583,"r":"CJ110614","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the old days it often happened that someone urged his companions to step aside for a passing funeral procession. That person was then the only one who could see the procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit hat faek forteld fan lju dy't ûnderweis wienen mei oaren yn 'e nacht en dat der dan ien sei: Even oan kant gean. Der mat in lykstaesje passeare. Sûnder dat de oaren it seagen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29607,"r":"CJ110709","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You must never walk in the middle of the road at night, because you may run into a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne by nacht, hwant dan kin men tsjin in lykstaesje oanstompe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29616,"r":"CJ110805","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A mother urges her little son to step aside for a passing funeral procession. The son, however, does not see the procession. It is a premonition: four weeks later a real funeral procession passes at that same spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit syn pake Gauke Jansma fortelde: Doe't ik in jonkje wie fan in jier of tsien gong ik mei myn mem nei Nyegeasterhoek. Doe sei mem tsjin my: \"Mast even oan kant gean, hwant der komt in bigraffenisstoet oan.\" Ik gong oan kant, mar ik ha neat sjoen. Mar ús mem seach it wol: Fjouwer wiken letter wie der op datselde plak in bigraffenis.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29637,"r":"CJ110912","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You must never walk in the middle of the road at night, because you may run into a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Nachts mat men noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant dan kin men wolris tsjin in lykkoets oanrinne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29642,"r":"CJ111005","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You must never run in the middle of the road in the evening, because you may be driven aside by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By jountiid mat men noait midden op 'e wei rinne. Hwant dan kin men oan kant stompt wurde. Yn 'e Wylgen is sa ris ien fan 'e wei smiten woarn. Letter kaem dêr dan in bigraffenis lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29712,"r":"CJ111307","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You must never walk in the middle of the road at night, because you may be struck by an invisible hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men moat by nacht noait midden oer de wei rinne. It is faek gebeurd dat ien dan in stomp krige fan in lykwein, dy't passearde. Men mat nachts altyd rûmte jaen op 'e wei. Men kin noait witte of der soms in lykstaesje yn oantocht is, dy't men net sjocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29730,"r":"CJ111403","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A girl often foresees deaths at night in passing funeral processions. Once she sees a lot of children walking behind a hearse. It is an omen: later, when someone from a family of dwarfs dies, the very small relatives walk behind the hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw in dochter hawn, dy seach allerhande dingen fan tofoaren. Meastal wienen 't lykstaesjes yn 'e nacht. Hja wenne hjir yn 'e Westerein op Vogelzang. Op in moarn sei se: \"Nou ha 'k fannacht hwat sjoen, dat kin noait wier wêze. Ik seach in lykstaesje, mar dêr roannen allegear bern yn 't swart achter de kiste oan.\"\nMar it kaem wol deeglik nei. Ael, âlde Jan Lammerts syn frou kaem to forstjerren. Dy famylje, dat binne allegearre hiele lytse minsken, krekt liliputters; de bern èk. Dy hie hja dy nachts sjoen. It kloppe dus wòl.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29731,"r":"CJ111404","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One night a girl sees two small coffins being carried to a hearse, followed by a funeral procession. It is a premonition: shortly afterwards two children die one right after the other.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde ek op 'e Vogelzang dat myn dochter dêr yn 'e nacht seach, dat se twa lytse kistjes fan bern nei de lykwein ta droegen. De lykstaesje kaem dêr achteroan. 't Wie achter de earmkeamers. Ridlik gau dêrnei stoaren dêr achter de earmkeamers twa bern fuort op elkoarren. Dat hie hja sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29738,"r":"CJ111411","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man on his way one evening to help a baker suddenly finds it has gone completely dark around him. The next moment he is lifted up and put in the ditch. As long as it stays dark, he cannot climb up the bank. When it suddenly gets light again, he hurries out of the ditch. The man was seized by a funeral procession because he was walking in the middle of the road. Once the procession had passed, it became light again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer Knjillis soe op in joun nei âlde Knjillis-bakker ta om dy by it bakken to helpen.\nDoe't er in eintsje ûnderweis wie, waerd it ynienen hielendal donker. Knillis-om fielde dat er optild waerd en yn 'e sleat set. Mar hy koe neat sjen, hwant it wie allegear donker om him hinne.\nSa lang it donker bleau koe er net wer by de wâl opkomme, mar ynienen wie 't wer ljocht. Doe koe Knjillis-om út 'e sleat wei komme.\nHy hat neat sjoen, mar it hat in lykstaesje west, dêr't er tsjinoanroun wie. Hy roan midden op 'e wei, en dat wie net goed. Doe't dy lykstaesje passeard wie, waerd it wer ljocht en koe er fierder gean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29767,"r":"CJ111505","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You should never walk in the middle of the road at night, because a funeral procession may drive you to the side.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy mochten jouns noait midden op 'e wei rinne. Dat is ús altyd yndruid woarn. Dat doch ik nòch noait, dêr hâld ik my altyd oan. Hwant dan kin men troch in lykstaesje oan 'e kant smiten wurde. Dat is faek gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29802,"r":"CJ111606","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"It happens that at night someone urges another person to step aside for a passing funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wienen wol mear lju dy't hwat seagen by nacht, sûnder dat dat bikend woarde. Ik ha faek fortellen heard, as sa'n ien ûnderweis wie mei in oaren, dat er dan soms sei: \"Even oan kant gean.\" Dan seach er, dat der in lykstaesje passeare moest.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29925,"r":"CJ111714","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You should never walk in the middle of the road, because a funeral procession may pass you.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy mochten froeger noait midden op 'e wei rinne.\nEn as der in reed oer in stik lân gyng, rounen wy by jountiid oer it gers, net oer de reed, hwant der wie gjin rûmte genôch op sa'n reed om in lykstaesje passeare to kinnen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29953,"r":"CJ111803","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One evening two brothers see a funeral procession. It is a premonition: a few days later someone dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen froeger yn 'e Westerein, in bytsje apart. Heit handele yn reiten stuollen en wie stuolwynder, mar hy hie ek hwat buorkerije. Ik wie sahwat tsien jier âld, doe seagen myn broer en ik op in joun, doe't it skimerich wie, in lykstaesje. Myn broer seach it allegear folle dúdliker as ik. Forskillende minsken dy't achter it lyk oan roannen, koe er ûnderskiede. In dei of hwat letter wie de echte bigraffenis der en deselde minsken dy't myn broer sjoen hie, roannen achter 't lyk oan. 't Wie in man dy't stoarn wie. Wy wienen doe op in reedtsje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30024,"r":"CJ112101","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"When a funeral procession passes at night, usually on a sandy road, a death is coming. It is an omen. Such a procession cannot be seen with the ordinary eye. If you do not step aside for it, you are driven off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Gebeurde hjir wolris dat ien yn 'e nacht in lykstaesje passearen seach en dat dan in skoftsje dêrnei de echte bigraffenis der wie. Dat wie in algemien forskynsel.\nMeastal wie sa'n lykstaesje op in âlde sânwei.\nMei 't gewoane eech wie sa'n lykstaesje net to sjen.\nMakke men net dat men oan kant kaem, dan waerd men fan 't paed ôfreage. Dat is wol gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30054,"r":"CJ112206","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People born with a caul often foresee deaths at night in passing funeral processions. If you walk in the middle of the road at night, a passing funeral procession may drive you off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir ha wol guon west dy seagen soms nachts in lykstaesje. Sokken wienen mei de helm geboaren, seinen se.\nMen mat nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant dan kin men sa'n lykstaesje yn 't paed rinne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30071,"r":"CJ112309","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You should never walk in the middle of the road at night. An invisible funeral procession may drive you off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is hjir wolris gebeurd dat der ien by nacht oan kant set waerd, as der in lykstaesje passearde, sûnder dat dyselde hwat seach. Men mat dêrom by nacht noait op it midden fan 'e wei rinne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30112,"r":"CJ112406","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Because funeral processions need the space, it is best not to walk in the middle of the road at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Noait mat men by nacht midden op 'e wei rinne, fanwegen in lykstaesje, dy't altyd paed ha mat en dy't dan wolris tsjin jin oanstompe kin.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30363,"r":"CJ112901","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Early in the morning a man is pushed off the road, bicycle and all. A funeral procession has to pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit soe op in moarn nei 't wurk ta op 'e fyts.\n't Wie noch o sa bitiid en 't wie noch tsjuster.\nYnienen wurdt er mei fyts en al oan kant set en komt sa yn 'e feart tolânne.\n't Wie in rjochte wei. Der kaem in lykstaesje lâns, mar dy hat er net sjoen. 't Gebeurde hjir yn 'e Westerein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30364,"r":"CJ112902","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A boy has repeatedly seen a funeral procession pass at night. When the boy greets it, his greeting is never returned. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ierde Prins fan 'e Westerein hie forkearing mei in faem yn Twizelerheide. Forskillende kearen is 't him oerkaem, dat er ûnderweis in lykstaesje seach. Dat wie dan altyd yn 'e nacht. Ierde sei dan tsjin dy minsken Goedenavond, mar hy krige noait gjin antwurd werom, hwant it wienen gjin èchte minsken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30366,"r":"CJ112904","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Children are warned never to walk in the middle of the road at night, since a passing funeral procession may strike them.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem sei altyd: tink der om, rin nachts noait midden op 'e wei, hwant dan kinst in stomp fan in lykstaesje krije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30388,"r":"CJ113020","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman sees a funeral procession pass. It is a premonition: later someone really does die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn frou hat op ljochtskyndei op 'e Boppewei in lykstaesje sjoen. It wie in spûkbigraffenis. Letter gyng dêr in echte lykstaesje lâns. 't Wie foargedrús.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30390,"r":"CJ113022","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You should never walk in the middle of the road at night, since a passing funeral procession may drive you off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By nacht mat in minske noait midden op it paed rinne, wol er net fan 'e wei treaun wurde troch in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30430,"r":"CJ113111","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People born with a caul often foresee deaths in passing funeral processions. You should never walk in the middle of the road at night, because you may end up in a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon seagen lykstaesjes fan tofoaren. Dat gebeurde hiel folle. Sokken wienen mei de helm geboaren. Midden op 'e wei rinne by nacht wie gefaerlik. Jy koenen dan tsjin sa'n lykstaesje oprinne.\nIt wie in eigenaerdich forskynsel. Der wie neat en dochs wie 't in bigraffenis. Wienen der twa, en ien dy seach it, dan sei er: Even oan kant, der mat hwat passeare, dat mat rûmte ha.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30855,"r":"CJ113902","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A woman born with a caul urges people to step aside for a passing funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De wenne in frou yn Wâlterswâld, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. As der ien mei har oproun koe 't gebeure dat se sei: \"Even oan kant, der komt in lykstaesje oan.\" 't Wie Geale Postma syn frou.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30886,"r":"CJ114110","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man foresees that another man will lose his daughter: he sees the funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining ^ fan Boelensloane hie sjoen dat Frans Tuinstra in famke forlern hie. De hiele lykstaesje hat er sjoen mei alle minsken dy't der achter roannen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30962,"r":"CJ114708","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"When you are out at night, you should keep well to the side of the road, or else a funeral procession may drive you aside.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Is men by nacht op in paed, dan mat men altyd oan kant gean, hwant dan is der gefaer. Dan kin der wolris in lykstaesje oankomme dy't jin oan kant set.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30970,"r":"CJ114716","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"At night someone is driven to the side of the road by an invisible funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw ien kend, dy is ris troch in lykstaesje oan kant set. 't Gebeurde by nacht. Hy hie neat sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":129753,"r":"VODA_022_19","p":"Eindhoven","v":"N.-Br.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Someone born with a caul: has second sight; is not wounded as a soldier; does not drown as a sailor; draws a lot exempting him from conscription; is good at learning. If the caul fell into someone else's hands, the person born with it had to clear away obstacles for the funeral processions he saw. This happened at night.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Ben Janssen: ‘’Uh, hij kon voor als soldaat, kon ‘t niet gewond raken. En als zeeman kon ie niet verdrinken. En als loteling lootte hij vrij. Hij kon in de toekomst kijken. Hij kon iemands dood voorspellen. Maar hij leerde ook erg vlot op school. Nou ik wou even nog, meneer Brand, teruggaan op het feit dat ‘t.. Eene helm niet verkocht mocht worden. Of niet begra.. Of uh wel begraven mocht worden, maar niet verkocht mocht worden, of ook niet dat de vroedvrouw of de dokter met die helm ging lopen. Want dan, dat was heel gevaarlijk voor dat kind, want dan moest dat kind, moest dan zelf in de begrafenisstoeten die hij zag, moest ie dan meelopen.’’\nJaap Brand: ‘’Ah.’’\nBen Janssen: ‘’Uh, niet zozeer om in die begrafenisstoet mee te lopen, maar dan moest hij wel de, de, de obstakels, die de begrafenisstoet tegenkwam, moest ie dan uit de weg ruimen.’’\nJaap Brand: ‘’Nee..’’\nBen Janssen: ‘’Dus hij moest voor de begrafenisstoet uitlopen om de obstakels uit de weg te ruimen. Kwam dan ook meermalen voor vroeger dat een boerenknecht, die met de helm geboren was, plotseling ’s nachts uit bed moest, met alle geweld – die kon niet in bed blijven – uit bed moest, de deur uitvloog en het erf opliep en alle hekken openzette.’’\nJaap Brand: ‘’Aha. Ja, ja, ja, ja.’’\nBen Janssen: ‘’Daar heb je wel eens van gehoord misschien?’’\nJaap Brand: ‘’Daar heb ik wel eens van gehoord. Om de stoet door te laten g"},{"n":129745,"r":"Voda_022_12","p":"Eindhoven","v":"N.-Br.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Between twelve and one at night someone saw a funeral that took place five days later.","i":"H.E.","o":"In Eersel, daar zag vroeger een inwoner ’s nachts tussen twaalf en één uur een rouw voorbij trekken. Voorop zag hij vier dragers met de lijkbaar. Achter hen stapte twaalf mannen met rouwmantels om en omfloerste hoed en verder veertien vrouwen in falies gewikkeld. Vijf dagen later werd zijn buurman begraven. Gevolgd door evenveel mannen en evenveel vrouwen als hij die nacht gezien had."},{"n":129749,"r":"Voda_022_16","p":"Eindhoven","v":"N.-Br.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A clergyman saw his own funeral. Four men with a bier kept walking behind him all night. He later died on that same road.","i":"H.E.","o":"Een geestelijke uit Oirschot zag eens zijn eigen begrafenis. Op een nacht ging hij van Oirschot naar Best. Daar hoorde hij achter zich iemand lopen. Toen ie omkeek, zag ie vier mannen die een baar droegen. Hij wilde wachten, maar toen hie stil bleef staan, bleven ook de dragers stilstaan. En als ie verder ging, gingen ook de dragers verder. Zo bleven deze vier mannen met de baar de gehele nacht achter de geestelijke lopen. Die was blij dat ie eindelijk in Best aankwam, waar hij van de schrik kon bekomen. Enige tijd later moest de geestelijke weer naar Best. Daar stierf hij plotseling. Toen droeg men het lijk van de geestelijke over dezelfde weg die hij gelopen had toen de dragers met de baar hem volgden."},{"n":129751,"r":"Voda_022_17b","p":"Eindhoven","v":"N.-Br.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"When a man sat down on a doorstep, someone there died. He had been born with a caul, but someone else had stolen it. And so that man became a danger.","i":"H.E.","o":"En dan heb ik er hier nog eentje uit Waalwijk. Daar woonde vroeger een man waar iedereen erg bang voor was. Hij had het tweede gezicht. Als hij voor het huis van iemand op de stoep ging zitten, was het zeker dat er iemand in dat huis binnen drie dagen zou sterven. Iedereen die wilde, mocht over zijn linker schouder meekijken naar de lijkstoet die hij dan zag. Maar niemand durfde het, omdat men bang was zijn of haar eigen lijkstaatsie te zien. Bij zo’n man, die was dus met de helm geboren, maar dan had uh de dokter of de vroedvrouw uh de helm uh meegenomen, gestolen, zelf als amulet gebruikt. En zo’n man, dat was dus uh.. Die kon niet alleen vooruitzien, maar die was ook een gevaar, vanaf die tijd. Als een.. Als een kind op een.. Op ‘n stoep speelde, dan was er binnen drie dagen, in dat huis waarvoor dat kind speelde, een sterfgeval, als men die.. Dat vlies meegenomen had."},{"n":129752,"r":"Voda_022_18","p":"Eindhoven","v":"N.-Br.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Two people are sitting with a man on a cart, which suddenly stops for a funeral procession they do not see. Two days later a funeral procession passed that spot.","i":"H.E.","o":"Da is uh.. in, in Helmond gebeurd. Daar.. Is nog niet zo heel lang geleden. Daar was iemand die uh.. D’r waren twee personen en die zaten bij een voerman op de wagen. En plotseling stopt die wagen, en de voerman die licht zijn pet op en die zegt: ‘’We moeten een ogenblikje wachten want er komt een lijkstoet voorbij.’’ Want die andere mensen zagen niks. En toen zette die man uit.. Die voerman uit Helmond zette, een minuutje later, z’n pet weer op. En twee dagen naderhand kwam er op diezelfde plaats een lijkstoet voorbij."},{"n":129754,"r":"Voda_022_20","p":"Eindhoven","v":"N.-Br.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A child was pulled aside because a funeral procession was going to pass. In another case, another child had to take off his cap.","i":"H.E.","o":"Heb ik trouwens hier een verhaaltje van. Van een oude vrouw die mij eens vertelde dat ze als kind door haar grootmoeder opzij werd getrokken met de woorden: ‘’Opzij, er komt een lijkstaatsie voorbij.’’ En ‘k heb er hier nog eentje van een vader die met z’n zoontje over de weg liep en die plotseling tegen z’n zoontje zei: ‘’Zet uw pet af, want er komt een lijkstoet voorbij.’’ Die jongen zag er niets van maar die vader wel, dus die vader was dus met de helm geboren. Zo zijn er nog heel veel meer voorbeelden te noemen, van mensen die met de voorloop, met de helm geboren zijn."},{"n":31918,"r":"CJ120508","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1978,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People born with a caul foresee deaths in passing funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn de Pein ha wol guon west, dy wienen mei de helm geboaren. Dy seagen fan tofoaren lykstaesjes, mar ik wit der gjin foarbylden fan to neamen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12966,"r":"YPFOE125b","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1978,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A midwife sees a funeral procession pass by. She is surprised, because as far as she knows nobody has died. A few moments later one of the three farmers who live at the nearest farm is standing there. He has probably had a fatal accident. A funeral exactly like the one the midwife has just seen follows shortly afterwards.","i":"Y.P.","o":"Lykstaasjes\nWy hienen foarhinne by ús heit-en-dy in âld baakster, Bouwe Bet. Dy rûn op in kear fan Wergea nei Warstiens en doe kaam har in lykstaasje tsjin. Se gong oan 'e kant stean en seach der mei alle studzje nei. Se tocht, dat is in frjemd spul—ik ha noait witten, dat hjir ien dea is. En doe in skoft letter stoar der ien fan'e trije boeren dy't dêr wennen. Hokker wit ik net, hy moat ferûngelokke wêze. Mar it kaam presys sa nei mei dy begraffenis as Bouwe Bet it tefoaren sjoen hie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":12972,"r":"YPFOE125h","p":"Hollum","v":"Fr.","y":1978,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A clairvoyant woman sees a funeral procession come out of the schoolhouse in the middle of the night. The fourth man in the procession is wearing a grey suit, which is still very unusual at that time. Later someone does indeed die in the schoolhouse. The fourth man at the funeral is wearing a grey suit.","i":"Y.P.","o":"Lykstaasjes\nDer war hier un ôde frouw, deer diende ik as mêske. Dy frouw fe'telde: 'Ut war aves laat, of midden in 'e nacht en ik keek út op ut skoalhus. Ut war maanlicht. Dan gaat de deur open, in der kwam hier un Iykstaasje foa'bij'. Dat was nyt echt, dat saag se. In de fie'de man had un griis pak an. Ut war doe nog heel ongewoan om op un begraffenis met un griis pak te lopen.\nIn doe later ging der ien doad in utselde skoalhús. In bij de begraffenis had de fie'de man un griis pak an.\n(Nes, Amelân)","l":"Fries"},{"n":31325,"r":"CJ116613","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"You should not walk in the middle of the road at night: a funeral procession may drive you aside.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne. Men rint dan de kâns dat men troch in lykstaesje oan kant reage wurdt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31575,"r":"CJ118604","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"One evening a man sees a hearse pass carrying the coffin of a young person. It is a premonition: shortly afterwards a fourteen-year-old girl dies. On the day of the funeral the man stands at the same spot where he had the premonition.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Binne-om roun ris op in joun achter op 'e Sumarreheide Romke de Vries syn reden del en kaem sa by pake Tamme.\n\"Heit,\" sei er, \"hwat hie 'k nou in nuver gefal. Niis is der my in lykkoets foarby riden. Dêr stie in kiste op; 'k soe sizze foar ien fan in jier 13, 14.\"\nIt gebeurde de wyks dêrop dat de dochter fan Joeke Veenstra stoar. It bern wie 14 jier âld. De deis dat hja nei 't hôf brocht waerd stie Binne-om op itselde plak, dêr't er in dei of hwat lyn dy lykstaesje sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31577,"r":"CJ118606","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man urges a companion to step aside for a passing funeral procession. The companion pays no attention to this 'talk', but a moment later he is driven aside by an invisible funeral procession. Later the new cemetery was built on the spot where it happened.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn swager Anne Veenstra fan 'e Harkema wie mei syn maet op in joun bûten op 'e wei. Syn maet wie Wyberen.\nDoe sei Wyberen tsjin him: \"Dû mast der om tinke, dêr komt in lykstaesje oan.\"\n\"Ei, dû mei dyn praetsjes\" sei Anne, en hy gong net oan kant.\nMar hy waerd oan kant smiten, sûnder dat er hwat seach.\nOp datselde plak is letter it nije bigraefplak yn 'e Harkema kaem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31791,"r":"CJ119703","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A boy who often has premonitions predicts that a sick man will not recover, as his son thinks, but will soon die. The clairvoyant has already seen the hearse. The premonition comes true: a few years later the sick man dies, and the hearse is exactly the one the boy saw before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn soan sjocht de dingen soms foarút. Op in kear praette er mei syn maet. Dy syn heit wie siik. Mar de soan sei: \"Hy knapt aerdich op de lêste tiden. Hy sil wol gau wer de âlde wurde.\"\nMyn soan sei: \"Dat kinstû wol sizze, mar ik haw sjoen dat er mei de boerewein nei 't hôf brocht wurdt.\"\nIt wie yn Garyp. In pear jier letter wie de man dea.\nDe lykstaesje op in boerewein wie krekt sa, lyk as myn soan it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31793,"r":"CJ119705","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A clairvoyant who often has to get up at night to see funeral processions takes along his friend, who refuses to believe he has premonitions of deaths. When the procession does approach, the clairvoyant urges his friend to step aside, but the friend sees nothing and stays put. Shortly afterwards he is flung onto the verge, struck by the horse pulling the hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Greate Sjoerd wie ek sa'n man dy't der soms yn 'e nacht út moest om nei bigraffenisstoeten to sjen.\nJurjen van der Leest hat in kear mei him west. Dat hie er Jurjen biloofd, as der wer sa'n gefal wie soe Jurjen der by wêze. Jurjen woe dat graech ris bilibje. Doe naem er Jurjen mei oan 'e Sânwei-bosk ta, krekt by de âld tramwei. Dêr hat doe in lykstaesje west. \"Oan kant, oan kant\", sei greate Sjoerd tsjin Jurjen. Mar Jurjen hie neat sjoen en wie stean bleaun. Mar fuort dêrnei lei er yn 'e berm. It hynder hie him oan kant stompt.\n\"En dòch haw ik noait hwat sjoen\", sei Jurjen letter.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31894,"r":"CJ120303","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A young man sees a funeral procession approaching. According to him the coffin is not that of an adult. It is a premonition: shortly afterwards a young girl dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn pake Tamme hat wenne yn in hûs, dat [op] in kampke lân achter dat fan myn broer Tamme stie op 'e Gariperheide (it wurdt altyd by Sumarreheide rekkene). Pake wenne dêr mei twa soannen: Jelle en Binne, dy't doe noch net troud wienen.\nOp in joun kaem Binne let thús. Hy sei tsjin Jelle: \"Dêr hie 'k in nuvere moeting nyskes. Dêr kaem my in lykstaesje yn 'e mjitte. De kiste stie op 'e wein. 't Wie net ien foar in folwoechsenen ien.\"\nAl gau dêrnei stoar dêr op 'e heide in fanke fan ± 17 jier.\nDoe seach Binne deselde bigraffenis noch ris wer, mar nou yn werklikheit.\nDy nachts wie er oan kant gien. Dat fanke skreau har van der Heide.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31973,"r":"CJ121014","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul foresees a death in a passing funeral procession. The premonition comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e wei fan Gariperheide nei Garyp hawwe se ris yn 'e nacht de lykstaesje sjoen fan in broer, dy't 14 dagen letter stoarn is. Syn beide foshynders rieden foar de wein.\nDy't dat seach wie mei de helm geboaren, seinen se, dy wy heldersynde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31989,"r":"CJ121108","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man born with a caul is often driven out of bed at night to foresee deaths in passing funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Westerein wenne in man, Bontsje Keke. Se seinen, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy seach nachts lykstaesjes. Dy mòest er sjen, dan koe er net op bêd lizzen bliuwe.\nIn pear dagen letter wie dan meastal de èchte bigraffenis.\nMar hy hie dan alles al fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31990,"r":"CJ121109","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"People never walk in the middle of the road, because a funeral procession may push them aside.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De minsken roannen hjir noait midden op 'e wei. Oars koenen se troch in lykstaesje oan kant reage wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32223,"r":"CJ123301","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"In the middle of the night a man sees a funeral procession. From the people walking behind the hearse he concludes that his neighbour has died. It is a premonition: a week later the neighbour dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Krúswei yn 'e Harkema seach Fokke Veenstra midden yn 'e nacht in lykstaesje. Oan it folk dat achter de lykwein roan koed er sjen dat it lyk fan ien fan 'e buorlju wie. In wike letter stoar syn buorman.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32224,"r":"CJ123302","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A mother urges her children to walk on the verge late in the evening, because a funeral procession could drive them off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As wy jouns let noch om boadskip moesten foar ús mem om foar 2 sinten griene oalje to heljen om dêr in ierappel yn to brieden, sei se: \"Pas op, bern tink der om en rin yn 'e berm. Dêr kin jim ris in lykstaesje tomjitte komme.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32280,"r":"CJ123908","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1980,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"A man sees a funeral procession floating a metre above the ground. It is a premonition.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us pake seach ris in bigraffenis foar him. Dy wie sahwat in meter boppe de groun. Dy sweefde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":128660,"r":"ENGELB_19_029","p":"Weerselo","v":"Ov.","y":1983,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Name of a bogeyman in the rye field; do not walk in the middle of the road.","i":"H.E.","o":"S: Zeeman, vrogger ha'j de rogge almoal an akkers en dan zatn der van dee grupn tusn. Dan mogn wie der nich in, want dan kwam de zeeman oe teegn.\nE: Zeeman in de row doar?\nS: Joa. Dan kwam de zeeman oe teegn, doar mogn ie nich in.\nE: Dat he'k nooit heurd.\nS: De zeeman, zeadn ze dan.\nE: Ne zeeman in de row hè?\nS: In de grupn dee der tusn deurleupn. In de grupn dee der tusn deurleupn.\nE: Dat he'j oet Slaghaarn. Nich hier. Doar he'k nooit wat van heurd.\nS: Moeder de zeeman. Dat wör altied zegd, ie möt nich in de row grupn loopn, want dan kwam de zeeman oe teegn. Doar dusn ie van schrik nich in.\nE: Dat is t zölfde ok met den liekweg, Schleepers, a'j doar owwer henlöapn, dan kon ok ineens passeern, da'j de liekwaag ok tegn kwamn, en vuural a'j tusschen de spuurs duur löapn. Dat zöagn ie nich, mer ineens, dan kreagn ie ne klap, ie völn umdaal, dan mos dee koets mos der langs.","l":"Twents"},{"n":42673,"r":"RKOMA143","p":"Kaatsheuvel","v":"N.-Br.","y":1983,"c":"SINSAG 0481","d":"Around midnight the sound of bells can be heard at the Kerkenakker in Kaatsheuvel and a funeral procession can be seen. The horse of Jan B. and Just once bolted when singing could be heard. Whoever digs a hole in the ground and puts his ear in it hears the singing.","i":"R.A.K.","o":"'Er gebeurden wonderbare dingen bij die akker [RK: vlakbij de 'alde kercke' was de 'Kerkenakker']. Oudere mensen ter plaatse weten te vertellen, dat hun grootvader of overgrootvader er 's nachts een begrafenissttoet heeft zien rondtrekken en wie er 's nachts rond twaalf uur een kuiltje graaft en er zijn oor aan te luisteren legt, kan er klokken horen luiden. De begrafenisstoet bestond meestal uit een oude lijkwagen met paarden ervoor en een aantal wenende mensen erachter.\nBekend is b.v. het verhaal van Jan B. en zijn broer Just. Het zal nu ongeveer honderdentien jaar geleden zijn, dat zij met paard en kar op een stormachtige novemberavond door de Waalwijkse baan reden. In de buurt van de 'Kerkenakker' aangekomen, weerklonk er plotseling op de akker een gezang. Het paard sloeg van schrik op hol en kon pas in de Grotestraat te Waalwijk tot staan worden gebracht. Zo zijn er nog enkele verhalen over de 'Kerkenakker' bekend, maar ik zou zeggen, overtuig u zelf en ga een keer rond het middernachtelijk uur naar deze plaats en graaf een kuiltje in de grond of luister of je het gezang hoort.'"},{"n":69799,"r":"DYKFRIES2195","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"In 1865, near Poppingawier, a farmer had a vision of a funeral. Over the coffin lay a white sheet, indicating that a woman had died in childbed. To make sure this would not happen to his own wife, he made an alteration to the house. Later he moved away to live elsewhere. His successor undid the alteration, but not long afterwards his wife died in childbed and everything happened exactly as the farmer had seen.","i":"W.D.","o":"In 1865 is het gebeurd dat een boer in de nabijheid van Poppingawier het verschijnsel eener begrafenis te zien kreeg. Hij zag dat een doodkist met een wit laken er over, ten teeken dat er het lijk eener kraamvrouw in lag, de hoofd- of lijkdeur van zijn huis werd uitgedragen. <<Dat zal mijne vrouw niet gebeuren,>> zeide hij bij zichzelven. En den volgenden dag liet hij die deur uit den muur nemen en de opening dichtmetselen. Eenigen tijd daarna vertrok deze boer metterwoon naar elders. Zijn opvolger op de plaats te Poppingawier vond de weggenomen deur met het kozijn nog bewaard. Hij achtte 't beter en gerijfelijker, dat zij weêr in den muur werd gezet. Kort daarna overleed zijne vrouw in het kraambed en zij werd die deur uitgedragen, op dezelfde wijze als de vorige boer het vooruit gezien had."},{"n":69800,"r":"DYKFRIES2196","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A minister's wife sees her own coffin and funeral. Her husband will not believe her, but when the woman gives birth for the second time, she dies in childbed. Everything goes exactly as she had foreseen, despite the minister's attempts to prevent it.","i":"W.D.","o":"Sommige menschen zien hun eigen dood vooruit. Het is reeds langer dan tweehonderd jaren geleden, dat de predikantsvrouw te Pietersbierum, op zekeren nacht naast haren man te bed liggende, midden in het vertrek eene doodkist zag staan. Zij was eene moedige vrouw en tevens nieuwsgierig: zij verliet het bed om te zien wie er in de kist mocht liggen. En tot haren niet geringen schrik zag zij daar haar eigen beeld in doodsgewaad. Zij wekte haren man en verzocht hem ook te zien. Hij zag echter niets, berispte haar over hare dwaze inbeelding en gaf haar den raad te gaan slapen. Zij begaf zich wel weêr te bed, maar kon niet rusten en evenmin het oog van die kist of houden. Het duurde niet lang of er kwam een man, gekleed in een rooden hemdrok binnen de kamer. Hij nam eenige schroeven van den schoorsteenmantel en schroefde het deksel op de kist. Nu werd er een witte doek over gehangen, waarop de dragers kwamen en de kist weghaalden. Daar nu de vrouw zich in zwangeren staat bevond, maakte dat gezicht haar nog weer beangst. Haar man, die niets had gezien, schreef alles toe aan ziekelijke verbeelding. En met dien man in den rooden hemdrok was het tenminste gekheid, meende hij, omdat er in het geheele dorp niemand was, die zulk een kleedingstuk droeg. De bevalling der vrouw, die kort daarop volgde, liep voorspoedig af. Zij bracht een flinken jongen ter wereld en toen deze na verloop van een"},{"n":8789,"r":"CBAK0174","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"The informant and a group of friends have their fortunes told by a fortune teller at the fair. Most hear the usual things. One girl has to look behind her and to her horror sees her own coffin. A few days later she dies. A boy is told he will get an illness he will die of, which indeed happened.","i":"C.B.","o":"Hierop ging mijn verhaler voort: Ja, ik heb rare dingen beleefd. Ik was als vrijgezel met mijn meisje (zijn overleden eerste vrouw) met acht andere paren te Overleek te kermis. We besloten ons eens te laten waarzeggen, hoewel wij er niet aan geloofden (?).\nOpeens zei het wijf tegen één der meisjes: \"Nou, wees jij maar zoo vroolijk niet, kijk jij maar eens achterom.\"\nToen zij dat deed, werd ze zoo wit als een doek.\nMen vroeg natuurlijk waarvan zij zoo schrok en het antwoord luidde: \"Daar stond mijn eigen doodkist.\"\nDrie dagen later was zij een lijk.\nNou, aan de anderen werden de gewone foefjes verteld van hoeveel kinderen ze zouden krijgen, dat ze een erfenis zouden krijgen enzovoort, enzovoort.\nMaar tegen den broer van Willem Kennedy, die nou nog in Broek woont, zei ze, toen hij schoppen of klaveren aas trok (dit wist mijn zegsman niet precies meer): \"Dat is ook niet van het mooiste, man.\"\n\"Wat zou dat dan?\" zei hij.\n\"Wel, jij krijgt een fistel en sterft er aan.\"\nWerkelijk heeft hij later een fistel gekregen, en heeft het sigarenmaken nog moeten leeren om in huis nog wat te kunnen verdienen. Eindelijk is hij gestorven. Zo kunnen ze het soms toch wel eens goed hebben ook."},{"n":9419,"r":"CBAK0558","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"Young people have their fortunes told at the fair for fun. One girl, who looks back when told there is nothing to be cheerful about, sees her own coffin standing there. Three days later she has died. A man is told he will get a fistula and die of it.","i":"C.B.","o":"Het was kermis te Overleek (tusschen Monnikendam en Ilpendam). Een Zuiderwouder ging er heen met zijn meisje en nog acht andere paren. Voor de aardigheid besloten ze zich eens te laten waarzeggen, hoewel ze er geen geloof aan hechtten (?).\nOp eens zei het wijf tegen één van de meisjes: \"Nou wees jij maar zoo vrolijk niet, kijk jij maar eens achterom.\"\nToen ze dat gedaan had, werd ze zoo wit als een doek. De anderen vroegen natuurlijk, wat haar scheelde en het antwoord luidde: \"Daar stond mijn eigen doodkist.\"\nDrie dagen later was ze een lijk.\nNou, aan de anderen werden de gewone foefjes verteld, van hoeveel kinderen ze zouden krijgen, dat ze een erfenis te wachten hadden enzovoort, maar tegen den broer van W.K., die nu nog in Broek woont, zei zij, toen hij schoppen- of klaverenboer trok (dat weet ik zoo precies niet meer):\n\"Dat is ook niet van het mooiste, maat.\"\n\"Wat dan,\" vroeg hij.\n\"Wel, jij zult een fistel krijgen en daaraan sterven,\" zei het wijf.\nEn dat is uitgekomen ook. Hij heeft later een fistel gekregen, moest zijn gewonen boerenwerk na eenigen tijd opgeven en heeft het sigarenmaken moeten leeren om in zijn onderhoud te voorzien. Ten slotte is hij er aan gestorven.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.112.)"},{"n":15733,"r":"CJ002910","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A soldier on leave during the First World War goes home. On the way he sees the coffin of his own child. A few days later his child dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e oarloch fan '14 op '18 wie in soldaet op reis nei hûs ta mei forlof. Hy wenne yn Kollum.\nDoe seach er ûnderweis it kistje fan syn eigen bern. In dei of hwat letter kom it bern to forstjerren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15736,"r":"CJ002913","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man from Twizelerheide [Twijzelerheide] is lying in bed and sees a coffin being carried inside. He wonders whether it is meant for him. A few weeks later a girl from Hamsterheide comes to stay, and she dies. The coffin is carried in just as the man had seen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Twizelerheide lei yn 'e nacht in man op bêd. Doe seach er, dat der in kiste by him ta 't hûs yn brocht woarde. Hy tocht: \"Soe ik dêr yn matte.\" Mar in wike of hwat letter kom der in dochter út 'e Hamsterheide by him útfanhûs. Dy kom dêr ûnforwacht to forstjerren. Sy brochten de kiste ta de keamer yn krektlyk as hy it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21807,"r":"CJ0287A13","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1951,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"One night a farmhand, Jan, sees a coffin with a dead person in it standing in the room. Jan cuts a lock of hair from the dead person. The next morning Jan himself has a piece missing from his hair. Frightened, Jan quits his job and flees. When weeks later he nevertheless returns to his old master, he promptly drops dead in the farmyard. His coffin is placed in the same spot Jan had seen earlier. It was a vision of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Burgumer Nijstêd wenne in feint by in boer. Dy feint seach op in nacht in deakiste oer de flier stean. Hy hiet fan Jan. Hy miende dat er droomde. Hy frege: \"Och heden, hwa mat dêr yn?\" Deselde dy't yn 'e kiste [lei] sei: \"Jan.\" Doe gong Jan fan 't bêd ôf en hy nom de skjirre en hy knipte deselde dy't yn 'e kiste lei in stik út it hier.\nDe oare moarns sei de boerinne tsjin 'e feint: \"Heden Jan, dû hast in stik út it hier.\"\nJan woarde bleek doe't er dat hearde en hy makke maeije mei de lju. Hy woe der net langer bliuwe. Hy bistege him ergens oars. Mar nei forrin fan in jier twa, trije, woed er syn âld boer doch us wer opsykje.\nHy giet der hinne, mar falt samar dea del op it hiem. De kiste kom op it plak to stean, dêr't Jan altyd slept hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":131038,"r":"KEUNING003804","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man who has seen a coffin standing in the bedroom no longer wants to live in the house and leaves his wife. Shortly after he has gone back to his wife, he dies.","i":"S.K.","o":"A. fan K.H. kaem op in nacht thús. Doe hy op bêd soe seach hy, dat der in deakiste foar syn bêd stie. Hy stapte der oer hinne en gong op bêd. Fan binaudens birolle hy him hielendal yn de tekkens. De oare moarns sei hy, dat hy net langer yn it hûs wenje woe. Hy gong by it wiif wei en wer by de âldeljue yn. Letter kaem hy dochs wer by syn wiif, mar doe wie hy ek gau dea.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131073,"r":"KEUNING004010","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A son who sees a coffin standing in front of the door fears that his sick mother will die. She says she will live another five years. After five years she dies, and the coffin stands in front of the house with the pall blowing up, as seen before.","i":"S.K.","o":"Heit kaem ris op in joun thús. Doe seach hy in deakiste foar de doar stean. It kleed, dat oer de kiste laei, waeide hwat omheech. Beppe wie doe krekt siik. Heit wie bang, dat hja stjerre soe. Hy fortelde yn de hûs ek, hwat hy sjoen hie.\n\"Meitsje dy mar net ûngerêst\", sei beppe. \"Ik libje noch wol fiif jier.\"\nFiif jier letter wie beppe dea en de kiste stie krekt sa foar it hûs, sa 't heit it sjoen hie. En ek nou waeide it kleed omheech.","l":"Fries"},{"n":43206,"r":"WEV005704","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man who sees a coffin being brought into his house and which people are present turns out to have seen his own funeral.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop\nIn ain van de veenkolonies heft n vent woond, dei zien aigen begravvenis zain het. Zien moeke het 't aan mien mouder verteld. t Was n male, onverschillige vent. \nOp n dag zèg e teegn zien moeke:\n“Kiek es, wordt n kiste bie ons in huus brocht. \nDei is dr bie en dei.”\nZai zee nog:“Stil, jong, wordst dr kold van.”\nHai zag nait, dat t veur homzulf bestemd was.\nMoar n joar noatied is e sturven.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":130194,"r":"BIJLSMA000509","p":"Raerd","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A girl suddenly cannot go any further and tells her sweetheart that the coffin she sees standing on the road is for her. The girl dies that night.","i":"T.B.","o":"Dêr op 'e Greate Wierren wenne ek in boerefaem, dy't op in joun let troch har feint thúsbrocht waerd. Doe't hja in stikhinne oan 'e pleats ta wiene, bleau de faem stean: hja koe net fierder.\nDe feint sei: hwat is der to rêdden, skeelt dy hwat?\nHja sei: \"Dêr stiet in deakiste op it paed, sjochste it net?\"\nDe jongkeardel seach it net en sei: merakels, allegearre.\n\"Né,\" sei de faem, \"ik sjoch it klear, en ik moat yn dy kiste\".\nIn amerij letter wie it fuort en gongen hja nei hûs. Deselde nachts kaem de faem to forstjerren.","l":"Fries"},{"n":11499,"r":"CJ000208","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A house is haunted at night. Rattling is heard among the clogs, and then a coffin is carried up the ladder. The people move out, and afterwards everyone is afraid of that house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn it hûs fan Thys Jansma op 'e Tike spoeke it altyd by nacht. Earst wie der in gerattel tusken de klompen en dan waerd der in deakiste by de leider opdroegen. En dat joech altyd in bulte gedinder en gerattel. De minsken gyngen der út to wenjen. Elk wie sûnt bang foar dat hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":49778,"r":"GENDT127","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man sees a carpenter with a little coffin for a child. His wife sees nothing, but a few days later a child dies and the carpenter comes by.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Ik heb dorover duk iets heure vertelle, da bé’j ons ien de buurt zou gebeurd zien. Man en vrouw ware es same thuus. De vrouw zat te nèje bé’j ’t raam. Opens zèj de man: “Dor kumten timmerman on meed’n liekkisje vör ’n kiend op de schouwer”. De vrouw zèj: “Ik zie niks”. Mar ’n por dage lotter was er wel ’n kiend gesturve bé’j die minse, en kwam de timmerman wel meed’t kisje op de schouwer ien huus.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":12333,"r":"CJ001423","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"Hindrik Vaatstra saw a coffin standing in his yard. Some time later his wife died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hindrik Vaatstra seach mei eigen eagen in kiste op it hiem stean. Koarte tiid dêrnei kom syn eigen wiif to forstjerren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16829,"r":"CJ006216","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A woman often has to go out in the evening to see something. Once she sees a coffin standing in the middle of a narrow path. A cart could just get past. Later someone in the neighbourhood dies there. Another time she sees a wheelbarrow with a coffin in which no one was lying. The man for whom the coffin was meant died a few days later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha in buorfrou hawn, dat wie in sekere Janke.\nSy moest der nachts faek ôf, dan moest se hwat sjen.\nDoe seach se op in kear in deakiste op Hamsterheide. Dy stie op in smel paed, dêr koe net in wein lâns. Letter kom dêr ien to forstjerren, dy wenne bot achterôf en doe moesten se dêr lâns mei de kiste.\nEk seach se in kear in platte kroade mei in kiste der op. Doe wie 't al yn 'e moarn. Der wie neat yn dy kiste, de man leefde noch. \"Hea, hwat sil dit hjir wêze\", tocht se. In pear dagen letter woarde de kiste brocht. Doe wie dy man stoarn. Dat hie Janke sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17455,"r":"CJ009302","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"One night, while her husband is not home, a woman sees a coffin being carried into the house. The coffin is too small for the man and the woman and too large for the children. When she tells her husband the story, he no longer wants to live in the house and the family moves. Another family comes to live in the house; the sons are in poor health. One day one of the boys dies, and he fits exactly in the coffin the previous occupant had seen back then.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Surhústerfeanster Mieden wenne in húshâlding mei bern. It gebeurde al us op in nacht, wylst de man net thús wie, dat de frou in kiste seach. Dy woardde ta 't hûs yn brocht. Sy foun it fremd, hwant sa'n kiste wie foar har of har man to lyts en foar de bern wied er to great, dat sy bigrypte der neat fan. Doe't de man thús kom, fortelde se hwat der gebeurd wie.\n\"Nou wol ik hjir net langer bliuwe\", sei se, en sy forhuzen nei in oar plak.\nDer kommen oare minsken yn 't hûs to wenjen. Dy hienen twa jonges, dy 't sukkelen. Twa maend letter stoar ien fan dy jonges. Hy kom yn in kiste, krekt sa great as dy frou it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17663,"r":"CJ010702","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A boy takes part in a spiritualist séance. Suddenly he sees a coffin standing by the box bed. He looks away, but when he looks again, the coffin is still there. When he looks for the third time, the coffin is gone. A fortnight later the woman of the house dies and her coffin is placed in the same spot in front of the box bed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By Wopke Hoekstra oan 'e Spekloane op 'e Boelensloane hâldden se in spiritistyske séance. Myn jongste broer Megiel siet der ek by. Doe't er oerside seach, stie der by 't bêdsket in deakiste. Fuort seach er de oare kant wer út, mar doe't er wer nei 't bêdsket seach, stie de kiste der noch. Wer seach er in oare kant út, mar doe 't er foar de trêdde kear seach, wie de kiste fuort. \nFjirtsjin dagen letter stoar de frou dêr. De kiste kaem op itselde plak to stean, dêr't myn broer him sjoen hat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17683,"r":"CJ010802","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"When a boy comes home from work at night, he sees that the windows of the house are open. When he goes inside, there is a small coffin on the floor. When his little sister's health starts to fail, he sees the little coffin again. Now it stands outside against the wall. When the sister dies, the little coffin stands inside in the same spot where the boy first saw it. When the body is carried out, he runs hard after it. The little coffin is placed in the same spot by the wall that he had seen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is us in kear gebeurd, dan kaem ik thús fan 'e klaei. Dêr hie 'k oan 't wurk west. 't Wie sahwat ien ûre yn 'e nacht. De finsters fan ús hûs stienen heech opskoud en de gerdinen waeiden der troch hinne nei bûten ta. Ik seach ûnder 't finster troch. Der stie iten foar my op 'e kachel. Doe gong ik der yn en ik bigong to iten. \nDoe seach ik in lyts deafet oer de flier stean. Dêrnei gong 'k op bêd.\nDe oare moarns sei 'k: \"Hea, nou binne de finsters wer del.\"\n\"Hoe dàt sa?\" frege mem. Mar dêr hie 'k my hast forpraet, hwant ik woe net ha dat mem wite soe dat der mei koartens in deaden komme soe. Dêrom sei 'k : \"Ik ha droomd.\"\nIn goed healjier letter rekke myn jongste suster oan 't sukkeljen.\nIk kaem wer us op in joun thús en doe seach ik itselde deafet bûtendoar by de muorre stean. \nAl ridlik gau dêrnei kaem it bern to forstjerren.\nYn 'e hûs kaem it kistke op itselde plak to stean, dêr't ik it sjoen hie. Doe't it lyk nei bûten droegen waerd, roan ik it hurd achternei. En ja, hja setten it by de muorre del. \nDoe't heit my even letter forwiet, dat ik sa hurd nei bûten stoud wie, en dat op in bigraffenis, lei ik him it gefal út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17722,"r":"CJ011205","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A boy came home one night. The windows had been pushed open and the curtains were flapping outwards. In the corner of the room he saw his youngest brother lying in a small coffin. That was witchcraft. The child was already ill at the time and died soon afterwards. The boy had said nothing to his mother, so as not to make her sad. But when the child was dead, he told her he had already known, because he had seen the little body in a coffin.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us Boardzer kaem op in nacht thús, doe stienen de finsters by ús opskoud en de gerdinen wapperen nei bûten ta. \nDoe't hy der yn kaem, seach er yn in hoeke fan 'e keamer syn jongste broerke yn in deakistje lizzen. Dat wie allegear foartsjirmerije. Mar it bern wie doe al siik. Gauachtich dêrnei is it stoarn.\nBoardzer hie it net tsjin ús mem sein omt er har net treurich meitsje woe en fan 'e wize bringe. Mar doe't it bern goed en wol dea wie, sei er: \"Och mem, dat ha ik al lang witen dat jimme dat bern misse moesten. Ik hie syn lykje al yn 't kistje sjoen.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19535,"r":"CJ013303","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man once saw a coffin being carried into a hearse in front of a house. Not long after, the occupant of the house died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear kom ik by de faem wei sahwat om trije ûre hinne yn 'e moarn. Myn faem wenne ûnder Twizelerheide. Doe't ik yn Twizelerheide sels wie, tocht ik: \"Hwat is dàt.\"\nIt wie net tsjuster. Ik seach in lykwein en in hynder mei in kleed en mannen. Ik gong alhiel oan 'e kant fan 'e wei lâns. Ik wie der sahwat in hûslingte fanôf. De mannen droegen de kiste nei de wein ta en setten him dêr op. Ik sil sahwat fjouwer en twintich jier west ha en wie alhiel net bang.\nIn setsje letter stoar de man, dy't dêr yn dat hûs wenne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19568,"r":"CJ013508","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"Through the window of a house a man saw a coffin being slid out. The coffin was laid on the cart, and the women in the procession behind the cart wore rain clothes. Not long after, someone really died in the house, and everything happened exactly as the man had seen beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Rinse Hamstra seach us in kear, dat se yn Droegeham in deakiste net troch de doar krije koenen. Doe skouden se in finster omheech en dêr woarde de kiste troch skoud. Doe woarde de kiste op 'e wein set en hy seach it folk der achteroan. De froulju hienen regenkleden om. Sa gong de staesje toch de buorren. 't Wie jountiid.\nYn datselde hûs forstoar in skoftsje letter ien.\nDe kiste skouden se ûnder 't finster troch. Rinse hie alles foarút sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20848,"r":"CJ021812","p":"Aldeboarn","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A widow always sat on the same side of her sick son's bed. The woman had been born with a caul. When one day she sat on the other side, the boy understood that his mother had seen a coffin in the place where she usually sat. Three days later the boy died, and indeed the coffin was placed in that very spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Aldeboarn wenne in widdou mei in soan. Dy soan wie al tiden siik en lei op bêd. It woarde minder mei him. De mem hie har sit altyd op itselde plak yn it hoekje tsjin 't bêdsket oer.\nMar doe op in kear gong hja oan 'e oare kant de tafel sitten.\n\"Hwerom giet mem dêr sitten?\" frege de jonge.\n\"Ik wol dy ek us fan in oare kant sjen\", sei hja.\nMar de jonge koe syn mem wol. Hy wist, dat se mei de helm geboaren wie en hy sei: \"Dêr mat myn kiste aenst stean.\"\nTrije dagen letter stoar de jonge en de kiste kom op it plak to stean, dêr't de widdou altyd sitten hie.\nLetter fortelde hja, dat de jonge gelyk hawn hie. Hja hie dêr wei matten, hwant de kiste kaem der oan. Doe hie hja dêr net mear sitte kind. Dêrom wie hja nei de oare kant ta gien om to sitten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":44384,"r":"WEV013201","p":"Klazienaveen","v":"Dr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A coffin is seen on the threshing floor, which later turns out to be for the daughter. A friend bumps into something invisible; later a coffin is placed on that spot.","i":"F.W.","o":"O mensn, spookn en heksn, dei binnen er. Wordt nou ja niet veule meer over proot, maar vrogger.\nEn er gebeurn wonderlieke dingen heur.\nMien eign moe hef et metmaakt, dat ze ies op n keer in de schuur schrokn is. Ze giet naar achtern en dan ropt ze: “O, wat is dat?”\nMien va dr op af, maar die zag niks. Mien moe zag daar n kiste stoan. Ze dacht toen, dat olle oma wel staarvngung, die bie heur inwoonden; maar et wier mien zussien.\n\nZoiets gebeurn trouwens wel met meer mensn.\nEen kameroad van mie liet mie es n maal zien been zien. \nDe hiele scheen was blauw; ik heb et met mien eign oogn zien.\nIe was ook op de deel teegn wat aanloopn; ie vuulden et dudelk. \nEn toch stond r niks. Maar ook daar is later n liekkiste henzet. \nZukke dingen gebeurden vrogger.","l":"Drents"},{"n":16509,"r":"CJ005401","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"Next to the house in Zwaagwesteinde where the narrator lived in her youth lived a woman who had been born with a caul. Once she said that one of her boys would die. At night she had seen the coffin standing in the wrong corner of the room, because otherwise it could not be turned. Half a year later one of the neighbour's sons did indeed die. It went exactly as she had seen it.\nAnother time she had seen the narrator's parental home burning. Less than three months later it burned down. What that woman saw always came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Njonken ús yn 'e Westerein wenne in frou, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Op in kear sei se tsjin ús mem: \"Der komt ien fan ús jonges to forstjerren. Ik ha de kiste fannacht stean sjoen. Hy koe net op it plak stean dêr't er hearde, dan koenen se de swaei net krije, dat hy stie yn in forkearde hoeke yn 'e keamer. Ik ha der fannacht twakear út west. Beide kearen ha 'k hwat sjoen.\"\nUs mem leaude neat fan sokke praetsjes. Mar in healjier letter stoar ien fan 'e buorfrou har soannen. Se soenen de kiste op it plak sette, dêr't er hearde, mar dat koe net fanwege de swaei. It gong krekt sa lyk as hja it sjoen hie.\nOp in oare kear sei se tsjin ús mem: \"Fannacht ha ik jim hûs brânnen sjoen.\"\n\"Praetsjes\", sei ús mem.\nMar noch gjin fearnsjier letter brânde it op. It kom altyd nei, hwat dat minske seach.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20026,"r":"CJ016402","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A woman tells how she saw her uncle lying bareheaded in a coffin. When the uncle actually dies, he lies exactly as the woman had seen earlier. It was a vision of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem hat sels forteld dat hja Hindrik-om foar syn dea mei de bleate holle yn 'e kiste lizzen sjoen hie, krekt sa't hy der letter yn kom to lizzen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20027,"r":"CJ016403","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man sees his uncle lying in a coffin. A fortnight later the uncle actually dies: he lies just as the man had seen earlier. It was a vision of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Iksels ha Piter-om fan Eastemar (Piter Ophuis) fjirtstjin dagen foar syn dea yn 'e kiste lizzen sjoen. Hy lei op it iene wang, in bytsje oerside.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20031,"r":"CJ016407","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A clay worker suddenly sees a small coffin while at work. He hurries home, where his little son lies dying. He has only just got home when the boy dies. The little coffin was a vision of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mem har mem wie in suster fan Willem Ophuis. Dy wie us op 'e klaei oan 't wurk. Hy sliepte yn 'e skuorre yn 't strie by oare arbeiders.\nOp in joun sei er tsjin 'e oaren: \"Hwat jimme wolle, matte jimme wite, mar ik mat nei hûs ta. Ik ha dêr it kistje sjoen. Dêr mat ik by wêze.\"\nEn hy gong fuort op stap nei de Harkema. De hiele joun en de hiele nacht roan er troch. Doe't er thúskom lei syn jonkje op 't stjerren. Hy wie krekt op tiid kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20104,"r":"CJ016903","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"One night a woman suddenly can no longer move because she has to see something. A coffin stands against the wall. The woman tells her husband, who tells her to keep quiet. Seven years later the husband actually dies. His coffin stands in exactly the same spot the woman had seen earlier. It was a vision of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in nacht moest ik der ôf to pisjen. Doe't ik de pot krije soe, koe 'k my ynienen net mear forroere. Ik moest sjen. Doe stie der in deafet by my yn 'e keamer, tsjin 'e muorre oan, tsjin my oer. Ik gong nei Tseard ta (har man), dy't op bêd lei. Ik sei: \"Tseard, ik ha ús skeiding ek sjoen.\"\n\"Hâld dy stil en praet dêr net oer\", sei Tseard. 't Wie sawn jier letter, doe is Tseard stoarn. Syn deafet stie krekt op 't selde plak, dêr't ik it stean sjoen hie, tsjin 'e muorre oan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20113,"r":"CJ016912","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"The son of a woman who used to be clairvoyant turns out to have the same gifts his mother once had. One day he sees an empty coffin standing in the room. The mother predicts that it will be almost two years before her son dies. And indeed, within two years he dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Is nou fiif jier lyn, doe kom myn soan us by my. Hy wenne yn Jistrum. Ik seach wol oan him dat der hwat oan skeelde.\nHy sei: \"Sjocht mem noch wolris hwat?\"\nIk sei: \"Né, ik sjoch noait mear hwat en ik hear noait mear hwat. Dat hat de Heare my ûntnom.\"\nDoe sei er: \"Ik haw in eigenaerdich gefal hawn. Justerjoune, goed seis ûre, sieten wy by de itenstafel. Doe sei 't wiif: \"Ik ha de molke forgetten. Ik sil even guon helje.\" Dat sy gong der út en ik joech my salang del yn in greate stoel en dêr woarde ik slûch yn. Ik die de egen ticht. Doe hearde ik geskarrel yn 'e keamer. Ik sei tsjin 't wiif: \"Hwat biskripstû.\" Hwant ik miende dat hja der wie.\nMar sy wie der net en doe't ik de egen iepen die, stie der in deafet oer de flier. Ik gong der op ta. 't Wie net botte lang, mar wol breed. Ik roan der omhinne.\"\nIk sei: \"Jonge, lei der ek ien yn?\"\n\"Né,\" sei er, \"allinne in kessentsje.\"\n\"Dan wie dat dyn eigen deafet, jonge\", sei 'k.\nHy wie net great, mar wol moai dûbel.\n\"'t Wie om in ûre of seis hinne, seist, datst it seachste? Dan duorret it noch sahwat twa jier mei dy.\" Dat sei ik tsjin him.\nDoe hat er noch alle war dien om dêr wei to wenjen, mar hy koe net in oar plak krije. Hy woe 't ûntrinne, mar soks ûntrint men net. Binnen de twa jier wied er wei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20311,"r":"CJ018306","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"While at work, a clay worker suddenly sees his wife and child before him, together in a coffin. Shocked, he hurries home, where he actually finds what he had seen. It was a vision of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Beppe fortelde, dat der hie froeger in arbeider wenne oan 'e polderdyk, ûnder Aldegea, dêr't wy ek wenne ha.\nDy wie de klaei oer oan 't wurk. Doe seach er dêr yn 'e nacht syn wiif dea yn 'e kiste lizzen mei in dea popke by har. Hy is fuort nei hûs ta gong en doe't er thús kom lei syn wiif mei it popke al dea yn 'e kiste.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20609,"r":"CJ020407","p":"Tzummarum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"The husband of a pregnant woman once saw people carrying a coffin into his room. A few days later his wife died in childbirth, as did the baby. Then he saw exactly the same thing as a few days before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Rinse de Valk syn frou wie yn forwachting, dy forwachte in lytsen. Op in kear gong er it gongkje troch en soe nei de keamer ta. Doe't er yn 'e doar stie, seach er dat guon in kiste swaeiden yn 'e keamer.\nIn deimannich letter stoar syn frou mei de bifalling tagelyk mei it berntsje.\nDoe seach er dat de buorlju de kiste yn 'e keamer swaeiden. It wie krekt deselde draei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21185,"r":"CJ024705","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"One night someone saw a coffin being slid through a window. A few days later that really happened. The coffin would not go through the door.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Tike wie 't froeger allegear foartsjirmerije. Sa seach ien op in nacht, dat der in deakiste troch 't finster skoud woarde. In deimannich letter gebeurde dat èk. De kiste hie net troch de doar kind.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21405,"r":"CJ026605","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A young man was once visiting an elderly couple when he suddenly saw a coffin standing there. A fortnight later the woman was dead.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer wie us op in joun by Wopke Hoekstra syn âlden. Wylst er dêr sa siet seach er ynienen in deakiste oer de flier stean. Hy skrikte en seach gau ergens oars hinne. Doe't er wer seach wie de deakiste fuort.\nFjirtsjin dagen letter wie de frou dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21630,"r":"CJ027603","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"Two brothers were once out hunting polecats when one of them saw a coffin with a white cloth. The other saw nothing. A white cloth over a coffin meant that the person had died in childbirth.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek in kear, doe wienen wy der wer togearre op út to murdejeijen. Wy wienen achter it Dwarsdjip.\n\"Sjoch\", sei Wessel ynienen.\n\"Hwat sjochstû\", sei 'k.\n\"In kiste mei in wyt kleed der oer\", sei er.\nDan wie der ien yn 'e kream stoarn as der in wyt kleed oer de kiste lei.\n\"Ik sjoch neat\", sei 'k.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21633,"r":"CJ027606","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"One night the husband of a pregnant woman saw two men enter his bedroom and put a child's body in a coffin. When he got up, there was nothing to be seen. From then on the man was convinced that the child they were expecting would be stillborn. The child was not stillborn, but died a few hours after the birth.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wessel en Jan Opslach (= J. v.d. Heide) wienen us togearre yn 't boskje oan 'e Trije Roede. 't Wie yn 'e nacht. Der lei in stikje bou yn dat boskje. En dêr sieten faek hazzen yn. Dêr wie 't Wessel en Jan om to rêdden. Mar Wessel syn wiif wie oan 't omfallen ta. Mar dêr steurde Wessel him net oan. Sy sieten dêr stil op 'e hazzen to passen. Hwant mei 't berntsje kom it net goed. Dat hie Wessel fan tofoaren sjoen. \"Ik hoef my net to haesten,\" sei er tsjin Jan Opslach, \"ik ha 't lykje al sjoen.\"\nHy hie op bêd lein njonken syn wiif. Doe wienen der twa keardels yn 'e keamer kom. De iene hie in swart baerdtsje en in swarte snor. De oare hie allinne mar in snor. De iene hie in bernelykje yn 'e earm hawn en hie dat yn it kistje lein dat de oare droech. Doe hied er it kistje op 'e groun set. Mar doe hienen se 't kistje dêr wer wei krigen en yn in oare hoeke fan 'e keamer delset. Doe hienen se beide nei 't bêd sjoen en doe wienen se der út gong.\nWessel wie fuort fan bêd ôfkom en roan nei de doar ta. Mar alles siet fêst en der wie net in kistje to sjen.\nHwa wie dy man mei 't swarte baerdtsje? Dat wie Oebele Boomsma. Dy wie krekt út Dútslân weikom fan 't wurk. Hy hie de snor en 't burd groeije litten. De oare wie Hindrik Bekkema. Dat wienen de beide mannen dy't it kistje dêr delset hienen.\nWylst Wessel en Jan dêr yn 't boskje sieten, hearden se ien roppen.\n\"'k Hoef der net hinne,\" sei Wesse","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":46183,"r":"WEV016404","p":"Gasselternijveen","v":"Dr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A pregnant woman sees a little coffin standing on a chair. The child lives only a short time, and the little coffin stands on that very chair.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mijn vrouw zag nog ergere dingen.\nZe kwam eens in de kamer en daar ziet ze op een stoel een lijkkistje staan. Zo iets wordt maar eventjes gezien, dan verdwijnt het weer.\nMijn vrouw was in verwachting; het kindje dat geboren is, heeft slechtskort geleefd. Het kistje stond op de bewuste stoel."},{"n":46270,"r":"WEV017601","p":"Muntendam","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"The father of a sick child sees the door open and a man place a small coffin on the threshing floor. After the child has died, the coffin is placed on the spot where he saw the man put it down.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nAin Muntndammer vertelde mie:\n“Wie harn n kind zaik. Ik zat op n oavend nog loat op en de vrouw was al op berre. Opains gait de deure lös en n kerel kompt binnen en zet n liekkissie op dele. Ik schrik door zo van, dat k moar gauw biet wief onder de deekns schoot. tWur mie te kold heb ik teegn heur zegd. \nOns kind is sturm en t kissie kwam op t stee te stoan, woor ik t zain har.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":22021,"r":"CJ031407","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"At night a woman very clearly sees a coffin with a cat on it in her room. The cat jumps to the floor with a thud and starts climbing up the woman's body from the foot of the bed. It is a nightmare. The wife of a later occupant comes to lie in the coffin. It is a vision of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik lei op bêd. 't Wie hjir yn dit hûs. Ik seach in deakiste. Op dy kiste wie in kat. Dy kat sprong mei in plof op 'e groun. De kiste seach ik tige dúdlik. De hantfetten en alles koe 'k bêst ûnderskiede.\nDoe kaem der hwat by my op bêd. Ik lei op 'e rêch. Datselde kaem op 't fuottenein by my en gong sa by my op oan 'e hals ta. Ik koe net sjen hwat it wie. En ik koe gjin lûd jaen. Ik koe my ek net omdraeije.\n't Wie in nachtmerje. Ik hie 't ôfgryslike binaud.\nDy kiste dy't ik doe sjoen ha, dat is neikaem. 't Wie de kiste fan in great-minske.\nKlaes de Ruiter kaem letter yn ús hûs to wenjen.\nSawn jier neitiid stoar syn frou. Har kiste hie ik sjoen.\n(Vraag: hoe kon dat in het huis waar ze nu in woont?)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22767,"r":"CJ035318","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A girl foresees that her mother will die during the night because she has seen her lying in a coffin. The vision comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Lammert Smeding yn Twizel hie in dochter. Dat wie doe in fanke fan sahwat in jier of tolve. Sy gong nei skoalle ta, myn frou siet by har yn 'e klasse. Doe kom se op in kear yn skoalle, doe sei se: \"Us mem giet fannacht ek dea. Ik ha der fannacht ôf west en doe ha 'k har yn 'e kiste lizzen sjoen.\" Myn frou hat it sels heard en 't is ek gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22934,"r":"CJ036721","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man warns his wife to step over a small coffin he has seen standing in the room. Seven years later the couple lose a child. The little coffin is placed in the same spot the man had seen earlier.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wenne yn 'e Boelensloane by Bareld Bijma yn 't keammerke. Wy wienen krekt troud. Wy wienen sahwat seis en twintich jier en hienen al in pear bern.\n't Is nou sa'n fyftich jier lyn.\nWy leinen op bêd. Doe sei 'k tsjin myn frou: \"Ik ha hjir in kistje yn 'e hûs sjoen. Dêr matte wy oerhinne stappe as wy fan 't bêd ôfkomme.\nSawn jier letter ha wy in jonkje forlern. Wy wennen doe yn in oar hûs. Mar der wie oars gjin plak foar 't kistje of foar it bêd. Wy moesten der oerhinne stappe as wy út it bêd kommen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23520,"r":"CJ039803","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A young man once saw a coffin standing in front of a house. When he tried to touch it, his hand went through it. Not long after, a child from that house died, and the coffin was really there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear kom myn man op in joun let thús. Hy wie noch net troud. Doe seach er njonken har hûs yn 'e daem in kistje stean. Hy taestte der mei syn hân nei mar de hân gong der dwars trochhinne en doe wie it kistje ek wer fuort.\nNjonken myn man har folk wennen minsken, dy hienen in fremd famke yn 'e hûs, dat wie dêr bisteld. Dat hienen se dêr yn 'e kost. Dat bern stoar letter. En doe kaem dat kistje dêr by de daem to stean, krekt lyk as myn man it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23750,"r":"CJ041602","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"One night a woman saw an acquaintance lying in a coffin in a white garment. That same night the man had indeed died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy leinen us mei 't skip yn Kollum mei pulp.\nKoarte tiid tofoaren hie de ferver fan Stiensgea, Japik Groenland, ús skip fan binnen opferve. Mar doe't wy dan in skoftsje letter yn Kollum leinen, seach myn wiif Japik Groenland op in nacht yn 'e kiste lizzen. Hy hie in great wyt ding oan. 't Wie yn 1933. Yn dy selde nacht wie Japik Groenland yn Stiensgea stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24163,"r":"CJ044501","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"One night a man saw himself lying dead in a coffin. He took out insurance for ten thousand guilders. Then he died. His wife received the payout and married his brother.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Drachtster Kompenije wenne Klaas Schuurman. Dy wie troud. Hy seach op in nacht himsels dea yn 'e kiste lizzen. Doe liet er him forsekerje foar tsientûzen goune. Dêr moest wyks in ryksdaelder foar bitelle wurde. Doe't er de polis goed en wol hie, doe stoar er. Doe koe syn wiif útkearing krije en har letter rêdde. Hja is doe troud mei syn broer Harm.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24316,"r":"CJ045703","p":"Peize","v":"Dr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man suddenly sees a few men carrying a coffin along. It is an omen: the next day someone actually dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer wenne hjir yn Moarmwâld. Dy forlear in famke. Myn op-ien-nei-âldste broer wenne yn 'e Westerein. Dy moest biricht ha. Ik kom dêr in bulte, sadwaende moest ik it ek mar even sizze. Myn eigen fyts hie net in lantearne. 't Wie yn 'e hiele lette hjerst en op 'e joun. Ik liende in fyts yn Ikkerwâld fan in timmerman.\nDêr rekke ik mei nei myn broer ta yn 'e Westerein.\nIt siet dêr altyd gesellich, dat ik bleau dêr nochal lang, wol oan in ûre of acht, njoggen ta. Doe gong 'k werom. Sa kom ik op 'e hoofdwei. Doe hie 'k ynienen mannen foar my dy't in kiste droegen. Ik koe der hast net by lâns.\nSy raemden my yn 'e hage. Sy gongen troch 't hekje.\n'k Seach de minsken klear mei de kiste tusken har yn.\nDêr wenne in sike faem fan ien en twintich jier. Ane.\nIk tocht by my sels: \"Ane is dea.\" Dêr wie 'k wis fan. \nDoe't ik by myn broer kom, sieten heit en dy dêr ek. Ik sei, sa en sa. \"Ane is dea, se hawwe nyskes de kiste der hinne brocht.\" Ik wist net better of dat wie sa.\nDe oare deis die bliken, sy wie net dea. 't Hie foartsjirmerij west. Hwat muoide it my dat ik forteld hie dat se dea wie.\nDe jouns stoar se.\nIn skoft letter kom har heit by my. Dy hie heard hwat ik sjoen hie. \"Hastû it witten?\" frege er. Ik sei \"ja\" en fortelde him de tadracht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24384,"r":"CJ046113","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A woman hears sounds as if a coffin is being made ready. It is a portent of her own funeral: when she herself dies, the same sounds can be heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie in frou dy lei al skoften siik op bêd. It minske hearde op in kear dat se de kiste yn 'e hûs brochten. De hânsels klapten hwat. It deksel woarde opskoud. Dy lûden hearde se allegear. Sy fortelde dat oan har man.\nIn skoftsje letter stoar se. En doe gebeurden al dy dingen mei har eigen dea. De kiste waerd der ynbrocht en al sa mear. Hja hie de foarklank heard fan har eigen bigraffenis. Us heit hat dit wolris forteld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24667,"r":"CJ049201","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"At night a boy sees in the corner of the room a 'small wooden box with a black cloth over it'. It is a vision of the future: the following year the family loses a daughter. Her little coffin is placed in the same spot in the corner.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn jonge - Jehannes - wie in jier of tolve, hy gong noch nei skoalle. Wy wennen yn 'e Houtigehage.\nOp in kear gong hy der yn 'e nacht ôf en doe seach er skean nei in hoeke fan 'e keamer. Dêr bleau er mar nei stean to sjen.\nIk sei: \"Jonge, hwat sjochstû dêr?\"\n\"Ik sjoch in houten bakje,\" sei er, \"mei in swart kleedtsje der oer.\"\nSahwat in jier letter forlearen wy in lyts famke. Har kistje kom yn 'e hoeke fan 'e keamer to stean op it plak dêr't ús jonge doe nei seach.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25131,"r":"CJ051605","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man foresees the death of his own little son. He urges his mother to step aside for the coffin being carried through the hallway. The vision comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Letter hie Jan Visser nòch sa'n gefal, nou mei syn eigen jonkje. Doe wie er al troud en hy wenne yn Kollum. Dat wie doe't syn jonkje stoar.\nHy soe der krekt even op út mei syn mem, dy't by har yn wenne. Sy stienen al yn 'e gong. Doe sei Jan: \"Gean even oer side tsjin 'e muorre oan stean.\"\nHja gongen oer side.\nDer gong in kistje foarby. Jan seach it, syn mem net. Op dat stuit leefde it berntsje noch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25464,"r":"CJ054403","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"One evening a woman hears a sound as if something is being thrown on the floor. It is an omen: when her daughter is killed the next day, the coffin bearers make the same sound.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De jouns foar har dea woarde der hwat by ús oer de flier smiten.\nDoe seinen wy: \"Hark ris.\" Wy tochten dat de kat it die op 'e souder.\nMar letter, doe''t hja dea wie, kommen de dragers hjir en dy smieten twa bankjes oer de flier, dêr't de kiste op stean moest. Dat wie krekt itselde lûd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25736,"r":"CJ056602","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A woman once saw two men put a small coffin in the room, but in reality there was nothing. A few weeks later she lost a child, who had died of fits.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem hearde ris op in jountiid ien by de doar. Doe seach se dat der twa man ynkommen. Sy seach hiel dúdlik dat dy in baerke delsetten rjocht tsjin 'e muorre oan, hjir yn 'e keamer.\nHja siet yn 't hoekje fan 'e keamer. Sy woarde sa bleek as in doek. It swit bruts har út, sa binaud woarde se. Even letter wie alles wer fuort.\nIn pear wiken dêrnei kommen der echt twa man mei in baerke. Sy setten it op itselde plak del, dêr't mem it sjoen hie. 't Kistje wie der net.\nDoe hienen mem en dy in berntsje forlern, dat stoarn wie oan termynsetten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25868,"r":"CJ057502","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man came to his sick mother and saw a coffin in her house. But his mother was not dead and she lived another five years. Later the coffin really came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit syn mem wie o sa min. Mem wie nei har ta gong. Heit kom even letter. Hy wie oan 'e doar ta, doe stie dêr de kiste al, mei 't kleed der oerhinne. It kleed waeide in bytsje op, doe't de doar iepenkom.\nDoe't er yn 'e keamer stapte, wìe beppe der noch. Sy hat noch wol fiif jier leefd. Mar hwat heit foarút sjoen hie kom dêrom letter wol krektsa út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":46305,"r":"WEV018204","p":"Barger-Oosterveld","v":"Dr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man who has to climb in through the window at night steps on a coffin with an unknown dead person, from whom he cuts a lock of hair. When he sees the next day that he himself is missing some hair, he asks to be transferred. Years later he returns with his family to the boarding house, where he falls ill and dies. The coffin is placed on the spot where he once stepped on the coffin.","i":"F.W.","o":"Woar gebeurd.\nWas n keer n grenskemies bie ain in de kost. Op n nacht komt e in huus; deurn binnen dichte en doorom schoft hai n roam omhoog en krop dr deur. Hai schrikt, want hai stapt boovn op n liekkiste. Hai zugt ain lign, moar kent hom nait. Den pak e n mes en snit n plukje van t hoar van de dode of. Ander dag bie toafel bekikt hai ze allemoal, moar gainaine mist n stuk hoar. Noat eetn zugt hai in de spaigel en den maarkt e, dat e zulf n beetje hoar kwiet is. Gauw vragt e den overplaotsn aan en gait loater trouwn. Joarn goan veurbie en hai is t gebeurn in dei nacht misschien al vergeetn. Op n dag zegt e teegn zien vrouw: “Ik wil nog es n moal noar mien olle kosthuus van vrouger.” \nMit t haile gezin raizen ze dr hen. t Is dr aal nog goud en ze binnen bliede, dat ze mekoar zain. Moar den wordt de kemies door zaik en staarft. De kiste zetn ze onder t roam op stee, woor e joarn heer op stapt was.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":25605,"r":"CJ055614","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A young man once came home and saw the window open and the curtains flapping. On the floor he saw a small coffin. Not long after, his little brother died. The little coffin had to go out under the window. The curtains flapped exactly as the young man had seen earlier.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining, myn neef, kom us op in joun thús, doe tocht er: Hwat wappert dat by de glêzen. It glês wie omheechskoud en de gerdinen wapperen op 'e wyn. Der hie in deakistje oer de flier stien.\nKoarte tiid dêrnei stoar syn broerke. It kistje moest ûnder 't finster troch. 't Waeide nochal hwat, de gerdinen wapperen foar 't iepen finster.\nAlles hie krekt sa west lyk as hy it sjoen hie. (Boardzer is myn neef)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25896,"r":"CJ057608","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man who had been born with a caul was once at a farmer's. He told the farmer that he saw the little coffin of the farmer's son standing in the room and that this meant the child would soon die. Indeed the boy died fairly soon afterwards.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Douwe Stavasius syn heit Fokke wie us in kear op 'e klaei by in boer yn 't wurk.\nHy siet by de boer yn 'e keamer en sy dronken in pantsje thé. Fokke dy siet mar nei ien punt to staren en hy sei hielendal neat.\n\"Is der hwat?\" sei de boer.\n\"Dat kin ik jo net fortelle\", sei Fokke.\n\"Hwerom net?\" frege de boer.\n\"Omdat it jou jonkje is\", sei Fokke.\nDe boer hâldde oan, hy woe it wite. \"Fortel it my mar\", sei er.\nDoe sei Fokke: \"Jo sille jou jonkje misse.\" (It jonkje boarte wylst bûtendoar. De boer hie ek mar ien bern.)\nFokke hie it jonkje yn 't kistje lizzen sjoen, dat by harren yn 'e keamer stie. Dêr hied er sa nei stoarre.\nIt duorre net lang, doe stoar it jonkje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25906,"r":"CJ057707","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A woman once saw a coffin being brought into her house. It bumped against the door frame. Later her husband died, and the situation was exactly the same.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wenne in frou, dy seach dat se in kiste by harren yn 'e hûs brochten. Hy stompte tsjin 't kezyn oan.\nLetter stoar har man, doe wie dêr deselde sitewaesje. En ek deselde stomp. Dat hie hja fan tofoaren al heard en sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25939,"r":"CJ057904","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man saw a coffin being pushed into his house under the windowsill. Later his wife and children died, and a coffin really did come in under the windowsill.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mem fortelde ek: Us heit hie syn earste frou forlern en twa berntsjes, doe wenne er noch to Earnewâld.\nFoardat syn frou stoar hied er sjoen, dat se har kiste ûnder 't finsterbank troch skouden. Dat is letter ek gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26090,"r":"CJ058807","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A woman once saw a coffin pass by her mother. Not long afterwards the woman began to ail, and she died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Annemoai wie us by ús beppe yn 'e Rotfalle op bisite. Doe gong Annemoai der even út. Doe wie 't krekt as gong der in lykkiste by beppe lâns. Annemoai rekke oan it sukkeljen en frij koarte tiid dêrnei stoar se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27167,"r":"CJ063907","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"At night my brother hears noise at the doors and sees bearers carrying a coffin into the house. They tell him that his son is dead. The son is asleep, and later he does indeed die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer lei op bêd. 't Wie yn 'e nacht. Doe hearde er hwat by de doarren. Doe seach er dragers en in kiste, dy't se yndroegen.\nDer woarde tsjin him sein syn soan wie dea.\nOp dat momint lei syn soan op bêd to sliepen. Letter is er stoarn en gebeurden deselde dingen dy't myn broer doe sjoen hat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27265,"r":"CJ064405","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"Thomas and Clare live in Houtigehage and employ the boy Folkert. One day they see a coffin being carried into the house, but they cannot see who is lying in it. A short time later Folkert dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Thomas en Clare wennen op 'e Houtigehage. Sy hienen in jonge, dy hiet fan Folkert. Dy jonge wie sa'n fjirtsjin jier âld.\nOp in joun seagen se dat der in kiste ta 't hûs yndroegen woarde. Doe soenen se yn 'e kiste sjen, mar doe hie dy kiste ek wer fuort west.\nKoarte tiid dêrnei stoar Folkert. It hie foartjirmerije west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27397,"r":"CJ065304","p":"Rohel","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"Two men once saw a coffin covered with a white sheet being carried to the churchyard, while in reality there was nothing there. Later a woman in childbed from the neighbourhood died and the funeral really took place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Harm en Janke wennen oan 'e Swâdde yn 'e gemeente Kollumerlân. Sy hienen twa jonges. Letter krigen se der ek noch in famke by.\nDoe't dat famke noch net geboaren wie, doe seach ik al dat se de frou nei 't tsjerkhôf droegen.\nIk stie oan 'e kant fan 't paed. Knjillis Veenstra stie der ek al. Knjillis moest alle bigraffenissen sjen. Hy wist it altyd fan tofoaren hwa't stjerre soe, lyk as ik soms ek.\nKees sei tsjin my: \"Dû mast net sa nei by my komme, dan kin de lykwein net tusken ús troch.\"\n't Wie yn 't holst fan 'e nacht. Ik seach dat der in wyt lekken oer de kiste hinne lei. Ik wist doe noch net hwat dat bitsjutte. Ik sei tsjin Kees: \"Hwat is dat, jong?\"\n\"Dat sil 'k dy letter wol sizze\", wie syn antwurd.\nJanke krige letter in fanke. Mar hja-sels stoar yn 'e kream. Dêrom lei dat wite lekken oer 'e kiste.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27461,"r":"CJ065717","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A girl dreams that her little brother is lying in a small coffin while her grandmother and mother stand looking at it. Some time later her little brother dies and her grandmother and mother stand looking at the little coffin.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie in famke fan in jier of tsien. Ik hie in bruorke, dat wie doe trije en in healjier âld. Foeke hiet er.\nIk droomde op in nacht dat Foeke wie dea. Hy lei yn 't kistje, dat stie foar 't finster. Beppe wie der ek en dy hie mem by de hân. Ik gûlde yn 'e sliep. Doe kom mem fan 't bêd ôf en sei: \"Hiltsje, hwat mankeart dy nou? Hwerom droomstû sa?\"\nIk sei mar gau, ik droomde, dat ik oan 't fechtsjen wie mei bern út skoalle. Ik woe net sizze hwat ik sjoen hie yn myn droom.\nDyselde hjerstmis woarde Foeke siik. Binnen trije dagen wied er dea. Hy lei yn 't kistje, foar 't finster. En beppe en mem stienen by 't kistje. Beppe hie mem by de hân beet.\nDoe sei ik: \"Mem hat my doe dy nachts frege hwat ik droomde. Dit ha ik droomd, dit haw ik sjoen. Beppe hie mem by de hân beet.\"\nIk forjit dit noait wer.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27631,"r":"CJ067802","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"People once saw a coffin standing at their friends' house. A few days later one of the friends died and the coffin really stood there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn frou har twadde heit en dy har mem wie us yn Twizel, by lju. Doe seach se dêr ynienen in kiste stean.\nIn pear dagen letter stoar de man dêr. De kiste kom op itselde plak to stean dêr't se him earder sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27802,"r":"CJ069121","p":"Franeker","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man had made a pact with the devil. He once saw a coffin being carried into a house. Later someone in that house died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Hindrik Skifink hie in forboun mei de duvel sluten.\n Hy seach in kear dat se in greate swarte kiste by ien ta de doar ynsjouden. Letter is der yn dat hûs ien stoarn.\nHy seach wol faker sokke dingen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27973,"r":"CJ070801","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A farmhand slept in the box bed in the empty stable. One night he saw himself lying there in a coffin. He was badly frightened and left the farmer. He thought he could escape his fate that way. Years later he came to visit the farmer. There he died suddenly. The coffin was taken into the stable, and so he came to lie there after all.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie in boerefeint, dy lei yn 'e nacht op bêd. 't Wie yn 'e simmer. Hy sliepte yn in bêdsté yn 't leech bûthús.\nDoe seach er dat se in kiste yn 't bûthús delsetten. Hy gong der ôf om to sjen hwa 't dêr yn lei. Doe seach er him sels yn 'e kiste lizzen. Hy woarde tige kjel.\nHy gong by de boer wei. Hy tocht sa it needlot to ûntrinnen. Nei jierren kom er ris by dy boer op bisite. Doe rekke hy dêr ûnforwacht dea.\nSy brochten syn kiste yn 't skjinne bûthús. Dêr kom er yn to lizzen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27977,"r":"CJ070805","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A woman saw a coffin standing in her house, and after a few days it was gone again. Later her daughter fell ill and came to stay in her house. She died there, and then the coffin really stood there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sa'n trije jier lyn kom âlde Antsje fan 'e Twizelerheide yn 'e hûs (sjoch B65-168 en 169), doe stie der in deakiste by har oer 'e flier. Antsje tocht: hoe kin dit? Sy skrok der tige fan. In skoftsje letter, doe wie de kiste wer fuort.\nHja koe 't har net begripe hwat dat bitsjutte moest.\nIn troude dochter fan har, dy't net sa jong mear wie, rekke siik. By har thús wie 't in drokke húshâlding mei bern. By Antsje wie 't rêstich, sadwaende kom dy dochter by Antsje.\nDêr is se stoarn.\nDoe kom har kiste dêr by Antsje oer 'e flier to stean. Dat wie dyselde kiste dy't se doe sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28080,"r":"CJ071704","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A little boy once saw from his bed two men bringing a small coffin into the house. He was too afraid to get out of bed. Later his little sister died and the men really came to bring the coffin.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie in jonkje fan sa'n fjouwer jier. Ik gong noch net net skoalle. Heit wie faek yn Dútslân oan 't wurk. Dan slepte ik by ús mem yn 'e lege weech.\nOp in nacht moest ik der ôf to pisjen. Doe seach ik in pear keardels by ús yn 'e hûs, dy setten in bakje yn 'e hoeke del.\nIk woarde sa binaud, dat ik doarst net út bêd.\nLetter stoar der ien fan myn susterkes, Etsje. Doe kommen der twa mannen mei in kistje oandragen, deselden, dy't ik doe yn 'e nacht sjoen hie. En sy setten it kistje op itselde plak del as dêr't ik it stean sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28081,"r":"CJ071705","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A woman often saw in advance that someone would die. Once she saw a coffin with a white cloth over it. Then she knew that a woman would soon die in childbed. That came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Hindriks Janke fan 'e Harkema koe altyd krekt fortelle hwannear't der ien op 'e buert stoar. Sy plichte it wol gauris tsjin ús mem to sizzen, dan wist dy it ek.\nUs mem hie fiif kear in bern forlern en dêr hie se it tige mei to dwaen hawn.\nDoe sei Janke op in kear tsjin mem: \"Der komt wer in sterfgefal op 'e buert.\"\n\"Och heden,\" sei mem, \"as 't wer by ús is, dan hoop ik, dat ik it bin.\"\n\"Né,\" sei Janke, \"dû bist it net en ek net ien fan dyn bern, hwant it is ien, dy't yn 'e kream stjert.\"\nRidlik gau dêrnei stoar Knjillis Antsje, dy't in poppe krige. Sy leinen har in wite doek oer de kiste. Dat hie Janke fan tofoaren sjoen, dêrtroch wist se dat it in kreamfrou wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28087,"r":"CJ071711","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man once saw a coffin being brought into his house. Shortly afterwards his wife died. The coffin was placed exactly where he had seen it. Later the man also foresaw his own funeral.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir oan 'e Fjouwer Roeden wenne âlde Tsjerk van der Veen, yn 't lêste húske, it tichtste oan 'e Rottefalle. Dy seach op in kear dat der in kiste by him yndroegen woarde. Hy tochte: \"Dy is foar my sels.\" Hwant hy hie 't oan 't hart.\nMar even letter stoar syn frou. De kiste kom op itselde plak to stean dêr't hy him sjoen hie.\nDoe't Antsje al in skoftsje yn 'e modder lei, hearde er har op in kear roppen \"Tsjerk! Tsjerk!\" Ridlik gau dêrnei is er stoarn. Hja hat him nei 't tsjerkhôf ta roppen.\nTsjerk hat syn eigen begraffenis fan tofoaren sjoen. Hy hat oan minsken noch forteld hwa't er allegear by syn lykstaesje sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28144,"r":"CJ072002","p":"Burum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man was born with a caul. Once he saw the door of the house open and a coffin come in. A few days later his wife died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Kees Veenstra wenne yn Kollumersweach, by 't spoar. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren.\nOp in kear siet er by syn frou yn 'e hûs. Doe gong de doar iepen en doe woarde der in deakiste ta de keamer yn brocht.\nKees woarde sa bleek as in doek en it swit roan him by de kop del. Doe sei syn frou tsjin him: \"Hwer sjochstû sa nei?\" Mar dat woed er net sizze.\nIn pear dagen letter rekke syn frou wei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28225,"r":"CJ072907","p":"Kornhorn","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"People once saw a coffin being carried into the house of a sick person. A few days later the sick person died and the coffin was really carried into the house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Er waren hier mensen die zagen dat ze een doodkist ergens in een huis droegen. In dat huis was een zware zieke.\nEen poar doagen loater stierf die zieke. Toen brachten se dan echt een kist in huus.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28329,"r":"CJ073905","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A woman once saw two figures dressed in black put something wooden in the shed. A few weeks later one of her children died, and the men came to put a coffin in the shed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanmem wie in gelovich minske dy't alhielendal net bygelovich wie. 't Wie us op in kear yn 'e hearst. Op in joun. Skoanheit wie der op út. Skoanmem gong út 'e keamer wei troch 't gonkje. De achterdoar wie fêst, op 'e skoattel.\nDoe kommen der twa mannen yn 't swart troch de tichte doar en dy brochten hwat yn 'e loads. Dat setten se oan 'e kant del. Hja hearde it hout op 'e stiennen flier.\nEven letter kom mem wer yn 'e hûs. Doe sei se tsjin 'e bern, sy moesten fral net oangean, mar har stil hâlde.\nIn pear wiken letter gong der ien fan har bern dea, in jonkje. Doe kommen der twa lju, dy wienen yn 't swart klaeid. Dy hienen twa skammels by har, dêr't de kiste op stean moest. Dy skammels setten se yn 'e loads del. Sy kommen troch de achterdoar. De beide mannen dy't se earder sjoen hie, wienen de foarboaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32708,"r":"CJ082904","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"At night a farmer suddenly hears noises and shortly afterwards sees two coffins being slid over the stones. It is a vision: soon afterwards both his daughters die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit hat froeger boerefeint west yn Grinzer Pein. Hy slepte altyd yn 't bêdsté yn 't bûthús. Doe't er dêr ris wer in kear lei yn 'e nacht, hearde hy leven yn 'e molkenkelder. De molkenkelder wie tichteby 't bûthús. Hy hearde dat der hwat oer de stiennen skoud woarde. Heit gyng dêr ôf en sette nei de molkenkelder ta. Doe woarde dêr in kiste delset. Heit seach der nei en gong even letter wer op bêd lizzen.\nHy lei noch mar even of dêr hearde hy deselde lûden wer. Dy lûden kommen fan 't selde plak, út 'e molkenkelder wei.\nHeit der wer ôf en der hinne. Doe stienen dêr twa deakisten, flak njonken elkoar.\nIn skoftje letter forlear de boer syn beide dochters. Dêr hie heit de kisten fan sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33776,"r":"CJ094109","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A woman had seen bearers bring a small coffin into the house, and knew that her child would die. Not long afterwards the child fell ill, but because it was wearing something that had been sewn on a Sunday, it could not die. Only when they took off the little shirt did the child breathe its last.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As jo op jou stjerbêd in ding oan ha, dêr't op snein oan naeid is, dan kinne jo net stjerre. Beppe hat it meimakke mei in berntsje dat wie noch mar sawn maenden âld. It wie hiel bot siik. Mar it koe noait stjerre. \"Hat er ek hwat oan dat op snein naeid is?\" sei doe de buorfrou.\n\"Ja,\" sei beppe, \"dat himdsje.\"\nDoe ha se him dat himdsje útdien en doe blaesde er samar de lêste sykjes út.\nBeppe wist al fier fan tofoaren dat se dat berntsje net hâlde mocht. Hja hie op in jountiid sjoen dat de dragers by har yn 'e keamer kommen en it kistje foar it bern yn in hoeke delsetten. Doe wie 't bern noch soun.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36140,"r":"CJ096708","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A father and mother had twins. At nine months one of the children fell ill and died. At the churchyard the father said that their other child would die too. He had seen it lying in a little coffin. When they came home the other child had died as well.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en mem hienen twillingen. It iene berntsje woarde siik, doe wie 't njoggen maenden âld. It stoar en sy brochten it nei 't hôf ta. Doe sei heit: \"It oare berntsje hâlde wy ek net. Ik ha 't al yn 't kistje lizzen sjoen.\" Doe't se weromkommen fan 't tsjerkhôf wie 't oare berntsje ek dea.\nHeit en mem wennen doe yn 'e Twizeler Mieden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36296,"r":"CJ097701","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"The narrator's mother could see things before they happened. For instance, she saw the neighbour woman lying in her coffin before her death. The coffin could not be carried through the door. Later everything went exactly as she had predicted.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem seach de dingen faek fantofoaren gebeuren. Wy wennen yn 'e Westerein njonken âlde Willemke. Op in kear sei ús mem: \"Ik ha âlde Willemke dea lizzen sjoen yn 'e kiste. De kiste gong ûnder 't glês troch, sy koenen him net troch de doar krije.\"\nDoe wie Willemke hielendal net siik.\nTwa dagen letter is se ûnforwacht stoarn. It gong allegear krekt sa sa't mem it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36297,"r":"CJ097702","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"The narrator's mother saw in advance that two of the neighbours' children would die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem hat ek sjoen dat twa berntsjes fan ús buorlju stoarn binne. Dat wienen Geale en Tsjimkje, broer en suster fan Jehannes' Minke. Mem sei: \"Se sille sahwat tagelyk stjerre, hwant ik ha se tagelyk yn 'e kistjes lizzen sjoen.\"\nEn dat is ek útkom, hwant sy woarden beide tagelyk nei 't hôf ta brocht.\nMem sei doe ek noch: \"It sil hjir op mear plakken gebeure dat der twa tageyk yn ien húshâlding stjerre.\" En dat is ek gebeurd; fuort dêrnei yn Twizelerheide.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36331,"r":"CJ097811","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"The narrator's little sister died as a child. Before it happened, her father had already seen her little coffin standing in a particular spot in the house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik noch thús yn 'e hûs wie is der by ús in famke stoarn. Dat wie myn susterke.\nDe dragers kommen by ús yn 'e hûs en seinen: \"'t Kistje mat dêr stean.\" En sy wiisden in plak oan.\n\"Né,\" sei heit, \"it liket my better ta dat it dêr komt to stean.\" Doe wiisde er nei in hiel oar plak. Heit hie 't kistje dêr al dagen fan tofoaren stean sjoen. Hy wist dat er 't famke net bihâlde mocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29517,"r":"CJ110415","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A clairvoyant man sees a coffin standing in the house. Shortly afterwards his daughter drowns herself.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Keke syn dochter hat harsels fordronken yn in gat by 't spoar. Keke hat ek hàr kiste by him yn 'e hûs stean sjoen.\nHja wenne noch by him yn 'e hûs. Hy hie net sjoen dat hja fordronken wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29579,"r":"CJ110610","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A woman, born with a caul, foresees that her little son will die and predicts exactly where the little coffin will stand. The vision comes true: soon afterwards the boy dies of pneumonia. The coffin is also placed where the woman saw it before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e lêste oarloch wenne ik noch op it Kattegat, op 't Wytfean, flak by de Leijen. Dêr wienen doe ûnderdûkers, dêr't ik faek mei praette. Twa rijnaken leinen der, en de lju, dy't dêr yn wennen krigen altyd molke fan my. De skipper fan ien fan dy beide rijnaken kaem ris by my op in joun, doe sei er tsjin my: \"Sil ik jo ris hwat bûtengewoans fortelle? \n't Betreft ús eigen húshâlding. Myn frou is mei de helm geboaren - It is seis jier lyn nou. Wy hienen doe in jonkje, dat hiet fan Harry. 't Wie oardel jier âld. Op in snein-to-moarn sieten wy to kofjedrinken en doe sei se tsjin my: 'Sil ik dy ris hwat sizze? Us lytse Harry giet dea'.\nIk wist, dat hja mei de helm geboaren wie en ik woarde o sa kjel.\"\nDoe hie dy man sein: \"Hoe wytstû dat?\"\n\"Ik ha 't fannacht allegear sjoen\", sei se. \"Dû mast der dy mar op klear meitsje. 't Kistje stie dêr. En ik ha sjoen dat ús lytse jonge dêr yn lei.\" En doe wiisde se it plak oan dêr't se it sjoen hie.\nKrekt fiif wiken letter krige 't jonkje longontsteking en binnen twa dagen wie 't dea.\nDoe tocht ik: as se no aenst 't jonkje biklaeije, dan siz ik net hwer't se 't kistje delsette matte.\nDoe't se 't bern biklaeid hienen, krigen se 't kistje en setten 't del.\nDoe't se fuort wienen, sei myn frou: \"Se ha 't kistje wòl op 't selde plak delset, dêr't ik it sjoen ha.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30885,"r":"CJ114109","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0483","d":"A man who lost his daughter had already foreseen her death weeks in advance: one night he saw the coffin standing in the room. He also saw his daughter being taken to the churchyard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tabe Bergsma fan Drachtster Kompenije fortelde dat hy hie in famke forlern. Wiken fan tofoaren hie er it famke al yn 'e kiste lizzen sjoen, by syn bêd. 't Wie yn 'e nacht, doe't er it sjoen hie. Hy lei doe op bêd.\nSa hat er 't ek sjoen, doe't it bern nei 't hôf brocht waerd. (Tabe Bergsma wennet nou op 'e hoeke fan de Knipe).","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34737,"r":"CBOEK232","p":"Ommen","v":"Ov.","y":1881,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog sits down by a house and howls, someone there will die; likewise if many magpies fly around the house.","i":"M.W.","o":"Als een hond in de nabijheid van een huis gedurig zit te huilen, zien velen daarin een voorteken van een in dat huis op handen zijnd sterfgeval. Hetzelfde meent men, als er veel eksters om 't huis rondvliegen."},{"n":39509,"r":"CBOEK421","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1881,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"All kinds of superstitions: omens, folk remedies, etc.","i":"J.C.A.v.R.","o":"Bijgeloof\n\nVan een spin: 's Morgens geluk, 's middags druk, 's avonds een ongeluk.\nAls er een hond huilt, sterft er iemand.\nAls er een lijk op Zondag blijft staan, komt er gauw weer een doode. (N-Br.)\nMet een mes draaien, twee messen kruiselings, met een stoel draaien of eierdoppen verbranden geeft ruzie.\nDe lap van een wond verbranden [veroorzaakt] verergering der wond.\nAls men het haar verbandt of weggooit, dan valt het haar uit.\nEen cent met een gat [brengt] geluk.\nVoor de koorts: Men schrijft op een turf: \"Koorts, koorts, ik ben niet thuis,\" en gooit hem dan in het vuur, dan verbrandt zij.\nAls er een vrouw met de helm geboren voorbij gaat, dan sterft er iemand.\nVoor de wratten neemt men een touwtje, legt daar zooveel knoopen in als er wratten zijn, stopt dat in den grond, loopt er een half jaar over (voor de deur b.v.) en de wratten zijn weg."},{"n":39347,"r":"CBOEK348","p":"Amstelveen","v":"N.-H.","y":1892,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a mirror, a windowpane or a glass breaks, the owner's death soon follows.","i":"S.H.M."},{"n":39615,"r":"CBOEK461","p":"Bathmen","v":"Ov.","y":1892,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In Dijkerhoek people believe that if a hen carries a straw on its neck, there will soon be a death in the close family, but if it carries the straw on its rear, a wedding will soon follow.\nWhen you hear a ticking like a watch in the box bed, when the horse shies in front of the wagon, or when magpies peck each other on or near the house, there will soon be a death.\nIn Koersbaas (Wibbelink)'s barn, where he made the coffins, it used to be haunted too. A few days before someone died, people could already hear the coffin planks being thrown about.","i":"J.V.","o":"In Dijkerhoek onder Holten gelooft men als een kip een stroospier op den nek draagt, komt er spoedig een dood in de naaste familie, draagt de kip het stroospier echter op zijn achterste dan volgt er spoedig bruiloft.\nWanneer men in de bedstee een getik hoort als van een horloge, wanneer het paard voor de wagen schrikt, wanneer de eksters elkaar op of bij het huis bijten, komt er gauw een doode.\nIn Koersbaas (Wibbelink) zijn schuur, waar hij de doodkisten maakte, spookte het vroeger ook. Daar hoorde men een paar dagen vóór er iemand stierf reeds met de planken der doodkist gooien.\nVolgens sommigen komt er een doode als zich de eksters kort bij de huizen ophouden; en als ze elkander op de huiden bijten is daar binnen twist."},{"n":39642,"r":"CBOEK488","p":"Kwadijk","v":"N.-H.","y":1892,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a body is not buried on a Sunday, another death will soon follow. The church bell then sounds dull.","i":"L.K.","o":"Als op Zondag een lijk boven aarde blijft staan, zal er spoedig weêr een doode zijn. De kerkklok klinkt dan dof."},{"n":39495,"r":"CBOEK408","p":"'s-Heerenberg","v":"Gld.","y":1894,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"All kinds of signs that predict death (quarrels and the like)","i":"J.M.","o":"Het volksgeloof zegt: \n\nHet roepen van den kerkuil is een voorteeken des doods; hij zegt \"liek\" (lijk).\nHet huilen van een hond wordt als hetzelfde voorteeken aangemerkt.\nEen kraaiende hen brengt ongeluk.\nVijf eksters voor de deur geeft een lijkstoet.\nWil een paard een huis niet voorbij, dan komt dáár een doode.\nEén schreeuwende ekster voor het huis geeft groot nieuws.\nValt een ketting voor een huis, dan komt daar een doode.\nVallen een paar messen kruiselings over elkander, dan zal er twist ontstaan.\nDe wachtel zegt: \"Riek bun ik.\" (rijk ben ik)\nDe leeuwerik: \"Onze lieven Heer één keurentje (1 korreltje)\", doch hij doet dit dan alleen, als hij zoo recht in de lucht opstijgt, om zijn voedsel af te bidden.\nVan een vogeltje in het voorjaar (ik weet niet juist welk) zegt men: Hij roept \"Vrouw spin dit.\" Men legt dat uit, dat er vlug moet gesponnen worden, omdat de veldarbeid weldra zal beginnen.\nDoor het geluid van den specht worden de oude paarden naar de wei geroepen."},{"n":69803,"r":"DYKFRIES2199","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"An elderly widow gets the feeling that something terrible will soon happen after hearing strange noises. Not long afterwards the eldest daughter falls fatally ill. When it is thought she will die, the mother walks up the stairs to warn the grandmother. Then the daughter dies. The grandmother declares that the sound of the mother coming up the stairs to tell her the daughter would probably die was the same as the sound she had heard earlier.","i":"W.D.","o":"Eene bejaarde weduwe woonde sedert den dood van haren man in bij haren gehuwden zoon, wiens huis ietwat eenzaam stond. De oude vrouw had haar slaapplaats op een klein bovenkamertje en daarnaast sliepen een paar groote jongens, kleinzoons van haar. Het gebeurde eens, dat zij op zekeren nacht een poosje slapeloos was en even overeind ging zitten. Nu meende zij op den trap zachte voetstappen te hooren als van iemand die op kousen liep of behoedzaam was om niet gehoord te worden. Eerst dacht zij, dat een der jongens naar beneden was geweest. Doch toen de persoon boven kwam ging hij niet naar de plaats waar zij sliepen, maar opende even de deur van haar kamertje, zuchtte zwaar en ademhaalde snel en trok zich toen weêr terug. De oude vrouw ontstelde; zij wist niet wat te moeten denken en hield zich eene poos doodstil. Bij verder nadenken meende zij te mogen gelooven dat er wel een vreemde met verkeerde bedoelingen in huis geslopen kon zijn. Zij wekte daarom de jongens en bracht het zoover, dat weldra ook haar zoon en het verdere mannelijk personeel des gezins op de been was. Men doorzocht het geheele huis, maar vond niets wat reden gaf tot ongerustheid. Men begaf zich weêr ter rust; er viel dien nacht verder niets bijzonders voor; des morgens bij daglicht zag men nog eens alles na, maar vond geenerlei grond voor het vermoeden, dat er iemand, die er niet behoorde, in huis was geweest.","l":""},{"n":8627,"r":"CBAK0030","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1899,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One evening it seems as if the peat turfs are being knocked over, but when the woman goes to look nothing has happened. She does see a shade in the form of a dove flying. That must have been an omen of her brother's death a few days later.","i":"C.B.","o":"In Watergang woont een vrouw van dertig jaar. Voor twee jaar zat ze op een avond alleen aan tafel. Opeens hoorde ze boven geraas alsof de turven omgegooid werden. Aangezien ze niets bang was (?), ging ze in 't donker de trap op. De turven lagen nog netjes opgestapeld, maar ze zag een schim in de gedaante van een duif vliegen. Een paar dagen later was haar broer dood. Dit was dus bepaald een voorteeken geweest."},{"n":8628,"r":"CBAK0031","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1899,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man hears an unexplained rumbling in the house a few days before his little daughter drowns.","i":"C.B.","o":"Eveneens heeft een ander Waterganger een paar dagen voor dat zijn dochtertje in het kanaal is verdronken duidelijk hooren rommelen en stommelen in huis, zonder dat ze de oorzaak wisten."},{"n":8784,"r":"CBAK0169","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man may no longer visit a friend's house because the friend's wife has seen him without a head in her dreams. That means he will die if he enters that house.","i":"C.B.","o":"Een Broeker vertelde mij dat hij bij een inwoner van Volendam niet meer in huis mag komen, hoewel hij zeer met hem bevriend is. De vrouw des huizes heeft namelijk gedroomd dat ze hem zonder hoofd gezien heeft, wat een onfeilbaar teeken is dat, als hij dat huis binnentreedt, [hij] spoedig zal sterven."},{"n":8798,"r":"CBAK0183","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"It cannot be seen who tapped on the window. The next evening there is tapping on the window again: someone has died and must be laid out by the informant's wife. So the tapping of the previous evening was a forewarning.","i":"C.B.","o":"Mijn zegsman sluimerde naast zijn ega. Opeens hoorde hij op het raam tikken.\n\"Ik geloof dat er volk is, Trui, want er wordt getikt.\"\n\"Dat hoor ik ook, Klaas, gaan ers kaaiken.\"\nNou ik gong, maar ik zag niks. 't Was een stikdonkere nacht: nou, baldeedigheid kon het niet wezen, want deervoor was het te laat. Wat het was, deer begrepe we niks van.\nDe volgende avond wordt er weer etikt.\n\"Wie is deer?\" roep ik.\n\"Of je vrouw baai Gerrit Stukken wil komme uitkleede, want zijn vrouw het et ofelaaid.\"\nBepaald was het dus de vorige évond een voorbooi eweest.","l":"Waterlands"},{"n":8799,"r":"CBAK0184","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In the evening a farmhand sees a woman sitting in the farmhouse, weeping plaintively. He calls the farmer's wife and her son, but then the woman has vanished. The second time the son sees her too, but when the farmer's wife comes she has vanished again. The next day the farmhand has to fetch the doctor in a hurry, because the farmer's wife has colic and will die of it.","i":"C.B.","o":"Zoo diende ik as vrijgezel bij de moeder van Kees de Waart, die nou nog an het daaikent weunt. Ik kwam bij de maid vandeen en gong het gangetje deur, zuid an de stal. Deer zag ik opeens een vrouwmensch zitte dat zoo klagelijk zat te huilen, dat het me deur me toone heengong. Ik riep de vrouw en Kees, dat toe zoo'n opgeschote jonge was. Ze gonge mee, maar toe was er niks, zoodat ze me allemaal oitlachte. Ik gong er dus weer heen en zag dat waaif weer zitte. Ik weer terug.\nIk zeg teuge Kees: \"As jaai den nou niet bang benne, gaan jij dan mee, want nou zit ze der alweer.\"\nKees gong mee en, ja, nou zag ie er ook zitten en hoorde der metien kermen. Toe riepe we zen moeder, maar toe die kwam was ze weer weg en zoo gong het aldeur.\nDe volgende dag moet ik hoopstoops om de dokter omdat de vrouw beslote koliek had. Ze is er dan ook an esturve.\nJa dat hew ik zelf beleefd.","l":"Waterlands"},{"n":8800,"r":"CBAK0185","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The evening before a man dies, the informant sees a large white animal resembling a sheep in the farmyard.","i":"C.B.","o":"Nou, uwe weet nog wel dat er bij Klaas Schoon zoo veul in een huishouwe estorve benne? Wel ja, uwe heb er, meen ik, nog over egaan. Nou, de évent voordat Klaas esturve is, gong ik de werf op in toe zag ik een groot wit beest, net een scheep.","l":"Waterlands"},{"n":9089,"r":"CBAK0306","p":"Uitdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The day before a relative dies, the family hears a tremendous din, as if a flock of brent geese were passing over the house, but nothing can be seen.","i":"C.B.","o":"Behalve de gewone voorboden bij een naderende dood als een slag op de deur, rinkelen van de glazen enzovoort, enzovoort, wist hij te verhalen hoe bij Willem van der Hoek (zie vroeger) den dag vóórdat er één der huisgenooten stierf een oorverdoovend geraas werd gehoord in huis, alsof er een zwerm rotganzen over het dak heen trok. Ze gingen naar buiten, naar den zolder, maar zagen niets. Den volgenden dag stierf één der huisgenooten."},{"n":9136,"r":"CBAK0347","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1902,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man hears tapping on a windowpane at night but sees no footprints in the snow. Three days later there is tapping on the same window at the same time, to announce that a relative has died.","i":"C.B.","o":"Mijn zegsman hoorde 's nachts tikken aan het raam. Hij ging kijken en zag niets. In de sneeuw waren geen voetstappen (het was winter). Drie dagen later werd er aan hetzelfde raam, en de zelfde ruit, om den zelfden tijd getikt, en was er een familielid overleden."},{"n":9187,"r":"CBAK0373","p":"Uitdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1903,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman and her sister see a white woman standing there as their mother is dying.","i":"C.B.","o":"Een Uitdammer vrouw zag, toen haar moeder op sterven lag, een wit vrouwspersoon tegen den hooiklamp staan. Zij ging tegelijk met haar zuster naar buiten, en deze zag het ook, en 'zij besturven beide zo wit as een doek'."},{"n":9188,"r":"CBAK0374","p":"Uitdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1903,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One evening, while her father-in-law is ill, a woman three times sees a cat that will not be chased away. When her husband is home there is a loud bang on the house, after which they conclude that things will not end well for the sick man.","i":"C.B.","o":"Toen haar schoonvader ziek was en haar man nog niet thuis was van 't visschen, ging zij naar buiten om eens te kijken of hij nog niet kwam. Ze kwam toen een kat met vurige oogen tegen. Ze gaf hem een schop, maar hij wou niet weg gaan. Toen ze weer eens naar haar man ging zien, kwam de kat weer, en voor den derden keer nog eens. Ze begon toen lont te ruiken, maar zei nog niets tot haar man bij zijn thuiskomst.\nNauwelijks waren ze gezeten, of er kwam een harde slag op het huis dat het bulderde. Toen heeft ze haar man haar bevinding van dien avond verteld, en met hem de prognose voor schoonpapa ongunstig gesteld. Hij is ook overleden."},{"n":9295,"r":"CBAK0438","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1911,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"An hour after a woman has heard a loud bang against the rain barrel, news comes that her sister has died.","i":"C.B.","o":"De vrouw van D. de Boer had vaak voorgevoelens. Haar zuster leed aan tering. Op een goeden dag ging vrouw De Boer naar het schuur. Opeens hoorde zij een harde klap tegen den regenton geven, waarvan zij zóó schrok, dat zij de lantaarn, die zij in de hand had, liet vallen. Een uur daarna kwam bericht dat de zuster overleden was. Men was er op voorbereid, omdat zij, in huis komende, gezegd had, dat ze dacht dat zuster dood was, omdat ze die klap gehoord had."},{"n":9296,"r":"CBAK0439","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1911,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman thinks her daughter keeps bumping into her chair, which then moves unpleasantly. As soon as she notices that this is not the case, she says something must be wrong with her sister. Later she hears that her sister has hanged herself.","i":"C.B.","o":"Een andere keer zat ze op haar stoel het kind van haar dochter te bakeren, die ten haren huize bevallen was. Een jongere dochter, die nog een jong meisje was, liep over huis te spelen. Telkens beknorde ze deze, omdat ze (naar vrouw De Boer dacht) telkens tegen haar stoel op liep, en die dan op een onaangename wijze bewoog.\nToen zij eindelijk bemerkte dat het meisje het niet deed, zei ze: \"Dan is het met mijn zuster niet goed.\"\nEen poos later kwam bericht, dat deze zich had opgehangen."},{"n":9342,"r":"CBAK0484","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1911,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A skipper thinks that the wrong stroke when the tower clock strikes the hour may concern him. The following week he dies during an operation.","i":"C.B.","o":"Die zelfde schipper was op 't Havenrak (een groote kom water in het dorp), toen de torenklok juist vol slag sloeg. Daar was een verkeerde slag bij.\n\"Die kon wel ers voor mijn wéze,\" zei die.\nEen week later werd ie naar Amsterdam gebracht om geopereerd te worden voor een beklemde breuk en is an de operatie bezwéke.\n(C. van de Nadort)","l":"Waterlands"},{"n":42183,"r":"JCOHEN50d","p":"Zutphen","v":"Gld.","y":1919,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In Breukelen an aanspreker (undertaker's man who announced deaths) visited a sick man. He should not have done that! For the aansprekers lure death, and death can be drawn to a person it had not thought of before. Death has wide wings... the sharp tips at the very edge can sometimes still touch a person far away. The aanspreker sat down by the sick man's bed and comforted him. \"You will not die!\" \"You are sitting in my brother's chair,\" said the sick man. \"Get away from there!\" But the aanspreker had already sat in the chair, of course with no ill intent. No one dared tell the brother. What would he think if he heard... A few days later he fell ill, and those who loved him sobbed. The sick man looked at them in surprise. \"Tomorrow I'll be better again!\" All who stood around him knew that he was under the shadow of death, for he had rowed to the very end of the sunlit river of life... \"Why do you look at me like that?\" They wanted to spare him. No one answered. He stretched out his hands to them. \"Tell me,\" he pleaded. No one told him that the aanspreker had sat in his chair. But of course he died, and all who had known him wept.","i":"L.d.B."},{"n":42185,"r":"JCOHEN50f","p":"Zutphen","v":"Gld.","y":1919,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In the same place lived someone who heard rummaging in the carpenter's loft at night. He thought: \"How can that wood be moving like that?\" for planks were knocking against planks, and coffins are made of planks. A few days later one of his good acquaintances died, and he was not surprised.","i":"L.d.B.","o":"In dezelfde plaats woonde iemand, die 's nachts op den\nzolder van den timmerman hoorde rommelen. Hij peinsde:\n\"Hoe kan dat hout zoo in beweging zijn?\" want planken\nsloegen tegen planken, van planken wordt de doodskist\ngemaakt. Eenige dagen later is een van zijn goede ken-\nnissen gestorven, en hij verwonderde zich niet."},{"n":42186,"r":"JCOHEN50g","p":"Zutphen","v":"Gld.","y":1919,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Someone was keeping watch by a sick person. It was very quiet and dark. The night stood at the windows and laid its dark hands against the glass. No sound came from the bed. The clock seemed to have stopped. This was the night of nights. Suddenly, in the middle of the room, the watcher saw a core of murky light, growing larger, pushing through the darkness. Gradually things took shape within that magical circle, and suddenly he noticed that a coffin was standing there. He did not dare to move. He knew the sick person must die. A few days later the women threw themselves weeping over the body and did not want to part from it. But death too has its rights, and the living and the dead each have their own realm. The man who had kept watch saw the bearers bring the coffin in, and he followed them to see where they would put it. They set it down on the very spot where he had seen it in fear and dream. Only then did he speak of it with others; and those who listened to him knew that beyond what our eyes see there is a whole world.","i":"L.d.B.","o":"Onder de vele geschiedenissen, welke bij dat dorp gebeurd\nzijn, behoort ook het volgende, dat zich te Westbroek\nheeft afgespeeld. \nIemand zat bij een zieke te waken. Het was heel stil en\ndonker. De nacht stond voor de vensters en legde zijn\nduistere handen vóór 't glas. Uit het bed klonk geen\ngeluid. De klok scheen stil te staan. Dit was de nacht\nder nachten.\nEensklaps, midden-in het vertrek, zag de wakende, dat\neen kern van troebel licht, die zichzelf vergrootte, tusschen\nhet duister drong. Langzamerhand kregen de dingen binnen\ndien tooverachtigen kring vorm, en plotseling bemerkte\nhij, dat er een doodskist stond. Hij durfde zich niet te ver-\nroeren. Hij wist, dat de zieke moest sterven.\nEenige dagen later wierpen zich de vrouwen weenend\nover 't lijk, en ze wilden er niet van scheiden. Doch ook\nde dood heeft zijn rechten, en de levenden en de gestor-\nvenen hebben ieder hun eigen rijk.\nHij, die gewaakt had, zag, dat de dragers de kist binnen-\nleidden, en hij volgde hen, om te weten, waar zij ze plaatsen\nzouden. Op dezelfde plek, waar hij ze in angst en droom\nhad aanschouwd, zetten zij ze neer.\nEerst toen sprak hij met anderen over; en zij, die\nnaar hem luisterden, wisten, dat buiten het zich onzer\noogen een gansche wereld is."},{"n":9458,"r":"CBAK0597","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A farmhand sees a weeping white figure, but the farmer, his wife and their son see nothing. The farmhand sees the same thing a second time; when the farmer and his son go along again, this time they do see the weeping white figure. The next day the farmhand has to fetch the doctor for the wife, who dies after a short illness.","i":"C.B.","o":"N.N. diende bij een boer. Toen hij op een zondagavond thuis kwam, zag hij een witte gedaante, die jammerlijk zat te huilen. Hij waarschuwde den boer. Deze ging met zijn vrouw en zoon mee kijken, maar ze zagen noch hoorden iets. Toen ging N.N. weer alleen er heen en deed dezelfde waarnemingen. De boer en zijn zoon gingen toen op zijn verzoek nog eens mee.\n\"En ja, toen zagen ze het ook!\"\nDe vrouw ging den tweeden keer niet mee. Den volgenden dag moest N.N. plotseling om den dokter, omdat de vrouw besloten koliek had, waaraan ze in korten tijd is overleden.\n\"Dat verklaart,\" zegt N.N., \"waarom wij niets hoorden of zagen, toen zij meegegaan was.\"\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.279.)"},{"n":39017,"r":"ZEEUW091","p":"Yerseke","v":"Zl.","y":1923,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A married couple are startled by a sudden bang on the table and hear afterwards that a family member died at that time.","i":"G.D.v.O.","o":"Spokerijen.\n\nOp een rustigen zaterdagavond zat L. E. uit Ierseke aardappelen te schillen voor den volgenden dag, en B. haar man, dommelde zoo wat, toen er opeens zoo'n geweldige slag op tafel werd gegeven, dat haar man wakker schrok, en zij van schrik de schotel van haar schoot liet vallen.\nBeiden waren overtuigd dat hierop iets zou volgen, en het bleek waar te wezen, want maandag kwam de doodstijding uit Vlaardingen van een familielid, dat zaterdag plotseling was overleden."},{"n":35860,"r":"VVUNL321","p":"Brunssum","v":"L.","y":1926,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The old mother of a miner heard a mysterious knocking at the back door and says it is Death wanting to come in. Three days later her son died in a mining accident.","i":"G.L.","o":"Voorteken van de dood \n\nOp de staatsmijn Wilhelmina te Terwinselen verongelukte, jaren geleden, een mijnwerker uit de buurt van Simpelveld. Tevoren had de oude moeder van deze mijnwerker telkens een geheimzinnig kloppen gehoord op de achterdeur, en ze zegde: 'Dat is de dood, die binnen wil treden.' De 'dood' trad wel niet daadwerkelijk in dat huis, doch drie dagen later verloor de zoon der oude vrouw op een ongelukkige wijze het leven op de mijn."},{"n":21806,"r":"CJ0287A12","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1951,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a few drops of blood fall down, there will be a death in the family. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Inkelde bloeddrippen (3) dy't falle, jowe in deaden yn 'e famylje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21814,"r":"CJ0287A20","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1951,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A skipper hears cries for help, but when he goes to look there is nothing to be seen. Later someone drowns at the same spot. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In skipper roan nêst in fyftich jier (± 1903) fan Eastemar nei Burgum, om hier to biteljen. Syn omkesizzer hied er by him.\nDoe't se oan it Mienskar ta wienen, hearden hja dúdlik Help! Help! roppen. Hja gongen dy kant út, dêr't it lûd wei kom en fregen: \"Hwat is hjir?\" Mar sy krigen gjin antwurd. Sy koenen ek neat ûnderskiede, hwant it wie jountiid.\nMar deselde winters is op dat plak ien fan it Heechsân fordronken, nei't er earst in kear of hwat om help roppen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23641,"r":"CJ040503","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1954,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When the birds go wild, the magpies cackle and the dogs howl ghostly, a death will follow.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de fûgels bot raesden, kaem der in deaden.\nAs de eksters skatteren ek.\nAs in spoekhoun lûd joech ek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":14720,"r":"LIJST001","p":"Scheveningen","v":"Z.-H.","y":1954,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"On the night the ship her son sails on is wrecked, a woman hears a crow tap three times on the window.","i":"R.K.","o":"I. De duivel\n1.\nZijn U verhalen bekend over mensen, die de duivel gezien hebben of omgang met hem hebben gehad (met hem gedanst hebben, met hem kaart hebben gespeeld), of kent U andere verhalen, waarin de duivel een rol speelt?\nGelieve elk verhaal te noteren op een afzonderlijk blad papier en in elk verhaal duidelijk aan te duiden hoe de duivel voorgesteld wordt (met bokshorens, bokspoten, paardenhoeven, sik, staat enz.).\n\nVerhalen over de duivel zijn mijn zegslieden onbekend. \nDe orthodox-Hervormde Scheveningers spreken liever niet over de duivel. Wel heb ik horen vertellen het verhaal van een oudere vrouw, wonend op een Schevenings hofje, die in een stormnacht drie maal op het raam hoorde tikken. Ze haastte zich naar buiten en zag een kraai wegvliegen. In dezelfde stormnacht verging de logger, waarop haar zoon voer. De zoon verdronk. De kraai als aankondiger van scheepsrampen is hier niet onbekend. Met de duivel heeft hij niets te maken."},{"n":13407,"r":"LYST156","p":"Wagenborgen","v":"Gr.","y":1957,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A magpie or crow near the house announces death.","i":"R.H.","o":"Kraaien of eksters als die dicht bij een huis waren, dan ging er een dood in dat huis. 't Is me bekend, dat er een ekster tegen 't raam tikte, de andere dag was de vrouw dood, in kraam overleden."},{"n":13449,"r":"LYST185","p":"Opheusden","v":"Gld.","y":1957,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People who are bewitched have pains in their stomach. When they find little boards in their pillow, they know they will soon die, for those boards are meant for their coffin. A family that is always ill moves to another place because they think they are bewitched. In that other place they feel as healthy as anyone else.","i":"J.M.","o":"Spookdieren\nHier in Opheusden werd vroeger heel erg over toveren en spoken gesproken, maar vanaf 't elektrisch licht gekomen is, hoort men er nooit meer over. Als hier de vroegere mensen betoverd werden hadden ze altijd pijn in de buik. Sommigen stierven die erg betoverd waren en werden dan niet stijf maar bleven slap. Allerhande figuren zaten bij de betoverde mensen in de hoofdkussen en als er plankjes in kwamen was het voor de doodskist en dan gingen ze dood. Ook is in mijn tijd hier uit Opheusden nog een familie van Leusden verhuisd naar Wageningen, dus de Rijn over, die meende dat ze betoverd waren en vanaf dat ze in Wageningen gingen wonen waren ze altijd goed als elk ander gezond mens en hier waren ze altijd ziek, dwz betoverd."},{"n":43251,"r":"AMPT000214","p":"Genemuiden","v":"Ov.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman believes that magpies signify a death.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"Eksters. Moeder zei: \"Daar hef ie weer zo'n smerig ding. Er sterft er een.\"\nEr zou een zeker iemand sterven."},{"n":43265,"r":"AMPT000311","p":"Hasselt","v":"Ov.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A crow on the mast foretells misfortune, but a woman's thought that her father will soon die does not come true.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"Een kraai op de mast bracht ongeluk. Tante Henderien zei: \"Kiek, een kroa up de mast dat kan mien vader wel wèze.\" Ze schudde met een touw om de vogel weg te jagen. (Ze had een ouwe vader, die alleen woonde.) Maar het was niet zo, hij leefde nog jaren.","l":"Overijssels"},{"n":43524,"r":"AMPT000608","p":"Hasselt","v":"Ov.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"On the road a black crow flies ahead of the horse and cart; in the storage, among the merchandise, is a mourning letter for the merchant's sister. The bird then flies away.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"Mijn man leurde met handel langs de deur, met een paard en een wagentje. Eens ging ik met hem mee en dan hadden we onderweg ergens handel opgeslagen om bij te vullen. De hele tijd vloog er een zwarte kraaie voor ons uit en hij wilde niet weg. Toen we bij de handel kwamen zat er tussen de handel een rouwbrief. Mijn man zijn zuster was gestorven. Toen vloog de vogel weg.","l":"Overijssels"},{"n":43526,"r":"AMPT000609","p":"Hasselt","v":"Ov.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Crows and magpies around the house announce a death.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"Als er kraaien en eksters rond het huis vliegen komt er gauw een dode.","l":"Overijssels"},{"n":43549,"r":"AMPT000705","p":"Zwolle","v":"Ov.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A bird on the pitchfork can mean a death.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"Als er een vogel op de gaffel zat, was dat een slecht veurteken. Soms kwam er een dode.","l":"Overijssels"},{"n":46419,"r":"BOO000304","p":"Kwadendamme","v":"Zl.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman watching over a sick person hears knocking on the shutters three times one night; each of the three times there is nothing to be seen or heard. Three days later the sick person dies.","i":"A.d.B.","o":"Klopgeest\nTante Nan was in d’r leste ziekte. Tante Ka, vader en ikke wêêkten om burte ’s nachs. Tante Ka sliep dan d’r êêzeslêêpje op de canapé.\nOp ’n nacht oarden ze buten op ’t blind kloppe. Ze gieng kieke – gin mēns te zien. Ze gieng wee op de canapé ligge, mè amper lag ze, of z’oarden awwee kloppe op ’t blind; dudelijk, ovva t’r êêjn in wou. Ze docht: “k Zà toenèt niet goed ekek’è.” Dust, ze goeng wee nî buten, riep: “Is t’r volk?” mè ze kreeg gin antwoord. Noggis rommetom ’t uus ekeke, mè niks te zien of t’oaren. Da’s toch eigenarig, doch ze en ze goeng wee ni binnen. Ze zou nog mèr even wachte mie te gî slêêpe. Nî Tante Nan ekeke, mè die lag têêmelijk rustig te slêêpen.\nAffijn, ze goeng wee mè ligge. Ze luusterden nog ’n stuitje, mè z’oarden niks. En ze rocht de wind kwiet (= viel in slaap).\nMè op ’n gegeve moment wor ze wakker en awwee, dus voe den derden kêêjr, oarden ze kloppe op ’t blind buten. Voe den derden kêêjr gêê se kieke, roept in den doenker, ovva t’r volk is… Niks t’oaren, niks te zien!\nVee ongerust goeng ze den uzen in en ze dust nie mî te gî slêêpe. Ze goeng mè wat an d’r rozenkrans leze en avvast mè ’t êêjn en ’t aar klèrmêêke voe den aren dag: bie ’n zieken in uus is t’r vee te doen dat à in ’n gewoon uusouwen nie voorkomt.\nZe docht liever mè nie mî an dat geklop.\nMè precies drie dêêgen lêêter is Tante Nan esturve.","l":"Zeeuws"},{"n":21294,"r":"CJ025602","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a little bird taps against the glass, there will be a death or an accident. This also happens when the magpies chatter, when the convent bell rings or when the rain cloths flap. And when people in a funeral procession do not walk properly in line, and when the weight of the clock falls.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in fûgeltsje tsjin 't glês oan hipte, kom der in deaden, of der gebeurde in ûngelok.\nAs de eksters skatteren ek.\nAs de kleasterklok deadsk lette of as de regenkleden wapperen, dan wie der gau in deaden yn 'e buert.\nAs hja yn in lykstaesje net goed achterinoar oan roannen kom der ek gau wer in deaden.\nAs it wicht fan 'e klok foel ek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":210435,"r":"ENGELS001103","p":"Maasbree","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A fireball bursting apart in the shape of a cross is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of misfortune.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Vuurbollen:\nHet volgende heb ik zelf beleefd, toen ik 8-9 jaar was:\nToen ik ’s avonds een keer door het raam keek, zag ik een grote vuurbol door de lucht zweven. Ik riep op grootvader, die in zijn stoel zat, en deze riep vader, die nog op stal was. Deze ging buiten kijken. Opeens spatte de vuurbol uiteen in de vorm van een vurig kruis, en viel daarna in vonken omlaag. Grootvader zei: “Dat is een teken, dat er een ongeluk te gebeuren staat.” \nEen week daarna ging Wullem Wijers, een buurjongen, wat paard rijden. Zijn broer Graad, die met mij naar school ging, kwam bij ons langs gelopen, en vroeg, of we Wullem niet hadden gezien. We zeiden, dat hij langs was gekomen. De jongen liep verder, en opeens zag ik, dat er rook uit zijn kleren kwam. Plotseling begon hij te wrijven en om zich heen te slaan. We liepen er heen, doch de kleren brandden hem van het lijf. Hij stierf enige dagen later.\nGrootvader zei: “Zien jullie ook, dat er een ongeluk van komt?” \nDe vuurbol zweefde op een hoogte van naar schatting 1 uur zonnestand.\n\nGeen omzetting in dialect van het verhaal door Engels."},{"n":210550,"r":"ENGELS001724","p":"Grashoek","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A bruise on the arm is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Bloedvlekken:\nMarie Gommans kreeg op zekere dag een z.g. “doodsvlek” op haar arm; een bont en blauwe plek. Ze beweerde, dat dit een aanwijzing voor haar was, dat er spoedig iemand van de familie zou sterven. Binnen een week stierf een nicht, die al een jaar aan kanker leed.\n\nVerslag 50, Omzetting van de verhalen, verteld door Leonardus Kluijtmans, Helden, doorgegeven onder no. L291-17, op 26-12-1962. Van Nederl. versie in plaatselijk dialect. Helden, 4 nov. 1969\n’n Nabbervrouw, “Marie Gommans” kreeg op zekeren daag, s’zonger det ze woos woevanne, ’n z.g. “Doeëdsvlek” op ten érm, (“ennen blonkte plak”). Ze beweerden, det ‘t ’n aanwiezing vör eur waas, tét d’r bènnekort eemes van eur femilie zo sjterve. Bènnen ’n wèèk sjtorf ’n neecht, die al e jaor an kanker leej."},{"n":209475,"r":"HOL000101","p":"Ingen","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At the spot where something is seen turning in the water, someone drowns that evening.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Willem van Zetten van Toon van Ewijk gehoord dat deze, met enkele andere mensen, bij het schut aan de Rijn (plaats in de buitenpolder, waar klein sluisje is om water te kunnen inlaten) aan het vissen was. Het gezelschap meende daar, het was 's morgens vroeg, iets in het water te zien draaien. De vissers zijn toen uit angst weggelopen. 's Avonds is er op dezelfde plaats iemand verdronken."},{"n":209484,"r":"HOL000110","p":"Ingen","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man foresees deaths and knows, on seeing a funeral procession, who is being buried; the screeching of owls is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of death.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Voorgezicht Hent van Orsel zag eens een \"jong\" van Teunis de Wit. Hij zei tegen de mannen, die bij hem stonden, dat die jongen over zes weken zou sterven. En het gebeurde ook. Hent had op een ander moment gezegd: \"Kunde wel geleuve, da takeind van mijn staarreve mot\" En hij had op zijn kind gewezen. 14 dagen later was het gebeurd. Hent wist ook, als hij een \"lijkstatie\" zag, wie er begraven werd. Hij herkende de mensen die achter de wagen gingen (De wagen was de gewone boerenwagen).\nBij iemand was een uil door de schoorsteen naar beneden gevallen. Een sterfgeval was daarop spoedig gevolgd. Ook had dit plaats, nadat uilen geweldig te keer hadden gegaan.\nOmdat toen Kobus (van Ingen) verleden najaar (1961) op het land plotseling dood neerviel, waren de uilen geweldig tekeer gegaan."},{"n":209581,"r":"HOL000514","p":"Ommeren","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman born with a caul foresees the coming of a hearse.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Een tante van Van Ommeren in Leersum, was met de helm geboren. Eens zag zij, dat er een lijkwagen aankwam. Zij zei tegen een kennis, dat zij uit de weg moest gaan en trok haar op zij. De volgende dag passeerde er werkelijk een lijkwagen"},{"n":209584,"r":"HOL000517","p":"Ommeren","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of news of a death; a chattering magpie is the deceased.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"In 1898 gebeurde het, op een zondag, dat de moeder van Van Ommeren, de voordeur hoorde opengaan, voeten hoorde vegen, de \"mildeur\" (de deur van de woonruimte naar de deel) hoorde opendoen en daarna de achterdeur. 's Avonds hadden de zoons het hele huis nog doorgelopen, maar niemand ontdekt. Op maandagmorgen hoorde zij dezelfde geluiden weer, maar toen kwam er iemand zeggen, dat grootvader in Leersum (bij de Darthuizerberg) was aangereden door de tram. Deze reed op een hondekar. 's Avonds, toen de vader van Van Ommeren met G. Briene in de boomgaard liep, zat er een ekster te \"schrèke\". G. Briene zei, dat dit grootvader was."},{"n":209602,"r":"HOL000535","p":"Ommeren","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death and the making of a coffin; the narrator can take away pain with a charm.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Nog een voorteken dat Van Ommeren van 3 verschillende personen, onafhankelijk van elkaar, heeft gehoord. Bij Hent v Ingen, de grootvader van een tegenwoordige timmerman in Ingen hadden de buren, de wed. H. van Ingen-van Esseveld, Roelof van Kalkeren en Kees van Hallum op een avond een geraas gehoord in de planken (waar doodkisten van werden gemaakt). Men had horen hameren en kloppen. Wat bleek: een kind van Van Die was gestorven en de volgende dag moest een doodkistje gemaakt worden.\n\n(V Ommeren is iemand die belang stelt in deze dingen. Hij heeft verschillende artikelen van prof. Tenhaeff over parapsychologie gelezen. Hij kent ook de formule, waarmee pijnen worden afgenomen, maar dat hij er werkelijk aan gelooft, kan men niet zeggen)."},{"n":209715,"r":"HOL001008","p":"Opheusden","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Forced to get up at night to open the churchyard gate.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Sommige mensen werden gedwongen 's nachts uit hun bed te gaan en naar het kerkhof te lopen om daar de hekken open te zetten voor de begrafenisstoet die daar binnen enkele dagen zou aankomen. Gradus en Willem (familienaam heb ik niet verstaan) moesten dit doen."},{"n":209720,"r":"HOL001012","p":"Opheusden","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"From the bleating of a goat it is concluded that something will happen; after the goat is killed, the owner's sister dies.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"De geit \"van den taoje\" (Van Dorland) (woonde achter de school) was op een dag aan het ble.rn (blaten) gegaan. Men meende in \"dat geble r\" te horen: \"Ge zal nog wa bele.vr, ge zal nog wa bele.vr.\" De volgende dag begon het beest weer. \"Den taoje\" werd toen kwaad en sneed het beest de hals af. Dit was fout. Spoedig daarop stierf zijn zuster. Het voorval moet voor een 40 jaar hebben plaats gehad"},{"n":130767,"r":"KEUNING000506","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The narrator's grandfather and sister can hear from the ringing of the church bells whether there will be a funeral within three days.","i":"S.K.","o":"Myn pake hearde oan de tsjerkeklokken, as se lieden, dat er binnen trije dagen ien op it hôf brocht wurde soe. It kaem grif nei. Myn suster koe dat ek.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130799,"r":"KEUNING000908","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman hears wailing without anything to be seen. A few days later a girl and her mother drown.","i":"S.K.","o":"Pake en beppe wennen yn de Wâlden, tichteby de sûkerijfebryk. Pake wier skipper. Op in middei wier beppe allinne thús. Doe sei se yn harsels: \"Hwat jammert dêr in frommes.\"\nHja nei bûten en om hûs hinne, mar der wier neat to sjen.\nDe freedtomiddei dêrop rekke it famke fan Annema's yn de sûkerij-wask. Hja raesde sa lûd se koe. Har mem hearde it, roun nei de kûle ta, seach har berntsje lizzen en raesde al like fûl. Hja sprong har bern nei en beide fordronken.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130800,"r":"KEUNING000909","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In the evening a farmer's wife hears a crowd of people on the canal, but there is nothing to be seen. Later there is ice with a mass of people on it, and someone drowns. The dead person is brought to the farm.","i":"S.K.","o":"In boer en syn frou soene op in joun op bêd. Mar se moasten earst noch efkes ôfljochtsje. (mei de lantearne troch de stâllen, om to sjen, ôf alles yn oarder wier). Se wiernen ek noch effen efter 't hûs.\n\"Hwat komt dêr de feart del,\" sei de frou.\nDe boer sei: \"Ik fornim neat.\"\n\"Der komt in hiele keppel folk de feart del!\" sei hja.\nFuort by kaem de feart yn it kanael út.\n\"It binne mar forbieldingsmar wy rinne effen oan de feart ta\". sei hy. Mar der wier neat to sjen ôf to hearren.\nFuort dêrnei wier it sterk iis. De oare dei fordronk flak by in jongfeint yn it kanaal. Doe 't se him der úthellen, wier der in hiele keppel folk op it kanaal. Se brochten him by de selde boer yn 'e hûs.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130803,"r":"KEUNING000912","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman knows of a death in advance.","i":"S.K.","o":"Folle slimmer is it, dat ik foarút sjoch, dat er ien stjerre sil. Dat ha ik ek wol hûnderd kear sa hâwn.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130813,"r":"KEUNING001104","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman's dream comes true: a hearse with a large coffin, and men she knows carrying the coffin into the house.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ús mem hat it ris hâwn, dy dreamde dat hja in lykwein seach mei in hiele greate kiste der op. Twa manljue sjouden de kiste yn in hûs. Hja koe de manljue wol en wist ek wol hwat hûs it wier. De minsken, dy 't dêr yn wennen, hierne in soan, dy 't ôfgryslike great wie. Hy wenne yn Snits. In pear dagen letter waerd hy thús brocht. Dea. De selde twa mannen droegen de kiste yn it selde hûs.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130820,"r":"KEUNING001201","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At night a woman sees a coffin standing crosswise on the road.","i":"S.K.","o":"In frou roun fan 'e Krúswei nei de Alde Wei. (Moarmwâld) It wier by nacht. Dêr seach hja in deakiste dwers op 'e wei stean. Hja doarst hast net, mar is der dochs omhinne gien.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130911,"r":"KEUNING002305","p":"Suwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man born with a caul dies a few days after a dog has sat howling by his house.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ús omke wier ek mei in helm berne. Op in joun siet der in houn op 'e reed to spûkgûlen. In pear dagen letter wier omke dea.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130925,"r":"KEUNING002601","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At a place where it was said blood would flow and hammering was heard, a slaughterhouse has been built.","i":"S.K.","o":"Der waerd sein, dat lâns in reedtsje hjir tichtby noch ris bloed strome soe. Ek hearde min dêr timmerjen.\nNou, foar oan dat reedtsje stiet nou in slachterij. Efter dat hûs wie in gat, wer it bargebloed yn stroomde. Nou leit der in rioel ûnder dat reedtsje lâns.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130972,"r":"KEUNING003106","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A death occurs in the direction in which the head of a ghost-howling dog points.","i":"S.K.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlde, soe der ien dea gean, de kant út, hwer hy de kop hinne hie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130982,"r":"KEUNING003203","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People are afraid of haunting in the churchyard. Bells that ring wrongly are a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of death.","i":"S.K.","o":"Der wiene hjir yn ús jongetiid noch hiel hwat minsken, dy net op it tsjekhôf komme doarsten. It spûke dêr.\nSoms letten de klokken forkeard. Dan soe der ien stjerre.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131017,"r":"KEUNING003605","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Before someone dies in a house, a woman sees a coffin being carried out of that house and who walks in the procession.","i":"S.K.","o":"Wy ha ek in âld minske kend, dy helle Freedtojouns altyd in pûde fol boadskippen út de winkel. Dêrmei gong hja dan by de streek to suteljen. Op in kear kaem hja by in hûs en doe seach hja, dat dêr in lykkiste nei bûten droegen waerd. En efter dy kiste rounen minsken, it wie in hiele bigraffenis. Hja fortelde ek hjir en dêr, hwat hja sjoen hie. Mar it wie der net echt.\nIn skoftsje letter is yn dat hûs in jonge fan sechtsjen jier stoarn. De âlden hearden der fan, dat dy frou dat sjoen hie. Hja binne noch by har west om to freegjen, of dit wier bard wie. En dat wie sa.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131023,"r":"KEUNING003703","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In the evening girls in the street are picked up and set down across the ditch. They see no funeral procession, but they do hear cloths flapping.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ús mem roun ris op in joun mei in kameraetske op in reed. Ynienen waerden hja samar opnaem en oer de sleat oan de kant fan de reed hinne set. Hja seagen gjin lykstaesje, mar hearden wol it geklapper fan de redenskleden.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131053,"r":"KEUNING003911","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The sound of a screaming child from a pool is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) that someone will drown.","i":"S.K.","o":"Hjir tichtby binne in pear puollen. Dêr raesde nachts faek in bern. Dan moast dêr ien forsûpe. As it iis wie, doarsten wy dêr hast net to riden.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131128,"r":"KEUNING004702","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At a child's funeral people enter through the churning house, just as someone had seen beforehand.","i":"S.K.","o":"Der wie by ús ek ris in man, dy fortelde, dat hy nachts in kloftsje minsken troch de tsjernherne hinne yn 'e hûs kommen sjoen hie. Trije wike letter fordronk dêr in famke en de minsken kamen troch itselde tsjernhûs op bigraffenis by de âlden.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131152,"r":"KEUNING005104","p":"Drachten","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A cock crowing and a dog howling at the same time is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"S.K.","o":"Min sei froeger, dat as in hoarne kraeide en tagelyk in houn gûlde, der ien stjerre soe.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131163,"r":"KEUNING005304","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A falling star is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"S.K.","o":"Min sei froeger: As der in stjer fan de loft falt, sil der ien stjerre.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131237,"r":"KEUNING006206","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Belief that the howling of a short-eared owl is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a sick person's death.","i":"S.K.","o":"It is sahwat fyftich jier lyn, doe kaem der in buorfrou by us, dy tige bygelovich wie. Ik wie doe noch al slim siik. Dy buorfrou sei tsjin myn frou: \"Hoe is it mei jou man? Wy ha in katûle sa razen heard. Myn man en ik seine tsjin mekoar: Hwat is it slim foar de frou, as hjar man der ôf rekket. As der in ûle sa gûlt, giet der binnen twa of trije dagen ien dea.\"\nLokkich leaude hja der hielendal net oan. De frou bidoel ik.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131308,"r":"KEUNING007013","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman predicts a child's death; the coffin is set down in the same place as had been seen earlier.","i":"S.K.","o":"Beppe siet yn 'e hûs mei har famke Wipkje. Pake wie net thús. Doe gong de doar iepen en twa mannen mei greate swarte snorren kamen der yn. Dy setten in lyts deafet efter de tafel en doe ûnder de klok. En doe gongen se wer fuort.\nDoe pake thús kaem, sei beppe:\n\"Alle, wy bihâlde ús famke net.\"\nIn jier letter stoar it.\nS. hie twa jonges. Dy arbeidden yn Dútslân. Mar doe wienen se krekt thús. Yn Dútslân hienen se de snor stean litten. Greate swarte snorren wienen it. En krekt dizze jongkerels setten it kistje yn 'e keamer. En se setten it earst efter de tafel en doe ûnder de klok.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131367,"r":"KEUNING007901","p":"Grou","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Hearing from the ringing of bells that someone will die.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ús mem koe oan de klok hearre, as der ien op it hôf komme soe.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131388,"r":"KEUNING008107","p":"Paesens","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man making his own coffin works slowly because he thinks he will die when the coffin is finished. When he dies, one plank is missing.","i":"S.K.","o":"Hjir wie ek ris ien, dy makke syn eigen deakiste. Mar it avvesearre net sa hurd, hwant hy miende, dat hy net earder stjerre soe, foar de kiste klear wie. Mar doe hy stoar, mankearde der noch ien planke oan.","l":"Fries"},{"n":50572,"r":"KOOIJMAN0026","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Hannes Hoek wakes up. The curtains move by themselves and he sees a little cross in the lamp. The next morning it turns out that his daughter-in-law died at around the same time.","i":"H.K.","o":"De ouwe Hannes Hoek heeft me eens verteld, dat hij op een nacht wakker werd: \"M'n gordijnen werden open en dicht geschoven\". Hij zag nog iets in de lamp van een kruisje of zo. Hij keek op de wekker. 's Morgens kreeg hij de boodschap, dat zijn schoondochter was overleden, op precies dezelfde tijd."},{"n":50573,"r":"KOOIJMAN0027","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman heard something behind the wallpaper, a very old rat. She was going to put down poison the next morning. That evening her daughter and son-in-law were visiting. The daughter stayed, the son-in-law left that evening. After he had gone, she heard a thud on the door. He fell ill and died after nine days. She saw the thud on the door as an omen.","i":"H.K.","o":"'s Avonds toen hoorde ik iets achter het behang. We hadden geen last van muizen. 't Was een verschrikkelijk leven. Ik denk: \"Dat is geen muis, maar bepaald een hele ouwe rot (1) die heel de boel kapot knaagt; morgen zet ik vergif'. Ik had die avond m'n dochter en schoonzoon op bezoek. M'n schoondochter is gebleven, ze liep van haar tweede baby en vooreerst zou er niets meer van (2) komen. M'n schoonzoon ging die avond weg. Toen hij al weg was, hoorde ik in- eens een bons op de deur. Dat was niets voor hem om dat te doen. Hij is ziek geworden en na negen dagen gestorven. Ik heb in die bons op de deur altijd een voorteken gezien.\n\n(1) rat \n(2) een bezoek"},{"n":50580,"r":"KOOIJMAN0034","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In the old days there were beds with hollow rods, painted white. If you took hold of such a rod and felt a vibration go through it, you knew you would die in bed.","i":"H.K."},{"n":50629,"r":"KOOIJMAN0089","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a tree bore fruit twice, they said: \"There will be a death in the family.\"","i":"H.K."},{"n":50640,"r":"KOOIJMAN0100","p":"Lopik","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Death announced itself by knocking on a sick person's door at night.","i":"H.K.","o":"Verscheidene mensen, die bij een zieke waakten, hoorden 's nachts op de deur kloppen. Een paar uur later stierf de zieke meestentijds. Men beweert, dat de dood z'n eige dikwijls aankondigt."},{"n":50910,"r":"KOOIJMAN0211","p":"Benschop","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a bird flies against the window, it foretells a coming death.","i":"H.K.","o":"Als er een vogel tegen het glas vliegt, is dat een doodsbericht."},{"n":50940,"r":"KOOIJMAN0240","p":"Langerak","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At the time of the cattle plague people tried to help one another by sharing and lending surviving cows. It was believed the cattle plague was announced by something like a bundle of wood shavings flying burning over the land.","i":"H.K.","o":"In 1866 had je de veepest*. Als je boer was met twintig koeien en je had d'r vijf over en een ander had er geen een over, dan leende je hum d'r een. En 't kwam dan niet zo krap, wanneer je die geleende koei terug gaf. Ik heb het teken van die veepest eens gehoord van vroegere mensen. Op een zekere tijd keken de mensen achteruit het land. Nou hebbie van die witte spaanders, afval van hoepels maken**. De mensen zaggen iets over het land gaan, net of d'r een spaanderbos brandend over de Langerakse polder vloog. 't Brandde maar 't verbrandde niet. 't Gong over de Langerakse polder tot aan de Poortse Weg toe en dan weer terug. Dan noemde ze het teken van de veepest. Al die plekken daar die spaanderbos heen gegaan was, daar kwam de veepest. Dat wier vast gegloofd!\n\n*De veepest hield verschrikkelijk huis onder de veestapels. Er waren hele boerenbuurten waar praktisch geen koe in leven bleef. Nu nog weet men in de buurt van de hofsteden de plekken aan te wijzen, waar hele veestapels van twintig, dertig of 'meer koeien liggen begraven.\n**van tenen"},{"n":50957,"r":"KOOIJMAN0257","p":"Langerak","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A friend of the narrator's father once saw a crow that kept hopping a bit further. Later his father was found dead among the cows. The narrator himself experienced something similar. He saw a finch singing and also hopping further and further. Later his wife's father died. The narrator, however, does not believe these are omens or signs.","i":"H.K.","o":"De vader van een kammeraad van me diende bij een boer. Op een avond gaat ie* naar huis, hij kwam van melkens af, en daar ziet ie een meter of tien voor 'm uit een kraai zitte. Iedere keer hipte die kraai weer een endjie verder. Toen die thuiskwam, hoorde die dat z'n vader bij de koeien dood gebleven was. Hij had z'n eige kwaad gemaakt op de koeien. 't Was op een zaterdagavond. Ik ga de deur nog even uit, naar de konijnen of zo, een uur of twaalf in de nacht. Je had daar een bogaard. Daar hoor ik een vogel zingen. Dat vinkie zat gewoon te zingen. Iedere keer een endjie verder. Ik ga nooit erges voor op de loop. Ik denk: \"Ik loop ok een endjie mee\". Iedere keer weer zat dat vinkie te zingen. Ik naar binnen en het tegen m'n vrouw gezegd. M'n vrouw zegt: \"Dat is een voorbode. M'n vader kan wel eens gestorven zijn\". 's Maandags kregen we de rouwbrief! Ik voor mijn denk, dat dat vinkie probeerde me van z'n nest weg te lokken. Dat doen ze wel meer, bij wezels ok. Behalve wanneer de wezel te dichtbij zit. Want dan blijve ze stijf zitten, dan kennen ze niks meer doen. Ik heb dat wel eens gezien, ik zat in de bogaard m'n boterham op te ete met de thermosfles naast me. Dat vogeltje wier gewoon gehypnotiseerd door die wezel of die hermelijn.\n\n*die kameraad"},{"n":50960,"r":"KOOIJMAN0260","p":"Langerak","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The death of a sick child was announced by a door that opened and closed by itself.","i":"H.K.","o":"Ik heb wel eens een vrouw horen vertellen, hier in Langerak, die had een kind zien leggen. 't Was er slecht an toe. D'r wier een deur open en dicht gedaan, zonder dat d'r iemand was. 's Nachts is dat kind gestorven. Dat noemden ze een voorbode."},{"n":50985,"r":"KOOIJMAN0284","p":"Stolwijk","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Every evening a cloud shaped like a peacock feather was seen in the east. This was an omen of the cattle plague.","i":"H.K.","o":"In die dagen van de veepest zagen ze in Benschup iedere avond in 't oosten een wolk an de lucht, net een pauweveer. Dat was een voorbode van de veepest."},{"n":51007,"r":"KOOIJMAN0305","p":"IJsselstein","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Scissors falling out of a sewing box turn out to be an omen of a death.","i":"H.K.","o":"VOORTEKENEN VAN STERFGEVAL\n\nBij ons in huis (in Schoonhoven) is 't gebeurd dat d'r een schaar uit de naaidoos viel. Niemand kwam d'r aan. \nM'n moeder zee:\n-Dat betekent: vanavond een sterfgeval. \nEen tante, die ziek was, is dezelfde avond gestorven."},{"n":51009,"r":"KOOIJMAN0306","p":"IJsselstein","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A screeching magpie is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"H.K.","o":"VOORTEKENEN VAN STERFGEVAL\n\nWe woonden in Schoonhoven. M'n moeder was bezig kinderponnetjes te strijken. Vroeger hadde ze van die mooie satijne nachtponnetjes. \nEen van de kindere was ziek. Een kind van vijf maanden. \nDie wagen met dat kind stond in de tuinkamer. \nVlak voor de tuinkamer stond een pereboompie. \nDaar zat een ekster in, te schreeuwe en tekeer te gaan.... \nM'n moeder zegt:\n-Dat kind kan dat ponnetje vanavond weleens aan moeten. \n 's-Avonds is het kind gestorven."},{"n":51010,"r":"KOOIJMAN0307","p":"IJsselstein","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A falling mirror is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"H.K.","o":"VOORTEKENEN VAN STERFGEVAL\n\nWe hadden opa in huis (in Schoonhoven). We hadden licht gemaakt, want we dachten, anders valt-ie van de trap af. \nIk sta me boven te wassen en de spiegel valt van de muur.\n M'n moeder zegt:\n-Dat betekent een sterfgeval. \n's-Nachts viel opa van de trap af. Twee dagen later is tie gestorven."},{"n":70094,"r":"KOOIJMAN0552","p":"Hoogblokland","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The howling of a dog means a death within three days.","i":"H.K."},{"n":70178,"r":"KOOIJMAN0617","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls horribly, a death follows within a few days.","i":"H.K.","o":"As een hond gruwelijk jankt, binne enkele dage een sterfgeval"},{"n":70299,"r":"KOOIJMAN0730","p":"Polsbroek","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Omens of misfortune: a piece of bacon falling from the chimney; the screeching of an owl; a thud on the door.","i":"H.K.","o":"Voortekenen van ongeluk: een stuk spek, dat uit de schoorsteen valt; het krijsen van een uil; een bons op de deur."},{"n":206952,"r":"KUSTERS003505","p":"Deurne","v":"N.-Br.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A carpenter has his own coffin ready.","i":"C.K.","o":"Er was 'n timmerman, die al lang z'n eigen doodskist klaar had staan."},{"n":208215,"r":"LINSSEN000306","p":"Beesel","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A bruise on the leg is an omen of a death.","i":"G.H.L./H.T.","o":"Voorteken.\nDe moeder van verteller kreeg voor de scheen herhaalde malen een blauwe plek als van geronnen bloed. Dit was voor haar een onfeilbaar voorteken, dat een familielid ging sterven. Moeder maakte hun daarop attent en zo heeft verteller wel drie of vier keer zich ervan overtuigd. Na zo'n sterfgeval verdween die plek."},{"n":208317,"r":"LINSSEN002305","p":"Sint Odiliënberg","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Seeing three magpies is an omen of a death.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Als iemand drie eksters bij elkaar zag, dan zou iemand uit de familie sterven."},{"n":42678,"r":"SPORTEL000101","p":"Scheemda","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A carpenter's wife hears knocking and planing in the evening, but there is nothing to be seen. Her husband says his next job will then be making a coffin. The next day he is commissioned to make a coffin.","i":"J.S.","o":"Naar aanleiding van de vraag over oude verhalen, klopgeesten etc. wist wed. A. Boedeltje-Stijkel het volgende te vertellen. \nToen haar ouders Karel Stijkel en Catharina Koers nog kort getrouwd waren, was het volgende gebeurd. Karel Stijkel was timmerman van beroep en in die tijd waren het lange werkdagen en de verdiensten laag. Haar moeder ging daarom uit werken. Tegen de avond haastte zich dan naar huis om het eten nog klaar te maken. 's Avonds wachtte dan nog haar huiswerk. 't Werd vaak laat op de avond dat ze vermoeid te bed ging. Haar man was meestal al eerder te bed gegaan. Op een avond was haar vader reeds te bed gegaan en haar moeder was nog druk aan 't verstelwerk bezig. 't Was al diep in de avond, toen hoorde ze in 't achterhuis, waar de werkbank van haar man stond, kloppen en schaven. 't Was alsof iemand druk aan 't werk was. Dodelijk verschrikt maakte ze haar man wakker en zei, dat er een inbreker in 't achterhuis was. Stijkel kwam het bed uit en ging op onderzoek uit. Er was echter niets te bespeuren. Toen moeder Stijkel volhield dat ze kloppen en schaven had gehoord, liet Stijkes zich ontvallen: \"Den mout ik zeker 'n kist moaken\". Daarop gingen ze ter ruste. De volgende dag kreeg Stijkel inderdaad een opdracht een doodkist te maken. Moeder Stijkel heeft toen gezegd: \"Dat is de eerste, moar ook de leste kist, dei toe moakst\". Daaraan heeft Stijkel zich ook gehouden."},{"n":209151,"r":"VRIES000601","p":"Zaamslag","v":"Zl.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man born with a caul foresees deaths and other things that will happen in the future.","i":"J.d.V.","o":"MET DE HELM GEBOREN. \n\"Over spookgeschiedenissen en zwarte kunst heeft mijn moeder ons als kinderen wel eens wat verteld, meneer, maar dat is al zo lang geleden, dat ik het moeilijk meer aan elkaar kan knopen\", zegt Jan Verhelst 81 jaar oud, die op het Zaamslagseveer B 78 woont.\nWat ik nooit ben vergeten is het verhaal dat moeder ons deed over \"den Ouwen Arjaan\", die ongeveer 1880 in het Achterstraatje te Zaamslag woonde. Zijn eigennaam weet ik niet meer, want men noemde toen de mensen meestal bij hun bijnamen.\nDie \"Arjaan\" dan was volgens moeder \"met de helm geboren\"! \nDe \"Minne\" (baker), die bij Arjaans geboorte tegenwoordig was, wist te vertellen dat er om het hoofdje van het kind bij de geboorte een soort van bandje liep, dat later verdween. Je mocht daar volstrekt niet aankomen; probeerde je het met water weg te wassen, dan zou het kind later verdrinken; probeerde je het met warme middelen, dan zou het kind op oudere leeftijd door het vuur sterven!\nBij het opgroeien deed zich bij Arjaan niets vreemds voor, maar toen hij reeds lang getrouwd was en de kinderen al groot waren kwam het nogal eens voor, dat Arjaan stil voor zich uit zat te staren. De familie wist dan, dat Arjaan \"iets zag\"!\n\"Zie je weer wat, Vader?\" vroeg de moeder dan.\n\"Ja, vrouwe, ze gaan weer voorbij; ik zie weer een lijkstoet!\"\n\"Is t verre?\" vroeg de moeder dan. Want dat wilde ze graag weten. Immers, reeds"},{"n":209162,"r":"VRIES000902","p":"Axel","v":"Zl.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Seeing mourning clothes and a radiant Mary as a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of dying.","i":"J.d.V.","o":"EEN BIJZONDERE GAVE.\n'k Woonde, 't was nog voor de eerste wereldoorlog, op Drieschouwen (gemeente Axel) en hield daar een café; mijn man deed kleine zaken.\nTegenover ons woonde een gezin met twee dochters, Zulma en Madeleine. Zulma was een beeldschoon meisje en we waren als buren heel goed met elkaar. Jammer genoeg liet de gezondheid van Zulma veel te wensen over en reeds voor de derde maal werd ze naar Vlissingen gebracht om te worden geopereerd. Toen ik haar op een dag ging bezoeken en ik te Vlissingen met de boot aankwam, was het zeer laag water. Men liep toen niet zo gemakkelijk van de boot de wal op, zoals nu. Een aantal glibberige trappen moesten eerst worden bestegen. Toen ik bezig was langs die trappen te lopen, waar wat werkmensen met herstelling bezig waren, zag ik stapels rouwgoed op die trappen liggen. Ik vroeg een werkman waarom dat goed daar lag. Maar de man, die zelf niets zag en mij misschien voor \"niet wel bij ’t hoofd\" aanzag, zei: \"Neem dat spul dan maar mee!\"\nIn het ziekenhuis gekomen bij Zulma zag ik wel, dat het haar niet best ging en was ik bij mijn vertrek erg bedroefd.\nToen ik buiten het ziekenhuis was gekomen zag ik in Noordwestelijke richting in de heldere avondlucht \"Onze Lieve Vrouwe\" als omkranst met stralen, zich voor mij aftekenen.\nEn zo ontsteld was ik daarover, dat ik een tijdlang op die plaats ben blijven staan.\nO.L.V. was voor mij \"als Maagd\""},{"n":209164,"r":"VRIES000904","p":"Axel","v":"Zl.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Seeing an image of Christ before the mother's death.","i":"J.d.V.","o":"EEN BIJZONDERE GAVE.\nOok de dag vóór mijn moeder stierf en dat is al heel lang geleden, is mij een dergelijk beeld verschenen. Maar het was het beeld van Christus aan het Kruis, zoals U het hier op de schoorsteen onder de glazen stolp ziet staan, maar dan levensgroot!"},{"n":209171,"r":"VRIES001101","p":"Hoek","v":"Zl.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Seeing funeral coaches driving through the fields is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of deaths.","i":"J.d.V.","o":"NOG ÉÉNMAAL RONDOM HOEK.\n\"Kinders\", zei moeder dan wel eens tegen ons: \"denkt er om, als je 's avonds een keer wat laat uit Hoek terugkomt, ga dan nooit langs \"'t Ouwe Jantje de Kraker\" of langs \"'t Sluusje\" (zie ook mijn verslag I 112-3 [Hernummering Collectie De Vries, verslag 3, Maria van Alten-Jansen]) want daar deugt het niet!\"\nWant moeder en ook andere mensen uit de buurt hadden meer dan eens in die omgeving van de Koudepolder, tegen de Noorddijk aan, gezien, dat in het schemerdonker 30 of 40 rouwkoetsen, allen met twee zwarte paarden ervoor gespannen, langzaam werden voortgetrokken, soms dwars door de landerijen! De paarden konden dan bijna geen poot verzetten of ze raakten een wild konijn. Zwermen van die beestjes dansten als het ware tussen de paarden en de wagens door.\nLang duurde dat gezicht nooit, maar wat wel vreemd was: als de een of ander zoiets had gezien, kon je ér vast en zeker op rekenen, dat er op Hoek of in de omliggende polders zich een paar plotselinge sterfgevallen voordeden."},{"n":42741,"r":"WEV000101","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog starts howling before deaths, and lies down on the spot where the carpenter later puts a coffin.","i":"F.W.","o":"De heer Hummel vertelt:\n\nWe woonden te Nieuw-Weerdinge. \nRondom was alles veen.  \nHier en daar stonden enkele huizen.  \nOnze naaste buren hadden een hondje, een dobermann. \n Ik weet zeker, dat het hondje van te voren wist, waar een sterfgeval zou zijn. \nHet begon dan erg te huilen. \nHet volgende heb ik mee gemaakt. \nDe hond stond eens voor een brug. \nDe buren riepen hem, maar hij wou beslist niet thuis komen. Tenslotte moest hij over de brug gejaagd worden.\nHet dier vloog de kamer binnen en ging onder de tafel liggen. Daar was het niet van daan te krijgen. \nWat gebeurt een paar dagen later? \nDe timmerman moet een lijkkistje weg brengen.  \nOnderweg gaat hij even bij de buren aan om een borrel te drinken. De mensen hadden namelijk een \"stille knip\". \nHet kistje zet hij zolang onder de tafel, op de plek waar de hond van te voren gelegen had."},{"n":42742,"r":"WEV000102","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog jumping against the back door of a house where someone has died is an omen that the coffin will go out through the back door. A man tries to prevent this by locking the back door, but while he is digging the grave the coffin goes out through the back door after all.","i":"F.W.","o":"De heer Hummel vertelt over dezelfde hond. \n\n In de buurt is een vrouw gestorven. De hond springt bij het sterfhuis steeds tegen de achterdeur omhoog. Mijn vader zei: Dat betekent, dat de kist op de dag van de begrafenis de achterdeur uitgaat. Maar deze keer krijgt die verwenste hond zijn zin niet. De dag breekt aan. Mijn vader zal zorgen, dat de achterdeur op slot blijft en dat de zijdeur wordt gebruikt. Maar wat wil 't geval? De graf-delver is die dag ziek. \nNu moet mijn vader invallen.\n En intussen gaat de kist door de achterdeur. \nPas op voor dobermann-honden. \nwij willen ze niet in huis hebben."},{"n":43212,"r":"WEV001402","p":"Mussel","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Sons do not believe their father's prediction that the new horse will carry him to the churchyard, but it comes true. Earlier the father saw wagons without horses; question of whether the blood he sees on the road is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of war.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ja, er bestaat toch zo iets als voorgezicht.\nBij de oude Terborg in Onstwedde kwamen zijn jongens eens thuis van de markt.\n\"Kiek,\" zeggen ze, \"wie hebt ain mooi wit peerd koft.\"\n\"Dat hadden ie nich doun möst, jongs, dat peerd brengt mie noar 't kerkhof,\" zegt de oude.\n\"Och, kom nou,\" antwoorden de zoons.\n\"Gleuf mie, jongs, hai brengt mie vot.\"\nMaar de oude is gestorven.\nEn de jongens zeiden: \"Het widde peerd zol nich veur de woagen.\"\nMaar ja, wat komen moet, dat komt.\nVan de andere paarden was de ene kreupel, een tweede onwillig, zodat de witte voor de wagen moest.\n\nDiezelfde Terborg heeft ook meer dan eens gezegd: \" 'k Zai aol man woagens zunder peerd op de weg tussen Mussel en Onstwedde.\" Dat waren later de auto's. \n\nOok heeft hij wel eens gezegd:\n\"k Zai aal man bloud, bloud, bloud.\n't Stroomt over de wegen.\" \nHeeft hij misschien de aprildagen van 1945 voorzien, toen hier de bevrijders tegen de Duitsers vochten? Of staat ons nog iets te wachten?"},{"n":43315,"r":"WEV001901","p":"Barnflair","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"No belief in witchcraft; belief that the screeching of a magpie and the howling of a dog were voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Van hekserij wil ik niets weten.\nVraag me er dus niet naar.\nDoe die lijst maar gauw weg, want ik geloof er niet aan.\n\"Ook niet aan ekster-gekrijs?\"\nJa, wat zal 'k daarop zeggen. Mijn vrouw gelooft er zeker aan. Omdat ze het heeft meegemaakt.\nMijn schoonmoeder was indertijd bezorgd over zo'n ekster. Het beest liep voor 't huis te krijsen. Of het zat in een \"wacholderbosje\" in de buurt.\nZe - schoonmoeder - zei dan: \"Jaag dat beest toch weg; dat belooft vast geen goeds.\" Haar man lachte er om, maar joeg de vogel toch maar weg.\nNu is het waar, dat de vrouw drie maand later is gestorven, maar trotzdem geloof ik niet, dat de ekster het geweten heeft. M'n vrouw twijfelt er niet aan.\n\nOok is hier een poos geleden een man gestorven, waar van te voren vaak een hond zat te huilen voor het huis.\n\"Zie je wel\", zegt mijn vrouw dan, \"zo'n beest weet iets\". Maar ik denk, dat het \"blooss\" toeval is."},{"n":43322,"r":"WEV002004","p":"Mussel","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A light above a pool is seen as an omen of an accident. Later a boy drowns there who had got drunk out of grief at being rejected by a girl.","i":"F.W.","o":"Achter de boerderij van mijn broer in Mussel was in het \"oal daip\" - de Mussel A - een diepe kolk. Zw. Tuin ziet op een avond boven die kolk een licht branden. Ze vermoedt een komend ongeluk. En dit komt.\n'n Poos later is er een feest. Een jonge man - G.D. - vraagt een meisje, of ze 's avonds met hem uit wil. Ze heeft er geen zin in. \nVan verdriet drinkt hij zich dronken.\nLater heeft 't kind spijt van haar weigering, want D. wordt de andere dag dood uit de kolk gehaald."},{"n":45323,"r":"WEV002301","p":"Nieuw-Buinen","v":"Dr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A new dog that howls because it is not used to its surroundings frightens older people, because the howling of dogs means disaster. Magpies are chased away, because they too are voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of misfortune.","i":"F.W.","o":"Om te beginnen, ik zelf geloof niet aan alles, wat op bijgeloof berust.\nWel wil ik vertellen, wat ik gehoord heb van mensen, die er waarde aan hechten; aan dierengeluiden bijvoorbeeld.\nIndertijd had mijn broer te 2e Exloërmond een hond met kar. Daarmee bracht hij de waren naar de klanten.\nZo moest hij ook eens naar het Moeras met een nieuwe hond voor de kar.\nHet beest was nog wat onwennig en jankte daarom telkens. Vooral als mijn broer lang in huis was bij de mensen. \nDaar komt hij dan met de korf bij een paar ouwe lui. Als hij de deur open doet, ziet hij de man handenwringend in de kamer staan. De man groet niet, maar kermt: “Oo, oo, oo!”\nMijn broer begrijpt er niets van. Hij loopt door naar de keuken en daar staat de vrouw te “jeuzeln.”\n“O, wat is ’t wat!”\nDan vraagt mijn broer:\n“Wat is hier toch aan de hand? Is er iemand ziek?”\n“Man,” zeggen ze dan, “hoor je hem niet?”\n“Wie of wat moet ik horen?”\n“Nou man, die hond toch van jou. Hij jankt al maar door en kijkt deze kant op. Nu gaot een van ons beiden dood.”\n“Welnee,’” zegt mijn broer, “Ik heb een nieuwe hond en die moet nog wat wennen. Maak je maar geen zorgen.”\nZo probeerde hij de oude lui wat gerust te stellen, hoewel het hem niet gemakkelijk viel. Want honde-gejank, dat voorspelde iets ergs. Dat is nu ongeveer vijftig jaar geleden.\n\nHet is misschien nog maar tien jaar geleden dat sommige mensen in Buinen de eksters wegjoe","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45341,"r":"WEV002405","p":"Stadskanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A howling dog and magpies pecking at the putty of a window pane are an omen of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Voortekens,\nJa hoor, die zijn er. Heel lang is het al geleden, dat de hond bij Z. enige tijd, voordat Z. stierf, voor de woning zat te huilen. Betrekkelijk kort geleden is het, dat er een hond zat te janken bij het huis van een buurvrouw, die eveneens even later stierf. Nadien was dan het gehuil afgelopen. Zo’n beest heeft dan toch een voorgevoel.\nIn Smeerling bij Onstwedde waren eksters boze voorboden. Ze pikten de stopverf uit het venster, ook bij een woning, waar daarop iemand stierf.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45349,"r":"WEV002502","p":"Barlage","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A pool in which a mill sank; a pool in which hay wagons vanished and in which a coach disappears after a voice in the water asked where the man is, for the time has come. A will-o'-the-wisp above the pool means that someone will drown or that a house will be built.","i":"F.W.","o":"De Mussel-Aa. \n“’t oal daip” was vroeger erg breed. \nIn de jaren veertien-vijftien is het kanaal gegraven. Daarvoor moest “’t aol daip” al het water vervoeren.\n’s Winters stonden uitgestrekte landerijen blank. Hier en daar waren diepe kolken. Toen ik osheer - kouheer of baistheer - was, heb ik wel eens met een stok geprobeerd, of ik de bodem raken kon, maar dat ging nooit\nDoor de ouders werd ook altijd tegen de kinders gezegd: “Kom nich bie de kolk’n.”\nZo is ’t er in Mussel een “meulenkolk.” Men zei vroeger, dat daar een molen in verzonken was.\nIn de Musselmee, tussen Mussel en Barlage, was een heel gevaarlijke kolk.\nDaar waren al wagens hooi met paard en al in verdwenen.\nOp een keer is er een stem uit het water gekomen.\n“De tijd is er wel, \nmaar de man is er niet.”\nEn zie, op ’t zelfde ogenblik komt er een koets aan. En par does stort deze koets met de man in de kolk.\n\nOp de Zandtangerweg werden boven de kolk altijd dansende lichtjes gezien. Men zei dan, daar verdrinkt nog een keer iemand of er komt een huis. Verdronken is er niemand, daar tenminste niet, wel een vijfhonderd meter er vandaan, nu zo’n zestig jaar geleden.\nMaar een huis staat er wel, zoals je weet. Want daar woon je zelf nu in.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45376,"r":"WEV002902","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog starts howling while looking at a house where a dead person is laid out; foreseeing a fire; seeing funeral processions.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mijn moeder was ook eens op een plaats, waar een lijkkist boven de aarde stond. Toen zag ze, dat er een klein hondje aan kwam, voor op de weg ging zitten, naar het huis keek en begon te huilen.\nIn ’t begin wou ze er niet over praten, later vertelde ze ’t ons.\nZe wist ook te vertellen van branden, die van te voren gezien waren; van personen, die lijkstaties zagen, maar ik ben de namen vergeten."},{"n":45389,"r":"WEV003002","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Omens of deaths; seeing funeral processions and the colour of the horse pulling the hearse.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mijn vader liep eens te Mussel met een vriend. ’t Was bij avond. Dan zegt de kameraad: “Kom hier, je valt zo meteen.” Vader liep echter door en zie, ineens ligt hij op de grond. “Je bent over die en die heen gekomen,” zegt dan de ander. En niet lang daarna is de man begraven, die mijn vader had laten strompelen.\nDe oude heer ging op een avond even uit naar de buren. ’n Poosje later was hij er al weer; ’t gezicht vol angstzweet.\n“Wat nou,” zeggen we.\nHij zegt: “Wat of het was, weet ik niet, maar er ging net vlak iets langs me heen; ‘k ben zo geschrokken.”\nMaar toen even later mijn moeder begraven werd, zei hij: “Dat is ’t geweest.”\nIk heb dus heel wat van de oude baas gehoord. Hij heeft iemand gekend, die van de lijkstaties ook de paarden zag. Zo eens een met een wit paard voor de wagen. Toen hij dat vertelde , zeiden de mensen: “Dat kan niet, want in de buurt zijn alleen zwarte paarden. De man zelf heeft een witte, maar dat is te vurig. Doch op de dag van de begrafenis waren de zwarte paarden onwillig, zodat toch het witte dier de wagen trok."},{"n":45390,"r":"WEV003003","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A voice calls from a tree that the time has come, but not the man. The next day a man falls from the tree and dies.","i":"F.W.","o":"In Onstwedde stond vroeger een boom. Op een dag hoorde men boven uit de takken roepen: “De tijd is er, waar is de man?” \nEen dag later moet de boom geveld worden. \nEen man klimt er in; bevestigt de touwen boven aan een tak en valt dan ineens naar beneden. Hij is dood."},{"n":45391,"r":"WEV003004","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Little lights as a portent of prison camps and the death of a cowherd boy.","i":"F.W.","o":"Nu zal ik vertellen, wat mijn vrouw en ik zelf gezien hebben in Sellingerbeetse. \nWe zagen lichten over de heide dwalen! \nWat verrees daar naderhand? Het kamp, waar in de oorlog Joden opgesloten waren en daarna de N.S.B.-ers.\nOok hebben we enige tijd een lichtje in een weiland zien dansen. Een slecht voorteken. Weet je, wat er gebeurde? Het zoontje van P. weidde daar na schooltijd de koeien. Op een keer heeft het jongetje het touw om de nek geslagen; de koe ging er van door en zo is ’t knaapje gewurgd. Daarna was het licht verdwenen."},{"n":129844,"r":"WOUDA023010","p":"Workum","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"During the search for a missing person a lantern suddenly goes out; the missing person turns out to have drowned.","i":"E.W.","o":"Oan de âld skatting ûnder Heech wenne froeger Bonne Bosma. Syn pakesizzer libbet noch. Dy man dronk, mar kaem altyd goed wer thús. Mar op in joun bleau er lang wei en de frou stjûrde de faem mei in lantearne der op út. Underweis fleach de lantearne út, samar sûnder bipaelde reden, want it wie stil waer, er stoun se yn 't tsjuster. De boer kaem net thús, mar letter waerd er foun yn de Easthimmer mar.","l":"Fries"},{"n":43569,"r":"AMPT000801","p":"Hasselt","v":"Ov.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Stubbing your foot against a stone means a funeral.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"A'j over de weg liepe en je stootte je voet tegen 'n stien dan kwam er een begrafenisse.","l":"Overijssels"},{"n":11562,"r":"CJ000507","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman born with a caul tells the neighbour's boy that they will both be at a funeral and that she will nod to him when he stands at the gap in the hedge. The boy's father dies. The boy resolves not to stand at the gap in the hedge, but he is pushed that way without noticing. When the neighbour woman sees him, she nods to him.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Sumarreheide wenne Antsje. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dat wist in elk wol. Op in kear makke har buorjonge in praetsje mei har.\nIs der ek hwat nijs? frege der.\nNé, ik soe 't net wite, sei Antsje.\nKomt der ek hwat nijs? frege de jonge doe. Antsje sei: \nAst it dan dochs wite wolst, ja. Der komt in sterfgefal. En dêr komme dû en ik beide by op bigraffenis.\nIkke? sei de jonge. Dêr woed er neat fan leauwe. Dat kin ommers net, sei er. Dan geane ús heit en mem ommers mei.\nDoe sei Antsje: Ik sil dy wol even taknikke ast foar 't gat fan 'e hage stieste.\nIn pear dagen letter krige de jonge syn heit in biroerte en kom to forstjerren. Doe tocht de jonge: As it nou bigraffenis wurdt, dan sil 'k oppasse, dat ik net foar 't gat fan 'e hage komt to stean.\nOp 'e dei fan 'e bigraffenis kom it folk ta it sterfhûs út. Der wie net folle rûmte op it hiem, dat der woarde sein: Hwat oan kant!\nEn sa gebeurde it, dat de jonge, sûnder dat hy der erch yn hie by it gat treaun waerd.\nDat seach Antsje en sy knikte de jonge ta.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11574,"r":"CJ000517","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People are afraid to skate at the spot where, in summer, boatmen have seen skaters fall through the ice and drown.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie yn 'e simmer en fier foar myn tiid. Doe foeren der skippers oer de Galle by Grou. Dy kommen fan Ljouwert. Sy seagen samar ynienen in baen mei ridersfolk. It wienen dûbelde banen. Alle minsken dy't op en by de banen wienen sakken troch it iis hinne en forsûpten. It wie in allerfreeslikst gejammer.\nLetter wienen de minsken fan Grou altyd skruten om dêr to riden. Foaral de âldere minsken hienen it der net op stean. Mar de ramp is noch net neikom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12204,"r":"CJ0007A02","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A girl sees a horse go wild and die, then be strung up and taken away. When she tells of it the horse is healthy, but a day later what she saw comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't myn suster in great fanke wie, sahwat in twintich jier âld, krigen wy in hynder. Dat hynder wie trije jier. Wy kochten it op in boelguod yn 'e Pein. Doe seach myn suster us op in nacht, wylst dat se op bêd lei, dat it hynder hiel wyld woarde. It sloech en it skopte sa bot, dat it trape de muorre der út. Doe sleepten se it hynder yn 'e skuorre en dêr stoar it. Doe hongen se it op oan in dwarsbynt. Doe kom der in hege wein mei twa hynders der foar en dy helle it op.\nFuort de oare deis fortelde se hwat se sjoen hie. Mar doe wie it hynder noch krekt sa soun as hwat. Der wie neat mei it dier to rêdden.\nMar in dei letter krige it hynder de kolyk. De muorre skopte er stikken. It hynder woarde yn 'e skuorre sleept, it stoar, it kom to hingjen en it woarde troch in hynsteslachter út Ljouwert ophelle yn in hege wein.\nIt gebeurde allegearre krekt sa lyk as myn suster it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":209749,"r":"HOL001107","p":"Eck en Wiel","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of an accident and death; weather predictions.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"V.d. Graaf noemde mij verschillende voortekens, die algemeen bekend zijn, zoals het krassen van uilen bij een huis, ook het tegen de ruiten tikken van deze vogels, het huilen van honden. Dit voorspelde een ongeluk of sterfgeval.\nMinder bekend was mij, dat sommige personen aan het luien van de kerkklok 's zondags meenden te kunnen horen of er spoedig iemand uit de kerkelijke gemeente zou sterven. Tante Siena van de Graaf en opa V.d. Graaf waren er van overtuigd, dat zij dit konden horen. Ze zeiden dan: dsr vron do.'jr sptel\nDat de kat, die zich wast, visite aankondigt, is een algemeen gezegde, maar de toevoeging van V.d. Graaf, dat als de kat daarbij met haar poot over de oren gaat, er mensen met hoeden komen, was nieuw voor mij.\nVeel weervoorspellingen, als die over het weer op Maria Lichtmis (2 febr.), over de groene Kerstmis en de witte Pasen, over dat zwaluwen, als ze laag vliegen, regen aankondigen over het voorkomen van een bonte kraai zijn algemeen bekend. Minder bekend was voor mij: vgsl mst (= mist) sw.intors vros gwt a.r tsjaor(veel mist in de winter, is een goed erwtenjaar. Een ouderwetse is nog: als met Lichtmis de das uit zijn hol kruipt en hij ziet vorst of sneeuw, dan kruipt hij er nog zes weken in."},{"n":209774,"r":"HOL001207","p":"Eck en Wiel","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"An owl calling near the house is a bad omen.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Het roepen van uilen vlakbij een huis was een ongunstig voorteken."},{"n":209795,"r":"HOL001308","p":"Eck en Wiel","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People who have to get up at night to open the churchyard gates for a funeral procession.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Er waren ook mensen, die 's nachts hun bed uit moesten om het hek van het kerkhof open te zetten voor de begrafenisstoet, die daar binnen enkele dagen zou binnentrekken"},{"n":209796,"r":"HOL001309","p":"Eck en Wiel","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The sound of the church bells tells whether there will be a death.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Ook de Van Ecken met Gerrit van Baaren beweerden dat zij 's zondags aan het geluid van de klok konden horen, of er die week iemand zou sterven"},{"n":209798,"r":"HOL001311","p":"Eck en Wiel","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A magpie brings news, which can also be a death.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Een ekster zag men niet graag dicht bij huis. Deze bracht \"nijs\", maar dat kon ook zijn tijding van een sterfgeval."},{"n":209824,"r":"HOL001408","p":"Kesteren","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A corpse lying unburied over a Sunday is an omen of a death in the new week.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Stond een lijk een zondag over, dan volgde er in de nieuw begonnen week weer een sterfgeval. Iemand had het juffr Scholten nog onlangs verteld, toen zij kwam condoleren na het overlijden van haar zuster."},{"n":209825,"r":"HOL001409","p":"Kesteren","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The sound of the bell tolled at a funeral indicates the time of the next funeral.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Aan de klank van de klok, die tijdens de begrafenis wordt geluid, kan men horen, of er spoedig weer een sterfgeval zal plaats hebben."},{"n":209826,"r":"HOL001410","p":"Kesteren","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Occurrences that are a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a funeral.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Het zien van een \"lijkstatie\" was een voorteken van een naderend sterfgeval, ook het gekras van uilen, het geschreeuw van eksters om het huis van een zieke. Gaart den Hoed vertelde dat het gerommel in de planken bij de timmerman dit ook was. Mijn zegslieden, alle 3 leden van een timmermansfamilie hadden het echter nooit gehoord."},{"n":209847,"r":"HOL001506","p":"Kapel-Avezaath","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Omen of drowning; other omens of misfortune.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Voortekens In 1956 is er in dit dorp een jongen verdronken. Dit had plaats op een zondag. De vrijdag daarvoor was die jongen op de fiets van het erf bij zijn huis afgekomen, op de weg slipte hij in het losse grint. Een naderende auto kon door hard remmen nog een aanrijding voorkomen. Het voorval op vrijdag werd als voorteken beschouwd.\nAndere voortekens van onheil waren: het roepen van uilen vlak bij een huis, het tikken van deze vogels tegen de ramen, het krassen van eksters, het huilen van honden."},{"n":209848,"r":"HOL001507","p":"Kapel-Avezaath","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Omen of death; hearing in advance the activities of the day of the funeral.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Van Zijtvelds moeder in 1926 gestorven. Zijn vader had, (het was in de zomer, vroeg in de morgen) in de kamer een vrouwengestalte in het wit zien lopen van het kabinet naar de slaapplaats van zijn vrouw. Spoedig daarna had haar overlijden plaats. Vader Van Zijtveld had dit gezicht aan niemand verteld, voordat zijn vrouw ziek lag. (De verschijning was gezien in de kamer waar wij tijdens de opname zaten). Van Zijtveld (mijn zegsman) had op de avond voor de begrafenisdag van zijn moeder gehoord, hoe in de aangrenzende kamer de kopjes werden goed gezet, terwijl er daar toch niemand aanwezig was."},{"n":209877,"r":"HOL001612","p":"Opheusden","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A corpse lying unburied over a Sunday is an omen of another death; it is not known that the sound of the bell on Sunday indicates the next death.","i":null,"o":"Stond een lijk een zondag over, dan volgde er spoedig weer een dode. (Dat men uit het luiden van de klok 's zondags kon horen, of er in de nieuwe week een sterfgeval zou plaatsen, wisten mijn zegslieden niet)."},{"n":209922,"r":"HOL001718","p":"Kesteren","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The sound of chairs being moved aside turns out to be a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a drowning.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Op het Zand (naam boerderij in Ochten) hoorde men op een dag (het moet zeker meer dan een eeuw geleden zijn) de stoelen in de kamer op zij zetten. Even later bracht men de dochter, die even haar schaatsen was gaan proberen, dood thuis. Zij was verdronken in één van de kolken, die er vlakbij liggen."},{"n":209937,"r":"HOL001733","p":"Kesteren","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog howling is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Nog een voorteken: Bij Vermeer had op een dag een hond vreselijk gehuild. Er was toen bij de familie Vermeer een jongen gelogeerd. Deze jongen werd even na het huilen dood binnengedragen, was verdronken"},{"n":209973,"r":"HOL001909","p":"Maurik","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Omens of death, fire and other misfortune.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Voortekens De moeder van A. van Dijk (caféhouder, die vlakbij V Weelderen woont) stond eens achter haar huis. Ze zag een aantal eksters vliegen en zei toen: \"Komde weer om mijn keint\" (Ze had al een paar kinderen verloren).\nToen de eerste vrouw van Huigen ziek lag, hoorde hij op een nacht honden aanhoudend huilen onder het raam. Zijn vrouw stierf de volgende dag. \nMoeder Gerritse zei, dat als er uilen om het huis vlogen, dit een teken was van naderend onheil. Ook kwamen deze wel aan de ruiten tikken.\nOp Pinkstermaandag in 1903 is in Ingen een gedeelte van de huizen op het dorpsplein afgebrand. De hond van mevr V Weelderen had die nacht telkens liggen huilen. (Haar eerste man was afwezig, aangezien hij als veldwachter die nacht dienst had)."},{"n":210029,"r":"HOL002111","p":"Maurik","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of misfortune; weather rules concerning rain.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Als uilen om het huis krassen, soms tegen het raam tikken, is dit een voorteken van een naderend onheil. Ook is dit het krassen van kraaien en eksters. Als de reiger roept, komt er binnen drie dagen regen. Als de koerduiven dit doen gebeurt hetzelfde, ook als er padden kruipen (Of voor deze twee laatste dieren de termijn van drie dagen geldt, weet ik niet. Aangaande de reiger werd gezegd: Binnen 3 dagen re.gen ofmst ofter re.ger kop.et)."},{"n":131397,"r":"KEUNING008302","p":"Ryptsjerk","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man says he saw beforehand that a boy would drown.","i":"S.K.","o":"Wy wienen ris foar skoaltiid oan it skoskesetten. Doe wy by skoalle kamen, siet de doar op it slot. Wy wienen fiif minuten to let.\nNou, dat spytte ús neat. Wy gongen wer nei de flakte en efkes letter nei de feart. Soe dy noch hâlde? Ien fan ús prebearre it. De hinnereis gong it goed, mar doe 't hy werom soe nei ús kant, sakke hy der troch en fordronk.\nDoe 't Jan Boukes it hearde, sei hy, dat hy foarút wol sjoen hie, dat dit barre soe.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131414,"r":"KEUNING008505","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Hearing the hammering of a coffin in advance, before the order comes to make a coffin.","i":"S.K.","o":"It is, nei min seit faek bard, dat in timmerman, as hy in deakiste meitsje moast, foar dat hy dit wist al it timmerjen oan 'e kiste hearde.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131415,"r":"KEUNING008506","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Ghost-howling of a dog when someone is dying.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ek siet der wol ris in houn by in hûs to spûkgûlen as der ien op stjerren laei.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131434,"r":"KEUNING008706","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A corpse that looks beautiful is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of another death soon.","i":"S.K.","o":"As it lyk yn 'e kiste der moai út seach, seinen se froeger altyd: \"Nou stjert der mei koarten wer ien.\"","l":"Fries"},{"n":131469,"r":"KEUNING009303","p":"Aldtsjerk","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A prediction of a death at the neighbours' comes true when a magpie sits by the neighbours' door.","i":"S.K.","o":"In frou yn Aldtsjerk sei op in kear, dat der ien stjerre soe, hwant der siet by de buorljue in akster foar de doar. De oare deis hinge dy buorfrou har op.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131499,"r":"KEUNING009608","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Owls screeching around a house are a sign that someone is dying.","i":"S.K.","o":"As katûlen om hûs hinne gûlden, dan laei dêr ien op stjerren.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131517,"r":"KEUNING010204","p":"Eanjum","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Sounds of slamming doors are a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of death.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ek yn 'e hûs hearde min faek by nacht frjemde lûden. Krekt as sloegen der doarren bygelyks. Min sei dan, dat der ien dea gean soe.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131519,"r":"KEUNING010301","p":"Eanjum","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman sees a child floating in the water; a day later the child dies.","i":"S.K.","o":"Mem kaem fan Skiermounseach. (Schiermonnikoog). Der wienen de minsken yn har tiid noch wol bygelovich. Sa wie der ek ien, dy koe foarútsjen, dat der ien stjerre soe.\nSa seach dy ris in bern yn it wetter driuwen. Sy seach ek hwat bern it wie. In dei letter wie it bern stoarn.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131520,"r":"KEUNING010302","p":"Eanjum","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A bird tapping on the window is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"S.K.","o":"Sy seinen dêr op it eilânek, dat as der in fûgeltsje oan it rút tikke, der in deade kaem.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131555,"r":"KEUNING010803","p":"Ljussens","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A rook and a magpie in the farmyard are a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"S.K.","o":"As der in roek en in akster op it hiem binne, dan sil der gau ien stjerre.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131558,"r":"KEUNING010902","p":"Ljussens","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Dreaming about fish is a harbinger of a death.","i":"S.K."},{"n":131583,"r":"KEUNING011306","p":"Nijewier","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The ghost-howling of a dog turns out to be an omen of a death.","i":"S.K.","o":"Doe hjir tichteby in houn iderkear stie to spûkgûlen, sei heit, dat der ien stjerre soe. It wie ek sa. In pear dagen letter stoar der in lyts bern.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131599,"r":"KEUNING011702","p":"Easternijtsjerk","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Mother does not believe that the chattering of a magpie is an omen of a death, but she does not like the sound.","i":"S.K.","o":"It is ek ris west, doe wy noch bern wienen, dat der in akster yn 'e beam by ús hûs siet to skatterjen.\n\"Hè.\" sei mem, \"ik woe, dat dat bist mar ophould mei syn geskatter. Net, dat ik der oan leau hjer, dat der ien stjerre sil, mar ik mei der dochs min oer!\"","l":"Fries"},{"n":131603,"r":"KEUNING011706","p":"Easternijtsjerk","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A bell ringing in the middle of the night is said to mean a death.","i":"S.K.","o":"Sa moat it ek ris bard wêze, dat midden yn 'e nacht de klok bigoun to lieden. Nou soe der ien stjerre, seinen se.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131614,"r":"KEUNING011905","p":"Hantum","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Some people hear in advance a coffin entering a house; then a death follows.","i":"S.K.","o":"Der wienen guon, dy hearden, dat der earne in kiste - deakiste - yn 'e hûs brocht waerd. Dan stoar der letter ien.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131654,"r":"KEUNING012701","p":"Burdaard","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Hearing what sounds like two planks knocking together. The next day the same sound is heard while a coffin is being made.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ús heit hat ús ris forteld:\nHy wie ris op in joun, hy wie doe skûtmakkersfeint yn Warten, ûnderwei's fan it Wartenster Wiid nei de buorren, en doe hearde hy in klap, krekt as sloegen der twa planken op elkoar. De oare dei stoar der ien en doe sy de deakiste makken, hearden se krekt sa 'n klap.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131666,"r":"KEUNING012902","p":"Blije","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog howling three nights in a row is an omen of a death.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ik ha ek noch in man kend, dy tige bygelovig wie. Dy saei:\n\"As der trije jounen oan ien in houn sit to gûlen, dan giet der ien dea.\"","l":"Fries"},{"n":131678,"r":"KEUNING013004","p":"Blije","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman knows three days in advance that someone will die.","i":"S.K.","o":"Oan 'e dyk wenne in âld minske, dat wist trije dagen foarút al as der ien stjerre soe.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131682,"r":"KEUNING013008","p":"Blije","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Many rooks are an omen of a death.","i":"S.K.","o":"As der in protte roeken yn 'e loft wienen, soe der ien stjerre.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131690,"r":"KEUNING013203","p":"Ferwert","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A magpie and a rook near the house and a howling dog are omens of a death.","i":"S.K.","o":"As der in akster ôf in âld roek om hûs wie, soe der ien stjerre, sei min. Ek oan it spûkgûlen fan hounen hienen sy doe in hekel.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131709,"r":"KEUNING013506","p":"Hallum","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog's ghostly howling and seeing a funeral procession at night are omens of a death.","i":"S.K.","o":"Der waerd wol sein, dat as in houn spûkgûlde en min seach by nacht in lykstaesje, dan soe der ien stjerre.","l":"Fries"},{"n":72515,"r":"KOOIJMAN1053","p":"Hoornaar","v":"Z.-H.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a corpse lay above ground on a Sunday, another person would die within a week.","i":"H.K."},{"n":72785,"r":"KOOIJMAN1276","p":"Well","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If someone had died on Friday or Saturday, they were not buried. If that corpse was still above ground on Sunday, someone else in the village would die within six weeks.","i":"H.K.","o":"En daar nog iets over dan. As nou een vroue of een man of een kend vrijdags of zaoterdags gesturve was, dan wier 't niet begrave. Ston da lijk bove aarde op zondag, dan kreeg de hier op 't dorp binne zes weke weer unne dode.","l":"Gelders"},{"n":72814,"r":"KOOIJMAN1300","p":"Woudrichem","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"There were fishermen who, coming home at night, met a funeral further along the way.","i":"H.K.","o":"Je had mense hier, van die ouwe vissers, as die 's nachts in den donkere thuiskwame, dan werd er verteld, een eindjie verder kwamme ze een lijkstasie tegen."},{"n":72829,"r":"KOOIJMAN1314","p":"Woudrichem","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howled, it meant a death within three days.","i":"H.K."},{"n":72927,"r":"KOOIJMAN1401","p":"Andel","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If an owl nearby screeches every night, a death can be expected within a few days.","i":"H.K.","o":"Een uil in de buurt die iedere nacht gilt: binnen enkele dagen een sterfgeval."},{"n":127543,"r":"KOOIJMAN2161","p":"Doeveren","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If someone in a family dies and the body has to lie over a Sunday, there will soon be another death in that family.","i":"H.K."},{"n":127614,"r":"KOOIJMAN2254","p":"Drunen","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If an owl called near the house in the evening, there would be a death in the family.","i":"H.K.","o":"Als er 's avonds bij 't huis een uil riep, dan kwam er een dode in de familie."},{"n":127819,"r":"KOOIJMAN2451","p":"Brakel","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Here in Brakel, when the wind was from the north, the bell could drone, such a heavy sound. Then people said: Before it is Sunday, there will be a death.","i":"H.K."},{"n":127831,"r":"KOOIJMAN2463","p":"De Moer","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"An owl screeching at night: a death in the neighbourhood.","i":"H.K."},{"n":127905,"r":"KOOIJMAN2474","p":"Hooge Zwaluwe","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If the night owl screeched right above someone's house, someone in that house would die very soon.","i":"H.K."},{"n":128046,"r":"KOOIJMAN2529","p":"Dongen","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If the rooster crowed while a dead person was laid out, there would be another death within three days.","i":"H.K."},{"n":128047,"r":"KOOIJMAN2530","p":"Dongen","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If the magpies screech in the tree: another death within three days.","i":"H.K."},{"n":207083,"r":"KUSTERS006606","p":"Mierlo","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Hearing running in the house is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of an occupant's death.","i":"C.K.","o":"In 'n huis hoorde men verschrikkelijk hollen. Later bleek dat de aankondiging te zijn geweest van de plotselinge dood van een der bewoners"},{"n":207247,"r":"KUSTERS008101","p":"Asten","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Wondering who the little cat is that appears on the road in the evening.","i":"C.K.","o":"Als een persoonlijke herinnering van rond 1910 in Asten wil ik eraan toevoegen: \nSoms, op donkere avonden, waren wij, op groeiende jongens en meisjes wel 'ns met Moeder op straat. 't Verkeer was nog niet druk en de straatverlichting miniem. Uit 'n zandweg, of van achter 'n huis sprong dan soms 'n katje voor ons op de weg. Wij zagen 't nauwelijks, maar Moeder wees 't ons dan: \"Kiek, wie zò 't zijn?\" \"Wie kan 't zijn Moeder?\" en zij dan: \"Jè dè wit me nie\". Natuurlijk lachten we er om - of fantazeerden mee. Maar ongetwijfeld voelde Moeder dan iets van het magisch geheimzinnige, dat in oude tijden dergelijke feiten omhulde. Zij voelde er beslist iets in van 'n naderend onheil."},{"n":208555,"r":"LINSSEN005402","p":"Wessem","v":"L.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A hare that keeps appearing when the midwife is being fetched is afterwards connected with the death of the pregnant woman.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Spookhaas. Van een inwoner van Wessem, die destijds scheepstimmerman was, had hij het volgende verhaal gehoord. In Grevenbicht moest een vrouw bevallen. Hij moest de vroedvrouw gaan halen in het aan de andere kant van de Maas, op Belgisch gebied gelegen dorp Ehlen. Het was avond en met een roeibootje moest hij zich overzetten. Vlak bij het water zag hij plotseling een haas zitten. Snel verdween hij weer en toen de man aan de overkantgekomen was met de boot, zag hij daar de haas opnieuw, die hem nakwam tot in Ehlen. Daar verdween hij. De vroedvrouw trof hij niet thuis en onverrichter zake keerde hij weer terug naar Grevenbicht. Weer zat de haas hem, zowel aan de Belgische als aan de Nederlandse oever van de Maas op te wachten. Toen hij aan het huis aankwam, waar de bevalling zou moeten plaats hebben, vernam hij dat de vrouw was overleden; hetgeen natuurlijk in verband werd gebracht met de spookhaas."},{"n":208667,"r":"LINSSEN006307","p":"Heel","v":"L.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog howling at night is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"G.H.L."},{"n":208668,"r":"LINSSEN006308","p":"Heel","v":"L.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The chattering of a magpie is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of danger, a marriage or a death.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Wanneer men in het bos een ekster hoort slaan, dreigt er gevaar. Het kan er ook op duiden, dat er binnenkort \"een bruiloft of een lijk\" komt."},{"n":208699,"r":"LINSSEN006605","p":"Hunsel","v":"L.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog howling is an omen of a death.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Wanneer 's nachts een hond huilde, was dat een voorteken dat er iemand binnen vijf dagen zou sterven. De richting waarin de hond dan de kop hield, was de richting waar de dode te verwachten was."},{"n":45397,"r":"WEV003101","p":"Musselkanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Mother told that a brother had seen a coffin being carried in at night. Beside the coffin stood a woman in a white cap. That would suggest that another brother, who was ill, would not live much longer. That did not come true. The brother recovered, but some time later the neighbour woman died. There a woman in a white cap did stand by.","i":"F.W.","o":"Het volgende vertelde mij m’n moeder.\n\n“Dou wie op de Hörsten woonden, hef mien aine bruier ’n keer wat veuroet zain. Onz A. was zaik en ’t leek nich zo best. Mien bruier J. zee op’n mörn teegn mie, dat onz A nich laonk meer leefde, want dat hai - J - wat zain har. Vannacht zag ‘k ’n kiste deur de achterdeure komen mit stro d’r in. Noast de kiste stön ’n vrou mit ’n opsloagen wit mutsie op. ’t Kwam nich allemoal precies oet, want A is weer beter worden. \nMan de buurvrou is ’n zetje loater wol overleden. D’r stön ook ’n vrou bie mit ’n wit mutsie en mit dai vrou is de buurman loater weer trouwd.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45404,"r":"WEV003202","p":"Valthermond","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog sits howling in front of a house for half a year before a death. After the former occupant has been buried from the house, the dog stays away.","i":"F.W.","o":"[Veurloop.]\nVan mien voader heb ‘k wat heurd over ’n jankende hond. t Gebeurde ook in de Muzzel.\nVoader vertelde dan:\n“Op ’t stee van Tuun woonde vrouger ’n S. Hai was kemies en vertrok loater wieder ’t land in. Joaren loater zat d’r zo nôn en dan ’n hond te janken veur ’t hoes.\n’t Het wol ’n haalf joar duurd. ’t Ding kwam nich alle doagen, man wol ’n half joar laank dus. Dou is S. overleden. Hai wör begroaven vanoet ’t hoes in de Muzzel. En noa de begravvenis is de hond d’r nooit weer west.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45413,"r":"WEV003209","p":"Valthermond","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Magpies near the house worry a very big pregnant woman.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik kwam op de Harpel ’n keer bie ’n vroumens, dai in verwachting was.\nZe was ekstroa dik en doar muik ze zuk zörge over.\n“Och man,” zee ze, “door loopt aal mor eeksters op de loane veur ’t hoes, as ’t man goud gèèt mit mie.”\nZai dochde, dat ze ’t in de kroam nich hoaln zol.\nIk heb ’t mens wat gerust steld.\n’t Is ook aal goud goan.\nMoar dei eeksters!\nDat veurspelde gain gouds.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45508,"r":"WEV003401","p":"Zaadstukken","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A light burning at night in a room is an omen of a child's death a few weeks later; a lamp stands by the coffin in the same room.","i":"F.W.","o":"konden vertellen, zijn er meest niet meer. Iets weet ik nog van de overlevering.\nHet zal zo’n zestig geleden zijn.\nOp de Blekslage woonde de familie T. \n’s Zondagsavonds gingen de jongens naar ’t wicht, en kwamen in de regel niet zo erg vroeg ‘thuis.\nNu is ’t op een keer gebeurd, dat een van de knapen naar huis kwam en toen zag hij nog licht op in de kamer.\nDat vond hij vreemd; z’n ouders nog op? Hij gaat naar binnen; het licht is nu uit en de ouwelui liggen in bed.\n“Zijn jullie net onder de wol”, vraagt hij nog.\n“Neen, we liggen er al lang onder.”\n“Ik zag zopas anders nog licht branden.”\n“Onmogelijk, het licht heeft niet gebrand.”\nEen poosje later komt de oudste thuis. Ook hij ziet een lampje branden in het achterkamertje.\nThuisgekomen, moet ook hij ontdekken dat het bedrog is geweest.\nMaar --- enkele weken later sterft er een klein broertje. De kist wordt in het kamertje gezet. Een lampje wordt er ’s nachts bij geplaatst.\nEn dat lichtje nu hadden de beide broers gezien. Want later is het er nooit weer geweest. De jongste van de twee woont nu nog in hetzelfde huis."},{"n":45513,"r":"WEV003403","p":"Zaadstukken","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Before a woman's death, a dog looks howling at the house where she lives. After her death the dog is calm.","i":"F.W.","o":"Bij M. in Onstwedde ging de hond een paar dagen erg te keer. Jankend keek hij naar het huis van een buurman. \n“Wat wil dat beest toch?” vroeg men.\nNu ’t was gauw bekend.\nDe buurvrouw stierf.\nEn daarna was de hond rustig."},{"n":45531,"r":"WEV003602","p":"Wedde","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"It often happened that if a funeral came to the churchyard along one road (of the two roads), the next funeral would come along the same road.","i":"F.W.","o":"In Blijham, had men eertijds twee wegen naar het kerkhof. Kwam er nu een begrafenis langs de ene weg, dan zou de volgende ook weer langs dezelfde weg komen. Zo zei men, en ’s kwam ook vaak uit. De situatie was dus zo\n ingang kerkhof\n\n--------- 3+4, 7+8 enz. -----------1+2, 5+6, enz."},{"n":45537,"r":"WEV003604","p":"Wedde","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog howling and a magpie screeching are a portent of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Hondengehuil en ekster-geschreeuw was altijd een voorbode van sterfgevallen. \nMijn moeder twijfelde daaraan niet."},{"n":45607,"r":"WEV003803","p":"Stadskanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman foresees the funeral of a young man and that a missing child has fallen into a rain barrel, and says her husband should have stepped aside for a funeral procession.","i":"F.W.","o":"Noast ons woonde indertied vrouw Proem. \nDei kon kwoad zain. ’t Mèns har d’r zölf last van. As zai wat zag, mös ze ’t huus uut en d’r noar kieken.”\nZo zag ze beveurbeld ain noar ’t zaikenhuus goan. Dat was toun nait best, want noar ’t zaikenhuus goan betaikende, dat ’t gau ofloopm was. \nD’r gung ais ’n jonge man noar ’t zaikenhuus. mor dei kwam levend weer. De mensken zee’den toun: “Hai is ja weerkomen.”\nMoar vrouw Proem zee: “Joawel, hai is weer in huus, mor hai moakt nait laank meer, want ik heb zien begravvenis al zain.”\n’t Olske hed nog gliek kreegn ook.\nD’r was ook ’n keer ’n kind vot. Alle buren aan ’t zuiken, moar ze vonden niks. \nTot ze bie vrou Proem kwamen.\n“Wat zuiken ie toch?” vruig ze.\n“Is ’n kind weg, en ’t is naarns te vinden.”\n“Kiek den eevm in ’t reegn-vat,” zee ze.\nEn joa heur, stumper was in de reegn-tonne verdronken.\nProem kwam ’n keer in huus en zee: “Ik bin zo-neisies woar bie op loop’n en d’r toun boovm of vaaln. Zol ’t ’n liekstoatie west weezn?”\n“Joa, zeker,” zee ze, “moar was den ook eevn biezied goan, den was d’r niks gebeurd.”\nProem kwam ’n keer in huus en zee: “Ik bin zo-neisies woar bie op loop’n en d’r toun boovm of vaaln. Zol ’t ’n liekstoatie west weezn?”\n“Joa, zeker,” zee ze, “moar was den ook eevn biezied goan, den was d’r niks gebeurd.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45617,"r":"WEV003902","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Hanging a slaughtered animal in a tree means the tree will die, because the life flows out of the tree along with the animal's blood.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mijn vader wilde beslist niet, dat we een geslacht dier aan een boom hingen. “De boom gaat dan dood”, zei hij. Eerlijk gezegd, ’t is ook twee keer gebeurd.\nWe hadden zeven haantjes. Op een dag gingen mijn broers en ik ze slachten. We hongen ze aan een appelboom. Daar komt vader thuis. Hij zegt: “Maar jongens, waarom aan die boom, was er dan geen paal? Nu gaat de boom er aan.”\nEn werkelijk, het volgende jaar was de boom dood. Volgens vader vloeide met het bloed van het dier ook het leven uit de boom.\n’n Poos later hing er bij buurman een konijn aan een pruimeboom. “Zo man, nu pluk je er nooit meer pruimen van,” roept mijn vader. \nBuurman lachte wat, doch het volgende voorjaar was de boom dood.\nIk weet nu niet meer, wat ik er van denken moet."},{"n":45657,"r":"WEV004102","p":"Vledderveen","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man foresees his neighbour's death and that the neighbour's horse will pull the hearse. At the funeral other horses are harnessed, but they will not pull, and the neighbour's horse is harnessed after all.","i":"F.W.","o":"In Onstwedde woonde in mien jonge joaren B.H., ’n roare kerel. Dei zag zo moar liekwoagens van te veuren. \nHai proadde d’r ook over. Zo zee op ’n moal:: “J. --- wordt gau begroaven en buurman P. zien peerd mout veur de woagen.”\nOp dag van begravvenis zeeden lu: “Wie hebben mit dai oale B.H. niks te moaken en doun d’r andere peerden veur.”\nDou d’r mit vot. Moar peerden woln nait trekken. Underweg bleven ze stoan. Ze mozzen d’r best weer veur vot en P. zien peerd kwam d’r veur.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45666,"r":"WEV004104","p":"Vledderveen","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Belief that howling dogs are an omen of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"As ’t hier in Vledderveen vragst, of ze aan hondegejank leuven, den binnen d’r nog verschaiden, dei “joa” zeggen. Moust reken dat hebben de mensken al zo voak mit moakt, dat d’r ’n staarfgeval komp noa hondegehoel, dat paddie lu doar nait aan twiefeln. Trouwens, ’n hekel heb ’k d’r ook aan.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45671,"r":"WEV004106","p":"Vledderveen","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The man who says that a corpse lying unburied over the holidays leads to another death dies a few days after a corpse has lain unburied over the holidays.","i":"F.W.","o":"Vertelde mie ’n keer aine: “As ’n liek de feestdoagen over stait, den gebeurt d’r wat.” En roar, en doar mout ’k voak aon denken, dou dat ais gebeurde ’n poar joar leden, dat d’r mit feestdoagen ’n kiste over stön, is dezulfde man, dei mie ’t vertelde, even loater deur ’n ongeluk dood komen.\nLeufst zo’n proatje nait, moar toch denkst d’r aan.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45773,"r":"WEV004403","p":"Mussel","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Fear of chattering magpies and howling dogs, because they are an omen of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"In de Spoanse griep binnen ja overal ’n bult mensen störven. Dou hast hier ol vrou M. wonen en dei was verschrikkelk baange veur eeksters. As dei schattern, zee ze: “Nô mout d’r weer aine vot.”\nVan hoelende honden zee ze ’t zulfde.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":41141,"r":"WEV004702","p":"Blekslage","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman was not born with a caul, but hears in advance sounds connected to events that happen later.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien moeke was nich mit helm geboren. En toch het ze ais wat heurd, dat loater oetkomen is. \nZai luip mit nog wat vroulu in de Selngderbeetse. Op ains heurden ze peerden klauen. En ’n stem ruip:“Dood-dood-dood.” Wat wil ’t gevol? Joaren loater wordt dat stee bewoond, d’r wordt ’n hoes zet. Binnen ook gounend mit peerd en woagen bie aan ’t waark. En dan komp d’r ’n peerd aan de kletter (= op hol). ’n Kerel rak under de woagen en is dood.\nZai har nog ’n geval. ’t Gebeurde voak, as ze op boet’n was, dat ze zee: “Ik heur aal man ’n doeve in hoes roupen.” Wie hadden gain doeve en wazzen ook nich van plan ain aan te schavven. Man ’t gebeurde ’n moal mit ’n aarvenis, dat d’r ’n roupdoeve overbleef en dou zee voader: “Geef mie hum man mit” Mouder zee dou: “Nôn is doeve d’r ja, dai ’k altied heurde.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":41143,"r":"WEV004704","p":"Blekslage","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A howling dog is voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death, because it is no longer seen after a death in the family.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ja, veurloop bestèèt. Wat hebben mien oln voak ’n hondje achter Jan F. aan lopen zain, ieder keer as dai de melkbuzzen bie de weg zedde. ’t Daier jankde toch. \nTotdat d’r staarfgevaln in de femilie veur völlen, dou zagen ie ’t hondken nich weer.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":41147,"r":"WEV004804","p":"Sellingerbeetse","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A family heard hammers knocking before the carpenter made the coffin in the house of the deceased.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nToun ik nog in Drente woonde, heb ik de volgende gevallen van veurloop heurd.\nIn Roswinkel overleed ain man. \nEn hou gung dat hail vrouger wel ais? \nDeur de grode ofstanden kwam de timmerman den in ’t staarfhuus de kiste moaken. \nDat gebeurde doar ook. Moar het kloppen van de hoamers had de femilie al lang veur tied heurd.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45853,"r":"WEV004902","p":"Musselkanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The howling of a dog is voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a drowning; a magpie brings news of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Voorloop.\nHonden waiten wat. ’k Heb ’t zölf mitmoakt. ’t Zel nou 35 joar leden wezen. \nOp ’n zoaterdag zaggen wie aal moar ’n hond bie daip langs lopen. Ik zeg nog: \n“Dat wai ’k nait, ’t liekt mie nait goud tou. Doar kon best gau aine verdrinken.” \nEn d’ander dag, toun ’k uut kèèrke kwam, ruipen ze mie al in de muide: “D’jong van P. is zo net verdronken.”\n’t Was ’n kwoajong, dei altied mit zien bruier in ’t daip zat. Dizze raize har ’e ongelukkig west. Noa tied hol ik honden in de goaten, as ze stoan te janken. En oksters ook; dei brengen ook berichten over, dat d’r gau ’n staarfgeval komt.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43011,"r":"WEV005104","p":"De Maten","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Sometimes wood for the coffin lies ready in advance; sometimes hammering is heard in that wood.","i":"F.W.","o":"Vrouger wazzen d'r wol mensken, dai al wied van te veuren 't holt veur de doodkiste op beune liggen hadden. “Noodholt” nuimden ze dat. 't Lag achter 't schöstain. \nMan nô gebeurde 't wol es, dat de lu under in de koamer 't kloppen van de hoamers op de spiekers al heurden.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43122,"r":"WEV005306","p":"Roswinkel","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The belief that crows and magpies screeching around a house are an omen of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Biegeleuf is hier nog nich hailndaal vot. Mien zuster is ook nog baange veur kreien en eeksters, dai um 't hoes tou schattern. Dan kan d'r 'n dode komen.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43192,"r":"WEV005604","p":"Nieuw-Weerdinge","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Two examples of why the narrator believes the howling of a dog and the chattering of a magpie are voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of an event.","i":"F.W.","o":"En as ie mie vroagen, wat dunkt joe van honds- en okstergejammer, den heb k toch te veul zain, om dit zo mor weg te gooien. Ik herinner mie nog wel wat.\n\nIn t veen wur n liekkiste voak droagen. n Woagen kon dr nait rieden. Den gebeurde t geregeld, dat dr even rust worn mos, omdat de kiste te zwoar wur. En nou mout ik joe toch verteln, dat dr op dat stee, woar de kiste hen zet wur, voak n hond zat te hoeln. Ie kunt dr van denkn, wat je wiln.\n\nEn wat dei oksters aanbelangt; ik wait nog, dat dr op n goie dag n haile vlocht oksters om n huus tou vloogn. Veul meer as anders en de haile dag. Ain dag loater is dat huus opbrand. \nDat is toch wel vrumd; temeer omdat de oksters dr nait weer west binnen in zo n menigte.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43182,"r":"WEV005605","p":"Nieuw-Weerdinge","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"More and more black cats walk around a lamppost near the house of a sick person.","i":"F.W.","o":"Was n moal zaike in n huus. Volgens andern zol dr aingoal zwaarde katn veur t huus om n lanteernpoale tou loopn hebben. D'r zoln ook aal mor meer komen weezn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43263,"r":"WEV005902","p":"Wessingtange","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Disbelief that a dog's howling is a bad omen disappeared after a death in the house a howling dog had been looking at.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nHondegehoel heb k zulf wol al oplet.\nk Har van andern wol heurd, dat t gejank n slecht veurbeduudsel is, man k kon t hoast nich leuven. Man op n dag zag k hier dan aine op n loane zitn achter n boerderij. Hai keek aal man in de richtn van t hoes en jankte oakelk. t Was man n poar moand loater, dat de boer overleden is. Noa tied is de hond dr nich weer west.\nt Was n hond mit dai gele vlekn boven de oogn. Dat soort dut veural.\nWant k heb ook n moal zo n hond verruild mit n Duutsker. Dai Mof zee:“t Is wal n besten hund, oaber hai schrout ja zo, wenn dr dode komp.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43267,"r":"WEV005904","p":"Wessingtange","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Man foretells a death; he can also pass through locked doors.","i":"F.W.","o":"In Onstwedde heb k als grode knecht daind. Dr was ook n lutje knecht en dai komp op n oavend in hoes en zegt:“Hier komp n staarfgeval in dit hoes.”\nIk zeg:“Jong, schei oet tezeurn.”\nMan d kwoajong kreeg wol gliek.\nt Was hailemoal n aigenoardige vent. Want ik trof m loater weer under dainst; ik was veur herhoaln en hai lag dr veur zien nummer. Zai wassen euvel mit hum aan; as e in de bak zat, können ze deuren nich zo stief ofgröndeln, of hai hai kwam dr weer oet. Loater hebben z um wegstuurd.\nt Binnen roare dingen, man k heb ze mitmoakt.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43362,"r":"WEV006406","p":"Nieuw-Weerdinge","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"General belief that the howling of a dog and the cawing of a magpie are an omen of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Algemeen dachte de mensen, dat honde-gehuul een dode betekende; ekstergekras was eveneens gevoarlijk. \nt Zal ook wel es n moal uutkomen weezn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43409,"r":"WEV006801","p":"Vriescheloo","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Man says he foresaw someone's death, and says he saw a house on fire, but the house is still standing.","i":"F.W.","o":"Het ainigste, dat ik van biegeleuf wait, dat is veurloop.\nZukke dingen heb k wel es acht op geevn.\nIk herinner mie n poar gevaln.\nJoarn leden gungen es n boer mit de knecht mit de woagn noar t land.\nt Wazzen beide zoepkalver en moggen geern borrel.\nMit heur doene kop hebben ze t peerd toun op de loop kreegn.\nDe boer is teegn n boom aan komen en was dood.\nMoar ol schoolmeester hier zee toun:“Dat heb ik n zet leden al zain.”\nHai har voaker zukke dingen bie de hand.\nToun e es n moal van de Pekel kwam, zag e t hoes van de stelmoaker in brand stoan. Dat vertelde-e teminste.\nMoar t hoes is nooit opbrand en stait dr vandoage nog.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43412,"r":"WEV006804","p":"Vriescheloo","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The howling of a dog and a magpie pecking at the window are omens of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Woor de mensn wel heurig veur wazn, dat was honne-gehoel.\nDen kun je dr op reekn, dat dr n dode kwam. Ik denk, dat dr nou nog wel zukke lu woonn.\nZo wazn z ook baange, as de oksters op vensterbaanke zitn gungen en aan t roam piktn. Den was [t] ook gau ofloopn mit aine.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43572,"r":"WEV006902","p":"Vriescheloo","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Prediction that something will happen by a canal; people with a light were seen crossing a road. Later a drowned boy was carried home along that path in the evening.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nOabram zag nog meer. Wazzen es n poar jongelu, dei zoln troun-n. \nToun de haile boudel veurmekoar was, woln ze de meubels koopn in Winschootn. t Wicht gung dr op of en de jong zol den in Winschootn bie heur koom-m. Hai bedochde zuk en verdronk zuk in n wieke.  \nMoar, en hier gait mie t om, oal Oabram har al joarn van te veurn zegd:“Doar gunders bie de wieke gebeurt nog es n keer wat. Ik zai dr mensn deur t veld trekn; langs dei loane goan ze en koom-m bie dei boerderij oet. Misschain verdrinkt dr wel aine. Ik zai ook, dat ze n lichie bie zuk hebben.” \nEn net zo is t gebeurd. Bie oavend hebben ze de jong langs t zulfde pad van de wieke noar hoes brocht.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43576,"r":"WEV006903","p":"Vriescheloo","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Cries for help are heard long before people drown at that spot in a canal dug later.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nMien voader kon asmis ook wat zain. Hai was dr nait zo staark in as Oabram, moar ik herinner mie toch wel wat dingn.\n Joarn veur dat t daip groaven is, kwam e es n keer in hoes en zee;“Wat door in t veen gebeurt, dat wai k nait. Wordt aal mor “help, help” roupn. Zol dr nog ais aine verdrinkn in de veenputn?” \nIe moutn reekn, t was toun aal nog veen in de richtn van de grens. Toun wur in 1914 t knoal groavn. Op n winterdag gun-gen wie mit n stel jongelu hen te scheuveln. t Ies was niks te staark en ik zee nog zo:“Ken best aine van ons verdrinkn, want mien voar het vrouger hier aine help roupn heurd.”\n En de zulfde dag binnen dr twei jonges verdronkn; ongeveer, woor voader dat geroup weg heurd har.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43584,"r":"WEV007002","p":"Drouwenermond","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Before a child drowns in the canal, a dog sits howling at that spot and will not be chased away; afterwards the dog stays away.","i":"F.W.","o":"In het knoal hier veur ons huus is n moal n kind verdronkn. n Tied van te veurn zat doar n week laank n hond te hoeln. t Was n zwaarde poedel. Ik zee wel es teegn de jonges:“Joag dei hond toch vot.” k Heb dr ook es mit n stok noar smeetn, moar t hulp allemoal niks. De hond zat bie t woater en jankte moar. Tot t kind verdrunkn is, toen is t daier vot bleevn.\nNog veul eerder hef hier n man woond, die zegd har: “In dit diep tussen dizze beide bruggen zel nog n keer ienen verdrinkn.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43611,"r":"WEV007202","p":"Buinen","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Omens of a death are the howling of a dog, a magpie's nest near the house, or always having magpies around the house.","i":"F.W.","o":"Woar men vrogger nog wel aan geleufde en nu summige mensn nog, dat was aan honde-gehuul. Dan kwam er n dode.\nEn as-ie n eksternust bie huus hadden en die beestn schettern zo, of vlogen al moar um t huus hen, den kon ie ook reekn op n staarfgeval.","l":"Drents"},{"n":43616,"r":"WEV007305","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Experience that a dog's howling is the harbinger of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"n Hail bult mensn geleuven nait aan honden, dei zitn te hoeln, dat dr den n dode komt. Moar t is wel zo, dat heb k ja mitmoakt.\n n Poar joar leden zat achter bie ons op de loane n hond te jankn. \nk Bin dr n poar moal hen west um t ding vot te joagn, mor hai zat dr direkt weer. Ik zee nog zo:“Dat is ja roar, door ken nooit n liekwoagn langs komen, want dr is ja gain weg en door woont gain mens.”\n Moar dou loater oal S. overleden is, konnen ze de weg nait langs en mozzen ze over oons loane. De hond het zuk nait weer zain loatn. \n Ie kennen t wel nait leuven wiln, moar zukke dingen nuim ik gain biegeleuf.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44125,"r":"WEV007405","p":"Musselkanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Fear of howling dogs and magpies. The narrator experiences a death after a dog has sat howling with its head raised.","i":"F.W.","o":"As kind heb ik kouheer west op Westerwolle bie Roomse mensn.\nt Olske was n hail goud mens, moar o zo biegeleuvig.\nZai kwam uut Duutsland; as der den femilie over was, den gung t altied over heksn en spookn. Ik was den sums zo benauwd, da k nait meer noar boetn duz om te pizzen. Dou k oller wur, wur k ook wiezer.\nDei mensn zulf geleufden aal dei vertelsels wel.\n\nVeur jankende honden was ze vanzulf baange, en veur oksters.\nMoar nou mou k joe d’r bie verteln, dat ik dat toch ook n keer mitmoakt heb, dat dr n hond aal moar zat te hoeln mit kop omhoog. En eevn noa tied was dr n staarfgeval. Ik wait wel, ie moutn dr nait aan geleuven, moar t is wel vrumd.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44128,"r":"WEV007502","p":"Veelerveen","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"After two owls that have sat screeching in front of a house are shot dead, two deaths occur in that house.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nKat-oeln moutn spookdairen weezn.\nWas ains n keer aine, dei altied gounend veur t hoes zitn har te schrou-en.\nOp n oavend krigt e t geweer en schut dr aine dood.\nd Ander dag nog aine.\nn Zetje loater komen dr in dat hoes twei staarfgevaln.\n\nAal dizze vertelsels binnen woar.\nIk heb ze zulf beleefd.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44131,"r":"WEV007504","p":"Veelerveen","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A skipper hears a voice saying that the time has come, but the man is not there. A man who is supposed to be with him falls off the gangplank and drowns.","i":"F.W.","o":"Kwam n keer n schipper t knoal deur. Hai stak t kop eevn tou t loek oet en toun heurde e n stem: \"De tied is dr wel, mor de man is dr nait.\"\nSchipper blift nog eevn kiekn en den zugt e n keerl aan komen.\nDei mout bie hom weezn. De man wil over de loopplaanke noar t schip.\nEn den vaalt e dr of en verdrinkt.\n\nAal dizze vertelsels binnen woar.\nIk heb ze zulf beleefd.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44132,"r":"WEV007505","p":"Veelerveen","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man who does not believe in ghosts and witches would like to see something for once. One night he suddenly stands in the middle of a bright light; a few weeks later, at the same place and the same time, but then in the afternoon, he meets a funeral. He also sees a fire that is not there.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik har n kameroad, dei wel es wat zain wol.\nHai har ja wel al verhoaln heurd van andern over spookn en heksn en zoks wat. Zulf zag e nooit wat en doorom geleufde e dr nait aan.\nMor goud, dou kreeg e den wat te zain.\nHai kwam n keer van t wicht oet Bennewol; t was s nachts om haalf twei-e.\nEn toun inains ston e in n grel licht; hai zat dr midden in.\nWat gebeurde dr nou n poar weekn loater ook om haalf twei-e en den s middoags? Toun kwam e op datzulfde stee n begravvenis teegn.\nToun was e dr van geneezn, om es wat te zain.\n\nMoar hai was dr nog nait of.\nn Zet noa tied was e weer s oavends loat bie t pad en toun zag e opains n hoes in brand stoan. Hai luip ja wat e kon om dr bie te weezn.\nToun e dichter bie kwam, heurde -e de baisten ook al bulkn; dei luipen om t hoes tou, zo dochd-e.\nMor gek genog, de vlam wur aal klainer. En toun e bie hoes was, was de haile brand vot. Joarn loater, toun gung t spul wel de fik in.\n\nAal dizze vertelsels binnen woar.\nIk heb ze zulf beleefd.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44134,"r":"WEV007506","p":"Veelerveen","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A prediction that someone will drown in a canal within a day comes true.","i":"F.W.","o":"Toun ze mit t knoal aan t groaven wazzen, moz dr in t leste nog n dam deurstookn wordn.\nWazzen verschaiden manlu bie aan t waark.\nToun kwam dr aine langs, bleef n rukje stoan en zee: \n\"Joa, 't is n mooi knoal worn; t is allaind zo jammer, dat dr binnen vaarntwintig uur ain in verdrinkn mout.\"\n\"Och, doe hest altied wat\", zeden de keerls, en zai smeetn hom mit n schop vol zaand noar de kop.\nMoar kiek, d ander dag, t luip teegn twaalf uur en de mensn woln gau eetn, zee dr n seldoat teegn zien mouder:\n\"Ik goa eerst nog eevn zwemmen heur, veur t eetn.\"\n\"Och, jong, blief hier toch\", zee ze, t is muide nait meer weerd.\"\nHai gung toch hen, mor is best verdronkn.\n\nAal dizze vertelsels binnen woar.\nIk heb ze zulf beleefd.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":210711,"r":"ENGELS002808","p":"Sevenum","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A shooting star is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death in the neighbourhood.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Voortekenen:\nAls ik vroeger als kind met vader ’s avonds ging wandelen, en de hemel was klaar besterd, vertelde hij graag over de sterren. Ieder mens had zijn ster. Ik vond het erg aardig, dat ook ik een ster aan de hemel had staan. Op een avond zag ik voor de eerste keer een ster verschieten, en neervallen. Vader verklaarde, dat, als er een ster viel, er weer een mens uit de buurt zou sterven. \n\nGeen omzetting in dialect van het verhaal door Engels."},{"n":210097,"r":"HOL002310","p":"Kapel-Avezaath","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Omens of misfortune and death; do not walk under a ladder.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Als uilen roepen om een huis, of eksters \"schrèke\", of honden huilen is dit een voorteken van een naderend onheil; meestal is dit een sterfgeval (De dochter van Koehein heeft nog angst voor het \"schrèke\" van eksters). Als men 's avonds zwarte katten zag, was dit ook niet best. Ook die kondigden onheil aan. Ook moest men niet onder \"een leer\" doorlopen, wilde men zich voor ongeluk behoeden."},{"n":210122,"r":"HOL002415","p":"Opheusden","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Bewitchment is revealed by planks in the bed and a wreath in the pillow.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Wilde men weten of iemand betoverd was, dan moest men in zijn bed kijken. Vond men daar planken in (dit mij zo gezegd) dan was het duidelijk. Dit waren de planken voor zijn doodkist. Kransen in het hoofdkussen was maar heel gewoon. Deze kransen waren niet louter van veren, maar allerlei mooi \"geraai\" was er in verwerkt (waren een soort grafkransen van nagemaakte bloemen, heb ik er van begrepen). Deze kransen hoefden niet verbrand te worden."},{"n":210172,"r":"HOL002613","p":"Tiel","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Seeing a funeral procession while the body is still in the house; foreseeing death; second sight of death.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mevr. Boudewijn heeft eens, toen zij op een begrafenis was, de hele stoet voorbij zien trekken op een muur. Het lijk was toen nog in huis. \nOok heeft zij de begrafenis van haar moeder gezien, vóór dat deze plaats had. Eveneens is het haar overkomen, dat zij mensen, die ze verpleegd had, op het uur van hun dood duidelijk zag in hun ziekenkamer."},{"n":210210,"r":"HOL002719","p":"Ochten","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Omens of death and other misfortune.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Kwade voortekens waren het roepen van eksters en uilen dicht bij een huis. Ook het janken van honden. Het horen van gerommel in de planken, waaruit de timmerman de doodkisten maakte, was een slecht voorteken. Op zo iets volgde een sterfgeval"},{"n":210236,"r":"HOL002809","p":"Varik","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A body that lies unburied over a Sunday is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the next death.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Stond er een lijk op een zondag boven aarde, dan volgde er binnen zes weken weer een sterfgeval. Onlangs had men dit nog opgemerkt."},{"n":210270,"r":"HOL003008","p":"Varik","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A body lying unburied over a Sunday is an omen of a death.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Als een dode een zondag overstond, dan volgde er spoedig weer een sterfgeval."},{"n":210290,"r":"HOL003111","p":"Dodewaard","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The ringing of the bell on Sunday tells whether there will soon be a death.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"In Herveld meende men, dat men aan het luiden van de klok 's zondags voor de kerkdienst kon horen, of er in die week een sterfgeval zou plaats hebben."},{"n":210291,"r":"HOL003112","p":"Dodewaard","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a corpse lies unburied over a Sunday, another death soon follows.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Het geloof, dat als er een lijk op een zondag \"boven aarde\" staat, er spoedig weer een sterfgeval zal volgen, is vrij algemeen."},{"n":210293,"r":"HOL003114","p":"Dodewaard","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Someone born with a caul draws a lucky lot exempting him from conscription by taking the caul along; dreaming of fish by someone born with a caul is an omen of a death.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Met de helm geboren Hannes van de Kwikstart (= naam boerderij onder Welie) was \"met de helm geboren\". Deze \"helm\" was bewaard. Toen Hannes ging loten, stopte hij dit vliesje in de achterzak van zijn jas en zie: Hannes lootte vrij.\nVan Kraaikamp wist nog te vertellen, dat, als iemand, die met de helm geboren was, droomde van vissen, er dan één van de naaste familieleden binnenkort stierf."},{"n":210315,"r":"HOL003208","p":"Dodewaard","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Omens of death; the meaning of rattling roof tiles has remained unknown.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Het roepen van uilen, het huilen van honden, het schreeuwen van eksters (schrèke v. eksters) waren aanwijzingen, dat er in het huis, waarbij dit gebeurde, spoedig een sterfgeval zou plaats hebben. \n[Na 23] (Toevoegen bij 8).] Eens heeft men de pannen op het dak duidelijk horen rammelen. Wat de betekenis daarvan was, heeft men nooit kunnen nagaan."},{"n":208742,"r":"LINSSEN006916","p":"Ell","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Advice not to give a child the name of a child who has died.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Voorteken : Wanneer een kind in een familie gestorven was, ried men af om een volgend kind dat geboren werd, dezelfde naam te geven. \nIn de familie van verteller was het volgende gebeurd. In 1813 waren de Fransen hier nog de baas. Een oom van zijn vader had een zoontje verloren, genaamd Godefridus = Geurt. Een marketentster uit het franse leger ried hem af het in het jaar 1813 geboren zoontje de naam te geven van zijn broertje dat overleden was. Hij deed het toch. De jongen bleef in leven en werd later peter van tenminste drie kinderen die alle drie Geurt werden genoemd, doch ook alle drie jong gestorven zijn."},{"n":208799,"r":"LINSSEN007410","p":"Leveroy","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The chattering of a magpie is an omen of a death or an accident.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Het schateren van een ekster was een aanwijzing dat binnenkort iemand uit de familie zou sterven of dat hem een ongeluk zou overkomen."},{"n":208811,"r":"LINSSEN007510","p":"Leveroy","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A cherry tree forming new blossom in the month of May is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"H.L.G.","o":"Voortekens. Wanneer zich in de maand mei in de kersenboom een \"mei\" (heksenbezem) vertoonde zou er in de familie een sterfgeval plaats hebben."},{"n":44140,"r":"WEV007703","p":"Ommen","v":"Ov.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Dogs howling as voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Honden wisten eveneens, dat er een sterfgeval op komst was.\nZe gingen dan vreselijk janken. We noemden dat “doodjoelen”."},{"n":44142,"r":"WEV007705","p":"Ommen","v":"Ov.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A long line of churchgoers is seen as a funeral procession, and as an omen of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wanneer er veel mensen tegelijk naar de kerk gingen - in die tijd natuurlijk lopende - dan was dat ook een slecht voorteken.\nZo n lange rij mensen leek immers op een begrafenisstoet, zodat men weer met een sterfgeval rekening hield."},{"n":44260,"r":"WEV007903","p":"Nieuw-Weerdinge","v":"Dr.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Dogs howl and smell the odour of a corpse before a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Nait allain mensen wozzen van te veurn van nstaarfgeval, mor honden ook. Dei zatn al weken van te veurn te hoelen en roken de lieklucht al. Zo zeden de mensen teminste.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":130184,"r":"BIJLSMA000401","p":"Broek","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At night the hay wagons drive into the hay barn and the churning mill turns, but when people go to look, nothing is wrong. Across the canal where grandmother lives, calling is heard, and it is thought she will die. Nothing turns out to be wrong, and no one has called. A few days later the same sound is heard and grandmother dies.","i":"T.B.","o":"Fan oaren:\nTsjalling Terpstra, dy't hjir lang boer yn 'eSúd-Broek by de Jouwer west hat, forhelle my:\nDoe't er noch jong wie, wenne er mei syn âlden to Warten. Hja wennen op in buorkerij oan it wetter. Nachts hearden hja de haiweinen de skuorreed op en del riden, ek gong de tsjernmole. As hja der hinne gyngen to sjen, dan wie der neat en alles stil.\nOan 'e oare kant fan it wetter wenne beppe, dy't siik wie. Op in joun hearden hja roppen. Hja tochten, nou sil it mei beppe wol ôfrinne, en gyngen mei in boatsje nei de oare kant, mar der wie neat, en der hie ek nimmen roppen. In dei of hwat letter hearden se it selde lûd roppen. Doe wie it wol sa en roun it mei beppe nei it ein.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130200,"r":"BIJLSMA000601","p":"Haskerhorne","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"While lifting a dead cow a man counts to three, whereupon the maid says she heard the same words and sound the day before, though no one was there.","i":"T.B.","o":"Heit wie boerearbeider. Op in kear lei der in kou dea op ’e stâl. Men soe him der meiïnoar ôflûke. Heit telde dêrby: \"ien-twa-hup.\" De faem, dy’t ek mei loek, liet los en sei: \"Dy selde wurden en dat selde lûd ha ’k hjir juster ek heard, en doe wie der gjinien yn it bûthús\".","l":"Fries"},{"n":130240,"r":"BIJLSMA001004","p":"Scharsterbrug","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The father of a conscript soldier dreams that he walks through a large house in a strange city and meets a large head. That same night his son dies.","i":"T.B.","o":"Omke Anne Bethlehem to Terwispel hie destiids in soan, dy't to Amersfoort yn tsjinst lei. Omke dreamde op in kear dat er yn in frjemde stêd yn in great hûs kaem. It wiene dêr allegear keamers en gongen. Hy gie by de treppen op en seach opiens in dikke holle foar him. Deselde nachts wie syn soan to Amersfoort stoarn.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130282,"r":"BIJLSMA001605","p":"Sintjohannesga","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A few days after a dog sits howling beside its master, the man dies.","i":"T.B.","o":"Van der Wal syn oer-pake wie even nei de wetterfloed fan 1825 yn 'e feanderij yn it Skar ûnder Sint Jehannesgea. Dat wie yn de tiid dat der in greate stjerte wie, dat kaem mûlk fan it séwetter. Doe't er dêr yn it Skar wie mei syn houn, roun dy hieltyd foar him út en gong dan wer jammerdearlik foar him sitten to janken. Hy tocht, hwat skeelt dy houn, mar it bist wist fan gjin ophâlden en gûlde mar troch.\nTrije dagen letter wie de âld man dea.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130325,"r":"BIJLSMA002304","p":"Poppenwier","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman with second sight sees a black figure disappear at a house. A few days later someone dies there.","i":"T.B.","o":"In frommiske fan Tersoal wenne to Aldeboarn. Hja hie it twadde gesicht, seach mear as sljocht hinne en wer. Sa seach hja op in kear in swarte gedaente op har takommen oer it lân. Hja moast út 'e wei en it ding gie roerlings by har lâns. Sy stoarre it skynsel nei en seach it by in hûs weiwurden. Inkele dagen letter kaem der ien yn dat hûs to forstjerren.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130327,"r":"BIJLSMA002306","p":"Poppenwier","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Boisterous youngsters are seen as an omen of an event. The next day a girl dies. Noisiness is seen as a harbinger of misfortune or strong wind.","i":"T.B.","o":"Op in joun yn bisettingstiid gyng it jongfolk to Tersoal frijhwat oan. It wie gjin wonder, hja hiene oars ek net folle fordivedaesje. Men sei: hjir komt dalje op. De oare deis stoar der in famke to Tersoal.\n(Gauris brocht men eren lûdroftigens en in ûnk of sokssahwat mei elkoar yn forbân. Sa sei myn beppe wol: dy't foar achten sjongt, sil nei achten gûle. As de bern tige wyld en oerdwealsk en mei lûd geraes omfleane seit men nochwol: hear dy bern ris, wy krije hurde wyn. B.)","l":"Fries"},{"n":11492,"r":"CJ000201","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In Drachten there was a loose wooden bridge over the canal. The prediction that someone would drown comes true, because an uncle of the narrator drowns at that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Drachten oer de feart lei in barte, dy waerd neamd 'de hobbelplanke'. Ien hat sjoen, dat dêr ris ien fordrinke soe. It barde jierren letter. Doe is myn omke dêr yn 't wetter rekke en forsûpt. Krektlyk as dy persoan it sjoen hie, sa gebeurde it.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11500,"r":"CJ000209","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman sees that a man will drown in a canal.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e feart, tichte by de Nyegeaster tsjerke hat ús mem ris sjoen dat dêr in manspersoan fordrinke moast. Hy hie in horloazje mei keatling op 't boarst.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11501,"r":"CJ000210","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Women see in the cowshed that a cow's place is empty, with only the chain and halter lying there. A little later the cow is standing there again. A year later the cow dies. The chain and halter lie in its place just as was seen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik en myn dochter dy't op 'e Tike wennet stienen ris by ús yn 't bûthús. Doe seagen wy ynienen allebeide ien fan 'e stâllen leech, dêr't oars in grouwe koe stie. It ketting en 't lear leinen der allinne mar. \nWy wisten net hwat wy seagen. Mar fuort dêrnei stie de koe der wer en wie alles wer as tofoaren. Mar in jier letter kaem dy koe to forstjerren. Der wie him in stikje kramtrie dwars troch 't hart gong. De stâl kaem leech to stean. Mar krektlyk leinen dêr doe it ketting en it lear.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11519,"r":"CJ000303","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A corpse that lies in the house over a Sunday means that someone else will soon die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der ien stoarn is en it lyk stiet in snein oer, dan is der gau wer in deade.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11521,"r":"CJ000305","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The first person one meets on the way to the churchyard shows who will be the next in the family to die. If one meets a man, a man will die first; if a woman, a woman; if a child, a child.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hwat men tidens de gong nei 't tsjerkhôf by in bigraffenis it earste tsjinkomt, dat sil it earst yn jins famylje stjerre. Komt men in man tsjin, dan stjert der yn jins famylje in man, is it in frou, dan in frou, is it in bern, dan in bern.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11522,"r":"CJ000306","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One must not long for a beautiful deceased person, for then someone else in the family will die. That is why the dead look serene and beautiful.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de deade moai is, dat mat men noait bigeare, hwant dan komt der wer ien to forstjerren yn 'e famylje. Dêrom is de deade bliid en moai.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11523,"r":"CJ000307","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A magpie by the house means a letter announcing a death will arrive.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in ekster by hûs komt (swart mei wyt) komt der in roubrief. De ekster is de foarboade op it hiem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11535,"r":"CJ000319","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man hears wailing without seeing anything. The next summer he hears the same wailing. It comes from a little boy whose father has been struck by lightning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Achter Goaijengeahuzen wie ús heit yn 'e ûngetiid, mei noch inkelde oaren. Ynienen hearde hy in freeslik gejammer fan in bern. Mar der wie neat to sjen. Krekt in jier letter yn 'e simmer waerd it slim swier waer. Doe hearde heit wer itselde gejammer. It kaem út in tinte wei, dêr tichteby. Dêr jammere in jonkje yn. Syn heit wie troch de wearljocht rekke en deaslein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11539,"r":"CJ000323","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A warning to be careful at a bridge because someone will drown there, which indeed happens.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foar in tachtich jier stie der in âld man to Drachten by de draei. It wie in sekere Doeke. Hy sei tsjin 'e minsken: \"Jimme moatte jim foar dit plak hoedzje, hwant hjir komt ien to fordrinken.\" In pear jier letter gebeurde it.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11548,"r":"CJ000409","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Some people who die unexpectedly already carry little living creatures on them while they are alive.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon dy't ûnforwacht stjerre sille ha fan tofoaren, as se noch libje, al libbenen dierkes by har. It binne hiele ljochte sulverbeestjes, hwat greater as in groatkerl. It binne de leedbringers. Ik ha 't sels wol sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21864,"r":"CJ029004","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a bird comes onto the path beside the house, a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in fûgel it paedtsje fan in hûs lâns komt, dan bitsjut dat, dat der in deaden komt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21880,"r":"CJ029020","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man hears a dog howling eerily. A few days later, at the same spot where the howling was heard, a man dies after falling off his bicycle. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Sjoerd Bonnes-plaets yn Sumar hat Fokke van der Kuip feint west. Op in kear hearde er dêr in swart bont hountsje gûlen. Dat hearde aeklik. op itselde plak dêr't it hountsje stie to gûlen, foel in pear dagen letter in man fan 'e fyts. Hy wie fuort dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":210748,"r":"ENGELS003102","p":"Helden","v":"L.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Seeing open blossom on an apple tree as an omen of a marriage or a death.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Voortekenen:\nOp de Zandberg, een gehucht van Helden, was een zoon, die ongeveer 15 jaar oud was, al sinds jaren bedlegerig; vermoedelijk door de tering. Hij ging langzaam achteruit, en herstel was uitgesloten. Op een dag in de zomer zag zijn moeder aan een appelboom tussen de appels een open bloesem. Ze wees daar haar zoon op, en zei: “’n Bloom boeten tied, guft ’n broed of e liek!” “’n Broed kan ’t neet zin; daoröm zal ’t wel e liek zin!”\nDe zoon was door deze woorden van zijn lieve (?) moeder zo verontrust, dat hij uit zijn bed opstond, en in de boom de bloem af ging plukken. Zijn sterven, - geruime tijd later -, zal daar wel weinig mee te maken hebben gehad. \n\nVerslag 55, Omzetting uit de Ned. taal in dialect van Helden, van de verhalen, ... onder no. L291-31. Helden, 10-12-1969\nOp te Zangkberg wonde in ’t begin van deez ieuw ’n booren-hoeshaoën, det te naam hei van “vérkes-aechtig”, geerig, en groof onbesjaafd.\nDao laag enne jong al jaoren op bèd. Van jongsaaf aan hei d’r al gènne grongk ingezète. Wie e zoeëgét vieftieën jaor waas ès e gesjtorve. Hè zal wél de tering hebbe gehad, want hè sugkelde langszaam nao zien indj. Op ennendaag waas zie mooder in d’n hoof, en hè laag an d’n ope raam. De mooder zaag tössen de appelen an d’n boum ’n ope bloom sjtaon.\nZe wees tie eure zoon aan, en zaoch: “’n Bloom boeten tied, guft ’n broed of e liek! ’n Broed kan ’t neet zin, hei; daorö"},{"n":210800,"r":"ENGELS003707","p":"Blerick","v":"L.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Seeing a funeral procession in advance is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Spookbegrafenis:\nEr werd verteld van iemand, die in zijn droom een lijkstoet voorbij zag trekken, en aan de volgorde van de familie kon uitmaken, wie er wel gestorven was, en in de kist lag. Hij vertelde die droom aan zijn familie. Een week of wat daarna bleek zijn voorgezicht uit te komen door het sterven van de bewuste.\n\nGeen omzetting in dialect van het verhaal door Engels."},{"n":49691,"r":"GENDT057","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If someone knocks on your door a few times in the evening or at night and there is nobody at the door, it is an omen that someone will have an accident or die.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Soms kwam soaves of snachs iemes op de deur kloppe. As ge dan gieng kieke, was er niks. Da gebeurde zo inkele kere achter mekoare. Lotter hörde ge dan, dat er ’n ongeluk was gebeurd, of dat iemes dood was.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":49750,"r":"GENDT112","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man wakes with a start several times in the night from a dream about a big fish. His mother-in-law fears that someone will now die, because this is an omen. Her son dies shortly afterwards.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"’t Geet over ’n droom, die ’n vörbeduisel was. Ik was op ’n zaterdagoavend op de gewone tied, ongevèr elf uur, nor bed gegoan. Ik wier um zowat één uur wakker. Vör die tied had ik gedromd van een grote vis, die nor mien toe kwam zwemme. Ik het toe de lamp ongestoke en ’n poos gewach en zie toe wer ien sloap gevalle. Ik dromde wer over de vis. Hé’j kwam wer op mien on. Ik het toe wer de lamp ongestoke. Ik was nat bezweit. En bang en koud. Ik zie toe tot ongevèr vijf uur wakker gebleve. Ik doch bé’j mien eige: “Wa mot er toch gebeure?” Nie lang dornoa ziet ik wer ien sloap gevalle en heb rustig gesloape tot zondagmèr acht uur. \n Zondagsoaves gienge we nor mien schonmoeder. Ik vertelde toe alles van die droom. D’r wier um gelache en ik deej ok mee. Mar mien schonmoeder zèj: “Dor moj nie um lache. D’r kan iets gebeure. Dor kan ’n dooie op volge”. En da is ok uutgekomme. Hor zoon wier gaauw dornoa ziek. Vrijdagsmèrs wier ie bewusteloos en hé’j is soaves gesturve. Ze zegge wel es: “As ge droom van ’n grote vis, kumt er ’n grote dooie en as ge droom van ’n kleine vis ’n kleine”. Ik het ok wel es gehörd, dat as ge over eiere dromt, dat er dan ok gaauw ’n dooie kum.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":49752,"r":"GENDT114","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Sometimes when the sexton comes to the church in the morning the bar is already off the door, without anyone having been there (the door is still locked). This is said to be an omen of death.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Bé’j de ouwe kerk die ien den oorlog verwoes is zat op de grote vördeur on den binnenkant ’n boom um de deur af te slute. Soms was die boom er af, as Jan Joosten, den ouwe kuster, smèrs ien de kerk kwam. En d’r was niemes ien de kerk gewes, want die was nog op slot. Jan Joosten zèj dan tege mien voader: “Willem, dor kum wer gaauw ’n dooie, want ten boom was vanmèr wer van den hoak af”. Of ’t uutgekomme is, weet ik nie.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":50159,"r":"GENDT133","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Owls screeching and dogs howling are an omen of a death.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"As de ule krijse of de honde janke, dan kumt er gaauw ’n dooie ien de buurt. Da heb ik heel duk heure vertelle.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":50177,"r":"GENDT140","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A child in bed hears the parents praying together once more; the other children hear nothing and the mother denies it in the morning. A few days later the father dies and the neighbours come to pray for the deceased.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"’t Was bé’j ons thuus vroeger de gewoonte um soaves same de rozekrans en ’t oavendgebed te bidde. Voader bidde dan altied veur. En wé’j mozze dan noabidde [antwoorden]. Mar dor mekierde wels wat on. Op ’n oavend hadde we wer same gebid. We zèje mekoar wel te ruste en gienge nor bed. Voader en moeder ok. Toe we ’n hörtje op bed ware, zèj ik tège mien zusters die ien dezelfde sloapkamer sliepe: “Hör es, voader en moeder zien ien d’r sloapkamer nog ens ’t rozenuutje on ’t bidde”. Mien zusters zèje: “Och dern, da’s verbeelding, we heure niks”. Mar ik hördenet duidelijk. Ik zèj: “Hör dan mar, voader het krek veurgebid en nou antwoordt moeder”. Mar mien zusters zèje: “Och dern, ge ziet nie wies, we heure niks”. Mar ik bleef ’t duidelijk heure tot ’t bidde ophiel. ’s Mèrs zèj ik tège voader en moeder: “Wurrum het gellie gisterenoavend nog ’n keer de rozekrans gebid?” Moeder zèj: “Da hè we nie gedoan. Ge het gedromd dern”. \nInkele dage lotter stierf voader en toe kwame de minse uut de burt, zo es da toe de gewoonte was, bé’j ons on huus de rozekrans bidde vör den afgestörvene. En nou geleuf ik nog altied, da’k toe geliek gehad heb. ’t Was wel ’n vörbedujsel gewes.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":50167,"r":"GENDT144","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Calling owls, howling dogs and chattering magpies are an omen of a death in the neighbourhood.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Es de ule roepe, de honde janke en de eksters schettere, kumt er gaauw ’n dooie ien de burt. Teminste da wier vroeger wel gezeid.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":210350,"r":"HOL003318","p":"Tiel","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Seeing something unusual at the place where someone later dies.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Vermijns moeder is in de winter van 1944-'45 op Mariënwaard overleden. (Mariënwaard is een buiten bij Beesd. Daarheen waren de zieken uit de Tielse ziekenhuizen gebracht, toen de stad uit Maas en Waal geregeld door de Geallieerde legers werd gebombardeerd)\nOp 18, 19 jarige leeftijd was een nichtje langs Mariënwaard gekomen. Zij meende toen iets bijzonders te zien, iets, dat van belang zou zijn in haar leven. En dat is uitgekomen."},{"n":208963,"r":"LINSSEN009208","p":"Sint Joost","v":"L.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The number of magpies determines whether they are a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of good or bad luck.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Voortekens . Wanneer drie eksters zich toonden in de nabijheid van een huis, stond er groot geluk te verwachten. Een ekster daarentegen was een voorbode van ongeluk."},{"n":208981,"r":"LINSSEN009411","p":"Herkenbosch","v":"L.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Blossoming at an unusual time is an omen of a marriage or a death.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Voortekens: Wanneer een boom of bloem in de tuin bloeide op een ongewone tijd, was dat een voorteken dat binnenkort in het bijgehorende huis een \"broed\" of \"liek\" = (bruid of lijk) zou komen."},{"n":209003,"r":"LINSSEN009706","p":"Koningsbosch","v":"L.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A tree by a house blossoming at an unusual time is an omen of a death in that house.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Voortekens: Wanneer een boom bij een huis op een erf bloeide op een ongewone tijd, bijv. in het najaar, was dat een voorteken dat daar binnenkort iemand van de huisgenoten zou sterven."},{"n":44271,"r":"WEV008204","p":"Noord-Sleen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A turtle dove in the house as protection against whooping cough and dauwworm (a skin rash).","i":"F.W.","o":"Een torteldoeve in hoes was veurbehoedsmiddel tegen kinkhoest en dauwworm.\nZo wier verteld deur olde mensen.","l":"Drents"},{"n":130017,"r":"WEV008205","p":"Noord-Sleen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The screeching of a tawny owl is seen as a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of death.","i":"F.W.","o":"As wie 's oavends bie de weg lupen en wie heurden 'n kat-oele schrouwen, dan zeden wie maar niks, moar dochten: \"Er kump 'n dode.\"","l":"Drents"},{"n":44275,"r":"WEV008302","p":"Nieuw-Weerdinge","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog that howls for several evenings is an omen of a death. After a child has drowned, the dog stops howling.","i":"F.W.","o":"’k Heb het mitmoakt, dat er ’n hond op ’n schip zat te janken, oavend op oavend.\nWie zeden al: “Dat wordt ’n dode.”\nEn net zo, as ’t was.\n’n Zet loater is er een kind verdronkn; en de hond jankte nait meer.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44278,"r":"WEV008401","p":"Nieuw-Weerdinge","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Seeing a house burning when nothing is wrong with it is an omen of a death in that house.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik zel joe aigen belevenissen vertellen; alles is woar.\n\nIk zag ais ‘n brandend huus; ik d’r op of, moar toun ‘k d’r bie kwam, was er niks te doun.\nMien voader zee teegn mie: “Pas moar op, komp ain dode in dat huus.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44280,"r":"WEV008403","p":"Nieuw-Weerdinge","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A carpenter warns his mother not to walk between two stacks of wood, because he has encountered something there. When he walks there himself, he is killed by sliding wood.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik zel joe aigen belevenissen vertellen; alles is woar.\n\nIn de Tweide Exloërmond is dit werkliek gebeurd.\nBie ‘n timmerman stunden twei hoge stoapels holt. Nou zee de zeun altied tegen zien moeke: “Loop doar nait tussen deur.”\n“Woarom nait?” zee ze.\n“Och”, zee d jong, “ik bin door wat tegenkomen.”\nEn wat wil ’t geval?\nOp ’n dag lop jong d‘r zulf tussendeur; den begunnen de stoapels holt te glieden, en de jong vaalt d‘r onder dood.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44281,"r":"WEV008404","p":"Nieuw-Weerdinge","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When there is knocking in the wood for a coffin, nothing can be seen. Later a child drowns and the knocking stops.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik zel joe aigen belevenissen vertellen; alles is woar.\n\nVrouger hadden paddie lu ’t kistholt op beune liggen.\nNou gebeurde ’t es, dat mensn geklop bie dat holt heurden.\nZai gungen noar boven om te kieken, moar zaggen niks.\nDe lu waarkten ja allemoal in ’t veen. Moz ook koffie hen brocht worden.\nDat dee ’n wichie van negen joar; uut dat huus van zopas.\nOp ‘n mörn kwam ze nait; zai vonden heur in ’n sloot; verdronkn.\nEn toun was ’t klopn doan.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44291,"r":"WEV008605","p":"Emmen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The screeching of a magpie predicts a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ekster-geschreeuw was gevaarlijk.\nDat voorspelde een sterfgeval."},{"n":45299,"r":"WEV008704","p":"Wessinghuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A sick woman asks the minister to chase away the dog howling in front of the house, because it means misfortune.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik wait nog wol, dat doomnie vrouger bie n oal mens kwam, dai zaik was. Zat n hond te janken veur t hoes. Zai zee: \"Doomnie, joag dai hond toch vot; dat betaikent gain gouds\". \nDoomnie wol heur van dai gedachten ofhelpen, man hai har lou (geen) kans.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45303,"r":"WEV008708","p":"Wessinghuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man who sees funeral processions at night and then has to get up says that someone will drown. These people are born with a caul.","i":"F.W.","o":"In Onstwedde was n boer en dai zien grootknecht zag liekstoaties; altied s nachts. Dan möz e tou t berre oet en dat was wol es lastig. Boer zee in t leste: \"Goa dr man nich weer oet of vertel mie van te veurn, woor d ast hen gest.\nOp n nacht lag d jong weer te hunsken (janken) op berre, hai kön nich langer in hoes weezn.\nBoer zee: \"Moust n enne vot?\"\n\"Nee, man n endken\", zee d jong en dou is e vot goan. Eevn loater was e dr weer.\n\"Verdrinkt gauw aine\", zee e en t is gebeurd ook.\nZukke lu, dai dat könt, binnen mit de helm geboorn.\nAs de helm man doadelk begroaven wordt, zollen ze gain last hebben, heb k wol al zeggen heurd.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44537,"r":"WEV008901","p":"Jipsingboermussel","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Men see girls in white clothing rowing, who suddenly vanish. Later a child drowns at the place where the girls were seen.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik zel joe es wat vertellen over dingen, dei k zulf beleefd heb en dei dus ook woar binnen.\nWie woonden indetied op Stadsknoal; op n oavend zatn ik en mien vrund veur t huus op baanke.\nInains zee mien kameroad: \"Kiek doar ais, wat nuvere wichter en wat kennen ze voarn.\"\nIk keek en wat zaggen wie toun?\nGong n bootje, n soort kano deur t daip; zatn n stok of wat hail mooie wichter in; zai hadden allemoal widde klaier aan. En roeien dat ze konnen, t gong dr haard over.\nWie luipen netuurlijk gauw noar de wale om ze noa te kiekn. \nEn wat zaggen wie? Niks, hailemoal niks in t haile daip nait.\n\"Dat is ja roar\", zeden wie, \"wie hebben ze toch dudelk zain, dei mooie vroulu, gans en al in t wit.\"\nMoar nou komt t. n Weke loater verdrinkt r kind op datzulfde stee, woar wie t bootje zain harren. Ik leuf nog altied, dat dizze dingen wat mit mekoar te moaken had hebben.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44540,"r":"WEV008904","p":"Jipsingboermussel","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The call of an owl, a magpie on the windowsill and the howling of a dog predict a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Tou k jong was leufde ik in veul dingen, woor k nou niks meer om geef. Ie moutn reekn, de oal lu pruiten dr over en de buurn net zo goud en den neem je dat over.\nAs wie n katoele heurn, wozzen wie, dat er n dode kwam.\nn Eekster op vensterbaanke bedudde t zulfde.\nEn n hoelnde hond ook, moar den mozzen ie kiekn, woor de hond hen keek; in dat huus zol t gebeurn.\nDit biegeleuf gait de wereld wat uut, moar ik wol ze nait geern de kost geevn, dei dr toch nait hailemoal rustig op binnen.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44552,"r":"WEV009101","p":"Vledderveen","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In the evening a man hears cries for help from a thicket, but there is nothing to be seen. When the thicket is being cut down, a man gets caught on a branch, cries for help, falls to the ground and dies.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien voader hef mie wol wat verteld over veurloop.\nHai woonde dou in Onstwedde.\nOp n oavend steet e op boetn wat noar de steerns te kiekn en zo.\nNon stun n endkng van heur of n boskng. Oet dat bos heurt hai dan \"help\" roupn. Hai hef zuk dr nich an steurd en dochde, dat t wol verbeeln weden zol.\nWat e door heurd har, vertelde n zet loater aan zien neef. Dai zee ook: \"Komp mie roar veur, wel zol non in de winter s oavends in t bos loopn; as t non zömmer was, dan kön je nog vogels strikn wiln.\"\nMan wat wil t geval? As zai bie mekoar stoat te prootn, heurt ze non beide \"help\" roupn. In t zulfde bossie.\nZai dr hen um te kiekn wat of door loos is. Niks te zain.\nt Volgnde veurjoarwordt er boomm kapt in t bos. Jan Petersn - wur e nuimd- hai hedde anders en kwam oet de Muzzel - was dr ook bie en kwam aan n touge te hangn. \"Help\", ruip e, man t was al te loat; hai völ op de grond tou t boom oet. Zai hebt hum nog leevnd in hoes kreegn, man hai is dr wol aan hen gaon.\nKiek, dit is dudelk n geval van veurloop; mien oal heer loog zukke dingn nich.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44556,"r":"WEV009201","p":"Onstwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A magpie as an omen of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nIe heurt er heden ten doage ja hoast ja niks meer van; Bint ook dingen, woor n mensk nich aan leuven mout, man ik zeg joe, lacht nich overal um. Vogelgeschrei en honde-gehoel, op acht geevn mou-je dr ja nich, man t bestèèt wol.\nKomp ook nôn nog wel veur.\nVeur n poar joar zat hier in Wesnghoezn altied n eekster; hai vloog van de boerderij van H. noar de boerderij van M.; aingoal hen en weer. Zai schootn dr voak op, man ganaine kön hom roakn.\nHai kwam ook wol ais op de vensterbaanke en pikte teegn t glas van koustaln. En och, H. en de vrouw wazzen es op n oavend oet west en loat in hoes koomn. d Oal boas wur dou nich al te goud en is op berre kroopn. Dokter is dr nog bie west, man t as al te loat. Noa tied hebben ze van d eekster gain last weer had.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44557,"r":"WEV009202","p":"Onstwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a boy falls ill, dogs appear that try to get into the house. After the sick boy has died, the dogs stay away. The narrator thinks he should not believe in it, but is glad he no longer hears dogs howling.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nt Is al wat langer leden, man ik wait t nog hail best; was n jonge vent zaik van achttien joar. Dou e te lign kwam, kreegn ze liek oet deur honden um t hoes tou. Zai wazn nich te muitn (tegenhouden). As de mensn de deure oopn deden, schootn de honden heur tuschkn de bainen deur en zai gruiven goaten veur deure in de grond. t Wazzen deurgoans van dai honden mit vaier oogn. Ie waitn wol, oogn mit gele vlekn dr boovn. (Dit is de z.g. dobermann en voor ditzelfde ras wordt op Drente gewaarschuwd, zoals in een van de eerste verslagen is vermeld: F.W.)\nDe jongeman is overleden en de honden binnen dou wegbleevn.\nDoorum zeg ik: aan leuven mou-je dr ainlieks nich, man ik heb te veul zain en ik bin bliede, da k dat honne-gehoel nich meer verneem en k heb dr ook gain spier belang bie.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44562,"r":"WEV009301","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Hearing a turtle dove while there is no turtle dove in the house. The neighbours' turtle dove never calls, but does so when it is lodged with others while the neighbour's coffin is above ground. After returning to its owner, the turtle dove never coos again.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nWat woar is dat is woar. Binnen wel mensn, dei dr nait aan leuvn, moar wat ik toch beleefd heb en zain mit mien aigen oogn, proat mie gainmens uut de kop.\nWie woonden indertied in de Beetse. 's Mörns brochde mien vrouw de sikke noar boetn en den zee ze wel ais: \"Ik heur voak n törteldoeve roupm; t is net of e bie ons in hoes is.\"\nNou kon dat nait, want wie harn gain doeve. Ons buurman wel, dat was n oom van mie. Moar dei doeve ruip nooit.\nJoarn loater is oomke störvn. Dou mozzen wie dei doeve zo laank in huus hebben as kiste boovn oarde ston.\nEn wat roar, bie ons ruip dat daier dou wel.\n\"Kiek\", zee mien vrouw, \"nou rop dr toch n doeve in ons huus.\"\nNoa de begravvenis moz doeve ja weer vot noar mien taande.\nEn doar het e nait weer roupm; t was al n old daier.\nHou ken dat nou, he?","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44563,"r":"WEV009302","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"As long as someone is ill, a dog howls near the house, but it is no longer seen after the sick person dies.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nZo'n zestig joar leden luip dr altied n oal zwaarver deur de Beetse. n Huus har hai nait; hai sluip den hier, den door bie de boern in t heu. Ook voak bie mien schoonoln.\nOp n keer kwam e dr weer aan, hai zag dr niks te best uut.\nHai kreeg zien old stee op de hilde; slim waarm was t dr nait, moar verwend was e ja toch nait.\nd Oal man is nait weer beterd; bie schoonoln is e overleden.\nMoar nou komp, wat ik joe verteln wil.\nDou d oal man door zaik lag, kwam elk oavend taande Jannoa- dei woonde eindje van ons of, heur hond en gung bie t schoonoln op dam zitn en dee niks den hoeln.\nIeder oavend kwam e weer, net zo laank as ol A. door zaik lag.\nDou de man störm was, hewwe de hond nait meer zain of heurd.\nMien vrouw wait t ook wel, dit binnen gain proatjes.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44564,"r":"WEV009303","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Belief that magpies and starlings predict misfortune.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nEn zo k en k joe meer gevaln opnuimen van gounend, dei op honnen schootn, omdat ze flauw wurn van dat gejank; moar t huilp nooit.\nEeksters en sproi-en (spreeuwen) binnen eevnmin te vertrouwn.\nWordt nou nait veul geleuf meer aan schonkn, moar mien olle lu en mien schoonoln en goa zo moar deur, dei twiefelden nait aan zukke dingen. Dat kwam nait omdat ze dat bie heur gat opdochden, nee, zai konden t bewiezn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44578,"r":"WEV009407","p":"Schoonoord","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman tells her daughter she has seen a light in a stack of peat. Later the body of the daughter's son is carried around a stack of peat.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurgezicht.\nEr was een maal een wief; ze zat veur et raam en zag toen wat.\nIn de varte stonden turfbultn.\nSie zag, dat er een schienvat-lichien um een van die bultn gunge, en zee dat ook teegn heur dochter.\nDat olde mense leeft niet meer, maar de dochter nog wel.\nWat gebeurden een poossien later?\nDie vrouw heur zeune wuur in het vene vermoord.\nEt was ja een roege tied; et mes zat lös in de buus en er wuur veul zeupn.\nToen dan de buurn de jonge zuikn muzzen, namen ze een schienvat met; ze liepn toen ook um de törfbult hen met et liek, zoals de vrouw dat ezien hadde.\n\nDit is echt gebeurd.","l":"Drents"},{"n":44583,"r":"WEV009502","p":"Stadskanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Hearing knocking at night and seeing a row of people in top hats in front of a house is voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a funeral. People have to wait, because the coffin must go through the window. For that a window frame must first be removed.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien moeke vertelde es n moal en zai leufde dat ook en as kind muik ik mie door benauwd veur:\n\"Ik kwam op n nacht bie t scheepswaarf langs en heurde toun bie dat huus van Sennemoa klopperij. En toun ik goud toukeek, zag k ook n hail riege volk mit hoge houden op veur t huus stoan.\nDat was ja roar, want t kon ja hoast nait midden in nacht.\nMoar kiek, n poar moand noa tied staarft oal S.\nDen stoan er dus wel bult mensn om t huus tou mit de begravvenis.\nEn wat wil t geval?\nKiste ken nait tou t deure uut; den moar deur t roam. \nDat kon ook nait, of eerst mozzen de keziens dr uut houwen worn.\"\nEn dat was nou t geklop west, dat oal mens heurd had.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45009,"r":"WEV009602","p":"Holthe","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A married couple hears knocking and calling but gets no answer, and there is nothing to be seen. Three weeks later the neighbour knocks on the window in the same way to tell them his father has died.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wat ik joe vertelle, is woar gebeurd.\nEr is meer dan veule mensen denken. Doar is n zekere almacht.\nWel door an geleuft, lacht niet om alles en wet, dat niet alles te verklaarn valt; maar hij nuumt ook alles geen olle wieve-prooties, wat zo vake gebeurt.\nLuster maar ies uut mien eigen ervaarn.\n\nVeurgezicht numen ze dat; ik weet wel meer. Ook waar gebeurd.\nOp een avond zaten mien vrouw en ikke in de kamer.\nDaar wuur iniens op et raam geklopt; wie heurden et beiden.\nWie rupen: \"Wie is daar?\"\nGien antwoord. Ik gunge naar buten om te kiekn, maar er was gien mense. Maar vergist hadden wie ons niet.\nDrie weekn later klopt de buurman aan et raam. t Was etzulfde geklop op etzulfde raam. Wie gungen weer kiekn en toen verteln de buurman: \"Mien vao is zo net sturven.\"\nt Was dus alweer een veur bode west dat geklop.","l":"Drents"},{"n":45013,"r":"WEV009605","p":"Holthe","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman sees a small black coffin standing on the threshing floor, while her husband has seen nothing. When their child dies, neighbours bring a small black coffin and put it down on the spot where the mother saw it standing.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wat ik joe vertelle, is woar gebeurd.\nEr is meer dan veule mensen denken. Doar is n zekere almacht.\nWel door an geleuft, lacht niet om alles en wet, dat niet alles te verklaarn valt; maar hij nuumt ook alles geen olle wieve-prooties, wat zo vake gebeurt.\nLuster maar ies uut mien eigen ervaarn.\n\nIk zal oe nog meer verteln. \nToen ik kind was, komt mien moeder op een avond in de kamer en zeg teegn mien va: \"Wat veur een zwart kissien stiet er toch op de diele; hest doe die daar henne zet?\"\nMaar mien va wist van gien kissien af. Had um ook niet ezien.\nIk had een zussien en die is een poossien later gestorvn.\nDe buurn brachtn toen een zwart kissien en zetten die op de plekke, waar mien moe et al zien hadde.\nAs ie toch zulf zukke dinger beleevn, moe-je niet zeggen, dat er gien veurgezicht is.","l":"Drents"},{"n":45024,"r":"WEV009706","p":"Sleen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Fear of screeching magpies and howling dogs; they are an omen of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik kan joe wel over iets verteln; maar dat was veur mien tied en ik zelf leuve er niet aan. Mien ollers en meer andere mensn namen wat ik je vertelle veur waar aan.\n\nVeur schrouwende eksters en hulende honden wazzen de mensn slim bange. Dat betiekende eendode; daarom joeg men de ekstersweg of schoot men er op. En weetn ie, waarumme de honden zo hulen?\nZe hoorden al van te veuren de doods-klokken luden. Dat konden ze niet in de oren hebben en daarumme janken ze.\nZo wier verteld in de ouwe tied, maar met de mensen is ook et biegeleuf de wereld uut gaan. \nOp een kleine uutzondering na hier en daar.\n\nN.B. \nDit is de eerste keer, dat mij verteld is, dat de honden huilen, omdat ze doodsklokken zoudenhoren. (F.W.)","l":"Drents"},{"n":45035,"r":"WEV009810","p":"Emmen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A warning to cover the rain barrel, or else someone will drown in it, is not heeded. A child drowns in the barrel.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik heb een vrouw gekend, die zei: \"Dek die regenton af, anders verdrinkt er iemand in.\"\nMen heeft zich niet aan de waarschuwing gestoord; maar er is inderdaad een kindje in die ton verdronken."},{"n":45037,"r":"WEV009812","p":"Emmen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Whoever crosses a bridge where black cats sometimes jump from railing to railing risks dying.","i":"F.W.","o":"In Surhuisterveen was vroeger een brug. Zo nu en dan sprongen er zwartekatten van leuning naar leuning. Dat was heel gevaarlijk.\nWie het trof, dat hij of zij juist op dat moment over de brug moest, liep de kans, dat ze het met de dood moesten bekopen.\nEr waren dan ook wel jongens, die de brug meden, als ze laat van hun meisje kwamen en liever een omweg maakten des nachts."},{"n":45048,"r":"WEV010003","p":"Harpel","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A howling dog is an omen of a death. An incident in which a dog digs holes through the clay wall of a house and sits howling in the kitchen for many evenings. It stays away once someone has had a fatal fall.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurzain.\nVandoage aan de dag heurt ie dr nich zo veul meer over, man dat veurzain bestèèt, door bin k van overtuugd. Ik kan joe dat bewiezen, want mien pabbe en ik zulf hebben verscheiden keern wat mitmoakt. Verder heb ik al n boel heurd van ander lu.\n\nHonden. Honnegehoel verneemt ie vandoage ook nich meer veul van.\nMan vrouger, wat kwam dat voak veur, dat dr n hond zat te jankn en dat er dan gauw n dode kwam. k Heb t zo voak beleefd.\nOp de Ballege zag k as kwoajong n hond aankomen op n hoes of.\nIk zee al, de hoeskes wazzen n hail bult van laim optrokn.\nDe hond was zo wild, hai gruif goatn under de laimen mure deur en kroop zo in de keukn.\nDoor gung e zitn te hoelen. Kwoad dee e nich, man mensn können hum nich vot kriegen.\nOavend op oavend kwam t daier dr aan. As e oetjankt was, gung e weer vot. Net zo laank, dou gebeurde dr wat. Op n dag kwakde ain van de jonges van t beune of en vuil dood op dele.\nDe hond is dr nooit weer west. En woor kwam t ding hail heer?\nDat hebt ze loater underzöcht. Hail van de Pekel, altied zo 'n 15 kilometer vot. Hou t kan, ik wait t nich, man woar is t.\nIk heb wal voaker honnen komen zain, ook wal noar de Harpel, man de leste tied is t ofloopm.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43135,"r":"WEV010108","p":"Wollinghuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Magpies on the windowsill foretell that a death will occur in that house, for the narrator has experienced it himself.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ook heb ik n moal n köppel eeksters op n vensterbaanke zain bie aine; ze pikten teegn t roam aan. Mensen zeden al: \"Door komp n dode, want eeksters zitn anders nich op vensterbaanke.\" En nôn meugn ie t leuven of nich, man t is wol oetkomen. Is oal vrouw sturvn in dat hoes. As ie zukke dingen zulf mitmoakn, kunt ie dat gain biegeleuf meer vinden.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43138,"r":"WEV010111","p":"Wollinghuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At night there is knocking on the window, but nothing can be seen. Later, at night, there is again tapping on the same window, by men bringing the news that their son is dead.","i":"F.W.","o":"k Wait nog meer geschichtn. Man k heb ze van andere mensn. Dai ze mie verteld hebben, twiefelden nich aan de woarheid; ik zulf kan dr slecht bie. De vertellers wazzen gain proatjemoakers en eevnmin benauwde schieters dai overal baange veur wazn. Luster man es.\n\nt Volgnde is ook woar gebeurd op de B. t Is gain mooie geschichte.  \nBie de femilie X wur dr op n nacht aan t roam klopt. Man en vrouw goat dr oet um te kiekn, wel door op boetn stet. Niks. \nWas t verbeeln? Nee, toch nich.  \nn Zetkng noa tied heurden ze weer in de nacht op t zulfde roam tikn. Weer tou t berre oet en weer noar boetn. \nNon stönnen dr n poar manlu mit n male bösschop. Heur jong, dai in S. dainde as boernknecht, har zuk zulf te kört doan (van hetleven beroven). \ns Nachts mös dat nog aan de oln overbracht worn.\nIk zee al, nich zo mooi, man vrouger kwamen zukke dingen toch onteegnzeggelk veur.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43162,"r":"WEV010507","p":"Barger-Oosterveld","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Howling of dogs and screeching of magpies is an omen of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Honde-gehoel. \nDat is beslist n slecht taikn. Vrouger leufden de lu aan n bulde onzin en muikn zuk baange veur niks; moar alles mou-je nich weg gooien. Honden heb k al voak hoeln heurd tussen 12 en 1 uur s nachts. Dan wazzen ze oet hoeld. In veul gevaln kwam dr dan wol n staarfgeval in de buurt.\nMit eeksters was t net zo. Man dai schrouwden dan wol al n joar laank van te veurn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43169,"r":"WEV010604","p":"Zuidlaren","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Belief in omens of death, such as a dog howling behind the house, or a magpie or crow flying against the window.","i":"F.W.","o":"In mijn jeugd hechtte men wel geloof aan honde-gehuil. Als zo'n dier achter het huis van iemand niet ophield met janken, dan zou de eigenaar niet lang meer leven. Het moet wel eens uitgekomen zijn. \nNiemand maakt zich nu nog bang voor jankende honden. \nAls er een ekster tegen het venster vloog, was dit ook een voorbode van de dood. Anderen zeiden het van kraaien. t Is allemaal verleden tijd."},{"n":43170,"r":"WEV010605","p":"Zuidlaren","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man sees events that happen later.","i":"F.W.","o":"Voorgezicht kwam voor. Doch is dat wel zoveel bijzonders? Er was een schoenmaker, die er een Duitse knecht op na hield, Heinrich. \nHeinrich zag inderdaad dingen, dielater uitkwamen. Zo zei hij eens: \"Er verdrinkt binnenkort iemand,\" de plek vermeldde hij er bij, 'het lijk zal op een ladder thuis gebracht worden\", zo zei hij. \nt Is werkelijk gebeurd. De baas vond het tenslotte zo vervelend, dat hij Heinrich maar ontslag gegeven heeft."},{"n":43178,"r":"WEV010703","p":"Weende","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman is hindered while walking by a black thing. The explanation is that she is hindered by a hearse that later travels along the same path.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloopm.\nDoar ken ik joe hail wat stoaltjes van verteln, dei allemoal woar binnen.\n\nIn Duutsland het mien vrou ook n keer wat biezunders beleefd. Zai ken t getuugn, want zai zit dr bie (de vrouw deed dit inderdaad, ze had zich niet vergist, F.W.).\nWie woonden door mit n aantal kolonistn in de veenderijen. Slim gezellig was t dr nait en doorom zöchtn wie mekoar s oavend wel ais op. Zo ging mien vrou den ook n moal mit n buurvrou noar ain van de kennisn. 't Was oavend en löchte moane. Op t zandpad was niks te zain. Moar toun ze n zet loopm harn begon buurvrou aal langzoamer te loopm. In t leste steunde ze op mien vrou. Dei zee toun: \"Wat wolt toch wel wicht? Scheelt die wat?\" \"k Wait t nait\", zee t oal, \"moar ik aal moar wat veur de voutn, n zwaart ding, ik ken hoast gain stap meer doun.\"\nMien vrou zag gansliek niks en dochde dat heur kameroadske misschien misselk worn was. Doorom zee ze: \"Wie goan moar nait wieder en goan t eerste beste huus in; kenst wat opknapn en den goawe weer noar huus.\" \nBie n zekere Veldman binnen ze toun inloopm. Dat zwaarde ding bleef t mens tot aan de deure tou veur de voutn, zai kon biekans gain stap meer doun.\nBie Veldman zai mien vrou dat Graitje wat mekeerde en dat ze nait over zwaarde dingen veur de voutn kon en dat ze nait allaind weer mit heur terogge gung. Vrou Veldman is doorom ook moar mit goan. Weerom har Graitje hailemoal gain last. Schee","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43185,"r":"WEV010704","p":"Weende","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A farmhand sees a woman with a small black coffin that another person does not see. Perhaps the boy foresaw that a murder would later be committed on that spot.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloopm.\nDoar ken ik joe hail wat stoaltjes van verteln, dei allemoal woar binnen.\n\nIk heb ja joarn snikkevoarder west. \nWie hadden dr ook n lutje snikjong bie; om beurtn mozzen wie t peerd mennen. Moar bie Scheemda noar Zuudbrouk zee dei aine snikjong wizze: \"Winkel, nou nemen ie t peerd van mie over, want dit stok dou k nait.\"  \"Woorom nait?\", vruig ik hom. \"Ja, hier lop ain vrou mit n zwaart liekkissie onder de aarms,\" zee hai, \"ik duur beslist nait.\" \n Nou ja, dat stok gung ik den achter t peerd en ik zag niks. \nMoar t lutje snikjong dochde dr nait aan, zo baange was e.  \nWat is dr gebeurd doar tusn Scheemde en Zuudbrouk? \nBinnen n poar oal mensn vermoord. \nZodat t toch meugelk is, dat t jong door veurgezicht van had het.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43275,"r":"WEV010805","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Man hears the voice of an acquaintance by a canal, but sees nothing. When a little son of the acquaintance drowns, the man is with the screaming father of the drowned child, the same sound he heard earlier.","i":"F.W.","o":"Nou komen wie op t terrain van de spuikkiekers; en eerlijk gezegd dit mou-je leuvn. Teveul dingen heb ik heurd van zukke betrouwboare mensn, dat ie t wel aanneemm moutn. Mensn dei nait logen of snakken of benauwd wazzen, moar goi-e, lang nait domme lu, dei wat heurden of zaggen wat loater oetkwam.\n\nK. van Terwupping bie Onstwedde luip op n oavend langs t oal daip. \nDoor heurt hai den zo moar de stem van H., n bekende van hum. \nHai lop op t geluud of, moar zug ja niks. Was gain mens in de buurt. \nOver verloop van tied - hai har t verschiensel al laank verteld - binnen er kinder aan t speuln bie t daip. Ain jonkje van H. vaalt in t woater en verdrinkt. De andere kinder goan dat gauw in hoes verteln en den komp H. dr ook ja aanloopm. K. was dr ook bie. \nAs H. den stait te schraivn bie zien verdronkn kind, zeg oal K. \"Dat is non t zulfde geluud van dei bewuste oavend.\" \nDou heb ik H. dudelk schrouwn heurd.\"\n\nKiek, dizze dingen binnen mie verteld deur betrouwboare mensn en den zeg ik dat er vrouger toch meer beston den teegnswoordig.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43277,"r":"WEV010806","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A light above a pool is said to be an omen that someone will drown. Someone hears wailing at the pool that turns out to come from cats. The omen is then considered nonsense, but later a girl drowns in the pool.","i":"F.W.","o":"Nou komen wie op t terrain van de spuikkiekers; en eerlijk gezegd dit mou-je leuvn. Teveul dingen heb ik heurd van zukke betrouwboare mensn, dat ie t wel aanneemm moutn. Mensn dei nait logen of snakken of benauwd wazzen, moar goi-e, lang nait domme lu, dei wat heurden of zaggen wat loater oetkwam.\n\nLangs t oal daip (MusselAa) luip vrouger n diekje; spoukdiekje zeden ze dr teegn. Er zol nog es aine verdrinkn inde kolk, die dr in lag bie n bruggie; n lichje zag men smaanks ook boovn de kolk.  Op n keer luip dr ain langs en heurde gejammer bie de kolk. \nHai dr op of en och, toun zag e n poar katn. \n\"Proatjes, aal dei spuikerij\", zee hai.  Moar toch, nait veul loater verdronk in de kolk n wichje.\n\nKiek, dizze dingen binnen mie verteld deur betrouwboare mensn en den zeg ik dat er vrouger toch meer beston den teegnswoordig.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43417,"r":"WEV011002","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Howling dogs that jump up, magpies and church bells that sound duller mean a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Honden, eeksters en klokken.\n Jankende honden betaikende altied ain dode. Dat was hierzo bie ons, moar ook op andere ploatsen. \nMien schoonmouder (deze was erbij tegenwoordig en bevestigde het, dat het bij haar gebeurd was: F.W.) zag de hond veur et roam umhoog springen, toun eevn noa tied n staarfgeval in de femilie veurkwam. \nMit eeksters har zai t zulfde wel al mitmoakt.\nIn Boertange konden de mensn et ook heurn aan de kerkklokke. \nHet geluud van de klokke was den wat doffer; ze zeden: \"Nou, komp ook gauw weer n dode.\"","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43481,"r":"WEV011005","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If all the feathers in a sick person's pillow have been woven together into a wreath, the sick person dies.","i":"F.W.","o":"Krans.\nAs dr bie n zaike langzoamerhand n kranse in t kuzzen kwam, luip t op n ende. Zo 'n kranse wordt bie beetjes en stukjes kloar moakt net zo laank tot ale veern in mekoar vlochtn binnen. Den staarft de zaike. (Verteller bracht dit verschijnsel niet in verband met heksen, zoals in de regel op andere plaatsen: F.W.).","l":"Gronings"},{"n":47784,"r":"WEV011608","p":"Hooghalen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The narrator predicts that a cow will be struck by lightning and that his farm will burn down.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik ben soms in een zekere gemoedstoestand dat ik iets voorzie. \nPrettig is dat niet. \nHet zijn vage momenten, die kort duren; schrik heb je op zo'n moment niet. \nIk zal niet alles weergeven, omdat sommige mensen nog leven, van wiedan ik enkele dingen weet; \n\nIk werkte eens met iemand op het land. Er kwam een bui opzetten.\nDaarom gingen we naar huis. Ik zei tegen mijn vriend: \"Als we in huis zijn, slaat er een koe dood.\" \nWe waren nog maar net in huis of daar kwam reeds een donderslag. \nVoor ons huis liepen de koeien. Een werd er getroffen en lag meteen met de poten omhoog.\nOnze vorige boerderij is ook opgebrand in 1942. \nDie brand zag ik eveneens van te voren. \nt Was op een mooie dag. Ik zei tegen de vrouw: \"Mooi weer.\" \nEn meteen er achteraan: \"t wordt duister- duister- duister---- brand- brand- brand.\" \nDe bliksem is in de woning geslagen."},{"n":43689,"r":"WEV011707","p":"Elp","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man senses that the mayor has had an accident. He goes home, where he hears that the mayor has died in an accident.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ja, veurloop; ik heb hier in et darp iene kend, die veule dinger aan zag komen. Op een dag warkte ie met zien knecht op et land. Opiens zeg ie: \"Ik mut noar hoes; de burgemeester hef een ongeluk had.\" De knecht zeg nog; \"Maar daarumme hoef je toch niet noar hoes?\" Maar zie, dat kon die man dan niet laatn. \nSie goan dus noar hoes en daar heurden ze et al van de vrouwe: \"Onze burgemeester hef zuk doodreden.\"\nEn et was waar ook.","l":"Drents"},{"n":43691,"r":"WEV011802","p":"Rolde","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A sick girl sees men in front of and inside the house and hears coffee being ground. That night the girl dies; she had foreseen her funeral, because drinking coffee is a custom at a funeral.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mijn vader vertelde nog het volgende.\n \nOp een avond waren ze bij familie aan het kaarten. Een nichtje van mij was ziek; ze kaartte niet mee, maar keek naar het spel. \nOpeens zei ze: \"Vader, jaag die kerels toch weg, die daar voor het huis staan.\" Haar vader gaat naar buiten en zegt, dat er geen mannen zijn. Even later zegt het kind opnieuw: \"Vader, er zijn wel mensen en ze dringen zelfs naar binnen; ik hoor ook een koffiemolen malen.\" \nHaar vader ging nog eens weer kijken, maar er was natuurlijk niets. Ze kaartten dus maar rustig verder.\nIn die nacht is het kind gestorven. Ze heeft dus van te voren de mensen gezien, die bij haar op de begrafenis kwamen en het huis binnen drongen. Het is de gewoonte, dat er koffie gedronken wordt bij een begrafenis. Het malen van de koffie hoorde ze ook reeds. \nDeze verhalen zijn echt gebeurd; mijn vader zoog ze niet uit de duim."},{"n":130409,"r":"BIJLSMA003304","p":"Oppenhuizen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Noise in a carpenter's shop late in the evening and at night means that someone will die and a coffin will be ordered.","i":"T.B.","o":"To Toppenhuzen koe it der jouns let of nachts heislik omwei gean yn 'e timmerwinkel. Dan kaem der ringen ien to forstjerren en soe der in deakiste bisteld wurde. Dat wie to Abbegea en Kubaard ek sa.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130448,"r":"BIJLSMA003901","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a ragged man lies dying, the roof tiles rattle.","i":"T.B.","o":"J. Falkema op 'e Jouwer, dy't fan Aldegea W. komt, fortelde my: To Aldegea wenne jehannes Mosk. Hy roun mank, hie in ûngelok mei syn foet hawn. Mosk wie syn bynamme, hy hjitte De Jong. It wie net in fornamen ien, hy wie by de gatten om-ôf ticht.\nDoe't er op stjerren lei, rottelen de pannen op it dak.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130455,"r":"BIJLSMA004201","p":"Sondel","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Near the church tower a dog stays close to its master out of fear; it howls at a sick person's house until that person has died.","i":"T.B.","o":"Bakker kaem mei syn jeijen en fiskjen wol folle let thús en wie sa op 'e lette joun, ja, yn 'e nacht faek noch op 'n paed.\nOp in kear hied er jage op 'e Sondeler Leijen. Yn 'e nacht gie er op hûs oan. Syn hountsje Fike wie by him. By de Sondeler toer gie er skean it lân oer nei de Noarderreed, dêr't er wenne en noch wennet. As se sa ûnderweis wiene doarme Fike by him wei, mar doe't hja dêr by de toer wiene, wie Fike net by him wei to slaen. De houn roun deun tsjin him oan, sadat Bakker hast gjin foet forsette koe. \nBakker treau de houn by him wei en sei: hwat is der, hwat skeelt der oan. Hy koe de houn net ôfwarre; hy roun him sahwat tusken de skonken. Hwat wie der, hwat hat Fike sjoen, sa freget Bakker him ôf. Hwant dat de houn hwat seach, stiet by him fêst.\nFike wie dochs in bysûndere houn. Dêr oan 'e Noarderreed, tichte by harren, wenne omke Mathijs (Negerman). Doe't omke tige siik wie, stie Fike mei de foarste poaten yn 'e finsterbank en gûlde mei de kop omheech oan ien trie wei. Sadré omke dea wie hâlde de houn op mei gûlen en kaem thús. Dat neamd men spoekgûlen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130493,"r":"BIJLSMA004603","p":"Dijken","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Moaning that a man hears on a farm stops when he is in the farmyard and starts again when he leaves. A week later a man buried under hay moans and dies.","i":"T.B.","o":"Pier Lammerts wie boer to'n westen fan de Koufurd. Op in joun let kaem er fan Wâldsein. Doe 't er net fier mear fan hûs wie en de pleats fan Pier Bartlers foarby kaem, hearde er dêr immen ôfgryslik kjirmjen. Hy tocht, dêr koe wol immen yn need sitte, en hy gie op 'e pleats ta. Mar doe 't er dêr op it hiem kaem, wie alles stil en hearde er neat mear. Doe 't er wer in trêd of hwat fuort wie, bigoun it wer.\nIn wike letter sliepte by Pier Bartlers in man op 'e golle. Op in stuit hearde men de man freeslik âljen. Doe 't men der kaem, wie de golle omfallen. De man wie der ûnder rekke en al dea, doe 't men him foun.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130494,"r":"BIJLSMA004604","p":"Dijken","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Shortly after someone has seen a funeral procession in the evening, someone dies.","i":"T.B.","o":"Rijpkema to Goaijingaryp seach op in joun let in lykstaesje dêr op 'e dyk. De oare wyks stoar der immen yn dat lytse doarpke.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130495,"r":"BIJLSMA004605","p":"Dijken","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A child drowns the day after its mother dreams her little son drowns.","i":"T.B.","o":"To Wâldsein dreamde in mem dat har jonkje fordronk. De oare deis fordronk it jonkje en it gie allegear sa, sa 't de mem it yn 'e dream sjoen hie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130502,"r":"BIJLSMA004612","p":"Dijken","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Fear that the farm will burn down when no swallows come into the barn.","i":"T.B.","o":"Men hâldde it alear foar in faei teken as de sweltsjes net wer yn de skuorre kamen. Men wie dan bang dat de pleats ôfbrânne soe.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130517,"r":"BIJLSMA004902","p":"Langweer","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"From the tolling of the bell a woman can hear that someone is dying.","i":"T.B.","o":"As de klok de Langwar lette, dan sei beppe Klaske by âlds: \"Dêr hinget ien oan 'e klok\". Dêr woe hja dan mei sizze, dat der gau immen stoar. Hja koe it oan it let fan 'e klok hearre. In oar hearde it net. Har foarsizzing kaem dan ek út.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130518,"r":"BIJLSMA004903","p":"Langweer","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The eerie howling of a dog means that someone will die.","i":"T.B.","o":"To Eastergea by it klokhús stie alear de herberch \"Hof van Holland\". Der binne letter fjouwer wenten fan makke, dy 't der noch steane. Dêr wenne Jelle de Vries, dy hie in houn, dy koe alderôfgryslik spoekgûle. Dan gie der stéfêst immen dea. Op in kear wie it alhiel mâl hoe 't de houn gûlde. Daliks neielkoar kamen der yn dat lytse doarpke fjouwer to forstjerren.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130533,"r":"BIJLSMA005006","p":"Idskenhuizen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man does not believe that a dog's howling means a death, but when he comes home his mother-in-law turns out to have died.","i":"T.B.","o":"Hendrik Volmer en syn maet wennen to Rûgehuzen en hiene harren wurk yn 'e tsiismakkerij fan it fabryk to Sleat. Moarns fytsten se derhinne, en op in moarn, doe 't it nochal hwat waeide, waerd der ûnderweis net folle sein. Doe 't de earste bak tsiis klear wie, waerd der thédronken. Hendrik sei tsjin Anne: \"Hast wol heart hoe 't jim houn fan 'e moarn gûlde? Der komt grif ien to forstjerren.\n\"Bist net wiis, leaust oan sok âldwivepraet\", sei Anne.\nDe jouns doe 't de beide mannen to Rûgehuzen kamen, wie it earste hwat hja hearden, dat Anne syn skoanmem forstoarn wie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130535,"r":"BIJLSMA005008","p":"Idskenhuizen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"An irregularity in a funeral procession means there will soon be another funeral.","i":"T.B.","o":"Foarhinne roun men op in bigraffenis allegear. De froulju yn regenkleden, de manlju mei hege hoed en swart pak.\nAs der ien út de rige roun, dan kaem der mei gauwens wer in bigraffenis, sa waerd der sein.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130549,"r":"BIJLSMA005112","p":"Bantega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman's prediction that someone will die comes true, for she has already seen the coffin standing there.","i":"T.B.","o":"Alde Jeltsje (to Eastersé) hie in dochter Geeske, dy 't mear seach as in oar. Hja kaem by omke Siger, dy 't slim siik wie. Op ' weromreis sei hja tsjin de frou, dy 't by har wie: \"Siger komt de nacht net oer. Ik ha de deakiste al yn 'e keamer stean sjoen\". Sy fortelde fierder, hoe 't it allegear gean en wê ze soe, en it kaem krektsa út.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130618,"r":"BIJLSMA006601","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Prediction that if a dead person lies unburied over a Sunday, someone else will soon die.","i":"T.B.","o":"In âld minske to Eagmaryp sei as der in lyk in snein oerstie, dan kaem der gau wer ien to forstjerren.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130620,"r":"BIJLSMA006603","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Noise in a carpenter's timber store is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the making of a coffin.","i":"T.B.","o":"By in timmerman to Aldeskoat wie der soms frijhwat leven yn it hout. Dan kaem der ien to forstjerren en moast der in deakiste makke wurde.","l":"Fries"},{"n":12261,"r":"CJ001013","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man says he will die because the little owl called down the chimney that he would die this month.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit kom ris by in âld man op 'e Harste, dy't siik wie.\nHoe giet it? frege heit.\nIt komt net goed.\nEi, dat falt wol hwat ta, net?\nNé jonge, dat falt net ta, sei de âld-man. Myn dagen binne teld. De stienûle hat ta de skoarstien ynroppen \"In deze maand zult gij sterven.\"\nDyselde moanne ìs er ek stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12266,"r":"CJ001102","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Howling dogs mean a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":12280,"r":"CJ001116","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The call of the little owl means a death.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":12331,"r":"CJ001421","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"An aunt of the narrator always knows when a funeral is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In muoike fan my wist altyd dat der in bigraffenis op til wie. Dan wie se hiel bot ûnrêstich. Sy koe 't dan nergens bankje. \"Ik gean yn 'e hûs en ik gean út 'e hûs,\" sei se dan, \"mar hjir sil hwat gebeure.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12332,"r":"CJ001422","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Sjoukje Bonnema can see into the future. She saw her daughter's funeral.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Arjens Sjouk (Sjoukje Bonnema van der Tuin) sjocht ek alles foarút. Hja hat de hiele bigraffenis fan har eigen dochter fantofoaren waernom. Har Bearnom snútte him ûnderweis. En dat gebeurde ek krekt sa.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12344,"r":"CJ001505","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Children are not allowed to skate on the Leeuwenpoel, because someone will drown in this pool. Nor may they wear a red cap, because the one who drowns will be wearing a little red cap.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn bern mochten noait op 'e Liuwepoel komme to riden. Dat woe 'k net lije. Hwant dêr soe ien yn fordrinke. Sy mochten ek net in read mûtske op ha. Hwant deselde dy't dêr fordrinke moest soe in read mûtske drage.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12383,"r":"CJ001708","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a barn owl sits on the crosstree of the mast, it means a disaster will happen. Usually someone on the ship then dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in nachtûle op it skearhout siet (it skearhout is it hout, dêr't de fleugel fan 'e mêst fan in skip oan sit) dan bitsjutte dat in ramp. Meastal stoar der dan ien op it skip.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15627,"r":"CJ002521","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If the bell tolls in a deathly way, 'a dead person is hanging on the clapper'. Then someone will die later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem sei faek, as de klok op in deadske menier lette: \"Der hinget in deaden oan 'e bingel.\" Dan kom der in deaden letter.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15694,"r":"CJ002709","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When one morning a magpie keeps flying around the door of the house, a woman says this means someone in the family has died. The rest of the family laughs at it. Later they hear that a daughter of the woman's brother has died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in moarn skattere der hyltyd in ekster by ús om 'e doar hinne. \"O heden,\" sei mem, \"dit bitsjut hwat. Nou is der ien stoarn yn 'e famylje.\"\nWy laken der om en woenen der neat fan leauwe. Mar mem sei: \"Jimme matte de gek der net mei ha. Tink aenst mar ris om myn sizzen. De middeis kom der in boade út Sumar (Fennema), dy't it boadskip brochte dat in dochter fan har broer fordronken wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15695,"r":"CJ002710","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"An old couple has an old dog. One day the neighbours see the dog howling and raging on the east side of the house. A few days later the neighbour who lives to the east of the old couple dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wennen in âld-feint en in âld-faem njonken ús. Dy hienen in âld-houn, dy't se al jierren hawn hienen. Op in joun seagen wy dy âld houn achter hûs sitten mei de kop nei 't oasten ta en spûkgûle dat er die, 't wie hast net om oan to hearren. In pear dagen letter rekke har buorman Jan, dy't oan 'e oastkant wenne, ûnforwacht dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15883,"r":"CJ003813","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man sets out on a Saturday evening and passes the house of Anne Hoeksema. In the bend after it he is thrown to the side of the road, but nothing happens to him or his moped. A month later Anne Hoeksema has a child, and in the bend where the incident took place Douwe sees the coffin of the little child being carried to the churchyard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in saterdeijoune kom Douwe by de faem wei. It wie sahwat om ien ûre yn 'e nacht. 't Gebeurde hjir mar in eintsje fan ús ôf, in jier of fiif lyn. Hy moest it hûs fan Anne Hoeksma passeare, dêr't it wiif fan yn forwachting wie. Krekt even fierder by in skerpe bocht woardde er oerside set. Hy tocht: Hwat is dit? Hwant der wie abslút neat to sjen. En syn brommer, dêr't er op ried, mankearde ek neat oan.\nKrekt in maend letter wist er it. Anne en dy hienen in dea popke krigen en krekt op itselde plak yn 'e skerpe bocht seach er dat se it kistke fan it bern droegen nei it tsjerkhôf ta.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16070,"r":"CJ004304","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Sytske, the wife of Knjillis, said that once six magpies came one after the other to her at the pump. It was just like a funeral. Less than two weeks later her little daughter was dead. She was six years old.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Knjillis Sytske wenne by 't foetbalfjild. Sy hat baekstere by Frearke Tetsje. Lys, sei se tsjin my, as't leauste wolste, ja of né, op in kear kommen der seis eksters moai achterinoar oan by ús pomp lâns it paedtsje del. Krekt in bigraffenis. Gjin tsien wiken letter wie myn fanke dea.\nSy wie noch mar seis jier âld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16071,"r":"CJ004305","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When the little daughter of Tryn, Willem's wife, was run over and killed by a flour wagon, three magpies came into her yard to bring her the news.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't Willems Tryn har famke yn 1945 ûnder 'e moalwein deariden is, kommen der trije eksters by har op 't hiem, om har de tiding to bringen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16073,"r":"CJ004307","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A magpie came onto the windowsill at the narrator's grandmother's. It is bringing me the news, she said. Three weeks later she died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By ús beppe kom us in ekster yn 't finsterbank. Dy bringt my tiding, sei se. Trije wiken letter stoar se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16074,"r":"CJ004308","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One night the narrator's father went out to a post to fetch fuel. When he came home her mother said something had been brought into the house. It had scraped against the door and thrown the clogs across the floor. A month later her four-year-old daughter died. When the little coffin was brought that evening, she heard the sound again and the clogs were knocked over again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit wie us by nacht om in dikke peal út om dy op to stoken. Us mem gong op bêd.\nDoe't heit yn 'e hûs kom, sei ús mem: Hast hjir earder yn 'e hûs west? Hast hjir nyskes hwat yn 'e hûs brocht?\nNé, sei ús heit, hoe soe 'k dat dien ha.\nNou, hjir is hwat yn 'e hûs brocht. Dat skaefde tsjin 'e middeldoar oan en de klompen woarden tagelyk oer de flier reard.\nDû bist net wiis, sei heit.\nIn goed maend letter forstoar in famke fan harren fan fjirdel jier.\nEn de jountiids brochten se 't kistje. Doe hearde mem krekt itselde lûd, en de klompen woarden tagelyk oer de flier reard.\nDat ha ik doe heard, sei mem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16077,"r":"CJ004311","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Dogs howl eerily when someone is going to die. When Piter's mother had died, a fat, piebald dog stood howling eerily. However often it was chased away, it kept standing there howling.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hounen spûkgûle as der guon stjerre sille. Doe't Piter syn mem hast dea wie, stie hjir in dikke, bûnte houn to spûkgûlen. Hoe wy him ek smieten en fuortjeije woenen, hy bleau hjir mar stean en hâldde net op mei spoekgûlen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16110,"r":"CJ004413","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man from the neighbourhood once came to tell the narrator's mother that his daughter was being treated badly by her husband. While talking he would not sit down. Later he explained why he kept standing. The house had been completely full of people from a funeral. A few weeks later a sister of the narrator died. The man had seen it all beforehand when he came to talk about his daughter.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir hat in man wenne, dy syn dochter wie troud mei in sekere Marten. Sy wennen yn 'e Harkema. Dy man kaem ris in kear by ús mem. Hy fortelde mem, dat syn dochter forhongere dêr yn 'e Harkema. De keardel woe net in slach dwaen en bihandele har as in houn. Dat hy woe syn dochter wer thús ha.\nWylst er oan 't fortellen wie, sei mem al in pear kear: Gean dochs sitten. Mar hy gong net sitten. Ik mat hjir fuort wer wei, sei er. Mar hy bleau mar stean. Mem bigrypte der neat fan.\nLetter hat er forteld, hwerom er stean bleaun wie.\nHy hie net sitte kind. Safolle folk hie der by ús yn 'e hûs west. Dat hied er allegear sjen moatten. Allegear folk fan 'e bigraffenis. In suster fan my, Aefke, wie stoarn. Dat gebeurde in pear wiken letter. Aefke wie 18 jier, doe't se stoar. Hy hie dat allegear foarút sjoen op it stuit dat er by ús mem kaem om oer syn dochter to fortellen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16126,"r":"CJ004611","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If magpies sit chattering in a tree by a house, someone will die.\nIf the dog howls eerily, someone will die.\nIf the cat washes itself, visitors are coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters skatterje yn in beam by hûs, dan giet der ien dea.\nAs de houn spoekgûlt giet der ek ien dea.\nAs de kat him wasket, komt der bisite.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16165,"r":"CJ004910","p":"Noardburgum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If magpies chatter, visitors are coming. If dogs howl eerily, a corpse is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters skatterje by 't hûs komme der praters.\nAs hounen spûkgûle komt der in lyk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16827,"r":"CJ006214","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If someone is ill and will soon die, the dogs howl.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in minske in sykte ûnder 'e lea hat, dêr't er mei gauwens oan stjerre sil, dan gûle de hounen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16846,"r":"CJ006408","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"During the mobilisation of 1918, when the Spanish flu is raging, a man and a child set out early in the morning. One day they come to the churchyard of Beets. Magpies are flying everywhere there. They cannot be driven away. The man senses that something is happening and wants to go home. On the way back a boy comes towards them and says they must go home. The youngest child is ill. When they get home the child is dead.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Wie yn 'e mobilisaesje fan 1918, yn 'e tiid fan 'e Spaenske gryp. Ik wie elke dei mei ús heit to bûkelsykjen. Wy gongen der mei de hounekarre hinne. Moarns ier en bitiid by 't tsjuster gongen wy al fuort, as it bigong to skimerjen. Heit en ik togearre. 't Wie yn Beets by 't âldtsjerkhôf, dêr't wy sochten. Op in dei wienen it dêr allegear eksters. Dy wienen net by ús wei to slaen, se sieten ús hast yn 't hier.\nHeit sei: \"Der gebeurt hwat. Ik wol nei hûs.\" Ik woe dêr earst net fan wite, mar it woardde al mar slimmeroan mei dy eksters. Heit sei: \"Ik kin 't net langer úthâlde.\" It wie sahwat trije ûre, dat wy op stap gongen nei hûs ta. Underweis kom ús al in jonge tomjitte, dy wie op 'e fyts. \"Ik ha al nei de Sweach ta west,\" sei er, \"ik koe jim nergens fine. Jou jongste soan is doadlike min. Dat, as jo daliks thús kommen.\"\nMar doe wied er al dea. Hy wie stoarn oan 'e Spaenske gryp en oan longontsteking, de moarns sahwat om 10 ûre. Krekt op 'e selde tiid, doe't de eksters delsetten kommen. Dat ha de boaden fan 'e dea west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17368,"r":"CJ008910","p":"Sweagerbosk","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, it sees a funeral procession. Then people say: 'there's another one lying at death's door'.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt, sjocht er in lykstaesje. Dan seit men: \"Der is wer ien op stjerren.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17579,"r":"CJ010101","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, someone will die. Before the death of a boy, a dog howled for three nights. When he had died, the howling stopped.\nA woman heard the neighbours' dog howling eerily. The next day her own son died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt komt der ien to forstjerren. Lammert wie in jonge fan Wolter Veenstra. Dy is forstoarn. Fóár syn dea hat de houn wol trije nachten spûkgûld. Doe't Lammert stoar wie't spûkgûlen oer. \nYn Oerisel yn Oudleusen dêr hearde in frou de houn fan 'e buorlju spûkgûlen. Se hie der alhiel gjin erch yn dat dat ergens op doelde. Mar de oare deis stoar har eigen soan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17584,"r":"CJ010106","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In the evening a dog, with its paws on the windowsill, looks in at a man and his family. So the man goes to a devil banisher. He tells him he has come too late. Not long afterwards his child dies. In the dead child's pillow the family finds wreaths with all sorts of little rags wound around them. The rags are of the same fabric as the clothes the child wore on the day it died.\nIf the man had come to the devil banisher sooner, the child would have lived.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit hie in suster, dy wie bitsjoend. Jouns kom der by heit en dy in grouwe houn foar 't finster. Dy sette syn poaten yn 't finsterbank en seach ta 't finster yn. Doe hat pake dan nei de duvelbander ta west. \nIk wyt net mear hwa't dat wie, mar ik ornearje fan Frânse Hinke fan 'e Rottefalle.\n\"Soa, binne jo dêr al?\" sei se. \"Jo woenen hjir oars noait hinne. Mar 't is to let. Der is gjin rêdding mear mooglik.\"\nIt wie sa lyk as it minske sei. It bern is gauachtich dêrnei forstoarn (It wie myn muoike)\nPake en dy ha doe har kessen iepenmakke. Dêr sieten krânsen yn en dêr wienen allegearre lytse lapkes yn dy krânsen biwuolle, dat wie guod fan 'e klean dy't it bern deis oan hie.\nAs se earder by de duvelbander kom wienen, hie 't wêze kind dat it bern yn leven bleaun wie. \nIt is yn 'e Harkema gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17593,"r":"CJ010201","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Close to a very small house was a pool from which some people now and then very clearly heard cries of \"Help, help!\" People thought they were ghostly sounds. The mothers always warned the children: \"Don't come too near the pool, for someone will drown there one day.\"","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Smoarhoeke yn 'e Harkema hat men de Liuwe-poel. Dêr ha wy flakby wenne yn in hiel lyts húske. Guon ha dêr no út dy poel hiel dúdlik \"Help, help!\" roppen heard. De minsken wolle ha dat dat foartsjirmerije wie. Mem warskôge ús as bern altyd: \"Kom net to ticht by de poel, hwant dêr mat noch ien fordrinke.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17600,"r":"CJ010208","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A neighbour comes to tell a mother that her little son has drowned in a pool. When the mother tells her aunt about it right afterwards, the aunt says she already knew. The aunt tells her that the neighbour has just been to tell her too.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie in âlde muoike, dat wie Elske-moai. (Elske Mulder) Dy wenne by de poel op 'e Loane. It is nou sa'n fjirtich jier lyn. Wy hienen in jonkje.\nUs buorwiif kom by ús en brocht biricht dat ús jonkje yn 'e poel fordronken wie. Doe gong se nei Elskemoai ta om it to fortellen. Mar Elskemoai hearde der alhiel net fremd fan op. Sy sei: \"Dû hast hjir sakrekt ek al oer de flier stien. Doe hast neat sein, mar ik wist it al.\" (de buorfrou hie der noait west)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17617,"r":"CJ010313","p":"Noardburgum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A household of four people was going to move. Jehannes predicted that only three of them would leave. The man died before the move.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir tichteby wenne in húshâlding fan fjouwer minsken, dy soenen mei maeije nei de strjitwei forhúzje. \nDoe kom Jehannes op in kear by har en sei: \"Jimme geane dêr net mei jim fjouweren hinne, mar mei jim trijen.\" Sa is 't ek gebeurd. De man stoar noch yn 't âlde hûs. Jehannes hie dat fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17635,"r":"CJ010506","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"On the Feanster Heide a man heard something scraping against the window frame one night. When he saw nothing outside, he went back to bed. A little later something wooden was set down outside and something was thrown on top of it. Again the man went to look, but again he saw nothing. Two weeks later his son died. When the coffin was carried out of the house, it scraped against the frame. It was the same sound as fourteen days before. At the churchyard, where the bier was set down and the carrying poles thrown on top of it, the father heard the other sounds. The time between the sounds was the same as on that night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Feanster Heide lei in man yn 'e nacht op bêd, doe hearde hy ynienen dat der bûtendoar hwat tsjin it kezyn oan skaefde. Hy fan it bêd ôf en nei bûten, mar der wie neat to sjen. Hy joech him wer del. \nIn skoftsje letter waerd der bûtendoar hwat del set dat fan hout wie en der waerd ek hwat boven op goaid. Wer gong de man der op ôf om to sjen, mar ek dizze kear koed er neat gewaer wurde.\nTwa wiken letter kaem syn jonge to forstjerren. Doe men de kiste ta de hûs útsjoude, skaefde dy tsjin it kezyn oan. It wie itselde lûd dat de heit in fjirtsjin dagen tofoaren yn 'e nacht heard hie. \nOp it tsjerkhôf, dêr't se de bier delsetten, dêr't de draechstokken bovenop lein waerden, hearde hy de oare lûden. Tusken dy lûden wie itselde tiidsforrin as yn 'e nacht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17644,"r":"CJ010602","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man left for America with his family. When he arrived there, he wrote to his relatives that on the way they had heard a mermaid singing. A mermaid is a creature, half woman, half fish. On board they said that this meant there was a dead person on board, or that one would come. Then his little child died on board. They lowered the little coffin into the sea.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn Age-om is mei syn húshâlding nei Amerika ta gien. (Age van der Heide wie in broer fan mem). Doe't se yn Amerika oankaem wienen skreau er in brief. Sy hienen ûnderweis in sémearmin sjongen heard. In sémearminne dat is in wezen, heal frommes, heal fisk. Sy seinen oan board, dat bitsjutte dat der in deaden oan board wie of dat der ien kaem. Doe wie har berntsje dêr oan board stoarn. It kistke hienen se yn 'e sé sakje litten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17662,"r":"CJ010701","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People often hear the sound of a small child coming from the Popkepoel at night. They think it is an omen, but so far no child has drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Achter de iepenbiere skoalle op 'e Boelensloane is de Popkepoel. Dêr hearden se nachts faek it lûd fan in lyts bern út kommen. Dêr soe altyd in bern yn fordrinke, wie de hiting. Mar der is oan diz tiid ta noait ien yn fordronken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17672,"r":"CJ010711","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If the bell does not strike, a dead person is hanging from the clapper. If magpies flutter around the house, a death is imminent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de klok deadsk lette, sei myn suster, dan hong der in deaden oan 'e bingel. As de eksters om 't hûs hinne skatteren, wie dat in faei teken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17724,"r":"CJ011207","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman wakes early in the morning and goes into the garden. When the neighbour girl asks why she is up so early, she says the magpies on the windowsill woke her. And that points to a death. The neighbour girl says: \"The first one to come out the door will be the one, they say.\" The woman says she hopes it won't be her.\nA little later the neighbour girl goes to her sister. Her sister's husband has forgotten his work trousers, and the girl takes them after him. She had already caught up with him when she tripped and fell flat on the street. She was dead on the spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us Antsje (Veenstra; neamd nei Antsje Snipel) wie op in moarn ier en bitiid achter hûs yn 'e tún. De eksters hienen har wekker makke. Dy skatteren dat it hwat die en sy fottelen mar fan 'e iene doar nei de oare. Antsje tochte: dit is in min teken. \nDoe gong de doar by de buorlju iepen en de dochter Anne kom der út. It wie in great fanke, sy wie krekt út bêd.\n\"Hwat binne jo bitiid op 'e tún, Antsje\", sei se.\n\"Ja,\" sei ús Antsje, \"en ik ha noch neat dien.\"\n\"Hwat dogge jo dan bûten?\"\n\"Ik ha de eksters sjoen. Dy sieten hyltyd yn 'e finsterbanken. Dat wiist op in sterfgefal.\"\n\"Dy't it earst ta de doar út komt, dy sil 't wêze, sizze se.\"\n\"Dan bin ìk dat\", sei Antsje. \"Ik wyt wol, in jongen-ien kin stjerre en in âlden mat stjerre, mar ik hoopje dêrom net dat ik it bin.\"\nIn skoftsje letter rekke Anne nei har suster ta útfanhûs. Dat wie Fokje. Wylst se dêr wie rekke Fokje har man ta de doar út om nei 't wurk ta.\n\"Och heden,\" sei Fokje, \"nou hat myn man de broek forgetten dy't er yn 't wurk oer de oare hinne ha mat.\"\nDoe sei Anne: \"Ik sil him de broek wol gau even achternei bringe.\"\nHja hie him al ynhelle en soe him de broek tarikke, mar hja kom to stroffeljen en foel rjochtút oer de wei en wie opslach dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17726,"r":"CJ011209","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog stood howling eerily at the spot where a pram usually stands. The little child then died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha in bernsberntsje forlern. Op it plak dêr't syn bernewein gewoanlik stie, hat in houn fan to foaren stien to spûkgûlen. 't Wie ien fan in soan fan my.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17741,"r":"CJ011302","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The master of a state school once heard a voice from a pond say: \"The place is here, the man is not.\" A short time later a pupil drowned in it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ut in oare poel, ek út Surhuzum, hat de master fan 'e staetskoalle al us in stem weikommen heard. Dy stem sei: \"De plaats is er, de man is der niet.\" Ik wie doe noch mar in foech skoaljonge, doe't dat gebeurde.\nIn jonge, dy't by him op skoalle gong, is der gauachtich neitiid yn forsûpt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18140,"r":"CJ011801","p":"Gerkesklooster","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The narrator says that sometimes a voice of someone in great distress sounds from a small lake. This is said to foreshadow a later death by drowning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Boelensloane is in dobbe, dy't útbaggere is. 't Is der tige djip. Ut dy dobbe hearden se us de stem fan ien dy't yn greate noed siet. Dat wie de foartjirmerij fan ien dy't dêr letter yn fordrinke moest. Mar it is my net bikend of dat ek gebeurd is.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18146,"r":"CJ011807","p":"Gerkesklooster","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When the magpies start chattering, a death is often imminent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In man út 'e Harkema fortelde my ris, syn buorfrou wie stoarn. Mar syn mem hie 't wol yn 'e rekken hawn dat dêr hwat slims gebeure soe, hwant hja hie de eksters de deis tofoaren dêr wol skatterjen heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18182,"r":"CJ012004","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"On a Sunday four boys were swimming. One sang: What blooms today, falls away tomorrow. Two hours later he drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in snein-oerdei gongen us fjouwer maten foarby, dy soenen nei de Broeksterfeart ta to silen (= swemmen). Der wie in jongkeardel by. Dy song:\nWat heden bloeit\nvalt morgen weg.\nTwa ûren letter is dy jongkeardel fordronken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18196,"r":"CJ012018","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If magpies chatter in a farmyard, the man or the woman will die two or three days later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As op it hiem de eksters skatteren, dan stoar twa of trije dagen letter dêr de man of de frou.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19315,"r":"CJ012306","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If one heard knocking, it meant a death in the family. If you listened closely it was quiet. But as soon as you stopped paying full attention to it, it started again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As men bikkerkes hearde, dan bitsjutte dat de tiding fan in sterfgefal yn 'e famylje. Dan waerd der hyltyd kloppe. As men bot harke wie 't stil, mar as men der net folle oandacht oan skonk, dan bigong it wer. (is bikkerke itselde as deatikkerke?)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19352,"r":"CJ012511","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At night people often heard wailing and cries for help from a pond. If they went there, there was nothing. Later someone drowned in it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir oan 'e Nije Wei hat in poel west. Dêr hearden se wit hoe faek nachts ien razen. Dy jammere der oer en rôp om help. Gongen se der hinne, dan wie der neat. Letter is Jouke Bintsje dêr fordronken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19368,"r":"CJ012527","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a magpie chatters close to a house, there will be a death in that house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in ekster ticht by hûs skattert, dan komt der yn dat hûs in deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19369,"r":"CJ012601","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A fortune teller predicted to a man that he would not live another half year. He could live longer, but he would feel himself stifled. Six weeks later the man was taken off the threshing machine by the police and arrested. For stealing copper he got six months in prison. In the cell he felt so stifled that he hanged himself with a blue bottom sheet.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik 38 wie, haw ik nei in kaertlizter ta west yn Lukaswoude. Dêr wie it doe merke. Hja sei, ik wie to goed en dêr waerd wol misbrûk fan makke. Ik holp faek oaren en dêr waerd ik net nei bileanne. Ik soe 75 jier âld wurde. Ik bin nou 74.\nDoe wie myn maet oan 'e beurt, dat wie Berend Bakker fan Roan. Hja sei tsjin him: \"Foar jo ha 'k net sa'n moai biricht as foar jou kammeraet. (wy wienen beide like âld) Hja sei: \"Jo leve gjin healjier mear. Mar ik wol net sizze, dat jo dan net langer libje kinne. Mar jo tinke josels binaud. Jo binne yn 'e terskmesine?\"\nDat kloppe.\nIt wie doe yn 'e oarloch fan '14.\nDoe't it seis wiken fierder wie, waerden der trije man fan 'e terskmasine ophelle troch de plysje. Alle trije hienen se stellen. Kees Deukelaar hie 48 boeremetwoarsten stellen út in hutte by in boer út Ezinge.\nPiter Hoving fan Ezinge sloech in fette guos en in knyn dea by in boer.\nBerend Bakker, myn maet hie by in boer alle koperen wichten fan 'e baskule meinom en alle koperwurk fan 'e hynstetugen ôfsnien. Hy hie foar in tachtich goune oan koper nadere. Hja rekken alle trije yn 'e bak. Berend krige in healjier. Hy tocht him yn 'e sel sa binaud, dat hy hat himsels opknope mei bihelp fan in blau ûnderlekken.\n't Kom krekt sa út lyk as de wiersizter sein hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19374,"r":"CJ012606","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If magpies chatter close to the door, someone in the house will die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters ticht by de doar skatterje, giet der ien yn dat hûs dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19383,"r":"CJ012701","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, someone will die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By ús leaude men der fêst oan, as in houn spûkgûlde, dan bitsjutte dat, dat der ien stjerre soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19395,"r":"CJ012713","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A card reader predicts to a young couple that much will 'come between' them during their courtship. A year later the girl began to ail, and she died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie forkearing mei in faem yn Ljouwert. Iebel hiet se. Ik wenne doe noch yn Bûtenpost. Sy gong us nei in kaertlechster ta, hjir yn Ljouwert. Dy warskôge har foar in kammeraetske, dy't har wol us hwat ûntstiel. Dat klopte, dat wist Iebel wol.\nLetter ha Iebel en ik togearre nei dy kaertlechster west. Ik sei: wy ha forkearing.\nDoe seach it minske tige earnstich. Sy sei: \"Nou ja, wol forkearing, ja - mar - der komt hiel, hiel hwat tuskenbeiden. Jo krije gau in oare bitrekking.\nDer komt hiel hwat tusken.\"\nIk woarde tsiismakker. In jier letter is Iebel bigong to sukkeljen en is se forstoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19403,"r":"CJ012801","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a black jackdaw sits on the post in the farmyard, it means a family member who lives far away will die. But if one sits on the windowsill, someone from the household itself will go.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in swarte ka op 'e dampeal fan 't hiem stie, bitsjutte dat dat der ien út 'e famylje stjerre soe, dy't fierôf wenne.\nMar stie der ien yn 't finsterbank, dan gong der ien dea út eigen gesin.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19424,"r":"CJ012905","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"As punishment for his fickle and wild youth, a man foresaw the deaths of all his children. One night he had stood listening to whether all his children were still alive. Six weeks later four died of measles. Another time the man saw a funeral in his own house. There were no more children at home and he thought he would die himself. But one of his daughters who lived away fell ill and came to her parents' house to die there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Knjillis Veenstra wie in omke fan my. Dy moest alles sjen. Dat hied er ta straf krige. Hwant hy wie yn syn feintejierren och sa wilewalich en in forwoest man.\nHy hat njoggen bern forlern en dat hat er allegear foarsjoen. Seis wiken fan tofoaren hat er it wol foarsjoen. Dan wie hy der nachts ôf en harke der nei as dy en dy noch wol leefde. Fjouwer berntsjes hat er forlern oan 'e mûzels. Dat hat er ek foarsjoen. Doe't se fan 'e begraffenis fan 't iene berntsje weromkamen, wie 't oare dea.\nEk in kear doe seach er in bigraffenis by him út 'e hûs wei, doe tocht er net oars as dat wied er sels. Hwant doe wienen der gjin bern mear by him yn 'e hûs. Mar 't wie ien fan syn dochters. Dy wenne by 't spoar en rekke siik. Doe kom se by har âlden, dêr't se stoarn is.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19427,"r":"CJ012908","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Once people heard a sound coming from the ditch. A few days later a little boy drowned in it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer Eibert Veenstra hat hjir foaroer wenne. Hy hat in jonkje forlern fan fjouwer jier. 't Is yn in greate sleat forsûpt. Dagen fan tofoaren ha se syn lûd út 'e sleat heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19491,"r":"CJ013031","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A girl with red hair drowned in a pond from which cries for help had been heard earlier.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Harkema is in poel, dêr is in fanke yn fordronken mei read hier. 't Wie ien fan Jouke Elzinga. De wyks fan to foaren hienen se in stem út dy poel heard, dy't rôp: \"Help! Help!\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19504,"r":"CJ013112","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If magpies chatter in the farmyard, someone who lives there will die. Also if a dog stands howling eerily towards a house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters op it hiem skatterje, dêr ha'k it net op stean. Der wurdt faek biweard, dat der dan ien stjert fan deselden dy't dêr wenje. Dat is ek sa hwannear't in houn bigjint to spûkgûlen. Hy stiet dan mei de kop nei 't hûs ta dêr't dyselde stjerre sil.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19520,"r":"CJ013204","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Cries for help were once heard from a pond. People assumed someone with red hair would drown in it. Later a man drowned there while paddling.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn it Swartfliet (in poel, tichte by de Reitsmawei yn Harkema) ha se us in gejammer heard: Help! Help!\nDe hiting wie, dêr moest ien yn dy poel forsûpe mei read hier.\nIn jier of sawn lyn is der in jongeman yn fordronken dy't dêr oan 't poatsjebaeijen wie. Claus hiet er.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19542,"r":"CJ013402","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People once heard cries for help from the Leeuwepoel. Someone is still bound to drown in it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Liuwepoel ha se us rare gelûden heard. Help! Help! woarde der roppen. Dêr mat altyd noch ien yn fordrinke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19546,"r":"CJ013406","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"An old woman saw her son's funeral in miniature on the table before he had died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik slepte as jonge by myn âlde beppe. Har âld man wie stoarn. Doe sei se op in kear tsjin my: \"Sjoch, dêr rint in geitsje oer de flier mei in lang ketting om.\" Ik lei al op bêd. Ik sei: \"Ik sjoch neat, beppe.\"\n\"Hearst it ketting dan ek net?\" sei beppe.\n\"Né\", sei 'k.\n\"Sjoch dan,\" sei se, \"dêr rint it hinne.\"\nDoe sei se: \"Ik ha in lykstaesje sjoen yn 't lyts op 'e tafel.\" 't Wie de lykstaesje fan har eigen soan, dy't letter ûnder tsjinst overleden is. It is krekt sa gebeurd lyk as sy it op 'e tafel sjoen hat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19570,"r":"CJ013510","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A voice calling for help was once heard from a stream. A few years later a young fellow drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 't Swartfliet yn 'e Harkema ha se us in kear in stem heard, dy't rôp om help. Sûnt seinen se altyd dat dêr noch us ien yn fordrinke moest. In jier of hwat lyn is der in jongkeardel yn fordronken, dat wie in Claus.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19586,"r":"CJ013801","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One night people heard hammering and boards being broken away in the house, but there was nothing to be seen. When the father died about two weeks later, the same sound was heard. Because the coffin would not fit into the small house, boards had to be removed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ús heit al min wie, hearden wy by ús op in nacht timmerjen en weibrekken fan planken. Mar der wie neat to sjen.\nWy wennen yn in foech krot, dat doe't ús heit der ôf rekke, sa'n fjirtsjin dagen letter, koenen se de kiste net yn 'e hûs krije. Doe moesten der planken útbrutsen wurde. Dat wie itselde lûd dat wy in fjirtsjin dagen fan tofoaren dy nachts heard hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19601,"r":"CJ013909","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If you dream of fish, there will be a death in the family.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":19692,"r":"CJ014519","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, someone will die. Also if magpies chatter.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Spûkgûlde der in houn, dan leaude men fêst dat der in sterfgefal kom. De houn stie mei de kop nei de kant út to sjen dêr't ien stjerre soe.\nAs eksters skatteren kom der ek in deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19962,"r":"CJ015903","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A little boy sees an old man digging a grave. A few days later someone dies and the boy sees exactly the same thing. It was a voorgezicht (a vision of a future event).","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik in jonkje wie fan in jier of sawn, acht, seach ik us in âld man, dy wie oan 't graefmeitsjen. It sân woarde oan kant set, ik seach it tige dúdlik. Ik sei: \"Mem, hwa komt der op it hôf?\" \"Ei jonge,\" sei mem, \"net ien.\" Mar ik hie 't dúdlik sjoen.\nIn pear dagen letter brochten se ien nei 't hôf ta. 't Wie op 't âld tsjerkhôf. Deselde âld man dolde it graef. It sân woarde oan kant lein, krekt sa't ik it foarút sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20380,"r":"CJ018709","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At a certain place people often heard cries for help coming from a pond. A few years later someone did indeed drown in that pond. The cries for help had been a harbinger of the coming death by drowning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 't Swartfliet - in poel yn 'e Harkema - ha se us in stim heard. Der waerd roppen: \"Piter - mem! Help my!\"\nUs heit wenne foar dy poel. It wie in Piter Spinder. Mar heit hat noait ien helpe hoefd en der is yn heit syn tiid ek noait ien fordronken. In pear jier lyn is der in jongfeint yn forsûpt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20393,"r":"CJ018803","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a death is imminent, a dog always starts to howl eerily. The dog foresees the death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der ien tige siik wie en hy lei op stjerren, dan bigoun ús houn altyd to spûkgûlen. Hy seach it lyk fan tofoaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20394,"r":"CJ018804","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If the bells ring in a certain way, a death is coming. It is an omen of an approaching death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der ien tige siik wie sei ús mem wolris: \"Dy redt it net, hwant de klokken bongelje.\" Dan koe men der mar fêst fan op-oan dat sa'n ien mei koartens stoar.\nDe branjehandler fan Sumar sei ek: \"Ik hear it wol oan 'e klokken, der sil wer ien stjerre. It lûd wol net út 'e klok, dat doocht net.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20671,"r":"CJ020713","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, there will be a death within three days.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":20843,"r":"CJ021807","p":"Aldeboarn","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If the windmill stood with its sails in a cross, it meant death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de moune yn 't krús stie, dan wie dat in kwea teken. Dat bitsjutte dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27408,"r":"CJ065402","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man once saw a funeral procession pass by. A few days later the funeral procession passed there in reality.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Klaes Kooistra hie trije jier yn 'e gefangenis sitten.\nMei syn swager Tseard kom er thús. Doe't se oan 't plak ta wienen, dêr't nou it nije tsjerkhôf is yn 'e Harkema, sei er tsjin Tseard: \"Kear dy om. Der komt in lykstaesje oan.\" Mar Tseard seach it net. In pear dagen letter kom de echte lykstaesje. Doe koe Tseard it èk sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27409,"r":"CJ065403","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One evening a young man saw a funeral procession pass by. Everyone was dressed in black and silent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde oan 'e Nije Wei dat op in nacht de feint by de faem weikom. Mar even letter wie hy der al wer.\nEn hy wie sa bleek as in deaden.\n\"Hwat skeelt dy nou?\" sei de faem.\nHy sei: \"Der is hwat. Ik kom in lange lykstaesje tsjin. Alles wie yn 't swart en der woarde net in stom wurd sein.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27418,"r":"CJ065412","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog often howled eerily near a pregnant woman. The woman was very worried. Shortly after the birth the baby died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem wie yn forwachting, sy moest in lytsen ha.\nWy hienen in lyts dykje achter hûs. Dêr kom alle dagen in houn boven op en dy spûkgûlde mar.\n\"O heden,\" sei mem, \"dit komt net goed. Jij dû dy houn dêr us wei\", sei se dan tsjin my.\nDoe't it bern der kom stoar it fuort dêrnei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":207662,"r":"KUSTERS012109","p":"Asten","v":"N.-Br.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A magpie is a bad omen; a crow brings a death.","i":"C.K.","o":"'n Ekster is 'n slecht voorteken; 'n kraai brengt de volgende zondag 'n dode."},{"n":130055,"r":"VERHOEFF000505","p":"Strijen","v":"Z.-H.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Buying a black cap for the first time before one's wife has died is seen as a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event).","i":"L.V.","o":"Toen Tante Leun stierf, weet ik nog goed, dat Jan, d’r man, een tijdje daarvoor voor het eerst een zwarte pet had gekocht. Anders droeg hij altijd een gewone pet. En op de begrafenis zei iedereen: “Dat is vast een rouwpet voor Leun geweest”."},{"n":130056,"r":"VERHOEFF000506","p":"Strijen","v":"Z.-H.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People born with a caul see funerals; a crow on the roof and a howling dog are a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death; after a death on Sunday another death soon follows.","i":"L.V.","o":"Over beeldwit heb ik weleens horen praten, maar ik weet niet meer wat het precies was. Het waren mensen, die iets van begrafenissen konden zien. Ze zeiden trouwens ook, dat er een zou doodgaan als er een kraai op het dak zat of als eer een hond stond te huilen. En als er een sterfgeval op Zondag was, dan zou er nog gauw een volgen."},{"n":43706,"r":"WEV012006","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Magpies and jays foretell a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ons buurman was n moal aan t schaitn op eeksters. Mien voar zee: \"Dou dat moar nait mien jong, zai goat vanzulf weer vot; zai wiln die allaind moar wat verteln.\" Buurman lachde en schoot deur.  \nOch, et duurde hail nait zoveul doagn, toun sturf buurvrouw en de eeksters bleevn vot. Mien voader zee dat loater teegn buurman. En toun mos dei toegeevn, dat t zo was. \nBie ons vloog indertied s mörns hail vroug n schraiweekster (= vlaamse gaai) om t huus tou. Ik zee teegn mien man: \"Dat deugt nait, dr gebeurt hier wat.\" Mien man wol dr niks van waitn. \nMoar toun mien schoonmoeke overleed en dei schraiweekster vanof dei dag nait weer kwam, mos hai mie wel gliek geevn. \nIk wil moar zegn: \"t Is aal gain biegeleuf, wat er zo verteld wordt\"","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43713,"r":"WEV012105","p":"Weite","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event): a man sees lights burning everywhere when he comes home in the evening, though this is not the case. Weeks later one of the brothers becomes so ill that a night watch must be kept, with the light on.","i":"F.W.","o":"Dizze vertelsels hebben mien oln mie verteld. \nMisschien is dr niks van woar. \nWat wel woar is, en door loog mien oal heer nait om, is dit: \nAin van zien bruiers was n moal s oavends in huus komen en har zegd: \"Ie hebt ja overal löcht aan; in de schure, int kaarnhuus, op de kougaange, wat is dr toch te doun?\"\nMien oln zeden, dat dat nait zo was; naarns was löcht op. \nVaier weekn loater wur ain van de jonges zaik. \nHai is overleden en veurtied mos dr bie woakt worn. \nEn s nachts hebben ze toun de haile nacht de lampn aan had. \"Kiek\", zee toun dei jonge vent, mien oom dus, \"ik heb t löcht op dei oavend toch al van te veurn zain.\" n Geval van veurloop dus, dat meer veur komp.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43789,"r":"WEV012206","p":"Wessinghuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Dogs that sit howling in front of a house for a long time are a harbinger of a death. Shooting the dog does not help; the sick person dies anyway.","i":"F.W.","o":"Hier nog wat andere dingn, dai ik mie herinner oet mien jeugd.\n\nEn dan de honden netuurlijk. \nWee joe, as dai laank bie joen hoes zatn te jankn. Ie gungen dr aan.\nk Wait nog best dat er wol es n hond doodschootn is, umdat e nich vot wol as de mensn dr op smeetn.\nt Huilp wol niks, want n zaike in de buurt gung toch hen.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43797,"r":"WEV012207","p":"Wessinghuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The chattering of magpies is an omen of a woman's death. The narrator wants nothing to do with the screeching of birds.","i":"F.W.","o":"Hier nog wat andere dingn, dai ik mie herinner oet mien jeugd.\n\nIk zag n moal vaier eekster op n voldeure zitn van n boerderij. Was n oal mens in hoes. Ik har ja al voak heurd dat et kwaod betaiknde en doe heb ik dr op let. De eeksters zatn door man te schattern en sprongn wat henneweer. t Oal mens is best overleden.\nAingeliek mout ik niks hebn van biegeleuf en toch mout ik dat vogelgeschrouw nich bie hoes. Van kind of aan bin je baange moakt veur dai dingen en ie koomt dr nich makkelk of van n zekere angst: ie kunt nooit waitn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43819,"r":"WEV012306","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman twice hears knocking on the window while there is nothing to be seen. Later someone knocks on the window to say that the neighbours' boy has drowned.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloopn.\nt Gebeurde es n keer in Bennewol. \nWur aan t roam klopt bie aine. t Oal mens heurde t en vertelde dat aan heurschoondochter. Dei zee t weer teegn heur man, moar dei mainde, dat zien mouder zuk wat wies moakt har.  \nNait laank noa tied heurde de vrouw veur dtweide keer getik op t glas; was gain mens te zain, moar t klopn was dudelk heurboar. \nZe zee teegn heur kinder, dat er wat gebeurn zol binnenkört. \nt Oal mens wur wat uutlacht; hou kon dat nou? \nOp n nacht is er geklop. Op hetzulfde venster as dei vrouw et van te veurn heurd har. Zai van t berre of om te kiekn of dr nou den wat is. Joa, doar stait aine en zeg, dat de buurjong net in de wieke vonden is, verdronken. \nZeun en schoondochter mozzen dr toun ook wel uut om te helpn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43889,"r":"WEV012403","p":"Vriescheloo","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A white kale stalk is a bad omen; it means a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Waitn ie dat n widde mousstronke (boerenkool) tusken de andern in n slecht veurtaikn is? Dan komp dr n dode in de buurt. \nDat is n hail old volksgeleuf in dizze umgeevn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43918,"r":"WEV012603","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A star that a man sees falling on his neighbour's house was an omen of her death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Old volksgeleuf.\nd Olle heer zag voaker biezundere dingen. Door mozzen wie de gek nait mit drievn, want hai kreeg maistied gliek.\nZo zugt e op n oavend n steern vaaln op t huus van de buurvrouw.\n“Dat liekt mie nait goud tou”, zee hai, toun e dat in de koamer aan ons vertelde. Wie leufden dat, want voader kon t ja waitn. Hai wost t ook.\nOl buurvrouw is omkomen. Stumper heft kokend woater over zuk hen kreegn en door is ze aan sturven.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44048,"r":"WEV012902","p":"Buinen","v":"Dr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A few days before a death, a woman hears magpies chattering around the house.","i":"F.W.","o":"Dat veuruut zien komp trouwens meer veur.\nIn de oorlog hadden wie bie de zwienen een schetskaart.\nDat ding mus goed bewaard worden.\nOp een dag kreeg ik de kontroleur en die mus de kaart eevn met hebben naar huus. Maar wat dee de keerl?\nIe kroop onder n auto man en ie was meteendood. Weg was de kaarte. \nLater bin ik es naar zien moe reden of de kaart daar misschien nog lag, maar ook niet. En nou wolik oe dit feitelk verteln.\nToen ik bie zien kwam, zee ze: “Och ja Siebring, ik had et al een paar dagen dacht; gebeurt binnenkort n ongeluk, want de aksters schrouwen al n iele poos om ons hoes.” \nDe beestn hadden et al geweetn.","l":"Drents"},{"n":44086,"r":"WEV013006","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"An educated and distinguished woman warns not to leave Christmas decorations up until after New Year, or else someone will die.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wie kreegn n keer veziede uut Den Hoag. Haile veurnoame en lang gain achterlieke lu. De vrouw komp in de keukn en zug doar wat kerststukn stoan; hulst en wat dennetakn. Mien vrouw har dei noar nei-joar opbaargd, omdat zo mooi leek.\n“Och”, zeg dei Hoagse, “doe die kerststukken toch weg, anders durf ik hier niet te zijn.”\nMien vrouw zee: “Moar mens, dat liekt ja mooi, wat zol dat nou?”\n“Nee”, zee ze, “als u die dingen na nieuwjaar niet uit het huis doet, dan komt hier een dode.”\nMien vrouw hef de dingen dou vot doan, moar wat toch n biegeleuf van anders wieze mensn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44380,"r":"WEV013104","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A corpse that lies unburied over a Sunday means another death within six weeks.","i":"F.W.","o":"n Volksgeleuf was wieder, dat as ain liek n zundag overstun, dat er den binnen zes weekn weer ['n] staarfgeval komen zol.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44385,"r":"WEV013202","p":"Klazienaveen","v":"Dr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Dogs howl at places where a death will occur and can hear the moaning of a sick person from a distance.","i":"F.W.","o":"Nou heurn ie niet veul meer van doodjoelers; die honden, die weetn, dat er n dode komp. Ik heb er zelf zo n hond had; maar ik heb hum wegdaan; altied was e bie t pad te hoeln en ie kunnen dr op aan, dat er wat veurvaln zol in de naaste tied.\nEr woonde ook n grafdelver bie ons. Hie had ook zo n hond.\nEn daarom wus ie ongeveer, wanneer er wark veur hom komen zol.\nDat zit zo met die honden: Sie hebt n kort gezicht en hiel goede oorn; as er bieveurbeeld in Emmen iene ziek is en lig te karmen, dan heurn die honden dat.","l":"Drents"},{"n":43655,"r":"WEV013803","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A sick woman who hears a dog howling sees it as a sign that she will die soon. Small dogs cannot see misfortune.","i":"F.W.","o":"Toun vrouw P. hier n eindje van ons of n poar joar leden slim zaik was, gungen wie elke dag eevn kiekn, hou of t er mit gung. \nOp n dag kwam mien vrouw dr ook weer en toun zee t oal: “Wat is dat aal veur n gehoel op stroade?”\n“Och, doar zit n hond te jankn; k wait nait wat dei wil”, zee de vrouw. Moar zai dochde wel wat.\nEn toun zee vrouw P.: “Dat is gain best taikn; nou zel t wel gauw doan weezn.” En zo was t; t oal mens is overleden.\nWie hebben zulf ook al zo n hondje had, dei bie t pad gong, as dr wat veurvaln zol.\nDit is beslist gain flauwekul; allaind, honden onder de vaartig centimeter kennen gain ongeluk zain van te veurn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44681,"r":"WEV013907","p":"Genne","v":"Ov.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A death is coming when dogs howl and chickens walk around with a straw in their beak.","i":"F.W.","o":"Voorloop van sterfgeval is huilen van honden huilen, kippen die met strohalm over staart hebben of een strohalm in de snavel en over de deel lopen."},{"n":44715,"r":"WEV014005","p":"Zwartemeer","v":"Dr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A prediction comes true that after a fatal accident, another dead person will be carried out of the same house after seven weeks; also, something else will happen after four weeks.","i":"F.W.","o":"Zeven weken geleden gebeurde hier in de buurt een ongeluk.\nEen jongeman kwam om het leven. Een kennis van ons zei toen: “Met zeven weken wordt er uit hetzelfde huis weer een dode gedragen.” En t gebeurt nog ook. Van hetzelfde gezin is er deze week een tweede zoon verongelukt.\nNu moet er over vier weken weer iets ergs voorvallen.\nDat heeft de bewuste jongeman nu tenminste voorspeld.\n\nMisschien zeg je straks, als je weg bent, tot jezelf:\n“De man kon mooi vertellen, maar ik geloof het niet.”\nIk kan me dat best voorstellen; maar toch kun je alles gerust voor waar aannemen, want er is niks bij gelogen. Vraag mijn vrouw er maar op na."},{"n":44716,"r":"WEV014006","p":"Zwartemeer","v":"Dr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The howling of dogs has meaning; why a dog does not approach a group of people; a dog sees a funeral procession in advance; preventing a dog from howling.","i":"F.W.","o":"U gelooft niet, dat honden-gehuil iets te betekenen heeft? \nJawel heur.\nEen hond durft wel op je af te komen, als je alleen bent. \nMaar nooit, als er meer mensen zijn.\nDan wordt hij vaak bang.\nEen hond kan een begrafenisstoet van te voren zien en al die mensen bij elkaar maken hem schrikkerig. Daarom jankt ie.\nWie dicht bij een kerkhof woont, moet zijn hond dan ook een plaats geven, dat hij het gezicht er niet op heeft.\nDan jankt ie de hele dag niet.\nDe dokter hier heeft er een mooie sint-benhard om doodgeschoten. Dat was stom. Als de man het dier zijn hok had verplaatst, was het wel rustig geworden.\n\nMisschien zeg je straks, als je weg bent, tot jezelf:\n“De man kon mooi vertellen, maar ik geloof het niet.”\nIk kan me dat best voorstellen; maar toch kun je alles gerust voor waar aannemen, want er is niks bij gelogen. Vraag mijn vrouw er maar op na."},{"n":44725,"r":"WEV014106","p":"Vledderveen","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog howling in front of a house means something is going to happen. Prediction that a man with a brown horse will have a fatal accident.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mevr. N.: “Dat is meugelk, dat zo wat nait bestait, moar veurbeduudsels binnen dr zeker.\nIn Veele is n keer n kind verdronkn. Nou wol t geval, dat ain van onze buurn in Onstwedde al wat in de goatn har; zien hond har al voak zitn te jankn veur t huus, woor dat kind woonde. Hai keek er den ook hail nait roar van op.\nHai veurspelde wieder dat er in Veenhuuzn n kerel omkomen zol; dei kerel zol dr langs goan mit n broen peerd en stevels zol de man aan hebben.\nAin oom van mie dus doorom nooit n broen peerd koopn.\nMoar hier is tot nou tou niks van komen en zel wel nait deurgoan. \nt Andere is woar.”\n\nNaber: “Kiek, door he-je t ja al; n mens ken wel es wat veurspeln en touvallig gliek kriegn en den zeden de ezels vrouger, dat ze spuik-kiekn konnen.”\n\nMevr. N.: “Och, doe spotst overal mit; moar zokse dingen bestoan; dat binnen lu, dei mit de helm geboorn binnen.”\n\n“Och mens; n kind mit n helm is t zulfde as n bolle mit n puut.”\n\nUit zulke gesprekken blijkt, dat sommige mensen sterk aan die oude vertelsels geloven, terwijl anderen de schouders ophalen.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44763,"r":"WEV014107","p":"Vledderveen","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At night a woman hears someone go up to the attic, scoop grain into a sack there and come down. Later, after someone's death, she hears the same sound when rye is scooped for the bread for the funeral.","i":"F.W.","o":"“Kenst mooi proatn jong, moar ik leuf dr aan. Mien grootmoeke hef nog meer beleefd.\nZai lag op n nacht op berre en door heurt ze ain de ledder op loopn; t heurt net of hai n schubbe achter zok aansleept.\nOp beune lag koorn en hai begunde door wat van in n zak te schepn. Dou gung e mit de zakvol noar doale de ledder weer of. \nGrootmoe is dr kold van worn.\nEn nou moust heurn, wat er n poar weekn loater veur vuil.\nIn de buurte was n oal mens overleden; nou was t vrouger de gewoonte, dat dr den stoetn bakt wurn op de dag van de begravvenis. Op dei dag heurde grootmoeke t zulfde geluud weer en nou was t echt. Knecht van de boer, woor zai ook dainde, gung mit de schubbe noar boovn en schepde rogge in de zak; door gong hai mit noar de meuln, woor t buuld wur.\nIs dat nou veurbeduudsel of nait? Grootmoe loog zokse dingen nait.”\nNaber: “Joa mens, doekomst uut Onstwedde en doar harn ze zowat. \nAs n hond hoelt, den wil e noar n teve tou, anders niks.\nEn woorom zugt nou den gain mens meer wat?”\n\nOpmerking: Uit zulke gesprekken blijkt, dat sommige mensen sterk \naan die oude vertelsels geloven, terwijl anderen de schouders ophalen.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44868,"r":"WEV014206","p":"Barger-Compascuum","v":"Dr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"After seeing a red flame over the roof, a man touches the door handle, which is cold. That means a death. A hot door handle would have meant that the house would burn down.","i":"F.W.","o":"Oale spookverhoaln ken ik joe wel verteln, temeer omdat wie stomp aan de grens wonen; de bevolking is hier maist haalf duuts en n bult binnen net as ik “heimatlos”. \n\nWat ik zulf n moal zain heb, is dit.\nIk zat op stoule en keek tou t roam uut. Inainszai ik over t dak van n huus n rode vlam trekn. Ik denk: “Dat is mis.”\nIk bin gauw noar t huus hen loopn en heb aan de klinke vuild. Klinke was kold. Dou wos ik' tal; zol n dode in dat huus komen.\nEn t is net zo uutkomen.\nAs de klinke hait west har, den was t huus opbrand.","l":"Drents"},{"n":44908,"r":"WEV014305","p":"Meerland","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In a beekeeper's house someone will die when the bees become restless.","i":"F.W.","o":"As er ain iemen het en dei daiern worn onrustig, den wil dat zegn, dat er in t hoes van de iemker gauw ain te overlieden komp.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44921,"r":"WEV014405","p":"Weiteveen","v":"Dr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Removing swallows' nests means someone will die; the cowshed should not be cleaned between Christmas and New Year; passing on bezetten (the power to bind or charm) usually stays in the family.","i":"F.W.","o":"Volksgeleuf was dit: Zwaalvie-nustn mossen ie nait weg moakn, want den gong dr aine van t huus dood.\nTussen kerstmis en nei-joar mos men gain kou-grub schoon moakn.\nBezetn - en dat kwam veul veur; trouwens nog wel - kon n man over doun op n vrouw en n vrouw op n man.\nIn de regel bleef de goave in de femilie,","l":"Drents"},{"n":44940,"r":"WEV014504","p":"Nieuw-Balinge","v":"Dr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Dogs and magpies announce death during illness. Chasing away a howling dog at the house of a sick person.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik moet oe verteln, dat ik mien hiele leven op Nieuw Balinge woond hebbe en dat er bitter weinig bekend is over spookn en ander biegeleuf. Het was hier de plaats dr niet veur.\nHet volgende wiet ik nog.\n\nHonden en eksters waarn gevaarlijk, as ie ziek waarn. Sie kondigden de dood aan. Ik heb dat zulf beleefd.\nIk bin namelijk ziek west en toen zat er ook zo’n hond te joeln veur ons huus. Maar iedere keer joeg mien va hum weg; ie was inwendig bange, dat zien jongien dood gaan zol.","l":"Drents"},{"n":44843,"r":"WEV014602","p":"Erica","v":"Dr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man predicts a funeral and that the hearse bringing the deceased home will have to turn around.","i":"F.W.","o":"Hier woonde ook n mannegien, dat dingen veuruut zag. Ie woonde bie de diek en kon allerhande gebeurtenesn veurspeln. \nZo zeg e n keer teegn iene: “Er kump een begravvenis binnenkört. De waagn kump veurbie joe huus en dan draait ie weer umme. Ik kan niet niet zegn, wie of er begraavn wordt.”\n Dat was n roar geval; dat die waagn veurbie een huus reed en terugge gunk.\n Maar et was goed zien deur t kereltien.\n Er wur iene ziek, die noar t zieknhuus mos. Doar is ze sturvn; de waagn bracht heur noar huus, maar de lu wistn niet precies waar ze weezn moestn. Ze reden dus te var en daar vrugen ze et adres. Inderdoad moest toen de waagn keern en terugge vaarn.","l":"Drents"},{"n":130672,"r":"BIJLSMA007802","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman born with a caul predicts a death and who will lay the cloth over the coffin, and it comes true.","i":"T.B.","o":"Van Netten syn pake, Hylke de Jong, kaem út 'e Haske, dêr 't er yn it baggerwurk wie. Der wie in arkje, dêr 't in wyfke yn wenne, dy 't mei in helm berne wie. Op in kear leine se oan 'e wâl en hellen dan molke fan in boer. Doe sei it minske tsjin beppe Ybeltsje: De boerinne makket it net lang mear.\nEi kom, sei beppe, de frou is soun en goed.\nIt wyfke sei: nou it is sa 't ik Jo siz, binnen de trije wike is de boerinne dea. Ik ha har yn 'e kiste lizzen sjoen, en Jo sil it kleed oer de kiste lizze.\nBeppe woe it net leauwe, mar it kaem út sa 't it minske it sein hie. Doe 't de frou forstoarn wie en yn de kiste lei, frege men beppe oft se even helpe woe. Doe 't dat sa útkaem en beppe klearstie om it kleed oer de kiste to lizzen, skeat it har yn it sin hwat it wyfke foarsein hie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130673,"r":"BIJLSMA007803","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman born with a caul sees where a missing child lies and that it has drowned; she sees funerals in advance and sees who the dead person is; stepping aside for a funeral procession.","i":"T.B.","o":"Op in kear lei it baggerfolk ris oan de kant fan de Hegemermar. It barde dat der in bern fuort wie. Der waerd socht en fiske, en alleman wie drok mei oan it sykjen.\nDe frou út it arkje sei: ik sjoch it bern dêr en dêr lizzen, tusken skip en wâl. It bern is al wei. Men foun it bern op it oanwiisde plak, it wie al wei.\n\nDat wyfke seach ek wol bigraffenissen - in oar seach neat.\nFoar sa 'n bigraffenis moast men oan 'e kant gean, net trochrinne. De frou seach hwa 't der yn 'e kiste lei. Hja seach soks net sa 't men eat oars sjocht. Hja hie it twadde gesicht.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130680,"r":"BIJLSMA007901","p":"Sint Nicolaasga","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Hearing coffin wood being moved at night means someone will die. The way it is moved shows whether heavy or light wood will be used.","i":"T.B.","o":"Heit wie as jongmaetsje timmerfeint by Ybe de Ree to St. Nikelsgea. Nachts hearde men soms dat it kistehout forsteapele waerd. Dan kaem der gau in deade. Men koe oan it forsteapeljen hearre oft men swier of licht hout brûke soe. En dat kaem ek stéfêst út. Gie men der hinne, dan wie der neat to sjen of to hearren.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130681,"r":"BIJLSMA007902","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A calf tied to a certain staple in the roof beams will die.","i":"T.B.","o":"Beppe fan memmekant kaem út de Wâlde (Nijegea H.O.). Dêr wie in pleats, dêr siet in kram yn it bynt. As men oan dy kram in keal fêstsette, dan stoar it bist.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130684,"r":"BIJLSMA008002","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman dreams of details of the funerals of her husband and son, which then happen in reality.","i":"T.B.","o":"De frou har suster hat ris dreamd dat hja op 'e Grinzer piip to Ljouwert roun. It wie allegear minsken en hja moast ek mei. In skoftsje letter stoar har man, en hja gongen mei de bigraffenis oer de Grinzer piip.\nDoe 't har soan noch soun en goed wie, seach hja yn de dream lju yn it wyt (hja wiene roomsk) en guon yn it swart. In skoftsje letter stoar har soan, en hja bilibbe yn werklikheit hwat hja yn de dream sjoen hie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":18107,"r":"CJ011429","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One evening a woman predicted that she would be taken that night, because the magpies were cackling in front of her house. The next morning she lay dead in bed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De jouns flak foardat âlde Anne (hjir yn Hurdegaryp) stoar, skatteren de eksters hiel bot by har hûs. \nDoe sei se: \"Ik wurd fannacht helle.\" En dat is ek gebeurd. De oare moarns lei se dea op bêd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19855,"r":"CJ015404","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man hears a sound coming from the canal. When he goes to look, there is nothing to be seen. Later someone drowns in the same canal. The sound was a portent of the drowning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanheit wenne op Oerterperfallaet. Hy hearde us in kear in lûd dat út 'e feart wei kom. Hy gong der hinne, mar der wie neat to sjen. In skoft letter is dêr ien fordronken. Dat lûd hat de foarboade west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19878,"r":"CJ015508","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If the clock strikes wrongly and the dogs start howling eerily, a death is coming. Both are omens.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de klok raer let, komt der mei gauwens ien op 't hôf. Dat is ek it gefal, as der in houn bigjint to spûkgûlen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19884,"r":"CJ015514","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man foresees that someone will drown in the pond. It is someone wearing a red skirt, the man says. Later a boy with red hair drowns in the pond.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir achter is in poel, dêr mat ien yn forsûpe. Skoanheit hat it sjoen, dat is al wit hoe lang lyn. It mat ien wêze mei in reade rôk oan. \nNoch net sa lang lyn is der flakby ien yn in sleat forsûpt. Dat wie in soan fan Tije Alma. Dy hie read hier.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19885,"r":"CJ015515","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man has cancer and is dying. On his deathbed he is startled by knocking on the window: 'death', says a voice. A little later the man is dead.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Skoanheit lei mei kanker op bêd. Hy wie o sa siik. It roan om 't lêste. Doe kloppe der ien bûten op 't glês. Dy sei: \"De dood.\"\nDoe't se nei bûten gongen om to sjen, wie der net ien. Even letter wie skoanheit wei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19901,"r":"CJ015611","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog starts howling eerily, the death of a Jew is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt, seit men, dan leit der in joad op stjerren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19918,"r":"CJ015703","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, a death will come within three days.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt is der binnen trije dagen yn dy buert in deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19975,"r":"CJ016105","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If the magpies chatter in front of your house, someone will die. Also if a dog starts howling eerily, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters tichte by in hûs skatterje of by de doar komme, dan stjert der ien yn dat hûs.\nJan en Diuw hienen in hountsje, dat hat no in kear hiel bot oan it spoekgûlen west mei de kop nei it hûs fan syn buorman ta. Sy jagen dat hountsje dêr wei, sy ha it beest slein, mar it wie dêr fuort wer en dan bigong it opnij wer to spoekgûlen. Yn 'e nacht is de soan fan 'e buorman stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19976,"r":"CJ016106","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If the bell tolls the death knell, a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de klok sa deadsk oan 't lieden is, komt der in sterfgefal. Dat is foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19998,"r":"CJ016206","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The mother of a little boy hears the dog howling eerily. The dog then goes and stands with its face to the wall. Fourteen days later the child dies; the little coffin stands against the wall.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Sweagerbosk wie in húshâlding, dêr wie de mem allinne thús mei 't jonkje. Doe bigong har houn bûtendoar to spûkgûlen. Hy roan hyltyd mar achterút, al gûlendewei en sa ta 't hûs yn oan 'e fjûrpot ta. Dêr bleau er stean mei 't gesicht nei de muorre ta.\nFjirtsjin dagen letter kom 't jonkje to forstjerren. Syn kiste kom to stean tsjin 'e muorre oan op it plak, dêr't de houn sa nei sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19999,"r":"CJ016207","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The chattering of magpies is a harbinger of death.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":20000,"r":"CJ016208","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a swallow taps on the window, a death follows within three days. The narrator illustrates this with the death of a baby.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As it sweltsje tsjin 'e glêzen tikket, komt der mei trije dagen in deaden.\nOp it Wyldpaed gebeurde it, dat in lyts popke wosken en klaeid woarde. De mem lei noch yn 't kreambêd. It iene buorwyfke sei: \"Der tikket trije kear in sweltsje op 'e glêzen. Dat bitsjut dat der yn 't koart in sterfgefal wêze sil.\"\nTrije dagen letter wie 't berntsje wei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20001,"r":"CJ016209","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People speak of a 'doodskloppertje' (little death knocker) behind the wallpaper, also called a 'wekker' (alarm clock) or a 'wild horloge' (wild watch). When people hear that sound, it means a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in deatikkerke achter 't bihang is, seit men wol: der is in fremde wekker yn 'e hûs. Ek wol: in wyld horloazje. Dan komt der in deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20002,"r":"CJ016210","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a bell tolls as it does at a funeral, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de klok sadanich let krekt as op in bigraffenis, dan stjert der ek ien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20038,"r":"CJ016414","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Doodstikkertjes (little death tickers) are spiders behind the wallpaper. When they start ticking, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Deatikkerkes dat binne spinnen achter 't bihang. As sa'n spin bigjint to tikjen, dan komt der in deaden-ien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20039,"r":"CJ016415","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If three drops of blood fall from someone's nose, he will soon die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As ien trije drippen bloed út 'e noas falle, dan giet er ek grif gau dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20040,"r":"CJ016416","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"An old woman's skirt catches fire. She becomes very frightened because she knows it is an omen of an impending death. The woman does indeed die. (The recorder wonders whether this might have something to do with 'purgatory'.)","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us beppe stie yn 't achterhûs. Mem seach, dat har rok yn 'e brân stie. (yn werklikheit wie 't sa net) Soks bitsjutte dat der in deaden kom. Doe't se 't tsjin beppe sei, rôp dy: \"O heden, dat is net bêst, dat bitsjut in sterfgefal!\" Beppe hat noch even leefd, doe is se stoarn.\n(slacht dit op it fagefjûr?)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20090,"r":"CJ016803","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man is in poor health and one day foresees that within half a year he will be taken to the churchyard on the hearse. His son consults the doctor, who predicts that the father will die within two weeks. Fourteen days later the son, a clay worker, does indeed receive a telegram saying his father is on his deathbed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ús heit (Thomas Bruining) stoar, wied er ien en fyftich jier. Hy hie de hjerstmis nei Dútslân ta west. (seizoenwurk) Dêr kaem er siik wer wei. It hiele winterskoft sukkele er.\nOp in kear sieten wy by de itenstafel. 't Wie yn 'e Houtigehage. Heit sei: \"Ik mat der even út.\" Hy lei de furke del. Hy kaem fuort net werom. Us mem (Thomas Klare) rôp: \"Hwer bliuwste?\" Doe sei er: \"Sy ha my op 'e wein. Sy bringe my nei 't tsjerkhôf. Ik kin ten heechste noch in healjier leve. Dan is 't gebeurd.\"\nDe maitiids moest ik in fjirtsjin dagen nei Grinslân ta nei de bou. Ik frege dokter: \"Hoe is it mei heit?\" Hy sei: \"Jouw vader kan ten hoogste nog veertien dagen leven.\"\nDoe bigong ik to gûlen, hwant ik moest fuort nei de klaei om hwat to fortsjinjen. Ik hie folle leaver thús bliuwe wold.\nHeit seach dat ik skriemde, mar hy wist net dat ik mei dokter praet hie. Hy sei: \"Hja sil de tiding wol krigen ha.\"\nIk rekke nei Kloosterburen (Gr.) ta to wjudden. Nei fjirtsjin dagen kom der in tillegram: vader stervende.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20241,"r":"CJ018002","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman has a seriously ill mother. One time the daughter hears people outside bumping a coffin against the wall. She suspects her mother's death is imminent. When the mother does die, the daughter warns the pallbearers not to bump the coffin against the wall. It happens anyway. It had been an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Albertsje hat hjir njonken ús wenne. Har mem rekke siik. Doe't se al min wie, hearde Albertsje op in kear dat der guon mei de kiste by harren tsjin 'e muorre oan stompten. Sy hie fuort yn 'e gaten, dat dit de kiste wie fan har mem.\nDoe't har mem in wike letter wei rekke, sei se tsjin 'e buorren: \"Wolle jim der wol goed om tinke, dat jimme net mei de kiste tsjin 'e muorre oan stompe?\" Mar it gebeurde wol. Hja hearde krekt itselde lûd as de wyks tofoaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20300,"r":"CJ018215","p":"Burum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a bird calls differently than usual, a death is imminent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wanneer een fogel anders roept as gewoon betekent dat dat der een sal stervn, seiden se froeger.","l":"Fries"},{"n":20355,"r":"CJ018611","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a barn owl calls on the owl board, a death in the neighbourhood is imminent. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in katûl rôp op 't ûleboerd koe men der mar fêst fan op oan dat der in deaden kom, itsij yn datselde hûs of yn in hûs dêr tichteby. Dat gong altyd troch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20494,"r":"CJ019609","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If magpies chatter at night, a death is imminent. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der yn 'e nacht eksters op 'e naed fan 't hûs omskatterje, dan komt der yn dat hûs gauachtich in deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20603,"r":"CJ020401","p":"Tzummarum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One evening a young man heard a splash in the water behind the flax-breaking sheds. A few days later a neighbour drowned at exactly that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie sahwat tweintich jier. Wy wennen in eintsje bûten it doarp. Ik moast om thús to kommen in reedtsje del, foar hokken lâns, dêr't se wol yn braekten. Op in joun kaem ik thús. Doe't ik oan ien fan 'e braekhokken ta wie, hearde ik in plof yn it wetter dêr achter.\nIn pear dagen letter is op krekt datselde plak in buorman fan ús - Jil - dêr de moarns om in ûre of fiif hinne, fordronken. Hy wie de moarns yn it hok oan 't braekjen. Hy wie doe sahwat tritich jier.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20643,"r":"CJ020524","p":"Tzummarum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If the clock stops, it is an omen that someone will soon die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem sei froeger wol, as de klok lette: \"Hè hwat liet dy klok wer mâl. Wy ha gau wer in deaden.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20819,"r":"CJ021601","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If you heard hammering at the carpenter's at night, another death would soon follow. A coffin was being made then.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Soms hearde men yn 'e nacht timmerjen by de timmerman. Dan kaem der gau wer in sterfgefal. Hwant der waerd oan in deadskiste timmere.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20897,"r":"CJ021907","p":"Sweagerbosk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Dogs often howl eerily beforehand when a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hounen spoekgûle faek fan tofoaren as der in sterfgefal komt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20913,"r":"CJ022009a","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One summer evening a man was sitting on the little bridge in front of his house. He saw a funeral procession approaching, but just before it reached him, he could no longer see it. A moment later he saw the procession again, and it had already passed the bridge. A few days later the maid died. That was why the man had seen the funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn heit fortelde us: \"Op in kear siet ik op 't bartsje by hûs. 't Wie al let op 'e joun en yn 'e simmer. Doe seach ik, dat der noch hwat oankom. 't Wie in hiele rige, yn 't swart, en sy roannen stadich. Mar doe't se tichterby kommen, seach ik se net mear.\nMar in skoftsje letter seach ik se wèr, doe wienen se it bartsje al in moai eintsje foarby.\"\nIn pear dagen letter is dêr in faem forstoarn. Dêr hied er de lykstaesje fan sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20950,"r":"CJ022403","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man could not pass a house because he saw a funeral procession standing there. The woman of the house asked him whether it was her son who would die. But the man had not been able to see who was in the hearse. A week later the son died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Paulus fan Albert en Tet (Alma) wie in jonge fan achttsjin jier. Hy hie harsensykte en it like slim. Op in joun soe âlde Hindrik Vaartstra der noch op út. Doe't er oan 'e daem fan it hûs fan Albert en Tet ta wie, koed er net fierder. Dêr stie in lykstaesje. Hy seach de wein mei de kiste en 't folk. Doe is er weromgong.\nIn wike letter is Paulus stoarn.\nTet hearde der fan, dat âlde Hindrik dêr by harren in lykstaesje sjoen hie. Doe is hja nei Hindrik ta gong omt se bang wie dat se har jonge misse moest.\nMar Hindrik sei, hy hie net útmeitsje kind, hwa't der stoarn wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21017,"r":"CJ023104","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The bakers of Himrik knew beforehand when someone was going to die, because then the cake boards were thrown about at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der ien stjerre soe, wisten de bakkers yn 'e Himrik dat al fan to foaren. Hwant dan waerd der nachts by har yn 'e bakkerij mei de koekeplanken smiten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21018,"r":"CJ023105","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When the dogs howl eerily, someone will die.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":21038,"r":"CJ023311","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A married couple heard beforehand the wailing of their child in its death throes. Because of this they knew they would lose the child.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Terwispel wennen Jan Hakse en syn frou. Dy forlearen in bern. Fan to foaren hienen se it jeuzeljen fan it bern al heard, doe't it yn 'e deastriid wie. Sy wisten dus fan tofoaren al dat se it misse moesten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21041,"r":"CJ023403","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In a neighbourhood people once heard a voice. Not long afterwards a child drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha wenne oan 'e Mâllewyk to Bakkefean. Dêr is us in bern fan in jier of fiif, seis yn fordronken. Fan to foaren ha se dêr in stem yn dy wyk heard. Doe wisten se dat der ien yn fordrinke soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21080,"r":"CJ023916","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"On his way back from his girlfriend, a young man saw a funeral procession pass. A few days later old Meike died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sytse Wybenga kom yn 'e nacht us in kear by Manus Ael wei. Ael dat wie syn faem. 't Is nou sahwat in sauntich jier lyn. Doe seach er in hiele rige folk lâns kommen. Hy gong oan kant. It wie in lykstaesje.\nFuort dêrnei stoar âlde Meike. Dêr hie Sytse de lykstaesje fan sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21082,"r":"CJ023918","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A mother already knows beforehand that her little child will soon die; she has heard knocking.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha in berntsje forlern. Yn 'e nacht moest ik Antsje der útklopje. In wike foartiid hie Antsje al sein: \"Hja hâlde dat jonkje net. Ik ha 't klopjen al heard.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21091,"r":"CJ024004","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In Westereinde there once lived a man who was born with a caul. Sometimes someone knocked on his window and then he went outside. When he came back in, he said that soon there would be another death. Outside he had seen the whole funeral: a farm wagon with a coffin and lots of people following it. It always came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger wenne der yn 'e Westerein yn Garyp, yn it hûs dêr't Taeke Wagenaar wenne hat, in man, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Der woarde soms by him op it rút kloppe. Dan gong dy man der út en hy frege ek net hwat it wie. Even letter kom er wer yn 'e hûs. Dan sei er: \n\"Wy krije binnenkoart ek wer in deaden yn Garyp.\"\n\"O ja?\" sei syn wiif.\n\"Ja,\" sei er, \"ik ha de hiele bigraffenis sjoen: de boerewein mei de kiste en alle folk der achteroan. Dat kom altyd út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21097,"r":"CJ024101","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Once magpies were chattering behind an old woman's house. The woman believed this meant someone would soon die, which did indeed happen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Houtigehage wenne in âld-minske: Akke Stoarm. Der wienen us in kear eksters by har achter hûs oan 't skatterjen. Doe sei se: \"O heden, nou komt der gau in deaden yn 'e buert.\" Hja krige gelyk. Binnen trije dagen stoar der ien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21129,"r":"CJ024401","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man had seen his wife's entire funeral beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oebele Wagenaar hat njonken ús wenne. Syn earste frou forstoar yn novimber 1918 oan 'e Spaense gryp.\nHy fortelde ús: \"Ik ha de hiele bigraffenis mei alles hwat der achter roan klear fan tofoaren sjoen. It folk kom by my út 'e hûs wei.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21141,"r":"CJ024413","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, someone will soon die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"\"As ik in houn spûkgûlen hear,\" seit myn wiif, \"dan tink ik: - Hwa sil 't nou wêze? -\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21177,"r":"CJ024608","p":"Waskemeer","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man once saw a woman who had died in childbirth being laid out in his house. After that he no longer wanted to live in that house. Other people came to live there. Not long afterwards the woman died during childbirth. The previous occupant had already seen it beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Bakkefean wenne in man yn in hûs, dy seach op in nacht dat der yn dat hûs in kreamfrou biklaeid woarde. Doe woe hy der net langer yn wenje. Der kommen oare lju yn to wenjen. Dy wienen noch net iens sa lang yn dat hûs, as de frou stoar yn 'e kream. De foarige biwenner hie dat krekt sa fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21201,"r":"CJ024803","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A young woman was coming back from dancing when she saw two undertakers. She did not hear their footsteps in the snow: they were floating. Later an old woman from the neighbourhood died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us Hinke kom us op in kear mei in dochter fan Bouke Poppinga thús fan it dânsjen yn Drachten. Sy fytsten oer de Houtigehage en Boelensloane.\nDoe moest Hinke allinnich de fjouwer Roeden noch del. 't Wie yn 'e winter en der lei snie. Hinke wie goed twintich jier. Doe't se al tichte by ús hûs wie, seach se ynienen twa bigraffenismannen foar har op. Sy seagen der út as dragers. Sy hienen lange swarte jassen oan en hege huodden op.\nHinke bleau achter har. Sy koe dy mannen net gean hearre, hwant dêr ha wy har nei frege. Sy matte sweefd ha, hwant it wie froastich waer en dan kreaket de snie ûnder 't stappen.\nKrekt foardat Hinke thús wie, sloegen de beiden it sydweike yn nei lofts dat op 'e Lange Wyk útkomt.\nLetter wie der in âlde frou op 'e Lange Wyk wei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21289,"r":"CJ025504","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In Strobos they say that if a watch ticks wildly, someone will soon die. The same happens if a dog howls eerily, if the pigeons make a racket around the house, and if black jackdaws fly around the tower.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in wyld horloazje tikket, komt der gau in sterfgefal, sizze se yn Strobos.\nAs in houn spûkgûlet ek. (Strobos - Kollum)\nAs de skierroeken om 't hûs hinne heisterje ek.\nAs de swarte kaën om 'e toer fleane, ek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21290,"r":"CJ025505","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man was on his way from Strobos to his parents in Dokkum. His father was in a very bad way. On the way jackdaws flew over his head calling 'kaah-kaah'. Someone asked him what that meant, and he said they were calling 'too late, too late'. They were telling him he would reach his father too late. And indeed his father had already died when he arrived in Dokkum.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik roan fan Strobos nei Dokkum ta, dêr't myn âlden wennen. Heit wie tige min.\nUnderweis wienen der hyltyd kaën boppe myn holle. Dan wienen se wer achter my, dan fleagen se wer oer my hinne.\nAs se dan foar my wienen, kearden se har om en seinen: \"Kaah-kaah- \"\nDan sei ik: \"Te laat - \"\nDoe kom der ien njonken my to rinnen.\nDy frege: \"Hwat bitsjut dit?\"\nIk sei: \"Sy bringe my it boadskip, dat ik to let kom.\"\nEn it kom èk sa út. Ik kom to let yn Dokkum oan. Heit wie al wei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21360,"r":"CJ026201","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A pregnant girl once heard the bells ringing while she was working. Another girl heard nothing. She said that the ringing of the bells meant she would die in childbirth. And that is what happened. The little daughter she bore survived, but she in turn died in childbirth.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Janke fan Romke-om (Romke Skyt) en Trynmoai tsjinne yn Drachten. Hja rekke dêr yn forwachting. Hja moest in bern ha fan in joad Van Leer út 'e Hounestege.\nOp in middei wienen Mart en hja op it lân oan 't jirpelsykjen. Doe sei se: \"Hark, dêr liede de klokken al.\"\n\"De klokken?\" sei Mart, \"ik hear neat.\"\n\"Ja,\" sei se, \"de klokken. Dy liede al dat se my strak nei 't tsjerkhôf bringe.\"\n't Is ek sa gebeurd. Hja is yn 'e kream stoarn. Hja hat it fantofoaren witen. Har dochterke bleau yn leven, mar dy is letter ek wer yn 'e kream stoarn.\nDe deis foar de bifalling kaem Janke noch by Romke-om syn mem, dat wie èk in Janke. Dêr wie se nei neamd. Dy sei doe tsjin har: \"As alles yn oarder is, mast hjir mar gauris mei de poppe komme.\"\n\"Né,\" sei Janke doe mei klam, \"dat bilove wy net.\"\nDe oare deis rekke se wei. Sy wenne yn Sumarreheide.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21384,"r":"CJ026402","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman sometimes saw funeral processions. Once she saw her own husband dressed in black walking back and forth through the church. A week later the niece died, and the man did indeed walk through the church like that.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn suster op 'e Harste yn Sumar hat yndertiid alhiel ûnforwacht in famke fan trettsjin jier forlern.\nUs mem seach nachts wol gau us bigraffenisstoeten en sa. Sa seach se de wyks foardat it famke stoar yn 'e nacht ús heit alhiel yn 't swart by de Sumarre tsjerke hinne en wer kuijerjen.\nIt kom krekt sa út. Doe't it famke forstoarn is - in wike letter - hat ús heit de bigraffenis ôfwachte en roan er by de tsjerke hinne en wer. (It wie it âldste famke fan myn swager Harm Theunissen, dat doe stoarn wie)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21409,"r":"CJ026609","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman once predicted at an acquaintance's house that there would soon be a death because the clock was running wrong.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tseard Boomsma syn mem kom us by ús en doe sei se tsjin ús mem: \"Hè, hwat let dy klok hwer raer. Der komt wer in sterfgefal.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21410,"r":"CJ026610","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In the old days people were afraid when magpies came to the door, because that meant a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der eksters by de doar kommen wienen de minsken froeger bang. Hwant dat bitsjutte in deade.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21434,"r":"CJ026701","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One evening a woman saw a funeral procession pass by. Her daughter saw nothing. A few days later someone in the village died and the funeral procession really did pass by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw in dochter wenjen yn Westergeast. Dêr wie ik us. Doe gongen ik en myn dochter togearre dêr op stap nei it café, dêr't de heit en de broer fan myn skoanmem wennen. Doe't wy dêr in skoft sitten hienen wie 't al aerdich let, sahwat alve ûre. Doe soenen wy dan mar wer fuort. Myn dochter sei: \"Mem mat my mar yn 'e earm nimme, hwant it is nochal hwat glêd.\" Doe't wy in eintsje it tsjerkhôf foarby wienen, sei ik: \"Ho, even oan kant.\" Wy bleauwen stean, doe't wy oan 'e kant wienen.\n\"Hwat is der, mem?\" frege myn dochter.\nIk sei: \"Kom nou mar wer mei op 'e wei. Dêr wie in lykstaesje. It wie net sa'n greaten-ien, der roan mar in bytsje folk achteroan.\nDoe sei myn dochter: \"Der is optheden net ien siik yn Westergeast. Ik soe noait wite, hwa't dat wêze moest.\" Mar wy wienen de tsjerke foarby roan, doe't ús dy lykstaesje tsjinkom. It moest dus ien fan bûten it doarp wêze.\nTwa dagen letter kom de broer fan myn skoansoan, Folkert, by ús. \"Us âld buorwyfke is fannacht hastich forstoarn\", sei er.\nIk sei tsjin myn dochter: \"Dêr hast it al.\"\nIn pear dagen letter woarde de bigraffenis hâlden.\nDer roannen mar in bytsje minsken achter it lyk oan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21440,"r":"CJ026707","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman could always tell from the ringing of the bell that someone else was going to die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik yn Westergeast wenne, hearde ik dêr altyd dúdlik de klok lieden. Dan wist ik altyd krekt as der wer ien stjerre soe. Dat hearde ik oan it lieden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21472,"r":"CJ026908","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One evening a dog howled eerily towards the box bed. There was nothing wrong with the child. But a week later it was dead.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It spoekgûlen fan in houn hat bitsjutting. Ik ha hjir neist wenne, doe't dit hûs hjir noch net stie. Yn 'e nacht lei de houn ûnder 'e tafel. En dy bigoun dêr to spûkgûlen. En wylst seach er mar nei 't bêdsté, dêr in bern fan uzes yn lei. It bern skeelde doe noch neat. Mar in wike letter wie 't dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21547,"r":"CJ027011","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A newborn baby made very strange noises. Suddenly the people in the house heard a strange bang. The next day the baby died. When the little coffin was carried out of the house, they heard the same sound as before. It had been an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ien fan ús dochters wennet op Koatstertille. Sy krige in poppe en myn wiif rekke der hinne op bisite. De baekster wie der ek noch. De poppe lei boven. Dy wie siik. Dy wie lang net goed. It bern joech hiele rare lûden, it doochde lang net.\nMyn wiif sei: \"Dêr skilt hwat oan. Ik mei net oer sokke lûden.\"\nDoe hearden se ynienen in eigenaerdige slach, krekt in gong-slach. Dat klonk lang nei. Sy hearden it allegear.\nDe oare deis stoar de poppe. Doe't it yn it kistje út 'e hûs droegen woarde, wie krekt datselde lûd der wer. Dat hat foartsjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21582,"r":"CJ027311","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman knew in advance that someone would die. She often heard it. People always die in a triangle. If someone dies here, then one there, then someone in the third corner dies too.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Fleden winter doe't ik yn Westergeast wie by myn dochter, haw ik dêr in skoftsje ûnwennich west. Ik woarde dêr bang en op in nacht soe ik fuortrinne.\n\"Hwerom is mem bang?\" frege myn dochter.\nIk sei: \"Hjir komt in deaden op dit streekje.\"\n\"Hjir is ien siik, dy sil 't dan wol wêze\", sei Jitske, myn dochter. En dat wie ek sa, dat kom út. Har buorwyfke stoar. It minske wie o sa hastich.\nOp in kear sei se tsjin my: \"Ik bin sa forkâlden.\" Mar ik hearde it wol. It wie in freeslike hoarst dy't se hie. Ik sei: \"Gean nei hûs, gau, en lit dokter komme.\" Mar 6 wiken letter wie se dea.\nDer stoaren nòch twa, dêr hie 'k ek weet fan.\nDe minsken stjerre altyd yn in trijehoeke.\nAs hjir ien stjert, dan dêr ien, en dan dêr ek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21584,"r":"CJ027313","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Whenever the bells rang, a man always said that in three days someone else would go to the churchyard. It always came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha dat fan mem har heit. Dy wie ek sa.\nWy wennen flak by 't tsjerkhôf yn 'e Falom. As de klokken letten, dan sei er: \"Hark\".\n\"Hwat is der, pake?\" fregen we.\n\"Binnen trije dagen komt der wer in deaden op 't tsjerkhôf\", sei er. En dat gong altyd troch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21590,"r":"CJ027405","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Three horsemen once chased an old woman's sheep. One of them laughed at the woman when she got angry about it. She told him he would not come home that evening. That same evening he had a fatal accident.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Falom wenne in âld wyfke oan 'e loane. Hja hy bûten in skiepke rinnen. Doe kommen der trije ruters oan op hynders. Dy jagen dat skiepke fuort. 't Ald wyfke kom ta de doar út en wie lulk. Mar ien fan 'e jonge mannen lake har út, en rôp: \"Hwat kin ús sa'n âld wiif skele!\"\nMar doe sei 't wyfke tsjin him: \"Dû komst joun net wer thús.\"\nHy is dyselde jouns forûngelokke op 'e reed dy't nei 't oasten giet en op 'e Fallomsterfeart útkomt.\nDit is echt gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21597,"r":"CJ027412","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, someone will die.\n\nA dog always howled on the evening before someone was taken to the churchyard. People found this so unpleasant that they sold it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn deads spûkgûlt, giet der ien dea. Dat giet altyd troch. Koartlyn is 't hjir noch gebeurd. Mar de houn mat dan echt spûkgûle.\nYn Westergeast wennet myn dochter. De buorlju dêr hienen in houn. As der ien op 't hôf kom, gûlde dy houn altyd de jouns fan tofoaren.\nDêr hienen de lju sa'n hekel oan, dat sy ha him forkocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21603,"r":"CJ027418","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a mirror falls, there will be a death. If the mirror does not break, someone far away will die. If the mirror does break, someone nearby will die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in spegel delkomt, dan komt der in sterfgefal. Dat giet altyd troch. It is faker as ien kear by ús gebeurd. As de spegel net stikken is, dan is 't fier fan jin ôf. As er stikken is, dan tichteby.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21604,"r":"CJ027419","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If three drops of blood fall from someone's nose, he will die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der ien trije drippen bloed út 'e noas falle, dan giet er dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21609,"r":"CJ027505","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One evening a couple hears an old woman wailing, but there is no one to be seen. Not long afterwards three boys fall through the ice. When the grandmother of one of them watched the bodies being taken out of the water, she wailed just as the couple had heard earlier.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It sil sa'n sechstich jier lyn wêze. Ik hie nei de faem ta west. Sy brocht my in eintsje fuort. Ik sei: \"Halt, hwat is dat?\"\nWy hearden beide tagelyk in gejammer: Ooh... ooh...\nIt like op 'e stem fan in âld minske. Mar der wie net in minske yn 'e wide omtrek. 't Wie hjir yn 'e Westerein. \"Hjir gebeurt hwat\", seinen we.\nTichteby wie in petgat. Dêr binne in skoftsje letter trije jonges yn forsûpt. Sy binne dêr troch 't iis sakke. Dêr wie in de Bruin by en in Schaafsma. 't Wie op in middei. Ik ha sjoen dat se se der úthelle ha.\nDoe wie der in âld minske, dat wie de beppe fan ien fan dy bern, dy jammere hiel bot. Ooh... Ooh... sei se mar, krektlyk, sa't wy it dy nachts heard hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21672,"r":"CJ028014","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman sees a hearse standing at her neighbours' door. A week later the neighbour dies and the hearse stands in the same place. It was a voorgezicht (a vision foreshadowing an event).","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn suster yn Twizelerheide kom op in jountiid thús doe stie der in lykwein by har buorlju by de homeije. Even letter ried er fuort.\nHja tocht: dat wol 'k ûnthalde. Ik wol wite foar hwa't dat is.\nIn wike letter is har buorman forstoarn. Doe stie de lykwein op itselde plak.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21703,"r":"CJ028206","p":"Houten","v":"Utr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A mother hears noises at night as if someone is falling into the water. She is very afraid that this is an omen of a death by drowning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wij woonden in Asschat. Mijn oudste zuster was toen nog een klein kind, zo lang is het al geleden. Zij was toen nog de enigste. Daar in Asschat hadden wij toen een sloot voor het huis met een dam.\nOp een nacht hoort moeder een geflodder in de sloot, net alsof er een in viel.\nToen moest die sloot onmiddellijk dichtgemaakt worden, want moeder was doodsbenauwd dat het meisje zou verdrinken."},{"n":21707,"r":"CJ028210","p":"Houten","v":"Utr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The dog of a man who is mortally ill howls incessantly for an evening and a night. The next day the man dies. The dog sensed the death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tegen ons over heeft een man gewoond, die zwaar ziek was. De avond en nacht voordat hij stierf heeft de hond aan één stuk door vreeslijk gehuild. En anders hoorde je het beest nooit. De volgende dag was Jan dood."},{"n":21743,"r":"CJ028503","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Someone foresees that during the building of the church someone will fall from the tower. It really did happen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Wytgaerd foel ien fan 'e toer, wylst de tsjerke boud woarde. Ien seach dat fantofoaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21829,"r":"CJ028803","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A skipper hears wailing coming from the water. A week later a cattle dealer's son drowns and the same sounds can be heard. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ien fan Burdaerd reizge mei 't trekskip nei syn wurk ta. Op in kear hearde hy achter him in freeslik gejammer. Mar der wie neat to sjen. Mar in wike letter rekke de soan fan in fékoopman by 't skip del en fordronk. Doe hearde er krekt deselde lûden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21984,"r":"CJ031105","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dead girl lies in her coffin with a smile on her lips. A rag dealer suspects, given the girl's joy, that another death is approaching. A week later another man does indeed die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't myn suster sauntjin jier wie kaem se to forstjerren. Sy lei o sa moai yn 'e kiste. Hja hie in glimk om 'e mûle. 't Wie och sa'n beeld fan in faem.\nDer kaem in lapkekoopman út Dokkum by ús. Dy kaem altyd geregeld. Hy frege heit of er myn suster wol sjen mocht.\nHeit naem him mei nei har ta en hy hat in prachtich gebet foar har útsprutsen. Hy hie der earst om frege of dat wol mocht.\nDoe sei er: \"Der komt binnenkoart in sippe deaden, hwant sy glimket. Dan is sy blij.\"\nHeit syn broer hie kanker. Koarte tiid dêrnei is er stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21986,"r":"CJ031107","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a mirror falls down, someone will die within six weeks.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in spegel delkomt, komt der binnen seis wiken in sippe deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21987,"r":"CJ031108","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman who has just buried her husband suddenly hears a loud bang. When she sees that the mirror has fallen down, she suspects there will be another death within six weeks. Exactly six weeks later a woman does indeed die in childbirth.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn man syn heit kaem to forstjerren. 'k Wie op 'e bigraffenis. Doe't wy fan 't hôf werom wienen, hearden wy in hiele plof. Krekt as wie der in rút ynsmiten of in buordtsje út 'e diggelkast del kaem.\nMar doe't wy seagen, wie it de spegel, dy't oer de kachel hinne fallen wie. Hy lei yn alle diggels op 'e groun.\nIk sei: \"Nou komt der in sippe deaden yn seis wiken.\"\nMar der wie net ien siken yn 'e famylje.\nUs Jinke moest in poppe ha. Sy stoar yn 'e kream.\nIt bern bleau bihâlden. 't Wie krekt seis wiken letter.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22000,"r":"CJ031206","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man is startled at night by a knock on the window. When he goes to look with his dog, the animal creeps away in mortal fear. Later a man dies. The knock on the window was a portent of the approaching death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear waerd der op it gleske slein oan 'e sydkant. 't Wie yn 'e nacht. Albert gong mei de houn der út. 't Wie in forskuorrende houn, dy't altyd fuort tahapte. Elkenien wie der bang foar. Hy wie wol sa great as dizze tafel.\nAlbert waerd neat gewaer, doe't er bûten kaem. Mar de houn wie sa binaud, dy krûpte Albert fan bangens tusken de skonken. Dat wie op it stuit, dat skoanheit stoar.\nHy hat dit oan Remmelts Minke forteld en dy sei: \"Jimme houn hat noch wòl hwat sjoen, mar dû hast neat sjoen.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27075,"r":"CJ063502","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man who fears drowning drowns on a skating trip. The dead man looks so lifelike that people fear they are burying someone only apparently dead.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e winter fan 1890 op '91 forgaderde de iisklub to Eastemar. Der woarde forteld, dat der al inkelde lju fordronken wienen.\nDe feint fan Bakker Bouwes, Auke Westra, dy't sekretaris wie fan 'e iisklub, foun dat ôfgryslik. Neat, sei er, griisde him sa bot oan as fordrinke.\nDe oare moarns rekke er mei syn forloofde yn in wek op 'e Burgumer Mar. Hy hat syn faem salang boppe wetter hâlden, oant der help opdaegjen kaem. Doe ha se har der útlutsen. Mar hysèls sonk wei en is jammerdearlik fordronken.\nMyn mem (de frou fan Master Wybenga), dy't op 'e begraffenis de foargong hie, sei, dat se noait moaijer deade sjoen hie. \"Hy like krekt of er noch libbe, en ik wie suver bang,\" sei se, \"dat wy in skyndeade nei it hôf brochten.\"\n(opmerking van A.A.J.: Er is me wel eens verteld, dat hij 's avonds voor zijn dood, toen hij hoorde van een verdrinking, krijtwit moet zijn geworden en gezegd moet hebben: \"O, o, as dat my mar net oerkomt!\")","l":""},{"n":33016,"r":"CJ085704","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If seven magpies sit at the front of a house, a death will come. If they sit behind the house, there will be a celebration.\nA man heard a magpie chattering, and when he came home his little goat was dead.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der sawn eksters op 'e foarstrjitte binne, komt der in deaden.\nBinne se op 'e achterstrjitte dan komt der in feest.\nIk kom de Wide Pet del, doe skattere der in ekster.\nIk sei: O heden, der is hwat thús.\nIk kom thús, doe wie ús geitsje dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33221,"r":"CJ088003","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If magpies come close to the back door, someone in that house will die within three days.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters ticht by de achterdoar komme is der binnen trije dagen in lyk yn dat hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":50244,"r":"GENDT222","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If you hear cries for help from the water, you must be careful and not go towards them, or you will drown. If the cries are heard before twelve o'clock an accident will soon happen; if heard after twelve it may take longer. This applies to all omens.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"As ’t woater dich zit mee ies en ge hört hulpgeroep, zie dan vurzichtig. Goa nie ’t ies op. Want dan verdrinkt er en. As ’t geroep vur twoalf uur gehörd wier, gebeurde ’t ongeluk gaauw. As ’t geluid na twoalf uur kwam, dat kos ’t nog lang dure vurda ’t ongeluk gebeurde. Da was zo bij alle vörtekens.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":50330,"r":"GENDT258","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"An owl calling, a dog howling and a magpie chattering are omens of a death.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Vörbedujsels ware bijvoorbeeld ’t geroep van ’n uil, ’t janke van ’n hond en ’t geschetter van ’n ekster. Dan kos ’r ’n onverwachtse dooie komme.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":50357,"r":"GENDT267","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man foresees that someone will have an accident and drown.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Kees had ok ’t ongeluk van Nöl Tunnisse al drie of vier wèke vöraf gezien. Hé’j zèj: “Doar bé’j de Woal gebeurt ’n ongeluk. Dor löp veul volk nor ’t turfschip* on de loswal. Mar ik weet nie, wie ’r verongelukt. Drie weke lotter gebeurde ’t ongeluk. Nöl Tunnisse was van ’t schip afgevalle. Er wèjde ’n flinke störm. Dordeur sloeg ’r ’n luuk af. Da kreeg Nöl tegen ’m on. En hé’j sloeg over boord en kwam op zien kop ien de slemp [modder] terech. De schipper zat ien de roef koffie te drinke en had ’r dus niks van gehörd of gezien. Mar de werkminse on de kant hadde ’n schraauw gehörd. Ze liepe nor ’t schip en ze riepe de schipper. Die zèj: “Ik weet nie precies, woar ie van ’t schip gevallen is. Durrum durf ik niet te duke”. - Lotter hebbe ze Tunnisse opgedregd. Kees had wer geliek gehad.\n\n* Turfschepen legden vroeger aan bij de steenfabrieken langs de Waal. De turf werd gebruikt bij ’t stoken in de steenovens.\nDit verhaal werd ook, natuurlijk anders, verteld door J. v.d. Brink, verslag 5 augustus 1965 (nr. 175).","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":209115,"r":"LINSSEN010905","p":"Roermond","v":"L.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Seeing an omen that a sister is ill or dead.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Het was 1921. Ik was onderwijzer met verplichte hoofdakte aan de openbare lagere school te Weert-Hushoven. We woonden een goede 20 min. ten Z. van de stad aan de weg naar Roermond (villatje \"de Trumpert\")\nMijn vrouw was geboren te Leiden. We hadden twee kinderen.\nOp een dag kwam ik ongeveer vijf uur in de namiddag thuis uit school en vond mijn vrouw totaal van streek. Op mijn vraag wat er gebeurd was antwoordde ze. \"O ons Marie, o ons Marie, ons Marie, (was een oudere zuster, die ook getrouwd was en te Doorn woonde. Er was een koele verhouding tussen de twee). Natuurlijk vroeg ik nadere uitleg en toen kreeg ik het volgende te horen. Deze namiddag om een uur of drie zat ik in de keuken te naaien aan tafel en opeens zag ik voor mij boven de tafel een rookwolkje, dat met een zachte plof, pf, uit elkaar spatte en zachtjes verdween. Ik dacht dadelijk aan ons Marie. In meer dan een jaar hebben we elkaar niet meer geschreven. Misschien is ze ziek of dood, ze is nooit sterk geweest.\nNatuurlijk stelde ik vrouwlief gerust, praatte van inbeelding en zinsbegoocheling, maar ze heeft altijd volgehouden dat gehoord en gezien te hebben.\nOverigens zus Marie bleek sukkelend te zijn en is, naar ik meen, binnen het jaar gestorven."},{"n":130072,"r":"VERHOEFF000704","p":"Apeldoorn","v":"Gld.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Men hear cries for help. Years later a canal has been dug, and at that spot boys drown in a hole in the ice. The men hear the same cries for help as before.","i":"L.V.","o":"Mijn vader en de buurman stonden met elkaar te praten, dat was in 1912. Het was donker en ineens komt er een verschrikkelijk gekerm en hulpgeroep uit de hei. Ze vliegen er op af, ze bukken zich en ze horen het geluid vlak voor zich. Ze kwamen net zo wit als een lijk de kamer binnen en vader zei: “Kinderen, denk erom, dat je daar niet komt, want daar gebeurt wat”. In 1918 stonden ze weer met elkaar te praten, er was toen daar een kanaal gegraven, daar waren ze druk op aan het schaatsenrijden en precies op die plek zijn er twee jongens in een wak gereden en verdronken en het was hetzelfde geschreeuw. Ik was toen soldaat in Apeldoorn en ik had het al eens aan mijn vrouw verteld, we waren toen nog verloofd, en toen kreeg ik een brief en daar stond in, dat het precies gebeurd was, zoals vader en de buurman hadden gehoord."},{"n":130074,"r":"VERHOEFF000706","p":"Apeldoorn","v":"Gld.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A prediction that someone will drown in the new canal within twenty-four hours comes true.","i":"L.V.","o":"We hadden er bij ons in het dorp ook een, Malle Abraham noemden ze die. Toen dat kanaal gegraven werd, toen stond hij zo te kijken en hij zei: “Mooi kanaal, maar binnen de vierentwintig uur eist het een slachtoffer”. Nou, die veenjongens, die gooiden hem natuurlijk met schoppen zand om zijn oren. Maar er kwam een ssoldaat met verlof en die zei: “Ik ga nog evem wat zwemmen”. Ze zeiden: “Doe dat nou niet, want het eten staat klaar”, maar ze konden hem gewoon niet tegenhouden, want het was zondagmorgen twaalf uur bijna en dan was die vierentwintig uur afgelopen, toen is hij toch gaan zwemmen, kreeg de kramp en verdronk."},{"n":130076,"r":"VERHOEFF000708","p":"Apeldoorn","v":"Gld.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man sees a funeral procession and a fire in advance.","i":"L.V.","o":"Mijn oudste broer was drieëntwintig jaar en als ze over dergelijke dingen praatten, dan lachtte hij maar eens en zei: “Ik wou, dat ik ook eens wat zag”. Hij hunkerde er gewoon naar om ook eens wat te zien. Hij kwam eens van zijn meisje vandaan, alles ging toen nog lopende, bij een huis kwam hij toen even in een heel fel licht, direct was het weer donker. Precies tien dagen later kwam hij daar weer langs en op hetzelfde punt kwam hem een lijkstatie tegen van een buurvrouw die werd begraven. Nou, toen had hij een voorproefje gehad want nog geen vier weken later, kwam hij weer van zijn meisje vandaan en zag het huis van mijn opoe in de brand: de koeien die loeiden en de varkens die gierden! Hij vloog over de sloten en greppels tot hij er vlak bij was en toen was alles ineens stil. Nog geen drie maanden later kwam hij er overdag langs en toen brandde het huis echt; er zijn toen heel wat varkens en koeien verbrand."},{"n":130078,"r":"VERHOEFF000710","p":"Apeldoorn","v":"Gld.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A coffin that rises from a farm, floats to the churchyard and bursts apart there is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the farmer's death a few weeks later.","i":"L.V.","o":"We stonden ook eens ’s avonds voor ons huis en dan kon je die grote boerderijen zo zien liggen. Er steeg uit zo’n boerderij een lijkkist de lucht in en zweefde heel kalm door de lucht heen tot boven het kerkhof en spatte daar uit elkaar. Nog geen veertien dagen later stierf die boer en werd op dat kerkhof begraven."},{"n":130084,"r":"VERHOEFF000801","p":"Dordrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Knocking on the door at night and seeing a funeral procession are a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"L.V.","o":"Een neef van me, aigelek mit een nicht van me getrouwd, die z’n zoons hoorde zat er snachs op de deur wier geklopt en toen ze ginge kijke zagge ze een begrafenis de laan oitgaan. Maar ze dorste ’t niet tege vader en moeder te zegge. Een paar dage later ginge ze koeie aflevere op ’t Grôot Hôofd (= een aanlegplaats) in Dordt en toen is die neef van me zo maar ineens dôodgebleve.","l":"Hoeksewaards"},{"n":130085,"r":"VERHOEFF000802","p":"Dordrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Owls screeching on the roof at night are a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"L.V.","o":"As -t-er een man of vrouw ging sterve, dan hoorde je snachs de uile op ’t dak schreeuwe.","l":"Hoeksewaards"},{"n":131953,"r":"VODA_033_08","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man born with a caul walks one night past a dangerous pool and foresees that an accident will happen there with a horse and cart carrying a bridal couple. The groom will drown in the pool. The man knows this young man and warns him not to marry, because something will happen to him. The young man marries anyway and the prediction of the man born with a caul comes true.\nOn the wedding day the couple go by horse and cart to the town hall. The horse bolts. The bride manages to jump from the cart in time, but the groom falls into the pool and drowns.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Men had det hal vrouger wollenmoal veurspeld [geblader]. \nEn nou kommen wie op ’t terrain van veurspellings. Mensen dea lange tied van teveuren wat können veurspellen. Zeej zaggen dat. ’n Soort spoukkieken. En eerlijk gezegd, dat mo je kunnen g’luiben, want dea det neet g’luiben kan, och, doa is ’t eigenlijk geen proatje veur weerd. Maar doar warden vrouger zoveel dingen verteld van zulke vertrouwbare mensen dat je dat wel eigenlijk aannemen mössen, dat eur veurste… veurspelling vertrouwbaar werden. Dee… dat waren mensen dea neet g’louben, dea niks hadden te [snekken?], dea neet veul jenever dronken of dea benauwd was’n, maar goude, eerlijke, fatsounlijke en lang geen domme luu, dea wat heurden of zag’n wat loater oetkwam.\nZo woonde ‘r vrouger ’n man in de Mussel en dea was met ’n helm geboren. En deze mensen dea heb voak ‘n heul meule glend. ‘k Weet al niet wat ’t recht is, maar zo wordt d’r dan toch van verteld. Zee loop ’s nacht veul bee de weg, umdet ze ’t op bedde neet oetholden könt. Zeej mout van det wereldgebeuren kennisnemen en det wordt heur bee nacht geopenboard. \nZo luip deze man op zekere nacht voorbie de gevoarlikke draijkolk hie in-e Mussel. Hij zag doar ’n ongeluk gebeuren met ’n verdekte woagen. De verdekte woagens doa [….] ze vrouger al mit. Det was ’n gewone boerenwoagen, doa kwaam ’n dek over en doa gungen zo overal mit hen. Doa zat’n van die beugels onder e","l":"Gronings"},{"n":131968,"r":"VODA_033_11","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man and his neighbour see a light and hear cries for help behind the house. Three years later two boys drown in the canal at that spot. The canal did not even exist yet when the man and his neighbour heard the cries; it still had to be dug.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Wee…eh..zal noe nog ierst effe vertellen den van dea jông dea doar verdronken is in ’t kanoal. Eh… det heat mien eigen voader heat det ‘heurd. Drei joar vandeveuren doa was ’t kanoal d’r nog nait. Hij steit achter ’t huus te kieken, zien buurman die komt d’r ook nog aan, en inains doe zagen ze doar ’n licht in [.?.]weg en d’ nog niks as: help, help, help!\nDrei joar noa tied doa verdrinken d’r twee jongens […?...] Zee hebben al meute doan um ze d’r uut te kriegen, moar det holp nait. Eh…mien voader dea heat det drei joar vanteveuren al ’heurd, dus det was ’n ding det gebeurde. Is niet zo?","l":"Gronings"},{"n":131973,"r":"VODA_033_16","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog that kept barking at the same spot foretold a funeral. The funeral procession passed exactly there. After that the dog was never heard barking again.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"En dan hadden ze ook wel es die veurloupen. Do..eh..nou ja, aine wil ‘r wat van waite, ’n anner nait, maar ik bin d’r zulf wel ’n bietje van overtuugd en ik was […?…] wat van, dat doar wal ens woarheid in zit. Want eh… hoendegehoel wollen verschadene mensen ook niks van waiten, maar ik zeg det nait of. Want ik was twintig joar en ik was ook neet bange juust, doe ging d’r geregeld ’n hoend pluminus tweehonderd meter van ons huus of zitten op ’n boerenloane te hoelen. En dat was wel al drei weken goande, doe zeg ik: “Ik wil es noa die hond tou. Woar d’r nou eigenlijk doa zit.” En ik bin noa die hond tou’goan en toen zat hij d’r inderdoad, te hoelen, mit dea kop in dea nekke en mit de eh… kop noar ’t oosten….noar d’eh… noorden hin. Doe zeg mien moeke: “Dat ut wat uut?” \nIk zeg: “Kon wel wezen,” ik zeg… Maar zie woelen waal zeggen as zie ’oendegehoel heurden den zol dat ’n liekstoatsie uuthangen, doa zol ’n liek langeskom’n. “Moar det ken oast naajt,” zeat’, “zol gen liek langeskom’n kennen, want det is moar ’n boerenloane.” Moar ôs buurman die was oal ens zaaik achter ons, woar det eerste lichie ofbraande, woar ’n boerderij verschenen was. En ôs buurman is ’storben, maar wie zeiden de… dat zel lijk goan, dia gait noe geen boereloane langes, die geit altied de publieke weg nog langes. Det was ook ‘n zandweg, maar toch ’n publieke weg, ‘n woaterschopweg was ‘t aiglik. Want ’ij is eh","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45713,"r":"WEV015402","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Fear of howling dogs and magpies pecking at the window.","i":"F.W.","o":"Jankende honnen, woor ook zoveul volk baange veur was, zeden mie niks. En eeksters, dei aan t roam pikten, ook nait.\nOllere mensn wazzen door doodsbenauwd veur.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45714,"r":"WEV015403","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A prediction that they will go to the churchyard with one dead person and come back with another comes true when someone dies during a funeral.","i":"F.W.","o":"Dei kameroad van mien voar mout ook n keer zegd hebben: “Zai goan mit aine noar t kerkhof en zai nemen ook weer aine mit.”\nDat leek ja hailemoal roar. Toch gebeurde t. Tiedens ain begraffenis sturf er ain op t kerkhof. En dei dode hebben ze weer mit terogge nomen.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45715,"r":"WEV015404","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A rhyme in which magpies bring joy, death and marriage.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wat dei eeksters aan gait, schut mie nou n riemseltje in t zin; t ludde zo:\n\"Een ekster brengt vreugde.\nTwee brengen de nood.\nDrie brengen een huwelijk.\nEn vier de dood.\"","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45788,"r":"WEV015601","p":"Veele","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Belief that animals such as cows, magpies and dogs can foresee things like fire and death.","i":"F.W.","o":"As ik vrouger as kind bie t heerdvuur zat en lusterde noar de verhoaln van de manlu, dan was k in t leste zo benauwd, dat ik nich meer noar boettn hen dus te pisn. En as k eevn noar dele mus, dan gung t schienvat mit. Kinder binnen eerder slim ploagd mit aal dai vertelsels over heksn en spookn. Man ja, de mensn leufden er aan. Doorum zal ik joe gain foabeltjes verteln, man allennig dingen, dai woar gebeurd binnen.\n Wie hadden dan bie ons in hoes n rode kou. Op n nacht was dat baist slim onrustig; hai trok man aan de ketns en bulkte in ain stuk deur. De andere koi-en stunnen gewoon op staal en deden gain biezunders. Wie dochden doadelk, dat door wat achter zat en zo was t. Ons hoes is n zet loater opbrand. Dai kou, dat kan nich anders, mout door kennis van had hebben. Want daiern waitn asmis dingen veuroet. Wordt op t oognblik wol twiefeld aan zukse dingen, man ik veur mie wait dat sekuur. k Heb meer dan ains zain, dat de eeksters aan t roam pikten bie n zaik mens. Dat was zeker n taikn, dat dai zaike er nich meer deur komen zol. t Kwam voak veur bie mensn, dai nogal wuist leefd harn. Ook zag ik wol es, dat de eeksters nich van t dak of te kriegn warn; anders zitn ze door ja nooit. \nEn de honden. Ie kunnen dr van denkn wat ie wiln, man honden waitn wat. “Komp non nich meer veur”, zegn mensn, man ook dat is nich woar. Verleden joar heb ik nog n hond ain haile dag jankn heurd en i","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45802,"r":"WEV015702","p":"Musselkanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A child sees men with a small coffin at the house and hears a dog bark, while other children see nothing. Shortly afterwards a newborn baby dies, neighbours carry the small coffin, and a dog barks.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik kwam n moal mit de vrouw bie hoes en dou kwammen ons kinder ons in de muide. Ons G. van acht joar zee: “Pabbe, ik heb zonet twai kerels bie ons hoes zain, zai druign ain kissie tussen zuk in; de hond blafde ook.” De ander kinder begunden dou haardop te lachen enzeden, dat ze gek was, want er wassen gain kerels west. Ik zee dou teegn dai andern: “Kinder, lach G. nich oet en proot dr ook nooit weer mit heur over.” \nIk doch al wat, en t is oetkomen. Mien vrouw is eevn loater bevaaln en t kind is man drai doagn worn. Dou hebben twai noabers t kissie wegbrocht en de hond blafde. Gelukkig hef ons G. het er nooit meer over had en zai hef ook nich wat weer zain. Door bin k bliede um, want dat is n verdrait, as ie wat zain moutn. Van kinder har ik et ook nog nich eerder heurd. Van grootn wol.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45803,"r":"WEV015703","p":"Musselkanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Curfew is hard for someone who has to pass the house of dying people; his prediction that someone will not live long comes true.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ain bekende van mie kan t ook. In de oorlog, dou wie um acht uur in hoes weezn mozzen, was dat wat veur dai man. Hai was hoast nich in hoes te holn; hai mos bie de weg en langs t hoes fietsn, woor ain op staarvn lag. \nZien femilieleden hebben er dou wat mit beleefd. \nIk heb bie de waarkverschafn mit hum waarkt. Was ook n vent van Stadsknoal, dai van dat spouk-kiekn heurd har en door wol es wat meer van waitn wol. Man de olle man zee niks. De jonge vent huil man vol, as wie aan t schaftn wazzen. Hai vruig: “Woorom wiln ie mie niks verteln van wat ie zain; ik wol ja wel es wat waitn.” \n“Och mien jong, dat kan ik die nich verteln, doe wordst nich old”, zee de man dou. Zo wus de vent dus wat. Jammer veur hum, dat et oetkomen is; hai is nog gain daartig joar worn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45807,"r":"WEV015704","p":"Musselkanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog that goes to a house where someone is ill and howls there foretells a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"As oal D. zien hond hoelde, dan kunnen ie dr op aan, dat in de buurt n dode kwam. Dat heb ik zulf heurd en zain. De hond sprong bie deurn umhoog en mus ook noar t stee, woor de zaike was. k Zai dai grode zwaarde hond nog bie ons veur t hoes langs loopn. Hai kwam, hoelde n zet en gung weer vot. En twai keer hebben wie n staarfgeval mitmoakt.\nVerkloarn kan ik niks. Man dat zukke dingen ploats hebben, is woar.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45809,"r":"WEV015706","p":"Musselkanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man believes that walking through something one evening was the forewarning of walking through something again at the funeral of a relative.","i":"F.W.","o":"k Wait nog, dat mien oal heer op n oavend zee: “Ik goa eevn noar de buurn te prootn, heur.”\nHai gung vot, man n zetje loater was e dr al weer; zo wit as n dode. En hai zee man niks.\n“Wat non, scheelt die wat?” zee mien moetje.\n“Ik bin woor deur hen loopn en k wait nich wat of t was.”\nMien voader was wat biezunder en vuilde, dat er wat op komst was; vast ain of ander ongeluk.\nWie harn nog n oale taande bie ons in hoes en dai is overleedn. Bie de begravvenis hef voader zuk verbeeld, dat hai weer deur wat henloopn is; zo verkloarde hai loater zien schrik van dai aovend. Joa, de olle heer kun mooie stokjes verteln. Het maiste leufde zulf, moar hai loog ook wel es, dunkt mie.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":29922,"r":"WEV015804","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of misfortune are howling dogs, magpies on the roof, black cats, and hens that come out of the barn or threshing floor with crossed straws on their backs.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ongeluksboden. \nDat wazzen en binnen nog bie dei wat lu: honden, dei zitn te hoeln; eeksters op t dak; zwaarde katn en hounder, dei mit gekruuste strospiern op de rugge uut de schure of van de dele komen. Dat brengt altied ellende.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45862,"r":"WEV016103","p":"Munnekemoer","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Howling dogs, magpies and owls near the house predict a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"En netuurlijk har t volk hier en over de grnze angst veur n jankende hond; zo’n daier keekn ze tussen de oorn deur en et huusdat ze den zagn, doorin zol ain dode komen. Om dezulfde reden juigen ze eeksters en katoeln vot.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46166,"r":"WEV016204","p":"Klazienaveen","v":"Dr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A carpenter hearing knocking is an omen that he will soon have to make a coffin.","i":"F.W.","o":"Geklop.\nDat heurn die wat mensen bie de timmerman; bieveurbeeld s nachts als de man stil lag te slaapn. Dat was n tiekn, dat ie gauw een doodskist maakn zol veur iene uut de buurte.","l":"Drents"},{"n":46184,"r":"WEV016405","p":"Gasselternijveen","v":"Dr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The day before a woman dies, a dog sits howling with its head in front of the bed. On the day of the funeral the dog stays in its kennel, although otherwise it lets no strangers into the yard.","i":"F.W.","o":"Honden hebben een voorgevoel van onheil.\nWe hadden hier indertijd een politiehond. Wie op het erf kwam en later zijn fiets wou pakken, kreeg daar de kans niet voor. \nEen dag voor dat mijn vrouw is overleden, zat de hond bij het bed te janken met de kop in de nek.\nOp de dag van de begrafenis liepen er veel mensen om het huis; toen is de hond het hok niet uitgeweest.\nDat deed hij anders altijd, als er iemand bij onskwam."},{"n":46188,"r":"WEV016501","p":"Oudeschans","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Foreseeing a hearse and the horse pulling it; tripping over a coffin that is not there, at the spot where bearers later set down a coffin; foreseeing a fire, feeling the walls.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wat ik wait heb ik van mien moeke, dei in Olle Schans geboorn is en hier altied woond het.\nDat is nait veul, biegeleuf kwam hier hail wainig veur.\nIs in ons ploats gainaine, dei dr meer van wait as ik.\nMien moeke vertelde den: “IN Olle Schans woonde vrouger oal Hindertje-muike. Zai kon kwoad zain. Op n moal verteld zai van ain liekwoagn, dei ze zain har. Zai nuimde et peerd, dat et liek trekn zol. De tied kwam, dat er n staarfgeval zok veurdee. Het gezegde van oal Hindertje was bekend en doorom dee de boer, dei t peerd levern mos aal zien best, dat hai n ander kreeg den t oal mens zegd har. Hai luip bie de peerden langs en perbaierde n poar moal eine. Zai waigerden allemoal. In t leste schoot er niks anders over den t peerdte nemen, dat er veur bestemd was.\nHindertje luip ook es n moal deur t veld over n loane.\nOpains is ze vaaln over n kiste, dei dr hailndaal nait ston.\nVattien doagn loater wur dr ain begroavn. De kiste mos droagn worn deur n stok of wat kerels, omdat dr gain woagn langs kon. Zai wurn mui van t laange loopn en zetn de kiste eevn op de grond. Woor? \nLiek op t stee, woor Hindertje-mui oetgleden was.”\nt Is wel al 150 joar leden, dat dit gebeurd is.\nWazzen ook nog lu, dei n brand van te veurn zain konden. \nAs zai dat zagn, gungen ze dr op of. Was nooit n brand, moar den vuilden ze aan de muurn; wazzen dei kold, den kwam er n dode in dat huus; vuilden ze waarm aan,","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46193,"r":"WEV016602","p":"Gieterveen","v":"Dr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The sound of prying at a partition is an omen of a coffin for which the partition will have to be removed.","i":"F.W.","o":"Het nog in spookhuus bestoan hier. Op n nacht heurden mensn, dei op berre lagen, gestommel naost heur. Aan de andere kaande van de bedstee was n holtn schotje. t Heurde net of dr aan dat schot wrikt wur. Zai gungen es kiekn, wat of dr toch was, moar niks te zain. n Zet loater. Op t land verongelukt n jong van heur bie t waark. \nHai wordt in n kiste in huus brocht. Wat maarkn ze den? \nHet schot mout ofbrookn worn, anders ken de kiste dr nait langs. \nDit was dus n veurloop west, dat geluud.","l":"Drents"},{"n":46196,"r":"WEV016701","p":"Froombosch","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Someone born with a caul can see misfortune, such as funeral processions, and knows who the dead person is; examples of voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mit de helm geboorn.\nDoor heb ik wel al van heurd. Zo ain het dr woond in de buurt van Sapm-meer. Hai kon kwoad zain. Dat is hail wat aans as kwaod doun. Gain mens har last van hom. Moar wat hai veuruut zag, was altied wat slims. Beveurbeeld liekstoaties.\nDei kon hai zain goan over de weg. En de noam van de dode wos hai dr bie ook.\nAin staarfgeval konnen ie wieder verwachtn, as er honden zatn te hoeln in de buurt. Ook as ie ain zwaarte katte teegn kwammen en dat daier n schop gaven of mit n staine smeetn.\nAlles wat zwaart was, mos ie veurzichtig mit weezn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46213,"r":"WEV016804","p":"Schaaphok","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Women see a funeral procession; one woman concludes that it is her funeral, and later she tells details about her funeral and other matters.","i":"F.W.","o":"Zo bestoan dr veurloopn.\nMien aign moeke het ons door van verteld. \nZai zag es n liekwoagn over de weg goan. Ze zee teegn mien zuster, dat zai ook es kiekn mos. En dei zag t zulfde. Moeke vruig toun: “Zugst ons Haarm dr ook bie?”\n“Nee”, zee mien zuster. “Gelukkig, den is t veur mie zulf, dat is beter den veur zo’n jonge man”, zee t oal.\nLoater het zai oms dr nog meer van verteld.\nEr zoln twei seldoatn achter de woagn loopn; heur zuster zol t doodsklaid moakn en zai nuimde ook de deurn, woor de kiste deur goan zol.\nEn t is aal zo uutkomen.\nDe seldoatn wazzen twei van heur jonges, dei in dainst wazzen in de mobelesoatie.\nn Tied van te veurn zat er n hond te hoeln bie ons veur t huus.\n“Dat betaikent mien dood kinder”, zee ze teegn ons.\nWie wazzen verzekerd. Bie dood zol dr geld uutbetoald worn. Nou vertelde ze ons, dat dit gebeurn zol mit zuver rieksdoalders.\nEn ook dit kwam uut. De verzekernsagent legde f 50 op toafel; allemoal in rieksdoalders.\nDit alles hebben wie in ons aign gezin mitmoakt en is dus gain ploade.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46220,"r":"WEV016902","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Knocking on the window at night is voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death, when someone knocks on the window at night to report a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien moeke zee es teegn mie, ik was nog n kwoajong: “Goa es eevn noar boetn en tik teegn t roam.”\nIk vruig, woorom.\n“Goa hen jong”, zee ze.\nIk klopde n poar moal aan t glas en kwam weer binnen.\n“Het klopt”, zee t oal, “t zulfde geluud heb ik vannacht ook heurd, zel wel wat op handen weezn.” En zo was t.\nNait al te laank loater wur es s nachts op de roamen klopt; wie gungen dr of en vernamen, dat n buurvrouw overleden was. Ain van de andere buurn kwam ons t verteln.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46221,"r":"WEV016903","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman thinks that screeching magpies around the house are voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of evil. Not long afterwards the woman dies.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veur n poar joar hadden wie op n dag n koppel eeksters om t huus tou te roupn. Zai kwammen biekans op de vensterbaanke. Mien vrouw muik dr uut op, dat et kwoad te betaikn har en dat was ik wel mit heur ains. \nDe stakker; t was veur heur zulf bedould. Zai is eevn loater nogal stoef (plotseling) overleden.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46223,"r":"WEV017002","p":"Stadskanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Shortly after a white figure enters a farm, someone there dies.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien oal lu hebben mie vrij wat verteld over vrouger; spokerij en zowat, door geleufden ze nogal aan. In mien jonge joarn keb ik t zulf ook leufd, moar nou loater goud bekeekn komt t mie onwoarschienlek veur. De oale mensn twiefelden dr nait aan en ze vertel-ons den de volgende verhoaln:\nOp n andere moal luipn ze weer bis t pad en door zaggen ze inains n widde gedoante veur heur aan loopn. Zai muikn zok dr baange veur en bleevn dr n mooi end achter.\nt Spook zee niks; bie n boernloane sluig t of en luip in richtn van de boerderij. Mien oal lu bleevn stoan om te kiekn, wat of dr wieder gebeurde. t Widde ding dee deure van t huus oopn, gong noar binnen en dee deure weer tou.\nWat wast? Veurbeduudsel, want in t huus is ain sturm nait laank noa tied.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46227,"r":"WEV017101","p":"Wedde","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A white woman who makes a horse stand still and holds it by the head must be voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of evil.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik zel joe eerst verteln, wat hier vrouger in Wedde veurvaaln is.\nVrougg in de mörn voart dr ain karre over t stroade.\nVouerman zit wat te dommeln in zokzulf, is hoast nog gain mens op pad. \nOpains blift t peerd stoan. Man kikt en door zug hai, dat n klain vrouwmens in t wit zien peerd bie de kop vast holt.\n“Dat is ja roar”, denkt e, “wat mankaiert dat wief toch?”\nHai zeg: “Woorom dust dat?”\nKomp gain antwoord; de gedoante is inains weer verschwonnen.\nHai raist wieder noar t maart tou en gait loater op huus of.\nAalmoar mout-e aan dat spookgeval denkn.\nIn huus vertelt hai et aan zien vrouw en dei maint, dat et kwoad te beduden har. Ain of ander geest zol hom woarschouwd hebben veur n komend ongeluk.\nDe vrouw har dit goud bekeekn. Want zai het n doodgeboorn popke kreegn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46228,"r":"WEV017102","p":"Wedde","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"From a pool where a farmer and his horse drown, a voice had earlier come saying that a man would drown at that spot when his time came.","i":"F.W.","o":"In Wedde is ook n moal n woagn mit n vouer heu in ain kolk reden.\nBoer en peerd binnen dr bie verdronkn.\nIk heb t nooit heurd, moar ollere lu wozzen te verteln, dat al joarn van te veurn uut dei kolk n stem komen was,; t gong over n kerel, dei op zien tied op dat stee verdrinkn zol. Het juuste wait ik dr nait van.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46238,"r":"WEV017305","p":"Overschild","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Black crows in the garden are voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Zwaarte kraaien.\nDizze vogels op toene betaikende ain dode. \nMien grootmoe (woor ik veul verhoaln van heurd heb) kon precies verteln, as er n staarfgeval in de omgeevn komen zol.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46245,"r":"WEV017402","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman can see evil; she sees a fire that is voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death or a fire.","i":"F.W.","o":"Kwoad zain.\nMien moetje kon dat. As wie op berre gungen, mozzen wie eerst ja eevn moar boetn om te pizzen. Kinder en grootn ook. Op n oavend was moeke al boetn en zat bie t stroatje. Dou kwammen wie dr aan, moar t oalske juig ons in hoes. Wie woln waitn, woorom, moar dat zee ze nait. Loater wel; zai har n hoes brannen zain; dat kon ain dode of n brand betaikn; in dit geval ist n dode worn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46260,"r":"WEV017406","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The howling of dogs is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death; animals sense things.","i":"F.W.","o":"Hondegehoel.\nJoa zeker is dat n veurbode van n staarfgeval. Dat heb ik al meer den ainmoal beleefd. Daiern kennen dat op ain of ander menaier van te veurn waitn. Peerden binnen ook loos. Ik heb veul smokkeln doan. Nou heb k n keer n loos peerd had. As ik door mit in t veld was bie aovend, den kon k precies aan t daier vernamen, woor hausheern zatn; dei kaande mos ik den nait oet.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46265,"r":"WEV017505","p":"Weite","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When people are pushed aside in the evening, there will be a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Van de weg.\nIn t Hebrecht binnen wel es gounend van de weg oftrokn. Dat gebeurt bie oavend en kwam op meer steden veur. Door komt wat slims achteraan; zo ook hier.\nOp n dag wazzen de boern aan t eerappel-mennen. Kinder gungen voak mit op wupkoare. Op dat stee den is t peerd schrokn; ain kind is van t wupkoare ofvaaln, toun t peerd aan trok en t stumper kwam onder t rad. t Is dood reden. \nJoa, zokke dingen gebeurden.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":22019,"r":"CJ031405","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Early in the morning a woman hears loud wailing and crying. The next morning a woman wails and cries in exactly the same way because her little daughter has died. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ús Jinke stoar hearde myn suster Hiltsje de moarns fan tofoaren ien jammerjen en gûlen. \"Ik tochte,\" sa fortelde se letter, \"hwa soe hjir wêze. Ik lei noch op bêd. Ik gong der ôf en seach yn 't hok, mar der wie net in minske,\" sei se.\nMar de oare moarns bitiid kaem ús Joeke by har, skriemende en gûlende. Hy sei: \"Hiltsjemoai, ús Jinke is dea.\" En hy jammere en snokte krektsa as Hiltsje it de moarns fan tofoaren heard hie.\nIt hie it jammerjen fan ús Joeke west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22065,"r":"CJ031901","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Chattering magpies by the house herald an imminent death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters om 'e doar hinne skatterje, dan komt der yn dat hûs in deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22321,"r":"CJ034513","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Cries for help from a pond are a portent of an imminent drowning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Liuwepoel ha se us in stem heard. \"Help, help!\" rôp der ien. Mar der wie neat to sjen. 't Hat foartsjirmerije west. Dêr mat altyd noch ien yn fordrinke. Soks kin wol hûndert jier duorje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22718,"r":"CJ035010","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A magpie close to the house points to an imminent death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in ekster tichte by hûs komt, sei ús mem, dan komt der binnenkoart in sterfgefal.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22793,"r":"CJ035606","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man predicts a death because he has heard the dog howling eerily. The prediction comes true: shortly afterwards someone dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Douwe Baeije sei op in moarn: \"Der komt wer in deaden. Dat sil Ulkje wol wêze, hwant ús houn docht oars neat as spûkgûlen. Dan sit er mar foar 't lytse finsterke op 'e stoel en sjocht dy kant nei Ulkje hyltyd út.\"\nBaeije hat gelyk krige. Ulkje is koart dêrnei stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22841,"r":"CJ036119","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A girl sees a house with the curtains drawn in front of the windows. She suspects something has happened. It is a voorgezicht (a vision foreshadowing an event): two days later a dead person is laid out in the same house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn famke seach op in kear by Piter Vries - dy wenne oan 'e Skûlenburchsterwei de kleden ticht foar de glêzen.\nIt wie sa stil en sa deadsk allegear. Sy sei: \"Dêr is hwat gebeurd.\" Twa dagen letter is der in famke fan Piter Vries troch in oanriding dea rekke. Doe kom se yn dyselde keamer to lizzen yn 'e kiste mei de kleden ticht, krekt sa't myn famke it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22851,"r":"CJ036208","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If the dog howls eerily, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":22852,"r":"CJ036209","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A family loses a child. An old woman had already foreseen the death because her dog kept howling eerily.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha in broerke forlern. Der wenne in âlde frou tichte by ús yn 't earmhûs. Dy sei fan tofoaren al: \"Hjir komt gau in deaden, hwant ús houn spûkgûlt iderkear.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22980,"r":"CJ037007","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man has an uneasy premonition that someone is going to drown. Half a year later someone does indeed drown at the same spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie sa'n oardeljier lyn by de Kilometerwei ûnder Aldegea. Dêr stie 'k to sjen nei it terrein fan it ierdgas. Wylst ik dêr stie hie 'k hiel sterk it gefoel dat dêr ien fordronk. Ik sei: \"Ik mat hjir wei, ik kin hjir net bliuwe.\" Ik wist net hwa en hwat dêr fordrinke soe.\nNou in healjier lyn is Riemmer Benedictus dêr op 't selde plak fordronken.\nDat hat it doe west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23070,"r":"CJ037614","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At a certain spot people have sometimes heard cries for help. They say that someone is still bound to drown there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Dokkum op 'e Schreiershoek ha guon us 'help, help!' roppen heard. Dêr mat altyd noch us ien fordrinke, is it sizzen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23077,"r":"CJ037703","p":"Groningen","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman once saw a stately lady dressed in white go through the garden gate at the neighbours'. Suddenly she had vanished again. A few days later someone died at the neighbours'.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mijn tante woonde in Bussum. Toen zag ze op een keer een schone dame naderen. Die was helemaal in 't wit gekleed. Ze maakte 't hekje open van de tuin bij de buren. Langzaam en waardig kwam die dame er aan. Tante kende haar niet. Ze was ook opeens weer verdwenen. Tante voelde meteen dat dit iets met de dood te maken had.\nEen paar dagen later stierf er inderdaad iemand bij de buren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23079,"r":"CJ037705","p":"Groningen","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man saw his own funeral in advance. He saw the number of carriages and recognised all the people who were there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mijn grootvader zag zijn eigen begrafenis van tevoren. Hij zag het aantal rijtuigen en herkende alle mensen die er bij waren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23080,"r":"CJ037706","p":"Groningen","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man told his grandson that he would return from military service too late to see him again. And so it happened. The day before the grandson came back, the grandfather had died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In 1918 moest ik onder dienst. Mijn grootvader zei tegen me: \"Jij maakt nog een tijd mee, die verschrikkelijk is. Je gaat nu weg,\" zei hij tegen me, \"maar je komt even te laat terug, dan ben ik er niet meer.\"\n't Is net zo gebeurd. Ik heb de eerste en de tweede Wereldoorlog meegemaakt. En toen ik terugkwam in 1918 kwam ik net een dag te laat. De vorige dag was grootvader gestorven.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23082,"r":"CJ037708","p":"Groningen","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog stood howling in the street, there would be a death, people always used to say.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":23083,"r":"CJ037709","p":"Groningen","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a painting or mirror fell from the wall, a death would follow.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":23372,"r":"CJ038519","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Omens of death: a) The ghostly howling of a dog. Within three days someone dies. b) A magpie in the farmyard: a letter announcing a death. c) The death-tick, sometimes in the ribbons of the oorijzer bonnet (a traditional headdress with a metal head-band). d) When the owl calls. e) Three drops of blood falling from the nose. f) If a horse on its way to the farmyard scrapes with its hind leg, someone will die in the house in front of which it scrapes. g) If the weight of the clock falls down. h) If the bell tolls dully. Then a corpse hangs from it, people say. i) If the dead person looks beautiful. One must never covet the corpse, for then someone else will die. That is why the dead person is content and beautiful. j) If the corpse lies in the house over a Sunday, there will soon be another death. The wish of the dead person is then fulfilled. k) Whatever one meets first on the way to the churchyard will be the first to die in the family. If one meets a man, a man will die; if one meets a woman, a woman; if one meets a child, a child.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foarboaden fan'e dea:\na. Spûkgûlen fan in houn: binnen 3 dagen in deade.\nb. Ekster op it hiem (= in swart mei wyt - boade): in roubrief.\nc. Deatikkerke (soms yn 'e strikken fan 't earizerhuodtsje), ek in foarboade fan 'e dea.\nd. As der ûle ropt.\ne. Trije drippen bloed, dy 't út 'e noas fallen.\nf. As it hynder ûnderweis nei 't hôf ta mei de achterste poat skrabbel. Yn it hûs dêr 't det foar gebeurt, komt in deade.\ng. As it wicht fan 'e klok delfalt.\nh. As de klok deadsk let. Dan hinget der in lyk oan, sizze se. \ni. As de deade moai is. Dat mat men noait bigeare, hwant dan komt der wer ien ta forstjerren yn 'e famylje. (Dêrom is de deade bliid en moai)\nj. As it lyk in snein oer stiet, is der fan wer in deade. De winske fan 'e deade is dan forfolle.\nk. Hwat men ûnderweis nei 't tsjerkhôf it earste tsjinkomt, dat sil it earst yn juis famylje stjerre. Komt men in man tsjin, dan stjert der yn juis famylje in man, is it in frou, in frou, is it in bern, dan in bern.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23389,"r":"CJ038906","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls ghostly, someone in the neighbourhood will die.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":23557,"r":"CJ039920","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls ghostly, someone will die in the direction the dog is howling. If magpies chatter in the farmyard, a death will also follow.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in houn spûkgûlt, dan komt der in sterfgefal. Yn it hûs dêr't er mei de kop hinne keard stiet.\nAs de eksters op it hiem skatterje, komt der ek in sterfgefal.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23611,"r":"CJ040308","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One night two sisters heard a noise at the front door, quiet talking, and something being pushed in front of their box bed. A few days later their brother drowned. When his body was brought in, people talked quietly, and the coffin was placed in front of the box bed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy hawwe in broer hawn, dy hiet fan Okke. Hy is fordronken wylst er to riden wie op 't iis.\nIk en myn suster slepten yn 'e keamer hjir foar yn 't bêdsté. Wy ha in pear nachten fan tofoaren alles dúdlik heard. Wy hearden guon by de doar kommen en ien dy't hiel bot kleide.\nIn nacht letter hearden wy dat guon de fuotten fagen by de foardoar en dat der hwat swiers ta de gong yn skoud woarde. Dat kom by ús bêdsté to stean.\nDoe hearden wy guon sunich praten.\nFuort letter fordronk ús broer. Hy wie noch in jongfeint en wy wienen fan dy greate bern.\nSy ha 't lyk by ús yn 'e keamer set foar 't bêdsté.\nIt skouwen fan it deafet joech krekt deselde lûden, dy't wy fan tofoaren heard hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23623,"r":"CJ040401","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One evening a man saw a funeral. Someone else saw nothing. A few days later the man's wife died, and the funeral really took place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Taeke Taekema fan Suwâld wie foar de twadde kear troud. Op in joun doe't it tsjuster wie roannen hy en noch in man togearre de wei del. Doe sei dy oare man tsjin Taeke: \"Wy matte hjir even wei. Der komt in bigraffenis oan.\"\n\"Fan hwa is dy bigraffenis?\" frege Taeke even letter.\n\"Dat silst wol hearre\", sei er.\nTwa à trije dagen letter stoar Taeke syn frou. In pear dagen letter woarde se opdroegen. Dat wie deselde bigraffenis dy't dy man dy jouns sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23624,"r":"CJ040402","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A card reader once predicted to a man that he would have a strange accident. The man did not believe a word of it. But later, while swimming, he got a terrible cramp and drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Boarnburgum wenne Wyberen fan Hâns van der Wal, in frijgesel. Hy wie yn Easterboarn yn 'e ûngetiid by in boer. Op in snein-to-joun gong er nei Hinke Kaert ta, dy't op Nijebrêge wenne. Hinke lei him de kaert út. Hja sei, hy soe nuver ûngelok krije. Dat leaude Wyberen net, hwant hy wie geheelûnthâlder, dus fan 't sûpen soe it net komme kinne.\n't Wie op in kear gleonhyt waer. Doe sei de feint tsjin him: \"Sille wy nei de âlde Boarn ta to swemmen?\" Hy giet mei, mar dêr krijt er de kramp en fordrinkt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23811,"r":"CJ042112","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howled ghostly at night, someone died.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":23831,"r":"CJ042214","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The voice of a child was often heard coming from a small lake. It is said that someone will yet drown in it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Jan Brants dobbe, dêr hearden se faek in stem yn fan in bern dat raesde. Der wurdt ornearre dat dêr altyd nochris ien yn fordrinke sil.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23843,"r":"CJ042404","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls ghostly, someone in the area will die. If a cat washes itself, visitors often come the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlde, dan kom der in deaden op 'e buert. Dat kom faek nei. \nMei katten, as dy har waskje, komt it ek faek nei, dat der dy deis praters komme.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23857,"r":"CJ042507","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog once howled ghostly and terribly in front of the gate of a house where a sick girl lived. Three days later the girl died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw in suster hawn, dy hiet fan Antsje. Dy is útsukkele. Op in joun stie der in hountsje yn 't hekje en dat hountsje gûlde hiel bot, oan ien tried wei. It wie hast net oan to hearren. Us heit sei: \"Antsje leeft net lang mear.\" Trije dagen letter wie se dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23930,"r":"CJ042923","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The Liuwepoel is dreadfully deep. Cries for help have sometimes been heard there at night. This means that someone will drown in it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De Liuwepoel is ôfgryslike djip. Nachts ha se wolris ien roppen heard om help. Dat lûd kom út 'e poel wei. Dat bitsjut dat der nochris ien yn forsûpe mat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23933,"r":"CJ043001","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man once had the feeling that his wife was dead, and he saw her corpse. The next day the woman really died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De jouns foardat myn frou stoar, seach ik har as in lyk. Ik hie 't gefoel dat se dea wie en dochs is se de oare deis pas stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23962,"r":"CJ043303","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man once saw a funeral in his house and feared one of his youngest sons would die. But it was his eldest son who died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Douwe Stavasius had lutje en grote jongens. Hy had een begrafenis bij hem in huis sien en doe docht hij, dat het een van de lutje jonges was die begraven werd. \"Ik docht nooit dat 't Fokke was\", - zo hiete de oudste - zee die. Moar 't was Fokke die stierf.\nDouwe woonde hier achter ons huus in een spitkeet.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24007,"r":"CJ043701","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man always saw in advance that someone was going to die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ritske Vellink fortelde oan ien dy wenne op it streekje:\n\"Hjir by W. komt in sterfgefal.\" Even letter stoar dêr in famke. Dat hie er in pear dagen foarút al sjoen. 't Wie yn Ikkerwâld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24010,"r":"CJ043704","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One night a woman heard a sound as if a beam were tapping on the table. Later her little daughter died. Then she thought it had been an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Jeltsje woarde op in nacht wekker, doe wie 't krekt dat der in balke op 'e tafel tikte. 't Wie yn Ikkerwâld. Letter stoar der in dochterke. Doe tocht se dat it foartsjirmerij west hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24016,"r":"CJ043710","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People once heard something bang against the wall in the hallway. Not long afterwards the man of the house died. When the coffin was carried out of the house, it banged against the wall. This made exactly the same sound they had heard before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon hearden us in kear yn 'e nacht in stomp yn 'e gong by in hoeke. Even letter stoar de man. Doe't se de kiste der ta útdrage soenen, stompte de kiste yn 'e gong tsjin in skerpe hoeke oan. 't Wie deselde stomp, dy't se earder heard hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24093,"r":"CJ044210","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When the magpies gather, someone will die.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":24094,"r":"CJ044211","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A thatcher once told an acquaintance that that day magpies had been flying all around his house making a great racket. Not long afterwards the thatcher died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir achter my wennen twa reiddekkers. De iene wie David. Sy hienen in gazen hok mei hinnen.\n't Is nou twa jier lyn, doe sei David tsjin my: \"Hwat haw ik hjir hjoed hwat bileefd. Hoefolle eksters as hjir hjoed net om 't hûs flein ha, wyt ik net. En hwat in stik leven dat se makken! Ik haw ek noch ien yn 'e hannen hawn, dy fleach hjir tsjin 't gaes oan.\"\nIk sei neat, hwant ik tochte: \"Hjir komt in deaden.\"\nIt duorre mar in lyts setsje tiid, doe stoar David.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24095,"r":"CJ044212","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls ghostly, someone will die. A woman was once ill. When she and her husband were lying in bed in the evening, they heard a dog howl ghostly. Two weeks later the woman died in hospital.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt, dan giet der ien dea. Dat komt altyd út. Mar it is ûngelyk hoe't it gebeurt. Sy matte net fêst sitte. Dan binne se binaud. Dan gûle se altyd.\nMyn frou wie frijhwat siik. Wy leinen op in nacht togearre op bêd. Doe bigong der in houn to spûkgûlen. Ik tocht: As se dat nou mar net heart. As se nou mar slept.\n\"Slepste?\" sei se.\nIk sei: \"Ja, al hast.\"\n\"Hearst dy houn wol?\" sei se.\n\"Och,\" ik sei, \"hâld op. Wy matte sliepe.\"\n\"Hwat hast my forteld\", sei se. \"As in houn spûkgûlt, komt der in sterfgefal. It liket mei my net bêst.\"\nFjirtsjin dagen letter is se ûnforwacht nei Ljouwert, nei 't sikenhûs ta rekke. Dêr is se stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24096,"r":"CJ044213","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog once stood in the middle of a potato field howling ghostly towards the northwest. Not long afterwards someone who lived in that direction died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tusken it hûs fan Tsjalling Bijma en dat fan myn neef op 'e Tike lei in stik jierappel-lân. Midden op dat stik lân stie in dikke houn to spûkgûlen. Hy seach yn 't noardwesten op. Dêr wennen Sibe Wiersma en syn frou Marij. 't Wie by dei dat dy houn spûkgûlde. Doe't ik it hearde tocht ik: \"Hjir giet ien dea.\"\nIk makke 't net bikend. Fuort letter stoar Sibe syn wiif.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24097,"r":"CJ044214","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If magpies chatter close to a house and fly off in all directions, someone in that house will die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de eksters bigjinne to skatterjen flak by hûs en sy fljogge alle kanten út, dan giet der yn dat hûs ien dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24120,"r":"CJ044307","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man went to church with his son every Sunday. Another man, who often foresaw that someone would die, warned that if the churchgoing man took his son to church again that Sunday, the son would die. The man paid no attention. That Sunday the boy died in an accident with a milk cart.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Houtigehage wenne in man mei in soan fan achttsjin jier. Dy man wie tsjerks. Alle sneinen gong er mei de jonge nei tsjerke. Ik sei dy moarns tsjin 'e buorliuwe: \"As er dy feint nou thús bliuwe liet, hâldde dy jonge syn leven. As er him meinimt nei tsjerke, dan is 't de dood.\"\nEn dat is dy heit ek oerbrocht woarn, mar hy woe der neat fan witte, hy naem him de snein-to-moarns mei nei tsjerke.\nDoe kom der har in molkrider achter op. De jonge soe op 'e wein springe, dêr rekket krekt in tsjil los, dat komt tsjin 'e jonge oan en hy rekke dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24121,"r":"CJ044308","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man foresaw that a girl would shoot herself dead with a gun. Her brother had joined the marechaussee (military police) during his military service. Her boyfriend now wanted to do the same. The girl was afraid of losing her boyfriend, and so she killed herself.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wenne yn 'e Houtigehage in faem, dy har broer wie ûnder tsjinst maresjaussee woarn. Sy hie forkearing mei in feint, dy woe ek maresjaussee wurde. Mar dan moest er in hiel skoft ûnder tsjinst bliuwe. Dy faem tocht: dan reitsje ik him kwyt, en doe hat se harsels mei 't gewear deasketten.\nDat haw ik fan tofoaren sjoen. Ik warskôge se fan tofoaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24122,"r":"CJ044309","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man foresaw that another man would come home dead that evening. That is indeed what happened. The man had suffered from the heat and died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear stie 'k op 'e wei mei noch in pear minsken. Doe sei 'k: \"De man, dy't yn dàt húske wennet, komt joun dea thús.\"\nEn dy man kòm dy jouns dea thús. Hy hie tofolle fan 'e warmte hawn. Hy lei op hwat strie op 'e wein mei in swart hynder der foar. Sa brochten se him de jouns thús. 'k Hie 't allegear al sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24130,"r":"CJ044317","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls ghostly, a death usually follows.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt, komt der meastal in sterfgefal. Net altyd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24146,"r":"CJ044412","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls ghostly, someone will die. If magpies chatter near the houses, someone will also die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt komt der in deade.\nAs de eksters skatterje neiby de huzen ek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24208,"r":"CJ044905","p":"Harlingen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog once stood whining by the water. Later its owner drowned there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik heb het met maakt, dat er een hond bij 't water stond te janken. Later is zijn baas daar verdronken."},{"n":24219,"r":"CJ045007","p":"Peize","v":"Dr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In winter a baker often cycled across the ice to work, because it was much shorter. One day his wife warned him not to go across the ice that day. That night she had seen him fall through the ice and drown. But the man went across the ice anyway, and indeed he drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Feanwâlden, op 'e hoeke fan 'e Westerwâl wenne Fokke Boonstra. Hy wie bakker en wie ôfkomstich fan Burgum. Hy sutele altyd mei syn breaspullen en hie ek klanten yn Burgum sitten en dêromhinne.\n\"t Wie op in winter en 't iis wie sterk. Doe fytste Boonstra oer de Burgumermar, om gauwer by syn klanten to wêzen. Dat die er altyd as it sterk iis wie, hwant dat snie in hiel stik ôf.\nMar doe woarde it tij-waer. Doe die er it noch wol faek. Hy weage it lang.\nDoe sei syn frou: \"Dû mast net wer oer de Mar fytse, hwant ik ha dy fannacht foar my hawn, doe sakkest troch 't iis en forsûpste.\"\nMar hy die 't al. 't Wie sa maklik binnentroch.\nHy is dy kear fordronken.\nSyn frou hie 't allegear yn 'e nacht sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24242,"r":"CJ045117","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Sounds from a small lake are interpreted as an omen of death by drowning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der binne froeger lûden út 'e Blaudobbe weikom. Dêr mat altyd noch guon yn forsûpe, wol men ha.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24269,"r":"CJ045306","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog with four eyes is a ghost-howler. When the dog begins to howl ghostly, it is usually an omen of an impending death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie in houn mei fjouwer egen. Dat binne spoekgûlers. Sy ha twa ljochte flekken boven de egen.\nUs buorjonkje krige in sinnestek. Dy jouns om sa'n tsien ûre hinne bigoun ús houn hiel jammerlik to gûlen. Us oare buorman sei: \"Hjir gebeurt fannacht hwat.\" Dy nachts is it buorjonkje stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24287,"r":"CJ045411","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a painting falls down, a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in skilderij delfiel, dan seiden se: \"Der komt in doden.\" En dat komt ook út.\nWij hè 't bij ús thús had, doe fiel der in skilderij del. Doe sei myn moeke: \"Daar komt wat achter wei.\"\nDe ene rouwbrief na de andere kwam. Overal kwamen de berichten weg, allemaal van familieleden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24289,"r":"CJ045413","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People hear a sound coming from the water. It is an omen: later someone drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bij de brug in de Westerein stonden us in kear mensen, die hebben daar in geluut hoord. Dat kwam út it water. Later is daar een ferdronken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24314,"r":"CJ045701","p":"Peize","v":"Dr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At night people hear sounds as if a coffin is being made. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit wie timmerman. Wy sliepten as jonges achter, ús heit fóár. Soms hearden wy yn 'e nacht, dat der by ús in deakiste timmere waerd. Dan kom der de oare deis ien dy't in deakiste bistelde. It nuvere wie dat heit sels soks noait hearde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24335,"r":"CJ045808","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Children's screaming is heard by the water. It is an omen: later two children are narrowly saved from drowning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der ha froeger twa bern fan Simen Spinder yn 't Fliet sitten. Dy binne omtrint forsûpt. Simen hat se noch kret op 'e tiid ret. Fan tofoaren ha se dy bern dêr razen heard. Dat wie foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24337,"r":"CJ045810","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Someone foresees that a red-haired girl will drown in a pool. The vision has not yet come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn it poeltsje op 'e Dunen soe ien - in famke - forsûpe mei read hier. Der wie ien dy hie dat sjoen. Mar 't is noch net gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24350,"r":"CJ045902","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At a carpenter's house, wood for coffins is clearly heard being moved in the attic at night. It is an omen: the next day someone comes to order a coffin for a deceased person.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Ikkerwâld hearden se by in timmerman op in nacht dúdlik dat se op 'e souder yn 't kistehout omklauden. De oare moarns kom der in man om in nije kiste, omt der ien stoarn wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24374,"r":"CJ046103","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a funeral procession approaches, the dog already starts to howl ghostly in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit en dy hienen in houn. As der in lykstaesje oankaem, siet dy houn even fan tofoaren to gûlen. Dan siet er op 'e hoeke. Dat die er grif alle kearen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24421,"r":"CJ046309","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When someone is going to die, the dog begins to howl eerily. The dog keeps its head turned toward the one who will die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der ien stjerre sil, bigjint de houn to spûkgûlen. Hy hâldt de kop keard nei deselde dy't stjerre sil. Wy ha 't sels ûnderfoun mei ús famke, dêr't Piter de Graaf fan sjoen hat dat se deagean soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24449,"r":"CJ046503","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When there is a sick person on board at sea, the fish come swimming around the ship. It is an omen: the sick person will soon die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw to Den Oever timmere. Dan praette 'k wol ris mei in âld fisker. Dy fortelde my, as der in siken oan board wie op sé, dan kommen de fisken om it skip hinne swemmen. Dan sei it folk: \"Dy giet dea.\" En dat gong ek fêst troch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24473,"r":"CJ046805","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man hears cries for help from the water and clearly sees the face of the person in need. It is a foreshadowing of an impending drowning: that same night the drowned person is dragged up from the water.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie op in saterdei-to-joune nei de faem ta west. Dy wenne yn 'e Broek. Let yn 'e nacht kom ik werom. Ik kom oer de brêge dy't oer de Swemmer leit.\nDoe tocht ik: Heare, hjir ropt ien fan help. Mar ik seach neat en it lûd wie ek samar ynienen fuort. Mar doe't ik in wike letter krekt om deselde tiid dêr wer lâns kom, doe hearde ik in ploemp yn 't wetter. Ik ha fuort in boatsje krigen, mar it roeide min. It waeide sa bot en 't gong yn 'e wyn op. It gesicht fan de persoan ha 'k noch sjoen, mar ik koe him net rêdde. Doe wie er al sonken. It 'help'- roppen ha 'k noch dúdlik heard.\nDeselde nachts noch ha de skipper Gaukema en de plysje de drinkeling opdregge. 't Wie Theunis Elzinga.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24509,"r":"CJ047101","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Magpies near the house, a dog howling eerily, a barn owl calling and the death knell of the bell are all omens of a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de eksters op it hûs kommen, dan kom der in sterfgefal. Dêr wie ús mem deabinaud foar.\nEk as in houn spûkgûlt en as de katûl ropt.\nEn ek as de klok deadsk lette.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24600,"r":"CJ047805","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog howling eerily is an omen of an impending death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlde, wie dat in teken, dat der gau ien stjerre soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24669,"r":"CJ049203","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man hears a number of magpies chattering. It is an omen of an approaching death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn heit siet op in snein foar 't glês. Hy seach nei bûten. \"Fanke,\" sei er tsjin mem, \"hwat in eksters, en hwat skatterje dy!\"\nMem waerd deabinaud doe't er dat sei.\nTrije wiken letter rekke myn heit dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24840,"r":"CJ049712","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In the old days people often heard death knocking. If there were three knocks, death came to fetch you.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon hearden hjir froeger de dea klopjen. As der trije kear kloppe woarde, dan koe men der mar fan op oan dat de dea jin ophelle.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24849,"r":"CJ049805","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman always hears the bells ringing when a death is approaching.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hear altyd fan to foaren de klokken lieden, as der ien op 't hôf komt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24908,"r":"CJ050508","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Once a child's screaming was heard at a small lake. People suspect that a child will drown.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Blaudobbe ha se ris it lûd fan in razend berntsje heard. Dêr sil nochris ien yn fordrinke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24914,"r":"CJ050602","p":"Earnewâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A skipper's daughter hears cries for help. She suspects someone has fallen through the ice, but there is nothing to be seen. It is an omen: a few days later someone drowns.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn frou is in skippersdochter. Sy leinen us in kear mei 't skip yn 't Beetster kanael. Sy hienen famylje wenjen yn Beets. Dy fortelden har, dat sy sieten in kear yn 'e hûs, doe waerd der 'help' roppen. 't Wie yn 'e winter en der lei iis. Sy tochten: der is ien trochsakke. Sy der út en sjen, doe wie der neat.\nMar in pear dagen letter waerd der wer roppen fan 'help'.\nDoe is der ien fordronken. 't Gebeurde yn 't Beetster kanael.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24915,"r":"CJ050603","p":"Earnewâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When rooks sit on the roofs two days in a row, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de roeken hjoed op it dak kommen to sitten en moarn wer, dus twa kear, dan kom der yn dat hûs in sterfgefal.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24916,"r":"CJ050604","p":"Earnewâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When the dog howls eerily, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de houn spûkgûlde ek. By 't hiem dêr't er stie, dêr kaem in deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25119,"r":"CJ051508","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Omens of a death: a dog howling eerily, a barn owl calling and spiders ticking against the wallpaper - the so-called 'wilde horloges' (wild clocks). A falling mirror also points to something bad about to happen. Chattering magpies in the yard announce a letter of mourning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt, mat der ien stjerre.\nAs de katûl ropt ek.\nAs de spinnen tikje tsjin 't bihang (wylde horloazjes), dan komt der ek in sterfgefal. \"De wylde horloazjes tikken my wer sa yn 'e mûtse,\" sei mem, \"ik wist wol dat der in sterfgefal komme soe.\" (doe wie der in famyljelid stoarn)\nAs de spegel falt, dan gebeurt der hwat slims.\nAs de eksters skatterje op 't hiem komt der in roubrief.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25166,"r":"CJ052001","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At night a family suddenly hears a loud bang in the little hallway, though there is nothing to be seen. It is an omen: when the father of the house dies, the hallway has to be hacked away because the coffin cannot get through. If the noises are heard before midnight, the death will not be long in coming. If they are heard after midnight, it points to a death further in the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik noch by uzes thús yn 'e hûs wie hearden wy ris yn 'e nacht in hiele botte slach. Us hûs hie in hiel lyts bihyndich gonkje. 't Wie krekt as de slach dêr wei kom.\n\"Hwat is dat?\" sei heit. Wy hearden it allegearre. De houn blafte. Heit wie doe al net rjocht goed, mar hy gong der ôf om to sjen. Der wie neat. Heit gong wer op bêd.\nHeit woarde minder en minder en hy kom op 't lêst to forstjerren.\nDoe moest er yn 'e kiste. Mar sy koenen de swaei net krije yn 't lytse gonkje. Der moest rûmte foar makke wurde. It gonkje moest der út slein wurde.\nDat woarde dien. En doe hearden wy presys itselde lûd as dy nachts.\nHeart men it lûd fóár tolwe ûre, dan duorret it koart. \nHeart men it lûd nei tolwe ûre, dan duorret it lang.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25169,"r":"CJ052004","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People have had a premonitory vision of two people drowning. The vision has not yet come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Blaudobbe to Houtigehage ha guon sjoen dat twa fordrinke soenen. Mar it is oan diz tiid ta net gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25211,"r":"CJ052308","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man sees a dead little child lying on a chair. It is a premonitory vision: a few days later a little child dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining fan Boelensloane fortelde my ris: \"Ik kom us in kear thús, doe hie 'k nei de faem ta west. 't Wie moai ljocht-moanne-waer.\nMem hie 't glês sa'n eintsje yn 'e hichte. Myn ierpeltsjes stienen waerm op 'e kachel.\nDoe't ik yn 'e hûs kom, stienen der in pear stuollen yn 'e hoeke, mei in lekken der op.\nIk gong sitten. Doe't ik it iten op hie, seach ik oer de stuollen hinne. Dêr lei in dea berntsje op. Op dat wite lekken.\nIn pear dagen letter wie der in berntsje fan uzes dea.\nIk ha op 'e stuollen fan 'e geasten sitten to iten.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25223,"r":"CJ052404","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman repeatedly sees a scantily dressed man walking to the water. It is a premonitory vision: shortly afterwards an alcoholic drowns himself. The alcoholic is dressed only in his underclothes.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Beppe werkte in bult yn 't werkhûs yn Grinzer Pein.\nHja hie fan tofoaren al in pear kear sjoen dat der ien nei 't wetter ta gong. Dat wie in djip baggelgat. De gedaente dy't dêr hinne gong wie ljocht yn 'e klean.\nOp in kear kom beppe wer by 't werkhûs, doe wie dêr in man fuort. Hy wie net to finen. Hy wie yn 'e ûnderklean fuort gong, hwant de boppeklean hongen noch oer de stoel.\nDoe sei beppe fuortdaliks: \"Ik kin jim wol sizze hwer't er is. By 't djippe gat. Gean dêr mar hinne.\"\nDoe't se der kommen stienen syn beide klompen oan 'e kant.\nHy hie him dêr forsûpt. It wie in drankman.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25271,"r":"CJ052701","p":"Ons Belang","v":"Utr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman predicts a drowning from a voice coming out of the water. The prediction has not yet come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Boelensloane ha jo de Popke-poel. Dêr swommen de jonges simmers wol yn. Flak dêrby wenne in widdou: âlde Elske. Dy helle altyd wetter út dy poel. Sy sei dan tsjin 'e jonges: \"Jimme meije wol oppasse, hwant hjir sil nochris ien yn 'e poel fordrinke; 'k ha de stem heard.\"\n't Is oant nou ta noch net gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25335,"r":"CJ053305","p":"Ons Belang","v":"Utr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a barn owl sits on the roof, a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der woarde altyd sein, as der in katûle op it dak siet, dan stoar der mei koarten ien yn dat hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25336,"r":"CJ053306","p":"Ons Belang","v":"Utr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When the dog howls eerily, a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de houn spûkgûlt stjert der ien. Wy ha der wol om út bêd west, sa binaud wienen wy, as wy dat nachts hearden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25361,"r":"CJ053401","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":25423,"r":"CJ053808","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When magpies chatter in the garden by the house, a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters op 'e tún by hûs skatterje, dan komt der in sterfgefal.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25463,"r":"CJ054402","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One night the narrator's daughter saw all kinds of bustling people in the house. It is a premonitory vision: when the daughter drowns fourteen days later, the house is swarming with people.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha in dochter forlern, dy tsjinne yn Ljouwert. Dy is dêr forsûpt.\nOp in joun kaem se thús, hjir by ús yn 'e Harkema. Dat wie sahwat in fjirtsjin dagen foardat se stoar. De oare moarns sei se: \"Mem, 't wie hjir fannacht sa drok yn 'e hûs. 't Wienen allegear minsken.\"\nIk tocht fuort oan foartjirmerij en sei: \"Dû hiest sjen matten.\"\nSy sei: \"Ik ha sjoen, mar ik koe neat sjen.\"\nDat hat it folk west, dat by ús kom, doe't wy hearden dat se forsûpt wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25465,"r":"CJ054404","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A boy cannot get into his house through the front door. When he manages to open the front door three quarters of an hour later, he sees someone opening the door of the room. The light in the back of the house is also on. It is a premonitory vision: the men were undertaker's assistants. A week later the boy's sister dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sahwat in wike foar har dea kom myn soan Geart op in joun thús. (Geart wennet hjir nou flak achter ús.) Hy woe ta de foardoar yn, en de doar siet los, mar hy koe der net yn komme. Wit hoe lang prebearre hy it, mar it woe net.\nDoe is er bûten op 'e gjersrichel sitten gong. Wol trije kertier hat er dêr sitten. Hy kom by de faem wei.\nHy tocht, de jonges ha my tofiter (syn bruorren). Mar op 't lêst kom hy der yn.\nDoe gong krekt de keamersdoar iepen. Noait liker as stapte der ien út. Mar hy seach neat. En 't ljocht brânde yn 't achterhús.\nIt hat foartjirmerije west. Dy't ta de keamersdoar útgongen wienen de beide biklaeijers","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25658,"r":"CJ056109","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, there will be a death. Also when a lot of rooks or magpies come into the yard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt krijt men in sterfgefal.\nAs der in hoop roeken of eksters op 't hiem komme, ek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25878,"r":"CJ057512","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Some people have heard a voice calling for help from the Leeuwenpoel. People think that someone will drown in it some day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Harkema ha guon in stem út 'e Liuwe-poel roppen heard: Help! De hiting is, dat dêr noch ien yn fordrinke mat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":129961,"r":"VODA_029_05","p":"Zalk","v":"Ov.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman waits at the door of her house for her husband. She is expecting her first child and is enjoying the lovely evening. Suddenly she sees a large grey animal. She does not know what kind of animal it is. It looks like a donkey or a dog, but it is neither. She suddenly feels quite unwell and cold.\nLater, lying in bed, the woman still does not feel well, and after a while her baby is born far too early.\nHer husband buries the baby. When the woman asks where he buried it, it turns out he buried it exactly at the spot where the animal had gone.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Mien opoe die g’leub’n ook in veurteek’ns. Ze hef ‘r ook heel wat gezien, verschillende ding’n. En zo hef ze ook mee’emaakt, toen ze de eerste keer in verwachting was, toen woonde ze an de Spiekerboersweg, heel eenzaam, op Kampevene. ’s Oab’ns, ’t was mooi weer, zie stond eens buut’n te kiek’n. Heure man die zou gauw weer koom’n. Zie dacht: och, Evert kump wel [?] an. ’t Was mooi weer, beetje nevelig over ’t land, hè. Zie stond rustig te’en de deur an en zie was blie dat ’t mooi weer was en det ze op heur man wacht’n en zie was blie met heur kindjien det ze verwacht’n. D’r was helemaal niks aan de hand woar ze heur bezörgd over maakt’n. Ze had zich nie druk ’emaakt dan. Zie stond doar gewoon rustig te kiek’n. Toen dacht ze: huh, wat heur ik doar? Wind is d’r nie. ’t Is net of d’r geritsel beej de struuk’n is. Toen keek ze opzie en een groot, gries dier kwam op heur af. Net zoals een soort ezel, zeg ze. ’t Was geen ezel en ’t was geen hond, maar ’t leek toch zowat. Zie wus neet wat veur dier dat was. En zie waar’n kold en griezelig. Zie wus zelf niet wat dat was. Zie most heur vasthold’n aan de deure. Och, dacht ze, as Evert noe maar kwam, want wat mut ‘k noe toch. En zie gink weer in huus. Heure man die kwamp weer, die zeg: “Klaasie, wat scheelt-e toch? Wat is d’r toch gebeurd? Wat kiek-ie toch naar uut.”\n“Och,” zeg ze, “ik weet ’t niet. Zal mie wel wat verbeeld heb’n. Goa maar","l":"Sallands"},{"n":46281,"r":"WEV017802","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A light moving around a house in the evening must be an omen.","i":"F.W.","o":"Schoonmoetje har meer van dei meroakels.\nZai laggen n keer in t daip hier in de buurte. t Oal mens stait s oams op dek en zugt dat er n licht beweegt noar en van t huus van Teelkemeu. Zai moakt dr uut op, dat et wat veurspelt. En t oal kreeg gliek ook, want olle Teelke is overleedn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46290,"r":"WEV018002","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Seeing by moonlight a black figure walking to a house where someone later dies.","i":"F.W.","o":"Zwaarde gedoante.\nDei har oal Beernd zain. Beernddei har boetn stoan te kiekn en toun zag hai bie moan licht n zwaart geval aankomen. De gedoante was n dam indraaid, achter t huus hen loopn en wieder wos Beernd nait, wat of dr gebeurd was.\nWel kon e verteln, dat er in dat hoes staarfgeval komen was. Nait laange tied doarnoa.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46296,"r":"WEV018008","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"All that remains of superstition is fear of howling dogs and chattering magpies, which foretell a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Van alle biegeleuf dat er west het, is allain dit overbleevn, dat er nog gounend schrik hebben veur n janknde hond of veur schetternde oksters. Dat gef t n dode.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46299,"r":"WEV018103","p":"Weiteveen","v":"Dr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"How second sight is passed from dog to human and vice versa.","i":"F.W.","o":"Kwaad zien.\nIn de buurte was een jonge vent, die kwaad zien kon. Meestal siend et ollere mensen, die et kunt, maar dizze vent was er al vrog bie. s Nachts liep hie uut bedde om te zien of er n dode wegdraagn wur op de waagn.\nZien oln vunden dat arg beroerd. Ze vroegen mie, hoe of ze daar met aan moestn. Ik zee: “Hoe is die jongen dr aan komen?”\nSie zeggen: ‘Hij heft n hond, die zat te jankn, tuskn de oorn deur keekn en toen is de kunst op hum overgaan; nou kan e zien, waar n staarfgeval kumpt.”\nIk zeg: “Dan is er maar ien middel; hij mut nou veur n jankende hond staan gaan en dan mut die hond over de jong zien oorn kieken. Dan giet de kunst weer op de hond over.”\nDat hebben ze daan. De jong keek op n keer naar n huus, waar n dode komen zol en toen hebben ze de hond achter hum neer zet zodat ie over de vent zien oorn kiekn mus.\nToen was de jongen ervan verlost en de hond had et weer.","l":"Drents"},{"n":46300,"r":"WEV018104","p":"Weiteveen","v":"Dr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Seeing father painting a small coffin at night is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of what later really happens.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik heb ook es wat zien. t Was op n nacht. Ik mus eevn van bedde um te pissen en toen zag ik mien voar in de kamer zitn. Hij zat bie de tafel mit n ding veur zuch, waar ie aan zat te prutsn.\nIk zee: “Wat moakt ie daar?” Moar hij zee niks. Ik vun t wel gek, want hij waarkte s nachts anders niet.\nn Paar maand later wur mie alles dudelk. Toen zat ie werkeliek aan de tafel; de eerste keer was et veurgezicht west; dat merkte ik de andere dag, want vaor zee, dat ie er s nachts niet uut west was. \nNa die paar maand dan zat ie n liekkissie te varven veur n kind uut de buurte. Et kissien stun veur hum op de toafel.\nEn ie muik dezulfde beweegns, die ‘k in die nacht zien had.","l":"Drents"},{"n":46302,"r":"WEV018202","p":"Barger-Oosterveld","v":"Dr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Newborn black cats and dogs are killed, because they have to do with the devil and bring bad luck. Black animals that have been allowed to live foretell evil.","i":"F.W.","o":"Zwaart. \nAlles wat zwaart was, mos dood. Dat wil zegn, pasgeboorn jonge katn en honden; zai harn ja wat mit duvel te moakn en zoln ongeluk brengen. As dr toch nog zwaarde daiern overbleevn, den was t zaok, da-je ze nait teegn kwamen. Op zo’n dag mozzen ie op kwoad reekn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":21352,"r":"CJ026101","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a woman died, a neighbour said that she had already heard a dog howling eerily by the back of the house that week.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ús buorfrou stoar, sei ien fan ús buorlju: \"Fan 'e wike ha 'k de houn sa bot spûkgûlen heard by harren achterhûs, dat doe wist ik wol dat it gau ôfrinne soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25582,"r":"CJ055505","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman had lost two children in a short time. She still had a son and a daughter left. She asked her sister to take care of her son soon. She would die soon, and her daughter too. That is how it turned out.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Drachtster Kompenije wenne in frou, dy hie yn in koartstondige tiid twa bern forlern. It minske sukkele sels. Twa bern hie se oerhâlden, in jonge en in famke.\nDoe wienen dy beide bern us oan 't boartsjen by 't sângat.\n't Frommes dy't it my fortelde wie in suster fan dy frou.\nHja hie tsjin dy suster sein: \"Nou is dat sjesa. Ik bin hjir net lang mear. Kinstû dan op 't jonkje passe?\"\n\"Dû mei dyn jonkje,\" hie har suster sein, \"der is ommers ek in famke.\"\n\"Ik bin hjir net lang mear\", hie se sein. \"Ik ha 't sjoen. 't Lytse famke boartet nòu noch, mar 't is hjir mei fjirtsjin dagen net mear.\"\nDy suster hie sa forbouwereard west, dat se wie fuort nei hûs ta gong.\nNei in fjirtsjin dagen wie 't famke stoarn en fuort dêrnei it minske sels.\n't Wie krekt sa neikom lyk as hja sein hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25628,"r":"CJ055905","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One night a man heard a dog howling eerily in front of a house. Shortly afterwards someone in that house died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In âld man yn Sumar hearde yn 'e nacht in houn spûkgûlen foar in doar. Hy sei: \"Hjir stjert yn 't koart ien.\" Dat wie ek útkom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25629,"r":"CJ055906","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man once saw a funeral in advance. He predicted that a black and a white horse would pull the wagon, which went against custom. It came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dyselde man seach ek in bigraffenis fan tofoaren. Hy sei: \"Der rint in wyt en in swart hynder foar de wein.\" Dat leauden se net, hwant dat gong tsjin 't gebrûk yn. Mar 't kòm wol sa út.\nTroch omstandichheden moest der in wyt hynder by.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25676,"r":"CJ056209","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, someone is dying.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":25709,"r":"CJ056404","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"An old woman warned her daughter not to step on the black ribbon. The daughter saw no ribbon at all. A week later the old woman was sitting outside and again saw a black ribbon. Another week later she died. The black ribbon was the funeral procession. She had seen it in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem siet by myn suster. Doe wie se al âld en minnichjes. Sy seach nei in plak op 'e flier en sei: \"Tink der om, net op dy swarte lint traepje.\"\n\"Is dêr dan in swart lint?\" frege myn suster.\n\"Ja,\" sei se, \"sjoch, dat rint nei 't finster ta en dêr giet it by op.\"\nMar myn suster seach neat.\nIn wike letter siet mem yn 't sintsje bûtendoar. Doe hie se 't ynienen wer oer 't swarte lint. \"Sjoch,\" sei se, \"dêr is it, it komt fan 't finster en it giet dy kant út.\" En sy wiisde nei de kant fan 't tsjerkhôf.\nDe wyks dêrop is se stoarn. De kiste koe yn 'e hûs de swaei net krije, doe moest it finster omheech skoud wurde.\nIt swarte lint dat wie de lykstaesje. Dy hie hja fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25760,"r":"CJ056801","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People once heard cries for help from the Leeuwenpoel. It is said that someone is still bound to drown there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Liuwepoel hearden se in kear 'help' roppen. Dêr mat altyd noch ien yn fordrinke, is 't sizzen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25837,"r":"CJ057215","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man always saw funeral processions in advance. Because of this he always knew who would die and what the procession would look like. Once people wanted to keep his prediction from coming true by harnessing a different horse to the wagon. But that animal refused, and then the horse the man had predicted would pull it was put in front after all.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Westergeast wenne in famyljelid fan my, dy seach ek alles fan tofoaren. Hy fortelde altyd hwa't der stjerre soe. Hwant hy seach de hiele lykstaesje. Hy sei dan, sokke hynders komme der foar, en alsa mear.\nDoe seinen se us op in kear: \"Nou sil 't us net sa gebeure as hy it forteld hat. Wy sille der in oar hynder foar spanne.\" En dat ha se dien. Mar it gebeurde wòl sa't hy it sjoen hie. It hynder dat se der foarspanden woe net lûke. Doe moest it oare der wol foar. Dat hie h_ sjoen. 't Kaem wòl krekt sa út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25841,"r":"CJ057219","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If you dream of fish at night, someone in the house will die soon. If you dream in the second half of the night, it will be a while before someone dies. If you dream in the first half of the night, it will happen soon.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As jo yn 'e nacht fan fisk drome, dan stjert der mei koarten ien yn 'e húshâlding.\nDroomt men it yn 'e neinacht dan duorret it noch in lang skoft. Droomt men it yn 'e foarnacht, dan gebeurt it al gau.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25897,"r":"CJ057609","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man once heard a bang, but his son had heard nothing. Some time later the son died. When a relative took one more look into the coffin, he was so startled that he let the lid fall shut with a bang. The same bang the father had heard earlier.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Douwe was ook us in kear met syn seun Fokke in 't heidefjild oan 't sodesteken. Ynienen hoorde hij in klap.\nHij sei teugen Fokke: \"God, Fokke, wat is dat?\"\n\"Wat bedoelt heit?\" sei Fokke.\n\"Hestou die klap niet hoard?\"\n\"Ik hè niks hoard\", sei Fokke.\nDie seun Fokke kwam in skoftsje letter te sterven.\nDe broer fan olle Douwe kwam op 'e begraffenis. Hy wou Fokke nog 's even sien. Doe liet hy fan skrik it deksel fan 'e kist falle.\nDat was dieselfde klap, die Douwe hoord het op it heidefjild.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25903,"r":"CJ057704","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If someone dreams about fish, there will soon be a death in the family.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der froeger fan fisken droomd woarde, dan kom der yn 't koart in sterfgefal yn 'e famylje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25929,"r":"CJ057808","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A young couple once saw a great light on the way back. When she got home the girl asked her father why the light was on. The father said the light was not on, and that if she had seen a great light anyway, it was an omen. Four weeks later the man was dead.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Frou van der Molen - hjir út 'e Pein - en har earste man wienen us op in joun fuort west to praten. 't Wie hjir achter yn 'e Juliana-buert. Sy wienen noch net troud. Doe stienen se ynienen yn 't ljocht. Sy wienen noch net oan hûs ta.\nDoe't se thús kommen sei se tsjin har heit: \"Hwerom ha jim de lampe sa heech brânnen?\"\nDoe sei har heit: \"Wy ha de lampe net op hawn. Mar astû hjir in ljocht sjoen hast, dan gebeurt der aenst hwat.\"\nFjouwer wiken letter wie har heit dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25969,"r":"CJ058104","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man had been born with a caul. One Sunday he heard a child calling for help from the water, but there was nothing to be seen. Later someone drowned at that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw in man kend, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. 't Wie in sekere de Wilde. Op in snein hearde hy ûnder Lippenhuzen dat dêr in bern raesde. \"Der gebeurt hwat\", tocht er. \"Ik tink dat der ien forsûpt is.\" Hy der hinne to sjen, mar hy woarde neat gewaer. En doch hied er heard dat ien 'help!' rôp.\nLetter wie dêr op dat plak ien fordronken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25971,"r":"CJ058106","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At a certain spot people sometimes heard a terrible racket and strange noises. Later a man stabbed his wife to death at that spot. Then the same noises could be heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Grins haw ik wenne oan 'e Fryske strjitwei. Dêr doochde it net op dat buertsje. De buorlju kommen by my, omdat ik net bang wie. It wie dêr net plús, en sy woenen ha, ik soe der op ôfgean.\nIt wie nachts noait liker as woarde der ien formoarde. It wie in lawaei! En rare gelûden, freeslik! De hiele buert wie der fan oerstjûr. De lûden kommen út 'e púnhopen wei.\nIk ha mei Sjouke Hoekstra dêr in hiele nacht wekke. \nIk hearde neat, 't bleau hyltyd rustich. Mar letter kommen dy lûden wer.\nLetter hat dêr in man syn frou delstutsen. Hy hat har formoarde. Doe hearden se deselde lûden.\nMar doe't dat gebeurd wie, wie 't foargoed dien. It hat foartjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26119,"r":"CJ059011","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, a death will come. One day a dog would not stop howling eerily. Shortly afterwards the woman of the house died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt, dan komt der in deaden. Ik ha 't sels fan ûnderfining. Wy hienen in houn dy hiet fan Bruno.\nDy siet op in dei hyltyd to spûkgûlen. Hy hâldde mar noait op. \"Dy forrekte houn\", sei 'k.\nEven letter stoar mem oan in hartforlamming.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26178,"r":"CJ059407","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, it hears a corpse coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wyt noch wol, doe't ik in bern wie hearde ik us in houn spûkgûlen. Ik sei tsjin heit: \"Hwat is dat?\"\nHeit sei: \"Dy houn sjocht in lyk oankommen. Dêrom gult er.\"\n\"O heit, as dat mar net ien fan ús is\", sei ik doe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26199,"r":"CJ059609","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man who was born with a caul foresaw that his own daughter would drown. He also saw a train accident between Westereinde and Buitenpost. But that did not happen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Knjillis Veenstra wenne hjir oan 't spoar. Hy is mei de helm geboaren. Hy hat sjoen dat syn eigen dochter fordronk.\nMar hy hat ek sjoen dat der in trein forûngelokke tusken de Westerein en Bûtenpost. Mar dat is net gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26211,"r":"CJ059701","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man who was born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. He foresaw funerals, and it always turned out just as he had seen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Opperkoaten wenne in man, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest der nachts soms ôf en dan wie er hiele nachten fuort.\nDe frou lei dan allinne op bêd. Hy seach dan de bigraffenissen fan tofoaren. 't Kom altyd krekt sa nei as hy it sjoen hie.\nSyn frou hat it my sels forteld. Syn namme wie Gauke Haarsma. Hy wie gâns alder as de frou. Hja hiet fan Ankje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26300,"r":"CJ060605","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Dogs with spots above their eyes are eerie howlers that foretell death by their howling.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hounen mei stippen boppe de egen binne spûkgûlers. As se oan 't spûkgûlen binne komt der in deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26308,"r":"CJ060802","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, a death will follow.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":26842,"r":"CJ061304","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman sees in her dream a black woman in rain clothes, after which a death follows in the family or the neighbourhood.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wienen guon dy seagen yn har droom swarte froulju. Dat wienen froulju yn regenkleden. Dan kom der letter in sterfgefal yn 'e famylje of yn 'e omgeving.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26852,"r":"CJ061403","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A molecatcher is once working away from home near Almelo and is in no mood for it. A couple of magpies keep chattering around him, and that day he gets a telegram saying his father is very ill and he must come home. The magpies were the harbingers.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik molle froeger gauris. 'k Wie op in kear fan hûs, ik siet yn 'e buert fan Almelo. Dy deis hie 'k gjin sin oan moljen. It wie krekt as drukte my hwat.\nDer kommen in pear eksters by my, dy skatteren hyltyd om my hinne. De jouns krige ik in tillegram. Myn heit wie slim siik, ik moest thúskomme. De eksters wienen de boaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26897,"r":"CJ061708","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Someone once said that a girl would drown in a pool, but this never came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wie in dobbe, en dêr woarde altyd fan sein, dat dêr noch ris in fanke yn fordrinke soe - ien hie dat ris sjoen -, mar dat is net útkom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27136,"r":"CJ063803","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Someone foresees a funeral. Later there is a death in Pein. He gets out of bed to see hearses.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon sjogge fantofoaren in bigraffenis. Doe't der ris ien stoarn [wie] yn 'e Pein, sei Bearn v.d. Woude: \"'k Ha 't tiden fan tofoaren al sjoen.\" Bearn moest nachts fan bêd ôf om lykstaesjes to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27137,"r":"CJ063804","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In Parken there is a deep peat pit. A man from the workhouse foretells that he has seen someone drown, and three weeks later it happens.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn 'e Parken wie in djippe klyndobbe. In man fan it wurkhús sei: \"Hjir forsûpt nochris ien, ik ha 't sjoen.\"\nTrije wiken letter fordronk dêr ien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27154,"r":"CJ063821","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, someone dies within three days.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlet, komt der binnen trije dagen in deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27241,"r":"CJ064314","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Wibe Alma loses his eighteen-year-old brother Paulus, and a man from Harkema had already foreseen this funeral.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanheit (Wibe Alma) hat in broer forlern fan achttsjin jier (Paulus). Der wie in man yn 'e Harkema, dy hat de hiele bigraffenis fan tofoaren sjoen yn alle bysûnderheden. Hy sei it fan tofoaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27272,"r":"CJ064412","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Auntie lives in Houtigehage and is ill and old. One night a dog comes to howl eerily at her house and will not be chased away. Shortly afterwards Auntie dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Muoike wenne yn 'e Houtigehage. Hja wie siik en âld. Sy hie linnen op 'e bleek lizzen. Doe kom dêr dy nachts in houn by to spoekgûlen. Se jagen de houn fuort, mar it dier kom like linich wer op itselde plak. En 't gong wer op in spoekgûlen. Even dêrnei is muoike stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27273,"r":"CJ064413","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Chattering magpies around the house mean that there will soon be a death in that house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der eksters om 't hûs hinne skatteren, dat bitsjutte ek, dat der yn dat hûs mei gauwens ien stjerre soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27310,"r":"CJ064611","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, someone who lives nearby will soon die. It usually takes about three days.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt stjert der gau ien dy't tichteby wennet.\nGewoanlik duorret it in dei of trije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27325,"r":"CJ064909","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily or the magpies chatter, someone will die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Als een hond spûkgûlt of de eksters skatteren komt der in dode.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27348,"r":"CJ065105","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, someone will die soon.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn bigjint to spûkgûlen kin men der mar fan op oan dat der mei koarten dêr ien forstjert.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27354,"r":"CJ065111","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If you see a funeral procession at night, someone will die. If it happens after midnight, it may still take a while. It is just the same with wild lanterns and with hammering.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sjocht men in lykstaesje foar middernacht, dan komt der gau in deaden. Sjocht men it nei middernacht, dan kin 't noch in hiel set duorje.\nSa is 't ek mei wylde lantearnen en ek mei timmerjen ensa.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27373,"r":"CJ065201","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The little brother of a girl who had just died heard the coffin being brought. But in reality there was nothing. Only an hour later did the coffin really come. The boy heard exactly the same sounds again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn âldste suster wie twa jier âlder as ik. Sy stoar.\nMyn broer en ik leinen op bêd. Krekt in ûre foardat se de kiste foar myn suster brochten, hearde ik tige klear en dúdlik dat se 't hynder by ús útsloegen. De izeren sile foel op 'e groun. 't Wie jouns. Doe hearde ik dat se hwat tilden en dat yn 'e hûs brochten.\n\"Dêr binne se\", sei 'k tsjin myn broer.\n\"Hwat ding?\" sei myn broer, \"ik hear neat.\"\n\"Sy bringe de kiste\", sei 'k. Mar myn broer fornom der neat fan. Ik hearde alles klear en dúdlik.\nIt wie in ûre letter, doe gebeurde 't allegear presys sa. 't Wie doe noch yn 'e tiid fan 'e boereplicht. Buorman hie de kiste helle mei hynder en wein en brocht him dy jouns by ús yn 'e hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27395,"r":"CJ065302","p":"Rohel","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"On his way back in the dark, a young man once saw a hearse. He stepped over it. Two weeks later an old fellow from the neighbourhood died, and the hearse really came by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik kom us op in kear fan Hiltsjemuoiwâlden fan 'e froulju.\nIk roan it Wyldpaed lâns op wei nei hûs ta. 't Wie yn 'e nacht. Doe stapte ik ynienen yn in gat. Ja, 't wie in gat en ek wer gjin gat. Ik stapte oer in lykwein hinne.\nAchter wie 't heger, ik stapte der yn del. 't Wie in boerewein. Dêr woarden doe de minsken noch mei nei 't hôf brocht.\nTwa wiken letter stoar dêr in âld keardel. Dy woarde dêr lânsbrocht nei 't baerhúske ta.\n't Hie foartsjirmerij west. Ik ha 't der twa dagen fan yn 'e rêch hawn, fan dy stap yn 'e bidelte.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27480,"r":"CJ066101","p":"Frieschepalen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, someone from the neighbourhood will soon die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt kin men mar in sterfgefal forwachtsje, dêr flak by.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38675,"r":"CJ066209","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The eerie howling of a dog announces a death.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":27494,"r":"CJ066406","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A magpie once came to the sister of a sick woman. Then it turned out that the sick woman had died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn mem har suster yn Stiensgea - Klaske-muoi - wie tige siik.\nHja hie longûntsteking. Mem wie neat net bygelovich.\nDer komt in ekster oanfleanen by ús mem. Dy komt tsjin 't sydgleske oan. Doe blykte dat har suster overleden wie. De ekster wie de boade fan 'e dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38661,"r":"CJ066502","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When the dogs begin to howl eerily, a death will soon follow.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de hounen bigounen to spûkgûlen, dan soe 't net lang mear duorje as der kom in deaden yn 'e buert.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27522,"r":"CJ066611","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, someone will soon die. When a barn owl screeches, someone will also die soon.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt giet der mei gauwens ien dea, wurdt der altyd sein, en 't komt ek wol faek út. As in katûle earmoedich raest, komt der èk gau in deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27553,"r":"CJ066905","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At a sick woman's bedside the ticking of a watch was heard, though there was no clock at all. It was an omen; that night the woman died. This was called a wild watch.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik noch faem wie moest ik faek oppasse by in minske dat swier siik wie. Der siet ek in kear in frou by. Dy frou sei tsjin my: \"Hearst it wol, der tikket hyltyd in horloazje. Nou duorret it net lang mear.\"\nEn dochs wie der gjin horloazje. Men neamt dat in wyld horloazje.\nDeselde nachts noch is it sike minske stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27575,"r":"CJ067108","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Douwe Stavasius (born with a caul) once foretold to a mother that her child would soon die. Within three weeks the child died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear doe siet Douwe Stavasius by ús. Der stie op it hiem in buorfrou mei in lyts bern op 'e earm. Hy sei tsjin har: \"Ja, Janke, dû silst net lang mear mem fan dat bern wêze.\" Binnen trije wiken wie it bern dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27685,"r":"CJ068304","p":"Noordwijk","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People once saw a little light above a fen and thought that someone might drown in it one day. But that has not happened yet.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen op Uleflecht ûnder Sumar. Achter ús wie in poel. Wy seagen us in kear ljochtsjes flak boven dy poel. Doe seinen se: \"Dêr sil wol ien fordrinke matte.\" Mar 't is by myn witen noait gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27688,"r":"CJ068307","p":"Noordwijk","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, someone will die soon. When magpies make a racket, that also means someone will die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In houn dy't spûkgûlt sjocht in lyk fan tofoaren.\nAs eksters bot tokear gean bitsjut dat ek in dea-tiding.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27706,"r":"CJ068503","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When magpies chatter close to a house, a death will follow. The same goes for when a dog howls eerily.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters skatterje tichte by in hûs, dan komt dêr in sterfgefal. Spûkgûlt dêr in houn, dan is it krektengelyk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27794,"r":"CJ069113","p":"Franeker","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, someone will die soon.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As hounen spûkgûle s[t]jert der mei gauwens ien. Dat is algemien bekend. Dêr leauwe se hjir ek oan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27815,"r":"CJ069402","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Every evening a dog howled eerily in front of the house of people with a sick baby. After a few days the baby died. The howling had been an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir tichteby stie in hûs, dêr wennen minsken yn, dy hienen in popke. Dat wie tige siik. Elkenien koe sjen dat it net goed kom. Dat popke rekke wei.\nAl in pear jounen fan tofoaren gong dêr in âld houn nei dat hûs ta en dy siet dêr de hiele joun foar dat hûs to spookgûlen. Se jagen him fuort, mar even letter wie hy der wer en dan gong 't wer op in spookgûlen.\nDoe stoar it popke. Dat spookgûlen fan 'e houn wie 't foarteken der fan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27859,"r":"CJ069811","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Mermaids can sing very beautifully. If a skipper saw a mermaid, the ship would be wrecked. They lure sailors into the sea so that they drown.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sémearminnen koenen moai sjonge. As de skipper ien seach forgong 't skip. Sy lokken de manlju yn sé. Dan fordronken dy.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27873,"r":"CJ070001","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If sailors see a mermaid, the ship will meet with an accident.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in sémearmin har fortoant, dan gebeurt der in ûngelok op 't skip.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27974,"r":"CJ070802","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman could always tell from the ticking of the clock that someone would die that week.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As ik yn Westergeast by myn dochter útfanhûzje, en de klok fan 'e toer let, dan gebeurt it faek dat ik siz: Hark, nou wurdt der fan 'e wike ien op 't hôf brocht. It mist my noait. Ik hear it oan 'e klank fan 'e klok. Hjir yn 'e Koaten hear ik it trouwens krekt like goed. It sit him net yn 'e klok, hwant in oar heart it net. It sit him yn my sels. Ik haw it net fan fremd. Pake - ús mem har heit - hie 't ek. Ik wit sa skoan dat pake soms sei: \"Hark\" - hwannear't de klok lette. Dan wisten wy wol dat der wer ien op 't hôf komme soe.\nNet ien fan myn bern dy't soks hat. Mar ìk haw in bernsbern, dêr bin 'k wol hast wis fan, dat dy 't ek heart.\nIk hie 't al doe't ik sa'n famke wie. Jo wurde der mei geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28040,"r":"CJ071305","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Before someone died, a man sometimes saw a funeral procession pass by. He then knew that he would soon have to ring the bells again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie in suster, dy wie net goed. Hja wie sawntjin jier. Doe reizge heit op in kear nei Joast Wiersma yn Jistrum om guod foar har. Ik gong mei. Wy gongen mei de hounekarre.\nDoe soenen wy op 'e weromreis yn 'e Boelensloane mei de karre om 'e hoeke, doe sei heit tsjin my: \"Gean even fan 'e karre ôf, Jel.\" It wie by de hulzene hage. De karre moest even oan kant, en de houn moest sa lang stean bliuwe.\nEven letter sei heit: \"Gean nou mar wer sitten.\" Heit hie in lykstaesje sjoen. Mar ik seach neat.\nDoe't heit thús kom, sei er tsjin ús mem: \"Nou mat ik ek noch klokliede yn 't koart.\" (Heit wie ek kloklieder)\nIt wie in frommeske, dat stoar, in sekere Havenga. Heit hat de klok let. Hja kaem yn 't Surhústerfean op 't hôf.\nHeit hie 't wol faker dat er fan tofoaren lykstaesjes seach.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28084,"r":"CJ071708","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, someone will die soon.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem sei altyd as der in houn oan 't spûkgûlen wie koe men der mar fan op oan dat der in deaden op 'e buert kom. Der binne nòch in hiele protte lju dy't dat leauwe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28085,"r":"CJ071709","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a magpie comes to the window, someone will die. If a magpie chatters in the yard, that also means something is about to happen, but it need not be something unpleasant. It can also announce a birth.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in ekster by 't glês komt bitsjut dat ek in deaden. De ekster is dan de boade. It is like folle as in roubrief. As in ekster op it hiem omskattert wol er ek in tiding bringe. Mar dan hoeft it net in minne tiding to wêzen.\nIn jier of hwat lyn skattere hjir ek in ekster om. Doe hie myn dochter in lytsen krigen. Dat wie 't nijs, dat er bringe woe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28145,"r":"CJ072003","p":"Burum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man had been born with a caul. Once he came to fetch a saw from his neighbour, when suddenly he could not walk any further. He said a corpse was passing by. A few days later the neighbour's father, who lived with his daughter, died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear kom Kees by de buorlju. Dêr moest er in sage weihelje. De frou stie yn 'e keamer. Doe't er omtrint oan har ta wie, koed er ynienen net fierder. Hy bleau stean.\n\"Hwerom bliuwe jo stean?\" frege hja.\nHy sei: \"Der moest my in lyk foarby.\"\nIn pear dagen letter stoar dy frou har heit, dy't by harren ynwenne. (Hy seach nachts faek bigraffenissen)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28154,"r":"CJ072101","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman was going home late one evening when she saw a black figure wearing a large cloak. He rattled the whole time. The next day the woman received word that her neighbour's child had died. The messenger was a man dressed entirely in black, with a cocked hat on and a large thing on his chest that rattled. What the woman had seen the evening before had been an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Lyske wenne op 'e Bulten yn 'e Harkema yn 'e Malmoune (een vierkant huis voor vier gezinnen). Dy wie by ús to praten, doe wennen wy op 'e Bulten. 't Wie al aerdich let op 'e joun, doe gong Lyske by ús wei, mar even letter, dêr wie se al wer. Wyt om 'e holle en alhiel fan 'e wize. Sy hie in swart ding sjoen mei in great kleed om. En dat rattele allegear.\nDoe haw ik har de jouns thús brocht.\nDe oare deis krige Lyske tiding dat har buorman syn bern wie overleden. 't Wie in boade dy't it har oansei, de man wie alhiel yn 't swart, mei in steek op en in great ding op it boarst - dat hie it ratteljen west. 't Wie foartjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28259,"r":"CJ073203","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If magpies come into someone's yard and start chattering, they bring news of death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters by jin op it hiem komme en dy bigjinne to skatterjen, dan bringe se in tiding fan 'e dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28278,"r":"CJ073222","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Where people used to see wild lanterns, new houses were later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr't se froeger yn Jobbegea wylde lantearnen seagen, kommen letter huzen to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28286,"r":"CJ073308","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If you dream of a horse, a death will follow.\nA man once dreamed of running horses. The following week a relative died. The horses in the dream had been the horses of the hearse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As jo fan in hynder drome, dan komt der in deaden. Ik lei op in kear op bêd. 't Wie midden yn 'e nacht. Ik hearde de hynders dúdlik rinnen. En ik seach se klear foar my. Ik seach se foar de doar lâns gean. Ik tocht: nou komt der hwat.\nDe oare wyks stoar it jonkje fan ús Piter. De hynders dy't ik sjoen en heard hie, wienen de hynders fan 'e lykkoets.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28287,"r":"CJ073309","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If you dream of a pike, a death will follow. The finer the fish, the closer the dead person is in the family. If you dream of a snake, you are keeping company with bad people.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As jo fan snoek drome dan komt der èk in deaden. Hwat moaijer de fisk is, hwat tichter de deade yn 'e famylje is.\nAs jo drome fan in slange, dan geane jo mei falske minsken om.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28330,"r":"CJ073906","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman heard footsteps outside at night and could not sleep because of them. Later that night her brother came to say that the little son of another relative had been run over by a milk cart. Ever since, the child's mother had been walking back and forth at that spot. Those were the footsteps the woman had heard all night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is nou krekt seis en tritich jier lyn. Wy wennen yn Koatstertille. Myn wiif koe dy nachts net sliepe. Sy sei: \"Der rint hyltyd ien om hûs hinne. Krekt as rint dyselde hoasfuotling.\" Hja hat de hiele nacht net slept.\nOm fjouwer ûre yn 'e moarn kom har broer by ús. Hy sei: \"Us Tryn en dy's jonkje is fannacht oerriden woarn troch in molkwein.\" 't Gebeurde yn 'e Omloop by Surhústerfean, yn in skipke. Doe't Tryn it hearde, roan se hyltyd mar hoasfuotling by 't skipke lâns.\nDat hat myn wiif dy nachts fornom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28376,"r":"CJ074210","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man once heard the barn owls calling. He predicted that the sick neighbour woman would die. That happened soon after.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy hienen in âld buorfrou, dat wie Minke. Dy wie siik. Op in kear sei heit: \"Hear dy katûle ris roppen. It komt net goed mei Minke.\" Heit krige gelyk. Minke is al gau dêrnei stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28377,"r":"CJ074211","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If the weight of the clock fell, it meant that someone would soon die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in gewicht fan 'e klok foel bitsjutte dat dat der yn 't koart in deaden komme soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28378,"r":"CJ074212","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Just before a boy died, lots of magpies had been sitting around his house. After his death the canary never sang again.\nWhen a man died, a cat kept wanting to sit on his coffin. Not long after, all the cats in the house died.\nIf a dog howls eerily, someone will soon die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foardat ús Marten stoarn is, wienen it allegearre eksters by ús om 'e doar hinne. Ik ha der doe gjin acht op slein, mar even letter hat hy it ûngelok krigen.\nDoe't Marten dea wie, hâldde de kanarje him stil. Hy hat nei dy tiid net wer sjonge wold.\nDoe't ús heit stoar, gong ien fan 'e katten by him op 'e kiste sitten. Jagen se him der wei, dan wie hy der even letter wer. Op 't lêst lieten se him mar sitte. Alle katten binne koart dêrnei stoarn. Spûkgûlt der in houn, dan stjert dêr yn dy buert ek ien mei gauwens.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28394,"r":"CJ074228","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Sometimes there was knocking behind the wallpaper. Then a death would come to the house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Soms woarde der achter 't bihang kloppe. Dan kom der in deaden yn 'e hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28443,"r":"CJ074715","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When the mermaids sing, a death will follow. A mermaid is half human, half fish.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de sémearminnen sjonge komt der stoarm. In sémearmin is heal minske, heal fisk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28449,"r":"CJ074721","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, there will soon be a death. Sometimes such a dog lies in front of the door of the person who is going to die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spokgûlt, is der in sterfgefal op til. Soms giet er lizzen foar de doar fan deselde, dy't gau stjerre sil. Wy ha 't faek meimakke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28476,"r":"CJ075306","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Mrs Wiersma of the Salvation Army was born with a caul and saw in advance her own daughter drowning in the water near Snits.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In frou, dy't wy wol kinne - sy is ek by 't Leger des heils - dy is èk mei de helm geboaren. Frou Wiersma is it. Sy hat fan tofoaren har eigen dochter fordrinken sjoen yn it wetter to Snits","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28479,"r":"CJ075309","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Old Black Jantjse was born with a caul and is a witch. Once, in the middle of a conversation, her face turns pale and she stares at a particular spot on the other side. She sees a corpse coming out of the door. The others do not believe it, because nobody is ill. Three weeks later someone in that house does indeed die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde swarte Jantsje wenne op it Fliet to Ljouwert. Dy koe mear as in oar. Sy wie mei de helm geboaren en sy seinen ek dat it in tsjoenster wie.\nOp in kear doe stie se mei lju to praten. Ynienen bilûkt har gesicht en sy sjocht nei in bipaeld plak oan 'e oare kant.\nDoe sei se: \"Sjoch, dêr komt in lyk ta de doar út.\"\nDe lju seinen: \"Dat is sa net. En 't kin èk net. Dêr is net ien siik.\"\nMar trije wiken letter stoar der ien yn dat hûs. Jantsje hie 't wòl goed sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28548,"r":"CJ075910","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Black Jantsje is doing her shopping in the shop and looks very closely at another woman. She always talks about the dead and funeral processions. When the woman has been served and walks out of the shop, Jantsje says she will be dead within three days. And so it is, for she falls down the stairs at the district court and dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Swarte Jantsje fan 't Fliet (to Ljouwert) stie us in kear yn 'e winkel. Sy moest boadskippen helje. Elkenien hie hwat in hekel oan har omdat se altyd fan dat nuvere praet hie oer liken en lykstaesjes ensa. Elkenien - de winkelman ek - hie mar leafst dat se sa gau mooglik wer fuort gong. Doe't se dêr dy moarns yn 'e winkel stie wie dêr ek in frou. Dy seach se in skoft tige opmerksum oan en doe kearde se har om.\n\"Hwat mat Jantsje ha?\" frege de winkelman - hy frege har foar har beurt om har mar kwyt to reitsjen.\nJantsje sei: \"Help dizze frou earst even.\" Dat wie it minske dêr't se sa nei sjoen hie.\n\"Ja, sjoch,\" sei se, doe't it minske der út wie, \"dat minske is binnen de trije dagen dea.\"\nBinnen de trije dagen wie se dea. (It minske wurke by 't kantongerjocht. Der bruts in roede fan 'e trap. Hja stroffele, foel by de trappen del en wie dea)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28561,"r":"CJ076012","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Willem Pyk has a dog that sometimes howls eerily. According to his wife Jits this is an omen of a death, while their neighbour thinks the dog is seeing the devil.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Willem Pyk (= Ophuis) hie in houn. Dy spûkgûlde soms. Dan sei Jits, syn wiif: \"Der giet wer ien dea.\" Har buorman sei, as de houn spûkgûlde: \"Dêr sjocht er de duvel, wer, Jits.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28783,"r":"CJ078903","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, someone will die. A chattering magpie brings news or foretells a death. According to father, magpies are witches dressed in black.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As hounen spûkgûle, komt der in deaden. As eksters skatterje bringe se nijs, of der komt in deaden. Heit wie bang foar de eksters, hy jaechde se fuort. 't Binne heksen, sei er, sy ha swart oan har en al hwat swart oan him hat, is forkeard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28875,"r":"CJ079601","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Father's grandmother is very ill, and once while she is sitting in a chair, a pigeon flies into the window outside and is killed. The woman says this is an omen of her death, and a few days later she dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit fortelde, syn beppe wenne to Westergeast. Hja wie tige siik. Op in kear doe wie hja fan bêd ôf en siet op 'e stoel. Doe kom dêr fan bûten in dou oanfleanen, dy fleach tsjin 't glês oan en wie dea.\nDoe hie 't âld-minske sein: \"Dat is in teken; it teken fan myn dea.\" In pear dagen letter stoar se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33668,"r":"CJ092507","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man once heard chopping in the back of the house. Shortly afterwards his wife died and straw was chopped to put in the coffin. Then he heard the same sound again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear hearde Likele de Hoop dúdlik dat der kapt woarde yn 't achterhús.\nFuort dêrnei kaem syn frou to forstjerren en doe kapten se op 't selde plak yn 't achterhús strie, om dat yn 'e kiste to lizzen. Dat wie krekt itselde lûd, dat er heard hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29306,"r":"CJ080502","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Early in her marriage, a woman once dreamed that she would have three children, all three of whom would die. After that she would have one more child, and that one would live. It came true exactly like that.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Skoanmem hat faek forteld, hja hie yn 't bigjin fan har trouwen droomd, dat sy soe trije bern krije en dy ek alle trije forlieze. Dan soe der letter noch in neikommerke geboaren wurde en dat soe libjen bliuwe. 't Is krektsa útkom. Dat neikommerke, dat is myn frou.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29332,"r":"CJ080607","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People once heard a sound coming from the water. A little later someone came driving along, ended up in the water and drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem hat wolris forteld, dat guon in lûd hearden dat út it wetter wei kom - dan moest der ien forsûpe.\nEven letter kom der ien oanriden en dy rekke yn 't wetter en forsûpte. Ik wyt net mear hwer't dat gebeurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29339,"r":"CJ080614","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, there will soon be a death in the neighbourhood.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt, komt der mei gauwens in deade op 'e buert. Ik ha 't sels meimakke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29410,"r":"CJ081204","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, there will soon be a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt, kin men der mar fan op oan dat der mei gauwens in deaden komt. Dat giet altyd troch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29414,"r":"CJ081304","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman once saw in advance a funeral procession with horses passing by, and so she knew that someone would die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e oarlochstiid is der in jonge forstoarn fan Atse fan der Heide fan Houtigehage. Skoanmem hie klear de lykwein fan tofoaren oankommen sjoen mei de hynders der foar. Hja wennen doe oan 't Spûkeloantsje ûnder Drachtster Kompenije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29419,"r":"CJ081309","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Dreaming of fish or of horses means a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As jo drome oer fisk of oer hynders, dan komt der in sterfgefal.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29422,"r":"CJ081403","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howled eerily, there would be a death within a short time. This was also the case if the clock made a different sound than usual.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us beppe wie der fêst fan oertsjûge, spûkgûlde der in houn, dan soe der gau ien stjerre.\nAs de klok hwat oars as oars lette, sei se: \"O, hwat liedt dy klok fremd, der wurdt gau wer ien bigroeven.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29445,"r":"CJ081514","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, a funeral procession will later pass by that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt, dan komt der letter in lykstaesje by dat plak lâns, dêr't de houn sit. Ik haw in minske kend, dêr spûkgûlde doe ek in houn. Hja wie bang dat it by har sels yn 'e hûs wêze soe, mar 't wie op in oar plak.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29463,"r":"CJ081704","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog sometimes howls eerily when someone is going to die. It then stands with its head towards the place where the funeral procession will pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In houn spûkgûlt soms as der ien stjerre sil. Dan stiet er mei de kop nei 't plak ta, dêr't de lykstaesje lâns giet.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32666,"r":"CJ082307","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a magpie sits on a fence post, a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Limburch seinen se: (Hoensbroek): As der in ekster op in hekkepealtsje komt to sitten, dan komt der in deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":207931,"r":"EGGEN002403","p":"Cadier en Keer","v":"L.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A black cat, a crow, a howling dog, or seeing a white horse is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"C.E.","o":"In C. en K. was 'n bepaalde boerderij, waar men via 'n voetpad langs de oven kwam. Kwam daar 'n zwarte kat uit, dan kon men rekenen op 'n sterfgeval in de familie. Hetzelfde gold voor 'n krijsende kraai, 'n huilende hond en 't zien van 'n wit paard."},{"n":32915,"r":"CJ084803","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A boy loved his dog Nero. But one evening he was terrified of the animal. It walked with its tail between its legs, and the boy would not let it into the house. The next day they found the animal lying dead on the tram track. The dog must have had a premonition, but why was the boy so afraid?","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear - 't wie de jouns let - kom ik thús fan 'e sjongforiening. Ik moest earst even nei de W.C., dy wie by de skuorre. Doe seach ik Nero dêr ús houn. Nero wie myn greatste freon altyd, mar doe't ik him op dat stuit seach, woarde ik deabinaud. Hy kom by my mei de sturt tusken de poaten. Ik doarst net nei him to sjen, sa bang wie 'k. Ik smiet de doar fan 't húske ticht, dat er mar net by my komme soe. Mem rôp my noch fan 't bêd ta: \"Mast de bûtendoar los litte, hwant heit en Hindrik matte noch thús komme. Dy binne nei de Pein, nei beppe ta.\"\nIk die de doar ticht, sa hurd ik koe en ik wie net earder rêstich as doe't ik goed en wol yn 'e hûs wie sûnder Nero. Der wie gjin better houn as Nero, en ek gjin goeder en trouwer dier. Moarns gongen wy altyd mei de hounekarre to melken en 't soe noait misse as dat earme dier stie al tusken de tiksels ús op to wachtsjen.\nMar de oare moarns wie Nero der net. Hoe't wy rôpen, der kom gjin antwurd. Doe sykje. En doe founen wy him dea lizzen op 'e trambaen. Hy wie troch de tram oanriden woarn.\nIt beest mat der grif in foargefoel fan hawn ha. Mar hoe koe it nou, dat ik sa bang wie foar it beest?","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33053,"r":"CJ086305","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If the rooks made a racket while people were working with the potatoes, it meant there would be a funeral. Likewise if the magpies chattered loudly.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de swarte roeken sa to kear gongen by it jirappeldollen op it lân dan komt der in bigraffenis. Ek as de eksters bot skatterje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33058,"r":"CJ086401","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One night a married couple saw that the pane had been taken out of the window in the front wall of the house. Yet it was not really so. When there was a death later, they could not get the coffin out of the house. Then the window had to be removed, exactly as they had seen before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Krist en Pyt wennen yn 'e Feansterheide yn in hiel lyts húske. Op in nacht seagen se dat by har yn 'e foarmuorre it finster mei ramt en al der út wie. Hja seagen it beide klear. En dochs wie 't sa net. Se wienen wekker woarn troch gestomp en geskou.\nLetter tochten se dêr net mear oer, mar doe kom dêr in sterfgefal. Doe moest de kiste der út. Dy koe de swaei net krije troch de doar. Doe moesten se 't finster mei 't kezyn der út nimme. Dêr moest de kiste troch.\nDat hienen Krist en Pyt dy nachts sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33059,"r":"CJ086402","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man always worked on a praam (flat-bottomed barge). Once he had a strong feeling that he should not go to the barge. He also kept forgetting something, so that he had already gone back home three times. That same week he drowned while swimming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn heit wenne yn Feansterheide. Op in moarntiid soed er nei 't wurk ta. Dat wie yn 'e Poffert (Hoogkerk) by Grins.\nHeit wie leiker op 'e preammen, hy moest dêr leikje.\nMar dy moarns koed er min fuort komme. It wie krekt as woarde er keard, as moest er thúsbliuwe. 't Wie op moandei. It wykein wie heit altyd thús.\nHeit wie al in ein op stap, doe sloech er him op 'e bûse: gjin tabaksdoaze. Hied er de tabak forgetten! Hy werom op hûs yn.\n\"Bist dêr noch, Ypk?\" sei er tsjin mem. \"Ik ha myn tabaksdoaze forgetten.\" Doe't er dy hie, gong er wer fuort.\nMar ûnderweis kom 't him yn 't sin, dat er syn ekstra sokken forgetten hie. By 't leikjen waerd er faek wiet, dan die er jouns in pear droege sokken oan.\n\"Fordomme,\" sei er, \"ik forjit ek alles.\"\nHy gong wer werom en helle de sokken op.\nTrije kearen hat er sa werom west. Krekt as mòest er thúsbliuwe.\nDyselde wyks is er dêr yn 'e Poffert by 't swemmen fordronken. Hy wie doe noch in jongkeardel, ik wie twa jier âld.\nMyn beide bruorren wienen 16 en 17.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34445,"r":"CJ086603","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When magpies chatter by a house, someone there will die. When dogs howl eerily, someone will soon die as well.\nPeople used to warn that you should never walk in the middle of the road at night. Otherwise you could be pushed off the road by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters tichte by hûs bigjinne to skatterjen, komt der in deaden. As hounen spûkgûle stjert der ek gau ien.\nWy waerden froeger altyd warskôge: rin yn 'e nacht noait midden op 'e wei, hwant dan kin 't treffe dat jy tsjin in lykstaesje oprinne, en dan wurde jy fan 'e wei reage.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33155,"r":"CJ087501","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People once heard a coffin being pushed through the door. Three days later someone in that house died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mem fortelde, ergens yn 'e Rottefalle sieten ris guon op in joun yn 'e hûs mei de lampe op. Doe hearden se dat dêr in kiste ta de doar yn skoud woarde. Se hearden ek de hingsels tsjin 'e kiste oanfallen.\nTrije dagen letter forstoar der ien yn dat hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33172,"r":"CJ087605","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, there will soon be a death.\nOnce when a dog howled terribly, its mistress died the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt, dan giet der gau ien dea. Us herdershoun hat ris op in nacht ôfgryslik spûkgûld. Even letter stoar ús mem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33291,"r":"CJ088409","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a group of magpies sits near a house, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr't in protte eksters om 'e hûs om rinne dêr komt in sterfgefal, dêr kinne jo mar gerust fan op oan.\nDe wyks foardat ús heit stoar ha wy in wike oan ien de eksters by ús yn 'e buert hawn (heit wenne njonken ús). Der wienen altyd in stik of seis, sawn by elkoar.\nDat is foar 100% de goudearlike waarheid.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33299,"r":"CJ088417","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man once saw lots of people and bicycles at his house, but in reality there was nothing. A week later one of his children had died and the people and bicycles were really there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem en dy ha in berntsje forlern, dat is forbrând. 't Wie op in tongersdei-to-joun. De wyks fan tofoaren kom heit op in joun thús. Doe tocht er: hwat hjir is to dwaen, wyt ik net.\n't Wienen allegearre minsken en fytsen. - Mar der wie neat.\nIn wike letter hiene jy deselde sitewaesje. Mar doe wie 't echt. Heit sei: Ik wist hwat der gebeure soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33413,"r":"CJ089908","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man once saw a funeral procession coming from a house. A few days later a girl in the house died unexpectedly.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Fokke en Sytske wennen tichte by de Liuwepoel. Sy hienen in famke. Op in joun kom heit thús. Hy wie to foet.\nDoe seach er in lykstaesje. Hy telde alve man. Sy kommen by de hoeke wei, dêr't Fokke en Syts wennen. It bern mankearde doe noch neat. It duorre mar in dei of hwat doe wie it bern dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33417,"r":"CJ089912","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man had sometimes heard cries for help from a pool, and was convinced that someone would one day drown in it. That is why his children were never allowed to skate there. People also thought there was a monster in the pool.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mem en dy wennen flak by de Liuwepoel. Mar as it winter wie mochten se noait op 'e Liuwepoel ride. Dat fortroude pake net. Hwant hy wie ris in kear op in joun by de Liuwepoel lâns kom, doe hearde hy roppen: help. En even letter wer, en doe nochris wer. Trije kear.\n\"Dêr forsûpt nochris ien,\" sei pake, \"dat màt gebeure.\"\nMar ik leau net dat der oant diz tiid ta ien fordronken is.\nDe Liuwe-poel is op plakken ôfgryslike djip. Dêr kin men gjin boaijem bifiemje.\nGuon wolle ha, der sit in monster yn 'e Liuwepoel. Froeger hat dy poel folle greater west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33439,"r":"CJ090302","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man once saw a funeral procession. A few days later an acquaintance died and the procession was really there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Koatstertille hienen de Kamminga's froeger in mostermoune. Piter Kamminga syn pake hat ris de lykstaesje sjoen fan in man dy't doe noch yn leven wie. Hy koe de minsken samar opneame dy't achter it lyk oan roannen. \nKoarte tiid dêrnei is dy man stoarn. Doe seach er deselde lykstaesje nochris wer.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":208172,"r":"EGGEN006102","p":"Wijnandsrade","v":"L.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The deceased woman knew she would die after magpies had been at the door.","i":"C.E.","o":"onderwerp : aanzeggen van de dood.\nplaats : wijnandsrade\ntijd : tot + 1940\n\nich kin mich nog euverdinke, wie hie, twië hoezer wiejer, plötselich 'n vrouw doäd ging.\n'n buurvrouw wis dat evel al. die hauw gezien, tot de aèstere pès aan de déur waore gewaes. en dat waor e teike, tot eine doäd zouw goon.","l":"Limburgs"},{"n":208177,"r":"EGGEN006107","p":"Wijnandsrade","v":"L.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A priest refuses to read prayers over a child struck by the evil hand, who dies after Death knocks.","i":"C.E.","o":"onderwerp: de dood.\nplaats: wijnandsrade\ntijd : ?\n\nn.b.: zie kemp, lb. 5.6..\n\noppe blauwesjtein woënde 'ne màn mèt z'n vrouw en e döchterke. 't kind waor neet oetgegreujd, ech 'ne kröppel. \n't maedsje waor van 'n koaj hand geroak. de màn hauw de pèstoër al dèks gevraog 't kind te euverleze, mèh dae wou neet zoë èrreg. \noppenen aovend hoërt 'r eine oppe déur hauwe. 'r versjrik zich en geit kíeke. niks. dat ging e paar kiër zoë.\nnao de lètste kiër zaog 'r evel get duusters wegloupe ..... de doäd. dae hauw geklop, veur bìnne te kòme. \ntoen 'r bie 't bèd van 't kind kaom waor 't doäd.","l":"Limburgs"},{"n":33521,"r":"CJ090905","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Two men once heard cries for help from the water. A few days later someone drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit kom wol gauris by Remmelt Kroes; dy wenne yn Kûkherne. Op in joun sei Remmelt tsjin heit: \"Hark, dêr ropt ien. Hearst it wol Jehannes?\"\nDoe hearde heit it ek. It kom út it wetter wei ta in pear kear ta. Doe stoar it lûd wei.\nIn pear dagen letter fordronk der ien yn 'e Swette. Dêr hienen Remmelt en heit doe de lûden fan heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33526,"r":"CJ090910","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howled eerily, a death would come. The dogs never howled as much as during the Spanish flu in 1918.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de hounen bot gûlden dan sei heit: \"Der gebeurt gau wer hwat.\" Dan woarde der mei gauwens wer ien fuortbrocht. Noait ha de hounen sa bot spûkgûld as yn 'e tiid fan 'e Spaenske gryp, dat wie yn 1918. Doe stoar de iene nei de oare.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33566,"r":"CJ091206","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man who was born with a caul once saw a funeral procession coming from a farm. A few days later one of the farm's daughters fell through the ice and drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Koaten wenne in boer, dy hiet van der Ploeg. Hy hie trije dochters en in soan.\nOp in nacht gong de plysje dêr lâns, doe seach er in lykstaesje ta de homeije útkommen. 't Wie yn 1890, in hiele stringe winter.\nIn pear dagen letter gongen de fjouwer bern to riden op 't iis. Se rieden op 'e Burgumer mar. Se wienen fan tofoaren warskôge, it wie net fortroud dêr to riden. Mar dêr hienen se har net oan steurd.\nDoe is ien fan 'e dochters dêr fordronken. Jan van Zalen hat der noch in liet op makke. Sytske van der Ploeg hiet se.\nDêr hie de plysje de lykstaesje fan sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33595,"r":"CJ091501","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman was once upset for a whole day because she had the feeling her husband was dead. The next day her husband really died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In suster fan myn heit wie ris op in dei hiel bot oerstjûr. Hja hie 't gefoel dat har man dea wie. Mar 't wie sa net, hy leefde en der skeelde him neat.\nMar in deimennich letter wie er dea.\nHeit hat it faek forteld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34521,"r":"CJ091909","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One day a dog sat outside by a tree the whole time, howling eerily in the direction of a house. Later that day a little boy who lived there was brought home dead.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt, dan komt der in sterfgefal, dêr kin men wis fan op oan. Wy ha 't sels meimakke, noch net iens sa mâlle lang lyn, mei ús eigen houn. Us mem leefde doe noch. Ik wie net thús. Mem wie allinne yn 'e hûs.\nWy hienen hwat in fremd hountsje. Hy gong dy deis by de dikke beam sitten, mei de kop omheech en dat spûkgûlde mar. Wylst seach er de kant nei it westen út. 't Wie by dei. It wie in aeklich lûd en ús buorman sei tsjin mem: \"Dy houn mat yn 'e hûs. Dat is net oan to hearren.\"\nDoe brocht mem him yn 'e hûs. Mar it dier hie dêr rêst noch duer. Hy wòe der út. Hy rekke der èk út. Doe gong er wer op 't selde plak sitten by de dikke beam, mei de kop omheech en seach it westen út. En dat bigong wer to spûkgûlen.\nDoe sei buorman tsjin mem: \"Nou wolle wy der om tinke, hwat hjir achterwei komt. Hwant dit doocht net. Dit docht de houn oars noait.\"\nOp 'e middei woarde der in jonkje fan dyselde minsken dea thúsbrocht. Dat jonkje hie in ûngelok hawn. De houn hie hyltyd it gesicht hawn op it hûs fan dy minsken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34528,"r":"CJ092203","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howled eerily, people believed someone would die. Someone would die in the direction the dog pointed its head.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlde miende men dat der yn 'e buert mei gauwens in sterfgefal wêze soe. Dêr't de houn mei de kop hinne seach, dêr soe it sterfgefal wêze. Dêr loerde er hinne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33676,"r":"CJ092608","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. He knew that someone would then die again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn swager Willem Postma seach geregeld lykstaesjes. Dy moest der om út bêd wei. Dan gong er oan 'e kant fan 'e wei stean. De oare deis sei er dan: Der gebeurt wer hwat; ik ha fannacht wer in lykstaesje sjoen. Mar hy sei noait hwa't der stjerre soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33717,"r":"CJ093603","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"It happened that at the homes of the mortally ill, people heard a coffin being brought in, even though nothing could be seen. That was an omen that the sick person would soon die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie ien yn 'e Rottefalle tige siik. Hy wenne yn in hiel âld hûs mei bihindige doarren. De famylje fan 'e sike wie yn dat hûs oanwêzich, omdat de pasjint min wie en it net sa lang mear meitsje soe. Doe hearden se ynienen it lûd fan it skouwen fan in kiste ûnder it finster troch. Mar yn werklikheit gebeurde der neat.\nSe hienen bigrepen hwat dit bitsjutte. Se wisten nou mei wissichheit dat deselde dy't siik wie it net lang mear meitsje soe. (Alde Mulder hat dit forteld).\nIt is ek in kear yn 'e Rottefalle gebeurd, doe wekken der guon fan 'e famylje by in siik minske.\nYnienen woarde de doar iepenklapt, mar sy hearden der net ien ynkommen en seagen ek neat. Dit hie bitrekking op it sike minske dat mei gauwens weireitsje soe. It wie de dea sèls dy't der yn kom.\n\n~","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33719,"r":"CJ093605","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People had sometimes heard on the water the sound of wood and tools being thrown onto a praam (flat-bottomed barge). A few days later someone drowned in the water. To fish out the body, tools and wood were taken along on a barge. So then the men heard the same sound again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Piter Postma, byneamd Piter Kûper wie myn omke. Hy fordronk op 'e Leijen. Hy foel achter de boat mei hout yn it wetter. Swimme koed er net, 't wie min waer, der stienen hege baren.\nIt wie al gau bikend yn 'e Rottefalle dat er fordronken wie. Alde Hindrik en Wijke wennen tichte by de Leijen. Dêr gongen se hinne om in pream dêr't se allerhande ark yn brochten om myn omke op to fiskjen.\nSe ha doe mei man en macht nei him socht en sy ha him ek foun.\nMar âlde Hindrik en Wijke hienen op in nacht, in pear dagen foar dat omke fordronk al heard dat der planken en oar ark yn 'e pream smiten woarde.\nIn pear dagen letter hearden se dyselde lûden dus wer, mar doe gebeurde it echt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33721,"r":"CJ093607","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, a death is coming. Also if magpies sit chattering near a house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlde koe men der mar fan op oan dat der in sterfgefal yn 'e buert kom.\nMem hie 't net op eksters bigrepen. As der in minske op stjerren lei kom der in hiele kloft eksters op it hiem en dy skatteren mar om 't hûs hinne.\nWy ha 't sels bilibbe mei in ekster. Doe't ús heit tige min wie kom der in ekster by ús op 't hiem. Dy gong op 'e hekke sitten en bigoun to skatterjen.\nDoe sei heit: \"Sjogge jimme 't wol? Dat is om my.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33722,"r":"CJ093608","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One morning a woman chased away a magpie several times. That afternoon her little son drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde by de Koba ûnder de Pein dat der by lju dy't dêr wennen hyltyd in ekster by 't sinkgat stie. De frou tocht: Hwat mat dy fûgel dêr? En sy jage him fuort. Mar hy kom hyltyd wer. Doe is dêr de middeis in jonkje fan harren yn dat sinkgat forsûpt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33723,"r":"CJ093609","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If someone on a ship was very ill, the sharks would come to it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In séman hat my wolris forteld, as der oan board ien tige siik wie, dan kommen de haeijen der op ôf.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33774,"r":"CJ094107","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, a funeral procession will pass by. Once a dog howled eerily towards the house of a pregnant woman. The baby was stillborn.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As hounen spûkgûle, dan komt der in lykstaesje lâns. In houn kin foarútsjen. Sa'n dier sjocht dan de lykstaesje al.\nYn Houtigehage spûkgûlde in houn mei de kop nei in hûs ta, dêr't in frou yn forwachting wie. Der woarde in skoftsje letter in dea popke geboaren. Dat kom dêr doe lâns mei de dragers.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33775,"r":"CJ094108","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Dreaming of fish or lice means a death in the family.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As jo oer fisken drome giet er ien dea, wie froeger altyd de hiting. As jo oer luzen drome ek. 't Is ien fan jins neiste famylje of jo binne it sels.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33801,"r":"CJ094321","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People once heard cries for help from a pool in Houtigehage. Someone is still to drown in it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alle poeltsjes binne ôfgryslike djip neffens it sizzen. \nYn Houtigehage is in poel, der ha se in kear ien yn roppen heard: Help! Help! Dyselde mat dêr altyd noch yn fordrinke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33814,"r":"CJ094409","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, a death is coming. Usually in the direction in which the dog howls.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de houn spûkgûlde koe men der mar fan op oan dat der in deaden kom. Ik wit noch bêst dat der by ús yn Twizelerheide in houn sahwat de hiele dei spûkgûlde. Hy hie de kop omheech en seach mar ien kant út. Der is doe ien stoarn, tichteby, de kant út dêr't de houn de kop hinne draeid hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33817,"r":"CJ094412","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a wild watch ticks by the bed, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde horloazjes tikken altyd by 't bêd. Dan komt der in deaden. Ik hear it nòch wolris.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33819,"r":"CJ094414","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People once heard cries for help from the water. Later someone drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By de Spoarbrêge yn 'e Westerein ha se ris ien lûd om help roppen heard yn 't wetter. Mar der wie net ien. Letter is dêr by dy brêge in skoalmaster fordronken. It wie Rinse Monsma, dy wie dêr oan 't swimmen. Dy hat doe ek om help roppen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33864,"r":"CJ094807","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman saw lots of blowflies at her house and was afraid her goat would die. Indeed, a few days later the animal was dead.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn suster wenne dat in eintsje út. Hja hie in âlde buorfrou, dy hie in geit. Dy geit, dat wie suver har breawinning. Dêr hie se de molke fan en dan makke se ek noch bûter en tsiis.\nOp in kear kom se by myn suster en sei: \"O o, 't is net bêst, it binne allegear dragers by my yn 'e hûs (dragers = aasvliegen). As de geit mar net dea giet!\" (Hja tocht dat dy dragers, dat dat foartsjirmerije wie).\nIn pear dagen letter sei se: \"De geit is dea. Ik sei 't al. Der binne sa'n dragers by myn yn'e hûs.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":207819,"r":"VODA_041_12","p":"Herten","v":"L.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A house fire was seen as a harbinger of a death in the family.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"- Gaat uw gang.\n- Een ander ding, ook liggende op dat gebied van dat eh.. volksbijgeloof, eh.. was eh.. dat wanneer iemand plotseling werd geconfronteerd met een huisbrand, dat men dan sidderde van angst, omdat in..in.. dit een onheilspellend teken was, namelijk dat iemand in de familie zou sterven."},{"n":36161,"r":"CJ096902","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When dogs howl frighteningly, a death will follow.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":36174,"r":"CJ097008","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Magpies and dogs can announce a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As hounen spûkgûle sil der ien stjerre. Ek as de eksters om 't hûs hinne skatterje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36175,"r":"CJ097009","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People with supernatural gifts go out at night and can foretell deaths.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon dy't mei de helm geboaren binne gean der yn 'e nacht op út. Dy witte altyd fan sterfgefallen foarút.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36191,"r":"CJ097110","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The frightening howling of a dog announces a death.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":36287,"r":"CJ097616","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Many people still believe that the frightening howling of a dog announces a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt, dan komt dêr yn dy buert in sterfgefal. In hopen minsken hjir leauwe dat nòch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36428,"r":"CJ098304","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howled frighteningly, someone would die.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":36467,"r":"CJ0985A02","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Magpies can announce a funeral or visitors. The frightening howling of a dog announces a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters skatterje yn 'e beam komt der in bigraffenis.\nAs ien ekster flak by de doar komt krijt men bisite.\nSpûkgûlt der in houn, dan komt der mei gauwens in deade.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36518,"r":"CJ098807","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When the narrator and her husband were visiting her mother, she got a rash on her head. One day her mother said they had better leave. She was afraid her child would die, because a dog had howled frighteningly the night before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wienen noch mar even troud en wennen achter Dokkum. Ik wie in pear nachten by mem útfanhûs. Myn man kaem ek, hwant dy krige ûngemak oan 'e hân en koe doe net arbeidzje.\nIk krige bot útslach oan 'e holle, dat seach der raer út. De oare deis, neidat myn man kaem wie, sei mem tsjin ús:\n\"Nou matte jimme mar wer fuort, net?\"\n\"Hwerom?\" sei 'k. Hwant ús mem hie ús altyd graech by ús.\n\"Bern,\" sei se, \"der hat fannacht in houn sa bot oan 't spûkgûlen west. Ik wie deabinaud datstû dea gean soeste omdatstû sa'n útslach haste.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36519,"r":"CJ098808","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a cat washes itself, visitors are coming. If it washes behind its ear, they will be strangers. Magpies around the house announce a death. Just before an uncle died, there were black birds sitting on the roof.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de kat him wasket komt der bisite.\nAs er him achter 't ear wasket komt der in fremden op bisite. As eksters by hûs skatterje komt der in deaden.\nYn Twizel hie ik in omke en in muoike to wenjen. Omke waerd siik. Doe kamen der swarte fûgels op it dak. Doe is omke ridlik gau dêrnei stoarn. Dy swarte fûgels wienen de boaden fan 'e dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36556,"r":"CJ098845","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Someone in Westerein drowned when he went out skating. Before it happened, people had already heard wailing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Westerein wenne in meester. 't Wie yn 'e winter en hy sei: \"Ik wol even in eintsje ride op redens.\" Mar hy is by de Kûkhernster brêge fordronken. De minsken hienen dêr fan tofoaren al gejammer heard. It lei dêr by de brêge iepen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36558,"r":"CJ098901","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A tramp was walking down the street when a dog came running at him. According to the tramp, a dog that comes at you and snaps at your calves announces a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wenne in man, dy roun to skoaijen. Ik wie sa'n jonkje fan in jier of tsien, ik stie tsjin in peal oan op 'e hoeke fan 'e Sikkesstrjitte. Doe kom dêr dy skoaijer oan. Hy hie in sekfol skoaijersguod by him. Sa komt der in houn by in hûs wei. Dy houn bigjint to blaffen en op 'e skoaijer ta to rinnen.\n\"Soed er ek lulk wêze, jonge?\" sei de skoaijer tsjin my.\n\"Dat falt wol hwat ta,\" sei 'k, \"'t is de houn fan Sikke Boukes.\" \"Ik ha 't der net op stean,\" sei er, \"hwant as in houn op jin ta komt en hy byt jin hast yn 'e kûten, dan bitsjut dat in deaden.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36559,"r":"CJ098902","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howled frighteningly, it meant someone would die.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":36565,"r":"CJ098908","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One evening the narrator's grandfather was walking outside. On the way he saw a big black dog. When he told his brother, the brother said there would be a death in the family. Some time later the grandfather fell ill and died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De Verlengde Stasjonswei hiet froeger Lange Loane. 't Wie doe noch in lânwei. By de bocht wie in leech plak yn [in] streek fan sa'n 5 m, dêr stie by 't hjerst altyd wetter yn. Myn pake soe ris nei famylje ta op in joun. 't Wie donker. Doe seach er in grouwe swarte houn, sa great as in Sint Bernard, mar mei in greate, lange bek. Hy sjocht him foar him lâns gean op 't plak dêr't oars wetter stie.\nDoe't er by de beide âlde omkes wie fortelde er hwat er sjoen hie. Doe sei Geart-om: \"Nou jonge, dat is net in moai foarútsicht.\"\n\"Hoe dàt sa net?\" frege pake.\n\"Dû kinst der mar gerust op oan dat der aenst yn ús famylje in sterfgefal komt. Dat duorret net sa lang mear.\" Pake leaude dat wol.\n\"Hwa is dat dan?\" frege er.\n\"Dat kin 'k dy net sizze\", sei Geart-om.\nIn skoft letter wurdt pake siik. It wie in ûngeneslike kwael. Myn heit (syn skoansoan) hat der noch foar nei Joast Wiersma, to Jistrum, west, mar hy mocht gjin baet mear fine. Hy hat net lang sukkele, doe wied er dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36584,"r":"CJ098927","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Magpies around the house announce a death.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":36637,"r":"CJ099307","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When magpies come into the farmyard, someone in the house will die. Magpies foretell death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der eksters op it hiem komme, komt der yn dat hûs in deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36651,"r":"CJ099406","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, someone in the neighbourhood will die within 4 days.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlde seinen se, gong der binnen fjouwer dagen ien dea yn net to fiere omtrek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36694,"r":"CJ099801","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"One morning, when we were lying with the ship in Petersburch to load potatoes, my sister said she had very clearly seen in her dream that Jehannes Boom suddenly died. That simply couldn't be, since he was perfectly healthy. A little later a skipper came with the news that Jehannes Boom had died suddenly.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy leinen mei 't skip yn Petersburch by Donkerbroek, om jirpels to laden foar 't jirpelfabryk yn Huzum.\nOp in moarn sei myn suster: \"O, hwat haw ik fannacht in rare droom hawn!\"\n\"Hoe dat sa?\" seinen wy. Wy seagen wol dat se hwat fan 'e wize wie. \"Ik ha droomd,\" sei se, \"dat Jehannes Boom wie dea. Ik seach foar myn egen dat er stoar. It wie allegear sa dúdlik.\"\n\"Fanke,\" seinen wy, \"hoe komst der by? Jehannes Boom skeelt ommers neat.\"\nOp 'e neidei kom Jehannes Keimpema fan Earnewâld der oan farren mei syn skip. Hy kom fan 't jirpelfabryk to Huzum en soe nei Apelsgea om nije lading.\n\"Ik ha in raer boadskip,\" sei er, \"Jehannes Boom is samar ynienen stoarn.\" (Jehannes Boom wie in skipper, ôfkomstich fan Eastemar en bisibbe oan Rommert v.d.Meer.)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36705,"r":"CJ099908","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog that roams about like a ghost is an omen of a death, just like the hooting of owls.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Spûkgûlde der in houn, dan bitsjutte dat dat der mei gauwens wer ien stjerre soe. Ek as de ûle rôp.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36732,"r":"CJ100009","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When someone is sick at sea, sharks come swimming around the ship. They wait until that person is dead. Sharks are the harbingers of death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der op sé ien siik is, komme de haeijen om it skip hinne. Dêr wachtsje se oant dyselde dea is. De haeijen binne op sé de foarboaden fan 'e dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36800,"r":"CJ100309","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, someone nearby will die soon. A cat washing itself with its paws foretells visitors. If the cat washes behind its ears, the visitors come from the neighbourhood.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt stjert dêr mei gauwens ien yn 'e omkriten is it sizze altyd.\nAs de kat mei de poat sit to waskjen komt der bisite.\nWasket er him achter de earen dan komt de bisite omfierrens wei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36816,"r":"CJ100509","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, it is an omen that someone nearby will die soon.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlde bitsjutte dat dat der hiel yn 't koart ien deagean soe dy't tichteby wenne. Dêr wienen de minsken froeger o sa bang foar.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36819,"r":"CJ100603","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When dogs howled eerily, someone would die. Dogs were afraid of funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Spûkgûlde der in houn, dan gong der ien dea. Wy wienen dêr froeger bang foar. As der in lykstaesje oankaem wienen de hounen bang.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36834,"r":"CJ100618","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When my father was run over by a truck, my mother had seen it coming: eight black rooks flew into the farmyard and kept coming back whenever she chased them away. A few days later father had the accident and was killed instantly.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ús heit deariden is, sei ús mem krekt fan tofoaren:\n\"Duvel, hjir gebeurt hwat.\" Wol acht swarte roeken wienen der op 't hiem. Mem forjage se, mar sy kommen like gau wer.\nMem wie der alhiel fan oerstjûr. In pear dagen letter krige heit it ûngelok. Hy is ûnder in truck rekke en wie opslach dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36925,"r":"CJ101226","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, it usually means someone will die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt, dan sjocht er hwat. Dat bitsjut meastal in sterfgefal.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36955,"r":"CJ101406","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, it means a death.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":37014,"r":"CJ101603","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man once said he had had a strange dream: a child had fallen into the water and then drowned together with the father who had tried to save it. The next day I heard that my son-in-law and his child had both drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw yn 'e Noard-oastpolder wurke. Dêr wie doe ek in man oan 't wurk dy hiet fan Majoor. Dy fortelde my: Ik hie ris in hiele rare droom op in nacht. Ik droomde dat der wie in bern yn 't wetter fallen. De heit wie dat bern neisprong en doe wienen se beide forsûpt. Dat wie de droom. De oare deis krige ik biricht dat myn skoansoan en syn bern wienen beide fordronken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37015,"r":"CJ101604","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Tabe said he had seen the death of his child days in advance: he had seen the coffin standing on the chair and foreseen all sorts of other details of the funeral.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie ek in sekere Tabe Bergsma by ús oan 't wurk.\nDy fortelde fuort dêr achteroan, dat der wie ris in bern fan him overleden en hy hie dagen fan tofoaren al syn kistje op 'e stoel stean sjoen en alle bysûnderheden fan 'e bigraffenis. Doe hie 't bern noch neat skeeld. 't Wie krekt sa neikaem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37027,"r":"CJ101616","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man always predicted that one day he would go suddenly. Once he gave the cows two buckets of water, and as he stepped back he said: there's the trouble already, and dropped dead.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der hat hjir in man wenne, dy sei altyd, hy soe hjir nochris ûnforwacht weireitsje. Op in kear joech er de kij twa ammerfollen wetter. Doe't er dat dien hie soed er wer op 'e mjilling stappe, doe sei er: \"Dêr ha jy 't gedonder al.\"\nEn dea wied er.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37087,"r":"CJ101902","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When the church bells ring clearly, it means someone will soon be added to the churchyard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de tsjerkeklok helder let komt der mei gauwens ien op it tsjerkhôf.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37098,"r":"CJ102002","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Black rooks around the house foretell death. Magpies in the farmyard mean a visit from people who rarely come. A dog that howls eerily foretells a death. A bell that rings foretells a death. The same goes for a painting falling off the wall, a weight falling off a clock, or death knocks in wood. When someone died, a cloth was hung over the mirror and the clock was stopped. The flowers were taken away from the windows.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Komt der in swarte roek by hûs, dan bitsjut dat in deaden.\nKomme der eksters op 't hiem, dan bitsjut dat dat der bisite komt fan guon dy't men net folle sjocht.\nSpûkgûlt der in houn, dan bitsjut dat in deaden.\nKlept de klok yn 'e toer, dan bitsjut dat in deaden.\nFalt der in skilderij del yn 'e hûs, dan bitsjut dat in deaden.\nFalt der in gewicht fan in klok, dan bitsjut dat in deaden.\nTikket it deatikkerke yn 't môgige hout, dan bitsjut dat in deaden.\nBy in sterfgefal komt der in doek oer de spegel en wurdt de klok stilset. De blommen foar de glêzen wurde út 'e keamer weihelle.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37101,"r":"CJ102103","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Once people heard cries for help in the Leeuwepoel. Later someone drowned there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Harkema, yn 'e Liuwepoel ha se ris in kear 'help' roppen heard. Letter is dêr ien yn forsûpt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37143,"r":"CJ102504","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Woodworms, howling dogs and chattering magpies announce a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de houtwjirms kloppen yn 't môgige hout bitsjutte dat dat der in sterfgefal kaem.\nAs de houn spûkgûlde ek; dêr wienen âlde minsken deabinaud foar.\nAs eksters skatteren op it hiem kaem der ek in sterfgefal.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37194,"r":"CJ103101","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"At the spot where a woman later drowned, people had earlier heard cries for help.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Burgumermar hawwe guon alris ien om 'help' roppen heard. 't Wie in frouljuslûd, fortelde heit. Letter is dêr op dat plak in frommeske fordronken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37220,"r":"CJ103210","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog howling eerily foretold a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in houn spûkgûlde yn Feanwâldsterwâl leaude men fêst dat der mei gauwens ien yn 'e buert stjerre soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37318,"r":"CJ103904","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A magpie by the front door means a death. Because of its white and black colours, a magpie looks like a mourning letter. A magpie brings mourning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der eksters op it hiem kamen oan 'e foardoar ta bitsjutte dat dat der yn dat hûs yn 't koart ien stjerre soe.\nIn ekster is wyt mei swart en hat dus de gedaente fan in roubrief. In ekster bringt de tiding fan 'e rou.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37329,"r":"CJ103915","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Before a woman died, the vases had fallen off the cupboard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't Piter syn frou stoar sei er tsjin my: De stelten binne fan to foaren fan 'e kast fallen. Dat wie de foarboade.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38175,"r":"CJ108204","p":"Feanwâldsterwâl","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Father cries and sees water on the night his brother drowns.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem fortelde, dat in broer fan heit - dat wie Albert, in omke fan my, soe nei 't Godloas Tolhûs ta to praten. Doe't er wer nei hûs ta soe, is er fordronken.\nUs heit wie dy nachts tige ûnrêstich, hy hie lûd gûld. 't Wie allegearre wetter, dat er seach.\nDe oare deis brochten se heit syn broer as fordronkene thús.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38201,"r":"CJ108403","p":"Feanwâldsterwâl","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman hears beforehand how a nephew falls into the water and drowns.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bartele Hiltsje hearde fan tofoaren in muoikesizzer fan har doe't dy yn 't wetter rekke en fordronk. Letter is dy jonge fordronken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38216,"r":"CJ108502","p":"Feanwâldsterwâl","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman has a strange feeling at night and hears her nephew at the door, though he is not there, saying that her brother is dead. A few days later the nephew knocks and says her brother has died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik in lyts jonkje wie, is it folgjende ris gebeurd. Us mem hie in omkesizzer, dat wie Gaetse. Op in nacht koe mem net sliepe. Se wie sa raer hyltyd. Doe hearde se ien by de doar. En doe hearde se it lûd fan Gaetse, har omkesizzer. Hja hearde dat er sei dat har broer Hâns dea wie.\nHja sei it de oare moarns: Myn omkesizzer hat fannacht by de doar west. Sa en sa.\nMar hy hie der net west.\nMar trije dagen letter wie Gaetse der wol. Hy kloppe op 'e doar en sei dat mem har broer Hâns overleden wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38217,"r":"CJ108503","p":"Feanwâldsterwâl","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"In a house the pages of the tear-off calendar fly around the lamp, though nothing is wrong. After the death of someone living in the house, a quarrel breaks out over dividing the inheritance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is hjir op 'e Wâl gebeurd, dat it der op in joun yn in lyts húske sa bot oan wei gong, dat de skeurkalenderbledtsjes fleagen om 'e lampe hinne. En dochs wie der neat to rêdden. In frou hie it sjoen.\nRidlik gau dêrnei forstoar der ien yn dat húske en doe gong 't op in erven en partsjen. Doe woarden se sa fjûrslach deielsk, dat de pompierren fleagen de minsken om 'e earen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38268,"r":"CJ108718","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man predicts that he will die of a spot on his nose. He does indeed die of cancer of the nose.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jehannes hie in plakje oan 'e noas. Hy sei: \"Dat wurdt myn dea.\" En dat is ek sa kaem. Hy krige der kanker oan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38287,"r":"CJ108737","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man hears beforehand the same sound that is heard after someone's death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha ús beppe by ús yn hawn. Dy is 93 jier âld woarn. Hja lei op it lêst yn 't ledikant by ús yn 'e keamer. Fjouwer wiken foar har dead leinen heit en mem op in nacht op bêd. Doe hearde heit hwat oer 't hûs. Hy sei tsjin mem: \"Ik hear dat der hwat ûnder 't finster troch skoud wurdt. Dat komt by 't stalt fan 'e feart wei. Sa is 't by de kant op kaem en oer 't hiem hinne rekke. En dat is hjir ûnder 't finster troch gong.\"\nFjouwer wiken neitiid wie beppe wei. De kiste waerd mei de pream brocht, by 't stalt op tild en oer 't hiem droegen. Omt er net troch de doar koe, waerd er ûnder 't finster troch skoud.\nDat hie heit allegear fantofoaren heard. 't Wie foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38310,"r":"CJ108817","p":"Feanwâldsterwâl","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog howling eerily means a death in the family.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlde koe men der fêst fan op oan dat der in sterfgefal yn 'e famylje to wachtsjen stie. Us mem hat it faker as ienkear meimakke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38331,"r":"CJ108920","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman sees beforehand that the farmer she works for is murdered.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir op 'e Heide wennet in frommeske, dy hat froeger as faem wenne by Knjillis Gearts van der Veen oan 'e Simmerdyk by Hurdegaryp. Dy boer is doe formoarde woarn.\nHy hat fan tofoaren witten, dat dat gebeure soe. Hja hie fan tofoaren sjoen dat ien him formoarde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38332,"r":"CJ108921","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog howls eerily on seeing a funeral procession. Shortly afterwards a man dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem hie to praten west nei har swager. Doe't se dêr wie spûkgûlde dêr in houn. 't Wie yn 'e Westerein. Wylst dy houn spûkgûlde wienen der twa froulju oan it sjongen. Doe sei mem tsjin dy froulju: \"Jimme matte ophâlde fan sjongen hwant de houn sjocht hwat.\"\n't Wie èk sa, de houn seach in lykstaesje.\nTwa wiken letter forstoar dêr mem har swager (in broer fan heit). De houn hie de lykstaesje al fantofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38345,"r":"CJ109006","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A sick sister wants to lie in the box bed in the living room, because she has heard the shaft of the cart creak. When she dies shortly after, she is taken to the churchyard on a farm cart whose shaft creaks.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie in suster, dy krige de Spaenske gryp. Dy is stoarn yn novimber 1918.\nHja lei achter yn 't hûs yn in bêdsté. Doe sei se tsjin heit: \"Lit my op mem har bêd stjerre.\" Dat wie in bêdsté foar yn 'e keamer, dêr't se de minsken om har hinne hie.\n\"Bring my dêr hinne,\" sei se, \"hwant ik ha de wein al heard. It tiksel dat kreake sa.\"\nHeit sei: \"Dû mast sa raer net, bern.\"\n\"It is sa,\" sei se, \"leau my mar.\" Doe brochten se har foar yn it bêdsté. En dêr is se yn stoarn.\nTwa dagen letter wie se dea. Hja waerd nei 't hôf brocht op in boerewein. Dat wie doe noch sa de gewoante.\nIt tiksel kreake.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38360,"r":"CJ109101","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A neighbour sees the coffin of his father, who is in hospital, standing in his house. His father does indeed die in hospital.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy hawwe hjir in buorman hawn, dat wie Jelle Bouma. Doe wennen wy noch op 'e Hoek. Syn heit lei yn it sikenhûs.\nDoe sei er: \"Hy giet dea, hwant ik ha syn kiste hjir al by ús yn 'e hûs stean sjoen.\" Hy hat gelyk krige. De âld man is yn 't sikenhûs stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38389,"r":"CJ109203","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People were afraid of eerie howling. It was believed that a death would then follow.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foar spûkgûlen wienen de minsken froeger och sa bang.\nSokken binne der trouwens nòch wol. Der waerd algemien sein dat it op in sterfgefal útdraeide.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38411,"r":"CJ109225","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People hear a voice in the water saying that the time has come, but the man not yet. Later someone drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der stienen ris guon op 'e Lange brêge dy't oer de Swemmer hinne leit. Doe hearden se in stim út it wetter wei kommen. Der waerd sein: \"De tiid is der, mar de man is der noch net.\" Even letter is dêr ien fordronken.\nDat haw ik faek fortellen heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38439,"r":"CJ109323","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People know beforehand whether someone will hang himself.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":38459,"r":"CJ109401","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A few days before someone dies, a boy sees a man in black standing in front of the house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer Piter wie in jonge, doe seach er yn 'e krimpe fan in hûs op 't Skier yn 'e Westerein in man stean, dy wie hielendal yn 't swart. 't Wie in man fan 'e bigraffenis, in drager of sa. Mar yn werklikheit wié dy man dêr net.\nMar in dei of hwat letter forstoar dêr ien yn dat hûs.\nEn dóe stie dy man dêr wol echt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38460,"r":"CJ109402","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man tells that one night there was knocking against the underside of his bed. After the third time he gets up, for otherwise he would be thrown out of it. The door and the gate are opened, and he is driven to a house where someone has died. On the way back the gate is opened for him again, but he has seen no one.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit wie stuolwynder, dy swalke alles ôf om stuollen to reaparearen. Hy die alles to foet.\nSa kaem er ek ris in kear yn Kollumersweach by ien, dy hie in soan dy't syn forstân net hie.\nDy man makke in praetsje mei ús heit. Hy hiet fan Kees Veenstra, mar de minsken neamden him Bontsje Keke.\nHy sei tsjin heit: \"Ik ha hwat meimakke fannacht.\nDer waerd ûnder tsjin 't bêd oanstompt, mar ik bleau lizzen. Doe woarde der foar de twadde kear kloppe. Ik bleau nòch lizzen. Doe hearde ik it de trêdde kear. Doe bin ik der út gien. Oars waerd ik der út set.\nIk ha my oanklaeid en de doar waerd foar my iependien. Ik bin der achteroan gien en de hikke waerd foar my iependien, en doe't ik by it hûs kaem, dêr't ik hinne dreaun waerd, wie dêr ien overleden.\nDoe bin 'k allinne wer nei hûs ta gien. Hy die de hekke wol wer foar my iepen, ek werom, mar ik ha noait in minske sjoen op 'e weromreis.\"\nWylst er dat fortelde, wie heit oan 't stuolwinen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38461,"r":"CJ109403","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man sees beforehand that his daughter drowns.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Keke syn soan Klaes hie syn forstân net.\nHy hat syn eigen dochter fan tofoaren fordronken sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38565,"r":"CJ109820","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"On his deathbed a man sees three hearses. He dies, and so do the two neighbours next to him.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wiger Hoekstra wenne op 'e Streek yn Feanwâldsterwâl.\nHy wie tige min, hy moest hjir wei.\nSyn beide buormannen wienen soun.\nDoe't er op syn stjerbêd lei, sei er: \"Ik sjoch hjir fóár my trije lykweinen kommen.\"\nOan 'e iene kant stoar in buorman fan him en oan 'e oare kant stoar ek in buorman. En hy sèls stoar èk.\nDe iene gong nei Wiger ta om to sjen. Hy kaem thús en siet even letter dea op 'e stoel.\nIt is dus krekt sa útkaem. Wiger hie 't fan tofoaren sjoen.\n't Wie tjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38571,"r":"CJ109826","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog howling eerily and a group of magpies mean a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt komt der in deaden.\nAs der in protte eksters by elkoar binne komt der ek in sterfgefal.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38598,"r":"CJ109853","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A fortune teller predicts that of three young men one will have children, another will stay a bachelor and the third is on the black card. It comes true; the third man dies not long afterwards.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Trije jongemannen út 'e Finnen gongen nei de waarzegster ta.\nHja sei:\nDe iene sil bern ha.\nDe oare sil frij feint bliuwe.\nDe trêdde stiet op 'e swarte kaert.\nDe lêste, dat wie Meint. 't Is krekt sa útkaem. Meint is mei gauwens stoarn. 't Gebeurde to Ljouwert op 'e merk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38605,"r":"CJ109860","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A person cannot say just anything. A woman who says she does not want children never gets that far, for she is run over and killed by the tram.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is net likefolle hwat in minske seit.\nKobe fan Jitse en Hindrikje sei, hja woe gjin bern ha, hwant dat wie sa fiis. Hja is der net oan ta kaem, hwant de tram hat har deajage.\nJe matte oppasse hwat jo sizze.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38616,"r":"CJ109909","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog howling eerily means a death in the area. A clock ticking fast also means a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in houn spûkgûlde koe men der mar fêst fan op oan dat der yn 'e omkriten ien deagean soe.\nUs mem plichte to sizzen: Hjir tikket in wyld horloazje oan 'e muorre. Dat bitsjutte ek dat der ien weireitsje soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38617,"r":"CJ109910","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Magpies and rooks near the house mean a death. The rook is the gravedigger or bearer, the magpie is the messenger.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Eksters en roeken by hûs bitsjutte ek in sterfgefal.\nDe roek is de deagraver of de drager, de ekster de boade.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38636,"r":"CJ110014","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A minister tells that people hear a voice from the water saying that the time has come, but the man has not. Shortly afterwards a carriage drives into the canal, and the man in the carriage drowns.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ds. Koelstra hat hjir op 'e heide stien. Dy fortelde ús ris, op in plak, hjir net fier wei, dêr stienen ris guon oan 'e kant fan 'e feart. Doe hearden se in stem út it wetter wei: \"De tiid is om en de man is der net.\"\nFuort dêrnei wie der in sjeas oanriden kaem. Dy wie net oer de brêge hinne riden, mar pardoes op 'e feart yn.\nDe man yn 'e sjeas is dêr fordronken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38657,"r":"CJ110035","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A dog howling eerily means a death in the area.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":10682,"r":"CJ110108","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily or the bell clangs at a funeral, another death is coming. A woman once foresaw the death of a little boy. The vision came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt komt der wis in deaden yn 'e buert.\nAs de klok klept mei in bigraffenis ek.\nSyberen en Hinke wennen yn Sweagerbosk. Dy hienen in dochter Hinke. Har muoikesizzer hie sjoen dat Hinke har jonkje stoarn wie. De hiele bigraffenis fan it jonkje hied er sjoen. It is krekt sa neikaem. Hinke wennet yn Kollum.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29488,"r":"CJ110206","p":"De Wilgen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in houn spûkgûlt, komt der binnen trije dagen in sterfgefal tichteby. Dat is yn Nij Beets wol faek gebeurd. \n't Kaem altyd nei.\nHjir yn Drachten op 'e Houtloane wenne in frou, dy hearde op in nacht in houn spûkgûlen. 't Wie in fremde houn. Hy stie gewoan op 'e dyk, tichte by 't hûs, dêr't in pear dagen letter in man yn stoarn is.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29489,"r":"CJ110207","p":"De Wilgen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The father of a sick child suddenly sees a magpie hopping around him. It is an omen: two days later the little boy dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn pake hie in jonkje, dat wie siik. Hy hie syn wurk yn Tsjalleberd, dêr wie er oan 't turfstekken. Wylst er dêr mei dwaende wie, kaem der in ekster by him.\nDy wipte hyltyd om him hinne.\nTwa dagen letter wie 't jonkje dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29523,"r":"CJ110421","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, a death is approaching.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Spûkgûlde in houn, dan seinen se, dat der mei gauwens ien dea gong.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29524,"r":"CJ110422","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If old rooks or crows fly over the house, there will soon be a death in the house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der âlde roeken of kaën oer 't hûs hinne fleagen, soe der yn dat hûs gauachtich ien stjerre.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29525,"r":"CJ110423","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Magpies come to the house to bring a message, not necessarily news of a death. If the weight of the Frisian clock falls down, there will be a death in the family. If the bell clangs at a funeral, there will soon be another funeral. Wild watches ticking behind the wallpaper also signify an approaching death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters om 't hûs hinne skatteren brochten se in biricht. Dan gebeurde dêr gau hwat. 't Hoefde gjin sterfgefal to wêzen.\nFoel 't gewicht fan 'e Fryske klok del, dan kaem der ek in deaden yn 'e famylje.\nAs de klok klepte tidens it lieden mei in bigraffenis, dan wie der gau wer in bigraffenis.\nTikken der wylde horloazjes achter 't bihang, dan bitsjutte dat dat der gau ien yn dat hûs stjerre soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29557,"r":"CJ110504","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, there is usually a death three weeks later. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlde, wie der meast in wike of trije letter in sterfgefal.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29560,"r":"CJ110507","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If seven black rooks fly over the house, a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der sawn swarte roeken oer 't hûs hinne fleagen, kaem der yn dat hûs in deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29561,"r":"CJ110508","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If magpies come to the house, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der eksters by in hûs kamen, dan kom der in sterfgefal yn 'e buert. De eksters binne dan de boardskippers.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29609,"r":"CJ110711","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt, dan duorret it net lang of dêr komt in deaden yn 'e buert.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29643,"r":"CJ111006","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, a death is coming. It is an omen. The dog foresees the death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt, komt der in deaden. Dat gebeurt binnen trije dagen. Sa'n houn sjocht dat.\nOp 'e Pipe (to Drachten) hat de houn ek fan tofoaren gûld, doe't âlde Fokke dêr stoarn is.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29691,"r":"CJ111202","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If the bell rings strangely, a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem sei soms, as se de klok lieden hearde:\n\"Hwat let de klok wer raer. Der komt wer in deaden.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29702,"r":"CJ111213","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A sick woman suffering from tuberculosis says she hears the sound of hammering. It is an omen: she hears her coffin being made. Shortly afterwards she does indeed die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn suster lei mei t.b.c. hjir njonken. Hja wie tige min. Op in moarn kaem ik by har. Doe sei se tsjin my: \"It is sa fremd, ik hear hyltyd dat se oan 't timmerjen binne.\"\nFuort dêrnei is se stoarn. Hja hat it timmerjen oan har eigen kiste heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29703,"r":"CJ111214","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman expecting twins gives birth to two stillborn babies. A woman in the neighbourhood declares she had already suspected something was going to happen, because her dog kept howling eerily with its head turned towards the house of the twins' mother.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik krige op in kear twalingen. Beide berntsjes waerden dea geboaren. Doe't it hjir bikend woarde, sei in minske in eintsje fierderop: \"O, ik tocht al, dêr is hjir op 'e streek hwat gebeurd, hwant ús houn hat hyltyd mar stien to spûkgûlen, mei de kop dy kant út.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29716,"r":"CJ111311","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog starts howling eerily, an old woman and her son suspect that a death is coming. The old woman fears she will soon breathe her last. The son is very afraid of losing his mother. Shortly afterwards the son shoots four police officers dead. The dog had been howling for the death of the four officers.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw IJe Wykstra fan Greategast skoan kend. Ik ha wol by him west. Even foardat er dy fjouwer plysjes deasketten hat, siet der by har in houn foar de doar to spûkgûlen. IJe wenne by syn âlde mem yn. Doe't er dat spûkgûlen hearde, sei er tsjin har: \"Dat bitsjut in deaden. Doe sei syn âlde mem: \"Dan sil ik dat wol wêze, ik bin al âld.\"\nDe hiele nacht hie IJe lêst hawn fan dy wurden. Hy koe der net fan sliepe. Hyltyd wie it by him dat er syn âlde mem misse moest.\nMar even letter skeat er fjouwer plysjes dea, dy't by him op 't hiem kamen. Dat hie it spûkgûlen fan 'e houn west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29735,"r":"CJ111408","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Near the house of a gravely ill man, strange sounds come from the ditch every evening. When the man lies on his deathbed, both his sons have to come home from abroad. The sounds were an omen: the dying man makes exactly the same sounds. When his boys come home, the man stops making the sounds and dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tsjip en Neeltsje wennen yn 'e Westerin. Tsjip woarde siik. Doe hearden de minsken dat der hyltyd in gelút út 'e sleat wei kaem. Net ien wist hwat dat wie. Alle jounen wie dat gelút dêr. En dochs wie der neat to sjen.\nTsjip hie twa jonges: Wytse en Anne. Dy rekken nei Dútslân ta to werken.\nDe âld man syn sykte woarde slimmer. Doe't de beide soannen hearden dat har heit slim siik wie, kamen se wer thús.\nDoe makke Tsjip krekt deselde lûden as dy't de minsken al fier fan tofoaren heard hienen. Tsjip lei op bêd, en 't like krekt as wie er al dea. Syn egen wienen brutsen en syn mûle wie al forgankelik. Mar út dy mûle kamen dy geluten. Dat duorre krekt sa lang oant de beide soannen thús wienen. Doe stoar de âld man.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29785,"r":"CJ111523","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily or a magpie chatters close to the house, a death is coming. These are omens.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Spûkgûlt der in houn, dan komt der in deaden.\nEk as de eksters tichteby skatterje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29955,"r":"CJ111805","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, a death is coming. When magpies chatter loudly, something is also about to happen. With magpie chatter it is less clear what is going to happen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt komt der altyd in deaden wurdt der sein.\nAs eksters skatterje gebeurt der hwat. Dat hat in bitsjutting. Hwat dat is, dat wite de minsken meastal net.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29957,"r":"CJ111807","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When the village bell clanks as it is rung, a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de doarpsklok op in bipaelde menier let (as er klept) komt der mei koarten in deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30109,"r":"CJ112403","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman foresees that her neighbour will die, and so it happens.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear sei 'k tsjin myn man: \"Us buorman leeft net lang mear.\" Ik hie sjoen dat er dea wie. Doe wie er net iens siik. In pear wiken letter wie er wei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30110,"r":"CJ112404","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman's prediction to some children that their father will not live much longer comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In healjier fan tofoaren sei 'k tsjin ús bern: \"Heit leeft net lang mear.\" Der skeelde him doe neat, mar ik hie al sjoen dat er overleden wie. It kaem presys sa út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30117,"r":"CJ112505","p":"Hijum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, a death is coming within a certain time. It is an omen. People used to be very afraid of it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De minsken wienen froeger bang as der in houn spûkgûlde. \"Nou is der binnen koarten tiid in lyk, dat hjir passeart\", seinen se. Binnen safolle tiid. Yn mem har jonge jierren leauden se dêr noch oan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30452,"r":"CJ113201","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger leaude men hjir algemien: hwannear't der in houn spûkgûlde, kaem der in lyk.\nOp Smelle Ie is 't gebeurd dat der alle jounen in houn mei de kop oer 't wetter hinne stie to spûkgûlen mei de kop omheech. Fuort dêrnei kaem dêr in pream lâns farren mei in lyk der yn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30453,"r":"CJ113202","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When the owl sits on the same spot on the house every evening and calls, there will be a death close by. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de ûle joun op joun op itselde plak op in hûs sit to roppen, dan komt der yn 'e omkriten in deade.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30460,"r":"CJ113209","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A coffin maker knows in advance when he will get an order, because he hears the sound of hammering beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir hat in man wenne yn Aldegea, dy makke deakisten. As er wer in bistelling krige, dan hearde hy fan tofoaren al dat der oan it hout timmere waerd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30546,"r":"CJ113603","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man can tell from the deathly sound of the bell that a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Greate Eise wenne op 'e Sumarreheide. Dy wie gefoelich foar lûden. \"Hark,\" sei er, \"der komt ek wer in sterfgefal.\" Dat hearde er oan 't lieden fan 'e klok. Dat lieden klonk dan deadelik. Dat kaem nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30565,"r":"CJ113622","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a little bird flies against the window, a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der froeger in fûgeltsje tsjin 'e glêzen oan fleach, dan leaude men fêst dat der yn dat hûs ien kaem to forstjerren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30889,"r":"CJ114203","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Whenever a certain woman dreamt of horses, a death in the family would follow within a short time.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in muoike fan my oer hynders droomde, dan koe men der mar fan op oan dat der mei koartens in deaden yn 'e famylje kaem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31228,"r":"CJ116004","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A woman suddenly turns deathly pale: she says she has seen a black dog that came to bring news of a death. A family member will die. A few days later someone in the family does indeed die. The dog was the messenger of death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanmem wenne yn den Haech. Op in joun siet se mei de bern yn 'e keamer. Doe seagen de bern har ynienen bleek wurden. \"Hwat is der, mem?\" frege ien.\n\"Ik seach hjir sakrekt in swarte houn,\" sei se, \"dy roun om 'e tafel hinne en is der doe wer útgien troch dy doar. Dy houn bringt it boadskip, dat der gau ien út 'e famylje deagean sil.\"\nIn pear dagen letter stoar har suster. Dy wenne yn Sélân. Dêr kaem se sels ek wei.\nDy swarte houn wie de boade fan 'e dea. De bern hienen noait in houn sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":128385,"r":"ENGELB_01_017","p":"Gammelke","v":"Ov.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man can smell where a death will occur.","i":"H.E.","o":"Ik: \"Heb ie nooit heurd van leu, dee de tookômst kôn'n vuurspel'n?\"\nIk heb wa es heurd, zoas mien zwaoger, den is nô dood, den hef mie wa es vetöl'n, den was as posbore köm'm owweral, den zer doa en doa geet der gauw een dood. Ik vreug, hoe kan dat dan? Dat kaan'k roek'n, zer he. En dan was 't ok zo.","l":"Twents"},{"n":128386,"r":"ENGELB_01_018","p":"Gammelke","v":"Ov.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Where an owl screeches, someone will soon die.","i":"H.E.","o":"Woa nen oel schreeuwt, heb ik wa es heurd, doa krie'j gauw nen dooi'n.","l":"Twents"},{"n":130015,"r":"VODA_030_13","p":"Uitgeest","v":"N.-H.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A mole is digging under the window. Within three days there will be a death in that house.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"- “O kijk,” zei ze dan, “aan de overkant, zie je die mol?”, zei ze dan. Die zat onder het raam te graven. En dan zei ze: “Over drie dagen is daar een dooie.” En dan was het ook zo. Maar ja, hoor, dat zijn verhalen die m’n moeder me vertelde, …\n- Ja. Ja, ja.\n- … dus dat weet ik natuurlijk niet. Maar in ieder geval, mijn moeder vertelde ons die verhalen, want ze was al… moeder is heel jong getrouwd en die zat altijd met ons alleen en eh… dan wou ze het natuurlijk wel eens spuien en dan vertelde ze dat…"},{"n":210899,"r":"VODA_046_07","p":"Beverwijk","v":"N.-H.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man was walking home and saw a man without a head standing there. Others came to look too, but saw nothing. The man had seen his own death. He went to bed and never woke up again.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"[Fluitend vogeltje op de achtergrond.] \nMijn vader die komt van een schippersfamilie af, die hebben allemaal gevaren, Katwijk, Egmond. Mijn vader zegt, we hadden het over vernoemingen, ik zeg: “Nou, ik ben niet naamziek.” \nHij zeg: “Nou, ik ook niet,” zeg ie, “maar waar ik naar vernoemd ben, die heb z’n eigen dood gezien.” \n“Zo, hoe dat zo?”\nJa, hij zeg: “Die kwam met zijn plunjezak van zee af en hij loopt zo dat steegje door en op de hoek, we woonden op een hoekhuis in Katwijk, en hij kijkt,” hij zeg, “staat te praten met een man zonder hoofd, je ziet er helemaal geen hoofd. En hij gaat naar binnen toe, hij zeg: “Nou, dat is ook wat.” Hij zeg: “Staat er hier op het hoekje van die poort,” zegt ie, “een man zonder hoofd.”” Nou, dan gaan ze allemaal kijken, ze zien niets. Hij is naar bed gegaan en is nooit meer wakker geworden."},{"n":128509,"r":"ENGELB_12_021","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Seeing a fireball as a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death; suppositions about the meaning of seeing a fireball.","i":"H.E.","o":"Kleissen: doe koomp he d’r an, he wol goarn dinger hebn vuur de radio, wat nen öldern keerl in de vieftig, want n öldstn zön van mie den hölp verscheedn moaln met radio’s maakn en elektrisch maakn en dit en dat en zo meer en doe kwam mie d’r ok zo owwer an t kuiern, he was van Niejland. Ik zeg, doe vuur n joar of wat teruw he’w nog wa iets zeen, ik zei, dat har wat met veur te maakn. De vrouw en ik hebt heb zeen, ne grote ballon, ne grote veurbal as t ware, zo opkomn, God, zeg he, mien zuster hef t zölfde zeen, zeg he, ik zeg, hoe kan dat, ja zeen zuster was n paar joar ölder as he en dee har tzölfde zeen en hij was in hoes kömn loopn, o God o God, doar bie oons oons boavn de put was ineens nen grootn bal veur opkömn en doe is he noar boavn hengoan, ie wet wa, dat kort d’rop oe vare stöarvn is, joa, zeg he, ik heb t nooit per slot van könn achterhaaln. le hebt hem met oe beedn zeen, zeg he, ik zej, joa, absoluut, ik zej, ik vertel oe gen lögns.\nEngelbertink: Ik heb d’r toch wa ne veronderstelling bie, ik wet nich of dat woar kan wezn. Rechtevoort wördt dat oetlegd as wiesmakerij, de hel en t vagevuur van vrower, oeteindelik t is al bear veur. Dee veurgeschichte, dat was ok veur. At dee leu in den biebelsn tied misschien ok a wa zeen hebt.\nKleissen: Den veurbal hef de vrouw nich zeen, doe wie bie n buurman warn en inblievn, mer van den veurbal en van dat lecht, dat hef de vrouw","l":"Twents"},{"n":128516,"r":"ENGELB_12_028","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of deaths among people and livestock.","i":"H.E.","o":"Kleissen: No wo’j owwer de heamennekes gangs?\nKl.H.: Doar wet ik niks van, no goa ik vot.\nBen: Ik wol nog efkes koffie doon.\nKl.H.: Ik wil niks hebn.\nBen: Met ne vlak kreantnwegn\nKl.H.: Nen bongn vuur op t hoes, dat wet ik almoal nich, dat kaan’k nich precies biehooldn, op n vuureand, dat gif, boe lang at dat doert, nem mer an van n joar, kan ok wa dree weg weazn, dan gif d’r nen dooin in t gezin, mer at op n achtereand valt, dan he’j t met n veestapel, dan mot d’r wat gebuurn, met ie könt better op n achtereand hebn as op n vuureand en dat hoof zich ok niemand, ooit hoof d’r bie mie te komn en zegn, dat kan nich, man, schei d’r oawer oet, want ie wet d’r gen duvel van, a’j t onderveundn hebt, dan wet ie t ok, dan kos ie te kort, zeg ik dan,","l":"Twents"},{"n":128517,"r":"ENGELB_12_029","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A kind of fireball as a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of deaths.","i":"H.E.","o":"Kleissen: Wat dat oald S. betreft, woar ik straks oawer har, har n stuk laand an gin kaant kanaal en doar hef t ’s oavnds ok nog laat an t weark west, met doe was he in tweedoonkern nog laat an t kanaal an t weark west, en doe har he de kinder ok almoal nog klean en doe per slot van rekn, doe zöt he bie de F. de beum en alns lecht wördn, de teuw an de beum, ineens zöt he ok nen grootn bong en t koomp van vuur van t hoes en geet noar achtern hen. de moor stearft doar. tzölfde geval bie K. bie van der A. an t kanaal bie oons, zöt t ok, he hef t ok zeen doar, dat zag ok verschilnde dinger zo, ik heb d’r ok wa völ meer zeen, wat ik vertel van N., dat is per slot van rekn misschien nog gen tien joar lîedn, en doe zee ik doar ok ne grote bong veur, ik breng de busn vot, ik har t melkn doan ’s oavnds en de busn in tweedoonker was t nog nich ees, en doe zee ik ok zo’n bong veur, net as de moan of zun opgeet, is zoln wa deankn, dat is de moan, mer, he, doar zat de moan ok wa mangs in dea richting, God, t is mer n moment, en dan is t ok vot, zeg t met, zag ik ok opgoan, t t was t oldershoes van dee leu, woar ik straks van vertöl, doe is W.B. is d’r doe kort d’rop stöarvn.","l":"Twents"},{"n":128521,"r":"ENGELB_12_033","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Knocking as a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the later death of someone who dies in the thirteenth night after the knocking on the wall.","i":"H.E.","o":"Kleissen: Mien vaar dan per slot van rekn, in oons hoes, woar wie dan vorger geboorn zint, dat was de Boerrigter en doar ze twee, dree oolde eumkes in hoes hadn en ne tante, den eenn was he aait zo donders gek altied met, he slöap d’r an de delnkamer, zeg mer en doarnöast was n muurke, ze hadn almoal berstiejn, en doar was he zo dondersgek met, met dat eumke, he hef d’r twaalgn daagn bie waakt, alle daagn en nachtn, dachn at he stearft en har den oom zegd: J. goat mer röstig noar ber hen, ie hebt in 12 daagn en nachtn zowat gen sloap meer had, goat no mer röstig noar ber hen en n derteendn nacht, of he geet ok noar ber hen en n derteendn nacht, doe har mien vader har dat klopn a dat klopn n paar joar eerder heurd en n derteendn nacht, he slap per slot van rekn in de kamer d’rnöast en klopn an de muur, klopn an de muur en n oom den stöarf.\nEngelbertink: Koomp dat duur dat oongeluksgetal, derteen?","l":"Twents"},{"n":128522,"r":"ENGELB_12_034","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man who hears knocking outside wants to go there. When the parish priest comes with his black dog to give him the last rites, he thinks the priest comes from the devil.\nThe next day the priest is able to give him the last rites.","i":"H.E.","o":"Kl.H.: Dat heb ik ok metmaakt, bie oons ham n oold meanske, hef mien zuster a zeen, n oold meanske, dat doar stöarf, dat oolde meanske hef lest tied bie oons west, dat was a stokoold en doe gung ze ’s nachtns oet ber en doe zer ze, no mö’k vot, doar klopt d’r een boetn, ik mot d’r weazn, ach, T., doar is niks, goat toch gaauw wier noar ber. Joawa, zie hebt mie klopt, zie wocht op miej, ik mot d’r weazn. Affijn, oolde leu lopt d’r duur, natuurlik dat kan, helemoal normaal, mer zie wördn als mer minder, en de pastoor, ik zer, zee mos bedeend wördn. Pastoor kon d’r niks met beginn, pastoor kwam d’r an met zonnen grootn zwartn hoond bie zich, doar kwam he doe met in dee tied, de pastoor in Geestern, nen grootn zwartn hoond, den har he altied bie zich. He zit in ber, he dach, he zer, ie komt van de duvel, ik mot niks van oe hebn, goat gaauw vot, ik wil niks van oe wetn. Wie konn d’r niks met beginn en niks met beginn, het was de duvel en t bleef de duvel, almoal niks, proatn met hem, he kon d’r niks met beginn, he wol n bedeenn. Toe, zeg de pastoor, ik kom morgenvroeg wel en dan is het wel in orde. En de pastoor kwam ’s morgens wier, bedeent T.: ik wou je wel bedienen. Oh, dat is good, doar zin ik bliej van. Joa. He’j ooit zo iets metmaakt. He is bedeend en zundaagns was ze dood, ja, wat is dat dan?","l":"Twents"},{"n":128523,"r":"ENGELB_12_035","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Lights and fire as a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"H.E.","o":"Kleissen: Doe was ik nog nich geboorn. En wat n breurke van mie is, dat is, loa´k es kiekn n joar of acht junger as ik, of ölder as ik west, vuur mien tied was dat, ik was doe nog nich geboorn en doe ha´w bie oons ne meid H.H. v. S., doar woont d´r ok wat van in Haarbig of Geestern, in ieder geval per slot van rekn, moder was in de kökn, vrower ha´w nog nen bovnkamer an t hoes en doe hadn ze H.H. hadn ze bie oons vuur meid, dee hebt ze joarn had vuur meid, onwies best meanske en ik zeg a wa, t is n joar of wat vuur mien tied west, doe dat jeunkn dan störvn is, mien breur, en doe per slot van rekn, hadn ze H.H. vrower nog, wat zedn ze vrower ok, n kokhoes, of nee, boe neumn ze dat vrower ok n bakhoes, noar t bakhoes har ze hen west, tuffel en spul har ze kokt vuur de vearkn of zowat en doe har t ineens de boavnkamer in voln glorie zeen stoan, alles verlicht en verlecht, doe koomp t in hoes loopn en zeg, Dieka, har t zegd tegn mien moder, hes doe doar wat an had of wat hes doe doar toch in de boavnkamer had? Het was almoal veur en lecht. God, har mien moder zegd, van alns niks; kort d'rnoa har mien breurkn longontsteking, dood, en dat har doe H.H. ok almoal a zeen.\nKl.H.: En net a´j zegt, doar is gelöaf biej.","l":"Twents"},{"n":69992,"r":"VODA_009_02","p":"Terneuzen","v":"Zl.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If people see a procession of funeral carriages with black horses at dusk, it is an omen of a death.","i":"H.E.","o":"M’n moeder die kon d’r toch zo mooi van vertellen he. Zij zei altijd tegen ons: “kinders denk d’rom hoor, als je ’s avonds een keer wat laat uit Noek terug komt, dat je nooit langs de [… de kraker] of langs [suusje] gaat, want daar deug het niet hoor.” M’n moeder en andere mensen uit de buurte die hadden dan meer dan eens in de omgeving in de kouwe polder zo tegen de Noordiek aangezien dat er in ‘t schemerdonker dertig, veertig rouwkoets, nou met twee zwarte paarden ervoor gespannen langzaam voortgetrokken, soms dwars door de andere heen. En die paarden die konden geen poot verzetten of ze raakten een wild [knietje] Zwermen van die beesies dansten de ’s morgens tussen de pijlen en de wagen door. Dat gezegd, dat duurt nooit zo lang he, maar wat wel vreemd was, als die of een ander zoiets gezien hadde, dan kon je d’r vast op rekenen dat er zo eigen in D’n Noek of in de omliggende polders een plotselinge sterfgeval zou voordoen."},{"n":70058,"r":"VODA_009_15","p":"Terneuzen","v":"Zl.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A girl dreams that an innocent lamb is lying in her little brother's cradle. The next morning it turns out the boy has died.","i":"H.E.","o":"Da’ gaat nu eens een keertje nie over spoken en over geesten, maar over een bijzonder gave, namelijk een soort van helderziendheid. De mensen in Axel, die kennen d’r allemaal en ze noeme ze [Douwe Correlie]. ‘Wel,’ zegt Corlie, ‘de mensen in Axel die weten het wel meneer, da’ ik soms dingen zie die d’r voor andere nie ben. Ik zou nie kunnen zeggen hoe dat komt. Ik zit er nie aan te denken, maar opeens moet ik het zien, ook al zou ik het niet willen. Ja, ‘k heb ’t er soms heel moeilijk mee, maar kan me d’r niet tege verzetten. Moe wel een gave zijn zeggen ze, maar ik kan ’t niet verklaren. Begon bij mie al vroeg als meisje van zes of zeven jaar. Moeder had toen een kindje gekregen, mijn broertje, Oscar. ’T was en bleef maar [sukkel] met dat ventje. Als moeder ’t op d’r schoot nam, dan zag je dat [skwimen]. Ik hield veel van mijn broertje, dat nu zes maanden oud was en ik was bang dat da’ ventje zou sterven. Op een avond da’ ik naar bed was gegaan, kon ik ’s nachts nie in slaap komen. We sliepen allemaal in één vertrek en moeder zei tegen vader: ‘Toe, neem jij Corlie, da’ was ik dan, eens op een arm, ik weet nie wat dat kind hed.’ ‘En waarom ga je nie slapen?’ vraag moeder en alle [schijn] vertel ik hur dat ik maar steeds een zelfde beeld voor me zie. ‘Maar wa’ zie je dan?’ vraagt moeder. ‘Ik zie een [mn eigene] een grote bos van zwarte roosjes en in ’t wiegje, waar broertje in l"},{"n":70065,"r":"VODA_009_18","p":"Terneuzen","v":"Zl.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"An owl on the roof is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death, as is the second blossoming of fruit trees.","i":"H.E.","o":"‘Een uil op ’t dak baas,’ zegt hij dan, ‘da’ staat nie hoog mee. Dat betekent altijd ongeluk, ‘k heb ’t thuis driemaal meegemaakt en telkens kort daarop stierf er een kind bij ons en ze mocht d’r ook nooit op verheugen als den appel- of perenboom voor de tweede maal in den bloei komt, want ‘t zij bij uzelf in huis, ’t zij bij uw naaste buren, kunt ge een plotseling sterfgeval verwachten"},{"n":69856,"r":"VODA_007_04","p":"Druten","v":"Gld.","y":1976,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The narrator has experienced a poltergeist that announces when someone is going to die. Every time a little bell rings, someone dies within 14 days.","i":"H.E.","o":"Nou ik denk aan iets wat eh misschien meer te maken heeft met eh met parapsychologie eh het verschijnsel van de klopgeesten, kent u dat? Nou, dat is iets wat ik in mijn jeugd eh direct gewoon bij mij thuis veel meer te maken heb gehad. Met het aankondigen van een doodsbericht. Nou ik zal u het verhaal zo kort mogelijk vertellen. Wij leerde als kinderen van ons vader en moeder in een verhaaltrant dat het een keer gebeurt was dat er in een hoek van de kamer een geluid te horen was als van een wekker. Maar van een zeer onregelmatige wekker he, harder, zachter, sneller, langzamer. En men had eruit geleerd, of begrepe destijds en ervaren ook dat dan binne veertien dagen, drie weken, er iemand uit de familie of kennissenkring zou sterven. Dat verhaal hadden we als kinderen gehoord en het had ons ook altijd eh, nogal verbijsterd he, maar ja wij hadden het begrepen als een verhaal uit een lang vervlogen tijd. Het is geweest in maart 1942 - ik ben de oudste bij ons thuis zodoende kan ik me dat goed herinnere – toen voltrok zich het verschijnsel waar ik bij was. Ik hoorde dat getik en ik zei tegen me vader en moeder: “ik hoor dat klokje waar jullie over verteld hebben”. En me vader en moeder die reageerde op een wijze waarop blijkt dat’s ‘t dus dat ze het ook gehoord hadden maar niet leuk vonden dat ik het gehoord had. Afijn dat werd een beetje onder tafel gemoffeld he, van ach, kom, ja"},{"n":69816,"r":"VODA_007_06","p":"Druten","v":"Gld.","y":1976,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"An old man died on a Friday. That meant his body stayed unburied over Sunday. A corpse that stays unburied over the weekend means that someone else will soon die.","i":"H.E.","o":"Ehm, toen ik hier eh, pas kwam, toen leerde ik in dat dorpje waar ik eh pastoreel werkzaam was de volgende ervaring. Der was een man gestorven, een hele ouwe man in de negentig, en het ongeluk was dat die man was op een vrijdag gestorven. Dat had nogal wat complicaties want het betekende dat die de zondag overstond. En als er in een dorp eh, een overledene overstond in een weekend betekende dat dat er in zeer korte tijd nog iemand zou sterven. En men was erg bang omdat dit een hele oude man was dat de volgende een hele jonge mens was maar de praktijk heeft uitgewezen dat dat niet per se het geval hoeft te zijn."},{"n":128694,"r":"VODA_015_07","p":"Helden","v":"L.","y":1976,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Blooming out of season brings a wedding or a death.","i":"H.E.","o":"En dat was met eh, met die bloei, wie in de zomerdag, dan bleut al het fruit. Maar als dat nao gaat bloeien, en dan haeje de bloem, en dat is wel gebeurd, dat er een ganzen baum totaal in de bloei stond. Dan zagden de oaje mensen: ‘E bloeme nao den tied, nao den haust, nao den tied, dat geft een brulloft of een liek,’ maar het kwam dan goed.","l":"Limburgs"},{"n":128693,"r":"VODA_015_08","p":"Helden","v":"L.","y":1976,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If someone is not buried before a Sunday, another person will die.","i":"H.E.","o":"En dan haeje ze auch dit: ‘Als een liek op enne zondeg bleef staon, dan volgde sjrouwe nog narein op.’","l":"Limburgs"},{"n":128717,"r":"VODA_017_03","p":"Heerlen","v":"L.","y":1976,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Around Christmas, Carnival and Easter there are more accidents in the mine than usual. A mysterious knocking at the back door was said to come from Death wanting to come in. The miner who goes in and out through this door dies three days later in an accident in the mine. Miners made their Christmas confession early because it was thought that the mine claimed its victims around Christmas.","i":"H.E.","o":"Men zegt welles bijvoorbeeld omstreeks Kerstmis, of, of omstreeks eh Carnaval of Pasen dan eh, eh gebeuren er meer ongelukken in de mijn dan eh normaal. En eh men brengt dit ook weer in verband hè, zoals de verhalen wel eens soms zijn hè, met de gebeurtenissen en met eh verzeggingen hè, dat er eh omstreeks de Kerstmis als je dan niet eh niet gauw genoeg je kerstbiecht had gesproken, zogenaamd hè, dan kon je ook wat gebeuren dus deze dingen die hadden een, een zeer diepe religieuze achtergrond, hm. En zo had je nog meer verschillende van die dingen, bijvoorbeeld eh op de Wilhelmina ook verongelukte jaren geleden eens een mijnwerker uit de buurt van Simpelveld. En tevoren had de ouwe moeder van deze mijnwerker telkens een geheimzinnig kloppen gehoord op de achterdeur. Eh, die, die achterdeur welke de zoon steeds in en uitging eh als ie van de mijn kwam of naar de mijn toeging. En daar zei ze bij zichzelf: ‘Dat is de dood die wil binnentreden.’ De dood trad niet daadwerkelijk in dat huis, doch drie dagen later verloor de zoon van de ouwe vrouw op een ongelukkige wijze het leven op de mijn. De kelder zegt dat jaar op jaar telkens in de dagen voor of na de kerstdagen de mijn zijn slachtoffers eist. En dat is verscheidene keren uitgekomen hier, jazeker, jazeker, en we hoorden van mijnwerkers die hun kerstbiecht reeds veertien dagen voor de Kerstmis deden. Ook vlak voor en tijdens de"},{"n":31006,"r":"CJ115010","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man dreams of the funeral of a relative. The dream comes true: two days later a relative dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit droomde ek ris op in nacht fan in bigraffenis. Hy koe net sjen hwa't bigroeven waerd, mar hy koe oan 'e stoet, dy't achter it lyk oan roan sjen dat it famylje fan him wie.\nTwa dagen letter waerd der by heit en dy op it raem kloppe: \"Jimme matte op 'e Streek komme, hwant Aeltsjemuoi is samar plotseling overleden.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31007,"r":"CJ115011","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a cyclist tries to remove a branch from his front wheel while riding, he goes head over heels. The man has a sprained little finger but predicts that this will be his death. The prediction comes true: he dies within the year.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit wie boerearbeider by Kees Oostenbrug op Quatrebras. Op in kear kaem er op 'e fyts fan 't wurk. Hy ried nei hûs ta. Doe krige er in takke yn 't foarste fjild. Dy soe hy der ridendewei úthelje, mar doe sloech er oer de kop. Doe hied er in stikkene pink. Dat wie nochal hwat oankaem, hwant hy moest dêr om nei 't sikenhûs ta. Trije dagen hat er dêr tahâlden. Doe't er thúskaem, sei er tsjin ús mem: \"Ik kom net wer oan 't wurk en ik gean hjir dea oan.\"\nBinnen 't jier rekke hy hjir wei. De lêste wiken hat er yn 't sikenhûs lein, dat wie yn 1954. De dokters seinen: \"Dêr leit in soune man op bêd to stjerren.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31008,"r":"CJ115012","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a man smells the odour of a corpse near the churchyard, a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurt my wolris, hwannear't ik by in tsjerkhôf lâns kom, dat ik in lyklucht yn 'e noas krij. Dan kin men der mar wis fan op oan, dat dêr mei gauwens ien op 't hôf komt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31284,"r":"CJ116401","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When people hear hammering or see flames, it means houses will be built or burn down, respectively. These are omens. Helmdragers (people born with a caul) have to get up at night to foresee deaths in passing funeral processions. When a dog howls eerily or black rooks appear at the door, a death is coming. Wild lanterns were foreshadowings of the later bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit hat it faek hawn oer foartjirmerije. Dan seinen de lju: dêr en dêr komt skielk in hûs to stean. Se ha it timmerjen al heard. Ek seinen se wol: dat hûs mat nochris in kear opbrânne. 't Brânnen is al sjoen woarn. Dat mei it bouwen en timmerjen kaem altyd nei, mar ik kin sa net sizze hokker huzen dat wienen. Yn Garyp gongen dy forhalen.\nHeit fortelde ek oer minsken dy't mei de helm geboaren wienen. Dy moesten nachts út bêd wei om nei in lykstaesje to sjen. Dyselde dy't dan lyk wie, leefde op dat stuit noch. Sokken ha se wol yn Garyp hawn.\nWie der in houn dy't spûkgûlde, dan kaem der ek in sterfgefal. It wienen bipaelde hounen dy't dat dienen, net alle hounen.\nWienen der swarte roeken om 'e doar, dan bitsjutte dat ek in sterfgefal.\nFroeger seagen se yn Garyp huplantearns. Dat wienen ljochtsjes dy't biweegden. Dat hie in bitsjutting, seinen se. Dêr kaem dan in nije wei. De ljochtsjes dat wienen de fytsen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":128529,"r":"ENGELB_13_003","p":"Rossum","v":"Ov.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Screeching owls and a house that seems to be on fire as a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"H.E.","o":"H.E.: Doa he’j ok van die verhaaln, dat ze in de tookomst wat könt zeen, met doadgoan en zoa, dat ne oel ...\nE.M.: A’j nen palmbos bie t hoes hebt en doar zatn van dee uulkes zatn doar in. Dan ko’j net verteln was wis, mer dan gung der en doad, ik heb verschilnde moaln, oons moder ok, nich, en dat ding dan moal schreewde en jaagn hem dan vot, nich,\nH.E.: Is oe dat a mangs passeerd, Eduard, at dat is oetkömn? At dee katoeln doar zatn te schreeuwn.\nE.M.: Ik heb doar nooit zoavöl op oet doan, mer zee löawv dat vrowern nich, Zee löawn dat, nich.\nG.M.: Ja dee leu löawn doar in. En vrower hebt ze toch ok wa mangs zeen, at der een störf, wees wa, n wek of wat vuur tied, dat dan dat hoes in braand steet.\nE.M.: Eh, ja.","l":"Twents"},{"n":128531,"r":"ENGELB_13_005","p":"Rossum","v":"Ov.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A bell that rings during Mass is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"H.E.","o":"H.E.: Ik heb ok wa, Eduard, heurd, as t precies midn onder de mis, he, onder de consecratie, wanneer dan de klokn luudt.\nE.M.: Dan stearft der een.\nH.E.: Is oe dat ok wa es passeerd?\nE.M.: Dat is ok wa mangs oetkömn.\nG.M.: Doar he’k t es moal met ouns vaar owwer had, doe den nog lewde, wees wa, en den har t der es moal met de pastoor owwer had, wees wa, dat kon elkn zundag wa. Want vrower in de oolde keark, dat wees doe ok nog wa, zat ok ne klok in. En at zie preakn, dan kon ze wa precies noagoan. Doe zas t wa nich meer wetn in de oolde keark. Doar achter in doar zat ne klok, met grote wiezers, net as vuur n toornt zit, dan konn ze dat wa precies noagoan. En dee hadn d’r owwer had, mien vader was vrower bie t zangkoor en har t der wa es met de pastoor owwer had, wees wa, dat was nich woar, dat was niet te geloven har he dan wier zegd.\nH.E.: Was dat Dames west?\nG.M.: Dat hef ne aandere pastoor west vrower. Kearkhof of wel hef dat west, wie warn ja misdeender, wie konn ja aait precies zeen, boo laat as t was.\nH.E.: Ja dat ko’j doe nog in dee tied\nG.M.: Mer ik heb wa bie pastoor Dames misdeender west. Wel der in dee tied west hef, dat wet ik nich - Ik, n acht daag, doe hef he ouns doalik bedaankt\nE.M.: ... Ik en Bosch en oold-Vrielink en dat was ja measter Bosch ... en Breewnks Johan met oons veern. Ik gung der op n lestn eand nich meer hen, nich, Bosch dat gung nog wa, mer oold-V","l":"Twents"},{"n":128545,"r":"ENGELB_13_018","p":"Rossum","v":"Ov.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of deaths; a man sees a corpse lying there and cuts off a lock of its hair. The next day he notices that he himself is missing a lock of hair.","i":"H.E.","o":"G.E.: Dee hadn der es moal loopn tusken Mös-Gerrad en Stej-Greads en ik wet nich, of ze noa Hobbelt hebt ze löaw’k weelt, noa Hobbelt hen kaartn\nE.M.: Dien vader hef löaw’k noa Hobbelt goan noa Jannöakn.\nG.M.: Doar hebt ze hen weelt.\nE.M.: Zövnteen joar löaw’k.\nG.M.: Joa dat is eerlik woar, dat hef he zölf a moal vertöln en doe hebt ze doar loopn, wes wa, tuskn Mös-Gerrard en Stej-Greadskn, now en doar bint ze op n ding kömn, doe bint ze heelmoal oet mekaar rapt, loa’k mer zegn, en doe har de Muller zegd, wees wa, woar ik hier op zit, mag de grote God van bovn wetn, kiek en doe achterof, wes wa, doe hadn ze dat noagoan, n paar daag later was doar n liek langs kömn, mer vader har ok a moal vertöln, wes wa, ik wet nich, wat vön knecht, at dat west was en die was ’s oavnds ok in hoes kömn en die was n nienduur inkömn en die was owwer de del hengoan en op de del was he zoawat van de beenn rold en doe he t good bekekn har, wes wa, doe har’t liek west en doe har he toch dacht, wes wa, doe har he de schear kregn, wes wa, en nen vosn hoar afsnedn, en doe har he ’s anderdaagns in t spegel kekn en doe har he zölf nen vosn hoar van n kop of had.\nH.E.: Zol dat hier passeerd wezn?\nG.M.: Woar dat passeerd is, wet ik nich, mer dat he de vaa verscheidne moaln vertöln.\nH.E.: En doe hef he wa ne schrik kregn vanzölf.\nG.M.: Doe nooit heurd, Eduard?\nE.M.: Ik heb t wa es heurd.\nH.E.: Dus he wus zöl","l":"Twents"},{"n":31398,"r":"CJ117402","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1978,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a barn owl or a magpie sits near the house, something serious is about to happen: it is an omen of, for example, death. When two magpies sit near the house, visitors are coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in katûl op 'e nael fan 't hûs sit, dan is dat in min teken. Dan gebeurt der hwat slims.\nAs der in ekster by 't hûs komt, is dat ek in min teken. It is faek in boade fan 'e dea.\nMar binne der twa eksters by hûs, dan wol dat sizze, dat der bisite komt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31909,"r":"CJ120404","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1978,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A girl dreams that a certain man has died. The dream comes true: the man does indeed die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy leinen op in kear yn Klein Groningen - dat is oan diz kant Donkerbroek - mei 't skip to ierdappelladen. Ik wie noch net troud en ik slepte foar yn 'e durk.\nUs Sjouk wie noch in jongfaem. Dy roun op in iere moarn troch de warring hinne nei ús ta. Hja sei: Nou ha 'k sa nuver droomd: Jehannes Boom is dea. (Jehannes Boom wie in âld Eastemarre skipper.)\nDe oare deis kaem Jehannes Keimpema fan Earnewâld ús mei syn skip foarby. Dy moest nei Appelsgea to om ierdappels. Hy sei tsjin heit: \"Sjirk, nou kin 'k jo hwat nijs fortelle. Se ha Jehannes Boom justermoarn dea op bêd foun.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31915,"r":"CJ120505","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1978,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A certain dog howls eerily whenever a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bleeker fan Surhústerfean hie in âld houn. Dy spûkgûlde altyd as der in minske stjerre soe. Nachts seach dat beest it blykber.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31916,"r":"CJ120506","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1978,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man sees a magpie in his yard and suspects a relative has died. The suspicion proves well founded: a mourning letter arrives in the post.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By in sikere Sjirk yn 'e Pein kaem op in moarn in ekster op it hiem stappen. Sjirk sei tsjin syn frou: Nou is der ien yn 'e famylje stoarn.\nJa, sei syn frou, ik soe fan 'e moarn de geit melke; 't beest wie pûr.\nDyselde moarns krigen se in roubrief oer de post. Der wie ien út 'e famylje stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31493,"r":"CJ117914","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When the bell rings in a certain way or a dog howls eerily, a funeral is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 't kloklieden by in bigraffenis koe men hearre of der mei koarten wèr in sterfgefal komme soe.\nDatselde koe men ek fan in houn gewaer wurde. Dy spûkgûlde dan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31506,"r":"CJ118011","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, a death will come very soon. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Spûkgûlen fan in houn tsjut op in sterfgefal. It komt altyd út. As in houn spûkgûlt stjert der fêst ien hiel gau.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31507,"r":"CJ118012","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When the bell tolls deathly, a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de klok deadsk lette, seinen se, kom der ek hiel gau in sterfgefal.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31508,"r":"CJ118013","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a corpse remains unburied over a Sunday, another death will soon follow.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":31805,"r":"CJ119717","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha hjir op 'e heide in houn hawn dy't spûkgûlde. Hy die it allinne as der in sterfgefal tichteby op komst wie, oars hearde men him net. Mar sokke tiden wie er net to hâlden, dan moest er nei bûten ta.\nMem prebearre him dan wol yn 'e hûs to hâlden, mar dat koe se eins noait rêdde. Hy gong dan bûten sitten mei de kop achteroer en dan mei de eagen rjochte op it hûs dêr't in deaden komme soe.\nDe buorlju hienen in jonkje, dat wie siik, mar it waerd aerdich better. Syn mem sei: \"Hy rêdt it op.\"\nMar mem seach wol oan 'e houn dat er 't nèt oprêdde. Hy siet mar achter de hutte to spûkgûlen mei de kop achteroer en draeide de kop nei de reed ta dêr't it lyk lâns moest. Fuort dêrnei, de oare deis al, is it bern stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31892,"r":"CJ120301","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A man claims to have grazed his hand on a coffin during the night and suspects something is going to happen. It is an omen of his wife's death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Pake fan memme kant wenne oan 'e Heidereed. De earste nacht doe't er dêr wenne, gebeurde der hwat. Hy sei de oare moarns: \"Wy kinne hjir wolris hwat bileve. Ik bin hjir fannacht mei de hân tsjin in deakiste oanskaefd, dy't hjir yn 'e keamer stie.\"\nItselde jier hat er syn frou forlern. Hja mat sa'n 40 jier west ha. It is sahwat yn 1873 gebeurd. Us mem wie in famke fan sa'n jier of acht, mar dy wist it har letter noch bêst to herinnerjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31903,"r":"CJ120312","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Spûkgûlet in houn, dan komt der ien to forstjerren. In soad minsken hâlde stellich fol dat it sa is.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31971,"r":"CJ121012","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, a death is coming in the neighbourhood. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Spûkgûlde in houn, dan bitsjutte dat dat der in minske yn dy buert stjerre soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31991,"r":"CJ121110","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men leaude hjir fêst, dat, hwannear't in houn spûkgûlde, dat der dan in sterfgefal op komst wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32115,"r":"CJ122405","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, a death is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn spûkgûlt komt der in sterfgefal. Jan Wiberens de Haan fan Garyp hat yndertiid syn frou forlern. Hja hienen in moai hountsje. Alle nachten spûkgûle it beest. Doe't de frou forstoarn wie, wie 't dien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32181,"r":"CJ122909","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"People are very afraid of a dog starting to howl eerily, because that is supposed to be an omen of something.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foar it spûkgûlen fan in houn wienen de minsken hjir deabinaud, hwant dat kaem altyd nei. Us heit en ús mem ek. Se hawwe 't faek ûnderfoun. Sa'n dier wit mear as in minske formoede kin.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32191,"r":"CJ123004","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When magpies chatter loudly near the house, there will be a death in that house within three days. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters skatteren by hûs, dan wie der binnen de 3 dagen in deaden yn 'e hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32194,"r":"CJ123007","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"When a dog howls eerily, someone is dying.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn oan't spûkgûlen wie, dan bitsjutte dat dat der ien op stjerren lei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32231,"r":"CJ123309","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a magpie chatters close to the house, a death is coming in one's own circle. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Skatterje eksters ticht by hûs, dan komt der in sterfgefal op 'e buert of yn eigen húshâlding.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32232,"r":"CJ123310","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"If a dog howls eerily, a death is coming. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":128572,"r":"ENGELB_15_009","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A screeching owl is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death. An owl that nods at someone is not shot at.","i":"H.E.","o":"H.E.: En oeln? He’j dee wa es mangs heurn schreeuwn?\nF.Ve.: Zeker, dat wet ik nog wa.\nH.E.: Is der ok een stöarvn?\nF.Ve.: Nee, nooit, nooit.\nVr.Vr.: Joa, dat zedn ze vrower altied, at der nen oel schreeuwn, dan stöarf der ean.\nVr. [Wolberink, Jan]: Van dee kwikuulkes ... katoeln.\nF.Ve.: Katoeln, bie oe ha’j der ander joarn, dat mean ik ok. Jan, doe was ik n joar of zes zeuvn\nVr.: as doar ne oel zat ... doar har ik n paar doevn in had\nH.E.: Dat zint dee kleann.\nF.Ve.: Katoeln dat zint dee grootn.\nVr.: No zit ze völ bie de Meier in de rognschuur en in t oolde hoes.\nVr.Vr.: at der ne oel schreeuwn, dan stöarf der gaaw een. Och dat he’w hier vaak had, nich hier wied vandan, oh vaak genog heurn schreeuwn.\nH.E.: Nog nooit wat gebuurd?\nVr.: Dan mosn ze mer dat geweer griepn en der opscheet weelt op de oel. Doe was he wier kömn en zegd “Ik heb der mer nich op schötn. He nikn mie too”.\nVr.Vr.: Wat is t wat e zegn.\nVr.: Vrower warn de leu naa biegeleuvig.","l":"Twents"},{"n":128585,"r":"ENGELB_16_001","p":"Oldenzaal","v":"Ov.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"No belief that the screeching of an owl is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"H.E.","o":"Eng.: Ie hadn t zevn owwer n peerd, he, met dee zintuugn, dat he völ meer wet as n meanske, at dat almoal völ better is ontwikkeld. Zoa he’j ok verhaaln van oeln, wanneer n oel schreeuwt, dan zol der ok een stearvn.\nSp.: Men zeg t wal es, mer ja, ik leuw der nich in.\nEng.: Nee, mer zo’t nich könn verkloarn, zee könt de locht van n meanske, wat sterft, zee hebt dan ne locht bie zik hangn\nSp.: Joa, dee hebt ne locht bie zik hangn.\nEng.: No, dat kan n oel toch roekn? ... n zintuug ...\nSp.: ik heb ze in de weinterdag wa verscheidene moaln heurd, dan zedn ze, ja no, der zol dan binnkort in dee buurt zol der een stearvn.\nVr.: Dat heb ik nog nooit heurd.\nSp.: Joa, dat heb ik wa es heurd, mer t kwam nich oet.\nEng.: Dat is nog nooit passeerd?\nSp.: Nee, in dee moandn of in dat halve joar, dan ko’j ze ’s oavnds wa es heurn schreeuwn, dat zedn ze wa, dat ze dee oeln op dezölfde tiedn wa schreeuwn, in dee buurt zol moal n stearfgeval komn, mer ik heb nooit zegn könn, dat t oet kwam.","l":"Twents"},{"n":128586,"r":"ENGELB_16_002","p":"Oldenzaal","v":"Ov.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Pigeons and goldfinches die after a few days from the smell of a corpse.\nWeather forecasting from animal behaviour.","i":"H.E.","o":"Eng.: En vrower onder de mis, onder de consecratie, wanneer dan precies um elf of tien uur, wanneer de klokn dan t uur angafn en t was precies onder de consecratie en dan zol t ok passeern, dat dan ok een of ander zol stearvn. He’j nooit heurd?\nSp.: ik heb wa heurn verteln, at dat wa kon, of t no gebeurd is, nee\nEng.: zukke gevaln we’j nich\nSp.: Ik nich. Wie hadn nog wa nen voggel hier binn had hangn, nen putter. Dee mot heel gevoelig weazn en dee zol ok stervn, at hier n sterfgeval hier in hoes was, en ie zoln hier nen putter hebn hangn, dan zol t binn de twee daag dan zol den putter ook dood weazn, alleen van dee doodlucht, mos t zik antrekn, a’j in leavn wol heldn, dan mo’j hem votbrengn noam buurman hen aans gung he onherroepelik gung he dood, tenminste dat hadn ze in Losser a metmaakt, at dat veur kwam, nich een moal, mer meerdere moaln, woar zonnen keerl, den dan vöggel har, den n voggel binn har en der zol n sterfgeval weazn dan zol dee doodlucht, zol den voggel antrekn.\nEng.: Ie könt wa noagoan, dat verrottingsproces.\nSp.: en dee zoln der an doodgoan, heb ik wa heurd, dee vöggel hadn\nEng.: Aandere vöggel dan?\nSp.: Aandere vöggel nich.\nEng.: alleen nen putter?\nSp.: alleen nen putter, dee was der gevoelig veur, mer aander wet ik nich\nBr.: Mer doe hes doevn in dee kouw zitn, at der dan n sterfgeval is, at dat meanske dan vot is, begraavn is, dan zol dee doew ok met n paar","l":"Twents"},{"n":128614,"r":"ENGELB_18_011","p":"Enschede","v":"Ov.","y":1981,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Foreseeing a fire by feeling the doorpost; the screeching of an owl is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"H.E.","o":"E: Ik heb wa es mangs heurd, dat een wel at dat van te vuurtn zöag en at den der hen gung en he höl de haand der an an n post, at t dan woarm was, dan gebuurn t rap, wat t koold, dan kon der nog wa nen heeln zet owwer hengoan, vuurdat dat hoes zol ofbraandn.\nWit: Ja, dat weet ik nich, mer doar heb ik t fiene ok nooit van heurd. Zoo deadn ze t en zoo was t.\nE: Wat dach ie van nen oel dan? Nen oel, wel at der schreeuwt. Nen oel, at der nen oel schreeuwt.\nWit: Och doar doo ik nich völ op oet. Nen oel schreeuwt ok at t mooi weer is. En at t slecht weer, schreeuwt he ok, doar hebt ze bie oons ok nooit wa op oet doan, dat leuw'k ok nich at dat zo internoat (?) is, at der nen oel schreeuwt. t Is n akelig geschreeuw en a'j oe dan wat op de hoed haalt, ja no dan kö'j dat wier der noar too wearkn, mer ja at t is, wat wat in zich hef, dan leuw'k niks van.\nWil: Ja, wat leu zint der toch wa bang vuur, want ...\nWit: Dat zeg ik oe, ie möt der op reageern, mer n eenn is völ sapper, n hoond was nich bang en ie möt nich bang weazn, doar kö'j nog wa nen heeln zet met proatn, eer at ze die van n stok afproatn, dat was nog lang zoo nich kloar.\nE: Nee, mer een wel at der rap stearft, den hef a misschien luk de doadslocht bie zich hangn, at nen oel dat rok.\nWit: Ik kan t nich verstoan.\nE: Een wel at der rap stearft, den hef misschien nen doadslocht bie zik hangn. Kiek en at nen oel dat rok, at he dan","l":"Twents"},{"n":128633,"r":"ENGELB_19_002","p":"Weerselo","v":"Ov.","y":1983,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"Seeing in advance that someone has drowned.","i":"H.E.","o":"S: He hef t van te veurtn zeen. Ook a n breur van mien zwoager, van Koster, dat was de oldste zeune en toe komt der nen buurman en zeg he, denk goed um oe kinder, want gistern hebt ze oom Bernard uut t kanaal haald. Net bie t hoes, doar ko'j net tusschen deur veurn, mar n dag of wat later, haaln ze oom Bernard der wa oet. Dood.\nE: Dat zint dan de dinger dee'j van te vuurtn könt vuurzeen, hè.","l":"Twents"},{"n":128639,"r":"ENGELB_19_008","p":"Weerselo","v":"Ov.","y":1983,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"The screeching of an owl or a dog is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death; people resemble the person they are named after.","i":"H.E.","o":"E: Owwer die vuurgeschichtn um doarop teruw te komn hè, zoa-as met de oeln dee könt ja ok vuurspeln, dat der een doad geat, he'j doar ok wat van?\nS: Anders niet, at der ne oele schreeuwt, dan zegt ze, dan komp der ook nen dooin.\nE: En is oe dat er passeerd?\nS: Nee, dat ik zoo weet niet.\nE: En zie zegt ok wa es mangs, at t midn oonder de mis is en at dan de klokn sloat, dan zal der ok gauw nen doadn komn.\nS: Heb ie dat wa es heurd, vrouw?\nV : Nee.\nS: Joa at der ne oele schreeuwn, oh doar geleuft ze in, ja hier en in de Pruuse, overal.\nE: He'j doar nog me verkloaring vuur, of nich?\nS: Ikke nie en as der nen hond hoelt.\nV: At der later zonnen hoond huult ...\nE: En is oe dat wa es owwerkömn?\nV: Joa a zoo vaak\nE: At nen hound huult, dan zal der gauw ...\nS: Nen dooin komn.\nE: He'j doar ne verkloaring, woo at dat no eagnlik koump?\nV: Nee. Hoe kan dat?\nE: He'j was es dacht, zoa verkloar ik. Ik wet nich of t zoa is. Kiek een wel der doad geat, den hef duch mie a wa luk dee locht bie zik.\nS: Ja en dee geest, doar geef ook ma es goed let op; woar'j noar nuumd bint die geest, van woar'j noar nuumd bint, giet in t noageslacht over, want ik bin noar de grootvader van mien moeders vader nuumd; mien broer in Denekamp is noar Derk-ome nuumd, oom Gait, die was zoo eerlik as gold, die is failliet goan, die hef net zoo lang werkt, totdat he der boovn op kwam en die lustn geern n börrelkn, wat hij","l":"Twents"},{"n":128662,"r":"ENGELB_19_031","p":"Weerselo","v":"Ov.","y":1983,"c":"SINSAG 0486","d":"A shooting star means a death.","i":"H.E.","o":"S: Dan is der weer een dood, hè, dan is der weer een dood. Is der weer een ofstöarven, want dan möt der völ valn onder weazn.\nE: Ik heb alleen mer heurd, at der zonne vallende steern, dan ma'j alleen mer ne weans doon.\nS: Nee, dan was der een dood.\nE: Dan was der een doad.\nS: Dan was der een dood.\nE: Is dat wa es passeerd, dat he heelmoal op de ground is daal kömn?\nS: Dat weet ik niet.\nE: Dat he kapot is pleerd?\nS: Ze zegt, dan lig der n heupke sliek, mar ik heb t nooit zeen.\nE: Nee, nee, dat we'j dus nich.","l":"Twents"},{"n":39612,"r":"CBOEK458","p":"Bathmen","v":"Ov.","y":1892,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Assorted folk beliefs: omens and the like.","i":"J.V.","o":"Als een zwaluw zijn nest aan een huis timmert, blijft dit bewaard voor blikseminslag.\nAls men een mes op tafel werpt, valt het meestal opzij; valt het echter met het scherpe naar boven, dan komen er ongelukken; valt het integendeel met de rug naar boven, dan komt er een bruiloft.\nWanneer de koffieboonen in den trom springen, komt er spoedig wind.\nAls de poes zich wascht, of als de ketting boven het vuur, waaraan de pot of ketel hangt, verschiet, komt er volk (men krijgt bezoek).\nAls de vrouw koffie schenkt en er blijft in het kopje bruis op de ingeschonken koffie boven drijven, dan krijgt men geld.\nAls de kippen 's avonds laat naar 't rik [?] gaan, regent het den anderen morgen; als de kippen schreeuwen of kraaien, komt er wind.\nAls de koeien sneulen (d.i. met hun snuit op de deel drukken), komt er regen en wind.\nAls de wilde ganzen vroeg in den herfst van het oosten naar het westen vliegen, komt er een strenge winter. \nAls een jongen aan een meisje (en omgekeerd) een speld geeft met de punt vooruit, dan steekt dit de vriendschap af. (Dalfsen)\nWanneer in de thee een steeltje der theestruik drijft, krijgt men een erfenis.\nAls te Bathmen iemand begraven wordt en het regent dan, zoo is dit een teeken, dat zij de katten niet goed heeft gevoederd.\nAls men 's winters bij koud weder door een vloo wordt geplaagd en gebeten, dan zal de koude nog strenger worden.\nWanneer de zwarte aansla"},{"n":69801,"r":"DYKFRIES2197","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A skipper once heard a strange sound coming from behind his ship. When he went to investigate, he could find nothing. A long time later, when the skipper sailed past the same spot, he fell from his ship into the water. The sounds he made getting back to the bank were the same as those he had heard before, so he knew it had been a voorspook (a ghostly forewarning).","i":"W.D.","o":"Een schipper, in den nacht bij kalm weder zeilende, hoorde iets achter van zijn schip in het water ploffen. Onderzoekende, kon hij niet ontdekken, dat er eenig voorwerp op het dek ontbrak. Toch was er eene polsende beweging in het water zoo geweldig, dat geen snoek van de grootste soort zoo iets zou kunnen doen. Dit gewoel, gepaard met gespat, ging achter het schip om, dwars door de vaart naar den wal, en daar hield het op. Dit was reeds een lange poos geleden, toen dezelfde schipper bij dag langs hetzelfde vaarwater voer. Zonder er aan te denken, wat hem daar wedervaren was, deed de man een mispas en stortte van het schip af. Het vaartuig lag te hoog boven het water om er op te klimmen, de schipper zag zich genoodzaakt dwars door de vaart naar den wal te komen. En nu hoorde hij in het water geheel dezelfde beweging als in dien nacht toen hij nets had kunnen ontdekken. Hij begreep nu dat het toen gebeurde voorspook was geweest."},{"n":69844,"r":"DYKFRIES2233","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"During the repair of a village church tower in 1888, an old woman predicted that a workman in grey stockings would fall from the tower. So as not to risk being that unfortunate man, all the workmen wore black stockings for as long as the work lasted.","i":"W.D.","o":"Bij de herstelling van een dorpskerktoren in 1888 voorspelde eene oude vrouw, dat daar een werkman met grijze kousen van den toren zou vallen: om niet de kans te loopen die ongelukkige te zijn, trokken alle werklieden zwarte kousen aan zoolang dat werk duurde."},{"n":9185,"r":"CBAK0371","p":"Uitdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1903,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man sees the sky turn fiery red and brightly lit. The light becomes an ever narrower strip that finally looks like a sabre. Shortly afterwards a war breaks out.","i":"C.B.","o":"De vader van mijn Uitdammer heeft eens, toen hij van Holysloot naar Uitdam ging, gezien dat de lucht vuurrood en hel verlicht werd. Dat licht werd al smaller en smaller, tot het per slot van rekening een smalle strook werd, precies gelijkend op een sabel met een gevest. Kort daarop brak een bloedige oorlog uit."},{"n":9385,"r":"CBAK0524","p":"Uitdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Shortly before a war breaks out, a fiery red, brightly lit sky can be seen. The light finally becomes a narrow strip that looks like a sabre.","i":"C.B.","o":"Een oude Uitdammer heeft, toen hij van Holysloot naar Uitdam ging, gezien dat de lucht vuurrood werd en hel verlicht. Dat licht werd al smaller en smaller, tot het per slot van rekening een smalle strook werd, precies gelijkend op een sabel met een gevest. Kort daarop is een bloedige oorlog uitgebroken (opgeteekend in 1903).\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.91-92.)"},{"n":42726,"r":"KEMP095","p":"Broek","v":"L.","y":1925,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the high Peel, apparitions are seen in the sky in warm weather. The labourers fear these images as harbingers of momentous events such as disasters and wars.","i":"I.S.","o":"LUCHTVERSCHIJNSELEN.\n\nIn de hooge Peel worden bij heel warme dagen luchtverschijnselen waargenomen. De arbeiders zien in de schepen, torens, huizen en wagens, die zich dan in de lucht vertoonen, voorboden, ,,veurbuukes\" of profetieën van gewichtige gebeurtenissen, als oorlog, rampen en dergelijken. Zij zien deze luchtverschijnselen om die reden niet gaarne."},{"n":42727,"r":"KEMP097","p":"Broek","v":"L.","y":1925,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A priest in the monastery hears bells ringing around bedtime. None of the other brothers hears it, only he. The next day he learned that his mother had died at exactly the time the bells rang.","i":"I.S.","o":"DE DOODSBEL.\n\nIn het klooster te......... hoorde een van de paters bellen, tegen den tijd, dat de kloosterlingen gewoon waren naar bed te gaan. Hij lette er eerst niet op, maar toen het met tusschenpoozen bleef voortduren, dacht hij: hoort de broederportier dat gelui nu niet? Daar het nog langer aanhield, verliet hij zijn cel, ging naar zijn mede-paters en vroeg, of zij het niet hadden hooren bellen. Zij verzekerden hem, niets te hebben gehoord. Hij wilde het niet gelooven, hij had het te duidelijk gehoord. Aan den broederportier gevraagd? Deze had ook niets gehoord.\nOndertusschen duurde voor hem het luide gebel maar steeds voort. Hij ging met den portier naar de poort, opende en zag niets dan nacht. Den volgenden morgen kreeg hij bericht, dat op hetzelfde uur, dat alleen hij het voortdurende bellen had gehoord, zijn moeder overleden was."},{"n":42728,"r":"KEMP098","p":"Broek","v":"L.","y":1925,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In Sweykhuisen near Schinnen, a small black gentleman with a top hat and black gloves always came to ring at the door of the rector of Sweykhuisen whenever someone in the village was about to die.","i":"I.S.","o":"DE DOODSBODE VAN SWEYKHUISEN.\n\nTe Sweykhuisen onder Schinnen kwam altijd een klein zwart heertje met een hoogen hoed op en zwarte handschoenen aan schellen bij den rector van Sweykhuisen, wanneer er iemand in het dorp ging sterven."},{"n":42729,"r":"KEMP099","p":"Broek","v":"L.","y":1925,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In Geleen a clergyman was seen several times in the evening, accompanied by an altar boy in a red tunic. They would walk up and down a few times in front of the house where someone would die within a few days.","i":"I.S.","o":"DE BERECHTING.\n\nTe Geleen werd meerdere malen 's avonds een geestelijke, bekleed met stool en rokket, gezien. Hij was dan vergezeld van een misdienaar in roode tuniek, dragend de schel en het Iicht. Zij liepen dan eenige malen op en neer voor het huis, waar binnen eenige dagen iemand zou sterven."},{"n":42730,"r":"KEMP100","p":"Broek","v":"L.","y":1925,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When the last baron De Keverbergh, lord of Aldenghoir castle near Haelen, lay dying, three hard, short blows were suddenly heard on the iron castle gate. It was Death, who always knocks on gate and door to take the last of a line along on the great journey.","i":"I.S.","o":"DE DOOD KLOPT.\n\nToen de laatste baron de Keverbergh, heer van den burcht Aldenghoir bij Haelen te sterven lag, werden er plots drie harde, korte slagen op de ijzeren burchtpoort gehoord. Het was de dood, die op poort en deur slaat om den laatsten van een stam mee te nemen voor de groote reis. Dat deed hij ook aan den Aldenghoir. Daar had hij met den grooten bronzen klopper op de ijzeren poort geslagen en de ziel van den laatsten de Keverbergh d'Aldenghoir meegenomen."},{"n":42731,"r":"KEMP101","p":"Broek","v":"L.","y":1925,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Young people from Vijlen-Vaals saw a fire broom fall on the house of one of their friends. They thought someone there would soon die. One boy did not believe it, but just recently a streak of light had fallen on his own house. Within a week a sister of their friend died, as did the mother of the boy who claimed not to believe in \"fire beings\".","i":"I.S.","o":"DE VURIGE BEZEM.\n\nEenige jongelui van Vijlen-Vaals gingen 's avonds laat naar huis en zagen een vurigen bezem uit de lucht vallen op het huis van een van hun vrienden. \"Je zult zien, dat iemand uit dat huis gaat sterven\", zeiden ze tot elkaar. Er was er echter één bij, die daarom moest lachen. De anderen vonden dat zoo belachelijk niet. Hij beloofde het te zullen gelooven, indien het uitkwam. Want eenige dagen van te voren had ook hij zulk een lichtende streep op het huis van zijn ouders zien vallen.\nBinnen den tijd van een week stierf een zuster van hun vriend en de moeder van den jonkman, die beweerde niet te gelooven aan \"vuurwezens\"."},{"n":42733,"r":"KEMP103","p":"Broek","v":"L.","y":1925,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening the youngest son of a widow sees a small white man coming up the stairs. It happens at the very moment his older brother, who is serving in the Indies army, dies.","i":"I.S.","o":"DE DOODSBODE.\n\nIn de z.g. \"oude katoenfabriek\" aan de Van Hasseltkade te Maastricht, woonde een weduwe met twee kinderen, waarvan de oudste zoon in bet Indische leger diende. Op zekeren morgen kwam die weduwe terug van de water en vuurvrouw en stond het jongste zoontje boven aan de trap op haar te wachten in de opening van de kamerdeur. Hij zag, hoe vóór zijn moeder een klein wit rnannetje de trap opkwam. Het had een wit hemd aan en droeg op bet hoofd een witte slaapmuts. Het gelaat was niet goed te onderscheiden. Toen het ongeveer bij hem was, verdween het plotseling. Hij schrok zoo, dat hij het geziene eerst drie dagen later aan zijn moeder durfde te vertellen.\nEenigen tijd later kreeg de weduwe een brief uit Indië. Daarin werd haar bericht, dat haar zoon daar was overleden. En wonder, het uur en de dag van bet overlijden waren dezelfden, als toen haar zoontje het kleine witte mannetje vóór haar de trap had zien opkomen."},{"n":42734,"r":"KEMP104","p":"Broek","v":"L.","y":1925,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the evening a man sees a glowing figure. She is wearing a wedding dress and holding a bridal bouquet. At a mansion the door opens for her by itself and closes behind her again. Such apparitions are also counted among the messengers of death.","i":"I.S.","o":"DE DOODSBRUID.\n\nIemand kwam op zekeren avond, na middernacht, van zijn werk. Voorbij de Capucijnenstraat te Maastricht komende, zag hij vooraan in de straat een gedaante, die als het ware licht van zich gaf. Hij was niet van de bangsten en wilde daar meer van weten. Hij volgde de gestalte, die er uit zag als een bruid in witte zijde en voile gekleed. Bij het heerenhuis van Tielens gekornen, schreed zij daar den stoep op. Ze keerde zich daarbij half om en toen zag de man, dat zij een grooten ruiker ,,fleurs d'oranges\" het traditioneele bruidsbouquet in de hand hield. Hij zag ook hoe de deur van het heerenhuis zich vanzelf opende. De bruid trad binnen en de deur sloot zich weer vanzelf achter haar. Ook deze verschijningen worden tot de doodsboden gerekend."},{"n":42736,"r":"KEMP105","p":"Broek","v":"L.","y":1925,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On 26 June 1678 an illuminated cross was seen in the sky above the Greatheide, accompanied by an army being attacked by a giant, also with an army, led by a lion. About a month later a battle was fought on the same spot between the French and the Allies.","i":"I.S.","o":"WONDERLIJK VERSCHIJNSEL IN DE LUCHT.\n\nOp 26 Juni 1678 werd boven de Graetheide, tusschen Sittard en Urmond, een helderschijnend kruis in de lucht gezien, vergezeld van een grooten man en gevolgd door voetknechten en ruiters. Van de tegenovergestelde zijde verscheen ook een reus met een talrijk leger, dat werd aangevoerd door een leeuw. Toen de beide legers elkaar genaderd waren, viel de leeuw op den man van het kruis aan en velde hem neer de legers spatten vervolgens uit elkaar, terwijl de leeuw zich op zijn achterpooten richtte en verdween. Ter plaatse waar dit verschijnsel in de lucht werd gezien, werdden 10 en 20 Juli 1678 een gevecht geleverd tusschen de Franschen en de Geallieerden."},{"n":42737,"r":"KEMP106","p":"Broek","v":"L.","y":1925,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the year 1488 three suns are said to have been visible. That year there was such scarcity in and around Maastricht that people were forced to eat ground straw.","i":"I.S.","o":"DRIE ZONNEN.\n\nIn het jaar 1488 zouden er drie zonnen zichtbaar zijn geweest. Er was dat jaar te Maastricht en omgeving zulke schaarschte, dat de menschen genoodzaakt waren gemalen stroo te eten."},{"n":42330,"r":"LAAN016e","p":"Lellens","v":"Gr.","y":1930,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man calls out to an empty horse and cart to halt. The horses stop. You should not walk along the side of the road at night, for then the hearse will drive you into the ditch. But do not walk in the middle of the road either, for then you will end up under it.","i":"E.F.","o":"Binnen ook gounent, dij meer kinnen as 'n aander. 't Was 's mörns om 'n uur òf tien, dou wie mit 'n man òf vief zes in Moushòrn stonden in Midwòlle.\nHail in de verte kwam der 'n boerenwoagen aan. Dood bedoard zee Braauwer: zek dij woagen es stil stoan loaten?\nHai keek strak de weg langs; 'ho!' zee e. 'n Poar tellen loater ston de woagen stil.\nDer was gain sproake van, dat peerden 't heuren konden; woagen was nòg wel 'n ketaaier wied weg. \nWeer 'n poar tellen loater zee Braauwer: 'Zo is 't goud; vot mor weer!' De peerden zetten weer aan; 't was de boerenwoagen van Veldhoes, twij peerden der veur, grootknecht op 't vouerkistje.\n\nMor van veurlopen gesproken. Ie mouten 's oavends nait aan de kaant van de weg lopen; din kìnje van 'n veurloop mor zo in sloot schoven wòrden. Ook mòie nooit in 'n woagenspoor lopen; veur ie der om dìnken, lig ie din onder de woagen; dij hòldt naarns veur stil. Ook midden op de weg mout ie nait komen. Weest verzichtig!","l":"Gronings"},{"n":47339,"r":"SINUTSAG034","p":"Utrecht","v":"Utr.","y":1938,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"After Halley's comet appeared in the sky, the emperor became mortally ill. On the Bayeux Tapestry the people can be seen pointing at the comet in fear.","i":"M.H.","o":"Kometen.\n\nWat sleept een staertster al ellenden\nEn jammer na!\nAls Goden zulk een voorbo zenden\nDan dient men dra\nDeez' springkaer naer te speuren,\nTe mercken uit\nWat bron het spruit\nDat vleck en volck zal treuren.\n\nJ.v.d. Vondel \"De Leeuwendalers\" \n\nAnno 1066 in April ging keizer Hendrik IV naar Utrecht om het paaschfeest te vieren. Toen verscheen daar een verschrikkelijke komeet, wel veertien dagen lang. Kort nadien, in de maand Mei, werd de keizer doodziek; hij lag ter neer te Fitzlar in Hessen en de artsen hadden hem al opgegeven. Deze staartster was de komeet Halley, wier verschijning vermeld wordt in alle kronieken die handelen over den slag bij Hastings (1066). Op het vermaarde tapijt van Bayeux ziet men o.a. koning Harold, den tegenstander van Willem de Veroveraar op zijn troon zitten, terwijl uit zijn blik groote ontsteltenis spreekt. Boven het paleis ziet men de komeet, waarnaar het volk in de stad met angst wijst. Bij de staartster zijn de volgende woorden in het tapijt geweven: Istimirant(ur) stella(m), d.w.z. \"zij daarginds zien met verbazing naar de ster.\""},{"n":47341,"r":"SINUTSAG036","p":"Utrecht","v":"Utr.","y":1938,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Shooting stars were said to point to the approaching end of the world.","i":"M.H.","o":"Andere voorboden van onheil.\n\nEen groot aantal vallende sterren, een verschijnsel dat om de drie-en-dertig jaar terugkeert, wees op het naderend einde der wereld. \"Anno Christi 713 heeft men hier overal zulcke ongewoonlijcke en vreemde commotien des nachts aen den hemel gesien, dat et scheen, alsof de sterren van den hemel vielen; doch daerop is gevolghd sulcken harden, fellen en schrickelijken winter, dat men niet en heeft konnen tellen de menichte der menschen en beesten, die louter door koude zijn gestorven.\""},{"n":47342,"r":"SINUTSAG037","p":"Utrecht","v":"Utr.","y":1938,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A solar eclipse was seen as a miracle.","i":"M.H.","o":"Andere vooorboden van onheil.\n\nOok een zonsverduistering was een wonder, waarvan de heugenis voor immer bewaard moest blijven. Omtrent de laatste dagen van de maand Mei 1033 zag men, dat de zon haar licht aan de aarde ontzegde, \"aentrok een sapphiers couleur, verthoonende een halve ronde, ghelijck aen een groeyende maen waardoor de menschen elkander aenmerkende saegen een doodtverve in hun aenschijn, alle andere schepselen scheenen geluwe te wezen.\""},{"n":72550,"r":"SINNINGHE02","p":"Arnhem","v":"Gld.","y":1943,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The monastery of Monnikhuizen is said to have been founded in 1328 by Count Reinoud II of Gelre in memory of fallen soldiers. He did this on the spot where an old man claimed to have heard angels singing and seen lights years before.","i":"J.R.W.S.","o":"In het jaar 1328 behaalde Reinoud II van Gelre een groote overwinning op de Luikenaars, die tegen hun bisschop waren opgestaan. Uit dank voor die overwinning en ter wille van de zielen der gesneuvelden besloot hij een klooster te stichten.\nLang bleef het bij een belofte, maar eens in 1342, toen de hertog met zijn gevolg in den omtrek van Arnhem toefde, vertelde een oude man hem, dat hij op een bepaalde plek, jaren geleden, gezang der engelen had gehoord en schitterende lichten had gezien.\nDe abt van Marienweerd, die met den hertog was, knielde toen neer op die plaats om God te loven en hoorde een stem die sprak: ''Ik heb mij die plaats uitgekozen.''\nOvertuigd door die teekenen besloot hertog Reinoud hier een klooster te bouwen voor de Karthuizers."},{"n":20078,"r":"CJ016713","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If you dream of a funeral, a wedding will follow.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":20082,"r":"CJ016717","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A few people hear the fisherman Hanne moaning in his little boat, but when they go to look there is nothing to be seen. Two days later the same fisherman breaks his leg and moans exactly as had been heard before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon hearden us op in joun Hanne Foekes, de fisker, dy't to Eastemar by de opslach yn syn aekje lei, oatmoedich kjirmjen. Hja dêr hinne, mar de aek wie leech. Twa jounen letter bruts Hanne Foekes de skonk. Hy kjirme krekt sa, lyk as de minsken it tofoaren heard hiene.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20083,"r":"CJ016718","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Three brothers hear people chopping wood three evenings in a row. When they go to look, there is nothing to be seen. On the fifth day people really are chopping wood. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Trije bruorren to Eastemar hearden trije jounen achter elkoar op 'e dyk fan Sapelân guon oan it houtkappen. Mar alle trije kearen, dat se der hinne gongen, wie der neat to sjen. Mar de fyfte dei woarde op dyselde dyk it hout kapt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20084,"r":"CJ016719","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If it is cold at the moment you receive an omen, what you have seen or heard will happen in the distant future; if it is warm, in the near future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wie it op it stuit dat ien hwat hearde of seach, kâld, dan duorre it lange tiid dat it neikom.\nWie it waerm, dan gebeurde it mei gauwens.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24615,"r":"CJ048301","p":"Oosterwierum","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A farmhand warns his mates to leave, because a ship is coming across the water. It is a vision of the future: a year later the land floods.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 1824 wienen der minsken yn 't lân op in moarntiid yn 'e Sensmeer ûnder Blauhûs. Doe sei in jonge ynienen: \"Minsken, wy matte hjir wei! Der komt in skip oan! 't Is allegearre wetter!\"\nMar de minsken seinen: \"Dû bist net wiis!\"\n't Wie moai sinneskyn-waer.\nMar it oare jiers, yn 1825 streamde alles oer. It séwetter brûsde oer de diken hinne. Dat hie dy jonge sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24616,"r":"CJ048302","p":"Oosterwierum","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man foresees that he will fall from the church tower when the church is built. The vision comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Wytgaerd foel ien fan 'e toer, doe't de tsjerke boud waerd. Hy hie dat fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21722,"r":"CJ028310","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1951,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On his way to sell mats, the narrator's father sees two armies approaching in the clouds. The clouds descend and a battle is fought. It is an omen of the First World War. When the real war breaks out, the father knows he will live through the whole war and that in the end neither side will win it. This came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Winterdeis flochten wy thús matten. Mem sutele se faek út mei de karre, mar heit ek wol us. Heit hie ûnder tsjinst by de jagers west en koe de hiele soldaterije.\nHeit ried us mei de mattekarre fan Boelensloane nei Holwert. Hy soe nei 't Amelân ta.\nHy wie tusken Dokkum en Holwert yn mei de karre.\n't Wie likernôch yn 1907.\nDer kommen greate wolkens oan 'e loft. Hynstefolk, soldaten kommen der oan. Fan 'e oare kant kom ék in great leger. Hja wienen omtrint oan elkoar ta (Fantofoaren hienen se al sketten, dat duorre wel trije ûren). It wie allegearre soldatenfolk.\nDoe sakke 't fan beide kanten del. 't Fechtsjen wie dien.\nDoe 't yn 1914 de oorloch útbriek, sei heit: \"Dizze hiele ooloch bileef ik. Ik ha de ein der fan sjoen oan 'e himel. Gjin fan beiden wint it,\" sei er.\nHy hat it bileefd. Hy is stoarn yn 1938.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24611,"r":"CJ048001","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1951,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman and a maid hear footsteps and the sound of a key in the lock, although there is nothing to be seen. It is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event): later someone appears and the same sounds are heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e goudsmitswinkel fan Kylstra to Drachten hearden de frou en de faem it op 'e stoepe: Stap-stap-stap- \nDe kaei woarde yn 'e doar omdraeid. De faem en de frou sieten op 'e toanbank. Dit wie Kylstra, net ien oars, mar it wie syn geest.\nIn skoft letter presys deselde stappen, wer krektsa de kaei omdraeid en dêr forskynde Kylstra","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21921,"r":"CJ029906","p":"Kûkherne","v":"Fr.","y":1953,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman hears a strange sound outside. When she goes to look, there is nothing to be seen. The following winter she hears an odd fellow making the same sound. It was a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie by de houten brêge to Kûkherne. It stoarme hiel bot. Ynienen hearde ús mem in fremd lûd bûtendoar. Sy gong derút om to sjen, mar der wie neat.\nEven neitiid woarde it winter. Doe hearde hja it lûd wer. Der stie in ploech jongfolk. Ien fan har hie dat lûd. It wie in fremden-ien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15512,"r":"CJ002302","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1954,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One day a woman walks past the house where a man has died and hears a hellish racket coming from the barn, as if planks and beams were being thrown around. Later, after an inheritance, the house is demolished and a new one is built on the same spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Antsje Pûde kom us in kear yn it hûs, dêr't Popke Simens yn forstoarn is. Hja fortelde, it gong der wol sa bot oan wei yn 'e skuorre. De lju smieten mar mei balken en planken om.\nLetter is troch erverij it hûs der ôf kom en ha se der in nije plaets delset. 't Wie yn 'e Hamster Pein. De nije biwenner wie Frâns van der Burg.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21785,"r":"CJ0286B14","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1954,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A minister is being driven home by horse and cart when a stone wall blocks the horse's way. It is a voorgezicht (a vision of a future event): later a bridge is built on that spot. If the vision comes in the small hours, it takes a long time before what was seen actually happens; if it comes in the early part of the night, it takes only a short time.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Rypke Paulusma wie rider fan ds. v. Herwaarden fan Garyp. Hja rieden us in kear nei Ljouwert om healwei seizen yn 'e winter. Samar ynienen woarde it reau op 'e berm set. Der stie in muorre foar 't hynder, it beest koe net fierder. Dêrom moest it wol oerside.\nDe doomny en Rypke seagen de muorre allebeide.\nLetter kom dêr de tsjintwurdige brêge.\nIt gebeurde yn 'e neinacht en it duorre dus lang eardat it neikom. Gebeurt it yn 'e foarnacht, dan duorret it koart. (ik meen me te herinneren, dat het de Fonejachtsbrug was A.A.J.)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23647,"r":"CJ040509","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1954,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once heard strange noises coming from a ship. Later the person living on the ship was attacked, and the same noises were heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Master Veenstra fan Stiensgea fortelde us:\nIk wie noch in jonge man. Us mem wie widdou. \nDoe roan ik us by de Feanster feart lâns. Dêr lei in wenskipke, dêr't in âld man yn wenne.\nDer kommen rare gelûden út dat wenskipke wei.\nLetter is dêr in âld man oerfallen, doe woarden dyselde rare lûden heard. 't Wie sahwat yn 1910.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23648,"r":"CJ040510","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1954,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a man heard a bang. He saw a few men running off in different directions. Later an accident happened, and it was exactly the same scene.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Readskuorre stie in âld boerespultsje mei in boven- en ûnderdoar. 't Wie yn 'e nacht en ljochtmoannewaer. Pake soe der út to pisjen.\nHy heart ynienen in slach. In pear roannen de reed del nei 't westen, doe in pear nei 't oasten. Twa oaren kommen op it hiem.\nPake die de doar ticht. Letter gebeurde dêr in ûngelok mei krekt deselde sitewaesjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15761,"r":"CJ003011","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1955,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening some people in Kûkherne see a little boy on crutches walking onto the farmyard of a young couple. The following year a boy is born to that couple who later has to walk on crutches.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in joune let kommen guon dy't to jounpraten west hienen werom. Doe seagen se dat der ergens yn Kûkherne in jonkje foar har oproan op krukken. It jonkje roan in hiem op, dêr't jonge minsken wennen. Yn dat hûs woarde it oare jiers in jonkje geboaren, dat letter op krukken roan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15763,"r":"CJ003013","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1955,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Two men hear hammering and knocking at night on a piece of land near the Kollumersweagerlânnen. Later a farm is built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Kollumersweagerlânnen hearde ien us sa'n 60 jier lyn om sahwat twa ûre yn 'e moarn in klopjen en in timmerjen op in stik lân. Hy kom fan 'e faem werom. Syn maet wie al om 12 ûre fan 'e faem thúskom. Dy hie it èk heard. Letter is dêr in boerespul kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15764,"r":"CJ003014","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1955,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People hear a thud on the Twizelerheide, and some time later a barn is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wienen minsken, dy hearden op 'e Twizelerheide in greate plof. In skoftsje letter woarde dêr in skuorre delsmiten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":43469,"r":"AMPT000508","p":"Hasselt","v":"Ov.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A red sky is seen as an omen of war.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"Het was voor 1914. Ik was op een vergadering geweest en ik kwam thuis. Ik was toen net nog met mijn eerste vrouw getrouwd. Ze was erg bang. De hele hemel was rood geweest aan de noordzijde. Alles was bloed. Er zou nu wel gauw oorlog komen. Ook andere mensen hadden het gezien en inderdaad kwam toen al gauw de oorlog 1914-18."},{"n":43550,"r":"AMPT000706","p":"Zwolle","v":"Ov.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man believes it is a bad omen when all the lines on a ship are stuck, and sees the later storm in which everything on deck is washed away as the result.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"Eens zat bij mijn vader op het schip alles vast en het was een heel werk om alle lijnen weer los te krijgen. Mijn vader zei: \"Dat is een kwaad veurteken.\" Er kwam later een grote storm en alles op het dek sloeg weg.","l":"Overijssels"},{"n":21237,"r":"CJ025102","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On the spot where a Reformed church now stands, psalm singing was heard in the old days.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op it plak dêr't nou de grifformearde tsjerke stiet, ha se froeger fan tofoaren psalmsjongen heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":69270,"r":"ENGELS000327","p":"Kessel","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Robbers leave when a knife struck into the table begins to quiver.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Rovers:\nIn Beesel viel vroeger een roversbende van 8-10 man gedurende de Kerstmis een boerderij binnen, waar een oude moeder en de dienstmeid alleen thuis waren. Ze bonden de meid met een prop in de mond op een stoel, en dwongen de vrouw, alles aan te wijzen. Een der rovers sloeg een groot dolkmes in de tafel, en bleef daarbij de wacht houden. Letterlijk alles, wat het meenemen waard was, werd geplunderd, o.a. linnen, geld, en koperen vaatwerk.\nOpeens begon het mes in de tafel te trillen. De rover sloeg alarm, en de bende ging er tussenuit, precies vóórdat het kerkvolk thuis kwam. Later zag de boer zelf koperwerk uit de buit op de markt in Roermond te koop aanbieden."},{"n":209684,"r":"HOL000904","p":"Lienden","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Meowing by white cats foretells misfortune.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Spookdieren. Als witte katten liepen te miauwen, voorspelde dit niet veel goeds."},{"n":130739,"r":"KEUNING000107","p":"Feanwâldsterwâl","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hearing hammering at the neighbours' at midnight, but there is nothing to be seen. Later a chicken coop is built. Hearing the scraping of skates when there is no ice; a few days later there is skating. Hearing the sound of trains that do not come.","i":"S.K.","o":"It is es bard, dat wy (hja, dy 't dizze forhalen fortelde, en gezin) nachts om toalf ûre hinne, altyd getimmer hearden by de buorljue. Wy binne der wol is ôfgien, om to sjen hwat hja dienen, mar dan hearden en seagen wy neat. In pear dagen letter timmeren de buorljue in hinnehok efter it hûs.\nIt wie faek yn 'e winter dat min op 'e brêgge hjir efter de buorren redens krassen hearde. En der lei noch gjin skyltsje iis yn de feart. Mar in pear dagen letter koe min dan fêst ride.\nOp it selde plak hearde min ek faek in trein oankommen. En der kaem net ien oan.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130783,"r":"KEUNING000703","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On a spot where men hear hammering at night and see a timber frame standing, though there is nothing there, a farm is later built.","i":"S.K.","o":"It is ek es bard, dat se wer to mudzjen wierne, doe hearden se midden op de Kloksheide yn 'e nacht timmerjen. En hja seagen in almachtig great byntwurk omheech stean. Femme sei tsjin Albert: \"Dat wurdt gâns in pleats.\" Mar der wier neat fansels. In skoft letter is dêr in pleats set.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130802,"r":"KEUNING000911","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Correct prediction of a child's sex.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ik ha acht oerbeppesizters. It binne allegearre jonges. Ik wist it altyd foarút al. Mei de leste fregen myn bern al: \"Hwat wurdt it mem? In famke. nou?\"\n\"Ne,\" sei 'k, \"it wurdt wer in jonge.\" \nDoe 't it bern der wier, riedt de heit hjir forby. hy skodde de fûst nei my. Mar it wier mar gekhyt hear.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130804,"r":"KEUNING000913","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One magpie by the house means misfortune, two magpies mean there is news.","i":"S.K.","o":"Hiene je ien akster om 'e doar, dan bisjutte dit, dat er in ûngelok barre soe. Wierne der twa, dan bitsjutte dit nijs.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130878,"r":"KEUNING001805","p":"Wâlterswâld","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Seeing the Northern Lights means war is coming.","i":"S.K.","o":"Alde T. sei in kear tsjin ús, doe 't wy it Noarderljocht sjen koene: \"Nou krije wy oarloch.\"","l":"Fries"},{"n":130890,"r":"KEUNING002005","p":"Westergeast","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Where will-o'-the-wisps go out, an accident will happen.","i":"S.K.","o":"Min seach froeger faek hipljochten. Op it plak, hwer 't dy ljochten útgiene, soe in ûngelok barre.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130919,"r":"KEUNING002402","p":"Suwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A schoolmaster believes that a sound like planks being thrown about is an omen of later building. It turns out pigs are the cause, but the schoolmaster holds on to witchcraft.","i":"S.K.","o":"Op in kear wier ús skoalmaster by ús. Wy hearden iderkear in lûd, krekt as der mei planken smiten waerd.\nMaster sei: \"Hjir wurdt yn it koart hwat bouwd. Ik hear se al mei planken smiten.\"\nDoe wy nei efteren gyngen, waerd it lûd dúdliker. En doe 't wy by it bargehok kamen, waerd alles dúdlik. It greate hok wier mei skutten yn aparte hokken fordield. Dy skutten wierne fan losse planken makke. Dy planken leine fansels yn gleuven. Sa koene wy maklik fan twa lytse ien great hok meitsje. Nou tilde in baerch iderkear mei syn snute sa 'n planke op en liet him wer ploffe. Dat wier it lûd. Mar master leauwde dochs noch mar oan tsjoenderij.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130929,"r":"KEUNING002703","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On the spot where a stable has been built, the sound of hammering was heard beforehand.","i":"S.K.","o":"Der waerd hjir ek al ris timmerjen heard sûnder dat der ien oan it timmerjen wier. Letter waerd op dat plak in bûthus boud.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130973,"r":"KEUNING003107","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A chattering magpie is a good omen, a silent magpie brings misfortune.","i":"S.K.","o":"As in akster op it hiem kaem en hy skattere, dan wier it goed, mar as hy der stil op kaem, barde der in ûngelok.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130974,"r":"KEUNING003108","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A bird tapping on the window is a sign of a letter coming.","i":"S.K."},{"n":131037,"r":"KEUNING003803","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Little lights that floated through the air are later seen as an omen of bicycle lamps.","i":"S.K.","o":"Froeger seagen se faek ljochten troch de loft fleanen. Doe 't er letter fytsen kamen mei lantearnen der oan, seine de minsken: \"Dy ljochten fan froeger is fêst foartsjirmerij west.\"","l":"Fries"},{"n":131113,"r":"KEUNING004507","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Magpies by the house bring messages, or if two magpies chatter, someone is bewitched.","i":"S.K.","o":"As der aksters by hûs wienen, brochten se biricht oer. Wiene der twa, dy 't skatteren, dan wie dêr ien bitsjoend.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131114,"r":"KEUNING004508","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The top of the lamp wick burning is a sign that a witch is coming.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ús mem sei altyd, dat, as der in kop op de laempekous barnde, der in tsjoenster komme soe.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131153,"r":"KEUNING005201","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A prediction of the place and time a house will burn down comes true.","i":"S.K.","o":"It wie yn 'e maeitiid. Ús heit trof in man, fan hwa sein waerd, dat hy foarspellingen die, dy 't altyd útkamen.\nHeit sei tsjin him: \"Hoe is it, sjoch je noch wol ris hwat?\"\n\"Ja,\" sei de man, \"it twadde hûs oer de brêge sil ôfbarne. Sa om Drachtster merke hinne.\" En it kaem wer út.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131157,"r":"KEUNING005205","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The seller of a sheep that drowns shortly after the sale says he already knew it would happen.","i":"S.K.","o":"Der wie hjir ris in arbeider, dy hie in pûr bêst skiep. It joech sa bêst, dat de buorljue sprutsen der fan. En doe forkoft hy op in kear dat skiep.\n\"Hoe kin jo sa 'n skiep nou forkeapje,\" seinen se tsjin him.\n\"Ik bin hwat yn 'e war west,\" sei hy.\nMar 5 dagen letter fordronk it skiep. En de arbeider fortelde, dat hy dat wol witen hie, dat dit barre soe.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131185,"r":"KEUNING005603","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Haunting at an uninhabited farm where livestock still in the stable, though securely tied up, is soon loose again.","i":"S.K.","o":"Yn in pleats yn Bomburgum spûke it ek, hat myn man, dy dêr weikomt, my wol ris forteld. Dizze pleats waerd net mear biwenne. Mar de stie noch al fé op stâl. De arbeiders doarsten der jouns hast net hinne to fuorjen. Bisten, dy goed fêst makke wienen, rounen in skoftsje letter los.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131187,"r":"KEUNING005605","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Seeing will-o'-the-wisps or wild lanterns, which were later said to have been the first bicycle lamps.","i":"S.K.","o":"Der waerd ek forteld, dat it op de Hegebrechster Loane spûke. Ek wylde lantearnen. Letter waerd der sein, dat it de earste fytslantearne by ús wie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131200,"r":"KEUNING005804","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Where wild lanterns flew, houses were later built.","i":"S.K.","o":"Op altyd it selde plak seach min froeger wylde lantearnen fleanen. Letter binne dêr huzen boud. Jouns sjocht min nou de ljochten fan de huzen, wer foarhinne de wylde lantearnen wienen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131220,"r":"KEUNING006006","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A chattering bird is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a witch coming.","i":"S.K.","o":"As der in fûgel yn de beammen tige lûd siet to skatterjen, dan waerd der sein: \"Der is fêst in tsjoenster op komst.\"","l":"Fries"},{"n":131259,"r":"KEUNING006414","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A noise turns out to have been an omen of a barn collapsing.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ús beppe sei ris tsjin mem: \"O heden G. hwat sille wy nou bilibje, hwat in lawaei. Hwat sille wy nou bilibje.\" Ús mem hearde neat, mar in pear dagen letter stoarte de berch yn. Dy siet fol biezemriis.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131260,"r":"KEUNING006415","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A white figure turns out to be an omen of a white dog that is bought and roams about in the evening.","i":"S.K.","o":"Mem en beppe seagen ek ris in pear kear op in joun in wyt ding om 'e hûs.\n\"O, o, as dat mar net hwat fan de duvel is.\" sei beppe.\nIn skoft letter kocht ús heit in houn, dy wie hielendal wyt. Hy slepte yn in heabulte. Sadwaende seagen sy him jouns faek rinnen. It wie krekt it spûk, dat sy sjoen hienen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131276,"r":"KEUNING006702","p":"Earnewâld","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On the spot where there is now a bridge, the sound of a hammer was heard earlier.","i":"S.K.","o":"Goed hûnderd jier lyn leinen der fiskers mei in tichtset op it plak, wer nou de brêge tusken Warten en Geryp leit. Se hearden dúdlik hammerjen, mar der wie neat. Letter kaem dêr de brêge.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131277,"r":"KEUNING006703","p":"Earnewâld","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On the spot where a steamboat now passes, people hear thumping like that of a steamboat.","i":"S.K.","o":"Sa hearden se ek op in plak it stampen, krekt as foer der in stoomboat foarby. Letter farde dêr de Drachster boat lâns.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131278,"r":"KEUNING006704","p":"Earnewâld","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hearing the shop bell when no one is to be seen means it will be busy.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ien út Earnewâld wie ris by syn omke yn Dronryp. Dy wie dêr bakker. De omkesizzer hearde dúdlik de skelle.\n\"Is dêr ien?\"\n\"Né, dat bitsjut: drokke nearring.\" (Der soe drokke nearring komme","l":"Fries"},{"n":131296,"r":"KEUNING007001","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A magpie as a harbinger of a death, the arrival of a letter, or a lawsuit.","i":"S.K.","o":"As der in akster yn de finsterbank sit, bitsjut dit, dat der ien dea giet, as der fiif aksters om hûs binne, dat der in brief komt en as der sawn binne, dat der ien foar de rjochtbank komme moat.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131354,"r":"KEUNING007607","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Dreaming of horses means a strong wind is coming.","i":"S.K.","o":"Min sei altyd: \"As min nachts fan hynders droomde, kaem der hurde wyn.\"","l":"Fries"},{"n":131358,"r":"KEUNING007703","p":"Warstiens","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A chattering magpie means visitors are coming.","i":"S.K."},{"n":50659,"r":"KOOIJMAN0119","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A hare came by a farmer's place in Lopik (which never boded well) and sat beating its front paws together in the farmer's yard. The washing on the line got dirty and the hay harvest failed.","i":"H.K.","o":"Als een haas voorbij kwam, dan voorspelde dat niet veel goeds. Bij een boer in Lopik kwam een haas voorbij, die ging met z'n voorpootjes in elkaar zitten slaan, bij die boer op de werf. Dat was niet erg in orde. De was hing aan de lijn en die werd vuil en de hooioogst mislukte!"},{"n":50911,"r":"KOOIJMAN0212","p":"Benschop","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Knocking over the salt cellar foretells a quarrel.","i":"H.K."},{"n":50912,"r":"KOOIJMAN0213","p":"Benschop","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If a knife lies on its back, it announces a quarrel.","i":"H.K."},{"n":50936,"r":"KOOIJMAN0236","p":"Reeuwijk","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If a smith sees a tar bubble in the fire in the shape of a little man, it means prosperity in his work.","i":"H.K.","o":"Als je nou smid ben hè en je hebt vette kolen, dan wil daar wel is teerbel inkomme. Door die lucht in die teer die gloeiend heet wordt. 't Is een teerbel met een overhangende punt. Dat noemen ze dan een mannegie of een kereltie in 't vuur. Als je dat ziet, krijg je veel werk. 't Schijnt nog uit te komen ook!*\n\n*Dit volksgeloof geldt in de omgeving van Gouda, maar ook van Arkel, waar men spreekt van een andere smid in het vuur."},{"n":50959,"r":"KOOIJMAN0259","p":"Langerak","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Stars were seen flying across each other in the sky. It was said this foretold a disaster. Scholars, however, explained the phenomenon as bits of meteor.","i":"H.K.","o":"We hebben 't ok nog eens gehad, dat d'r allemaal sterren deur mekaar vlogen. As je naar de lucht keek, je ees* d'r van. Toen wier gezegd: \"Zo zelle later de mensen deur mekaar vliegen!\" Want dat voorspelde een ramp. De geleerden verklaarden, ze konden het niet goed ontcijferen, maar ze hadden het over stukken van een meteoor.\n\n*ijsde"},{"n":51000,"r":"KOOIJMAN0299","p":"Tienhoven","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator learned a rhyme from his uncle about predicting with tea leaves. If the stalks float in the tea, news will come from a woman; if they stand upright, news will come from a man.","i":"H.K.","o":"Een ome van me uit Arkel heb me eens een rijmpie geleerd.\n\nEen stokje dat drijft\nIs iets van een wijf,\nMaar een stokje op z'n end \nDat is iets van een vent.\n\nIn de thee drijve wel eens van die ronde stokkies, je weet wel. Dat betekent nieuws of een brief, van een vent, as 't stokkie staat, van een vrouw as 't stokkie drijft."},{"n":51001,"r":"KOOIJMAN0300","p":"Tienhoven","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If your backside itches, it foretells a good year for butter.","i":"H.K.","o":"En als je achterwerk jeukt, dan krijg je een goed boterjaar, zeggen ze in Arkel altijd."},{"n":51038,"r":"KOOIJMAN0320","p":"Brandwijk","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The behaviour of animals can be an omen of various events (regarding death (dog or magpie) or the weather (ducks)).","i":"H.K.","o":"Als er iemand gestorven was en hij stond nog boven de aarde en d'r lag een hond te huile op de dijk, of je hoorde een ekster, dan was d'r gauw weer een sterfgeval. Als eenden zo stil worden en ze zitte an d'r dons te trekke en te pikke, dan krijg je vorst. Als de eende zo rumoerig worde, dan krijg je slecht weer."},{"n":70295,"r":"KOOIJMAN0726","p":"Polsbroek","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Cups that start to tremble mean that an accident will happen.","i":"H.K.","o":"VOORTEKEN VAN ONGELUK\n\nDe koppies op 't theeblad begonne te danse...te trilIe, dat was een voorteken van ongeluk. (Vlist).","l":"Zuid-Hollands"},{"n":45902,"r":"KUSTERS000801","p":"Heeze","v":"N.-Br.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A parish priest's prediction that no priests will come from Heeze for a long time comes true.","i":"C.K.","o":"Pastoor Egidius van de Voort was hier pastoor en most in kòj tij onderduiken; ik geleuf det ie òk nog in Ommel is geweest. Hij ha vurspèld det ur in heel laang, ik wit nie precies hoevul jòr, geen priesterzonen uit Heeze zón komme en zo is 't ook gebeurd. Nauw pas kort gelèje is dien tijd um.","l":"Brabants"},{"n":47185,"r":"KUSTERS003410","p":"Deurne","v":"N.-Br.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Shortly after someone sees soldiers marching through the sky, war breaks out.","i":"C.K.","o":"In Liessel stond 'n vrouw buiten haar huis en zag 'n troep soldaten door de lucht marcheren. Kort daarop kwam de Frans-Duitse oorlog."},{"n":47208,"r":"KUSTERS003503","p":"Deurne","v":"N.-Br.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man cannot leave; shortly afterwards a storm damages the house.","i":"C.K.","o":"'n Boer moest 'ns naar 'n vergadering maar kon niet wegkomen. 'n Geheimzinnige macht hield hem terug. Even later leed z'n huis grote schade door 'n plotselinge storm."},{"n":209163,"r":"VRIES000903","p":"Axel","v":"Zl.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Dream vision of a theft; dream vision preceding a death.","i":"J.d.V.","o":"Mijn man, die vele jaren hard heeft gewerkt werd minder en minder en de dokter lichtte mij er over in, dat ik mijn man na een lang ziekbed zou komen te verliezen. Hij leed aan de gevreesde ziekte, de kanker. \nHij kon toch nog wat blijven eten en lustte graag vis.\nFreeken, een viskoper uit België kwam iedereDonderdag de grens over met zijn karretje vis, die hij ging uitleuren.\nOp een keer, toen hij na zijn ronde uit SasvanGent en Westdorpe bij mij aankwam, zag ik op zijn kar wat oude Belgische kranten. \"Geef ze mij, Freeken,\" zei ik, dan heeft mijn man wat te lezen.\nZo las ik dan zelf ook in zo'n Belgische krant en trof me een stukje waarbij een oude arme man in België van een luttel sommetje van 34 frs. was beroofd. De oude man, als getuige voor het \"Tribunaal\" gekomen, dorst de van diefstal beschuldigde persoon niet als dader aan te wijzen, daar hij bang was voor latere wraak. De dief werd daarop wegens gebrek aan bewijs vrijgesproken.\nDie nacht, misschien één meter van mijn bed af, zie ik bij een kastje een vent, die bezig is met de diefstal van 34 frs. Een grote grijze kuif met slappe pet op het hoofd en gekleed in een oud versleten pak. \nZijn gehele gelaat was duidelijk voor mij zichtbaar.\nDan is plotseling het beeld weer verdwenen!\nAls volgende week Freeken weer bij mij aankomt en ik hem nauwkeurig mijn \"nachtelijke verschijning\" beschrijf, roept hij uit: \"Maar dat is de d"},{"n":209166,"r":"VRIES000906","p":"Axel","v":"Zl.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Predicting the end of the war on the basis of apparitions.","i":"J.d.V.","o":"EEN BIJZONDERE GAVE.\nIk zei U in het begin, dat velen in Axel van mijn gave afweten. \nWelnu, 't was misschien enkele maanden vóór de bevrijding (voor Axel was die datum 20 september 1944) dat mijnheer Kruisse, die nu overleden is en mijnheer Oggel, nog een vrij jonge man, mij vroegen: \"Coralie, kunt ge ons niet zeggen, hoe de oorlog zal aflopen?\"\nKom maar eens over enkele dagen terug, zei ik. En al denkende over de oorlog, maar dat deden we eigenlijk elke dag, meneer, zie ik opeens een beeld voor mij oprijzen. Het was daarginds bij die put (ze wijst naar een rioolput aan de overzijde van de straat).\nEen Duits officier staat een heleboel namen af te roepen van soldaten: \n\"Herman,\" zo begint hij en dan volgen nog veel meer voornamen. Maar geen enkele antwoordten dat kon ook niet, want rondom de put zie ik massa 's Duitse soldaten liggen, bloedend uit het hoofd, uit de borst, uit de buik, kortom alle zie ik ze dood voor me liggen. En dan verdwijnt langzaamaan weer dat beeld.\nIk heb de heren verteld, wat ik heb gezien en hun gezegd, dat de Duitsers de oorlog zouden verliezen. Trouwens, dit had ik in het begin van de oorlog ook al reeds gezegd, op grond van andere verschijningen, maar ik was er voorzichtig mee, want men moest in 1940/1941 erg oppassen!"},{"n":42767,"r":"WEV000201","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At the spot where men see a blue flame in the field one evening, to someone else a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death, a shepherd later dies.","i":"F.W.","o":"Voorloop.\n\nDe heer Schoenmaker vertelt. \n\nOp een donkere avond liepen we met enkele kameraden te Kopstukken.\n Daar ontdekten we op enige afstand een blauwe vlam, ergens in het veld. \nMijn grootvader, die zich nimmer vergiste als het veurloop betrof, zei tegen me: \n\"Doar komp ain dode.\" \nEen half jaar later was het zover. \nDe oude scheper Haan loopt daar met een paar schapen.\nJuist als hij een \"stikker\" in de grond wil steken, valt hij voorover en is dood."},{"n":42771,"r":"WEV000202","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A prediction that a house will be built on a certain spot comes true after the house that was built elsewhere burns down","i":"F.W.","o":"Voorloop, verteld door Schoenmaker.\n\nDoe waist wol, jong, woar Geert Mestmoaker zien hoes stait, hè? \nNou, dat is mien schold, dat 't hoes doar stait aon 't daip en nich op Kopstukken.  \n'k Zal die 't verteln. \nDou ik heurde, zo'n daortig joar leden, dat Geert timmern wol, bin ik noar hem tougoan en heb zegd. \n\"Geert, doe krigst 'n hoes op Kopstukken mit grode roamen.\" \n\"Hou waist?\" zee Geert.\n \"Umdat ik 't hoes al stoan zain heb\" \nMoar Geert zee, \"dai oale Beernd Schounmoaker zal zien zin nich kriegen\" \nDoarom hed hai timmerd op 'n aander stee aon 't daip. \nMoar 't hoes, dat ik al zain har, is 't er wol komen.\nDoe waist, loater is Bos zien spul opbraond. En dai hef dou ain nei hoes zet mit grode roamen, op 't zulfde stee, woar ik 't zain har.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":42966,"r":"WEV000603","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A little light is seen as a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the building of a farm.","i":"F.W.","o":"[3.] Voorloop.\nMijn opa liep eens met oom Jaan - zijn zoon - door de Mussel.\n't Was bij avond. Plotseling blijven ze staan voor een lichtje.\nToen zei opa: \"Hier komp ain boerderij. Moar ik zai 't zo wied vot, dien kinder beleven 't nog nich.\"\n't Haile hoes beschreef hij.\n't Was, waar nu de Veldwachterslaan is.\nDe boerderij is er nog steeds niet, maar 't zal er wel eens komen."},{"n":43087,"r":"WEV000905","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Before there is a road, the sound of a dog cart and the barking of dogs is heard.","i":"F.W.","o":"Maar wel is het waar, dat veel mensen in het veen een hondekar hebben horen ratelen. Ook hoorden ze de hond blaffen.\nLang voor er een weg was en voor er later inderdaad een hondekar langs trok."},{"n":43088,"r":"WEV000906","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Before a house is built, the sound of roof tiles sliding over the roof is heard.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ook hoorde men het glijden van pannen over het dak van een huis, dat pas na jaren werd gezet."},{"n":43204,"r":"WEV001201","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Predictions that a sick man will recover, will plough first with a white horse and later with a black horse, and that the black horse will pull the hearse, come true. The horses first harnessed to the hearse refuse, so the black horse has to be harnessed.","i":"F.W.","o":"Voorloop. \nSchoenmaker vertelt.\n\nOal Kamies noast ons was de haile winter al aon 't sukkeln.\n't Gung dan veur-, dan achteroet,\nBuurman Wessels was 't er op 'n dag hèn west te kieken, hou d' oale 't muik.\n\"Kamies gait achteroet, hai hoal 't nich meer,\" zee hai.\nMoar opa, oal Steffen, zee.\n\"Nee Wessels, Kamies wordt weer beter.\nHai hef nou 'n wit peerd. En 't volgend veurjoar plougt hai 't land mit 'n zwaarde. \nDat zwaarde peerd brengt hum vot.\" \n't Widde wör verkoft en 'n zwaarde kwam d'r veur in de ploats.\nEen buurman hef hiermit de grond pluigd.\nVolgende zömmer störf Kamies.\nVeur de woagen zol 'n peerd van de buren.\nKamies zien aigen har er nog nooit veur west en doarum wol ze hom laiver nich broeken. Moar wat anders nooit gebeurde, gain ain peerd wol stoan.\nDou mos in 't leste toch de zwaarde d'r veur."},{"n":43320,"r":"WEV002002","p":"Mussel","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A school is built on the spot where a light was seen, and schoolchildren now walk along the path.","i":"F.W.","o":"Dwaallicht.\nIk liep eens op een avond van Oomsberg naar Mussel door het veld. \nVoor me aan ging in snelle vaart een licht. In Mussel bleef het ergens staan. Daar staat nu een school en langs datzelfde pad lopen nu schoolkinderen."},{"n":43321,"r":"WEV002003","p":"Mussel","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A light appears at the place where a boy later drowns, follows the same route along which the dead boy is carried, and stops at the door through which he is brought inside.","i":"F.W.","o":"Op de Horsten - bij Musselkanaal - had R. Kramer geruime tijd een licht gezien. Het ontstond te Oomsberg, trok langs de weg en bleef tenslotte staan voor de baanderdeur van een boerderij. Wat gebeurt er? Er verdrinkt te Oomsberg een knaap uit de bewuste boerderij. Het lijk wordt langs de weg vervoerd, waarlangs het licht was getrokken en ging door de baanderdeur naar binnen. \nDaarna is het licht niet meer gezien."},{"n":43324,"r":"WEV002006","p":"Mussel","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman sees a mother and daughter walking where the house they live in is later built.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik zag zelf eens hier van uit het venster oale Aike lopen met haar dochter over 't land. Ik denk, wat moeten ze daar nou?\nMaar kijk, ze zijn ook al weer weg.\nEn wat is er nu gebeurd?\nOp diezelfde plek staat nu een huis.\nEn wie heeft daar gewoond? Die oude vrouw en haar dochter ook."},{"n":45316,"r":"WEV002201","p":"Sellingen","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Men see and hear soldiers in the peat bog in Germany in advance; hearing hammering and will-o'-the-wisps over the bog are a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the searchlights of prison camps built later.","i":"F.W.","o":"Op Rijsdam woonde in mijn jeugd Jan Potse in een hut. Eens staat hij boven op die hut en zegt: “Ik zai aal man seldoat’n in ’t Duutse moor. Zai koomt dizze kaande oet.” “n Gans groot heer.” En molenaar Smeenk in Sellingen ziet ze ook vanaf de molen. Tevens hoort hij het dreunen van de laarzen.\nIk stond eens aan de grens te praten met een schildwacht. Die zei: “D’r woont hier vlak bij een oude Pommer in een hut, die soldaten in het veen heeft gezien. Ze joegen burgers voor zich uit. \nOok hoorde hij hamergeklap. Er zouden gebouwen verrijzen.”\nVaak heb ik zelf dwaallichten gezien. Ze scheerden in brede banen over ’t veen. \nWeet je, wat er na 1933 gebouwd is? \nKampen voor Joden, en politieke gevangenen. De soldaten joegen ze voort.\nEn zoals de dwaallichten flikkerde het licht van de schijnwerpers over ‘t “moor.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45335,"r":"WEV002402","p":"Stadskanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On hearing hammering, a prediction that a smithy is sure to come; on the spot where the beating of flails was heard, a farm was later built; rattling heard during a thunderstorm, and in a later thunderstorm tiles slide off the roof.","i":"F.W.","o":"Geluiden\nhebben de mensen vaak gehoord. \nMijn buurman, die smid was, heeft indertijd hamergeklop gehoord ergens op een onbebouwd terrein. Hij zei wel eens: “Daar komt vast een smederij.” En de smederij staat er nu reeds lang.\nMijn vader heeft eens het slaan van dorsvlegels gehoord op een plek, waar nu een boerderij staat. Kijk, die dingen heb ik toch zelf gehoord van die mensen. \n‘k Was nog ongetrouwd en toen hoorde ik thuis ook eens wat. ‘k Lag in bed en daar was plotseling het ratelen van een zwaar onweer in de verte.\nDe andere dag vroeg ik, of men het in huis eveneens vernomen had. Niemand had iets gehoord. Maar wat gebeurt veertien dagen later? Een geweldige bui trekt er over. Daar glijdt een pan over het dak. En is dat nu niet precies hetzelfde, als het geluid, dat ik indertijd gehoord had?","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45337,"r":"WEV002403","p":"Stadskanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man sees a new house standing where a paraffin lamp is being lit. When he wants to take a closer look, everything has vanished. Later a house of the same shape is built on that spot.","i":"F.W.","o":"Gezien \nheb ik ook een keer wat.\nHet is 26 jaar geleden. Ik fiets op een avond van Onstwedde naar Mussel. Als ik bijna thuis ben, kijk ik opzij en zie een nieuw huis staan. Dat is toch gek, ben ik verdwaald? Duidelijk zie ik ook een verlichte kamer; een vrouw steekt net een petroleumlamp aan. Ik stap van de fiets, om nader toe te kijken.\nMaar dan -- is alles plotseling weg. \nIk kijk over een stuk vlak land.\nDoch de woning staat er nu. Zeventien jaar later is het gebouwd. \nHet huis heeft dezelfde vorm als ik toen heb gezien. Dat lijdt geen twijfel.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45347,"r":"WEV002503","p":"Barlage","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Dancing lights above a pool are seen as an omen of a drowning or the building of a house. No one drowned, but a house was built.","i":"F.W.","o":"Op de Zandtangerweg werden boven de kolk altijd dansende lichtjes gezien. Men zei dan, daar verdrinkt nog een keer iemand of er komt een huis. Verdronken is er niemand, daar tenminste niet, wel een vijfhonderd meter er vandaan, nu zo’n zestig jaar geleden.\nMaar een huis staat er wel, zoals je weet. Want daar woon je nu zelf in.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45363,"r":"WEV002604","p":"Nieuwe Pekela","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator and his brother see the light of a bicycle approaching in the field. As it comes close they step aside, and the light has vanished.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wat ik zelf eens heb meegemaakt, is ook eigenaardig en geloof je misschien niet. \nIk liep met mijn broer - we waren kinderen - op een zandweg door ’t veld.\nDaar zien we een fiets naderen, tenminste het carbid-lantaarn-licht. Als het licht ons is genaderd op een afstand van zo’n vijftig meter, gaan we op zij om de fietser ruimte te geven. En dan ineens is het licht weg. We zien noch horen iets meer. We lopen dan weer door, kijken nog schuw naar alle kanten en zetten ’t op een lopen."},{"n":45375,"r":"WEV002901","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman takes hearing creaking, as if beams were giving way, and seeing flames as an omen of fire or a lightning strike.","i":"F.W.","o":"Het huis te Sterenborg bij Onstwedde, waar ik geboren ben, daar was wat mee. Mijn moeder heeft me ’t verteld. Zo nu en dan begon het achter op de deel geweldig te kraken. ’t Was net, of de gebinten naar beneden vielen. Als men kijken ging, was er niets aan de hand. Soms ook sloegen de vlammen er uit. Mijn moeder dacht, dat er misschien nog eens brand zou komen; dat de bliksem er wel in kon slaan.\nMaar tot dusver is er nog niets gebeurd."},{"n":11558,"r":"CJ000503","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man suddenly sees that a row of houses has disappeared and been replaced by grass on which people are kicking and making a lot of noise. A football pitch was later built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Houtigehage wenne in man, dy hat forkearing hawn mei in suster fan myn man. Hy hat ris forteld: Op in snein-to-joune seach ik ynienen dat der in streekje huzen fuort wie. It wie dêr gewoan lân woarn, dêr't neat mear op stie. Allegear gjers.\nMar o, o, hwat gong it der dêr op dat lân alderheislikst oan wei! It gong dêr op in skoppen en traepjen en smiten, dat ik sei: Hwat hjir gebeurt, wyt ik net. Mar it liket slim. Sa'n stuk leven wie dêr. Even letter stienen de huzen der wer, en 't wie der wer stil.\nMar letter is dêr it foetbalfjild kom. De huzen wienen ôfbrutsen. En doe gong it der krekt sa om en ta as er earder heard en sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11559,"r":"CJ000504","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The lights a man sees coming towards his house must have been the headlights of the cars that would later drive on the roads built afterwards.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit syn heit, dat wie Harmen van der Zee. Dy wenne yn Sigerswâld. Op in joun doe soed er op bêd. Hy stie al yn 'e ûnderbroek. Mar it pypke wie noch net alhielendal leech. Dat woed er earst leech roke. Beppe lei al op bêd. Wylst pake ta 't finster út seach kommen dêr twa greate, felle ljochten lyk op him ta. Hy rôp: Geeske, Geeske, hwat sil dit wurde!\nMar doe't it oan 't hûs ta wie, wienen de ljochten samar ynienen út. Doe wie der neat mear.\nLetter binne dêr allegearre wegen kom mei in drok forkear. It ha moai wis ljochten fan in auto west de fjûrballen, dy't er doe sjoen hat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11560,"r":"CJ000505","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening people see all kinds of little lights, including red ones, just like the rear lights of today's bicycles and cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dwaelljochtsjes, dat is ek foartsjirmerije. Op in snein-to-joun kom myn folk de Geriperwei del. Dat is wol 70 jier lyn. Doe seagen se dêr allegear ljochtsjes. Ek reade, lyk as nou de achterljochtsjes fan fytsen en auto's ensa. Dy ljochten ha se doe allegear fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11561,"r":"CJ000506","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A fireball and red streaks in the sky mean war.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sjocht men in fjûrbol oan 'e loft dan wol dat sizze dat der oarloch komt. Reade streken oan 'e loft bitsjut ek oarloch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11564,"r":"CJ000508","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A farmer sleeping on a praam (flat-bottomed barge) loaded with hay cannot get to sleep. He sees many people walking on the barge. Later a road was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Aldegea wenne in boer, dy hiet fan Harmsma. Hy helle hea fan 'e Headammen mei syn beide arbeiders. Dat wienen Foppe en Alle. Dat hea woarde op in pream laden en dêr farden se mei nei Aldegea ta. De nachts slepten de boer en de arbeiders yn 't hea op 'e pream.\nMar de boer koe net yn 'e sliep komme. Hy seach dy nachts klear dat der allerhande folk oer de pream hinne gong. Letter is der op datselde plak dêr't se leinen in wei kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11566,"r":"CJ000510","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Dreaming of pigs or piglets means coming into contact with the police.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in minske droomt oer bargen of biggen krijt er mei plysjes to meitsjen, sa wurdt der altyd sein.\nIk ha 't in kear bileefd. Doe droomde ik yn 'e neinacht, dat der roannen allegear biggen om my hinne. Dyselde deis ha 'k oan twakear ta mei de marechaussees en de plysjes to dwaen hawn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11569,"r":"CJ000512","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Whoever is dealt the ace of clubs at cards will soon go to a strange place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei 't kaertspyljen klaveraes krige, soe hiel yn 't koart nei in frjemd plak ta gean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32449,"r":"CJ126103","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears carpentry sounds, although there is nothing to be seen. It is a premonition: later the railway is built at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As wy moarns ier de skiep nei Ljouwert ta dreauwen, hearden wy oan 'e oare kant Hurdegaryp dúdlik timmerjen. It wie yn myn jonge jierren.\nLetter is dêr it spoar kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32453,"r":"CJ126107","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man sees another man busily hammering. When he comes closer, there is nothing to be seen. It is a voorgezicht (a vision of the future): only a few days later does he find the same man hammering away at a pigsty.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Wie op in joun let. Ik wie even bûten. Doe seach ik Gurbe, dy wie noch drok oan 't timmerjen achterhûs yn 't tsjuster. Mar doe't ik der by kom wie der neat.\nOp itselde plak kom in dei of hwat letter in bargehok. Gurbe timmere it. Dat hie ik fan tofoaren sjoen. Ik wie sahwat 35 jier.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":210621,"r":"ENGELS002306","p":"Meijel","v":"L.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Dreams about incidents involving water are a good sign; dreams about fire are a bad sign.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Voortekenen:\nMen hechtte vroeger ook geloof aan bepaalde dromen. Zo werd me altijd verteld, dat dromen over gevallen met water een gunstig, en met vuur een ongunstig teken waren. \n\nGeen omzetting in dialect van het verhaal door Engels."},{"n":209813,"r":"HOL001326","p":"Eck en Wiel","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Seeing a black cat is an omen of misfortune or a death.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Ziet men een zwarte kat aan de kant van de weg, dan voorspelt dit een ongeluk of een sterfgeval."},{"n":209858,"r":"HOL001517","p":"Kapel-Avezaath","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Indelible bloodstains in the room where the devil took Faust; voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the building of houses.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Bloedvlekken op de muur moeten er zijn in het kasteel te Waardenburg, in het kamertje, waar de duivel Faust gehaald heeft.\n(Verhaal van mevr. V Zijtveld, die uit Leersum afkomstig is: Een schaapherder in de Leijen, dat nu Bilthoven heet, zei (het zal ± 100 jaar geleden zijn, dat, als hij op de grond ging liggen, hij timmeren en metselen hoorde. Er kwamen huizen, lanen, een kerk)."},{"n":209910,"r":"HOL001707","p":"Kesteren","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hearing in advance the sounds of soldiers later billeted there.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Van den Brenk en zijn vrouw gingen 's nachts slapen in hun tegenwoordige woning, die toen verder leeg stond. Zij woonden toen nog in het huis er naast, waar nu hun zoon woont. Ook de dochter, die de opname gedeeltelijk heeft meegemaakt, sliep op een nacht met haar tante in dit huis\nEn die nacht werden alle vier wakker van het lawaai in huis. Ze hoorden mannen de trap oplopen. Het was net of ze in de kamer beneden aan het geld tellen waren. De dochter hoorde, dat er telkens 46 werd gezegd. In 1939 werd het 46e regiment (het zal wel een gedeelte er van geweest zijn) bij hen ingekwartierd."},{"n":209911,"r":"HOL001708","p":"Kesteren","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Seeing in advance houses that stand there now.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Jan van de Peel (de overbuurman, naam boerderij, zijn achternaam was Van Lutterveld) zag eens, toen hij uit het café van Van Kleef kwam en de Boveneindse straat inliep, een rij huizen. Hij schrok geweldig, zijn haren rezen te berge. De huizen staan er nu werkelijk."},{"n":131432,"r":"KEUNING008704","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Worry about the future when a magpie chatters. Warning not to walk in the middle of the road at night because of funeral processions.","i":"S.K.","o":"Us mem sei, as hja in akster skatterjen hearde faek: \"As hjir mar net hwat efter wei komt.\"\nSy woe ek net leije, dat wy jouns midden op 'e wei rounen fanwege de lykstaesjes.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131458,"r":"KEUNING009103","p":"De Trieme","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Seeing lights is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the lights of houses built later.","i":"S.K.","o":"Se ha hjir op in plak op in joun al ris ljochten sjoen. Dy wienen ek sa wer wei. In pear jier letter seach elts dy selde ljochten. Mar doe kamen se út huzen, dy dêr doe boud wienen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131566,"r":"KEUNING011007","p":"Nijewier","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman predicts that her coffin will not be long enough.","i":"S.K.","o":"Doe ús mem op stjerren laei, sei hja: \"As jim my yn 'e kiste lizze, sil jim sjen, dat dy to lyts is. En sa wie it ek. Doe se ús mem yn 'e kiste lizze soenen, wie dy to koart. Heit sei, dat er in greatere komme moast.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131615,"r":"KEUNING011906","p":"Hantum","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man sees events beforehand that others do not see.","i":"S.K.","o":"Hjir is noch in man, dy sjocht fan alles barren, hwer in oar neat fan sjocht. Bygelyks sei hy: \"Hwerom slagge sy dêr sa yn dy beam om.\" Of: \"Hwat moatte al dy minsken hjir.\"","l":"Fries"},{"n":131696,"r":"KEUNING013304","p":"Hegebeintum","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A strange object flying past is a forerunner of the bicycle.","i":"S.K.","o":"Der stie in man op 'e brêge. Doe fleach der him hwat fremds forby. Letter seinen sy, dat dit foartsjirmerij wie. Doe de fytsen der kamen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131729,"r":"KEUNING013807","p":"Koarnjum","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A magpie in the farmyard is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of visitors.","i":"S.K."},{"n":72566,"r":"KOOIJMAN1083","p":"Nieuwerkerk aan den IJssel","v":"Z.-H.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Black crows around the house mean a death.","i":"H.K.","o":"VOORTEKEN\n\nAs d'r veel zwarte kraaie om 't huis heen vloge, dan betekende dat een sterfgeval.","l":"Zuid-Hollands"},{"n":72666,"r":"KOOIJMAN1171","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If a white horse went by, you would get visitors.","i":"H.K."},{"n":72670,"r":"KOOIJMAN1175","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Those little lights over the land, those were will-o'-the-wisps. Then something was coming, a war or a disaster.","i":"H.K.","o":"Van die lichies over 't land, dat wazze dwaallichies. Dan was d'r vast wel wat op til, oorlog of ramp.","l":"Zuid-Hollands"},{"n":72756,"r":"KOOIJMAN1251","p":"Capelle","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman who was born with a caul said that she always gets upset before something happens.","i":"H.K.","o":"D'r was een vrouwen die zeet: \"Ik ben ok mee den helm geboren. En nou as d'r wat gebeurt, dan ben ik altijd van tevore van strekel\" . Ze hebben diejen helm nie bewaard.","l":"Noord-Brabants"},{"n":72834,"r":"KOOIJMAN1318","p":"Rijswijk","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone born with a caul could do more than others. The caul had to be buried in the hearth and slowly smoulder away. Otherwise those children would be unhappy.","i":"H.K.","o":"Jao, me den helm geboren, ik he d'r een gekend. Die kon meer dan een ander. Ze wete alles. Den helm moes in den haerd en dan graafde ze 'm diep in 't vuur. Hij moest langzaam versmeule. Anders waere de keindere ongelukkig.","l":"Brabants"},{"n":72858,"r":"KOOIJMAN1339","p":"Giessen","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A comet foretells the end of the world.","i":"H.K."},{"n":72910,"r":"KOOIJMAN1385","p":"Woudrichem","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A hunchback on the ice meant that it was going to thaw.","i":"H.K."},{"n":72922,"r":"KOOIJMAN1396","p":"Andel","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People born with a caul were bulletproof. They did not need to be afraid in a war. They also had the gift of prophecy. If the midwife buried the caul in the wrong place, the child would be unhappy all its life.","i":"H.K.","o":"[Met de helm geboren:] Waren kogelvrij. Die hoefden in oorlog of revolutie geen bang te hebben. En ze hadden een waarzeggende geest. Ik heb wel is hore vertellen, dat een jonge ongelukkig was. Want hij was met den helm geboren. En de baakster had de helm op de verkeerde plaats begraven. \"Nou is die jonge z'n leve lang ongelukkig\", werd d'r gezegd."},{"n":125563,"r":"KOOIJMAN1444","p":"Woudrichem","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A black cat was something special. If one walked past, something was to be expected.","i":"H.K.","o":"Een zwarte kat, dat was iets bijzonders. D'r liep een zwarte kat heen, dan was dat of dat te wachte."},{"n":125596,"r":"KOOIJMAN1474","p":"Poederoijen","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If the cat washes itself, visitors are on their way.","i":"H.K."},{"n":125611,"r":"KOOIJMAN1487","p":"Oosterwijk","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If a magpie sat with its back towards you, it would bring bad luck. Facing you, on the other hand, it was a good sign.","i":"H.K.","o":"Een ekster met de rugkant naar je toe, brengt ongeluk, met de voorkant naar je toe, dat was een goed teken."},{"n":125612,"r":"KOOIJMAN1488","p":"Oosterwijk","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If you were out on the road and the clock struck twelve, something could happen.","i":"H.K.","o":"As je op de weg was en de klok sloeg twaalf uur, dan kon er iets gebeure."},{"n":125631,"r":"KOOIJMAN1497","p":"Nieuwegein","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Whoever is born with a caul has the gift of foresight.","i":"H.K."},{"n":125793,"r":"KOOIJMAN1601","p":"Rijswijk","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Whoever was born with a caul was clairvoyant.","i":"H.K."},{"n":127632,"r":"KOOIJMAN2267","p":"Heesselt","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If the magpies fight, something is going to happen.","i":"H.K."},{"n":127798,"r":"KOOIJMAN2431","p":"Waspik","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If you heard an owl call in the evening, an accident would soon happen.","i":"H.K.","o":"Als ge 's avonds een uil hoorde roepen van die kleine uilen, dan gebeurde er binnenkort een ongeluk."},{"n":127806,"r":"KOOIJMAN2438","p":"Maren","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If an owl came and sat on the house three times, that was dangerous. It meant there would soon be a death in the house.","i":"H.K.","o":"Als een uil drie maal op het huis kwam zitten, dat was gevaarlijk. Dat betekende binnenkort een dode in huis."},{"n":207237,"r":"KUSTERS008002","p":"Heeze","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A blood-red sky in which people wipe away the blood is a sign of war.","i":"C.K.","o":"Lang geleden was de lucht boven Sterksel bloedrood. Men zag mensen in de lucht dat bloed wegvegen maar hun gezichten waren onkenbaar. 't Was 'n teken van oorlog."},{"n":207302,"r":"KUSTERS008422","p":"Geldrop","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Halley's Comet was said to be an omen of the end of the world or other disasters.","i":"C.K.","o":"Verteller heeft de staartster van Halley gezien. Dat leek toen 'n slecht voorteken voor het einde der wereld of voor andere rampen."},{"n":207313,"r":"KUSTERS008509","p":"Leende","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Prediction of war and of a carriage without a horse.","i":"C.K.","o":"De profecei zee: \na) \"'t Zal oorlog worden eer de smid het 4° hoefijzer onder 't paard heeft geslagen\". \nb) \"Er zullen rijtuigen rijden zonder paard\"."},{"n":208693,"r":"LINSSEN006511","p":"Grathem","v":"L.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The cawing of a magpie is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of news arriving.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Wanneer men een ekster hoort krassen, betekent dit, dat er nieuws op komst is."},{"n":208697,"r":"LINSSEN006603","p":"Hunsel","v":"L.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Events attributed to the presence of spiders.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Aan het verschijnen van spinnen werden sommige gebeurtenissen toegeschreven. Zag men de spin 's morgens dan was dat een teken dat er een zorgvolle dag zou aanbreken. Spinnen in de avond zou geluk brengen. Bij sommige mensen schijnt heden ten dage de spin nog een bijzondere bescherming te genieten. Ze zullen een spin in huis niet dood maken, maar levend aan de buitenlucht brengen."},{"n":45400,"r":"WEV003103","p":"Musselkanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Sounds heard earlier on a sandy track were an omen of the traffic that now goes along a road.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wat mie hier op ’t knoal zölf wol al overkomen is, dat bint geluden, dai ‘k biezetn heurd heb.\nDou de zandweg nog veur ’t hoes lag, heurde ik soms net ’t geluud van raimen, dai aan mekoar langs schuren. \nIk vruig de kinder dan: “Heurn ie ’t ook wol?” Man kinder heuren nooit wat.\nMan kiek, nô de stroade d’r is, is ’t gau verkloard. Nô is d’r geschuur en geroas van ’t verkeer over de weg.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45403,"r":"WEV003201","p":"Valthermond","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Seeing a light in advance is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the building of a house; hearing wagons on the threshing floor in advance is a voorloop of the building of a farm.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nMien moeke kon ook wat zain. Zai zee es ’n keer: “Doar gunnes bie de diek komp ’n hoes.\nIk zai d’r licht branden.” ’t Hoes is er ook komen; J.E. woonde er loater.\nOp ’n ander moal wus ze te vertellen: “Op dat stuk land van B. komp ain boerderij.”\n“Woarum?” vruigen wie.\n“Nô, ‘k heb d’r woagens rappeln heurd over de dele; dou ‘k over de weg kwam.” \nDe boerderij stèèt d’r nô. Beide gevallen gebeurden in de Muzzel, woar wie toun woonden.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45406,"r":"WEV003204","p":"Valthermond","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A not too bright girl, while peeing in the canal, hears the water rushing in the lock and sees it as an omen of the building of a lock.","i":"F.W.","o":"[Veurloop]\nvreselk um lacht.\nZai dainde bie W. op de Zandtange.\n’t Knoal lop doar nou vlak bie hoes langs en d’r is ’n sluus in. Dat verloat het zai broezen heurd.\nWie wazzen d’r op kediet mit wat jongelu. ’t Wicht mös d’r eerm oet noar boeten. Dou ze d’r weer in kwam, zee ze: “Hier komp nog ’n keer ’n verloat in de buurt.”\n“Hou waist dat?”zee’n wie.\n“Nou,” zee ze, “net toun ‘k op boeten zit’n gung te pissen, brak ’t verloat lös.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45612,"r":"WEV003804","p":"Stadskanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Heard stories about pools that make noise, lights that predict trouble, and howling dogs that mean a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"’k Heb ook wel heurd van kolken, woar geluden uut kwamen; van lichten, dei onroad veurspelden; van jankende honden, dei ’n staarfgeval beduden, moar ’t heft op mie wainig indruk moakt. Doarom ken ’k doar nait veul over verteln.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":13761,"r":"WEV004501","p":"Exloo","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator has noticed little of witchcraft; has once seen a little light at the spot where a house was later built in which a night light burns.","i":"F.W.","o":"Voorboden.\nIk heb altied in Exel woond. Mien voar was scheper, mien grootva en overgrootva waren ’t ook. Van hekserij heb ik niet veule markt. Wel van voorboden. Dat bestiet dan ook. Zölf heb ik ies ’n veurgezicht had van een husien. ’t Was ’n keer schemerdonker en ik lupe deur ’t darp. Doar zie ik bie een dannebossien een lichien. D’r was geen lanteern en ook anders gien lampe. Het lichie stön onbeweegliek. Ik zee, noe wil ik toch es dit plekkien in de gaten houden. En inderdaad ontstön bie dat bossien een husien.\nAs ie ’s oavends doar veurbie lupen, zag ie in een kamertien een nachtlampien stoan. Toen bemerken ik, dat dit het lichien was, dat ik zien had.","l":"Drents"},{"n":13762,"r":"WEV004502","p":"Exloo","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A person born with a caul has to get up at night; foresees a funeral procession; sees a train running before the railway is built.","i":"F.W.","o":"[Voorboden.]\nToen mien vader nog scheper was, had ie een kameroad, die nog veule meer zien hef. Dat was ook al een schepertien, die met de helm geboren was. Luuster maar.\nMien va had indertied de nachtwacht. Dan gebeurde ’t wel, dat ie zien kameroad ontmuutte. ’t Schepertien mos d’r dan weer uut, umdat ie niet in huus blieven kon.\nZo zegde ies ’n keer tegen va: “Kom S. hier even aan de kaante, door komt vrouw R. aan, zie wordt hen brocht noar Oring.”(Odoorn). En niet lange doornoa is de vrouw begraven.\nWat mout ie door nou van denken? Va heft het alles zölf heurd. Dat schepertien was vriegezel en was bie een boer in de kost. De boer wis al, dat zien kostganger voak uut bedde ging.\nOp een murgen zeg de scheper:\n“Wat ik vannacht wel ezien hebbe, dat wet ik niet. Hier vlak achter de boerderij roasde wat langs mit een gruwelijke voart. Het was een zwart monster en ie truk een lange sliert met lichies achter zich aan.”\nJoaren loater is d’r de spoorliene aan legd. Hie luup vlak langs de boerderij. De scheper had de trein dus gezien. De liene is nou weer weg.","l":"Drents"},{"n":13772,"r":"WEV004605","p":"Sellingen","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Seeing a little light is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a drowning, a murder, the building of houses.","i":"F.W.","o":"’k Luip es ’n moal mit aine over de weg. \nDou zee ’e: ”Kiek doar es, ’n lichie.”\n“Ik zai niks,” zee ’k.\n“Nee, doar ja, in ’t veld. Doar gebeurt vast ’n keer wat.”\n”Och,” zee ik, “wat zol d’r gebeuren?”\n“Kan van alles wezen. Kan aine verdrinken, kan aine vermoord worden, kan wat anders wezen, man ’t bedudt wat.”\nDai man kön kwoad zain, zee ’n ze dan. \nWeer andern zaggen ’n lichten, woar loater hoezen kwamen. En voak kwam er ook wol ’n hoes.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":41135,"r":"WEV004608","p":"Sellingen","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A dog is restless for a few days before the death and calms down afterwards, but the narrator does not believe that the howling of dogs is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Honnegehoel, joa, ik leuf d’r nich aan. Man andern wol weer. In de Spaanse griep heb ’k ain kend, dai dou overleden is. ’n Poar doagen van te veuren luip d’hond as ’n gekke over dele. Noa tied was ’e rustig. “Kiek”, zeden mensken dan, “’n hond wait ’t wol.”\nMan ik hol schollers op.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":41144,"r":"WEV004801","p":"Sellingerbeetse","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man who can see the future knows which horses of which colour will pull a hearse.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nToun ik nog in Drente woonde, heb ik de volgende gevallen van veurloop heurd.\nIn Roswinkel was ’n zekere P., dei d’r aan dee. \nOp Ter-Aopel verdrunk ies ’n zoeplabbe in ’t knoal. Toun wos P. mit ain te vertellen, welke peerden veur de liekwoagen kwamen. De kleur had ie zölfs al zain. En ’t kwam uut ook.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":41145,"r":"WEV004802","p":"Sellingerbeetse","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A family very often sees something standing briefly against the wall. After a child dies, the coffin is deliberately not placed at that spot, but the bearer puts the coffin down at the place where something had been seen beforehand.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nToun ik nog in Drente woonde, heb ik de volgende gevallen van veurloop heurd.\nBie Roswinkel woonde varder de familie H. \nOp ’n dag zain ze iets in de koamer stoan. \nZo tegen ’t schot aan. ’t Was ook zo weer vot. Dat gait zo mit veurloop. ’t Is moar ’n moment, dat men wat zugt. As ie beter toukiek’n wil’n, is ’t altied vot. Wat dei lu den ook precies zagen, wait ik nait. Moar aalgedurig was t’r weer. Den komp d’r ’n kind te overlieden. “Loat we nou oppazzen,” zee de familie, “en zet’n ’t kissie nait op de plekke bie ’t schot.” ’t Kwam den ook op ’n ander stee te stoan.\nDe dag van de begravvenis komp. \nMien vao was droager. Hij pakte ’t kissie op en gait d’r mit noar boeten. Het wör toun aan een raime droagen. Op boeten denkt ’e: “’t Zit toch nait recht goud.” \nDoarom gaait ’e eev’m weer noar binnen um ’t kissie beter vast te moaken. En den zet ’e ’t op de grond hèn, net op dat stee aan ’t schot. Roar, hè? Moar ’t is woar gebeurd. \nVeurloop is gain biegeleuf.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":41148,"r":"WEV004805","p":"Sellingerbeetse","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When a sheepfold is being built, it is said that the sound had already been heard beforehand.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nToun ik nog in Drente woonde, heb ik de volgende gevallen van veurloop heurd.\nToun wie hier in de Beetse kwamen, hebben wie ’n schoaphok timmerd. Even loater kwamen d’r mensen bie ons en zeden: “Dat wozzen wie wel, dat hier wat kwam te stoan; wie hebben al voak genog kloppen heurd.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45855,"r":"WEV004903","p":"Musselkanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman says she knew beforehand that manholes would be put in the street, because her back wheel went up as if she were riding over manhole covers.","i":"F.W.","o":"Voorloop.\n’t Is nog moar ’n poar joar leden, toun kwamen hier in de stroade zinkputjes. \nAin van de buurvroulu zee: \n“Dat heb ik al ’n haile zet waiten. Want iedere keer, as ik doar langs fietsde, wupte mie ’t achterrad ’n eindje umhoog. Net as nou, as ’k over de putdekseltjes rie.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43001,"r":"WEV005102","p":"De Maten","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Where little lights used to dance in a row, there is now a road where bicycle lamps travel in a row one behind the other.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop. Doar prooatten ze vrouger meer van. Nôn heur je dat nich meer zo. Zölf kan 'k mie nog herinnern, dat ik vrouger, as 'k over de heide keek, aal man lichies dansen zag. In 'n laange riege achter mekoar aan. As ik nôn goud noagoa, dan mou'k zeggen, dat doar nô de weg lop, woar de fietslanteerns 's manks net zo in 'n riege achter mekoar aan huppeln.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43002,"r":"WEV005103","p":"De Maten","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hearing the knocking of hammers and the ticking of a watch turns out to be a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the building of houses.","i":"F.W.","o":"Er bestaait ook veurloop mit 't oor. Den heur je dus wat veuroet. \nZo is 't twai moal veurkomen in 't veen bie Roswinkel. Luip 'n keer 'n doomnie deur 't veen. Doar heurd 'e kloppen. \nIn de haile buurt is niks te zain. Toch heurt hai hoamers. Noaderhand binnen doar hoezen komen. \nWas ook 'n keer 'n veenarbaider, dai mit zien kameroad hen gung te baggeln. Zai goan even op koare zitten om oet te rusten. \nDan zeg d' aine: “Gek, ik heb gien hallosie bie mie en toch heur 'k dudelk ain tikken.” \n“Hier komp vast nog 'n keer 'n hoes.” \nEn dat is ook goud komen. \nDoomnie en dai aarbeider wazzen gain mensen, dai man zo wat fanteseerden.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43118,"r":"WEV005302","p":"Roswinkel","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The rattling of a coach and the tread of horses is heard on a sand road where a brick road is later laid.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien mouder har asmits ook dingen dai ze van te veuren wus. 't Was zo vrouger de gewoonte, dat d' lu eerst even noar boeten gungen, veurdat ze 's oavends op berre gungen. Zo gèèt mien mouder ook es 'n moal mit mien zuster noar boeten. Zai wil'n net zitten goan, dan zèg moetje: “Stil es, wat heur ik doar? Ain koetse?” \nJoa heur, dou hef zai ain koetse rappeln heurd. En peerden klettern over de stroatstainen. \nAlles was hier dou nog zaand. Joaren loater is d'r 'n klinkerweg aanlegd.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43194,"r":"WEV005701","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hearing the sound of a trowel on a stone is a sign that a house will be built there at a later time.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nIk heb in t veen waarkt. t Is mie n keer gebeurd, dat ik wat heur. k Was rustig aan t törf groaven. En door verneem ik t geluud van n truffel op n staine.\nWas gain stain in de buurt. Loater is door n huus bouwd. \nToun k beter tou heuren wol, was t geluud vot. Dat is altied zo. Ie vangen wat op, moar as ie t underzuiken wiln, is t vot.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43260,"r":"WEV005901","p":"Wessingtange","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At the spot where a house was later built, a little light had been seen earlier.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nUm te begunnen, dit hoes, woor wie nôn in zitn, is al laank van te veurn zain. \nt Was dou ter tied nog veen en heide. \nAs dr dan mensken langs kwamen, zagen ze op dit stee geregeld n löchie brannen. \nNoaderhand, dou t hoes dr komen is, was dat löcht verdwenen.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43289,"r":"WEV006102","p":"Kopstukken","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A little light is seen above a canal at the spot where a child later drowns.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nJoa lu, dat bestèèt.\nDat heb ik ja wol heurd van mensn, dai absoluut betrouwboar warn.\n\nDezelfde oal luchies zagn ook mennigmoal n löchie.\nBoovn t oal daip.\nDat vertrouwden ze nich, umdat dat n slecht veurbeduudsel was.\nZai hadden t al weer goud bekeekn.\nWant op dat stee is n keer n kind verdronkn. In t oal daip wazzen door vlode stee-n, woor je deurloopn können. Man dat kind is in n kolke trechte koomn. Noa tied was t löchie vot.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43290,"r":"WEV006103","p":"Kopstukken","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A prediction comes true that the horse pulling the hearse refuses to cross a bridge.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nJoa lu, dat bestèèt.\nDat heb ik ja wol heurd van mensn, dai absoluut betrouwboar warn.\n\nn Ander geval van veurloop.\nWas aine, dai begravvenisn zag.\nDou zeg e es n moal;“Ik heb op Blekslege n liekwoagn aankomen zain. t Kwam bie n boerderij vot in de richtn van t daip. t Peerd wil net over de badde goan en dan bliv-e stoan; dreit zuk um en gèèt weer trugge.\nDe liekmenner zee dou:“Hai altied mit zien proatjes, dat zal mie nich overkomen.”\nMan as e op dag van begravvenis mit woagn veur de brugge komp, zug e, dat door n groot gat in is. t Peerd kan dr onmeuglik over. De kiste wordt dan van d woagn of tild en wieder droagn.\nOok dit mout gebeurd wezen.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43294,"r":"WEV006203","p":"Harpel","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"General feeling that the howling of a dog, the screeching of a magpie and the hooting of an owl are omens of misfortune.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nOch, ja jong, honne-gejank, eekster-geschrou en kat-oeln-gehoel warn allemoal veurboodn van t ain of ander onheil.\nKiek es, zo roar as wie dat nôn vinden; en zo weinig as door nôn aan leufd wordt, zo hail gewoon was dat dou en zo algemain wör dr in mien jonge joarn deur elk en aine aan leufd.\nDeur aarmen en riekn, kinder en grootn, rooms en protestant.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43297,"r":"WEV006302","p":"Dikbroeken","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A farmer is thrown aside while ploughing; a few years later the plough breaks at that spot.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurbode.\nt Is ook n keer gebeurd, dat k aan t plougen was. Wie hadden mor ain peerd. En omdat t slim drok was, mos ik s nachts ook nog aan t waark bie lichte moane. \nk Luip achter t ploug en toun inains wur k biezied smeetn. \nNet zo achter t ploug vot. t Peerd luip stil deur.  k Bin dr weer achter goan en dr is verder niks gebeurd. \nEn toun vul dr wat veur, twei joar loater. \nDatzulfde stuk land wur toun egd. En nog wait k nooit, hou of t ken, mor t ploug luip inains inmekoar. Alles was verboogn. \nEn t was ook nait meer uut mekoar te kriegn. \nIk vroag joe, hou ken dat en wat is dat west?","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43298,"r":"WEV006303","p":"Dikbroeken","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man who has to go at night to places where something happens says that only his spirit sets out, while his body stays at home.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurbode.\nWazn meer mensen, dei veurboden zaggen.\nk Heb aine kend, dei s nachts bie t pad luip, omdat e noar stee-n mos, woar wat gebeurde.\nHai zulf zee:“Mien geest huift dr allaind mor hen, mien lichoam blift op berre.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43365,"r":"WEV006501","p":"Roswinkel","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A caul must be eaten or burned, otherwise the person born with it can see the future; the narrator's caul was burned in a fire; a boy draws a lucky lot exempting him from service with a caul in his coat pocket; a woman sees deaths in advance and predicts the Second World War and Germany's defeat.","i":"F.W.","o":"In de helm geboren.\nIk bin zulf in de helm geboren. Nu zeden ze vroeger, dat die helm opeetn worn mus of verbrand. Anders kun de persoon, waar die helm van was, veuruut zien. Hij bracht ook geluk. \nDie van mie is niet opzettelijk verbrand, maar later n keer, toen t huus verbrandde. Ik heb ook niet veuruut zien kund. \nMoar de helm hef wel geluk bracht. Jongkerels, die in dienst muzn, en die met de helm geboorn waren, lootten meestal vrij. \nEn toen dr n jong van goeie kennisn loten mos, gaf mien moeder mien helm mit. Die zat in n rond deussien; de jong wus dr niks van, moar zien moe hef m in zien jasbuutse stopt. \nMoar hij hef zuch best vrij loot. \nEen tante van mie was ook in de helm geboorn. Zij zag wel veurboden. Ze wist soms, woar n sterfgeval komen zol. \nDe leste oorlog hef ze ook veurspeld. Ze har almoal sterren vaaln zien in t oosten. “Doar komp de vijand vot”, zee ze. \n“Moar hij krig het aan de kont” (d.w.z. hij verliest het)” \nEn hij hef het aan de kont kreegn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43577,"r":"WEV006904","p":"Vriescheloo","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Father looks towards Vlagtwedde and sees a windmill turning that cannot be the Vlagtwedde mill. When he looks more closely, the sails have vanished. Now the Vrieschelo mill stands on that spot. Someone had seen the same sails turning a hundred years earlier at full moon.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nVoader het meer zain.\nHai ston es n moal op t land te spitn en kik es eevn in de richten van Vlagtwedde. Hé, denkt e, ken k nou inains de meuln van Vlagtwedde hier draain zain; dat is toch onmeugelk. As e wat schaarper tou kiekn wil, binnen de meulnwiekn inains vot.\nMoar nou stait op dat stee de meuln van Vraiskelo.\nTwintig joar veur tied het mien voader hom toch wel zain.\nVoader zag de meuln dus overdag.\nOal Oabram het deizulfde meuln zain. Dat was nog veul eerder, nou wel al honderd joar leden. Hai het de wiekn draaien zain bie lichte-moane. Op t zulfde stee.\nAs kwoajong heb ik dei verhoaln heurd en hier is den ook gain flauwekul bie.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43580,"r":"WEV006906","p":"Vriescheloo","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A prediction that one day many soldiers would come with wagons without horses. When the Canadians arrive in 1945, someone remembers this.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nt Is n hail zet leden. Oabram zee es n moal: “Hier koomt nog ais n haile bult seldoatn. Ik zai ze bie t hoes van H. en bie K en op t haim van Z. Zai hebt woagens bie zuk zunder peerden.\n Toun in 1945 de Canadezen kwamen, was dr nog aine oale, dei zuk dat vertelsel van de spoukkieker in t zin schoot. Hai lag op berre en kun nait best wat zegn, omdat e verlamd was. \nMoar zoveul begreepn wie wel van zien “hoi, hoi”, dat e zegn wol:“Oabram zee t ja al?”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43583,"r":"WEV007001","p":"Drouwenermond","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"After a visit, the narrator and his wife see a cyclist going to their house. At the house there is no bicycle to be seen, and they did not notice it disappear. Two days later the doctor who comes for a sick child puts his bicycle in the same place where they had seen the bicycle.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nHet is mien vrouw en mie zulf overkoom-m; in t begun toen wie hier woonn. Op een oavend wazzen wie op bezuik west bie de buurn. \nToen wie noar huus gungen, zeg ik:“Kiek, doar giet nog ene noar ons huus.” Wie zaggen allebei n fietse ankomen; de lanteern was aan. Moar toen wie thuus kwamen, was dr gien fietse te zien. En we harn ook niet markt, dat e weer vot goan was. Twee doagen loater wordt er een kind bie ons ziek. De dokter mut komen. \nDie zet de fietse teegn t huus aan op hetzulfde stee, woar wie hum die oavend stoan zien hadden. Dit was wel dudelk n veurbericht; het is zo woar as ik hier zit.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43588,"r":"WEV007005","p":"Drouwenermond","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Floating little lights are seen as a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of, among other things, the building of a house, the laying of a road, the digging of a canal.","i":"F.W.","o":"Lichies zweefden hier vroeger genog over de venen en de moerassen. \nEr wazzen wel mensn, die den zeden, dat er wat komen zol; een huus of n weg. Loater is t knoal groaven. “Kiek”, zeden die ollen, “wie hebben t ja al zegd vroeger.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43612,"r":"WEV007301","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hearing bolts sliding and a side door opening and closing must have been a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the arrival of the doctor, who walks along the same path and goes through the same door as was heard.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nWat ik vertel, is allemoal woar; woorom zol k t laigen?\n n Poar joar leden heurden mien vrou en ik s oavends op berre de deurn op zied van t huus oopn en tou goan. Dudelk vernamen wie, dat de grundels vot schoovn wurn. Ik bin nog van t berre of west um es te kiekn, wat dr te doun was, moar niks te zain. \nMien mouder leefde dou ook nog, en zai heurde aine loopn teegn t huus langs; de grundels en deure hef ze ook heurd. \nWie hebben dr wel over proat, wat of t weezn kon, moar wozzen doadelk gain verkloaren. \nLoater is mien mouder ziek worn en dou mozzen wie op n oavend dokter hebben. Ik bin hen west te beln; en dou s nachts de dokter dr aan kwam, luip e langs t zulfde pad, woor mouder de stapn eerder heurd had. Ik har de veurdeure al oopn doan, den kon e door ja in. Moar nee heur, hai luip teegn t huus langs en gung deur de zieddeure. Noa dei tied hebben wie deure en grundels nait weer vernomen.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43613,"r":"WEV007302","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator thinks that the little light and posts grandmother saw are a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the cars and the telephone poles.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nMien grootmoe zat hier vrouger vaok veur t roam en den zee ze: \n“Kiek es, doar goan aal mor löchies achter mekoar aan. Eerst n rode en den n widde.” \nWie zaggen den niks en lachden dr wat om.\n “En toch zai ik ze, kinder,” zee ze, k zai ook poaln stoan.” \nLoater heb k dr voak aan docht, as ik over de weg de auto s vlaigen zai. En de poaln binnen dr komen, telefoonpoaln, precies op stee, woor grootmoe ze zain hef.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43615,"r":"WEV007304","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"An indifferent man admits that something exists after a fire in which all the trees are scorched black, but a magpie's nest still has green leaves.","i":"F.W.","o":"Dit heb k zulf mit moakt. \nJan B. was n onverschillige vent; hai wol naarns van waitn.\nMoar op n dag mos e toch erkennen, dat dr wat bestait.\nOp Taange brandde een huus op. Ale bomen in de buurt verschroeiden nog; takn e n bloarn warren allemoal zwaart. Moar nou kump t wonder. \n In ain van de bomen zat n eeksternust. Zo'n nust wil ja meroakel brannen. En dat nust is zitn bleevn; n poar bloarn dr um tou warn nog gruin en aal t andere was zwaart. Hou ken dat nou?\n Ik ken dr gain verkloarn veur geevn, moar t betaiknt wat.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":210663,"r":"ENGELS002516","p":"Grashoek","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A girl points at a line of large vehicles, but the adults see nothing. After the liberation a column of tanks comes from that direction.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Voorteken:\nIn 1943 zag een dochtertje van 5 jaar van de familie van den Beucken, Vliegert, dat bij haar ouders was, toen deze met mijn vrouw achter hun huis stonden te praten, een verschijnsel, dat geen der anderen konden waarnemen. Het meisje wees achter het huis in de richting van de Raom, en riep: “Kiek ens dao! Wat es tet allemaol? ’n Ganse reij hieël groeëte, en hieël zjwaor wage’s! En dao! Nag mieër reije!”\nDe drie volwassenen zagen niets, en hielden haar voor de gek, doch zij hield vol, dat zij het duidelijk zag.\nBij de bevrijding kwamen uit deze richting zoveel Britse tanks met kanonnen in kolonnes , dat er metersdiepe sleuven door het land kwamen. Het kind moet dus een voorteken gezien hebben.\n\nGeen omzetting in dialect van het verhaal door Engels. \n\nAanvullend verslag van verteller Leonardus Kluijtmans, Helden. Helden, 29-4-1964"},{"n":210680,"r":"ENGELS002610","p":"Maasbree","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A rising light that grows larger is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the building of a chapel.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Ik woonde in mijn jeugd eens als boerenknecht in Grubbenvorst in “de Heierheuf”. Met kameraden gingen we ’s avonds wel eens “buurten” naar het gehucht Californië, bij de Venloseweg. Er was daar een plaats, waar ingevolge een stichting, een kapel gebouwd moest worden. We zagen eens op deze plaats hoog in de lucht een klein blauw licht, dat opsteeg en groter werd; op het oog met een doorsnee van ½ Meter. Naderhand zagen we dat meermaals. Ook anderen, bv. jongens van Melderslo zagen dit. Toen naderhand het kapelletje gebouwd was, zag men het niet meer. Het ligt aan de weg rechts, naar Californië. Ik was toen 16 jaar oud. Het was ongeveer 1900.\n\nVerslag 53, Omzetting van de Ned. tekst in de verhalen van Hubertus Janssen, Neerkant, en van andere losse bronnen [E. Zelen, Ant. van de Kerkhof, Piet Vossen, Hendrik Hilkens, Pier Mertens]; gegeven in rapport no. L291-26, in het dialect van Helden. Helden, 27-11-1969\nIn miene jongen tied wonden ich as boore-knèècht in de Heier-heuf in Grubbevoorst. Mèt kommeraote gong ich s’aoves wél èns buurte nao Californië, e geheucht an de Vènnelse weeg. Rèèchs van de weeg waas tao enne plak, oe ’n kapél gezat mos wère, vanwegen ein belofte. \nWe zogen dao boven èns enne kieër allemaol hoeëg in de looch e klein blauw leecht, dét ömhoeëg sjteeg, en groeëter woordt. Op ’t aug waas ’t zoeëgét ennen halve meter in doorsjnee. Daonao hebbe we dét nag dökker"},{"n":210681,"r":"ENGELS002610","p":"Maasbree","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A rising light that grows larger is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the building of a chapel.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Ik woonde in mijn jeugd eens als boerenknecht in Grubbenvorst in “de Heierheuf”. Met kameraden gingen we ’s avonds wel eens “buurten” naar het gehucht Californië, bij de Venloseweg. Er was daar een plaats, waar ingevolge een stichting, een kapel gebouwd moest worden. We zagen eens op deze plaats hoog in de lucht een klein blauw licht, dat opsteeg en groter werd; op het oog met een doorsnee van ½ Meter. Naderhand zagen we dat meermaals. Ook anderen, bv. jongens van Melderslo zagen dit. Toen naderhand het kapelletje gebouwd was, zag men het niet meer. Het ligt aan de weg rechts, naar Californië. Ik was toen 16 jaar oud. Het was ongeveer 1900.\n\nVerslag 53, Omzetting van de Ned. tekst in de verhalen van Hubertus Janssen, Neerkant, en van andere losse bronnen [E. Zelen, Ant. van de Kerkhof, Piet Vossen, Hendrik Hilkens, Pier Mertens]; gegeven in rapport no. L291-26, in het dialect van Helden. Helden, 27-11-1969\nIn miene jongen tied wonden ich as boore-knèècht in de Heier-heuf in Grubbevoorst. Mèt kommeraote gong ich s’aoves wél èns buurte nao Californië, e geheucht an de Vènnelse weeg. Rèèchs van de weeg waas tao enne plak, oe ’n kapél gezat mos wère, vanwegen ein belofte. \nWe zogen dao boven èns enne kieër allemaol hoeëg in de looch e klein blauw leecht, dét ömhoeëg sjteeg, en groeëter woordt. Op ’t aug waas ’t zoeëgét ennen halve meter in doorsjnee. Daonao hebbe we dét nag dökker"},{"n":210714,"r":"ENGELS002811","p":"Sevenum","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Personal story about astonishment at folk belief in a German town, and the attitude of the population.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Voortekenen:\nOp 10 oct. 1944 werd ik bij een razzia door Duitsers opgepikt, en als dwangarbeider tewerkgesteld aan een kunstmestfabriek in Bodenwerden, in het Weserdal, in de buurt van Holzminden en Hamelen. Ik heb me daar altijd verbaasd over de gering ontwikkeling, en de grote bijgelovigheid van de, overwegend protestantse bevolking aldaar. Overal zag men boven of langs achterdeuren, - zelfs aan de fabrieken -, witgekalkte kruisen, die nog regelmatig bijgewerkt werden. Even vóór de ineenstorting, - toen de geallieerden doorstieten in het Rijnland -, bleek, dat ze nog te dom, of te apatisch, waren, om te beseffen, dat dit een deel van hun eigen land was. Inzake bijgelovige dingen kon een goed verteller bijna alles aan hen kwijt voor waarheid. Nagenoeg niemand ging meer naar de kerk. Hun “Pastor” was ingelijfd bij de “Folkssturm”, en liep met een geweer over de straat. Dit gewillig in het gareel lopen van hun herder zette veel kwaad bloed bij de bevolking, die oorlogsmoe was.\nDe fabriek lag op een hoogte, en het dorp in het rivierdal. Op een dag hing er een mistig waas over het dal, waardoor het dorp aan het oog onttrokken werd. Een paar bijgelovige Duitsers beweerden, dat er iets in de lucht hing van een onheilspellende gebeurtenis. Iedere Duitser kwam er van onder de indruk. Ik zei: “Als jullie menen, dat er iets is, ga dan eens kijken!”\nDoch niemand durfde. “Dan zal ik wel e"},{"n":208746,"r":"LINSSEN007003","p":"Ell","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A cat washing itself is an omen of visitors; a magpie cawing is an omen of bad news.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Voortekens : Als de kat zich 's morgens vroeg wast, is er bezoek op komst. Wanneer men een ekster hoort \"Sjekkeren\"(krassen) komt er slecht nieuws."},{"n":208751,"r":"LINSSEN007008","p":"Ell","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A black cat in the evening is a bad omen.","i":"G.H.L."},{"n":208771,"r":"LINSSEN007205","p":"Posterholt","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of death, disaster and the coming weather.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Voortekenen van dieren: Wanneer een ekster vlakbij de woning schaterde, zou spoedig een dode in de familie te betreuren zijn.\n\nVleermuizen en uilen bij avond in de nabijheid der huizen voorspelden weinig goeds.\n\nBij het gekwaak van kikkers was goed weer op komst. Het geroep van de koekoek kondigde regen aan."},{"n":44144,"r":"WEV007801","p":"Vledderhuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man who earlier heard roof tiles sliding down hears the same sound when a house is demolished.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik zal joe vertellen van dingen, dei ik zulf beleefd heb.\n'k Was nog n jongkerel, dou k es moal mit n poar kammeroaden s oavonds op boeten stun.\nIk zeg: “heur es, door glieden aal mien pannen noar doale.”\nt Was in de buurt van oal Jan Scheper zien hoes. Dei andere jonges heurden niks. n Zet loater is Scheper zien hoes ofbrookn; k heb dr bie west en dou de pannen noar doale gleden, docht ik bie mie zulf: “Kiek, dat geluud hest eerder heurd.”\n\nVeurloop nuimen ze dat. Dai wat mensen binnen door staark in.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44145,"r":"WEV007802","p":"Vledderhuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On the spot where a woman hears the sound of rattling plates and spoons in plates, a house is later built.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop nuimen ze dat. Dai wat mensen binnen door staark in.\nMien mouder hef ook voak wat veuroet heurd.\nHail wat bin 'k netuurlijk vergeetn, as kind stoa je door nich zo slim bie stil.\nk Wait nog dat ze op 'n oavend in hoes kwam en zee: “Nou heb k toch weer wat mitmoakt; ik loop over de weg en heur op t land van B. aal man tellers rappeln; k heur ook dat dr gounend mit lepels in tellers houden, net of dr mensken aan t eetn binnen.”\nEn wat wil t geval? Joarn loater is op dat stuk grond t hoes van Van der Heide zet; wie kwamen door wol in hoes; as de lu dan bie toafel zatn te eetn, heurde mouder t geluud van lepels en vörkn in tellers net as vrouger.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":130203,"r":"BIJLSMA000604","p":"Haskerhorne","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A dancing light is seen; the butter factory was later built where it disappears. Hammering has also been heard at night in the same place.","i":"T.B.","o":"Op in joun roun in man de dyk lâns en opiens dounse der in ljochtsje foar him út. It fordwoun dêr hwer’t letter it bûterfabryk yn 'e Hoarne boud waerd. Men hearde dêr op it selde sté foar 'e tiid by nacht ek wol timmerjen, bûtsen en slaen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130204,"r":"BIJLSMA000605","p":"Haskerhorne","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A girl senses in advance what is going to happen. For instance, she makes a movement as if to pick something up before a cup falls; she cries before she falls.","i":"T.B.","o":"Der wennen lju dy hiene in famke, dêr't men fan sei dat hja de dingen foar 'e tiid dat se barden al oanfielde. Sa koe it wêze dat it bern in biweging makke as woe se hwat opheine dat fan de tafel foel. Even letter foel der dan in kopke fan 'e tafel. Ek koe it barre dat it bern samar bigoun to skriemen, sûnder dat der hwat wie. In skoftsje letter stroffele it famke en rekke to fâllen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130205,"r":"BIJLSMA000606","p":"Haskerhorne","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hearing bells ring when the bell is not ringing means a death.","i":"T.B.","o":"Somliken hearden eartiids kloklieden sûnder dat de klok lette. Dat wie dan in teken dat der ien kaem to forstjerren.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130235,"r":"BIJLSMA001001","p":"Scharsterbrug","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The sound of a spade being thrown into a boat is heard, but there is nothing to see. Later the sound is heard again; then father has come home and thrown the spade into the boat.","i":"T.B.","o":"De famylje Oord wenne to Langsweagen oan it wetter. Jouns hearden se dat it spit yn it boat smiten waerd. Hja gyngen dan bûtendoar, mar dan wie der neat to sjen. In skoftsje letter hearden se it selde lûd. Wer der hinne, en dan wie heit thús kommen en hie it spit yn it boat smiten.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130252,"r":"BIJLSMA001102","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A prediction that carriages will drive without horses. The first car causes a stir.","i":"T.B.","o":"Foar sa'n tachtich jier sei beppe: \"nachts dan ride hjir weinen sûnder hynders troch de Midstrjitte\". Folle letter kaem de earste automobiel, dêr't men frjemd fan opseach. It doarp roun by dat earste forskinen op ien ein.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130254,"r":"BIJLSMA001104","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"After cries for help are heard on a canal during a frost, nobody skates there any more.","i":"T.B.","o":"Op de greate grêft fan Herema-state waerd alear winters in soad riden. Ek waerden der wol hurdriderijen hâlden. Op in kear ha somliken sjoen en heard dat der in greate smite folk op 'e grêft gear wie, en hja hearden doe in jammerdearlik helpgerop.\nDer waerd sein: dat is in faei teken, der moat net wer op 'e grêft riden wurde. Dat is ek net wer bard, ek nou riidt men der net.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130271,"r":"BIJLSMA001502","p":"Sintjohannesga","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Seeing a bright patch in the sky in which soldiers on horseback are fighting is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the First World War.","i":"T.B.","o":"Op it Westerskar ûnder Rotsterhaule seach Andries de Jong, dy't dêr buorkerij hie en yn 'e tsjerkerie to Sint-Johannesgea siet, in ljocht plak yn 'e loft, en daliks dêrop yn dat ljocht soldaten op hynders. It gie op in fjochtsjen. It duorre sa even en doe wie it fisioen wer fordwoun. In skoft letter briek de earste wrâldoarloch út -.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130292,"r":"BIJLSMA001804","p":"Sintjohannesga","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Battles are seen in the sky involving various countries, except the Netherlands. Some time later the First World War breaks out.","i":"T.B.","o":"Foar de earste wrâldoarloch wie Andries Bleeker mei oare mannen oan it wurk yn it Skar ûnder Rotsterhaule. Hy sei: mannen, sjogge jim neat yn 'e loft. Né, nimmen seach hwat. Hy sei: ik sjoch fjochterij yn 'e loft. Underskate lannen bin derby bitrokken. Lokkich, ik sjoch ús lân der net by.\nIn skoftsje letter briek de oarloch út.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130293,"r":"BIJLSMA001805","p":"Sintjohannesga","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man senses that his daughter is ill, which turns out to be true.","i":"T.B.","o":"Hindrik de Groot en Jozef de Vries wiene as spitter en minger yn 'e feanderij to Dolsterhuzen oan it wurk. Hindrik sei: ik wit net, it is net yn oarder, ik tink dat ús famke siik is. Ik moat nei hûs. Sa wie it ek.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130295,"r":"BIJLSMA001807","p":"Sintjohannesga","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A church is later built on the spot where a light was seen.","i":"T.B.","o":"Eartiids waerd der to Sint Jehannesgea by joun in great ljocht sjoen. Letter waerd dêr it apostelgebou boud.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130326,"r":"BIJLSMA002305","p":"Poppenwier","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the summer of 1914 the young people are so exuberant that a woman cries out that this will have consequences. A month later the First World War breaks out.","i":"T.B.","o":"Tersoalster merke waerd eartiids yn 'e lette hjerst hâlden. Dat wie faek heukerjen en dêrom waerd it nei de simmer forskoud. Sa waerd de merke to Tersoal yn 1914 foar it earst yn july hâlden. It gie der doe frijhwat omwei. It jongfolk wie slim útlitten en bolbjirken. De jouns namen de jongemannen de kastleinske yn 'e govert. Hja stiek de hannen omheech en rôp: \"Hjir komt in slach op!\".\nIn moanne letter briek de earste wrâldkriich út.","l":"Fries"},{"n":11517,"r":"CJ000301","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"During the war a woman hears the roof of the house nearly coming down, but when her husband comes home nothing has happened. A year later a few bombs fall near the house, causing exactly what the woman heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broers wiif wie ris in kear allinne thús. Hja wenne to Aldegea. Hja bigoun ynienen lûd to razen, hwant it hiele dak kaem hast del. De pannen der ôf en in stik leven en alles fan 't plak. Hja wie deabinaud en krûpte ûnder 't bêd. Doe't myn broer thúskaem, sei se: \"Ik wol hjir wei, hwant it giet hjir raer.\" Mar der wie neat gebeurd. Mar in jier letter foelen der by harren hûs in pear bommen del. Hwant it wie yn 'e oarloch. Doe gong it mei it hûs krekt sa lyk as hja it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11537,"r":"CJ000321","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In a place without houses a man sees people carrying on wildly, but also shaking hands at the end. A football pitch was later built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Houtigehage wenne in âld man, dy sei op in kear: \"Noch noait haw ik sa hwat raers sjoen. Se sloegen dêr freeslik yn elkoar om. It giet dêr wol sa bot op in skoppen en traepjen en fjochtsjen, mar it wûndere is, dat de iene fijân oan 'e ein de oare de hân jowt. Ik seach it tusken dy twa huzen troch. Ja, dy huzen binne der ek al net mear.\"\nLetter kaem op dat plak in fuotbalfjild. Dat hie hy fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":11544,"r":"CJ000405","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The number of knots in the rope used to rock the cradle shows how many children a couple will have.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger leinen de lytse bern yn in reiden widze. Dêr siet in tou oan fêst, dêr't de widze mei roeike woarde. Dy't der mei widze die der gauris in knoop yn. Safolle knopen as der yn dat widzetou sieten, safolle bern krigen de âlden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21877,"r":"CJ029017","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On a slope, mysterious sounds announcing a future event can often be heard. They are portents.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e helling wie altyd foartsjirmerije. Dêr wisten se fantofoaren altyd as der hwat komme soe. Dan woarde der yn 'e nacht mei stikken hout smiten en it gong op in timmerjen en in klopjen. Myn âldste suster wie naeister en kom dêr ek. Hja hat it faek heard en it kom altyd nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":49642,"r":"GENDT013","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People born with a caul can see things before they happen.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Ze hemme vroeger duk verteld, da ome Jan, ’n bruur van mien schonvoader, mitten helm gebore was. Zo iemes kan van alles van teveure zien.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":50200,"r":"GENDT176","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A fireball in the sky as an omen of the First World War.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Mien grötmoeder het ons duk verteld, dat er es ’n vuurbol on de loch had gestoan en dada ’n vörteike was gewes van den erste wereldoorlog.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":50201,"r":"GENDT177","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A fruit tree blossoming twice a year means a bride or a death.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"As ’n vruchboom twee keer per joar bloeij, ista gin bes teike. Da gebeurden es bé’j Hannes Moerkerk. De pèrebom ston dor vör de twedde keer te bloeije. Vrouw Moerkerk zèj toe: “Da zie ik nie gern. Da gif ’n bruud of ’n liek. ’n Bruud da kan nie mer, want ze zien bé’j ons allemol getrouwd. Dus mot ’t ’n liek worre”. Kort dorop is Bart, de schoonzoon, gestörve.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":208833,"r":"LINSSEN007801","p":"Horn","v":"L.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A fireball falling in the garden during a childbirth is an evil omen that comes true.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Vuurbol In Berkelaar moest een vrouw bevallen. De vroedvrouw werd gehaald. Juist toen de bevalling geschiedde, viel er een vuurbol in de tuin. Dit was een kwaad voorteken. En inderdaad . Volgens het zeggen van de buurtbewoners groeide de jongen op en werd een grote vlegel."},{"n":208876,"r":"LINSSEN008207","p":"Heythuysen","v":"L.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A magpie screeching near the house is an omen of a death.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"In de buurt van Aldenghoor spookte het ook. Van Rooy die ook zo'n spookhuis bewoonde, bood het te koop aan. Er kwam geen bod op. \nDe pastoor werd ermee in kennis gesteld. Hij zegende het huis, Men maakte bovendien 3 kruisjes op de dorpel. Het huis was en bleef echter onverkoopbaar tot eindelijk Weynen Jan het aandurfde het huis voor een zacht prijsje te kopen. Hij zou de oorzaak van de spokerij wel opsporen. Op een avond ging hij zich verdekt opstellen in een hoek op de zolder en bleef wachten. Daar sprong opeens een zwarte kat uit de spanten en gordingen van de zolder en kwam terecht op het zolderluik, dat hevig begon te klapperen. Dit was echter geen echte heks want ze droeg een witte vlek op de borst.\nTwee andere gitzwarte katten, zonder enig vlekje werden echter gevangen en heel ver weggevoerd op uren afstand van het huis. \nMet de spokerij was het gedaan"},{"n":208890,"r":"LINSSEN008313","p":"Posterholt","v":"L.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The chattering of a magpie is an omen of a death.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Ekster Het \"sjekkeren\" van een ekster kondigde aan dat in het huis waarbij de ekster zich ophield, iemand binnenkort zou sterven."},{"n":208914,"r":"LINSSEN008607","p":"Ohé en Laak","v":"L.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator does not believe that the chattering of a magpie is an omen of visitors.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Voortekens: Wanneer een ekster \"sjekkert\" heeft men bezoek te verwachten, vertelde men vroeger. Ook dat geloof ik niet, zei vertelster, die nu een huis bewoont in het open veld, want ik zie elke dag zoveel eksters, dat ik dan doorlopend bezoek zou moeten hebben."},{"n":209042,"r":"LINSSEN010111","p":"Echt","v":"L.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"An owl at night or in the evening is a bad omen.","i":"G.H.L."},{"n":45298,"r":"WEV008703","p":"Wessinghuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Seeing a little light is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the building of a house and of people living in it.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ons hoes is al laank veur tied zain. Op n oavend luipen dr n poar manlu deur t veld en dou hebben ze n löchie brannen zain op dit stee.\nIn n leeg hoes zaggen ze ook n moal löcht brannen en n zetje noa tied was t bewoond.\nDit binnen taikens van veurloop, dat bestèèt.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45305,"r":"WEV008709","p":"Wessinghuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Noise in the horse stable in the evening is an omen that a horse will kick something to pieces.","i":"F.W.","o":"t Gebeurde wol is, dat ze s oavends wat in t peerdstaal heurden. Kiekn deden ze maistied nich, man ze wuzzen wol, dat t peerd gauw wat stukn hou-en zol; door was t n veurbeduudsel van.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44558,"r":"WEV009203","p":"Onstwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man who wants to convert his farm into a bakery sees the complete bakery standing there one evening. When he opens the door everything has vanished; later the bakery is built just as he saw it.","i":"F.W.","o":"veurloop.\nAnder geval, woar gebeurd in Onstwedde.\nt Is joarn leden, dou was dr n jonge vent, dai n bakkers zoak veur zuk zulf hebben wol. Hai kofde n olle boerderij um dai te verbouwn. Op n oavend lop hai noar dat hoes en wat zug e dan?\nDe bakkerij stèèt doar al; ovend dr in en hangen lampn aan de beune. Hai gèèt dr ja gouw op of en döt deure oopn, man mit is alles vot. Loater wordt bakkerij toch zo zet as hai hum dou op dai oavend zain har. Woar gebeurd, ik moak joe niks wies.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44559,"r":"WEV009204","p":"Onstwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When a man who can see things in advance has visited and does not come back, it means disaster.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nNôn woont hier nog ain in Onstwedde, dai veul veuroet zug.\nAs e op n dag bie joe west hef, en hai komp dan nich weer, dan is t nich best; reekn dr dan man op.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44577,"r":"WEV009406","p":"Schoonoord","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Glow-worms predict the coming of a road with streetlights.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurgezicht.\nSums zaggen ie in et veld van die glimwormpies.\nDan zeden de mensn: \"Daar komp een weg met laampen.\"","l":"Drents"},{"n":44579,"r":"WEV009408","p":"Schoonoord","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Grey horses bring bad luck and are never used to tow ships.","i":"F.W.","o":"Biegeleuf was dr trouwens net zogoed.\nEr waarn ja veule scheepjagers; zulf heb k t scheepsjaagn ook nog doan. Maar nooit zol een schipper een wit peerd veur zien schip doen; dat gaf ongelukn. k Hebbe dan ook gien schimmel veur n schip zien, zolang ik leefd hebbe.","l":"Drents"},{"n":44582,"r":"WEV009501","p":"Stadskanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"To avoid misfortune, boat-towers never use a white horse.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik zel begunnen joe te verteln, dat ik joarn scheepsjoager west bin; bie tied en ontied bie t pad sjouwd heb en nog nooit wat teegn komen bin, woor ik mie baange veur moakt heb.\nIk wait wel, dat er in mien jonge tied n hoop mensn wazn, dei zok van alles en nog wat inbeeln en biegeleuvig wazzen. Bieveurbeld: in hail mien levend heb k nooit n wit peerd veur n schip zain; n wit peerd bedudde n ongelukkige vracht of andere rampen.\nGain scheepsjoager zol zok door den aan woagen.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45008,"r":"WEV009601","p":"Holthe","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man suddenly sees a light in the meadow. Later the land is bought. When the thickets are cleared, tractors make the same movement the fire made earlier.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wat ik joe vertelle, is woar gebeurd.\nEr is meer dan veule mensen denken. Doar is n zekere almacht.\nWel door an geleuft, lacht niet om alles en wet, dat niet alles te verklaarn valt; maar hij nuumt ook alles geen olle wieve-prooties, wat zo vake gebeurt.\nLuster maar ies uut mien eigen ervaarn.\n\nEt gebeurde bie ons in Elp, dat op een avond mien va en nog iene de koenen uut et laand haaln muzzen.\nOpiens giet daar een licht om heur henne; dat dreit om heur toe.\nSie loat de koene, woor sie bint en sneln naar huus.\nLater is datzulfde nog ies n maal passeerd.\nEn wat is er nu jaren later gebeurd?\nDe Staat hef hier laand aankoft; de bossies muzzem umhakt worn; en toen kwamen er trekkers. Die maakten precies dezelfde beweging in de rondte as veur de tied dat vuur.\nIk vertelle beslist gien smoesies; die dingen komen veur.","l":"Drents"},{"n":45012,"r":"WEV009604","p":"Holthe","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hearing planks being thrown is the voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the building of a house.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wat ik joe vertelle, is woar gebeurd.\nEr is meer dan veule mensen denken. Doar is n zekere almacht.\nWel door an geleuft, lacht niet om alles en wet, dat niet alles te verklaarn valt; maar hij nuumt ook alles geen olle wieve-prooties, wat zo vake gebeurt.\nLuster maar ies uut mien eigen ervaarn.\n\nMien vrouwe en ik heurden es gegooi met plankn naast ons huus.\nWas niks te zien en wie konden et niet verklaarn.\nn Poossien later wel; toen wuur er een huus bouwd naast die van ons.\nZie ie nu wel, dat er een onverklaarbare macht is, want ligen doe k niet.","l":"Drents"},{"n":45039,"r":"WEV009902","p":"Noord-Sleen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A road with houses is seen in advance; a woman born with a caul predicts a drowning in the churn.","i":"F.W.","o":"Vooruitzien.\nIk weet dat er eens woonwagenvolk voorbij trok.\nEen paar mannen zeiden: \"Hier komt nog eens een weg met enkele huizen; we hebben ze al zien staan met licht en al.\"\nVerder hoorde ik eens iets van iemand, die met de helm geboren was. t Was een vrouw. \nEn wat ik nu vertel, is geen praatje.\nZe waarschuwde de buren vaak, dat ze goed op de kinderen moesten passen, anders zou er een in een karn verdrinken. \nOp n dag, toen er even niet op een kind gelet werd, is dat werkelijk in een karn gevallen en verdronken."},{"n":45047,"r":"WEV010002","p":"Harpel","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A sound as if part of the side wall has fallen, but nothing can be seen. Two weeks later the horse kicks a piece out of the wall.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurzain.\nVandoage aan de dag heurt ie dr nich zo veul meer over, man dat veurzain bestèèt, door bin k van overtuugd. Ik kan joe dat bewiezen, want mien pabbe en ik zulf hebben verscheiden keern wat mitmoakt. Verder heb ik al n boel heurd van ander lu.\n\nDou wie op de Ballege woonden, heurden wie allemoal n stuk van de ziedmure umvaaln. Dat kön ja, de muurn waren van laim. En wie dochden dat t peerd dr n stuk oet hou-en har. Wie gungen kiekn, man nee, dr was niks te zain. Twai weekn loater gebeurde t wal; t zulfde geluud en t peerd trapde n stuk tou de mure oet.\nVerkloarn ie nôn zowat man es; ik kan t nich; man woar is t.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45049,"r":"WEV010004","p":"Harpel","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A sound of roof tiles sliding off the roof, but nothing can be seen. Later the carpenter slides roof tiles down and the same sound is heard.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurzain.\nVandoage aan de dag heurt ie dr nich zo veul meer over, man dat veurzain bestèèt, door bin k van overtuugd. Ik kan joe dat bewiezen, want mien pabbe en ik zulf hebben verscheiden keern wat mitmoakt. Verder heb ik al n boel heurd van ander lu.\n\nWie zatn keer bie mekoar in hoes en zeden teegn mekoar: \"Door gliedt ja pannen van t hoes of.\" Wie heurden ze dudelk noar doale rappeln.\nWie gungen noar boetn, keekn en zaggen gainain pane liggen op de grond.\nn Poar weke noa tied muzzen wie de timmerman hebben bie n schure; dou luit dai pannen noar doale glieden en wie heurden t zulfde geluud.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45050,"r":"WEV010005","p":"Harpel","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the French period a man sees a line of dead people coming out of Onstwedde. After the churchyard is later moved, the dead leave Onstwedde at every funeral.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurzain.\nVandoage aan de dag heurt ie dr nich zo veul meer over, man dat veurzain bestèèt, door bin k van overtuugd. Ik kan joe dat bewiezen, want mien pabbe en ik zulf hebben verscheiden keern wat mitmoakt. Verder heb ik al n boel heurd van ander lu.\n\nNôn zal k joewat verteln over dingen, dai andern heurd of zain hebben. Eerst mou k nhail ende terugge, noar de Franse tied.\nDou dai Fransn in de buurt kwamen, was dr zekere B. in Onstwedde en dai zee teegn de menskng: \"Moak joe grode hekn of of hoge heegn um de boerderijen. Dan kunt ze nich zo man bie joe op t aarf koomn. Ik heb riegn doden oet Onstwedde goan zain.\" \nDe dikke boern hebt t ook doan um dai Fransn te muitn.\nt Huilp netuurlijk niks, man dat hadden ze nich in de goatn.\nDai riege doden is ook niks van komen in dai tied. Man loater wal en dat mout dai olle B. zain hebben, zunder dat e dat wus.\nt Kerkhof is loater verploatst. En bie elke begravvenis goat de doden non tou Onstwedde oet.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43134,"r":"WEV010107","p":"Wollinghuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"After a bang is heard, nothing is seen outside. Later the same bang is heard and it turns out the tram has derailed.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wie beleefden zulf n keer wat. \nt Was op noavend en wie zatn mooi bie toafel mit mekoar. \nDan heuren wie inains n klap op boetn, dat wie allemoal tou t hoes oet stoeven um te kiekn wat of dat betaiknde. \nNiks te zain. \nMan n poar weekn door noa heurden wie dezulfde klap. Weer noar boeten en wat was dr gebeurd? De tram, de O.G. van Winschoot noar Troapel was ontspoord. Dat was toch n dudelijke veurloop.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43141,"r":"WEV010203","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"For the first three years storks throw something out of the nest. Under their wings sit bouwmannetjes (little builder men). Whoever sees a bouwmannetje (little builder man) for the first time without much money will have little money the whole year.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ooievoars. Wat door van zegd wordt, is zo.\nt Eerste joar dat hai n nust bouwt, gooit hai ai uut t nust; t tweide joar n jonk en t daarde joar n vere. \nNoa dei tied niks meer, want den is de störk ingebörgerd; door komp dat van. \nWat ze vrouger ook zeden? \nMit de störken komen de bouwmannegies, dei zitn onder de vleugels van de störkn. Wieder wur dr van dei vogels zegd: \"Wel veur de eerste keer n bouwmannegie zugt en den nait veul geld het, zel t haile joar zunig bie kas weezn.\"","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43176,"r":"WEV010701","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A factory that is not there is seen. Years later a factory is built.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloopm.\nDoar ken ik joe hail wat stoaltjes van verteln, dei allemoal woar binnen.\n\nIk ree es n moal mit aine in de umgeevn van Appingedam. \nWie kwamen mit ons baidend van t waark. \nOpains zeg ik teegn mien kameroad: \"Wat stait doar toch veur n febriek; de lampen brannen ja? \"\nMien vrund zag de febriek ook stoan; moar dr was gainend. \nJoarn noa tied is dr aine bouwd. \nVergist hebben wie ons wizze nait.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43191,"r":"WEV010706","p":"Weende","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A spinning wheel heard in the past may have been a foreshadowing of the noise knife grinders now make when turning their stones, and not of a woman sitting spinning.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloopm.\nDoar ken ik joe hail wat stoaltjes van verteln, dei allemoal woar binnen.\n\nWie wonen hier op de Spinbaarg. Hier mout vreuger n wief zeetn hebben te spinnen; t oal mout ook heksn hebben kend. \nMoar waitn ie, wat ik denk?\nIn t bossie, hier n endken vandoan, heb ik hail voak zain dat de scheernsliepers aan de gang wazzen om stainen rond te kriegen. \nZai zöchten den n staine op; dei wur bekapt en noaderhand in t ronde draait om hom mooi rond te moakn. Dat gung dr den vreselk heer en t rappelde ja wat t moar kon.\nDat spinnewail, dat de mensn toun vrouger dus heurd hebben, is misschien wel n veurbode west van t lewaai dat de scheernsliepers muiken.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43415,"r":"WEV011001","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man believes that meeting a black cat or someone with a hunchback brings bad luck.","i":"F.W.","o":"Zwarte katten.\nIn de oorlog 1914/18 wur hier in Boertange vanzulf geweldig smokkeld. L. was dr ain van. Hail gain domme kerel, want loater was e nog veurwaarker bie de haidemoatschappij. \nMoar as hai op pad was noar de grens en kwam hom n zwaarde kadde teegn, den gong e weerom. Want den geleufde hai, dat e betrapt worn zol. En hai gong ook weer noar huus, as e n mens teegn kwam mit n bochel; dat betaikende net zo goud ongeluk.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43434,"r":"WEV011004","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Fog smells like smoke, with the thought that there will soon be a fire. Others see fires in advance, and can feel at the door latch whether a fire or a death is coming.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mist op de weg. \ns Maanks lig dr zo 'n nevel over de weg. As de mensn door deur luipn, zeden ze: \"Rook, zel wel gauw wel n huus opbrannen.\" \nWazzen verder lu dei de huuzn van te veurn in brand zaggen. \nOm te waitn, of er brand kwam of n dode, luipn ze dr hen en vuilden aan de klinke. Waarme klinke beduudde n brand en ain kolle was veurbeduudsel van n staarfgeval. (In de regel wordt er aan de muren gevoeld, maar de heer V. zei, dat het de klink was: F.W.).","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43647,"r":"WEV011603","p":"Hooghalen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Advice to the buyer of a cow not to keep the animal long because prices are falling.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik ben soms in een zekere gemoedstoestand dat ik iets voorzie. \nPrettig is dat niet. \nHet zijn vage momenten, die kort duren; schrik heb je op zo'n moment niet. \nIk zal niet alles weergeven, omdat sommige mensen nog leven, van wiedan ik enkele dingen weet; \n\nHet was in de dertiger jaren. \nIk verkocht een koe en zei tegen de nieuwe eigenaar: \"Het dier is goed; toch moet je het niet te lang houden, want de prijs daalt!\" Dat kwam werkelijk uit; niet lang daarna."},{"n":43648,"r":"WEV011604","p":"Hooghalen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Narrator foresees that a cow will fall ill, recover, fall ill a third time, then not recover and be worth nothing.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik ben soms in een zekere gemoedstoestand dat ik iets voorzie. \nPrettig is dat niet. \nHet zijn vage momenten, die kort duren; schrik heb je op zo'n moment niet. \nIk zal niet alles weergeven, omdat sommige mensen nog leven, van wiedan ik enkele dingen weet; \n\nMijn broer kocht eens een koe. Ik ging het beest bekijken. \nToen zei ik: \"Dat dier is ziek; het wordt wel weer beter, ga het dan verkopen; het wordt daarna opnieuw ziek en of het dan ook geneest weet ik niet.\" Hij lachte me uit, want ik was ja gek. \nMaar de koe werd ziek. Toen zei mijn schoonzuster: \"Wat heb jij met die koe?\" Ik zeg:\"Ik niks, maar jullie.\" \nHet dier knapte inderdaad weer op, zoals ik gezien had. \nEen poos later had het echter dezelfde ziekte weer. \nVoor de tweede keer zeg ik tegen mijn broer: \"Verkoop dat beest, als het weer goed is; het kan voor de derde keer de kwaal krijgen en dan moet het misschien afgemaakt worden.\" \nDe koe is toen dan verkocht aan iemand in Assen. \nMijn broer vertelde de koper mijn voorspellingen er bij. \nOp een dag komt die man uit Assen bij mij en zegt: \"Wat heb jij met die koe?\" Ik zeg:\"Ik niks, maar jij.\" \n\"Ja\", zegt hij, \"het dier heeft de ziekte voor de derde keer en is nu bestemd voor de noodslachting; niet veel meer waard.\""},{"n":47781,"r":"WEV011605","p":"Hooghalen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"After the owner is advised to sell his horse quickly, the horse dies not long afterwards.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik ben soms in een zekere gemoedstoestand dat ik iets voorzie. \nPrettig is dat niet. \nHet zijn vage momenten, die kort duren; schrik heb je op zo'n moment niet. \nIk zal niet alles weergeven, omdat sommige mensen nog leven, van wiedan ik enkele dingen weet; \n\nMijn buurman kocht eens een mooi paard. \n\"Wat een dier, he?\" zegt hij. \nIk zeg: \"Ja, en toch zou ik het maar gauw van de hand doen, want je hebt er niet lang plezier van.\"\nBuurman lachte me uit natuurlijk. Maar even later is het mooie paard dood gegaan."},{"n":47782,"r":"WEV011606","p":"Hooghalen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator foresees a dry summer and takes measures.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik ben soms in een zekere gemoedstoestand dat ik iets voorzie. \nPrettig is dat niet. \nHet zijn vage momenten, die kort duren; schrik heb je op zo'n moment niet. \nIk zal niet alles weergeven, omdat sommige mensen nog leven, van wiedan ik enkele dingen weet; \n\nIn 1921 was ik aan het dicht gooien van greppels. \nEr kwamen mensen langs die zeiden: \"Man, doe dat toch niet; waar moet het water straks door?\" \nIk zei: \"We krijgen een heel droge zomer; er behoeft geen water door.\" Dat was nog in Winterswijk; de mensen haalden de schouders op. Het werd evenwel een droge zomer; greppels waren niet nodig.\n In 1959 voorzag ik ook een droge zomer en heb daarom al van te voren wat vee verkocht, omdat ik wist, dat er geen gras genoeg zou komen."},{"n":47783,"r":"WEV011607","p":"Hooghalen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator foresees the time of the economic crisis and the high value of gold, and warns against hoarding gold and of a coming war.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik ben soms in een zekere gemoedstoestand dat ik iets voorzie. \nPrettig is dat niet. \nHet zijn vage momenten, die kort duren; schrik heb je op zo'n moment niet. \nIk zal niet alles weergeven, omdat sommige mensen nog leven, van wiedan ik enkele dingen weet; \n\nDe crisis-tiid en de hoge waarde van het goud zag ik ook aankomen. \nZelfs heb ik indertijd advertenties in de krant gehad. \nDaarin waarschuwde ik de mensen.\nBijvoorbeeld in rijmpjes, zoals: \"Het goud moet gebruikt worden met verstand; en rollen door het land. Als het wordt opgepot, dan slaat de vlam er in.\" Tevens waarschuwde ik de mensen voor een komende oorlog, die niet uitblijven kon. Een jaar kon ik niet noemen.\nMaar dat er oorlog kwam, was voor mij zeker."},{"n":47787,"r":"WEV011609","p":"Hooghalen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator sees someone who has yet to be born commit a murder.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik ben soms in een zekere gemoedstoestand dat ik iets voorzie. \nPrettig is dat niet. \nHet zijn vage momenten, die kort duren; schrik heb je op zo'n moment niet. \nIk zal niet alles weergeven, omdat sommige mensen nog leven, van wiedan ik enkele dingen weet; \n\nIk heb een moordaanslag zien gebeuren op iemand door iemand, die toen nog heel niet geboren was. Dat is later allemaal uitgekomen."},{"n":130368,"r":"BIJLSMA002604","p":"Vegelinsoord","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hearing hammering at night is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the news that the contract to build a mill has been awarded.","i":"T.B.","o":"Klaren's pake fan memmekant wie timmerman en molemakker to Oranjewâld. Der soe in mole boud wurde en hy soe dat kerwei graech útfiere. Op in nacht hearden se leven, getôch en geklap mei balken en planken. In wike letter krige hy birjocht dat it wurk him gund wie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130375,"r":"BIJLSMA002701","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At night the work done during the day is heard. When someone looks, nothing is going on.","i":"T.B.","o":"Op in buorkerij to Appelsgea hearde men nachts hwat der oerdei dien waerd. Sa hearde men de frou op har learen toffels yn 'e koken op de estrikken flier. De pankoekspanne waerd mei papier omrost, de side spek waerd yn 'e kelder tsjin it sket ophongen en dan hearde men hoe't dy spekham tsjin it sket oansljurke en dan ta rêst kaem. Sa ek it skûtelwaskjen en sa mear. Men gie der hinne to sjen, mar dan wie it stil, wylst alles op syn plak stie.\nWer op bêd fornaem men de selde lûden wer, oant it nei in skoft ophâlde.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130376,"r":"BIJLSMA002702","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hearing shovelling in the attic at night is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of growing buckwheat, which is afterwards turned over with shovels in the attic.","i":"T.B.","o":"To Nijeberkeap wie in pleats dêr't men nachts hearde hwat letter barre soe. Sa hearde men op in nacht op 'e souder drok skeppen. Nou en dan foel der in skeppe, sa't by sok wurk barre kin. De frou sei tsjin har man: \"Dou silst boekweit forbouwe, der wurd al skept\". De man sei: \"Ik tink der net oer\". Hy hie oars net as greide. Hja gongen mei in stallantearne nei boppen; neat to bikennen. In jier letter joegen de omstandichheden it sa op dat de boer boekweit forboude, en dêrnei waerd op 'e souder yn werklikheit omskept, sa't men dat foarhinne yn 'e nacht heard hie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130377,"r":"BIJLSMA002703","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A shop bell is heard at a remote farm. Later more houses are built and the farm is converted into a shop.","i":"T.B.","o":"Faek hearde men in hiel hoart neat en dan op in kear wie it wer geande. Sa is it ek ris west dat men dêr yn 'e nacht in winkelskille hearde. Dat wie frjemd, hwant men hie gjin winkelplannen en it boerespultsje lei op 'e romte. Jierren letter, doe't hja dêr net mear wennen en der in tropke huzen byboud wie, rekke de buorkerij oan kant en it hûs ta winkel forboud. Doe gie der de winkelskille.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130419,"r":"BIJLSMA003501","p":"Jubbega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Even before the bell has been installed in the tower, the bell rings one evening.","i":"T.B.","o":"Pieter van der Wal is berne yn 'e Fryske Wylp, dêr't syn âlden ek wei kamen. Doe't Van der Wal sa'n foech jonge wie, krigen se dêr yn de Wylp in klok yn 'e toer. Op in joun - de klok wie der noch net - hearden se dêr de klok lieden. Letter waerd de klok let, en it wie itselde lûd dat men op dy joun heard hie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130433,"r":"BIJLSMA003604","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At stove makers, coopers, wheelwrights and shipyards there is sometimes noise at night, a portent of work to come.","i":"T.B.","o":"By bidriuwen as kachelsmidden, kûpers, weinmakkers en ek op 'e helling koe it der by tiden nachts nochal hwat omwei gean.\nDan wie der wurk op til, en dat kaem dan ek wis.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130434,"r":"BIJLSMA003605","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Shortly after cries for help are heard at a canal, someone drowns.","i":"T.B.","o":"Eartiids hat men ris helpgerop op de greate grêft fan Herema-state heard. Even nei dy tiid is Kryn Taconis dêr fordronken.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130458,"r":"BIJLSMA004204","p":"Sondel","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At night the sound of a hammer driving a post into the ground. When a man goes to look there is nothing to see or hear, but as soon as he leaves it starts again. A few days later he hears the sound again; then it turns out a horse is caught in the barbed wire, and it is freed.","i":"T.B.","o":"Op in nacht waerd Bakker wekker. Hy hearde dat der mei in slaei op in peal slein waerd. Hy tocht, se binne by Harmen Kramer, in boer dêrneist, oan it stekjen. Mûlk siet it hynder yn it stikeltried, dat der stekke wurde moast. Miskien kin 'k helpe, sei er by himsels. Hy gie fan 't bêd en foar it finster stean.\nNé, der wie neat en it houwen en bûtsen wie ek oer. Bakker tocht, mûlk wie it forbylding of haw ik it dreamd. Hy gie wer op bêd, mar hy lei noch net of dêr wie it wer geande, wer itselde. \nHy der wer ôf en nei bûten, mar wer neat to sjen of to hearren.\nIn dei of hwat letter rekke it hynder fan Otto Bruinsma yn it stikeltried en der moast stekke wurde. Dat waerd fansels oerdei dien, en it wie itselde lûd, dat Bakker yn 'e nacht heard hie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130476,"r":"BIJLSMA004306","p":"Gauw","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hammering and talking are heard in advance at the spot where a butter factory was later built.","i":"T.B.","o":"Immen, dy't by nacht troch Sibrandabuorren roun, hearde dêr timmerjen en minsken praten, wylst der dochs neat to bikennen wie. It wie dêr in sodzich en ûngaedlik sté om to bouwen. \nLetter waerd dêr de bûterfabryk boud.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130522,"r":"BIJLSMA004907","p":"Langweer","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A prediction that iron will float on water comes true. Later there are iron ships.","i":"T.B.","o":"By âlds hat in âld minske to Langwar ris foarsein dat it izer op it wetter driuwe soe. It is útkommen; letter kamen der izeren skippen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130524,"r":"BIJLSMA004909","p":"Langweer","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"White horses are seen at night, although there are no horses.","i":"T.B.","o":"Op in stik lân to Legemar seach men yn 'e nacht in soad wite hynders byelkoar, wylst der dochs gjin hynders wiene.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130529,"r":"BIJLSMA005002","p":"Idskenhuizen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A dog that otherwise likes to go along in the boat refuses to come when a sack of stones has been put in the boat to drown it.","i":"T.B.","o":"Bisten kinne somlike dingen foarút oanfiele.\nDe buorman fan De Jong syn âlden to Sleat hie in houn, dy 't altyd mei de mar opgyng. Hja gyngen dan mei in skou. De Jong en syn maten gyngen ek mei, doe noch skoaljonges. Hja swommen, en dehoun wie der gek om om mei. Optlêst waerd de houn âld en krige lek en brek. Om de houn foar lijen to biwarjen woe buorman de houn mar fan kant bringe. Hy lei in sek mei stiennen yn 'e skou, en in skoft letter soe men, lyk as sa faek, mei de skou it wetter op. De houn lykwols bleau op in distânsje en woe net mei. Hy gie mei de sturt tusken de poaten nei hûs.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130530,"r":"BIJLSMA005003","p":"Idskenhuizen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A cat is restless when the skipper is away from home. When the cat sits by the waterside in the morning, it is a sign that the man will come home that day.","i":"T.B.","o":"De turfskipper Franke van Benen to Sleat hie in kat, dy 't altyd by him wie. Mar soms gie Franke om baelder nei Grinslân. De kat bleau dan fansels by de frou oan wâl, wie slim ûnwennich en der wie 'm hast gjin iten ta to krijen.\nDe skipper bleau soms dagenlang wei en men wist net hwannear er thúskaem.\nMen koe it oan 'e kat sjen hwannear 't er thúskaem. De kat siet dan de moarns al op 'e wâl, en dan kaem de skipper fêst dy deis thús.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130531,"r":"BIJLSMA005004","p":"Idskenhuizen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Pigeons refuse to enter their loft. That night the loft is destroyed by a storm.","i":"T.B.","o":"De Jong syn heit to Sleat hie douwen. Op in kear woene de douwen net yn it hok. Men wist sa noch net fan waerbirjochten. De nachts stiek der in stoarm op, dy 't, sa 't De Jong foarstie, it eilân Urk tige tamtearre hat.\nDe oare moarns bliek dat it douwehok fan boppen reage en alhiel fornield wie. De douwen hiene dat sa 't liket oanfield.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130532,"r":"BIJLSMA005005","p":"Idskenhuizen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the evening the dogs will not get into their basket, which stands under a clock. That night the clock weight falls into the dog basket.","i":"T.B.","o":"In man hie in pear hounen, dy 't nachts altyd yn 'e gong tahâlden. It wie in gong mei estrikken en omt dat kâld opjoech, sliepten de hounen yn in greate koer. Op in joun hie de man de hounen útlitten, en doe’t se wer thúskamen, woene se net yn 'e koer. Yn 'e nacht hearden de man en syn frou in slach, dy 't troch it hûs klonk. De man op ûndersiik út, fornaem dat in greate klokswicht fan de klok, dy't yn 'e gong hong, fan boppen kommen wie. It swiere wicht wie yn 'e hounekoer delkommen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130539,"r":"BIJLSMA005102","p":"Bantega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A house was later built on the spot where hammering sounds had been heard in the evening.","i":"T.B.","o":"J.P. hat mei oaren ris op in joun mei lokeinen by it Lemster Hop west. Hja hearden dat der net fierôf timmere waerd. Letter waerd dêr in hûs boud.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130604,"r":"BIJLSMA006302","p":"Goingarijp","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Noise is heard at night at a farm; shortly afterwards the farm is rebuilt.","i":"T.B.","o":"Oan de feart nei it noardein stie in pleats, dêr 't men, as men der by nacht lâns kaem, slaen en bûtsen hearde. Even letter waerd dy pleats forboud.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130648,"r":"BIJLSMA007301","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Lights are seen at a spot where houses are later built.","i":"T.B.","o":"Har heit wenne alear op 'e Grinzer Pein. Op in joun let seach er in ein ôf op in sânwei in hiele rige ljochtsjes. Dat koe net, hwant dêr stie gjin hûs. Heit der hinne, mar der wie neat to sjen. Tsien jier letter waerden oan dy sânwei troch in stichting in rige huzen boud. Doe seach heit by joun deselde ljochten, en nou wienen se der yndied.","l":"Fries"},{"n":12251,"r":"CJ001003","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Parents heard hammers knocking at night, but there was nothing to be seen. The next morning, before the cows are let into the meadow, a gate is built, with the same knocking as in the night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem en heit ha wol forteld, op in nacht hearden se hiel dúdlik hammers klopjen tsjin planken oan.\nMem sei: Hwat is dat?\nIt kom net botte fier wei, njonken 'e doar. Heit gong der út om to sjen, mar hy koe neat gewaer wurde.\nDe oare moarns woarden yn it kampke lân njonken ús kij litten. Mar earst woarde der in hekke yn elkoar timmere. Doe hearden se krekt itselde klopjen fan 'e hammer dat se dy nachts ek heard hienen. It wie op 'e Boppetike, tichte by de Leijen. Men neamt dat de voorklank.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12264,"r":"CJ001016","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Before the tramline is built, people hear the sound of the tram.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foardat de tram der wie, hearden se in gebolder. Dat wie de 'voorklank' fan 'e tram. 'Voorklank' is noait fan 'e wereld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12267,"r":"CJ001103","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Years in advance a man says that soldiers will march along a road that is being built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn omke wenne op 'e Dunen yn Harkema, yn 'e buert fan Abe Nauta. Doe't se de betonwei troch Harkema leinen sei er: dat dogge se foar de soldaten. Hwant hy hie dúdlik sjoen, dat der Dútske soldaten oer de wei marchearden en dat der ek soldaten oer de Dunen kamen. Dat wie yn 1935. 5 jier letter hie men de sitewaesje sa't hy dy sjoen hie. Hy seach wol faker dingen fan tofoaren, dy't leter gebeurden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12279,"r":"CJ001115","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A dirty stork means bad weather, a clean stork means fine weather.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de oaijefaer smoarch wie bitsjutte dat, dat der min waer op komst wie. Wied er skjin, dan kom der moai waer.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12297,"r":"CJ001210","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears an enormous noise in the cowshed, but there is nothing to be seen. The same sound is heard when the cows are in the shed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit hat yn Goaijingahuzen yn 'e ûngetiid west. Op in kear gong it der op 'e stâl hiel bot oan wei. Mar der wie neat. Letter, doe't de kij op stâl kommen, wie 't selde lûd der wer. Dat hat foartsjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12307,"r":"CJ001304","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Though no one can be seen, banging is heard on the front door, which is never used. The narrator says it means something. Her [family member] falls ill; nine days later the same banging is heard on the front door. It is the doctor.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear sieten wy allegear yn 'e keamer. It wie op in moarntiid. It wie o sok kâld waer en der wie net in minske bûten to sjen. Doe rattele der ynienen ien oan 'e foardoar om. Mar der wie net ien. Dy foardoar woarde noait brûkt. Ik sei: Dit hat hwat to bitsjutten. Myn man woarde ridlik gau dêrnei siik en dokter mast komme. Krekt njoggen dagen letter hearden wy krekt itselde gerattel oan 'e foardoar. Doe wie 't de dokter, dy't nei myn man ta soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12363,"r":"CJ001604","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night I heard the sound of hammering near my house. I woke my daughter, but she heard nothing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in nacht koe ik net sliepe, sa bot gong it op in timmerjen. Ik gong der ôf en makke myn dochter wekker. Ik sei: \"Mast ris hearre fanke, sa giet it op in timmerjen. Der komt grif in nij hûs achter op 'e tún.\" Mar myn dochter hearde der neat fan. Mar koarte tiid dêrnei woarde der in nij hûs op 'e tún delset.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12365,"r":"CJ001606","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Once Feikje comes rushing in and says that soldiers are coming and the war is about to begin. This came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek op in kear kom Feikje der oanfleanen mei de klompen ûnder 'e earm en sy rôp: \"O heden, der komme in hiele bult soldaten oan. It wurdt allegearre oarloch.\" Dat is ek neikom (14-'18).","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12500,"r":"CJ001822","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Fifty years ago a woman saw little lights going on and off along a sand road. Those were the later streetlights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanheit, dat wie Hindrik van der Tuin. Dy seach foar in 50 jier hjir op 'e heide allegear ljochtsjes op- en útgean. 't Wie hjir doe noch in sânwei.\nDy ljochtsjes, dat binne de lettere strjittelampen woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15611,"r":"CJ002505","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman sees bicycle lights on a road in the distance. The lights suddenly come and go. Later these become bicycles.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem seach fier fan to foaren de fytslampen op 'e wei. Mem seach dy ljochtsjes kommen en gean.\nSy wienen samar foarby. Dat wienen letter de fytsen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15621,"r":"CJ002515","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One day there is very heavy thunder and lightning. A fireball comes down and a voice says that Friesland will last the longest, but will fare the worst.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us beppe fortelde - en sy hie it wer fan har beppe - , dat op in dei wjerljochte en tongere it hiel bot. En doe kom der in greate fjûrbol oan 'e loft.\nEn doe hie der in stim west, dy't sei: \"Friesland zal het langst bestaan, maar Friesland zal het zwaarst vergaan.\" (opm. A.A.J.: nei alle gedachten in profesije út it boekje fan Intsje Jans)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15704,"r":"CJ002801","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"No one dares to sleep on a farm, because at night there is a tremendous noise. There is hammering and sawing; every night it seems as if the place is being rebuilt.\nA man refuses to believe it, so he stays there one night. At midnight he hears and sees carpenters climbing the ladders and runs away in fright. Years later the farm really is rebuilt, so it was a premonition.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 't West yn Aldegea stie in boereplaets, dêr doarst net ien sliepe, hwant dêr gong it yn 'e nacht altyd bot oan wei. Dêr reizgen altyd guon om yn 'e stâl en yn 'e skuorre en op 'e souder en dan wie 't in lawaei fan jewelste. Der wenne in man yn Aldegea, dat wie âlde Thomas Elzinga. Dy woe 't net leauwe. It binne praetsjes, sei er. De feint, dy't op dy plaets wenne wist wol better en hy sei tsjin âlde Thomas: dan matte jo hjir mar ris in nacht komme. De feint slepte yn in bêdsté yn 't bûthús en dêr gong âlde Thomas ek lizzen. Mar doe't it tolve ûre woarde, woarde der in timmerkiste op 'e koesouder set, der kom allegear folk oan, dat gong by de leiders op, der woarde mei ark omsmiten, it wie in op en delrinnen en it gong op in slaen en klossen. It wie ien stik allegear lawaei. De âld man woarde deabinaud. It swit roan him by alles del. Sa is er dêr weirekke.\nLetter is dy plaets fortimmere, dat it sil wol foartsjirmerij west ha.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15802,"r":"CJ003501","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In de Tike, clear sounds of carpentry are heard in a house one Sunday while the man of the house is not at home. Later the house is renovated; so it was a vision.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Tike hearden wy op in snein tige dúdlik guon timmerjen yn in âld hûs, dat tsjin uzes oer stie. Mar soks wie ûnmooglik, hwant de man, dy't yn dat hûs wenne, roan op 'e wei om.\nMar in skoftsje letter woarde datselde hûs fortimmere. It hat dus foartsjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15803,"r":"CJ003502","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Two people living on the Hege Wei hear hammering. They think someone is hammering outside but can see nothing. Later a new building is put up opposite their house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik en myn suster wennen hjir al oan 'e Hege Wei, doe stie it nije hûs hjir tsjinoer noch net.\nWylst ik en myn suster hjir yn 'e hûs sieten, hearden wy dúdlik dat it hjiroer op in timmerjen gong.\nWy seinen tsjin inoar: \"Der wurdt bûten timmere.\" Mar doe't wy nei dat plak tagongen, wie der neat to sjen. Letter kom de nije plaets dêr to stean, dy't der nou noch stiet.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15804,"r":"CJ003503","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People see little lights by the road from Wierren. Later houses are built there. The cyclists' lamps were the lights the people had seen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy seagen ljochtsjes by de reed fan 'e Wierren lâns. Mar der wenne doe noch net ien. Letter kommen dêr hûzen to stean en doe fytsten der jouns wol us guon lâns mei lantearnen oan 'e fyts. Dat ha dy ljochtsjes west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15877,"r":"CJ003807","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On his way home from his girlfriend's, a man sees a wagon that is taller than normal. Later a car really does come to stand in front of the door. That is the car the man had seen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Letter hat er wer us hwat sjoen, doe kom er ek by my wei. Dat wie noait liker as wie 't in auto of in rydtúch of sa. 't Wie heger as in gewoane wein en 't stie by harren thús foar de doar. Letter ha se syn heit (healwize Gradus) nei Wagenborgen ta brocht. Doe kom der echt in auto foar de doar. Dat hat it grif west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15878,"r":"CJ003808","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When a couple bring planks into the house to build a barn, at night they hear the sound of wooden planks being lifted onto shoulders. Only a week later does this really happen, and the husband and wife hear the same sound as that night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy soenen in nij hok ha fan 'e gemeente. De planken hienen wy al thús. In wike fan tofoaren, op in joun, doe't wy al op bêd leinen, sei 'k tsjin Piter: Hark, sa'n leven is dêr. Hearst it wol? Sy lûke de planken by de souder op. Piter hearde it ek dúdlik. Mar der gebeurde fansels neat.\nMar krekt in wike letter wienen se drok mei it nije hok oan 'e gong. En doe hearden wy dúdlik krekt itselde lûd. Doe woarden der ècht planken by de souder oplutsen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15879,"r":"CJ003809","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone clearly hears hammering. A fortnight later a new house stands on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek hearde ik op in kear dúdlik timmerjen, op in plak flak by ús. In 14 dagen letter setten se dêr in nij hûs del.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15880,"r":"CJ003810","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Edzers Griet says that a new house will be built across the road; she has already heard the hammering. Later a new house is built there, which Sibe and Gearte move into.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Edzers Griet (^) sei op in kear tsjin my: Hjir foar my oer komt in nij hûs to stean. Hjir oer de wei. Ik ha it timmerfolk al op 'e balken slaen heard. Even letter kom dêr werklik in nij hûs to stean. Sy hie 't goed heard. Sibe en Gearte kommen der to wenjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15891,"r":"CJ003901","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone sees a lamp burning on the heath, where there is nothing but broom. The mother says that a house will be built there. This turns out to be true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr't dit hûs nou stiet wie 't froeger allegear bremerheide, krekt as in eintsje fierder nou nòch. Mar ik ha der al us op in joun hiel dúdlik in hinglampe brânnen sjoen.\nIk sei tsjin mem: Mem, dêr brânt in lampe.\nDan komt dêr in hûs, sei se.\nIn pear jier letter woarde it hûs hjir set en der kom in lampe yn to brânnen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15892,"r":"CJ003902","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People often see flying little lanterns on the heath. Later, bicycles and mopeds come to ride there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha faek fleanende lantearnen oer de heide sjoen. Dat woarden letter de fytsen en de brommers.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15893,"r":"CJ003903","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Feikje Pot saw a tram running across the heath, but it never actually came. She also predicts that war is coming, because she has seen soldiers walking over the Feanster bridge. This really comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Feikje Pot hat hjir yndertiid de tram lâns kommen sjoen. Mar dy is der noait kom.\nSy hat ek foarspeld, dat it oarloch wurde soe, hwant hja hie de soldaten oer de Feanster brêge kommen sjoen. Dat is echt neikom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16059,"r":"CJ004211","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator's mother once saw a light burning. She predicted that a new house would come there, because the light was already burning. Shortly afterwards a new house came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wit noch wol, dat mem op in kear sei: \n\"Sjoch, dêr skynt in ljocht. Dêr komt in nij hûs, hwant it ljocht brânt der al.\" Ridlik gau kòm dêr in nij hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16067,"r":"CJ004301","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator had seen the lamp of their house burning in advance. That spot was otherwise dark.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha de lampe fan ús hûs fan tofoaren brânnen sjoen, doe wie 't hjir oars net as heide.\nIt wie in hinglampe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16068,"r":"CJ004302","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator's family had heard the hammering on the Malmoune in advance (the Malmoune was a square house for four antisocial families; it was demolished a few years ago).\nThey also heard in advance the sawing and throwing of beams for the house that Sjoerd Stienstra came to live in.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha fan tofoaren it timmerjen heard oan 'e Malmoune. (de malmoune wie in fjouwerkant hûs foar fjouwer a-soasiale gesinnen; in pear jier lyn waerd dat hûs ôfbrutsen)\nEk hearden wy fantofoaren it saegjen en 't smiten mei balken fan it hûs dêr't Sjoerd Stienstra, hjir oer de wei, yn kom te wenjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16072,"r":"CJ004306","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When her niece Anne, the daughter of her sister Saek, was at the narrator's home, the magpies chattered loudly in a tree. The narrator said that an ambulance would soon be standing there. Indeed, the ambulance stood on that very spot when Anne broke her arm.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Anne fan ús Saek wie hjir. De eksters skatteren wol sa bot yn 'e hege beam, dat ik koe 't net langer forneare. Ik smiet der nei mei stiennen. Sy skatteren mar troch. Ik sei: Nou stiet hjir gau de sikenwein hjir. En 't is ek gebeurd. Under 't selde plak dêr't dy eksters sa skatteren, hat de sikenwein stien, doe't Anne de earm bruts.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16121,"r":"CJ004606","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening the narrator saw lots of lights from her parental home. Her mother then said that a busy road might well come there. Two or three years later that road came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha hjir yn 'e buert yn in âld hûs wenne.\n\"Sjoch,\" sei 'k op in joun tsjin ús mem, \"it binne dêr allegear ljochten.\" \"Ja,\" sei se, \"dêr kin wolris in drokke wei komme.\"\nIn jier twa, trije lettere is dy wei der kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16967,"r":"CJ007302","p":"Sweagerbosk","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At the place where a house was later built, people had earlier seen a light burning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Twizelerheide ha se op in stik lân in ljocht baernen sjoen. Letter bouden se op datselde plak in hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16972,"r":"CJ007307","p":"Sweagerbosk","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wild lanterns are omens of later houses and lights along the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnens biskôgen se froeger as foarboaden fan huzen en ljochten oan 'e wei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17353,"r":"CJ008816","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wild lanterns of the past were the forerunners of the bicycle.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De wylde lantearnen fan froeger haw ik altyd biskôge as de foarboaden fan 'e fytsen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17375,"r":"CJ009001","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator and his wife saw lights near the churchyard in the evening. Later, street lighting came there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sahwat in sechstich jier lyn seagen ik en myn wiif allebeide jouns ljochten by it nije tsjerkhôf. Letter binne dêr strjitlampen kaem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17473,"r":"CJ009402","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"It is summer and twelve men are lying in the sand. It is around half past one at night when they hear the sound of hammers further on. When they go to look, the sound stops. This happens three times. Some three or four years later the new Reformed church would come to stand on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Wie yn 'e simmer en tige waerm. Wy leinen mei in man of tolwe as Westereinders mei in man of tolwe yn in droege sleat yn 't hite sân. 't Wie sahwat ien ûre à healwei twaën yn 'e nacht. It waer wie to moai om yn 'e hûs to gean. Doe hearden we sa'n sawntich meter fan ús ôf forskeidene hammers tagelyk timmerjen. Mar der wie abslút neat to sjen. Wy woenen der mear fan wite en roannen der hinne, mar doe wie der gjin timmerjen mear to hearren. Doe gongen we wer nei 't selde plak ta en krûpten yn 't sân. Doe't wy goed en wol leinen bigong it wer to klikjen mei de hammers. Wy der wer hinne. Mar ek nou wienen de lûden fuort, doe't wy der kommen. Dat gong sa oan trije kear ta. Nei in jier trije, fjouwer kom op datselde plak, dêr't wy it timmerjen hearden, de nije grifformearde tsjerke fan 'e Westerein to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17489,"r":"CJ009418","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone used to see wild lanterns often. When bicycles and cars later made their appearance, people said those lanterns had of course been the lights of the bicycles and cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Mieden seagen wy froeger wol wylde lantearnen. Letter, doe't de fytsen en de auto's kommen, seinen se: Dat ha dy ljochtsjes west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17498,"r":"CJ009506","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone once heard psalm singing in the air. That was the forerunner of the radio.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Douma har heit hearde froeger psalmsjongen yn 'e loft. Dat hat de foarboade west fan 'e radio.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17500,"r":"CJ009508","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When the magpie chatters, something bad is about to happen. When the bird flies against the glass, a death is imminent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de eksters skatterje, dan komt der hwat nijs. Meastal is it gjin moai nijs. As der in fûgel tsjin 't glês oankomt, dan bitsjut dat in sterfgefal.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17580,"r":"CJ010102","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A father-in-law and his family once hear a thud in the house. Outside there is nothing to be seen. But the next day, when a thatcher falls off the roof, they hear exactly the same thud for real.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Skoanheit en dy wennen op 'e Trije Roede. Se sieten in kear yn 'e hûs, doe hearden se ynienen in plof. Doe't se nei bûten ta gongen wie dêr neat to sjen. Mar de oare deis hienen se in dekker by 't hûs. Dy foel fan 't dak ôf en dat joech krekt deselde plof. It hie foartsjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17588,"r":"CJ010110","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The will-o'-the-wisps that used to be seen here were omens of the lamps. People later got much more light.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De wylde lantearnen dy't se hjir froeger seagen wienen de foartekens fan 'e lampen. De minsken krigen letter folle mear ljocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17599,"r":"CJ010207","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Will-o'-the-wisps could often be seen at the Fjouwer Roeden. If you were thinking about them in the dark, you saw them. Hindriks Lol said that will-o'-the-wisps were signs of new houses. And indeed new houses soon appeared.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't wy op 'e Fjouwer Roeden wennen, wienen dêr faek dwaelljochtsjes to sjen. As âlde Hindriks Lol har man fan hûs wie, siet se faek by ús. \"Nou wolle wy joun us oppase, Bouk,\" sei se dan tsjin my, \"dêr dwale hjir altyd ljochtsjes lâns.\"\nWy bleauwen dan yn 't tsjuster sitten om dêr om to tinken. Dan seagen wy se. \"Dêr komme allegearre nije huzen skielk\", sei Lol. \"Tink us om myn sizzen.\"\nSy hat gelyk krigen. Der binne nije huzen kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17650,"r":"CJ010608","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man heard every time at the same spot: \"You will come to live here.\" He did not like that at all, because there was nothing but heath and wilderness at that spot. After five years the man moved to another house, but he still heard every time at that one spot that he would come to live there. He always heard it behind him, never in front of him. After four years he did indeed come to live there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha hjir trije en fyftich jier yn 'e Boelensloane yn dit hûs wenne. Earder wenne ik yn in oar hûs hjirre. Doe stie hjir noch net in hûs. Mar njoggen jier fan to foaren al, as ik nei myn folk ta reizge, - doe wie 't hjir noch allegear heide en wyldernis - krige ik de tynge, dat ik hjir wenje soe. Ik hie wolris sein: \"Ik soe hjir noait wenje wolle.\" Omdat it ien en al wyldernis wie.\nMar doe waerd der ris tsjin my sein: \"Hjir komstû to wenjen.\" Mar ik seach neat. Dat waerd wit hoe faek tsjin my sein, altyd op ditselde plak. Fiif jier lang gong dat sa. Doe forhuze ik nei in oar hûs. \nMar sa faek ik hjir lâns kaem, hearde ik it wer klear: \"Hjir komstû to wenjen.\" Ik hearde 't altyd achter my, noait foar my. Dat hat noch fjouwer jier sa duorre. Doe bin 'k hjir dan ek kaem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17651,"r":"CJ010609","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Once a drunken man is sleeping in the woods. He was woken by the sound of hammering, but he saw nothing at all. Later 'de Huchte' was built on that very spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie froeger hwat in raer man. Ik mocht graech in buorrel. Op in kear lei 'k yn 'e bosk. 'k Hie tofolle hawn en ik slepte. Ik woarde wekker fan timmerjen, krekt op it plak, dêr't ik lei. 't Klonk wit hoe lang troch. Mar der wie neat to sjen. Op datselde plak dêr't ik lei ha se letter \"de Huchte\" set.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17652,"r":"CJ010610","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A family used to see rows of wild lanterns on the Folgersterloane. It looked just like a number of wagons one behind the other. That was later the tram from Drachten to Grins.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn wiif har folk seagen froeger allegear wylde lantearnen op 'e Folgersterloane. 't Wie in rige ljochtsjes achterelkoar. \"Sjochris,\" sei skoanmem, \"sa'n weinen achterelkoar.\" Dat woarde letter de tram fan Drachten nei Grins.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17664,"r":"CJ010703","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A boy often hears hammering at night. Later a house is built on that spot. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer Megiel wennet yn 'e Parken. Se timmerje dêr yn 'e nacht altyd om. Myn broer wol der eins net rjocht oer prate. Mar 't is al faek neikom. Hy hearde 't by harren sels yn 'e hûs, dan wienen se letter oan 't fortimmerjen","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17668,"r":"CJ010707","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the past many wild lanterns were seen. They were omens of the later street lamps.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen wienen hjir froeger in hiel soad. It tsjutte op 'e lettere strjittelampen","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17701,"r":"CJ011004","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A shoemaker always hears sounds of hammering at night near the public school. Later two new houses were built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha in âld omke hawn, dat wie in broer fan ús mem. Hy wie skuonmakker en sprong op krukken en wenne yn in hûs tsjin 'e iepenbiere skoalle oer. Hy sei: \"It timmert hjir achter altyd, hjir gebeurt hwat.\" Hy hearde it nachten oanien. \"Hjir komme huzen\", sei er. Mar der wie noait hwat to sjen. \nHy hat gelyk krigen. Letter kamen dêr twa nije huzen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17720,"r":"CJ011203","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a man hears, close to the bridge, the noise of stones being loaded, hammering and tools being thrown about, and yet there was nothing to be seen. A short time later a construction factory was built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jan Veenstra kom us troch Koatstertille op in nacht ± jier lyn. Doe't er sahwat by de brêge wie, hearde er skean achter him in lawaei fan stienladen en timmerjen en smiten mei ark en doch wie der neat to sjen. Koarte tiid dêrnei ha se dêr de konstruksjefabryk delset.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17721,"r":"CJ011204","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a man hears hammering in his house without seeing anything. He could not understand what it was. Later the house was renovated.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn syn eigen hûs gong it ek op in timmerjen yn 'e nacht, sûnder dat der hwat to sjen wie. Hy koe 't him net bigripe hwat dat wie. Letter woarde it hûs fortimmere.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17725,"r":"CJ011208","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If a mirror falls and breaks into shards, there will be a death in the house or something else bad will happen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de spegel falt en dêr komme diggels, dan komt der in sterfgefal yn 'e hûs of der gebeurt oars hwat slims.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17737,"r":"CJ011220","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the past there were many wild lanterns here. They were the forerunners of bicycles and buses.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen wienen hjir froeger in soad. It wienen de foarboaden fan fytsen en bussen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17750,"r":"CJ011311","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At an empty spot, people often heard hammering in the evening from nine o'clock on. Years later a farm came there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Surhústermieden by de feart wie in plak, dêr gong it nachts faek op in timmerjen. Njoggen ûre jouns dan bigong it. Altyd klunderen se dêr nachts om. Mar der wie dêrom neat as men der hinne gong.\n\"Hjir komt fêst in hûs\", seinen wy tsjin elkoar.\nIt hat noch jierren duorre, doe is dêr in nij spultsje delset woarn, flak by de brêge.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17751,"r":"CJ011312","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Near a canal people once heard hammering, but there was nothing to be seen. Two years later a wooden house was put up there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie yn 1888 en 't gebeurde op it Blaufallaet. Doe wie dêr noch net it greate kanael, mar noch in gewoane feart. Myn mem wenne dêr. Sy is greatbrocht woarn by in âldomke fan my op it Blaufallaet. \nSy wie sawntsjin jier, doe stie se mei har omke op in joun bûtendoar. Oan 'e oare kant de feart gong it drok op in klunderjen. Mar der wie neat to sjen. \nMem sei: \"Dêr sil op in duer wol in hûs komme.\" Twa jier letter, yn 1890, woarde dêr in houten hûs delset. Greate Marten (Kalsbeek) kom der yn to wenjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18127,"r":"CJ011601","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Two men hear sounds of hammering at night. At first they think a coffin is being made for an unexpected death, but when they go to look, the sound stops. When they try to walk away, they hear the hammering again. Later a house was pulled down on that spot and a new house built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit (Tseard Veenstra; byneamd Tseard Kuorke) en syn buorman Theunis Veenstra wennen yn Boarnburgum.\nOp in nacht let wienen se oan 't murdzjen. Doe kommen se by in plak, dêr gong it drok op in timmerjen. Dêr wenne in timmerman.\n\"Hark,\" sei heit tsjin Theunis, \"dêr sil noch wol ûnforwacht ien stoarn wêze, dat se dêr in deakiste meitsje sa let yn 'e nacht.\" Mar doe't se der oan ta wienen, wie der neat mear to hearren en alles wie tsjuster.\nSy tochten: \"Nou sille de lju dêr wol op bêd lizze.\" Mar doe't se it hûs in eintsje foarby wienen, bigong it wer. Doe gongen heit en dy werom. Sy wienen nijsgjirrich woarn. Mar doe't se oan 't hûs ta wienen, wie alles wer tsjuster en stil. \nIn tiidsje letter kom it hûs der ôf. Der kom in nij hûs foar yn 't plak.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18128,"r":"CJ011602","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A married couple has a small plot of land in front of the house. The neighbours always see a little light burning there in the evening. When a child of the couple marries, the father builds a small house on that very spot. The lamp that burns there from then on is the same lamp the neighbours saw back then.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn ex-skoanâlden wennen yn Drachtster Kompenije. Hja hienen in kampke lân foar hûs lizzen. De buorlju dêr omhinne seagen op dat kampke lân alle jounen in ljocht brânnen. De âlde minsken seagen it sels ek. As se der by kommen, wie 't ljocht út. Doe is ien fan 'e bern troud en doe boude de âld man dêr in arbeidershúske op dat kampke lân foar de jonge lju. Doe't dy dêr yn kommen to wenjen, wie 't selde ljochtsje dêr to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18141,"r":"CJ011802","p":"Gerkesklooster","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"An old man, who is called a prophet, hears the sound of hammering at night. He also hears a voice calling 'make it strong, for it is for the devil'. Later the Reformed church came to stand on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tusken Surhuzum en Stiensgea stiet de grifformearde tsjerke. Der wenne yn Stiensgea in âld man, dat wie in profeet. Hy profetearre wol soms. Hy kaem us op in nacht achter de bosk lâns. Doe stie de tsjerke der noch net. Doe hearde hy op dat plak timmerjen, hoewol der neat to sjen wie. En der wie in stem dy't sei: \"It mat sterk, hwant it is foar de duvel.\"\nOp datselde plak ha se de tsjerke delset.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18142,"r":"CJ011803","p":"Gerkesklooster","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator says that houses are often later built at places where people hear sounds of hammering.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Se ha my wit hoe faek forteld dat se op plakken (yn Stiensgea en omkriten) fan to foaren timmerjen hearden. Dêr kamen dan letter huzen to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18148,"r":"CJ011809","p":"Gerkesklooster","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone sees a little lamp floating in the air at night. Later a factory was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik seach us op in kear in lampke hingjen yn 'e loft boppe Koatstertille. 't Wie yn 'e nacht. Letter is der op dat plak in great fabryk kom","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18149,"r":"CJ011810","p":"Gerkesklooster","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People often see a little light floating at a certain place. Later a new house was built on that spot. Such a floating light is a wilde lantaarn (wild lantern).","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Achter de plaets fan Jehannes Atsma op 't Surhústerfean stie froeger in âld plaets, in pear stikken lân del. \nDeselden dy't dêr lâns gongen, dy seagen dêr alle moarnen en jounen in ljochtsje, dwarsoer nei Boelensloane ta. Doe seinen se: \"Dêr komt in nij hûs.\" In skoftsje letter is der in nije plaets kom, in lyts eintsje fan 'e wei ôf, dêr't nou dan Atsma wennet. Wy neamden sa'n ljochtsje: in wylde lantearne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18150,"r":"CJ011811","p":"Gerkesklooster","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People see a little lamp floating above the canal. Later modern electric street lighting was installed on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha wenne achter de Bosk yn Stiensgea. Doe seach ik in kear in lampe boven it kanael (nou Prinses Margrietkanaal). Letter kamen der op dat plak elektryske lampen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18179,"r":"CJ012001","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a place where the sound of carpentry used to be heard now and then, houses were later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn Broek haw ik yn myn jonge tiid nou en dan wolris op plakken timmerjen heard, sûnder dat der hwat to sjen wy as ik der by kaem. Letter kamen dêr dan huzen to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18180,"r":"CJ012002","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a place where the sound of carpentry could sometimes be heard in the past, new farms were later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek fan de nije spullen yn 't Bûtenfjild hearde ik fan tofoaren it timmerjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18181,"r":"CJ012003","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone saw a lantern for just a moment late one evening. When the same thing happened two weeks later, a baby was just being born.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen froeger in lyts eintsje fan 'e Singel ôf. \nIk kaem us let op 'e joun thús. Doe kaem der in lantearne by ús de reed del. En dy waerd ek samar wer wei. In fjirtsjin dagen letter wie dêr krekt deselde lantearne. Doe kamen se om mem to heljen, hwant der wie ergens in lytsen geboaren. Us mem bakere wol.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18191,"r":"CJ012013","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a place where wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns) were often seen in the past, farms were later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op it Bûtenfjild ha de lju faek wylde lantearnen sjoen. Letter is dêr de wei kommen mei de pleatsen der oan. Dy pleatsen dat ha de lantearnen west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18193,"r":"CJ012015","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On the spot where a church now stands, organ music used to be heard often.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr't nou de kristlik-grifformearde tsjerke stiet, hearden se froeger faek oargelspyljen. Dat is neikaem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18205,"r":"CJ012102","p":"Rinsumageast","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man could not go any further along a road because a large wave was washing over it. According to the man this was an omen of a flood, but that has not happened yet.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ien fan 'e Feddema's fortelde, hy hie us nei de Broek ta sild en doe hie der ynienen in hiele greate baer (= golf) oer de wei west. Doe koed er net fierder. Dit sloech neffens him op in lettere oerstroming dy't komme soe. 't Wie foartsjirmerij. Mar dy oerstroming hat der noch net west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18212,"r":"CJ012109","p":"Rinsumageast","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns) that were sometimes seen in the past were omens of the later bicycle lights and houses.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnens seagen se hjir froeger in hiel soad. Letter kommen de fytsen. Dy wylde lantearnens, seinen se hienen de foarboaden fan 'e fytsljochten west. \nSe seagen ek wol us by joun in ljochtsje op in bipaeld plak. Op sa'n plak kom dan letter in hûs to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19326,"r":"CJ012317","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Magpies are telegrams. They bring people news of misfortune.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Eksters binne tillegrammen. Sy bringe tidingen fan ûngelok by de minsken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19327,"r":"CJ012401","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a building site the sound of hammering could often be heard in the evening, while nothing could be seen. It was the hammering of the following day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn it houtstek fan Dalstra yn 'e Westerein ha guon timmerjen heard, wol forskeidene kearen tusken njoggen en tolwe ûre op 'e joun, as se dêr lâns kamen. Mar as se der hinne gongen wie der neat to sjen en wie alles yn 'e rêst. It wie it timmerjen fan 'e oare deis, dat se hearden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19340,"r":"CJ012414","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The future can be foretold not only by laying out cards, but also by looking at coffee grounds in a cup. Someone who can do this is called a kopjeskijker (cup reader).","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de lju hjir de takomst wite woenen, gongen se nei âlde Klare ta. Dy koe kaertlizze. Mar hjir wenne ek in âld-wyfke, dy lei de takomst út mei kofjedik yn 't kopke. Dat skodde se dan hinne en wer. It wie in kopkekykster.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19345,"r":"CJ012504","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man often heard flax being broken in the flax shed before anyone was at work there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit hat in protte braekt. It braekhok siet oan 't hûs fêst. It gebeurde faek dan hearde heit fan to foaren de brake al gean, sûnder dat der ien yn 't braekhok tahâldde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19370,"r":"CJ012602","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once went to a fortune teller who read cards. After shuffling three times, she laid out three cards. At the first she said: \"You do not value this.\" At the second: \"You do not expect this.\" And at the third: \"This will certainly happen.\"","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha ek wol by Thomas Clare west. Dy wenne yn Feansterheide. Dat wie dêr in rûge húshâlding. Dêr wienen allegear greate jonges yn 'e hûs.\nClare skodde de kaerten trije kear troch. Dan lei se der trije kaerten by wei, dy lei se omkeard op 'e tafel.\nSy kearde doe earst de earste om en sei: \"Dit acht je niet.\" Doe kearde se de twadde om en sei: \"Dit verwacht je niet.\" Doe kearde se de trêdde kaert om en sei: \"Dat komt je wis.\" Doe lei se my dy lêste kaert út.\nIk wie eins mar hwat bang foar Clare.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19371,"r":"CJ012603","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At the beginning of the Second World War a man had his palm read. The woman predicted that he would soon make a long journey. Shortly afterwards the Germans sent him to the south of France.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 't bigjin fan 'e lêste oarloch haw ik yn Oud-Beierland west. Dêr wie 't merke. Doe liet ik my de takomst sizze troch in frommeske. Dy lies it út myn hân. Hja sei, ik soe yn 't koart in hiele fiere reis meitsje.\nIk wenne doe yn Stiensgea. Dêr moesten fan 'e Poepen in tritich gesinnen fan nei Dútslân of nei Frankryk ta. Dêr wie ik ek by. Ik hie wol yn Dútslân wurke, dat ik tocht: \"Lit my mar nei Frankryk gean.\"\nSa bin ik yn Súd-Frankryk tolânne kom. It minske hie dus wol gelyk krigen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19375,"r":"CJ012607","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If the ground coffee in the drawer of the coffee grinder lies unevenly mixed, a hard winter is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de mealde kofje yn 't bakje fan 'e kofjemoune ûnegael trochinoar leit, komt der hurde wyn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19376,"r":"CJ012608","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If the flame in the stove is blue, frost is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de flam yn 'e kachel in blauwe kleur hat, komt der froast.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19394,"r":"CJ012712","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a wedding a card reader predicts to one of the guests that he will court a black-haired woman and that to reach her he will have to cross the same water twice. Years later he courted a woman with jet-black hair, and to reach her he had to cross the same water twice by a little bridge.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Feankleaster wie us in brulloft. Tichteby wenne ien dy koe kaertlizze. Dy kom dêr de nachts om to kaertlizzen. Myn broer Eabe wie der ek. Dy wenne by de boer op Lytsewâld achter in feart.\nDy kaertlizter sei, Eabe soe forkearing ha mei in hiel swart frommes. Hy moest om by har to kommen, twa kear oer 't selde wetter hinne.\nEabe tocht der letter net wer om, hwat dy kaertlizter sei. Mar jierren letter krige er forkearing mei Tryn. Om by har to kommen moest er twa kear oer in brêge, dy't oer 't selde wetter lei. En sy wie roetswart. Hja wenne by Oebele Vries ûnder Kollum as faem. Dat is syn frou woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19409,"r":"CJ012807","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Some labourers once went to a card reader to ask what would happen with the money their employer refused to pay them. But they had barely set foot over the threshold when the card reader told them to just go home. The money was waiting for them there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en dy kommen us fan in great wurk weom. Doe gongen se yn Nijebrêge oan by Hinke Kaert om de kaert lizze to litten. Hwant de man by hwa't se arbeide hienen woe it putjild net jaen. Dêr wachten se op. En nou woenen se fan Hinke to witen komme, hoe't it rinne soe.\nMar se hienen noch mar krekt de foet oer de drompel, of Hinke sei: \"Nou mannen, ik wyt jim boadskip. Gean mar nei hûs en as jim thúskomme, lizze de sinten foar jim klear.\" En sa hie 't ek west. It jild lei thús.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19410,"r":"CJ012808","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Two friends went to the card reader. The fortune teller told one girl that she would court a brown-eyed stable hand. The other would get a husband who would later get a stiff leg. It all came true exactly like that.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mem en har kammeraedtske Aeltsje kommen fan 'e Grinzer klaei, dêr't se oan 't wurk west hienen. Doe gongen se yn Grins nei in kaertlizter ta. It minske sei tsjin mem: \"Jo krije in feint, dy is nou yn tsjinst by de hynders. En hy hat brune egen.\" Dat kloppe as in bus.\nTsjin Aeltsje sei se: \"Jo sille in man ha, dy krijt letter in stive skonk.\" En dat kom ek út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19423,"r":"CJ012904","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One day the voice of a woman is heard wailing: \"Oh, my dear husband!\" But the woman was not there at all, and nothing was wrong with her husband. A week later, at exactly the same time, the same thing was heard again. Her husband had then broken his foot on the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't wy yn 't oare hûs wennen oan ditselde paed, hearde ik op in kear klear de stem fan Keimpe Wybenga syn frou. Dy wenne oan 'e hurde wei. Sy jammere: \"O, myn leave man! Myn leave man!\" Mar yn werklikheit wie hja der net en der skilde Keimpe neat.\nIn wike neitiid, krekt op deselde ûre wie 't gejammer der wer: \"O myn leave man! Myn leave man!\"\nDoe hie Keimpe op 'e wei syn foet brutsen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19490,"r":"CJ013030","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Four young men once heard the sound of carpentry while nothing could be seen. Not long afterwards there were builders' huts there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik nog jong wie roan ik us mei Diuwe Jelle en Durk - en Willem Mozes de Sânwei del yn 'e Harkema, dat nou de betonwei is, de Wytfeanster kant út. Doe hearden wy alle fjouwer klear dat se dêr oan 't houtendakspikerjen wienen. It timmere dêr hiel ûngelyk.\nMar dêr stie neat, gjin kerl, noait ien spier, fordomd.\nEven letter stienen dêr de boufakhuzen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19458,"r":"CJ0130[30]","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In an area where there were no houses at all, the sound of carpentry was heard one night. Not long afterwards new houses were built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen oan 'e betonwei yn 'e Harkema.\nOp in nacht woarde der tichte by ús hiel bot timmere. It hearde krekt as wienen der wol in man of sawn oan 't wurk. Ik sei: \"Hwat giet it der dêr oan wei.\"\nDer stie net in inkel húske om ús hinne.\nLetter hearden wy neat mear. Mar ridlik gau dêrnei kommen dêr nije huzen to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19494,"r":"CJ013103","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a place where farms were later built, wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns) had been seen before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Beppe hat wol us forteld, yndertiid seagen se oan 'e Haasterwei (gemeente Mearum) allegearre ljochtsjes. 't Wienen wylde lantearnen. Ik ha letter faek oan har wurden tocht. Hwant nou stean dêr wol achtsjin, njoggentsjin buorkerijen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19517,"r":"CJ013201","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One morning people heard glass shattering in the kitchen, but nothing could be seen. In the afternoon a large painting fell upstairs. The glass of the painting and the vases on the mantelpiece broke. It made the same sound they had heard that morning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in moarn hearden wy hwat rinkeljen yn 't keukentsje. It wie krekt as woarden alle glêzen dêr ynslein.\nWy der hinne, mar der wie neat to sjen. Mar de middeis kom der in great skilderij fan boven.\nDer siet in glês foar. Dat wie yn gruzels en de faeskes dy't op 'e skoarstienmantel stienen, kommen mei. Dy wiene ek yn diggels.\n't Wie 't selde lawaei, dat wy de moarns heard hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19518,"r":"CJ013202","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once recognised the footsteps of an acquaintance at the door, but no one was there. Hours later he heard the footsteps again, and this time the acquaintance was indeed at the door.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear hearde ik hiel dúdlik ien stappen, dy't op ús hûs takaem. Ik sei tsjin 't wiif: \"Hearst wol hwa't dêr oankomt? Dat is ús Sibe.\"\n\"Ja,\" sei 't wiif, \"dat is Sibe.\" Hy stapte mei gewelt. Mar der kom net ien by de doar. Der wie ek net ien to sjen.\nMar in ûre letter, dêr wienen deselde stappen wer. De doar woarde iependien en dêr stie Sibe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19519,"r":"CJ013203","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening two men heard the sound of carpentry at a place where nothing could be seen. Not long afterwards a house was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us Sibe en in kammeraet fan him roannen us op it paed, dat nou de betonwei is. 't Wie let yn 'e joun. Doe hearden se dêr op in plak allebeide hyltyd getimmer. Mar der wie neat to sjen.\nIt duorre net lang, doe kom dêr in nij hûs to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19531,"r":"CJ013215","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman often saw little lights at a certain place in the evening. Later street lamps were put up there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De frou fan myn broer Albert seach froeger by joun allegear ljochten oan 'e Nije Wei, omheech yn 'e loft. 't Liken krekt allegearre lampkes. Letter kamen dêr de lantearnen to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19534,"r":"CJ013302","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The sound of carpentry could often be heard at a certain place, but nothing could be seen. Later a farm was built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Fogelsang yn 'e Westerein waerd op in plak algeduerigen timmerjen heard, mar der wie neat to sjen. Letter setten se dêr in boerespultsje del.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19541,"r":"CJ013401","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In Harkema there was a small farmer who brought Christianity to the village. He held his sermons in a little shed. At night people heard hammering at that spot, but nothing could be seen. Not long afterwards a church was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Warmolds wie de man dy't hjir yn 'e Harkema it kristendom brocht hat. It wie in boerke. Hy hâldde earst syn preken yn in hokje. Doe wienen der minsken, dy hearden dêr nachts timmerjen. Mar as se der hinne gongen wie der neat to sjen. Ridlik gau dêrnei ha se der in gebouke achter set. Op dat plak stiet nou de herfoarme tsjerke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19554,"r":"CJ013414","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns) of the past were forerunners of the later street lamps. It was sorcery.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger seagen wy hjir faek wylde lantearnen. Dat wie allegearre foartsjirmerij. Hwant letter kommen dêr de strjitlantearnen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19567,"r":"CJ013507","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The little lights that could be seen in the past were the lamps of the bicycles on which people later went to a quack healer.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Rudolf Jehannes Folkertsma wie in soart fan wûnderdokter. De minsken dy't fyk oan 'e finger hienen, founen altyd baet by him. Hy wenne yn 'e hoeke, dêr't de Lytse Wei op 'e Harkema útkomt. Ek yn rêchkwalen wied er hiel hwat mâns.\nGuon seagen dêr froeger ljochtsjes hinne gean. Doe wenne Rudolf der noch net. Dat wie foartsjirmerij. Letter wienen it de fytsljochten fan 'e fytsen dy't nei him ta gongen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19592,"r":"CJ013901","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Before an extra bed was added to a house, the occupants had already heard sawing and hammering.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy hawwe it froeger wol faek saegjen heard yn 't achterhûs. Wy as jonges gongen der dan mei ús trijen hinne to sjen mei in lantearne. Allinne doarsten wy net. Mar dan wie der noait hwat to sjen. It wie foartsjirmerij. Hwant dêrnei woarde der in bêd by makke. Alle kearen as dat gebeurde, hearden wy fan tofoaren it timmerjen al.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19593,"r":"CJ013902","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Before a chicken coop was built by the house, a man had already heard hammering.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek haw ik it saegjen en timmerjen heard, foardat der by ús in skjippehok boud is. Dat wie ek foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19598,"r":"CJ013906","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the past a little light could be seen on the heath, even though there was not a single house there. Later a house was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Sevenhuzen (Zevenhuizen) wie 't froeger allegearre heide. Se seagen dêr jouns in ljochtsje brânnen op 'e heide, hoewol der net in inkel hûs stie. Letter is dêr in hûs delset.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19599,"r":"CJ013907","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns) that people used to see often were omens of the later bicycles.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen woarden hjir froeger folle sjoen. Dat binne letter de fytsen woarn. 't Wie foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19617,"r":"CJ014101","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening a young man heard someone say 'halt' three times in front of his house, but no one could be seen. His mother predicted that war would break out within half a year. Three weeks later three German troops halted in front of the house one after another.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik leefde mei ús mem yn 'e Surhuzumermieden. Elke wike gong ik in kear nei de grifformearde manljusforiening ta. Dan kom ik jouns sahwat om kertier foar tsienen thús. Mem hie dan de kofje ré. Op in kear - dat wie yn 1940 - sieten wy krekt oan 'e kofje, doe hearde ik klear in stem.\n\"Halt!\" sei der ien. Ik dronk de kofje op en mem geat wer yn. In skoft letter hearde ik wer \"Halt!\". Noch us tsien minuten letter klonk der wer \"Halt!\" Dat wie de trêdde kear.\nIk sei tsjin mem: \"Ik wol us bûten sjen. Der matte guon stean.\"\nMem sei: \"Né, jonge, dû sjochst neat. Mar binnen it jier, of miskien ek wol binnen it healjier, dan is it hjir oarloch.\"\n't Wie helder waer. Ik gong der út, mar der wie neat to sjen.\nIk sei sa: \"It sille wol merakels wêze.\"\nMar trije wiken letter, doe wienen de Poepen hjir. Sy hienen de keukenwagen by har. Sy kommen fan Doezum ôf en roannen foar ús hûs lâns.\nIk stie foar hûs, ik woe wite of it ek neikom hwat wy heard hienen.\nFlak foar ús glêzen sei de overste: \"Halt!\" Doe stie dêr in leger fan sa'n tritich minsken.\nIk frege de overste of der hwat defekt wie.\n\"Nein, nein,\" sei er, \"alles gut.\"\nDoe sei er: \"Sind die Kühe von dir?\" Hwant hy seach fé yn 't lân rinnen. \"Ich will Milch kaufen,\" sei er.\nIk sei: \"Nein, ich habe kein Milch.\"\nDoe roannen dy tritich man fierder.\nIn twintich minuten letter kom der wer sa'n ploech oan. Dy bleauwen ek flak foar de glêzen stean. \"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19628,"r":"CJ014202","p":"Feanwâldsterwâl","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hammering at night means that busy times are coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e helling op 'e Wâl hearden se yn 'e nacht faek getimmer. Dat wie altyd fan to foaren as der wer drokte op til wie. 't Wie de foarboade.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19664,"r":"CJ014311","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns) are forerunners of paved roads, bicycles, cars and stations.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As men wylde lantearnen sjocht, dan komt der hwat to dwaen. Dan sil der boud wurde.\nDoe't de Wedze noch modder wie, tilde it dêr fan 'e wylde lantearnens. Dat binne ljochte fûgels.\nDan komt der fan alles.\nDer is èk fan alles kom: Hurde wei, fytsen auto's, in stasjon.\nFoardat dat der allegear wie gong it dêr ôfgryslik oan wei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19677,"r":"CJ014504","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People sometimes heard someone approaching or the door latch moving. Yet there was no one to be seen. Later the person they had heard earlier always did arrive.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By ús op 'e Noarder Dwarsfeart gebeurde it wol dat wy dúdlik ien oankommen hearden, wer letter gong de klink fan 'e doar. As wy der hinne gongen om to sjen hwa't der wie, wie der net ien by de doar. Mar in skoftsje letter kom dyselde wol degelik. Dan hearden wy de selde fuotstappen en dan gong de klink fan 'e doar. Dat wie dan de foarboade west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19716,"r":"CJ014805","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man often sees little lights, wilde lantaarnen (wild lanterns), floating. He thinks they were the omens of modern bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hindrik Houwink wenne op 'e Lânsbuorren yn Sumar.\nHy sei: \"Doe't de fytsen der noch net wienen, seach ik de ljochtsjes fan 'e lampen al. 't Wienen wylde lantearnens.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20372,"r":"CJ018701","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A boy hears hammering at night. Shortly afterwards a new chicken coop is built. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jierren lyn gebeurde it dat ien fan ús jonges de hiele nacht timmerjen hearde. Hy lei op bêd en bleau der wekker troch. Hy wie sahwat in twintich jier âld. Hy hat der hinne west to sjen, hwant it lûd kom flak njonken 't hûs wei. Mar der wie neat to sjen.\nHy fortelde 't ús de oare deis, hwant de jonge siet der fol fan.\nMar wy laken der om. Skytmerakels, seinen we.\nMar in setsje dêrnei woarde der in great hinnehok op ús hiem delset. Dat hie de jonge heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20373,"r":"CJ018702","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A group of boys were waiting for a man with a wheelbarrow. When they heard the sound of a wheelbarrow, they thought he was coming. But when they went to look, there was nothing to be seen: the man would only actually appear an hour later. The sound of the wheelbarrow was a forerunner.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik as jonge noch by ús yn 'e hûs wenne, gebeurde 't wol, dat Marten-om heit syn kroade helle to brûken.\nOp in kear wie dat wer it gefal.\nDoe't wy de middeis by elkoar sieten yn 'e hûs, seinen we: \"Hark, dêr komt Marten-om wer mei de kroade oan.\"\nWy hienen balstiennen achterhûs en it wie skoan to hearren dat dêr in kroade oer riden waerd.\nMar der wie net in Martenom en gjin kroade.\nWol in ûre letter, dêr kom Marten-om earst oan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20396,"r":"CJ018806","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot people often see two little lights floating in the evening. Later two new houses are built on that spot. The will-o'-the-wisps were an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By de polderdyk ha guon dúdlik dêr twa ljochten sjoen jouns. Letter waerden dêr twa huzen delset.\nAntsje Kak en Bearn Dekker kamen dêr to wenjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20400,"r":"CJ018810","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot people often see little lights floating. Later a new house is built there. The will-o'-the-wisps were an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't it hûs fan Bouke Sjonger der noch net stie, ha se op dat plak fantofoaren ljochtsjes sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20401,"r":"CJ018811","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot people often hear hammering. Later a new house is built there. The hammering was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op it plak dêr't nou Koos Landheer syn hûs stiet, hearden se fantofoaren hyltyd timmerjen.\nKoarte tiid dêrnei waerd it hûs dêr delset.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20666,"r":"CJ020708","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman saw things in advance. She said there would be wagons without horses and that all sorts of things would travel through the air, flying just like birds. Those were the later cars and aeroplanes.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Tsjerke Iebel seach de dingen foarút. Sy sei: \"Dêr ride weinen sûnder hynders der foar en der boldert fan alles yn 'e loft om en dat fljocht krekt as de fûgels. Dat ha de auto's en de fleantugen west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20667,"r":"CJ020709","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In places where hammering was heard, a new house was later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha wol gauris timmerjen heard op plakken, dêr't letter in nij hûs kom. Doe wie'k noch tige jong. Dat is wol sa'n sechstich, sauntich jier lyn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20842,"r":"CJ021806","p":"Aldeboarn","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One magpie brings bad luck, two magpies mean visitors.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":27411,"r":"CJ065405","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once heard the sound of hammering. Not long after, a new house was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By ljochtmoannewaer hearde ik op in joun hiel dúdlik dat guon mei latten oan 't fêstslaen wienen en doe sei de iene tsjin 'e oare: \"In bytsje heger.\"\nMar der wie neat, abslút neat.\nIk sei tsjin 't wiif: \"Dêr komt in nij hûs, sa en sa.\"\nIt duorre net lang of sy setten dêr in hûs del.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27412,"r":"CJ065406","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Early one morning a carpenter saw a new house being built. But in reality there was nothing there. Later a new house did go up on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In timmerman út 'e Harkema gong op in moarn ier en bitiid nei syn wurk op Readskuorre. Underweis seach er hoe't se dêr mei in hûs oan 't útsetten wienen.\nMar doe't hy der op ta roan en der by kom, wie der neat. Mar op datselde plak setten se letter in hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33018,"r":"CJ085802","p":"Harlingen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Sometimes people heard knocking, but when they opened the door, there was no one there. Later someone would come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Gebeurde wol dat der kloppe woarde by de minsken en as se der dan hinne gongen, wie der neat. Letter wìe dyselde der dan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":50182,"r":"GENDT156","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The call of an owl, the howling of a dog, or a magpie walking to the right of someone means misfortune.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Zi zèje vroeger wel ’s, as ’n uul ruup, ’n hond jank en ’n ekster over de weg lup, ista ’n slech teike. Teminste, as de ekster rechs van ou trippel. Da’s nie goed. Want ze zegge: “Hoe rechter, hoe slechter”.\nVgl. Bandopname III, verhaal 3.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":50192,"r":"GENDT168","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man visits a fortune teller who shows him a photo of his future wife and has him draw seven cards, from which she concludes that he will later work with sharp objects. Both come true.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Toe ik bé’j Veenhuus in Huse as smidsknechje diende, was er nog ’n knech bé’j die smid. Op ’n keer sproke we samen af um es nor ’n woarzegster in Oarem te goan. ’t Was alleen mar uut spitsboeveré’j. Toe we bé’j de vrouw kwame, liet ze mien ers ’n foto zien. En ze zèj: “Hier, die foto is van een meisje, waar je later mee zult trouwen”. Ik keek er heel goed nor. Lotter kreeg ik verkering. En ik zag drek al bé’j de erste kennismaking, dat ’t de eigeste dern was, die ’k bé’j de woarzegster opte foto had gezien. En ik bun er mè getrouwd en gelukkig mè gewes. ’t Was dus wel uutgekomme. Dornoa noom de vrouw ’n stel koarte. Ik mos er zeuve uuttrekke. Ik deej ’t. En de vrouw noom ze over. Toe gieng ze d’r mè de haand over hin en zèj: “Ge zul lotter veul omgoan mè schèrpe voorwerpe”. En ok da is uutgekomme. Want nie zo bar lang dornoa bun ik slachter geworre. En toe mos ik natuurlijk veul umgoan mè schèrpe messe.\nVgl. Bandopname III, verhaal 15.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":209078,"r":"LINSSEN010409","p":"Roosteren","v":"L.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A magpie near the house is an omen of news.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Voortekens: Eksters in de nabijheid van huizen was een voorteken van nieuws."},{"n":43700,"r":"WEV012002","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A gravedigger in a red shirt is seen; a wagon is heard arriving at the house and leaving again; men carrying a coffin are seen; a funeral is seen with acquaintances in the procession, the people as small as matchsticks.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien voar kun verschaiden lu, dei kwaod zain konnen. \nDat wazzen nait altied olle mensn, heur. \nZo was dr n vent, dei teegn zien oal heer zee: \"Ik zai ain grafgroaver op t kerkhof mit n rode hemdrok aan.\"\nZien voader zee: \"Bist gek jong, moakst die zulf wat wies.\"\nMoar t kwam wel uut heur. \nOp n oavend heurt deizulfde jong - zai zitn biemekoar in huus - ain woagn aankomen. Dei ridt bie heur teegn t huus hen en den heurt hai hom weer vot goan. Zai goat noar boetn om es te kiekn, moar dr was niks te zain. \nNaitlaank noa tied staarft er n kind in dat huus. \nEn den komp dei woagn ja; hetzulfde geluud wordt heurd en hai moakt ook dezulfde draaiende beweegn. \nVerder zee hai es teegn gounend: \"Ik zai n poar manlu mit n kiste over n vonder goan. Aine van de kerels strompelt doar bie. Hai stait wel weer op en den goan ze weer wieder.\" \nVolgens mien voader mout et aal zo uut komen weezn.\nt Kwam ook veur, dat hai n begravvenis zag. \nDe mensn, dei achter de woagn luipn, kon hai ook.\n t Vrumde was, dat dei mensn ongeveer zo groot wazzen as lucifers-stokkies. (Dit laatste hoorde ik voor de eerste keer, wat betreft die lijkstaties: F.W.)","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43719,"r":"WEV012107","p":"Weite","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man makes people unable to move by holding their wrist. Looking along his stick he sees white caps in the peat bog; later women wearing white caps work there.","i":"F.W.","o":"Achter in t veen bie Veelerveen woonde vrouger oal Oabram. \nt Was n wat zunderlieke kerel; waarkn dee hai nooit en zien vrouw mos heide-bezzems binnen en door mit bie de weg leurn. \nAs ie nou biehom in de hudde kwammen den kon e moar zo zegn: \"Ie bint dr non toch; blieve man n zetng bie mie zitn.\"\nDen pakde hai joe bie de polse, huil dei eevn vaaste en den kon gain mens meer weg koomn. Ie zatn gewoon vast op de stoule; net zo laank tot hai joe weer lös muik. Kwammen doorom ook nait veul.\n\nOok zee e wel es tegen gounend: \"Kiek es bie mien stok langs, dan zait ie aal man widde mutsn.\"\nHai huil zien stok den recht veuruut in de richtn van t veen. De maiste mensn zaggen netuurlijk niks, moar dei wat toch wel. \nd Oal Oabram het dat toch waitn; toun dr loater in t veen waarkt wur, wazzen doar verschaiden vroulu bie mit widde mutsn op.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43723,"r":"WEV012201","p":"Wessinghuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man sees things in advance: someone will one day own four horses, a funeral going to a churchyard that is laid out later, the colour of the horse before the hearse, wagons without horses.","i":"F.W.","o":"Was es n keer n zekere Vos achter de Holte, dai veuroet zain kön; spuik kiekn nuimen ze dat. \nWur voak over hum verteld, man ain ding muik ik zulm mit. \nIk stön n moal op de dele; ik keek noar de peern en dou kwam d oale dr aan. \n\"Kiek\", zee hai, \"ie hebt doar vaier peern bie de krubbe stoan en dat heb ik vieftig joar leden al zain.\"\n Mien boerderij stön dr dou nog nich en toch zag dai olle Vos dat er vaier peern bie de bak stönnen te hoaver vreetn.\n\nZo zag dai olle ook begravvenisn. \nDoar kwammen wol es wonderlieke dingen bie veur, dai hai nich verkloarn kön, man dai loater toch oetkwammen. \nZo zag hai n liekstoatie deur t dörp goan, man nich noar t kerkhof tou. \"Blikgat\", dochde, \"woor goat ze toch wol mit dat liek hen?\" \nLoater kwam dat aal goud, wör ja n nei kerkhof aanlegd boetn t dörp. \nDe eerste dai door begroavn wur, har de oale Vos zain.\n\nOp n andere moal zag e n liekwoagn mit n wit peerd dr veur. \nDatgebeurde ja nooit. Woorum zo 'n geval zuk veurdee, wus hai nich. Dat mus noa tied altied bliekn. \nNon ja, was weer aine dood; de woagn mit et zwaarde peerd stèèt kloar, man dan wordt dat peerd steetsk. (onwillig).\nDat kwam zo: t was n pluusterig weer (wind en regen).\nDe olle vroulu kwammen mit de reegn-klaier aan. \"Reegn-klaier\" wazn grode zwaarde umsloagn over de schollers; as t weide, wappern ze nogal wat. Door schrok dat peerd van en was nich van t stee te kriegn. \nZod","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43799,"r":"WEV012208","p":"Wessinghuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A sound that is heard while nothing can be seen is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the collapse of the back wall of a stable.","i":"F.W.","o":"Hier nog wat andere dingn, dai ik mie herinner oet mien jeugd.\n\nNich wied van ons of heurden n poar olle mensn s oavends voak gestommel achter op dele. t Was net of dr wat kroakte en wat noar doale vuil. Zai dan hen te kiekn, man nooit wat te zain. \nWol begreepn ze al dat er n keer wat gebeurn zol, dat kön nich anders. t Gebeurde ook.\nn Moal op störmachtige oavend weide de achter mure in. \nEn dou vernammen ze datzulfde geluud. \nNoa tied was mitain ofloopn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43807,"r":"WEV012303","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears a voice saying the brown one must step over. At a funeral the brown horse is told to step over the harness.","i":"F.W.","o":"Stemmen.\nOok heurde mien voader es n moal n stem dei zee: \"Tou broene, dr over.\" n Zet loater heurde deizulfde stem bie n begravvenis. \nt Peerd dat de woagn trekn mos, ston al wat te zeurn en toun wur dr zegd: \"tou broene, dr over.\" 't Daier mos mit de poot over t ainspan stapn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43814,"r":"WEV012304","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Narrator has heard voices indicating that accidents, illness or other harm are to be expected.","i":"F.W.","o":"Stemmen.\nZulf heb ik ook wel stemmen heurd. \nWie zatn es 'n keer biemekoar in huus en toun proatten dr gounend bie ons op stoebe. \nTeminste, zo heurde t; in werklijkhaid was dr niks. Nou hebben zukke stemmen altied n waarschuwende betekenis, meneer. \nHet wordt de mensn aanzegd, dat er iets veurvaln zel; n ongeluk of n zaikte; in elks geval watkwoads. \nZo was 't in dit geval ook. \nOver verloop van tied wur mien bruiertje in huus brocht; hai was op t ies vaaln en har n gat in de kop.  \nLoater ston ik op de sloapkoamer en door heur ik weer stemmen. \nKiek, ie verstoan dr gain woord van; t is meer n gemompel; ondudelk moar geef der acht op, want et het joe wat te zegn. Dizze keer gold et mie zulf; eevn noa tied mos ik opnomen worn in t zaiknhuus weegns n nier-operoatie. \nMoar waitn ie wat et is? Mensn letn zo wainig op; geevn gain acht op zukse dingen en lachen joe uut as ie dr over proatn.\n.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43816,"r":"WEV012305","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A carter hears his two horses talking, saying they will be sold if he keeps drinking, but he ignores the warning, after which he has to sell his wagon and horses.","i":"F.W.","o":"Stemmen.\nWas es nmoal n vouerman, dei nog al wat dronk. Bie elke kroeg mos e eevn aan. Hai har twei peern veur de karre. Dei daier wozzen dat ook al wel en begreepn wel, dat et zo nait deur gaon kon; op n duur zol e gain geld meer hebben en den zoln zai vot moutn. \nOp n keer zeg ain van de peern teegn de ander: \"t Zel wel nait laank meer mit ons duurn.\" \nVouerman denkt: \"Hee, kennen n peerd proatn?\" Hai van de woagn of om te lustern wat of ze zegn. Moar as e bie heur komp, zwiegn ze weer en krigt e niks te heurn. \nVan de waarschuwing het hai zuk niks aantrokn en bleef moar zoepm. Net zo laank, tot et mis gung. \nt Geld roakde op; de woagn mos vot en de peern dr bie.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43917,"r":"WEV012602","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the evening a man hears sounds of work on both sides of the church, but nothing can be seen. Later the rectory on one side is torn down and a new rectory is built on the other side.","i":"F.W.","o":"Old volksgeleuf.\nMien voader luip op n aovend deur t dorp en den heurt hai geklop noast de kerke.\n\"Hee\", dekt e, \"binnen door nog gounend aant waark, ik mout ja es kiekn.\"\nHai dr hen, man, nee, niks te bespeurn.\nEn den heurt hai aan de andere kaande van t kerke gehoamer en gekroak. Moar door is eevn min wat te ontdekn.\n\"Roar geval\", denkt e bie zuk zulms.\nn Poar joar loater wordt hom t haile zoakje dudelk.\nDe pasterie noast de kerke wur ofbrookn en aan de andere zied is n nei-e zet. tGeluud van ofbreekn en timmern was hom op dei oavend al veurzegd.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43920,"r":"WEV012605","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A prediction that a star will appear in front of the moon does not come true. But a diamond shape appears in the sky with a snake in it that crawls out of the diamond and moves eastwards. The narrator believes the snake is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of Hitler coming to power.","i":"F.W.","o":"Old volksgeleuf.\nHet volgende heb ik ook beleefd.\nt Was in 1933.\nOp t waark was dr overdag over proat, dat dr s aovends n steern veur de moane komen zol.\nIk wol dat ja wel es zain en gung op boetn stoan te kiekn.\nNou was dat van dei steern veur de moane moar larie, door kwam niks van uut; moar ik zag hail wat anders.\nIk kiek zo naor de heldere lucht en den zai ik n ruut <> aan de hemel komen.\nIn dei ruut ontstait n slaange; kop, bek en tonge binnen dudelk te onderschaiden.\nEn den komp dr beweegn in t daier.\nDe slaange kropt tou de ruut uut en beweegt zuk in de richtn van t oostn.\nHai was ongeveer zo dik as n aarm en kroop langs de lucht.\nIk dochde: \"Dat is mis; nou komp dra in of ander onhail over de wereld.\"\nIk proatte dr mit andere lu over.\nWas nog aine, dei t ook zain had, moar d andere mensn zeden t nait haardop, moar dochden et wel: \"Hai is gek.\"\nWaitn ie, wat dat bedud het, dei slaange in 1933?\nToun is Hitler aan de macht komen, dat kreeg ik loater in de goatn; doorom bewoog dat ding noar t oostn.\n\nIk zeg den ook voak: “Geef acht, is meer den veul lu mainen.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44091,"r":"WEV013007","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Knives lying crossed over each other predict a quarrel.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik ken ook nog mensn, dei gain messen over mekoar lign loatn duurn; den mou-je op roezie reekn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44362,"r":"WEV013101","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Perceiving events in advance: the clatter of horses, later horses bolt; seeing ships on the heath, where a canal is later dug; seeing a white figure, later a hearse gets stuck in the snow at the place where the ghost was seen.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien oal mens het vrouger et veurgezicht had.\nOp n middag was ze wat aan t dommeln; zai schrikt wakker en door heurt ze wat op de stroade; peregekletter en woagens.\nHet geval wil, dat n zet loater heur aigen peern op de loop goan en toun heurde ze et zulfde geluud weer.\nIk wait ook nog, dat ze es n moal zee: “Ik zai scheepn vaorn over de haide.” Wie zaggen niks en lachden dr wel ais om.\nToch voarn er nou scheepn op datzulfde stee; t nei-knoal lopt dr nou langs.\n\nt Is gebeurd dat ze n spook zag. t Was bie oavend en toun mout ze n widde gedoante zain hebben op de weg.\nDe winter kwam. Wur aine begroavn; lag n dik pak snei-e en de liekwoagn is in de sneibultn vast steekn bleevn. Loopnd binnen ze mit de kiste wieder goan. Moar woor zat de woagn vaste? Op plek woor moetje t spook zain had.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44366,"r":"WEV013102","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Whoever has money in their pocket when first hearing a wagtail or lark sing in spring will never be short of money. The reverse is also true, which is why children are given money in spring.","i":"F.W.","o":"t Volksgeleuf zeg hier: As ie in t veurjoar n bouwmannegie (een kwikstaartje) veur t eerst zingen heurn en ie hebben den geld op zak, den wordt t n goud joar; ie zeln nooit geldgebrek hebben. Omgekeerd is t netuurlijk net zo.\nOns moetje gaf ons ook altied wat buusgeld in t veurjoar.\nVan t laaiwerikje wordt t zulfde verteld.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44393,"r":"WEV013106","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A variegated kale plant among the green ones means a wedding in the family.","i":"F.W.","o":"As dr n bonde mousstronke tussen de gruinen stait, den komp dr bruloft in de femilie. Ook n volksgezegde.\nN.B.: Hier dus eens geen dode, zoals meestal. (F.W.).","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44395,"r":"WEV013301","p":"Weiteveen","v":"Dr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a birth: the midwife hears knocking on the window.","i":"F.W.","o":"Opmerking: Onderstaande verhalen komen uit het veengebied van zuid-oost Drente; het bijgeloof heeft er welig getierd blijkbaar en men is nog niet vrij van. (F.W.)\n\nMien moeder was baker. Dokters wazzen dr ja niet. Meermaaln is het gebeurd, dat ze klopn aan t venster heurde. Dat was n veurbeduudsel, dat er weer gauw n popke op wereld komen zol.\nEn noa n zekere tied kwam dat dan ook uut.\nDan wier er echt klopt aan t zulfde venster.","l":"Drents"},{"n":44467,"r":"WEV013403","p":"Muntendam","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A cat washing itself predicts visitors. A magpie on the windowsill that pecks and screeches is an omen of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wie hebben twei katn en as dei zok wasken, den komt er veziede. \nVanmiddag zag ik ze nog bezig zok of te slikn en zee: “Taande zel nog wel eevn komen.” Moar nou zitn ie dr. Komt altied uut. \nNet as oksters, deiop de vensterbaanke zitn te pikn en te roupn; den mou- je op n dode reekn in de buurt. Ik heb toch zo’n hekel aan dat goud.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43659,"r":"WEV013802","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the building of a church: hearing organ music and the singing of hymns.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurbeduudsels wordt wel es omlacht, moar et bestait inderdoad. Ik ken joe verschilnde gevaln opnuimen.\nMien schoonmouder was es n keer mit de schoapn in t veld.\nZai was stomp allain in de buurt van de Bunermond.\nt Was toun nog allemoal haide in dei streekn.\nOpains heurt zai wat in de lucht.\nZai kikt om zok tou, moar zugt niks. Toch heurt ze dudelk, dat erop n orgel speuld wordt; ook heurt ze n gezang zingen.\nt Haile vers het ze tot de leste regel mit zongen.\nToun was t weer vot.\nEn wat is er gebeurd? In dei buurte is loater n kerke zet.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43657,"r":"WEV013805","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the years when both world wars begin, a man sees little snakes growing through the veins of tree leaves.","i":"F.W.","o":"Kiek, de ain ken meer as d ander. Moar as ie opletn en om joe tou kiekn, ken je ook wel wat ontdekn.\nIn de zömmer van 1914 zatn op de bloarn van de kaarseboom klaine broene slangegies. Nait dr boovn op, moar deur de naarven hen gruid.\nIn 1939 heb ik t zulfde woarnomen bie de bloarn van de baark. \nt Ken touvallig weezn, moar t is wel roar, dat in dei baide joarn de oorlog begonnen is. Dei slangen hebben zeker kwoad bedud. Moar ja, maiste mensn vaalt zoks nait op.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44714,"r":"WEV014004","p":"Zwartemeer","v":"Dr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man sees someone crawl out of the water with a bundle of straw. Later the man falls into the water and is saved when someone throws him bundles of straw.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik liep eens met mijn vader langs het kanaal; daar blijft hij staan en zegt: “Kiek es, doar ligt n kerel in t woater en kropt er mit n stuk stro weer uut.”\nIk kijk, maar zie niks.\n“k Zie niks gien biezunders”, zee ik tegen de oude heer.\n“Ie smerige jong; ik wies joe de plekke aan, woar die man ligt en ie zien niks; k zul joe toch n trap geevn.”\nJa, mijn vader werd nog kwaad ook; maar ikzag nou een keer niks. \nIn huis vertelde ik het aan mijn moeder en die zei, dat vader best iets gezien kon hebben.\nEen paar weken later.\nMijn vader fietst langs het kanaal en komt in het water terecht. Gelukkig is er net een vrouw in de buurt. Ze loopt daar met een kruiwagen met stro. Ze komt op de man af en probeert eerst met wat aan elkaar gevlochten vodden de drenkeling te helpen. Maar dat mislukt.\nDan grijpt ze de bossen stro en gooit die mijn vader toe. \nEn op die manier gelukt het haar hem te redden.\nZo had hij zich zelf zien drijven, zonder dat hij dit wist."},{"n":44722,"r":"WEV014104","p":"Vledderveen","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Fear of a woman who learned witchcraft from her mother. Shaking up potatoes in a pan is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the building of a house.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mevr. N.: “Ken wel weezn, moar ik heb n taande had, woor ik as kind baange veur was; heur moetje kon heksn en zai zol t ook kunnen loater.\nEn mien grootmoe kon veuruutkiekn. t Gebeurde es n moal, dou ze in huus kwam, dat ze zee: “Op dat stee van Van der Heide komt nog n huus te stoan; ik luip dr langs en heurde net, dat de eerappelspot opschud wur. (Men gebruikte toen ouderwetse potten die aan een ketting boven het haardvuur hingen, bij het schudden hoorde men dus het hengsel van de pot rammelen.).\nEn t huus is er komen.”\nNaber: “Ken wel weezn, den is dat touvallig west.\n\nUit zulke gesprekken blijkt, dat sommige mensen sterk aan die oude vertelsels geloven, terwijl anderen de schouders ophalen.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44859,"r":"WEV014203","p":"Barger-Compascuum","v":"Dr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The mother of a pregnant girl abandoned by a young man hopes he breaks his neck. Later a horse bolts, the young man falls from the wagon and breaks his neck. A cross stands where it happened.","i":"F.W.","o":"Oale spookverhoaln ken ik joe wel verteln, temeer omdat wie stomp aan de grens wonen; de bevolking is hier maist haalf duuts en n bult binnen net as ik “heimatlos”. \n\nIk wait van n vent, dei n wicht loopn loatn het \n (ze verwachtte dus een kind van hem). \nDe moetje van t wicht was verschrikkelk lelk en zee teegn hom: \n“Ik hoop, dast nog n keer de nekke brekst.”\nKreeg t niedige wief heur heur zin ook nog.\nDe jong kwam op n dag van t land mit peerd en woagn; peerd komp op de loop en vent vaalt van de woagn of. Hai brekt op stee zien nekke. Op dei ploatse is n kruus hen zet; zo’n kruus betaikent, dat er wat gebeurd is op dei plekke.\nZo zain ie hier vlak bie over de grenze wel n stok of wat stoan.","l":"Drents"},{"n":17754,"r":"CJ011401","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A married couple hears sawing in the house one night. Later the house is completely renovated.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Garsthuzen (Grinslân) hearde ik op in nacht dúdlik saegjen yn 'e hûs. Wy leinen op bêd. Ik sei tsjin myn man: \"Sil ik der us ôf gean om to sjen, hwat dat is?\" Mar hy sei: \"Ei jonge né, stil lizzen bliuwe.\" Dat ik ha der net nei sjoen. Ik wie doe sahwat acht en twintich jier.\nLetter is 't hûs hielendal fortimmere woarn. De namme fan it hûs is 'Kraaibek'. Dat stiet noch op 'e gevel.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18085,"r":"CJ011407","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man in a fairground tent was given a little portrait of a woman he would marry. He did indeed marry her.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn man hat us yn Grins op 'e kermis west, doe wied er noch feint. Doe hat er dêr ek in tinte yn west en doe krige er in portretsje fan 'e frou dêr't er mei trouwe soe. Dat wie ik. Ik hie in greate hoed op. Hoe is soks nou mooglik, soe men sizze.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18087,"r":"CJ011409","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wild lanterns were the forerunners of bicycle lamps.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Burgumerheide seagen de lju wylde lantearnen. Letter seinen se, dat hienen de foarboaden west fan 'e fytslampen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18106,"r":"CJ011428","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One magpie seen: not good.\nTwo magpies seen: joy.\nThree magpies seen: news from afar.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy seinen froeger as bern:\néén ekster gezien: niet best.\ntwee eksters gezien: vreugde.\ndrie eksters gezien: bericht van veraf.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19727,"r":"CJ014904","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man always foresees things, for example impending deaths in the family. Once he also knew that a woman would tear her skirt at a funeral - and this happened too.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Suwâld wenne in man, dy seach de dingen foarút. Hy wist altiten hwannear't der in deaden yn 'e famylje kom. Op in kear sei er tsjin 't wiif: \"Dû matst in feilichheitsspjelde meinimme, hwant ien fan 'e froulju sil har rok opskuorre ('t Wie by in bigraffenis), dy mat by skerpe trie lâns. 't Kom krekt sa út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19782,"r":"CJ015201","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At night a man very clearly hears hammering and other sounds connected with building a house. When he goes to look, there is nothing to be seen. A year later a house has been built on that spot. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit wenne op 'e Sumarreheide. Op in nacht hearde hy hiel dúdlik timmerjen, kroadzjen, mei stiennen smiten, balken forsjouwen en alsahwathinne. Hy tocht: Hwat hat dat to bitsjutten yn 'e nacht? Dat hy gong der ôf om to sjen. Mar der wie neat to sjen en ek neat mear to hearren.\nIt oare jiers woardde der op dat plak in nij hûs delset.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19895,"r":"CJ015605","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People often see wilde lantaarnen (wild lanterns) at a certain spot. Later modern lighting was installed there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It Bûtenfjild, dat wie froeger allegear ûnlân. Dêr seagen se wylde lantearnen boppe. Nacht op nacht waerden dy dêr sjoen. Letter kom dêr in wei mei lantearnen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19902,"r":"CJ015612","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot people often hear hammering. It is an omen: later a new house is built on that spot. Work on this new house was even done on Sunday. People suspect the house will burn down because you are not allowed to work on Sunday. So far it has not happened.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 't sté, dêr't nou de plaets fan Tsjalling Wiersma stiet, ha se fan tofoaren timmerjen heard, foardat de plaets der stie.\nSy ha dêr sneins en deis trochtimmere oan dy pleats. It sizzen is, dat sa'n plaets iens opbrânne mat, omdat der op snein oan timmere is. Mar it is noch net gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19953,"r":"CJ015809","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A clairvoyant woman tells the owner of the pottery shop that one of these days there will be a loud 'rattling'. Some time later a whole lot of earthenware does indeed fall down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Frytsen wie de beppe fan Willem Mulder. Sy hat wenne op it Waltsje yn Eastemar. Hja wie mei de helm geboaren. Op in kear kom se yn 'e pottewinkel fan Rikele Pot. Doe sei se tsjin Rikele: \"Der sil hjir in greate rammeling gebeure.\"\nIn pear dagen letter kom der by Rikele yn 'e winkel in hiel boerd mei diggelguod del.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19955,"r":"CJ015811","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man sometimes sees little lights floating. It is a forerunner of the later, modern lighting.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Pake ried froeger us troch de Harkema. Doe wie dêr fan alles noch neat to sjen.\nDoe't er thús kaem, sei er: \"Nou ha ik raer hwat sjoen! It wie allegearre ljochtsjes yn 'e Harkema!\"\nLetter wie 't dêr allegearre ljocht. Strjitlampen, fytsen en alsamear.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20004,"r":"CJ016212","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When you are about to have an accident, you are always warned by the birds. A man is screeched at three times by magpies before he is hit by a car. He survived.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As men in ûngemak ha sil, wurdt men fantofoaren warskôge troch de fûgels.\nIk haw it sels meimakke. Trije kear fantofoaren skattere der in ekster, doe rekke der ien ûnder 'e auto. Hy is net dearekke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20005,"r":"CJ016213","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If your nose itches, you will get a quarrel or a drink.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":20047,"r":"CJ016507","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"As a little boy a man often saw a little light floating. On the spot where he saw the wilde lantaarn (wild lantern), a new house was later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik in jonge wie, doe wennen wy op 'e hoeke fan 't Kleasterbreed, dêr't nou it monumint stiet. Doe ha 'k dêr flak by ús in ljochtsje sweven sjoen op it plak, dêr't se letter in nij hûs delset ha. Dat hat in wylde lantearne west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20088,"r":"CJ016801","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears hammering at night and a while later the house is actually renovated. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit sei us in kear tsjin ús mem: \"Hwat is 't der hjir fannacht oan wei gong. Hwat ha se by ús yn 'e hûs oan 't timmerjen west.\"\nIt duorrre mar in skoftsje, doe woarde 't hûs forboud. Dat wie yn 'e Houtigehage, flak tsjin it hûs oer, dêr't nou myn suster wennet (yn Boelensloane; de wei is de grins tusken de beide doarpen)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20093,"r":"CJ016806","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wilde lantaarnen (wild lanterns) are forerunners of a house to be built later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger wie der nou en dan wol us in wylde lantearne yn 'e Houtigehage. Dan kom der letter op sa'n plak in hûs to stean. Wylde lantearnen binne foarboaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20244,"r":"CJ018005","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A few young people are looking for peat by moonlight when they suddenly see a little red light floating. The light sometimes disappears, but keeps reappearing and follows the peat gatherers. They become very frightened and run home. There their mother says it was a warning of approaching disaster.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wienen froeger klynpôllen yn 'e Wierren ûnder Aldegea. Dêr baggeren se wol. Beppe hat dêr ek wol baggere. By 't hjerst bleauwen dêr wolris baelders sitten.\nOp in winterdei doe't it tige krap wie, soenen mem en ús buorman dêr us in kear togearre hinne om in sekfol turf. It wie ljochtmoanne waer.\nDoe't se der hast oan ta wienen, kom der in read ljochtsje út 'e reiden wei en dat woarde even letter ek wer wei. Mar in skoftsje letter, doe wie 't der wer. Doe roannen se in oare kant út, mar doe wie it ljochtsje dêr. It wie sa tichteby, dat sy woarden binaud. Mem sei: \"Dit is in warskôging foar ús. Wy meije hjir net hinne. 't Is spûkerij.\"\nDat doe binne se sûnder turf werom kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20260,"r":"CJ018106","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When people in the old days saw wilde lantaarnen (wild lanterns), they knew that something was going to happen at that spot: for example, a new ditch would be dug or a new house built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De minsken seinen froeger wol us: \"Dêr is wer in wylde lantearne. Der sil wer hwat gebeure.\" Dan woarde der in nije sleat groeven of der kom in nij hûs of sahwathinne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20289,"r":"CJ018204","p":"Burum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People often heard hammering at a certain spot. Later a new house was built on that spot. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Moeke fortelde, aan de grote rijksstraatweg stonden weinig huzen. Bij de Kollumerzwaag, waar nu café Wolda staat, daar hadden de mensen de timmerlui al fanteforen gehoord. Se hoorden dat se stenen dwarsdoor sloegn om te metselen. Toen 't huus daar kwam, zeidn se: \"ja, dat zijn de voortekens weest.\"","l":"Fries"},{"n":20302,"r":"CJ018217","p":"Burum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone once foresaw that one of the bridges on the Groningen-Leeuwarden railway would collapse during a festive occasion. Fortunately it has never happened so far.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Een fan 'e bruggen, waar het spoor Groningen-Leeuwarden over heen gaat, sal een keer inzakken bij een feestelijke gelegenheid. Dat het één sien. Mar 't is gelukkig noch nooit gebeurd.","l":"Fries"},{"n":20308,"r":"CJ018303","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A young woman once very clearly sees her mother walking towards her, holding her youngest daughter by the hand. As suddenly as they appeared, they vanish again. The next day the mother and daughter come walking up in exactly the same way as the woman had seen before. It was a vision of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie yn 1910. Ik wie doe noch tige jong, mar ik wie al troud. Ik wenne doe op 'e Sumarreheide.\nDoe seach ik op in kear tige dúdlik ús mem der oankommen mei myn jongste suster by de hân. Ik soe se tomjitterinne, mar doe wienen se der net. De oare deis wienen se der àl en sy kommen der krekt sa oan lyk as ik se sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20331,"r":"CJ018503","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Will-o'-the-wisps, floating little lights, were often seen at a certain spot. Later a new house was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Burgumerheide ha wy gauris ljochtsjes sjoen op plakken, dêr't letter huzen kommen to stean. Nuver, dat men soks nou net mear sjocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20366,"r":"CJ018622","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A floating little light can often be seen at a certain spot. Later a house is built on the same spot. The will-o'-the-wisp was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 'e Keale wei stie in hûs. Doe't dat der noch net stie ha myn skoanâlden dêr wit hoe faek in ljochtsje brânnen sjoen. Dat wie foartsjirmerije.\nLetter is datselde hûs wer ôfbrutsen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20430,"r":"CJ019021","p":"Waskemeer","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears a cat making a racket in the attic. When he goes to look, the animal is nowhere to be found. An hour later he hears the same sound and this time the cat is there. The sound was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Klaes Duursma wenne to Bakkefean. Hy hearde op in kear tige dúdlik in kat op 'e souder. Hy gong der hinne en rôp: Kaets - kaets - mar der wie net in kat. Sahwat in ûre letter hearde hy krekt itselde lûd. Doe wie der wòl in kat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20431,"r":"CJ019022","p":"Waskemeer","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a boy hears his brother, who is a soldier, come home. A little later he sees him very clearly reading the newspaper in a corner. A month later the brother actually comes home and withdraws with his newspaper in exactly the same way as the boy had seen before. It was a vision of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer hat as soldaet yn Amersfoort west.\nIk wie in jonge fan fyftsjin jier. Op in nacht hearde ik him dúdlik thús kommen. Ik seach hoe't er it skuonsekje oer 't skouder droech en hoe't er in plysjemûtse op 'e holle hie en al syn fierdere klean seach ik hiel dúdlik. Heit siet yn in hoekje to krantlêzen.\nIn maend letter kom er thús. Krekt sa't ik it sjoen hie, ek heit siet yn 'e hoeke to krantlêzen, hwat er mar selden die.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20448,"r":"CJ019212","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman foresees that a train accident is about to happen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Keke hat fantofoaren sjoen, dat de trein in ûngelok krige. De tsjettel knapte de middeis om ien ûre hinne. De trein stie stil, mar der kommen gjin deaden. Sy fornommen it yntiids. 't Gebeurde by Sweagerbosk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20538,"r":"CJ019806","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot wilde lantaarnen (wild lanterns) were sometimes visible. These will-o'-the-wisps are forerunners: it happened that a house was later built on the same spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik gong froeger wol út to naeijen, en by dy gelegenheit haw ik hjir - dêr't nou Jan de Boer wennet - us in wylde lantearne sjoen. Soks wiist op op ien of oare dat dêr yn 'e takomst gebeure sil. 't Is wol gau us dat der dan in hûs komt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20543,"r":"CJ019811","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A married couple hear hammering at night, but when they go to investigate there is nothing to be seen. Later the carpenter's house is built on that spot. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik en myn man krekt troud wienen, - yn Twizelerheide - hearden wy yn 'e nacht dúdlik timmerjen. It wie njonken ús hûs. Mar der wie neat to sjen.\nLetter kom dêr it hûs to stean fan in timmerman.\nJapik de Haan wennet der nou yn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20579,"r":"CJ020201","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening a farmhand heard hammering three times, but there was nothing to be seen. Three years later the front of the farmhouse was rebuilt.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie boerefeint yn Tytsjerk. Ien kear wyks roan ik nei de jongelingsforiening yn Suwâld. Dat wie in ûre rinnen. Omt ik der oars net op tiid komme koe, iet ik fan to foaren mar ien stikje brea. As ik dan de jouns let wer thús kom, iet ik it oare op. Sa wie 'k wer us thús kom, ik siet to brochje-iten yn 'e tsjernherne. 't Wie op 'e Lytse Geast. Ik tochte: - hea, dêr wurdt noch timmere - Ik hearde it klear. \"Hwa timmert nou noch - \" tocht ik.\nIk der út om to sjen, mar der wie neat.\nIk wie wer oan 't iten, doe hearde ik it wer. Ik wer der út, mar ek nou wie der net ien to sjen en it timmerjen hâldde op.\nDoe hearde ik it foar de trêdde kear. Doe gong ik nei de boer ta, dy lei op bêd.\n\"Dit is in nuver spul\", sei 'k tsjin 'e boer. Sa en sa.\nDoe de boer der ek ôf. Mar doe wie der neat to hearren.\nTrije jier neitiid woarde de foarein fortimmere. Doe is der in nije foarein foar kom.\nDat hie ik heard. 't Wie foartjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20587,"r":"CJ020209","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns) that people used to see were forerunners of the later cars and bicycles.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger seagen wy hjir wol us wylde lantearnen. Dat hat foartsjirmerije west, sizze se wol. Letter kommen der auto's en fytsen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20606,"r":"CJ020404","p":"Tzummarum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When the mermaid came into the shipping lane, it was a bad sign.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de sémearmin yn 't farwetter kaem wie dat in min teken. Dêr hienen de skippers it net op stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20614,"r":"CJ020412","p":"Tzummarum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If you put a corner piece of peat in the stove, unexpected visitors will come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger seinen se, die men in hoekturf yn 'e kachel, dan kaem der ûnforwachts bisite.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20615,"r":"CJ020413","p":"Tzummarum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If the gate bangs, unexpected visitors will come.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":20616,"r":"CJ020414","p":"Tzummarum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A family was so poor that they almost never had money for meat. Once in a while they smelled roast meat. A few days later they would indeed eat meat.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy hienen it by mem en dy thús o sa krap. Fleis seagen wy hast noait op 'e tafel. Mar soms, in inkelde kear, dan sei ien fan uzes: \"It rûkt hjir nei in braedtsje.\"\nDan koe men der mar fêst fan op oan dat der koarte tiid dêrnei fleis op 'e tafel kaem. Dat kaem altyd út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20617,"r":"CJ020415","p":"Tzummarum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A skipper's wife always heard clapping two days before the ship came back.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer Sippe Harkema wie skipper. Myn skoansuster hearde twa dagen fan tofoaren it klappen.\nDan sei hja: \"It skip is yn oantocht.\" It kaem altyd út. Twa dagen letter wie hy der.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20644,"r":"CJ020601","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man saw a fire in a house somewhere. When he looked at the front of the house, he saw a small lamp burning on a counter. At the back he saw fire everywhere inside. And yet there was no house there at all. Later a bakery was built there. The bread would be sold by the lamp on the counter, and the ovens would be at the back.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie op Haulerwykster merk. Ik siet op in snein-to-joun yn 'e herberch. Doe seach ik Jan Sterk dêr.\n\"Wij hebben ons kampien ook verkocht, hoor\", sei er.\n\"Oan hwa?\" frege ik.\n\"'t Is een Bergsma; Jannes heet-ie.\"\n\"Wat wil die kerel daarmit?\" frege ik.\n\"Hij is bakker\", sei er.\nDoe kaem âlde Merk der yn.\n\"Wat he'k nou wat beleefd\", sei er. \"Ik kwam meester syn kampien langs.\" Doe fortelde er, hy hie dêr in fjûr sjoen. Der wie brân yn in hûs. Hy woe 't better witte en wie der hinne gien. Doe wied er tsjin 'e muorre oanroan. Sa roan er by de muorre lâns. Doe hie dêr in winkel west mei in toanbank. En op dy toanbank stie in lampke. Doe wied er dêr wei gong en oan 'e kant gong nei in oar plak fan 't hûs. Dêr hie 't allegear fjûr west.\nEn dat, wylst der hielendal net in hûs stie.\n\"Jo ha gelyk,\" sei Jan Sterk, \"dêr komt in bakkerije. Jo ha de oven brânnen sjoen. En dat lampke op 'e toanbank, dêr forkeapje se skielk har breaspullen.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20645,"r":"CJ020602","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A widow heard hammering in the house night after night, but in reality there was nothing. Later her brother-in-law did carpentry work there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde widdou Bergsma wenne op 'e Skieding. Hja hie dêr nachten lang timmerjen heard, mar yn werkelikheit wie der neat. Mar letter hat har swager Germ Bergsma dêr timmere. 't Kaem dus wol út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20649,"r":"CJ020606","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns) were seen above a small lake. They were omens of bicycle lamps.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr't wy froeger wenne ha wie in dobbe, sa'n twahûndert meter fan ús ôf. Rink Hof wenne net sa fier fan ús ôf, oan 'e oare kant fan 'e wyk.\nJouns as 't donker wie, seach er ljochtsjes boppe de dobbe, meastal mei ûnwarich waer. Dy ljochtsjes waerden dan wer wei. Wylde lantearnen seinen se der tsjin. 't Wie doe yn 'e tiid fan 'e earste fytsen en dy ljochtsjes, sei er tsjutten op 'e fytslantearnen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20684,"r":"CJ020805","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On a spot where the sound of hammering had once been heard, a house was later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Surhuzum wie froeger in soad foartsjirmerij.\nIksels ha 't ek us meimakke. Ik wie doe sa'n twintich jier. It wie sahwat sawn ûre op 'e joun doe hearde ik hiel dúdlik timmerjen, in lyts eintsje fan ús ôf. Ik gong der hinne om to sjen. Mar der wie neat. \nLetter kom op dat plak in hûs to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20690,"r":"CJ020902","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night two brothers heard hammering in the back of the house. Not long afterwards the back of the house was rebuilt.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Fokke fortelde ek, hy sliepte by syn broer, doe hearde er op in nacht dúdlik timmerjen by harren yn 't achterhús. Hy makke syn broer wekker en makke der him yndachtich op.\n\"Och jonge, dû bist net wiis\", sei dy.\nLetter hat er 't wer us op in nacht heard.\nIn skoft dêrnei ha se alles yn 't achterhûs fortimmere. Doe koe men deselde lûden hearre.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20711,"r":"CJ021107","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man foresaw that war would come. Blood ran into the canal, so fierce was the fighting. But it did not happen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw in omke hawn, dat wie Ynse Graanstra. Dy hat fan tofoaren sjoen dat se hjir oarloch hienen. It bloed roan ta de feart yn, sa waerd der fochten. Mar dat is net gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20713,"r":"CJ021109","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A postman once walked into a tree, though there was no tree there at all. Later a telephone pole was put there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der hat hjir in âlde postboade west, dy roan ûnderweis yn 't Haulerfjild tsjin in beam op.\nMar der wie hielendal net in beam. Letter kamen de tillefoanpeallen dêr lâns. Dêr hat it foartjirmerij fan west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20822,"r":"CJ021604","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"An old man once said he had seen the mill turning with only one sail. A year later the mill was struck by lightning, and only one sail was left.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der kaem ris in âld man by ús heit, dy gong yn 'e hoeke sitten en skriemde.\n\"Hwat nou,\" sei ús heit, \"is der hwat Jurjen?\" It wie oars sa'n flink âld man.\n\"Ja\", sei er \"ik ha sjoen dat de moune mar mei ien roede draeide.\"\nIen à twa jier letter sloech de tonger yn 'e moune hjir yn Haulerwyk. Doe hat er mar mei ien wjuk draeid.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20948,"r":"CJ022401","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Five weeks before a fire, a woman had already seen the house burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn wiif Sjouk hat it hûs fan Ate en Ynsk hjir yn 'e Harkema sa'n fiif wike foar dat it echt opbrânde al yn 'e brân sjoen. \"Och Heare,\" sei se, \"Ate en Ynke har hûs brânt op!\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20949,"r":"CJ022402","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman had heard the sound of hammering a year in advance on the spot where her later house was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hja hat wol mear sokke dingen meimakke. Hja hat ek fan to foaren it tikjen en hammerjen heard fan it hûs dêr't wy nou yn wenje. Dat wie wol in jier fan tofoaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20951,"r":"CJ022404","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a woman heard the sound of hammering. Later a new house was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik noch yn 'e hûs wie - wy wennen oan 'e Grinslânse wei ûnder Surhústerfean - sei ús mem op in moarn: \"Ik ha fannacht de hammers slaen heard op 'e spanten en houten. Hjir kin wol us in nij hûs komme.\" Dat is ek gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20966,"r":"CJ022501","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman had seen a house burn down in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw by de Spekloane wenne. Dêr is myn hûs yndertiid ôfbrând. Achter ús wenne in frou, dy hie 't hûs fantofoaren al brânnen sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20970,"r":"CJ022505","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When the first bicycles with lights came, people said: \"Here come wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns).\"","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't de earste fytsen kamen dy't ljocht ophienen, seinen de lju: \"Dêr komt in wylde lantearne oan.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21013,"r":"CJ023007","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When bad weather is coming, the mermaid rises up.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As it min waer wurdt, komt de sémearmin omheech, wurdt der wol sein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21014,"r":"CJ023101","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A young man often sawed boards from tree trunks his father bought. One night he heard the sound of tree trunks being thrown. But when he wanted to start sawing the next day, there was no tree at all. The trees only came the following week.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't wy to Himrik wennen beamsagen wy winterdeis faek. Heit kocht beammen en der sagen wy skroaten fan. Dêr woarden hekken fan makke.\nDoe't ik sa'n seis en twintich jier âld wie, lei 'k op in nacht op bêd en doe goaiden se mei de beammen dat it klonk der oer. Ik wie klear wekker.\nIk sei de oare moarns: wy kinne wol bigjinne to beamsaegjen. Mar der wie net in beam. It wie foartsjirmerij. De wyks dêrop wienen de beammen der.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21039,"r":"CJ023401","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns) of the old days were omens of the later lampposts and the lights of bicycles and cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha to Bakkefean wenne. Wy seagen soms boppe 't Mandefjild wylde lantearnen. Dat wienen de foarboaden fan 'e lettere lampen dy't oan 'e wegen kamen en de ljochten fan 'e fytsen en auto's ensa.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21101,"r":"CJ024105","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns) of the old days were omens of new houses.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As se froeger wylde lantearnen seagen, dan kom der op dat plak in nij hûs to stean. Dan hienen se de lampe al fan tofoaren brânnen sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21130,"r":"CJ024402","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once heard hammering and throwing, as if the place was being torn down. But there was nothing to be seen. Some time later a new house was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanheit dat wie Hindrik Land. Syn âlde mem kom us by him en sei: \"Hindrik mat gau komme, it giet hjir by ús achter yn 'e hûs sa bot op in timmerjen en smiten, dat ik bin bang dat se it hiele spul ôfbrekke.\" Mar doe't skoanheit kom, wie der neat to rêdden.\nMar in skoft letter setten se in nij hûs flak achter skoanheit sinen del. Dêr hie 't âld-minske it timmerjen fan heard. (It wie it hûs fan Epke v. d. Berg, dêr't de trije berntsjes yn forbrând binne; Jan van Zalen hat der noch in liet op makke.)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21171,"r":"CJ024602","p":"Waskemeer","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Near Bakkeveen there used to be little lights. Later houses were built there. So it was sorcery.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek boppe it Mandefjild ûnder Bakkefean wienen ljochtsjes, dy ha 'k sels wol sjoen. Letter kommen der op dy plakken huzen to stean. Dat hat dus foartjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21199,"r":"CJ024801","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A farm maid and a farmhand heard hammering every night, although building only went on during the day. It was sorcery.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn wiif Brecht hat boerefaem west op it Wytfean by Piter Tammes Oosterhof. Oebele van der Sluis wie dêr doe feint. 't Wie yn 'e tiid fan 'e Spaenske gryp fan 1918, doe gebeurde it dat Paulus van Minnen fan Eastemar dêr by har it lytshûs en de skuorre fortimmere. Doe hearde myn wiif dêr nacht op nacht timmerjen. Sy woarde der wekker fan. Mar yn werklikheit woarde der net timmere. Hwant de timmerlju bigongen earst yn 'e moarn.\nOebele van der Sluis slepte achter. Dy hearde dat timmerjen nachts ek en hy wie bang. \"Ik ha der in hekel oan\", sei er. Mar myn wiif sei: \"Dêr hoechstû net bang foar to wêzen, dat is foartsjirmerij.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21200,"r":"CJ024802","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On his way back from his girlfriend, a young man sees a light. When he comes closer, it suddenly disappears. Later a house was built there. It was a wilde lantaarn (wild lantern).","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie forkearing mei in faem yn 'e Harkema. Op in kear kom ik by har wei om in ûre of ien, twa hinne. 't Wie by de Krúswei. Ik soe nei hûs ta. Ik sei tsjin myn faem: \"Sjoch, dêr brânt ljocht. Dêr stiet in lantearne. Hwat dat bitsjut, wyt ik net.\" Ik gong op stap en hja gong yn 'e hûs. Doe't ik tichter by 't ljocht kom, sette ik de fyts yn 'e daem en roan der op ôf. Hwant ik woe der mear fan wite. Ik wie der omtrint oan ta, doe stapte ik hjir of dêr op. Even hie 'k doe it gesicht fan 't ljocht ôf. Doe't ik wer seach, wie 't ljocht fuort.\nIt hat nei alle gedachten in wylde lantearne west. Hwant letter is dêr in hûs kom to stean. Jan Wopkes is dêr kom to wenjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21220,"r":"CJ025001","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman heard hammering at the back of the house three nights in a row. Ten weeks later a new back was built on.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie yn 1907. Wy wennen yn 'e Warmoldsstrjitte, hjir yn 'e Harkema. Mem en dy slepten yn 'e foarein fan 't hûs, mar sy hearde nachts timmerjen yn 'e achterein. Dat hearde se wol trije nachten achter elkoar.\nMar der wie neat. Der woarde net timmere. Doe't se ècht oan 't timmerjen rekken, wie 't wol tsien wiken letter. Mar doe timmeren se oerdeis, mar net yn 'e nacht.\nSy krigen doe in nije achterein. Mem hearde krekt deselde hammerslaggen en itselde plankefallen as dat se doe yn 'e nacht heard hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21221,"r":"CJ025002","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once heard something going through the thatched roof, and she thought there was a break-in. But there was nothing and no one to be seen. A few days later potatoes were stolen. Then exactly the same rustling could be heard as before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mem hearde ek op in nacht dat der hwat troch it tek gong. Hja hienen in reiden tek en hja hearde hyltyd dat der hwat trochhinne gong. Hja tocht: \"Hjir is gjin rie ta. Sy brekke by ús yn.\" Mar 't wie dêrom sa net. Der wie net ien en der gebeurde neat.\nMar trije dagen letter, doe ha se de jirpels stellen. Doe stuts der ien syn holle troch 't tek hinne en wie der krekt itselde geritsel dat mem fan tofoaren heard hie. 't Hie foartsjirmerij west.\n(Myn man hearde de dingen ek faek fan tofoaren)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21222,"r":"CJ025003","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A girl heard children singing, and she saw little lights. She also heard the clatter of children's clogs and the words: \"You must sit still.\" In reality there was nothing. But later a Sunday school came, and then it all came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ús mem in famke wie, hearde se bern sjongen en sy seach ek ljochtsjes. Sy rôp beppe der by en sei: \"Mat mem hjir us sjen, sa'n moai ljocht is dêr.\" Sy hearde dúdlik it getrappel fan berneklompkes en dat der sein woarde: \"Jullie moeten stil zitten.\"\nYn werklikheit wie der doe neat. Mar letter hat âlde Warmolts op dat plak in lyts tsjerkje bouwe litten. Dat is bigong as sondagsskoalle. Der woarde doe ècht song en der klonken klompkes fan 'e bern. En âlde Warmolds sei: \"Jullie moeten stil zitten.\" Dat hie mem as famke allegear al fan tofoaren sjoen en heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21223,"r":"CJ025004","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman saw a wagon with no horse in front of it, which almost drove her and her niece into the hedge. In reality there was nothing. A month later her son murdered a carpenter. Then the police came to drag him from his bed. They drove one of the first cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Wierd Kooistra syn soan Rinse hat Rapke timmerman (Wijma) formoarde. In maend foardat dat gebeurde hat Wierd syn wiif hwat sjoen. Doe kom der in wein oan sûnder hynders der foar.\n't Hat sahwat yn 1912 west. Dy wein treau har en har nichtsje Pôpe Jantsje hast yn 'e hage. Mar der wie yn werklikheit neat.\nFjouwer wiken neitiid hâldde dêr in auto stil mei plysjes der yn. Dy hellen Rinse út bêd fanwege de moart op Rapke. 't Wie ien fan 'e earste auto's. Doe wie de sitewaesje krektsa as Rinse syn mem it sjoen hie. (Pôpe Jantsje koe knoffelbannen lizze)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21333,"r":"CJ026001","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man was lying in bed when he suddenly saw very clearly a road with cars driving over it. Later that road was indeed built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is al hiel lang lyn, doe wenne ik op 'e kooi ûnder Garyp. 't Wie yn 'e nacht. Ik lei op bêd en hie lyk as altyd de kleden iepen. Doe seach ik samar ynienen hiel dúdlik in wei, dêr't auto's lâns tuften. Der wie doe hielendal noch net in wei.\nMar dy wei is der kom: de Bolderenwei, en dêr tuffe nou alle dagen de auto's lâns. Dit ha 'k sels sjoen en dat kin net ien my út 'e holle weiprate.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21383,"r":"CJ026401","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On the spot where a woman often heard hammering at night, a new building was later put up.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoansuster Tite hearde yn 'e nacht altyd timmerjen.\nHja wenne to Koartehimmen. Letter is op dat plak it Woodbrookers-gebou delset.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21404,"r":"CJ026604","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns) of the old days are supposed to be today's street lamps and lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De wylde lantearnen fan froeger, dat hite nou de strjitlampen en ljochten to wêzen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21406,"r":"CJ026606","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man often heard things in advance. He often heard hammering in places where new houses were later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer út Greategast heart wol gauris dingen fan tofoaren. Hiel faek heart er timmerjen.\nDan komt der letter op sa'n plak in hûs to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21407,"r":"CJ026607","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man often heard strange noises in his house at night, but saw nothing. Later Salvation Army soldiers came to that house, and they often made a great commotion until late in the evening.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie hjir in omke to wenjen, dy sprong op krukken. Dy wenne yn in hûs, dêr gong it der soms heislik oan wei. Dan gong omke út bêd en krige er 't greate breames, mar dan wie der neat. Letter binne de heilsoldaten yn datselde hûs kom en doe gong it wakker op in spyljen en sjongen en merakeljen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21435,"r":"CJ026702","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One winter afternoon a woman heard a car in the yard, but she saw nothing. There were no car tracks to be found in the snow either. But the next day there was an accident on the road, and lots of people and cars came into the yard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde in pear jier lyn. 't Wie yn 'e winter, der lei snie. 't Wie op 'e neimiddei. Ik hearde in protte lawaei op 'e wei en by ús op it hiem. Ik hearde ek in greate auto. Doe't ik op it hiem kom wie der alhiel neat to sjen. En doe't ik de oare moarns doe't it ljocht wie, nei spoaren socht yn 'e snie, wienen dy der net. Doe wist ik it oare wol. De oare deis is hjir doe in ûngelok gebeurd op 'e wei. 't Wienen allegear auto's en minsken, ek hjir op it hiem. Se ha hjir doe noch in frou yn 'e hûs brocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21436,"r":"CJ026703","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman predicted to her son-in-law that his 88-year-old mother would not die in hospital but would come home again. The son-in-law did not believe her, but it came true all the same.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha in skoftsje yn Westergeast by myn dochter wenne. Sjoerd syn mem wie tige siik. Sy rekke deamin nei 't sikenhûs ta. Elkenien forwachte dat se stjerre soe. Mar ik sei tsjin Sjoerd: \"Jimme mem komt wer.\"\n\"Gjin sprake fan,\" sei er, \"dat kin ommers net. Sy leit op 't stjerren.\"\nIk sei noch us: \"Sy komt wer, sy rêdt it.\"\nIn fjirtsjin dagen letter koe 't âld-minske wer nei hûs ta. Sy wie 88 jier.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21437,"r":"CJ026704","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman very often heard hammering in places where new houses were later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wit hoe faek ha ik yn myn leven timmerjen heard oan huzen en hokken dy't letter pas boud woarden. Ik sei wol us tsjin myn soan: \"Hwat matte jim nou wer bitimmerje? 'k Ha 't wol heard.\" Dan duorre it mar even of de timmerderij rekke los.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21438,"r":"CJ026705","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once heard planks and beams being thrown about, and she predicted that a new house would soon be built on that spot. That came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik stie us in kear bûten. Doe sei 'k: \"Hjir komt in nij hûs, net fier fan ús ôf.\" Ik hearde klear hoe't se mei planken en balken ensa smieten.\nIt duorre net lang of sy setten der in nij hûs del.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21439,"r":"CJ026706","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man was once unable to cycle any further along a road. A few days later he had to stop there because a coffin had to pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn soan wie bûtermakker. Op in moarn gong er op 'e fyts nei syn wurk ta. Hy soe út 'e daem wei oer de wei, mar dêr woarde er keard. Hy stapte fan 'e fyts, mar der wie neat to sjen.\nIk sei tsjin him: \"Dêr komt earstdeis in lyk troch.\nEn 't wie ek sa. In wike letter gong dêr in man dea. It wie op 'e hoeke fan 'e wei nei Opperkoaten. De kiste moest rûmte ha, dêrtroch moest myn soan doe ôfstappe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21441,"r":"CJ026708","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman can always hear on the radio in advance whether a plane is going to crash.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in ramp komt fan it iene of oare flychtúch of sa, dan wyt ik dat ek altyd fan tofoaren. Dan hear ik dat oan 'e radio. Dan siz ik: \"Der komt wer in ûngelok.\" It komt altyd nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21442,"r":"CJ026709","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman often hears a voice in her dreams that makes predictions to her. She also often hears the sound of hammering in places where new houses will be built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e droom hear ik faek in stem. Dy dielt my dan it ien of oare mei. Dêrtroch wyt ik fan alles, hwat der gebeure sil.\nIk haw trije beppesizzers, dy moesten alle trije in pop ha. Dy stem sei tsjin my: Twa derfan dat wurde jonges. Se komme allebeide Anders to hiten. (Ik wist net dat de heiten fan 'e manlju beide Anders hieten)\nTsjin 'e trêdde beppesizzer sei 'k: \"Dû krigest in famke.\" Dat is ek útkaem. It woarde tsjin my sein. Dat binne fisioenen.\nSa't ik sei, ik hear hiel faek timmerjen, sawol by dei as by nacht. En 't komt altyd nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21446,"r":"CJ026713","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once saw part of a house on fire, but when she came closer there was nothing to see. A few weeks later the paraffin stove in the house caught fire.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie us by myn suster yn 'e Falom. Sy sei tsjin my: \"Sille wy us in eintsje 't lân del? It is sok moai waer.\" Ik sei: \"Goed\", en wy kuijeren hwat. Doe bleau ik ynienen stean.\n\"Hwat is der oan?\" sei myn suster.\n\"Dizze kant fan jimme hûs stiet yn 'e brân\", sei 'k.\nMar doe't wy thús kommen, wie der neat to rêdden.\nMar in wike letter is troch in petroaljestel it hûs yn 'e brân rekke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21449,"r":"CJ026716","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once heard noises in the attic. The next day a heavy thunderstorm destroyed part of the attic. When it was being repaired, the woman heard the same noises she had heard before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in nacht hearde ik lawaei op 'e souder. Dêr komt oars noait ien, dat ik woarde kjel.\nDe oare deis wie der in swier ûnwaer. Alle lampkes yn 'e hûs hjir rekken stikken en boven op 'e souder wie 't spul hwat forinnewearre.\nDoe ha se dat dêr letter wer opknapt, en doe hearde ik krekt deselde lûden, dy't ik dy nachts ek heard hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21450,"r":"CJ026717","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once saw a car standing in her son's yard, and a man in a black hat got out. But when the man came closer, he and the car suddenly vanished. The woman told her son that a car would soon be standing on that spot in the yard. The very next day the doctor came in his car. The daughter-in-law had unexpectedly had a baby.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in joun kom ik by de buorfrou wei en doe seach ik in greate auto by myn soan yn 'e daem stean. Myn soan wennet hjir njonken my. Der kom in greate man út dy auto, mei in hoed op.\nMar doe't ik der flak by wie wie der alhielendal gjin auto en ek net in mynhear. Mar ik hie goed yn my opnom hwer't ik dy auto stean sjoen hie, dat ik sette der in streek by.\nIk sei tsjin myn soan: \"Nou komt hjir in auto to stean\", en ik lei him de saek út.\nDe oare deis kom der al in auto, dy't krekt op 't selde plak stean gong. Dokter kom der út.\nMyn skoandochter hie noch ûnforwacht in poppe krigen.\nIt jonkje is letter stoarn, 't is fordronken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21565,"r":"CJ027105","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man always worked in Groningen during the week. He did not want his wife to visit her family then, because he had quarrelled with them. Once the wife wanted to go anyway, but halfway there she suddenly saw her husband's figure. She quickly went back home. An hour later the man came home. His figure had been a warning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hindrik de Boer wenne hjir yn 'e Harkema. Hy arbeide yn Grinslân op 'e klaei en wie altyd de hiele wike fuort. Tsjin syn wiif hied er sein: \"Dû meist net by dyn folk komme, dat wol 'k bislist net lije.\" Hwant hy hie spul hawn mei syn wive folk.\nMar op in joun, midden yn 'e wike, tocht se: \"Ik wol der even sjen.\" En hja gong op stap. Mar doe't se sahwat op healwei wie, seach se ynienen hiel dúdlik de gedaente fan har man. Hja bleau stean en sei: \"O heden. Dit is Hindrik, myn man.\"\nMar né, it koe Hindrik net wêze, hwant it wie midden yn 'e wike. En doe wied er ek samar ynienen wer fuort west. Hja giet werom, troch de stâl, by de beesten lâns, yn 'e hûs. Har bern lizze op bêd to sliepen. Doe tocht se: \"Ik gean ek mar op bêd.\"\nIn goed ûre letter, dêr kloppe Hindrik. Syn gedaente, dat hie foar har in warskôging west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21583,"r":"CJ027312","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Two sisters were once sitting in the dark with a tea light lit. One woman saw someone come through the door, but the other saw nothing. A little later someone really did come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn suster fan Twizelerheide wie hjir lêsten ien nacht. Wy sieten de jouns yn 't donker. Sa mei 'k altyd graech sitte, mei 't théljochtsje op.\n\"Dêr komt ien troch de doar\", sei myn suster.\nIk sei: \"Dêr komt gjin.\"\nMar letter kom der wòl ien troch de doar. Myn suster hie 't fan tofoaren sjoen. Sy hat it krekt sa as ik.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21587,"r":"CJ027402","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once heard a lot of noise in an adjoining room. But there was nothing to see. The next day a relative fell through the floor and landed in that room. That was the sound the woman had heard the day before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie op in kear by myn suster yn Twizelerheide. Wy sieten yn 't keammerke togearre by elkoar, doe hearde ik dat it der yn 'e oare keamer hiel bot oan wei gong. Myn suster fornaem it net. Ik sei: \"Hwat in lawaei.\" Wy der hinne. Mar der wie neat to sjen. Dat wy gongen wer nei 't keammerke ta to thédrinken.\nDe oare deis rekke de dochter fan myn suster troch de souder hinne boppe de keamer. De planken bijoegen har. Dat joech in stik leven. En dàt hie ik de foarige deis heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21608,"r":"CJ027504","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once heard someone knock on the window, but there was nobody to be seen. Fourteen days later there was a knock again at exactly the same time. This time it was the neighbours' boy; his father had been taken ill.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn âld buorman wie tige siik. Op in nacht woarde der by my op it finster kloppe, mar doe't ik rôp: \"Hwa is der?\" krige ik gjin antwurd.\nDer wie net ien. 't Wie om ien ûre hinne.\nIn fjirtsjin dagen letter krekt op 'e selde tiid woarde der wer by my op it finster kloppe. Krekt deselde klop.\nIk rôp: \"Hwa is der?\" Doe wie dat de soan fan myn sike buorman. Hy sei, it wie lang net goed mei syn heit. Of ik wol even komme woe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21610,"r":"CJ027506","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a woman heard the sound of hammering. Later a house was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Is sa'n fyftich jier lyn, doe wennen wy noch yn 't âld hûs hjirneist. Wy leinen op bêd, 't wie yn 'e nacht. Doe sei myn frou: \"Ik hear timmerjen, hiel dúdlik, hjir flak neist.\" Dêr ha wy in skoftsje letter in hûs krigen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21611,"r":"CJ027507","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone often hears 'volk' (anyone home?) being called. Then someone always arrives.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurt faek dat ik 'folk' roppen hear. Dan tink ik: Der komt aenst ek ien. En dat giet altyd troch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21624,"r":"CJ027520","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Will-o'-the-wisps are forerunners of the lamps of bicycles and cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By de Falom haw ik us wylde lantearnen sjoen yn 'e nacht, doe't wy dêr oan 't fiskjen wienen.\nDer wurdt wol sein dat dat de foarboaden wienen fan lampen fan fytsen en auto's ensa.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21628,"r":"CJ027601","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman often saw all kinds of events in advance. For instance, she had seen that a beautiful white house would stand on a certain spot, and it was indeed built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Iebeltsje, dat wie Teije de Haan syn mem, dy seach hiel faek hwat fan tofoaren. Sa hat hja tiden fan tofoaren sjoen hoe't de lju dwaende wienen mei de fundaminten fan 'e Wilhelmina-hoeve. Dat is op 'e Skieding. Sy seach de pealtsjes yn 'e groun stean. Letter seach se fan tofoaren it hiele hûs. 't Wie in moai wyt hûs, sei se, mei koperen krukken oan 'e doarren. Dat hat âlde Iebeltsje allegear foarút sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21659,"r":"CJ028001","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If you draw the ace of clubs at a fortune-teller's, you will get a letter. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As je by de kaertlizzer klaveraes lûke, dan krije jo in brief.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21660,"r":"CJ028002","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If a little bird taps on the window, a message will come. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in fûgeltsje tsjin 't finster tikket, komt der in boadskip.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21661,"r":"CJ028003","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If a magpie comes onto the land, there will be news, for the magpie is a bringer of news. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in ekster op 't hiem komt, dan komt der hwat nijs. In ekster is in nijs-bringer.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21662,"r":"CJ028004","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If the cat washes itself, visitors will come. People should keep a close eye on the cat. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de kat him wasket, komt der bisite. De minsken matte goed achtslaen op 'e kat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21663,"r":"CJ028005","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"What the cat looks at does not die. A sick person recovers at once if the cat casts a glance at the patient.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hwat in kat bisjocht, giet net dea. As der ien tige siik is en de kat komt by him en bisjocht him, dan wurdt dy pasjint wer better.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21664,"r":"CJ028006","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If a cat runs across the barley of a mown field, the farmer need not worry about the hay, because it will not rain.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in boer in stik lân ôfmeand hat en de kat rint oer it gers hinne, dan hoeft dy boer gjin noed to hawwen oer 't hea. Alles komt droech yn 'e skuorre.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21670,"r":"CJ028012","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If a toad crosses your path, you should be on your guard.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":21671,"r":"CJ028013","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Where a swallow builds its nest, luck will come. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":21674,"r":"CJ028016","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone sometimes smells cigar smoke in the morning when a visitor who smokes cigars is coming in the afternoon. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Soms kom ik moarns yn 'e keamer, dan tink ik: \"Hea, ik rûk sigarelucht.\" Dan komt der fêst de middeis in man dy't sigaren smookt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21675,"r":"CJ028017","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the morning a woman smells food burning, although she has nothing on the stove yet. Around mealtime the food really does burn, because she is standing at the door talking to someone. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in moarn rûkte ik dat myn iten oanbarnde. Mar ik hie noch net iens iten op 'e kachel stean. Ik sei by my sels: Dit komt my net oer. Mar 't gebeurde wòl. Wylst ik de moarns oan 't itensieden wie kom der ien by de doar. Ik praette hwat lang. Ik forgeat it iten. Dat brânde oan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21676,"r":"CJ028018","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Lights are sometimes seen at the place where a new road will be built. These will-o'-the-wisps are an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir tichteby komt in wei skeanoer. Ik ha de ljochtsjes al twa kear sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21680,"r":"CJ028022","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot people hear a cock crow at night, but there is nothing to be seen anywhere. Ten years later a small farm with hens and cockerels stands on the same spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Twizelerheide hearden se midden yn 'e nacht in hoanne kraeijen op 't keale fjild. Mar der wie neat. Tsien jier letter stie dêr in spultsje en dêr wienen ek hinnen en hoannen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21681,"r":"CJ028023","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A grandmother is convinced she had already seen her grandchild in a blue dress that morning. The girl was indeed wearing a blue dress in the morning, but did not actually visit her grandmother until the afternoon. The grandmother had had a voorgezicht (a vision of a future event).","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Fan 'e wike kom hjir in beppesizzer.\n\"Dû hast hjir fan 'e moarn ek al west\", sei 'k.\n\"Né, beppe\", sei se.\n\"Dû hast hjir west, 'k ha dy sjoen, dû hiest in blauwe jurk oan. Mar dû wytst it sels net.\"\n\"Ja,\" sei se, \"'k hie in blauwe jurk oan fan 'e moarn.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21682,"r":"CJ028024","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"It is a bad sign if you meet a black cat at night. You should then be on your guard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As men nachts in swarte kat moetet, dan is dat in min teken. Wêz dan op jou hoede!","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21695,"r":"CJ028113","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the past many will-o'-the-wisps were seen. People were often afraid of them, because they thought they were ghostly.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen woarden hjir froeger oeral sjoen. De lju wienen der deabinaud foar, hwant it wie spûkerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21742,"r":"CJ028502","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A farmhand warns his mates in the field to hurry up, because a ship is sailing towards them. His mates think he is mad, because there is no water to be seen anywhere. A year later the seawater rises so high that the ship really does sail past. The boy had had a voorgezicht (a vision of a future event).","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 1824 wienen der lju op 't lân ûnder 't Blauhûs, yn 'e Sensmeer oan 't wurk. Doe wie dêr in jonge, dy't rôp: \"Minsken, minsken, wy matte hjir wei, der komt in skip oansilen, lyk op ús ta!\"\nMar de minsken seinen: \"Dû bist net wiis.\" Hwant dêr wie neat to sjen.\nMar it oare jiers (1825) kom it séwetter sa heech opsetten, dat doe foer der ècht in skip lâns. Doe tochten se oan itjinge de jonge it foarige jiers sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21827,"r":"CJ028801","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man regularly hears caulking and hammering at a shipyard, which means there will be a lot of carpentry the next day. The yard boss thought this was very good, as it meant work was coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn myn jonge jierren ha 'k it op 'e helling yn Eastemar faek brouwen heard. Soms hammere it ek hiel lûd, dat wiisde der op, dat it dan de oare deis wer drok op in timmerjen gean soe.\nSibrich, it wiif fan 'e hellingbaes, sei, dat hja dêr wol graech oer mochten, dan kom der drokte.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21830,"r":"CJ028804","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In a play, the leg of one of the actors has to be amputated. A week later the same man's leg really has to be amputated.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Koaten die in sekere Taeke mei oan 'e komeedzje. Hy moest de skonk der ôf ha en dat gebeurde yn dat toanielstik, dêr't er yn meispile.\nIn wike of hwat letter moest er de skonk der werklik ôf ha. De man is stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21832,"r":"CJ028806","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone thinks he sees a boat coming across the land. It is an omen: later a canal is dug at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie in persoan, dy seach de kant út nei de Mar. Doe seach er hwat oankommen oer it lân. In feart wie der net. It like wol in skip, mar it hie gjin seilen. Letter die bliken, dat ding dat hie de Eastemarre boat west, dy't dêr letter farde op it plak dêr't se letter it kanael groeven ha.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21837,"r":"CJ028811","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Boatmen see a terrible disaster on the ice in which all sorts of people drown. The vision never came true, but the 'place of doom' has been avoided ever since.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Skippers to Grou seagen op in stik iis flak by Grou us in kear in freeslike ramp. In hiele smite minsken sakken der troch en fordronken. ('t Is noait gebeurd)\nLetter doarsten se dêr noait wer to riden. Mar dêr is oant nou ta noch noait in ûngelok gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21849,"r":"CJ028901","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At night a boy hears a sound as if the weight of the clock is falling down. When he goes to look, the weight is still hanging on the clock. Some time later the weight really does fall down. It was a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen froeger yn it húske, dat nou krekt ôfbrutsen is. It stie by de brêge, tusken Stiensgea en de Hamster Pein yn. Hwat yn 'e lichte. Dêr bin 'k geboaren en dêr ha 'k oan 1903 ta wenne.\nWy hienen dêr in stuoltsjeklok.\nWy slepten yn bêdsteden. Yn 't iene slepten heit en mem en ik slepte mei in pear bruorren yn 't oare. Der slepten ek noch guon achter.\nOp in nacht woarde ik kjel wekker. Ik hearde in swiere bouns. 't Wie dúdlik it lûd fan ien fan 'e koperen klokswichten. Dat kom del.\nIk wie noch sa'n jonge. Ik heit roppe. Heit! Heit! Hy wie fuort net wekker. Mar op 't lêst, hy der ôf en sjen nei de klok. It wicht hong der noch moai oan. Der wie neat ôffallen. Hy gong protteljend wer op bêd. Mar even neitiid foel 't wòl del. Doe woarde heit der sels kjel wekker fan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23414,"r":"CJ039101","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A group of boys once hear hammering, and some of them see lights. In reality there was nothing. But later new houses were built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn man wie noch in jonge baes, hy wie hjir us op 'e wei mei oaren. Sy praetten hwat, doe hearden se yn 'e Kule timmerjen. Guon seinen: wy sjogge ljochten. Mar dêr stie net in hûs.\nLetter is dêr boud woarn. Der binne nije huzen yn 'e Kule delset. Myn man hat it sels fan to foaren heard en sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23419,"r":"CJ039106","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wild lanterns that people used to see were the portents of the later bicycle lamps.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De wylde lantearnen dy't wy froeger seagen, dat ha de fytsljochten fan letter west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33225,"r":"CJ088007","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If you saw a will-o'-the-wisp, it meant an accident was going to happen. The eerie howling of dogs usually meant a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Seach ien in wylde lantearne, dan bitsjutte dat in warskôging foar in ûngelok dat op komst wie.\nSpoekgûlen fan hounen tsjut meast op in sterfgefal.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":130062,"r":"VERHOEFF000604","p":"Westmaas","v":"Z.-H.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Man has a vision of the end of the world.","i":"L.V.","o":"In Oud-Beierland was een man, toen was ik een jaar of twintig, die zei dat de wereld zou vergaan, daar had-tie een gezicht van gehad. Het was toen een errege slechte zomer, nat en zo.","l":"Hoeksewaards"},{"n":130069,"r":"VERHOEFF000701","p":"Apeldoorn","v":"Gld.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hearing knocking by working spirits is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the building of a barn. The knocking stops once the barn has been built.","i":"L.V.","o":"Ik was nog een kleine jongen en als er dan visite kwam ’s avonds, hoorde je de hele tijd maar kloppen. Dan gingen ze wel eens de ladder op om op de zolder te kijken, maar ze konden er nooit bijkomen bij dat geluid, want dan was het ineens weer ergens anders. M’n moeder zei altijd: “Dat zijn onze werkgeesten en die mannetjes werken maar door voor ons”. Toen er een nieuwe schuur werd gebouwd achter ons huis was het afgelopen met dat geklop. Je kunt het nog aan allerlei oude mensen bij ons in de buurt vragen, die hebben het allemaal gehoord, het was gewoon het werken aan de schuur dat we van te voren hadden gehoord."},{"n":130071,"r":"VERHOEFF000703","p":"Apeldoorn","v":"Gld.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Red, green and white lights on a sandy road are a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of bicycles with red, green and white lights.","i":"L.V.","o":"Wij woonden heel ver achteraf in het land en er liep een zandweg van de harde weg in Vriescheloo naar het kanaal 1), die zandweg liep een vierhonderd meter van ons huis af. ’s Avonds zag je dan ineens drie lichten heel hard gaan, een rood, een groen en een wit licht en die kwamen dan zo die zandweg af. Dan gingen wij er op af en dan stonden we aan de weg en dat licht scheen je dan even heel fel in je ogen en dan was het weg. Toen later de fietsen kwamen, dan zag je die carbidlampen, weet u wel, die haddem opzij een rood en een groen glaasje en van voren gewoon wit licht, dus dat is ook uitgekomen.\n1) Het Vereenigd Kanaal van Westerwolde."},{"n":130079,"r":"VERHOEFF000711","p":"Apeldoorn","v":"Gld.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Man predicts that a child will drown, which comes true.","i":"L.V.","o":"Die Malle Abraham waar ik straks al van verteld heb, was een wonderlijke man. Hij kwam eens bij mijn moeder binnenrennen en zei: “dat kind daar is in de sloot verdronken”. Mijn moeder vloog naar buiten, maar het kind zat in de zandbak te spelen. M’n moeder heeft het toen aan de moeder van dat kind verteld, maar toch is het kind binnen acht dagen verdronken. Wat die Abraham zag, moest onherroepelijk gebeuren. Dat was gewoon, wat zal ik zeggen, wat hij zag was voorzienigheid."},{"n":131972,"r":"VODA_033_15","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In places where people used to see small lights burning, houses and barracks were later built.\nGrandma saw white and red \"fireballs\" passing by. Later a road was built on which cars with white headlights and red taillights drove past. Grandma also said she saw masts; masts, but no ships. Later telephone poles were put up. Grandma had seen a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event).","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Nou, ik ken wel iets vertellen van mien geboorteploats, det is now den zestig joar ‘leden en die geboorteploats woar ik wegkom dea was vrouger den woest en ledig. En nou kin ik d’r ook waal bie zeggen wat ik doar ‘heurd en zain heb, want as e wee… doa in mien geboorteploats stunden dan maar drei huzen, of vaar ainlijk.\nDa’s van doar ord [?] bewoanboare streek is, maar ’t was hait en nog ens hait en veen en hoarten [?], da stak in… ’t was een woestenij. En den kon die ollen altied proaten over lichies. Eh… veurboden neumen wie zie den. En doa ik den acht joar was, ook nog een beetje aan de bange kaante, moar ik had ook nog oldere zusters in mien huus, den gingen wee ’s oabens as ’t dônker wui, wöl es noar boeten en dan zagen wee die lichies inderdoad branden, zo zet ze zain. Die grote fellen woa niks was brandden dan lichies. En net achter ons laand uut, det is plusminus zeub’n-, achthonderd meter achter ons huus uut, doa brand’ ook altied ’n lichie. Dan zeiden wie tegen ’nander, ik was misschien acht of tien joar, doa zal nooit geen huus kom’n ken’n. Want de ollen zeiden: dat bin veurboden. Doa kom’ allewees [?] overalle huzen. Moar wee wôsten dat ja nait, was ook ja niks, war ja woeste lede nog in dea tied. En in die grote Weenderveld, wat vandoage al land is, ’t is al ontgonnen, doa brandden zoveul lichies, d’ zeiden wee: “Wie waiten nait, maar det ken toch al geen huzen weze","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45808,"r":"WEV015705","p":"Musselkanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People keeping watch by a sick grandmother hear someone come at night, go to the cellar and rattle the preserving jars. After grandmother has moved in with someone, that person takes the preserving jars out of the cellar and takes them away.","i":"F.W.","o":"n Poar joar leden wur mien grootmoe zaik. Ik mus dr bie woakn. Ik zat zo allennig in de koamer en dou vernam ik gestommel op boetn. t Was net, of er aine mit klompen aan teegn t hoes langs luip. Hai dee de deure oopn, kwam in t veurhoes, muik de kelderdeure lös en gung de kelder in. Door zat hai bie de weckflesn te rammeln. Ik keek ja es tou, man zag niks. \nt Wur mie roar tou. Anderdagaovend vruig ik mien kameroad of hai mie gezelschap holn wol. Dat was best. Mit ons beidend passen wie op en door kwam in de nacht t zulfde geluud weer. Mien kameroad, dai toch al niks te driest was, keek zo wit as n liek. \nHai is ook nooit weer mit west; t wur hum te gek. \nNog meer van mien femilie hebben woakt en allemaol heurden ze dat wonderlieke geluud. Man de deurn bleevn wol tou.\n Aine van de woakers vul inains wat anders op. Wie harn door nog nich op let. Man as dat gestommel teegn t hoes begunde, dee mien grootmoe de hannen umhoog boovn de kop. En as t geluud weer vot was, gungen de hannen noar doale op de deekns. Ik heb mien beurt weer woakt, man verscheiden duzzen nich meer mit. \nMien grootmoe is beter worn; man zai was old en doorum is ze bie aine ingoan. t Hoes is leeghoald en non kan ik dat geluud in de kelder verkloarn. Dat mens, woor ze bie introkn is, hef alle weckflesn oet de kelder hoald en noar heur aign hoes brocht. \nDat veurspooksel moutn wie dou vernomen hebben. Zo denk ik e","l":"Gronings"},{"n":17317,"r":"WEV016004","p":"Barnflair","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Fastening a loose button on a coat or sewing on a new one must be done with the coat off, otherwise something will happen on the way.","i":"F.W.","o":"As ie vot wiln en vernemen, dat er n knoop lös zit aan de jazze, den moutn ie de jazze uut trekn, as de vrouw er n nei-e aan zetn wil of hom vaaste zetn. Holn ie de jazze aan en zai zet dr den n knoop aan, den reken moar, dat joe er onderweg wat overkomt.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46185,"r":"WEV016403","p":"Gasselternijveen","v":"Dr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Noise is heard in a church at night, but there is nothing to be seen. Later, when the church is being renovated, the same sound is heard.","i":"F.W.","o":"Vooruitzien bestaat ook.\nWe hebben dat meegemaakt in Friesland en eveneens in Drente. \nIn Marrum hoorden we op een nacht een vreselijk kabaal in de kerk. Wij gingen uit bed om te zien of er gevallen was. \nNiets te ontdekken.\nNaderhand is men begonnen de kerk op te knappen en toen hoorden we hetzelfde geluid: het vallen van stenen en het gooien met planken; dat moet dus van te voren door ons waargenomen zijn."},{"n":46200,"r":"WEV016705","p":"Froombosch","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"After a cow is stolen, a woman tells the farmer's wife that she dreamed who stole the cow. The cow turns out to be at that address.","i":"F.W.","o":"“Dreumen binnen bedrog”, zeggen de lu.\nDat is altied nait woar. Ik ken joe n wor verhoaltje verteln. \nt Was in de oorlog. Op n mörn was hier bie n boer ain kou vot. Stooln netuurlijk. Dat gebeurde zoveul in dei tied; baistn wurn stiekom slacht. Vrouw van de boer komt van t berre of en zegt teegn heur man: “Goa moar noar dei-en-dei in Wildervank, want door is e.”\n“Bist gek?” zee d boer, “hou komst dr bie?”\n“Ik heb t dreumd”, zee zai. Boer lachde dr eerst wat om, moar hai is toch mit zien zeun noar Wildervank trokn. De mensn, woor t bais stoan zol, zeden, dat ze nog nooit n kou in huus had harn. De manlu zöchten de schure toun of en vernamen, dat t baist verstopt was. Politie wur dr bie hoald en toun bleek, dat dat olle mens heur dreum hailemoal klopde. De kou hebben ze weer kreegn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46218,"r":"WEV016809","p":"Schaaphok","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Floating lights are an omen of an accident, the building of houses, or the construction of roads.","i":"F.W.","o":"Deur t veen in de buurt dansten vrouger “hiplichies”. Dat kon van alles beduden: in de regel was t n veurtaikn van n ongeluk; door in t veen.\nt Kon verder betaikn, dat dr huzen of weegn komen konden.\nZo vertelden de olle mensen vrouger bie de heerd.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46225,"r":"WEV017004","p":"Stadskanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A married couple hear cries for help by a canal, but see nothing. The same cries for help ring out when a child later ends up in the water.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien oal lu hebben mie vrij wat verteld over vrouger; spokerij en zowat, door geleufden ze nogal aan. In mien jonge joarn keb ik t zulf ook leufd, moar nou loater goud bekeekn komt t mie onwoarschienlek veur. De oale mensn twiefelden dr nait aan en ze vertel-ons den de volgende verhoaln:\nJoa, mien voader en mouder muikn hail wat mit. Op n dag heurden ze “help, help” roupn bie de wieke.\nZai dr hen, moar ze zagn niks en heurden ook niks meer, toun ze dr stomp bie wazzen. n Zet loater is datzelfde helpgeroup opnei heurd en toun lag dr n kind in t woater. t Is dr wel uut hoald en leefde ook, moar de olle lu heurden et toch van te veurn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46258,"r":"WEV017404","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The noise of building an extension to a house had been heard beforehand.","i":"F.W.","o":"Klopgeestn.\nDei heb ik zulm heurd. Wie allemoal trouwens in hoes. Was n gehoamer achter t hoes. Wie hen te kiekn, moar niks te zain. Gain geluud van kleine hoamertjes, moar van mokers.\nJoarn loater is dr n stuk bie t hoes aan zet; dou heurden wie t zulfde gehoamer.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46259,"r":"WEV017405","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"After people have been pushed aside on a road, a funeral often follows. The narrator was once held fast; he would rather not tell what happened next.","i":"F.W.","o":"Van de weg. \nOp n stee bie Blijham binnen verschaiden mensen van de weg trokn; t spookde door. Mien moeke ist ook overkomen. In de regel kwam dr n begravvenis achteraan.\nt Is mie nooit overkomen, moar wel bin k n moal stief staon bleevn. \nIk luip hier op t padje veur t hoes; door bie dei boom konk opains nait wieder; t was net of ik teegn holn wur. Ain moment moar, dou was t veurbie. Hier is ook wat achteraan komen; wat dat was zeg k laiver nait. t Is altied wat lilleks.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46266,"r":"WEV017506","p":"Weite","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A screeching magpie in front of the window predicts a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Eksters.\nAs er n okster bie joe veur t glas komp schrouwen, den duurt nait laank meer of iekriegn n rouwbraif.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":21766,"r":"CJ0286A09","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A pottery pedlar is in the habit of leaving the baskets with his wares at a certain spot overnight. At night the pottery promptly starts to clink and rattle as if human hands were rummaging in it. It is a foreshadowing of what will happen the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Hil (fan de Hale to Ikkerwâld) fortelde, dêr kom froeger altyd in man fan Dokkum mei twa kuorren oan 't jok. Dêr hied er allegear diggelguod yn. Der sutele er mei. Jouns liet er dy kuorren by de minsken stean. Dan sette er wer op Dokkum ta en dan gong er oerdeis wer oan 't suteljen.\nMar op 'e plakken, dêr't hy syn kuorren nachts stean hie, dêr gong it dan altyd op in ratteljen en rinkeljen. Krekt as klauden der guon yn dat diggelguod om. Soks gebeurde yn werklikheit pas de oare deis. It wie foartjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21815,"r":"CJ0287B01","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the evening a man hears hammering very clearly, although there is nothing to be seen. The next day a new cattle shed is built. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us buorman hearde us op in joun timmerjen by him achter hûs yn 'e Feanster Mieden. Hy der hinne mar der wie neat. Der woarde alhiel net timmere, en doch hied er it klear heard.\nDe oare deis woarde dêr in féhok timmere","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21971,"r":"CJ030805","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At night a daughter hears her mother making clogs, although her mother was not going to start that work until the next day. It is a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't myn dochter sa'n twintich jier âld wie hearde se my yn 'e nacht klompmeitsjen, wylst ik der pas de oare deis mei bigong. Dat wie tjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22017,"r":"CJ031403","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening a woman sees her husband, who works in Germany, standing at the window. The woman foresees his speedy return home: a few days later he is indeed on the doorstep.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie yn 't bigjin fan ús trouwen. Myn man wie yn Dútslân oan 't wurk. Ik wist noch net hwannear't er thúskomme soe.\n'k Siet op in joun by de tafel. Dêr stie myn man foar 't glês, in bytsje roungear. Hy hie roetswart hier en in swarte snor. Sa stie er foar 't glês to sjen.\nIk draeide my even om. Doe't ik wer seach, wied er fuort.\n\"Nou komt Kei gau thús,\" sei 'k tsjin 'e buorlju, \"hwant ik haw him sjoen.\"\n't Wie èk sa. In pear dagen letter doe kaem er.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22018,"r":"CJ031404","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Half an hour before the newspaper arrives, a mother and a daughter already hear the paperboy calling. It is a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik noch yn 'e hûs wie yn 'e Falom, rôp mem us op in kear: \"Hiske, dêr ropt ien fan 'de krante!'\"\nIk sei tsjin mem: \"Gean mar hinne, mar der is neat. Nei in healûre komt de krante wol.\"\n't Wie èk sa. In healûre letter waerd der roppen: \"De krante!\" En doe wie hy der werklik.\nDat wie alle jounen sa. Ik hearde 't altyd in healûre fan tofoaren al en nou hie mem it èk heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22022,"r":"CJ031408","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"New houses are built at a place where will-o'-the-wisps can be seen. They are forerunners.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't wy famkes wienen, wienen wy jouns wol us by meester op it skoalleplein. Dat wie yn Frijstêd, tusken Broek en Ikkerwâld.\nJouns seagen wy allegear ljochtsjes. Dy forskeaten dan fan 't iene plak nei 't oare. Wy fregen meester: \"Hwat is dat?\"\nMeester sei: \"Dat binne wylde fûgels.\"\nMar ús mem sei: \"Dêr matte jim letter mar us om tinke. Op it plak, dêr't jim dy ljochtsjes sjoen ha, komme letter huzen.\"\nEn sy hat gelyk krige. 't Stiet dêr nou fol huzen.\n't Ha foarboaden west, dy ljochtsjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22034,"r":"CJ031506","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At night a widow hears knocking on the window. Once it is a drunken fellow; the other time there is nothing to be seen. It is a forerunner of something that is going to happen in the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie allinne thús. Myn man wie al dea. 't Wie sahwat tolve ûre yn 'e nacht. Ik lei op bêd. 'k Hie al even slept. Doe kloppe der ien in pear kear op 't glês. Ik gong der hinne, mar der wie net ien to sjen.\nIn dei of hwat letter woarde der wer kloppe op deselde tiid. Doe wie der wòl ien. 't Wie in dronken keardel.\n't Wie tjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22042,"r":"CJ031701","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At night a man hears hammering. A few months later he hears the same sounds when a new house is built close to where he lives. The hammering heard earlier was a forerunner.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Oerterp, dêr't wy wenne ha, hearde ik wol fjouwer, fiif nachten achter elkoar timmerjen wylst ik op bêd lei. Mar der woarde nergens timmere om ús hinne.\nIn pear maenden letter kom der in eintsje fan ús ôf in hûs. Doe hearde ik deselde lûden wer. En sy kommen fan 't selde plak. De man dy't yn dat nije hûs kom to wenjen wie Aen Bron. Hy wenne oan 'e Ljippenwyk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22045,"r":"CJ031704","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman sees will-o'-the-wisps at the place where her later house is built. It is a forerunner of the later lighting in the house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha yn Drachtster Kompenije wenne. Dêr woarde in hûs boud, dêr binne wy sels yn kom to wenjen.\nIk haw fan to foaren de ljochtsjes fan 't hûs sjoen. 't Wie yn 't bigjin fan ús trouwen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22050,"r":"CJ031801","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A married couple are woken at night by the sound of hammering. When the man goes to look, however, there is nothing to be seen. A year later the couple build a little shop onto their cottage. The same hammering can be heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy kommen to wenjen yn 'e Harkema njonken de Kristlike skoalle. Dêr hienen wy in hûske kocht, in lyts burgerhûske. Ik wie dêr ferver.\nOp in nacht sprongen ik en myn frou beide kjel oerein yn 't bêd. Der woarde timmere en wol sa dúdlik as gebeurde it flak by. Ik der ôf om to sjen. Mar der wie neat to sjen. Ik roan de hiele buorren lâns, hwant ik woe 't wite. Mar der wie neat.\nBinnen 't jier bouden wy sels in winkeltsje oan ús hûske. Doe hearden wy krekt itselde klopjen en timmerjen. Dat hie it west. Ik wie doe sa'n fiif en twintich jier.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22061,"r":"CJ031812","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wild lanterns are often forerunners of houses yet to be built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Seagen de lju froeger wylde lantearnen, dan woarde der sein: \"Dêr komt in hûs to stean.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22119,"r":"CJ032507","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If you spill coffee, winter is on its way. It is a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Antsje seit, as de kofje bot yn 't laedtsje fan 'e kofjemoune omstout, dan krije wy winter.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22146,"r":"CJ033301","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman often hears hammering. A while later a new hut is built at the same place. It was a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit hat us in kear in hutte boud by 't hûs.\nFan tofoaren sei ús mem: \"Hwat giet it der hjir jouns doch oan wei. It giet altyd mar op in timmerjen.\" Dat sei se tsjin heit. Doe sloech heit letter dat hutsje. Dat wienen de lûden dy't se heard hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22147,"r":"CJ033302","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"'Foartsjirmerij' (a foretelling sound) is a mysterious sound that announces an event. If you also see something, it is a vision.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foartsjirmerij dat is allinne mar it lûd. As men fan tofoaren hwat sjocht, dat is gjin foartsjirmerij, dat is in fisioen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22158,"r":"CJ033313","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If a white butterfly comes towards you, you will get a letter. It is a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in wite flinter op jin ynkomt dan bitsjut dat dat men in brief kriget.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22175,"r":"CJ033501","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At night a man hears the sounds of threshing in the field. It is a portent: the next day there really is threshing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Pake fortelde, 't wie faek gebeurd, dat se yn 'e nacht terskjen hearden op it lân. Dan woarde der in dei of hwat letter ek werklik tursken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22231,"r":"CJ033901","p":"Ons Belang","v":"Utr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A farmer hears hammering behind his house and goes to see what is going on. He sees nothing, but is held fast in a certain spot by an irresistible force. The man is commanded to learn the gospel. He builds a small wooden church and begins to preach the faith. Later the Reformed church was built at the same place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Warmolts, dat wie in boer. Hy wenne yn 'e Harkema op in plaets oan 'e feart nei Surhústerfean. Op in kear, doe stie er achter 't hûs. Doe gong it bot op in timmerjen. Hy gong it lân yn, hwant hy woe wite hwer't dat timmerjen wei kom. Doe kom er op it plak dêr't nou de grifformearde tsjerke stiet. Dêr woarde er tsjinhâlden. Hy koe net fierder. Der woarde tsjin him sein, hy moest dêr evangelisearje. (Der wie doe noch hielendal net in tsjerke of sokssahwat yn 'e Harkema)\nBareld Kootstra kocht dêr in stikje heide en dêr woarde in lyts houten tsjerkje op boud. It bigong mei in sneinsskoalle foar bern. Letter preke er foar de greaten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22250,"r":"CJ034001","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At night a man hears hammering. Sometimes he also sees lights floating. They are forerunners: a few years later new sheds are built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen hjir yn 'e Harkema yn in hûs oan 'e Warmoltsstrjitte. Myn man sei op in moarn: \"'k Ha de hiele nacht timmerjen heard hjir op 'e tún. En der woarde mei balken omsmiten en mei stiennen. Hjir kin wol ris hwat komme.\"\nIn pear jier letter woarden der trije greate timmerhokken boud op 'e tún. Doe wienen wy 't hiele gefal al forgetten, mar 't kom myn man wer yn 't sin.\nMyn man hat ek de ljochten fan dy hinnehokken fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22282,"r":"CJ034315","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man excitedly tells that he has seen a closed wagon with no horses in front of it. It is a vision of the future: much later the car is invented.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Roel Nicolai (Mekke Roel) sei us op in kear:\n\"Nou sil 'k jim hwat fortelle! 'k Ha in fordekte wein sjoen sûnder hynder der foar en dy ried - !\"\nLetter wienen de auto's der.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22288,"r":"CJ034321","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman often hears hammering. Later a new house is built at the same place. It was a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem hearde froeger wol us timmerjen hjir en dêr. Dan kom der letter op sokke plakken in hûs of in hok to stean. Dat gong altyd troch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22289,"r":"CJ034322","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man sees will-o'-the-wisps floating. Much later cars drive at the same place. The little lights were a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek sei se in kear: \"Ik ha allegearre ljochtsjes sjoen, dy't biweegden. Der komt hjir foroaring.\" Doe kom dêr letter in hurde wei, dêr't de auto's lâns snuorren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22290,"r":"CJ034323","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A girl thinks she already hears the baker's cart, although it does not actually arrive until a quarter of an hour later. It is a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Auke Karre kom saterdei-to-jouns altyd by ús mei bakkerswaren. Hy kom fan Eastemar of sa, dy kusten út wei.\nOp in joun sei 'k tsjin mem: \"Hark, dêr is Auke Karre.\" Ik hearde dúdlik de karre en syn gong en ek it swypkjen fan 'e koer mei bakkersguod.\nIk wie yn 'e gong om wetter op to heljen.\nMar doe't ik nei de doar ta gong wie der yn gjin fjilden of wegen in Auke Karre to sjen. Sahwat in kertier letter, dêr wied er. 't Wienen krekt deselde lûden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22291,"r":"CJ034324","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman hears hammering. Shortly afterwards a new house is built at the same place. It is a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem hat ek faek timmerjen heard op it plak dêr't se letter sels in hûs krigen ha. Myn broer wennet nou noch yn dat hûs. 't Is oan 'e Nije Wei, in lyts eintsje achterút.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22327,"r":"CJ034519","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain place many will-o'-the-wisps are visible. The floating lanterns are forerunners of car and bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op it Skeanpaed yn 'e Harkema seagen wy froeger wol wylde lantearnen yn 'e nacht. Dat bitsjutten fytsen en auto's.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22676,"r":"CJ034604","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A married couple see light shining through windowpanes. It is a vision of the future: later a new house is built at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen oan 't Wyldpaed. Ik en myn frou sieten togearre yn 'e hûs. Doe seinen wy op dy joun tsjin elkoar: \"Sjoch, dêr binne ruten. Dêr skynt ljocht troch.\" 't Wie flak by.\nMar der wienen fansels hielendal gjin ruten.\nLetter kom der op dat plak in hûs to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22750,"r":"CJ035301","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone hears hammering at night. It is a forerunner: shortly afterwards a boat is built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op Reahel wienen twa hellings. Ik roan ris by de skuorren lâns yn 'e nacht en doe gong it dêr tige op in timmerjen. Ik hearde dat dêr wol faker. Dan woarde dêr koart dêrnei wer in boat makke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22751,"r":"CJ035302","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At night someone sees a ship sailing straight across the meadow. It is a forerunner: the following year a canal is dug at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By 't Knjillisdjip seach ik us fuort by de Twizelerfeart in skip oankommen op it griene lân. 't Wie yn 'e nacht. Ik wenne dêr doe. 't Oare jiers woarde dêr in feart groeven en koart dêrnei farden de skippers der. Wy ha der sels ek fard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22752,"r":"CJ035303","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A group of young people see a ship come sailing over the land. It is a forerunner: later a canal is dug at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie us op in joun, mei in keppeltsje jongfolk by de Hamster feart. Doe seagen wy allegear dat der in skip oanfarren kom. It iene ein wie feart, 't oare ein wie lân. It skip gong it lân yn. Wy seagen it ljocht oer it lân gean. Letter ha se de feart troch groeven.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22794,"r":"CJ035607","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If the cat washes itself, you will get visitors. It is a portent.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":22824,"r":"CJ036102","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If you step on a snail, it starts to thunder.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":22842,"r":"CJ036120","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman foresees when she will get visitors.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn man en ik soenen op in kear to praten. 't Wie yn 't bigjin fan ús trouwen. Wy wennen yn Bûtenpost.\nDoe't wy op stap soenen, sei 'k tsjin myn man: \"Wy kinne better thús bliuwe, hwant it is my ynjown, dat dy en dy aenst komme sille.\"\nWy gongen fuort, mar de minsken dy't ik forwachte binne wol kom.\nIk sjoch soks wol mear. Dan wyt ik hwa't der komme sille.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22914,"r":"CJ036701","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days will-o'-the-wisps were often seen: forerunners of new roads.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger seagen wy faek wylde lantearnen oer de fjilden hinne.\nDan kommen der nije wegens, seinen se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22929,"r":"CJ036716","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In summer, a few people suddenly hear cracking as they lie under the trees by their houseboat. It is a forerunner: in winter the ice will crack when the houseboat is pulled across it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy leinen mei in woanskip yn 't wetter de kant nei de Wide Pet út, op Blauhûs by de Boelensloane.\n't Wie sahwat alve ûre op 'e joun. 't Wie yn 'e simmer. Wy wienen mei ús trijen: Myn frou en ik en Jille Pultrum. Wy leinen bûten op in gerspôlle ûnder 'e beammen.\nDêr bigong it ynienen to kreakjen om ús hinne krekt as kapten se de hiele beamwâl ôf. 't Gong fan achteren nei foaren ta.\nEn der gebeurde neat.\nDyselde winters kom der iis. Doe ha se 't woanskip oer it iis hinne lutsen nei de opslach ta. Doe wie der krekt itselde lûd, dat wy earder heard hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22931,"r":"CJ036718","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman hears someone coming, but when she goes to look there is no one. It is a forerunner: an hour later someone is at the door.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op Boelensloane is 't us gebeurd, dat de frou op in joun gedomp hearde. 't Wie dúdlik to hearren dat der ien oan kom. Wy der hinne, mar der wie net ien by de doar.\nIn ûre letter wie dyselde stap der wer. Doe wie dyselde der. 't Wie yn ús jonge tiid.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22932,"r":"CJ036719","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone hears hammering at night. It is a forerunner: later new houses are built at the same place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't wy yn 'e Boelensloane wennen ha wy us timmerjen heard yn 'e nacht. Faker as ien kear. Letter kommen der tichte by ús boukommisjehûzen to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22950,"r":"CJ036901","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Will-o'-the-wisps are forerunners of houses yet to be built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Achter de kaserne to Bûtenpost ha wy froeger wol wylde lantearnen sjoen. Dat tsjutte op nije hûzen, seinen se. Dy binne der letter ek kom. En dêr is èk in nije wei kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22974,"r":"CJ037001","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People hear the sound of milk churns and a pump in the evening. It is a portent: later a dairy factory was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen froeger yn Aldegea oan 'e wei. Achter ús wie in klearmakker. As wy jouns yn 'e hûs sieten, hearden wy de lûden fan molkbussen, dy't se delsetten en legen. En wy hearden de lûden fan in pomp. Doe wie dêr noch neat. Mar letter kom op datselde plak in molkfabryk. Dêr brûkten se earst in hânpomp, letter gong it allegear masinael.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22981,"r":"CJ037008","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A young lad foresees where he will live later on. It turns out exactly right.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik tsien jier âld wie, doe is my sjen litten hwer't ik letter komme soe to wenjen.\nIk seach tige dúdlik twa nije húskes. De doar, de finsters, it dak, it hiele model seach ik sa klear, dat ik it noait wer forgetten ha. It ienen húske is letter ôfbrutsen.\nDoe't ik troude bin 'k yn 't hûs kom to wenjen. Ik herkende it. Dat wie sahwat yn 1910.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22989,"r":"CJ037016","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If you step on ground ivy, it starts to thunder.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy mochten as bern net op 'e tongerblomkes traepje, dan bigong it to tongerjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22991,"r":"CJ037018","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps, are portents of bicycles and cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De wylde lantearnen, dy't wy froeger seagen wienen de foarboaden fan 'e fytsen en de auto's.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23011,"r":"CJ037201","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A married couple living in a shack would dearly love to live in an ordinary house. But they are very poor. One evening the woman hears the voice of the good Lord telling her she must be patient for two more years. And indeed, after two years they are able to move into a house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik gong froeger jouns faek fuort, dan wie myn frou allinne thús mei de bern. Wy wennen dan yn in houten keet en hienen it tige earmoedich. Wy woenen graech út 'e keet wei.\nOp in kear gong se de jouns op bêd. Doe hearde se in stem ta har praten. It wie ús leaven Hear. Dy sei: \"Heb nog maar twee jaar geduld. Dan komt u er onder uit.\"\nEn sa wie 't ek. Nei twa jier kommen wy út 'e keet.\nDoe kommen wy yn in hûs to wenjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23039,"r":"CJ037401","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Several people heard the sound of hammering at a certain spot, but there was nothing to be seen. Later a new house was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik bin geboaren yn 1893 op 'e Sumarreheide. 't Hûs stiet der noch. Dêr hearden heit en dy geregeld timmerjen flakby, wylst dêr doch net in timmerman oan 't wurk wie. Ek oare lju, dy't tichteby wennen, hearden it.\nLetter ha se op dat plak, dêr't de lûden weikamen in nij hûs del set. Dêr kom Foppe de Graaf yn to wenjen.\nDat hûs is nou ôfkeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23040,"r":"CJ037402","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A few men out hunting polecats once saw a light, as if it were burning in a house. But there was no house there at all, and they could not manage to get any closer to the light. Later a house was built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Houtsjepaden yn 'e Sumarreheide wienen froeger us in pear murdejagers. 't Wie yn 'e nacht. Doe't se by in wâl wienen, tochten se: \"Hea, dêr is noch in ljocht.\" Sy woenen der hinne, mar sy koenen noait by dat ljocht komme. Sy prebearren 't fan alle kanten, mar sy bleauwen wol fjouwer kampen fan dat ljocht ôf.\nIen fan dy murdejagers, dat wie Binne Hooijenga. It like krekt as stie dêr in ljocht yn 'e hûs to brânnen.\nLetter kom dêr in hûs to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23044,"r":"CJ037406","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wild lanterns were the portents of cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De wylde lantearnen dat wienen de foarboaden fan 'e auto's. Ik ha se faek sjoen yn 'e Earnewarren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23057,"r":"CJ037601","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man often saw lights in the sky in the evening. Those were the later street lamps.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit gong der jouns wol gauris út, dan seach er nei de stjerren. It gebeurde dan wol us, dat er allegear ljochten oan 'e loft gewaer woarde. Dat binne letter de ljochten (strjitlampen) oan 'e wei woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23065,"r":"CJ037609","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a woman heard lots of bangs outside. The next day lots of planks were thrown over the fence, and that made exactly the same sound.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jan Broersma syn mem wie in Hinke Pruik. 't Wie famylje fan ús. Sy wenne èk yn Ikkerwâld.\nDer wenne hjir in Heine Uiterdyk, die forkocht skalen (planken), dy krige er fan Dokkum. Dêr kom dan in weinfol skalen wie.\nOp in kear, doe moest Jan Broersma syn mem fan dy skalen brûke. Dy nachts fan tofoaren op bêd hearde hja, dat it by har op it hiem hyltyd bot klapte. De oare deis kom de wein mei skalen. Sy smieten dy skalen oer de hage, op elkoar. Doe klapte dat krektsa lyk as hja dat yn 'e nacht heard hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23068,"r":"CJ037612","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a man heard the sound of hammering. A week later a new shed was built in his back house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jan Tuinstra, hjir to Ikkerwâld, hearde op in nacht iderkear timmerjen. In wike letter woarde der by him achterhûs in great hok delset.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23091,"r":"CJ037901","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening a newly married couple hear wailing and moaning moving back and forth. But they saw nothing. Later the woman's mother came to live with them. She had a heart condition and often walked up and down the room moaning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ús heit en mem noch net sa lang troud wienen, leinen se us op in nacht op bêd en doe woarden se wekker fan in gewéklaech en in gekjirm by har yn 'e keamer. Sy slepten yn 't bêdsté. Dat gewéklaech gong hinne en wer. Dan wie 't hwat tichterby, dan wer hwat fierderôf. Sy gongen der ôf en dienen 't ljocht op, mar der wie neat to sjen.\nLetter kom beppe (mem har mem) by ús yn to wenjen. Dy hie in hartkwael. Sy hie forwiding oan 't hart. Dy roan hjir dan troch de keamer hinne en wer en dêrby joech se krekt deselde lûden dy't mem en heit doe heard ha.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23097,"r":"CJ037907","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A family once hears the sound of hammering and of planks and stones being thrown. But there was nothing to be seen. Later the back of the house was rebuilt, and exactly the same sounds could be heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in snein-to-joun siet ik mei myn âlden en ús heit syn broer by de tafel to iten. 't Wie sahwat sawn ûre.\nDoe wie 't ynienen allegear lawaei. Der woarde timmere en mei planken en stiennen smiten. Wy hearden 't allegear hiel dúdlik en woarden der kjel fan.\nDoe't wy nei 't bûthús gongen om to sjen, stienen de kij allegearre oerein, dy hienen 't èk heard, hwant oars leinen se om dy tiid altyd.\nLetter is de hiele achterein fortimmere woarn. Doe wienen der krekt deselde lûden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23098,"r":"CJ037908","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A boy once heard the sound of hammering. A few months later a room was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek op in kear, doe kom myn broer fan 'e jongelingsforiening thús. 't Wie sahwat tsien ûre op 'e joun. Hy soe op bêd, mar doe wie 't ynienen allegear lawaei. Der woarde mei stiennen en latten smiten en der woarde timmere. It lûd wie op it plak dêr't er sahwat wie. Hy gong net earder op bêd foardat it lûd út wie. Hy stie der nei to harkjen en wachte oant it ophâldde. In pear maend letter is der op dat plak in keammerke timmere woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23099,"r":"CJ037909","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A girl once saw people unloading flour from a ship. But there was no water there at all. Not long afterwards the canal was dug there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn mem wie in Formsma. Sy gong by Aefke op it naeijen, doe wie 't in great fanke. Aefke wenne op Burgumerdaem, op Ûleflecht. Doe fortelde Aefke har: \"Ik en myn jonges seagen hjir tsjalken lizzen. Dêr wienen se op oan 't moallossen. Wy seagen de minsken dragen. 't Wie allegearre ljocht.\"\nDêr wie doe gjin wetter. Letter (ridlik gau) woarde de feart forlein en kom dêr in brêge, dêr't de skippen ek leinen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23152,"r":"CJ038402","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A newly married man had put up a hedge but had not got round to the boards, as he had to go and work on the Frisian clay. When he came home after a week, the fencing was finished. His wife said that one evening she had heard a lot of noise outside and had been very frightened. The man went outside to finish the last bit himself. His wife came to tell him that it was exactly the same sound she had heard before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik troude sa'n sechstich jier lyn mei in wyfke fan Hurdegaryp. It fanke hie oars noch noait hwat dien as by de huzen lâns naeije.\nWy krigen hjir in nij hûs op 'e Tike.\nIk moest nei de Fryske klaei ta to meanen, it wyfke bleau sa lang thús.\nIk hie de wyks fan to foaren in hage by de hiele reed lâns boud. Doe soe dêr in skroat bovenoan. Mar dat hie 'k net mear oan tiid hawn, doe wie 'k nei de klaei ta rekke. Ik bleau in wike wei. Doe't ik thús kom, siet de skroat der oan. Dat hienen oaren wylst foar my dien. Der lei noch in bosk skroaten bûtendoar, dy hienen se oerhâlden. Dêr achter stie in skuorke, dêr siet neat yn.\n\"Hoe hat it dy foldien?\" frege ik myn wyfke.\nHja hie har suster út Hurdegaryp dy wyks by har hawn. \n\"Net bêst,\" sei se, \"wy ha hjir hwat bileefd.\"\nHja sliepten togearre yn 't bêdsté tsjin 'e muorre oan. Op in nacht hienen guon mei planken tsjin elkoar oan slein op 'e telle en se tsjin 'e muorre oan set.\n\"Wy wienen sa binaud,\" sei se, \"dat wy krûpten djip ûnder 'e tekkens.\"\n\"'t Hat forbeelding west\", sei ik.\n\"Né, wier net,\" sei se, \"freegje myn suster mar.\"\nIk kom bûtendoar en sette de skroaten tsjin 'e middelmuorre oan. Dat die 'k twa by twa. Se klapten tsjin elkoar oan.\nDoe kom myn wyfke nei bûten ta en sy sei: \"Dat binne de lûden, dy't wy heard ha.\" 't Wie foartjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23355,"r":"CJ038502","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the past, the narrator's family often had to carry out emergency slaughtering at other people's homes. Often there was already a knock before the people had even reached the narrator's house. This happened both at night and during the day. Sometimes the sound was like a stick tapping on the window. Then a little later someone would come with a stick and tap it on the window. Sometimes a fortnight passed between the omen and the actual event, but it always came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha hjir jierrenlang de needslachting hawn. As der hwat slachte wurde moest wienen dat faek ûnforwachte needgefallen. Hwat binne wy faek even fan toforen kloppe woarn. Mar dan wie der noch neat. Even letter wie de man der sels dy 't kloppe. 't Gebeurd wol yn 'e nacht, mar ek wol us oerdei. Soms wie 't it tikjen fan in stok op it glês. Dan hie sa 'n ien even letter ek echt in stok by him, dêr 't er mei op 't glês tikke. 't Wienen altyd needgefallen. Soms wie der ek wol us in tiid fan fjirtsjin dagen tusken, mar it kom altyd nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23373,"r":"CJ038801","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wild lanterns of the past were omens of the later bicycle lamps.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 'e Hegebrechsterloane yn Oerterp wie in wylde lantearne. Dêr wienen se allegear bang foar. Letter kommen dêr fytslampen. Dêr hat it foartsjirmerije fan west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23384,"r":"CJ038901","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wild lanterns are portents of new houses.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op it plak dêr't de wylde lantearnen út gongen, kom in nij hûs to stean. De wylde lantearnen wienen de foarboaden fan nije huzen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23401,"r":"CJ039002","p":"Siegerswoude","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wild lanterns that people used to see flying around are the later cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger seagen wy allegear ljochtsjes fleanen om ús hinne. Dat wienen wylde lantearnen. Dat binne nou de auto's mei har ljochten. Dy fleane krekt sa.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23402,"r":"CJ039003","p":"Siegerswoude","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Two men once saw a great light. Later a new house was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer wie hjir ris by ús. Doe seach myn man samar ynienen in ljocht achter ús hûs. \"Sjoch, dêr achter is wer in ljocht\", sei er tsjin myn broer. Hy woe der mei myn broer hinne, mar sy ha 't net dien. Letter stie der op dat plak in great hûs. Dat hie dat ljocht west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23403,"r":"CJ039004","p":"Siegerswoude","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once saw a great light next to a house. Later a lamp post was put there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha hjir njoggen en fjirtich jier yn dit hûs wenne.\nAuke Bottema wie de boer, dy't hjir njonken ús wenne. Dy sei us in kear tsjin ús: \"Der stiet in great ljocht by jimme op 'e hoeke.\"\nHy hat gelyk krigen. Dêr stiet nou in lantearne by de hekke, dy't de hiele nacht trochbrânt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23518,"r":"CJ039801","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a man heard the sound of hammering. But there was nothing to be seen. Later the house was rebuilt.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in nacht hearde heit timmerjen en klopjen. Hy gong der ôf en nei de jonges ta. Hy sei: \"Hwat wie dat? Hwat dogge jimme?\"\nMar de jonges leinen to sliepen, der wie alhielendal neat. Doe't heit op bêd gong bigong it timmerjen en sa wer opnij. Letter is 't hûs fan binnen fortimmere woarn. 't Gebeurde yn 'e Smoarhoeke yn 'e Harkema.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23527,"r":"CJ039810","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once thought he had seen a covered wagon with no horses in front of it. It was going terribly fast. Later the cars came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Roel fan 'e Harkema sei, hy hie in fordekte wein sjoen sûnder hynders der foar en 't gong hurd, hurd, hurd. Letter kommen de auto's.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23570,"r":"CJ040006","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A mother could always tell from the lamp glass that her sons would get another summons from the police. In her coffee cup she could always see whether the police were coming. And if the coffee in the saucer moved back and forth a lot, they would get hard words.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wienen froeger net fan dy makke knapen en krigen wolris mei de plysje to dwaen.\nIk hear ús mem noch sizzen: \"Der sit wer in brief oan 'e lampe. Der komt wer in dachfaerding oan foar de jonges.\"\nDan siet der in tútsje oan 't lampeglês.\nSy seach ek wolris yn in kofjekopke. \"Der komme ek twa plysjes,\" sei se, \"jim ha fansels wer hwat útheve.\" It kom altyd wol aerdich út.\nAs de kofje bot hinne en wer gong wie yn 't laedtsje, dan krigen wy hurde wyn, sei se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23609,"r":"CJ040306","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Children always heard their mother's footsteps in the hall and on the mat before she was actually home.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem gong noch wol gau us to praten nei de Burgumer Nijstêd, dêr't har âlden kwekerije hienen.\nFoardat se wer thús wie, hearden wy ús mem har fuotten al yn 'e gong slepen, en op it matsje ôffeijen.\nDan seinen wy: \"Dêr is mem ek wer.\" Mar dan wie 't sa net. In skoft letter kom se earst werom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23613,"r":"CJ040310","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"An old man often saw wild lanterns. Those were the later bicycle lamps.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Fije turfskipper wenne op Uleflecht ûnder Sumar. Dy seach faek wylde lantearnen. Dat wienen de lettere fytsljochten, sei er.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23700,"r":"CJ041102","p":"Peize","v":"Dr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wild lanterns that people used to see were the portents of the later bicycle lamps.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De wylde lantearnen dy't wy froeger seagen, dat wie foartjirmerij. Dat wienen de lampen fan 'e fytsen, dy't letter kommen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23724,"r":"CJ041301","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a man heard wooden planks being dragged. Half a year later wood was delivered at night, and the sound was really there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr't âlde Jille Pultrum wenne, wenne earder syn heit Durk. Dy lei op in nacht op bêd, doe hearde er planken ratteljen.\nIn healjier letter troude Bareld Pultrum, in broer fan Durk. Doe moesten se hout leegje yn 'e nacht. Doe hearde Durk krekt itselde lûd wer, mar nou wie 't werklikheit. Doe kom Bareld Pultrum dêr to wenjen. Dêr bouden se in hûs foar.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23742,"r":"CJ041501","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once heard people singing in the church. But the church was empty. The next day they sang exactly the same psalm in the church that the man had heard the day before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alle Murdtsje wie mollefanger en wenne op it Hegelân. Hy kom faek by ús, wy wienen kammeraten. Op in saterdeijoune let wienen wy noch yn 'e Jistrumer buorren. Doe sei 'k tsjin Alle: \"Hark, dêr sjonge se yn 'e tsjerke.\" De hiele tsjerke siet fol sjongende minsken. De manljus- en frouljuslûden wienen bêst to ûnderskieden. Mar de tsjerke wie leech fansels. 't Wie der allegear tsjuster.\nDe oare moarns songen se dêr yn tsjerke krekt deselde psalm, dy't ik heard hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23808,"r":"CJ042109","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening a woman heard groaning in the cowshed, but there was nothing to be seen. A few days later she heard exactly the same groaning again. It was a cow lying there groaning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear kom ik let thús. 'k Rin de skuordoarren foarby. Ik tink: \"Forrek, hwat is der doch yn dy âld skuorre?\" Ik hearde gekreun. Doe der hinne to sjen. Der wie neat. \"Eigenaerdich\", tocht ik.\nDe mandei-to-moarns dêrop kom ik by de froulju wei. Ik hearde wèr itselde gekreun. Ik kom mei de tilbry thús. Itselde gekreun.\nDoe't ik seach, lei der in koe to kreunen yn 'e skuorre. Hy wie binnen de ûre dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23813,"r":"CJ042114","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One must never remove a stork's nest; it brings luck.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In oaijefaersnêst bringt gelok oan, dat mat men noait útroegje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23827,"r":"CJ042210","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a ship riveter heard the sound of riveting. But there was nothing to be seen. The next day riveting really took place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw us praet mei in man út Wynskoat, dat wie in scheepklinker, dy fortelde my, hy wie op in skip en dêr woarde nachts klonken. It wie sa dúdlik to hearren. Mar doe't se seagen wie der neat to dwaen. De oare deis waerd der echt klonken. 't Wie foartjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23841,"r":"CJ042402","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people thought houses would be built on the heath because they saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, ghostly lights) there. That did happen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oer 't heidefjild seagen se froeger faek wylde lantearnen. Se mienden dat dêr huzen komme soenen. Dat is ek gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23944,"r":"CJ043203","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Once, at a certain spot, a woman heard psalms being sung. Later a Reformed church was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us beppe wie in kear nei de Tille (= Kootstertille) ta om bargetermen op to heljen. Ik kom har in ein tomjitte. Doe't wy yn Droegeham wienen, sei se: \"Hark, sa binne se hjir oan 't psalmsjongen.\" Ik hearde neat. Mar beppe hie 't wol goed, hwant in skoft letter ha se op datselde plak in Kristlik grifformearde tsjerke delset.\nDer lei doe in stien, dêr ha wy noch op sitten, doe't beppe dat sei. Ik wie doe acht jier. 't Gebeurde yn 1903.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23945,"r":"CJ043204","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once saw something burning fly through the sky. She predicted that in the future cars would fly through the air. Those turned out to be the later aeroplanes.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek in kear, dat wie yn dyselde snuorje en ek yn 'e Ham, doe fleach der us hwat troch de loft en dat brânde.\nDoe sei beppe: \"Der fljogge aenst auto's troch de loft. Tink us om myn sizzen.\" Dat ha de lettere flychmesines west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23946,"r":"CJ043205","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People regularly heard clearly that someone was coming to the door. But when they went to look, there was no one. Yet later that day someone always did come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha 't faek hawn, dat wy dúdlik hearden dat der ien by de doar kom. Mar as wy der hinne gongen wie der net ien to sjen. Mar men koe der fêst fan op oan dat dyselde in skoftsje letter kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23960,"r":"CJ043301","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once heard hammering at a place where nothing could be seen. Shortly afterwards a new farmhouse was built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hier woonde een zekere Douwe Stavasius. Die zei op een keer tegen ons: \"Ik heb hier vlakbij timmeren gehoord. Een eindje die kant út. Hier komt in nije boerderij, der werd timmerd.\"\nNa korte tijd kwam der in nije boerderij. Hier vlakbij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24006,"r":"CJ043616","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Animals are often clairvoyant. A dog knows two hours in advance that a thunderstorm is coming. Then it is restless and frightened.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dieren binne faek heldersynde.\nSa wyt in houn twa ûren fan tofoaren al as der tonger komt. Dan is er ûnrêstich en binaud.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24015,"r":"CJ043709","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a man saw a wagon driving without a horse in front of it. That happened a good thirty years before there were cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hindrik Gerks Hoekstra seach us op in nacht in wein riden sûnder hynder der foar. It wie yn 'e foarige ieu, wol tritich jier foardat der auto's kommen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24039,"r":"CJ044001","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People once saw a little light at a certain spot. But when they came closer, there was nothing to be seen. Later a house was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 'e Boppewei yn 'e Westerein, dêr seagen guon ris in ljochtsje. Doe gongen se der op ta, mar doe wie der neat to sjen. Letter kom dêr op datselde plak in stjelpke to stean en dat stiet der nou noch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24040,"r":"CJ044002","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"By the railway in Westereinde people sometimes saw a wilde lantaarn (wild lantern, ghostly light). Later a new house was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By 't spoar yn 'e Westerein seagen se ris in wylde lantearne. Letter kom der op dat plak in hûs to stean. Dat hûs stiet der nou noch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24042,"r":"CJ044004","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On a very narrow road people once saw a wide wagon of peat pass by. In reality that was quite impossible. Later a proper road was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't wy earst by 't spoar wennen wie 't noch in hiel smel paedtsje. Doe seagen guon op in kear dat dêr in wein lâns ried mei lange turven der yn.\nDat koe fansels net, dêr wie 't paedtsje fiersto smel foar, mar sy hienen 't dúdlik sjoen.\n't Wie foartjirmerij. Letter is 't in wei woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24060,"r":"CJ044101","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On the path from Zwagerveen to de Triemen a foal with a wooden head always haunts at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der rint in paedtsje fan Sweagerfean nei de Triemen ta, dêr roan by nacht altyd in fôlle mei in houten kop.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24064,"r":"CJ044105","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot people often saw a great many lights and often heard knocking. Later new houses were built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir njonken ús op 'e Saedkamp, dêr seagen se froeger in hiele protte ljochten en sy hearden dêr gedurich klopjen. Dêr soe in protte boud wurde, waerd der ornearre. En dat is ek gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24140,"r":"CJ044406","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people sometimes still saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, ghostly lights). Those were the lights that are now on bicycles and cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wienen froeger noch wol gau us wylde lantearnen. Dat wienen de ljochten, dy't nou oan 'e fytsen en de auto's sitte.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24181,"r":"CJ044601","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People once heard noise as if there was fighting, but there was nothing at all to be seen. They thought a pub would come there. Later a coffeehouse was built. Once there was a terrible fight there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e hoeke fan 'e skieding ûnder Grinzer Pein hawwe guon ris heard dat it der dêr slim oan wei gong. Der waerd fochten en rúzje makke, der waerd slein en houd, it wie raer.\nMar der wie hielendal neat. Doe ha se sein: \"Dêr komt in kroech.\"\nLetter is dêr in kofjehûs kom by de tramhalte. Doe is dêr ris in kear freeslik fochten woarn. Sy kapten mei de seinen yn elkoar om. Dêr wie ik doe sels by.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24183,"r":"CJ044603","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Whenever people found a cat in front of their door, something always happened. Someone died of the cold or a child fell ill. That cat was a witch.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn froeger tiid is 't gebeurd, dat der ergens yn 'e Grinzer Pein by minsken hyltyd in fremde kat by de doar siet. Ik wie doe noch mar in jonge. As dy kat der wie, gebeurde der altyd hwat. Der stoar in kou of ien fan 'e bern waerd siik of sokssahwat. Dat die dy kat, dat wie in tsjoenster. It wie de mem fan Sierd Polderdyk dy't it die. As de frou de kat by harren op it hiem seach, sei se: \"De kat is der wer, nou gebeurt der wer hwat.\" Sy ha krânsen foun yn 'e kessens, dy ha se forbrând. Dy hie Sierd syn mem der ek yntsjoend.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24196,"r":"CJ044802","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, ghostly lights). That could mean all sorts of things: new houses, new roads, bicycles, cars, street lamps, etc.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanheit seach froeger wylde lantearnen. Dat koe fan alles bitsjutte: nije huzen, nije wegens, fytsen, auto's, strjittelantearnen en gean sa mar troch.\nSkoanheit wie der skruten foar.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24218,"r":"CJ045006","p":"Peize","v":"Dr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days a woman always saw lots of wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, ghostly lights) on the dyke at Murmwoude. She claimed that Murmwoude would later turn into a town. The place did not become a town, but if you stand on the dyke in the evening now, there are so many lights to be seen that it does look like a town.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Skoanheit syn mem, dy wenne yn Moarmwâld. Dy sei: \"As ik jouns op 'e dyk stean, dan binne it allegear ljochtsjes.\" Dat wienen de wylde lantearnen.\n\"Dat is in foarboade,\" sei se, \"Moarmwâld sil in stêd wurde.\"\nSy hat wol hwat gelyk krige. It plak hat him ôfgryslik útwreide en as men jouns alle ljochten sjocht fan 'e lampen, liket it wol in stêd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24223,"r":"CJ045011","p":"Peize","v":"Dr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In Groningen some farms were haunted. At night the wagon sometimes rattled across the floor. That was a forewarning of the bustle of the coming day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Grinslân wienen plaetsen, dêr spokke it. De wein rattele dêr soms yn 'e nacht op 'e telle om. Dat wie de foarboade fan 'e drokte fan 'e kommende deis.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24234,"r":"CJ045109","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, ghostly lights) are often forewarnings of, for example, bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen seagen wy froeger faek. It wienen swevende, swermende ljochten, de foarboaden fan fytsljochten ensa.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24251,"r":"CJ045201","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People living in a caravan hear their neighbours hammering at night. It is a forewarning of a new house to be built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen yn in woanwein oan 'e Suderhegewei by Drachten. Dêr hearden wy en ús buorlju nachts timmerjen en klopjen flakby. Wy seinen tsjin elkoar: \"Dêr komt grif in nij hûs.\" 't Wie sahwat yn 1924. 't Selde jiers woarde dêr in nije boereplaets delset. Dy plaets is der nou wer wei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24293,"r":"CJ045418","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the shed of people who hire out cars, the cars start humming by themselves at night. It is a forewarning. Ticking can often be heard too. That is also a forewarning: a house will later be renovated.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hè buurlui had op Kollumerzwaag, die ferhuurden auto's. As die auto's in de schure stonden, dan begonnen se in de nacht te brommen en een lawaai te maken. En der kwam toch niemand bij. Se deden 't út haar sels. De deuren waren op slot.\nEn dan begonnen se ook al te tikken. Op 't laatst klopte 't overal. Ik sei: \"Dat is een teken, dat 't huus fermaakt wordt.\"\nEn dat is later ook gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24315,"r":"CJ045702","p":"Peize","v":"Dr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, ghostly lights) turn out to be a forewarning of the later street lighting.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir flakby wie froeger in âld modderwei. Dêr seagen wy froeger wylde lantearnen, soms wolris acht tagelyk. \"Dat is foartjirmerije,\" seinen se, \"dat komt letter nei.\" En dat is ek gebeurd. Der is nou in hiele rige strjitlantearnen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24328,"r":"CJ045801","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man sees four lamps burning and suspects that a school will be built. No school came, but a house for four families did. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Lytse Wytske sei yndertiid, der soe in skoalle op 'e Bulten komme. Hja hie fjouwer lampen brânnen sjoen, dat wie fierstofolle foar in hûs. Mar doe setten se letter op dat plak in hûs del foar fjouwer gesinnen, de saneamde 'malmoune'. Dat hat it west. Sy ha 't hûs letter ôfbrând, doe wie 't alhiel útwenne. (De jonges seinen doe al: der komt in skoalle op 'e Bulten. Wytske hat it sjoen)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24329,"r":"CJ045802","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Near a meadow a woman clearly hears sounds as if stones are being thrown. It is an omen: the meadow later became a brick-paved road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem en dy moesten froeger Sytske al us in kear ophelje. Dy wenne by 't monumint op 't Bomkleaster.\nHja soe komme to naeijen, mar sy koe sels de naeimesine net drage. Mem droech de naeimesine. De krúswei moesten se passeare, dy wie doe noch net forhurde.\nDe oare deis fortelde mem, se hienen dêr by de krúswei sa bot mei stiennen smiten, dat hie se dúdlik heard. 't Wie de jouns, goed acht ûre west. Ridlik gau dêrnei is de Krúswei in klinkerwei woarn. Dat hie mem doe heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24342,"r":"CJ045815","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, ghostly lights) are a forewarning of the later bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De wylde lantearnen, dy't wy froeger seagen, dat ha de lettere fytslampen west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24349,"r":"CJ045901","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One Sunday evening a woman very clearly sees a man with a lantern in his hand surveying the meadow. It is a voorgezicht (a vision of the future): later the land is surveyed and new houses are built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir njonken hienen se froeger perseeltsjelân. Us muoike wenne oan 'e oare kant de wei, dy seach op in snein-to-joun hiel dúdlik, dat der in man mei in lantearne yn 'e hân it perseeltsjelân deltrêdde. Hy meat it út. Doe wist noch gjin ien fan hwat.\nMuoike woe ris sjen hwat foar keardel as dat wie. Sy gong der út, mar doe't se op 't lân kom, wie der net ien. It wie foartjirmerij.\nIn skoft letter kommen dêr huzen to stean, mar earst ha se 't lân opmetten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24372,"r":"CJ046101","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At night a man clearly hears beams being thrown about. It is a forewarning of later carpentry work on a new house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit hat wenne oan 'e Lange wiken. Op in nacht hearde hy dúdlik dat der mei balken smiten woarde, net sa fier ôf.\nNei forrin fan tiid hearde er deselde lûden wer, mar doe hearden se it allegear, hwant doe gong 't op in timmerjen oan in nij hûs dat dêr set woarde oan 'e Lange wyk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24446,"r":"CJ046407","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears sounds of hammering, but there is nothing to be seen. It is an omen: later a house is built on the same spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit timmere wol ûnderhâns. Op in kear hearde er op in plak timmerjen, dêr wie neat to sjen. Doe sei heit: \"Hjir njonken giet it ek op in timmerjen, dêr komt skielk ek in hûs.\"\nDat is nei kom. By Ruerd Klaver woarde in great hok boud. 't Hûs wie to lyts. Ruerd Klaver wenne njonken myn folk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24450,"r":"CJ046504","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When a mermaid comes near a ship's rudder, bad weather is on its way. Porpoises are also forewarnings of storms.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De mearmin wie wol ris achter op it roer kom. Dan wie 't folk bang, hwant dan krigen se min waer.\nDy mearminnen joegen geluten.\nAs de brúnfisken tusken de kribben kommen, dan woarde it need waer, fortelde er.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24453,"r":"CJ046507","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, ghostly lights) are said to be forewarnings of the later car and bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sy seinen wol dat de wylde lantearnen de lettere lampen fan auto's en fytsen wienen. Men sjocht se nou noait mear.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24469,"r":"CJ046801","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears sounds of hammering, but there is nothing to be seen. It is a forewarning: later new houses are built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Lange loane yn 'e Westerein - nou Verlengde Stationsstraat - hearde ik ris op in nacht om in ûre of ien hinne timmerjen. Ik woe der mear fan witte en bleau stean. Doe bleau it stil. Doe't ik fierder stapte bigong it wer. Stie 'k wer stil dan wie 't wer oer. Doe't ik de kant út gong dêr't it lûd wei kom wie dêr neat to sjen. Letter binne dêr allegearre nije huzen kom. It sil sa'n tritich jier lyn wêze dat ik dat hearde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24470,"r":"CJ046802","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man suddenly hears shouting, although there is nothing to be seen. It is a forewarning: the next day he hears the same sounds when a boy who cannot swim almost drowns.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 'e Boskwei yn 'e Westerein wie snein-to-jouns altyd in keppeltsje jongfolk op it Singeltsje. Sy sieten dêr in soad to kaertspyljen, sy wienen ek wol oan 't knikkertsjen om sinten en oan 't streekjesmiten en sy dobbelen dêr ek wol. 't Wie in sânpaed.\nDoe't ik dêr in joun us op 'e Boskwei wie, hearde ik ynienen ien razen. 't Wienen rare geluten. Ik sjen en sjen mar ik koe neat gewaer wurde.\nDe oare deis wienen dyselde geluten der wer. Mar doe wie 't echt. Doe lei dêr in jonge yn 't wetter, dy't net swemme koe. Hy wie omtrint forsûpt, mar Jan Durks van Kammen hat him noch krekt op 't lêste nipperke ret. Hy sleepte him oer 't skouder der út. 't Wie Ielt de Jong, in soan fan Bouke Minke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24502,"r":"CJ046918","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A number of people hear the mill creaking. According to two women it is a forewarning of something bad.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hindrik en Durkje en frou van Peursen wennen njonken elkoar hjir op 'e Iest. Dy hearden op in kear de moune kreakjen. Sa mar út himsels. Neffens dy beide froulju soe der hwat slims achter wei komme.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24510,"r":"CJ047102","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If a magpie comes into the yard, you will get visitors.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":24511,"r":"CJ047103","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people often saw green lights. They were the forewarnings of the later tram lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't de tram der noch net wie, seagen de minsken al gleone ljochten. Dat wienen de ljochten fan 'e tram.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24512,"r":"CJ047104","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone hears sounds of hammering, although there is nothing to be seen. It is a forewarning: later a new house is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir dwars oer woarde alle jounen timmere. Mar as men der by kom wie der neat to sjen. Letter kom dêr in hûs to stean. Doe seinen de minsken: \"Sjoch, dàt hat dat timmerjen west.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24575,"r":"CJ047606","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, ghostly lights) are forewarnings of new houses to be built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As 't winter wie seagen wy soms froeger in wylde lantearne op 'e heide. Dan seinenn wy: \"Sjoch, dêr is in lampe.\" \"Dêr komt skielk in hûs\", sei mem dan. En dat kom ek nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24576,"r":"CJ047607","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wild lanterns are harbingers of houses yet to be built. Will-o'-the-wisps are also often seen before the houses are there. If they bob up and down hard, they are harbingers of the later bicycle lights. If they move calmly, the lights mean nothing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Willem Koekoek wenne yn 'e Sweagemer Mieden. Dy sei us in kear tsjin ús: \"Hjir komme skielk forskate nije huzen. 'k Ha allegear wylde lantearnen sjoen.\" 't Is neikom.\nWy seagen sokke ljochtsjes jouns ek wol foar de huzen. As 't stadich gong mei 't biwegen, dan bitsjutte it neat, seinen se. Mar as 't hurd gong, dan seinen se, 't wienen wylde lantearnen. Dan woarden it fytslampen of sa yn letter tiid.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24591,"r":"CJ047705","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wild lanterns are harbingers of the later bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De wylde lantearnen wienen de earsten dy't birichten dat de fytslantearnen komme soenen. 't Wienen de foartsjirmen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24659,"r":"CJ049102","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A married couple hear the sound of carpentry at night, although there is nothing to be seen. It is an omen: later a new house is built on the same spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wennen minsken yn Grinzer Pein. De man en de frou leinen op bêd. 't Wie yn 'e nacht. Doe sei de iene tsjin 'e oare: \"Hwat giet it hjir dochs op in timmerjen.\"\nSy hearden klear dat der mei planken smiten woarde.\nSy hienen mar ien buorman, dy wenne oan 'e lofter kant. Mar it timmerjen kaem fan 'e rjochtse kant, en dêr stienen gjin huzen.\nHja der ôf om to sjen hwat it wie. Mar doe wie 't stil en der wie neat to sjen.\nDeselde lûden wienen der nacht op nacht.\nIn goed jier neitiid stie dêr in arbeidershûs. Hja hienen it timmerjen fantofoaren heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24661,"r":"CJ049104","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man often goes poaching with his dog and a relative. After a night of poaching the man goes home; the relative looks for shelter elsewhere. As the man lies in bed, he hears knocking on the window. He recognises it as his relative's 'tap': long-short-short-short. Because his dog does not bark, the man concludes that no one can be at the house. The same scene repeats itself. Six weeks later there is knocking again one morning. This time the relative has really come home. The tapping in the night was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie in houn, dêr gong ik nachts faek mei it fjild yn. Ik gong faek to stropen en ek wol gauris to murdzjen. Op in kear hie 'k der op út west mei in famyljelid fan my. It hountsje dat wy hienen wie tige waeks. Dat blafte altyd fuortdaelks as der ien oan kom.\nYn 'e nacht gong ik wer mei myn hountsje nei hûs ta.\nMyn famyljelid socht ergens oars ûnderdak. Doe't ik dy nachts op bêd lei, hearde ik klopjen op 't glês. 't Wie de tik fan dat famyljelid fan my. - vvv. Ien fikse tik, dy't langer oanhâlden waerd en trije koarte tikjes.\nMar it nuvere wie, de houn, dy't yn in kûle lei bûten tsjin 'e muorre oan, joech net in kik.\nIk sei tsjin myn maet: \"Der wurdt kloppe.\"\n\"Ik hear neat\", sei er.\nMar ik gong der ôf om to sjen. Né, der wie neat en de houn lei moai yn 'e kûle. Ik gong wer op bêd.\nIn skoft letter waerd der wèr kloppe. Doe hearde myn maet it ek. \"Hark,\" sei er, \"der wurdt kloppe.\"\nIt wie wer it tikjen fan myn famyljelid. Mar de houn bleau ek dizze kear stil. Wy hienen 't nou allebeide heard. Ik der wèr út. Neat to sjen. 't Hountsje lei stil yn syn kûle. Der wie net ien.\nIt wie sahwat seis wiken letter, op in moarne bitiid.\nDoe woarde der wèr kloppe op 't selde glês. Deselde tikken. Wy leinen noch op bêd.\nDoe stie myn famyljelid dêr. Hy wie wer thúskom.\nDe houn blafte.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24668,"r":"CJ049202","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman sees little lights floating through the air. It is a harbinger of the later bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn âlde beppe wie op in joun bûtendoar.\n\"Bern,\" sei se, \"dêr komme allegearre ljochtsjes oan. En dy komme dit allegear út. Dat bitsjut hwat.\"\nLetter kommen de fytsen der. 't Wienen krekt deselde ljochtsjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24679,"r":"CJ049213","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears sounds coming from the small lake. He suspects that something is about to happen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De Blaudobbe is yn 'e Houtigehage. Alde Taeke hearde dêr alle jounen geraes yn dy dobbe. \"Dêr mat noch us hwat yn gebeure\", sei Taeke. Mar ik wyt net as der al us hwat gebeurd is.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24698,"r":"CJ049305","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Before the war broke out, a man had already seen troops of people: a vision of the future. The same man also often went door to door with strange wares. He also often went door to door singing New Year's songs.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining seach, foardat de oarloch útbriek, hiele troepen minsken, dy't nei Drachten tasetten.\nBoardzer roan mei in opstoppe keal mei twa koppen by de doarren lâns. Ek mei fremde aeijen. Ek mei in skip yn 'e flesse. Hy gong ek to nijjierroppen. Dan sei er hiele stikken op. Kom er by kristlike minsken, dan sei er in kristlik fers op, by oare minsken in werelds fers.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24705,"r":"CJ049401","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot will-o'-the-wisps can be seen. They are harbingers of the later car and bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e wei fan Feanwâlden nei Dokkum seagen wy froeger in rige ljochtsjes. Letter wienen dat de ljochten fan 'e fytsen en de auto's. Dy hienen wy al jierren fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24707,"r":"CJ049403","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A group of children often see will-o'-the-wisps in the dark. It is a harbinger of the later bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik bin geboaren yn Ikkerwâld, mar ik wie al gau wees en bin doe yn Moarmwâld greatbrocht. Tusken de Broekster strietwei en Moarmwâld, dêr wennen wy, in eintsje fan 'e wei ôf. As bern sieten wy jouns faek yn 't tsjuster foar 't finster. Dan fleagen der fise-ferse ljochtsjes op 'e greate wei foarby. Mar dy wienen der yn werkelikheit net. Dat hat foartjirmerij west. Letter wienen dat de fytsljochten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24845,"r":"CJ049801","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman has a sick daughter. One time in her house she suddenly has to turn around. Something catches her attention, but she cannot see what it is. The next day a stretcher is carried into her house because her sick daughter has to be taken to hospital. That is what the woman saw the day before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn dochter wie ris by my, doe woarde se siik. Doe't ik ris in kear yn 'e hûs kom, woarde ik yn 'e keamer keard. Ik seach net hwat it wie, dat my kearde. De oare deis moest myn dochter opnom wurde yn 't sikenhûs. Doe brochten se in draechbaer by ús yn 'e hûs. Dat wie it ding dat ik de foarige deis sjoen hie en dat my kearde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24846,"r":"CJ049802","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman asks what 'those three calves' are doing in the stable. The stable, however, is empty. It is a vision of the future: the next day there are three calves in the stable.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De dochter fortelt: \"Fan 'e wike kom mem hjir by ús yn 'e stâl. Doe sei se yn har sels: 'Hwat dogge dy trije keallen hjir?'\nIk hearde dat en ik sei: 'Hoe komt mem der by, de stâl is ommers leech.' Mar de oare deis sette myn man trije keallen op stâl. Sy hie 't wol goed sjoen.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24847,"r":"CJ049803","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman hears the sound of carpentry. It is an omen: later the house is renovated.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie yn Westergeast útfanhûs by myn dochter. Doe hearde ik dêr timmerjen en der waerd mei balken smiten ensa. Ik sei: \"Hjir sil skielk hwat gebeure.\"\nMyn dochter Klaske woe 't earst net sizze. Sy woenen 't stil hâlde, net ien mocht it noch wite, mar de saek soe fortimmere wurde. En 't is ek gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24864,"r":"CJ049915","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wild lanterns are often seen at a certain spot. It is a harbinger: later new houses are built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Earnewarren wienen froeger faek wylde lantearnen. Dat binne letter allegear huzen woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24865,"r":"CJ049916","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Two men see a tram running, while there is no tramline yet, or even a road. It is a vision of the future. Later roads are built. The men suspect that what they saw back then were buses. Those have yet to start running.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie in feint, dat wie Tseard Jongsma, dy hat njoggen jier lang by my tahâlden. Op in kear doe wied er achter hûs, doe rôp er: \"Kom hjir us even.\" Dat is nou in fiif en fjirtich jier lyn. 't Wie yn Aldegea.\nIk dêr hinne.\n\"Sjochst wol?\" sei er.\nDer ried in tram achter ús lâns, dy gong op Garyp yn. Wy seagen him krekt salang nei as wy koenen.\nDer wie doe net in wei of trambaen.\n't Is nou allegear gâns foroare. Der rinne nou twa wegen hinne. De trêdde wei binne se mei oan 'e gong en dy rint de richting út, dêr't wy doe dy tram sjoen ha. It ha grif autobussen west. 't Wie foartjirmerij. 't Mat noch neikomme.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24867,"r":"CJ049918","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot the sound of carpentry can often be heard. It is an omen: later a new house is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Aldegea hearden se faek fan tofoaren timmerjen, as der in nij hûs boud wurde soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24882,"r":"CJ050103","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot wild lanterns often float about. It is an omen: later a house is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger seagen wy wol us wylde lantearnen. Èk yn 'e buert fan 'e Skieding. Dan kom dêr letter in hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24905,"r":"CJ050505","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the evening a man hears the sound of carpentry, although there is nothing to be seen. It is an omen: later new houses are built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in joun wienen ik en myn wiif Marijke bûtendoar hjir op it Wyldfjild. 't Wie stil waer, wy stienen op 'e rûmte. 't Wie stjerhelder.\n\"Stil us even\", sei 'k. \"Hark, der binne guon oan 't timmerjen.\"\n\"Dat kin net\", sei Marijke.\n\"Nou,\" sei 'k, \"hear dan us, der wurde balken delgoaid.\"\nHja hearde it ek.\nIk sei: \"Ik gean dat út, ik wol 't wite.\" 't Wie allegear noch heide. Der wie neat oan 'e hân.\nIt oare jiers is hjir njonken my in stjelphûske boud en in bouforieningshûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24909,"r":"CJ050509","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Cries for help can be heard at a pond. It is an omen: later the same sounds are heard when people fall through the ice. The people are rescued.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Popke-poel ha se us in kear Help! roppen heard. Dêr binne letter guon troch 't iis sakke. Dy rôpen ek fan help. Sy binne ret woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24911,"r":"CJ050511","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A boy sees horseshoe prints in the sand. It is a vision of the future: only later will his father buy a horse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As jonkje moest ik op in moarntiid de molkbus nei de wei bringe. 't Wie droech en moudich.\nDoe seach ik in stik of hwat rounten yn 't sân op 'e reed.\n't Wienen de printen fan hoefizers.\n\"Kofjedrinke!\" rôp heit, mar ik sei: \"Sjoch, hjir hat in hynder west.\"\n\"Ja,\" sei heit, \"it binne dúdlike spoaren. Mar hoe kin soks?\" De hjerstmis ha wy in kedde kocht op Burgumermerke. It wienen de spoaren fan dy kedde west. 't Wie foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24913,"r":"CJ050601","p":"Earnewâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At night a man sometimes hears the key turning in the cabinet. It is an omen of something that is about to happen the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Spiekstra fan Warten hearde soms yn 'e nacht dat de kaei yn 't kammenet omdraeide. Dat wie yn werklikheit sa net, mar dan gebeurde it de oare deis wòl.\n't Wie foartsjirmerij. (Spiekstra wenne op 'e Túnpôlle)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25078,"r":"CJ051001","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At night two boys suddenly hear all the bells of the surrounding villages ringing. It is an omen: when the First World War breaks out in 1914, all the bells ring.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in nacht yn 1913 of 1914 stienen der twa feinten om sa'n tolwe ûre hinne op 'e Skoallehoek yn Broek ûnder Ikkerwâld (nu Broeksterwoude). Doe hearden se ynienen alle klokken fan 'e omlizzende doarpen lieden. Hja seagen alle kanten út, hwant hja tochten net oars of der koe wolris in greate brân wêze. Mar der wie neat to sjen.\nYn 1914 doe't de earste weareldoarloch útbriek wie 't wer krekt sa. Doe letten ek alle klokken. Dat hienen dy beide feinten dy nachts doe al heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25107,"r":"CJ051413","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wild lanterns are harbingers of the later bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen sweefden oer de lannen. Letter wienen dat de fytsen mei de carbid-lampen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25111,"r":"CJ051501","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People keep watch over a mortally ill woman. Suddenly at night sounds are heard in the outbuilding, as if something is falling. However, nothing can be seen in the outbuilding. When the woman dies shortly afterwards, the carpenter makes a coffin. When another woman trips over the coffin, the same sound is heard as during the earlier vigil. It was a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event).","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't beppe tige min wie ha se dêrby wekke. Beppe hie de kanker. Tidens it wekjen wie der op in nacht yn 't bûthús in gerattel fan jewelste en 't wie krekt as foel der hwat. Doe't se der hinne gongen to sjen wie der neat. In skoftsje letter stoar beppe. Mem en Mink-muoi en noch ien wienen der by. Dy ha har ôflein en biklaeid. Lytse Syberen wie timmerman, dy hie de kiste makke. \nDoe't alles klear wie woarde de kiste brocht. It lid fan 'e kiste woarde om 'e hoeke fan 'e keamersdoar set. Minkmuoi giet út 'e keamer, sy stroffelt oer it lid fan 'e kiste en falt der yn. Hja rekke fan har stokje.\n't Wie 't selde lûd dat wy doe hearden as in joune of trije fan tofoaren. Dat hie in foarboade west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25123,"r":"CJ051512","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The sound of threshing can sometimes be heard in a barn at night. It is an omen: the next day there really is threshing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Koaten wenne in boer, dat wie âlde Bartele van der Ploeg. It gebeurde wol dat se dêr yn 'e nacht yn 'e skuorre oan 't terskjen wienen. Dat hearden se dúdlik. Mar yn werklikheit woarde der pas de oare deis terske.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25125,"r":"CJ051514","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wild lanterns indicate that a new house will be built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger seagen wy yn Broek faek wylde lantearnen.\nSy ha wol by ús oan hûs ta west.\n\"Dêr komt wer in hûs\", seinen se dan.\nDy wylde lantearnen wienen altyd yn biweging.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25138,"r":"CJ051612","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"It sometimes happens that the sounds of churning are heard at night without the horse running at the churn. It is a harbinger of what is about to happen the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Gebeurde ek wol op guon pleatsen, dat der de nachts tsjerne woarde sûnder dat der in hynder foar de tsjerne roan. Dat wie dan foartjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25139,"r":"CJ051613","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears sounds at night, although there is nothing to be seen. A few days later a lot of little posts suddenly appear. The night-time sounds were a harbinger.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha 't al us hawn, doe wie 'k yn 'e Kule. Doe wie 'k bûtendoar yn 'e nacht. Doe woarde der dêr hyltyd mar ombûke. Mar der wie neat to sjen.\nIn pear dagen letter stienen dêr allegearre fredingpealtsjes. 't Wie foartjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25160,"r":"CJ051907","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"From a floating lantern, a man predicts the building of a house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hear it heit nòch sizzen: Sjoch, dêr komt skielk in hûs, hwant dêr brânt in ljocht. Dan seach er in wylde lantearne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25220,"r":"CJ052401","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot a man often hears hammering and carpentry, although there is nothing to be seen. It is an omen: later a new bridge-keeper's house is built on that spot and the same sounds are heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wenne op 'e Koatstertille, dat is nou sahwat in jier of tsien lyn, tink. Dêr hearde ik forskeidene jounen achter elkoar, as ik op bêd lei, hammerjen en timmerjen, altyd op itselde plak. Mar dêr gebeurde doe noch neat.\nDoe moest dêr in nij brêgehûs komme. Dat kom op itselde plak, dêr't ik it timmerjen heard hie.\n't Wienen krekt deselde lûden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25221,"r":"CJ052402","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In burning lights, a man foresees the coming of the tram. The vision comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sa'n fiif en fyftich jier lyn hat myn pake Ruerd Helbich de tram fan Drachten fan to foaren riden sjoen. Der brânden jouns ljochtsjes, dy rieden krekt as de tram. Ridlik gau dêrnei wie de tram der.\nPake wenne doe yn 'e Parken (Grinzer Pein).","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25222,"r":"CJ052403","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A farmer's maid hears the sound of the churn, although there is nothing to be seen. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Skoanmem wenne yn 'e Súdwesthoeke by Balk. Hja wie yn har jonge jierren faem by de boer.\nOp in kear sieten se yn 'e hûs to kofjedrinken.\n\"Hark,\" sei se, \"dêr giet de tsjerne.\"\nHja dêrhinne en doe wie der neat.\nHja sieten wer by de kofje, doe wie dat lûd der opnij.\n't Wie foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25259,"r":"CJ052606","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wilde lantaarnen (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) were omens of the bicycle and car lights that came later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De wylde lantearnen, dy't wy froeger seagen, dat wienen de foarboaden fan 'e ljochten fan 'e lettere fytsen en auto's.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25272,"r":"CJ052702","p":"Ons Belang","v":"Utr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears the sound of hammering although there is nothing to be seen. It is an omen: later a new house is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Errit van der Heide wenne op 'e Boelensloane. Dy fortelde ris: 't Is al lang lyn, doe stie 'k ris foar 't hûs. Doe hearde ik skean oer de heide timmerjen. Der woarden dikke balken mei lange rongen oan elkoar slein. Krekt as dienen se dat mei in moker, sa hearde it. Dan wie 't wer even stil. Dan krige dyselde wer in nije spiker - dan bigoun it wer to slaen - dan wer even stil - en sa gong dat mar troch.\nIk gong skean oer om to sjen hwat dat wie. Mar der wie neat. Hwat tichter ik by dat plak kom, hwat stiller it woarde.\nLetter kom op dat plak in hûs to stean. 't Wie foartjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25332,"r":"CJ053302","p":"Ons Belang","v":"Utr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The sound of hammering is often heard at a certain place. It is an omen: later there is renovation or new building on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Smoarhoeke hjir yn 'e Harkema hearden se wit hoe faek fantofoaren timmerjen. Dan woarde der letter in nij hûs boud of sy fortimmeren it ien of oare.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25396,"r":"CJ053606","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening a few people see wilde lantaarnen (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) floating. The will-o'-the-wisps stop at three spots. They are omens: houses and a school are later built on those three spots.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in joun seagen wy by de Skieding wylde lantearnen. Dy bleauwen dêr op trije plakken stean. Op dy trije plakken kommen letter twa hûzen en in skoalle. De skoalle stiet der noch, de huzen net mear. 't Wie op 'e Skieding fan Grinzer Pein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25462,"r":"CJ054401","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman often hears hammering at night. It is an omen: later her new house is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't wy hjir njonken wennen yn in âld keet haw ik it nachts wol faek heard dat se oan 't timmerjen wienen mei it hûs, dêr't wy nou yn wenje. Yn 'e Boelensloane hearde ik sokke dingen trouwens ek wol. 't Kaem altyd nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25517,"r":"CJ054902","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wilde lantaarnen (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) were omens of the bicycle and car lights that came later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde minsken sizze: De wylde lantearnen, dy't wy froeger sjoen ha, dat wienen de fytslampen en de autoljochten fan lettere tiid.\nYn 'e buert fan 't Blauhûs sweefde faek in wylde lantearne. Froeger wie de wei fan 't Blauhûs nei Boelensloane in sânpaed. Dat is letter in hurde wei woarn. Dêr kinne se nou fytse en autoride. Dy lantearne hat dat doe al oanjown.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25529,"r":"CJ054914","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain place the whistle of the tram is said to have been heard before the tram was invented. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op Luchtenveld wennen minsken dy hearden de tram fluitsjen, doe wie der noch net iens sprake fan in tram.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25622,"r":"CJ055805","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone once predicted that houses would be built all along the dike, because that person had seen toverlantaarns (magic lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) there. It came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wit noch bêst dat der - doe wie 'k noch in famke - ien sei: \"Ha jim justerjoun dy toverlantearne wol sjoen? Dy gong op 'e dyk lâns. It wurde hjir skielk allegear huzen.\"\nIt binne èk allegear huzen woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25657,"r":"CJ056108","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people sometimes saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) floating over the heath. Where they stood still, a new house would later be built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger sieten wy yn skimerjoun faek by mem en dy ta de glêzen út to sjen. Dan wienen der soms wylde lantearnen oer de heide. Sy sweefden boppe de tiene-bosk en oer de Feanster wyk. It ljocht gong tusken de beammen fan 't bosk hinne en wer. Dêr't it stean bleau, dêr kom in hûs to stean, seinen se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25737,"r":"CJ056603","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman often heard hammering at night, but in reality there was nothing. Later lots of new houses were built and she heard the same sound again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ús mem noch yn 'e hûs wie, wenne se yn in âld húske mei in reiden tek. Dat stie hjir doe allinne. Dit hûs, dêr't wy nou yn wenje en de oare huzen wienen der doe noch net.\nMem en dy hearden nachts altyd timmerjen. Mar der woarde yn werklikheit net timmere. 't Wie foartsjirmerij. Letter kommen der allegearre huzen om harres hinne. Doe hearden se deselde lûden wer.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26292,"r":"CJ060508","p":"Earnewâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In my brother's house there are ropes with blocks for hoisting and lowering the mainsail. One evening we hear the blocks fall down, but when we inspect there is nothing to be seen. Two days later they do fall.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 't hûs dêr't nou myn broer wennet hongen seilsfallen mei de blokken. Op in kear, doe sieten wy yn 'e keamer, doe wie 't ynienen 'boem'. Heit sei: \"Dêr donderje de blokken fan boppen.\" Wy gau dêr hinne om to sjen. Doe't wy kommen hongen se op 't selde plak as dêr't se hongen.\nTwa dagen letter foelen se àl. Dit wie yn Earnewâld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29291,"r":"CJ080202","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In a farmhouse people sometimes heard a clock strike, even though there was no clock at all. Later a clock did come, and it made exactly the same sound.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Burum wenne in boer Jan Melles Kooistra. Dêr wenne in faem by de boer, dat wie Tet. Mei dy faem haw ik forkearing hawn.\nDer sloech yn dat hûs nou en dan in klok, dy't der net wie. De faem hie 't my forteld, mar ik woe 't earst net leauwe.\nOp in kear sieten wy yn 'e keuken. Doe sloech der in klok twa ûre.\n\"Hearst it nou wol?\" sei Tet.\nJa, doe hearde ik it skoan.\nLetter is dêr in klok kom, dy't krekt sa sloech. 't Wie foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":43621,"r":"WEV017702","p":"Holte","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A spookkijker (person who sees apparitions) hears the sound of crockery and a lamenting voice. Later, during a house move, there is a woman who laments what has happened to her.","i":"F.W.","o":"Was es n moal n gezin, dat nogal wat schuln moakt har. \nDe hure kon nait betoald worn en de reekns eevnmin. \nToun mos t volk et huus uut. Bie nacht gungen ze vervoarn mit n proam. Nou har n spoukkieker in de wieke geluud heurd van kopkes en ander gedounte en ook n stem dei zee: “Wat komp mie toch over; wat komp mie toch over?”\nOp dat moment was dr niks te zain west in de wieke.\nMoar in dei nacht van vervoarn ree de massiezee achter de schuut aan en moande t volk te stopn.\nProam mos aan wale legd worn en toun het de massiesee de mensn de boudel afhoald.\nt Oal mens jeuzelde toun: “Wat komp mie toch over?”\nDit is dus n geval van veurloop.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43622,"r":"WEV017703","p":"Holte","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears cow chains rattling, and later a cowshed is built; he sees a threshing machine being lifted over the hedge at night, because a hearse has to pass.","i":"F.W.","o":"Bieons in de Pekel woonde oal Joakob, dei kwoad zain kon.\n Wie stonden es n keer boetn te proatn en toun zee Joakob teegn mien voader: “Ie kriegn ook nogn keer n schure achter et huus; ik heur de kouketns rappeln.” \n“Woor?” zee voader.\n Joakob begonde te treden en zee: “Hier op dit stee, hier heb ik de ketns heurd.”\nEn t is nog uutkomen ook. Inderdoad hebben wie loater de schure timmerd op t stee, dat hai aan wees. En door stonden ook de baistn dei mit de ketns rammelden.\n Joakob het ook n moal zain - dat zee hai teminste - dat n hail dörsmesien over n hege zet is. Dat gebeurde in n nacht. Toun t waarkvolk op n mörn dörskenwol, ston t mesien op n ander stee, over de hege tild. En dit mos, omdat over t pad voor t mesien ston, ain liekwoagn langs goan zol.  \nEn dat mout ook gebeurd weezn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46280,"r":"WEV017801","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On the spot where knocking was heard, a farm was later built. In another case, knocking means the werkgeesten (work spirits) are still under the ship, an omen that the ship will be given maintenance.","i":"F.W.","o":"Klopgeestn heb ik wel over proatn heurd. Hier in Bennewol lag n stok land en door het mien voader hoamergeklop vernomen; zoks wat beleefde hai bie nacht. Op dat stee is joar of wat noa tied ain boerderij zet.\nMien schoonoln harn n woonschip. Zai hebben ook klopperij mitmoakt. Ze kwamen n moal mitt schip bie huus en woln aan wale stapn.\nOp wale stonden wat lu heur op te wachten.\nMien schoonmoetje ruip heur tou: “As ie geklop heurn, den mou-je nait baange worn, moar de waarkmannegies zitn nog onder t schip.”\nDat geklop was n veurbeduudsel, dat t schip es weer n beurt hebben mos en dat de waarklu binnenkört begunnen zoln.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":25323,"r":"CJ053202","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On a summer night a man hears banging coming from the shed three times. When he goes to look, however, there is nothing to be seen. Half a year later the man gets a horse. He builds a stable for it in the shed. A year after that he hears the same sounds coming from the shed that he heard before. It turns out to be the horse stamping its legs on the stones. The earlier banging was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It mei sahwat in fiif en twintich jier lyn wêze. 't Wie yn 'e simmer. 't Wie yn 'e nacht en 'k lei op bêd. Doe hearde ik ynienen achter ús hûs: bouns - bouns -. Ik tocht: hwat mei dat wêze? Ik der ôf en nei bûten. 't Wie skymerich. De lûden wienen út it hok weikom, sa't it hearde. Mar doe't ik bûten stie hearde ik neat mear. En yn 't hok wie ek neat to rêdden.\nIk gong wer op bêd. Mar 'k lei noch mar even of ik hearde wer itselde geklop en gebouns. Ik der wer ôf en sjen. Mar ik koe neat gewaer wurde. Doe't ik bûten stie wie der neat mear to hearren.\nDat gebeurde oan trije kear ta.\nSahwat in healjier letter krige ik in petroaljerit mei in hynder. Dat hynder stie earst op 'e Langewyk, mar letter krige ik de saek thús. Ik timmere yn 't hok achter hûs in hynstestâl, op itselde plak, dêr't doe dy lûden weikamen.\nSahwat in jier letter hearde ik yn 'e nacht wer itselde gebouns as doe. It wie it hynder, dat mei de poaten op 'e stiennen stampte. It lûd wie presys gelyk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25324,"r":"CJ053203","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man intends to build a hay barn. Shortly afterwards the sounds of sawing and hammering are heard three times at night, although there is nothing to be seen. In the nights that follow, working sounds can be heard as well. It is an omen: when the hay barn is actually built, the same sounds are heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir njonken wenne in âld man mei trije bern. Der wennet nou in oantroude dochter fan him.\n't Wie yn 1938. Hja woenen it spultsje hwat útbreide en sy hienen it der oer, sy woenen in heakipe bouwe.\nOp in nacht, doe leinen se allegear op bêd, doe sloech de houn oan en der waerd sage, timmere en alsa mear. Se hearden it alle fjouwer. Hja kommen oerein en fan bêd ôf. 't Hountsje woarde losmakke, en doe sjen. Mar der wie neat. Doe gongen se wer op bêd. Mar even letter hearden se itselde wer: saegje, spikerje en sa. Dat gong oan trije kear ta dy nachts.\nDe oare nachts hienen jy it wer, en de dêropfolgjende nacht ek. Nacht op nacht hearden dy lju dat getimmer. Sy gongen der net mear ôf.\nDoe't de heakipe in pear wiken letter boud woarde, hearden se deselde lûden de oerdeis. It hie foartsjirmerije west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25531,"r":"CJ055101","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man heard someone outside calling for his wife, but there was no one to be seen. Half an hour later his wife really was called by the neighbour woman.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in moarntiid sieten ik en Kobe, myn frou, in kopke thé to drinken, doe hearde ik ien op 'e wei roppen. De lêste wurden dy't sein woarden, wienen: \"Kobe, hè?\" Doe't ik op 'e wei seach wie der net ien to sjen.\nIn healûre letter miskien hong Kobe in pear wiete dinkjes op 'e line. Dan kom ús buorfrou ta de doar út. Sy sei tsjin myn frou: \"It droeget wer hwat, Kobe, hè?\"\nIt wienen de wurden dy't ik in healûre earder al heard hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25532,"r":"CJ055102","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once thought he heard a young girl calling, but there was no one to be seen. Later that day a neighbour girl came calling.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in middei wie hjir in frou to praten. Myn frou en hja wienen drok oan 't petear, doe hearde ik ien by de achterdoar roppen fan 'follik!'\nIk sei: \"Hark, dêr ropt ien.\" Mar doe't ik dat sei lake dy frou, dy't by ús to praten wie, my út. Hja hienen der beide neat fan heard. Dy frou lake my út.\nMar ik hie 't klear heard. Ik sei, 't wie 't lûd fan ien, dat wie net in bern mear, mar ek noch net in folwoechsen frou. Ik sei, 't wie 't lûd fan in backfish.\nDeselde jouns ûnder iten wie 't selde lûd der wer. Mar dizze kear hearden wy 't alle trije. 't Wie in fanke fan sechstjin jier, dy't rôp fan folk. 't Wie ien fan ús buorlju.\nIk liet har deryn.\nDe frou, dy't by ús wie, biloek. Hja hat noait wer by ús west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25536,"r":"CJ055106","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The lights that people used to see in the old days were the car and bicycle lamps of later times.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr't wy froeger wol ljochten sjoen ha, dat wienen letter de auto- en fytslampen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25601,"r":"CJ055610","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) that people used to see were omens of the lights of the houses built later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen seagen wy froeger faek. Dat wienen de ljochtsjes fan de lettere huzen, dy't der kom binne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25606,"r":"CJ055615","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A nephew said it would rain on the day of his uncle's funeral; he had already seen it. That did indeed come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ús heit stoar sei Boardzer, op 'e dei fan 'e bigraffenis soe 't reinich waer wêze, hwant hy hie alles al fan tofoaren sjoen. Hy krige gelyk. It reinde dy deis.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25668,"r":"CJ056201","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man often heard hammering in the distance at night. Ten years later he heard that same hammering again. That was when a new school was being built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 'e nije wei njonken de winkel fan Tjeerdsma hjir yn Boarnburgum, dêr boude in timmerfeint in húske foar himsels. Doe't er dêr mei klear wie en sy der yn wennen, hearden se yn 'e fierte timmerjen. It gong hyltyd op in hammerjen en slaen, de iene nacht nei de oare.\nSahwat in tsien jier letter woarde dêr de bysûndere skoalle boud.\n\"Fordomme noch ta,\" sei dy timmerfeint, \"nou't dy skoalle boud wurdt, hear ik de lûden fan tsien jier lyn.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25719,"r":"CJ056414","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) that people used to see were the roads and houses of later times.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De wylde lantearnen dy't se hjir froeger seagen dat wienen de lettere wegen en huzen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25740,"r":"CJ056703","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once heard hammering early in the morning, but there was nothing to be seen. Later a new house was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Freark gong op in moarntiid bitiid nei 't wurk ta.\n 't Wie oeral noch nacht om him hinne. Doe't er by de Pauloane kom, tocht er, hea, hwat giet it dêr nou al op in timmerjen. Hy kom tichterby om to sjen, mar doe wie der net ien.\nIn jier letter stie der op datselde plak in hûs. Myn neef - ek in de Haan - hat letter yn dat hûs wenne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25741,"r":"CJ056704","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a place where a small church was later built, some people had already heard psalm singing beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op it plak, dêr't letter Warmolds syn tsjerkje delset hat, hjir yn 'e Harkema, ha guon fan tofoaren psalmsjongen heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25768,"r":"CJ056809","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people often saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps). Those lights foreshadowed the car and bicycle lamps of later times.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy seagen froeger wol gauris wylde lantearnen. Dy ljochten tsjutten op 'e lettere auto- en fytsljochten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25827,"r":"CJ057205","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot people used to see wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) often. Those were the bicycle lights of later times. Houses were built there too.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Sweager Mieden seagen wy froeger faek wylde lantearnen. Dat wienen de lettere fytsljochten, dy't dêr to sjen wienen. Ek woarden dêr huzen delset.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25830,"r":"CJ057208","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once saw ships sailing across a piece of land. Later a lake appeared there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr't nou de Swemmer is, dêr hat Sytse-om froeger de skippen silen sjoen. Doe wie 't allegear noch droech.\nDat wie foartjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25927,"r":"CJ057806","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Every year a man went to work for the same farmer with his brother. But one time the man dreamed that he would not go along that year. That came true as well. The two brothers did not speak to each other for years.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit en Ielke-om gongen alle jierren togearre nei deselde boer to ûngetiidzjen.\nDoe droomde heit op in kear - krekt foardat de ûngetiid bigong - dat heit koe net wer mei. Ielke-om soe de skoansoan meinimme.\nEn doe wìe 't ek sa. Heit en Ielke-om ha doe yn gjin jierren mei elkoar praet.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25937,"r":"CJ057902","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At the spot where people used to see wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) often, new houses were later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De kant út nei 't stoomgemael yn 'e Wierren seagen se froeger faek wylde lantearnen. Letter binne der huzen kom op dy plakken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25943,"r":"CJ058004","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people often saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) on the heath. The light was very bright. Later a farm was built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy seagen hjir froeger achter ús wylde lantearnen. Ien ljocht wie tige klear en helder. 't Wie dêr doe allegear heide. Letter kom dêr in buorkerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25944,"r":"CJ058005","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people often saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) on the heath. Later new houses were built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek op oare plakken haw ik wol ljochtsjes sjoen. Dêr wie 't èk allegear heide. Dêr kommen doe letter ek huzen. Soks komt altyd nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25945,"r":"CJ058006","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At dusk a man always saw twelve little lights in a row, while in reality there was nothing there. Later a new farm was built, with twelve small cowshed windows.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De earste plaets, dy't Jitse van der Vlugt boud hat, dêr seach heit fan to foaren de ljochtsjes fan, by skimerjoun.\nHeit koe him net bigripe hwat it wêze koe. 't Wienen tolwe ljochtsjes op in rige. 't Kom krekt nei. De plaets krige tolwe kouwerútsjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25974,"r":"CJ058109","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If people dream about lice, they will fall into poverty.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As minsken fan luzen drome dan komme se yn 'e earmoed to sitten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25975,"r":"CJ058110","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman tells that in the week before the German invasion she dreamed that the sky was black with aeroplanes.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw to Grins op 'e merk stien mei in kofjetinte.\nNjonken my stie in âld wyfke, dy fortelde op in kear, sy hie dy nachts droomd, it wie swart fan flychtugen west yn 'e loft. Dat wie krekt de wyks foardat de Dútsers yn oantocht wienen yn 1940.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25997,"r":"CJ058214","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night people heard hammering. Not long afterwards a new house was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en mem wennen by de Janke-dobbe. Op in nacht gong it bûtendoar lûd op in timmerjen. Mem sei de oare moarns: \"Och, och, hwat gong it der fannacht bot oan wei by de Janke-dobbe. En hwat gong 't op in timmerjen. Dêr koe wolris in hûs komme.\" 't Wie op 'e Skieding. Dat hûs kom der al gau.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25998,"r":"CJ058215","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a spot where people had seen wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) in the old days, new houses were later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mem seach dêr ek wylde lantearnen. Dêr kommen letter huzen. Dat wie ek op 'e Skieding, yn 'e buert fan 'e Janke-dobbe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25999,"r":"CJ058216","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A neighbour heard a clock ticking in an empty parsonage. But there was no clock at all. When the new occupants arrived, they hung a clock in the spot the neighbour had heard the sound coming from.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De âlde pasterije yn Greategast stie leech. De buorlju wienen tige lyts bihuze en hienen altyd krapte fan reinwetter.\nDoe hellen se wetter út 'e pasterije. Dat die de man jouns nei 't wurk. Doe hearde er dêr yn 'e pasterije in klok tikjen. En dochs stie it hûs leech. Hy gong nei 't plak ta dêr't er de klok tikjen hearde, mar der wie net in klok.\nFjirtsjin dagen letter wie de pasterije wer biwenne. Doe kom der in klok to hingjen op krekt itselde plak, dêr't hy it tikjen heard hie. En 't wie ek presys deselde tik.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26033,"r":"CJ058411","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once looked out of his window and saw a smooth strip across the land, just as if there were a skating rink. A few years later a motorway was built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit wenne letter op Driemunt. (Bearn v.d. Woude)\nOp in joun lei er op bêd, 't wie moai ljochtmoannewaer. Hy seach ta it sydfinsterke út en doe seach er in ljochte glêdde streek, krekt as wie 't in iisbaen, samar midden troch 't lân. Dêr leit nou de rykswei 43.\nHeit wie doe sahwat tachtich jier âld. It gebeurde in pear jier foardat de wei der kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26048,"r":"CJ058512","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people always heard hammering and sawing at a certain place, but there was nothing to be seen. Later new houses were built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir by de dwarsfeart stie froeger in hûs, dêr woarde alle nachten yn sage en timmere. Dan seinen de minsken: Dêr komt in nij hûs, mar dat gebeurde noait.\nMar nou komme dêr allegear nije huzen to stean. 't Is dus wol neikom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26071,"r":"CJ058702","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A mermaid is half fish, half human. She is a siren. With their beautiful singing they lure sailors to them. The sailors are then swallowed by the waves. If someone sees a mermaid, the weather turns bad and the ship will be lost. Mermaids sometimes make predictions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In sémearmin is heal fisk, heal minske. 't Is in sirene. \nSe kinne tige sjonge, dat klinkt hiel moai yn 'e fierte.\nMei har gesang lokje se de sélju oan. Dy wurde dan troch de baren forslonden. Dêr is 't har krekt om to dwaen.\nAs der in sémearmin sjoen wurdt, wurdt it swier waer.\nDan forgiet it skip.\nSémearminnen dogge wolris foarspellings.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26076,"r":"CJ058707","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) mean bad weather. They also mean that a new house will be built, or that the heath will fare badly that year. When a beekeeper died, the beehives were moved. Once when a beekeeper was buried, people claimed that lots of bees had been at the funeral.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen bitsjutten min waer.\n\"Dêr komt skielk in nij hûs to stean\", seinen de minsken, as se in wylde lantearne seagen.\nAs de bijkers in wylde lantearne seagen, seinen se: \"Nou is 't fan 't jier neat wurdich mei de heide.\"\nStoar der in bijker, dan woarden de bijekuorren forset. Doe't der in bijker stoarn is, dy't ik wol kend ha, seinen se, dat de bijen him nei 't hôf brocht hienen. 't Wienen allegear bijen op 't tsjerkhôf west.\nDy woenen by de bigraffenis wêze.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26089,"r":"CJ058806","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People sometimes saw lights over the land. That meant poachers would come a few days later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Soms seach men by ús yn 'e omkriten fan Bakkefean ljochten oer 't lân. Dan wienen der in pear dagen letter streupers mei ljochtbakken. Guon hienen har fantofoaren al sjoen. (foartsjirmerije)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26100,"r":"CJ058908","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People once heard the brass band playing, while in reality there was no band at all. Only later was a brass band founded.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is yn 'e Boelensloane gebeurd, dat guon dêr it fanfare spyljen heard ha, wylst it der net wie.\nIk ha 't sels ek heard. Ik wie doe noch in jonkje. Der wie doe noch net in korps yn 'e Boelensloane.\nIk stie op in joun bûten mei moai waer. Us Jehan wie der ek by. Ik sei: \"Heit, dêr spylje èk guon.\"\nDoe ha wy it fanfarekorps al spyljen heard dat letter yn 't evangelisaesjegebou oprjochte woarn is.\nDat is sa'n sechstich jier lyn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26101,"r":"CJ058909","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The mother of a son who was soon to go into military service invited a card reader. She predicted that he would not end up in the war, and that he would come out of it safely. That came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Blauwe Met wie in kaertlizter.\nIk moest yn 1917 ûnder tsjinst. 't Wie doe oarloch. Us mem leaude oan kaertlizzen. Ik moest yn novimber opkomme.\nOp Feanstermerke praette mem mei Met. Met kom by ús thús om de kaert út to lizzen. Ik moest der by wêze. Heit wie fuort. Met lei de kaerten op 'e tafel.\n\"Sjoch ris, Aefke\", sei se tsjin mem, \"'k sil jo de warheit fortelle sa wier as jo it leven ûntfongen ha en de dea skuldich binne.\"\nUs mem rekke fuort oandien.\nDoe rekke Met mei de kaerten oan 't fimeljen. 't Kom allegearre wol goed, sei se. Wy soenen net yn oarloch komme, en ik soe bihâlden bliuwe. Nou, dat is ek útkom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26112,"r":"CJ059004","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When people saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, ghost lights) above the heaths, they believed that another new house would be built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen seach men meast boppe de heidefjilden.\nAs de minsken ien seagen, seinen se: \"Sjoch, dêr komt wer in nij hûs.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26194,"r":"CJ059604","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, ghost lights). They were the forerunners of the lights of cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger seagen se hjir wol wylde lantearnen. Dat ha de foarboaden west fan 'e ljochten fan 'e auto's.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26220,"r":"CJ060001","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Back then, a married couple in Harkema, near the Smoorhoeke, sees little lights approaching that come round the corner up the winding path. They are wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, ghost lights). Later cyclists ride past with their lights on. They had seen the bicycle lamps in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn Pake en mem seagen hjir yn 'e Harkema yndertiid yn 'e Smoarhoeke ljochtsjes oankommen, dy draeiden om 'e hoeke de slingerpaedtsjes del. 't Wienen wylde lantearnen.\nLetter rieden de fytsen dêr lâns mei jouns de ljochten op.\nDy lampen fan ' e fytsen ha sy doe fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26222,"r":"CJ060003","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Mother goes to visit old Jantsje, and on the way she sees a big black wheel passing by with lots of silent people behind it. She realises this is a funeral procession, but the wheel remained unclear. In those days people are still taken to the churchyard on an ordinary farm wagon. Later the hearse with unequal wheels arrives. Only then does she know what it was.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem soe us in kear op bisite nei âlde Jantsje-muoi ta. Dy wenne yn 'e Stûken yn 'e Harkema. Underweis seach se in hiel great swart rad. Dat gong har foarby en wylst wie se oer side skoud woarn en der kommen allegear stille gedaenten achteroan. Hja hie fuort yn 'e gaten dat dit in lykstaesje wie, mar dat greate swarte rad koe se net to plak krije.\nHwant yn dy tiid woarden de minsken noch op in gewoane boerewein nei 't tsjerkhôf brocht. Doe't letter de lykkoets ynfierd woarde, jierren letter, seach se dat it dêr in rad fan west hie. It foarste rêd wie lytser as 't achterste. \n't Gebeurde yn 'e foarnacht. Hja hat itselde letter by dei wer sjoen. Doe wie 't werklikheit.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26228,"r":"CJ060009","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On the road to Readskuorre stands a little house with an upper and a lower door. A man cannot sleep, and at two o'clock at night he gets out of bed and leans over the lower door. When he sees two men in dark clothing pass by, he follows them. Suddenly they vanish again. Later there is a story in the village. They were two wegaanzeggers (death announcers) heading to the village. Panhuizen used to live at that spot; it is on the road that runs parallel to the Langepad.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op Readskuorre is in âld wei, dy rint achterút. Dêr stie in âld hûske mei in boppe- en ûnderdoar. 't Wie us op in nacht doe koe de man dy't dêr yn wenne, net sliepe. 't Wie moai simmerwaer en yn 'e neinacht. 't Wie sahwat twa ûre. De man wie út bêd wei gong en hie oer de ûnderdoar hinne leund. Wylst er dêr sa stie seach er twa mannen oankommen op 'e âld reed. Sy wienen yn donkere klean. Hy tocht: \"Hwat kin dat wêze?\" Hy woe der achteroan as se foarby wienen.\nSy wienen sahwat oan him ta, doe wienen se ek wer fordwenen, krekt as wienen se yn 'e groun weisakke.\nLetter is der op dat plaetske ien forstoarn. It wienen twa leedoansizzers dy't nei dat plaetske tagongen. Panhuizen hat froeger op dat pleatske wenne. 't Stie oan in reed dy't evenwijdig roan mei it Langpaed.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26243,"r":"CJ060108","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Before the Second World War, Boardzer Bruining from Boelenslaan sees the German army passing by his place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining fan 'e Boelensloane seach foar de twadde wereldoarloch it Dútse leger fan tofoaren yn ús lân kommen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26296,"r":"CJ060601","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days it was all heath as far as Mearum. An old woman sees wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, ghost lights) moving over the heath. Later roads come with bicycles, and she again sees lights in the same places, but now they are bicycle lamps. This had been foretold.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Wie hjir froeger allegear heide, oan Mearum ta. In âld minske seach dêr wylde lantearnen oer de heide gean.\nLetter kommen der wegens mei fytsen, doe seagen se wer ljochtsjes op dy selde plakken, mar doe wienen 't fytslampen. Dat hat foartsjirmerije west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26297,"r":"CJ060602","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When the heath is being reclaimed, people hear hammering at a spot where the Groningen hamlet of Pein later stands. That was the building of it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By de ûntginning fan 'e heide hearden se op in plak getimmer. Letter stie der op datselde plak in plaetske. Dat hat dat timmerjen west. 't Wie hjir yn Grinzer Pein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26304,"r":"CJ060701","p":"Groningen","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On my way home I see a bright light with a tail, as if it is burning. The others do not see it. This happened in 1937 in Groninger Pein. According to my mother it was an omen of the war.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik gong nei 't húske. Doe't ik dêr siet, seach ik in forskynsel tsjin 'e loft. It wie in ljocht mei in sturt. Net ien dy't it oars seach, buorman net en mem ek net, ik seach it allinne mar. 't Wie hiel helder, krekt as brânde it. Doe't de oaren it net seagen woarde ik sa bang, dat ik bin yn 'e kelder krûpt.\n't Wie yn 1937, yn Grinzer Pein.\nMem sei, 't wie in foarboade fan 'e oarloch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26305,"r":"CJ060702","p":"Groningen","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In Groninger Pein, a woman once sees the head of her future husband in the mist during misty weather. She is not yet married at the time.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek in kear doe wie 't hiel mistich. Jy koenen gjin hân foar de egen sjen. Ik wie noch net troud. Doe seach ik ynienen hiel dúdlik myn man syn holle boppe de mist. Mar hy wie der net. 't Wie yn Grinzer Pein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26306,"r":"CJ060703","p":"Groningen","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening Gabe Marij from Grinzer Pein is coming from Drachten and sees lights and money all around her. So she says that Drachten will become a big town with factories and wealth. It came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Gabe Marij fan 'e Grinzer Pein fortelde, hja kom us in kear rinnende wei op in joun fan Drachten. Sy seach om en doe seach se samar ynienen allegear ljochten en allegear jild foar har.\nIk koe 't jild samar gripe, sei se.\nDoe sei se al: Drachten wurdt in hiele greate stêd mei allegear fabriken en rykdom.\nEn sjoch nou ris! Of it ek útkom is!","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26784,"r":"CJ061103","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If people in Pein hear hammering, there will later be a celebration in that house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Pein seinen se wol gauris: Dêr komt fêst in hûs. It giet dêr altyd op in timmerjen. 't Wienen ek wol âlde minsken dy't dat hearden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26853,"r":"CJ061404","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When something is coming, for example the police, magpies give warning in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der by ús hwat extra's op komst wie, lyk as mei de plysje of sa, dan wienen der faek eksters by ús om 'e doar hinne to skatterjen.\nDy wolle 't jin dan fortelle fan to foaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26855,"r":"CJ061406","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone hears tapping on the window but sees no one. A little later he hears it again, and then someone is standing there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Faker as ienkear is 't gebeurd, dat der ien by ús op 't glês tikke. As wy seagen, wie der neat. In skoftsje letter hearden wy presys itselde tikjen en dan wie der ien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26878,"r":"CJ061510","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A farmhand comes to a girl who has heard from a fortune teller in Leeuwarden that he would drown before he turned 21. But the farmhand misheard the age. Until he is 21 he avoids ditches, canals, ponds and small lakes. Nothing happens, and he goes to live in Eiderburen. Around his forty-first year they are building a bridge, and in the evening the light has to be on. Then he trips, falls into the water and drowns.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hier kwam froeger in feintsje bij een meiske. Die had eens bij een waarsegster in Leeuwarden west. Se sei tegen hem, hij sou verdrinken krekt voor zijn een en twintigste. Moar dat een en twintigste het-ie ferkeerd ferstoan.\nHij kwam noait meer bij een sloot langs of een faart en hij kwam ook niet bij een dobbe of een meertje. Hij was haast een en twintig en hij was doodsbenauwd. Toen werd hij één en twintig en nog ouder en toen was hij niet bang meer. Hij ging noar Eider buren te wonen. Hij liep tegen de een en veertig. Se woaren doar met de brug oan 't moaken. 's Oavonds moesten doar de lichten oan. Hij doet 't licht op en stroffelt met syn foet, hij falt in 't woater en fordrinkt. Krekt voor syn éénenfeertigste. Hij woonde toen in een caféeke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26891,"r":"CJ061702","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Folkert Bruining's house on the Kaleweg is not right. One night he hears the loft being torn down, the roof tiles falling off the roof and the planks being thrown outside. When he goes to look, he sees nothing. He moves, and at the same time that he is building a sod hut, the old house is demolished.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn âlde buorman Folkert Bruining hat yn 'e Mieden wenne by de Keale Wei. It hûs, dêr't er doe yn wenne, dêr doogde 't net yn. Op in nacht hearden se klear dat de souder ôfbrutsen woarde en de pannen der ôf helle. Se hearden dat de planken nei bûten smiten woarden.\nMyn buorman fortelde: \"Doe't ik der ôf gong en 't ljocht op die, wie der neat. Doe bin ik hjir hinne gong to wenjen. Wy ha doe in spittekeet boud. Yn dyselde tiid sahwat woarde it hûs dêr oan 'e Keale Wei ôfbrutsen. 't Kom wòl nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26892,"r":"CJ061703","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When my uncle gets pneumonia, which he also dies of, I am living alone with him. One time he wants to get out of bed and I cannot turn him, so I go to my neighbour Gerrit Smit for help. Outside I hear his footsteps, but it is a good hour before he actually comes. It was a premonition.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie sa'n fjirtsjin jier âld. Myn âlde omke wenne by ús yn. Hy krige longontsteking en dêr is er ek oan stoarn. Ik wie allinne by him. Heit en mem wienen dea.\nOmke woe de jouns fan bêd ôf en hy wie in dikke, sterke âld-keardel. Hy wie fiifensawntich jier. Ik koe him net keare en hy moest op bêd bliuwe. Doe gong ik der út om myn buorman Gerrit Smit op to heljen. Ik wie krekt út hûs, doe hearde ik sekuer dat hy der oanstappen kom. Ik koe syn stap sa goed. Hy wie hast oan ús ta. Ik gong wer yn 'e hûs.\nMar it duorre noch wol in ûre foardat er kom. Hy hie der net earder út west. 't Hie foartsjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26895,"r":"CJ061706","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Taeke Struiksma always attends church in Burum and sets out while it is still night. Once on the Kaleweg he walks into a bare wall at a spot where Arend Bekkema's house later comes to stand. It was a premonition.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 'e Keale wei stienen yndertiid noch gjin huzen. Myn âlde buorman Taeke Struiksma gong altyd nei Burum nei tsjerke. Dêr kom er wei. Dat wie sa'n ein rinnen, dan gong er yn 'e nacht al op stap. Hy fortelde: \"Doe't ik op in nacht omtrint oan 'e Keale Wei ta wie, doe roan ik mei de holle tsjin in keale muorre oan. Letter stie op dat plak it hûs fan Arend Bekkema.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26962,"r":"CJ062202","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A mallemoel is a small bird, the size of a starling, that can swim and is only seen at sea. This bird in a net means bad weather the next day. Fishermen on the Dutch coast firmly believe this, just as people believe that a mermaid who shows herself brings bad weather.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De mallemoel is in lyts fûgeltsje, sa great as in protter, dat swimme kin en inkeld op 'e sé sjoen wurdt.\nAs jo de mallemoel yn 'e sleep krije, dan krije jo de oare deis min waer. Ik haw in pear kear sa'n fûgeltsje yn 'e sleep hawn.\nDe fiskers oan 'e Hollânske kust leauwe der sterk oan.\nKrekt as guon leauwe dat in sémearmin dy't har sjen lit, min waer bringt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26963,"r":"CJ062203","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The kees is a whale-like mammal whose head comes above the water from time to time. When it appears the fishermen are glad, because it is a sign that a lot of herring is coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De kees is in walfiskachtich beest. Fan tiid ta tiid komt dy mei de kop boppe wetter. 't Is in zoogdier. As dy him fortoant binne de fiskers bliid, hwant dat is in goed teken. Dan komme der gâns hearringen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26977,"r":"CJ062403","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In Parken there is a double house; an old woman lives in one half and a young couple in the other. One day four magpies are sitting in front of the young couple's half. In the evening a man comes to tell the young wife that Gerrit, her husband, has run off with the money. Gerrit sold fish for him and has gone to Nieuwstad in Groningen. The magpies were the omen of the visit.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In de Parken woonden wij noast in dubbelde woning. 't Was in olle fort. In de ene helft woonde een old minske, in de andere er noast in jonge huusholding.\nOp een morgen kwam ik der ôf. Doe woaren der fier eksters op 't strietsje foar de dunen fan dat dûbelde huus.\nDie eksters bleven hyltyd op 't ene straetje, bij de jonge minsken, niet bij 't âlde. Presys feur díe deur.\n's Oavends komt der in man oan. \"Gerrit is der fandeur met de sinten\", sei er. Gerrit dat was de man die in die ene helft woonde. Hy brocht it boadskip an de frou over. Gerrit ferkocht fis foor hem. Hy was noar Grunnigen noar de Nieuwstad gegoan.\nDat was de visite.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27027,"r":"CJ062911","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A magpie in front of the house means cheerfulness, and behind the house it means sadness.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As men eksters foar hûs sjocht, dan bitsjut dat fleurichheit.\nAs men eksters achter hûs sjocht, dan bitsjut dat treurichheit.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27065,"r":"CJ063401","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Thijs Pultrum visits his brother in Skieding and sees a light passing on the path behind the house, gets scared and quickly goes inside. He says there is a light there, but it disappears at once. It was voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event).","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer wenne hwat achterôf op 'e Skieding.\nWy wennen yn Drachten.\nMyn oare broer frijgeselle by him.\nOp in snein-to-joun gong ik der oan ta. 't Wie sahwat tsien ûre. Dêr achter roan in paedtsje lâns. Dy jouns gong dêr in ljocht lâns. Oars neat as ljocht. Ik woarde sa binaud, dat ik makke fluch dat ik by de syddoar fan it hûs fan myn broer kom.\nIk hime der oer. Doe sei 'k tsjin myn broer: \"Sjoch, dêr is in ljocht.\"\nMar doe wie 't fuort. 't Hat foartsjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27080,"r":"CJ063602","p":"Soesterberg","v":"Utr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At the unguarded level crossing in Den Dolder, a man meets two nuns who vanish without a trace immediately afterwards. The madhouse in which the nuns work is later built on this spot. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Zowat zo'n zesenzeventig jaar geleden passeerde een man een onbewaakte overweg te Den Dolder. Toen kwam hij twee nonnen tegen. Toen hij zich omkeerde om te zien waar ze gebleven waren waren die nonnen spoorloos verdwenen. Heel korte tijd daarna werd der op diezelfde plaats het dollehuis gebouwd, waar nonnen in werkten. 't Was een voorteken geweest."},{"n":27135,"r":"CJ063802","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On the Veensterheide you often hear hammering at places where a house later comes to stand. This has also been heard in Pein. You also hear knocking on the door while no one is there, and a little later someone really is there. Before a house burns down, people often see fire at that spot. This too is on the Veensterheide.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Feansterheide hearden se wol faek timmerjen op plakken. Dêr kom dan letter in hûs to stean. Ek ha 'k dat wol fan guon heard hjir yn 'e Pein.\nDer woarde yn Feansterheide ek wol kloppe op 'e doar. Gongen se der hinne, dan wie der net ien. Even letter hearden se 't selde klopjen wer, dan wie der ien.\nSa wie 't ek mei 't tikjen op 't rút.\nAs der in hûs ôfbrânde seinen guon: \"Wy ha 't fan tofoaren brânnen sjoen. Dat wie èk op Feansterheide.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27163,"r":"CJ063903","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Once when I take a horse to the meadow, I see a wilde lantaarn (wild lantern, ghost light) shining over the land, which stops at Wolter de Vries's and at another place where a school will be built. Wolter's house is later renovated.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik brocht us op in joun om sahwat healwei alven hinne in hynder nei 't lân. Doe seach ik in wylde lantearne skeef oer 't lân. Dy lantearne bleau stean by Wolter de Vries. Doe sette er ôf en bleau stean op in plak, dat wie wit hoe fier fan my ôf. Op dat plak kom in skoalle to stean en by Wolter de Vries woarde it hûs fortimmere.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27164,"r":"CJ063904","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"My mother and brother once come home together in the autumn. They see a light burning behind the house, and once they reach the yard they see that the light has moved. A back house was added to our house, and a new house was built at the other spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn mem en ien fan myn bruorren kommen us op in joun togearre thús. 't Wie yn 'e hjerst. Der brânde ljocht by ús achter hûs.\nDoe't se op 't hiem stienen hie 't ljocht him forplaatst. Doe wie 't in lyt eintsje fierder. Dêr, op dat plak is letter in nij hûs kom, en wy sels krigen in nij achterhús.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27168,"r":"CJ063908","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"We live on the Drachtsterweg near the woods, and sometimes at twelve o'clock at night we hear three blows of a sledgehammer in the Julianabuurt. Later the heath is reclaimed, and when the fencing is put up we hear the same sledgehammer blows.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen oan 'e Drachtster wei, tichte by de bosk. Nachts om sa'n tolve ûre hinne hearden wy soms trije klappen fan in moker yn 'e Julianabuert. Myn broer sei, wienen jy yn 'e Julianabuert, dan hearden jy dy trije slaggen op 'e hoeke.\nLetter is de bosk der útgong en de heide woarde ûntgonnen. Doe woarden der fredingen makke en dêrby hearden wy dyselde slaggen. \nFan tofoaren hie ik it in nacht of trije slaen heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27228,"r":"CJ064301","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A few years before Wide Pet was built, we heard workmen at work at night, though they cannot be seen. During the building we hear the same sounds again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In pear jier foardat de Wide Pet oanmakke woarde, hearden wy nachts altyd de arbeiders dêr oan 't wurk. Wy ha der wol hinne west to sjen, mar der wie net in minske.\nLetter, doe't se echt oan 't oanmeitsjen wienen, hearden wy dyselde lûden wer.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27229,"r":"CJ064302","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"We hear our own house being built with hammering before the new house actually stands on the same spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy hearden yn ús eigen hûs timmerjen it jiers foardat wy in nij hûs krigen op itselde sté. Yn dat nije hûs kommen wy doe to wenjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27253,"r":"CJ064326","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Detsje de Haan from Harkema always plays cards when she is pregnant. The child that is born then always has marks of playing cards on its chest and tail. This is the devil's punishment for playing cards, because he is in the cards.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir hat in frommes wenne yn 'e Harkema, dat wie Detsje de Haan. Dy kaertspile altyd as se yn forwachting wie.\nDe bern dy't geboaren woarden hienen de printen fan 'e spylkaerten op it boarst en stoaren allegearre. Dat wie de straf foar it kaertspyljen, hwant de duvel sit yn 'e kaerten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27274,"r":"CJ064414","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Boardzer Bruining and I are once catching moles, and on the way we see two magpies sitting on the left side of the verge. This is not a good sign, so we keep a close eye on the left side. There stand two policemen who want to catch us, because catching moles is forbidden.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining en ik hawwe ris togearre to moljen west. Doe't wy in ein riden hienen, troffen wy twa eksters. Dy wienen oan 'e linkerkant yn 'e berm. Doe sei Boardzer: \"Dit wiist net bêst. Wy matte goed de egen iepen ha en de linkerkant oer sjen. Hwant dy kant oer binne twa plysjes dy't ús attrapearje wolle.\" (It mollefangen wie yn dy tiid forbean.)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27275,"r":"CJ064415","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When a woman is expecting, she must not walk under a line, because then cords will wind around the child.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in frommeske in bern forwachtet, mat se yn dy tiid net ûnder 'e line trochrinne, hwant dan komme der stringen om it bern hinne to sitten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27283,"r":"CJ064502","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"I have sometimes heard hammering at night in Homaer. Houses were later built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn myn feintetiid, doe't ik noch yn 'e hûs wie, haw ik hjir yn 'e Homear wol gauris timmerjen heard yn 'e nacht.\nMyn maten ek wol. As wy jouns bûtendoar kommen wie 't dúdlik to hearren. Letter kommen dêr huzen to stean op de plakken dêr't wy it hearden. 't Wie tjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27346,"r":"CJ065103","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman sometimes heard hammering at a place where nothing could be seen. Later a new house was built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem fortelde dat se yn Drachtster Kompenije wolris timmerjen heard hie en planken forgoaid. Letter kom der op dat plak in hûs to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27349,"r":"CJ065106","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once saw a light at a small labourer's cottage. Later a farm came there, with a great many lamps.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem wie us mei ús Jelle, de âldste fan myn bruorren nei Jan Flik ta to skuonpassen, hwant Jelle moest in pear nije skuon ha. Wy as bern krigen de ynstruksjes, wy mochten der net útkomme.\nDoe seagen mem en Jelle in ljochtsje krekt oer de sleat.\nDêr stie doe in lyts arbeidershúske. Letter kom dêr in plaetske op. Doe wie 't allegear ljocht. Dat ljochtsje dat sy doe sjoen ha, wie foartjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27394,"r":"CJ065301","p":"Rohel","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A boy often saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, ghost lights). Later wagons came by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik bin geboaren yn Sweagerbosk. Dêr seach ik yn myn jongesjierren wolris wylde lantearnen. Dy seach ik by 't tsjuster. Ik wie jouns faek op 'e swabber. Letter kommen dêr weinen lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27396,"r":"CJ065303","p":"Rohel","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once heard hammering on the other side of the water. Half a year later a new little house was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie ris in kear yn 'e nacht by de Swâdde. Doe hearde ik hwat. Ik tocht: hwat is my dit. Ik harkje en harkje en harkje. De Swâdde giet fan Twizel nei Kollumersweach. Der lei gjin barte oer. Ik hearde timmerjen oan 'e oare kant. It timmere mar fuort en mar wei en de planken rattelen.\nIk sei: Dit is tjirmerij. Hjir komt in nij húske.\nIn healjier letter, dêr kommen de timmerlju al oan. Der woarde in nij húske delset.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27401,"r":"CJ065308","p":"Rohel","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Knjillis Veenstra predicted to a young man that he would marry and have a child, but that both would die. Then he would marry again and have a child, and then his second wife would also die. The man did not believe a word of it, but it did come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn omke Marten kom by Marij. Dêr hied er forkearing mei.\nLetter is er ek mei har troud. Doe't dat gebeurde sei Kees (= Knjillis Veenstra): \"Dy hâldtstû net sa lang.\"\n\"Hwerom net?\" sei omke Marten.\n\"Dû krijst der in poppe by,\" sei Kees, \"mar dy hâldst ek net. Sy geane beide dea. Dû silst letter wer trouwe.\nEn dat frommes krijst ek bern by, mar dat frommes giet ek dea.\"\nMartenom leaude der neat fan.\nHy forlear syn earste wiif mei 't bern. Doe troude er wer.\nMarten-om gong nei de Poes ta to wenjen (ûnder Surhuzum).\nHy woarde fêste arbeider by in boer. De moarns fjouwer ûre moest hy dêr wêze. Op in kear hied er him hwat forsliept. Doe kom er even nei fjouweren by de boer.\nSeis ûre joech Baeije-muoi de poppe noch drinken. Doe klaeide se har pûr-neaken út en gong de lannen troch. Doe kom se foar de feart. Dêr soe se troch om nei har suster ta. Doe forsûpte se.\nIk haw dat allegear fan tofoaren sjoen. Ik seach dat se fordronk, neaken. Sy gong troch de toarnen hinne, en plof. - Ik der as de duvel hinne. Mar der wie neat by de feart. 't Wie foartjirmerij.\nIk sei tsjin omke: \"Ik ha hwat sjoen fan Baeije-muoi.\"\nIk haw him alles forteld. Mar hy leaude my net.\nDoe koed er it letter sels sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27476,"r":"CJ066002","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once saw a big thing standing on the table, but did not know what it was. A week later she got a sewing machine in a cabinet. It stood on the table. That was the thing she had seen before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Sumar wenne myn skoanmem. Dy seach op in kear, wylst se op bêd lei in great ding op 'e tafel stean. Mar sy wist net hwat it wie.\nIn wike letter krige se in naeimasine mei in kast der omhinne. Dy stie op 'e tafel. Dat hie it ding west dat se de wyks tofoaren sjoen hie. 't Wie tjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27484,"r":"CJ066105","p":"Frieschepalen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman became afraid to sleep alone in the house when she regularly heard hammering at night. Later the house was renovated.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik noch yn Tolbert wenne mei myn man gebeurde 't faek dat myn man hiele skoften fuort wie nei de Grinzer klaei to flaechsteppen of nei de Fryske klaei to meanen en to ûngetiidzjen.\nDan wie ik allinnich thús. Myn buorfrou sei us in kear tsjin my: \"It spûket yn jimme hûs (dat is nou sechstich jier lyn).\nDoarre jo dêr allinne to wêzen?\"\nDoe bigong ik der acht op to slaen. Doe fornom ik, dat der nachts hyltyd timmere woarde. Ik woarde der binaud fan.\nIk sei tsjin myn man: \"Ik doar hjir nachts net langer allinne to sliepen.\" Doe krige ik in frommeske by ús to sliepen.\nIt húske stie oan ''t Stille pad'. Letter is 't fortimmere woarn, doe wennen wy der al net mear.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27492,"r":"CJ066404","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once clearly heard planks and beams being thrown about. But he saw nothing. Later a new orphanage was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie in dûmny dy wenne yn Neerbosch. Dy hearde op in kear dúdlik dat se mei planken en balken smieten, mar doe't hy der hinne gong wie der neat. Letter kom dêr op dat plak in great weeshûs to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27568,"r":"CJ067101","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the place where there is now a main road, people used to always see wild lanterns.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger seagen wy allegear ljochtsjes. Dat wienen wylde lantearnen. 't Wie op it plak, dêr't nou rykswei 43 is.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27668,"r":"CJ068014","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man often saw lights flying. Later he understood that they had been the forerunners of car headlights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us pake - Fokke Ulkes Boijus - wenne hjir achter de Bosk. Hy seach ljochten fleanen en wist doe net hwat dat wie. Letter woarde it him dúdlik. It hienen de foarboaden west fan 'e lettere autoljochten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27705,"r":"CJ068502","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People heard the sound of hammering and planks being thrown close to their house. But there was nothing to be seen. Later a new house was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en dy wennen yn 'e Harkema yn 'e Klontsjebuorren, ticht by de poel. Nachts hearden se dêr timmerjen bûtendoar. Der woarde mei planken smiten en al sokke lûden mear. Mar as se der hinne gongen to sjen, wie der neat. In skoft letter kom dêr in nij hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27762,"r":"CJ068901","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man heard hammering at night. Later a new house was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wenne oan 'e Bethlehemsreed yn 'e Boelensloane. Dêr hearde ik nachts timmerjen. Letter kom dêr flak by ús in hûs to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27782,"r":"CJ069101","p":"Franeker","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People once heard the sound of hammering, but there was nothing to be seen. Later a new house appeared.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Surhuzum wienen guon dy hearden timmerjen en smiten mei balken. Mar der wie neat to sjen. Doe seinen se: \"Dêr komt grif in nij hûs.\" En 't wie ek sa. De pleats fan Jan IJes waerd dêr letter boud.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27783,"r":"CJ069102","p":"Franeker","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People already heard the singing of psalms before a church was built in a certain place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ds. Warmolds hat in houten tsjerkje sette litten yn 'e Harkema. Dat wie ûnder 'e Smoarhoeke. Foardat se mei 't bouwen bigongen hearden guon it psalmsjongen dêr al op dat plak.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27807,"r":"CJ069202","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People once used to see wild lanterns. Later a new farm appeared on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Surhuzum seagen se froeger op in plak in wylde lantearne. Letter kom der op datselde plak in buorkerij to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27816,"r":"CJ069403","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When a peacock screams, rain is coming.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":27840,"r":"CJ069602","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People once saw a light in a certain place. Later a new house appeared on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Het was ook in Opende dat de mensen een licht gezien hadden ergens. Later kwam daar een huus te staan. Ze hadden de lamp al tevoren zien branden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27863,"r":"CJ069902","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once saw wild lanterns in a certain place. Later a new farm appeared on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us beppe dy seach us in wylde lantearne yn 'e Wierren.\nLetter kom der op datselde plak in boereplaets to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27864,"r":"CJ069903","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening a few children and their grandmother heard hammering outside. Later a new farm appeared.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in joun wienen wy as bern mei beppe bûtendoar. Doe sei beppe tsjin ús: \"Hear us hoe't it der dêr oan wei giet.\" Wy hearden earst neat, mar doe't wy ús goed nei harkjen setten, doe hearden wy ek dúdlik dat der timmere en klundere woarde en sa nou en dan wie 't klets. Krekt as woarde der mei planken en balken smiten. Letter kom op dat plak in plaets to stean. 't Wie yn 'e Wierren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27902,"r":"CJ070116","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People used to often see wild lanterns on the heath. They were the forerunners of bicycle lamps.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oer de heide to Boelensloane woarden froeger faek wylde lantearnen sjoen. Mem sei letter altyd: dat ha de foarboaden west fan 'e fytslampen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27975,"r":"CJ070803","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman regularly heard planks being flung about. She knew then that another new house would be built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hearde ek altyd dúdlik as se mei planken omsmieten. Dan wie der neat to sjen. Dan sei 'k tsjin 'e bern: \"Hjir komt wer in nij hûs, hear.\" 't Komt altyd nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27976,"r":"CJ070804","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman often heard in advance that her son would come by. She also saw in advance that her grandson would get his diploma.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn soan komt hjir jouns altyd om njoggen ûre om de doar op slot to dwaen. Mar ik hear him altyd al fan tofoaren. Alle jounen.\nMiddeis om in ûre of twa komt hjir faek ien om in praetsje. Dat wyt ik al om tolve ûre. Dan ha 'k dyselde al sjoen.\nIen fan myn bernsbern moest foarige maend examen dwaen. Ik sei: \"Meitsje dy mar net ûngerust, hear. Dû komst der troch. Mar dû mast it net tsjin jim heit en dy sizze.\"\nIk hie him in dei of trije fan tofoaren al mei 't diploma sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27978,"r":"CJ070901","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man was once walking past a house when he heard all kinds of noises. Stones and planks were being flung about. But there was nothing to be seen. Later the house was demolished, and he heard the same noises.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wenne yn Stiensgea as boerefeint yn 't Oast. Op in joun hie 'k nei myn suster ta west, dy biwosk my. Ik hie forskjinnersguod ophelle. Doe't ik al hast wer toplak wie, en oan in âld húske ta wie, doe hearde ik der by dat húske allerhande lûden fan smiten mei stiennen en planken. Doe't ik dêr hinne gong wie der neat to sjen.\nIn skoft letter kom dat húske der ôf.\nIk stie op in moarn op 'e skerne, dêr't ik oan 't wurk wie. Doe hearde ik krekt deselde lûden wer. Mar doe wienen se echt oan 't ôfbrekken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27992,"r":"CJ071001","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On a spot where people used to see wild lanterns, a new house later appeared.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 'e Skieding wie froeger in wylde lantearne. Op it plak dêr't er stean bleau is letter, nei safolle tiid, in hûs kom to stean. De minsken seinen doe al dat dat letter gebeure soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28009,"r":"CJ071109","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once heard noises as if planks were being thrown. There was nothing to be seen. Later a new house was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie ris op in kear oan 't houtsjen achter hûs, doe hearde ik ynienen in klap, krekt as woarden der planken delsmiten. Ik woarde der kjel fan. Op itselde plak dêr't dy klap weikom bouden se it jiers dêroan in nij hûs. It is it hûs dêr't nou suster Cats yn wennet.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28011,"r":"CJ071111","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Two men hunting polecats once saw a lamp hanging from a beam, and right after it had vanished. Later a new farm appeared on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn pake en de pake fan myn frou wienen togearre op in nacht oan 't murdejeijen yn Twizelerheide. Doe seagen se allebeide ynienen oan 't Wyldpaed heech byntwurk foar har, dêr't in gewoane lantearne yn hong. It wie ek sa ynienen wer fuort.\nIt oare jiers is der op dat plak op it lân fan 'e Kloksheide in boerespultsje set woarn - dêr hienen hja doe it byntwurk fan sjoen. 't Is in spultsje fan 'e Herf. tsjerke yn Twizel, dêr't nou Boele Westra op wennet.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28029,"r":"CJ071211","p":"Kornhorn","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When there are two magpies close to a house, something new will happen within a day and a half.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Als er twee eksters dicht bij huis zijn, dan gebeurt er nieuws, met een of anderhalve dag."},{"n":28038,"r":"CJ071303","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman often heard hammering in a certain place. Later a whole lot of new houses appeared there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen froeger yn Boelensloane. Us mem hearde dêr faek timmerjen yn 'e nacht. Dan sei se: \"It wurde hjir skielk allegearre huzen.\" En dat is ek neikom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28078,"r":"CJ071702","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night people heard hammering in their house. Not long after, the house was renovated.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 't hûs, dêr't wy nou yn wenje, hearden wy even foardat it fan binnen fortimmere woarde, yn 'e nacht hyltyd getimmer. Dat wie foartjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28083,"r":"CJ071707","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once heard children screaming in an empty house. She predicted that a family with children would soon come to live there. That indeed happened.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e hoeke fan 'e Skjippedrifte en 'e Boskwei (krekt ûnder Droegeham) wennen Fokke en Saekje. Dy gongen dêr wei en doe kom it hûs gâns in set leech to stean. Op in kear kom ús mem dêr lâns. Doe hearde se yn dat lege hûs dúdlik bern razen. En dochs wie der op dat stuit net ien yn.\nMem sei: \"Hjir komt in húshâlding mei bern yn.\" En 't wie ek sa. Ridlik gau dêrnei kom Jehannes Bergsma der yn mei syn wiif en bern.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28086,"r":"CJ071710","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"During the war a group of Frisians were once working in the fields. A magpie was chattering a few metres away, and they thought something was about to happen. Half an hour later the Krauts came with big trucks and took the men away.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wienen foar de poepen oan 't wurk yn 't Joadefjild oan dizze kant Mearum. 't Wie yn 'e oarloch. Doe kom der in ekster op ús ta, dy bleau op in pear meter fan ús ôf.\nWopke Hoekstra, in maet fan my, sei: \"Der komt aenst hwat to dwaen.\" Hwant dy ekster skattere mar. Hy woe hwat fortelle. Gjin healûre letter kommen der greate weinen oan fan 'e poepen. Dêr woarden wy ynladen om nei Appingedam ta, dêr moesten wy oan 't wurk. Guon seagen noch kâns om út to naeijen. Ik ha fjirtsjin dagen yn Appingedam tahâlden. Doe krige ik in ûngelok mei de hân. Ik die 't willemoeds. Doe koe 'k net mear hwat dwaen. Ik rekke nei hûs ta. De oaren woarden nei Dútslân transporteard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28110,"r":"CJ071817","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When the evening sun makes it look as if a house is on fire, a strong wind is coming. When the gulls glide high in the sky without moving their wings, a strong wind is coming too. When the sky is completely clear, without a single cloud, rain will come within three days.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As jouns de sinne gleon op 'e glêzen skynt en 't liket fan fierrrens krekt as stiet it hûs yn 'e brân, dan komt der hurde wyn.\nAs de kobben heech yn 'e loft soeije, sûnder dat se de wjokken biwege, komt der ek hurde wyn.\nAs de loft alhielendal klear is, sûnder in wolkje, komt der binne trije dagen rein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28119,"r":"CJ071826","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Never step on a snail. Then it will start to thunder. If a snail has mud on its tail, we will get rain.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Traepje noait op in slak. Dan bigjint it to tongerjen.\nHat in slak modder op 'e sturt, dan krije wy rein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28194,"r":"CJ072701","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Six soldiers were on patrol one night when they heard galloping horses and running dogs approaching. They quickly lay down on the ground. But they saw nothing at all go by. It was an omen of the Germans who crossed the border in 1940.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik lei ûnder tsjinst yn Brabân yn 'e jierren 1914-18, flak by de Belgyske grins. Goorle hiet it doarpke dêr. Ik moest mei noch ien patrouilleare yn 'e nacht. Der gong noch in trêdden frywillich mei. Yn 'e nacht metten wy noch trije.\nWy roannen mei ús seizen fierder. Doe hearden wy ynienen achter ús in hiel sterk lûd as fan in keppel hynders, dat der oan galoppearjen kom en dêr wienen grouwe hounen by, dy't blaesden. Se wienen flak by ús, wy koenen net mear út 'e wei komme.\n\"Gean lizzen,\" sei 'k, \"hwant sy rinne oer ús hinne.\"\nMar der wie neat. Der hat noait hwat west. En doch hearden wy 't alle seis, sa lûd wie 't. Wy wienen allegear sa wyt as deaden om 'e holle, hwant wy tochten net oars as: nou gean wy der oan.\nIt hat foartjirmerij west fan 'e Dútsers, dy't yn 1940 oer de grins kom binne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28220,"r":"CJ072902","p":"Kornhorn","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In a place where a house was later built, people had earlier seen a lamp.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op Hogerom onder Noordwijk het in huus stoan, dat is der nou of. Foardat dat der stond soagen de mensen doar in lamp, zo leek it. Ik sag it self ook.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28221,"r":"CJ072903","p":"Kornhorn","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Near Opeinde, people often heard hammering. A new house would then always appear on that spot later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In de buurt van Opende hoorden se faak timmeren van tevoren als doar loater in huus boud werd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28265,"r":"CJ073209","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once heard a hammer striking an anvil, while there was nothing to be seen. Later a smithy appeared on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dyselde Syberen Hofstra hearde ek op in kear by harren op in plak dêr't hielendal net in hûs stie, hoe't der mei in hammer op in ambyld slein woarde. Letter kom der op dat plak in smederij to stean. Nou wennet Douwe v.d. Molen dêr.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28266,"r":"CJ073210","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once heard wagons driving where there was not even a road. Later a road was built on that spot and wagons really drove there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Nijlamer wienen it froeger allegearre petgatten en wiken. Syberen Hofstra hearde dêr op in kear de weinen oer de diken (= wegen) riden. Letter is de hiele saek der ûntgonnen. Doe rieden de weinen dêr lâns. Dat hie er fantofoaren al heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28281,"r":"CJ073303","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People used to see wild lanterns now and then. Later a new house would appear on such a spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy seagen froeger wolris wylde lantearnen. Letter seinen se, doe't der huzen boud woarden: dêr ha wy froeger in wylde lantearne sjoen. Sa ha se ek in wylde lantearne sjoen op it plak dêr't letter Jelle de Wind wenne hat, op 'e Bulten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28312,"r":"CJ073701","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a woman heard hammering and the throwing of planks outside. A year later a new house was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en mem wennen yn 'e Houtigehage, sahwat krekt op 'e grins fan Boelensloane. Op in moarn sei mem tsjin heit: \"Der woarde fannacht sa timmere en mei planken smiten hjir op 'e heide, ik ha der net fan sliepe kind. Hjir komt grif in nij hûs.\" In jier letter stie dat hûs dêr.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28328,"r":"CJ073904","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People once heard hammering in the night. Later a new house appeared on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir oan 'e Bethlehemsreed hearden guon ris yn 'e nacht dat it op in timmerjen gong. Letter kom der op dat plak in hûs to stean. 't Wie foartjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28352,"r":"CJ074110","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People heard wagons driving at a certain spot. Later a new polder was laid out there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't de Nijlamer polder oanmakke woarde ha guon dat fan to foaren heard. Krekt even oer de Tsjonger hearden se de weinen riden. Letter is dat neikom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28358,"r":"CJ074116","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once saw her husband coming home with a sack of rags. But when it took very long for him to come into the house, the woman went outside to look. There was no one to be seen. The man only came home half an hour later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha wol yn fodden handele. Op in kear wie myn frou allinne thús. Doe seach se my oankommen mei in sekfol fodden.\nDoe tocht se: \"Hwat duorret dit lang foardat er by de doar is. Ik mei wolris even sjen.\" Hja nei de doar, dy't se iepen die en sjen. Mar ik wie der net. En doch hie se my klear sjoen. In healûre letter kom ik thús mei de fodden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28359,"r":"CJ074117","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A couple once saw an acquaintance approaching, and they opened the door. But there was no one outside. A quarter of an hour later that person really did arrive.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sa gebeurde 't ek us op in snein-to-middei. Ik en 'e frou wienen togearre thús. Doe seagen wy ien oankommen. Hy kom by de doar. Wy soenen de doar iependwaen en doe wie hy der net. Even letter - 't mei in goed kertier west ha - doe kòm er.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28374,"r":"CJ074208","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man once said that strange times were coming. He had seen a potato with a fork in it in the sky. Shortly afterwards the Second World War began.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear kom heit yn 'e hûs. Hy wie sa bleek as in doek en alhiel fan 'e wize. Hy sei: \"Nou krije wy in rare tiid. Der stiet in ierappel oan 'e loft mei in foarke der yn!\" Hy seach deabinaud. Fuort dêrnei krigen wy de oarloch fan '40 op '45.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28381,"r":"CJ074215","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A few young men once heard a droning in the sky. They were frightened. It was a foreshadowing of the aeroplanes that came later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn man Bounse fortelde, hy wie ris in kear mei in pear maten op 'e wei fan 't Wytfean nei de Rottefalle. Yn 'e hoeke, dêr't nou Jurjen Kloosterman wennet, hearden se ynienen in hiel lûd gebrom yn 'e loft. It wie sahwat boven Rottefalle dêr't it lûd wie. Sy woarden sa bang dat sy gongen yn 'e kant fan 'e sleat lizzen.\nDat hat de foarboade west fan 'e lettere fliegmasines.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28386,"r":"CJ074220","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once predicted that that month would be a very rough month.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Frou Reitsma sei, de septembermaend (69) soe in hiele rûzige maend wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28389,"r":"CJ074223","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman was to come and help at the birth of her daughter-in-law's child. When her son came to fetch her, she said she had already heard him knock twice that morning.\nA girl had to marry her boyfriend. A woman told another girl that the same would soon happen to her. Two months later it had already come to that.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn suster Roas fortelde ek. Ik moest ris in kear in bern ha. Wy wennen hwat ôfgelegen. As it ûnwaer woarde, soe myn man skoanmem helje (âlde frou Reitsma) en dêrnei nei dokter ta. De moarns kom er by syn mem.\n\"Kom,\" sei se, \"wiest dêr al. Ik tocht al, soed er hast ris komme, hwant ik hie dy fan 'e moarn al twa kear klopjen heard. Dit wie de trêdde kear.\"\nRoas fortelde ek:\nIn dochter fan Ruerd-molkrider moest trouwe. Us Pytsje har man sei tsjin har: \"Nou ryd ik dy.\" En hy helle it jonge spantsje op om nei 't gemeentehûs to bringen.\nDoe gong âlde frou Reitsma èk mei.\nDoe sei se tsjin ús Pytsje: \"Pas mar op, fanke, ditselde hinget dy ek gau boven de holle.\"\nSy krige gelyk. Nei twa maenden wie 't al sa fier mei ús Pytsje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28429,"r":"CJ074701","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A boy once heard hammering in an old school, but in reality there was nothing. Later the school was rebuilt.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn wiif har folk wenne achter de âld Staetsskoalle yn Broek. Op in kear doe kom har broer de jouns thús. Hy sei: \"Hwat wurdt der timmere yn 'e âld-skoalle.\" Dat wie foartjirmerij. \"Harkje ris\", sei er, en doe hearden de oaren it ek.\nDe hiele skoalle is koarte tiid dêrnei fornijd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28430,"r":"CJ074702","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot, in stormy weather, people saw lots of lights along the roads. Later many houses were built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As it ûnwarich wie en der wie rein en stoarm op til, dan kommen der allegear ljochtsjes by de reden lâns. Dat woarden letter allegear ljochtsjes by de reden lâns. Dat woarden letter allegear huzen. Ien fan dy ljochtsjes sloech ris in kear fêst yn in hage - dat hat dêr doe wit hoe lang brând. (Dy huzen kommen to stean tusken Frijstêd en Broek yn. Dêr wienen dy ljochtsjes doe ek. 't Wienen wylde lantearnen.)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28432,"r":"CJ074704","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone heard hammering at night. Later new houses were built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As ik op bêd lei yn 'e Falom hearde ik nachts it timmerjen oan 'e huzen, dy't der letter kom binne. Dat wie ek foartjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28477,"r":"CJ075307","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A brother of my wife's grandmother could also predict things. In 1825 he arrives pale at his sister's house and wants to leave again at once, because he has seen that the dikes near his home have burst and has seen the house floating. When he returns, the people in his house have indeed drowned and the house is floating on the water. He is a helmdrager (one born with a caul).","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In broer fan myn frou har beppe seach de dingen ek fan tofoaren. Hy wenne yn Hollân. It gebeurde yn 1825, dat er útfanhûze by syn suster yn Beets.\nOp in dei, doe kom er fan 't húske, sa bleek as in doek. En hy seach sà raer.\n\"Hwat ha wy nou mei dy?\" sei beppe.\nHy sei: \"Ik ha hwat raers sjoen. Ik mat nei hûs ta.\"\n\"Dû bist hjir noch mar krekt,\" sei beppe, \"soest hjir ommers in wike bliuwe.\"\nDoe sei er: \"Hwat ik sjoen ha is net bêst. De diken binne by ús trochbrutsen. Ik ha myn hûs driuwen sjoen. Ik mat der hinne. Ik wyt net as ik myn folk wol wèr sjoch.\"\nHy is hals oer de kop fuortrekke.\nSyn folk hat er net wer sjoen. Se wienen allegear al fordronken en syn hûs dreau op it wetter. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28480,"r":"CJ075310","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In Feanwâldsterwâl people hear hammering all night at a certain spot, but see nothing. Later their son returns from America and suggests fixing up and remodelling the old house. These are the sounds they had heard earlier.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen yn Feanwâldsterwâl. Ik wie in jonge fan sa'n jier of tolve. Doe woarde der by ús folk sein: Dêr en dêr wurdt nachts hyltyd timmere. Altyd op 't selde plak. Hwat mei dat wêze? Der gebeurde lykwols neat.\nIn skoft letter kom der in soan thús út Amerika, dy syn âlden wennen yn it hûs, dêr't it yn 'e nacht op in timmerjen gong.\nDy soan sei: \"Dit âld hûs wurdt ek minder, net?\"\n\"Ja\", seinen syn âlden.\nHy sei: \"Ik ha nou aerdich hwat sinten. Wy sille 't hûs opknappe en fortimmerje.\" En dat is ek gebeurd.\nDat wienen de lûden dy't de minsken al earder heard hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28496,"r":"CJ075601","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In Harkema people hear hammering at night at a spot near Smoarhoeke, but there is nothing to be seen there. Later a house is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Smoarhoeke yn 'e Harkema hearden guon yn 'e nacht dúdlik timmerjen op in plak. Sy gongen der hinne, mar doe wie dêr net ien en sy hearden it timmerjen ek net mear.\nLetter kom der op dat plak in hûs to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28500,"r":"CJ075605","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"An old man falls ill and says at one point that there are many people in the house, naming them all. At that moment only one of them is present. When the man dies, the very people he named do indeed come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wenne in man dy wie al op jierren. Hy woarde siik.\nDoe sei er op in stuit: \"Och, och, hwat binne hjir in minsken yn 'e hûs.\" Hy koe se samar opneame. Doe wie der op dat stuit mar ien.\nIn skoftsje letter stoar dy âld man. Doe kommen der in protte minsken. It wienen deselden dy't hy opneamd hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28588,"r":"CJ076403","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Harm Schievink once predicted that Harkema would become a town, though he would not live to see it himself. Now it is starting to look that way, and Harkema is the largest place in the municipality.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Harm Schievink hat ris foarsein, Harkema soe nochris in stêd wurde, mar hy soe 't net mear bileve. 't Is wol fyftich jier lyn dat er dat sein hat. Hy ried mei de hounekarre. It bigjint der al op to lykjen. Harkema is 't greatste plak fan 'e gemeente.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28593,"r":"CJ076408","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hindrik Schievink lives in Harkema and his daughter in Brabant. When she is pregnant, a bird comes to his door and Hindrik knows he is going to be a grandfather. It always comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hindrik Schievink wenne hjir yn 'e Harkema. 't Wie al in âld man. Syn dochter wenne yn Brabân.\nAs syn dochter wer in lytsen forwachte, kom der in fûgel by him by de doar.\nDan sei Hindrik: \"Ik wurd èk wer pake.\" En it kom altyd nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28605,"r":"CJ076510","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"I hear omens myself too, because I worked in the mines in Limburg and heard hammering sounds there, at places where something later changed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Iksels fornim ek wolris dingen fan tofoaren. Ik ha fiif jier lang yn Limburch west yn 'e minen. Dêr hearde ik soms de lûden fan timmerjen. Dan woarde dêr op datselde plak letter hwat foroare. Dat kom altyd nei. Soms hearde ik it wol in healjier fan tofoaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28640,"r":"CJ077204","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In Noordermeer people regularly hear hammering at the corner by the Simmerdijk, on the spot where Jan Vonk's house was later built. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen yn Noardermar. Guon hearden dêr geregeld timmerjen op 'e hoeke by de Simmerdyk.\nLetter is dêr in hûs delset, dêr't Jan Vonk yn kom is to wenjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28674,"r":"CJ077606","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man who has never been to Amsterdam nevertheless knows his way around there; he knows exactly where he has to go.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit (skoanheit) siet froeger yn 'e tsjerkerie. Doe moest er ris mei guon nei Amsterdam nei de klassisforgadering.\nDat wie doe mei Geelkerken en 't Hersteld Verband.\nSkoanheit hie noch noait fierder west as Drachten. En hy hie nei de Grinzer Klaei west to wjudden. Mar Hollân dêr hied er noch noait in foet set.\nDoe't er yn Amsterdam kaem, sei er fuort: \"Dêr matte wy wêze.\" Hy herkende dêr alles. \"Ik ha hjir earder west\", sei er.\nHy wist it allegearre en 't kloppe as in bus.\nYn syn droom hied er alles fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28694,"r":"CJ077901","p":"Nieuweschoot","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man in the work crew sometimes clearly sees someone and even talks to him, while in reality that person is not there. He only really arrives later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie froeger in man by my yn 'e wurkploech, dat wie in skrandere keardel. Dy fortelde my, hy hie 't soms, dan wie der ien by him, dy seach er dúdlik en dêr praette er ek mei, mar yn werklikheit wie dyselde der net. Sa'n ien kom dan earst in skoft letter yn werklikheid.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28695,"r":"CJ077902","p":"Nieuweschoot","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"My neighbour in Nieuweschoot is expecting a child, and when the time comes he will knock on the window. One night I hear someone knock and say that it is time. Then my wife can assist the family. Nothing is happening yet, but the next day the child is born. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By myn buorman forwachten se in poppe, hjir yn Nijskoat.\nDer wie ôfpraet, as it sa fier wie soe myn frou de minsken bystean.\nDoe hearde ik op in nacht tige dúdlik klopjen op it glês.\n\"It is sa fier, hear\", woarde der sein.\nIk makke myn frou wekker en wy der ôf.\nMar der wie neat to rêdden.\nDe oare deis waerd it berntsje geboaren. Doe wie 't earst sa fier.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28696,"r":"CJ077903","p":"Nieuweschoot","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"My neighbour has a cow that is about to calve and needs my help. One night I hear knocking and go to the farmer, but the cow is not ready yet. That only happens a few days later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek in kear, doe hie myn buorman, dy't boer wie in koe, dy moest kjelje. Hy sei tsjin my: \"As 't sa fier is, en 't keal mat der ôflutsen wurde, wolle jo my dan helpe?\"\nIk sei: \"Dat komt yn oarder.\"\nDoe hearde ik yn 'e nacht dúdlik klopjen.\nIk der ôf en nei de boer ta, mar de koe wie noch net oan kealjen ta. Dat gebeurde pas in dei of hwat letter.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28709,"r":"CJ078109","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When a skipper at sea sees a pestvogel (plague bird), he becomes afraid, because then plague will break out on the ship.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in skipper op sé farde en hy seach in pestfûgel, dan woarde er bang, hwant dan kom de pest op it skip.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28736,"r":"CJ078401","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A little light burns in the Leeuwenpoel, and once people hear hammering there while there is nothing to be seen. Later part of the pool is drained, and on the spot where they saw the light and heard the sound a house is later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit fortelde, yn 'e Harkema, yn 'e Liuwe-poel brânde froeger altyd in ljochtsje. Forskeidene lju hienen it sjoen.\nHeit en dy gongen dêr ris op in joun lâns, doe hearden se dêr klear timmerjen. En dêr wie neat. Letter makken se in stik fan 'e Liuwe-poel droech.\nOp it plak, dêr't it ljochtsje brând hie en dêr't se letter timmerjen heard hienen, waerde in hûs delset.\n't Hie foartjirmerij west.","l":""},{"n":28766,"r":"CJ078707","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night Eatse hears hammering close to his house in Twijzelerheide, but there is nothing to be seen. Later a house is built on the same spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie in omke, dy hiet fan Eatse. Dy hearde ris op in nacht hoe't it tichte by syn hûs yn Twizelerheide op in timmerjen gong. Hy gong út bêd wei en nei bûten ta om to sjen hwat dat wêze koe, mar doe't er bûten wie fornom er neat mear, en der wie ek neat to sjen.\nDoe gong er wer op bêd. Hy lei noch mar even of doe hearde er it wèr. Hy tocht: Hwat dat is, wit ik net. Mar hy hearde sekuer timmerjen.\nLetter bouden se op dat plak in hûs. Doe kom 't him yn 't sin dat er dêr dy nachts timmerjen heard hie. 't Hie foartsjirmerije west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28770,"r":"CJ078802","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Father hears hammering at night in Harkema. Three years later his old house is demolished and a new one is built. This is what he heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik bin yn 'e Harkema yn 'e Bosk geboaren, skean tsjin Sjoerde Rienkje oer.\nOp in moarn kom ik fan bêd. Doe sei heit: \"Hwat is 't hjir op in timmerjen gong fannacht.\" Dat is nou krekt seisensechtich jier lyn.\nTrije jier dêrnei moest ús âld hûs der ôf. Doe woarde der in nij hûs delset. Dat hie heit heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28773,"r":"CJ078805","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At the corner of the Kleineweg, where cycle repairman Hager now lives, Tseard tells father they must step aside, because there is a big pig that is flying into the ditch. Father, however, sees nothing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De Lytse wei, dat wie froeger in modderpaed. Heit en myn broer Tseard roannen dêr togearre ris lâns. 't Wie op in joun. Sy wienen op 'e hoeke, dêr't nou de fytsmakker Hager wennet.\nDoe sei Tseard tsjin heit: \"Gean dêr even wei. Sjoch, dêr is in hiele grouwe, swarte baerch.\"\nHeit sei: \"Bist nou mâl, dû mei dyn fratsen altyd.\"\nMar Tseard sei: \"Sjoch, dy baerch fljocht dêr yn 'e sleat.\"\nHy hat letter altyd folhâlden dat er dêr in baerch sjoen hat.\nHy hat him ek wol deeglik sjoen, mar heit seach it net.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28775,"r":"CJ078807","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In Harkema, Anna and Baeije live in the woods, which belong to the municipality while the house belongs to the family. When the municipality buys the land too, the house is demolished. Father had heard this beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Harkema, yn 'e Bosk, stie in âld húske op 'e tippe, dêr wenne beppe yn mei har twadde man. Anne en Baeije hieten se. Heit sei altyd Anne-om tsjin him.\nOp in moarn sei heit: \"Anne-om kin fannacht wolris mei 't hûs oan 't ôfbrekken west ha, sa gong it der oan wei.\"\nIk wie doe noch in bern. De Bosk wie fan 'e gemeente.\nMar 't hûs dêr't Anne-om yn wenne mei 't hiem der by, dat wie fan ús famylje. Doe kocht de gemeente d_ groun èk. Doe kom 't hûs der ôf. Dat hie heit dy nachts fan tofoaren heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28776,"r":"CJ078808","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wild lanterns are often seen, and they later turn out to be bicycle lamps. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen ha wy wit hoe faek sjoen. Dat wienen de lettere fytslampen, biwearden se. 't Wie de foartsjirmerije fan 'e fytslampen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28778,"r":"CJ078810","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On the spot in Harkema where Warmolds later had a small wooden church built, people already heard trumpet and horn music beforehand. Later these instruments are played there during the sermons.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op it plak dêr't Warmolds letter yn 'e Harkema in houten tsjerkje delsette litten hat, hearden de minsken fan tofoaren al muzyk. 't Wie muzyk fan in trompet en in hoarn.\nLetter spilen se dêr op by de preken. Dat wie foartjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28796,"r":"CJ079001","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When father cannot sleep at night, he goes for a walk. After one such night he predicts the building of a new house, because he has heard hammering by the Bosweg. Some time later Lubbert Elzinga does indeed put up his house there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen yn 'e Bosk yn 'e Harkema. As ús heit nachts net sliepe koe, gong hy der út to kuijerjen. Dat hied er wer ris op in nacht dien. De oare moarns sieten wy om 'e tafel hinne. Heit siet der ek by. Doe sei er: \"Dêr komt in nij hûs.\"\n\"Hoe wyt heit dat?\" seinen wy.\n\"Ik bin fannacht bûten west,\" sei er, \"en doe hearde ik tsjin 'e Boskreed oer, yn 't hoekje dúdlik dat it dêr op in timmerjen gong. Wy laken der om, mar ús heit stie der fêst op.\nEn hy krige gelyk. In skoft letter sette Lubbert Elzinga dêr in nij hûs del.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28888,"r":"CJ079614","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"I am once out with a friend on the sheep track and, at the spot where the reed fence now stands, hear a strange sound coming from the Knjillisdiep. Later factories are built here and people hear the same sound we heard back then.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik sa'n twintich jier âld wie, wie 'k ris mei myn kammeraed op 'e Skieppedrifte. Wy wienen sahwat by it hoekje dêr't nou dy reidsketten steane. Doe hearden wy allebeide tagelyk in fremd lûd. Sa'n lûd hienen wy noch noait heard. It kom by 't Knjillisdjip wei.\nFolle letter kommen dêr fabriken to stean en nou heart men dêr krekt deselde lûden dy't wy dêr doe ien kear heard ha.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28906,"r":"CJ079718","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"There have been people who, on their way to the milking place, hear the sound of milk squirting into the pails while they are not there yet. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha guon kend, as dy moarns nei de jister ta soenen to melken, dan hearden se fan fierren al de speten fan 't melken yn 'e earnamers. Dan wienen se der noch lang net oan ta. Dat wie foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28924,"r":"CJ079908","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wild lanterns foretell the later bicycle lamps, and we used to see them very often in Bos.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen wie de foartsjirmerije fan 'e lettere fytslampen. Doe't wy froeger yn 'e Bosk wennen seagen wy se hiel folle.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33663,"r":"CJ092502","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A week before renovations were to start in a house, hammering could already be heard there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By ús Arentom en Jantsjemoai (Arent de Boer) soenen se timmerje. Hja hearden wol in wike tofoaren it timmerjen al en it forsetten fan planken yn eigen hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33667,"r":"CJ092506","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people sometimes saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, wandering lights). They were omens of the houses and bicycles that came later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen woarden der by de Skieding folle sjoen. It doelde op huzen en as se biweegden op fytsen ensa, dy't dêr letter komme soenen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29305,"r":"CJ080501","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a woman heard hammering. Within a year a new house was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie yn 't bigjin fan ús trouwen, wy wennen noch yn Jistrum. Wy leinen de nachts op bêd, doe hearde myn frou ynienen dat it bûten drok op in timmerjen gong. Sy tocht: hoe kin dit nou sa, midden yn 'e nacht?\nDe oare moarns sei se tsjin Sibbele Tryntsje, de buorfrou: \"Ha se by jimme fannacht sa timmere?\"\nIt minske wie forbaesd en sei: \"Né minske, hoe komme jo der by, der is noait timmere woarn.\"\n\"Nou,\" sei myn wiif, \"ik ha 't dochs klear heard.\"\nHja hie 't wol goed heard, hwant binnen 't jier krigen wy dêr in nij hûs, dat ha wy dêr doe timmerje litten.\nDêr wennet nou in broer fan my. 't Hie foartsjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29329,"r":"CJ080604","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman sometimes heard hammering. Later a new house would always be built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mem hat faek forteld, dat se froeger timmerjen hearden yn 'e Harkema op plakken dêr't dan letter in nij hûs kom to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29356,"r":"CJ080710","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wild lanterns were lights that people saw from afar. When they came closer, the lights had vanished. Later a real lamp post or a house would always appear on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen, dat wienen ljochten, dy seach men fan fierrens, mar as men der by kaem, dan wienen se fuort. 't Wie foartjirmerije. Letter kom der op sa'n plak in echte lantearne of in hûs. Ik ha 't sels wol meimakke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29382,"r":"CJ081001","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On a farm people sometimes heard hammering coming from the barn, while in reality there was nothing there. Later the socialists held noisy meetings there. Sermons were also preached there, and a pulpit was built for them. And later still the Reformed held Sunday school there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen yn Boelensloane tsjin 'e iepenbiere skoalle oer.\nWy hienen dêr buorkerije. 't Wie yn 1898, doe hearden mem en ik timmerjen en oar lawaei by ús yn 'e skuorre. Mar yn werkelikheit wie der neat to rêdden. Mar letter hâldden de soasialisten har forgaderingen yn 'e skuorre, dan gong 't der soms bot oan wei, en noch letter, doe't de tsjerke op 'e Loane net mear brûkt wurde koe, doe preken se by ús yn 'e skuorre.\nDoe woarde der in preekstoel yn timmere en mear sokke dingen. Nòch wer letter hâldden de grifformearden dêr sneinsskoalle. Aldy dingen hienen wy fan tofoaren heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29411,"r":"CJ081301","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman often heard hammering at night and predicted that new houses would be built. That came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanheit dat wie de bikende spylman Pije Rasp. Hy wenne mei syn frou meastal yn in woanwein. Dy stie faek yn 'e buert fan 'e Pipe to Drachten.\nSkoanmem hat faek forteld, dat se dêr gauris klopjen heard hie yn 'e nacht. Dan sei se: \"'t Wurde hjir skielk allegear huzen by de Pipe-brêge.\"\nEn dat is ek útkom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29418,"r":"CJ081308","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman often saw wild lanterns. Those were the later bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanmem seach faek wylde lantearnen. Dat wienen de lettere fytsljochten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29421,"r":"CJ081402","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once saw lots of little lights. She predicted that new houses would come. That came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Gryt-muoi (= Taeke Griet) sei yndertiid tsjin mem: \"'k Sjoch allegear ljochtsjes jouns yn 'e Harkema. Dat wurde stik foar stik nije huzen.\" It minske krige gelyk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29447,"r":"CJ081601","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man often heard hammering and planks being thrown at a certain spot. When he went to look, there was nothing to be seen. Later a large farm was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie in jonge fan sa'n jier of alve, tolve, doe haw ik ris ierappels socht op lân, dat lei oan 'e Hegewei by de Aldegeaster dyk. Der wie in âld mantsje, dy socht mei. Sy neamden him Jurjen bultsje omdat er miswoechsen wie, mar hy hiet Jurjen de Vries. Syn soan Knjillis bultsje socht ek mei.\nMoarns sawn ûre kom ik dêr op it lân. Dan bigoun de âld man fuort to fortellen oer foartsjirmerij, spûkerij en alsamear.\nOp in kear fortelde âlde Jurjen bultsje my: \"Ik wenne as boerefeint op 'e Nyegeaster hegewei. Der wie in lapskroar, dy biwosk my. Dêr kom ik dan jouns tsien ûre wei as ik har de smoarge wask brocht hie. Mar op 'e hoeke fan 'e Aldegeaster wei en de Kilometerwei hearde ik dan altyd stienbikjen en der woarde mei balken omsmiten ensa. Ik gong dêr dan hinne, op it lûd ta, mar dan wie der neat. Op 't lêst doarst ik der hast net mear lâns omdat der noait hwat wie en ik it dochs altyd klear hearde.\nMar doe is dêr letter in greate pleats delset woarn. Dy hearde oan 'e herfoarme tsjerke fan Nyegea.\"\nIk roan fan 'e Hegewei nei Aldegea. Dan moest ik dêr lâns.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29448,"r":"CJ081602","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot people often saw lights in the evening. Later a new house was built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By de Skieding op 'e Tike, op it plak, dêr't Paulusma nou syn garage hat, dêr seagen guon froeger altyd ljochten. Dat wie fansels altyd jouns. Se woenen biweare dat dat de ljochten wienen fan it hûs dat dêr letter delset is, dêr't Jan Tuinstra yn kom is to wenjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29449,"r":"CJ081603","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people sometimes saw a light flying over the heath. Later a tram came to run there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't wy bern wienen wennen heit en dy yn 'e Wierren by de polderdyk. (nou Tike). Doe wienen der gâns lju, dy seagen in ljocht fleanen oer Sumarreheide. Se woenen biweare dat dat it ljocht west hat fan 'e tram, dy't dêr letter kom is.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29460,"r":"CJ081701","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot people often saw a little light. When they came closer, the light went out. This happened up to three times. Later a new house was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr't nou it húske stiet fan greate Sije (= Sije Hoekstra) op 'e Skieding hjir, tichte by Paulusma, dêr brânde froeger in ljocht. As wy tichterby kommen gong it ljocht út. As wy dan wer fuort gongen, seagen wy it wer. Dat gong sa oan trije kear ta. Letter kom op dat plak it húske to stean, dat der nou nòch stiet.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32621,"r":"CJ081909","p":"Dokkum","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If you stamp a toad to death, thunder and rain will come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Een pad mochten we nooit doodtrappen, want dan kwam er onweer en regen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32662,"r":"CJ082303","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Little lights can be seen in a certain place in the evening. It is a portent: later a road is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By Mountsjetille oan 't Knjillisdjip seagen se froeger ljochtsjes by jountiid. Doe seinen se: \"Dêr komt in wei lâns skielk.\" En dy wei is der èk kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32742,"r":"CJ083104","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A churn that keeps turning all night is a portent of work that will be done the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Gebeurde wol dat de tsjerne de hiele nacht trochdraeide. Dat wie foartsjirmerij, dan soe der de oare deis wer brûkt wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32743,"r":"CJ083105","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears hammering in the middle of the night, although there is nothing to be seen. It is a portent: later a house is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Skoanheit soe op in moarn bitiid, om trije ûre hinne nei Eastemar ta to werken. Doe't er op 'e Bulten kom, gong it dêr bot op in timmerjen. Skoanheit bleau stean, it timmere mar troch. En doch wie der neat. Letter is dêr in nij hûs delset. De izerjoad kom dêr to wenjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32772,"r":"CJ083401","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the evening a child hears the sound of skipping rope when she is going to do it the next day. It is a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem hat wolris forteld, dat, as se toudounsje soe mei oare famkes, doe't hja noch in bern wie, dat hja dat dan de jouns fan tofoaren al hearde en fornaem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32776,"r":"CJ083405","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days, when will-o'-the-wisps were seen, a new road would soon be built on that spot. It was a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 't foarige hienen de minsken it wol gauris oer wylde lantearnen. As dy sjoen waerden, seinen se, dan soe dêr letter op dat plak in nije wei komme.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32823,"r":"CJ084105","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A mother predicts that her family will not live much longer in a certain place because she has heard sounds as if the house were being demolished. The sounds were indeed an omen: a few months later the house is really demolished.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha wenne yn in húske achter de Lange Wyk, in eintsje achterút. Doe sei ús mem op in kear: wy bliuwe hjir net lang mear to wenjen, hwant der wurdt mei balken en stiennen smiten. Ik ha 't klear heard. In pear maenden letter woarde 't hûs ôfbrutsen. 't Kom krektsa út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32831,"r":"CJ084113","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When magpies chatter close to the house, one of the residents will have an accident or something of the kind. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hja sizze, as de eksters skatterje tichte by in hûs, dan kriget der ien fan dat hûs in ûngelok of sa.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32914,"r":"CJ084802","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening a farming family heard a clattering of buckets of water and brooms. But when the eldest son went outside to look, there was nothing to be seen. A few days later someone came who really set about cleaning, and they heard exactly the same sounds again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Pein stie in boerespul yn de Bosk. Op in joun sieten se allegear by de tafel. Doe hearden se ynienen lawaei. Der woarde mei amers wetter smiten en mei luiwagens en biezems. En dat hie sa'n leven jown, dat sy wienen der allegear binaud fan woarn. \"Hwat mei dêr wêze,\" sei de boerinne, \"dêr doar ik noait hinne. Hwa fan jimme doart nei de doar ta.\"\nDoe wie de âldste soan op it lêst mar nei de doar ta gong, mar der wie alhiel neat to rêdden. 't Wie deastil. Sy bigrypten der neat fan. Mar twa dagen letter rekke lytse Ruerd de Graaf dêr oan 't hûshimmeljen. Doe hearden se presys deselde lûden en doe krigen se yn 'e gaten dat it foartsjirmerij west hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32959,"r":"CJ085012","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People sometimes heard hammering along a sandy road, but there was nothing to be seen. The hammer blows did not follow each other quickly. Some time later a new house was built, and they heard the slow blows again. The carpenter was rather lazy and so did not hammer very fast.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en dy ha froeger oan 'e Singel wenne yn 'e Smoarhoeke. Dat wie doe in sânwei. Op in joun sieten se byelkoar yn 'e hûs.\nDoe hearden se ynienen timmerjen. 't Wie tichteby. It wie in lome slach. Sy gongen der út om to sjen, mar doe wie 't dien. Doe't se wer yn 'e hûs sieten, hearden se 't wer.\n\"Hea, hwat kin dit wêze\", seinen se. Der wie bûten abslút neat to sjen.\nIn skoft letter krige dêr skean foar oer Sytse Nicolai in nij hûs. De timmerman dy't dêr by brûkt woarde, wie lui. Dy hie in hiele lome slach. Hy hie in hiele greate hoed op, tsjin 'e sinne, dat er goed yn 't skaed sitte koe to timmerjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32992,"r":"CJ085212","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A mother dreamt that her son would go to live in a new house. When not long afterwards he did indeed move, she recognised the house from her dream.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Fuort dêrnei hie heit syn âlde mem in droom hawn.\nHeit hie de kroech net krige. Hy moest der út en der wie noch gjin plak foar him.\nDoe droomde syn mem, hja seach in hûs. Hja hie der yn west. Hja wist krekt hoe't it der útseach. Dêr soe heit yn wenje. Dat soe heit keapje.\nDoe kocht heit yn 'e Harkema oan 'e lettere betonwei in arbeiderswente, dêr't ek hwat plak by wie foar fé.\nLetter kom heit syn mem by heit en dy om it hûs to bisjen. Oan 'e foarkant wie in ûnder- en bovendoar. Dy koe mei in ketting op slot set wurde.\nDoe sei beppe: \"Ja, dit hûs haw ik sjoen. Hjir haw ik west. Dit is it hûs, dat ik yn myn droom sjoen ha, Albert. Dit is it, bern.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33005,"r":"CJ085404","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Sometimes on a dark summer evening you would get little moths on your bicycle lamp. That was a bad sign.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jouns by donker wienen der simmers wolris lytse flinters op 'e fytslampe. Dat wie in min teken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33032,"r":"CJ086010","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the evening a man always heard the drone of some kind of engine, but he could not find where it came from. Not long afterwards his sons, who both had a lorry, came to visit. That was the sound he had heard before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jierren lyn gebeurde it dat ús heit en dy, as se jouns op bêd leinen, altyd hwat hearden dat se net thús bringe koenen.\nIt hie in soad fan motorgeronk, mar sy koenen har net bigripe dat it dat wêze koe, hwant der wienen dêr gjin moters.\nAlle jounen wie dat lûd der wer.\nDoe kochten myn broer en ik elk in frachtauto. Wy kommen der op in joun mei delsetten. De auto's kommen by heit en dy op it hiem to stean.\n\"Hark,\" sei heit tsjin mem, \"dêr is datselde geronk.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33065,"r":"CJ086408","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People often heard hammering nearby at night. Not long afterwards new houses were built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanâlden - Sytse Jager en 't wiif - wennen yn 'e Harkema yn in húske, dêr't nou de febryk fan Spimeta is.\nSkoanmem hearde dêr nacht op nacht de timmerman oan 't wurk. 't Gong der altyd mar op in timmerjen.\n\"Sytse, mast ris hearre,\" sei se tsjin skoanheit, \"sa timmerje se hjir.\" Skoanheit hearde it èk.\nKoarte tiid dêrnei ha se in nij achterein foar 't fé oan 't hûs krige. Dat wie it timmerjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33112,"r":"CJ087101","p":"Hallum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A farmhand often had prophetic dreams. Once he told the farmer he would stop working because he was going to get an ailment. The following year the farmhand got asthma, and then he did indeed stop working. He had been born with a caul.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wenne in man yn Hallum, dat wie in boerearbeider. Dy keardel wist allerhande dingen foarút, dy seach er dan yn syn droom. Op in kear sei er tsjin 'e boer: \"Ik gean út it wurk wei.\"\n\"Hwatte,\" sei de boer, \"dû út it wurk wei?\"\n\"Ja,\" sei er, \"ik krij in kwael. Dat haw ik droomd.\"\n\"Dû bist gek\", sei de boer.\nMar 't oare jiers krige er in kwael. Hy krige asthma en dat boaze sa hurd oan, dat hy rekke út it wurk wei.\nDy arbeider wie Pyt Soepboer.\nTsjin my hat er ris sein: \"Dû wurdtst net âld.\" Mar dêr hat er my, tink, mei bangmeitsje wold. Ik bin al ien en sauntich.\nFan sokke lju, dy't bigraffenissen ensa foarútsjen kinne sizze se hjir: dy binne mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33169,"r":"CJ087602","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A grandfather told his grandson, who lived with him, that he had heard hammering that night. Not long afterwards the man died. The grandson refurbished the room the old man had lived in. The man had heard that in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen yn 'e Harkema op 'e Bulten. Dêr ha wy fiif jier wenne, doe bin wy nei de Singel forhuze. Dat wie 't húske, dêr't mem har heit yn wenne. Dat kochten wy en doe kom pake by ús yn. Froeger hienen pake en beppe dêr in winkeltsje yn dat húske hawn. Dat foroaren wy doe yn in keammerke. Dêr kom pake yn en wysels wennen yn 'e keamer.\nPake hat net sa lang yn dat keammerke wenne. Hy kom to forstjerren en doe biwennen wy it hiele hûs. Doe ha wy dat keammerke fan pake nochris fortimmere.\nIn wykmannich foar syn dea sei pake op in moarn tsjin my: \"Hwat hastû justerjoun lang timmere. Wol oan tolve ûre ta.\"\nIk sei: \"Hoe krijt pake 't yn 'e holle, ik ha noait oan 't timmerjen west.\" Ik moest moarns fjouwer ûre by de boer wêze, dat ik gong jouns altyd bitiid op bêd.\nDoe't de âld-man weirekke woenen wy it keammerke foroarje. Nei in maend hie 'k it klear.\nOp in joun leinen myn wiif en ik togearre op bêd. Doe kom 't my samar ynienen yn 't sin hwat pake dy moarns alris sein hie. Ik sei tsjin 't wiif: \"Pake hat it net om 'e nocht sein. Ik ha twa jounen achterelkoar timmere oan tolve ûre ta. De âld-man hat wol gelyk krige.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33173,"r":"CJ087606","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once heard wood being unloaded from a wagon. Later a new house was built and she heard the same sound.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mem wenne tichte by it café fan Ruerde Baeije yn 'e Harkema. Op in joun hearde se dat der in wein oanroljen kom. Dêr woarde hout ôfsmiten. 't Wie dúdlik to hearren.\nHja sei: \"Hjir wurdt yn 't koart boud.\" En 't kom ek út. In skoft letter woarde dêr in nij hûs timmere. It hout woarde op in wein oanfierd en ôfladen. Dat hie sy heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33196,"r":"CJ087719","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman always heard in advance when the lime trees were going to be sawn down. One night she had heard it again. Her husband wanted to prove her wrong and ordered that the tree should not be sawn but chopped down. But when the labourer could not reach a branch, he took the saw, and the woman was proved right after all.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By de plaets fan Jan Gabes de Vries op it Wytfean stienen eartiids linebeammen foar de gevel. It woarde tiid dat dy wer opsnoeid wurde moesten.\nOp in nacht sei de frou tsjin 'e boer: \"Hark, sy saegje ek wer yn 'e linebeammen om.\"\nDe boer tochte: \"Dizze kear sil se ris gjin gelyk krije.\" Hy sei tsjin 't folk: \"De linebeammen matte bihimmele wurde, mar der mei net sage wurde. De takken wurde kapt.\" Hy woe de frou forbluffe.\nDe arbeider krûpt mei de leider yn 'e beam op. Hy sil de beam ynkoarte. Dat docht er mei de bile. Mar der is ien tokke, dy is hwat to fier fan him ôf. It handicht him net mei de bile.\nHy tocht: \"Nou krij ik de sage.\"\nWylst er oan 't saegjen wie, sei de frou: \"Hark, hearst it wol? Sy saegje yn 'e linebeam om.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33201,"r":"CJ087801","p":"Dokkum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night people heard hammering outside, but there was nothing to be seen. Later new houses were built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanheit wenne yn Ikkerwâld. Op in joun let mei moai helder waer hearde hy hiel bot timmerjen. 't Gong der och sa oan wei. Sy koenen har net bigripe hwat dat wêze koe, hwant 't wie dêr op 'e bare rûmte. Bûten har eigen hûs stie dêr nergens ien. Doe't se nei bûten ta gongen wie der neat to sjen. Mar in skoftsje letter bigongen se dêr to bouwen. In hiele rige hûzen woarde der delset, fan Patrimonium. Dat hie it timmerjen west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33202,"r":"CJ087802","p":"Dokkum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people sometimes saw will-o'-the-wisps flying along the road. They were the forerunners of bicycle lamps and car lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy seagen earen wolris wylde lantearnen. Sa'n lantearne fleach de wei lâns. Dat ha de foarboaden west fan 'e fytslampen en de autoljochten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33250,"r":"CJ088201","p":"Schagerbrug","v":"N.-H.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a woman heard hammering, though there was nothing to be seen. Later a new inn was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De frou fan Melle van der Wal, dy't nou op 'e Tike wennet, wenne alear op 'e Harste. Dêr hearde se op in nacht tige klear dat der timmere woarde. In skoft letter kom der op dat plak in herberch to stean. Dat wie it nije café fan Teunissen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33253,"r":"CJ088204","p":"Schagerbrug","v":"N.-H.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"All the will-o'-the-wisps seen on the heath were omens of things that came later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie soms allegear ljocht op 'e heide. Allegear wylde lantearnen. Dat hie altyd in bitsjutting; dan soe der letter hwat komme.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33287,"r":"CJ088405","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening people heard hammering. Not long afterwards a new house was built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By de Wopkepoel yn 'e Harkema stie in hûs, dêr wenne âlde dôve Tryn yn. Op in joun stienen wy bûten, ik mei noch in pear maten - 't wie noch fóár myn trouwen - doe gong it dêr hiel bot op in timmerjen. Wy hearden it dúdlik.\nEven letter is dêr in nij hûs kom. Der kôm Fokke fan Mekke Nicolai yn to wenjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33412,"r":"CJ089907","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People sometimes heard hammering at night in a certain spot. Later new houses were built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 'e Reitsma-strjitte steane twa huzen. Yn 't iene wennet Wopke van der Veen, yn 't oare Albert van der Veen. Foardat dy beide huzen der stienen ha de omwenners nachten oanien hyltyd timmerjen heard. Dat wie foartjirmerije. Dat is foar 100% de goudearlike warheid. (dat zegt hij af en toe)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34472,"r":"CJ090213","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, wandering lights) on the heath. Later new houses were built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger wienen 't hjir op 'e heide allegear ljochtsjes by jountiid. Dat neamden se wylde lantearnen. Dat binne letter allegear huzen woarn. Dêr wie 't foartsjirmerije fan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33438,"r":"CJ090301","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man sometimes heard an alarm clock ticking at night, but there was no alarm clock at all. Later a bedroom was built, and an alarm clock was put in it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie ien en tritich jier en ik wenne op 'e Iest hjir yn Jistrum. Dêr hearde ik op in joun tige dúdlik it tikjen fan in wekker. Dat gebeurde nei dy kear wol faker. Mar dêr wie gjin wekker. Letter woarde der op dat plak in sliepkeamer boud. Dêr kaem ek in wekker yn. Dy wekker hie ik fan tofoaren heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33450,"r":"CJ090313","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If you killed a snail, it would start to thunder.\nIf a dog howled eerily, someone would die.\nIf a magpie sat on a post, visitors would come, from the direction of its tail.\nIf a cat passed its paw over its ear while washing, talkative visitors would come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger woarde ús forteld, as men in slak dea die, dan bigoun it to tongerjen.\nAs in houn spûkgûlde gong der ien dea.\nAs in ekster op in pealtsje siet kom der bisite. De kant dêr't de ekster de sturt hie, fan dy kant kom de bisite wei.\nAs in kat him wasket en hy slacht him mei de poat oer 't ear dan komme der praters.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34510,"r":"CJ090724","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, wandering lights) are omens of houses, bicycles or cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen binne foartekens fan huzen of fytsen of auto's.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33517,"r":"CJ090901","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People once heard hammering on the heath, but there was nothing to be seen. Later new houses were built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen op in boerespultsje oan 't Wyldpaed ûnder Twizel. Dat spultsje stie tichte by de Kloksheide. Op in joun gongen heit en mem to jounpraten.\nDoe't se op 'e Kloksheide wienen, sei heit tsjin mem: \n\"Mast ris hearre, Sjut, sa giet it dêr op in timmerjen.\"\nMar der wie neat to sjen.\nNei forrin fan tiid woarde de hiele Kloksheide fol boud mei huzen. 't Wie by 't Wyldpaed. Heit en mem hienen fan to foaren dúdlik it klop-klop-klop fan it timmerjen heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33520,"r":"CJ090904","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people saw will-o'-the-wisps in a certain place. Later houses and a road were built there. The little lights were omens.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Se ha dêr letter wol faker wylde lantearnen sjoen. It wie foartsjirmerij, hwant de wei woarde forhurde en doe kamen dêr nije huzen. De ljochtsjes dêr fan jouns, dat wienen de wylde lantearnen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33527,"r":"CJ090911","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When magpies chatter, talkative visitors will come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters skatteren kommen der praters, wie 't sizzen altyd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33579,"r":"CJ091219","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Swallows' nests bring luck. But if someone destroys them, they bring bad luck.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Swellenestkes mat men noait útroegje, hwant se bringe gelok oan. Docht men it al dan komt der ûngelok achter wei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33581,"r":"CJ091221","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When a dog starts howling eerily, it is a bad sign.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":33593,"r":"CJ091409","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If you have a swallows' nest and leave it alone, it brings luck. If you take the eggs away, it brings misfortune. The eggs are poisoned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy mochten noait oan in swellenestje komme, en net heal de aikes úthelje. Der sit in forburgen iets yn dy aikes, se binne forgiftich. De sweltsjes binne feninich. Men mocht se gjin kwea dwaen, dan kom it net goed. Der sit in segen yn as men se by jin hat en men lit se gewurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33623,"r":"CJ091801","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A young man sometimes saw a lamp burning at a certain spot. Others saw nothing. Later two new houses were built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie sa'n foech jonge en wenne by bakker Vonk.\nJouns gong ik faek nei Brant en Mintsje ta. Dy wennen, krekt as Vonk, èk yn Drachtster Kompenije. (De man hiet Brant Pool). Hja hienen in dochter, dêr hie 'k wol hwat bistek op. Op in joun wie 'k dêr wèr.\n\"Ha jim hjir in nij hûs krige?\" frege ik. Hwant ik seach achter it hûs fan Brant Pool in ljocht brânnen; krekt as fan in petroaljelampe, dy't troch 't finster hinne ljochtet.\n\"Gjin sprake fan,\" sei Brant, \"hoe komst der by.\"\n\"Nou,\" sei 'k, \"der brânt ommers in ljocht.\"\n\"Der ìs gjin ljocht, jonge\", seinen Brant en Mintsje tagelyk.\n\"Ik sjoch it dúdlik,\" sei 'k, \"sjoch dan sels.\"\nMar hja koenen gjin ljocht gewaer wurde.\nIk seach it ljocht letter wer, faker as ien kear. Mar de oaren koenen it net sjen.\nSa'n twa, trije jier letter setten se dêr twa nije huzen del.\nYn 't iene kom in sekere Helder to wenjen, dy wie doe krekt fan Dútslân werom kom. 't Gebeurde sahwat yn 1918.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33716,"r":"CJ093602","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At one spot, people once heard planks and beams being carried around and thrown down. But there was nothing to be seen. Later a farm was built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op it sté dêr't nou Jille Tsjoelker wennet, hat froeger in boereplaets stien. Foardat dy der stie kom dêr op in joun ris ien lâns. Dy tocht: hwat giet it hjir op in smiten mei balken en planken, krekt as woarde der allegear materiael hinne brocht dat foar it timmerjen fan in hûs noadich wie. Hy woe der mear fan wite en gong der hinne. 't Wie in man fan 'e Houtigehage, dy hat it mysels forteld.\nMar der wie neat to sjen.\nIn healjier letter woarde dêr dy boereplaets boud.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34595,"r":"CJ093705","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People said the world would come to an end, but an old merchant said: \"The world will only end when the sea becomes land and straight roads appear on which things drive, without horses, all by themselves.\" Some of those things have come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn myn jonge jierren seinen se wol faek dat de wereld forgean soe. Dêr haw ik wol faek tige bang foar west.\nDoe wie der in âld man, in koopman, dy hiet fan Hoekstra, dy sei: \"De wereld forgiet noch lang net.\"\n\"De sé wurdt lân,\" sei er, \"dat mat earst noch woun wurde. Dan komme der allegear rjochte wegens en dêr sille dingen op ride sûnder hynders derfoar. Dy ride út harsels.\"\nDat seach er allegear foarút. Guon fan dy dingen binne neikom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34609,"r":"CJ093902","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days wandering lights were often seen. They were the lamps of bicycles and cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tsjin wylde lantearnen seinen wy ek wol swerfljochtsjes. Dy woardden froeger faek sjoen. It wienen de lettere lampen fan 'e fytsen en fan 'e auto's, ornearren se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33746,"r":"CJ094001","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people sometimes heard hammering. Then a new house would later be built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Westerein is 't faek gebeurd dat de minsken it timmerjen al fier fan tofoaren hearden fan in hûs dat noch boud wurde moest, mar ik kin sa net sizze fan hokker hûzen dat it gefal wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33806,"r":"CJ094401","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman once saw a light. Later a new house was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By 't spoar hat myn skoansuster alris in ljocht sjoen. Doe sei se: \"Dêr komt skielk in hûs.\" Dêr is èk in hûs kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33809,"r":"CJ094404","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People once heard knocking on the window, but no one was there. Later that evening they heard exactly the same knocking again. Then someone came to tell them they had to fulfil their duty as neighbours because someone had died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By ús buorlju yn Twizelerheide is 't ris foarfallen dat se dêr op in joun ien op 't glês klopjen hearden. Hja dêrhinne om to sjen, mar doe wie der neat. Deselde jouns woardde der noch ris wer kloppe, krektengelyk as de earste kear. Mar doe wie der wol ien. Hy brocht de tiding dat der ien overleden wie en hja moasten helpe om buorreplicht to dwaen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33815,"r":"CJ094410","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If magpies come into the yard in the morning, something pleasant will happen. If they come in the evening, there will be a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters op 't hiem komme, tichte by hûs, gebeurt der hwat. As se moarns komme gebeurt der hwat nijs. (net treurich)\nAs se jouns komme komt der in sterfgefal.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33816,"r":"CJ094411","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If butterflies fly close to the house, visitors will come.\nIf a cat washes itself, visitors will come.\nIf the cat washes itself with its paw over its head, a man wearing a cap will come to visit.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de flinters tichte by 't hûs omflodderen krige men bisite.\nAs de kat him wosk èk.\nAs de kat him mei de poat oer de kop hinne wosk, kom der in man mei in pet op op bisite.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33818,"r":"CJ094413","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people sometimes saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, wandering lights) on the road. They were omens of the bicycle lamps and car lights that came later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen ljochten froeger op 'e wei. Dat wienen de tekens fan de lettere fytsljochten en de autolampen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33849,"r":"CJ094702","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, wandering lights) that people used to see were forerunners of the bicycle lamps that came later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Nei Eastemar út seagen se dêr froeger gauris ljochtsjes. Dat wienen wylde lantearnen, sa neamden se dy ljochtsjes. It ha de foarboaden west fan 'e fytslampen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33850,"r":"CJ094703","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People once heard hammering, knocking and so on. Later a new church was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit hat ek faek forteld dat der minsken wennen oan 'e Hearrewei dy hearden dêr op in plak hyltyd timmerjen en klopjen en mei balken smite ensa. Letter is op datselde plak de grifformearde tsjerke kom. 't Wie foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33867,"r":"CJ094810","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people sometimes heard ticking in bed. These were forerunners of the clocks and watches that came later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger wienen der gjin wekkers en ek gjin horloazjes. Dan tikke it achter it bêdsket en ek wol ûnder 'e weech. Dat wienen de wylde horloazjes! \"Dat binne de wekkers woarn,\" sei ús mem, \"dy't nou op it bêdsbuordtsje stean.\"\n(foartsjirmerij)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36025,"r":"CJ095901","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"I was standing in Jistrum and heard hammering behind me while there was nothing to be seen. Could it be some kind of omen? It turned out to be, because later we would get a house there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik stie op in joun to Jistrum achter hûs. Doe hearde ik dat it skean achter my drok op in timmerjen gong.\nMar dêr wie neat to sjen. Ik tochte by my sels: Kin dit ek foartjirmerij wêze?\nEn dat hat it west. Letter ha wy op datselde plak in hûs krige. Ik wist der doe noch neat fan dat wy dêr in hûs sette litte soenen. Wy binne letter yn dat hûs kom to wenjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36044,"r":"CJ096101","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, wandering lights) above Grinzer Pein. Later houses were built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boven Grinzer Pein seagen se froeger by jountiid wylde lantearnen. Dan woarde der sein: \"Dêr wurde skielk noch ris hûzen boud.\" Dat is letter ek gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":207820,"r":"VODA_041_13","p":"Herten","v":"L.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Certain things were seen as omens of an accident or disaster, such as a magpie chattering by someone's house, breaking a mirror, or scissors lying crossed on the table. Finding a safety pin foretells a quarrel.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Een ander ding dat was bijvoorbeeld als een eh.. een ekster op iemands huis of in de buurt hiervan zat te schetteren, als ik het zo mag noemen, dan voorspelde dit ook voor betrokkene een groot onheil. Eveneens was een ongeluk op komst indien men een spiegel brak of indien een schaar toevallig in kruisvorm op tafel lag. En vond men een toespang, dus een veiligheidsspeld, dan betekende dit dat er ruzie op komst was [moet lachen]."},{"n":36082,"r":"CJ096303","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"My grandmother heard the sounds of a train on the rails long before there was a railway between Leeuwarden and Zwaagwesteinde.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Beppe en dy wennen yn Sweagerbosk. Al fier foardat it spoar der wie fan Ljouwert nei de Westerein hearden hja de lûden fan 'e trein dy't oer de rails hinne skoude.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36090,"r":"CJ096311","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days we often saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, wandering lights) floating through the air. They were forerunners of the aeroplanes.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn myn jonge jierren seagen se faek wylde lantearnen troch de loft sweven. Letter wienen dat de flychmesines. 't Wie foartjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36105,"r":"CJ096501","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening I saw a bicycle approaching behind our house, or so it seemed, because the light did not come any closer. Later 2 new houses were built on that spot. It was by the little wood.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie ris op in joun by uzes achter hûs yn Drachtster Kompenije. 't Wie op in joun. Ik sei: \"Heden, dêr komt noch in fyts oan.\" Sa like it krekt. Mar it fremde wie, it ljocht kom net tichterby.\nLetter kommen dêr op dat plak, dêr't ik doe dat ljocht seach, twa nije huzen to stean. 't Wie yn 'e Bosk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36160,"r":"CJ096901","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A friend of the narrator heard hammering. He said a new house would surely be built soon. The narrator himself heard nothing, but a new house was indeed built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear wie 'k mei in kammeraetske op 'e Fjouwer Roede. \"Hark,\" sei se, \"sa wurdt dêr timmere. Der komt skielk fêst in nij hûs.\" Mar ik hearde neat. 't Wie tsjuster en der wie neat to sjen.\nMar hja krige wol gelyk. Al gauachtich dêrnei ha se dêr in nij hûs delset.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36219,"r":"CJ097403","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Before Albert de Boer's house was built, someone had already seen a light burning on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ljibbe fan Geart de Vries fortelde my, foardat it hûs fan Albert de Boer boud wie, stie der noch neat op 'e heide (Sum. heide). Doe kom hy dêr ris op in joun lâns en doe seinen se: \"Sjoch, dêr brânt in ljocht op dat lân!\" Doe wie der noch hielendal gjin sprake fan dat dêr boud wurde soe. Letter kom dêr it hûs fan Albert de Boer.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36277,"r":"CJ097606","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people in Westerein saw lights in the place where cars would later drive.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As wy froeger yn 'e Westerein op 'e hoeke stienen seagen wy jouns wolris wylde lantearnen, skean oer de greiden. Dat wienen foartekens fan 'e auto's.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36322,"r":"CJ097802","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man from Sanbulten was clairvoyant. He predicted a train accident. Others saw car lights where a road would later be built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op Sânbulten wenne in mantsje, dat wist ek allegear dingen foarút to sizzen. Yn myn fammejierren - doe wie 'k yn Grinslân oan 't wurk op 'e bou - foarspelde dat mantsje dat der soe nochris in great treinûngelok komme yn Sânbulten. Dat is ek gebeurd. Der is nêst jierren in trein tsjin in bus mei brulloftsgasten oanrekke. Dêr binne doe forskeidene by dea rekke en oaren woarden swier gewond. Dat mantsje wie mei de helm geboaren.\nSan 30 à 35 jier lyn is der in nije wei troch de mieden oanlein. Foardat dy wei der wie seagen wy wylde lantearens dêr troch 't lân hinnefleanen. Wy seinen doe: dat kin net ljochten fan minsken wêze, hwant it is dêr allegear greidlân. Mar doe't de wei der goed en wol wie tuften de auto's dêr deis en jouns lâns. Dàt hienen de wylde lantearens west, de ljochten fan dy auto's.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36358,"r":"CJ097917","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"An old woman could see lights on the road. These turned out to be bicycle lamps, which would only come much later. There were no bicycles yet at the time.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In âld minske hjir sei us: 't Is allegear wylde lantearnen op 'e wegen. It wurde skielk allegear ljochten. Dat wie krekt foar de tiid dat de fytsen útkamen. It wienen de fytslantearnen, dy't hja sjoen hie fan tofoaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36402,"r":"CJ098137","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A farmer lived in an area with a lot of water. Once he heard the rattling of milk churn lids there. Later farms were built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tusken Feanwâlden en Mounein wie 't froeger allegear wetter. Dêr wenne in boer, dy line op in joun oer de ûnderdoar hinne. Doe hearde er ynienen buslidden ratteljen oer 't wetter. Mar dêr wie neat to sjen.\nLetter waerd dat terrein dêr allegearre droech makke en doe kommen der allerhande buorkerijen to stean.\nIt hie foartsjirmerije west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36433,"r":"CJ098402","p":"Wjelsryp","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In Westerein (Zwaagwesteinde) some people could already hear the sound of the train before any trains ran.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Forskillende minsken yn 'e Westerein hawwe it foargedrús fan 'e trein heard. Doe wie der dus noch gjin trein, doe hearden se him al.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36474,"r":"CJ098603","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator's mother heard at night the sounds of building work that would later take place on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem en dy wennen yn Feanwâlden op 'e Finnen, neist de helling fan Wageningen.\nOp in nacht hearde mem timmerjen en slaen om 't leven op 'e helling. Mem wie widdou en tocht: hwat mei hjir gebeure. Hja gong der út om to sjen hwat der to rêdden wie. Mar der wie neat to rêdden.\nHja sei tsjin ús: Hwat dit hjir is, dat snap ik net. Dat slacht en hout hjir om en giet men der hinne dan is der neat.\nHja joech har wer del.\nIn dei of hwat letter doe sei de hellingbaes van Wageningen tsjin mem: \"Jou húske sil der wol ôf matte, hwant de helling wurdt útbreide. Dan moatte wy de groun brûke.\"\nMem hierde it húske fan 'e hellingbaes.\nIn skoft letter gebeurde dat en doe hienen jy deselde lûden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36475,"r":"CJ098604","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The neighbour was upset because the cradle in her attic kept rocking all the time. Later she had a baby, who was laid in that cradle.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear kaem buorfrou by ús mem, alhiel fan 'e wize.\n\"O frou, frou,\" sei se, \"hwat is 't nou hwat. Der stiet in skommelwidze by ús op 'e souder en dy skommelt al mar troch. Ik bigryp der gjin kloaten fan. As ik him stil hâld bigjint er út himsels wer.\"\nIn skoft letter krige buorfrou in lytsen yn 'e widze.\nIt hie foartsjirmerije west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36476,"r":"CJ098605","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people already saw lights passing by in the place where the railway would later come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen op 'e Swette tusken Burgumerheide en Feanwâlden. Achter ús wie de spoarwei.\nPake fortelde my, hja hienen dêr oan 't wurk west, doe wie der noch gjin spoarlijn. As hja dêr jouns wienen, gong dêr hyltyd in streek ljocht lâns, op in bipaelde tiid.\nJierren letter kaem dêr de trein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36512,"r":"CJ098801","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Some time before the neighbour's house was demolished, a loud thud could already be heard. It sounded as if a wall was falling.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in nacht, noch net sa lang lyn waerd ik ynienen wekker troch in lûde plof; krekt as foel der in muorre del.\nDe oare moarns roun ik om 't hûs hinne om to sjen hwat der gebeurd wie, mar der mankearde neat oan.\nBinnen 't jier waerd it âlde húske fan myn buorman ôfbrutsen. Doe hearde ik krekt wer itselde lûd, doe't der in stiennen muorre delkaem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36517,"r":"CJ098806","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator could hear the singing of the 'Latter-day Saints' two years before they arrived.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hear by de 'Heiligen der laatste dagen'. Wy wennen yn in hûs, dêr siet gâns rûmte yn. Dêr hat in winkel yn west. Op in nacht sei 'k tsjin ús mem: \"Mat mem ris hearre, sa moai binne se oan 't sjongen.\" It wie flakby.\nSahwat twa jier letter waerden der yn 'e keamer fan ús hûs byienkomsten hâlden fan 'e 'Heiligen der laatste dagen'.\nBy dy byienkomsten waerden lieten song. En dàt wie it dat ik fan tofoaren heard hie. Doe't ik ús mem der yndachtich op makke, hearde dy it ek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36524,"r":"CJ098813","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Near the Twizeler Weg people used to see lanterns, which are said to have been the bicycle lights of later times.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By de Twizeler wei seagen se froeger faek ljochten. Dat neamden se wylde lantearnen. Se wolle wol ha dat dat de lettere fytsljochten wienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36615,"r":"CJ099211","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people saw many wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, wandering lights). They were omens of the bicycle lamps that came later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen hie men hjir froeger in soad. Dat wie foartsjirmerije. 't Wienen de fytslampen fan letter tiid.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36655,"r":"CJ099410","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Juke Spukguler was clairvoyant. Other people also saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, wandering lights). They were forerunners of bicycle lamps.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jûke Spûkgûler seach allegear dingen foarút.\nMar wylde lantearnen woarden ek wol troch oare minsken sjoen.\nDat wie foartsjirmerije, seinen se letter. It doelde op 'e fytslampen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36668,"r":"CJ099504","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days people saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, wandering lights) in places where the train would later pass. They had been omens of its lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hja seagen froeger wylde lantearnen op 'e plakken dêr't letter de trein lâns kom. Dat ha de ljochten fan 'e trein west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36674,"r":"CJ099601","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Mother often told us that even before a tram ran on the Folgesterloane, people heard the sound a tram makes on the rails, and hooting as well.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem is ôfkomstich fan Drachtster Kompenije. Hja hat ús faek forteld, foardat de tram de Folgersterloane lâns ried nei Drachten ta hienen hja de lûden heard dy't de tram makke op 'e rails en ek hyltiten wer toet-toet-toet.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36698,"r":"CJ099901","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night Jan Tolsma came home late. From afar he saw a fire at his parents' house. He ran home as fast as he could, but there turned out to be no fire. Later, at Christmas, everything on that spot burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Beets stie in boerepleats, dy hearde oan in sekere Tolsma. Jan, de soan fan Tolsma kaem op in nacht thús. Hy hie der op út west. Doe seach er fan fierrens al dat de pleats yn 'e brân stie. Hy is fan 'e strjitwei it lân delroun, sa hurd er mar koe om thús to kommen.\nDoe't er thús wie wie dêr gjin brân.\nMar itselde jiers om krysttiid hinne brânde it spul op.\n(In soan fan Jan Tolsma wennet yn Drachten)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36699,"r":"CJ099902","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Before the canal at Beets existed, people already saw a ship with sails and a mast sailing straight across the land. Later the canal was dug there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e tiid dat it kanael yn Beets der noch net wie, seagen guon in skip silen mei mêst en seilen, samar it lân del. Yn deselde richting as dat skip sylde is letter it kanael groeven woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36703,"r":"CJ099906","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) were omens of the lights in the houses that would later be built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen ha 'k froeger fakernôch sjoen. Der waerd biweard, dat wienen de ljochten fan hûzen, dy't dêr letter set wurde soenen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36706,"r":"CJ099909","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Magpies in the farmyard mean that visitors are coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der eksters op it hiem kamen bitsjutte dat dat der praters komme soenen. Eksters brochten nijs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36724,"r":"CJ100001","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A skipper always has to carry cows for a certain Sytsma. One time he dreams that he has to carry sheep instead, and the next day those sheep turn out to be on the ship.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy farden mei de boat op Ljouwert en op Grins. Wy namen altyd fé mei fan Grins nei in koopman ta út Wurdum. Dat wie in sekere Sytsma. It wienen altyd kij, noait oar fé. Mar doe op in kear, yn 'e nacht seach ik dat wy fiif skiep meinimme moesten út Grins wei. Ik tochte: it is in droom, mar ik seach dy skiep dúdlik foar my. Doe't wy de oare deis yn Grins kamen, wienen der werkelik de fiif skiep, dy't ik de nachts op bêd sjoen hie en dy't nei Sytsma ta moesten. Hoe kin soks nou?","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36733,"r":"CJ100010","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"It is haunted at the Lange Sleatten. Once a daughter was alone on the ship. In the twilight she saw someone beckoning from the other side. She rowed over to ferry the man across, but as she came closer she saw that he had no feet: he was floating. She died of fright.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By de Lange Sleatten spûke it. Dêr hat in man tahâlden, dy wenne dêr mei syn dochter yn in aek. Op in kear wie dy man net thús. Syn dochter wie allinne yn 'e aek. Doe seach se dat der oan 'e oare kant fan 'e feart ien stie to winken. Dy woe oerset wurde. 't Wie skimerjoun. Hja roeide nei him ta, mar doe't se tichterby kaem seach se dat er gjin fuotten hie. Hy sweefde. 't Wie 't spûk fan 'e Lange Sleatten. Hja krige de skrik sa topakken, dat hja is der fan stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36735,"r":"CJ100012","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A nightmare is a dream that later comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In nachtmerje is in soarte fan droom, dy't de minske ha kin. Sa'n droom, dy't letter altyd neikomt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36737,"r":"CJ100102","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Father and a few others once heard wailing at night from the direction of the canal, but nothing had happened. Later, in winter, three people drowned there, two of them from one household. Someone had also seen it in his sleep the night before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit wenne yn 'e Westerein. Heit en dy hearden ris op in nacht gûlen: Oe-oe-oe-oe-. Der wienen mear dy't dy nachts dyselde lûden heard ha. Dy lûden kamen út it kanael wei. 't Wie in freeslik gejammer. Mar der wie neat gebeurd. De winters dêroan fordronken dêr trije. Dy sakken troch it iis. 't Wie flak by de spoarbrêge.\nDoe hearden se presys itselde gejammer. Mar doe wie 't echt. Fan de trije dy't doe fordronken kommen der twa út ien húshâlding. Se ha der noch mei in ljedder hinne west mar sy ha se net rêdde kind. It wie yn 't Djip Gat. Der hat de nachts dêroan noch ien yn 'e sliep nei dat Djip Gat ta west om to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36738,"r":"CJ100103","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"My parents said they often heard hammering at night in places where houses were later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn âlde lju ha faek forteld dat se timmerjen heard hienen yn 'e nacht; dan kom dêr letter op sa'n plak in hûs to stean, mar ik wit net mei hokker huzen as dat it gefal west hat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36740,"r":"CJ100105","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"My father was once fishing at night. He saw little lights moving along the canal for hours. The following summer people drowned there, and they were searched for with lanterns for a very long time.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit fiske graech by 't kanael. Op in kear lei er dêr wer to poeren. 't Wie yn 'e nacht. Doe seach er ynienen allegear ljochtsjes by de feart lâns.\nLetter binne dêr guon fordronken. Doe ha se yn 'e nacht mei lantearens dêr nei socht. Dat gebeurde de simmers dêrop.\nIt hat wol in pear ûren duorre, sa lang seach heit dy ljochtsjes dêr lâns de wâl. Dy gongen al mar hinne en wer. Heit hat der hinne west, mar doe wie der neat to sjen.\nLetter hat er yn 'e gaten krige hwat it west hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36763,"r":"CJ100128","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If a ghostly dog is roaming about, it is a sign that someone will die soon.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":36778,"r":"CJ100203","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening, when she was home alone, a fisherman's daughter heard someone calling to be ferried across. She went outside to help. Through the fog she saw only the top of the man, but when she came closer the man suddenly vanished. She was so frightened that she later died of it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op Foanejacht, tusken Garyp en Warten lei in aekje. Dêr wenne in fisker yn mei syn dochter. Op in joun wie de fisker net thús, de dochter hâldde allinne yn 'e aek ta.\nDoe hearde se fan 'e oare kant ien roppen. Dy woe noch oerset wurde. Hja gong nei bûten ta om dyselde to heljen. 't Wie mistich waer. Hja seach allinne mar de boppekant fan in man. Doe't se oan him ta wie wie de man ynienen fuort, krekt as wie er yn 'e groun weisakke. Hja hat dêr sa'n skrik fan krigen dat hja is dêr letter fan stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36792,"r":"CJ100301","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Before the first church was built, people already heard psalms being sung on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foardat it earste tsjerkje yn Harkema boud woarde, hearden guon dêr al fan tofoaren op dat plak psalmsjongen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36794,"r":"CJ100303","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In Harkema wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) often floated over the heath. According to father they were omens of fine weather.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger sweefden der yn 'e Harkema faek wylde lampkes oer de heide. Heit sei dat bitsjutte dat it moai waer wurde soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36801,"r":"CJ100310","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) are the omens of the lights of the cars and bicycles that came later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen tsjutten op 'e ljochten fan 'e lettere auto's en fytsen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36808,"r":"CJ100501","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"When I was a boy, we got a new house. We went there by praam (flat-bottomed boat) at eleven o'clock to look, when the house was not yet finished. From afar we saw lights, but when we came closer there was no light to be seen. Those were omens.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie in jonge fan sa'n alve jier. Wy kamen út Grinslân en krigen in nij húske yn 'e Sweachster Mieden (ûnder Kollumersweach).\nDoe't wy dêr oankamen op in jountiid om alve ûre hinne mei in pream, seagen wy healwei de brêge in ljochtsje brânnen by ús yn 'e hûs. Doe't wy tichterby kamen wie 't út. 't Hûs wie noch net klear, wy moesten earst in skoft yn in keet wenje.\nDit wie foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36817,"r":"CJ100601","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At the bridge people heard cries for help while no one was there. Later a young man drowned on that spot, and the same cries for help were heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By de brêge yn 'e Westerein hearden guon op in kear 'help!' roppen. Mar der wie neat. Letter is dêr in jongfeint forsûpt. Doe hearden se krekt itselde help-gerop.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36828,"r":"CJ100612","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A neighbour saw lots of little lights: wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps). A road would later come there. At first there were only two houses, but many more were built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oer 't spoar yn 'e Westerein, dêr seach ús buorfrou allegear ljochtsjes. Dat wienen wylde lantearnen. 't Wie de kant nei Kûkherne oer. Hja sei: \"Dêr komt noch ris in wei lâns.\"\nEn dat is èk gebeurd. Der stienen doe yn dy tiid mar 2 húskes en in wei wie der net. Nou bin 't allegear huzen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36833,"r":"CJ100617","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Magpies in a tree in the farmyard foretell visitors or news. Black jackdaws foretell death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der eksters op it hiem binne by de huzen yn in beam, dan bitsjut dat: nijs. Dan kin der bisite komme of in tiding.\nSwarte kaën bitsjut: rou.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36836,"r":"CJ100620","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If the thread with which a shroud was sewn is bitten off, all your teeth will later fall out.\nThe comb of the corpse must always go into the coffin. If someone combs himself with it, all his hair will fall out.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As de tried, dêr't it deadshimd mei naeid is, ôfbiten wurdt, falle de tosken út.\nDe kaem dêr't it hier fan it lyk mei kjimd is, kaem mei yn 'e kiste. Brûkten jy dy letter sels, dan foel alle hier út.\nDit sei oerbeppe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36843,"r":"CJ100704a","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"My wife always had to get out of bed at 4 in the morning to let a labourer in. Once it was only 3 o'clock, but she clearly heard footsteps and the door handle. Yet there was no labourer to be seen. When she heard the same sound at 4 o'clock and got up again, it really was the labourer.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn dyselde tiid lei myn frou dêr ris ier yn 'e moarn op bêd. Hja moest der altyd om 4 ûre ôf om de arbeider yn to litten. Doe wie 't ris op in moarn 3 ûre. Hja hearde dúdlik de fuotstappen fan 'e arbeider en fuort dêrnei de klink fan 'e doar. Hja der ôf om de arbeider yn to litten.\nMar doe't se by de doar kaem wie der neat. Hja gong wer lizzen. Krekt om 4 ûre hearde hja deselde fuotstappen wer en gong de klink fan 'e doar. Doe wie de arbeider dêr werklik en liet hja him der yn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36857,"r":"CJ100802","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hearing psalm singing was a portent of the radio and television that came later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Omke hearde ek psalmsjongen yn 'e loft. Dat wie de foarboade fan 'e radio en de t.v.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36900,"r":"CJ101201","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"I used to often see lights over the fields by the farm. Those were wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps): portents of the cars that came later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jierren lyn wennen wy op in buorkerij oan 'e Dwarsfeart.\n't Wie op in joun dat wy bûten stienen. Och, och, sei 'k, hwat in ljochtsjes oer de wereld yn 'e lânnen. Allegearre wylde lantearnen. Myn man wie doe krekt wei, skoanheit ek. Ik haw faek oer dy ljochtsjes neitocht.\nKom ik nou jouns bûtendoar dan sjoch ik allegear ljochtsjes fan 'e rondwei. Dy komme der allegearre oanfleanen. Dat binne de ljochten fan 'e auto's dy't dêr lânssnuorje. Dat ha doe dy wylde lantearnens west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36901,"r":"CJ101202","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman predicts that they will get a snow-white cow. Her husband thinks she is out of her mind, but not long after he comes home from the market with a cow in calf. It gives birth to a white calf. It was even in the newspaper, it was so white.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is al lang lyn, doe sei ik op in moarn tsjin myn man: \"wy krije in sniewite kou.\"\n\"Dû bist net heal wiis,\" sei er, \"dû kinst dy fan alles wol yn 'e holle helje.\" Mar ik hie in spierwite kou by ús op 'e stâl stean sjoen en 't wie my net út 'e holle wei to praten.\nHwat wie 't gefal? Myn man gong nei Drachtster merke.\nDat die er altyd en dan kocht er ris hwat en hy forkocht hwat. Dy kear kom er mei in blaubûnte kou thús. Dy kou wie al drachtich. En dy kou brocht in wyt keal doe't er kealle. 't Wie hielendal wyt, der siet net in oar plakje oan. 't Hat noch yn 'e krante stien.\nSa krigen wy in wite kou op 'e stâl.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36902,"r":"CJ101203","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"My brother was poaching in an orchard at night with friends. They heard noises: beams being thrown, and mud, while no one was there. Later that spot was built on.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer wie in great jonge. Mei syn maten wied er op in nacht oan 't hôfkesjongen. 't Wie yn in great hôf dêr't se wienen, mar dêr stie mar in lyts húske by. Doe hearden se dêr samar midden yn 'e nacht lûden krekt as waerd dêr mei balken smiten en waerden der dongposten delgoaid. En der wie neat! Letter ha se op dat plak in greate plaets boud.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36907,"r":"CJ101208","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"I saw in advance the spot where our dog would be buried. I saw snow, mud and the spade it was done with.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw fantofoaren sjoen it plak dêr't wy ús houn bigrave soenen. Ik seach de snie en de modder en de lodde, dêr't se it gat mei groeven. 't Is krektengelyk sa gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36931,"r":"CJ101232","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Magpies in the farmyard mean news. Rooks and jackdaws foretell a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Krije jy eksters op it hiem, dan bitsjut dat nijs.\nRoeken en kaën op it hiem bitsjut in deaden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36953,"r":"CJ101404","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Near the hamlet of Topwear people saw little lights in the evening. Later a house was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By Grinzer Pein is in gehuchtsje: Topwear. Dêr seagen guon alle jounen in ljochtsje. Dêr kaem letter in hûs to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36956,"r":"CJ101407","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If magpies chatter in front of the house, visitors are coming; if they chatter behind the house, it means a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As eksters foar hûs skatterje komt der bisite.\nAs eksters achter hûs skatterje komt der in sterfgefal.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36968,"r":"CJ101506","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Long ago Janke drowned in the Janke-dobbe (Janke's pond). Some had already predicted that someone would drown there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In pear hûndert meter hjir fandinne is in dobbe, dêr stie froeger in âlde jasker by. It is de Janke-dobbe. Yn dy dobbe is in sekere Janke forsûpt. It wie fantofoaren al bikend dat dêr ien yn forsûpe soe. Guon hienen dat sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36969,"r":"CJ101507","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Before the Reformed church stood there, people had already heard psalm singing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Drachtster Kompenije stiet in grifformearde tsjerke.\nFoardat dy dêr stie ha de minsken op dat plak al psalmsjongen heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37099,"r":"CJ102101","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In Harkema people saw lights that were not there. They were the portents of the bicycles.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Harkema seagen se ljochtsjes, dy't der yn werkelikheit net wienen. Letter biriddenearden se dat it de foarboaden fan 'e fytsen west ha.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37140,"r":"CJ102501","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"My uncle once felt a gust of wind pass him at the spot where a tram would later come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn omke fortelde, hy roun ris fan Drachten nei Lippenhuzen. Hy wie sahwat healwei Beetstersweach en de Trijehoek, doe gong der him ynienen in wynpûst foarby en krekt as rattele der hwat by him lâns. Trije jier letter ried de tram dêr lâns, krekt op 't selde plak.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37158,"r":"CJ102705","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"We were telling each other stories in a dry ditch when we suddenly heard hammering very clearly. Then it stopped. Later the Reformed church was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Wie goed sechstich jier lyn yn Twizelerheide. Wy leinen yn in âlde droege sleat. 't Gong drok op in fortellen. 't Wie de nachts al let, likernoch twa ûre.\n\"Hark,\" sei der doe ien fan ús, \"dêr binne noch guon oan 't timmerjen.\" Wy hearden 't allegear dúdlik, mar der wie net in minske to sjen. Ik wie doe sahwat 14 jier.\nWy hearden it timmerjen trije kear achter elkoarren. 't Wie mar in 50 meter fan ús ôf. Doe roannen wy dat in eintsje út. Wy hearden it net wer.\nOp itselde plak kom letter de grifformearde tsjerke to stean. Dêr hienen wy it timmerjen fan heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37217,"r":"CJ103207","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Eabele predicted that Veenwouden would become a suburb of Leeuwarden. He also heard a bell ringing, which foretold the later station bell.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Healwize Eabele fan 'e Westerein dy hat foarspeld dat Feanwâlden de foarstêd fan Ljouwert wurde soe, en dat der in poartebelle hingje soe. Dy poartebelle hied er lieden heard. Dat wie yn 'e tiid foardat de trein dêr ried.\nDer kaem letter yndied sa'n belle op it stasjon to hingjen.\nDy belle waerd let as de trein fuort gong.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37230,"r":"CJ103302","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On the spot where the Reformed church now stands, people heard psalm singing even before that time.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Surhuzum, op it plak dêr't nou de pypketsjerke (= grifformearde tsjerke) stiet, dêr hearden se fan tofoaren al psalmsjongen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37315,"r":"CJ103901","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) that were seen were said to mean the lights of the houses built later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen seagen se froeger faek op 'e Ikkers. It soe bitsjutte dat it de ljochten wienen fan 'e lettere wenten dy't se bouden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37464,"r":"CJ104516","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A ghostly howling dog means a death. Black rooks near the house mean a death and are portents of mourning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in houn spûkgûlde bitsjutte dat dat der ien deagean soe.\nAs de swarte roeken om 'e doar kamen bitsjutte dat in sterfgefal. 't Wie de foarboade fan 'e rou.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37522,"r":"CJ105024","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The lights that floated above the road were the portents of the carbide lamps on bicycles that came later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen ûnder Surhústerfean, tichte by de Fjouwer roede.\nDêr seagen de minsken yn myn bernejierren allerhande ljochten jouns. Dy wienen op in rige en sy sweefden.\nLetter seinen se, dat hienen de foarboaden west fan 'e karbydlampen fan 'e fytsen dy't dêr letter lâns kamen. 't Wie boppe de wei dêr't dy ljochtsjes lâns sweefden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37523,"r":"CJ105025","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a farm, a strange cry of fear was heard coming from the barn one evening. There turned out to be nothing to see. The next morning they heard the same cry again. It was the farmhand, who had fallen from the loft. The first cry had been a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op it Wytfean, oan 'e oare kant de Lange Wyk, dêr wenne in dikke boer, dêr gong it altyd like rûch om en ta.\nOp in joun sieten se dêr by elkoar yn 'e hûs, doe kaem dêr in hiel raer lûd út 'e skuorre wei, it wie in bange skreau.\nSe waerden der allegearre kjel fan en gongen nei de skuorre ta to sjen. Mar der wie neat foarfallen.\nDe oare deis kaem der wer sa'n lûd út 'e skuorre wei. Mar doe wie 't yn 'e moarn. Hja der hinne to sjen, doe wie de feint by de hynstesouder delfallen. 't Wie krekt deselde skreau as de foarige jouns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37526,"r":"CJ105028","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At night, the sound of carpentry was often heard at a spot where a house was later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr't wy froeger wenne ha, tichte by de Fjouwerroede ha se yn 'e nacht faek timmerjen heard [en] is der letter in nij hûs kaem. Dat fortelden heit en dy dan, mar hokker hûzen dat wienen wyt ik net mear.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37575,"r":"CJ105504","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"It was said that some people already heard organ music at the place where the church was later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der is my wolris forteld woarn dat guon al orgelmuzyk hearden op it plak dêr't letter de tsjerke kaem to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37606,"r":"CJ105602","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One evening a man heard a lot of strange noise, and a farmhouse was later built on that very spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw heit wol fortellen heard dat it der hjir yn Eastemar op in nacht ergens tige oan wei gong wie. Op dat selde plak ha se letter in plaets boud. Guon hienen de lûden al fan tofoaren heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37622,"r":"CJ105618","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days you saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) everywhere; later people said these had been portents of bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen hienen jy froeger oeral. Se seinen letter, 't wienen de fytsljochten west: foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":130008,"r":"VODA_030_07","p":"Montfort","v":"L.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A seer predicted that the vast area of marsh, water and heath between Echt, Waldfeucht, Montfort and Posterholt would be reclaimed and turned into fertile farmland with a church, monastery and village on it. This actually happened.\nThis seer also predicted the following: when the Wandering Jew finds a home, women can no longer be told apart from men, and people fly through the air like birds, then the antichrist will be born. And when the antichrist is grown, the world will end.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"[voorbijrijdend verkeer] Eh… ja, ’t is al lang eer ik geboren werd, maar mijn ouders hebben de man nog gekend op een boerderij ‘In de Klinkhei’ genoemd tussen Montfort en Diergaarde. Daar woonde in een tot woning verbouwd bakhuis een ouwe man, Drees waarvan de… Klinkhei. Eh… hij had niets als een kudde schapen en daar was ie ook altijd mee op pad. En deze Drees eh… dat scheen een merkwaardig man geweest te zijn, want ze noemden hem de ‘Zeener van de Klinkhei’, een soort profeet dus. \nEh… hij heeft veel voorspeld wat anderen ook voorspeld hebben, maar hij heeft ook dingen gezegd die anderen niet… nooit voorspeld hebben en waar ze ook geen weet van kunnen hebben. Zo zei hij onder andere: “Hie in de Pieël…” nu moet ik even zeggen: de Peel noemde men eh… een uitgestrekt moeras- en watergebied en heidegebied dat tussen Echt, Waldfeucht, Montfort en Posterholt ligt eh… langs ’t hoogterras eh… van de Duitse grens. Een heel uitgestrekt gebied waar toen eh… niemand woonde en ook niemand kon wonen en waar ook niemand eh.. z’n brood zou kunnen verdienen. Tenzij dat ‘r soms bezembinders en vissers in kwamen. De bezembinders om de hei te snijen voor bezemen te binden op de droge plekken. \nMaar die Drees die zei: “Deze grond die zal ontgonnen worden en dat wordt vruchtbare akkergrond. En hier komt een kerk en een klooster en een dorp.” Enne… volgens m’n ouders is dit zowat geweest in de jare"},{"n":210859,"r":"VODA_045_09","p":"Barger-Compascuum","v":"Dr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People used to experience all sorts of things. Sometimes they frightened themselves and others. They heard knocking, saw people carrying a coffin, saw something in the form of a black dog or a black fellow. People often saw a big fellow walking around with a dog. Later a minister came who did indeed walk through the village with his dog.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"I: interviewer\nV: dhr. Veringa\n\nI: Wat we nog zo had van ehm… wat mensen hier metmaakt hebt, met geesten of iets van dien aard, klopdingen...\nV: Ach... je moet zo rekenen, ze moken vroeger vanalles met. Dan heurden ze wat kloppen. Dan hadden ze sommige mensen met ’n doodkist zien dragen. Dan was d’r iemand [gekraak] die had weer wat zain in de geest van een.. een.. een eh.. zwarte hond of van een zwarte kerel of wat ook. Maar je moet wel begriepen dat de mensen zich ook hail vaak bang mukken. Maar dat verhaal dat deut dan de ronde. Daor wuurd ’n ander ook bang van. Toen ik een jaor of acht, negen was, toen kwammen ze vertellen dat ‘r kwam altied een zwarte kerel deur de Maatschappij, met een hónd bie zich. Toen later zo’n dominee De Weerd kwam, toen kwam die werkelijk met ’ne hónd deur de Maatschappij. Zal wal louter touval waest hebben [gekraak], maar ze zeiden toch maar: “Kiek, dae hebben we hier zo vaak zain, een grote kerel, met een hond, en dat is dominee De Weerd waest.” En inderdaad gong dae man vaak naor zo’n Dolfing, dae woonde toen in de Maatschappij en dae was geleuvig aan zien kerk, dus hij gong d’r in op huusbezoek en he kwam daor vaak, over de weg. [gekraak]","l":"Drents; Nedersaksisch"},{"n":38229,"r":"CJ108601","p":"Quatrebras","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a slipway there is sometimes no work for a long time. When people hear hammering in the evening, they say work will come again, which always comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Feanwâldsterwâl hat in helling west, tichte by de brêge. Soms wie dêr op 'e helling hiele skoften gjin wurk.\nDe hellingbaes hiet Lútsen. Dan gebeurde 't soms ynienen dat der jouns guon op 'e brêge stienen en dy hearden dan op 'e helling timmerjen en sa. 't Wie dêr dan allegear drokte. Dan seinen se: \"Dêr komt gau wer wurk op 'e helling.\" En dat kom ek altiten nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38359,"r":"CJ109020","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People hear hammering outside while there is nothing to see. Later a new house is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir op 'e Vogelzang hearden guon by nacht, wylst se yn 'e hûs sieten, bûtendoar timmerjen. 't Gong der bot oan wei. Se gongen dêr hinne om to sjen, mar doe wie dêr neat. Letter woarde dêr in nij hûs set.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38405,"r":"CJ109219","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"It often happens that people say a house will be built because hammering is heard at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde hjir wol faek, dat minsken seinen: dêr komt skielk in hûs, hwant wy ha 't hjir yn 'e nacht wit hoe faek timmerjen heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38435,"r":"CJ109319","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman sees beforehand a road on which carts drive without horses.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jierren herwaerts - ik wie doe noch mar in jonkje, - doe wenne der op 'e Hoek ûnder Feanwâlden in âld-minske, dat sei: \"Der komme aenst weinen to riden sûnder hynders der foar. Ik ha se riden sjoen. En de wei, dêr't se op ride, dy komt troch 't Bûtenfjild to rinnen.\"\n't Is presys sa útkaem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38567,"r":"CJ109822","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman sees that not Veenwouden but Hoek will become the village.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir hat in âld minske yn Feanwâlden wenne, dy sei: \"Feanwâlden is it doarp net, mar de Hoek, dat sil it doarp wurde.\" Dat hie se sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38568,"r":"CJ109823","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman predicts that the cemetery will be located in a certain place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In oar âld minske sei dat it tsjerkhôf soe op 'e Hoek komme. Dat hie hja sjoen. Dat is ek gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38575,"r":"CJ109830","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hearing hammering at a shipyard at night means work is coming again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Feanwâldsterwâl timmeren se nachts soms ek op 'e helling. Dat wie tjirmerij. Dat bitsjutte dat der wer in karwei yn oantocht wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38623,"r":"CJ110001","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People hear hammering in the evening although no hammering was actually going on. Later a house was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha faek fortellen heard dat minsken hjir yn Twizelerheide jouns timmerjen hearden sûnder dat der yn werklikheit timmere waerd, en dat der dan letter op sa'n plak in hûs kaem to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38625,"r":"CJ110003","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The wilde lantaarn (wild lantern, will-o'-the-wisp) is a portent of bicycle lamps.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"\"Dêr is ek wer in wylde lantearne\", sei ús heit froeger, en dan gongen wy nei bûten ta om to sjen.\nSokke wylde lantearnen wienen de foarboaden fan 'e lettere fytslampen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38635,"r":"CJ110013","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People hear organ playing and singing at the place where a church is later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw wolris fortellen heard, dat guon oargelspyljen en sjongen heard hienen op it plak dêr't letter in tsjerke boud waerd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":10675,"r":"CJ110101","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator cannot bear to stay in a certain spot because loud sounds of work can be heard there every night. It is a premonition: later a new house is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw hjir in ein fierderop wenne yn in hûs, doe wie 'k izerkooopman. 2 jier ha 'k dêr tahâlden. Mar wy woenen dêr graech wei. 't Wie dêr net út to hâlden.\nAs wy jouns healweitsienen op bêd leinen, dan gong 't der njonken ús alderheislikst oan wei. 't Wie krekt as smieten se mei grouwe bolstiennen. Altyd wie dat leven dêr, en der wie noait hwat to sjen.\nLetter is dêr in nij spul delset. It hat foartsjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29486,"r":"CJ110204","p":"De Wilgen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man dreams that he gets a flat tyre on his bicycle. The dream comes true: the next day he gets a flat. The man was very frightened by it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wenne yn Drachten en ik soe nei myn omke ta yn Nij Beets. Dat wie in âld man. De nachts fan tofoaren droomde ik, dat ik krige in lekke bân tusken Beets en Boarnburgum. Ik wie op 'e fyts. Ik seach it allegear klear foar my. De oare deis stapte ik op 'e fyts. En wrachtich wier, op itselde plak tusken Beets en Boarnburgum, dat ik yn 'e droom sjoen hie, krige ik in lekke bân. Dêr bin 'k doe rare kjel fan woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29490,"r":"CJ110208","p":"De Wilgen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People hear psalm singing and organ music at a certain place. It is an omen: later a church is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Beets stiet in houten tsjerkje. Foardat dat boud woarde, hearden de minsken op dat plak psalmsjongen en oargelspyljen. Dat wie foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29503,"r":"CJ110401","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People see a light burning at a certain place. It is a portent: later a house is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Kollumersweach oan 'e Boskreed yn 'e lânnen stie in âld hûs, dêr ha ús heit en dy yn wenne. Fan tofoaren ha minsken dêr neist in ljocht barnen sjoen.\nNei dy tiid ha heit en dy dêr in nij hûs sette litten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29504,"r":"CJ110402","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People see little lights moving back and forth on the road. It is a portent of the later bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Fan datselde plak ôf seagen wy froeger ljochtsjes hinne en wer gean op 'e wei. Dat wienen de foarboaden fan 'e lettere fytslampen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29530,"r":"CJ110428","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People heard the sounds of the train before the train even ran. Other people predicted that there would be wagons without horses. Those wagons were the later cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wennen minsken dy ha fan tofoaren it spoar riden heard, foardat it der wie.\nDe âlde minsken seinen, der soenen weinen komme/ride sûnder hyns der foar. Dat wienen de lettere auto's, dy't se doe al sjoen hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29584,"r":"CJ110615","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Witches have magpies in their power. If a magpie starts chattering in the morning on the windowsill or in the trees near the house, something bad is about to happen to the livestock or the people of the house. It is an omen. The witches have brought it about.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tsjoensters hienen de eksters yn bidwang. As de eksters dan moarns yn 't finsterbank of yn 'e beammen om 't hûs hinne sieten to skatterjen, dan kaem der ûngelok oer dat hûs. Dan krigen se hwat mei 't fé of mei de minsken dy't dêr wennen.\nDat wie dan 't wurk fan in tsjoenster.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29613,"r":"CJ110802","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days floating lights were often seen at certain places. They were said to be portents of the later bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us pake fortelde ek dat se froeger in ljocht seagen, dat foarby fleach. Dat seagen se wol faker en op allerhande plakken. Hja biwearden dat dit de lettere ljochten fan 'e fytsen wienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29614,"r":"CJ110803","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain place singing can be heard without anything being seen. It is a portent: later a house is built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in plak op 'e Tike hearden se sjongen bûtendoar, sûnder dat dêr in minske to sjen wie. Letter stie dêr in hûs. Dit fortelde heit.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29628,"r":"CJ110903","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain place where a church will be built, church singing can already be heard before the church stands there. It is a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der mat in plak wêze, dêr soe in nije tsjerke set wurde. Doe ha de minsken op dat plak dêr de tsjerkelieten sjongen heard, sûnder dat der noch in stien fan 'e tsjerke stie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29640,"r":"CJ111003","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain place noise can often be heard at night. It is a portent of something that is going to happen in the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn Drachten wie in helling op 't Bûtenfallaet. (by de Pipe). Faek gong it dêr midden yn 'e nacht op in klinken. Yn werkelikheit wie dat sa net fansels.\nMar dan koe men der mar wis fan wêze, dat der wer drokte kaem. Dat gong altyd troch. 't Wie foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29644,"r":"CJ111007","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Sometimes hammering sounds are heard at night. It is an omen: later a house is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Faek gebeurde it - û.mear yn 'e Wylgen - dat men fan tofoaren al wiste, dat der ergens in nij hûs set wurde soe. Dan hearden se yn 'e nacht allegearre lûden dy't by 't timmerjen hearden. Dan seinen se: \"Hjir komt skielk in hûs.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29652,"r":"CJ111101","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A boy hears the sound of people skating although there is no ice. It is a portent: a few days later there is skating.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde op in winterdei, dat der gjin iis yn 't wetter lei. Ik wie doe noch jong. Doe hearde ik de minsken riden op it iis. Dúdlik hearde ik it streekjen fan 'e redens en de minskestemmen dêrby. En 't wie doe noch iepen wetter.\nIn dei of hwat letter lei der iis en doe gong 't op in riden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29654,"r":"CJ111103","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain place the sounds of hammering and planing can sometimes be heard in the evening. It is a portent of work that will be done shortly afterwards.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e helling yn Feanwâldsterwâl hearden se froeger gauris jouns let allegearre leven. Dan gong 't op in timmerjen en skaven. Dan duorre it net lang of it wie dêr allegearre wer wurk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29655,"r":"CJ111104","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Music is said to have been heard in a clearing. It is a portent: later a church is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha wolris heard dat der op guon plakken, samar yn 'e iepen loft wijde musyk heard waerd. Dan waerd der letter op sa'n plak in tsjerke boud.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29656,"r":"CJ111105","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears footsteps at his door and recognises from the steps who it is. But when he goes to look, there is nobody to be seen. It is a portent: later the person whose footsteps he heard actually appears.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw it wol meimakke dat der by ús ien by de doar kaem. Ik hearde dan oan 'e stap wol hwa't it wie. Ik gong dan nei de doar ta en sei: \"Bistû dêr?\" Mar dan wie der net ien. In skoftsje letter kaem dan dyselde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29670,"r":"CJ111119","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days wild lanterns were often seen. They were the portents of the later bicycle, car and train lights. Other people saw the train running before the railway was there. It was a vision of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger seagen wy wol wylde lantearnen. Dat wienen ljochtsjes yn 'e nacht. Gong men der hinne, dan wie der neat. It wienen de foarboaden fan 'e lettere auto- en fytslampen, en ek fan 'e treinljochten.\nMyn âlde lju ha de trein riden sjoen doe't der noch gjin spoar wie. De trein flitste dêr lâns en der wie net in baen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29695,"r":"CJ111206","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days wild lanterns could often be seen. Some people did not dare to pass the will-o'-the-wisps, because the lights would then come at them.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy seagen hjir froeger de wylde lantearnen yn 'e fierte.\nDer wienen minsken, dy doarsten dêr net lâns, hwant dy wylde lantearnen kamen dan op har ta, biwearden se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29717,"r":"CJ111312","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"You can get an omen of many things that are going to happen in the future. If hammering sounds are heard at night, you can be sure that a new house will be built. If you see a house on fire, it actually burns down shortly afterwards. If you hear cries for help from the water, someone will soon drown.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foartjirmerij wie hjir in hiele protte froeger. Men hearde timmerjen yn 'e nacht, dan kom dêr letter in hûs to stean. Men seach in hûs yn 'e brân, dat brânde dan pas letter op. Men hearde om help roppen yn it wetter. Letter fordronk der ien op dat plak.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29728,"r":"CJ111401","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman hears her neighbour wailing loudly in the field. The neighbour denies it. It is an omen: when two of the neighbour's children die four weeks later, the same wailing is heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is jierren lyn gebeurd, dat de buorlju hjir yn 'e Westerein my jammerjen hearden. It lûd wie achter út it lân wei kaem.\nDoe't se my fregen hwat der oan skeelde, sei ik: \"Ik ha dêr noait achter yn 't lân west en ik haw noait jammere.\" En dochs hâldden se fol, dat it myn lûd west hie.\nSa'n fjouwer wiken letter woarden der twa fan myn famkes siik. Se krigen de kroep. Binnen de trije wiken stoaren se allebeide. Doe wie ik sa bot oerstjûr, dat ik roan achter it lân yn en dêr haw ik bot gûld en raesd.\nDat lûd wie dus foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29729,"r":"CJ111402","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A mother and daughter hear the neighbour crying out in panic at night: 'My child! My child!' But when they go to look, the neighbour is simply asleep. The mother suspects that something is going to happen. It was indeed an omen: ten weeks later the neighbour's child drowns and the same wailing is heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie noch in famke. Doe woarden ús mem en ik op in nacht klear wekker. Wy hearden beide ús buorfrou roppen: \"Myn leave pop! Myn leave pop!\"\nSy jammere it út. It lûd kaem by de feart wei. Wy makken gau dat wy der ôf kamen en doe gongen wy nei it hûs fan buorfrou ta om to sjen hwat der oan skeelde. Mar dêr wie neat to rêdden: buorfou lei moai to sliepen.\nDoe sei mem tsjin my: \"Moarnier neat sizze, hear, hwant dit is gjin goed spul. Hjir gebeurt yn 't koart hwat.\"\nIt wie sahwat tsien wiken letter, doe fordronk har jonkje. Hja foun it bern yn 'e feart. By dy gelegenheid hat it minske och sa bot jammere.\nEn d_ lûden hienen mem en ik dy nachts heard. Dat wie dus ek in gefal fan foartsjirmerij.\nIt gebeurde yn Twizelerheide.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29763,"r":"CJ111501","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain place psalm singing can be heard. It is an omen: later a church is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Harkema ha se yndertiid in nije tsjerke boud. Op it plak dêr't dy tsjerke kaem to stean, hearden guon fan tofoaren al psalmsjongen. Dit fortelde de skoanmem fan myn dochter, frou Veenstra, dy't yn 'e Harkema wennet.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29765,"r":"CJ111503","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wild lanterns are said to have been portents of the later bicycle, car and aeroplane lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen waerden hjir froeger in soad sjoen. It hie hwat to bitsjutten seinen se. 't Wie foartsjirmerije. It tsjutte op 'e lampen fan 'e fytsen, de auto's en de fleantugen fan letter.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29805,"r":"CJ111609","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days many wild lanterns were seen at a certain place. They are portents of the later car and bicycle lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Sweagermieden seagen se froeger allegear ljochten. Dat neamden se wylde lantearnen. Yn letter tiid binne dêr allegearre wegen oanlein, en dêr fljogge nou de auto's en de fytsen ensa lâns. Dêr ha dy ljochten de foarboaden fan west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29933,"r":"CJ111722","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Omens of various things that are going to happen in the future can often be perceived. If hammering sounds are heard, a new house is later built on that spot. If a house is seen on fire, it later actually burns down. If cries for help come from the water, a death by drowning soon follows.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hiel faek hearden wy dat guon ergens timmerjen heard hienen. Dan bouden se op sa'n plak letter in hûs.\nEk waerd in brân soms fan tofoaren waernomd. Dan brânde sa'n hûs letter op.\nEk hwannear't der ien fordronk hearden se it helpgerop soms dagen fan tofoaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29934,"r":"CJ111723","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"The narrator often saw wild lanterns floating above the land in the old days.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen sweefden froeger boppe de lânnen. Ik wit de bitsjutting der net mear fan, mar ik haw se wol faek sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29951,"r":"CJ111801","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman hears the sounds of hammering and sawing and other work. It is a portent: later new houses are built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn en om 'e Verlengde Stationsstrjitte, dêr't wy nou wenje binne sa'n 55 jier lyn in soad nije huzen boud. Myn suster, dy't nou yn Limburg wennet, hat dat allegear fan tofoaren heard. Hja hearde timmerjen, saegjen, skaven en smiten mei balken, en alsa mear. Oeral hjir hearde hja dat. Dat is allegear neikom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30030,"r":"CJ112107","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A wagon with a load of hay starts moving by itself, without a horse in front. It is a portent: later the tractor is invented.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wenne in boer dy hie op in joun in weide hea yn 't lân stean litten. 't Hea stie op 'e wein. Der wienen doe noch gjin trekkers.\nFeddema fortelde: 'k Stie dêr nei to sjen - 't wie skimerjoun - en dêr bigjint my dy wein to riden sûnder dat der in hynder foar rint. De wein ried moai nei de pleats ta.\nDat hat foartjirmerije west fan 'e lettere trekker.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30032,"r":"CJ112109","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the old days wild lanterns were often seen at a certain place. The will-o'-the-wisps are said to have been portents of the later bicycle and car lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oer/Yn 't Bûtenfjild ha wy froeger wol faek wylde lantearnen sjoen. Guon woenen wol ha dat dat de foarboaden wienen fan 'e fyts- en autolampen fan letter, as der wegen oanlein wurde soenen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30033,"r":"CJ112110","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the nineteen-thirties a man often heard the sounds of milk churns and machines. He suspected that a dairy factory would come. His suspicion did not come true. Later, however, the land was reclaimed. During the reclamation all kinds of sounds could be heard as well.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wibe v.d. Veen wurke froeger faek as reidsnijer op 't Bûtenfjild. Hy fiske dêr ek wol. Dat wie krekt foar de krisistiid, de tritiger jierren. Hy hearde doe dat dêr lawaei wie fan bussen en masinen. Hy tocht: Hjir komt skielk in molkfabryk. Sokke lûden wienen it krekt.\nMar dat is der net kaem. Wol waerd ridlik gau dêrnei it Bûtefjild ûntgonnen. En doe wienen dêr ek allerhanne lûden fansels.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30041,"r":"CJ112118","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man who is milking is addressed by a little man with a beard that almost drags along the ground. The little man warns him to leave this place at once, because strange things are about to happen. The man leaves immediately.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Broek siet in man yn 't bûthús to melken. Dêr komt in hiel lyts mantsje yn 't bûthús. Syn burd sleepte hast op 'e groun lâns.\nDat mantsje sei tsjin him: \"Nou mast gau sjen datst hjir wei komst to wenjen, hwant ast' hjir bliuwste, dan bileefst rare dingen.\"\nDoe is dy man dêr ynienen wei gien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30049,"r":"CJ112201","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People heard the train rumbling before it even ran. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us beppe fortelde, foardat de trein der wie hearden guon yn 'e Mouneein brommen yn 'e loft. 't Wie 't selde lûd dat de trein letter makke dy't troch Hurdegaryp ried.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30095,"r":"CJ112332","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a place where a railway line now runs, wild lanterns could be seen in the old days. The will-o'-the-wisps were a portent of the later train lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen wienen der froeger, dêr't nou de spoarlijn is. Dat wienen de ljochten fan 'e lettere trein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30096,"r":"CJ112333","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People heard the sound of the train before it was even running. The sounds were a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't der noch gjin sprake wie fan in spoar hearden guon minsken hjir hyltyd in gebolder. Dat wie it lûd fan 'e lettere trein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30108,"r":"CJ112402","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman dreams that her husband comes home with a clock and a table. A few weeks later he buys a pendulum clock and a table.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear sei ik tsjin myn man: \"Dû komst aenst thús mei in klok en in taffeltsje.\" Ik hie 't klear yn myn dream sjoen.\n14 dagen letter reizge er nei in boelguod, dêr kocht er in pendule en in taffeltsje, dy't er my brochte.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30111,"r":"CJ112405","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman is not frightened by terrible things, because she knows everything in advance, although she was not born with a caul. Children born with a caul whose caul is removed forwards are bound to see everything. If the caul is removed backwards, there is nothing to worry about.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sokke dingen haw ik altyd. Ik wurd noait kjel fan hwat freesliks dat se my fortelle, omdat ik it altyd al fantofoaren wyt.\nIk bin net mei de helm geboaren, mar sokken binne der wol. As se de helm foaroer weihelje dan mat sa'n bern letter alles sjen, helje se him achteroer ôf, dan net.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30118,"r":"CJ112506","p":"Hijum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot the sounds of carpentry can be heard. It is an omen: later a new house is built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foartjirmerij hienen se hjir froeger yn Hijum ek genôch. Mem hat wol faek forteld dat se fan tofoaren it timmerjen al hearden fan in nij hûs, dat der letter set waerd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30369,"r":"CJ113001","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot, around midnight, the sounds of carpentry and other work can be heard. It is a portent: later a farmstead is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wurke froeger op 'e sûkerij-fabryk yn 't Oasten fan Broeksterwâlde. Dêr moest ik yn 'e nacht fan snein op mendei om tolve ûre wêze. Doe't ik dêr wer ris in kear om dy tiid hinne wie, doe kaem der in maet by my, dy sei: \"Och, och hwat gong it dêr sakrekt wer oan wei, ik hearde dat der timmere waerd en stienbikke en mei planken smiten, hjir flak by. Der gebeurt hjir yn 't koart hwat. 't Is allegear foargedrús.\nTichte by de fabryk, mei ien kampke lân der tusken is in boereplaets boud woarn fan Jehannes van der Mei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30370,"r":"CJ113002","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A butcher's children often hear animal body parts fall to the ground with a thud, although their father has not yet started work. It is a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn heit wie sa'n bytsje slachter. Wyks slachte er in skiepke of in barchje. It gebeurde wolris dat wy seinen: Hark. Dan wie der in lever of sokssahwat delfallen. Dat lûd wie der. Gongen wy der hinne to sjen, dan wie 't sa net. Mar in skoftsje letter gebeurde it wòl. 't Wie foargedrús.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30395,"r":"CJ113027","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man sees wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns) flying. It is a portent of the later car headlights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Anne Douma fan Broeksterwâld seach de wylde lantearnen samar oer de groun fleanen. 't Wienen greate ljochten, krekt as fan auto's. 't Wie foargedrús.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30403,"r":"CJ113035","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Sometimes the sound of the butter churn can be heard at night. It is a portent of work that is to be done later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde hjir faek, dat de tsjerne út himsels gong yn 'e nacht. Sa hearde it krekt, mar kamen se der by, dan wie 't sa net. 't Wie foargespús.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30429,"r":"CJ113110","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a spot where a new church is being built, organ music had been heard earlier. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha fortellen heard dat der ergens in nije tsjerke delset woarde op it plak, dêr't se earder oargelspyljen heard hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30459,"r":"CJ113208","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"It brings bad luck to see a black cat crossing the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in swarte kat foar jin dwars oer de wei rint, dan bitsjut dat in ûngelok.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30583,"r":"CJ113640","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A father and son very clearly hear the sounds of threshing at night. It is a portent of work that will be done later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en ik hienen ris togearre yn 'e Sumarreheide oan 't murdejeijen west. 't Wie sahwat twa ûre yn 'e nacht. Wy kamen werom. Doe wienen wy sahwat op dat plakje, dêr't noch heide is, flak by it boskje fan Jelke Algra.\nDoe sei heit tsjin my: \"Mast ris hearre!\"\nDoe hearden wy beide hiel dúdlik dat der trije man op 'e maet oan 't terskjen wienen by Jan Bonnes yn 'e skuorre. 't Wie foartsjirmerij. Ik wie doe in jonge fan 16 jier. 't Gebeurde op in winternacht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30854,"r":"CJ113901","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Someone hears the sound of the train on the rails before the train is even running. It is a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Twizelerheide hearde ien de trein lâns kommen. Hja hearde him riden op 'e rails. Der wie doe noch gjin sprake fan in trein. Jierren letter kaem der pas in spoarwei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":128462,"r":"ENGELB_09_001","p":"Tilligte","v":"Ov.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Seeing a black dog before the dog is actually there.","i":"H.E.","o":"Ik: At d'r nô es een zer, dat of dat zôl d'r gebeurn, he'j wa es metmaakt, dat dat is oetkömn?\nM: Dat heb ik zölf persoonlik nich metmaakt, mer mien moder hef dat wa zegd, dat dat precies klopde, a wa verschillende dinger, doe dat kanaal is maakt, dee dukers vuur 't Oageler Brook, ja dat warn grootn, dee hebt ze d'r inheid. En den Huunnboarg, den hebt ze es losgraavn in 1916.\nIk: Professor Holwerda was d'r bie oet Leidn.\nM: Professor Holwerda was d'r bie, dee bestoat nog, den kleinzoon d'r van. Dee vrouw van dokter Holwerda, dee hef ne pentekening maakt van mien grootvader. 't Koomp veur in \"Het Land van Katoen en Heide van van Deinse\" doar koomp 't veur, den vrouw van den natuurvorser, mer den har d'r ne woonwaag stoan, wie warn zukke veant nich en den har nen grootn zwartn hoond, veur roofovervaln; joarn veur dee tied, ne halve eeuw, doe hebt ze den hoond a zeen loopn, wie hebt vaak last had met den zwartn hoond, den zag oe niemand anders as he alleen (den man was zonnen speuknkieker), mer den zag van alles, den hef ok den hoond zeen loopn, en zee wusn heelmoal nich wat dat ôp 'n duur zôl wördn, nich, mer doe kwam den man dan met dat onderzoek oet Leidn dan veur dee ôpgravingn met den zwarte hoond.","l":"Twents"},{"n":128463,"r":"ENGELB_09_002","p":"Tilligte","v":"Ov.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hearing a bell and seeing people looking out of a hole.","i":"H.E.","o":"Zee hebt ok a 'n moal ne klok heurn sloan, dee hadn natuurlik ne klok in de waag had, zee hadn ne klok heurn sloan, doe bint ze noar 'n Huunnboarg deur de gracht ôp 't hoes an, mer van schrik, he hef ok jôngs oet de groond zeen kiekn, dat warn dee ôpgravings, den man zag van alns.\nIk: Wel was dat dan?","l":"Twents"},{"n":128464,"r":"ENGELB_09_003","p":"Tilligte","v":"Ov.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Predictions about events in the Second World War.","i":"H.E.","o":"M: Hier Ool Hengel, dat was 'n oom van mie, den was dat, joa he zag van alles, mer dat is ne gave, dat holdt verbaand met hypnose en striekkeerls, wenzeukers, dat kan den jông van hier, den oomzegger ok.\nIk: Dat is ok ne gave.\nM: Vroeger ha'j dat völ, dat was nen man in Denkaamp, zee kômt vaak en sigaarn koopn en zo, nich, dat is café Wintels, nen ole baas, vrijdaags is hier Hitler ingoan, Duutslaand en zoaterdaag's oavends was ik doar, nem nog 'n kistjn sigaarn met, zeg he, kost mer zes ceant, kistke Ario, ik heb ze joarn bewaard in 'n oorlog, nich, wie warn owwer an 't proatn owwer de bezetting owwer de Pruusn en he kwam oet Beuningn, zonne jônge veant, den kofn doar 'n pekke sigaretn en dee lachde doar um, joa, zer de oolde baas, doe kaans d'r wa umlachn, jông, mer doe zös ze ok wa brandend oet de lôcht komn, nich, vliegtuign, vleegmachienn, wel dach d'r doe an, 'n eerstn dag was dat nog, an vliegtuign.","l":"Twents"},{"n":128473,"r":"ENGELB_10_002","p":"Lonneker","v":"Ov.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A light burning on a spot where a house was later built.","i":"H.E.","o":"... Ja doe was ik zon tweintig joar, ik was d'r net wier oet 'n deinst, ik heb bie de huzaarn, doar heb ik 26 moand west en 't deerde moal, dat ik doar kwam, wol 'n dokter mie hebn ofkuurd in Amersfoort, dat weet ik nog best, doe zer ik, ik har last van hertkrampn en of ik doar gen last van har, ik zer, doar kaan'k niks van wetn, joa, ik har 't toch, mer of ik dan nich wol wördn ofkuurd, ik zer, doar ha'k weinig belang biej, ik gaf d'r ok niks um of ik in deinst môs, ik zin dan ok wa in deinst goan, ik heb aait an alns metdoan, ik heb d'r ok nooit gen last van had ...\n.... Ja dat is nô wa liêdn, zon dik in de zestig joar, mer doe woundn doar bie ouns ean, wat nô 't vliegveal is en dat was nog iets familie van ouns en doe ik bie ouns kwam, doe hadn ze van wierskaantn een peard met ouns tehoop en wie hölpn ouns owweral mekaar met en doe ik doar 's oavnds, nô ja, doar was gennen fatsoenliken weg hen, het was almoal hei en dann en veald, dat mô'j zeukn, ha'k hoast zegd, mer as ik 's oavnds noar hoes hen veurde vandoar, dan kôn ik aait ne laamp zeen braandn van ouns ôp 't Hof Espelo an, 'n Hofmeyer zeadn ze vrower en ik kôn nooit en d'r stun neargns gen hoes woarvan ie ne laamp zeen kônn, doe later begunn ze doar wat te bouwn, ja en zo is 't eigenlik goan, doe is d'r doar ean verbraand, nich zoa veer van ouns of .... en 's oavnds, wie hadn nog gennen poump en 's oavnds, wie worn nog","l":"Twents"},{"n":131057,"r":"VODA_032_02","p":"Ommen","v":"Ov.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman saw a cart without horses that was going very fast. Cars did not exist yet then, but this was probably a voorspooksel or voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the car.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Ja, over spoeken ’esprokken, hebben we namelijk van vroeger, da spoeken. Want spoeken, wat weard daar nu eigenlijk onder verstaan? Wie hadden vroeger ook veurspoeksels.\n’t Is gebeurd bie ons in de buurte en da was ’n tolhekke en daen man daen hiete Tolkloas en die vrouwe ging eens op ’n oamd noa buut’n [gekraak van een stoel] en toe kump ze helemoale van streek weer in huus en toe zeg ze te’en dae man: “Kloas, wat ‘k noe ’zien hebbe, da ka-je nooit ra’en. Doar is ‘m … ’n waag’n is d’r deur ’egaang’n zonder peerd. Ja, en zo hard as det dink gunk. Ik kon ‘t hoast… ’t was maar eventies of ’t was weg.”\nJe kan ‘t wel begriepen, veurspoeksels, dat was dan misschien ‘ne veurspoeksels veur de auto’s, want die bestunden toen nog nie in d… dagen. Want d’r was helemoal nog geen sproake dat d’r ooit een auto kommen zol, want ‘t waren allemoal peerd en wagens.","l":"Sallands"},{"n":131133,"r":"VODA_032_10","p":"Ommen","v":"Ov.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Little lights seen at the place where houses would later be built.\n\nA woman said that at her home they used to see little lights burning against the hill. Years later houses were built there (exactly where the lights had burned).","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Ik sprakke nie zo lange geleden een vrouwe in Stiëgen, naam nuum wee‘k nie. Maar dea vertelde det ze, vrôger beej haar thuus, hadden ze tiëgen ’n berg aan lichies gezien en völle joaren later waren op diezelfde plekken waren huzen woar de lichten brandden [voorbijrijdend verkeer].","l":"Sallands"},{"n":128488,"r":"ENGELB_12_001","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A whirlwind destroys a great deal, but the Sacred Heart statue is spared; a prediction that terrible things will happen elsewhere.","i":"H.E.","o":"Klein Haarhuis: Vrielink, de kapper bie oons, he, dat wusn wie a wa twee moand van te vuurtn, toe was mien moor en zien zuster, wat in Vas is trouwd, doe warn ze doar boetn, t is onveer tien uur, half elm, in een moal kwamn ze in hoes loopn, o God, wat wie no hebt zeen, no hebt zeen. No wat he’j dan? zer ik, ding, ne zwarte wolk, nen langn stert d’ran, völ lawaai d’rbie en n lawaai d’rbie, en den is bied ouns langs de tuffelkoed langs goan, zee, den kwam van B. of bie de tuffelkoel langs en precies op P ... zien hoes an en d’r was zoavöl lawaai bie. Doe zeg mien vaar, dan zal’t zich wa oetwiezn, dan zal t wa komn, holdt doar mer reknschop met. En precies zoa-as ’t gebuurd is, ... precies n zölfdn weg ... heelmoal alles kapot, nooldn Mei zat heelmoal onder ’t puun, vast onder t puun, dikke pöal warn ok ofweajd, n ooldn Mei zit vast onder t puun, hef nog n wek of vief zes bie ouns west, want zie haar gen onderdak meer, doar stun nen beeln glaazn koepel in de glaaznkast, dat hadn ze vroger, zonne stölp en dat stun, ik vertel t hier, zoa woar as God in n hemmel is, in ne muurkast, alles was bovn H.Hartbeeld ofknapt alns was vot en t heilig Hartbeeld was nich kapot.\nEn dat was alleen t ennigste, wat d’r in hoes bespoard was, want n iemnkôarf hebt ze later vundn nog, dree veer km. van t hoes of, de kat en t spek hebt ze vundn nen kilometer van t hoes of, ik zeet nog stoan, ik kom doa","l":"Twents"},{"n":128490,"r":"ENGELB_12_003","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Seeing in advance that an accident is going to happen.","i":"H.E.","o":"Klein Haarhuis: Joa, dat klopt, n zeker aantal leu, dee könt dat zeen ... alle hebt de gave. Ik was moal bie ten Coat en nen machtign tank mos doar komn, dat was nen tank, den wöag zeker wa twintig ton, ne geweldig grootn waag, ne politiescorte d’rbie, den kwam doar oet ne kwekeriej, doar oet Hollaand, oet Westn, Westzaan of doar en ze woln hem bie ouns gebroekn as verwarming van dee tuinders, wee’j nich, ze woln bie ouns t hele fabriek met verwöarmn, wee’j nich. No dat ding stun op dee aanhangwaag, dat hok, den kelder, woar he in mos, was a kloar, mer ja, zee hadn hem nog nich van de waag of, ik was nen jong, wat was ik, ik deank n twintig, tweetwintig joar mer Hans zeg tegn mie, Herman blief iej d’r ok evn bie, dan kö’j de bool ok meteen wier op slot doon, ik was ja veertig joar bie ten Coat west, Doe steln ze den dreepoot, dee steln ze doar op en ik stun d’r zoa biej, ik prakkezeern d’rop, ik zer, dat kan nich, dat kan geelsnich, doarbe goat ze grote ongelukn met. Temet dan mos dar ding hoog de locht in en dan mos den grootn kettel den mos d’r precies inkomn, tank zit d’r in, aands konn ze d’r nich in komn, dat geet nooit goad, dat wördt brokn. Ik zeg: Keerls, - ik was de jungste - dat kan nich, wa’j doar doot. Joawa, ik zeg: Doar krieg’j n oongeluk met, doar is t eand nich van te zeen, dat geet nich goad, Wat dan? Temet a’j op t heugste punt stoat, dan gebuurt d’r rare ding","l":"Twents"},{"n":128491,"r":"ENGELB_12_004","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Narrator has a premonition that he must brake so as not to drive into the water.","i":"H.E.","o":"En doarum ie möt ok wa es mangs de hersens loatn wearkn. En in dat geval spölt dat ok wa de hoofdrol, mer ie hebt ok wa es verscheidene valn da’j van te vuurtn dat anveult. ik heb t had, dat was bie Gait Roelofs., de Höfter oet Tubbig, Gait, den is no doad, nen beste keerl, koump wier oet de kolnmien, doar lewwern te Coat alle waagns an, nich. En doe mosn wie doar ne wek hen en doe komt wie wier, kom wie wier, mer de koppelingsplaat kapot, hebt ‘m op de stroat mötn repareern, we’j nich. En doe koump d’r ne most opzetn, wie woln ’s oavnds noar hoes hen. Mer ik wus goad in de plet, dat doar, hoo het dat water ok, doar bie Tiel, doar mö’j de Waal owwer en dat was n poond we’j nich en dat was zonne hevige mist. Gait zat nich in de waag, he zat zoawat nöast op t spatbord, doar stun he en heel zachtjes veurn, zo’n vieftwintig, dertig km, he, en in t lestn, wie hadn a zonnen bestn zet riedn, ik zej, no mö’w ok moal an dat water wezn, o, zeg he, volgns mie zi’w d’r nog lang nich en wiej jagn duur, en in eenmoal, ik trap op de rem. Bats, pats, a’k wat zeen heb, mag ze mie n haals ofsniedn, ha’k hoast zegd, dat zekt ze vrower mangs, dat is ok nich nöarig. He zeg: Wat doo’j no? Ik zeg, Gait, ik veul mie nich meer veilig. [in kantlijn door Engebertink met pen geschreven:] net zo wuurachtig at d’r nen god in ’n hemmel is De vuurwieln, dee raakn de ketn en n poond lag an de aandre kaant, dan","l":"Twents"},{"n":128499,"r":"ENGELB_12_012","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Prediction that an apostate will ask for a clergyman on his deathbed.","i":"H.E.","o":"Kl.H. Doar kan ik nich owwer oordeeln, meestieds dee dinger, ik zeg altied zoa. No as ik wet, dat dat kan, dat wat leu dat zeen könt en dit en dat, geleuf ik stellig, dat dat almoal nen achterground hef. D’r is hoast niks of doar zit wa nen achterground an, a’j doar deper op ingoat, want ik heb es iemand sprökn, nich sprökn, ik d’r bie wearkt, he was vrower misdener west, hele fienn warn dat vrower, ik heb gennen misdeaner west, goad trouw, dat heb ik zölf metmaakt en den man döar aajt raar owwer de geestelikheed owwer de pastoor en kaploans enorm, he gung nich meer noar de keark hen, meen je, dat ik me laat wijsmaken, zeg he, vroeger wel, maar nou niet meer, ik zeg: Jan, no mö’j es goad begriepn, ie hebt katholiek west, ie hebt misdeaner west en no kan oe wat zegn, op oe stearfbed kom ie doar wier op teruw, a’j de kaanst d’r vuur kriegt, nich eerder, dat nem ik ok aan, dree van ziene zöns warn bie ouns, he zölf, geneen van ziene dree zöns gungn nog noar de keark, hadn d’r gen schoold an, want de vaar en de moor gungn ok nich meer noar de keark, mer ik kenn hem goad, ik kon d’r nich meer eerlik bie blievn, in n auto doar wol he aait benzine in hebn en dat mog ik nooit opschrievn, ik zeg, at ie benzine wilt hebn, dan noteer ik, ie kriegt bie mie gen lieter benzine, of ik noteer t, want ik gung owwer de poomp, ik was op t lest ondeer, ik har d’r gen leavn meer bie, ik zeg tegn n","l":"Twents"},{"n":128508,"r":"ENGELB_12_020","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A small light is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the building of a house. A flame is seen rising and falling in the street.","i":"H.E.","o":"Ben Kleissen: Doe in dee tied zöagn ie ok aait n lempke braandn bie t putke doar.\nKleissen: Ja, in dee daag ha’j ok zuk verrek slecht water, zo’n dertig meter van hoes of ha’j zonne put. Ne putring met ne poomp, doar har ne poomp opstoan, en doar zat werkelik good water in, wie mosn al t water um koffie van te dreenkn en vuur t waske of zuks wat, wie mosn d’r alns vandan haaln. Wie hadn op del wa ne poomp en ne putte, doar boetn n paar meter d’rof, ja den was n meter of tien deep en doar haaln wie t water altied vandan. En net iedereen a’w d’r langs kwamn en net zölfde wanneer, zagn wie d’r n lechtke brandn, ik dachn altied bie miezölf, altied precies in dee richting en wat is t geval waarschtig: n joar of dree, veer later en doar steet n hoes en ie kiekt nog alle oavndn noar dezölfde laamp, precies doar langs den boom, doar langs doar is t, dat was L.J., Mer n joar of wat teruw, dat is no n joar of veer lîedn, nee, dat is t nog nich ees, dree joar lîedn en doe bie n buurman, den har gen hoesblievn bie de kinder, wie zoln bie n buurman in hoes mötn blievn, de vrouw en ik en doe oawerleadn wie dan. Bennie was ok nog bie t hoes, mer dan was in dee daag ok nog wa drok met leern of wat ha’j toch ok? Mer in iederg geval, wie goar noar n buurman hen, wie blieft doar in hoes en doe goa’k doar verschillende moaln, het was mooi weer, t was weenterdag, zeg mer, het was november of zo-iet","l":"Twents"},{"n":128515,"r":"ENGELB_12_027","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Hearing sounds and seeing a small light at a spot is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the building of a house.","i":"H.E.","o":"Kl.H.: Doe’k doar kwam, was alns vot, met ja, dat is n vertelsel. Ik kan nich aands oordeeln, of ik mot d’r achter stoan. En zoa he’j wa zoavöl van dee verhaaln, ik goa d’r wa es mangs deper op in, zoa-as doe ik vrower bouwd heb an de Delma, doe zeg mien moder tegn mie: Herman, ie hebt n steen glad op n verkeerdn eand stoan, doar koomp t hoes nich te stoan. Ik zeg: Ja, moder, dat wet ik wa, mer zee hebt t d’r verkeerd ofzet. Oh, dat wol ik zegn, doar koomp t hoes te staon, dat klopt wa, dat he’k a zoa vaak heurd, en doe vrower doe at - ten Coat woont op de Delma - doe was mien moder en doe mosn ze tuffelweidn, doar lagn ze daag in met de haandn, dat was te völ kwek en dan heurn ze altied op de Delma op dee acht beunder dann, vleegdann en heed altied n haann kreain, de hoonder keakeln, ne bel, ne bel, ne hoesbel, mö’j good begriepn, klingelingeling, ne bel, en ieder moal a’k doar kom, heur ik dee bel doar ok wier en ok dee hoonder kreain, dan zal doar wa n hoes komn, ten Coate d’r op, hoonder in n bos, de bel an t hoes, zölfde, o God, zeg he, wat he’k dee bel vrower a vaak heurd. A’k um zes uur, a’k de wichter mos roopn, gung de bel, dan mosn de wichter in hoes komn, klingelingeling, he har ne hele grote bel, he, doar ko’j zoa an trekn, klingelingeling, God, zeg he, wat heb ik dee bel a vaak heurd, mer vuur dee tied, hoo vaak zint ze nich, woar no mien hoes steet, op dat lempke","l":"Twents"},{"n":31050,"r":"CJ115116","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot people hear a tremendous noise, although nothing can be seen. It is an omen: later a house is built on that spot which collapses shortly afterwards. When it collapses, the same noise is heard as before. Nobody dares to build on that spot any more, because the devil is said to be in the ground.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Surhústerfean hearden guon ris in great lawaei, krekt as kom der fan alles fan boppen. Mar der wie neat to sjen. Letter kom der op dat plak in hûs to stean, dêr bigounen se mei to bouwen. Mar doe't it noch lang net klear wie, sakke it yn elkoar. Dat wie it lawaei dat se doe heard hienen. Se ha dêr letter net wer boud, hwant, seinen se, de duvel sit dêr yn 'e groun.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31107,"r":"CJ115502","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"If hammering is heard at a certain spot, new houses will come. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sa gebeurde 't ek dat guon seinen: dêr en dêr sille huzen komme. Wy ha it timmerjen al heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31117,"r":"CJ115512","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot lights can often be seen in the evening. It is a portent: it is the lighting of houses that will be built later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De Spekloane del yn 'e Boelensloane seagen forskeidene lju by jountiid ljochten. Letter die bliken dat se de ljochten sjoen hienen fan 'e huzen dy't dêr doe letter boud binne. Dat wie foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31211,"r":"CJ115903","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man sees little lights on a stretch of heathland in the evening. It is an omen: later houses are built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us pake wenne op it Wytfean. As er jouns dy kant nei de Harkema útseach, dan seach er dêr allegear ljochtsjes. It wie dêr doe noch heide, en minsken wennen der hast net. Mar letter is Harkema bot oanboud en doe kamen der ek in soad ljochten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31212,"r":"CJ115904","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears the sound of a moving train and a voice saying 'Harkema-Opeinde, all change!', although no train runs there yet. It is perhaps an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit fortelde ús froeger, in man út Droegeham hat klear heard dat der yn 'e Harkema sein waerd:\nHarkema-Opeinde Uitstappen! En dêrby hearde er it lûd fan in ridende trein. Dat doe waerd der tocht dat der yn 'e Harkema noch in trein komme soe. Miskien gebeurt it noch. Harkema is it greatste plak fan 'e gemeente woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":128536,"r":"ENGELB_13_010","p":"Rossum","v":"Ov.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a fire, of the laying of a tram line; hammering is heard.","i":"H.E.","o":"H.E. Eduard: n Oortmöskediek en de spoorlien en zuk ding, he, dee konn de leu a mangs van te vuurtn zeen ankomn, dan zöagn ze ok eargns n lechtke duur t veald hengoan, terwijl at der toch genne spoorlien was.\nE.M.: Oh joa, dat was vrower ok doe den tram hier vrower kwam, nich, doe hadn ze ok al dee lechtkes zeen, nich, al dee lechtkes zeen en later doe kwam dee tram, nich, en later zedn de leu gewoon, dat zint vuutgezichtn west, nich\nH.E.: En dat van ne braand, he, ja doar hef Gerrard net ok a owwer had. Dat zee dat van te vuurtn a zeen ankomn.\nE.M.: Dat he’j ok vaak.\nH.E.: Mer a’j dan dichter biekwamn, dan was t heelmoal nich in braand, en a’j dan an de pöst veuln en as t woarm was, dan zol den braand binn kort komn. En was t nog koold, dan kon t nog n zetke anholdn.\nE.M.: Dat kan best wezn.\nH.E.: We’j dan zoa geval hier in de buurt?\nE.M.: Nee, nee, nee dat we ik nich\nG.M.: Mien vader hef nog wa vertöln, doe den tram hier hef loopn, wel at ze doe noa den tram hebt mötn brengn, hef dat n ooldn Plegt nich west of ophaaln dat wet ik nich, dat hef mien vader west, n ooldn Plegt hef der ok wa mangs met vuurd\nE.M.: Op n Ham ... doar hef vrower ok n hoes stoan, dat is al bie Bos kömn\nH.E.: Doar he’k wa papiers van trouwens. Mer Gerrard en Eduard, um doar wier op teruw te komn, met t geval van n neid hoes bouwn ergns, dat ze van te vuurtn ok n vuurgezicht hadn.\nG.M.: Wat heurn timmern","l":"Twents"},{"n":31406,"r":"CJ117410","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1978,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man suddenly sees a white figure floating across the road. The ghost looks like a human being.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ien fan 'e soannen fan Durk Jarings hie yn 'e herberch west to Jistrum. Hy soe nei hûs ta. 't Wie let yn 'e joun. Doe seach er dêr tichte by de Spûkloane in wite gestalte, dy't dwars oer de wei hinne sweeft nei de oare kant ta. 't Like de gestalte fan in minske. Hy is werom gien nei Jistrum, hy doarst dêr net lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31930,"r":"CJ120520","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1978,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A will-o'-the-wisp is a premonition of a road that is built later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy sieten froeger altyd achter in ljochtsje oan jouns. Joun op joun wie dat ljochtsje dêr. 't Wie op Topweer.\nOmke sei: \"Tink der om, dêr komt skielk in wei.\"\nEn hy hat gelyk krigen. Dêr is letter in hurde wei kaem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31315,"r":"CJ116603","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A few people very clearly see a house standing at a certain spot, although there is no house there. It is a portent: later a house is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tusken Earnewâld en Garyp wienen wy yn 'e âlde feanen oan 't wurk. Gjert van der Iest hie dêr in protte âlde feanen kocht. Hy woe dêr wol hinne to wenjen, mar elkenien sei, hy krige dêr noait in hûs, hwant hy hie gjin jild.\nMar op in joun seach heit it fjild oer dy kant út nei Earnewâld en doe sei heit: \"Gjin hûs? Sjoch, dêr stiet in hûs: in stjelp.\" En doe seagen myn broer Bouwe en ik it ek hiel dúdlik. Mar dêr stie net in hûs. It wie foartsjirmerij. It hûs kaem dêr sa'n jier of trije letter, krekt sa't wy it sjoen hienen. It stiet dêr noch. Ik wie doe 17 jier.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31317,"r":"CJ116605","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A group of men spending the night in a tent suddenly feel something heavy coming over them. It is a portent: later a dike is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By de Lange Sleatten wie froeger net de ringfeartdyk.\nOp in nacht leinen dêr twa mieren yn har tinte. Doe wie 't krekt as der hwat swiers oer har hinne kaem, dat har bineare. Hja forsetten de tinte in eintsje, doe wie 't goed. Letter kaem dêr de ringfeartdyk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31416,"r":"CJ117509","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot, boatmen hear the sound of wagons driving over a bridge. Only much later is the bridge actually built. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Al hiel lang lyn, doe't de strjitwei fan Ljouwert nei Grins der noch net wie, hearden skippers op it Swartkrús geduerich dat der weinen oer in brêge rieden.\nDer wie doe noch net in brêge, mar letter is dy brêge dêr kaem. Dat wie foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31481,"r":"CJ117902","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain spot little lights can be seen again and again. It is an omen: two years later a farmhouse is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Garyp seagen se op in plak jouns hyltiten ljochtsjes.\nTwa jier letter kaem op dat plak in boerespultsje to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31483,"r":"CJ117904","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Two friends agree to walk to meet each other. When one woman sees her friend approaching in the distance, she says 'There you are already'. As soon as she has spoken the words, the friend suddenly vanishes. When she walks on to her friend's house, it turns out the friend has not even left home yet. It was a vision of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem fortelde, hja soe op in kear in prater ha.\nDat wie Hinke-muoi, dy wenne by it tolhek to Sumar.\nHja hienen ôfpraet, hja soenen elkoar tomjitte rinne. Us mem roan de Burgerreed del. Doe seach se Hinkemuoi oankommen. Doe't se by de hekke wienen sahwat op healwei sei mem tsjin Hinke-muoi: \"Kom, dêr wiest al.\" Hja hie 't net sein of hiele Hinke-muoi wie fuort. Se wie der net mear. Mem waerd rare kjel. Sy is doe trochroan nei it hûs fan Hinke-muoi.\nDoe wie dy oan 't forklaeijen. Se moest har noch rémeitsje foar de bisite. Hja hie noait fan hûs west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31502,"r":"CJ118007","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A farm maid often hears the hay wagon driving at night. It is a portent of what is going to happen the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem tsjinne, doe't se noch net troud wie, as boerefaem by Jan Jelkes yn Garyp. \"Wy ha 't faek hawn,\" sei se, \"dan hearden wy de wein mei hea oer de telle roljen yn 'e nacht, en dochs wie dat net it gefal.\"\nDe oare deis gebeurde dat echt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31526,"r":"CJ118110","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A boy hears his father coming back from a meeting while he has not actually come back yet. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As heit nei in forgadering wie, gebeurde it soms dat mem nei in skoft sei: ik hear heit al praten, hy is op komst. Mar dan wie hy der net. Efkes letter kaem er.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31541,"r":"CJ118205","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"On a sand track, a sound is suddenly heard as if a wagon is driving over a stone road. It is a portent: only later is a paved road built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr't nou de betonwei is yn 'e Harkema hienen jy froeger in sânwei. Us pake en dy wennen dêr oan dy sânwei.\nIt wie sahwat yn 1850, doe kaem dêr by pake en dy in Eastemarder mei de wein. De wein hie er op it sânpaed stean. Doe't er dêr in skoftsje by pake yn 'e hûs sitten hie, sei er: \"Heden, hwat is dat dêr in gerattel op 'e sânwei. Krekt as giet der in wein oer de stiennen hinne.\"\nDoe gongen se dêr hinne to sjen, mar dêr wie neat.\nFuort letter kaem dêr de strjitwei. It wie tjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31576,"r":"CJ118605","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man sees a beautiful new farmhouse with blue roof tiles. It is a vision of the future: later a man who had long been planning to build a new farmhouse builds one that looks just like it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 't petlân fan Sjoerd Ielkes yn 'e Earnewarren, dêr wennet nou Teade Smedes. Dêr wienen heit en myn beide bruorren Bouwe en Hedzer oan 't wurk.\nIt wie de middeis om iterstiid hinne. Se wienen mei 't iten oan 'e gong. Ierappels waerden yn griene oalje opbakt.\nGjert van der Iest soe yn dy tiid in plaets sette litte by de Tsjerk-wei, by de feart. Dêr wie al in moai skoft sprake fan, mar finansieel koe er it net foar inoar krije.\nDy deis sjocht dyselde fan uzes, dy't oan 't itensieden wie, tafallich de Tsjerk-wei út en dêr wurdt er in gloednije plaets gewaer mei foar blauwe pannen op it dak en achter reid. De sinne flikkere op 'e blauwe pannen.\nDoe sei dyselde: \"Nou moatte heit en dy ris sjen, dêr stiet al in plaets: de nije plaets fan Gjert van der Iest.\nSe seagen alle trije. De plaets wie kant en klear. Se seagen him alle trije hiel dúdlik.\nDe jouns sei heit tsjin Hette Grypma, dy't op in spul wenne op in stik lân dêr njonken: \"Gjert van der Iest hat dêr al in plaets stean, hè?\"\n\"Hwatte?\" sei de man.\n\"Ja,\" sei heit, \"wy ha 't hjoed klear en bleat sjoen. Hy hat itselde model as jouwes, mar hy is hwat langer.\"\nDe man skodholle.\nDe oare deis gongen heit en dy wer it lân yn, mar doe wie der neat to sjen.\nMar deselde maitiids kaem dy plaets dêr, krekt sa 't heit en dy him sjoen hienen, mei blauwe pannen foar, en fierder in reiden tek. En hy wie ien stâl langer as dy fan Hette Grypma","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31578,"r":"CJ118607","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Two men are spending the night in a small tent when one of them suddenly wants to leave because he feels something heavy pressing on his head and chest. It is an omen: later a dike is built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en âlde pake Tamme wienen ris by de Prikwei oan 't meanen. De Earnewâldster polder wie der doe noch net.\nHja hienen de tinte, dêr't se yn slepten, deun tsjin 't kanael oan stean.\nDoe sei pake yn 'e nacht: \"Jelle, wy matte hjir wei.\"\n\"Och,\" sei heit, \"hwat merakels binne dat nou wer. Jow jo dochs del.\"\nMar de âld man hâldde oan. \"Wy matte hjir wei,\" sei er, \"hwant it is krekt of se my in swier gewicht op 'e holle en op it boarst drukke.\"\nDoe ha se dêr yn 'e nacht de tinte in 20 à 30 meter it lân yn set. \"Hjir komt hwat, dat mist net\", sei pake.\nLetter kaem dêr de polderdyk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31579,"r":"CJ118608","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man keeps hearing hammering at a certain spot, although nothing can be seen. It is a portent: later new houses are built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Tsjibbe Westra wenne op 'e Sumarreheide. Alle jounen hearde hy timmerjen, mar dêr wie neat to sjen.\nIt wie de Aldegeaster dyk út dêr't er it hearde. In skoft letter waerd dêr in rige huzen set fan 'e woaningbou. It wienen huzen fan 'e gemeente.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31580,"r":"CJ118609","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A glass carriage with a horse in front of it is suddenly pushed off the road. It is an omen: later the road in question is rerouted.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By de Wartenster dyk ried in glêzene wein lâns. Dy waerd samar ynienen mei hynder en al oan kant set.\nLetter mei it bouwen fan 'e nije Foanejachtsbrêge is de wei dêr forlein. 't Forkear gong doe de nije wei lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31582,"r":"CJ118611","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Floating figures are often seen at a certain place. It is a voorgezicht (a vision of the future): later cyclists ride at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger gebeurde it wol gauris dat guon gedaenten sjoen hienen dy't sweven. Dat ha foarboaden west fan 'e lettere fytsers.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31623,"r":"CJ119106","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A woman often sees two rows of little lights floating in opposite directions at night. It is a premonition: later a motorway is built at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Antsje wenne to Sigerswâld ûnder Garyp yn in lyts húske njonken de koaipleats. Antsje fortelde: As ik op bêd liz, sjoch ik allegear ljochtsjes, twa rigen, de kant út nei Ljouwert en de kant út nei Earnewâld.\nHja hat it goed sjoen. Letter kaem dêr de snelwei fan Drachten nei Ljouwert en de wei nei Earnewâld, dêr't de auto's lâns stouden, mei jouns de ljochten op.\n't Wie foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31642,"r":"CJ119218","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain place a few people see a little lamp floating. It is a premonition: later a house is built at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der hienen minsken to ierappeldollen west, dy kamen op in joun thús fan har wurk. It hûs, dêr't nou Tamme Hedzers Hooijenga wennet (myn broer) stie der doe noch net - it hat sahwat yn 1870 west - doe rounen dy minsken troch in âlde drûge sleat, dwars oer, dat wie it koartste.\nDoe sei der ien: \"Sjoch, dêr stekt ien de tútlampe op.\"\nDat wie op 't selde sté, dêr't letter Tamme kaem to wenjen.\nIt hûs stie der doe noch net. Pake hat dêr in kampke lân kocht en 't hûs dêr sette litten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31789,"r":"CJ119701","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the past, wild lanterns were often seen at a certain place. They are the forerunners of the later car headlights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen sweefden hjir froeger faek oer de heide. Men wol ha dat dat de lettere auto's binne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31797,"r":"CJ119709","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At night a girl hears threshing sounds very clearly and becomes very frightened. It is a premonition of the work that is to be done the next morning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie in fanke fan in jier of 14, 't wie yn 'e nacht, ik lei op bêd. Ik wie wol klear wekker, hwant ik siet op 't lêst yn bêd, sa bang waerd ik. Ik tocht: se binne hjir yn 'e skuorre oan 't terskjen, ik hearde it hiel dúdlik. Mar 't wie net sa fansels, hwant dat koe net. De oare moarns ha se dêr terske. Ik hie 't dus de nacht tofoaren al heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31800,"r":"CJ119712","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a married couple hears all kinds of sounds, although there is nothing to be seen. It is a premonition: later a new farm is built at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem en heit wienen ris op in nacht togearre to murdejeijen. Doe kamen se op in plak - it wie yn Wergea - dêr waerden bussen delsmiten en se hearden amers ratteljen en al sa mear.\nBinnen it jier waerd dêr in nije pleats boud. 't Wie foartjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31801,"r":"CJ119713","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"In the evening people often see a little light burning at a certain place. It is a premonition: later a house is built at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op it plak dêr't nou ús hûs stiet, dêr't wy yn wenje, dêr seagen guon alle jounen in lampe brânnen. Doe stie dit hûs der noch net.\nItselde jiers noch waerd dit hûs boud. En doe wie de lampe der echt. It ljocht skynde jouns troch de ruten hinne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31803,"r":"CJ119715","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"An old woman sees a light coming straight at her and suspects she is having a voorgezicht (a vision of the future) of a road that will be built later. It is indeed a voorgezicht and it comes true: twenty years later a road is built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr wenne in âld minske yn Garyp-Sigerswâld, dy seach in ljocht rjocht op har takommen fan 'e rjochting Earnewâld. Doe sei se: \"Hjir komt skielk in wei, dat is sa wis as hwat.\" En 't is ek neikaem. Mar it hat wol in 20 jier duorre, ear't dy wei der wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31804,"r":"CJ119716","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears carpentry sounds and suspects it is a premonition of something that will be built later. Later a carpentry business does indeed come to that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Garyp wenne âlde Adolf. Dy hearde yn 'e nachten guon timmerjen flak njonken syn hûs. Hy sei: \"Hjir wurdt timmere, hjir komt hwat.\" Doe kaem dêr gaueftich dêrnei in timmersaek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31893,"r":"CJ120302","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain place psalm singing can clearly be heard. It is a premonition: later the Reformed church is built at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Harkema moest in nije grifformearde tsjerke boud wurde. Dêr moest in plak foar opsocht wurde. In pear mannen fan 'e tsjerkerie moesten om har hinne sjen. Doe kamen se op in plak dêr hearden se dúdlik psalmsjongen hoewol dêr neat to sjen wie. Op dat plak ha se de tsjerke letter boud.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31941,"r":"CJ120903","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a haunted place a hunter suddenly sees a glowing thing floating. When the ghostly thing disappears into the ground, the hunter starts digging in the ground. Shortly afterwards the hunter can hardly breathe, because he feels as if a heavy weight is resting on his shoulders.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tichte by de Skieding is de Janke-dobbe. Dêr is al ris in sekere Janke yn fordronken, dêrtroch hyt er sa. Dêr wienen ris op in nacht mei ljochtmoannewaer in pear murdejagers. Flak dêrby roun in paedtsje skean oer de heide. Doe seagen dy murdejagers ynienen in gleon ding, dat fleach oer it paedtsje hinne yn in heidepôlle. De hounen kamen werom mei de sturt tusken de poaten. Se wienen deabinaud.\nDe iene murdejager sei: \"Ik wol wite hwat dat is, of is 't de duvel ek.\" Hy gong nei 't plak ta dêr't dat gleone ding delkaem wie. Hy klaude mei de hannen yn 'e heidepôlle om.\nRoungear stie hy der oerhinne en doe bigoun er to rocheljen.\n\"'t Wie krekt,\" fortelde er, \"as kaem der in gewicht fan hûndert poun op myn skouders, krekt as hie ien my achter by de nekke beet, ik koe amper sykhelje.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31982,"r":"CJ121101","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain place a man hears carpentry sounds, although there is nothing to be seen. It is a premonition: later a house is built at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Egbert Baarsma fan 'e Westerein hearde ris op in joun timmerjen. Hy gong der út nei it plak dêr't de lûden wei kamen, mar dêr wie neat to sjen.\nIn pear jier letter waerd op datselde plak it hûs fan Sikke Boukes boud.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31983,"r":"CJ121102","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A farmer's wife and her son hear carpentry sounds at night. It is a premonition of work that is done the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik noch in jonge wie waerd de boereplaets fan Gosse Venema fortimmere troch Bergstra fan Surhústerfean. Myn broer wie timmerfeint by Bergstra en timmere ek mei oan 'e plaets.\nWylst hja oan 't timmerjen wienen kaem frou Venema, de boerinne by de timmerlju en sei: \"Dizze selde lûden hawwe myn soan en ik fannacht al heard.\" Dat wie foartjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31985,"r":"CJ121104","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain place psalm singing can be heard. It is a premonition: later a church is built at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der is my ek forteld woarn dat guon minsken it sjongen fan psalmen hearden op it sté dêr't se letter de tsjerke delsetten. Ik leau hast dat it yn 'e Broek wie, mar dêr bin 'k net wis fan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32012,"r":"CJ121503","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Will-o'-the-wisps are premonitions of houses or roads that are later built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger waerden der jouns faek twa ljochtsjes sjoen oer de dyk. Dan seinen se: \"Dêr komme mei de tiid huzen to stean.\"\nMar dy huzen steane der noch net.\nWol sil dêr in nije wei komme, tsjin 'e Skieding oer, dêr't wy wenne ha.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32023,"r":"CJ121606","p":"Schoonoord","v":"Dr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A light is always visible at a certain spot. It is an omen: later a wijk (canal) is dug at that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In Schoonoord zagen ze ergens een licht 's avonds.\nDat kwam telkens weer. Later kwam daar een wijk, waar ze turf langs voeren."},{"n":32052,"r":"CJ121817","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man sees something floating in the air that looks like a big cigar. It is a voorgezicht (a vision of the future) of the later zeppelin.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer seach ris in ding yn 'e loft dat der útseach as in hiele greate sigaer. Hy tocht: Dat komt tsjin 'e tsjerketoer oan, mar 't wie sa net. Hy siet der sa fol fan, dat hy fortelde 't elkenien.\nDat wie de lettere Zeppelin. Dy hie hy al fier fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32060,"r":"CJ121904","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man hears carpentry sounds, although there is nothing to be seen. It is a premonition: later a farm comes to stand at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in joun kaem der ien fan Sumarreheide de pasterijelânnen del. Doe hearde hy ynienen dat it hiel bot op in timmerjen gong. Der waerd mei planken en balken smiten en op 'e nael omkloppe en timmere. Dat wie oan 'e heidewei.\nDe pleats fan Jehannes Romkes de Vries stie der doe noch net, mar hy sei: \"Dêr komt skielk in hûs. Ik ha 't sa dúdlik heard.\" It hûs is dêr kaem, de pleats fan Jehannes Romkes, mar it hat omtrint wol 20 jier duorre foardat it sa fier wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32062,"r":"CJ121906","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A father and his two little sons very clearly see a newly built farm standing there, although it does not actually exist yet. It is a premonition: only a year later is the farm really there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Gjert en Griet hienen in stik âlde feanen kocht ûnder Earnewâld en woenen graech in pleats op dat stik lân sette litte. Mar sy hienen der gjin sinten foar. Dat doe't Gjert nei de timmerlju to Garyp gong woenen dy net foar him timmerje. Njonken dat stik lân fan Gjert stie in pleatske.\nOp in kear wie omke Jelle mei twa fan syn jonges yn dy buert oan 't wurk. Hja wienen sa'n heale k.m. fan Gjert syn stik lân ôf. Doe sei omke Jelle tsjin 'e jonges: \"Sjoch, dêr stiet Gjert van der Wiel syn nije pleats.\" De oare beiden seagen it ek. De pleats stie dêr kompleet. Hy wie twa stâllen langer as dy dêr njonken.\nIn jier letter kaem de pleats dêr to stean, krekt sa't hja him sjoen ha. Omke Jelle hat it faek forteld.\nDe pleats stiet der noch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32112,"r":"CJ122402","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Carpentry sounds are heard at a certain place. It is a premonition: later a new house is built at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Garyp stiet oan 'e wei nei de polderdyk in hûs, dêr wennet nou Lammert Slofstra. Froeger stie dêr in âld hûs foar, doe wie 't nije dêr noch net. Mar guon wisten fan tofoaren al dat it nije dêr komme soe. Dy hienen dêr timmerjen heard en oare lûden dy't men by 't bouwen observearret.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32114,"r":"CJ122404","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Wild lanterns can be seen at a certain place. It is a premonition: later a road is built at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon yn Garyp seagen yn 'e Broek (to Garyp) wylde lantearnen. \"Dêr komt in wei lâns\", seinen se. It duorre lang ear't it sa fier wie. Mar de wei is der kaem troch ruilverkaveling. Sy ha wòl gelyk krigen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32151,"r":"CJ122603","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A man sees two lights floating in a certain direction. It is a premonition: later a road is built at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr stie in wettermoune oan 'e Swarte broek, ûnder de Moune-ein. Dêr wie in polder dy't ûntstien is yn 1866. Dêr fan ôf/foarby roun in reed fan Hurdegaryp dwars oer nei Ikkerwâld. Dat wie de Papereed, dêr troch de monniken oanlein.\nOp in nacht moest heit mealle. Heit wie mounder. Doe seach er fanôf Hurdegaryp twa ljochten oankommen, rjochting Ikkerwâld, oer de Papereed.\nDêr rint nou de nije wei lâns: de Ottema-wei.\nDit wie foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32182,"r":"CJ122910","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain place a man sees a fine farm standing, although it does not actually exist yet. It is a voorgezicht (a vision of the future): only a few years later is the farm built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Gjet van der Iest wenne yn Garyp. Hy handele en hie froeger yn Dútslân west. Dêr hie er by in boer tsjinne.\nHy koe slachtsje en dy boer hie in miltvuur-bolle. Dy slachte Gjet en dêr hat er syn earm omtrint mei forspile. Dêr koe er letter net folle mear mei dwaen. Gjet hie in spultsje op 'e Tuie yn Garyp. Hy hie in greate húshâlding en koe dêr eins net rjocht bistean. Der waerd yn 'e krisisjierren in protte lân forkocht fan 'e Panhuyzens en dêrby wienen ek âlde feanen yn Earnewâld. Ien fan 'e banken fan Ljouwert kocht dêr in âld fean. It bistie út wol sa'n 30 pounsmjit greid mei reid en wetter. Gjet fan der Iest kocht dat lân fan dy bank. Dêr moest er syn eigen âld hûs op 'e Tuie foar forkeapje, oars koed er net ta de sinten komme. Hy woe graech in pleats op dy âld fean ha. Hy gong nei de timmerlju ta yn Garyp en sei: \"Nou wol 'k dêr op myn lân in pleats ha krekt lyk as dy fan 'e diaken fan Garyp.\" Dêr op dy oare pleats wenne Hette Grypma. \"Sa'n pleats wol ik der op ha\", sei er. Mar dêr wie net ien bank dy't him sinten jaen woe. Doe seinen de minsken: \"Gjet krijt dêr net in pleats op. Hy is to ratterich. (Hy hat gjin jild dêr foar.)\"\nDoe gebeurde it dat Jelle-om en twa fan syn jonges oan 't meanen wienen yn in âld fean, dat oanmakke wie fan 'e administrateur Sjoerd Breeuwsma fan Burgum. It wie prachtich waer. Hja stienen dêr alle trije to meanen. Doe seach Jelle-om even op. Hy s","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32188,"r":"CJ123001","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Horses become frightened when they pass a certain place. It is a premonition: later a slaughterhouse is built at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tusken Reitsum en Ginnum stiet in slachthûs.\nFoardat it dêr stie moesten se dêr de hynders altyd beet krije, as se der lâns kamen, hwant dan wienen de dieren angstich. It wie foartsjirmerije.\nLetter kaem it slachthûs dêr en doe moesten de hynders altyd yn toom hâlden wurde as se it passearden. Hynders binne altyd bang foar in slachthûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32190,"r":"CJ123003","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"Several places are haunted. The cry of a barn owl is often a premonition of something bad.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op alle binnenwegen yn 'e Mouneein spûke it. By nacht doarsten de measte minsken dêr net lâns. Nei Readtsjerk gong men troch de bosk. Dat bosk hiet Grikenlân.\nDêr wie in hazzepaedtsje, dêr't net ien lâns doarst.\nDêr wienen 't allegearre lûden. As men dêr in katûle hearde wie dat in faei teken. Dat bitsjutte in ûnk of in slimme sykte.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32200,"r":"CJ123101","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"People foresee all kinds of things.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Forskate lju fan 'e Sumarreheide hienen de tram al riden heard doe't hy der noch lang net wie. Ek seagen se de reade ljochten. Ek hûzen hearden se oan timmerjen dy't der noch net stienen en hja seagen brânnen dy't der pas letter kamen. Sokke dingen wienen doe algemien. It tsjirme dêr altyd yn dy streken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32283,"r":"CJ124001","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"One night a man sees two little lights floating. It is a premonition: later a road is built at that place on which cars and bicycles drive.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in nacht seach heit de kant fan Hurdegaryp út wei twa ljochtsjes dizze kant út kommen. 't Gong oer de polder hinne. Dêr wie wol in âld modderreed, mar dy wie sa min en sa drekkich, dêr koe noait in minske fytse. En dochs wienen it krekt fytsljochten. Mar dêr wie gjin forkear mooglik. Auto's wienen der doe noch net. De oare deis hat heit dêr hinne west om to sjen of dêr ek spoaren wienen. Mar dêr wie neat to sjen. Heit praette der net fierder oer. In skoft letter kaem dêr in wei. Nou ride de auto's en fytsen dêr lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32284,"r":"CJ124002","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"At a certain place a bread seller hears a rushing and whooshing sound, although there is nothing to be seen. It is a premonition: when a butter factory is later built at that place, the same sounds can be heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In âld-omke fan my, Romke van der Wal wenne yn Ryptsjerk. Hy sutele mei bôlle- en breaspul foar bakker Kloosterman fan Gietsjerk. Hy moest altyd fan Ryptsjerk nei Gietsjerk om it bôlleguod op to heljen.\nElke dei moest er mei de hounekarre oer de Riid. Dêr wie doe in brêge, mar de molkfabryk stie dêr noch net. Op in kear ried er dêr wer lâns, doe tocht er: \"Hea, hwat rûst en hwat sûst it hjir.\" \"Eigenaerdich,\" tocht er, \"hiel oars as oars.\"\nLetter kaem dêr it bûterfabryk to stean, dat nou wer opheven is. \"Doe hearde ik krekt deselde lûden\", sei er. It wie in serieus man.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32287,"r":"CJ124005","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"According to the minister, a new church must be built at a certain place because he once saw or heard something there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yndertiid wie ds. Zantinge hjir foargonger fan 'e grifformearde tsjerke. De tsjerke - it wie mar in foech tsjerkje - stie doe oan in sândyk tusken Mouneein en Gietsjerk.\nDêr soe in nije tsjerke komme. Mar hwer?\nDoe wiisde ds. Zantinge op in kear it plak oan. 't Wie yn Oentsjerk, dêr't er nou nòch stiet. Hy hat dêr hwat heard of sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":128624,"r":"ENGELB_18_021","p":"Enschede","v":"Ov.","y":1981,"c":"SINSAG 0487","d":"A little light at the place where a house is later built.","i":"H.E.","o":"E: Nen gooldn toafel zeg oe dat wat?\nWit: Nen goold toafel he'w bie oons vundn.\nE: Doar zol nen gooldn toafel lign?\nWit: Joa.\nE: Woar zol den zoawat lign dan?\nWit: An de oolde Almelose weg. Dan kom ie in Gammelke oet.\nE: Van Oldnzel op Gammelke an.\nWit: Van Oldnzel op Gammelke an.\nE: Is dat nich an t Gammelkerströatke dan?\nWit: Joa, dat is Gammelkerströatke.\nE: En doar zol nen gooldn toafel. Of hebb ze doar wa es mangs graavn?\nWit: He?\nE: Hebt ze doar wa es mangs graavn?\nWit: Graavn hebt ze doar wa genoog doan.\nE: Doar hebt ze niks vundn.\nWit: Ze hebt doar de toafel nich vundn.\nE: Mer doar an t Gammelkerströatke op n Tij, zegt ze dat doar, op n Tij.\nWit: Dat is no Tijdhof.\nE: Mer doar hebt vroger grafheuvels legn. Dat doar vroger wat begraavn zint.\nWit: Dat lig wa veur de haand, dat is net bie de stad.\nE: Mer doe was der nog genne stad.\nWit: Ze deedn ze doar toch ook nich begraavn.\n-Toen was het bandje afgelopen-\nE: Woar is dat gebuurd dan?\nWit: Woar is dat gebuurd. Oons hoes was nog nich verkof en oonze groond en doe, zeg dan mer, braandn doarginder n lechtke, aait n lechtke en doar ha'w aait nen grootn mesthoop stoan, wee'j wa, zukke böam met twee peer veurn der tegn op en dan der wier of en dat mos dan al op t laand, doar mos ruumt vuur weazn. No en wat is no t geval? Doe oons plaats verkoft is, doe har oons Jens zovöl ceantn stiekum in n tuk, umdat dat toch almoal nich meer","l":"Twents"},{"n":69808,"r":"DYKFRIES2204","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"One or more people who are out on the road or still outdoors at night or late in the evening can sometimes hear, at some distance, frightened cries for help that seem to come from a nearby waterway or lake. If they go there, they find there is nothing. But then winter comes; the water freezes and people start skating. Then it is usually the same people who hear the same cries for help again at the same place. But now they really come from people who have fallen through the ice and are in mortal danger. Such accidents announced by voorspook (a ghostly apparition foreshadowing an event) usually end in death.","i":"W.D."},{"n":69809,"r":"DYKFRIES2205","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"Some craftsmen hear ghostly sounds when someone is about to die. They hear the knocking and planing of people making a coffin. On one of these occasions she heard a bump against the frame of the front door. This was inexplicable, because the door was quite far from the workshop. But not long afterwards someone died and the event came true, exactly as it had been heard.","i":"W.D.","o":"Handwerkslieden hooren soms bij nacht in hunne werkplaats, als daar niemand is, een leven alsof er minstens twee of drie personen druk in de weer zijn. Het komt meest voor wanneer er in zulk een werkplaats buitengewone drukte op handen is, waarvan men op 't oogenblik nog niets weet of vermoedt. Timmerlieden, wagenmakers en meubelmakers zijn op de dorpen ook altijd doodkistenmakers als 't zijn moet. Het was vroeger geene zeldzaamheid, en het zal nog wel eens voorkomen, dat genoemde handwerkslieden het altijd eenige weken vooraf te weten komen, wanneer in het dorp een sterfgeval te wachten staat. Zij hooren dan 's nachts in hunnen winkel geklop en geschaaf en merken aan alles wel dat daar een doodkist wordt gemaakt, niet in werkelijkheid, maar zij zijn er zeker van dat dit eenige weken later zal geschieden. En dit mist ook niet. Eens echter hoorde men bij zulk eene gelegenheid een stomp tegen het kozijn der voordeur. Dit was onverklaarbaar, omdat deze deur tamelijk ver van de werkplaats verwijderd was. Maar niet lang daarna stierf een bij den baas inwonend persoon. En toen nu op den dag der begrafenis de kist het huis werd uitgedragen, stompten de buren bij ongeluk daarmee tegen het kozijn der deur."},{"n":39016,"r":"ZEEUW090","p":"Westdorpe","v":"Zl.","y":1923,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"A man hears someone calling who has, however, been working in the mines in Germany for 15 years, and afterwards hears that the man has had a fatal accident in the mine.","i":"P.A.E.","o":"Spokerijen.\n\nOnze Peet die wier es wakker, in hij hoorden Jan van Kruisen roepen. IJ docht, da' kan toch nie', want ge moe' weten, Jan van Kruisen die zat al vijftien jaar in Duitsland in de mijnen. In onze Peet die riep: \"Wat is 't er, Jan?\" — \"Helpt er mij eens van onder,\" riep Jan. En anders riept-ij niks, maar onze Peet die kost van 'eel den nacht nie mêêr slapen.\nIn 'nen tijd later 'ôôrdeme vertellen da' Jan van Kruisen in de mijnen verongelukt was.","l":"Zeeuws"},{"n":209978,"r":"HOL001914","p":"Maurik","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"Hearing someone call who is far away.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mevr. van Weelderen was als meisje eens voor hulp bij een ziek familielid in Neerbos. Toen zij stond te karnen, meende ze, dat zij geroepen werd. Dit was ook het geval geweest. Haar moeder, die ziek lag, had haar geroepen."},{"n":210356,"r":"HOL003324","p":"Tiel","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"Knocking on the door at the moment of an accident.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mevr Vermijn heeft eens in een nacht kloppen op de deur gehoord. Toen zij ging kijken, zag zij niemand. Haar man was niet thuis, was bezig aan een verhuizing. Toen hij thuis kwam, vertelde hij, dat er een ongeluk was gebeurd. Eén van de wagens was van de dijk gerold of iets dergelijks (ik meen bij Papendrecht of Sliedrecht), juist op de tijd, dat mevr. Vermijn het bonken op de deur had gehoord"},{"n":21288,"r":"CJ025503","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"One night a man heard his son calling out in fear. He went to look, but the boy was sleeping peacefully. He also heard himself wailing. Six weeks later the son got lost in the fog on the mudflats and drowned. When the father received the bad news, he wailed just as he had heard himself do before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dat der foartsjirmerije bistiet, ha ik sels bilibbe.\nSeis wiken foardat myn soan op it wad yn 'e mist fordronken is haw ik him op in nacht oatmoedich oan my roppen heard. Ik gong fan bêd ôf om nei him to sjen. Mar hy lei rêstich to sliepen. Letter haw ik mysels jammerjen heard, krekt sa't ik jammere ha, doe't ik de tiding krige, dat myn soan fordwaeld wie en stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23415,"r":"CJ039102","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"A boy and his parents once hear a younger child calling and raving, but when they go to look nothing is wrong. Some time later the child really raved and died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn man wie in great jonge, syn heit en mem leefden noch. Doe sei er op in kear: \"Hearre jim Baeije wol roppen en razen?\" De oaren seinen: \"Wy matte der gau us hinne to sjen.\" Mar doe't se der hinne gongen wie der neat to rêdden mei Baeije.\nMar in skoft letter raesde se krekt sa as dy kear. Doe wie har bern forstoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23517,"r":"CJ039705","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"Several people sometimes heard strange sounds coming from a house. Later the sixteen-year-old daughter, who was treated rather badly, hanged herself in the barn. When her parents found her, they screamed. That was exactly the sound people had heard before.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Houtigehage snieën se froeger rusken. Dêr makken se matten fan. Dy woarden dan wer útsutele. It wienen de jonges meastal dy't yn 'e nacht dy rusken ôfsnieën.\nDe heit hie it deis drok en moest nachts syn rêst ha. It wienen greate jonges, dy't it dienen. Op in nacht kommen dy jonges thús en seinen: \"Wy doarre net mear. Der komme sokke rare lûden út in hûs wei.\"\nLetter woarden dyselde lûden noch wer heard út dat hûs wei.\nYn dat hûs wie buorkerije. Dêr wie in fanke yn dat hûs, dat wie dêr altyd de fuotfeger. 't Wie in hiel swier kreas fanke. Mar hja wie der oer en tofolle. Sy moest dêr alles dwaen. Hja wie sechstjin jier.\nSy sieten de jouns by de tafel. Sy soenen elk in hunichbrochje ha. Doe sei de heit: \"Der matte ek noch twa beesten molken wurde.\"\nWytske kom oerein en sei: \"Dat sil ik wol even dwaen.\" Doe't der hwat tiid forroan wie, seinen se: \"Wyts is der net, hwer soe Wyts sitte?\"\nSy seagen om har hinne en sa kommen se ek yn 'e skuorre. Dêr seagen se it fanke hingjen. Hja hie har sels fan kant brocht.\nTrochdat dy âldens har gewetens net suver wienen, hienen se 't útraesd.\nDatselde lûd hienen dy jonges en letter ek oaren fantofoaren heard. Dat wie dus foartsjirmerij.\nIt wie myn patroan dy't it fanke lossnien hat. Hy hat my it hiele forhael forteld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25114,"r":"CJ051504","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"A man hears cries for help and sees wailing women wearing white caps. They are omens: later someone drowns.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Westerein is ien forsûpt yn 'e Swâdde. Lytse Roel van Kammen hat it fan to foaren sjoen en heard yn 'e nacht. Hy hearde ien roppen en seach froulju mei wite mûtsen op dy't jammeren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27355,"r":"CJ065112","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"Cries for help have sometimes been heard from a pond. People still expect that someone will drown in it one day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Boelensloane yn 'e Poel by âlde Elske ha se ris in kear 'help' roppen heard. It is de hiting dat dêr altyd noch ien yn fordrinke mat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28571,"r":"CJ076201","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"When someone is standing on the bridge at Veenwouderwal, he hears a sound below as if someone is calling for help. A while later two boys skate into a hole in the ice, and then the same sound as before is heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It hat ris west, doe wie der in echo op Feanwâldsterwâl.\nAs wy op 'e brêge stienen, bigoun it ûnder 'e brêge lûd to jaen, krekt as waerd der roppen om help. Net ien dy't bigriip hwat dat to bitsjutten hie.\nIn skoft neitiid rieden der twa jongkeardels yn in wek.\nDoe koe 't iis noch net rjocht hâlde. Doe't dy fordronken (binne) hearden se 't selde geskreau as dat se earder heard hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28601,"r":"CJ076506","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"In winter you should not go onto the ice of the Leeuwenpoel, because someone with red hair still has to drown there. A woman with red hair often lies there calling 'help'. Later a girl with red hair drowned in this pond. I myself have heard cries for help at night, so someone else still has to drown.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik in jonge wie wennen wy yn 'e Smoarhoeke, flak by de Liuwe-poel. Wy wennen yn in plaggehutte. As 't winter wie sei heit tsjin ús: \"Pas op en kom net op it iis fan 'e Liuwe-poel, hwant dêr mat noch ien yn forsûpe.\"\n't Wie ien mei read hier, dy't dêr yn forsûpe moest.\n't Minske lei faek midden yn 'e poel en dan rôp se: Help! Help! Help!\nLetter is der ien yn forsûpt: in jong fanke mei read hier. 't Gebeurde mei iis.\nIk ha sels wol ris 'help' roppen heard yn 'e Liuwe-poel. Ik hearde 't allinne by nacht, as 't raer, donker waer wie. It is noch net iens safolle jieren forlyn, dat ik it foar 't lêst heard ha. Der mat nòch ien yn fordrinke.","l":""},{"n":32986,"r":"CJ085206","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"People have sometimes heard cries for help coming from the Leeuwenpoel. It is believed that someone will drown in it one day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon matte ris heard ha, dat der yn 'e Liuwepoel ris in kear roppen woarde: Help! Help! 't Hie in manljuslûd west.\nMen wol ha dat dêr nochris ien yn forsûpe mat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33187,"r":"CJ087710","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"A grandmother heard her newborn grandchild screaming. When she inquired, it turned out the child had indeed been carrying on around that time.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoandochter krige in poppe. Doe't it bern twa dagen âld wie hearde myn wiif har om fjouwer ûre yn 'e middei tige dúdlik razen. Hjir by ús yn 'e hûs. Fuort dêrnei die se neifraech. 't Kom krekt út. Om fjouwer ûre hie de poppe bot raesd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33669,"r":"CJ092601","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"A woman once heard cries for help from the water, but she saw nothing. Later three children drowned there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanmem hat wol faek forteld, hja stie ris by de brêge hjir yn 'e Westerein, doe hearde se trije kear hiel dúdlik 'help!' roppen. Mar hoe't hja ek seach, der wie neat to sjen.\nDy winters binne dêr op dat plak trije bern forsûpt.\nUs skoanmem sei altyd: \"Dat haw ík fan tofoaren heard.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36972,"r":"CJ101510","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"A boatswain of a steamboat carrying pleasure-trippers went overboard. He called for help, but nobody heard him and he drowned. His cries for help had already been foretold by people.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Doezum wie ris in stoomboatsje mei plesierfolk op 't wetter. De boatsfeint rekke bûten board en is dêr forsûpt. Hy rôp om help, mar sy ha him net rêdde kind. Datselde help-gerop ha se dêr earder al heard yn 'e feart.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":10677,"r":"CJ110103","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"At a certain place cries for help can be heard from the water, though nothing is to be seen. It is an omen of an approaching drowning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tusken Harkema en Surhústerfean by de feart, sahwat by Buma, ha se trije kear 'Help!' roppen heard. Mar dêr wie net in minske to sjen. Letter is dêr de frou fan Marten Veenstra yn 'e feart rekke. Dat wie sahwat sawn, acht wiken letter. Dy is dêr doe forsûpt. Dat minske hat doe ek om help roppen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29653,"r":"CJ111102","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"People hear someone calling for help, although there is nothing to be seen. It is a portent of an approaching death by drowning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn it Bûtenfjild is it ris gebeurd dat guon minsken ien roppen hearden om help. Doe't se dêr by kamen, wie der neat to sjen. In dei of hwat letter forsoop dêr ien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30034,"r":"CJ112111","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"People hear cries for help coming from the water. It is a portent: later a drowning person really is in mortal danger.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha wolris fortellen heard dat guon dúdlik 'help!' roppen hearden út it wetter wei. Gongen se der hinne dan wie dêr neat to sjen. Mar letter wie dêr echt in drinkeling dy't 'help!' rôp.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30121,"r":"CJ112509","p":"Hijum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"At a certain place by the water people hear cries for help. It is an omen: later someone drowns and the same sound can be heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De Kuorfeart rint fan 'e Hijumerfeart nei de Hallumer feart. Dêr yn dy Kuorfeart hearden guon út Hijum alris 'Help!' roppen. Hja setten dêr hurd op ta. Mar doe't se dêr kamen, seinen se: \"Forrek, dêr is neat.\"\nLetter is dêr ien fordronken, in eintsje fierder op. Dy rôp ek fan 'Help!' 't Wie krekt itselde lûd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30147,"r":"CJ112601","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"During the German occupation, many young men always stood guard at night to detect any trouble. On one of those nights two boys very clearly hear a plaintive voice calling for help. One morning a married couple repeatedly hears the same cries of someone in distress. When the couple follows the sound, they find someone who has fallen under a train while hurriedly trying to jump onto it as it moved. The victim dies shortly afterwards. The earlier sounds in the night were a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie yn 'e Dútse tiid. De jonge bazen rounen altyd gefaer of se oppakt wurde koenen. Hjir op 'e Bûterwei wienen altyd guon dy't nachts de wacht hâldden. As der ûnrie oankaem, koenen se de oaren gau warskôgje. De iene nacht hâldden dizzen de wacht, de oare nacht dy. Op in nacht wienen it myn soan en Kees, in soan fan ien fan 'e buorlju.\nHja sieten togearre achter 'e hage en smookten in sigretsje. Doe sei Kees: \"Hark, hearst dat?\"\n\"Ik hear neat\", sei myn soan.\n\"Der wurdt 'help!' roppen\", sei Kees.\n\"Ik hear it net\", sei myn soan. \"Ik haw in goed gehoar, it sil wol forbeelding fan dy wêze.\"\n\"Om 'e donder net,\" sei Kees, \"it is in hiel klaeglik lûd as fan ien dy't yn greate need sit.\"\nIt duorre even, doe sei Kees: \"Hark, dêr ropt wer dyselde om help.\"\nDer forrounen in pear wiken. It wie op in moarn, der lei gâns snie. Wy wienen krekt fan bêd ôf. 't Wie tsjuster. Myn man soe de jiskebak leegje. Dêr hearden wy beide hiel oatmoedich om help roppen. \"Dy is der net bêst oan ta\", sei 'k. Mar myn man sei: \"'t Binne oanslaggen fan jongelju, dy't mei de trein geane. Dy tjirgje har.\"\nWy hearden noch in pear kearen deselde gjalp. Doe ried de trein fuort.\nMar doe't dy fuort wie hearden wy 't wer. Ik sei: \"Dit doocht net. Der sit ien yn noed.\"\n\"Ik mei der wol hinne\", sei myn man.\nIt wie in freeslik lûd, en 't waerd al swakker en swakker. \n't Wie glêd. 't Wie hjir flakby. Myn man moest troch de","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30383,"r":"CJ113015","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"Cries for help can be heard by the canal, although there is nothing to be seen. It is a portent: later someone drowns at that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Broeksterwâlde hearden se op in kear yn 't farwetter (yn 't kanael) help roppen. Doe't se der hinne gongen wie der net ien yn 't wetter. Mar letter binne der guon op dat plak fordronken. Dat wie ek foargedrús.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30420,"r":"CJ113101","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"At night a woman suddenly hears terrible screaming, although there is nothing to be seen. It is said to be a portent of an approaching death by drowning. According to the narrator, nobody drowned afterwards.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Syberens Ytsje wie in âld-muoike fan my. Hja wenne yn Burgumerheide. Op in nacht hearde se in freeslik jammerjen en skriemen, dat kom út 'e Kije Ale-poel wei. Doe't se dêr hinne gongen wie alles stil en dêr wie neat to sjen. De hiting is dat dêr altyd noch ien yn fordrinke mat. By myn witen is 't noait gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30859,"r":"CJ113906","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"Someone hears terrible screaming, although there is nothing to be seen. It is a portent: when someone later drowns, the same sound can be heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem fortelde, oan 't Suderbolwurk, by 't Dokkumer âld-tsjerkhôf, dêr hat hja ris in freeslik geraes heard. Doe't se dêr kaem, wie der neat.\nLetter is dêr ien fordronken ûnder in boat. Doe wienen dyselde lûden der wer.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32030,"r":"CJ121701","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0488","d":"A boy and a girl hear a woman plaintively cry 'O my boy! O my boy!' It is an omen: shortly afterwards the woman's son drowns and she cries the same words.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie sahwat tolve jier ald. Ik soe nei hûs ta en roun fan 'e Suderstasjonswei nei de Kule. Wy wennen op it Skier.\nIk wie noch sa'n foege hûndert meter fan hûs ôf, doe kaem Grytsje Zuidema my tomjitte. Gryt wie in fanke fan sa'n fjirtsjin jier. Ik bleau stean en sei: \"Hark ris, sa ropt Eiberts Jap.\" (Eiberts Jap dat wie Eibert Veenstra syn frou.)\n\"Ja,\" sei Gryt, \"ik hear it ek.\" (Eibert Veenstra wenne sa'n twahûndert meter fan ús ôf.)\nIt minske rôp: \"O, myn jonge! O, myn jonge!\"\nEfkes letter kaem ik thús. Doe sei 'k tsjin heit en mem:\n\"Hwat wie Eiberts Jap niis ûnstjûr. Hy rôp hyltyd mar: 'O, myn jonge! O, myn jonge!' Ha mem en dy dat net heard?\"\n\"Né\", sei mem.\nIk sei: \"Nou, ik wol. Gryt Zuidema en ik ha der beide nei stien to harkjen.\"\nDe oare deis om in ûre of fiif yn 'e middei rôp Jap deselde wurden. Doe wie de jonge fordronken yn in sleat fuort by har.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":35073,"r":"BOEKV192","p":"Hoog Soeren","v":"Gld.","y":1892,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"When the child is born, the mother asks what time it is. \"Two o'clock,\" says the child. The midwife cannot believe it and asks again. Then the child says that the year will be good and fruitful, but will be followed by a year of blood. After this prediction, which came true, the child dies.","i":"G.J.B.","o":"Van een sprekend kind.\n\nEene vrouw was in gezegende omstandigheden en zag hare bevalling te gemoet. Het \"wief\" (1) was present en hare hulp was weldra noodig.\nToen het kindje geboren en opgebakerd was, en de kraamvrouw verzorgd, vroeg deze: \"Hoe laat is het?\" \"Twee uur,\" antwoordde het kindje. Het \"wief\" kon hare ooren niet gelooven en vroeg dus ook eens: \"Hoe laat is het?\" \"Twee uur,\" zei de pasgeborene heel duidelijk.\nDaarna sprak het kind nog: \"Dit jaar zal een goed en vruchtbaar jaar zijn, maar dan volgt er een jaar des bloeds.\" Na deze voorzegging, die inderdaad is uitgekomen, stierf het.\n\n1. vroedvrouw."},{"n":13061,"r":"CBOEK023","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1892,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman is giving birth. The midwife has washed and swaddled the baby and tended to the mother. The mother asks what time it is. Twice the baby answers that it is two o'clock. Then it makes a prediction about the coming years and dies.","i":"H.B.","o":"Eene vrouw moest bevallen. Het wief (de vroedvrouw) was present. Toen het kindje geboren en opgebakerd was, de kraamvrouw bezorgd, vroeg deze: \"Hoe laat is het?\" \"Twee uur,\" antwoordde het kindje. Het wief kon hare ooren niet gelooven en vraagde ook eens: \"Hoe laat is het?\" \"Twee uur,\" zei de pasgeborene heel duidelijk. Daarop sprak het kind nog: \"Dit jaar zal een goed en vruchtbaar jaar zijn; maar dan volgt er een jaar des bloeds.\" Na deze voorzegging, die goed is uitgekomen, stierf het kindje."},{"n":34695,"r":"CBOEK190","p":"Poeldijk","v":"Z.-H.","y":1894,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Someone born with a caul foresees funerals as well as weddings.","i":"G.P.","o":"Een vertelling van iemand die met de helm geboren is.\n\nEen man, die met de helm geboren is, ziet in den nacht al verscheidene dagen van te voren de begrafenis van een persoon, welke noch fris en gezond daar henen loopt en binnenkort sterven zal. Hij ziet dat alles zoo duidelijk, dat [hij] de genen die bij hem zijn verzoekt om uit den weg te gaan, dat de dragers er voorbij zouden kunnen. Somstijds vraagt hij noch of zij ook niets van dat alles zien. Zoo is het ook met een bruiloft. Deze ziet hij ook een geheelen tijd vooruit. Van zoo iemand zegt men, dat zijn nageboorte gestolen is."},{"n":69794,"r":"DYKFRIES2190","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Discussion of second sight. People who know when someone will die, often through a kind of prediction. One example is seeing an event that is yet to take place. People born with a caul have a particular gift for this. They can, for instance, see a funeral procession at night. People born without a caul cannot see this procession, but can still be troubled by it.","i":null,"o":"Eene afzonderlijke soort spokerij is bet voorspook. Tusschen de jaren 1840-1860 woonde in Leeuwarden, nabij het Vliet, eene schoenmakersvrouw, die, langs de huizen gaande, kon ruiken waar binnen kort een doode zou zijn. Het voorspook bestaat evenwel meest in nachtgezichten, die een voorspellend karakter hebben en zeer zeker moeten nakomen. Ook gebeurt het, dat men iets komt te hooren zonder te zien. Dit is het wat men in 't Hollandsch wel voorgespens en in 't Friesch foartsjirmerij noemt. Menschen, die met een helm geboren zijn, krijgen voorspellende nachtgezichten; voorgespens kan worden gehoord door ieder, die in het huis of nabij de plaats is, waar het gebeurt.\nDe helm is een vlies dat een pasgeboren kind als een koolsblad over het aangezicht ligt. Wordt dit vlies er afgetrokken van boven naar beneden, dan ziet de persoon in het vervolg altijd naar boven en zal voorteekens in de lucht kunnen zien. Neemt men den helm af van beneden naar boven, dan zal de persoon, als hij tot zijn verstand is gekomen, zijne aandacht meest aan aardsche dingen wijden en verschijningen op den grond zien. - Het wordt gewoonlijk niet als een gewenscht voorrecht beschouwd, voorspellende nachtgezichten te kunnen zien. Daarom zijn ouders en nabestaanden er op uit, bij de geboorte van een kind met een helm het vlies onmiddellijk te verbranden, dan heeft het niet de evengemelde uitwerking; wél als het b"},{"n":69797,"r":"DYKFRIES2193","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"In the south of Friesland a funeral procession is called a begangel. Some people can have visions of a benangel. One of these people with second sight once saw the funeral of a farmer in a vision. Against all custom, the hearse was pulled by a white horse. The farmer died and his funeral procession looked exactly as in the seer's vision.","i":"W.D.","o":"Een lijkstoet noemt men in het zuiden van Friesland een begangel. Hierin ligt de beteekenis van begaan, meêgaan, meêdoen om een overledene de laatste eer te bewijzen. In sommige streken wordt het woord alleen gebruikt voor het visioen eener begrafenis. Menschen die zulk een visioen nu en dan te zien krijgen, waren vroeger minder zeldzaam dan thans. Zoo iemand gevoelde zich 's nachts soms door een geheimzinnige macht gedrongen om het bed te verlaten en naar buiten te gaan, enkel om een begangel te zien. Een dergelijke ziener zag eens in den nacht een begrafenistrein het erf van eenen hem welbekenden boer afkomen. Het merkwaardige hierbij was, dat de lijkwagen was bespannen met een zwart en met een wit paard. Dit nu was geheel tegen den regel; een wit paard wordt nooit voor een lijkwagen gebruikt. Hierbij kwam dat geen der naaste buren van den boer een wit paard bezat. Hij zelf wel, maar het is een even vaste regel, wanneer in een boerengezin iemand sterft, dan mag het lijk niet door eigen paarden naar het kerkhof worden gereden. De naaste buurman is verplicht een hooiwagen met twee, liefst zwarte paarden en een man te schikken om den doode grafwaarts te rijden. Het nachtgezicht duidde natuurlijk aan, dat er in het gezin van den boer eerlang iemand zoude sterven, maar dat witte paard was iets onverklaarbaars. Na verloop van eenigen tijd stierf de boer. Op den dag der begrafenis k"},{"n":69798,"r":"DYKFRIES2194","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Sape has second sight because he was born with a caul. He sees a man's death and funeral before the man has actually died. Against all custom, a white horse has to be harnessed to the hearse. He tells his vision and everything goes as he saw it.","i":"W.D.","o":"Op eenigen afstand van een dorp in Dantumadeel woonde voor jaren een gezin, bestaande uit man, vrouw en eenige kinderen. Het gebeurde dat de man ernstig ziek werd, en de vrouw hoorde dag aan dag een ekster schateren in de omheining van den tuin. Wat zij ook deed, zij konde dat gehate dier nooit veel langer dan een kwartier uit het geboomte verwijderd houden. Op zekeren morgen komt Sape, de mollenvanger, even bij Uilke in huis geloopen en vindt den man doodziek. Hij kon geen toespraak meer hebben. Sape wenkt bij zijn vertrek de vrouw des huizes om hem te volgen naar het achterhuis. Daar gekomen zei hij : <<Het gaat verkeerd met je man, vrouw! <<Och ja,>> zuchtte zij, <<er is geen hoop meer; er is onophoudelijk een ekster in den tuin.>> - <<Binnen drie dagen is alles afgeloopen,>> zeide Sape; <<ik heb eene openbaring gehad. Ge weet, dat ik met een helm geboren ben.>> - <<O ja!>> snikte de vrouw, <<en die verschijningen komen altijd uit, niet waar? >> - <<Wel zeker,>> zeî Sape, <<altijd; 't is met mij nog nooit gemist. Het was gisteravond even voor tienen toen ik de lijkstaatsie zag. En schrik nu niet, mensch! maar 't ging vreemd. Ik moet eerlijk zeggen, dat ik het zelf niet recht begrijp. Hier in den geheelen omtrek heeft niemand een wit paard, en toch was de lijkwagen bespannen met een wit en een zwart paard. De witte was dartel en de knecht van uwen buurman kon het gespan niet"},{"n":69804,"r":"DYKFRIES2200","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul sometimes also see at night a house, a mill or another building on fire. If they then have the chance to touch the walls of such a building and find them cold, it will not burn down, but a new building will replace the old one without a fire. If, on the contrary, the walls are warm, it must burn down. This will happen within a short time if the foreshadowing apparition is seen before midnight. If it is seen after midnight, it takes a long time, sometimes years, before the fire comes. This also applies to other night visions. When the begangel (funeral apparition) stands on the graves and no person sees it, the horses that pass the churchyard still see it. They then become skittish, make wild leaps and can easily bolt if the driver is not on his guard.","i":"W.D."},{"n":8599,"r":"CBAK0001","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1898,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman who can work magic and predict the future is said to have been born with a caul, which her parents did not burn but sold to sailors. Only when the ship carrying the caul is wrecked is the woman freed of her gifts. She predicts that the doctor will not earn much from her, and dies a few months later.","i":"C.B.","o":"In 't begin van mijn verblijf te Broek leefde er een oude vrouw, op Zuiderwoude geboren. Die kon kollen en de toekomst voorspellen. Volgens het verhaal was zij met een helm geboren. De ouders hadden de helm niet verbrand (wat een noodzaak is), maar verkocht aan zeelui die hem mee op een schip hadden genomen. Nu werd zij niet van die rare dingen verlost, voor het schip waarop de helm vergaan was. Eens heeft ze gezegd tegen mij: \"Je zult aan mij niet veel verdienen.\"\nEen half jaar later werd ze dood aan den weg gevonden (overtuigend bewijs van den voorspellenden geest). Haar naam was G. Holleman (zie later)."},{"n":8606,"r":"CBAK0008","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1898,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Woman announces death: when someone is going to die, she goes to the place where that person lives.","i":"C.B.","o":"De bewuste Grietje Holleman kondigde altijd een dood aan. Als zij zich in een buurt veel bewoog, volgde er gauw een doode. Zij begaf zich tegen het sterven van iemand naar de plaats waar hij woonde, ofschoon ze er anders nooit kwam."},{"n":8610,"r":"CBAK0012","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1899,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Clairvoyant woman tells another woman she will die. When someone else dies two days later, the woman thinks the clairvoyant was mistaken. Three days later she dies after all.","i":"C.B.","o":"Aaltje Jonker stond aan de deur.\nGrietje Holleman kwam voorbij en zei: \"Jij zult niet lang meer leven.\"\nTwee dagen later stierf een dochter van oude Daatje.\nGelukkig, dacht Aaltje, dus heeft Griet zich vergist. Drie dagen later kreeg ze evenwel een beroerte en stierf."},{"n":8615,"r":"CBAK0017","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1899,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Announcement that a woman will die in three days comes true.","i":"C.B.","o":"Trijntje Kubbe kon ook kollen. Een vrouw bracht met haar zuster een tobbe naar Monnikendam. Men ging langs Trijntje.\nDeze zei als terloops tot haar: \"Over drie dagen zult ge sterven. Het is den laatsten keer dat je een tobbe naar Monnikendam brengt.\"\nWerkelijk was ze drie dagen later een lijk.\nMijn zegsman was blij dat G. Holleman, P. Huisman en T. Kubbe en al die oude testen dood waren. Ik kreeg de indruk dat test oud akelig wijf beteekende."},{"n":8636,"r":"CBAK0039","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1899,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Woman keeps looking at the ground and upwards at a house. The next day the painter working there falls off the ladder.","i":"C.B.","o":"G. Holleman liep langs een huis en keek telkens naar de goot en naar boven. Den volgenden dag viel de schilder die te werk was van de leer af."},{"n":8638,"r":"CBAK0041","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1899,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Prediction that a child will not live long. The child indeed dies at the age of six.","i":"C.B.","o":"Grietje Holleman heeft tegen een broertje van een Broeker dame gezegd dat hij niet oud zou worden. Op zes-jarige leeftijd is hij overleden."},{"n":8747,"r":"CBAK0144","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1899,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Boy born with a caul does not dare pass the house of someone who is going to die and starts crying when he is at the house. Once the person has died, he dares to pass it again.","i":"C.B.","o":"Aan de Zaan was een jongen met een helm geboren. Als ergens een persoon zou sterven, durfde hij al dagen te voren diens huis niet voorbij. Hij liep er aan toe, barstte dan uit in huilen omdat hij een lijk zag. Als de persoon dood was, ging hij het huis weer voorbij."},{"n":8812,"r":"CBAK0196","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"In the evening a woman known as a witch walks past or stands still in front of people's houses shortly before they die. The lantern she carries goes out when someone approaches.","i":"C.B.","o":"Grietje Holleman (zie vroeger) liep 's avonds voorbij het huis van, of bleef staan tegen het huis van Hannes Marees, Kees Posch en dominee Korteweg, kort voor daar huisgenoten gestorven zijn. Ze had dan een lantaarn bij zich, die uitging als iemand naderde."},{"n":8833,"r":"CBAK0204","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Maid who knows what is being eaten while she is not present is dismissed when it turns out she knows even when all traces of the meal have been removed.","i":"C.B.","o":"Grietje Holleman diende als jong meisje aan de Lagendijk bij Monnikendam.\nAls het haar uitdag geweest was, zei ze altijd 's avonds als ze thuis kwam tot den boer en boerin: \"Wat ben jelui vandaag raar aan het kokkeren geweest.\"\n\"Hoe dat zoo?\"\n\"Wel, jelui hebt dat gegeten, het zoo klaar gemaakt (enzovoort).\"\n\"Hoe weet jij dat? Jij zat toch in Broek?\"\nEens besloten ze eens een proef te nemen. Ze maakten wat klaar: iets heel vreemds, waschten alles af enzovoort, enzovoort, zoodat niemand 't in de verste verte kon vermoeden wat ze gegeten hadden.\nToch zei Griet weer: \"Wat ben jelui raar aan het kokkeren geweest.\"\n\"Wat hebben we dan gegeten?\"\nEn Griet zei het weer precies.\n\"Maar dan ben jij een kol,\" zei de boer, en ze is op staande voet moeten vertrekken."},{"n":9054,"r":"CBAK0280","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Fortune-teller who says where stolen goods are and that something is wrong at home gets angry when someone doubts it. She mentions a number of past events that are true, and predicts that the man will die before sixty, which happens.","i":"C.B.","o":"In de Purmer was gestolen. De vader van de heer D. Schuurman ging met iemand naar een waarzegster in Amsterdam. Deze vertelde dat het gestolene in de pottenkast lag, maar tevens dat ze wel gauw mochten zoeken dat ze thuis waren, want dat het niet goed bij hun thuis was. Schuurman lachte.\nToen werd de waarzegster kwaad en zei: \"Jij gelooft me niet? Dan zal ik je ers wat zeggen. Jij hebt een klein vrouwtje, jij wilde onlangs een wit paard koopen, maar je vrouw had liever een zwart. Toen heb jij erg opespeuld. Jij zult 59 jaar worden, maar de zestig haal je niet.\"\nAlles was waar, en zijn vader is op 59-jarige leeftijd gestorven."},{"n":9091,"r":"CBAK0308","p":"Uitdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Man born with a caul can predict events, which does not make him happy. For instance, before the botters (fishing boats) at sea notice anything, he can predict that high water is coming, and also death.","i":"C.B.","o":"Jan Bakker op Durgerdam was met een helm geboren. De boeren hebben daar evenals te Uitdam land buiten de zeedijk liggen. Daarop grazen geen koeien, maar het wordt gemaaid. Nu kunnen ze daarmee zeer gelukkig of ongelukkig zijn, want als het in den tijd dat het gras ligt te drogen, begint te stormen en het wordt hoog water, dan spoelt alles weg. Hij wist dat altijd te voorspellen.\nAls de botters in zee nog niets bespeurden, zei hij: \"Mannen, haal jelui gras binnen, want we krijgen hoog water.\"\nOok kon hij natuurlijk de dood voorspellen enzovoort. Hij vond het hoogst onaangenaam, en heeft vaak verklaard, dat hij wel heel wat zou willen geven als hij er af was. De man zag er slecht uit en was zoo mager als een lat."},{"n":13360,"r":"SAMSTE20","p":"Uitdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Man born with a caul can predict events, which does not make him happy. For instance, before the botters (fishing boats) at sea notice anything, he can predict that high water is coming, and also death. Once he warns his farmhand in vain to step aside. The farmhand is then pushed aside by a funeral procession.","i":"C.B.","o":"MET DE HELM GEBOREN\nJan Bakker, die in Durgerdam woonde, was met de helm geboren. De boeren uit dat dorp hadden indertijd land buiten de zeedijk liggen, waar geen koeien op graasden maar waar wel gras groeide, dat men maaide om hooi te hebben voor het vee. Het gras lag daar om te drogen en dan kon het gebeuren dat het begon te stormen op de Zuiderzee en dat het water steeg, zodat het gras wegspoelde. Bakker wist altijd vooruit wanneer het zou gaan stormen en als de botters op zee nog niets merkten zei hij al: \"Mannen, haal jullie gras binnen, want we krijgen hoog water\". Natuurlijk kon hij ook voorspellen wanneer er iemand in de buurt zou sterven. Hij vond dat heel erg en verklaarde vaak dat hij ik weet niet wat er voor zou geven als de gave van voorspelling van hem zou worden afgenomen. Hij tobde erover, dat kon je merken, want hij zag er altijd slecht uit en hij was zo mager als een kat.\n\"Zo het de ouwe me dikwijls verteld dat er op Durgerdam 'en boer was die met de helm was geboren. Die boer kwam op 'en goeie morgen met de knecht oit 'et land. De knecht jukte een gang melk. \"Gaan op zaai, maat\", zaai de boer. De knecht keek vreemd op want de weg was breed en er kwam niks an. \"Gaan op zaai, maat\", zaai-ie nog eris, maar de knecht liep deur. Op iens wordt ie me deer met emmers en al op de grond 'egooid. \"Wat is dat nou? \", kermt ie. \"Ja, ik hew 'et je wel 'ezaaid\", zaai de boe"},{"n":9137,"r":"CBAK0348","p":"Ransdorp","v":"N.-H.","y":1902,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Woman says an especially warm goodbye to a man because she has foreseen that he will die the next day. The next day the man drowns while skating.","i":"C.B.","o":"Eens nam G. Holleman, terwijl ze nog diende, bizonder hartelijk afscheid van een vertrekkenden persoon.\nDe baas was daarover verwonderd en zei: \"Je doet alsof je hem nooit terug zult zien.\"\n\"Daar heb je gelijk in,\" zei Griet, \"want morgen is hij dood.\"\nWerkelijk is die man denzelfden dag bij het schaatsenrijden verdronken."},{"n":9167,"r":"CBAK0356","p":"Uitdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1903,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Men lodging with a woman who can tell fortunes grumble among themselves about the food. The woman says they should say it to her face. She says that a man who was to come that evening will come the next day, because he is busy on behalf of a rosy-cheeked woman. The man turns out to have fetched the doctor the evening before for a rosy-cheeked woman. The narrator refused to learn it, because a book of magic can only be passed on to someone with a feeling for it.","i":"C.B.","o":"Mijn roeier gelooft niet aan waarzeggen, maar hij is er bang voor. Hij heb zelf beleefd dat ie op Nieuwendam werkte, en dat ze bij een vrouw thuislage, die dat kon.\nOmdat ze iederen dag aardappele met kool gestampt krege, mopperde ze onder mekander.\n\"Hooris manne,\" zei de vrouw, \"as jullie wat te zegge hebbe, moet jelui het teuge main zegge, maar niet onder mekaar moppere.\"\nNou zou Klaas Ploeger ook die dag ekomme hebbe, maar die kwam niet.\n\"Wil ik zegge waarom die niet komt?\" zei ze.\n\"Jawel,\" zeide ze.\nNou, toe nam ze de kaarte en zei: \"Morge vroeg komt ie, en nou is ie bezig om een blozend vrouwspersoon.\"\nDe volgende ochtend kwam Klaas. Hij had om de dokter na Broek emoete, omdat de vrouw van Lubbert de Jong in arbeid was de vorige avond. Zooas uwe wel weet, is vrouw De Jong nogal blozend en het is gebeurd toe ze die jonge ekrege heb.\nZe wou het ons leeren, ze had er een boekie voor. Maar ik bedankte, want ze wille wel zegge, dat je van die boekies niet of ken kome, al wil je ze verbrande, of al gooi je ze weg, en dat je ze alleen kwijt ken rake as je iemand tref, die er zenieigheid in heb.\n(Uitdam)","l":"Waterlands"},{"n":9186,"r":"CBAK0372","p":"Uitdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1903,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Woman starts crying in advance when someone is going to die. Asked to visit a gravely ill woman, she answers that she will come when the patient has recovered. The patient does indeed recover.","i":"C.B.","o":"De moeder van Sijmen Buis te Uitdam heeft elf kinderen gehad. Tien ervan heeft zij overleefd. Telkens als er een zou sterven, deed zij niets dan huilen. Als zij bij een zieke kwam en zij begon te huilen, volgde de dood zeker. Toen de moeder van mijn Uitdammer doodziek was en ze reeds het doodskleed klaargelegd hadden, liep hij even naar buurvrouw om te vragen of zij ers wou komen kijken.\n\"Och,\" zei ze, \"ik zal wel ers komen als je moeder beter is.\"\nWerkelijk is ze hersteld.\n(Het nageslacht van Sijmen Buis ken ik. Dat telt vele zenuwlijders waaronder idioten, krankzinnigen en zelfmoordenaars)."},{"n":9266,"r":"CBAK0410","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1903,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Man born with a caul foresees his brother's death. After a visit he says goodbye so warmly, even kissing his brother, that others are surprised. Shortly afterwards a beam crushes the brother's head.","i":"C.B.","o":"Lauwrens Honingh (broeder van vrouw Houtman) was met een helm geboren. Daardoor kon hij altijd vooruit weten of iemand dood zou gaan. Eens was hij bij zijn broeder te Zuiderwoude te gast. Hijzelf woonde te Ransdorp. Bij het afscheid nemen, was hij buitengewoon hartelijk, zóó zelfs dat hij zijn broer een zoen gaf, waarover de omstanders zich verbaasden en waarvoor ze den neus optrokken. Een dag of twee, drie later brak een bint van den hooizolder en werd de broer zijn hoofd nagenoeg verpletterd.\n(Zuiderwoude)"},{"n":9267,"r":"CBAK0411","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1903,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman regarded as a witch walks back and forth over the bridge under which a man who set sail despite a storm has passed. The boat capsizes and the man drowns.","i":"C.B.","o":"Manus Duif ging er's met een zeilschuitje bij een hevigen storm van Broek naar Zuiderwoude. Grietje Holleman liep almaar over den Langenbrug, waar hij onderdoor was gegaan, heen en weer. Op 't Boozemeer gekomen, sloeg de schuit om en is Manus verdronken.\n(Zuiderwoude)"},{"n":9316,"r":"CBAK0459","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1911,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"In an inn, a woman known as a kol (witch) tells a man that he will not be coming any more next week. The man does indeed die that week.","i":"C.B.","o":"Grietje Holleman (zie vroeger) was eens op een dinsdag (marktdag) in den herberg van C. Kelderman, die familie van haar was. Daar kwamen veel boeren iets verteren.\nTegen een daarvan zei ze: \"Jij zelt hier de volgende week niet meer komme.\"\nInderdaad was hij de volgende week reeds overleden. Ze mocht nooit meer bij haar familie te Purmerend komen."},{"n":9317,"r":"CBAK0460","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1911,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"In the night before a woman drowns herself, a woman known as a kol (witch) circles in front of her house.","i":"C.B.","o":"In de nacht dat de vrouw van Van der Helm, een timmermansknecht, zich verdronken heeft met haar kindje op den rug, liep G. Holleman aldoor voor het huis te draaien."},{"n":41749,"r":"COHEN009","p":"Zutphen","v":"Gld.","y":1918,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman dreams of her own death: she sees herself lying in a coffin that is then screwed shut by a man in a red undershirt. Then someone else lays a white cloth on her coffin. Everyone, even her husband, dismisses her dream as nonsense. A year after a carpenter with a red undershirt comes to live in the village, the woman dies. The coffin cannot go into another room, screws from the windowsill are used after all, and a white cloth is put over the coffin after all.","i":"L.d.B.","o":"De Roode Hemdrok\n\nDe vrouw van den predikant in Pietersbierum lag ziek te bed, en ze kon\nniet slapen. Ze woelde heen en weer, en ze bad om slaap, die haar kon\ndoen vergeten. Wat wilde ze anders dan vergeten, buiten deze wereld\nvan pijn en zorg zijn, al ware het slechts enkele uren? Haar oogen\nwaren wijd-geopend, en ziet! daar spalkte de nacht uiteen.\n\nMidden in de kamer stond een doodkist.\n\nZe stond op, om te weten, wie gestorven was en ze naderde de kist. Wie\nlag erin? Zijzelve.\n\n\"Moet ik sterven?\" dacht ze, en ze wekte haar man.\n\n\"Kijk de kist in de kamer,\" zei ze. De man richtte zich iets op,\nen staarde den nacht in, welke voor hem niets was dan het duisterste\nduister.\n\n\"Wat moet ik zien?\" vroeg hij verwonderd. Ze antwoordde, in 't midden\nder kamer staande:\n\n\"Deze baar, waarin ik als lijk lig.\" Hij werd kwaad, en zei korzelig:\n\n\"Je verbeeldt je mooie dingen! Schaam je, en ga slapen.\"\n\nLangzaam liep ze naar haar bed terug, doch ze wendde zich, zoodra ze\nweer lag, met het gezicht naar de kist, welke bleef staan. Ze dacht:\n\n\"Dus moet ik sterven.\"\n\nEn ze sliep niet. Korten tijd daarna kwam een man binnen. Hij was\ngekleed in een rooden hemdrok. Hij bleef even zwijgend staan, en\nschreed toen rustig naar den schoorsteenmantel. Hij boog zich iets\nvoorover, en ze bemerkte, dat hij iets van den schoorsteenmantel nam,\neen paar dingen van ijzer. Ze richtte zich iets op, om beter te kunn"},{"n":41759,"r":"COHEN018","p":"Zutphen","v":"Gld.","y":1918,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The Black Death brings death and destruction, also in the village of Ruurloo. There it poisons all the wells except the castle's. Instead of Death, the Jews are blamed. All the Jews flee the village except old Abraham and his beautiful daughter Mirjam. They are taken in at the castle of a young knight. One day his mother compels the knight to kill Mirjam and her father. Mirjam hears this and says that if her father is killed, the knight's days are numbered. His bride-to-be, the rich and beautiful lady Machteld, also orders him to kill Mirjam and her father. The knight agrees, but Mirjam has vanished without a trace and only the old man is killed. On the wedding day a fortune-teller is let into the castle. The fortune-teller predicts that the lady will become a widow, then reveals her face. The fortune-teller turns out to be Mirjam, who kisses her knight one last time: the kiss of death.","i":"L.d.B.","o":"Mirjam, sage uit den Achterhoek\n\nHet was in den jare veertien honderd negen en dertig, dat er Groote\nSterfte over de menschheid kwam, en de taak van den Dood niet wilde\neindigen. Zwart waren Zijn knokels. Op een zwart paard reed Hij,\nzwart waren de toomen, zwart het zadel, zwart 't ijzer van de zeis,\nwaarmede Hij sloeg. Men noemde Hem den Zwarten Dood.\n\nWaar was Hij niet geweest?\n\nUit het Oosten was Hij gekomen, over de Hongaarsche landen tot Weenen,\nwaar Hij langen tijd had vertoefd. Verder was Hij gegaan, als een\nonverwinbaar held. Weeklachten waren er aan alle kanten. Hij reed\nstapvoets langs de wereld, maaiende, alwaar het leven had gezaaid. Lees de oude kronieken over Hem. Bij honderdtallen verzamelden zich de\nmenschen, mannen en vrouwen, om Hem te vermurwen: gezamenlijk vereenden ze zich ten gebed, ze geeselden zich en elkander. Doch de Zwarte Dood zag en hoorde niet naar hen, want Hij was gekomen, om te verderven, en het Noodlot bestuurde Zijn onstuitbaren tocht.\n\nOok in het dorpje Ruurloo was Hij binnengereden, en sinds dien week Hij\nniet meer. Eenige dagen voor zijn komst hadden pelgrims uit het Heilige\nLand bij de bron overnacht, ze waren bij het eerste zonnelicht weder\nverdwenen. De meisjes uit 't gehucht waren den uchtend naar de bron\ngetrokken, en hadden de kruiken vol met water geschept, gelijk 't hare\ngewoonte was. En daarna werd ieder, die van het water had gedr"},{"n":42083,"r":"JCOHEN32","p":"Zutphen","v":"Gld.","y":1919,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"In Opende there once lived a man who was born with a caul. When he stood behind the counter in his inn, he often ran his hand over his head because his thoughts burned fiercely. He thought nothing of it. One day his mother saw him stroking his head and asked what was wrong. He said he was just thinking. She asked whether he saw anything while thinking, but he denied it. One night the innkeeper looks outside. In the distance he sees a hearse approaching the village. He thinks to himself: \"the dead are not buried at night\". He asks his mother who has died. She answers that no one has died. Then he tells her what he has seen. When she comes to look, they see nothing. The man does not understand, but the mother understands that her son has had a vision. When he tells others the next day, nobody believes him and they mock him. But not long after, a contagious disease breaks out in the village. Many people die and the hearse comes and goes constantly. After a while the man realizes he has had a premonition. He tells the village and asks them to prevent his whole prediction, about the burial at night, from coming true. But fate cannot be turned, and in the end people are buried at night as well.","i":"L.d.B.","o":"De begrafenis in den nacht.\n\nEr moet in Opende een herbergier hebben gewoond,\ndie de gave van den voorloop bezat. Maar hij wist dit\nniet, want geen mensch had hem ooit verteld, dat hij met den\nhelm was geboren. Ja, niemand scheen het te weten: de moeder,\nde tantes, de baker, die in zulke gevallen de wonderlijke tijding wel\nver in de rondte zaaien, zwegen.\nDit is niet goed, neen, dit is niet goed. De kinderen, die met den helm\ngeboren zijn, moeten — als de helm niet is verbrand — tijdig begrijpen,\nhoeveel smart zij zullen lijden. Voor hen vloeit toekomst en verleden te \nzaam. het wonderlijke was, dat de herbergier noch zijn omgeving ooit\niets van den voorloop hadden gemerkt. \nAls knaap onderscheidde hij zich in niets van zijn vrienden. \nAls jongeling vrijde en won hij een jong meisje. Als man\nzette hij zijn zaak op, en achter de toonbank bepraatte hij de dingen van\nden da met zijn klanten. over veilingen in de omtrek, over sterfgevallen, \nen huwelijken, en den stand van het graan. \nHet leek, of hij sterven zou, zooals hij geleefd had: zonder dat iemand\nter wereld bevroedde, welk een man hij was.\nDat hij meermalen, als er weinig menschen in de jachtweide zaten, droomerig \nachter de toonbank stond, en soms met zijn hand langs zijn voorhoofd streek, \nzooals zij doen, bij wie de gedachten fel in het brein branden, vond hij\nniets bijzonders. dat zijn moeder, die bij het haardvuur in"},{"n":42082,"r":"JCOHEN33","p":"Zutphen","v":"Gld.","y":1919,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"One night a skipper from IJmuiden dreams of his mother. She comes to visit him and gives him her beloved Bible. Then she disappears. When he arrives back in IJmuiden he is told that his mother has died. He tells of his dream. It turns out his mother died that very night. She had asked that the little Bible be given to him.","i":"L.d.B.","o":"De vreemde droom.\n\nOp een nacht droomde een IJmuidensch reeder, die\nmet zijn schip ter vischvangst was, al heel wonderlijk.\nHij zag zichzelven liggen, roerloos, in de kajuit, waar hij\nwerkelijkheid lag. En terwijl hij zijn eigen\ngelaat, den onduidelijken vorm van zijn lichaam, dat onder\nde dekens lag, bemerkte, onderscheidde hij tegelijkertijd\nde dingen om zich heen.\nHij wendde het gelaat niet. Hij keek geen oogenblik\nin de richting der deur. toch wist hij, dat er iemand binnentrad,\ndie hij goed kende. Wie was het? zijn moeder.\nZij naderde zacht zijn kooi. \"Wat komt ze bij me doen?\"\ndacht hij. \"Neen, een droom is 't niet.\"\nAls een figuur der werkelijkheid, zóó zeker, ging ze.\nZe droeg iets in de hand. Plotseling werd hij ontroerd,\ntoen hij bemerkte, wat het was. Het bijbeltje, dat ze zoo\nlief had.\nZe lichtte het hoofdkussen op en vroom legde ze het\nbijbeltje neder. Daarna verdween ze.\nEenige dagen later kwam hij in IJmuiden aan. Zijn\nkennissen groeten hem schuw. Hij peinsde.\n\"Er zal toch niets gebeurd zijn?\"\nDe gordijnen voor zijn huis waren neer. Zijn vader trad\nhem tegemoet. Hij droeg iets in de hand. Hij noemde den\nnacht, dat de reeder zoo vreemd had gedroomd.\n\"Toen is je moeder gestorven!\" zei hij. De zoon keek\nnaar zijn vader's hand.\n\"Hier, mijn jongen, is het bijbeltje......je moeder heeft\ngezegd, dat ik het je dadelijk zou geven!\""},{"n":9421,"r":"CBAK0560","p":"Beets","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"At the fair a fortune teller predicts to a girl that she will marry a man from Gelderland and be happy with him. That same evening a man from Gelderland asks her to dance, and they spend the rest of the evening together. They keep seeing each other, marry in time and are happy together.","i":"C.B.","o":"Eenige meisjes gingen op de kermis naar een waarzegster. Een van haar werd door die vrouw apart geroepen en toen voorspelde zij haar, dat ze met een Gelderschen heer zou trouwen, dat ze veel van hem zou houden en zeer gelukkig met hem zou zijn. Nog denzelfden avond vroeg een onbekende heer haar ten dans; hij viel in haar smaak en zij in de zijne, en daarom gingen ze voor het verdere gedeelte van den avond met elkaar uit. Dit had ten gevolge dat zij na afloop van de kermis de kennismaking voortzetten en na eenigen tijd met elkaar trouwden. Die heer kwam uit Gelderland; het meisje hield veel van hem en ze zijn zeer gelukkig met elkaar geweest.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.113.)"},{"n":9423,"r":"CBAK0562","p":"Uitdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul can predict the weather.","i":"C.B.","o":"Een Durgerdammer, N.N., die met een helm geboren was, kon het weer voorspellen. Als de botters van Marken nog rustig in zee lagen te visschen en niemand er aan dacht dat er slecht weer in aantocht was, ried hij den boeren, die het gras van de zeedijken gepacht hadden en dit buitendijks lieten drogen, aan, om het zoo spoedig mogelijk naar huis te halen. Nog dien zelfden dag kwam er dan regen en harden wind of storm.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.267.)"},{"n":9425,"r":"CBAK0564","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"After a visit, a man born with a caul takes leave of his brother in an unusual way. The next day the brother is killed by a falling beam.","i":"C.B.","o":"N.N. kwam met zijn vrouw en zijn broer en diens vrouw bij familie te Zuiderwoude te gast. Toen het tijd was om naar huis te gaan, nam hij hartelijk afscheid van zijn broer, zóó hartelijk zelfs, dat hij hem een zoen gaf, wat in deze streken geen gewoonte is en waar men dus hartelijk om lachte. Den volgenden dag werd de broer doodelijk getroffen door een balk, die van den hooizolder boven op hem viel.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.268)"},{"n":9426,"r":"CBAK0565","p":"Uitdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A mother starts crying days in advance when one of her children is going to die. Later she becomes short of breath and goes about crying when someone in the neighbourhood is going to die. People who cannot learn enough from the doctor about a sick person's condition go to her. If she is cheerful, the sick person recovers; if she is short of breath, the sick person will die.","i":"C.B.","o":"De moeder van N.N. heeft al haar elf kinderen overleefd. Telkens als er een stierf, liep zij dagen van te voren te huilen. In later jaren kreeg zij het ook benauwd en liep dan te huilen, als er iemand in den buurt spoedig zou sterven. Slimmerikken gingen bij haar op bezoek als de dokter niet voldoende uitsluitsel gaf over een zieke. Stond haar gezicht vrolijk, dan wisten zij dat de patiënt herstellen zou, maar was zij benauwd en zat zij te huilen, dan kon men zijn doodshemd gerust klaar leggen.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.268.)"},{"n":9427,"r":"CBAK0566","p":"Wormer","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A boy walks to the house of a sick person, where he bursts into tears and keeps crying until the sick person has died.","i":"C.B.","o":"N.N., een jongen aan de Zaan, liep als iemand in zijn buurt zwaar ziek was, telkens naar diens woning toe en barstte daar in huilen uit. Dat duurde net zoo lang tot de patiënt overleden was. Dan eerst kwam hij tot bedaren."},{"n":9442,"r":"CBAK0581","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Doctor Bakker remarks to a woman who is seen as a witch that she stays so healthy. The witch says the doctor will not earn anything from her. Shortly afterwards she is found dead by the roadside.","i":"C.B.","o":"G.H. Over deze kol moet ik wat uitvoeriger zijn. Ik heb haar in de eerste jaren van mijn verblijf te Broek vaak ontmoet en meermalen gesproken, maar nooit onder behandeling gehad. Eens zei ze heel demonstratief tegen mij: \"Jij zult ook niet veel aan mij verdienen\", nadat ik haar schertsend geplaagd had, dat zij altijd maar gezond was. Ik nam van dat gezegde geen notie, maar enkele weken later werd zij dood aan den Monnikendammer jaagweg gevonden.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.272.)"},{"n":9443,"r":"CBAK0582","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A maidservant knows what was eaten on her day off, even though care was taken that no leftovers remained.","i":"C.B.","o":"Volgens de over haar in omloop zijnde verhalen, was zij reeds als jong meisje zoo bizonder. Als zij, als dienstbode, haar uitgaansdag had, wist zij altijd den volgenden dag te vertellen, wat haar meesteres op dien dag gegeten had. Men kocht dan wel eens iets bizonders en zorgde, dat er geen restjes van overbleven, maar toch wist Griet het.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.272.)"},{"n":9444,"r":"CBAK0583","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman predicts that her child will not live long. The child does indeed die at the age of two.","i":"C.B.","o":"Een Broeker dame voorspelde zij eens, dat haar kind, dat er gezond uit zag, niet oud zou worden. Het stierf toen het twee jaar oud was.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.272)"},{"n":9445,"r":"CBAK0584","p":"Ransdorp","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman says goodbye to a man so warmly that someone else says it seems as if she will never see him again. The next day the man drowns while skating.","i":"C.B.","o":"In Purmerend nam ze van een persoon hartelijk afscheid, zoodat iemand de opmerking maakte: \"'t Is of je hem nooit meer zult zien.\" Den zelfden dag is hij bij 't schaatsenrijden verdronken.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.272.)"},{"n":9446,"r":"CBAK0585","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"When a death is coming, a woman becomes short of breath, goes outside and turns back and forth at the house where the death will occur.","i":"C.B.","o":"Als er een sterfgeval op komst was, kreeg zij het benauwd, vluchtte het huis uit en liep telkens voor het aanstaande sterfhuis heen en weer te draaien.\n(Om misverstand te voorkomen, stip ik even aan, dat haar prognose lang niet altijd met de mijne overeenstemde en dat zij niet altijd gelijk had.)\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.272-273)"},{"n":9447,"r":"CBAK0586","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Before a painter's assistant falls from a ladder and dies, a woman keeps looking upwards.","i":"C.B.","o":"Eens was een schildersknecht aan een dakgoot te verwen. Zij keek al maar naar boven. Een poos later viel de man van den ladder en was morsdood.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.273.)"},{"n":9448,"r":"CBAK0587","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"During a heavy storm a woman watches a barge go, which later capsizes, and the man on board drowns.","i":"C.B.","o":"Een anderen keer bleef zij, toen het hard stormde, iemand nakijken, die met een schuitje naar Zuiderwoude zeilde. De man is met zijn schuit omgeslagen en verdronken.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.273.)"},{"n":9449,"r":"CBAK0588","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman walks back and forth in front of the house of a woman who has just given birth, before the new mother drowns herself and her child.","i":"C.B.","o":"Voor het huis van een kraamvrouw liep ze ook eens al maar op en neer te wandelen. Dien zelfden dag heeft die vrouw zich met haar kind in den arm verdronken.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.273)"},{"n":9455,"r":"CBAK0594","p":"Ransdorp","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man of nearly eighty is afraid he will die soon, because a fortune teller once predicted he would live to be eighty.","i":"C.B.","o":"Voor een jaar of wat werd ik bij een ouden man van 79 jaar en 11 maanden gehaald. Hoewel hij lichamelijk gezond was, riep men mijn hulp in, omdat hij zoo gedeprimeerd was, niet at, slecht sliep enzovoort. Bij navraag bleek dat hij in zijn jongelingsjaren bij een waarzegster was geweest, die hem voorspeld had, dat hij 80 jaar zou worden. Dat had hij heel genoegelijk gevonden, maar nu de termijn bijna verstreken was, gevoelde hij zich zeer onbehagelijk. Alle redeneeringen er tegen hielpen geen steek. Eerst toen de fatale datum voorbij was en hij niet gestorven was, knapte hij langzamerhand op en heeft nog enkele jaren geleefd.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.278.)"},{"n":12403,"r":"CBAK0603","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A baker's assistant who thinks nobody is home moves on, but is called back by the woman. He jokingly says he did not see her head, which frightens her. She believes that when a kol (a person with second sight) sees someone without a head, that person will soon die. The woman tells everyone what happened to her and that the man is a kol. The priest has great difficulty convincing everyone that it is a misunderstanding.","i":"C.B.","o":"Een inwoner van Broek in Waterland diende voor meer dan dertig jaar op Edam. Voor zijn patroon, een bakker, moest hij dagelijks het brood uitventen te Volendam. Eens had hij zich verlaat, zoodat het al donker was, toen hij daar aankwam. Hij haalde ergens een deur open, doch trok die weer dicht, nadat hij zich overtuigd had dat er niemand thuis was. Toen hij verder wilde gaan, werd hij teruggeroepen door de vrouw des huizes, die hem tevens vroeg, waarom hij wilde doorgaan, zonder brood af te geven.\n\"Dat komt,\" antwoordde hij gekscherend, \"omdat ik je hoofd niet zag.\"\nDit antwoord had ernstige gevolgen, want als kollen iemand zonder hoofd zien zitten is dat een teeken, dat die persoon gauw sterven zal. De vrouw schrok dan ook hevig, vertelde ieder wat haar overkomen was en dat de bakkersknecht uit Edam een kol was. De vrouw zond haar man, die op zee was, bericht, dat ze gauw sterven ging en het heele dorp was in rep en roer over die gebeurtenis. De volgende dagen werd de bakker met wantrouwen begroet, ja enkelen namen een beslist vijandige houding tegen hem aan. De toen daar staande R.K. geestelijke heeft groote moeite gehad om de vrouw te overtuigen, dat haar meening op een misverstand berustte en de bevolking te kalmeren en haar de overtuiging bij te brengen, dat de bakkersknecht maar een gewoon mensch was. Hij is toen in zijn dienst kunnen blijven, maar werd nog lang met wantr"},{"n":43062,"r":"KEMP234","p":"Broek","v":"L.","y":1925,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A village constable's chickens are often stolen. A fortune teller sees the culprits in the flames of a very hot fire and can also say where they live. The man hardly dares believe it, but later finds that she is right. His hair has turned grey from fear.","i":"I.S.","o":"Gestolen kippen\n\nHet is verteld geworden in een van de grensdorpen, in de tijd van de grote Europese oorlog, door een veldwachter aan een van de militairen van de grenswacht.\nBij die veldwachter werden al een geruime tijd kippen gestolen. De man kon er niet achter komen, wie dat deed en kon evenmin de minste aanwijzing vinden. Ten einde raad ging hij naar een waarzegster en zette haar zijn geval uiteen. De waarzegster hoorde hem aan en vroeg hem toen of hij niet bang was. Dat was hij niet en ook nooit geweest. Dan zou hij haar maar eens volgen.\nZij ging hem voor en nam hem mee naar een schuur, tot waar deze eindigde in een soort onderaardse ruimte. Daar bracht zij de man bij een vuur, zo hevig als de hel, en daar toonde zij hem in de vlammen de mensen, die hem zijn kippen ontstolen hadden. Hij herkende ze, doch wist ze niet te wonen. De waarzegster wees hem nu aan, waar de kippen woonden. Zij voegde er nog bij, dat in de schuur bij die mens, de kip die zij het laatst bij hem gestolen hadden, nog onder een korf zat.\nDe veldwachter ging naar huis, en overlegde de zaak nog eens bij zichzelf, want na hetgeen hij gezien had, wilde hij toch voorzichtig zijn. Eindelijk besloot hij toch, zijn goed recht te laten gelden en begaf hij zich in de richting van het huis dat de waarzegster hem had aangewezen. Toevallig passeerde daar een jongetje. Hij riep het manneke en vroeg hem of hij niet"},{"n":15735,"r":"CJ002912","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A skipper comes to Jistrum. He tells a grain miller that the church will no longer be standing that evening. That very afternoon the church burns down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der lei in skipper to Skûlenboarch yn it Knjillisdjip. Hy kom to Jistrum by in moalker. Hy sei tsjin dy moalker: \"Dat hûs dêr by de tsjerke, dat stiet der joun net mear.\" Dyselde middeis brânde it op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15737,"r":"CJ002914","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"One evening a girl tells her mother that old Antsje has already been laid out. The next day Antsje is still alive. A few days later, however, she suddenly dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Twizelerheide sei in famke us op in joun tsjin har mem: \"Sy ha âlde Antsje ek al biklaeid.\" Sy hie 't sjoen. Mar de oare moarns leefde Antsje noch. Mar in dei of hwat letter is âlde Antsje samar ûnforwachts forstoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21796,"r":"CJ0287A02","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1951,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A cow is to be put down because it supposedly has lung disease. Hinse the devil-banisher says the cow is not ill but has a piece of leather in its throat. Hinse reaches into the cow's mouth and promptly pulls out an old shoe sole.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie yn 'e tiid fan 'e longsykte ûnder 't fé.\nDer wie in boer, dy hie ek in sike koe. Dy moest ôfmakke wurde. Der stienen twa plysjes by en twa féartsen.\nDoe woarde Hinse der by helle. Dy sei: dy koe hat gjin longsykte. Hy hat in stik lear yn 'e hals.\nDoe strûpte er de mouwe op en gong mei de earm ta de bek fan 'e koe yn. Hy helle der in âld skuonsoale út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21797,"r":"CJ0287A03","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1951,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Three rascals want to fool the devil-banisher Hinse and add their own urine to that of the cattle. Hinse examines the water and predicts that whoever added his urine last will soon die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Trije jonge bazen woenen us in grap útheve mei Hinse Jehannes. Hja nommen wetter mei fan fé. Dêr dienen se wetter fan harsels troch en sa brochten se de flesse by Hinse.\nHinse biseach it wetter en frege doe, of hja ek wisten hwa syn wetter der lêst yn kom wie, hwant dy leefde net lang mear.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21800,"r":"CJ0287A06","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1951,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The devil-banisher Hinse foresees that polecat dogs will steal his turnips.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Hinse Jehannes fan 't Swartfean wie nergens binaud foar. Op in nacht kom er fan Feansterheide thús. Doe sieten der murdejeijers ta syn rapen. Doe't er by har wie, seach er se ûnforskrokken lyk yn 'e egen, dat sy lieten de rapen falle. De hounen wienen binaud.\n\"Dat wist ik justerjoune al,\" sei Hinse, \"dat jim hjir wêze soenen.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21778,"r":"CJ0286B07","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1954,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The devil-banisher Piter Poes foresees when someone is coming to fetch a healing potion.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hwannear 't der ien kom by de duvelbander Piter Poes fan Sumarreheide, sei er: \"Kom, bist dêr al? Ik ha de drank lang al klear hawn.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":14823,"r":"LIJST104","p":"Steggerda","v":"Fr.","y":1954,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"An exorcist takes a feather wreath out of a sick mother's pillow. The boy who goes along with the exorcist finds that he can read minds and see a real event at a great distance.","i":"A.K.","o":"I. De duivel\n5. Zijn U bepaalde personen bekend, die als duivelbanner of duivelbanster worden geraadpleegd? In welke gevallen gebeurt dat?\n\nBijlage\nDe duivelbanner\nEen 70 jaar geleden woonde de duivelbanner, die in Steggerda geroepen werd, in de Knijpe, ten O. van Heerenveen. De Knijpe lag van Steggerda af zo ongeveer 15KM. En alles moest lopende gebeuren. Maar daar zag men in die tijden niet het minst tegen op.\nMeestal werd hij gehaald bij zieken. En veelal vond hij in het kussen, waarop de zieke sliep, een krans van veren. De krans werd er ogenblikkelijk uitgehaald. Of genezing telkens volgde? Ik denk het wel niet. Een buurvrouw - oud is de regel - kreeg gewoonlijk de schuld, dat zij de zieke betoverd had.\nÉén geval, dat nog door de persoon zelf verteld is, diene ter illustratie. \nHij vertelde mij het volgende:\n'k Was een jongen van 17 à 18 jaar, toen mijn vader mij naar de duivelbanner in de Knijpe zond om hulp. 'k Trof het, hij was thuis en hij ging dadelijk met mij mee. 't Was een uur of negen in de avond en pekdonker.\nToen ik bij 't hekje kwam aan de straatweg, dacht ik zo bij mezelf: \"Zol ie oonze mem kunnen genezen?\" En daarop eens hoorde ik een zware stem zeggen: \"Ja wisse kan ik dat.\" Dus hij was ook gedachtenlezer.\nEn toen we op de weg waren van de Knijpe naar Gorredijk er werd weinig gezegd - bleef de man ineens stokstijf staan. \"Hoor\" zei hij. \"Door vaalt een kiend"},{"n":43252,"r":"AMPT000215","p":"Genemuiden","v":"Ov.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A fortune teller's prediction that someone will drown comes true.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"Een veerknecht ging met Pasen uit met z'n vrienden. Ze bezochten een waarzegster. Die zei: \"Morgen gebeurt er een ongeluk, er verdrinkt een man.\"\nDe andere dag verdronk er bij het veer een man!"},{"n":50562,"r":"KOOIJMAN0014","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"At a birth, Miet de Wissel said to pray that the Lord would take the child away, because it would bring little joy. The child did indeed become a nuisance.","i":"H.K.","o":"Toen m'n zuster werd geboren, zei Miet de Wissel: \"Bid Onze Lieve Heer maar, dat hij dat kind weghaalt. Daar zal je weinig plezier van hebben\". En 't is goed uitgekomen. Heel de familie heeft last van haar gehad, al toen ze een kind was. Als ze bij een boer werkte en ze wou weg en ze mocht niet, dan gooide ze de petroleumkan leeg in de melkkuip. Zulke dingen deed ze. Maar soms kon ze alles missen."},{"n":50571,"r":"KOOIJMAN0025","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A fortune teller comes to tell a farmer that there is still a drowning to come. The farmer thinks of his children, but in the end he drowns himself.","i":"H.K.","o":"Dirk Hoogenboom was boer op Het Paradijs (1). Toen kwam er een vrouw aan de deur, een waarzegster. Die zei: \"Er is altijd nog een verdrinkeling (2) bij\". Een poosje later zei die boer, dat er geen een verdronken was (3). Maar later is hij zelf verdronken in de IJssel. Toen was hij al boer af. Hij woonde toen op het Jaagpad.\n\n(1) boerderij vlak bij Haastrecht \n(2) drenkeling \n(3) doelend op zijn kinderen"},{"n":50586,"r":"KOOIJMAN0042","p":"Polsbroek","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul are clairvoyant.","i":"H.K.","o":"Vroeger zeiden ze hier, wanneer je met de blinde belie (1) ben geboren, dan heb je de gave van de helderziendheid. Soms bleef de helm rondspoken. Dan zeiden ze: \"De blinde belie spookt!\"\n(1) de helm"},{"n":50605,"r":"KOOIJMAN0062","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul can do anything. They are bulletproof. And the seventh son knows remedies for many ailments.","i":"H.K."},{"n":50619,"r":"KOOIJMAN0077","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"When you went to a fortune teller, he always had a black dog lying beside him or under the table.","i":"H.K."},{"n":50892,"r":"KOOIJMAN0192","p":"Meerkerk","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"In the past there were people who could sense that the eels were coming up out of the mud (and so it was time to fish).","i":"H.K.","o":"Vroeger waren er mensen, die an d'r lijf voelden als de paling loskwam."},{"n":50935,"r":"KOOIJMAN0235","p":"Reeuwijk","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman can predict deaths; she foresees funeral processions.","i":"H.K.","o":"M'n zwager z'n moeder, dat was een eigenaardig vrouwtje. Die had het tweede gezicht. Ze zag vooruit begrafenisstoeten. Ze woonde in Bodegraven."},{"n":50975,"r":"KOOIJMAN0274","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Some people can see the future and predict their own death. They can then make all the preparations for their funeral themselves.","i":"H.K.","o":"Sommigten zagen vooruit d'r eigen begrafenis. Ze zagen vooruit d'r eigen dood aankomen. Ze zagen de stoet al in d'r droom. Ze bestelden zelf d'r eigen kist en doodskleed en ze lieten zelf d'r bidprentjie maken."},{"n":51039,"r":"KOOIJMAN0321","p":"Moordrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The narrator's father saw his own father drown, while he was at a completely different place at that moment.","i":"H.K.","o":"M'n grootvader, ok 'n visser, is verdronken an de Moerdijk. M'n vader was op 't moment dat dat gebeurde in Capelle*. Hij was d'r niet bij en toch heb die 't allemaal zien gebeuren.\n\n*aan den IJssel"},{"n":44016,"r":"KUSTERS000201","p":"Asten","v":"N.-Br.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Prediction of telephoning and of a change of climate in summer and winter.","i":"C.K.","o":"Ik was zowat 17 jr. toen ik dikwijls werkte in Frenkens' Bos. We gingen dan niet naar huis om te eten maar 'n heél oud manneke, Pirke Kösters bracht ons dan de streuf en de pap. Pirke waar 'n aarig. D'r waar in dien tijd gin radio en gin televisie mer de mensen zagen veul dingen in de löcht. Dè kös Pirke ook en hij zee: \"d'r zal 'n tijd komme, dè de dur duvelsdrui dur de locht pröte\" telefoneren\n\n\"d'r zal 'n tijd komme, dè de winters nie mir uit de zomers kaant kenne\"\nen kie, dè is nauw, in de winter eest dik zo schone weer en in de zomer eest kauw.\"","l":"Brabants"},{"n":32451,"r":"CJ126105","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man is often driven out of bed at night to have visions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sjoerd Koedriuwer wenne oan 'e Sumarre achterwei. Hy moest der nachts faek ôf om to sjen. Dan wied er sa binaud, dan spielde it swit him by de holle del.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":210591,"r":"ENGELS002106","p":"Neer","v":"L.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"At the moment her son is killed in action, a soldier's mother sees his death and the place in a dream.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Voorteken:\nEen zuster van mij woont in Hamont (België). Vlak bij haar huis werd in de laatste dagen van de oorlog hevig gevochten, en vonden de partisanen in een bosje een gesneuvelde Duitser, die niet geïdentificeerd kon worden, en daar werd begraven. Mijn zuster constateerde, dat het een soldaat was, die daags daarvoor bij haar in huis was geweest. Later bleek, dat men door verkeerde opgave van het legernummer een vergissing had gemaakt. De moeder van de soldaat had een bericht van vermissing gekregen.\nOp zekere dag kreeg mijn zuster een brief van deze vrouw, met verzoek om inlichtingen. Kameraden van haar zoon hadden haar verteld, dat hij bij Klein Brogel gesneuveld zou zijn, en dat ze zijn lijk nog in een bosje hadden gelegd. De moeder kwam op bezoek bij mijn zuster, om het graf van haar zoon te zoeken. Ze had door nasporingen ontdekt, dat hij bij haar in kwartier gelegen had. Ze vertelde, dat ze op het tijdstip van zijn dood een droom had. Ze zag haar zoon over een vlak veld vluchten, en dodelijk gewond neerstorten. Toen zag ze zijn kameraden het lichaam in een bosje slepen. \nBij haar bezoek herkende ze de plaats zonder dat iemand haar deze had aangewezen.\n\nGeen omzetting in dialect van het verhaal door Engels."},{"n":72682,"r":"KOOIJMAN1186","p":"Blokland","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People who were born with a caul were bulletproof.","i":"H.K."},{"n":72839,"r":"KOOIJMAN1323","p":"Rijswijk","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Those who did not see the funeral procession coming had to step aside. But those born with a caul did see it.","i":"H.K.","o":"Dan kwam d'r een lijkstaatsie voorbij, diegene die 't niet zage, moest op zij. Maor de mense die me den helm gebore ware, die 't zien."},{"n":72873,"r":"KOOIJMAN1352","p":"Sleeuwijk","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul can bewitch other people. And they had the gift of foresight.","i":"H.K.","o":"[Met de helm geboren:] Die kanne heel wat as ze iemand niet genege zijn. Dan legde ze d'r hand op oewe schouwer. Dan zijde betoverd. Dan moete zelfhullie een klap op d'r hoofd geve, dan is de toverij afgeweerd. Ze hadde een vooruitziende blik."},{"n":72908,"r":"KOOIJMAN1383","p":"Woudrichem","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul had the gift of foresight.","i":"H.K."},{"n":125536,"r":"KOOIJMAN1420","p":"Andel","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul could do more than others: foretell and cure illness, and stroke horses to heal them.","i":"H.K.","o":"[Met de helm geboren:] Die konden iets meer dan een ander, ziekte voorspellen en genezen, paarde strijke."},{"n":125544,"r":"KOOIJMAN1427","p":"Woudrichem","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Witches were extraordinary people. They had been born with a caul.","i":"H.K.","o":"Dat weet ik nog uit mijn jeugd, d'r werd over toverhekse gesproke. Dat ware buitengewone mense. Dan ging 't verhaal: \"Ze ware met den helm gebore, ze hadde een netje voor d'r oge\"."},{"n":125564,"r":"KOOIJMAN1445","p":"Woudrichem","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul could, for example, enter a house while the door was not open.","i":"H.K.","o":"Met den helm gebore, die mense konde bijvoorbeeld in een woning komme waar de deur niet van ope was.","l":"Noord-Brabants"},{"n":125809,"r":"KOOIJMAN1613","p":"Nieuwaal","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Whoever is born with a caul is especially lucky, free of all misfortune, and had the gift of foresight.","i":"H.K.","o":"Wie met de helm was geboren, was bijzonder gelukkig, van alle onheilen vrij en had een vooruitziende blik."},{"n":207082,"r":"KUSTERS006605","p":"Mierlo","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Seeing someone lying in a ditch at the same moment that someone is drowning in a ditch elsewhere.","i":"C.K.","o":"'n Verpleegster in huize Voorburg te Vught zag 'ns duidelijk iemand in 'n sloot liggen. Later bleek, dat op die tijd Pastoor van Dijk in Nuland in 'n sloot was verdronken en er werd gevonden."},{"n":126564,"r":"Kooijman1954","p":"Deil","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul are bulletproof if they possess the caul. If not, they have to go to the churchyard at night when someone dies.","i":"H.K.","o":"MET DE HELM GEBOREN\n\nJa, dat werd gezegd, mensen met de helm geboren....\nAs die helm maar in z'n bezit bleef, dan was die kogelvrij. \nMaar as de helm gestolen was, dan werd beweerd, dat zo iemand met een sterfgeval 's-nachts om 12 uur 't bed uit moest en van z'n huis naar 't kerkhof moest en as d'r dan wat in 't wagenspoor liep, dat werd d'r afgezet.","l":"Gelders"},{"n":21869,"r":"CJ029009","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul predicts that his horse will perish. The prediction comes true: the animal dies in a fire at an inn.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't de herberch fan Rienk de Poel - 'de murdehoale' - opbrânde, kom it hynder ek yn 'e flammen om.\nFrytsen hat fan tofoaren al de hynsteklap heard.\nFrytsen wie mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21871,"r":"CJ029011","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant predicts where two lost sheep are: the shepherd does indeed find his animals at that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der kom us in man by Sjoerd Mounder to Eastemar.\nDy sei: \"Ik ha in nuver boadskip. Ik mis twa skiep. Doe ha 'k nei greate Wopke ta west. Dy sei: 'Jou skiep rinne to Eastemar yn in stik lân, dat hyt fan Wobbekamp'. Is hjir sa'n stik lân?\"\n\"Ja\", sei Sjoerd Mounder.\n\"Soenen jo mei my dêrhinne gean wolle?\"\n\"Jawol.\" En Sjoerd Mounder gong mei.\nIt wie by de Heidbuorsterwei. Doe sei dy man: \"Sjoch, der rinne se.\" De man kom mei syn beide skiep werom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21872,"r":"CJ029012","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A folk healer is taken home after successfully helping with a cow's difficult calving. At a farm he says that there is a cow there about to calve, but that all will go well. On inquiry this turns out to be true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Hinse (Hinse Jehannes de Boer fan it Swartfean) woarde us by in boer yn 'e Koaten helle, hwant sy koenen it keal net fan 'e koe krije. Hinse woarde troch de boer yn 't rydtúch helle. Hy spile it klear mei de koe. It wie in moai keal.\nDoe brocht de boer Hinse wer nei hûs ta.\nUnderweis to Eastemar yn 'e pleats, dêr't nou it hûs fan Tsjitse Jansma is, - njonken de herfoarme pasterije - sei Hinse: \"Hjir stiet ek in koe, dy wol kealje, mar 't giet allegear goed.\"\nDe Koatster boer tocht op 'e weromreis: \"Nou woe 'k doch wol us wite of dat sa is.\" Hy gong by de Heechsânster boer oan en frege. En wrachtich, it wie sa, hja hienen dêr krekt in keal fangd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21875,"r":"CJ029015","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman born with a caul hears a horse kicking and stamping. Some time later the horse perishes in a fire, kicking and stamping.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der is in hynder yn 'Het witte paard' forbrând. Dat hat ôfgryslik skopt en trape. Alde Frytsen, de mem fan Willem Mulder, dy't mei de helm geboaren wie, hat dat skoppen fan tofoaren heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":43591,"r":"WEV011502","p":"Wierum","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A card reader's prediction that a girl will marry a fisherman, that he will drown and that she will have many children comes true.","i":"F.W.","o":"Er was eens een jong meisje. \nZe ging op zekere dag naar een kaartlegster om de toekomst te vernemen. \nDe vrouw zei tegen haar: \"Uw man zal een visser zijn; deze zal verdrinken; verder zult u veel kinderen krijgen.\"\nAlles is ook zo uitgekomen."},{"n":43645,"r":"WEV011601","p":"Hooghalen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Man can foresee things; how he foresaw something as a little boy.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik ben soms in een zekere gemoedstoestand dat ik iets voorzie. \nPrettig is dat niet. \nHet zijn vage momenten, die kort duren; schrik heb je op zo'n moment niet. \nIk zal niet alles weergeven, omdat sommige mensen nog leven, van wiedan ik enkele dingen weet; \n\nIk was nog pas 5 jaar en woonde in de Achterhoek. \nIk zeg tegen mijn moeder: \"Vandaag komt er een boer met zijn wagen in het veen vast te zitten; maar vader en ik gaan er met onze paarden heen om die man te helpen.\"\nEn het gebeurde. \nIk kende die man niet; had alleen wel eens zijn naam gehoord. \nToch wist ik die naam te noemen. \nVader en ik zijn er samen geweest om de in de modder weggezakte wagen weer vlot te krijgen.\nDat was de eerste keer en daarna heb ik zoveel dingen zien gebeuren; enkele wil ik wel vertellen. \n\nZo weet ik nog wel meer, maar die gebeurtenissen grijpen nogal diep in een mensen leven en daarom verzwijg ik die."},{"n":43646,"r":"WEV011602","p":"Hooghalen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"At home the narrator sees people lying by a gate; it is his son's motorcycle accident.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik ben soms in een zekere gemoedstoestand dat ik iets voorzie. \nPrettig is dat niet. \nHet zijn vage momenten, die kort duren; schrik heb je op zo'n moment niet. \nIk zal niet alles weergeven, omdat sommige mensen nog leven, van wiedan ik enkele dingen weet; \n\nMijn zoon had indertijd zin in een motor. Ik zeg tegen hem: \"Koop diemotor niet; een bromfiets kan geen kwaad; je broers kunnen zich ook rustig een aanschaffen, maar jij krijgt er een ongeluk mee.\" \nHij heeft toch een motor gekocht. Zijn vrouw zei trouwens, dat ik gek was. Twee kleine ongelukken overkwamen hem, waar hij geen letsel van overhield. \nIn 1962, ik was thuis met iets bezig, zag ik heel vaag een hek. Bij dat hek lagen twee mensen of een mens met wat kleding er naast; zie je, erg duidelijk merk je die dingen niet op. \nWat gebeurde er? \nIn Assen had toen mijn zoon het derde ongeluk. \nHij is er nog steeds niet helemaal van hersteld en zal nooit meer de oude worden."},{"n":130489,"r":"BIJLSMA004501","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A silent figure walks along with a man and suddenly vanishes. A daughter who lives elsewhere sees her father standing in a corner of her room at the moment he dies.","i":"T.B.","o":"L. Alkema, hat amtner by P.T.T. op 'e Jouwer west, 70 jier âld, fan Aldhoarne fan komôf, fortelde mey my:\nHeit wie turfskipper. Omke Auke roun ris op in joun yn 'e line. In ein roun der in man mei him op. De man sei neat, en ynienen wie er samar fordwoun.\nPake wie by harren to Aldhoarne stoarn. Op itselde stuit hie muoike, dy't dêr net wenne, pake yn in hoeke fan de keamer stean sjoen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":12505,"r":"CJ001903","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The narrator's great-grandmother sees things that will happen in the future. She sees the lime tree in front of the house being sawn down. The great-grandfather is indeed planning to do that. Instead of sawing, he now chops it down. One branch, however, cannot be chopped and is sawn off. So the great-grandmother is right after all.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn oerbeppe wenne op 'e Teijen ûnder Drachten. Sy wie troud mei Errit Errits de Jong. Se seach en hearde allerhande dingen foarút. Har man woe dêr neat fan wite en leaude der net oan, mar it kom altyd nei, hwat se sei. Op in kear sei se: Fannacht haw ik heard, dat se foar hûs yn 'e linebeammen omsagen. Har man wie werkelik fan doel dat de oare wyks dwaen to litten. Mar hy tochte, nou lit ik de takken ris net ôfsaegje, mar ôfkappe. Dat gebeurde. De arbeiders bisnoeiden de linebeammen mei de bile. Sa hie de boer it tsjin har sein. Mar doe wie der ien takke by, dy bruts hwat raer ôf. De arbeider tocht: dy mat ik hwat bysaegje. Hy krige de sage en dat gebeurde. Doe sei oerbeppe tsjin oerpake: Hark. Dat is itselde lûd, dat ik lestennachts yn 'e linebeammen heard ha. Sa krige se dochs noch gelyk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15589,"r":"CJ002401","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"One winter there was so much ice that a dead child could not be taken away across the water. But when the ice is about to be hacked away, a witch says it is not necessary, as it is going to thaw anyway. This prediction comes true, because the witch was born with a caul. Once she is also called in to cure a sick child, but she suggests fetching an exorcist, because the child is bewitched.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn ien fan 'e polderketen dy't oan 'e Geeuw stienen wie in berntsje forstoarn. 't Wie yn 'e winter en der lei allegear iis. Hja koenen net mei 't lykje nei 't Wêst ta farre, der moest earst iis weislein wurde. Doe't se dêr mei dwaende wienen, kom âlde Martens Ale by har en dy sei: \"Jimme hoege it iis der net wei to slaen. Ik ha 't al sjoen. It iis is al fuort as it bern op 't hôf komt.\"\nIt wie ek sa, de oare deis tijde it sa bot, dat suver alle iis rekke fuort. Martens Ale wie mei de helm geboaren.\n\nYn 't West wie in bern, dat altyd siik wie. Doe hellen se Ale der by. Ale sei doe't se it bern sjoen hie: \"Ik kin jim dit wol sizze: it bern is bitsjoend. Mar ik kin fierder neat foar it bern dwaen. Jimme matte de duvelbander der by helje.\" Doe binne se nei Piter Poes fan Sumarreheide tagong en dy hat makke, dat it bern wer better woarn is mei allerhande kunsten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15607,"r":"CJ002501","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Around 1915 Sikke Antsje foresaw that a child would drown in the Feanster canal. Soon afterwards a child drowns there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Feanster feart by de Melle Poalsreed hat in frommes om likernôch 1915 hinne sjoen dat in jonkje forsûpe moest. Dat frommes wie Sikke Antsje.\nFuort dearnei is dear in jonkje forsûpt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15670,"r":"CJ002539","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman returns from the funeral and hears a voice saying: \"The sword shall not depart from your house.\" Shortly afterwards the third child dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't heit stoarn wie en mem weromkom fan 'e bigraffenis hat se dúdlik heard: \"Het zwaard zal van uw huis niet wijken.\" Dearnei binne der trije bern stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15778,"r":"CJ003103","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Knjillis Veenstra was born with a caul. At night he often has to go out to see something, sometimes during the day too. Gates and doors then open for him by themselves. Once he says that a funeral procession will soon pass with a white horse in front. A week later that happens.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn Kollumersweach wenne in man, dat wie in sikere Knjillis Veenstra. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy hat in protte sjoen, dat in oar net seach. Nachts moest hy der faek ôf.\nOp in kear wied er mei in kammeraet yn 'e ûngetiid achter Ljouwert. Hy moest der wer ôf om hwat to sjen. Doe tocht syn kammeraet: \"Ik wol us mei him.\" Hy folge him, sûnder dat Knjillis it fornom. In hiel ein gong Knjillis fuort. Op it lêst kom er werom. Doe sei syn kammeraet: \"Hwat hastû altyd in gebongel yn 'e nacht.\"\n\"Ja,\" sei er, \"ik ha hwat sjoen. Hjir komt hiel yn 't koart in lykstaesje lâns, mei in wyt hynder der foar.\"\nIn wike letter gebeurde it.\n\nAs Knjillis der op út gong, gongen de hekken en de doarren fansels foar him iepen, hwant hy moest der troch om hwat to sjen.\nIt wie meastal yn 'e nacht, dat hy der op útgong, soms ek wol us op dei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15809,"r":"CJ003508","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"When children are born with membranes over their eyes, the doctor or midwife removes and keeps them. The child can then later see into the future. The child was born with a caul.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wienen bern, as dy geboaren woarden, hienen se flueskes foar de egen. De baekster of de dokter nom dy der ôf. Dy flueskes woarden biwarre en dat bern koe dan letter yn 'e takomst sjen. Sa'n bern wie mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15910,"r":"CJ004005","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A light phenomenon foretells the coming of a house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 't Skoalpaed seach ús heit faek in ljochtsje. Dêr is doe ek in hûs kom to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15911,"r":"CJ004006","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A fortune teller can successfully see into the future by laying cards. She sees marriages, deaths, accidents, lawsuits and earnings.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Thomas Klare fan Houtigehage koe kaertlizze. Ik en myn maet ha ris nei Ljouwerter Merke ta west. Dêr wienen njoggen kaertlizters. Wy ha by alle njoggen west, mar sy seinen it alle njoggen oars.\nMar ik ha ek ris mei twa fan myn maten by Hinke Kaert west to Nijebrêge. Hwat Hinke sei, dat kaem altyd út.\nSy bea ús bier oan. De hearen ek in potsje? sei se. Jawol Hinke, seinen we.\nAnne Wytkop is ek dea, hè? En Minke Anne is ek forstoarn, hè? Jimme komme út it Noardoasten wei.\nIk wie de earste, dy't oan 'e beurt kom.\n\"Dû mast trouwe, hè?\" sei se.\nJa, sei ik.\nNou dyn wente komt to stean skean tsjin it hûs fan dyn heit en dy oer. 't Is in boerespultsje.\nDat kloppe as in bus.\nSit ik ek yn aksje, Hinke? frege ik.\nDêr ha 'k net omtocht, jonge, sei se. Mar 'k sil wolris sjen. Doe skodde se de kaerten, lei guon út en sei: \"Dû hast ien in slach tsjin 'e kop jown. It proses verbael leit hjir yn 't Hearrenfean. Mar dû hoechst net bang to wêzen, hwant der komt neat fan.\"\nDoe kom myn kammeraet oan 'e beurt.\nDû krijst in jong dinkje, sei se. En dat wie ek sa, hy troude mei in fanke fan sawntjin.\nTsjin 'e trêdde sei se: Dû krijst ien mei in lape op 'e skelk. Dêr bidoelde se in widdoufrou mei.\nDoe't wy fuort soenen, sei se: Nou matte jimme oppasse, hwant jim krije aenst ek noch in ûngelok ûnderweis. En dat kom ek al wer út, hwant myn beide maten rekken mei de stjûren fan 'e fytsen yn inoar.\nSy sei e","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16058,"r":"CJ004210","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A fortune teller once predicted to a capitalist that he would become as poor as the Lady of Stavoren. They became even poorer.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir hat in wiersizter wenne. Hwat dy foarspelde, kaem út. Der kom us in kapitalist by har. Dy wenne hjir. Sy biseach de kaerten en sei: \"Sjoch, jimme wurde sa earm as 't vrouwtje van Stavoren.\"\nSy binne nòch earmer woarn as dat wyfke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16840,"r":"CJ006402","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Uncle Piter was a knife grinder; he was murdered on the Wildpad on the Twizelerheide. Our dad saw that murder happen at night while he lay in bed. He thought: I know that person, but he could not see his face. There was a thunderstorm. He got out of bed and was completely beside himself. However hard he tried to see who was being murdered, he could not. From the bearing and build he clearly saw that he knew the person. That same day he received the news: it was his brother.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn omke Piter wie skearsliper. Hy is formoarde op it Wyldpaed ûnder Twizelerheide. Us heit hat deselde nachts dat dat gebeurde de hiele moard sjoen, wylst er op bêd lei. Hy tochte: dy persoan ken ik. Mar hy krige noait syn gesicht to sjen. Hy gong der ôf en wie hiel bot fan 'e wize. It tongere en wjerljochte, wylst it gebeurde. Om 4 ûre hinne bikom it swiere waer. Heit hat letter faek sein al hoe'n muoite er ek dien hie om to sjen, hwa't formoarde woarde, hy koe 't noait sjen. Mar oan hâlding en stal seach er dúdlik, dat er de persoan koe. It wie syn eigen broer. Dyselde deis (saterdei) krige er de tiding.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16847,"r":"CJ006409","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"It is said of Piter de Graaf, who lives in Pein, that he was born with a caul. He can predict when someone will die. He is always right.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Piter de Graaf wenne yn de Pein. Hy is mei de helm geboaren. Hy koe op 'e dei om't ôf sizze as der ien dea gean soe. It kloppe altyd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16968,"r":"CJ007303","p":"Sweagerbosk","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man can see in advance what is going to happen. He goes to places where a funeral will come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn Sweagerbosk wenne in sikere Bontsje Kuipers. Dy moest altyd nei de plakken ta, dêr't in begraffenis kaem. Fan tofoaren seach er alles.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17030,"r":"CJ007712","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A certain woman always foresees deaths.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Frou Pander seach altyd fan tofoaren as der guon dea gean soenen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17031,"r":"CJ007713","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A certain woman always foresees the arrival of visitors a day in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Elske Jongsma seach altyd in dei fan tofoaren as der guon by har komme soenen. Kaem der ien, dan sei se: Juster hast hjir al by my op 'e strjitte stien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17335,"r":"CJ008707","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"During the German occupation a boy from the narrator's family is arrested and transported to Germany. Before he comes home quite unexpectedly, the narrator's father has already seen the boy arriving.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In jonge fan ús is yn 'e Dútse bisettingstiid oppakt en nei Dútslân transporteard. Krekt foardat er thúskaem, alhiel ûnforwacht, sei heit: de jonge komt werom, ik ha him al sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17385,"r":"CJ009011","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman has a vision of a girl in a red apron drowning in a pond. Shortly afterwards the narrator's thirteen-year-old sister drowns in the pond when she falls through the ice while skating. She is wearing a red apron.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Janke Houneloper hat in goed sawntich jier lyn in fanke sjoen mei in read skelkje foar, dat forsûpte yn in poel. (Dy poel is der net mear. Dy wie sahwat op 't plak dêr't nou it jeugdgebou stiet) Koart dêrnei is myn suster fan trettsjin jier dêr by 't reedriden op dy poel troch 't iis sakke en fordronken. Sy hie in read skelkje foar. Geeltje Elzinga hiet se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17395,"r":"CJ009021","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man was born with a caul. He sees everything in advance. He also saw in advance the house where the narrator's mother-in-law and her family lived burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Janke Mozes wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy seach alles foarút. Dy hat ek fantofoaren sjoen dat it hûs, dêr't skoanmem en dy yn wenne ha, opbrânde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18163,"r":"CJ011824","p":"Gerkesklooster","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often has to get out of bed at night to see something. He often has visions because he is clairvoyant.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Stiensgea wenne Romke Laanstra. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest der yn 'e nacht faek út om hwat to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20375,"r":"CJ018704","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often has to get up at night to see things. Usually he sees funeral processions pass by. The processions foreshadow an impending death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sytse Rapkes wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy wenne achter yn 'e Smoarhoeke yn 'e Harkema. Deis siet er altyd yn 'e stoel doe't it in âld man wie, mar nachts moest hy der op út, hwant hy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dan switte hy der soms oer, sa seach hy der tsjin oan. Mar hy moest hwat sjen. Dat wienen dan altyd lykstaesjes dy't er to sjen krige.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20392,"r":"CJ018802","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often has to get up at night to see things. He often foresees deaths in passing funerals. Although the man's caul was destroyed at his birth, he always has visions of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bearn Dekker wie mei de helm geboaren. Sy hienen dy helm wol forneatige, mar likegoed seach er alles. Hy moest der nachts faek út, dan waerd er dreaun. Dan seach er in bigraffenis.\n't Kom altyd krekt sa nei lyk as hy it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27410,"r":"CJ065404","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man was once sitting on the windowsill and saw the funeral of his wife. His wife was still alive at the time.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wessel Gal fortelde, hy hie de hiele bigraffenis fan syn wiif fan tofoaren sjoen. It wie op ljochtskyndei. Hy siet yn 't finsterbank foar hûs. Doe leefde syn wiif noch. (Wessel Gal kocht mollen op)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":44023,"r":"WEV012802","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul; a howling dog, seeing floating lights and a burning house are omens of a death; mocking the devil; being held fast by the devil, a way to get free.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wel mit de helm beboorn was, har altied geluk.\nHai hof nait in dainst en zien zoakn gongen ook goud.\nIe heurn nou nooit meer van mit de helm beboorn, omdat dat ding nou votdoadelk weg doan wordt deur verpleegsters en zo.\nVrouger wur e opbaargd.\nZo ain kon ook begravvenisn zain van te veurn.\nLichtgeleuvig bin ik nait, moar dat er veurloop bestait leuf ik wel. Door hebben ie de honden bieveurbeeld.\nOp de Hörsten heb ik door op let. Was n jonge vent zaik en toun kwam dr n hond - wie zegn mit vaar oogn, hai het vlekjes boovn d oogn - hail van Muzzelknoal en gung zitn te jankn veur t huus van de zaike. De jonge man is best overleden; en de hond heb k nooit weer zain. k Wil doorom ook nait zo n daier hebben.\nIk heb dr n beetje schrik veur kreegn.\nMoar ja, vrouger, toun was men overal benauwd veur.\nHier spookde t en door deugde t nait, dat was t proatje van oale mensn.\nMien oal heer zag ook voak spookn.\nIk wait nog, dat hai n keer teegm mien bruier en mie zee:\n\"Doar bie t huus van Bos deugt t nait, ik zai aal moar lichies zweevn achter t huus.\"\nDat was ja gevoarlijk, want al meer har hai schimmen zweevn zain of n huus in brand en noaderhand was dr n dode komen.\nNou was Bos aan de beurt.\nIk zee: \"Wie goan dr op of.\"\nd Oale gung zulf mit, moar baange was e wel.\nEn joa, was n beweegn van licht te zain bie Bos, moar wat was t geval? Bos luip over dele mit n schienvat, omdat hai eevn uut d","l":"Gronings"},{"n":19734,"r":"CJ015002","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The card reader Hinke Kaert can predict the future from cards. She predicts to two brothers what will happen on their way back home, and it does happen. Hinke tells the brothers' mother that one day she will cry harder than she ever has in her life. When one of the brothers is later murdered, the mother indeed begins to wail uncontrollably.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hinke Kaert wenne to Nijebrêge. It wie in bitûfte kaertlizter. Us Hindrik-om hat us nei har ta west. Hy woe de kaert lein ha. Hja sei tsjin him: \"Dû matst aenst oer in planke, dêr komt dy ien yn 'e mjitte, dy sil dy om hwat freegje, datstû yn 'e bûse hast. Hindrik-om gnyske. Hy leaude der neat fan. Hy hie forkearing hawn mei in fanke, dat wie útrekke. Hy wie oan 'e planke ta, dêr wie se. \"Hindrik,\" sei se. \"ik woe myn bûsdoek wol ha. Hast dy by dy?\"\nDoe't er thúskom fortelde hy it.\nDoe woe Piterom ek hinne (allebeide bruorren fan heit; Piterom is letter formoarde oan 't Wyldpaed)\nHinke sei: \"Ik wol dy de kaert net lizze, hwant dû hast doch oeral de gek mei.\"\n\"Né,\" sei Piterom, \"wier net. Ik wol èk wol us hwat wite.\"\nDoe sei se, hy soe in ponge mei jild fine en in dronken keardel nei hûs ta bringe, en sa mear.\nDoe kom er thús, sy laken der om.\nDoe woe beppe ek hinne. Hinke Kaert sei: \"Minske, ik sil jo neat fortelle. Ien ding sil 'k jo àl sizze, jo sille noch us in kear gûle, sa't jo noait earder gûld ha.\" Dat is útkom. Doe't ús Piterom formoarde woarde hat beppe ôfgryslik gûld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19957,"r":"CJ015813","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"When a child is born with a caul, the doctor keeps the caul. If the caul is kept, the child sees things in advance; if the caul is destroyed, the child loses its clairvoyant powers.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in bern geboaren woarde mei in helm biwarre de dokter sa'n helm. De dokters wienen der gleon op. Sa lang dy helm yn stân bleau seach deselde, dy't der mei geboaren wie, de dingen foarút. Waerd de helm forneatige, dan wie dat dien. Guon dokters forkochten dy helms djûr.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20098,"r":"CJ016811","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul sees a witch combing the horse's mane. He has a premonition that the horse will soon die, and so it does.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit tsjinne by in boer. Hy hie der us op in kear op út west en kom op in joun thús.\nDoe stie Rikele Myt by de boer op 't hiem. Hja stie by 't hynder en kaerde 't yn 'e moanjes om. Rikele Myt wie in tsjoenster.\nDe oare moarns sei heit tsjin 'e boer: Dat en dat haw ik sjoen - \"Ik doar wedzje,\" sei er, \"dat it hynder fan 'e wike dea leit.\"\n't Kom krekt sa út. Heit wie mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20114,"r":"CJ016913","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man visits a fortune-teller together with his wife's sister. The fortune-teller sees that the sister has had a very hard time and predicts that she will soon give birth to a fatherless child, a girl. This comes true exactly. The fortune-teller also predicts that the man will end up in a place where he will no longer need his own butter and milk. This is also right: the couple later have their own farm.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik en myn man ha twa jier yn in wein wenne. Doe sei er us op in moarn: \"'t Is hjoed Drachtster merke, dêr wol 'k hinne.\"\n't Wie sutrich waer. Ik sei: \"Hwat silst dêr hinne dwaen.\" Mar hy sette syn sin troch. De jouns stie 'k út to sjen. Op 't lêst, dêr kom er oan. Heal bisopen.\nWy sieten even. Doe sei er: \"Ik ha yn 'e waarseggerije west. Ik en Durkje togearre (Durkje dat is myn suster).\n\"Hwat seinen se? Hoe gong dat?\" frege ik.\n\"Earst kom Durkje oan 'e beurt. 't Wie mar in gewoane kop dy't fortelde. Oars neat as in kop.\"\n\"Hwat moesten jim jaen?\"\n\"In kwartsje.\"\n\"Hwat hat dy kop Durkje forteld?\"\n\"Sy sei tsjin Durkje, hja hie in swiere tiid hawn. Earst in jonkje forlern en doe har man forlern. Sy soe skielk 'forleid' wurde en in 'vaderloos kind' krije fan 't 'vrouwelijk geslachte'.\" (Dat is letter allegear krekt sa útkom.)\nDoe kom ik sels oan 'e beurt.\n\"Ik siet op 'e boom fan in sleat, krekt as in kikkert. Dy kikkert woe graech út 'e sleat wei, mar hy koe der noait út komme. Op it lêst, nei gâns muoite, rekke hy der dòch út. Hy kom op in plak tolânne, dêr't er syn eigen bûter en molke net noadich wie.\"\nDat is ek krekt sa útkom, hwant dat lêste, dat wie ik. 't Is echt sa gebeurd. Wy ha hjir buorkerije hawn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20145,"r":"CJ017204","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man was born with a caul and foresees the death of his brother.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Klaes Hiemstra dy't wennet op it middenpunt fan 'e Krúsdobbe oan 'e polderdyk yn Earnewâld is mei de helm geboaren. Hy hat fantofoaren sjoen hoe't syn broer Franke opdroegen woarde. \"Franke giet hjir wei,\" sei er, \"ik ha 't sjoen.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20184,"r":"CJ017513","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman visits a fortune-teller. The fortune-teller predicts that the woman will die within the year. The woman becomes frightened and wastes away completely. She grows weak and spends almost a year in bed. When she is still alive after a year, she suspects the fortune-teller has deceived her and cheerfully jumps out of bed. The woman recovers at once and eventually lives to a great age.","i":"J.W.","o":"Yn 'e Trynwâlden wenne in faem, dy gong nei de wiersizter ta. Dy fortelde har, hja soe binnen it jier stjerre. De faem wie alhiel forbûke. Alle fleur wie der út. Sy bigong to kwinen en rekke op bêd. Sa gong der in jier foarby, mar doe't dat jier òm wie, leefde se nòch. Doe sprong se út it bêdsté wei en rôp: \"Dat smoarge wiif hat it allegear liichd!\"\nSy die har wurk wer en knapte by de dei op. Sy is hiel âld woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20185,"r":"CJ017514","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman is seriously worried about her future. The fortune-teller Hinke Kaart reassures her and tells her that she will soon live in a little wooden house with lots of fine tall trees around it. The woman goes home reassured. Shortly afterwards she dies and is buried in a wooden coffin in a churchyard where tall trees stand.","i":"J.W.","o":"By Hinke Kaert op Nijebrêge kom us in minske, dat makke har soargen oer de takomst. Hinke sei tsjin har: \"Jo hoege jo nergens soargen oer to meitsjen. Jo komme mei koarten yn in houten húske to wenjen, ûnder it skaed fan hege beammen. Jo hoeve nergens foar to soargjen, foar gjin húsrie noch oare spullen.\"\nDe frou wie gerêst en gong nei hûs ta.\nMar koarte tiid dernei rekke se dea. Men lei har yn 'e kiste en brocht har nei it tsjerkhôf ta, dêr't hege beammen stienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20249,"r":"CJ018010","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul always has to get up at night to see things. He often has visions of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dikke Sjoerd Koedriuwer (= Sjoerd Dykstra) fan Sumar moest der nachts ek altyd ôf. Dy wie èk mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20292,"r":"CJ018207","p":"Burum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul can foresee things that are going to happen in the future. Sometimes, for example, they see a funeral procession pass by: later someone really does die. People born with a caul have other gifts too: they can also heal the sick.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Die met de helm geboren werd, dat was een soort van profeet. Die kon ook zieken genezn. Die kon allerlei byzondere dingen doen en zegn. Ook lykstaasjes sag ie vanteforen. Soms duurde het een half jaar voordat het krektzo gebeurde.","l":"Fries"},{"n":20330,"r":"CJ018502","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A cheerful man suddenly becomes very gloomy and quiet. He assures his wife that nothing is wrong, but remains downcast. In the end he tells his wife that they are about to lose two children, because he has seen their funeral. Some time later it comes true exactly. The man was born with a caul and can foresee things that are going to happen in the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wytse (van der Meer) en Rinskje wennen yn Burgumerheide. Wytse wie in plezierich man dy't altyd wille hie. Mar dat hâldde samar ynienen op mei Wytse. Hy woarde stil en hy seach altyd mar earnstich. Syn wyfke Rinskje frege him: \"Is der hwat?\"\n\"Né,\" sei Wytse, \"hwat soe der wêze?\"\nMar hy bleau altyd mar stil en earnstich. Rinskje frege al us wer en us wer, mar hy sei altyd mar, der wie neat.\nMar doe op in kear, nei forrin fan tiid, sei er tsjin Rinskje: \"Ik sil 't dy ek wol sizze. It is der nou doch hast oan ta. Wy forlieze aenst twa bern. Ik ha de bigraffenis al sjoen.\"\nWytse wie mei de helm geboaren. 't Kom krekt sa út lyk as er sein hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20346,"r":"CJ018602","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman born with a caul predicts the death of her neighbour, because she has already seen her funeral. Three or four weeks later the neighbour does indeed die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn wiif komt fan 'e Keale Wei yn Grinslân, dy't fan Koartwâld nei Doezum rint. Tichte by harren wenne in âld wiif, dy wie ek mei de helm geboaren. Hja sei op in kear, har buorwiif soe dan en dan op it hôf komme, hwant hja hie de bigraffenis al sjoen. Mar op dat stuit skilde it buorwiif noch neat. Mar in trije of fjouwer wiken letter wie se dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20525,"r":"CJ019725","p":"Sweagerbosk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A fortune-teller who can see the future in coffee grounds always has many visitors. Card readers also get many callers. A card reader predicts that a woman will soon marry, and it comes true exactly.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Westerein wenne Rixt Dykstra. Dat wie in kopkekykster.\nDêr reizgen faek guon hinne om de takomst to witen to kommen.\nMyn wiif hat us mei har kammeraetske nei Thomas Klare west. Dat wie in kaertlizter. Dy wenne doe noch yn 'e Houtigehage.\nKlare forspelde de krekte tiid dat har kammeraetske trouwe soe. Hja soe swier foar de burgemeester komme, sei Klare.\nDat is allegear krekt sa útkom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20536,"r":"CJ019804","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A sailor's wife is very anxious about her husband's fate and calls in the help of the minister. The minister asks her if he may sleep on her bed for a while to see how the man is doing. The minister stretches out comfortably and is soon fast asleep. When he gets up a short while later, he says the woman need not worry about anything, because her husband, the sailor, has just posted a letter that will probably arrive within a few days. It comes true exactly as the minister predicted. Afterwards the couple want nothing more to do with the minister, because they believe such arts are the devil's arts.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie in frou, dy wenne op it Amelân. Har man farde op sé. Hja hie yn lang gjin tynge fan him hawn, dat sy makke har slim ûngerust.\nDoe kom dûmny by har. Dy fornom wol, dat se ûngerust wie.\nHy sei: \"Woenen jo graech wite, hoe't it mei jou man is?\" Nou, sy woe fansels neat leaver as dat. Dûmny sei, dan moest hy in skoftsje op har bêd lizze. Dat foun dy frou wol hwat nuver, mar it gebeurde doch. It duorre net lang of dûmny snoarke der oer, sa sliepte er.\nEven letter kom er wer út it bêd wei.\n\"Jo hoeve net ûngerust to wêzen\", sei er. Jou man hat krekt in brief yn 'e bus brocht foar jo. Ik haw him sjoen. Miskien hat er my ek wol sjoen, mar dat wyt ik net sekuer. Binnen inkelde dagen krije jo syn brief. Hy is goed soun.\"\nIt kom krekt sa út. Nei inkelde dagen kom der in brief fan him. Hy skreau: \"Kin 't wêze, dat ik ús dûmny hjir sjoen ha?\"\nLetter woenen dy man en dy frou neat mear fan har dûmny wite. Hwant sokke kunsten wienen duvelskunsten, seinen se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21673,"r":"CJ028015","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The narrator has had visions of the future since childhood, and they always come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik fiif jier wie seach ik al dingen foarút. It kom altyd nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21677,"r":"CJ028019","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A card reader who also reads cups, that is, coffee grounds, often makes predictions about the future. Her predictions always come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen yn 'e Westerein. Alde Kik (Richtsje) en har dochter, in âld-faem krigen gau us besoek. Hwant âlde Kik koe kaertlizze en kopkekike. Ik ha fan dat oangeande in protte fan har leard. 't Kom altyd út hwat se sei. Wy neamden har 'beppe'. Hja hat my op 'e wike ôf sein hwannear't myn man stjerre soe - dat is nou al fjirtich jier lyn - Ik soe in protte wederwaerdichheden ha dêrnei en ik koe wol tsien man wer krije, mar ik soe net wer trouwe. Hja hat ek krekt it hûs biskreaun dêr't ik letter yn wenje soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21679,"r":"CJ028021","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman predicts that her daughter-in-law will be visited by her mother in the afternoon. It comes true exactly.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Fan 'e moarn hat myn skoandochter hjir west om my to helpen. Dy komt hjir elke moarn om it wurk hwat to dwaen. Ik sei fan 'e moarn tsjin har: \"Dû meist wol oanmeitsje. Hwant dû krijst fan 'e middei bisite. Ik leau fan jimme mem.\"\nNou is har mem der al.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21704,"r":"CJ028207","p":"Houten","v":"Utr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A dying woman foresees that a great war will come over the world. The following year the First World War broke out.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In 1913 is mijn schoonmoeder overleden. Gerritje van de Vuurs-Wolfswinkel heette ze. Tijdens haar doodsstrijd zei ze: \"Er komt gauw een grote oorlog over de wereld.\" Het was maar een gewoon boerenmens. Ze wist van politiek niets af. En toch is het nagekomen. Het volgend jaar brak de oorlog uit."},{"n":21828,"r":"CJ028802","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A fisherman often goes out at night to see things.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Albert Postma wie de heit fan Klaes Oersetter. Hy wie fisker en gong der yn 'e nacht algeduerigen op út, mei syn boatsje. Hwerom, dat wie net bikend, mar men tocht, dat er dan hwat sjen moest.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21834,"r":"CJ028808","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man often has to get up at night to see things. He has visions of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Frytsen to Eastemar moest der yn 'e nacht om tolve ûre út. Hja koe yn 't tsjuster sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21835,"r":"CJ028809","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man always has to get up around midnight to see things. He has visions of the future.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":21836,"r":"CJ028810","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A little old woman foresees a disaster in the pottery shop: a few days later all the goods are smashed to pieces.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Frytsen stie us yn 'e winkel by Rikele Pot. Doe sei se: \"Hjir komt in ramp yn 't koart.\" In pear dagen letter sakke der in ramt yn en alle potte- en panneguod dat der op stie, kom nei ûnderen en rekke yn diggels. (Frytsen wie de beppe fan Willem Mulder to Eastemar)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21898,"r":"CJ029210","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"If you pull the caul upwards on children born with a caul, they will be clairvoyant and have visions of the future. If you pull the caul downwards, they will not.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wienen bern, dy woarden mei de helm geboaren. As dy helm omleech lutsen woarde, mei de geboarte, dan moesten dy bern alles sjen. Lutsen se de helm omheech, dan net.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21994,"r":"CJ031115","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant is often driven out of bed at night to see things, for example funeral processions. People say it is a torment from the devil.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Falom wenne in man, dy moest nachts altyd út bêd wei om hwat to sjen. 't Wie in hiele bêste man. Hy moest soms ûrenfier rinne om by de lykstaesje to kommen.\nMem sei al ris tsjin him: \"As jo nou us lizzen bliuwe, hwat dan?\"\n\"Ei minske,\" sei er, \"dan wie 't net bêst. Dan waerd ik der út smiten.\"\nIt binne pleagen fan 'e duvel, as men der nachts út mat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22003,"r":"CJ031209","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A father wants to sell the caul of his clairvoyant child. Whoever owns the caul is bulletproof.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us pake en dy hienen in helm fan ien fan 'e bern. Dêr wie dat bern mei geboaren. Dy helm koe pake djûr forkeapje. De dokter wie der tige hyt op. Hy sei: \"Daar wil ik van der Veen wel veel geld voor geven.\" Mar pake die't net. Letter hat pake dy helm fuort dien.\nDy't sa'n helm yn besit hat is kûgelfrij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22011,"r":"CJ031308","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant predicts that a little boy called Ealse will drown. Forty years later an Ealse does indeed die by drowning. An old woman had also foreseen this.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Kei syn pake wie in Gerrit. Dy fortelde ris, der soe in jonkje yn ús famylje fordrinke, in lytse Ealse. Dat wie him iepenbiere.\nGoed fjirtich jier letter is 't gebeurd. Der waerd letter net wer oer praet, nei't hy dat sein hie. Mar elke kear dat der wer in Ealse geboaren waerd, waerd der om tocht. Wy ha in stik of hwat Ealses yn 'e famylje.\nFjirtich jier letter krigen wy in Ealse. Wy wennen yn 'e Falom.\nAlde beppe, de frou fan pake Gerrit, koe kopkekike.\nOp in kear sei ik tsjin har: \"Fortel my ekris hwat.\"\n\"Bern,\" sei se tsjin my op sa'n eigenaerdige toan, \"dat komst gau genôch to witen.\"\nIn pear dagen letter fordronk ús lytse Ealse.\nBeppe fortelde dat se dat al in skoft fan tofoaren witen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22013,"r":"CJ031310","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman predicts that her sister, who lives in great poverty, is now past the hardest times. It comes true exactly.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik siet froeger bot yn 'e earmoed. 'k Hie trettsjin bern, twa wienen stoarn. 't Kaem o sa krap om.\nOp in kear kaem myn suster Hiltsje by ús (= H. Reitsma- Wijbinga, Koaten B65-267, 273, 274, 280)\nDoe't se wer fuortgong brocht ik har in eintsje. Doe lei se my de hân op 't skouder en sei: \"Hiske, dû hast dyn greatste earmoed hawn, hear!\"\nHja hat it goed sjoen. 'K Ha gjin lijen wer hawn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22014,"r":"CJ031311","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman tells her sister that her husband has bought a house. It comes true exactly.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear doe hienen wy ús hûs forkocht. Mar wy hienen noch net in oar hûs, dat wy wisten net, hwer't wy de maeijes komme soenen.\nHiltsje kaem by my. Wy wennen doe noch oan 't Wyldpaed. Hja woe wite of wy al wer in hûs hienen.\n\"Hast al plak?\" frege se my.\nIk sei: \"Né. Kei is der om fuort. 'k Wyt net hoe't it komt.\"\nKei bleau wei. Hiltsje gong op 't lêst fuort en ik brocht har in eintsje.\nUnderweis sei se ynienen tsjin my: \"Dû hast plak. Kei hat it hûs kocht.\"\nIt wie sa. Doe't Kei thúskaem, fortelde er my dat er it hûs kocht hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24605,"r":"CJ047903","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul predicts the time of a farmer's death to the minute. He also foresees that the neighbour's horse will be harnessed to the hearse, because the farmer's own horses refuse.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Surhústerfean wenne in man, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Syn kammeraet frege him us in kear: \"Wyst ek hwat?\"\n\"Ja,\" sei er, \"der komt in greate boer to forstjerren.\" Hy neamde dy en dy datum en de ûre en de minút der by.\n\"It hynder,\" sei er, \"dat se foar de wein spanne wol net lûke. Dan wurdt it oare hynder fan 'e boer foar de wein spand. Mar dat wol likemin lûke. Dan spanne se it hynder fan 'e buorman der foar. Dàt hynder lûkt wòl.\"\nIt wie krekt sa útkom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24606,"r":"CJ047904","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A labourer astonishes those around him by selling his favourite sheep. When people ask him why he sold the beloved animal, he answers that he has 'his reasons'. Two days later the sheep drowns. The labourer had foreseen the drowning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit hat in arbeider kend, dy hie in prachtich skiep. Dêr wied er tige wiis mei en hy woe 't net heal misse. Safolle koenen se him net biede. En doch forkocht er it op in dei. Dat like fremd. Us heit frege him: \"Hwerom ha jo dat skiep forkocht? Jo wienen der sa wiis mei.\"\n\"Dêr hie 'k in reden foar\", sei dy arbeider.\nTwa dagen letter fordronk it skiep.\nDat hie de arbeider foarút al sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24607,"r":"CJ047905","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul predicts that the inn will burn down on market day. It turns out exactly that way.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Pein, dêr wenne froeger ien, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Heit frege him us in kear: \"Wite jo ek noch hwat fan 'e takomst?\"\n\"Ja,\" sei er, \"de herberch brânt op 'e joun fan Drachtster Merke ôf.\"\n't Kom krekt sa út. 't Wie de maitiids doe't heit him frege hie en yn 'e hjerst, krekt mei Drachtster Merke, is de herberch opbrând. (by de brêge; op itselde plak, dêr't nou nòch in herberch stiet.)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24609,"r":"CJ047907","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul predicts the moment of a farmer's death to the hour. The clairvoyant also foresees that two black horses will refuse to pull the hearse. In the end a piebald horse will be harnessed to it. It turns out exactly that way.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Surhústerfean wenne in man, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy sei, op dy en dy dei en op dy en dy ûre soe dy en dy boer stjerre.\n\"'k Wyt noch mear\", sei er. \"As se de wein yn oarder meitsje sil de arbeider twa swarte hynders by de boer út it lân helje.\" (De boer hie wol fiif hynders) \"Mar dy hynders sille net in stap gean kinne. Dan sil er in bûnt hynder helje en dat wurdt foar de wein spand. Dan komt it goed.\"\nIt kom krekt sa út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":41585,"r":"OIRSCHOT096","p":"Udenhout","v":"N.-Br.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"In Udenhout, Bet went from door to door telling fortunes. She predicted how long you would live and whether you would become poor or rich. None of it ever came true, however.","i":"L.H.","o":"Handlezen\n\nIn Udenhout kwam regelmatig iemand, die de toekomst kon voorspelle en de hand kon leze. Die kwam altijd aan de deur, een oude vrouw met 'n doek om, een zeker Bet, geloof ik. Maar d'r kwam nooit iets van uit, maar toch ware er veel mense, die erin vloge. Ze kwam gewoonlijk met 'n kind achter op d'r rug in zo'n doek. Ze ging dan zegge hoe lang ge nog leefde, of ge rijk of arm zou worde.","l":"Noord-Brabants"},{"n":22015,"r":"CJ031401","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman predicts to her unmarried, pregnant niece that the future will not turn out badly for her. It comes true exactly.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear kaem myn suster Hiltsje by my, doe siet myn dochter ek by ús yn 'e hûs. Dy hie in poppe oerwoun. Dêr hie se net in man foar. 't Like dus net sa aerdich foar har. Sy wie hwat fortrietlik.\nDoe sei Hiltsje tsjin myn dochter: \"Nou fanke, dû hoechst net muoilik to wêzen, hear. Dû krigest it hiel bêst.\"\nEn 't is ek sa kaem. 't Giet har nou hiel goed en har jonge kin tige leare. (Hiltsje, zie B65-267, 273, 274)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22016,"r":"CJ031402","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman already had visions of the future as a young girl.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hiltsje hie soks al oan har, doe wie 't noch mar in fanke. Doe seach se al dingen dy't letter gebeure soenen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22041,"r":"CJ031607","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"If someone is born with a caul, you would do well to burn the caul. Otherwise the person will be constantly driven out of bed at night to foresee deaths in passing funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wie ien mei de helm geboaren, dan moest dy helm opbrând wurde. Dienen se dat net, dan moest sa'n ien letter altyd út bêd wei en der op út om lykstaesjes to sjen","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22055,"r":"CJ031806","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"It is said that of seven daughters, one remains childless. It does not always come true, for in one particular family all seven daughters had children. One of those girls always has visions of the future: she often has to get up at night to see funeral processions pass by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By Albert Land fan 'e Harkema wienen sawn dochters. Der wurdt altyd sein, as der sawn famkes binne, kriget ien dêrfan gjin bern. Mar dizzen hienen allegear bern. Mar der wie al ien by - dy leeft noch - dy mat nachts altyd út bêd. Dan mat se lykstaesjes sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22056,"r":"CJ031807","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Wopke the devil-banisher gives a man tormented by nightmares a potion to take home. He must guard the bottle well on the way home, for the devil will try to take the medicine from him to prevent his cure, says Wopke. Wopke's prediction comes true: a little man smashes the bottle with a stick. When the man sets off home a second time with a new potion, Wopke predicts that a fellow with two dogs will come towards him. Wopke advises the man to keep his hand firmly on his chest while he walks in a wide arc around the fellow. The man follows Wopke's advice and manages to escape his second attacker.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Pake hie lêst fan de nachtmerje. Doe gong er nei greate Wopke ta. Dy wenne yn Kûkherne. Doe joech Wopke him in drank. Hy sei tsjin pake: \"Tink der om, dat se dy de drank ûnderweis net stikken slagge.\"\nDoe sei pake: \"Hwa duvel soe my dy drank stikken slaen.\"\nDoe't der in eintsje op stap wie, kom der in mynhearke oan, dy swaeide mei syn stok en rekke it drankje.\nIt drankje wie yn flarden.\nDoe pake werom nei Wopke.\n\"Hwat ha 'k dy sein?\" sei Wopke.\nPake krige foar de twadde kear in drank. \"Nou komst aenst in keardel tsjin mei twa grouwe hounen. Dêr stapst wiid om hinne en hâld goed de hân op 'e bûse dêr't de drank yn sit.\"\n't Kom krekt sa út. Mar pake paste nou wol op dat de drank hiel bleau, en hy kom der goed mei thús.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22077,"r":"CJ031913","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"In the past many people consulted a certain fortune-teller, Thomas Klare, when they wanted to know the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Thomas Klare fan Houtigehage, dêr gongen se meastal hinne as se de takomst wite woenen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22078,"r":"CJ031914","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Two men have a little old woman tell their future from coffee grounds. It comes true exactly as the woman predicts.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie us op in kear mei de autobus yn Ljouwert.\nPiter Schievink fan 'e Harkema dy wenne doe by de Singel, dy wie by my.\nPiter sei: \"Sille wy us nei de wiersizter ta?\" Ik sei \"Ja\".\nWy der togearre hinne. Dat minske seach alles út it kofjedik. Sy fortelde Piter syn hiele levensgeskidenis. Hwat der mei him gebeurd wie, dat kloppe allegear presys.\nSy sei tsjin him: \"Dû giest aenst oer 't wetter en fuort.\"\nDat wie oer de Feanster feart nei Grins ta. Dat is neikom. Piter is nei Grins ta gong to wenjen.\n\"Dêr silst hiel hwat bileve\", sei se. \"Nei jierren silst in lyk wer nei Harkema tabringe. Ast dat dien hast, dan nimste smokkel mei yn 'e lykwein.\"\nDat is útkom. Hy hat yn 'e oarloch syn frou forlern. Sy is yn 'e lykwein nei Harkema ta brocht en hy hat yn dyselde lykwein in deade baerch werom nei Grins ta smokkele.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22120,"r":"CJ032601","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A card reader tells a woman that she is going to have a very hard time. Shortly afterwards the woman is widowed and left with nine children. Coffee-ground readers are also often consulted to foretell the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mem hat us by in kaertlizter yn Ljouwert west. Dy hat tsjin mem sein: \"Hwat krije jo in swier jok to dragen, frou. Mar hâld de moed der yn.\"\nMem hat heit al jong forlern. Sy bleau sitten mei njoggen bern. Hja hat it o sa swier hawn.\nDe lju gongen ek wol nei Thomas' Clare, mar dy koe 't sa goed net. Dy seach yn 't kofjedik (anderen vertellen dat ze kaarten gebruikte).","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22168,"r":"CJ033407","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A card reader tells a woman that she will not marry her current boyfriend. The courtship will soon end and shortly afterwards the woman will marry another, blond, man. It turns out exactly that way.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie forkearing, en ik hie ek earder forkearing hawn.\nDoe kom ik us in kear by âlde Tryn Snipel yn 'e hûs. Dy wenne oan 'e Spekloane. Tryn die de blinen ticht. Doe lei se de kaert.\n\"Ien, twa, trije, fjouwer, dat stiet dy wis\", sei se, en doe: \"Ien, twa, trije, fjouwer, dat komt dy oer\", en wylst krige se de kaerten fan 'e tafel.\nMei deselde dêrstû nou forkearing mei haste, dêr silst net mei trouwe. Dû troust mei in oaren ien, dat is in blonde man, en it duorret net lang mear.\nSe krige gelyk. Trije wiken letter rekke myn forkearing út.\n7 wiken letter troude ik mei de blonde man. Dat wie myn earste man: Rinse van Houten fan Eastemar, in soan fan Marten van Houten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22252,"r":"CJ034003","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman born with a caul often has to get up at night to see things.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As fanke gong ik wol mei de klaei op. Yn Uthústermeden wienen wy nachts yn in skuorre. Heit wie dêr keppelbaes. Dêr wie ek in frou by ús, dat wie Durk Mozes syn muoike. Dat minske moest der nachts faek op út. Ik frege heit: \"Hwerom docht se dat?\"\nHeit sei: \"Sy is mei de helm geboaren. Sy mat hwat sjen.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22293,"r":"CJ034326","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant woman is often driven out of bed at night to see things.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw in kammeraetske hawn, dy gong der nachts wol ôf. Dan moest se hwat sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22330,"r":"CJ034522","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A card reader tells a woman that she will have two children. It turns out exactly that way.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Akke Kaert wenne yn Ljouwert (onjuist). Hja wie kaertlizter. Op in kear kom der in faem út 'e Harkema by har. Dy woe wite, hoefolle bern as se krije soe. Akke Kaert rekkene en rekkene. Sy hâldde even op, doe sei se: \"Och heden, der binne twa.\" 't Is sekuer útkom. (Sjoerd Kooistra hat sels 2 bern. Wie 't syn wiif?)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22342,"r":"CJ034601","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant farmhand with a sore arm turns out to have been injured at night when he was roughly thrown out of his bed to see things.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wenne in man op Koatstertille, dat wie Gauke Haagsma. Anders Faber wie de boer by hwa't er wenne. Gauke hie op in kear in seare earm. Doe wienen wy by de boer yn 'e skuorre oan 't terskjen. Ik frege him hoe't er dat krige hie. Mar dêr woed er net rjocht azem op jaen. De oare deis klage er wer oer de earm. Ik sei: \"Hwat skeelt der eins oan dy earm?\"\nDoe sei er: \"Ik sil 't dy ek wol sizze. Ik bin fóársjend en mei de helm geboaren. Ik lei earjusternacht op bêd. Doe moest ik der hiel hastich út, ik koe sa hurd net. Doe bin ik der út smiten woarn. Doe kom ik mei de earm tsjin 'e pomp oan. Dêr haw ik my sa oan stompt. Ik moest doe alhiel nei Burgum ta rinne.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22343,"r":"CJ034602","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul foresees the arrival of German soldiers in the Second World War twenty-five years beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear wienen hy en ik op 'e Alddyk. De boer sels wie der ek by. Doe sei Gauke: \"Hjir komme skielk soldaten. Dy sille hjir skoftsje. Sy komme de kant fan Grins út wei. Dat kin noch wol twintich jier oanhâlde, ek wol fiif en twintich jier.\"\nWy wienen doe mei ús trijen oan 't skoftsjen doe't er dat fortelde.\nIt is neikom yn 1945. Doe binne de Dútsers hjirhinne kom en sy ha by Koaten skofte. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22344,"r":"CJ034603","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A little boy is born with a caul. The doctor fears that the child will have visions of the future at night all his life.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn Bûtenpost is us in jonkje geboaren noch net sa mâlle lang lyn. Dy hie ek in helm oer de egen. Dokter sei: \"As ik it flues der forkeard ôflûk, dan is de jonge syn libben lang ûngelokkich. Dan mat hy der nachts ôf to sjen.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22679,"r":"CJ034607","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man foresees the funeral of his daughter, who drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Under Kollumersweach wenne Knjillis Veenstra. Dy hat de bigraffenis fan syn eigen dochter fan tofoaren sjoen. Hja is fordronken yn 'e Spoarsleat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22765,"r":"CJ035316","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant often has to get up at night to foresee funerals.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Twizeler Mieden wenne froeger Gearte Wekke.\n(Letter hat Jelke van der Valle yn dat hûs wenne)\nWekke seach bigraffenissen fan tofoaren. Sy moest der dan nachts út. Sy koe ûnmooglik lizzen bliuwe.\nSoms moest se hiele einen fuort om to sjen. As se it dan sjoen hie dan sei se de oare deis soms: \"Dy en dy stjert gau. Ik ha de bigraffenis sjoen. En ik haw èk sjoen hwa't der by roannen.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22766,"r":"CJ035317","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant often has to get up at night to foresee funerals.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Eibert Veenstra syn heit wenne yn 't Wêst fan Bûtenpost. Dy moest ek altyd nei bigraffenissen sjen. Hy moest der yn 'e nacht út. En dan mocht er net op 'e wei lâns gean, mar alhiel oan 'e kant.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22825,"r":"CJ036103","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Many young girls visit a coffee-ground reader to have their future foretold.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Burgum wenne âlde Albertsje Brjit oan 'e Menno van Coehoornweg. Dy Albertsje koe kopkekike. Dêr gongen faek jongfammen hinne om de takomst fan har to fornimmen. Hja seach yn 't kofjedik. It kom altyd wol aerdich út, seinen se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22831,"r":"CJ036109","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Whoever has a caul can see into the future.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":22848,"r":"CJ036205","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman always foresees sad things such as illnesses and deaths.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wenne in frou yn Bûtenpost, dy fornom ek dingen fan tofoaren. Dat wienen altyd treurige dingen, lyk as sykte en forstjerren ensa. 't Forrin fan 'e sykte en de dea fan har man hat se allegear fan tofoaren krekt sa sjoen as it gebeurd is. Letter is se nei Grins ta gong to wenjen. Sy is nou al dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22875,"r":"CJ036404","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A fortune teller makes predictions to two men about their future work and home and warns them to be careful of loose pieces of wood on the road to avoid accidents. Her predictions come true exactly.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie mei Bareld de Meer nei Snits ta to monsterjen. Mei de strikel yn 'e binnenbûse, om to ûngetiidzjen. Mar wy krigen beide gjin wurk. Bareld sei: \"Sille wy even nei Lytse Kjille ta op 'e Gerdyk? Dat wie in wiersizter.\nWy der hinne.\nKjille sei tsjin my: \"Binne jo troud?\"\n\"Ja\", sei 'k.\n\"Krij dan mar safolle kaerten\", sei se. Hja hie de kaerten út it laed helle fan 'e tafel. Hja gong by in stove op, sa kom se op 'e stoel. Sa lyts wie se.\n\"Om wurk út west?\" sei se. \"Ungetiidzje?\"\n\"Ja.\"\n\"En gjin wurk krige?\"\n\"Né\", sei 'k.\n\"Mar jo hà wurk\", sei se. \"Dêr geane jo moarn of oaremoarn hinne. Dêr fortsjinje jo fiifentwintich of seisentwintich goune. Der komt ek in nije wei by jimmes. En jimme komme yn in nij hûs to wenjen, in hoekhûs.\"\nDoe sei se tsjin Bareld: \"Gean jo mar by de wei lâns om skrobbers to forkeapjen. Dêr kinne jo mear fortsjinje as by 't wurk.\"\nIk wie noch mar krekt thús, of dêr kom Anne, dy hie in brief by him. Hy hie in boer biloofd, hy soe nei him ta to ûngetiidzjen, mar hy seach der tsjin oan. Hy woe der graech frij fan. As ik it wol fan him oernimme woe.\nDe oare moarns gong ik mei de brief nei de boer ta.\nHja hie ek noch sein ik moest dêr oer de bartsjes hinne en sy hie my warskôge, ik moest net oer dy bartsjes hinne fytse, hwant dan kommen der ûngelokken. Ik moest der oer hinne stappe.\nIt kom allegear krekt sa út. Der leinen bartsjes. Ik bin der altyd oer hinne st","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22876,"r":"CJ036405","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A fortune teller tells a man that he will receive an inheritance, but that his brother will receive more than he does.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear haw ik wer us nei Kjille west. Doe sei se: \"Der sil yn 't koart in erfdiel wêze. Mar jou broer krijt mear as jo\", sei se. Dat is ek gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22877,"r":"CJ036406","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A fortune teller tells two women that one of them will have five more children and the other one more. It turns out exactly that way.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha der ek us west mei Anne Pultrum. Doe sei se: \"De iene fan jim sil noch fiif bern ha en de oare sil noch ien bern ha.\" Doe't ik it thús fortelde, sei myn wiif: \"Ik hoopje net dat ik dy fan fiif bin\". (Hwant wy hienen al seis.) Anne Pultrum hie mar twa.\nMar 't kom wol sa út: Anne krige letter noch ien en wy noch fiif.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22878,"r":"CJ036407","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A fortune teller predicts that a boy held on suspicion of arson will be released. It turns out exactly that way.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw ek by in frommes yn Grins west. Dat wie in sikere W. Kortstra. Sy wenne yn 'e Meeuwerderstraat. Us hûs op 'e Dwarsfeart wie krekt ôfbrând. Myn soan hie nei de faem west mei de auto. De nachts nei de brân woarde myn soan om ien ûre oanhâlden troch de plysjes.\nDe oare deis gong ik nei de kaertlizter ta, hwant ik woe wite hoe't it komme soe. Ik liet har it portret sjen fan myn soan, dy't oanhâlden woarn wie.\n\"Kinne jo hwat fan dizze persoan fortelle?\" frege ik har.\nHja lei kaerten om 't portret hinne.\n\"Mijnhear,\" sei se, \"deze persoon is op wandeltocht. Hij is al losgelaten en praat al met iemand buiten.\"\nIt kloppe as in bus. Se hienen him nei in pear ûren wer loslitten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22879,"r":"CJ036408","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A fortune teller makes all kinds of predictions about a man's future. Nearly all of them come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ien fan myn soannen hat in healjier lyn nei har ta west.\n\"Gehuwd?\" frege se.\n\"Ja\", sei er.\n\"'k Sjoch ien bern,\" sei se, \"mar 't is krekt as ha jo mear hawn. Sitte der elders ek bern?\"\nHy sei: \"Ja, yn Ljouwert. Ik ha earder troud west.\"\n\"Binne dy bern by de mem?\"\n\"Ja\", sei er.\n\"Binnen trije wiken kinne jo út jou ramen brân sjen, tichte by jo.\"\nBinnen trije wiken seach er de brân, 't wie in garagebrân.\n\"Yn 't foarjier,\" sei se, \"sille jo forhúzje en dan sille jo in saekje keapje en in âlder iemand sil jo dêrta helpe. Jo sille der gjin jild foar ha, mar jo wurde holpen. Jo sille mei twa jier it saekje lyk ha en mei sawn jier boppe Jan wêze.\nMyn soan hat in saekje kocht yn 'e Westerein - in pataetsaek - en dêr hat in oar him ta holpen. Yn 't koart forhûzet er nei de Westerein. It oare leit noch yn 'e takomst.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22922,"r":"CJ036709","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"One of seven boys always has to get up at night to see things. He is clairvoyant.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jasper en Jinke fan 'e Boelensloane hienen sawn jonges. Ien fan dy sawn jonges moest nachts ta 't hûs út om hwat to sjen. Dat wie Gerke Veenstra.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24245,"r":"CJ045120","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often has to get up at night to see things, for example a dead person being carried out of a house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon binne mei de helm geboaren, dy matte der nachts altyd ôf. Ik praette us mei sa'n ien út 'e Harkema, dy seach doe krekt dat der ergens in lyk út 'e hûs droegen waerd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24252,"r":"CJ045202","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often has visions of the future. For instance, he foresees exactly when his neighbour's sick child will die and what the funeral will be like.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn buorman wie Piter de Graaf. Dy leeft noch. Hy wennet nou yn it wurkhûs yn Grinzer Pein. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren. Hwat dy ús allegear wol net forteld hat! Hy seach alles fan tofoaren.\nOp in moarn kom ik by harren. \"Hoe is 't mei 't famke?\" frege syn frou. Wy hienen in famke, dat sukkele. 't Bern wie geestlik ek net hielendal goed.\nIk sei: \"Och, wol goed.\" It bern tsjirme, mar dêr wie 'k al sa oan wend, dat dan sei 'k mar \"wol goed\".\nDoe't ik fuort wie, hied er tsjin syn frou sein: \"Sy seit: - Wol goed - Hja moest ris wite, dat it der moarn al net mear is.\" Hy hie alles fan tofoaren sjoen: hwannear't se stoar, hwer't it bern hinne gong en hwa't der fóárgong en alle minsken dy't op 'e begraffenis kommen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24253,"r":"CJ045203","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul advises his wife not to buy school things for their child, because he foresees that the child will die before then. It turns out exactly that way.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear sei Piter de Graaf syn frou: \"Us berntsje mat nou binnenkoart nei skoalle ta. Wy matte hwat klean foar har keapje.\"\nPiter sei: \"Dat hat noch wol tiid, dêr kinne wy noch wol hwat mei wachtsje.\"\nDe deis dat it bern nei skoalle soe, brochten se har nei 't hôf ta. Dat hie Piter fan tofoaren al sjoen. Dêrom hied er sein: \"Dat hat noch wol tiid.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24254,"r":"CJ045204","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often has to get up at night to see things.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Piter de Graaf gong der nachts faek ôf. Dan gong er foar 't glês stean en die de kleden oan kant.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24255,"r":"CJ045205","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul foresees countless deaths.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Piter de Graaf gong froeger wol to nijjiersroppen.\nSa kom er ek us in kear by ús buorlju to nijjierroppen; dy hienen in siik famke.\nFuort dêrnei kom er by ús. 't Wie noch yn 'e iere moarn, doe sei er: \"As ik aenst werom kom, dan is dat famke hjirneist wei.\" Dat is útkom.\nTsien ûre kom er werom, doe wie 't bern al stoarn. (Deselde dy't it berntsje forlern hat, wie Antsje Bruining sj. )\nIk moest doe krekt bifalle. Doe hat er tsjin myn man sein - sûnder dat ik it wiste - : \"Jimme berntsje wurdt dea geboaren.\" Dat is ek útkom. \nUs berntsje en dat fan 'e buorlju binne tagelyk op 't hôf kom.\nHy foarspelde dy kear noch mear. \"As ik rjochts sjoch,\" sei er, \"dan falt dêr ien, dêr't net ien op fordacht is. 't Is in jongkeardel, ien fan Piter Kats.\" (Even letter is dy stoarn)\nDoe sei er: \"Sjoch ik even fierder, dan falt dêr in jong fanke, dêr't net ien op fordacht is.\" ( Dat wie in famke fan sechstjin jier, in dochter fan in sekere Haitsma oan 'e Houtigehaechster wyk, dy't har sels mei 't gewear deasketten hat fanwege forkearingspul)\n\"As ik fierderop sjoch nei rjochts,\" sei er, \"falt dêr in heit út in húshâlding.\" Dat is ek útkom.\nDurkje Bruining (sjoch ), har man foel yn 'e ûngetiid troch in sinnestek.\nDat hat er allegear fantofoaren sjoen. Hy fortelde 't allegearre op nijjiersdei.\nIk wie bang foar dy man.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24257,"r":"CJ045207","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant woman, born with a caul, often foresees funerals.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem seach de dingen ek foarút. Hja hat ek de hiele bigraffenis fan myn soan fan tofoaren sjoen. Hja wie ek mei de helm geboaren. Myn suster ek. Myn pake ek. Twa neven en in nicht ek. 't Sit yn ús famylje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24258,"r":"CJ045207a","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"When the narrator dreams of horses, there is always a death in the family. The more calmly the horses walk, the further off in the future the death is.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As ik oer hynders droom komt der altyd in sterfgefal yn ús famylje. Hwat kalmer as dy hynders binne, hwat langer it duorret mei sa'n sterfgefal.\nAs de hynders wyld binne komt sa'n sterfgefal hiel gau. Dan komme de hynders wyld op my ta. 't Komt altyd út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24294,"r":"CJ045419","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul foresees the death of his own daughter.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hier in 'e bosk (Sweagerbosk) was een man, die sag syn eigen dochter fan teforen dea. Hij was met de helm geboren en ging der 's nachts altyd af. (Knjillis Veenstra?)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24332,"r":"CJ045805","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The narrator's mother often has a premonition that certain things are about to happen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem wist de dingen faek fan tofoaren. Dan sei se: \"Ik ha in bygefoel. 't Leit my sa raer by, der komt hwat.\" Dan wienen wy deabinaud. Hwant dan gebeurde der fêst hwat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24430,"r":"CJ046318","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Two well-known card readers are Thomas' Clare and Tryn Snipel. Tryn was better at it than Clare.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wennen twa kaertlizters yn dizze kriten. Thomas' Clare yn Houtigehage en Tryn Snipel yn 'e Boelensloane. Tryn koe 't folle better as Clare.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24451,"r":"CJ046505","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A card reader tells a young couple in love that they will not stay together. It turns out exactly that way: the woman later commits adultery.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tryn Snipel dat wie hjir de kaartlegster. Ik kom us in kear by har mei myn faem. Doe seach se yn 'e kaert en sei: \"Hwat ha jim elkoarren leaf. Mar jimme krije elkoar net.\"\nDy faem wie Wypk de Ruiter. Sy is my ûntrou woarn, doe't ik yn Dútslân arbeide. Doe haw ik it útmakke.\nSnipel hie 't goed sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24467,"r":"CJ046701","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"During the First World War, an illiterate old man predicts that yet another war will break out in 1940. The man predicts that a city in the south of the country will suffer heavily and that the queen will flee. The man makes more predictions connected with the war. All the predictions have come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Douwe wie in boerke, dy wenne yn Kollumersweach. Tidens de oarloch fan '14 op '18 sei er: \"As dit ôfroan is, krije wy yn '40 noch in hiele slimme oarloch.\"\nIt mantsje koe lêze noch skriuwe.\n\"In stêd yn it suden fan ús lân,\" sei er, \"kriget der hiel bot fan. Ik bileef it net,\" sei er tsjin myn man syn broer, \"mar jimme sille 't noch wol bilibje. De bern dy't nou nei skoalle gean krije 't swier. En ek deselden dy't noch geboaren wurde.\" Dat wienen de ûnderdûkers.\n\"Yn dy oarloch sil de koaningin fuort gean. Hwant Nederlân sil ek yn 'e oarloch bitrutsen wêze.\nAs se de minsken hjir op Sweagerfean oppakke, dan sil de oarloch gau dien wêze.\"\nDat is útkom: yn jannewaris '45 ha se ds. Hazenberg, Hille Veenstra en dokter Theo de Jager en meester Riemersma ophelle. Doe wie der in frou, dy sei tsjin my: \"Nou, as âlde Douwe gelyk krijt, dan is de oarloch hjir gau ôfroun.\" 15 april binne wy bifrijd. Hy hat gelyk krige.\nYn 't earst fan 'e oarloch soenen se sizze: \"Amerika komt, mar 't wurdt neat.\" As Amerika wer kaem, dan kaem Dútslân ûnder 'e treurebeam. Dan soenen de poepen it forlieze.\nDe koaningin soe ús forlitte. As se wer kaem, dan soe se net folle mear to sizzen ha. En dy't har opfolge, noch minder. Wy soenen in oar regear krije. De negus? soe de earste wêze dy't wer op 'e troan kom.\nDer soe in gebaende wei troch de woastyn komme.\nDe Sahara soe fruchtber lân fan makke wurde.\nDe Jo","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24468,"r":"CJ046702","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Some people visit an illiterate card reader; others want nothing to do with fortune telling.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wenne in kaertlizter, dat wie Japiks Fokje.\nIt minske koe lêze noch skriuwe. Dêr kommen faek minsken út oare doarpen om de kaert lizze to litten. Hja hie gâns oanrin. Mar hjir út Sweagerfean gong net ien nei har ta. Har eigen man sei: \"'t Is wysmakkerij, oars neat.\" Mar hy sei der fuort achteroan: \"Sy kin 't like goed as de minsken út Ljouwert.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24471,"r":"CJ046803","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul always has to get up at night to see things. He often foresees funerals at night. He even foresaw the funerals of his own son and daughter.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Knjillis wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy wenne oan 't spoar ûnder Kollumersweach (Knj. Veenstra).\nWit hoe faek woarde der yn 'e nacht by him kloppe. Dan moest er út bêd wei en de wei út. Soms moest er hiele einen rinne. It is wol gebeurd dat er hielendal nei 't tsjerkhôf fan Kollumersweach ta moest. Dêr woarde dan ien bigraven. Dat moest hy sjen. 't Wie meast yn 'e nacht.\nHy hat de bigraffenis fan syn eigen dochter ek fan tofoaren sjoen. Doe't de kiste by him oer de flier stie koe hy de rotten der mei de heafoarke hast net by wei hâlde.\nHy hat de bigraffenis fan syn soan ek sjoen. Dy wenne yn Grinslân. Dy hat him hjir by syn heit en dy yn 'e parrebeam ophong.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24513,"r":"CJ047105","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman born with a caul often has to get up at night to see funeral processions pass by.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Jochums Antsje wenne dêr't nou de widdou Popma wennet. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren en moest der nachts ôf om lykstaesjes to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24567,"r":"CJ047510","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often foresees funerals. If the caul is pulled forward at birth, the person has no visions of the future. If the caul is pushed upward, the person does have visions of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining is mei de helm geboaren. Hy sjocht de bigraffenissen foarút.\nAs se by de geboarte de helm foaroer lûke, is it goed.\nLûke se de helm omheech, dan sjogge se letter alles.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24662,"r":"CJ049105","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often foresees funerals, down to the smallest details. He also predicted the funeral of his own daughter.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie in kammeraet, dat wie Klaes. Hy wennet yn Grinzer Pein. Syn heit wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy seach alle bigraffenissen foarút. Hy koe fantofoaren sizze: dêr en dêr wurdt ien útdroegen en hy telde altyd de lju dy't achter it lyk oan roannen.\nOp in kear moest er nei de klaei ta to arbeidzjen. Mar de moarns dat er fuort moest, sei er: \"Ik kin wol thús bliuwe, hwant ik mat leed dwaen.\"\nDeselde deis noch stoar der in dochterke fan him. Dat hie er foarút sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24682,"r":"CJ049216","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"One of seven boys or seven girls is clairvoyant.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wienen der sawn jonges of sawn famkes yn 'e hûs, dan wie ien fan harren in persoan dy't alles altyd sjen moest.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24687,"r":"CJ049221","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A card reader predicts to a girl who already has a few children born out of wedlock that she will soon give birth again. It happens exactly so.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Thomas Clare wie kaertlizter.\nIk en noch in faem hawwe us in kear by har west. Dy faem hie al in pear bern oerwoun. Hiltsje Veenstra hiet se.\nClare skodde de kaerten en sy naem der ien út en sei: \"Dit achtsje ik net, dat forwachtsje ik net. Mar famke, dû leist mei dyn njoggen maendtsjes yn 'e skoat.\" Hiltsje sei: \"Och stumper, dat komt my net oer, dan meitsje ik my fan kant.\"\nMar Clare sei: \"'t Komt dy wòl oer, fanke.\"\nEn Clare krige gelyk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24813,"r":"CJ049604","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A girl predicts that an accident is going to happen. That same evening she breaks her arm.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sjoerd de Graaf syn soan hie in famke. Sy wie us in kear oan 't boartsjen, doe sei se tjin har mem:\n\"Der gebeurt joun in ûngelok.\"\nDeselde jouns bruts se it earmke. Dat der hwat gebeurde soe, wist it bern fan tofoaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24814,"r":"CJ049605","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A labourer predicts that an accident is going to happen. That same day he himself has an accident and dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Rapke de Vries wie yn Olterterp yn 'e bosk oan 't wurk. Hy sei: \"Der kin hjoed wolris in ûngelok komme.\" Deselde deis krige er in ûngelok en hy gong dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24815,"r":"CJ049606","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often has to get up at night to see funeral processions pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Piter de Graaf (sjoch B65-443 en 445) wenne op 'e ein fan 'e Dwarsfeart. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren en moest der gauris nachts ôf. Dan seach er hwat. 't Wienen yn 'e regel lykstaesjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24826,"r":"CJ049617","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Card reader Kjille predicts to two men that one of them will never amount to anything. The other will go quite far, according to Kjille. It happens exactly so.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Lytse Kjille wie kaertlizter. Sy hat yn Drachten wenne yn 'e Hounestege en op 'e Bopperein. Letter wenne se op 'e Gerdyk. Hwat Kjille sei kom wol aerdich nei.\nTwa maten gongen us nei har ta. Dat wienen Waetse de Jong en Hindrik de Jong.\nHja sei tsjin Hindrik: \"Jo wurde noait hwat yn 'e wereld.\" Dat is ek útkom, hy hat it noait fierder as arbeider brocht. (Hindrik leeft noch).\nMar tsjin Waetse sei se: \"Jo bringe 't aerdich fier.\"\nDat is ek útkom. Waetse krige in greate meubelsaek op 'e Noard-Kade yn Drachten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24848,"r":"CJ049804","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman predicts that a mortally ill man will not die. Everyone declares her mad, but the woman is proved right: the man is still alive.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn buorman Bauke Brinkman wie tige min. Hy hie kanker en sy seinen allegear, hy soe stjerre. Hy lei yn 't sikenhûs. Mar ik sei: \"Bauke giet net dea en hy komt wer.\"\nDe lju seinen: \"Dat kin net. Hy is sà min.\"\nMar ik sei: \"Hy bliuwt yn libben.\" Hwant ik hie mear sjoen. Hy libbet nòch. 't Is nou al jierren lyn.\nSyn soan wennet nou op 'e buorkerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24884,"r":"CJ050105","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant often has to get up at night to foresee deaths in passing funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Piter de Graaf moest der nachts út. Dan seach er lykstaesjes. Hy koe samar sizze: yn dat en dat hûs giet ien dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24946,"r":"CJ050806","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman born with a caul foresees funerals.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op Fryskepeallen wenne Alle Bergsma. Hy wie skuonmakker. Syn frou wie mei de helm geboaren, dy seach de bigraffenissen foarút.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25066,"r":"CJ050902","p":"Earnewâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul warns a comrade that a funeral procession will soon pass. He already knows the name of the deceased as well. The comrade ignores the warnings and stays standing in the middle of the road. He is promptly seized by the procession and thrown off the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde alris yn Earnewâld dat der twa by elkoar stienen to praten. Doe sei de iene - dy wie mei de helm geboaren - : Dû mast der om tinke, der komt aenst in lykstaesje lâns. Dy en dy is 't en dy komt hjir op 't hôf. Sjoch, sei er, dêr komt it oan.\nDe oare sei: Ik sjoch neat, dû kinst wol méár sizze.\nGean oan kant, sei de oare.\nDoe gong er oan kant, mar net lang genôch.\nHy waerd yn 'e midden fan 'e lykstaesje oppakt en oer 't lân smiten.\nWolst it nou wol leauwe tink, sei deselde dy't mei de helm geboaren wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25085,"r":"CJ051102","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"In the old days people already foresaw that there would be carriages without horses and ships without sails. The premonitions have come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In de tijd van mijn moeke's vader seiden se al: \"Der komme wagens sonder peerden en skippen sonder seilen.\" Dat is útkommen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25088,"r":"CJ051201","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Card reader Hinke Kaart often makes predictions about the future that come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik kom wol us by Hinke Kaert. Dêr mocht ik graech hinne gean. Hwat dy sei dat kom sekuer nei. Jy koenen ek oer óáre minsken hwat to witen komme by Hinke. Hwa't jy mar neamden, dêr fortelde se hwat fan.\nHja hie tichte by har in snúfdoaske stean, dat brûkte se sa nou en dan.\nMyn skoanheit wie widner. Myn skoansuster wenne by him. Ik woe hwat fan 'e takomst fan har wite. Hinke sei, hja krige in lyts swart mantsje. It kom út.\nIk siet der ris wer op in snein, doe kommen der trije froulju yn. Ik siet der by doe't Hinke 't tsjin dy froulju hie.\nTsjin ien fan dy froulju sei se: \"Nou ha jo forkearing mei sa'n bêste feint, mar jo binne net mei ien tofreden.\"\nDy faem krige sa'n kop!\n'k Hie myn swager hwat jild liend foar in skip.\nHinke sei tsjin my: \"Dat jild kinne jo wol ûnder 'e soal fan jou skoech strike.\" Dat wie èk sa. Ik krige 't net wer.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25090,"r":"CJ051203","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often has to get up at night to see funeral processions pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Egbert de Jong fan 'e Himrik wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest der nachts út. Dan gong er foar 't glês stean en dan seach er lykstaesjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25130,"r":"CJ051604","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man foresees the funeral of an acquaintance down to the smallest details. The premonition comes true: a few days later the acquaintance dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jan Visser fan 'e Westerein seach by dei de bigraffenis foarút fan Jan Meijer, dy't achter him wenne.\nDoe frege Jan Visser syn mem him of er it wol goed sjoen hie.\n\"Jawis ha 'k it goed sjoen\", sei er, en doe neamde er de nammen op fan 'e lju dy't der by wienen.\nIn pear dagen letter stoar âlde Meijer. Deselden dy't er sjoen hie roannen achter 't lyk oan.\nJan Visser wie doe noch frijgesel. Doe't er troud wie kom syn mem by him yn to wenjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25142,"r":"CJ051616","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A card reader makes all kinds of predictions. She predicts to two young women that they will each get a new bicycle. The two women each have a child.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Thomas Clare wie kaertlizter.\nIk ha 't ris meimakke, doe sieten der twa jonge froulju. Ik siet der flak by, mar sy koenen my net sjen.\nMar ik koe alles hearre.\n\"Dû hast in swarten,\" sei Klare, \"dy loert op dy.\"\n\"Nòch ien, dy wol der tusken.\"\n\"D_ is wòl fortroud, d_ nèt.\"\n\"Jimme krije èk hwat nijs, beide in nije fyts.\"\nHja krigen beide in poppe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25168,"r":"CJ052003","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul are bulletproof. Doctors are very keen on the cauls.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't in helm hat, is kûgelfrij. In dokter wol sa'n helm wol keapje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25219,"r":"CJ052316","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A card reader keeps drawing a card showing a little black man with a yellow note and suspects it means something. It is an omen: the following Monday a little black man appears with a telegram, a 'yellow note'. The card reader's father turns out to have died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Kloosterburen wie in keppeltsje folk by de boer oan 't wurk. 't Wie snein en it reinde. Auke Pultrum en Boardzer Bruining fan Boelensloane wienen der ek by.\nBoardzer sei: \"Wy forfele ús. Sil ik jim de kaert lizze?\"\nDoe helle der in spul kaerten foar den dach.\n\"Lûk dêr mar guon út\", sei er.\n\"Heden,\" sei er doe, \"ik ha iderkear in swart mantsje mei in giel briefke. Hyltyd wer. Dat bitsjut hwat -\"\nDe moandeis kom der in telegram yn 'e keet. 't Wie in swart mantsje dy't it brochte. 't Telegram wie giel. It telegram wie foar Boardzer Bruining bistimd. Boardzer die 't telegram iepen.\n\"Us heit is overleden\", sei er. \"Ha 'k jimme snein net sein, dat der in swart mantsje wie mei in giel briefke?\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25267,"r":"CJ052614","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A fortune teller reads a man's palm and predicts that he will not marry his current sweetheart and will receive a large sum of money from an inheritance. The predictions come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ienkear haw ik by in wiersizter west. Dat wie lytse Kjille. Dy wenne doe yn 'e Hounestege yn Drachten. Sy seach my yn 'e hân. \"Jo ha in faem,\" sei se, \"mar dêr trouwe jo net mei.\"\nDat is ek útkom. Ik ha trije jier forkearing mei har hawn, mar ik bin net mei har troud.\n\"Jo sille ek noch sinten erve\", sei se. Dêr leaude ik neat fan, hwant der wie by ús famylje neat to erven. Mar sy hat wol gelyk krige. Doe't ik letter troude, haw ik fan famylje fan myn frou in moai dofke jild erfd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25302,"r":"CJ052907","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A person born with a caul is one from a family with an odd number of boys. Those who see funeral processions are werewolves.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei de helm geboaren wurdt is ien fan in ûneven tal jonges. Deselden dy't lykstaesjes sjen matte, dat binne wjerwolven.\nMyn broer Hindrik is mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25309,"r":"CJ053004","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often has to get up at night to see things.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Rapke Wijma syn heit Sytse Wijma wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy moest der yn 'e nacht faek ôf. Hy hie 't der net bêst mei.\n(Rapke Wijma werd vermoord. Er is een bekend straatlied van. A.A.J.)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25350,"r":"CJ053320","p":"Ons Belang","v":"Utr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The caul of a newborn is burned or pocketed by greedy doctors. The caul of a person born with a caul is worth a lot of money. People born with a caul have premonitions and often have to get up at night to see, for example, funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Woarde der in bern geboaren mei in helm, dan woarde dy yn 'e measte gefallen fuort opbrând. Mar de dokters knoffelen sa'n helm ek wol us achterút, hwant sy koenen him djûr forkeapje.\nDy't mei de helm geboaren binne, matte alles sjen. Sy geane nachts fan bêd ôf en der út. Dan treffe se lykstaesjes, dy't ûnderweis binne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25364,"r":"CJ053404","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A person born with a caul whose caul was removed the wrong way at birth often has premonitions. Usually such people see funeral processions. The narrator knew someone who was often driven out of his house to see things.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei de helm geboaren is moat fan alles fan tofoaren sjen. Meast lykstaesjes. Tominsten as se de helm der forkeard ôflûke.\nSa'n mantsje hat hjir wenne. Bontsje Keeke neamden se him (= Knjillis Veenstra). Dy koe noait thús bliuwe as hy der út moest. Dan woarde er út it bêd weiraemd. Hwant hy mocht net to let komme.\nHy fleach yn in sucht oer de hekken hinne, doe wie er al net sa jong mear.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25395,"r":"CJ053605","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A certain man was born with a caul.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":25445,"r":"CJ054101","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A fortune teller makes all kinds of predictions to a former prisoner. The predictions come true exactly.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie fochten. 'k Hie ien in wân op 'e hûd jown.\nDoe krige ik in jier gefangenisstraf.\n'k Sei: \"'k Wol us nei Hinke Kaert ta. Dy wenne op Nijebrêge.\"\nDoe't ik der oan ta wie, kom der krekt in âld-mantsje wei. 't Wie in skipper. Hy lei dêr mei 't skip.\n\"Sy hat my wiis makke, ik krige in nij skip, yn 't koart\", sei er. \"Hwat tinkt jo dêrfan?\"\nIk sei neat.\nDoe sei er: \"It nije skip, dat is myn deakiste.\"\nDoe't ik by Hinke wie, sei se tsjin my: \"Jo ha ek al in fiere reis makke.\"\nIk sei: \"Kin ik hjir net lizze mei in wenskip?\"\n\"Né,\" sei se, \"jo wenje dêr en dêr yn in hûs.\" It kloppe.\n\"En jo ha èk forkearing\", sei se.\nIk bearde dat ik fan neat wist en sei: \"Né, wol?\"\n\"Ja,\" sei se, \"'t is famylje fan de jonge, dy't se fêsthâlden ha. Jo binne in ûngelovige Thomas. Sil 'k jo ris sizze, hwat jou gedachten wienen ûnderweis? Ik sil Hinke hwat wysmeitsje.\"\nIt wie sa. Ik tochte: \"Nou sil 'k fierder iepen kaert mei har spylje.\"\n\"Jo komme wer foar 't rjocht,\" sei se, \"hwant jo ha nòch hwat útheve. Dêr easket de ofsier nòch méar foar, mar 't wurdt neat.\"\nIt is krekt sa útkom.\nDoe sei se: \"As jo út 'e gefangenis komme, is Hinke der net mear.\" \"Nou ha 'k in soan,\" sei se, \"dy is mei de lulke holle nei Amearika gien. Hy antwurdet my net mei syn stive holle op myn brieven.\"\nIk ha in healjier út sitten.\nHinkemoai wie dea doe't ik los kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25482,"r":"CJ054502","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A card reader predicts to a young man that he will get new clothes. The prediction comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Antsje Snipel koe kaertlizze. Sy koe èk tsjoene, seinen se.\nIt kaertlizzen kostte in kwartsje. Mar har suster Tryn Snipel koe 't better. Dêr gong ik us in kear mei myn neef hinne. Ik wie doe sawntsjin jier.\nIk frege har: \"Ha jo ek hwat ûnder 'e koark, Tryntsje?\"\n\"Né, nou net\", sei se. Hja forkochten dêr wol drank.\n\"Wolle jo ús de kaert lizze?\"\n\"Jawol,\" sei se, \"dat kostet in kwartsje de man.\"\nHja skodde de kaerten trochinoar. Wy moesten útlûke.\nDe kaerten dy't wy útlutsen lei se út elkoar op 'e tafel del. Doe sei se tsjin my: \"Jo krije ek in pakje klean.\"\nDat hie se goed. Mem wie dy deis krekt om in pakje klean foar my nei Drachten ta.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25994,"r":"CJ058211","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man who was born with a caul had predicted in advance that there would be a cinema in the church.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining fan 'e Boelensloane hat foarspeld, dat it tsjerkje fan ds. Overdyk op Luchtenveld, dêr komt skielk in bioskoop foar yn 't plak. Boardzer is mei de helm geboaren, dy kin 't wite.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26056,"r":"CJ058520","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Douwe Stavasius was born with a caul. A boy had an accident with the chicken cart. He was carried to the road on a ladder as quickly as possible. Douwe said it was no use, the boy would die anyway. He had already seen the funeral. The boy died on the way.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Douwe Stavasius wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy wenne yn Grinzer Pein. Dêr wenne ek in jonge, dy krige in ûngelok mei de kipkarre. Doe woarde er op 'e leider nei de wei ta brocht.\nDouwe sei: \"Dat kinne se wol dwaen, mar 't jowt neat. De jonge komt dea werom.\" En 't wie ek sa. Hy is ûnderweis stoarn. Douwe hie syn bigraffenis al sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26068,"r":"CJ058612","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Two men were going to Groningen together to work. The day before, one of them said he would not go because he had seen that one of his relatives would die. A few days later one of his children died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Douwe Stavasius soe mei dikke Yntsje fan 'e Grinzer Pein to sichtsjen nei de klaei. De deis fan tofoaren sei Douwe tsjin Yntsje: \"Ik gean moarn net mei.\"\n\"Né?\" sei Yntsje.\n\"Né,\" sei er, \"hwant ik ha sjoen dat der ien by ús stoarn is.\"\nIn pear dagen letter stoar ien fan syn bern.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26298,"r":"CJ060603","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Douwe Stavasius was born with a caul and predicts deaths, and he laid out his own mother in advance. They live in a sod house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir achterút hat in man wenne, dat wie Douwe Stavasius. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy seach allerhande sterfgefallen foarút. Hy hat syn eigen mem mei ôflein. Dat die er fan tofoaren al, wylst se noch libbe. Letter hat er it ècht dien.\nSy wennen yn in spittekeet.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26919,"r":"CJ061811","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Hindrik Pikelhearring is walking with someone else in Pein when he foresees that a dead person is coming by and that they must make way. They step aside. He sees funeral processions in advance because he was born with a caul.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hindrik Pikelhearring (= H. v.d. Molen) roan us mei in man op hjir yn 'e Pein. Underweis sei er tsjin dy man: \"Mast even oan kant gean, der komt in lyk oan.\"\nDy oare die dat. In koart skoftsje dêrnei wie der in lyk. \nDy Hindrik Pikelhearring wie mei de helm geboaren, dy seach altyd lykstaesjes. (dy oare dat wie ús heit. Hy sei op syn Grinslâns: Moest even oan 'e kant goan, Been, want der komt wat oan.\")","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26992,"r":"CJ062604","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Douwe Stavasius can foresee things, such as someone's death, or a sick person who later dies, whose entire funeral procession he already sees.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wenne in man, dat wie Douwe Stavasius. As der ien dea gong, dan moest er dat sjen. As der ien tige siik wie, dan kom er by 't glês. Dan seach er fan dyselde de hiele lykstoet. Sa'n ien stoar dan faek al gau.\nHy moest it sjen. 't Kom altyd nei hwat er seach.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27113,"r":"CJ063619","p":"Soesterberg","v":"Utr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman in Zeist has an expensive gold watch and loses it. A man from Soesterberg points out the spot where the watch is and also says that the cleaning lady wants to steal it. The man is clairvoyant.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Een vrouw in Zeist had een duur gouden horloge. 't Kostte achthonderd en vijftig gulden. Dat raakte ze kwijt. Toen kwam er toevallig een man uit Soesterberg bij haar, die ik heel goed ken. Die zei tegen haar: \"Ik zie je horloge, je bent het niet kwijt.\" Hij wees de plek aan. 't Was voor niemand zichtbaar. 't Zat achter de haardplaat voor een Engelse schoorsteen.\nHij zei: \"Ik weet ook wie het daar heeft neergelegd. Je arbeidster, die het stelen wil.\" Die man was helderziende."},{"n":27206,"r":"CJ064112","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Someone born with a caul can see everything. Tsjitske Spinder is such a person.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ien dy't mei de helm geboaren is, mat alles sjen. Njonken ús wenne Tsjitske Spinder. Dy seach èk alles.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27280,"r":"CJ064420","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Thomas Clare, Antsje Snipel, Tryn Snipel and Durkje Snipel are all card readers. They work as follows. They look at the pictures, get nine cards, lay them on the table counting aloud and look at the cards one by one. Someone will, for example, get into trouble with the police but will not have to go to prison, and a small inheritance also awaits him. She shuffles the cards again and lays them out again. She always adds: 'this you don't expect and that you don't expect' and 'across the broad road a house, but that will surely turn out well'. Then she tells of coming events in a person's life. It costs a quarter.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Thomas Clare wie ek in kaertlizter. Sy hie 't fan har mem Antsje Snipel leard. Antsje har suster Tryn Snipel koe 't ek. En Clare har dochter Durkje kin it ek. Sy dienen it allegear neffens itselde resept:\nClare sei: \"Even yn 'e printsjes sjen.\"\nDan krige se njoggen kaerten en sei, wylst hja se dellei op 'e tafel: \"Ien, twa, trije, fjouwer, fiif, seis, sawn, acht, njoggen.\"\nSy krige in kaert, biseach him, en sei: \"'t Liket net sa bêst foar dy.\" Dan krige se in oare kaert en sei: \"Dat liket èk net sa bêst. Krigest drokte mei de plysje. Hoechst net bang to wêzen, dû giest de kast net yn.\"\nHja krige wer in kaert en sei: \"En der stiet dy èk noch in lyts erfskip to wachtsjen.\" En sa gong dat mar troch.\nDan nom se de kaerten wer by inoar, skodde se even troch en lei se wer út. En hja sei wer: \"Ien, twa, trije, fjouwer, fiif, seis, sawn, acht, njoggen.\" En dan sei se der altyd achteroan: \"Dit acht je niet en dat verwacht je niet.\" En \"Oer de brede wei in hûs mei greate beammen. Mar dit komt seker wis\": En dan bigoun se to fortellen, hwat der fierder yn 't libben gebeure soe. (Earmoed, yn 't Sikenhûs en alsamear)\n't Kostte in kwartsje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27400,"r":"CJ065307","p":"Rohel","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Knjillis Veenstra was born with a caul. He saw in advance that his own son would hang himself. He also saw in advance that his daughter would drown in the ditch. And he foresaw the death of his eldest daughter.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Knjillis Veenstra wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy hat fan tofoaren sjoen dat syn eigen soan Egbert him opknoopte.\nHy hat ek fan tofoaren sjoen dat syn dochter har yn 'e sleat forsûpt hat.\nHy hat ek de dea fan syn âldste dochter fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27488,"r":"CJ066302","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man sees a woman's funeral in advance; she dies in childbirth.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Grinzerpein wenne in jonge faem, dy moest bifalle. Hja skreau har Weima. Doe wie dêr in man dy hat har bigraffenis fan tofoaren sjoen. Hja is yn 'e kream forstoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27549,"r":"CJ066901","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man who was born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. That way he knew in advance that someone was going to die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy moest nou en dan út bêd wei nachts, dan moest hy der út om hwat to sjen.\nWy hienen in famke dat siik wie. Hy sei tsjin my: \"Jimme hâlde dat famke net, hwant ik haw de lykstaesje sjoen.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27550,"r":"CJ066902","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man who was born with a caul saw that a healthy man would soon die. It came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wyt ek noch dat er us sei: Hedzers Baeije Hedzer is nou noch soun, mar dat duorret net lang mear. Ik ha sjoen dat er to hôf brocht wurdt. It is neikom. It duorre mar in pear wiken doe woarde er siik en doe is er stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27573,"r":"CJ067106","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man who was born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. That way he always knew in advance that someone would die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Douwe Stavasius wenne op 'e (Grinzer) Peinder heide. Dy gong der nachts wol op út. Dan stie er oan 'e kant fan 'e wei en seach in lykstaesje foarbygean. Hy sei fantofoaren: \"Dy is nou oan 'e beurt.\" 't Kom altyd út. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27601,"r":"CJ067405","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Boardzer Bruining always saw funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn 'e Boelensloane wennet Boardzer Bruining. Dy moest altyd lykstaesjes sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27671,"r":"CJ068017","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man saw funeral processions passing by at night. A while later there was then always a real funeral.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw wol ien kend yn Surhuzum, dy seach wolris fan tofoaren dat der in lykstaesje foarby gong. In skoftsje letter wie der dan in echte bigraffenis.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27784,"r":"CJ069103","p":"Franeker","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman always saw many things happen in advance, including funerals.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Janke Mozes fan 'e Harkema - de dochter fan Klaes Mozes - seach in hiel soad foarút. Sy wist ek altyd krekt hwannear't der wer in bigraffenis komme soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27817,"r":"CJ069404","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman who was born with a caul saw funeral processions in advance. That way she always knew that someone would die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir hat in frou wenne, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy seach fan tofoaren lykstaesjes. Hja wist altyd as der ien stjerre soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27862,"r":"CJ069901","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Eight years after a woman has seen her nephew's funeral in a dream, the funeral becomes reality, exactly as she dreamed it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn man hie in suster dy hie in jonkje, dat hiet fan Bokke. Dy wie nei myn man neamd. It bern wie sa soun as in fisk.\nHy wie fjouwer jier, doe droomde ik op in nacht. Wylst ik op bêd lei seach ik in hiele bigraffenis. It wie Bokke dy't stoarn wie. Ik seach de kiste, de krânse, de skoalbern, de skoalmaster, alles seach ik. 't Wie yn 'e neinacht, yn jannewaris.\nAcht jier letter as doe't ik it droomde is 't gebeurd.\nBokke wie doe tolve jier en gong op skoalle. De master, de skoalbern, alles wie der achteroan. Krekt sa't ik it doe foar acht jier yn 'e droom sjoen hie. 't Is allegear útkom.\nIk wyt noch dat ik dy nacht, doe't ik dat droomd hie, tige binaud wie. Ik die de fuotten bûten 't bêd om mar goed wekker to wurden en 't fan my ôf to setten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28056,"r":"CJ071408","p":"Kornhorn","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman saw the funeral of her sick husband in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Toen mijn man siek was sag ik sien begrafenis. Ik sag de mensen lopen. Fer fan tofoaren. Ik wist alles fooruut.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28183,"r":"CJ072401","p":"Dokkum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman who was born with a caul had seen a funeral. All the men wore top hats except one, who wore a cap. The next day someone from the neighbourhood died. A few days later he was taken to the churchyard. His eldest son walked behind wearing a cap; the other men all wore top hats.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Toen ik nog een jongen was woonde er een oude vrouw naast ons, die was met de helm geboren. Op een keer zei ze tegen mijn moeder: \"Ik heb ook een begrafenis gezien. Allemaal hoge hoeden hadden ze op, maar één van de mannen had een pet op.\"\nDe volgende dag stierf oude Folkert van der Kooi en een paar dagen later werd hij naar 't kerkhof gebracht. Zijn oudste zoon liep er achter met de pet op, de andere mannen droegen allemaal een hoge hoed.\nDie vrouw woonde in Dokkum op de Streek (toen nog Oost-Dongeradeel)"},{"n":28184,"r":"CJ072402","p":"Dokkum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman who was born with a caul once predicted that a towboat would be carrying a corpse that day. Indeed, that evening a towboat arrived with its flag at half-mast.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Diezelfde vrouw zei ook eens een keer tegen moeder: \"Het trekschip neemt vandaag een lijk mee.\"\nAls je een lijk aan boord hebt, moet je de vlag halfstok hangen. Dan heb je bij alle deuren en sluizen de voorrang. Mijn moeder loerde 's avonds op de trekschuit, en ja hoor, de trekschuit kwam aan met de vlag half stok.\nDie vrouw hiette Iemkje. Een kleinzoon van haar is hier in 't rusthuis."},{"n":28258,"r":"CJ073202","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"One night a boy saw a vision of his brother in socks that were far too big. The next day his brother fell into the canal and was given a pair of dry socks by the schoolmaster.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't wy froeger nei skoalle gongen yn Jobbegea, hienen wy altyd in pear ûren skoft. Dan gongen wy wol gauris nei de Gordykster feart ta to boartsjen. Dêr wienen stappen fan hout, dy't nei de feart ta gongen. Yn 'e wâl wienen allegear ynhammen, gatten. Wy sprongen dan fan 't stap ôf oer sa'n gat hinne. Op in kear mislearre 't my en ik rekke yn 'e feart. Mei de wiete krous kom ik yn skoalle. Doe krige ik fan master in pear droege sokken, dy't my fiersto great wienen. - Dat hiele tafriel hie myn broer de nachts fan tofoaren èk sjoen. Hy seach my yn 'e greate sokken omstappen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28354,"r":"CJ074112","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man knew he would die by fire. He was struck by lightning.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Hofstra fan Skoat is troch de wjerljocht forûngelokke. Dat hat er sels allegear fan tofoaren sjoen. \"Allegear fjûr\", sei er. Wylst er ûnder in koe siet woarde er troffen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28368,"r":"CJ074202","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A boy was born with a caul and saw things in advance. Once he said that a woman had come by three times that day. But in reality she only came the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn swager hat in jonge, dy is mei de helm geboaren. Hy sjocht de dingen dy't gebeure sille nou en dan fan tofoaren. Op in kear doe wienen myn swager en 'e frou fuort. Doe't se thús kommen, sei er: \"Hjir hat hoed ek in frou by de doar west. Dy seach der sa en sa út. Trije kear hie se der west. Mar sy wie der yn werklikheit net west. De oare deis kom se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28514,"r":"CJ075619","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Jille Antsje lives in Petten, was born with a caul and sees everything in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jille Antsje wenne yn 'e Petten. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren.\nIt minske seach alles foarút.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28597,"r":"CJ076502","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Father can read cups and predict the future from coffee grounds. He gets paid for this.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit koe ek kopkekike. Der kommen wolris jonge froulju by ús dy't de takomst wite woenen. Dat koe heit út it kofjedik sjen. Hy krige dêr twa dûbeltsjes of in kwartsje foar.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28602,"r":"CJ076507","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Wibe Alma from Harkema was born with a caul and can foretell things. When something is coming, he is knocked out of bed in the middle of the night, and later he tells what he has seen and who will die. It always comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wibe Alma ^ fan 'e Harkema wie mei de helm geboaren.\nDy moest alles sjen. As der hwat wie woarde hy der yn 'e nacht útkloppe. Dan mòest er datselde sjen. Hwat er dan seach fortelde er letter. Dan sei er, dy en dy giet èk dea. Dat kom altyd út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28604,"r":"CJ076509","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Father is clairvoyant and knows already at his wedding that he will have a bad life. It is a bad marriage; he is very unhappy, cannot get along with my mother and falls ill. He went about with cancer for years. It was deep poverty.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit wie ek heldersynde. Doe't er troude, wist er wol, dat er in min leven krije soe. Dat hat er my ris forteld. Hy krige in leven as de hel. It houlik wie och sa ûngelokkich, hy koe net mei ús mem oer de wei. En hy woarde siik.\nHy krige de kanker. Dêr hat er jierrenlang oan sukkele. En 't wie djippe earmoed.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28641,"r":"CJ077205","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Someone on the Langelaan in Noordermeer was born with a caul and sees funeral processions in advance. Another person from Bergum can predict that someone will drown, and that comes true too.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der ha guon wenne op 'e Langeloane to Noardermar, dy wienen mei de helm geboaren. Dy seagen lykstaesjes fan tofoaren.\nDer wenne yn Burgum ek ien, dy wist fan tofoaren dat der ien forsûpe soe. Dat hied er sjoen. 't Is ek útkom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28771,"r":"CJ078803","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"When my eldest brother is sent to the shop he soon comes back, because he has seen the devil in the hedge on the way. My other brother wants to see that for himself, and at widow Mozes's house they see the sheep still standing outside, which is the devil. Taeke was born with a caul and goes along. On the way back, at his insistence, they walk along the little dike. Later he hears that Taeke saw a funeral procession approaching with Jille van Houten. A week later one of Jille's children dies quite unexpectedly.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie twa âldere bruorren. Op in joun woarde de âldste nei de winkel fan Hindrik Holthuis tastjûrd om boadskippen. Mar hy kom al gau werom.\nMem sei: \"Hast nou al hinne west?\"\n\"Né,\" sei er, \"hwant de duvel sit dêr yn 'e hage.\" (Der wie in hage oan 'e Boskreed)\nMem sei: \"Hwat biweecht dy jonge - de duvel yn 'e hage.\"\nMyn oare broer sei: \"Dan sil ik ris mei dy hinne en dan sille wy ris sjen hwer't de duvel is.\"\nIt wie sahwat op it plak, dêr't de widdou Mozes wenne.\nOan 'e oare kant fan 't paed wie in koart dykje. Doe't hja dêr oan ta wienen seagen sy it. De widdou Mozes hie 't skiep forgetten yn to heljen. Dat wie dêr noch en dàt wie de duvel.\nDoe't se wer thús kommen sei mem: \"Dan mat Taeke mar even mei nei de winkel (Taeke, dat wie dy jongere broer, dy't èk mei nei de 'duvel' west hie. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren).\nSy gongen togearre hinne en togearre gongen se werom.\nDoe't se op 'e weromreis by 't swarte dykje wienen sei Taeke tsjin myn âldere broer: \"Mast op it dykje gean, jong.\"\n\"Op it dykje?\" sei de oare.\n\"Ja,\" sei Taeke, \"ik gean ek op 't dykje.\" (Oerdei roannen se dêr wolris oer út aerdichheit, mar by nacht wie dat in hiel geknoffel)\n\"By nacht?\" sei myn âldere broer.\n\"Ja\", sei Taeke.\nHja rinne 't dykje del en komme thús.\nDoe frege myn âldere broer: \"Hwerom moest ik bislist op 't dykje lâns?\"\nMem hearde dat. Dy sei: \"Moestû op 't dykje lâns?\"\n\"Ja\", sei Taeke, hwant der is","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28772,"r":"CJ078804","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Taeke was born with a caul, which was destroyed at his birth; otherwise he would have foreseen everything. Now he only sees what crosses his path. Doctors sell cauls for a lot of money to officers and sailors, because they then become bulletproof or safe from shipwreck.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Taeke wie mei de helm geboaren. De kreamheinster hat by syn geboarte de helm forneatige. As dat net it gefal west hie hied er alles sjen matten. Nou hoefde hy der nachts net út. Hy seach allinne dat hwat tafallich op syn paed kom.\nDer woarde wol sein dat de dokters dy helms djûr forkochten oan ofsieren en sélju. De ofsieren binne dan kûgelfrij, wurdt der sein en in kaptein fan in boat, dy't sa'n helm hat kriget noait skipbreuk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28798,"r":"CJ079003","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Tsjerk Boonstra's wife was born with a caul, and when we visit her once she accuses us of having stolen apples from the orchard the night before, because she saw it. When I ask why she did not come outside when she knew, she threatens to box my ears.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tsjerk Boonstra wenne oan 'e Mûzegroppewei. Dy syn wiif wie èk mei de helm geboaren. Wy kommen dêr ris in kear lâns, doe woarde it minske lulk op my. Sy sei: \"Sy ha fannacht de apels by ús stellen.\" Sy hienen in apelhôf. Doe sei se: \"Ik hie 't justernacht wol sjoen.\"\nIk sei: \"Hwerom gongen jo der dan fannacht net hinne to sjen, as jo dat wol wisten, of doarsten jo net?\"\nDoe sei se: \"Smoarge jonge, sil 'k dy in draei om 'e earen jaen?\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28914,"r":"CJ079803","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"When my sister is standing on the quay in Visvliet, a skipper moored there tells her that a funeral procession will pass, because he saw it that night. That same afternoon there is indeed one. The skipper was born with a caul.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn suster wenne to Visvliet, oan 't wetter. Op in moarn soe se nei 't stap ta. Doe lei dêr krekt in skip yn 'e feart.\nDe skipper sei tsjin har: \"Hjir komt ek in lykstaesje lâns.\"\n\"Né, wol?\" sei myn suster.\n\"Ja,\" sei er, \"ik ha 't fannacht sjoen.\" Safolle manlju en safolle froulju en sa en sa.\nDe middeis wie 't sa. 't Kom krekt sa út as er sein hie.\nDy skipper wie mei de helm geboaren. Dan kinne se alles sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32807,"r":"CJ083803","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Someone predicts that a relative will die six weeks later. The prediction is exactly right.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e famylje fan myn wiif to Burgumerheide wie ien tige min. De famylje kom delsetten. (Mar hy is wer better woarn).\nDoe sei ien fan 'e famyljeleden: \"Mei seis wiken binne wy wer byinoar.\"\nOp 'e kop om't ôf, krekt seis wiken letter stoar der in broer fan skoanheit. Dat wie Sjouke Dykstra.\nDyselde hie 't dus wol goed sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33713,"r":"CJ093501","p":"Dokkum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman was born with a caul. One night she had seen a corpse in the water. Two weeks later someone did indeed drown.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wij woonden hier te Dokkum aan de Streek. Daar achter was het water. Wij woonden beneden en boven ons woonden twee hele ouwe mensen. Die frou was met de helm geboren.\nOp een keer zei ze tegen ons moeke: \"Hè, wat heb ik weer een rare nacht had.\"\n\"Wat was er dan?\" vroeg ons moeke.\nSij had een lijk sien, sei se, dat foer troch de Ie.\nZo'n veertien dagen later ferdronk der een man in de Ie, die werd in een praam daar langs brocht over de Ie.\nZe had het goed sien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33714,"r":"CJ093502","p":"Dokkum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman was born with a caul. Once she had seen a funeral procession. All the men except one were wearing a hat. Later a man was buried. His eldest son wore a cap.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Een andere keer had se sien dat er aan de Achterweg een lykstaesje was. Alle mannen droegen een hoed, behalve één. \nZowat een week later was de begrafenis.\nIk was zeventien jaar toen ons moeke it fertelde.\nDe man syn oudste zoon had een pet op.\n't Kwam presies so uit. Moeke het it self sien toen de echte begrafenis der was.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29386,"r":"CJ081005","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man was born with a caul and therefore saw funerals in advance. He then knew who was going to die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tiense Boomsma fan 'e Boelensloane wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy sei: \"Ik mat alles sjen.\"\nDoe't der ris in jongeman stoarn wie, sei er fan tofoaren al: \"Ik ha de bigraffenis sjoen. Deselde dy't stjert wennet op 't plak dêr't Houtigehage yn Boelensloane oanslút.\" 't Is dy en dy, sei er. It kloppe as in bus.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29462,"r":"CJ081703","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man often had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions. Later there was then always a real funeral procession. But the man did not yet know who would die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bearn Boonstra fan Sumarreheide seach fan tofoaren lykstaesjes. Dat kom altyd nei; nachts moest hy der foar út bêd wei. Mar hy koe noait sizze hwa't der stoarn wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32616,"r":"CJ081904","p":"Dokkum","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul tells his girlfriend that he has to step aside for a passing funeral procession. The girl cannot see the procession and thinks the young man is out of his mind. It is a vision of a funeral. Many people are keen to get cauls because they protect against shipwreck, for example. The caul must be removed the right way at birth.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Moeke woonde in Hantumer Uutbuurt. Daar had se forkering met in fint. Op in avond kuijeren se togearre. Doe moesten se in weg passeare. Doe sei hy teugen Moeke: \"Wacht even Tryn, ik mat even oer de sleat.\"\nDoe sei Moeke: \"Wat is dat met dy?\"\nDoe sei hy: \"Der giet in lykstaesje foarby.\"\nMoeke sei niks. Doe sei se: \"It is sa't is, jonge, ik meitsje 't út.\"\nDy jonge was met de helm geboaren. Sulke mensen moeten alles sien.\nDe dokters hielden die helms achterút. Want as de sélui so'n helm hadden kregen se geen skipbreuk.\nBij 't afnemen moest de helm de goeije kant uitgaan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32641,"r":"CJ082103","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"In a dream, a man foresees that his sheep will die while carrying three lambs. The dream comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie in hiel bêst skiep, dat wie swier mei lammen.\nDêr wie 'k tige wiis mei. It wie yn 'e winter. It skiep wie al swier en joech gâns molke.\nIk sei tsjin 't wiif: \"Ik wol 't skiep misse.\"\n\"Dat silst my dochs wol lige\", sei se.\nIk sei: \"It giet ta de doar út. Ik ha 't fannacht hingjen sjoen. Trije lammen kommen der út.\"\nIk hie droomd, it skiep gong dea en der sieten trije lammen yn. Ik forruile it oan in oar skiep.\n't Kom krekt sa út as ik droomd hie. It skiep dat ik earst hie gong dea en 't brocht trije lammen. 't Wie oardel maend lyn dat ik it droomd hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32642,"r":"CJ082104","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul keeps having to get up at night to have visions of funerals.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei de helm geboaren is, mat bigrafenissen sjen.\nOp 'e Boppetike wenne sa'n man, dy moest der nachts altyd ôf.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32651,"r":"CJ082113","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman dreams that one of her sons-in-law dies. The dream comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hiltsje Dykstra, myn âldste suster, wennet op 'e Boelensloane. Dy droomde, ien fan har skoansoannen stoar. Hja koe net útmeitsje hokker skoansoan it wie. Dat wie krekt fan tofoaren dat Jan Brouwer út de Pein dea gong. Dat wie ien fan har skoansoannen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32678,"r":"CJ082319","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A fortune-teller makes predictions about the future. The predictions all come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Thomas Clare wenne yn 'e Westerein oan 'e Swâdde.\nMyn beide susters ha dêr ris hinne west, hwant Clare koe wiersizze. Fan myn iene suster sei se, dy soe trouwe mei in swarte man en sy soe oan 't wetter komme to wenjen. 't Is neikom: har man wie roetswart en sy kommen yn Gerkeskleaster to wenjen oan 'e feart.\nDer wie ek noch in nichtsje by. Dy har âlden koenen och sa min mei elkoar, dat wie in great lijen, dat ús nichtsje sei altyd: \"Ik wol noait trouwe.\"\nClare sei tsjin har: \"Jo sille èk trouwe.\"\n\"Ik trou nèt\", sei ús nichtsje.\n\"Ja hear,\" sei Clare, \"jo sille trouwe mei in widner mei bern.\"\nEn 't is èk gebeurd. Clare hie 't wol goed sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32744,"r":"CJ083106","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant woman keeps having visions of all sorts of things at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Geale Antsje fan 'e Harkema moest nachts alles sjen. Net allinne lykstaesjes, ek allerhande oare dingen: alles.\nEk as ien in skiep stiel. Dat wist se altyd to fortellen.\nLetter is se nei Drachten gong to wenjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32786,"r":"CJ083502","p":"Dokkum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman born with a caul foresees that her husband will fall out of the window. The vision comes true: three days later the man falls.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wennet in frou yn Dokkum, dy har man is út it raem fallen. Hja hat trije dagen fan tofoaren al sjoen dat dat gebeurde.\n\"Ik sag het je ankommen,\" sei se, \"ik wist dat it gebeuren ging.\" Dy frou is mei de helm geboaren, sizze se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32822,"r":"CJ084104","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"One night a mother foresees that her son will have an accident. The vision comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem seach op in kear yn 'e nacht, doe't se op bêd lei klear dat ús Jan in ûngelok krige. Hja seach harsels sitten mei Jan op 'e skoat en de earms om him hinne. It kom sekuer út.\nRidlik gau dêrnei krige myn broer Jan in ungelok: hy bruts syn earm, en doe siet mem mei him op 'e skoat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32824,"r":"CJ084106","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"When a neighbour of a man born with a caul dies, it is hard to find someone to lead the funeral. The man born with a caul advises choosing a certain man to lead it. He had earlier had a vision that this man would lead that funeral.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't Berend, de buorman fan Boardzer Bruning fan 'e Boelensloane kom to forstjerren, koenen se dêr earst net in foargonger by krije. Mar Boardzer hie al fan tofoaren sjoen dat Durk Pultrum de foargong ha soe. Dêrom sei er: \"Gean mar nei Durk Pultrum ta, dy wol wol.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32826,"r":"CJ084108","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man suddenly sees lots of soldiers marching and suspects war is coming. The vision comes true: shortly afterwards the Second World War breaks out and German soldiers appear.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruning hat ris op in kear allegearre soldaten op 'e wei rinnen sjoen. Hy sei: \"Nou komt hjir gau oarloch.\"\nEn 't wie èk sa. Ridlik gau dêrnei bruts de oarloch út. Doe kommen de Dútse soldaten op 'e lappen, dy't Boardzer sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32827,"r":"CJ084109","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A mother foresees that she will lose her son. The mother resigns herself to it when a voice speaks to her. The vision comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mem wist fan tofoaren dat se ús Minne forlieze moest. Dat hie se sjoen. Minne wie 19 jier doe't er stoar. Dêr hie mem it hiel bot mei to dwaen. Hja wie hast in bytsje forstandeloas, sa slim wie 't.\nKrekt fóár syn dea sei mem tsjin him: \"Is 't goed mei dy, Minne?\"\n\"Jawol,\" sei Minne, \"ik kom goed toplak.\"\nMar mem wie dêr net gerêst oer. Hja twifele der oan omdat Minne noait nei tsjerke ta gong. Hja siet der bot oer yn. Dat woarde sa slim, dat op 't lêst hie se hiele gesprekken op bêd.\nDoe kom der ris in kear in stem by har. Dy stem sei, hy wie to plak, hja mocht him net wer bigeare.\n\"Hij slaapt de slaap des rechtvaardigen\", sei dy stem.\nDoe hat se har der by del jown.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32912,"r":"CJ084801","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Some time beforehand, a boy dreams that a drowned girl is lying in a woman's arms.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us oerpake hat alris in bijeflecht foun. Doe't er yn Napoleonstiid in namme opjaen moest sei er: van der Flecht. Fanwege dy bijeflecht. Mar dat mocht net omt 'Flecht' in Frysk wurd wie. Doe is 't 'Vlugt' woarn. Hy hiet sûnt Wibe Popkes van der Vlugt.\nIt gebeurde yn 1856 of '57. Itske wie myn omke, in broer fan heit. Sy wennen yn in greate plaets oan 'e Folgerster loane. Itske wie doe sechstjin jier. Hy kom op in moarn fan bêd ôf en sei: \"O, o, hwat haw ik fannacht in rare droom hawn. Ja, 't wie eins mear in 'gesicht' as in droom. Hwant ik wie wekker. Ik hearde mem gûlen en heit èk en Popke ek (dy wie sawn jier) en Wibe ek (± 18 jier). En Romkje, de faem stie ek to gûlen. Ik ha Romkje mei Jeltsje ('t lyts famke) op 'e earm stean sjoen. Jeltsje wie fordronken.\"\nItske wie der o sa raer fan.\nIn wike of hwat letter, op in snein, gongen Itske en Wibe nei tsjerke ta. 't Wie de herfoarme tsjerke fan Rottefalle. Doe't de preek dien wie gongen se wer nei hûs ta. Sy moesten oer in houtsje om op it hiem to kommen. Itske tocht: Hea, dêr leit hwat yn 'e sleat. Doe sjen, en doe seach er lytse Jeltsje dêr yn lizzen. Hy helle har der fuort út, mar sy wie al dea.\nDe oaren hienen by in skiep wêze matten wylst de beide âldste jonges nei tsjerke ta wienen. Dat skiep liet him net maklik krije. Doe allen der achteroan. Sadwaende hienen se Jeltsje út it eech rekke en dy kom dêrtroch yn 'e sleat torjoc","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33054,"r":"CJ086306","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man was born with a caul. He always knew in advance when there would be another funeral. He also said people should never walk in the middle of the road at midnight, because they might run into a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining fan 'e Boelensloane wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy sei: In minske mat om 12 ûre yn 'e nacht noait midden op 'e wei gean hwant dan kin er tsjin in lykstaesje oprinne.\nHy wist altyd krekt fan tofoaren hwannear't der wer in bigraffenis wêze soe. 't Kom altyd út. Hy krige der altyd tynge fan, sa't it liket.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33199,"r":"CJ087722","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A young man was once lying in bed and saw that the road to his girlfriend was blocked. The next day the road was indeed completely covered with trees because of a storm.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn op ien nei jongste soan hat forkearing. Op in kear doe't er op bêd lei seach er dat de wei dêr't er lâns moest, alhiel forsperd wie.\nDe oare deis bigoun it to stoarmjen. Der wienen safolle grouwe takken fan 'e beammen waeid, dat hy der de jouns net lâns koe nei de faem ta.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33275,"r":"CJ088306","p":"Schagerbrug","v":"N.-H.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman who was born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. One night she saw her own daughter's funeral. Not long after, the daughter died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Jochums Antsje fan Sumarreheide wie mei de helm geboaren. Hja moest der nachts ôf om bigraffenissen to sjen. Op in nacht seach se troch 't gleske hinne, doe seach se de bigraffenis fan har eigen dochter. Dy leefde doe noch, mar se lei al op 't sykbêd. In skoftsje letter is dy stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33284,"r":"CJ088402","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man was in France, and one night he saw someone smash a window at his parents' house. When he came home a week later, a window had indeed been smashed on that very night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie yn 'e oarloch. Ik siet yn Frankryk. Doe seach ik op in nacht presys hwat der by ús thús gebeurde. Ik lei op bêd.\nDe oare wyks rekke ik nei hûs ta, nei de Harkema. It earste hwat ik seach, dat wie it nije rútsje, dat yn it sydglês fan 't hûs siet.\nIk sei: Dat haw ik yn 'e nacht yn Frankryk sjoen. Ik ha sjoen hwa't it rút ynsmiten hat en ek hwer't er it mei dien hat.\nIt wie krekt deselde nachts gebeurd, dat ik it sjoen hie.\nEn 't kloppe allegear presys.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34476,"r":"CJ090601","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People who were born with a caul often saw funerals in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Tsearde Antsje (_) fan Hiltsjemuoi-wâlden seach fan tofoaren bigraffenissen. Hja fortelde gewoan hwa't der stjerre soe. Hja roan noait midden op 'e wei by 't tsjuster, hwant dan koe se samar tsjin in lykstaesje oprinne, sei se.\nJouns wie se faek warber. Dan wie der wer in bigraffenis to sjen. Har broer Boardzer Bruning (_) fan Houtigehage wie èk mei de helm geboaren en moest èk alles sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34497,"r":"CJ090711","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man was born with a caul. Because of this he often had to get up at night to see funerals. He always knew in advance that someone would die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tichte by Sânbulten wenne in man, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. It wie in âld man, dy hie dêr in krús mei.\nAs der in sterfgefal op til wie dan krige hy dêr op de ien of oare geheimsinnige wize tynge fan. Hy wist it altyd krekt as der in bigraffenis komme soe. Dy seach er fantofoaren. Dan moest er út it bêd wei, as er woe of net en hy moest dy bigraffenis sjen. Soms moest er wit hoe fier rinne yn 'e nacht, oer hekken en stekken hinne.\nHy wenne by it boskje oan 'e Tsjerkereed. Myn frou sei, har mem woe noait lije dat hja dêr lâns gong, hwant it doogde dêr net.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33565,"r":"CJ091205","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man was born with a caul and often saw funerals and funeral processions in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger hienen jy minsken, dy wienen mei de helm geboaren. Sa wie der ek in plysje yn 'e Koaten, dy hiet fan Ruerd Houtvester. Dy moest alles sjen.\nHeit wie arbeider by de boer. Dy boer hâldde bijen. Op in kear moest heit foar dy boer mei de bijen nei Súdfelde ta yn Drinte. De plysje (Ruerd Houtvester) gong mei. Doe't se al in eintsje yn Drinte op wienen sei de plysje tsjin heit: \"Gean even oan kant, Sibe, dêr komt in bigraffenis oan.\"\nHeit gong oan kant, mar hy seach neat.\nEven letter sei de plysje: \"Gean nou mar wer fierder. Dêr wie in lykstaesje, dêr roannen 24 minsken achter oan.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33626,"r":"CJ091804","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman was born with a caul and saw funeral processions in advance. Once she knew that it was not a sick man who would die, but his wife. It came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Marten Skeet wenne yn Aldegea, yn 't lêste hûs.\nSyn frou hiet Doekel, dy koe mear as in oar, seinen se. Dy seach allerhande dingen dy't in oar net seach. Hja wie mei de helm geboaren en moest dan de lykstaesjes fan tofoaren sjen.\nOp in kear wie der in keardel yn Aldegea tige siik. Dat wie Jan Sjirks. Hy hie longontsteking en it like o sa slim.\nDer stie op in joun in kloftsje minsken yn Aldegea byelkoar, dy praetten dêr oer. \"Hy sil 't wol net rêdde\", seinen se.\nDoe kom Doekel der oan. \"Jimme hoege net oer de man yn to sitten\", sei se. \"Dy redt it wol. Mar mei hàr is 't minder. Ik haw hàr lykstaesje sjoen. Dêr roan de man àchter.\"\nLetter stoar de frou, wylst har man Jan Sjirks wer better woarde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34545,"r":"CJ092803","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man saw funeral processions in advance. He was also able to tell details of his own daughter's funeral beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit seach fan tofoaren lykstaesjes. Soms fortelde hy it fan tofoaren, ek wolris nei de bigraffenis. Heit en mem hienen in famke, dat woarde siik en it kom to forstjerren. It wie doe twa jier âld; ik wie der doe noch net. Doe't se stoarn wie, sei heit tsjin mem: \"Ik wist wol dat wy har misse moesten. Dêr op dat plak komt it kistje to stean. Der komme twa biklaeisters by. Dy dogge tofolle strie yn 't kistje. Dêr mat wer hwat út.\"\nIt is krekt sa gebeurd, lyk as heit it oan mem fortelde. Hy hie 't allegear fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34547,"r":"CJ092805","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man always saw all sorts of things in advance. He would then tell his wife. What he told her always came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As heit hwat oan mem fortelde, dan paste mem der op of it ek neikomme soe. Hwant hja twifele soms oan syn wurden. Mar it kom altyd út. Hwat hy fan tofoaren sjoen hie, dat gebeurde letter.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33752,"r":"CJ094007","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman was born with a caul and sometimes saw funeral processions. Then she knew that someone would die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei in helm geboaren wie moest alles sjen.\nAlde Tsjits, de widdou Rekker seach altyd lykstaesjes.\nOp in kear stie se yn 'e nacht op in hoeke bûtendoar.\nDoe seach se allegear regenkleden, dy't wapperen en hja woarde oan kant skoud. Hja hie de lykstaesje yn 'e wei stien.\nHja fortelde 't hjir de oare moarns.\nDe oare wyks wie der in sterfgefal op 't plak, dêr't hja stien hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33759,"r":"CJ094014","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman had seen in advance that the boy next door would have an accident.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tsjits seach foarút dat de jonge fan har buorlju, dy't yn Hollân wenne, dêr in ûngelok krige. Hja hat it ús forteld. (Tsjits wennet nou yn Talma-oard yn Feanwâlden, har holle doocht net mear).","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33772,"r":"CJ094105","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man was born with a caul. At night he often had to get up to see funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Suderdwarsfeart hjir to Drachten hat in man wenne, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest alle bigraffenissen út 'e omkriten sjen. Dêr moest er wit hoe faek om fan bêd ôf.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33773,"r":"CJ094106","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A farmhand had seen that the farmer's wife would die in childbed. It came true: a white cloth lay over the coffin.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der hat in boerefeint op 'e Suderdwarsfeart wenne, dy wie ek mei de helm geboaren. Dy tsjinne to Drachten by in boer op it Súd. Tichteby wenne in arbeidersfrou, dat minske wie yn forwachting. Mar hja wie sa soun dat, hja die al har wurk oan it lêste ta.\nIt fremde wie, as de feint tafallich by har wie of mei har praette, wie er och sa stil en seach mar treurich. Der wienen guon dy foel dat op. Doe't se him fregen hwerom hy sa earnstich wie, woed er dat earst net sizze. Mar op 't lêst hat er 't ien fortelt. It minske soe yn 'e kream stjerre. Hy hie de bigraffenis al sjoen. Der lei in wyt ruft oerhoeks oer de kiste.\nDy't it hearde woe 't net leauwe. It minske wie ommers sa fleurich en 't like allegear like bêst.\nMar hy krige gelyk. Hja stoar yn 'e kream en it ruft lei oer de kiste.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33808,"r":"CJ094403","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman was born with a caul. She often had to get up at night to see funerals. She then knew that someone would die, but not who.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wennet in frou, dat is in sekere Pytsje, dy is sahwat 55 jier. Hja is mei de helm geboaren en sjocht allerhande bigraffenissen foarút. Nachts mat se der faek út om to sjen. Hja wit nèt hwà't der stoarn is.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36137,"r":"CJ096705","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The narrator was lying in bed and in her dream saw men with tin headgear coming over the dike. A year later the Second World War broke out, and the Germans came over the dike wearing helmets, exactly the way the woman had dreamed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen yn Dokkumernijesilen. Myn âldste jonge moest noch geboaren wurde. Ik lei op bêd en ik hie in rare droom. 't Wie yn 1939. Ik seach dat der mannen oer de dyk krûpten mei blikkene dingen op 'e holle. Ik woardde der raer fan.\nDe deis dat de Dútsers hjir kommen yn maeije 1940 en se alles ûnder wetter rinne lieten binne dy Dútsers presys sa oer de dyk klommen. Hja hienen helms op. It wie sprekend gelyk sa't ik it yn 'e nacht sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36139,"r":"CJ096707","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The narrator's sister had a little son who was in hospital. She and her husband received word that their child's condition was critical. The husband wanted to hurry to the hospital, but his wife stayed calm. She had seen the sheets of the little bed being carried outside: so their son was already dead.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn suster hie in jonkje yn 't stêdssikenhûs yn Ljouwert to lizzen. Dat wie tige min. Myn suster wenne sels ek yn Ljouwert. Doe krigen se biricht dat de tastân fan it bern krityk wie.\nMyn swager wie hastich en sei tsjin myn suster: \"Toe, dû mast oanmeitsje. Wy matte der hinne foardat it to let is.\"\nMar myn suster sei kalm: \"It hoeft net mear, hwant ús jonkje is al wei. Ik ha sjoen dat se de tekkentsjes fan it ledekantsje al bûten brocht ha.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36162,"r":"CJ096903","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"In Nijega two old people were murdered. A man was walking along the Wytfeanster paths pushing his blind father in a wheelbarrow. The blind father saw the murderers coming. At that moment they were walking some way further on.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der binne ris twa âlde minsken yn Nyegea formoarde woarn. It wienen in heit en in soan dy't dat dien hienen. Dol hieten se (= Dalstra).\nDyselde nacht ried pake mei de kroade de reden del nei Eastemar ta. Pake syn heit siet op 'e kroade, dy wie blyn. Se wienen op it Wytfean, doe sei de âld man: der komme guon de reden del. Mar it is slim, o sa slim.\nDer wie net ien to sjen. Mar de beide moardners binne op dat stuit dêr passeard, in reed of hwat fierder, oer de Wytfeanster paden. De bline hie dat fornom.\nDoe wie de moard al gebeurd. Se gongen werom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36206,"r":"CJ097212","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"With her card readings Tryn Snipel always predicted wealth, which people liked to hear.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tryn Snipel wie kaertlizter op 'e Boelensloane. Hja sei altyd: \n't Wurdt allegear rykdom! Dat mochten de lju wol hearre.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36238,"r":"CJ097502","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man dreams at night that someone is murdered. That same night his brother is murdered.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in nacht is myn omke Piter Veenstra oan it Wyldpaed formoarde. Heit hie dyselde nachts in droom. Hy droomde dat der ien formoarde woarde. Mar hy koe de gesichten net goed ûnderskiede. Heit wie altyd tige mâl mei Piterom.\nDe moardner is noait bikend woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36239,"r":"CJ097503","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"When both her parents died, the narrator suffered from melancholy. Both times she sensed that something bad was happening, while she did not yet know anything about the deaths.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sels haw ik it ek. Doe't ús heit stoar wie ik slim swiersettich. Der drukte hwat op my. Ik wist dat der hwat slims gebeurde, mar fan heit syn stjerrren wist ik neat ôf.\nDoe't mem forstoar wie 't èk sa mei my. It lei my by dat der hwat hiel slims gebeurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36240,"r":"CJ097504","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Shortly before he was murdered, Piter [Veenstra] heard groaning sounds on a trip to the toilet. When his brother went to listen, he heard nothing. Piter's brother later said that he had heard his own death throes then.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Koarte tiid foardat Piter-om formoarde wie, útfanhûze er in pear nachten by heit en dy. Doe kom er in kear yn 'e hûs, doe hie er krekt nei 't hûske ta west. Hy sei: wylst ik op 't hûske siet, hearde ik hyltyd dat der kreune woarde.\n\"Nou,\" sei heit, \"dan wol 'k dêr ek ris hinne.\"\nHeit der hinne, mar dy hearde neat. Doe Piter-om der wer hinne. Dy hie 't kreunjen wer dúdlik heard.\nUs heit sei letter altyd: hy hat syn eigen deastriid heard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36298,"r":"CJ097703","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The narrator's father wanted to drown one of their two dogs because they were short of money. His wife, however, warned him that the dog would not die in the water. The father nevertheless went to the water with the dog, put him in a sack with a stone in it and drowned him. But when he got home, the dog was standing at the window. The family then kept the dog, and he later died at their home.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy hienen froeger by ús yn 'e hûs twa hounen. Mar dat wie ien tofolle. Wy hienen 't och sa earmoedich, heit wie gebrekkich en wy koenen 't net bitelje om twa hounen fretten to jaen. Spits hiet de iene houn.\nHeit sei: \"Ik sil Spits forsûpe.\"\nMem sei: \"Wybren, ik warskôgje dy, datstû dy houn forsûpste. Dû kinst him wol yn 't wetter dwaen, mar hy giet net dea. Astû wer thús biste, is de houn der even letter èk wer.\"\nMar heit steurde him dêr net oan. Hy sei: \"ik doch in stien ûnder yn 'e sek, dan rêd ik der wol mei.\"\n\"Hy komt werom,\" sei mem, \"dû silst it sjen.\"\nHeit gong mei Spits en in sek en in stien op stap de kant nei Kûkherne út. By it earste flapbrechje yn Kûkherne hat er de stien yn 'e sek dien, de houn der by en dêr liet er him sakje yn 't wetter.\nDoe gong er werom op hûs ta.\nWy sieten krekt to iten, dêr hienen wy Spits wer.\nMem hie krekt fantofoaren sein: \"Aenst is de houn hjir en dan kloppet er op 't glês.\"\nEn dêr stie Spits op 'e achterste poaten by 't glês op en de foarste poat gong oer 't glês hinne.\nDoe ha wy de houn hâlden, hy is by ús stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36299,"r":"CJ097704","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The narrator's mother predicted that Marten van Kammen, who suffered from TB, would soon die. After his death she took her daughter to his body. She rubbed her wrist over his forehead, and so the daughter got rid of her warts.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Marten van Kammen hie t.b.c. Hy lei yn in tintsje.\nOp in joun sei mem: \"Ik mat der mar ris hinne.\" Doe't se weromkom sei se: \"Hy leeft gjin twa dagen mear.\"\nDe oare deis stoar er. Syn frou sei: \"Ik hie 't der noait oan sjoen dat it sa hurd gean soe.\" Mar mem hie him al fantofoaren as lyk sjoen.\nIk hie seis rare stikelwarten op 'e pols. Doe't Marten dea wie nom mem my mei nei syn lyk ta. Hja hie myn pols beet en dêrmei struts se oer syn foarholle hinne. Ik rekke alle seis warten in skoftsje letter kwyt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36302,"r":"CJ097707","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Knjillis Veenstra could see funerals before they happened, including that of his own daughter.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Knjillis Veenstra (Minke Knjillis) fan Sweagerbosk wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest alle begraffenissen foarút sjen. Dêr siet in drang achter. Hy hat de bigraffenis fan syn eigen dochter ek sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36304,"r":"CJ097709","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The narrator's father saw the moon landing before it took place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit wurke by de Baersma's. Op in kear kom er thús. Doe wie mem al wei. Doe sei er: \"Ik ha hwat sjoen, bern. Ik ha sjoen, dat se op 'e moanne komme. Dy minsken hienen fjouwer wjokken oan har en in bus op 'e rêch. Ik bileef it net mear, mar jimme sille 't sjen.\"\nHwat ha 'k faek oan dy wurden fan heit tocht, as se wer ris nei de moanne ta gongen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36305,"r":"CJ097710","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A narrator's mother saw a corpse come floating over the water from Dokkum. A little later a corpse from Dokkum was indeed found in the water.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear sei ús mem: \"Der komt in lyk oan út Dokkum wei oer it wetter. Se fine it aenst yn 'e buert fan Ljouwert. Ik sjoch it spielen.\"\nIn ûre letter founen se in lyk yn 'e Bonkefeart. 't Wie it lyk fan in geestlik gestoarde, fan Dokkum ôfkomstich.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36332,"r":"CJ097812","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Some children are born with a caul. That is a thin membrane over the eyes. If you remove it, you must stroke it backwards. Otherwise the child will later have to see everything [become clairvoyant].","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem bakere wol. Hja hat it wol meimakke dat bern mei de helm geboaren woarden. Dat wie in flueske dat har foar de egen siet. Dat moesten se achteroer strike, net foaroer, hwant dan moest it bern letter alle dingen sjen; dan gyng 't gesicht foar har wei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36422,"r":"CJ098211","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Knjillis Veenstra was clairvoyant. He could see things in advance, and they always came true. So his prediction that a white horse would pull a hearse also came true: it snowed that day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wenne froeger Bintsje Knjillis. Bintsje Keke (= Knjillis Veenstra) waerd er meast neamd. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy moast der nachts faek út. Dan roan er soms hiele einen. Hy waerd dreaun. Dat wie algemien bikind. As hy der út moast en hy hie hwat sjoen, dan kaem dat altyd nei. Dat miste noait ien kear.\nOp in moarntiid kaem Keke der ôf en sei: \"Der komt mei gauwens wer in sterfgefal. Ik moast der fannacht wer út en deselde dy't stoarn is wurdt bigroeven mei in wyt hynder foar de wein.\"\nDe minsken seinen: \"Ja, Keke, mar dit komt net nei.\" Hwant it wie in fêst gebrûk dat der in swart hynder foar de wein roun.\nMar Keke krige wòl gelyk. In dei of hwat letter wie der ien dea en op 'e dei fan 'e bigraffenis snijde it tige. Der roan in wyt hynder foar de wein, hwant it siet ûnder 'e snie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36429,"r":"CJ098305","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman from Westerein predicted that a child would drown in the canal.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In frou út 'e Westerein hat ris sein, der soe mei gauwens in berntsje yn 'e Swemmer fordrinke. Hja hie it sjoen. Dat is doe ek koarte tiid dêrnei gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36495,"r":"CJ098708","p":"Noardburgum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Piter Kooistra murdered old Liuwe on the Iestwei. Just before this happened, he walked along that road with his father-in-law. At a certain point his father-in-law could not walk any further; he saw a black streak running across the whole road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Piter Kooistra fan Jistrum wenne oan 'e Iestwei. Dêr op 'e Iest hat er in âld man formoarde. 't Wie âlde Liuwe.\nKrekt fan tofoaren wie er mei skoanheit oan 't kuijerjen - hja hienen nei de buorren ta west. Doe ynienen seach skoanheit in swarte streek dwars oer de hiele wei hinne. Doe koed er net fierder.\n\"Hwerom giestû net fierder?\" hie Piter frege.\n\"Ik kin net\", sei skoanheit. En sa wìe 't èk, hy kòe net.\nFuort dêrnei hat Piter âlde Liuwe formoarde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36513,"r":"CJ098802","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant midwife often foresaw things. She often went out at night. She also saw the death of her daughter in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem hie in baekster, dy wie mei de helm geboaren.\nMem frege har in kear: \"Ha jo wolris hwat sjoen?\"\n\"Och minske,\" sei se, \"ik ha der wit hoe faek op út west yn 'e nacht. Dan kòe 'k net thúsbliuwe.\nDoe't myn dochter fordronken is haw ik dat ek allegear foarútsjoen.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36514,"r":"CJ098803","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Knjillis Veenstra could see in advance who would die during the measles epidemic. He also saw his daughter's death before it happened.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn 'e Westerein hat yndertiid de blau-mûzel gien (een soort mazelen). Doe stoaren der in hiele bult. Der wie ûnder mear in húshâlding mei fiif bern, dêr foelen fjouwer by wei. It wienen allegear bigraffenissen, dei oan dei. Alde Knjillis (= Bontsje Keke; Veenstra) hat dat allegear fan tofoaren sjoen. Hy sei: \"Hjir gebeurt aenst raer hwat, ik koe net op 'e wei wêze. Ik moest ûnder 'e hage troch, sa'n liken gongen my foarby.\"\nDoe't in dochter fan him overleden is hat er dat ek fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36541,"r":"CJ098830","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Clare was a card reader. A squeaking sound came from her chest. She predicted that the narrator would meet a man at a party, and that came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Clare wie de kaertlizter fan 'e Westerein. As fammen ha wy dêr ris hinne west. Ik tocht: \"Hwat pipet it dat minske yn 't boarst.\" Hja hie in pykje by 't boarst yn. Fanwege de waermte. Dat pykje wie net goed en dat pipe hyltyd.\nHja sei tsjin my: \"Dû silst nei in feestje yn Twizelerheide ta. En dêr krigest in feint.\" Dat kaem út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36560,"r":"CJ098903","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Ymke de Vries's grandfather had seen that a church would be built. He also heard organ music. Later it happened exactly like that.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie in kammeraed hawn, dat wie Ymke de Vries. Dy syn heit Jehannes wie in eigenaerdich man.\nYndertiid is hjir in herfoarme tsjerke boud, dy is der nou net mear. Foar dat dy tsjerke dêr stie sei Jehannes tsjin Ymke: \"Sjoch jonge, op dit plak bouwe se skielk in tsjerke. Ik ha 't sjoen en ik ha de oargelmuzyk al heard.\"\n't Is krektsa gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36562,"r":"CJ098905","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Knjillis Veenstra is clairvoyant. He often had to go outside at night. The gates would then open for him by themselves.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Keke (= Knjillis Veenstra) is mei de helm geboaren. Hy moest der nachts faek út. Dan gongen de hekken fansels foar him iepen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36563,"r":"CJ098906","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The mother of Kees, who drowned, knew before his death that someone would drown.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"± 30 jier lyn is hjir ien by de brêge fordronken. Kees hiet er. Syn suster Teatske sei: ik bin net lichtgelovich, mar myn mem hat hjir ris in kear hwat forteld, doe sei se tsjin my: \"Hjir sil neiby yn 'e Westerein ien fordrinke.\"\nDy drinkeling is har eigen soan woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37164,"r":"CJ102902","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Albertsje Brjit was clairvoyant and could see into the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Burgumer Nijstêd wenne Albertsje Brjit. Dy koe kopkekike. Dêr gongen de fammen wolris hinne om de takomst útlizze to litten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37197,"r":"CJ103104","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"My wife is disabled and can see funerals in advance. She also says that you should never walk in the middle of the road at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn frou is slim ynvalide. Hja sjocht bigraffenissen, meastal fan foaroansteande minsken. Hiele greate bigraffenissen. Hja seit ek dat men nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne mat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":207303,"r":"VODA_038_17","p":"Rekken","v":"Gld.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The maid Janna was clairvoyant. She often saw things before they happened. One day she was very sad because she had seen that the master would die. Nobody believed it, but one morning the master was indeed found dead in bed. He had been given an ointment by a quack for a wound on his leg. Because of it the wound had closed too quickly and the \"bad substances\" in the leg could no longer get out.\nNow that Janna had been proven right again, the other maid no longer wanted to work with her. Janna was allowed to stay and the other maid found a position elsewhere.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"En zo was ’t nog ‘ne kere met.. doe d’ olde baas onverwachts storf. Ehn.. doe word’n de andere meid zo bange vuur die d’r bee steet, die.. doe was ze aan ’t gienen: “Wat heb i-j toch weer, Janna?”\n“Onze olde baas giet dood.”\n“Och kom, […?] steet net zo goed.”\nMaor op ‘ne morgen leit e dood in bedde. Het been dat open was was dicht’egoan en dat had eigenlijk neet emôt volgens dokter [Illepek?], ’ne grootvader van Ties [Nillenbek?] die noe hier is, een drogist. Ja..\nE..nge..daor ’s waal ook waal weer ‘ne geschiedenis aan voor um, ‘ne dokter die ’t vuur.. oet nietied hèf vuur ’n schoer in’evlucht is, dae‘f ezegd: “O,” eh j..ja..wa, “baasie liek mie nog waal kras, olde wa.”\n“Jaaa, alleen ik heb ’n gat bie eh.. now m’ bee..”\n“En wat zeg d’n dokter d’r van?”\n“Dae kiek d’nao en duut ‘r.. duüt d’r niks op. Niks eh.. neet vulle […?]”\n“Now, dan krieg e van mie ’n zalfke, dan zul je es zien hoe mooi dicht dat wordt.”\nEn dat..g.. ke.. eh..d.. dokter [ies?] ging voort, […?] dichte. En hie lee op ‘ne morgen dood in bedde.\nToen zei olde Bek.. Öllebek meteen nadat e ’t bedde opsloëg: “Wat is hier gebeurd?”\n“Ja, zus en zo.”\n“Ach, laot mie die zalf es zien. Die heb ik ook wal mak. ‘k Wis wal dat de baas niet.. det ’n old man niet […?] kon. Dat eh…die verkeerde stoffen die z’te bee zich had die môsten d’r oet.”\nNou, en zo was dat en zo kreeg Jannao alweer geliek. En toen wol de andere meid d’r ni","l":"Gelders; Nedersaksisch"},{"n":10678,"r":"CJ110104","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A certain man born with a caul often foresees deaths in passing funerals. The clairvoyant also foresaw that Juliana would come to the throne. He also foresaw that a terrible war would come under Beatrix. That war would claim very many victims: only a small number of people would be left.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei de helm geboaren wurde, sjogge bigraffenissen fan tofoaren. Bontsje Keke fan Kollumersweach moest ek altyd bigraffenissen fan tofoaren sjen.\nMar Keke seach ek oare dingen foarút.\nTidens de oarloch hat er sjoen dat Juliana op 'e troan komme soe.\nDer soe noch in forskrikkelik greate oarloch komme as Beatrix op 'e troan kaem. Dan soenen se om 'e fuotstappen fan 'e minsken sykje matte, sa'n bytsje minsken soenen der oerbliuwe. De oarloch soe hast alle minsken hjir weinimme.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29483,"r":"CJ110201","p":"De Wilgen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"An unmarried, reserved woman often has foresights of funerals at night. The foresights almost always come true shortly afterwards, about three days later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wenne yn Beets in frou, dy wie net troud. Har namme wie Fokje Slager. Dat minske praette net folle, hja wie yngetogen fan aerd. Hja seach bigraffenissen foarút. As se sa'n bigraffenis sjoen hie koe men der mar fan op oan, dat der trije dagen letter ien stoar. 't Gebeurde meastal yn 'e nacht. Hja waerd dreaun.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29487,"r":"CJ110205","p":"De Wilgen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People who regularly foresee deaths in funeral processions are caul-bearers.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon dy't geregeld lykstaesjes sjogge fantofoaren binne, nei't se sizze, mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29497,"r":"CJ110215","p":"De Wilgen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A certain woman born with a caul must have a foresight of a death every so often, so as not to die herself. The same is true of witches.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Fokje Slager, dy't mei de helm geboaren wie, moest om de safolle tiid ien sjen, oars gong se sels dea.\nMei tsjoensters wie dat ek sa.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29511,"r":"CJ110409","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A pregnant woman is very frightened when a clairvoyant man visits her, because the clairvoyant always foresees deaths. The clairvoyant keeps looking at a certain corner of the room. The child the woman gives birth to dies after 23 weeks. The little coffin stands in the corner where the clairvoyant kept resting his gaze.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger wienen wy oan 't flaechs braekjen. Myn broer en ik moesten altyd ús heit en mem helpe, dan koenen wy deis in kwartsje de man fortsjinje. Heit hie in izeren slypbrake, wy hienen in houten brake. Elke bundel dy't wy makken woech seis poun en twa ûns. Mem kaem der noch by. Dy hie in lear oer de knibbel. Hja moest de lêste skjûden (?) der mei 't mes úthelje. Dan draeide se se ta in bundel, krekt sa lang oant der seis poun en twa ûns wie.\nMei ús fjouweren fortsjinnen wy mei elkoar in goune deis. Wy dienen 't foar in boer, 't wie winterwurk.\nOp in middei wienen wy wer mei ús fjouweren oan 't braekjen. Doe kom Bontsje Keke by ús yn it hok. Hy sei tsjin mem: \"Hoe is 't Aeltsje, sille wy hast hwat thé ha?\"\nDat wie in fremde fraech, soks frege men yn dy tiid net.\nMar 't wie krekt, as fielde mem dat hy der in bidoeling mei hie. Se sei: \"Dat kin wol.\"\nMem giet yn 'e hûs en makket thé ré. Hja wie yn forwachting en moest in bern ha. Dat wisten wy doe net. Mar Keke wist it wol, dy seach alles.\nMem makke har binaud. It wie bikend: dêr't Keke kom stie rouwe to wachtsjen. Mem folge de egen fan Keke. Keke hie iderkear yn ien en deselde hoeke fan 'e keamer sjoen. Mem tocht: \"Komt er, omdat ik in bern ha mat?\" Hja makke har birekkening, hwannear't it bern forwachte wurde koe. Doe frege se: \"Knjillis, as jo hwat sjogge, hoe lang kin dat ûntstean?\"\nHy antwurde: \"Dat is ûngelyk, yn hoe'n tastâ","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29512,"r":"CJ110410","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant man visiting the narrator keeps staring at a house across the street. Half a year later a young woman dies in that house.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Neitiid hat er wer ris in kear by ús west. Doe seach er iderkear ta 't glês út. Wy wennen doe oan 'e Heidereed. Hy seach nei de Boskreed. Dêr stie in hûs oan, dat wie skean oer.\nSahwat in healjier letter is dêr in dochter fan sa'n sawntsjin, achttsjin jier forstoarn. 't Wie ien fan Jan Visser.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29513,"r":"CJ110411","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant man is driven out of bed at night by an invisible force to receive foresights. Outside, the railway gates spring open for him.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Keke moest nachts faek út bêd wei. Dan waerd er dreaun, seinen de minsken. Us hat er wolris forteld, dat er it wol hawn hie, dat er net woe, dan wied er lizzen bleaun.\nDan hie 't krekt west as waerd er stutsen mei spjelden en dan wie 't swit him útbrutsen.\nGuon ha him troffen by nacht. Dan stienen de spoarhekken foar him iepen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29514,"r":"CJ110412","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant farmhand foresees that the farmer's wife will die in childbed. The foresight comes true. The clairvoyant foresees the whole funeral in detail. He also urges them to lay a white nappy over the coffin, because he has foreseen this.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Keke wie arbeider by Gosse Venema, in greate boer.\nDy boer forlear syn wiif yn 'e kream. De jonge, Piter, bleau yn leven. Dat hie Keke allegear fan tofoaren sjoen. Hy seach de hiele lykstaesje.\nDoe't se mei 't lyk fuort gongen op 'e dei fan 'e bigraffenis hied er sein: \"Ho even. Dit is hjir net yn oarder. It is oars as sa't ik it sjoen ha. Der lei in wyt ruft hoeks oer de kiste hinne.\"\nDoe hienen se in ruft ophelle en dat oer de kiste lein, dy't op 'e boerewein stie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29515,"r":"CJ110413","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A mocking sinner, who would later have foresights himself, ridicules a clairvoyant man. The clairvoyant, who has just foreseen a death in a funeral procession, says the sinner will be able to have foresights too. He urges the sinner to look over his (the clairvoyant's) left shoulder. The sinner sees the funeral procession as well. Later it turns out that the clairvoyant transferred his second sight to the sinner as punishment for the mockery. All of this was brought about by the devil.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Keke wie froeger in forwoest man. Hy joech om God noch syn gebot en wie in great spotter. It gong him noait to mâl. Doe't er tusken de fjirtich en fyftich wie, lei er ris op in kear to jirappelsykjen op in stik lân op 'e Sweach, dat oan 'e wei lei.\nDoe hie dêr in man west, dy't alles sjen moest.\nKeke hie dat doe noch net; dy seach doe noch gjin lykstaesjes foarút.\nDy man wie nei de wei ta gien. Doe hie dy man dêr in lykstaesje sjoen. Doe hie Keke dêr de gek mei hawn.\nDoe hie dy man tsjin Keke sein: \"Dû kinst it ek wol sjen. Dan mast mar by my oer 't linker skouder hinne sjen.\"\nDoe hie Keke dat dien. En doe hie Keke 't èk sjoen.\nLetter hie dy màn it kwyt west en hie Keke it fan him oer krige. It wie de straf foar syn spotten.\nDe kweade hie 't bioardere.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29518,"r":"CJ110416","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant man always foresees exactly how many women and men will walk in a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Keke wist altyd krekt hoefolle manlju en hoefolle froulju der yn in lykstaesje meirounen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29522,"r":"CJ110420","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant man sometimes has to travel enormous distances, straight through ditches, to receive a foresight of a death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Keke roan hiele lange einen om by de lykstaesje to kommen. Hy gong dan troch sleatten en alles hinne. Neat koe him keare. Se ha my forteld, dat er soms it einekroas noch yn 't hier sitten hie, as er thús kaem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29531,"r":"CJ110429","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant man keeps having foresights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Kollum wenne Jan Visser, dy moest ek alles sjen, seinen se. Hy wie fan myn âldens.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29541,"r":"CJ110439","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"If someone is born with a caul and the caul is pulled off the face the wrong way, that person has foresights all their life. Greedy doctors often try to push cauls backwards because they can resell them at good prices.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei de helm geboaren woarde, moest letter alles sjen, as dy helm der forkeard ôflutsen woarde.\nDe dokters wienen tige hyt op de helms. Dy waerden djûr forkocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29551,"r":"CJ110449","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A card reader tells the fortunes of two brothers. The predictions come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By 't spoar wenne âlde Clare. Dy koe kaertlizze. Ik haw ris op in snein-to-joun mei myn broer en noch ien nei har ta west.\nHja tyspele hwat yn 'e kaerten om, doe bigoun se tsjin myn broer to praten. Hja sei, hja seach de skoarstien by him rikjen. \"Dû bist in man, dû kinst dy wol rêdde\", sei se tsjin him. Dat is útkaem. Hy is ridlik gau dêrnei troud - doe rikke syn eigen skoarstien. En hy hat him ek altyd tige skoan rêdde kind.\nDoe kom ik oan 'e beurt. Hja sei tsjin my: \"Der binne twa froulju, dy loere op dy.\"\nDat wie ek sa. De iene is myn frou wurden, dy sit hjir tsjin jo oer. De oare, dat wie Kobe, dy't ek in eechje op my hie. Hja sei fierder: \"Dû slachst mei in lyts swart fanke om.\"\nDat kloppe èk; dat wie Jehanne, myn nicht. Dat wist net ien, mar hjà wist it wòl.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29580,"r":"CJ110611","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"During the Second World War a woman predicts that on 5 May the flag can be hung out because the Netherlands will then be liberated. The prediction comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Wie yn 't lêst fan 'e oarloch. Dyselde minsken wienen noch altyd yn dy rijnaek oan 'e kant fan 'e Leijen.\nYn 't lêst fan febrewaris 1945 komt de man wer ris by my om molke en seit: \"Ik ha bliid nijs foar dy, Jan.\"\nIk sei: \"Is jou frou miskien wer yn forwachting?\"\n\"Né jonge,\" sei er, \"sil 'k it dy fortelle hwat myn frou nyskes sein hat? Hja sei: 'Dû mast Jan freegje of er noch in flagge hat. Dan mast him meinimme. Dan sil 'k him útwaskje.' Hwant hja hat nyskes tsjin my sein: '5 maeije kinne wy de flagge útstekke, dan binne wy bifrijd'.\"\n't Is krektsa op dy datum útkaem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29674,"r":"CJ111123","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul foresee deaths in passing funeral processions. They are driven out of bed at night to walk ahead of the processions and accompany them. If you walk in the middle of the road at night, you can be pushed aside by a funeral procession. People born with a caul never lose their second sight.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Minsken dy't mei de helm geboaren binne, sjogge lykstaesjes. Dy't dy eigenskip hat, kin dat noait wer kwyt wurde. Ik haw net sa'n ien kend, mar ik wit wol dat se der binne. Nachts matte hja der út. As der ergens in lykstaesje is - dy't hja dan fan tofoaren sjogge - dan matte se dêrby wêze. Dêrtroch binne se nachts faek warber. Sa'n lykstaesje matte se liede. Hja matte foaroan rinne.\nMen mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne by nacht, hwant dan kin men oan kant treaun wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29693,"r":"CJ111204","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul are often driven out of bed at night to foresee deaths in passing funeral processions. One man born with a caul was once struck by a hearse when he did not step far enough aside as it passed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei de helm geboaren wie, moest alles foarút sjen. Sa'n ien moast nachts faek fan bêd ôf, dan moest er nei in lykstaesje sjen, dy't passearde. Yn dizze buert hat ek sa'n man wenne.\n't Is ris in kear gebeurd, dat dy man de nachts wer thús kaem by syn frou, doe hied er in hiel sear plak oan 'e holle. Doe wie er net fier genôch oan kant gong, doe't de lykwein passearde. Dy man hat yn Bûtenpost wenne. It wie yn 't Wêst fan Bûtenpost dat er dy stomp fan 'e lykwein krigen hat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29713,"r":"CJ111308","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"If someone is born with a caul and the caul is removed the wrong way, that person must get out of bed all their life to watch funeral processions pass.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon wurde mei de helm geboaren. Wurdt dy helm op 'e forkearde menier forwidere dan mat sa'n ien letter altyd lykstaesjes sjen. Dy matte der dan nachts faek út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29732,"r":"CJ111405","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant girl predicts that something is about to happen in the family. That night she sees a funeral procession coming from her brother's place. The vision comes true: shortly afterwards the girl's brother dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear sei myn dochter: \"Nou wurdt it minder, nou komt it tichterby. Ik leau, der gebeurt nóu hwat yn 'e famylje.\" Doe hie se dy nachts by myn soan (har broer) in lykstaesje weikommen sjoen. Hja makke der har ûngerust oer.\nRidlik gau dêrnei krige myn soan in âld man yn 'e kost, en dy hie dêr noch mar even west, doe kaem dy to forstjerren. En dàt hie myn dochter sjoen.\nDat gebeurde èk yn 'e Vogelzang yn 'e Westerein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29733,"r":"CJ111406","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant man often has to get up at night because he has a vision. Once he sees his son hanging dead in an apple tree. The vision comes true: the next day the son hangs himself.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wenne in âld man op 'e Sânbulten, dat wie Bontsje Keke. Dy hat in min leven hawn. Dy moest ek alles fan tofoaren sjen en dan koed er net op bêd bliuwe. Dan mòest er der út.\nOp in nacht seach er dat syn soan dea yn in apelbeam hong. Dy hie himsels ophong. Keke seach it wylst er op bêd lei.\nDe oare deis moest Keke der op út. De jouns kaem er thús. Doe wie syn soan net yn 'e hûs. Doe gong de âld man nei 't apelhôf ta en dêr sjocht er syn soan hingjen oan in apelbeam.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29734,"r":"CJ111407","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant man sees his daughter lying dead in the lake. The vision comes true: a few days later the girl drowns herself.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Gebeurde èk op in nacht, doe seach er syn dochter dea lizzen yn 'e dobbe. Dy hie harsels forsûpt.\n't Kaem krektsa út.\nIn pear dagen letter wie 't doe gebeurde 't echt. Doe foun er har yn 'e dobbe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29739,"r":"CJ111412","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant man is constantly driven out of bed to have visions. When he tries to stay in bed, a hand lifts him off it. Once the man has to walk a long way before he has a vision. He sees a decorated cart drawn by a white horse. He also sees a great many people and all sorts of other carts. He has foreseen the Queen's Day celebrations.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Keke hat wolris prebearre op bêd lizzen to bliuwen. Mar dat joech de man neat. Dan krige er in hân op 'e rêch en dy lichte him út bêd wei.\nOp in kear, doe moest hy der èk wer út. Mar doe wie 't net in lykstaesje. Hy moest alhiel nei Kollumersweach ta. Letter sei er: \"Hwat ik doe sjoen ha kinne jimme jim noait bigripe. Der roan in wyt hynder foar de wein, en alles wie forsierd. 't Wienen allegear minsken en allegear weinen. In hiele optocht.\"\nDoe hie er in koaninginnefeest fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29766,"r":"CJ111504","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul often foresee deaths in passing funerals and funeral processions. Their visions almost always have to do with death. It is told of one man born with a caul that he is driven out of bed at night to have a vision. An invisible force opens gates for him so that he can continue unhindered to the place where the vision is to appear.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der binne minsken dy wurde mei de helm geboaren. Dy ha 't letter neat to rûm. Dy matte allerhande dingen foarút sjen en 't binne hast altyd minder moaije dingen dy't se sjogge, lyk as bigraffenissen en lykstaesjes.\n't Hat hast altyd mei de dea to meitsjen. Hjir yn 'e omkriten hat ek sa'n man west. De stumper moest wit hoe faek fan bêd ôf, altyd by nacht. Dan koed er net lizzen bliuwe, dan mòest er de lykstaesje sjen. Dan waerden de hekken foar him iependien troch in ûnsichtbere macht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29801,"r":"CJ111605","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman suffers greatly from her frequent visions. She is very upset when she foresees deaths in passing funeral processions. One night, when she has to go out to have a vision, she stumbles. Through the fall she loses her second sight.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn beppe wie och sa'n gefoelich minske. Hja kaem ris in kear by ús, doe wie se hielendal fan 'e wize. Hja hie hwat sjoen en as hja hwat seach, dan grypte har dat bot oan. Dan hie se gjin rêst mear.\nMyn beppe seach wol faker hwat. Dat mòest se sjen. Dat wie sà kaem.\nPake wie in man mei soms nuvere, healwize oanslaggen. Hy wie tsiiskoopman. Hy sutele mei tsiis by de doarren lâns. Dy tsiis hied er dan yn in sek.\nOp in joun kaem er thús, doe hied er dy lege sek oer de holle hawn, en dat hie nuver like fansels.\nBeppe wie in skrikachtich minske. Doe't se dat seach, waerd se sa kjel, dat hja rekke hielendal oerstjûr.\nEn sûnt dat moment moest se foarút sjen.\n't Kaem frijwol altyd nei hwat se seach. Mar 't minske pakte der raer mei om. 't Wie in swiere straf foar har. As hja in bigraffenis fan tofoaren sjoen hie, moest sa'n bigraffenis earst fan kant wêze, dan kaem se wer by. Ik wie doe sa'n tsien jier âld, mar ik wit noch, dat der by ús yn 'e buert in berntsje siik wie.\nBeppe wie doe alhiel fan 'e wize. Hja hie de lykstaesje fan dat berntsje al sjoen.\nNachts moest se faek ta 't bêd út om hwat to sjen. As de saek dan goed en wol fan kant wie, klearre beppe wer op.\nOp in kear moest se der wer op in nacht op út. Doe is se stroffele en fallen. Troch dat fallen is sy it kwyt rekke. Doe hoefde se net wer hwat to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29923,"r":"CJ111712","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The seventh of seven sons is born with a caul.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Keke wie mei de helm geboaren. De sawnde soan fan sawn soannen wie mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29954,"r":"CJ111804","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul is often driven out of bed at night to have a vision. At the time of the Spanish flu (November 1918) the clairvoyant sees as many as seven funeral processions at once.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Knjillis wie algemien bikend. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren, dat wist elkenien. Nachts moest er faek út bêd wei om hwat to sjen. Dy't dat hat, kin net lizzen bliuwe. Dat mei nou ienkear net.\nOp in kear wie Bontsje Knjillis bot fan 'e wize. Doe hied er wol sawn lykstaesjes tagelyk sjoen. Dat wie yn 'e tiid fan 'e Spaenske gryp (novimber 1918).","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30070,"r":"CJ112308","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often has to get up at night to foresee deaths in passing funerals. He even foresaw the deaths of his own son and daughter, but he did not foresee that they would hang and drown themselves respectively.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Keke wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy wist altyd hwannear't der ien deagean soe. De bigraffenis hie er altyd al fan tofoaren sjoen. Dat wie meastal by nacht. Dan moest er út bêd wei, en soms moest hy der in hiel ein om rinne.\nSyn soan hat himsels ophong yn in apelbeam, yn 't hôf. Fan tofoaren wist Keke dat de jonge stjerre soe. \"Ik seach wòl,\" sei er, \"dat de jonge dea wie, mar ik seach nèt dat er him ophingje soe. Oars hie 'k dat wol keare kind.\"\nSa hat er ek witten dat syn dochter deagean soe. Dy hat harsels fordronken yn in âld dobbe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30116,"r":"CJ112504","p":"Hijum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A midwife pulls the caul of a newborn backwards off its face. The child will be spared from visions. (Only if the caul is removed forwards does the person foresee, for example, deaths in passing funeral processions.) A greedy doctor is furious because the midwife has burned the caul.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Beppe Gjetsje waerd as kreamheinster oeral hinne roppen. Op in kear gebeurde it dat ien in lytsen krige, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dat wie in flues dat it bern foar 't gesicht siet. Doe hat beppe dat flues der nei achteren ta ôflutsen, net nei foaren, dêr paste se wol foar op. Oars hie 't bern letter altyd lykstaesjes yn 'e nacht sjen matten.\nDoe't de dokter letter gewaer waerd dat dat bern in helm oer 't gesicht hawn hie, woed er dy helm mei alle gewelt ha. Hy wie lulk op beppe, doe't dy sei, dat se de helm forneatige hie. Beppe hie him opbarnd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30133,"r":"CJ112521","p":"Hijum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often foresees deaths in passing funeral processions. His visions always come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem fortelde, der wenne in man yn Hijum, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy placht to sizzen: Der komt binnenkoart wer ien op it hôf. Hy hie de hiele lykstaesje lânskommen sjoen. Hy fortelde dan hwa't der allegear achteroan rounen, en hwer't se lâns gongen. 't Kaem altyd út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30365,"r":"CJ112903","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul is constantly forced to foresee things.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der binne minsken, dy waerden mei de helm geboaren.\nSokken matte alles sjen. Bontsje Keke wie der ien fan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30389,"r":"CJ113021","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman born with a caul often has to get up at night to foresee deaths in passing funeral processions. The visions always come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoansuster Katrine wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest wit hoe faek nachts út bêd om in lykstaesje to sjen. Dan koe it minske net lizzen bliuwe. Dan hie se it krap. It kaem altyd nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30454,"r":"CJ113203","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul often foresee deaths in funeral processions at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wennen froeger guon, dy wienen mei de helm geboaren. Dy seagen nachts lykstaesjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30884,"r":"CJ114108","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man tells of his dream in which a skipper jumps in after his daughter to save her from drowning. The skipper and his daughter then both drown. It is a prophetic dream: the next day a skipper and his daughter die in that way.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wurke yn 'e Noard-Oastpolder. Dêr wie ek in man, dy hiet fan Majoor. Dy fortelde ús ris in kear, dat hy hie droomd, dat hy hie sjoen, dat in skipper syn famke neisprong dy't oer board fallen wie en dat se doe beide forsûpt wienen.\nDe oare deis krige er biricht fan syn famylje, dat syn skoansoan, dy't skipper wie, dy wie syn famke nei sprong doe't dy oer board fallen wie en dêr wienen se beide by fordronken.\nIk wie der sels by doe't dy brief kaem. De deis tofoaren hie er 't ús forteld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30888,"r":"CJ114202","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman dreams that a milkman comes to her bed to say that something bad is about to happen. The dream comes true: a few days later the same milkman comes to tell the woman that her friend is dead. It is whispered that a doctor poisoned the man.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Atsjemuoi en Trynmuoi wienen susters. Atsjemuoi wie troud mei Andersom en Trynmuoi hie forkearing mei Wibe de boer. Hja wie yn forwachting fan Wibe. Op in nacht wienen Anders-om en Tryn har oansteande togearre to mollefangen.\nDoe slepte Trynmuoi by Atsjemuoi op 'e Boelensloane. Hja slepten yn 't selde bêd.\nDoe droomde Trynmuoi, Manus Steensma, de molkrider kaem by it bêd, dêr't hja en Atsjemuoi leinen. Hy hie in swart kleed by him, en dat hâldde hy nouris boppe de iene en dan wer boppe de oare. Doe sei er: \"Dyselde dêr't ik it kleed opgoai, dy oerkomt in ûngelok.\" Op 't lêst hie er it kleed oer Tryn-muoi dellein. In pear dagen letter brocht dyselde Manus Steensma it biricht dat Wibe de Boer, Tryn har feint dea wie. (De nachts tofoaren wie Wibe biroerd woarn. Doe wienen se nei 't Fean ta gong, nei dokter Keizer, hwant Wibe wie skjin forlegen. Dokter Keizer hie yn 'e kroech sitten to kaertspyljen mei oaren. Hy woe net mei nei Wibe ta. Even letter wie der al wer ien kaem foar Wibe. Doe hie dokter Keizer op it lêst, heal dronken en flokkende in drank meijown. Dêr hienen se Wibe fan jown en doe wie Wibe alhiel opset rekke en syn tonge hielendal dik. Dyselde nachts wie er stoarn. De oare deis kaem dokter Keizer dêr. Hy hie it drankje krigen, dat er meijown hie, en dat hie er gau yn 'e bûse stutsen. \"Dat neem ik maar weer mee,\" hied er sein, \"daar heeft een ander toch niets aan.\" Se w","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":210901,"r":"VODA_046_09","p":"Beverwijk","v":"N.-H.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man had signed on to a ship, but when the moorings were cast off he quickly jumped ashore. The ship never returned. It was lost with all hands.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Een broer van mijn vader die heb.. die heb in de gevangenis gezeten voor mijn opa. Dat kon vroeger, hè, dat kon vroeger. Mijn opa die eh... was een Egmonder en die had monstergeld ontvangen, 25 gulden. Dat kreeg hij dan. Toen lagen de zeeën nog met mijnen van ’14 – ’18. Enne.. had al gemonsterd, dus hij moest werken, stapt aan boord, trossen worden losgegooid, legt al van de wal af, springt van boord af, twa.. te water, gaat d’r uit en gaat weer naar huis toe. ‘t Schip is nooit teruggekeerd [pief?], met man en muis vergaan."},{"n":210912,"r":"VODA_046_11","p":"Beverwijk","v":"N.-H.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Granny had a kind of sixth (in the text: seventh) sense. She felt that someone was in a very bad way and sent Grandpa there.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"D’r was ene Tijms uit Heemskerk, en daar werkte me moeder als kind zijnde, aardbeien plukken. Nou, en dan had je voor die school, ja, d’s eh.. wat bijverdienden en zo. Toen zegt me opoe tegen me opa: “Je moet eventjes naar ouwe Koerd toe gaan, want die hebt je nodig. \n“Ah, welnee.” \n“Die het je nodig, want het is heel slecht met ‘m.”\nNou, me opa die z.. die ging dan heen en ‘t was werkelijk heel slecht met ‘m. Want dat paard had tyfus. Had ie opgelopen en hij is er ook aan doodgegaan diezelfde avond. Had een doorntje van een singel in z’n hand gehad. En die heb ie d’r uit getrokken en toen heb die die paard aangeraakt en dat is... Toen was ’t niet meer te redden, en die is ook die nacht overe. overleden. En die zintuigen had me opoe allemaal, een soort zevende zintuig."},{"n":12431,"r":"DIVTX009","p":"Den Dungen","v":"N.-Br.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man is loading his cart with wood. A gentleman comes by and claims he should not load any more, because then the horse will not be able to pull the cart. The man pays no attention and puts more wood on the cart. But the horse indeed cannot pull the cart, and the man has to take off exactly as much wood as the gentleman had predicted.","i":"J.S.","o":"Marinus van der Heyden was hout op zijn kar aan het laden. Hij had er 60 à 70 'musters' op liggen, toen er een heertje voorbijkwam, dat zei dat, als hij er nog meer op zou laden, het paard de kar niet meer zou kunnen trekken. Maar hij sloeg er geen acht op en laadde gewoon verder. Toen hij aan wilde rijden kon het paard de kar niet trekken. Hij heeft er zoveel af moeten laden als er op lagen toen het heertje voorbijkwam."},{"n":12437,"r":"DIVTX015","p":"Den Dungen","v":"N.-Br.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Two farmers travel to town to sell their vegetables and fruit. There is a premonition that something will go wrong, so on the way they decide to have a drink at an inn. When they see another farmer go by, they actually want to catch up with him, but the landlady has the gift of foresight and says there is no need. When the farmers leave later, they catch up with the farmer after all: a wheel has come off his cart.","i":"J.S.","o":"Marinus Sanders ging met Hannes Eykemans naar de markt in Eindhoven om groente en fruit te verkopen. Ze reden langs een café en Hannes zei dat ze daar maar iets moesten gaan drinken omdat er anders iets mis zou gaan. Toen ze binnen zaten, zagen ze dat een boer het café niet binnenging en ze wilden snel weggaan omdat die boer anders eerder in Eindhoven zou aankomen. Maar de waardin zei dat ze zich maar geen zorgen moesten maken. Even later vertrokken ze en onderweg haalden ze de boer, die hen voorbijgereden was, in. Het rad was van zijn kar afgelopen."},{"n":128420,"r":"VODA_017_04","p":"Heerlen","v":"L.","y":1976,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"The woman foresees a death. His shirt was too small.","i":"H.E.","o":"Op een andere mijn eh was iemand doodgebleven en die droeve tijding die moest de vrouw worden overgebracht ja en dat was eh natuurlijk eh een van de minste eh makkelijke onderwerpen enne boodschappen die men kan gaan brengen hè. En toen zag de vrouw eh die angstig de deur openmaakte twee mannen staan en en en en ze riepe eh eh ‘Ohoh mijn man is doodgebleven!’ Hetgeen de twee mannen anders zomaar niet direct hadde willen zeggen, vanzelfsprekend niet, ze dachten de vrouw nog wat afleggende hoop te geven door maar maar te zeggen: ‘ja dood dood. De man is nog niet dood hè, alhoewel.’ En de vrouw viel hen in de rede hè. Die zei: ‘nou vertel het maar recht uit, hij is dood gebleven.’ Ze brak in tranen los. ‘Ik dacht het wel! Ik wist het wel! Toen ie wegging’. De twee mannen die stonden even verslagen hè. En, hoe kon ze dat nu weten? Een ongeluk kan men toch niet vooruitzien? Nee, niet vooruit zien, maar wel voor voelen. ‘Toen de man wegging’, zei ze, ‘was z’n hemd te klein en hij ging nie graag werken.’ ‘Hij ging anders überhaupt niet graag werken mevrouw.’ ‘Nee nee nee en hij zocht een reden om thuis te blijven. Hij is gegaan. Ik drong aan. En toen ie weg was, toen kreeg ik het voorgevoel. En nu is het dan toch werkelijkheid.’"},{"n":128580,"r":"VODA_017_15","p":"Heerlen","v":"L.","y":1976,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"An old woman born with a caul predicts the death of a miner.","i":"H.E.","o":"In een van die dorpen van de gemeente Kerkrade, daar moet een oude vrouw gewoond hebben of of of ja, die profetisch was. Zo gaat met de helm geboren jaa. Op een avond had men het erover in een herberg. Een mijnwerker die het aanhoorde lachte erom en die mengde zich in het gesprek: ‘Alai, ik bin dus benöwd watvoor wommes ‘t van mich zal sagen’, gekscheerde hij. Waarop de de vrouw geweldig begon door te halen hè. En de mensen die nog aan zulke quatsch geloofden, bespottelijk maakte. Ja maar enige dagen later trof het dat hij in aanraking kwam met de bewuste ouwe vrouw. En zij voorspelde hem à bout portant dat hij nog dezelfde dag in de mijnschacht zou vallen. Maar nog haarder en spottender loech de man, welgemoed nam hij z’n pungel, en stapte naar de Domaniale, waar hij werkte met de meddejdienst. Doch eer de dag om was, kwam van de mijn het bericht thuis dat de man was verongelukt, hij was in de mijnschacht gestort. Ennem had hem onder in de zoem verpletterd opgenomen."},{"n":31018,"r":"CJ115022","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul who is fond of a drink often foresees deaths in passing funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op Feanwâldsterwâl wenne Úlke v.d. Meer. Dy neamden se Úlke Bok omdat er altyd bokken en geiten hie.\nIk ha him wol kend. Hy wie bot oan 'e drank. Hy sûpte sa, sei er, omdat er mei de helm geboaren wie. Hy wie altyd fuort op 'e fyts. Hy mocht graech by sé wêze. Dan seach er de dingen net. Oars seach er altyd lykstaesjes. Hy wist altyd fan to foaren as der ien deagean soe, mar hwa't it wie wist er net.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31026,"r":"CJ115030","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A girl wants a fortune teller to predict her future. At first the fortune teller does not want to say, but when the girl keeps insisting she gives in: she has foreseen the girl's funeral. A few weeks later the girl does indeed die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem fortelde, in jongfaem fan Surhústerfean gong ris nei Ljouwert ta nei in wiersizter. Hja woe graech de takomst witte. Mar dy wiersizter woe it earst net sizze. De faem hâldde oan, hja woe it witte. Doe sei de wiersizter op it lêst, hja hie de bigraffenis fan dy faem sjoen. In pear wiken letter wie dy faem dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31113,"r":"CJ115508","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant foresees a death in a passing funeral procession. The vision comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining fan Houtigehage wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy moest alles sjen. En dat binne gjin fabeltsjes, dat wie de wierheit.\nBoardzer sei ris in kear tsjin my: \"Och Frâns, hwat haw ik in minne nacht hawn. Ik moest der fannacht wer ôf, hwant dêr wie in lykstaesje. Hy fortelde my fan hwa't de lykstaesje wie dy't er sjoen hie.\n't Wie dy fan Jan Veenstra (Jan Bron seinen wy), hjir yn 'e Houtigehage, net sa fier fan ús ôf. Ik waerd kjel, hwant Jan wie wol in âld man, mar hy like noch goed soun en hy die syn wurk noch by de boer. Mar de oare wyks wied er dea en de lykstaesje gong foar Boardzer syn hûs lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31114,"r":"CJ115509","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul foresees the death of his brother-in-law in a passing funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sa hat er ek de lykstaesje sjoen fan syn sweager Bearend, dy't mei Durkje troud wie. Dy wie yn 'e ûngetiid op 'e Fryske Klaei, doe't er stoar. Boardzer doarst it net to sizzen tsjin syn suster Durkje, mar de hiele bigraffenis seach er hjir yn Houtigehage.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31180,"r":"CJ115805","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant man is often driven out of bed at night to foresee deaths in passing funeral processions. Sometimes he can predict exactly who will die when he recognises the people in the procession. The visions always come true. The man was born with a caul - a membrane over the head. Greedy midwives are often after cauls to sell them dearly to doctors. If the caul is burned immediately after birth, the child has no clairvoyant gifts.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Jistrum wenne in man, dy moest altyd bigraffenissen fan tofoaren sjen. Heit hat dat wol faek forteld, mar ik wit de namme fan dy man net mear. Wit hoe faek gebeurde it yn 'e nacht, dat hy der út moest om sa'n bigraffenis to sjen. Hy moest der soms hiele einen om rinne. Soms koed er krekt sizze hwa't it wie, dy't yn 'e kiste lei. Dat seach er dan oan 'e minsken dy't achter it lyk oan rounen. It kaem letter altyd krekt sa út lyk as hy it sjoen hie. Sa'n ien wie mei de helm geboaren. Dat wie in flues, dat him oer de holle siet. De kreamheinsters woenen sa'n helm altyd graech ha. Dy knoffelen de helm achterút en forkochten him djûr oan 'e dokter. En dan moest sa'n bern letter alles sjen. As se de helm by de geboarte fuortdaliks forbrânden, hie it bern de gave fan it sjen net mear.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31209,"r":"CJ115901","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often has to get up at night to foresee deaths in passing funeral processions. The clairvoyant also foresees other things.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Frytsen wenne to Eastemar. Hja wie mei de helm geboaren. Hja moast altyd lykstaesjes sjen. Meastal wie dat yn 'e nacht. Dan gong Frytsen fan it bêd ôf. Mar hja seach ek wol oare dingen foarút. Op in kear kaem se by Rikele Pot yn 'e winkel. Dy hie in winkel yn galanteryën. Doe sei se: \"Der komt hjir binnenkoarten in greate rammeling by jo.\"\nDe oare deis kaem der yn 'e winkel in planke del, dêr't allegear potten pannen op stienen. Dy foelen yn diggels op 'e flier.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31214,"r":"CJ115906","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman warns two men not to go fishing: their boat will capsize and come back without them. The men ignore the woman and go fishing anyway. Her prediction comes true: both men drown; an empty boat comes back.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Twa manlju soenen to fiskjen op 'e Leijen. Hja waerden warskôge troch in frou, hja moesten net nei de Leijen ta. Hwant as se dêrhinne gongen, sei se, soe 't boatsje wol weromkeare, mar sûnder har.\nDe beide manlju steurden der har net oan. Hja binne op 'e Leijen fordronken. It lege boatsje is weromkaem en op 't selde plak lizzen gong dêr't de mannen ynstapt wienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31310,"r":"CJ116517","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman born with a caul foresees a death at night in a passing funeral procession. The vision comes true: a week later the real funeral takes place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Frou Groenhof fan Aldegea (H.O.) lei op in nacht op bêd. Wylst se dêr lei seach se in bigraffenis foarby gean. Hja wie doe siik. Sahwat in wike letter wie de echte bigraffenis dêr. Se seinen dat frou Groenhof mei de helm geboaren wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31311,"r":"CJ116518","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man has had a vision and predicts that a strange yellow flower will grow at a certain spot in the churchyard. The vision comes true: when the man dies shortly afterwards, a yellow evening primrose grows on his grave.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Eastemar wenne in man dy sei op dat en dat plak op it tsjerkhôf sil in fremde blom groeije. Hy hie dêr in fisioen fan hawn. 't Wie in giele blom, dy't er noch noait sjoen hie. Dy man is koart dêrnei stoarn. Doe kaem der op syn grêf in theunisblom to stean, dy't net ien thús bringe koe, hwant dy blom kaem yn Eastemar net foar.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31417,"r":"CJ117510","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"If the caul of someone born with one is destroyed just after birth, that person is not tormented by visions. People born with a caul often foresee deaths in passing funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wienen guon, dy wienen mei de helm geboaren. Dat flies moast fuort forneatige wurde, oars seagen se letter lykstaesjes fan tofoaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31482,"r":"CJ117903","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul foresee deaths in passing funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir op 'e heide wennen wol minsken dy't fan tofoaren al wisten dat der gau ien nei 't hôf ta brocht wurde soe.\nSe seagen dan fan tofoaren de lykstaesje. Sokken wienen mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31484,"r":"CJ117905","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"An old woman can tell who stole her gooseberries without having seen the thieves.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik en myn kameraed sieten op in nacht by in âld minske ta de krúslanders. It âld minske lei op bêd. Mar hja wist de oare deis wol to sizzen hwa't har krúslanders stellen hie. Hja hie 't sjoen sûnder dat se út it bêd wei west hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31505,"r":"CJ118010","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul often have to get up at night to foresee deaths in passing funeral processions. From the procession it is often possible to tell who will die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon wienen mei de helm geboaren. Sokken moesten alles fan tofoaren sjen. Sa'n man wie greate Sjoerd (Dykstra) fan 'e Achterwei to Sumar. Hy wie koedriuwer en moest der nachts soms ôf om nei in lykstaesje to sjen. Oan deselden dy't achter it lyk oanroannen koed er dan meastal wol birekkenje hwa't der stjerre soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31522,"r":"CJ118106","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man with a black-haired wife suddenly misses his purse. A card reader predicts that a 'black figure' has taken his purse. It turns out his own wife did it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Remmelt de Haan hat hjir wenne. Hy wie troud mei Maei, dy wie tige swart fan hier. Njonken harren wenne Hjerre Dykstra en Klaske. Op in kear hienen se mei har fjouweren út to riden west oer iis, op redens, doe miste Remmelt syn boekje mei jild. Maei sei: \"Ik ha 't net!\"\n\"Soenen Hjerre en Klaske it pakt ha?\" tocht er.\nDe oare moarns ried er oer iis nei Nijebrêge ta, nei Hinke Kaert, hwant hy woe wite hwer't syn jild bleaun wie. Hy lei de saek oan Hinke út.\nHinke Kaert sei: \"Jo ha in swarte gedaente dêr by jo, dy matte jo in bytsje yn 'e gaten hâlde, hear.\"\nDe oare moarns lei syn boekje mei jild ûnder 't kessen op bêd. Syn eigen wiif hie 't hawn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31574,"r":"CJ118603","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man's dream that a certain woman has died comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en pake Tamme meanden op in stik lân yn Wergea.\nOp in moarn waerd de âld man wekker.\n\"Jelle,\" sei er, \"ik hie fannacht in nuvere droom. Symens Bintsje (de frou fan Symen Bergsma) is fannacht overleden.\"\nSa wie 't ek. Dyselde nachts is se forstoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31635,"r":"CJ119211","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often foresees deaths.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Tike wenne Anne Tiekstra, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy moest bigraffenissen fan tofoaren sjen.\nTichteby wie in dobbe. \"Hjir sil nochris in bern yn dizze dobbe fordrinke\", sei er. Dat hie er sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31792,"r":"CJ119704","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul often has to get up at night to foresee deaths in passing funeral processions. He sometimes also has visions of other things.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wenne hjir in sikere Spinder, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest der nachts faek ôf om nei lykstaesjes to sjen. Hy seach ek oare dingen. Hjir wienen twa mannen dy krigen hevige rúzje om in reed. Doe moesten se foar 't kantongerjocht komme. Mar de iene liichde mear as de oare. Doe hat men Spinder der by roppen, omt dy heldersjende wie. Dy fortelde de wierheit. Hy wenne oan 'e Boskwei by de tramhalte.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31810,"r":"CJ119722","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A fortune-teller tells a widow that the first man who treats her well will become her second husband. The prediction comes true: shortly afterwards the widow marries her late husband's brother.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jurjen en Melle har heit wie overleden. De widdou bleau mei de beide jonges sitten, dat wienen doe noch mar fan dy baeskes. Doe sei greate Sjoerd op in kear tsjin har: \"De earste man dystû hjoed tomjitte komste, dat wurdt dyn twade man.\" En dat kaem ek sa. Har twade man dat wie Abraham van der Leest, in broer fan har earste man.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31895,"r":"CJ120304","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman sees a man drown. The vision later comes true. When the woman hears that someone has drowned, she knows at once who it is.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Antsje fan Sumarreheide, widdou fan Folkert Hountsje (= van der Wal) hie sjoen dat Paulus, in broer fan Folkert, fordrinke soe. Doe't it dan echt gebeurde en hja hearde dat der ien forsûpt wie, sei se: \"Dan sil dat ús Paulus wol wêze.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31896,"r":"CJ120305","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"An old man keeps saying that a certain woman had died that night. The man is right: the woman in question turns out to have died that same night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger gong ús famylje faek to meanen nei de Earnewarren.\nOp in simmer wie pake Tamme mei twa fan syn jonges Binne en Jelle dêr yn 'e blaugerzen by de Krúswetters.\nJelle hie even nei hûs west om hwat op to heljen en kaem de oare moarns bitiid werom.\n\"Hoe is 't hjir?\" frege Jelle-om.\n\"Wol goed, jonge,\" sei Binne-om, \"mar 't wurdt mei de âld man minder. Hwant dy praet de hiele moarn mar oer Simens Bintsje (de frou fan Simen Bergsma). Hy biweart mar dat dy fannacht stoarn is. Hy hie it stjerren meimakke.\"\nDoe sei Jelle-om: \"De âld man hat it by 't rjochte ein. Bintsje is fannacht overleden, ik ha 't nyskes krekt heard.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31986,"r":"CJ121105","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman foresees that a man will drive his horse and cart into the canal. The man does not believe it, but the vision comes true all the same.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't de brêge yn 'e Westerein makke is - dat hat yn 1915 of 1916 west - hat Jehannes Janke - de frou fan Jehannes de Jong - hwat fan tofoaren sjoen. Janke wenne flak by de brêge, yn 't earste húske oan 'e Boppewei.\nDêr wie doe in pont, salang se mei de brêge dwaende wienen. De molkrider Japik Hoeksma moest ek mei dy pont oer. Hy hie in swiere wein mei twa hynders der foar.\nDoe sei Janke op in kear tsjin him: \"Jo reitsje mei jou hynders yn 'e feart.\"\nMar dêr gebeurde neat en de lêste reis mei de pont soe wêze. De oare deis soe de nije brêge yn gebrûk komme.\nDoe sei de molkrider: \"Nou mat it dan gebeure, oars hat Janke gjin gelyk.\" Hy sei it sa'n bytsje spottend. Doe wie er mei de pont der oer, mar de pont lei noch net fêst. De beide hynders wienen al op 'e wâl. De hynders lutsen oan 'e wein. Mar trochdat de pont net fêstlei gong dy troch dy swiere wein achterút. En doe rekke de wein yn 'e feart mei de beide hynders derby.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32014,"r":"CJ121505","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman born with a caul often has visions of all sorts of events, such as deaths. The same woman can also make a bottle of liquor appear with the jack of spades.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Antsje Grupstra seach alle dingen foarút. Hja seach in skip op it lân, dêr soe letter in feart komme.\nHja stjûrde skoppenboer nei de kroech ta, dan kaem der in flesse mei drank werom. Dy flesse sweefde. De doar gong fansels iepen, en de flesse kaem der al draeijende yn. As dat gebeurd wie, dan wie se alhiel fan 'e kaert.\nHja wie mei de helm geboaren. hja seach alle bigraffenissen út 'e omkriten foarút, mar hja hoefde der net ôf.\nSoms seach se ek deaden. \"Sjoch,\" sei se, \"dêr is dyselde èk. Dy is út syn grêf opstien.\" Dan wiisde se him mei de finger oan, mar in oar seach neat. Dan sei se: \"Mast mar ris even oer 't linker skouder hinne sjen.\" Dat sei se tsjin har man. \"Dan kinst it èk sjen\", sei se.\n\"Sjoch,\" sei se tsjin har man, \"mast even oer side gean, hwant dêr komt hwat oan. Dochst it net, dan bist forlern.\"\nIt hountsje fornaem ek altyd as der hwat wie. Dat waerd dan bang. Hja en 't hountsje seagen it beide.\nHja hat de bigraffenis fan har eigen bern foarút sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32017,"r":"CJ121508","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"Someone once had a vision of a death by drowning. Children are anxiously kept away from the water. The vision has not yet come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy mochten froeger as bern net by de Poel komme.\nDat wie de Kaatspoel yn Grinzer Pein. Hwant dêr soe altyd nochris ien yn forsûpe, wie de hiting. Guon hienen dat fan tofoaren sjoen. Oant nou ta is dêr noait ien yn fordronken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32035,"r":"CJ121706","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man born with a caul foresees deaths in passing funerals. People born with a caul can do all kinds of things that 'ordinary' people cannot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Knjillis wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy moest altyd bigraffenissen fan tofoaren sjen. Dat foarspelde er dan oan oare minsken en it kaem altyd út. Hy mat de bigraffenis fan syn eigen dochter ek fan tofoaren sjoen ha.\nDy't mei de helm geboaren wie koe allerhande handlingen dwaen dy't in oar net koe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32043,"r":"CJ121808","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A folk healer predicts that a soldier is very ill and that even the best doctor cannot cure him. A few days later the soldier dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der hat noait in bettere genezer west as Joast Wiersma fan Jistrum. Dûmny Prins roan sa fier mei him fuort, dat er him professor Wiersma neamde.\nOp in kear sieten se mei har fjouweren to kaertspyljen by Joast yn 'e hûs. Joast spile sels ek mei.\nDoe kaem dêr in jonge man yn 'e doar stean, in sekere Veltman. Dy wie ûnder tsjinst. Hy sei: \"Wiersma, ik soe jo freegje wolle of jo hwat foar my hienen, ik bin net to goed.\"\nJoast bleau op syn plak by de tafel sitten en sei tsjin him: \"Jonge, ik ha gjin guod foar dy, mar de bêste dokter is net to goed foar dy. Dû mast gau sjen datst by sa'n dokter komste.\"\nNei in pear dagen wie er dea. Hoe seach Joast dat sa mar?","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32143,"r":"CJ122515","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"People born with a caul often have to get out of bed at night to foresee deaths in passing funerals.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon dy't mei de helm geboaren wienen moesten bigraffenissen sjen, dy't in dei of hwat letter pleats founen.\nHja moesten dan faek yn 'e nacht fan bêd ôf om to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32218,"r":"CJ123206","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A man has visions because he has sold his soul to the devil. At night he often foresees deaths in passing funeral processions. The devil drives him out of bed to see the procession. The seer also predicts exactly how the funeral of the narrator's father will go. The man later hanged himself from the pear tree.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Knjillis (Veenstra) wie in broer fan pake Fokke. It wie dus myn âldomke. Dy hie himsels oan 'e duvel forkocht. Dêrtroch moest er alles sjen.\nHy seach altyd lykstaesjes en hast altyd by nacht.\nDan siet de duvel him achter. Dan lei er op bêd, mar hy moest er ôf. Fral winterdeis hied er dêr in ôfgrysliken hekel oan. Dan woe er net fan bêd ôf. Mar hy mòest. Dan wachte er soms to lang. Dan moest er rinne om op tiid op 't plak to kommen. Dan stie it swit him op 'e holle. Dan hied er soms allinne noch mar in ûnderbroek oan en in pear sokken. Mear tiid hie er net. Hy hie in lot! Doe't pake Fokke stoar troch in kronkel yn 'e term, kaem syn broer Bontsje Knjillis by beppe om har to kondolearjen. Hy sei tsjin beppe: \"Der sil gâns folk komme.\" Doe neamde er in namme. \"Dy komt èk,\" sei er, \"mast der mar om tinke. Dy giet by de skoarstienmantel stean en leunt dêr mei de earm op. En dy biedt m_ in stoel oan.\"\nBy de bigraffenis sei er tsjin beppe: \"Sjochst nou wol?\" It wie krekt sa útkaem lyk as hy sein hie. Hy hie alles al fan tofoaren sjoen.\nHy hie it lang net maklik.\nYn 'e parrebeam hat er him letter ophong.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32221,"r":"CJ123209","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"With children born with a caul, you must pull the caul off downwards. If you do it the other way round, the child will be troubled by visions. Nurses are often keen to get cauls because carrying one keeps them safe. (After all, if you carry a caul, you are bulletproof.) Cauls are also often sold on. Many Freemasons are said to have a caul.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Soms gebeurt it dat bern mei de helm geboaren wurde. Men mat dan it flues nei ûnderen ta der ôflûke.\nDocht men it krekt oarsom, dan mat it bern letter alles sjen. Pleechsusters yn 't sikenhûs stielen sa'n helm wol. Dy drage se by har. Dan binne se feilich.\nSe wurde ek wol forkocht. Dy't sa'n helm by him hat, dy is kûgelfrij.\nSe sizze dat alle frijmetslers sa'n helm ha.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32247,"r":"CJ123403","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A woman born with a caul foresees deaths in passing funeral processions. Some people also have visions of a fire. Others hear the sound of carpentry at a certain spot, although a house is only built there much later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Drachtster Kompenije wenne in frou, dy wist altyd fan to foaren, as der in bigraffenis komme soe. Hja seach de hiele roustoet fan to foaren. Dat minske wie mei de helm geboaren.\nDer wienen ek wol minsken, dy seagen ergens in hûs fan to foaren yn 'e brân. In skoft letter brânde it dan op. Ek hearden guon wol it timmerjen oan in hûs, dat yn werklikheit pas folle letter gebeurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32285,"r":"CJ124003","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant boy (born with a caul) predicts that his little brother will die. The prediction comes true. The boy often foresees deaths.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn 'e Mouneein wennet in jonge, dy is nou sa'n 20 jier âld. Dy jonge sjocht soms de dea fan 'e minsken foarút. Men seit wol, sa'n ien is mei de helm geboaren. Hy hie in broerke, dat wie in mongoaltsje. Dat jonkje wie twa jier âld, doe sei dy jonge tsjin syn mem doe't dat bern jierdei wie: \"Mem, dit is syn lêste jierdei.\" It kloppe presys. Datselde jiers is it bern stoarn. En dochs wie it net siik. De jonge hie 't sjoen. Dat is nou sahwat trije jier lyn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32286,"r":"CJ124004","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"A clairvoyant boy predicts that a man who has been in poor health for a long time will soon die. The prediction comes true: shortly afterwards the man dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn 'e Mouneein wenne in man dy hat hiel lang sukkele. It bleau altyd op ien hichte. Doe sei dy jonge ris op in kear: \"Dy man stjert.\" Ien of twa dagen letter is der stoarn. De jonge hie 't fan to foaren sjoen. Hy wie der sels alhiel ûnderstoboppe fan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":125692,"r":"KOORD015","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1981,"c":"SINSAG 0489","d":"During his art journey in Italy, Jacob van Campen visits a fortune teller and has his future told. Everything seems to have come true.","i":"C.K.","o":"Over de in 1595 te Haarlem geboren schilder en bouwmeester Jacob van Campen is veel en uitvoerig geschreven. Zijn machtigste en bekendste werk is ongetwijfeld het Paleis op de Dam, dat echter door velen ook nu nog als het stadhuis van Amsterdam wordt gezien en ook als zodanig werd gebouwd. Jacob had al op vrij jeugdige leeftijd de beschikking over een aanzienlijk vermogen, zodat hij de droom van elke jonge kunstenaar kon verwezenlijken, n.l. het maken van een kunstreis naar ltalië, om daar studie te maken van de architectuur en de schilderkunst welke in dat land zo'n grote bloeitijd beleefden. Hij bezocht o.a. Rome, Milaan, Venetië en Vicenza. De indrukken die hij gedurende de ca. twee jaar dat hij in Italië verbleef opdeed, hebben zijn werk aantoonbaar geïnspireerd.\n\nTijdens die Italiaanse reis kwam Jacob eens op een kermis terecht waar zoals gebruikelijk ook een waarzegster haar tentje had staan. 'Allemaal onzin die waarzeggerij,' hoor je veel mensen zeggen, maar in hun hart denken ze 'je kunt nooit weten.' Vandaar de populariteit van allerlei vormen van astrologie of sterrenwichelarij, waar nog steeds een grote consumentenkring voor wordt gevonden.\n\nJacob van Campen stapte bij de waarzegster naar binnen om zich 'voor de aardigheid' zijn toekomst te laten voorspellen. In het vrij duistere tentje zat een vrouw die volkomen beantwoordde aan alle eisen die aan een waarzegster ku"},{"n":13162,"r":"CBOEK127","p":"Ommen","v":"Ov.","y":1881,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"An alderman is herding sheep when he sees a house on fire. He crosses a river by boat to reach the house, but when he stands in front of it, there is no fire to be seen. Later it turns out the man had a clairvoyant vision, for that house actually burned down a number of years later.","i":"M.W.","o":"Bijgeloof\nDit heerscht nog zeer in deze streken. Eenige jaren geleden brandde er een huis af in de buurtschap Giethenen. Een man, die met den meesten van het buurtschap wandelde, vertelde het volgende: hij had in 1860 als knecht gediend bij een boer te Besthenen. Die boer hield ook een scheper. Toen deze eens met zijne schapen in 't veld was, zag hij een huis in Giethenen in brand staan. Hij liep er heen en moest de Vegge nog overvaren, om er te komen. Toen hij bij de schuit kwam zag hij den brand niet meer, waarna hij naar zijne schapen was teruggekeerd. Hij had het 's avonds thuiskomende dadelijk verteld en er bijgevoegd, dat het 't huis was geweest van Welink, den zoon van den boer, wien nu dit ongeluk getroffen heeft. De man, met wien dit gesprek gevoerd werd, verwonderde er zich dan ook volstrekt niet over, dat die brand had plaatsgehad, wijl genoemde scheper dit huis in 1860 al \"gleunig\" (gloeiend) had gezien."},{"n":9289,"r":"CBAK0432","p":"Broek in Waterland","v":"N.-H.","y":1910,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"One side of the body of a boy who has fetched bread in sacks becomes hot. The next day the neighbour's house on the side that was hot is on fire.","i":"C.B.","o":"De volgende verhalen zijn van een Broeker, doch geboortig uit Ermelo.\nHij bracht eenmaal als jongen brood naar huis. Daar kwam de bakker niet aan den deur, maar haalden ze het zelf in groote zakken.\nZijn eene zijde werd toen zoo warm, dat hij thuis komende riep: \"Pak gauw aan, wat is het heet.\"\nDen volgenden dag stond zijn buurmans huis in brand, en wel van dien buurman, die woonde aan de zijde, die heet geweest was."},{"n":42329,"r":"LAAN016d","p":"Lellens","v":"Gr.","y":1930,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man walked past a farm and heard people koekslaan (beating flax). He walked on and saw a barn on fire. When he came closer, it was gone.\nThree weeks later it was Bouldag and two weeks after that the barn burned down.","i":"E.F.","o":"Der was es 'n kerel, dij luip op 'n oavend om uur òf tien op grintweg tussen Midwòl en Scheemte. 't Was stil, - gain staarveling was ter te bekìnnen. \nKomt e 'n boerenploats verbie, mit 'n Ingelze aanleg ter veur. 't ìs roar, doar binnen ze aan 't koukhakken! Hai heurt dudelk de bielen op de koukblòkken.\nDin is 't weg, en hai gaait wieder. Hail dudelk zugt e tussen de bomen deur 'n grode schuur in braand stoan. Hai löpt al haarder en haarder, om de lu te woarschaauwen. Op honderd tree noa is e der bie; weg is 't!\nDrij week ter noa was ter bouldag op ploats, doar e de koukbielen heurd haar, en weer vattien doagen loater braandde de twijde ploats hailendal òf!","l":"Gronings"},{"n":20074,"r":"CJ016709","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A woman born with a caul always has to get up at midnight and then sees things that later come true. In this way she sees beforehand the fire in an inn and a shelf giving way in a pots-and-pans shop, so that the pots and pans fall and break.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Eastemar wenne froeger in âld minske. Frytsen hiet se. Se wie mei de helm geboaren. Om tolve ûre yn 'e nacht moest se der út en dan seach se dingen, dy't in oar net sjen koe. En it kom letter altyd krekt sa út as hja it fan tofoaren sjoen hie.\nSa wie it us doe seach se de herberch 'Het witte peerd' op 'e hoeke fan 'e Snakkerbuorren yn ljochte lôge stean.\nDe oare wyks brânde dy herberch ôf.\nSy kom ek us yn 'e pottewinkel fan Rikele Pot.\n\"Binnen twa dagen gebeurt hjir in ramp\", sei se.\nDe oare deis bijoech him in planke yn 'e winkel en der kom in hiele dracht potten en pannen del, dy't yn diggels foelen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":69424,"r":"ENGELS000713","p":"Hout-Blerick","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man thinks there is a fire in the place he is heading to, sees black smoke, assumes it is an oven; later it turns out a house has burned down.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Voorteken:\nOfschoon ik zelf nooit overgevoelig ben geweest, en mij niet bang liet maken voor deze verhalen, wil ik hier een ervaring vertellen, die mij overkwam, toen ik onder dienst was. Ik diende in Venlo, doch mijn afdeling lag in de oorlog 1914-18 in Arcen gedetacheerd. Ik ging dikwijls naar huis in vrije uren. Ik lag ingekwartierd bij een bakker. De commandant verzocht mij, omdat ik dat mee in de gang kon, het benodigde vlees voor de groep van de kazerne Venlo mee te brengen, omdat dit niet goed in voorraad kon blijven; dit als tegenprestatie voor het vele verlof. Op een keer, toen ik op weg ging van Venlo naar Arcen, drong de gedachte in mijn hoofd, dat er in de buurt van Lomm, waar mijn kwartier was, brand zou zijn, en dat ik zou moeten helpen. Nadat ik Velden gepasseerd was, zag ik een zwarte rook, en kwam de gedachte: “Heb ik dan toch goed gedacht?” bij mij op. Ik verwierp deze echter, en veronderstelde, dat het de bakkersoven zou zijn. Toen ik aankwam, bleek het huis van de buurman afgebrand!"},{"n":210471,"r":"ENGELS001217","p":"Maasbree","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"The priest urges people to go to Mass, otherwise a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a fire will come true.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Voorteken:\nOmstreeks 1891, toen ik 10 jaar was, riep vader ons op zekere avond op, met de mededeling, dat het hele gehucht Tongerlo, een groep van 9 boerderijen, in brand stond. We zagen het allen duidelijk. Vader liep naar “Tunnen Doeëres” om te helpen. Deze had nog niets gemerkt. Ook mijn vader zag, ter plaatse gekomen, geen vuur.\nDoeëres ging daags daarna naar de pastoor. Deze zei: “Dit is een “voorbericht”. Kom morgenvroeg allen (van dit gehucht) naar de H. mis, op één na, die op het huis past! Anders zal dit voorbericht uit komen.” Dit was pastoor Bloemen.\n\nGeen omzetting in dialect van het verhaal door Engels."},{"n":210485,"r":"ENGELS001301","p":"Beringe","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Fire coming down from the sky onto a house or place is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Geheimzinnige branden:\nMijn moeder vertelde mij van mensen, die meegemaakt hadden, dat ze een vuur uit de hemel omlaag zagen dalen op een huis of een plaats, waar binnen een paar dagen iemand ging sterven. Men noemde dit vuur hier “de Neerbrand”.\nMijn stiefmoeder Trien woonde vroeger op Maris, een gehucht aan Beringe. Op een keer was de meid bezig met de was. Opeens zag ze de Neerbrand uit de lucht vallen op het huis van de “Ketser”. De meid greep zich van schrik aan de wastobbe vast en schreeuwde: “Kijk eens daar!” Mijn stiefmoeder zag ook het verschijnsel. Een paar dagen later stierf bij de “Ketser” een ongetrouwde halfbroer van Jean Wilms.\n\nMie mooder vertèlde van minsen, die mètgemakt heijen, dé toet d’n hemel e vlammend veur ömlieëg kwaam op ’n hoes. Eur verwaochting dét ’t hoes aaf zoo borre, kwaam neet oet. Ze daochten al, dét ze zich zelf gét wies gemakt heijen. Mér: wie dao nao e paar daag eemes in dét hoes sjtorf, woost ze, dét ze “de Neerbrangkd” gezien heije.\n\nMien sjteefmooder Trien vertèlde, dét ze vreuger, wie zuu nag op Máres wonden, ’n maagd heijen, die op enne kier doonde waas mèt te wéés. Op èns zaag ze boven de boorderei van “de Ketser” de “Neerbrangkd” op ’t hoes neervalle. Ze greep zich van sjrik en de kuup vaost, en sjrieuwde: “Kiek èns tao.” Mooder zaag ’t auch. \ne Paar daag d’r nao sjtorf Ketsers Sjang zienen ongetrouwden half-broor.\n\nVerslag 58, Omzett"},{"n":210500,"r":"ENGELS001502","p":"Helden","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A flame seen earlier above the roof ridge is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a fire.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Voorteken:\nIndertijd, in mijn jeugdjaren, brandde de boerderij van “Faesse Janne”, een boer aan het gehucht Zandberg, die als onkerks en oneerlijk bekend stond, aan de grond af. Een week tevoren zag iemand uit de buurt, dat er een vlam boven over de “voorst” ofwel de nok van het dak van deze boerderij kroop. Dit verschijnsel noemde men hier de “Veur-buike”. \n\nVerslag 48, Omzetting in Heldens dialect van de verhalen, verteld door Reijnders, Petr. Johannes, Helden. Opgenomen onder no. L291-15. Helden, 17-2-1969. Aanvulling Helden, 1-3-1969\nIn miene jongen tied borden de boorderei van “Faesse Jan” op te Zankberg an de grongkt aaf. ’n Wèèk van te veure zaag eemes oet te nabber, det ter ’n vlam boven over de daakvoorst van die boorderei leep. Me numde dit “e veur-buijke”."},{"n":42679,"r":"SPORTEL000201","p":"Noordbroek","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Clay diggers are warned not to put their tools in a farm's barn that evening, because the farm will burn down during the night. The following night the farm burns down.","i":"J.S.","o":"De heer G. Duister te Noordbroek wist te vertellen dat zijn grootvader Geert Duister kleigraver was. Het gedeelte van Noordbroek grenzende aan de gem. Slochteren bestaat uit klei. Als Duister en zijn medegravers 's avonds het werk beeindigden, brachten ze hun spaden in een boerderij van de landbouwer Huisman. Op zekere dag brachten ze 's avonds weer hun gereedschap daarheen en ontmoetten daar een arbeider genaamd Jaap Dekker en wonende in 't veen tussen Noordbroek en Siddeburen. Toen hij hoorde dat ze hun gereedschap in de schuur van boer Huisman wilden zetten, zei Jaap Dekker, \"Doe dat niet want die boerderij brandt vannacht op. De mannen lachten er wat om. In de nacht daarop volgend brandde inderdaad de boerderij af. Volgens de mensen was Dekker een man \"dei kwoad kon zain\". De boerderij is later herbouwd en wordt tegenwoordig bewoond door de landbouwer Rademaker."},{"n":42965,"r":"WEV000602","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Man sees a house on fire and feels that the walls are warm, an omen that the house will burn down.","i":"F.W.","o":"2 Voorloop.\nOp een morgen ging ik naar het werk. \nDaar zag ik opeens het huis van Timp in brand staan.\nNu moet men daar zo snel mogelijk heen gaan.\nZijn de muren koud, dan komt er een dode in dat huis, zijn de muren warm, dan brandt het op.\nIk voelde dus, de muren waren warm.\nDadelijk ging ik naor de vrouw terug.\nIk zeg: \"Timp zien hoes brandt gauw op.\"\nHet heeft nog twee jaar geduurd, toen ging het."},{"n":42967,"r":"WEV000604","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Urgent advice to take out fire insurance, because someone has seen the house on fire. Some time later the house burns down.","i":"F.W.","o":"[4.]\nMijn opa kwam ook eens bij buurman Scheper. \"Hest dien hoes in de brandkaaste Beernd?\"\n\"Nee,\" zei Beernd.\n'n Paor dagen later opa er weer heen.\n\"Beernd, hest 't hoes in de brandkaaste?\"\n\"Nee, nog nich.\"\n\"Dou hum d'r doadeluk in, want ik heb 't branden zain.\"\nEen paar maanden later, daor ging 't huis."},{"n":43311,"r":"WEV001601","p":"Alteveer","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Men see a fire at a spot; one of them predicts that a house will one day be built there.","i":"F.W.","o":"Nee, zelf heb ik nooit iets gezien, dat verdacht voorkwam.\nWel hebben mijn kennissen wonderlijke dingen meegemaakt.\nMijn vriend Lutjeboer van Onstwedde kwam op een avond hier door Alteveer en dan zegt hij: \"Blikgat, doar is ja brand.\" \nHij loopt er vlug op af, maar ziet dan, dat de brand verder is. Thuis gekomen, deelt hij dit zijn ouders mee.\nZijn vader zegt dan: \"O, ik heb 't doar ook al wol brannen zain; pas es op, op dat stee komp nog 'n keer 'n hoes.\" \nEn het is uitgekomen ook.\nNu staat op die plek een huis."},{"n":43319,"r":"WEV002001","p":"Mussel","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Men see the mill house burning in advance, with the smoke going against the wind. Later the mill burns down, with the smoke going in the same direction as seen before.","i":"F.W.","o":"Dwaallicht\nHet zal al meer dan tachtig jaar geleden zijn. Ik was nog een meisje van ongeveer 10 jaar. Op een avond staat mijn vader met een kameraad te praten.\n Daar zien ze opeens vlammen en rook. \n\"Kiek,\" zeggen ze, \"'t meulnhoes stait in brand en de rook gaat tegen de wind in.\" \"Praat er maar niet over,\" zegt mijn vader nog.\n Na enige tijd is het huis bij de molen opgebrand. De rook ging toen inderdaad in de richting, zoals de mannen gezien hadden, want hij was gedraaid."},{"n":43323,"r":"WEV002005","p":"Kopstukken","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"People see a farm on fire, but nothing is wrong. The walls feel cold, a sign that the farm will not burn down but will be demolished.","i":"F.W.","o":"Te Kopstukken ziet men de boerderij van buurman branden. Er is evenwel geen brand. Dadelijk er op af. Men voelt aan de muren. Deze zijn koud. Dat is voor hen een teken, dat het huis niet zal opbranden, maar dat het ter zijner tijd wordt afgebroken. Dit gebeurt ook werkelijk. Nu ongeveer dertig jaar geleden."},{"n":207157,"r":"KUSTERS006927","p":"Geeneind","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A farm burns down after a cat has been seen on the gate.","i":"C.K.","o":"Harrie Heinsbergen woonde achteraf. 'n Boer klopte hem op de schouder en wees hem, dat op 't hek van de brug 'n kat zat. Kort daarop brandde de boerderij af."},{"n":45405,"r":"WEV003203","p":"Valthermond","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A woman sees a house on fire in advance but does not know which house. The owner of one of the houses mentioned therefore takes out fire insurance.","i":"F.W.","o":"[Veurloop.]\nIk wait zölf nog, dat ’n vrou op de Harpel brand zain hef. Schuun achter ons woonde ’n M. Dou hef dat mens ’n hoes brannen zain. Ze zee: “k Wait nich, wel zienent of ’t was; Bodewitz of M.”\nNou, ’t hoes van M. is d’r loater aangoan.\nMan voader, dai anders nich veul van verzekern waiten wol, trok zuk toch zoveul van ’t mens aan, dat hai ’t hoes doadelk in de brandkaaste doan hef.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45407,"r":"WEV003205","p":"Valthermond","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees a house on fire, but nothing is wrong. A warm or cold wall is an omen of fire or a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"[Veurloop.]\nMien schoonvoader luip ’n keer noar de Holte achter Onstwedde. Dou zag ‘e doar inains ’n hoes brannen. Hai d’r gau op of; man dou ‘e dichterbie kwam, vernam ‘e, dat d’r niks te doun was. Dou ‘e dat loater in hoes vertelde, zee’n zien olle lu: “Hast gau aan de muurn vuiln möst, of ze warm wazzen of kold; in ’t eerste geval zol d’r brand komen en anders ’n staarfgeval. Schoonvoader woonde hier in de Valthermond.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45520,"r":"WEV003601","p":"Wedde","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A person born with a caul sees a fire beforehand; a warm wall means a fire, a cold wall a death; sees funeral processions.","i":"F.W.","o":"Met helm geboren.\nHet werd me verteld door de dochter zelf. Vader Nobbe te Holte - onder Onstwedde - was met de helm geboren. Als die helm wordt vernietigd, is er niets aan de hand. Wordt hij bewaard, dan kan de bewuste persoon later kwaad zien. Vader N. kon dat ook; en de eigen dochter zal er toch niet om gelogen hebben.\nHij zag van te voren huizen branden. Meestal gebeurde zo iets ’s avonds en ’s nachts. In zo’n geval ging hij dan ook het huis verlaten en liep in de richting van het onheil. Bij zo’n geheimzinnige brand werd aan de muur gevoeld. Was deze warm, dan zou het huis in de as gelegd worden. Bij koud aanvoelen, kwam er een dode.\nLijkstaties \n zag hij ook. Vaak weer ’s nachts. Op boerenlanen kwam hij ze tegen, daarbij moest hij aan de kant van de weg gaan staan.\nIn Bellingwolde moet er nu nog een jonge man zijn, die zulks zien kan."},{"n":45654,"r":"WEV004101","p":"Vledderveen","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Flames are seen coming from a house; on coming closer there is nothing to be seen.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop\n‘t Is verteld deur G.W. te Onstwedde.\nHai luip es achter ’t huus en dou zag ’e wat brannen. Hai zee ’t ook tegen de mensen. \n“Ik keek noar J.F. zien hoes en door sluigen de vlammen oet. ’k Was d’r nog ’n mooi endken of, man bin d’r gau op of goan. En dou ’k d’r bie kwam, was d’r niks te zain.”\nMoar ja, ’t huus stait d’r nog. Is nog nooit brand in west.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":13765,"r":"WEV004503","p":"Exloo","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Where a fireball turns into a fire is an omen that a barn will be built on that spot. Later ball lightning causes a fire in the barn.","i":"F.W.","o":"Een veertig jaren geleden heurde ik nog een geval van veurloop. ’t Was iemand anders, die wat zien had, nog ’n jonge man. Die kwam van een feestavond en ging op huus aan. \nDaor ziet ie een vuurbol over de weide komen. Die löp veur hum langs en dan wordt de bol tot een vuur.\nPrecies op dezelfde plaats wordt later een heu-schure gebouwd. Moar op ’n keer is ’t er ’n onweer. Een bolbliksem rolt over ’t veld en steekt dan de schure in brand. Dat is toch wel ’n voorbode west, niet?","l":"Drents"},{"n":41142,"r":"WEV004703","p":"Blekslage","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man who can see events in advance advises someone to insure his house, because he has seen it on fire.","i":"F.W.","o":"Op Kopstukken woonde Broene B. Dai wös ook van veurloop. Op ’n moal zee ’e tegen aine: “Hest ’t hoes al verzekerd? As ’t nich zo is, moust ’t doun, want ik heb ’t brannen zain.” Dai ander het ’t hoes verzekern loaten, umdat ’e vertrou’n har in Broene. ’t Hoes is opbrand ook.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43121,"r":"WEV005305","p":"Roswinkel","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"People saw a haunted house on fire, but it was demolished instead of burned down.","i":"F.W.","o":"In Roswinkel stön vrouger 'n spookhoes. Meer dan aine hef 't hoes brannen zain. \nDit is nich goudkomen, want 't hoes is ofbrook'n. Altied kön je d'r dus nich op aan.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43196,"r":"WEV005703","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A prediction that a farm will burn down has not yet come true.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nAltied komt tnou weer nait uut. Hier in t veld stait n boerderij, dat ze 64 joar leden al branden zain hebben. Moar t stait dr nog.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43264,"r":"WEV005903","p":"Wessingtange","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"When his farm burns down, a man says he saw the house on fire long beforehand but kept quiet about it.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nJoarn leden is hier brand west. Ik huilp de boer mit alles. De man stön aal man stil te kiekn en zee:“Nôn brand e ja.”\nIk vruig:“Hou komst door bie, wat betaikent dat?”\n“t Is wol al tien joar leden”, zee e dou, “op n oavend kwam k bie hoes en dou stôn alles in lichtelaaie. k Heb dr nooit over proot, mit ganaine, man nôn brand e ja.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43280,"r":"WEV006001","p":"Smeerling","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"The belief is that a farm will one day burn down if several people see fire there at night. A woman has seen it too, but says the walls were cold when she felt them.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop\nHier stomp bie stön vrouger n grode boerderij.\nAl mennigmoal warn dr gounend, dai t hoes in stoan zaggen. \nMaistieds s nachts. d Lu zeden dan ook, datt nog n keer opbrannen zol. Totdat ze n Duuts meid kregen. Dai zee op n dag:\n“Ik heb t hoes ook brannen zain, man ie huivn joe gain zörge te moakn, want ik heb aan de muurn vuild, en dai warn kold.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43357,"r":"WEV006402","p":"Nieuw-Weerdinge","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Men see a fire, but the next day nothing is wrong with the house; a few years later there is indeed a fire.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nGezien heb k ook es iets. Ik luup met mien bruur deur Nei-Weerding op n oavend. \nIk zegge ineens:“Kiek es, doar steet n huus in de brand.” \nJa heur, de vlammen slugen uut het dak en kropen langs de muurn. Maar de andere dag stun alles er nog.  \nEnkele joarn loater is door n kapschure opbrand; het huus zelf is stoan bleevn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43413,"r":"WEV006801","p":"Vriescheloo","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man who can foresee evil sees little fellows walking on the roof of a house. Later he sees a little man waving on the roof and a fireball when the waving stops. Later the house burns down.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nVrouger hadden wie hier op Loo n oal Oabram K.  Dei zag staarke stokkies. Ik was toun n kwoajong en k heb dr hail wat meroakels van heurd.\n Oabram luip es n keer t dörp deur en toun zee e:“Kiek door ais op t hoes van Huzing. Loopn aal moar klaine kereltjes over t dak. \nVan veurn noar achtern en van achtern noar veurn. Dat bedut kwoad.” \nOal Oabram kon ook kwoad zain, dat was bekend. \nn Zet loater is e zulf bie dei Huzings in hoes en den zeg-e:\n“Ik wait t nait, moar door zit wat op t hoes.”\nZai goan noar boetn en joa heur, nou zugt Oabram ain kereltje op t dak zitn. Dei houwt aal moar mit de aarms op en doale. \nEn toun e door mit op huil, zag Oabram n vuurbale over t dak roln. \nEevn loater zag e t haile hoesin brand stoan. \nNoar verloop van tied is t hoes den ook werklek op brand.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43614,"r":"WEV007303","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A horse standing in the feeding trough is said to have been a forewarning of a later fire.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nZai vertelde ook van n femilielid, dei n kroeg har. \nDei harn n keer veziede kreegn van gounend, dei mit peerd en koetse komen warn. t Peerd mös mor zolaank op staal stoan.  \nDou de veziede s oavends weer vot zol, en ze noar t peerestaal gungen, stön t daier boovn in de krubbe; dat zol ja wat beduden. “\nDoor kump wat achteraan”, zeden ze. \nEn dr gebeurde wat, nog mor drei weekn loater is de kroeg opbrand.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44126,"r":"WEV007406","p":"Musselkanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Lights are seen as a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of fire.","i":"F.W.","o":"Lichten zaggen ze vrouger voak. \"dr brandt weer wat\", zeden ze, zel wel weer gauw n huus aan goan. Dat geleuf was algemain.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":210696,"r":"ENGELS002703","p":"Heythuysen","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"For lack of matches, a pipe is lit with a fireball; after the fireball has come down at a house, the house burns down the next day.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Vuurballen:\nVroeger werden er soms vuurballen waargenomen, zwevend door de lucht. Ze zweefden even boven de grond omhoog en omlaag. Als ze vlak bij een huis op de grond kwamen, brandde dit huis ’s anderendaags af. Mijn grootvader woonde vroeger op een grote boerderij, genaamd “Heiligerhoof”, gelegen in de buurt van “Vossenhof”, doch thans afgebroken. Hij was een hartstochtelijk pijproker, die geen uur zonder kon. Op zekere dag was hij op een perceel tussen struikgewas, aan het werk totdat het donker was. Hij wilde zijn pijp opsteken, doch nu bleek, dat hij geen “zjwègelkes” meer had. Hij stopte, en wilde maar naar huis gaan, doch zag daar een vuurbal laag komen aanzweven, en op de grond terecht komen. Hij was niet erg bang uitgevallen, en dacht: “’t Kan zeen wat ’t wildj; ich maak ter mien piep an aan; angers kan ich neet rouke!” De bal bleek een doorsnee te hebben van 3 dM, en te bestaan uit “bool” (poreuze) as, die rondom gloeide. Hij hield er zijn pijp aan, en zei: “Ich hob ondjervondje: Gé bedank Uch hertelik!” De vuurbal bleef daar gedoofd liggen. ’s Anderendaags verscheen de vuurbal weer boven Roggel, en kwam neer bij café Hogenwald op de “Groeëte Laak”. Het huis brandde daar een dag later af!"},{"n":208730,"r":"LINSSEN006901","p":"Ell","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A burning farm is not on fire when people go to look.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Geheimzinnige brand . De boerderij van Berks, gemeente Grathem, leek 's avonds heel vaak in brand te staan. Ging men dan naderbij om dit te bekijken, dan was de brand op eens verdwenen."},{"n":130191,"r":"BIJLSMA000506","p":"Raerd","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Long before a farm burns down, a fire is seen there while nothing is wrong.","i":"T.B.","o":"De pleats fan Sybrandy ûnder Dearsum is twaris ôfbarnd. Fier foar dy tiid hie men dêr al brân sjoen, wylst der neat to rêdden wie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130236,"r":"BIJLSMA001002","p":"Scharsterbrug","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees a farm on fire and hears roof tiles falling, but there is nothing to be seen. A few days later the farm burns down, and the man hears the roof tiles fall.","i":"T.B.","o":"Heit seach op 'n kear dat der in pleats to Langsweagen yn 'e brân stie. It wie net iens sa botte fier ôf, hy hearde de dakpannen nei ûnderen rotteljen. Doe't er der hinne soe wie it fuort en wie der gjin brân. In pear dagen letter barnde deselde pleats ôf. \nWer hearde heit de pannen rotteljen, lyk as fan to foaren.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130270,"r":"BIJLSMA001501","p":"Sintjohannesga","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"In the evening a rise in the land is bathed in a light glow, like a blanket of fire.","i":"T.B.","o":"Broer Akkerman to Sint-Johannesgea (74), yn syn jongejierren to Rotstergaest, letter boer to Rotsterhaule, fortelde my:\nIn âld minske op 'e Gaest seach op in joun in hichte dêrre yn ljochte gloede stean. It wie oft der in kleed fan fjûr oer it lân lei.","l":"Fries"},{"n":11538,"r":"CJ000322","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A woman sees her house burnt down with a scorched elder tree, but nothing is wrong. Much later the house burns down, with a scorched elder tree beside it, just as the woman saw it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem wie widdou. Op in kear hienen wy as bern mei ús mem nei beppe ta op bisite west. 't Wie yn Aldegea. Doe't wy omtrint oan hûs ta wienen, sloech ús mem biede hanne foar de eagen.\n\"Och heden,\" jammere se, \"ús hûs is forbrând! Der stiet neat mear fan. De forbrânde flearbeammen stean der njonken.\"\nHja koe net fierder en sakke op 'e groun del. Dêr bleau se sitten. De oare bern gyngen njonken har sitten. Doe gong ik allinne fierder. Ik sei tsjin mem: \"As it hûs der noch stiet, dan sil ik wapperje mei de skelk.\"\nIt hûs stie der noch. Der wie neat gebeurd. \nIk ha dit forhael faek oan myn bern forteld. Mar folle letter, doe't myn eigen bern al great wienen, is it hûs dochs forbrând. Alles wie forkoald. En de flearstrûken stienen dêr swart en forbrând njonken, krekt sa't ús mem it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21870,"r":"CJ029010","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees the cattle market next to the inn full of smoke. It is a voorgezicht (a vision of a future event): a few years later the inn burns down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dizze herberch stie oan 'e koemerk. In pear jier foardat er opbrânde, seach Atse Veltman de koemerk fol reek. De wyn wie sa dat de reek dy kant oergong, en doch stie der neat yn 'e brân. Letter stie yndied de koemerk fol reek. Doe brânde de herberch op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21874,"r":"CJ029014","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees smoke at a certain place, as if there is a fire. Some time later a fire really breaks out at that place. It was a voorgezicht (a vision of a future event).","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Atse Veltman fan Eastemar kom us op in nacht thús, doe seach er de koemerk fol reek. In skoftsje letter brânde 'Het witte paard' op. De wyn wie doe krekt sa, dat de reek oer de skoarstien gong.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":49678,"r":"GENDT048","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees a house on fire two days before it actually happens.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Mien schonvoader het duk verteld, dattie ’n keer soaves van de stenove kwam en toe duidelijk zag, dattet huus van Doeleman ien de Nimwegsestroat ien braand ston. En toetie d’r nève kwam, was er niks te zien. Mar twee dage lotter brien ’t wel af. Mien schonvoader hiel altied vol, as wé’j zèje, da we ’t nie gleufde, dattie ’t beslis goed gezien had en twee dagen van teveure. Hé’j kos ’r vuul um worre.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":49696,"r":"GENDT062","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"The fire in an inn is seen a few days in advance.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"D’r brien ’n keer Den Ouwen Dollen Hoed af, ’n herberg in Hulhuze. Inkele dage van teveure hadden ze ’t vuur al over ’t dak zien lope.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":50165,"r":"GENDT139","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Some people see a fire and a funeral procession before the event takes place.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Ien 1911 was ’t ’n bar dreuge zommer. Toe ister ien de Kommerdiek braand uutgebroke en verschillende huus zien afgebraand. Ok ’t huus van mien schoonouders. Minse, die opte stenove werkte, hadde de huus al ’n por dage van tevörre zien braande. Ze zegge, da sommige minse al van tevörre kunne zegge wanneer iemand doodgeet. Ze zien dan al inkele dage vöraf de liekstaatsie over de weg trekke, mee zien familie enz. er achter.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":44263,"r":"WEV008002","p":"Sellingen","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) was not regarded as anything special, and was believed.","i":"F.W.","o":"Dat dr van te veuren n brand zain wör, dat was gain bezunders meer. En de maiste mensn geleufden de verhoaln ook; is ook gain wonder. Kiek es, as joen voader zukke dingen vertelde en ie zatn door as kind bie te lustern, dan wör dat leufd.\nWat kind twiefelt non aan zien aigen voader?","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45300,"r":"WEV008705","p":"Wessinghuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of fire: rattling of roof tiles, seeing the fire beforehand. Burying an animal in the yard means fire.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wazzen ook mensen, dai heurden pannen rappeln.\nDat betaikende dan dat t hoes gauw opbrannen zol. Andern zaggen van te veurn n hoes in brand stoan. Ik wait van ain oet Onstwedde, dai zuks van te veurn zee en dat t hoes ook wekliek opbrand is. Nôn wazzen dr gounend, dai zeden: \"Begroaf nooit n dood daier op t aarf, want dan komp dr brand van.\"","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44547,"r":"WEV009004","p":"Holte","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A prediction that a farm under construction will never be finished proves right, because the farm burns down shortly afterwards.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nHeur ie non nich veule meer van, man ik heb toch wol zo t ain en ander zain.\nk Wait dat ze n keer mit n neie boerderij aan t zetn warn achter op de Holte. Dou was dr ain, dai zee, dat de boerderij nich kloar kwam. Is ook zo oetkoomn, want veur dat t hoes dr stön, is t al opbrand n poar weekn loater. Zai bint wol weer begund te timmern en dat hoes is dr non nog.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44576,"r":"WEV009405","p":"Schoonoord","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A falling star above a house can be an omen that the house will burn down.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurgezicht.\nNou zel ik daar iets van verteln.\nAs ie s avends een vaalnde ster zaggen, dan was dat gevaarliek.\nEt huus, waar boven dat gebeurde, zol later opbrannen kennen.","l":"Drents"},{"n":45011,"r":"WEV009603","p":"Holthe","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"During a fire someone says that two farms will burn down but that a threatened third farm will be spared, because he has seen this before. A prediction by night watchmen who see a glowing red sky that there will be a fire comes true.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wat ik joe vertelle, is woar gebeurd.\nEr is meer dan veule mensen denken. Doar is n zekere almacht.\nWel door an geleuft, lacht niet om alles en wet, dat niet alles te verklaarn valt; maar hij nuumt ook alles geen olle wieve-prooties, wat zo vake gebeurt.\nLuster maar ies uut mien eigen ervaarn.\n\nIn Elp is olle D. jaarn schaapherder west. En hij kon er hiel wat zien, meer dan andern.\nOp een dag stonden er twie boerderijen in braand. De vonkn stoovn naar een darde en zol ook wel gaan maar toen kwam D. en zee: \"Maak oe gien zurgen, er branden twie op en gien drie; ik heb dat al lange gezien.\"\nDe mensn dachten toen, hij is gek. Maar D. was niet gek; de darde boerderij is niet opbraand, al leek et wel eerst zo.\nEr was toen nog een nachtwacht in Elp.\nTwie mannen liepen door et darp om op te letn.\nOp een nacht zien ze de hiele lucht glunig-rood.\n\"Er zal wel brand komen\", zeggen ze.\nEn dat kwam alweer uut; opnei binnen er twie boerderijen aan gaan.","l":"Drents"},{"n":45028,"r":"WEV009804","p":"Emmen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Seeing an owl board with a burning post sticking out of it is an omen that the house will burn down.","i":"F.W.","o":"Voorloop of voorgezicht bestond ook; je hoorde er niet zoveel van als in Drente en Westerwolde.\nEr waren wel eens mensen, die een \"uleboard\" gezien hadden, waaruit een \"binpeal\" (in het Gronings \"ponterboom\", de paal die over een voer hooi gelegd wordt bij het binnenhalen van de oogst, vroeger op de boerenwagens of wipkarren). \nDie paal dan hadden ze zien branden. Dat betekende, dat het huis spoedig zou opbranden."},{"n":45032,"r":"WEV009807","p":"Emmen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"The northern lights are seen as an omen of fire.","i":"F.W.","o":"Op noorderlicht had men het niet begrepen.\nZie, dat scheen s avonds zo geheimzinnig op de dakpannen; de mensen waren bevreesd, dat ditook een voorbeduidsel was van een toekomstige brand."},{"n":45046,"r":"WEV010001","p":"Harpel","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees a house on fire with only a blue flame above the attic. Ten years later the house burns down and someone dies.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurzain.\nVandoage aan de dag heurt ie dr nich zo veul meer over, man dat veurzain bestèèt, door bin k van overtuugd. Ik kan joe dat bewiezen, want mien pabbe en ik zulf hebben verscheiden keern wat mitmoakt. Verder heb ik al n boel heurd van ander lu.\n\nDou mien pabbe seldoat was, en hai op n moal verlof kreeg, luip e zo op n oavend noar hoes en komp dan in de buurt van de Harpel.\nHai blif stoan en zeg: \"Hé, t hoeskng van Hinnerk D. in de brand?\"\nMien voar zug n blauwe vlam, man allennig boovn de beune.\nHai kik goud tou, man kan wieder gain brand ontdekn.\nTien joar, joa, tien joar loater brandt dat hoes werkliek op.\nEn dou is door aine bie umkomen, verbrand.\nNon wilt ze wel beweern, dat dai blauwe vlam dat verbrande liek beduud hef.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":130466,"r":"BIJLSMA004212","p":"Sondel","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man born with a caul has to get up at night because he has seen a fire or a funeral procession.","i":"T.B.","o":"Yn 'e Maren wenne eartiids Jehannes Huitema, dy't mei in helm berne wie. Hy moast der nachts út en hie dan binei gjin tiid om him oan to klaeijen. Hy roun dan yn de ûnderbroek de dyk op. Immen dy't him dan tsjinkaem sei: \"Hwat nou, jehannes?\" Jehannes sei: \"Der is brân, en ik moat earst nei dat plak, earder haw ik gjin rêst.\" Sa foarsei hy in brân to Koudum en ek in brân yn 'e tsjerke to Bakhuzen. Op dat stuit wie der gjin brân, allinne jehannes seach it dan. Mar in dei of hwat letter kaem de foarsizzing út. Sa seach er ek wolris in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130596,"r":"BIJLSMA006203","p":"Jirnsum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Not sawing off the ends of protruding wooden pegs in the timber frame, as protection against fire and cattle disease.","i":"T.B.","o":"R. de Graaf kaem al jong by de timmerman. Op in kear moast er in âldere man helpe by it byntwurk fan in pleats. Der waerden gjin spikers brûkt, mar houten pinnen yndreaun. Boppe-oan, oan beide kanten, stiken dan eintsjes fan dy pinnen út. De timmerman, dy 't der ek by wie, sei: \"Dy eintsjes moat der mar ôfseage wurde\".\n\"Om 'e deale net\", sei de âldman, \"as dy einen der ôfseage wurde komt der letter brân\".\nYn skuorren, dy 't yn 'e foarige ieu en yn it bigjin fan dizze ieu boud binne, kin men noch sjen, dat dy einen fan de houten pinnen der útstykje.","l":"Fries"},{"n":15612,"r":"CJ002506","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"In Harkema it often happened that someone had seen a house or barn on fire. This was an omen, for later that building often really did burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It praet gong froeger yn 'e Harkema gauris dat ien sei: Ik ha dy en dy skuorre of dat en dat hûs brânnen sjoen. Dan brânde dat letter op. Dat wie foartsjirmerije. Mar ik leau dat it ek wolris net útkom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15777,"r":"CJ003102","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"One morning a man drives to the market with two farmers. One of the farmers has a voorgezicht (a vision of a future event) of a fire. When they return in the evening, the farm turns out to have burnt down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir hat in man west út Grinslân. Dy fortelde my us, hy ried op in moarn mei twa boeren fan Hooghalen nei Hoogeveen nei de merk. Underweis moesten se trije plaetsen foarby. Al yn 'e fierte seagen se dat ien fan dy plaetsen yn 'e brân stie. Mar doe't se flakby wienen, wie der gjin brân to sjen.\nMar doe't se de jouns werom kommen fan 'e merk, wie dyselde plaets al ôfbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15897,"r":"CJ003907","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Durk Tabak sees the future house of himself and his girl Sweantje on fire. However, it is the house next to theirs that burns down, not Durk's.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e tiid dat myn suster Swaentsje forkearing hie mei Durk Tabak ha wy it hûs brânnen sjoen dêr't se letter yn kom binne to wenjen. Mar it stiet der nòch altyd. Us mem sei: Jim ha jim in hûs forsjoen. Hwant dat der neist stie is letter ôfbrand.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15908,"r":"CJ004003","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Cases of voorgezicht (a vision of a future event) of fire and building that came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger seagen wy hjir en dêr wolris in hûs yn 'e brân stean, dan brânde dat hûs letter op. Ek seagen wy by joun wolris op guon plakken in ljocht, dêr't dan letter in hûs kom to stean.\nIk wyt noch wol dat pake sei: Hjir by 't poeltsje dêr komt in nij hûs to stean. Dêr ha 'k wol hûndert kear in ljochtsje brânnen sjoen. Dêr is letter èk in hûs kòm.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16819,"r":"CJ006206","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"One evening people see a farm in Drogeham on fire. They go there, and the further they get, the fiercer it burns. But when they reach the Ham, the fire is out. The farm is still standing. But it is sure to burn down one day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in joun wienen der guon, dy seagen yn Droegeham in boereplaets yn 'e brân. Dy minsken wennen op Reahel. Sy lieten har oersette oer 't Knjillisdjip hinne en roannen de kant út fan de Ham. Hwat fierder se kommen, hwat fûlder it brânde. Se wienen oan de Ham ta, doe wie 't út. Dy plaets stiet der noch. Hy is noait opbrând. Mar 't gebeurt fêst in kear.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16820,"r":"CJ006207","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"One evening the narrator sees the water mill at the Wide Petten on the Polderdyk ablaze. But the next morning it is still standing. The following year, however, the mill caught fire during a storm. The narrator had already seen it a year beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger hat der in wettermoune stien by de Wide Petten, op 'e Polderdyk. Op in joun om 8 ûre kom ik thús. Ik seach de moune brânnen. Hy stie yn ljochte lôge. Ik fortelde it oan 'e minsken. Mar de oare moarns stie hy der noch, hy wie net ôfbrând. Mar it oare jiers, op in moarntiid mei in dikke bui en in stoarmwyn doe rekke de moune los, doe koe de mounder him net mear hâlde. Hy fleach yn 'e brân. Mar ik hie him in jier fan tofoaren al brânnen sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16859,"r":"CJ006507","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Fire as a harbinger of a fire. Some time later such a house then burns down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It fjûr as foarboade fan in brân wie hjir yn 'e Harkema algemien. In skoft letter brânde sa'n hûs dan op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16966,"r":"CJ007301","p":"Sweagerbosk","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"People saw an inn on fire long before it burnt down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Twizelerheide hat in herberge stien, dy ha se baernen sjoen. Doe't se der by kamen wie 't sa net. Letter is er ôfbaernd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17122,"r":"CJ008401","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man has seen a house on fire, but it has not burnt down yet.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sudema's jonges har heit, âlde Knjillis Sudema hat sjoen dat it hûs fan Douwe Veenstra yn'e brân stie. Hy sei altyd: \"Dat brânt nochris in kear op.\" Mar it is noch net gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17379,"r":"CJ009005","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Near the narrator's parents-in-law, the house where they used to lodge is on fire. Piter Schievink had already seen it on fire beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By myn skoanâlden yn 'e Bosk hat in hûs yn 'e brân stien. Myn skoanâlden hienen earder yn dat hûs wenne. Piter Schievink seach it fan to foaren al brânnen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17484,"r":"CJ009413","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Around 1910 a woman went door to door with wares. She sees a place in Sânbulten ablaze. But when she runs over to it, there is no trace of fire.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie sahwat yn 1910. Myn suster roan mei in tas mei negoasje by de huzen lâns. Doe't se de jouns thúskaem, sei se: \"Hjoed ha 'k hwat wûnders bileefd. In plaetske yn Sânbulten oer 't spoar hinne stie yn ljochte lôge, doe't ik der lâns kom. Ik roan der hurd op yn, hwant sa'n greate brân hie 'k noch noait sjoen. Mar doe't ik der oan ta wie, wie der neat fan in brân to sjen.\"\nHja wie nòch fan 'e wize doe't se it ús fortelde. Wy ha der letter altyd om tocht as it ek ôfbrânne soe, mar dat is noait gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17499,"r":"CJ009507","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Someone sees a fire as an omen. Later the house really does burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It spul dêr't nou Hindrik en Ael wenje, ha guon minsken fan tofoaren yn 'e brân sjoen. Letter brânde it op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":18184,"r":"CJ012006","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"People once saw a house on fire, but it was not really burning. Later it burnt down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 'e Broeksterfeart stie in hûs. Guon seagen it ris yn 'e brân. Mar op dat stuit barnde it net. Letter is it ôfbarnd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19544,"r":"CJ013404","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Some people saw a house burn down. In reality it was not burning. But later the house really did burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tichte by de Singel stie in âld húske by in dyk. Guon seagen fan to foaren dat it ôfbrânde. Yn werklikheit brânde it doe noch net. Mar 't wie de foarboade. Letter is dat hûs ôfbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19712,"r":"CJ014801","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A farmhand finds his sister terrified because she hears crackling sounds. He brushes her fear aside. When he comes home from work a week later, the stove has fallen over burning onto the floor. There is wood in the stove too, and the farmhand hears the wood crackling. The sister had foreseen the fire.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Tike wennen Bouwe en Jits. Har soan Sibe gong elke dei nei Hilke en Baeije ta to arbeidzjen.\nOp in kear doe kom er thús en doe sei syn suster Bouk: \"Ik bin sa binaud, it knapt hjir sa hyltyd yn 'e hûs en dêr is neat to sjen.\"\n\"Ynbeeldings\", sei Bouwe.\nDoe't er in wike letter wer thúskaem fan it wurk om deselde tiid stie de klompkachel oer de flier en dy brânde. Der siet hout yn en dat knapte.\n\"Dat binne nou de lûden,\" sei Bouk, \"dy't ik forline wike heard ha. It hat foartsjirmerij west.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20399,"r":"CJ018809","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"In the old days people sometimes saw houses on fire that later really burnt down. These were voorgezichten (visions of future events).","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Sumarreheide ha de minsken wol gauris huzen fan tofoaren yn 'e brân sjoen, dy't letter opbrânden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20661,"r":"CJ020703","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"In Harkema at least ten houses have burnt down that people had seen beforehand would burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der ha by myn witen wol tsien huzen yn 'e Harkema west, dy't letter ôfbrând binne en dy't se fan to foaren al yn 'e brân sjoen ha.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":43820,"r":"WEV012307","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man twice sees his house on fire when it is not really burning. Later the house burns down.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloopn.\nMien voader het et huus, woor hai in woond het, twei keer in brand stoan zain. Dat zag e, as e s oavends loat bie huus kwam; in de verte zag e den vuur in t huus en vlammen, dei tou t dak uutsluign. \nToun ze den verhuuzn gungen noar n ander stee, zee d pabbe: \"Wat bin k door bliede om, dat wie n ander huus kriegn, want in dizze gebeurt nog n moal wat.\" \nEn zo was t. Dat huus is opbrand.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43823,"r":"WEV012308","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A house that someone saw on fire is still standing.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloopn.\nNou komp et nait altied uut, wat de mensn zain. \nMien zuster komp es moal bie oavend van de Pekel. In huus vertelt ze, dat ze t huus van dei en dei brannen zain het.  \nMoar d ander dag stait dat huus dr nog. \nDoar kon ze ja nait bie; dat zai zuk zo verkiekn kon\n In dit huus is nooit brand komen, want et stait dr nog.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44092,"r":"WEV013008","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A prediction that all the white houses will burn down comes true; only the white church is still standing.","i":"F.W.","o":"Oal vrouw K. zag vrouger ale widde huuzn in Boertange brannen.\n“Zai brant aal op”, zee ze. En t oal hef nog gliek kreegn ook. Allaind de widde kerke stait dr nog.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45147,"r":"WEV014807","p":"Wachtum","v":"Dr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees a flame by some houses, but they are not burning. Later those houses burned down at the same time.","i":"F.W.","o":"Brand.\nDit is echt een keer voorgevallen.  \nEen vriend van me kwam eens met de boodschap in huis, dat hij hier in Wachtum tijdens een avondwandeling een vuurvlam had gezien. De vlam was van het ene huis overgeslagen op het huis ernaast. De huizen zelf brandden niet.\n En let nu es op; twee jaar daarna zijn die bewuste huizen om dezelfde tijd opgebrand. Deze jongeman heeft dus echt wel vooruit kunnen kijken. Als hij het na de brand had verteld, dan zou het fantasie kunnen zijn, maar ik weet nog best, wanneerhij mij het verhaal meedeelde."},{"n":19880,"r":"CJ015510","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man's cottage went up in flames after a lightning strike. Later it turns out that people had foreseen the fire.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De plaets, dêr't Atse Zijlstra to Surhuzum wennet, is in goed sechstich jier lyn troch de wjerljocht ôfbrând. Guon ha him fan tofoaren yn 'e brân stean sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19917,"r":"CJ015702","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"At night a hunter suddenly sees a house on fire. It is a voorgezicht (a vision of a future event): later the house really burnt down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik noch net troud wie, kom ik us in kear oer 't Wytfean. Ik wie oan 't murdejeien. 't Wie by nacht. Doe seach ik op 'e Bopperein in hûs yn 'e brân stean. Mar it brânde net. Letter is 't opbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20179,"r":"CJ017508","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"In a house two pots are smashed by lightning. A little later the whole house burns down. It was an omen.","i":"J.W.","o":"De moalkerij fan Piter van der Meulen to Eastemar is ôfbrând op in snein yn 1896. (it hûs dêr't nou in post-stasjon is)\nEven fan tofoaren woarden dêr twa skellingse potten troch de wjerljocht kapotslein. Dat wie de foarboade.\nEven letter brânde 't hiele hûs troch de wjerljocht ôf.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20624,"r":"CJ020505","p":"Tzummarum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A woman had seen a farm burning one night. A few days later the farm did indeed burn down; the hay had overheated.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir skeef tsjinoer hat in pleats stien. Dêr wenne Anders Reitsma op, dy is letter nei Froubuorren gong.\n1 augustus 1895 is dy pleats ôfbarnd. It waerd yn oktober fjouwer jier. Der wie heabroei, de arbeiders hienen oan 't headollen west.\nIk wit noch dat heit thúskaem en sei: \"Reitsma syn pleats stiet yn 'e brân.\nHein v.d. Burg wurke by Anders Reitsma. Hy wenne op 'e Bearepôlle yn in arbeidershûs. Dy hie in pear dagen fan tofoaren dold. Hy naem in topke hea mei, dat hied er yn 'e bûse. It hie in moaije kleur.\n\"Der is gjin gefaer mear by\", sei er tsjin syn frou.\nMar it minske sei: \"Ik hoopje dat it wier is. Ik haw de pleats fannacht brânnen sjoen.\"\nDe man lake. \"Dû hast droomd\", sei er.\nMar hja lake net. In pear dagen letter is er opbarnd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20646,"r":"CJ020603","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A young man once saw a house on fire by the bridge. But his mother saw nothing, and when he looked again a little later, he no longer saw it either. Exactly two years later a house burnt down on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen froeger achterút.\nIk wie sahwat in twintich jier âld. Ik seach de kant nei de brêge út.\n\"Mem,\" sei 'k, \"dêr by de brêge stiet in hûs yn 'e brân.\"\nMar mem seach neat. Ik hie my omdraeid, doe't mem der oankaem, mar doe't ik wer seach, wie der neat mear fan de brân to bispeuren.\nPresys twa jier letter rekke de plaets fan Jan de Boer troch de fetpanne yn 'e brân. Dy stie presys op 't selde sté.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20647,"r":"CJ020604","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A young man once saw a house on fire by the bridge. Exactly two years later a house burnt down on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jochum Dykstra wie net al to goed wiis. Syn mem sutele mei lapkes. Sy kaem ek wol us by ús.\nOp in kear sei se: \"Jochum hat in brân sjoen by Jehannes der Mooy, of dêr flak by.\nTwa jier letter wie der brân yn in hûs by de brêge. It brânde hielendal ôf. Ik der hinne. Ik wie sahwat fyftsjin jier, tink. It wie it hûs fan Jehannes der Mooy, dat ôfbrânde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20648,"r":"CJ020605","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man born with a caul saw the water mill on fire one evening. A little later there was nothing to be seen. Not long afterwards lightning struck the mill and it really burnt down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Merk wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy seach ek lykstaesjes. By 't Súdlaerdermeer moat hy ris sitten ha to fiskjen. Hy wie plysje. 't Wie tsjuster. Mar samar ynienen wie 't ljocht woarn. \"En seagen wy dêr de wettermoune net yn 'e brân stean oan 'e kant fan 'e Súdlaerder Meer?\" sei er. \"'t Wie sa ljocht, dat wy koenen de dobber en alles goed sjen. Krekt as wie 't dei.\" De wiken fan 'e moune wienen noch in pear kear yn 'e rounte draeid en even letter wie 't wer tsjuster.\nIn skoft dêrnei is de wjerljocht yn 'e moune slein en is er echt ôfbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20689,"r":"CJ020901","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"One evening a man saw a farm on fire. But in reality it was not burning. A year later it burnt down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Fokke Weening hjir fan 'e Harkema hat my us forteld: Hy wie sa'n twintich jier âld, hy lei op bêd. Doe seach er dúdlik in spultsje brânnen dat tichte by de fabryk Spineta stie. Mar yn werklikheit brânde it net. Sahwat in jier letter is it ôfbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20829,"r":"CJ021705","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A little boy once shouted that there was a fire, but nobody saw anything. A few days later two houses burnt down on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is us gebeurd dat der in jonkje wie yn Droegeham, dy rôp fan Brân! Brân! Brân! Alle minsken kommen to sjen, mar der wie nergens brân. It bern hâldde fol dat er it sjoen hie en hy wiisde it plak oan. Syn heit joech him in pak op 'e hûd.\nIn pear dagen letter der oan 'e Lytse Wei twa plaetsen op, dêr't dikke Marten en Bosma wenne ha. 't Wie de kant op dy't it jonkje oanwiisd hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21117,"r":"CJ024205","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A woman once saw her hut in flames. But when she came closer, nothing was wrong. Later, however, the hut did burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn wiif har beppe kom us thús en doe seach se fan fierrens de flammen ta de hutte út slaen. Mar doe't se der oan ta wie, wie 't sa net. Mar letter is dy hutte wòl opbrând. 't Gebeurde op Burgumerdaem. 't Ald minske sei: \"Sokke dingen mat men stil fan stean.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21588,"r":"CJ027403","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A woman had seen beforehand that a house would burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Falom hat us in brân wêst. Ik haw it hûs fan to foaren al forbrânnen sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21684,"r":"CJ028102","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man foresees a fire at the school building. The voorgezicht (a vision of a future event) does not come true, however.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De âld skoalle fan 'e Loane stie flak by de wei lâns. Meint Pama moest dêr us lâns. Hy hie nei 't Fean ta west. 't Wie doe noch sânwei. Doe stie dêr foar it skoallehûs in bult turf yn 'e brân. Dy bult stie dêr yn 'e rounte en Meint koe der net lâns. De flammen sloegen wit hoe heech.\n\"Bist der net hinne gong?\" ha se him letter frege.\nMar hy sei: \"Ik koe der net komme.\"\nHy is doe de Megielsreed lâns gong nei Houtigehage ta. De oare moarns is hy der hinne gong to sjen. Mar der wie neat. Gjin jiske, gjin branje, fan alles neat.\n\"Mar der hat wol hwat west\", sei er. Dat hâldde er fol.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":50332,"r":"GENDT259","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Some people see a fire while others see nothing, but later there really is a fire.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Vörbedujsels waren ok, dat iemand al van teveure kos zien, dat er èrs braand zou komme. Hé’j zag dan ’n huus ien braand stoan, mar as ie er langs kwam, was er niks te zien. Mar inkele dage of wèke lotter braandde ’t toch af.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":131957,"r":"VODA_033_10","p":"Bellingwolde","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a funeral procession and a fire.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Dan ’n klain stukje over, nou det is ook in Bennewolde gebeurd, dichtbie, det was van ’n…’n begrafenisstoet. Twee knechten die kommen doa van ’n boerderij hear en zie lopen de l… weg op en doe zeggen ze: “Ach, wat det geroar? Doe ‘r es licht aan. En wat komt doar aan?” zeggen ze. Doar komp d’r ook ’n halle begrafenisstoet komp d’r aan, ’liek op eur aan, de berg langs. Zij eh… goan ’n klain bietje oet ziet, maar doar ’t precies tegen eur is, is ’t weg.\n’n Half joar noa tied, doar precies woar zij uu…uu… van kant goan bin, doar eh…eh..eh.. geit ein te overlieden. En die boerderij die is in die… in dea tied ook precies zo of’brand, we det ze doa […] glend zain hebben. Lichten, zeiden ze, want det was glend, hè. En eh… doa loater doar mensen dea zover doa mit heen kom’n det doa môst ’n wacht wezen, want zeej wassen doodsverlegen det doa wat gebeuren zol weer, hè. Maar is nooit loater weer wat gebeurd.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":130163,"r":"VOORDE000202","p":"Borne","v":"Ov.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man on the road sees fire in a village, but when he gets closer there is nothing to see and nothing has happened. A few weeks later part of the village burns down.","i":"G.J.t.V.","o":"’n Vuurspooksel.\n\nMien vaar hef vaak verteeld, hoo zien vaar op nen Zoaterdagmiddag, met ’n ool’n Mösselboer, noar Zèender’n was goan hen biecht’n. ’t Was mooi weer wes en ze hadd’n d’r hèènig de tied too doan, het was oet oenz’n ool’n hook ze ’n goo drèe keteer goans. Op ’n good moal, ze wadd’n zo op de heugte van Wissink wes, har mien grootvaar ’n moal umkekk’n en hee har verbiesterd tieg’n Mösselboer zeg: “Boer, kiekt toch ’s um, heel Boorn stèet in broand, iej könt de vlamm’n zeèn kölder’n en ’t is ook noar oenze koante. Loa’w gaaw wier op ’t hoes angoan” Dat hadd’n ze vonzölm doan en dow ze good en wal achter op ’t Boornse Veeld wadd’n kömm’n was d’r op èes niks meer te zèen wes en in heel Boorn was niks gebuurd. \nMeer ne wekke later was de hele Hös, dat is de ooldste buurte van Boorn, ofbroand. Meer zèè hadd’n den broand a ne wekke van te vuurt’n zèèn !","l":"Twents"},{"n":45700,"r":"WEV015303","p":"De Maten","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A sound as if a plate rack falls off the wall is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of fire.","i":"F.W.","o":"Dit is mie ook verteld deur n man en ik wil aannemen, dat et gain leugn is.\n Dai man dan lag mit zien vrouw op bedde en inains heurn ze wat in de keukn. Vrouger harn de mensn wol n rikje mit tellertjes aan de mure hangen. Dat haile geval rappelt op n nacht noar doale en de diggels lign op de grond. Zo denkn ze teminste. De man mout in de underbuksm hen um te kiekn, man hai zug niks. Alles hangt stil aan de mure. \n“Dit bedudt wat”, zee e teegn zien vrouw.\n En zo was t. Nich laank loater is dat hoes ofbrandt. Dou völn detellers op de grond.\nZukke dingen komen veur.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46172,"r":"WEV016304","p":"Barger-Compascuum","v":"Dr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Foreseeing a fire or smelling a fire in advance.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurgeschichtn bestoan; zulf zag ik es n moal n brand, wat uutkomen is. Andern konden de brand van te veurn roekn; ook in dat geval gung et huus er aan.","l":"Drents"},{"n":22051,"r":"CJ031802","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A woman sees a house on fire, but nobody else sees any flames. It is a premonition: a year later the house in question really does burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Letter doe wennen wy fierderop yn 'e Harkema, omtrint by de brêge. De frou wie siik, dy hie de gryp. Sy lei yn 't bêdsté. Ik siet yn 'e keamer to krantlêzen.\nDe frou seach út it bêdsté wei nei bûten ta en sei tsjin my: \"Oebele, dêr stiet reade Willem syn hûs yn 'e brân!\"\nIk sjen, de kant nei de Pauloane út, hwant dêr wenne reade Willem, mar dêr stie net in inkel hûs yn 'e brân.\nIk sei: \"Dû liichst it.\"\nMar hja sei: \"'k Ha 't klear brânnen sjoen.\"\nBinnen 't jier brânde 't hûs fan reade Willem op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22713,"r":"CJ035005","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man, Rinse Loonstra, always foresees fires. This has earned him the nickname Rinse Brander (Rinse the Burner).","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Rinse Loonstra wenne achter ús, doe't wy noch oan 'e Lange Wyk wennen. (Yn dat húske wennet nou Eise Det). Dy seach altyd fan tofoaren dat der brân wie. Dêrom neamden se him altyd Rinse Brander.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22829,"r":"CJ036107","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"People see a house on fire. It is an omen: only some time later does the house really burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oant dizkant de grifformearde pasterije stie in hûs, (yn Jistrum), dêr hat Sake Jagersma yn wenne.\nFan 'e oare kant ôf seagen guon dat it hûs yn 'e brân stie. Mar dat wie sa net. It wie foartjirmerij. In skoftsje letter brânde it op. De lju dy't der doe yn wennen binne nei Burgum tagong to wenjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22915,"r":"CJ036702","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A girl sees a fire very clearly in her dream. It is a premonition: the next night the house next door burns down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't myn skoandochter sa'n trettsjin à fjirtsjin jier âld wie, seach se yn 'e nacht yn har droom in brân. Hja seach alles hiel dúdlik. 't Wie hjir yn Drachten op Uleflecht.\nDe oare nachts is it hûs njonken harres ôfbrând. 't Gebeurde krekt sa as sy it sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22928,"r":"CJ036715","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A boy sees a bright glow light up his grandmother's house. It is a portent of a fire: three weeks later the house burns down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik siet us in kear by alde Kei Anne (= Gerrit de Vries) yn 'e hûs to krantlêzen. 'k Wie noch in jonge. Dêr komt ynienen in hiel helle gloede, alles wurdt ljocht. Us beppe har hûs stiet yn'e brân. Sa'n trije wike letter is 't opbrând. Mar ìk hie 't al earder sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22930,"r":"CJ036717","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A group of men are talking when suddenly the house starts to creak and burn. It is a portent: later the house really does burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us Bareld komt op in joune thûs. \"'k Ha hwat bileefd\", sei er. \"Wy stienen to praten by Jille Pultrum. Ynienen bigjint dat hûs to kreakjen en to brânnen.\" Steven de Meer wie by Bareld. Sy binne togeare útnaeid. 't Wienen great-jonges. De hjerstmis brânde dat hûs ôf.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23064,"r":"CJ037608","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Some people once saw a mill on fire, but in reality there was nothing. Years later the mill really did burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon ha hjir yn Ikkerwâld de moune brânnen sjoen, langer as fyftich jier lyn. Mar yn werklikheit brânde er net. Forskeidene jierren letter is er pas opbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23086,"r":"CJ037801","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A boy and a girl once saw a fire from a distance, but when they came closer there was no fire at all. A year later a fire did break out at that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is jierren lyn. Ik en myn feint kommen us fan Sweagerfean. Wy moesten nei de Triemen ta. Wy roannen de Úlke-loane del by Swagerfean. Doe't wy sahwat midden op 'e loane wienen, en oer de feart seagen, seinen wy: \"Sjoch, dêr is brân!\"\nDêr woenen wy hinne en sa kommen wy op 'e Trekwei. Mar dêr wie neat to sjen. Alles wie tsjuster.\nIn jier nei dy tiid briek dêr brân út op in pleats, krekt op datselde plak, dêr't wy de brân sjoen hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23400,"r":"CJ039001","p":"Siegerswoude","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A married couple once saw something burning from their yard. But nothing stood there yet. Later a house was built, and later still it did indeed burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen yn 'e Grinzer Wylp yn in âld plaets oan 'e Keuningswyk. Op in joun kom myn man thús en doe stienen wy togearre op it hiem. Doe seagen myn man en ik in hiele greate flamme achter ús hûs. En dêr stie doe noch hielendal neat. Letter ha se dêr in nij hûs delset en nòch letter is dat hûs opbrând. Dat ha wy doe brânnen sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23947,"r":"CJ043206","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Someone once saw the town hall on fire. A little later it really burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oer de betonwei, achter 't earmetsjerkhôf seach ik in kear in gemeente-hûs yn 'e brân stean. It wie ien kleare klinkende lôge. Even letter brânde it op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24041,"r":"CJ044003","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man once saw a house on fire, but when he came closer there was nothing to be seen any more. Two years later that same house burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen tichte by 't spoar. Op in kear seach in buorman fan ús, dat dêr in hûs opbrânde. Mar doe't hy der nei ta gong om to sjen wie 't sa net.\nTwa jier letter is datselde hûs opbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24472,"r":"CJ046804","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"People see a house on fire. It is a premonition: later the house really does burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Feanwâlden is us in hûs opbrând. Guon ha dat hûs fan tofoaren yn 'e brân sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24504,"r":"CJ046920","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees a house burn down. It is an omen: later the house really does burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit seach op in kear it hûs brânnen fan Tsjibbe-om en Pytsje-muoi, dêr't nou Megiel en Aeltsje wenje, mar it brânde net.\nBinnen hiel koarte tiid is 't opbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24566,"r":"CJ047509","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"People see a house burn down. Only later does the house really burn down: it was a premonition.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sy seinen froeger wolris, dat hûs brânt ôf. Guon ha 't brânnen sjoen. Dan brânde it letter èk ôf.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24660,"r":"CJ049103","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A woman sees her little house on fire. It is a premonition: six months later the little house really does burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen froeger yn Drachtster Kompenije. Dêr wennen njonken ús lju, dy hienen earder yn 'e Fianen wenne (yn Houtigehage). Dy frou fortelde ús, sy wie us ûnderweis ergens hinne - doe wenne se noch yn 'e Fianen - doe gong se even by minsken oan ûnderweis, doe hie se achterom sjoen doe wie se allemachtige kjel woarn.\n\"O heden,\" hie se roppen, \"ús keet stiet yn 'e brân!\" (Sy wennen yn in spitkeet). Mar 't wie sa net. Doe't se der by kom wie der neat to rêdden. En doch hie se him dúdlik brânnen sjoen.\nIn healjier neitiid brânde de spitkeet op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24671,"r":"CJ049205","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees a house on fire. It is a premonition: later it really does burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining fan 'e Boelensloane hat fan tofoaren in hûs yn 'e brân sjoen. Hy sei: \"Dat hûs haw ik brânnen sjoen\", en letter brânde it op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24866,"r":"CJ049917","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees some stacks of peat on fire. The next day the peat stacks are still there. It is a premonition: a while later the peat really burns.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn heit moest ris op in kear lammesturtsjes barre fan Wopke Gerrems de Vries, in boer. Heit dêr hinne op in joun, kofjedrinke, lang prate, doe der wer wei, de gemeentewei lâns. Doe in ein modderwei, en sa troch 't mienskar.\nDoe stie er foar in wringe. Doe't er oan 'e wringe ta wie, tocht er: \"Jonge, dêr is brân yn 'e ien en twintich mêd by de sleat. Hoe kin dat?\" Dêr stienen greate turfhopen. Dy stienen yn 'e brân.\nMar de oare deis stienen dy turfhopen der noch. Se hienen dus yn werklikheit net yn 'e brân stien. Mar heit hie se brânnen sjoen.\nHeit en myn âldste broer hienen dêr twahûndert foer reid lizzen. Dat reid moest boun wurde, mar heit woe dêr net hinne to binen. Hwant hy tochte, as dy hopen turf ris yn 'e brân reitsje, krije wy de skuld, as wy dêr oan 't wurk binne. Dat hy gong oan 't gropjen de kant nei Earnewâld út.\nIn dei of hwat letter stienen de turfhopen echt yn 'e brân. Heit hie 't fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24907,"r":"CJ050507","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man worriedly tells a colleague that he has seen the colleague's house on fire. It is a premonition: later the house really does burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Fjirtich jier lyn kom ik op in moarn op 't wurk. Doe kom Wibe Doetsjes op my ta en sei: \"Jonge, hwat wie ik fan 'e moarn yn 'e war om dy.\"\n\"Om my?\" sei 'k.\n\"Ja, om dy. Dyn hûs stie yn 'e brân\", sei er.\n\"Dan wie 't niis al wer út,\" sei 'k, \"hwant ik kom nou krekt fan hûs.\"\n\"Ik ha 't brânnen sjoen\", sei er. \"Ik koe de lôge troch de popelieren beammen hinne sjen.\"\nIt wie yn maert dat er dat fortelde.\nDe hjerstmis - 'k hie nei de klaei ta west to sichtsjen, 't wie prachtich waer - doe sieten wy byinoar mei de bern yn 't skrobbermakkershokje, dat wy as wenning ynrjochte hienen.\n\"Hwat rûkt it hjir branderich\", sei Marijke. Mar der wie yn 't hiele hûs neat to finen dat brânde.\nWy gongen op bêd.\nDeselde nachts is dit hûs hjir opbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25255,"r":"CJ052602","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A group of friends see a house on fire from a distance. When they go to look, however, there is nothing to be seen. It is a premonition: shortly afterwards the house really does burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik roan us mei in stik of hwat oaren op in joune de Loane del. Doe seagen wy it hûs fan Piter en Sijke yn 'e brân. Wy der hinne om to sjen. Doe't wy der kommen leinen de minsken op bêd to sliepen en der wie alhielendal gjin brân. Mar in wike of hwat letter brânde it op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25905,"r":"CJ057706","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"If someone had seen a house burning, it would later really burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der woarde hjir froeger wol gauris sein: Dat hûs mat ek noch us in kear opbrânne; dy en dy ha 't brânnen sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26051,"r":"CJ058515","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man once saw a house on fire, but in reality there was no fire. Later it burned down after all. If you see a house burning in the early part of the night, it will soon really burn down. If you see it in the latter part of the night, it will take a while yet.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit seach froeger yn Surhústerfean in hûs yn 'e brân. Mar it brânde net yn werklikheit. Folle letter brânde it op.\nHwannear't men it yn 'e foarnacht brânnen sjocht, dan duorret it mar even. Sjocht men it yn 'e neinacht brânnen, dan duorret it noch in hiel skoft foardat it echt opbrânt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26854,"r":"CJ061405","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Someone is visiting his neighbours when people tell him his house is on fire. When he goes to look, however, it is not so. Not long afterwards the house does indeed burn down. If you see it in the early part of the night, it will not be long, and in the night itself it may take a while yet.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie in kear by de buorlju, doe kommen der minsken, dy fortelden dat myn hûs stie yn 'e brân. It hiele hûs stie yn ljochte lôge, biwearden se. Mar doe't wy der hinne gongen wie 't sa net. En doch hienen se 't dúdlik brânnnen sjoen.\nIt duorre net lang mear, doe brânde 't op.\nSjocht men it yn 'e foarnacht, dan duorret it mar koarte tiid mear, sjocht men it yn 'e neinacht, dan kin 't noch lange tiid duorje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26869,"r":"CJ061501","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Long ago a small farmhouse stood alone on a spot in the heath near the big church by the green cross building. Later a road was built there, and Nijboer now lives on this spot. The house spontaneously caught fire and the fire went out again just as quickly. Because people thought it was malice, people kept watch, but this turned out not to be the case. It remained a mysterious fire and the little house never burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Flak by de grote kerk bij 't groene kruis-gebouw de weg in woar nou Nijboer woont, doar stond froeger in ploatske. Verder was der niks. De reed is in hiel ein achteruut. Het boereploatske stond doar eensoam en ferloaten. 't Was doar toen nog allemoal heide. Nou is der in wegje, dat was der toen niet. Mem het foak forteld hoe it doar in dat ploatske goan is. Doar floog nachts zo moar it dak ien brand.\n't Ging ook so weer uut. Se dochten eerst dat it kwoadwilligheid was. Foaker as één keer hebben der fier man op wacht stoan. Net dat se der bij stonden floog it wéér in brand. Moar 't was ook so weer uut.\nToen dochten se dat 't eens sou opbranden. 't Is noait gebeurd. 't Was in geheimsinnige brand.\nEen omke fan mij was één van de oppassers.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26894,"r":"CJ061705","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"In Mieden a house is on fire one time, but when people go to look there is nothing to be seen. Later it does indeed burn down. It was a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Mieden stie us in kear in hûs yn 'e brân. Guon gongen der hinne om to sjen, mar doe brânde it net.\nLetter is it hûs ôpbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27162,"r":"CJ063902","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"In the house of Lammert v.d. Sluis on the Drachtsterweg, next to Ouwe van der Molen, a neighbour once saw a fire, and two years later it burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It hûs oan 'e Drachtster Wei, dêr't nou Lammert v.d. Sluis wennet, njonken Ouwe van der Molen woarde in kear troch it buorwiif yn 'e brân sjoen. Sa'n twa jier letter is 't opbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27345,"r":"CJ065102","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A woman once saw a house on fire, but in reality there was nothing. Later the house burned down after all.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Minderts Tryn fan 'e Grinzer Pein sei us op in kear: \"Sjoch, der brânt in hûs op.\" It wie it hûs fan Bareld Slotegraaf yn de Pein. Doe't se better taseach, brânde it net.\nLetter brânde it op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27399,"r":"CJ065306","p":"Rohel","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A boy of about ten saw his house on fire. A year later the house really burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha ús eigen hûs sels fan tofoaren brânnen sjoen, foardat it echt opbrânde. Ik wie doe noch in jonge.\nHeit wie to braekjen yn 't braekhok. Ik wie op 'e poel oan 't reedriden. Doe gong 'k ynienen as de duvel nei hûs ta, hwant ik seach dat ús keet yn 'e brân stie. Ik wie sa'n snotterige jonge fan in jier of tsien. Hwat fûlder ik taseach, hwat fûlder it barnde.\n't Wie wol in jier letter doe barnde ús hûs echt ôf.\nWy wennen yn Twizelerheide.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27493,"r":"CJ066405","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man once saw a house on fire, but in reality there was nothing. Later the house really burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Japik van der Kooi yn de Pein (Gr.) seach yn Topweer in hûs yn 'e brân. It wie it hûs fan Wiggele van der Meer. It brânde flink. Hy giet yn 'e hûs om dit to fortellen. 't Hûs stiet yn 'e brân.\nDoe't er wer bûten kom, wie der neat. Mar it hat net lang mear duorre, doe is 't opbrând. 't Is wier gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27555,"r":"CJ066907","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A house once burned down that people had already seen burning beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Jistrum is ris in hûs ôfbrând, dat hienen guon fan tofoaren al brânnen sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27707,"r":"CJ068504","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"People once saw a house on fire, but in reality nothing was wrong. Later the house really burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Harkema is 't us gebeurd dat guon in hûs yn 'e brân stean seagen. Mar it brânde doe net. In skoftsje letter is 't ôfbrand.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27708,"r":"CJ068505","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Even before the mill burned down, someone had already seen its sails on fire.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wiger Koaning hat sels forteld dat er de moune fan 'e Wide Pet yn 'e brân sjoen hat in skoftsje foardat er yn werkelikheit ôfbrânde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27979,"r":"CJ070902","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"People once saw a farm on fire. But when they came closer, nothing was wrong. Later the farm really burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn wiif fortelde wolris dat to Sybrandahûs - tusken Dokkum en Rinsumageast - seagen lju yn 'e nacht in boereplaets yn 'e brân. Hja hearden allerhande lûden en stemmen fan minsken. Sy gongen der hinne, mar der wie neat.\nLetter is dy plaets troch de tonger opbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28079,"r":"CJ071703","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A mother and her little son once saw a house on fire, but in reality there was nothing. Three weeks later the house really burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik in jonge wie wennen wy op 'e Bulten yn 'e Harkema. Op in kear wie 'k mei mem bûtendoar, doe sei mem: \"Sjoch, Piter Schievink syn hok stiet yn 'e brân.\" Ik seach it like dúdlik as mem. Mar it wie sa net.\nTrije wiken letter brânde it op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28257,"r":"CJ073201","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A boy once saw a house on fire. The next day the house really burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Jobbegea, oan diz kant de trêdde slûs ha wy froeger wenne. Op in nacht, wylst er op bêd lei, seach myn âldste broer hiel dúdlik it hûs fan ús buorman yn 'e brân. De oare jouns is it opbrând. It wie presys sa lyk as hy it yn 'e nacht sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28327,"r":"CJ073903","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man once saw a house on fire. But when he came closer, nothing was wrong. Later the house burned down after all.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie noch in lyts jonkje, doe kom der ien skean de lânnen oer op ús hûs ta. Doe't er oan ús ta wie, sei er tsjin heit:\n\"Né, 't is doch goed.\"\n\"Hwat is der dan?\" frege heit.\nHy sei: \"Ik seach jimme hûs yn 'e brân. It brânde alhiel op. Mar nou't ik tichterby kom, wie 't sa net.\"\n\"Dû hast dy forsjoen\", sei heit.\n\"Né,\" sei er, \"ik ha 't dúdlik brânnen sjoen. Dat it sil noch wolris opbrânne.\"\n\"'t Sil wol hwat tafalle\", sei heit.\nMar sahwat seis jier letter brânde 't op. Hy hie 't wòl goed sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28360,"r":"CJ074118","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A woman once saw a house on fire. Later that house really burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem hat yn Jobbegea fan tofoaren in hûs yn 'e brân stean sjoen, dat in skoftsje letter echt opbrând is.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28606,"r":"CJ076511","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"In Hamsterpein I once saw a fire at a farm beforehand, as did others. A few months later the farm does indeed burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Hamsterpein is ris in kear in buorkerije opbrând.\nIk wie doe noch in jong baeske. Ik seach de brân al fan tofoaren. Der binne trouwens mear dy't dy brân fan tofoaren sjoen ha. 't Duorre in pear maend, doe brânde er op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28774,"r":"CJ078806","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Sjoerd Rienkje lives on a road with an old house at the end, which is on fire two evenings in a row. A year later it does indeed burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By Sjoerde Rienkje yn 'e Bosk wie njonken 't hûs oan 'e rjochter kant in reed. As men dy reed in ein út gong stie dêr in hûs. Dêr wennen âlde Ruerd en Im yn. Dêr njonken, ek oan dy reed, stie nòch in âld hûs, dat wie ek fan Ruerd en Im.\nTwa jounen achter elkoar ha wy sjoen dat dat âlde hûs yn 'e brân stie. Ik wie doe in jonge fan tsien jier.\nIn jier letter brânde 't ôf.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29461,"r":"CJ081702","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"In the old days people sometimes saw a house on fire when in reality there was nothing. Usually such a house did burn down later. A man once also saw a little house on fire. When he came closer, nothing was wrong. Later that house was demolished.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw ek wolris fan guon heard dat se in brân fan tofoaren sjoen hienen, wylst it hûs pas letter opbrânde.\nIk ha sels ris in kear sjoen, doe wie 'k noch yn 'e hûs by ús heit en dy doe seach ik oan 'e Skieding in húske yn 'e brân stean. Doe't ik der by kom brânde 't net. Dat húske is letter ôfbrutsen, net opbrând. Dat haw ik dus net goed sjoen.\nDer stie in greate heaberch achter dat húske.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":128397,"r":"ENGELB_02_010","p":"Rossum","v":"Ov.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Someone regularly sees fire in a barn; others see nothing, except bits of charred wood.","i":"H.E.","o":"[OH:] Mien va is zes joa bie Häökman west as knecht, doa heb ik net ok a owwe verteeld, nich, en die hebt ze ok in die zes joa - disse ole schop hebt disse jôngs nog mè ofbrök'n, nich, disse jôngs nog mè ofbrök'n en in die ole schop hef de va zes joa west, mè dee hebt ze ok vea joa zeen bran'n en altied 's nachens, at de pöst der aolmaol gläönig hebt anstaon. Mè bie Häökman han'n ze vrowe gen kinne. 't Ool buurk'n en Dieka, die kwam'm van Veldhoes oet De Lut, mè die hebt der net zaolang gauws vuur doon laot'n, mis'n vuur les'n laot'n, at owwe was, mè doe 't owwe was en doe ze 't nich mea zein hebt, ouns vare zer altied, gao mè hen kiek'n jông, de pöst staot der aolmaol verbraand an; dat heb ik bie Häökman nog metmaakt, mè zie hebt der bie Häökman genôg vuur doon laot'n, nich, doa is late ok wa, wat van oongeluk wet ik nich, mè der is wa 'n oongeluk in die schop gebuurd, wat der gebuurd is wet ik nich; braand is owwe gaon, mè mien vare zer altied, Hennie, de pöst stun'n der aolmaol verbraand an, inderdaod ie kôn'n 't zein, ôppervlakkig, nich, het was nich zao slim verkoold as zein kouns, zie hebt in 't vuie west, mè zie wan'n inderdaad al verkoold.\nIk: \"Kan 't nich wen'n, at ze pöst hebt gebroekt van 'n oold boer'nhoes, wat a maol of is braand, at ze doa dee kapschuur of dee schop van hebt zet?\"\n[OH:] Ja, dat heb ik wa es metmaakt, at ze doa ne kapschuur, mè doa heur is late nik","l":"Twents"},{"n":33156,"r":"CJ087502","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A woman once saw a house on fire. Three days later the house really burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Harkema is in lytse sawntich jier lyn in arbeidershûs opbrând. Fjouwer bern binne doe yn 'e flammen omkom.\nJan van Zalen hat der noch in sang fan makke.\nTrije dagen fan tofoaren hat Sibe Antsje (= Antsje Tabak) sjoen dat dat arbeidershûs yn 'e brân stie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33170,"r":"CJ087603","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A woman once saw her house on fire and ran to it to get her little one out of bed. But when she arrived, nothing turned out to be wrong. Later the house really burned down, but by then she no longer lived there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem hat yn 'e Harkema in hûs fan tofoaren brânnen sjoen. 't Gebeurde op 'e Heidebulten. Hja stie by de wei to praten mei in âld kammeraetske fan har. Doe seach er ynienen dat de lôge oer de nael fan it hûs hinne rolle. 't Wie 't hûs dêr't se sels yn wenne. It berntsje lei op bêd, dat hja fleach dêr hinne. Mar doe't se by 't hûs kom wie der neat to rêdden. En doch hie se 't dúdlik brânnen sjoen.\nLetter is dat hûs opbrând, mar doe wennen mem en dy der al net mear. Ik bin yn dat hûs geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33283,"r":"CJ088401","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Two men once saw a shed on fire, but when they came closer, nothing turned out to be wrong. Later the shed did burn down after all.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in joun soe 'k nei pake en dy ta, 'k wie in jonge fan sa'n jier of achttsjin. Ik slepte altyd by pake en dy. Geartom hie 'k by my.\nDoe seagen ik en Geart-om it hok fan Gjert van der Veen yn 'e brân stean. Dat wie hjir oan 'e Mellereed. Op in distânsje fan 200 meter seagen wy 't brânnen. Wy seagen 't glêshelder brânnen.\nWy stapten hurd by pake en beppe yn 'e hûs. Dy leinen al op bêd. Ik haw se der útroppen. Doe gongen se foar 't sydgleske stean om nei de brân to sjen.\nIk sei: \"Wy matte rinne omke, om by de brân to kommen.\" Dan koenen wy mei helpe, tocht ik. Doe't wy op healwei wienen brânde 't noch. Mar doe't wy der oan ta wienen, wie 't út.\nIt hie noait brând. En dochs hienen wy it klear sjoen.\nBinnen 't healjier is 't opbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33288,"r":"CJ088406","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man once saw a farmhouse on fire, but when he came closer, nothing turned out to be wrong. Later the farm did burn down after all.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"yn 'e brân. 't Wie by de earste bocht as men gyng fan 'e brêge fan 'e Harkema nei Surhústerfean. Mar doe't omke der by kom, brânde 't net.\nLetter is dat spul ôfbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33518,"r":"CJ090902","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man once saw a house on fire. Later the house really burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 't Wyldpaed wenne Rinse Loonstra. Dy seach fan alles foarút. Op in kear sei er: \"Der brânt wer hwat op yn 't koart.\" Hy hie in spultsje brânnen sjoen. Doe't er dat sei woarden de minsken binaud, hwant hy sei der net by hokker hûs it wie. Koarte tiid dêrnei brânde it op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33596,"r":"CJ091502","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Someone once saw a house on fire. Later the house really burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Jistrum hat in hûs stien, dêr seinen se fan: dat sil nochris opbrânne. Hwant ien hie it brânnen sjoen. It is letter ek opbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34592,"r":"CJ093702","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"We lived next door. It was said that something would happen someday. They had heard a hellish racket and saw a red light. \"It will burn down one day,\" they said, but it hasn't happened yet.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha hjir neist wenne. Doe ha se ris sein: \"Hjir gebeurt nochris hwat.\" Se hearden in lûd, dat wie krekt as foelen der bynten del. En tagelyk seagen se in read ljocht yn 'e glêzen fan 'e skuorre.\n\"'t Sil in kear opbrânne\", seinen se.\nMar 't is noch net gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33807,"r":"CJ094402","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"People once saw a house on fire, but in reality there was nothing. They were convinced the house would burn down someday, but that has yet to happen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Twizelerheide, oan 't Wyldpaed, stie in hûs yn 'e brân. Us folk seach it barnen. Der allegear hinne, mar it stie net yn 'e brân. Ik wie doe in famke, 'k ha der ek noch hinne west to sjen. It is net opbarnd, mar de hiting is dat dat noch gebeure sil. Dat leauden ús heit en dy ek grif en ik sels èk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33860,"r":"CJ094803","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"People once heard a sound in a house as if the place were on fire, but there was nothing to be seen. Some still claim the house will burn down one day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy sieten meielkoar yn 'e hûs. Ik wie doe noch hiel lyts, dat ik haw der sels gjin herinnering mear fan. Mar myn trije susters wienen doe al jongfammen. Der wie ek in jonge buorman by ús. It wie op in joun.\nDoe hearden se ynienen in lûd, noait liker as rieden se mei in kroade oer de telle hinne en as foelen de bynten kreakjend del. En 't wie ien en al geknetter. As stie alles yn 'e brân.\nSe gongen allegear nei 't bûthús ta, alle trije susters gongen mei. Doe't se dêr kommen, stienen de beesten allegear achterstofoar op 'e stâllen, mei de kop nei de telle ta. En der wie net in inkelde koe dy't lei. Der wie hielendal neat to sjen fierder, dat sy gongen wer yn 'e hûs.\nDe jouns kom dy jonge buorman by syn frou thús. Doe sei dy frou: \"Hwat hienen jimme dêr nyskes in wille, net? Hwat gong 't der dêr oan wei.\"\nDoe fortelde de buorman it forhael.\nHjir wennet in âld frou, dy biweart noch altyd dat it hûs nochris in kear opbarne sil. It wienen de lûden fan brân, dy't se heard ha. Alles foel knetterjend del.\nDer hie foartsjirmerije fan west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36056,"r":"CJ096202","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Jehannes Mijnheer had a little shop on the spot where a school later stood. That is gone now too. Some people had seen Mijnheer's shop on fire, and later that indeed happened.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jehannes Mijnheer hat in winkeltsje hawn op 'e Boelensloane. Letter hat dêr in skoalle stien, dy is der nou ek al wer wei. Dat winkeltsje fan Jehannes ha guon yn 'e brân stean sjoen. Letter is it opbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36107,"r":"CJ096503","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"My mother-in-law lived on Alllardseach. Some people said they saw fire behind her house. Later, when she was already dead, the house indeed burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanmem wenne op Allardseach ûnder Bakkefean. Doe wienen der guon dy fortelden har dat se hienen har hûs yn 'e brân sjoen. Dat bitsjutte safolle as it soe letter ôfbrânne. It is ek gebeurd. Mar doe wenen skoanmem der net mear.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36183,"r":"CJ097102","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"In Boelenslaan people often saw in advance that a house would burn down, or that a new house would be built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha faek heard dat de minsken seinen: dat en dat hûs mat nochris ôfbrânne. Dy en dy ha 't brânnen sjoen. \nSa hearden se ek faek timmerjen op plakken dêr't neat wie, mar dêr't letter in hûs kom to stean. Dat wie hjir yn 'e Boelensloane algemien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36300,"r":"CJ097705","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"The narrator's mother predicted that two houses in their neighbourhood would burn down. In one of the fires all of Dedde Wybenga's livestock would perish.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Hindriks Kike wenne achter ús. Mem sei op in kear:\n\"Der sil ûnwaer komme, dan rekket âlde Hindriks Kike har hûs der ôf. Ik ha 't brânnen sjoen. En op 'e Foarwei sil de boerepleats fan Dedde Wybenga ôfbrânne en alle fé sil der yn omkomme.\"\n't Is allegear sa gebeurd. Hja sei: \"Ik sjoch allegearre fjûr.\" De oare deis gebeurde it. Der kom in greate klobbe fjûr, dy splitste him yn twaën, de iene helte gong dizze kant út, de oare helte de oare kant. Op ús tún forskroeide alles en sa rekke 't hûs fan Hindriks Kike ek yn 'e brân.\nDedde Wybenga syn pleats brânde ek hielendal op deselde deis. Myn broer hat der noch hinne west om it fé los to snijen, mar it wie forgees. It koe net mear. Mem wist wol dat dat net mear koe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36515,"r":"CJ098804","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man had seen that a little shop where someone lived was on fire. A little later it indeed burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wienen noch fan dy bern, doe wie der in man, dy sei tsjin ús mem: \"Ik haw in brân sjoen.\" It winkeltsje, skean tsjin ús oer hied er yn 'e brân sjoen. Dêr wenne in âld minske yn. Gauachtich dêrnei brânde it op. Mem wie doe noch bang dat er him forsjoen hie, dat it ús hûs wêze soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36858,"r":"CJ100803","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"We once saw the house of Hindrik and Ael across the Swadde burning. There turned out to be no fire, but later that whole house burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in joun soenen wy nei Grinslân ta to wjûden. Doe seinen wy: \"Sjoch, 't spultsje fan Hindrik en Ael stiet yn 'e brân.\"\nDat hûs stie oer de Swâdde. Mar it brânde net.\nIn setsje letter is it opbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36967,"r":"CJ101505","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Many people had seen a house on fire in advance that later burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Drachtster Kompenije is ris in hûs ôfbrând, dat ha se al folle earder yn 'e brân stean sjoen. 't Wie foartjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37013,"r":"CJ101602","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Ruerd, the brother of the painter Jan Planting, was a bit peculiar. Once he stood gazing into the distance. Asked what he saw, he answered that he saw a fire. The next day a house burned down there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jan Planting, de kunstskilder fan Drachten, hie in broer. Dat wie Ruerd. Dy wie in bytsje eigenaerdich.\nOp in kear stie er op 'e hoeke fan 'e Langewyk en doe seach er de kant út nei Oerterp.\n\"Hwat dochstû hjir, Ruerd?\" frege ik, hwant hy stie dêr mar to sjen.\nEarst sei er neat, doe wie it: \"Dêr komt brân.\"\n\"Hwêrre?\" frege ik.\n\"Dêrre\", sei er, en hy wiisde it plak oan.\nDe oare jouns stie Gosling Scholte syn hûs op it Oerterper Fallaet yn 'e brân.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37196,"r":"CJ103103","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"The same fellow once predicted a fire, which happened six weeks later when lightning struck.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mei dyselde maet wie ik to Kûkherne op in plaets fan 'e Veenlands. Der wenne in boer op, dat wie in Hoekstra. Dy hie in soan: Bouwe Hoekstra.\nMyn maet sei tsjin Bouwe: \"Dizze plaets brânt skielk ôf.\"\nSeis wiken letter gebeurde it. De wjerljocht sloech yn. Myn maet hie him fan tofoaren al yn 'e brân sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37449,"r":"CJ104501","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"From afar people see a house on fire, but at the house nothing is wrong. A few days later the house burns down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 'e Ds. Visser-wei yn 'e Houtigehage wienen guon dy seagen dêr ris in hûs yn 'e brân stean. Mar doe't se der by kamen wie der gjin brân. Mar in dei of hwat letter brânde it wol degelik op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37572,"r":"CJ105501","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"The grandparents are already in bed when uncle comes home and says there is a fire nearby. The grandparents see nothing, but uncle says many people are standing watching. As uncle goes towards the house, at first he sees the fire very clearly. When he reached the house it was not on fire at all.\nAbout a year later the house burned down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us pake en beppe wennen hjir yn dit hûs. Op in joune let leinen se op bêd, doe kaem myn omke thús. Hy gong nei 't bêd fan pake en beppe ta en sei: \"Der is brân, hjir tichteby. It hûs fan Wiggele van der Veen stiet yn 'e brân.\"\nPake en beppe kamen gau fan bêd ôf, om to sjen. Mar de beide âlde minsken seagen neat. \"Sjogge jimme it dan net?\" sei omke, \"it is ommers allegear fjûr, sjoch der is in hiele protte folk by.\"\nMar pake en beppe seagen neat. Doe gong omke der hinne. Earst seach er de brân hiel dúdlik, mar doe't er by it hûs kaem stie 't hielendal net yn 'e brân.\nSahwat in jier letter is 't opbrând. It hie foartsjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":210367,"r":"VODA_045_03","p":"Barger-Compascuum","v":"Dr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Some people could tell in advance where an accident would happen or where a house would burn down. This was not dangerous.\nThere were also [women?] who flew through the air and gathered at their own spot in the field. They were not very dangerous either.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"D’r waren ook veurbeduutsels, zeker. Maar die waren niet gevoorlijk. Da zagen die alleine maar in ’t veuren wat later nog gebeuren mos. Maar d’r weurden hee luuj vanach [geblader] dee u secuur vertellen können waor ’n óngeluk gebeurde, ob waor ’n hoes later ofbrandde en det kwaam toch ouk es altied oet. \nD’r wuurd ook nog waal ens [vrouwen gekleurd??], maar dee wuurden, [afstrijken lucifer] ach, dae wuurden ouch neet zo gevoorlijk. Dae vleugen alleine maar wat door de lócht. En dae hadden een eigen stee in ’t veld waor ze bie mekaar kwam’n.","l":"Nedersaksisch; Drents"},{"n":210410,"r":"VODA_045_08","p":"Barger-Compascuum","v":"Dr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"People sometimes saw strange things, such as little lights, at places where something would later be built, such as a canal, a road, houses or a whole town. A fire was sometimes seen in advance too. Often such a house or farm did indeed burn down later.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"I = interviewer\nV = verteller (Veringa)\n\n[Gelach]\nI: Ehm.. tweede gezicht, hè, dat veurspellen van wat ‘r gebeurt, zeg maar een woning zien staon of een weg deur ’t veen of lichtjes of zoiets, is dat… kennen jullie iets van?\nV: Je wilt zeggen: wat ‘r nog nooit was en later kwam? En wat ze veuroet zagen?\nI: Ja.\nV: O, hier op ’t veen, ja, natuurlijk. Kanaol. Wegen. Dat vertelden ze veuruut. Maar zo, wat ik zo sterk had in de Berkenrode, dat was vrouger een maatschappij, dat is vandaag is dat Berkenrode en dao liggen no’n straatweg... [gekraak van meubel] en dao zagen ze auto’s, vanteveuren, leeg, heil leeg, door ’t veen gaon. En dao kos ‘t niemand begriepen wat ’t waas, maar dae gong nie over t’bovenveen, niet over die Veenweg, nee, dae gong as ’t ware onder de Veenweg, zo diep waren dee. Weg in de grond, as ’t ware. En dat kos ook niemand begriepen. En vandage gaon de auto’s d’ natuurlijk met lichten langs, dat begriept u wel, doorveur ligt d’r nou een straatweg. Toen was alles nog veen, toen de mensen daor woonden. En toen was d‘r niks as ’n modderpad en.. en.. en zoiets. En now den, zo gauw des geen mens meer woont en was daor een goeien weg liggen. Maar die is niet veur de mensen, lui, die is natuurlijk veur de.. veur de firma [..?..] dae ’t land dao liggen had. Dat is al gewoon, dat weten we wel, hm.\n[onderbreking opname]\nI: Ehm, het vanteveuren veurspellen van d’r kompt een","l":"Nedersaksisch; Drents"},{"n":38438,"r":"CJ109322","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"It is known in advance that a house will burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie ek in hûs yn Feanwâldsterwâl, dêr wisten se fantofoaren al fan dat it opbrânne soe. Dat fortelde heit.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38548,"r":"CJ109803","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees a house on fire before it really burns down. Many do not believe it, but it comes true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bouke en Minke ha hjir mei har dochter njonken ús wenne. Ik haw dat hûs yn 'e brân sjoen, in jier foardat it yn werklikheit opbrânde. Ik ha doe sein: \"Dit hûs brânt ôf.\" Guon woenen 't net leauwe, mar ik hie it brânnen sjoen, en it kaem nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38624,"r":"CJ110002","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"People see a house on fire, although in reality it is not. The house later burns down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sa haw ik ek faek fortellen heard dat men in hûs yn 'e brân seach, mar yn werkelikheit barnde it net. Dan seinen se: dat hûs sil nochris opbarne. En dat gebeurde dan letter ek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":10676,"r":"CJ110102","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"People see a house on fire. It is a voorgezicht (a vision of a future event): later the house really does burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Harkema seagen se in hûs brânnen. It wie it hûs fan Hindrik Dykstra. Letter is 't opbrând. Der binne ek noch bern yn forbrând. De frou wie doe krekt by oare minsken om in bakje kofje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29764,"r":"CJ111502","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Somewhere a house is ablaze. When people approach the house, it turns out not to be burning. It is a premonition: a few days later the house actually burns down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Harkema is yndertiid in hûs ôfbrând. Guon seagen it fan tofoaren al yn 'e brân stean. It wie ien stik fjûr. Mar doe't se tichteby kamen, brânde it net. Mar in dei of hwat letter brânde it op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30031,"r":"CJ112108","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Some people are said to have seen a fire in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Gauris ha 'k fortellen heard dat der minsken wienen, dy't in brân al fan tofoaren sjoen hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30119,"r":"CJ112507","p":"Hijum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"People see a place on fire. It is a premonition: later the place actually burns down. At a certain spot where psalm singing is heard, a church later rises. The singing is also an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wit noch dat myn bepe fortelde hoe't hjir ris in pleats ôfbaernd is, dêr wisten se fan dat dat gebeure soe, hwant hja hienen him earder al barnen sjoen.\nEk fortelde se fan psalmsjongen op in plak, dêr't se letter in tsjerke boud ha.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":130013,"r":"VODA_030_11","p":"Uitgeest","v":"N.-H.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A postman ran in panic to the miller's house because the mill was on fire. But when the miller went to look at the mill, nothing turned out to be wrong. A few days later a fire did break out in the mill. So the postman had seen it in advance.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"[Geblader] Toen nog dit verhaal dat waar gebeurd moet zijn, want m’n moeder is daar getuige van geweest. \nZoals ik al zei: m’n grootouders woonden op enige afstand van de molen waarvan mijn grootvader eigenaar was. Op een dag kwam de postbode met z’n brieventas het erf van m’n grootouders oprennen en hij riep: “Mulder! Mulder! De molen staat in brand!” M’n grootvader vliegt naar buiten, ergens heen vanwaar hij de molen kon zien, maar hij zag geen vuur. Hij is er toen waarschijnlijk met paard en wagen heen gereden, maar d’r was niets aan de hand. De postbode, die nog helemaal ontdaan was, beweerde bij hoog en bij laag dat hij de molen had zien branden.\nEnige dagen later toen er een flinke storm woedde is er iets gebeurd, waarschijnlijk de vang van de molen is eh… losgegaan of zo, waardoor de boel warm is gelopen en de bovenkant van de molen helemaal verbrand is. De postbode had het dus wel goed gezien."},{"n":131058,"r":"VODA_032_03","p":"Ommen","v":"Ov.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a fire.\n\nA boy heard noise and saw a great fire at a farm, but suddenly the flames were gone. Later the farm really burned down. The boy had seen a voorspooksel or voorloop.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"En dan he’k nog ’n stukkie, ook over veurspoeksels. Daar was ’n jongen, Hendrik ’hieten en dean had verkering met ’n magie en dea ging s’oams doarheen en he ziet doar te wachten op dat magie. Toe in ien keer toe heurd-e een gekerm, en gejank. Het was ‘n [?] leben. En doe was doa beej ‘n kerk en doa leup ’n voetpad veurlangs en doe löp-e doa ook zo veurlangs, doa kwaamp det geluud vandaan en doe zeat-e eh… ’t was ’n heule vlakte en in de veerte doa was gg… ‘n grote brand. Was ’n boerenhuus, stund in volle vlammen [harde dreun, vuilniswagen die containers leegt?]. En he had ’t goedewel ‘ezien en foetsie was de hele mikmak. Was geen brand meer te bekennen. [nogmaals harde dreun] Maar wat wil ’t geval? Ienige tied doanoa doe brand die boel af. En dit is ook ’n woar verhaal, want dat hed ik zelf van ’n familielid, van een oldoom, dea was kameroad met dea jòng. En dea oldome zei altied: “Ich geleuve noe wel niet in die dinge, maar ik heb mien kameroad Hendrik ook nog nooit op leugen betrapt.” En mien ome dea was ook, wat dat an betreft, was ook goed betrouwbaar.","l":"Sallands"},{"n":128510,"r":"ENGELB_12_022","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1975,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"After twice hearing music and seeing a house burn, the third time there is a real fire.","i":"H.E.","o":"Klein Haarhuis: Dee oolde leu, dee hadn gen kinder, hadn gen kinder, warn wa trouwd, hadn gen kinder, zee warn wa oardig oold, zee warn allebear oold wördn, den een was acht en zeuvntig en den aander was zes en tachntig wördn, mer dee vrouw was op nen oavnd en pankook bakn, mich at ze dat wat later vertöl, mer dat vertöl ze vuuroet, was an t pankook bakn en ooldn J., den kröppeln met t been, den zat an n hook van n heard van t veur, an t pankook bakn en in eenmoal doe heurt ze boetn mooi muziek, dee vrouw, meuiste muziek, zear ze, kleunk mie in de oorn, ik zej: God, J. goa es met, ik doo de duur los, God, God, buurman steet in braand, zie loopt d’rhen, net langs den heg langs, zie lagn ongeveer 60 meter oet mekaar, nich veerder, en no zint ze doar halfweg, alles oet, tweed’n oavnd precies tzölfde, was an t ofwaske heur ik wier dat muziek, geet wier noar boetn, in braand, t hele hoes, vleagt d’r wier hen, dezölfde stie, wier verdweenn en t deerde moal, n wek of veer, vief, zes wek later, doe braandn he of en den keerl geer d’r nog um hen te springn en zeg he, zoavöl veur en zoavöl veur en no kaan’k nog de piep nich ankriegn, dat is eerlik gebuurd, dat kon ze vuur de tied, hadn ze dat a vertöln","l":"Twents"},{"n":31005,"r":"CJ115009","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man dreams that a farmhouse burns down. He sees very clearly a glowing ball on the owl board (gable ornament). The dream comes true: the farmhouse burns down fourteen days later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit wenne yn Feanwâldsterwâl. Hy wie sa'n 17 jier âld, doe hied er op in nacht in droom. Hy droomde dat yn it Bûtenfjild soe de buorkerij fan Kees Broersma ôfbrânne. Heit seach dúdlik in gleone bol op it ûleboerd. 't Wie in bol fan fjûr. En dy rolle oer de hiele naed fan 'e skuorre hinne nei de oare ein ta. Doe wie dy bol ynienen fuort.\n14 dagen letter is dy plaets troch in ûnwaer ôfbrând.\n(nei dy tiid is dy pleats nochris ôfbrând)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31179,"r":"CJ115804","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"At a certain place people saw a house on fire that really did burn down a few days later. It was a premonition.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Jistrum is it wol gebeurd dat minsken fan to foaren in hûs yn 'e brân seagen, dat in dei of hwat letter yn werklikheit ôfbrânde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31309,"r":"CJ116516","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees a farmhouse on fire. It is an omen: a week later the farmhouse actually burns down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op it Heechsân yn Eastemar stie de pleats fan Tsjerk-om en Piter-om. In wike foardat dy pleats opbrând is seach ien fan 't Heechsân him yn 'e nacht yn 'e brân stean. Dat wie foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31914,"r":"CJ120504","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1978,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees a certain house on fire three times. They are premonitions: right after the third premonition the house actually burns down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Japik van der Kooi fan Grinzer Pein hat trije kearen fan tofoaren it hûs, dêr't Wigle van der Veen yn wenne, yn 'e brân stean sjoen. Nei de trêdde kear hat it net sa lang mear duorre, doe wie 't sa fier. 't Is oan 'e groun ta opbrând.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31542,"r":"CJ118206","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"Someone sees a carpenter's shed on fire while it is not actually burning. It is a portent: shortly afterwards it really goes up in flames.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn it hûs dêr't nou Haga de fytsmakker wennet, op it hoekje oan 'e Lytse Wei wenne froeger in timmerman, in sekere de Jong. Hy hie dêr syn timmerhok njonken stean.\nBoven yn dat timmerhok sieten lytse doarkes, dêr koe 't hout, lyk as planken en balken, ta'n ynskoud wurde.\nOp in joun wie dêr ien, dy seach fjûr ta dy doarkes útkommen. Hy rôp: Dat hok stiet yn 'e brân! Mar doe't hy en oare minsken der by kamen, wie 't sa net.\nLetter is it hok opbrând. Dat wie èk tjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31961,"r":"CJ121002","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees a house on fire: a premonition. The premonition has not yet come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Douwe en Det wennen yn in hûs op Sumarreheide, dêr waerd fan sein dat it nochris opbrânne soe. Knjillis Sudema hie it brânnen sjoen, mar it stiet der altyd noch.\nHy mat fier foarútsjen kind ha -","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31987,"r":"CJ121106","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees an inn on fire, but when he goes there, there is no fire. Later the inn burns down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn broer fortelde: Twa bruorren, Atse en Wander Veltman, allebeide timmerlju to Eastemar kamen ris op in joune thús, doe sei de iene tsjin 'e oare: \"Sjoch, de herberch stiet yn 'e brân.\" Hy seach de minsken drok yn 't spier om der allegearre guod noch út to heljen.\nMar 't wie sa net. Hja rounen der hinne, mar dêr wie hielendal gjin brân. Letter is dy herberch opbrând.\nDat is sa'n 80 jier lyn, ik wie doe noch in jonkje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31988,"r":"CJ121107","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0491","d":"A man sees a small farmhouse on fire. It is a premonition: only years later does the farmhouse actually burn down.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn omke wenne yn Ikkerwâld. Hy kaem ris op in joun thús, doe stie dêr in pleatske yn 'e brân. De minsken kamen der út mei har rommel om to rêdden hwat der noch to rêdden wie. Omke fortelde oan oare minsken hwat er sjoen hie. It hûs stie net yn 'e brân. Mar jierren letter brânde 't wol ôf. En krekt sa't er it sjoen hie, tôgen de minsken mei rommel dy't se út 'e hûs hellen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":69805,"r":"DYKFRIES2201","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A seer in Eernewoude saw a steamboat sailing on the broad water beside this village, when no one yet dreamed that steamboats would be put into service from Drachten to Leeuwarden. Likewise, here and there people heard the roar of trains, years before there was any talk of railways in Friesland.","i":"W.D."},{"n":13619,"r":"LYST275","p":"Hardenberg","v":"Ov.","y":1937,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Someone sees and hears trains and ships passing over the land. Later a railway line and a canal are built there.","i":"H.J.G.","o":"Van sommige gebeurtenissen zouden enkele personen voorteekenen gezien of gehoord hebben. (In den volksmond \"veurspeukels\" genoemd).\nZoo hoorde ik van een zeer betrouwbaar persoon een pertinente verklaring, dat hij op een plaats, waar later de Noord-Oosten Waalspoor werd aangelegd, duidelijk een trein had hooren passeeren en dat toen van een in de buurt zijndes landbouwer de paarden begonnen te steigeren.\nVerder werd mij verteld dat het kanaal Almelo-Coevorden door iemand voorspeld was, door iemand die de schepen door het land zag zeilen."},{"n":15511,"r":"CJ002301","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1954,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man meets a big fellow at night and flees from him. Years later an electricity pole turns out to stand on that very spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie to jounpraten west. Ik gong in sânreed del.\nDoe stie der ynienen in hiele greate keardel foar my mei de strampels wiid fan elkoar. Ik roan dêr mei in bôge om hinne. Op itselde plak kom nei jierren in peal mei in strampel to stean foar 't elektrysk ljocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21794,"r":"CJ0286B23","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1954,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At a certain place a man thinks he sees a monster with glowing eyes. He also hears a whistling sound as if a heavy storm were blowing. Later the tram station is built on that spot: the glowing 'eyes' - lamps - and the whistling sound were a forerunner of the steam tram.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In man út Sumar, dy't nei Grins west hie foar ûndersyk yn it jier 1887 kom op it Barndelân by de Nije Wei in hiel great munster to sjen mei gleone egen. It wie stil waer, mar it sûze en bearde dêr as stie der in stoarm.\nLetter, om 1893, 94 hinne is dêr it tramstasjon boud, en doe wist er, dat it de foarboade fan 'e tram west hie, dy't stoom út 'e masine komme liet. Dêr wied er sa kjel fan woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15762,"r":"CJ003012","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1955,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A woman hears the trains from Grins to Harns and cannot sleep for the noise. Only later is the railway actually built.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In âld-man fan Kûkherne fortelde my ris, dat syn beppe hie faek sein, sy hie it spoar, dat fan Grins nei Harns gong al fan to foaren heard. Dan bromde en sûze it sa bot, dat sy koe der de nachts suver net fan sliepe. Dat hienen de foarboaden west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":43272,"r":"AMPT000402","p":"Holten","v":"Ov.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Will-o'-the-wisps a man thinks he has seen turn out to be the lights of cars and bicycles on a road built later.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"Jaren geleden kwam er een man op een avond laat onze boerderij binnen gevlucht. Hij was zeer geschrokken, want hij had ver weg in het Broek dwaallichten gezien, op plaatsen waar geen mensen konden zijn. We begrepen toen niet wat het geweest kon zijn, maar nu weet ik het wel. Die man had toen de lichten gezien van fietsen en auto's die nu sinds twee jaar over de nieuwe weg rijden die na de herverkaveling door het Broek is aangelegd. Hij moet met de helm op zijn geboren."},{"n":43545,"r":"AMPT000702","p":"Zwolle","v":"Ov.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Where a tram line later runs, people earlier see carts without horses at night that still move forward.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"Achter een herberg in Zwartsluis zagen de mensen 's avonds dikwijls wagens zonder paarden, die toch vooruit gingen. Later liep daar achter de tram. Ze hadden dus veuruut gezien.","l":"Overijssels"},{"n":130753,"r":"KEUNING000302","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A prediction that a train would run in the canal did not come true.","i":"S.K.","o":"Bontsje Knilles hat foarsjoen, dat der soe in trein yn 'e feart ride, oan disse kant fan Kûkherne. De trein soe út tije rydtugen bistean. It is oan nou ta noch net útkaem, hwant sûnt dy tiid is er nea in trein mei 5 rydtugen lâns kaem.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131170,"r":"KEUNING005402","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A light in the sky is a portent of a later tramline.","i":"S.K.","o":"Op Semarder Heide seagen se alle jounen in ljocht de loft lâns gean. Dat wie foartsjirmerij fan de tram, dy dêr letter lâns kaem to rinnen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131219,"r":"KEUNING006005","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"The sound of wagons is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the building of a tramway.","i":"S.K.","o":"By de polderdyk hearden se faek in gebolder, krekt as ried der in rigele weinen lâns, Letter kaem dêr de tramwei fan Drachten nei Ljouwert lâns.\nFrou fan forteller: \"Ja, dat gebolder hearden wy faek by ús thús op de souder.\"","l":"Fries"},{"n":131229,"r":"KEUNING006106","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At a place where noise was heard in the sky, a tramline was later built.","i":"S.K.","o":"It is ek ris west, dan hearde min altyd gebolder yn de loft. Letter is op it plak, wer min dat hearde, de tramwei kaem.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131319,"r":"KEUNING007024","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A bridge over a canal, ships and wagons without horses are seen before a canal with a bridge and a tramline are built at that place.","i":"S.K.","o":"Pake siet op Nigaster Hoek yn de herberg. Der komt noch ien yn.. dy wie hielendal fan de wize.\n\"Ik wie sapas yn 'e Pein,\" sei hy. \"En hwat seach ik dêr? In brêge oer in kanaal en allegearre skippen. En der kaem in rigele weinen oan riden. En der wienen net iens hynders foar.\"\nIn skoft letter is dêr wier in kanael groeven, wer in bulte skippen troch farden. En se leinen der in brêge oerhinne. En noch letter ried dêr de Drachtster tram.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131385,"r":"KEUNING008104","p":"Paesens","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Fishermen's wives foresee that a farm will burn down.","i":"S.K.","o":"De fiskersfrouljue sutelden mei fisk alle doarpen ôf, dy hja birinne koenen. Faek seinen se dan, dat in pleats ôfbarne soe. Dat seagen se dan al oankommen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":43089,"r":"WEV000907","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Hearing and seeing a steam train before there is any talk of a train running there.","i":"F.W.","o":"En mijn schoonvader heeft voordat de stoomtrein door Ter-Apel reed, hem al zien aankomen. Bovendien hoorde hij het fluiten.\nHij was weer geen man, die er om loog."},{"n":32450,"r":"CJ126104","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People see the lights of the tram before it even runs.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foardat de tram troch de Sumarreheide ried ha in soad minsken dêr it jiers tofoaren de ljochtsjes al sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":131494,"r":"KEUNING009603","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Hearing trains run where there is no railway line.","i":"S.K.","o":"Der wienen yn Kollumersweach froeger minsken, dy it spoar riden hearden. En der wie dêr doe noch gjin spoar. Netiens rails.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131549,"r":"KEUNING010701","p":"Ljussens","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Hearing a train run before any rails have been laid.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ús heit hearde ris in trein riden by Kollumerpomp. En dêr wie gjin trein. Netiens rails. Letter kaem dêr de spoarbaen fan Ljouwert nei Grins lâns. Dat neamden se by ús: foargespin.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131553,"r":"KEUNING010801","p":"Ljussens","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Two lights that are seen are the portent of a later tramline.","i":"S.K.","o":"L.C. seach hjir ris twa greate ljochten troch de kolken fleanen. Letter ried dêr it lokaeltsje fan Dokkum nei Anjum lâns.","l":"Fries"},{"n":43355,"r":"WEV006401","p":"Nieuw-Weerdinge","v":"Dr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man feels something pass by him but sees nothing, and hears a little bell and scraping over iron. This turns out to have been the voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a tram running.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nJa, dat is dr wel. Ik heb zulf wel al wat zien en heurd.\nk Kwam es n moal van Emmen en toen heurden ik iets langs mie goan. Ik zagge niks. t Was geluud van n bellegien en t schuurn over iezer. Loater werd mie het dudelk.\nToen kwam de tram van Emmen noar Teroapel. En die maken precies hetzulfde geluud as ik vrogger heurden. t Was altemoal nog modder, toen ik dr van Emmen kwam.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":130251,"r":"BIJLSMA001101","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At the place where a little light is seen, a tramline is later built.","i":"T.B.","o":"As men by joun op it Achterom op 'e Jouwer kaem, dan koe it barre dat men in ljochtsje sa fan de kant fan de simmerdyk ôf op 'e mole fan de Súd-westpolder oankommen seach.\nJierren letter waerd dêr de trambaen nei de Lemmer oanlein.","l":"Fries"},{"n":15596,"r":"CJ002408","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Before the tram came to Sumar, some people saw a row of stoves with glowing coals in them. These were the carriages.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Even foardat de tram yn Sumar kom ha guon minsken in hiele rige stoven sjoen mei brânnende koaltsjes der yn. Dat wienen de wagons.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15805,"r":"CJ003504","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People see the tram lights even before the tramline from the Hearrewei to Burgum is laid. That was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy seagen de ljochten fan 'e tram fan tofoaren al, foar dat de tram der wie. It gong de Hearrewei del en dan skean de heide oer. Wy seinen dan: \"Der giet ek noch in ljocht skean de heide oer op Burgum yn.\" Letter wie it de tram dy't dêr lâns ried.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15909,"r":"CJ004004","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Light phenomena foretell the coming of the bicycle.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De wylde lantearnen fan froeger, dat wienen letter de fytsen. Wy seagen froeger de wylde lantearnen de sânpaden delstouwen kommen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16060,"r":"CJ004212","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Some people here heard and saw the railway line beforehand.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":16517,"r":"CJ005801","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"The narrator's uncle had heard the heavy vehicles beforehand that later came to drive on the Groningen highway. They were exactly the same sounds.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn omke hat fantofoaren de swiere auto's al heard dy't letter op 'e Grinzer strietwei kommen to riden. It wienen krekt deselde lûden","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16844,"r":"CJ006406","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man is at a neighbourhood meeting in Skieding. Someone there said: \"I come through Mearumer Leech and three lanterns are burning there.\" A year later three stops for the tramline are built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in buorforgadering op 'e Skieding siet myn man ek, doe wied er noch jong. Doe sei der ien: \"Ik kom troch 't Mearumer Leech en dêr brânden trije lantearnen.\"\nIn jier letter kommen dêr trije halten foar de tramlijn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16870,"r":"CJ006518","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Lanterns out in the open are the forerunners of other lanterns (on bicycles and the highway).","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen binne de foarboaden fan oare lantearnen. (op fytsen en strjitwei)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17095,"r":"CJ008107","p":"Sweagerbosk","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"One evening the narrator's father comes home with the cart and two young horses in front of it. At the spot where the railway now runs, he and his father suddenly hear a hellish noise. The horses become agitated and break out in a sweat. Shortly afterwards the railway is built there, and they hear the same sound when the train runs over the rails.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It is sahwat krekt hûndert jier lyn. Heit wie noch feint, hy wenne by pake yn. Op in joun kom er thús mei de wein, dêr't er in pear jonge hynders foar hie. Pake wenne op in spultsje krekt oer 't spoar hinne. Mar it spoar wie der doe noch net. Doe't er oer it plak hinne ried, dêr't letter it spoar kom, wie der ynienen in heislik lawaei yn 'e loft. Heit waerd tige kjel en de jonge hynders rekken oerstjûr. Pake sei: \"Hwat switte dy hynders.\"\n\"Hat heit dat geraes dan net heard?\"\n\"Jawol.\"\n\"Nou, dêr bin de hynders kjel fan woarn.\"\nRidlik gau dêrnei waerd it spoar dêr oanlein. En doe hearden se krekt itselde lûd, doe't de trein oer de rails ried.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17123,"r":"CJ008402","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Many people saw the lights of the tram long before it ran.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Gâns minsken fan Sumarreheide ha fan to foaren de ljochtsjes fan 'e tram sjoen, foardat dy noch ried.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17376,"r":"CJ009002","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"The narrator and his wife sometimes see lights low to the ground along the canal near Surhuisterveen in the evening. People say a motorway will come there. The light sometimes crosses the canal too, so a bridge would also have to come. Some also say they are the lights of a train.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik kom us mei 't wiif op in joun fan Surhústerfean. Wy hienen dêr hinne west to praten. 't Wie yn 't bigjin fan ús trouwen. Doe't wy sahwat healwei de feart wienen seagen wy beide in ljocht. 't Wie nochal ticht by de groun en 't gong om in húske hinne. 't Gong hiel hurd, wy bleauwen allebeide kjel stean. Doe gong it by de wâl lâns en doe kom it werom. 't Wie sahwat om ien ûre yn 'e nacht.\nDer is letter noait hwat gebeurd, mar der wurdt sein, dat dêr noch in wei lâns komt. Sjoch, dan soe 't in auto wêze kinnen ha. Mar 't gong ek in kear oer de feart hinne, dat dan mat der ek in brêge komme. Ik haw ek wol heard dat se seinen dat it fan in trein wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19385,"r":"CJ012703","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At a place where a railway was built, the sound of a train running over the rails had already been heard earlier.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't it spoar hjir oanlein is, ha se dat tiden fan tofoaren yn Sânbulten al heard. Se hearden de trein oer de rails riden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19615,"r":"CJ014011","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"One day in 1862 a fireball was seen in daylight over a large part of Friesland and a terrible roar was heard. The next day the train from Leeuwarden to Groningen ran for the first time.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 1862 wie der de oerdeis samar ynienen in fjûrbol yn 'e loft. It joech in freeslik geraes. Oer in great part fan Fryslân is 't sjoen woarn. Us pake wie yn Feanwâlden oan 't feantsjen. Hy wie ynienen oan kant sprong, sa kjel waerd hy der fan. 't Lawaei kom út 'e loft. De oare deis hie foar it earst it spoar riden fan Ljouwert nei Grins. It hie foartsjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19627,"r":"CJ014201","p":"Feanwâldsterwâl","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"An old woman once saw a little light in her room that made the sound of a train. It had been an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wie in âld minske, dat seach us op in kear in ljochtsje by har yn 'e keamer. Mar doe't se der nei gripe soe, koe se it net krije. Doe joech it in stik lûd krektsa as hwannear't der in trein oer de rails glydt. Dat hat de foarboade west fan 'e trein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20397,"r":"CJ018807","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People often see a little light floating over the heath. Later the tram will run at that spot. The will-o'-the-wisp was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon seagen froeger altyd in ljochtsje oer de heide fleanen. Dat waerd letter de tram.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20837,"r":"CJ021801","p":"Aldeboarn","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"After a woman had died, the neighbours stood waiting in the yard out of neighbourly duty. They heard a sound of iron going over iron, but there was nothing to be seen. Later the tram ran past at that very spot. It was exactly the same sound.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Wijnjeterp wie in frou stoarn. De buorlju stienen op it hiem to wachtsjen. 't Wie buorreplicht. Op in stuit hearden se allegear in lûd, dat izer oer izer gong. 't Wie hiel dúdlik. Mar der wie neat to sjen. Letter ried op datselde plak de tram lâns. It wie presys itselde lûd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":43714,"r":"WEV012106","p":"Weite","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Screeching and creaking in front of the door with nothing to be seen. After the tram line is built, the tram stops in front of the house and makes the same sound.","i":"F.W.","o":"Dizze vertelsels hebben mien oln mie verteld. \nMisschien is dr niks van woar. Wat wel woar is, en door loog mien oal heer nait om, is dit: \nBie Snieders in Vlagtwedde heurden ze iedere oavend, as ze net op berre wazzen, n gegier en gekroak veur t huus. \nZai dr den of, noar boetn tou om te kiekn. Niks te zain of te doun. Dat het n haile zet zo goan, tot de tramliene aanlegd is. \nToun gung tram dr langs en stopde om n uur of tiene veur heur huus. Den kwam weer datzulfde geluud.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44471,"r":"WEV013405","p":"Muntendam","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A farmer milking in the field feels something brush past him. Later a railway line is built.","i":"F.W.","o":"Zatn n keer n boer mit de vrou te melkn int land.\n“Hai, wat strik door toch wel bie mie langs?” zee d boer.\nLoater wos e t wel; is n spoorliene aanlegd en nou stoft de train over dat stee.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":18086,"r":"CJ011408","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Even before railways were built, people heard the thunder of a train at that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Feanwâlden ha forskeidene lju it dinderjen fan 'e trein heard, noch foardat de spoarlijnen oanlein wienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19842,"r":"CJ015221","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A farmer is working with his farmhands when he suddenly sees a small cloud of steam in the air and hears a rumbling sound. Later the train makes exactly the same sound. The farmer had foreseen that the railway would come there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 't Miedlân to Eastemar wie in boer mei syn folk oan 't swyljen. Der forskynde in lyts wolkje oan 'e loft, dat ynienen freeslik bigong to rommeljen.\nDe boer woarde der sa kjel fan, dat hy foel der hinne. Letter fornamen se dat it spoar, dat ridlik gau dêrnei oanlein woarde, krekt itselde lûd hie.\nIt hie de foarboade west fan it spoar.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19883,"r":"CJ015513","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Many people heard the sound of the train long before it began to run. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In bulte minsken ha froeger fan tofoaren de trein riden heard, dy't fan Feanwâlden nei Bûtenpost giet.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20231,"r":"CJ017918","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At night light phenomena are seen. They are omens of the later flying machines.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in moarntiid, sahwat om fjouwer ûre hinne, kom der us in ljocht op my ta. Doe dwaelde 't ek wer ôf. Dat hat foartsjirmerij west. Dat binne nou de fleanmesines. Doe neamden we dat wylde lantearnen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20288,"r":"CJ018203","p":"Burum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A number of people often heard the sound of the train, while the railway was only built years later. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Een paar jaren voordat de spoorlijn Groningen-Leeuwarden hier langs kwam, hoordn sommige mensen dat.\nMaar ze wisten niet wat het was. Toen later de trein kwam te puffen, toen seiden se: \"Dat het it west!\"","l":"Fries"},{"n":20712,"r":"CJ021108","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A doctor once came into an inn completely shaken. He told the innkeeper he had nearly been run over by a train. But there was not even a railway.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Easterwâlde wenne in dokter van der Sluis, dy seach de trein riden. Hy kaem yn 'e herberch to Koudenburg, alhiel fan 'e wize.\nDe kastlein sei: \"Hwat mankeart dokter nou?\"\n\"Dat wie krekt op 't nipperke,\" sei er, \"dan hie 'k dea west. Hwant de trein is kantroerend foar my lâns riden. De coupé's wienen allegear forljochte.\"\n\"Hwer wie dat?\" frege de kastlein.\n\"Dat wie krekt oan diz kant de poel\", sei de dokter.\n(Mar dy dokter hat mis west, hwant der is noait in spoarbaen kom. Wòl in trambaen, mar dat wie net by de poel)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20926,"r":"CJ022203","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A labourer once heard a roaring coming from a small cloud in the sky. A year later the train came there, making exactly the same sound. So it had been sorcery.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Pake fan Readtsjerk wie oan 't turfmeitsjen tusken Readtsjerk en Feanwâlden. Doe hearde er gebolder yn 'e loft. Doe sprong er út 'e feandobbe wei op 'e kant om to sjen hwat it wie. Doe seach er in wolkje oan 'e loft, dêr kom it gebolder út.\nIt oare jiers kom de trein der. Dy makke krekt itselde lûd. It hie dus foartjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21090,"r":"CJ024003","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A woman in bed at night always heard the sound of iron on iron. Her husband heard nothing. Later the tram came past there. It made exactly the sound she had always heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn beppe dy wenne op 'e Tike. Dy sei: \"It is noait liker as slagge se altyd mar op izer om, krekt as rollet it iene izer oer 't oare hinne.\" Hja hearde it nachts op bêd. \"Toe Teade,\" sei se dan tsjin pake, \"hear dû ek us.\" Mar pake dy hearde it net.\nLetter is de tram dêr lâns kom. Dy hie krekt itselde lûd as dat hja heard hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21111,"r":"CJ024110","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Several people heard the tram beforehand, before it ran.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Forskate lju ha hjir de tram fan to foaren heard, foardat dy hjir lâns kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21157,"r":"CJ024429","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"In the past some people sometimes heard a train running through the dug-out peat canal. But a train never came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger ha guon ris de trein riden heard troch de wide pet hinne. Mar der is noch noait in trein kaem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21339,"r":"CJ026007","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"In Sumarreheide a few people saw the lights of the tram beforehand, before the tram was there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Inkelden yn Sumarreheide ha de ljochtsjes fan 'e tram al fier fan tofoaren sjoen, foardat de tram der wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21340,"r":"CJ026008","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A little girl once saw a tram locomotive turn the corner, while in reality there was nothing. Some time later the tram came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik in famke wie fan sa'n jier as seis - doe wennen wy noch oan 'e polderdyk - doe seach ik op in jountyd klear de lokomotyf fan 'e tram de hoeke om gean. It wie in great, swart ding. In skoftsje dêrnei doe is de tram dêr kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21467,"r":"CJ026903","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"In Westereinde many people had seen the train running beforehand. A few had also already heard the whistle.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In soad lju hjir yn 'e Westerein ha fan tofoaren de trein riden sjoen mei ljochtsjes en al. Auke van der Sluis fortelde my, dat er de trein tiden tofoaren yn 'e nacht faek fluitsjen hearde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":46195,"r":"WEV016604","p":"Gieterveen","v":"Dr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A row of lights gliding across the field is voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a railway; dogs and magpies as voorloop of a death.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien voader zag meer; de spoorliene Assen-Stadsknoal beveurbeeld laank veurtied; hai het n riege lichies zain, dei mit n gloepske gang over t veld nei-den.\nHai wos ook te verteln, dat er lu van de weg smeetn wazzen. Zai binnen woor teegn aanloopn of ain het heur oppakt. Is zulfs n keer aine deur verdronken; hai kwam in t woater terechte.\nHoelnde honden en schrouwnde oaksters wurn in Drouwenerveen en ook in Gaiterveen vot jagd. Mensn woln er nait aan herinnerd worn, dat dr gauw n dode in de buurt was. Ik wait nait, wa k dr van leuvn mout, moar honden schienen wat te waitn van dingen dei gebeurn moutn.","l":"Drents"},{"n":22052,"r":"CJ031803","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A woman thinks the world is ending when she sees a 'wagon without a horse, all full of fire'. It turns out she had a premonition of a later invention: the car, with its lights on.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanmem hiet fan Tijke. Dy wie troud mei Albert Land. Sy wennen by 'Driewegen' yn 'e Harkema.\nHar suster Antsje wenne yn 'e Smoarhoeke yn 'e Harkema.\nOp in kear wie Antsjemoai by skoanmem to praten west. 't Wie al op 'e joun en sy soe wer fuort. Mar sy wie noch mar krekt fuort of sy kom werom. Hja fleach der oer en rôp: \"Hearink, de wereld forgiet! In wein sûnder hynder en 't is allegear fjûr!\" Hja hie de lettere betonwei passeard en dêr hie hja fan tofoaren in auto sjoen, dy't der yn dy tiden noch net wienen. Dy hie de ljochten op hawn.\nDoe't se hwat bikom wie soe se wer fuort, mar doe seach se itselde forskynsel opnij. Doe kom se wer werom. Skoanmem hat har thúsbrocht, sa wie 't minske fan 'e wize. Letter doarst se noait wer by nacht de wei del. It wie foartjirmerije fan 'e auto. It fjûr dat wie 't ljocht fan 'e koplampen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22698,"r":"CJ034703","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Will-o'-the-wisps turn out to be a foreshadowing of the later tram lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wennen hjir minsken dy seagen de tram fan Feanwâlden nei Drachten fier fan tofoaren al, foardat er noch ried. Dan wienen der ljochten skean oer de heide. It wienen letter deselde ljochten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22732,"r":"CJ035202","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"In the days when no train ran yet, the sounds of the train could already be heard. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e tiid doe't er noch gjin trein ried fan Ljouwert nei Grins hearden se op it Blaufallaet al it sûzjen fan 'e fjilden oer de rails. Dat wie foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22778,"r":"CJ035411","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Before the tram started running in a certain place, people already saw its lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foardat de tram fan Drachten nei Feanwâlden der wie, seinen de lju fan Sumarreheide dat se de ljochten al sjoen hienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22788,"r":"CJ035601","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A woman heard the tram before it was even running. It was a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha yn Gariperheide wenne. Doe't de tram der noch net wie, hearde ús mem de lûden al. Sy hearde him oer de rails hinnegean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23134,"r":"CJ038305","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Before the tram came to run in a certain place, several people had already heard the sound of the tram there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foardat de tram hjir lâns kom ha guon him al heard. Hindrik de Jong wie de earste, dy't de tram roljen en tûtsjen hearde. Sake Elzinga de twadde. In pear jier letter lei de tram der pas.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23581,"r":"CJ040104","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"The two wilde lantaarnen (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) that people used to see flying over the fields were omens of the later tram.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hja seinen froeger, dêr fleagen twa wylde lantearnen troch de lannen hinne. Dat wie de lettere tram.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23737,"r":"CJ041314","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"The wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) of the past were portents of the later train.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger wienen der wol faek wylde lantearnen, fral oan 'e wei fan Olterterp nei de Himrik. Sy seinen doe, dêr soe noch wolris in trein lâns komme.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23758,"r":"CJ041610","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man heard the train before it was running.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wenne in man yn Lytsepost, dy hearde al fan to foaren, foardat de spoarlyn oanlein wie, de trein fan Bûtenpost.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23810,"r":"CJ042111","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"In the past people saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps). They were portents of the tram.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Minsken seagen froeger wylde lantearnen. Dy kant nei de Sweach en de Gordyk út. Dat wienen de foarboaden west fan 'e tram, woarde der sein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23855,"r":"CJ042505","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man once saw something flying towards the north. It was twelve or thirteen wagons in a row, without a horse, and it made a puffing sound. Later a train came past that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De trein fan Ljouwert nei Grins wie der noch net, doe sei in man: \"Ik ha dêr hwat fleanen sjoen troch 't Noarden. Tolve, trettsjen weinen achter elkoar oan, sûnder hynder en dat gong pof - pof - pof - pof.\"\nLetter kom de trein dêr lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23961,"r":"CJ043302","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man once saw lights at a place where there was nothing, and thought a waterway would come there later. But a motorway came instead. The lights were not from ships, but from cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe sei er een keer tegen ons: \"Der komt in foarwoater, dat is in Marumer Leger. Want ik zag doar lichten.\" Hij dacht dat het lichten van schepen waren, maar 't waren lichten van auto's. Want doar kwam geen voarwoater, zoals hij docht, maar een snelweg.\nDie weg leit der nu acht joar.\nHij zag het voor in voarwoater aan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24182,"r":"CJ044602","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People did see wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) at a place where the tram later ran.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't de tram der noch net wie, hawwe minsken fan 'e Skieding (ûnder Grinzer Pein) wylde lantearnen sjoen. De iene by de oare seach it. It wienen de ljochtsjes fan 'e lettere tram.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25871,"r":"CJ057505","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"In the past people often saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) moving at a certain place. Later a tram came there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foardat de tram hjir lâns ried ha de lju fan tofoaren iderkear wol ljochtsjes riden sjoen. 't Wie foartiermerij. 't Wienen wylde lantearnen dy't almar forweegden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25549,"r":"CJ055301","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People once came to a farmer to say that the train would run where his barn stood. The farmer said that was fine, but that he was not going to open and close the door every time the train passed through.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie yn 'e tiid dat der noch gjin trein ried fan Grins nei Harns. Doe wenne der in boer op in hiele greate boereplaets yn Grinslân yn 'e buert fan Grypskerk.\nDer kommen in pear man, dy moesten mei dy boer prate. De boer kom der oan. \"Hjir bin 'k en hwat wie der?\" sei er.\n\"Wy binne oan 't mjitten,\" seinen de hearen, \"hwant de trein komt der lâns en dy komt hjir midden troch de skuorre hinne. Dat kin net oars.\"\nDe boer sei: \"Ik sil 't tastean, mar jimme matte net tinke, dat ik hyltyd de doarren iepen en ticht doch, as de trein hjir trochhinne rydt.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25627,"r":"CJ055904","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man claimed to have seen wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) at a place where the tram later ran.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Piter Prikke biwearde altyd, dat er, foardat de tram ried, hy de lantearnen wol oankommen sjoen hie. 't Hienen wylde lantearnen west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25707,"r":"CJ056402","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"One evening a man saw a whole row of lights pass by on the horizon. Later a railway line came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Geart Zijlstra wenne oan 'e Fryske dyk ûnder Greategast tusken de Mieden en Strobos. Dy seach op in joun in hiele streek ljochten fleanen by de kym lâns. Hy wist net hwat dat wie. 't Wie allegearre ljocht.\nLetter kom dêr de spoarlyn lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25889,"r":"CJ057601","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"On a certain road a big light always came floating past at ten o'clock at night. Later a tram came to run there. It was a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Elke oavond om tien uur kwam der altyd in groat licht answeven by de Leidyk. Mem sei dan: \"Wat kan dat toch sijn\", want doar was in heel groat gat. Doar kon noait wat overheen rijdn. Dat licht kwam de kant fan Mearum út weg.\nLoater kwam de tram doar langs presys in deselfde tyd 's oavends tien uur. Dat het dat licht toen west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25990,"r":"CJ058207","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man saw lights somewhere, but in reality there was nothing. Five years later a tram came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De tram is hjir kom yn 1911. Mar fiif jier earder seach myn swager de ljochten al. By Likele Pama - tichte by de Wilhelmina-hoeve - wie in wissel. Dêr seach hy de tram doe al rikjen. Hindrik de Jong hiet myn swager.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26065,"r":"CJ058609","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People once heard a terrible noise coming from the woods. They saw the trees bend to the ground in a line about two or three metres wide. Later a railway line came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Bearne-wyk - dêr is ús mem geboaren -, dêr wie 't yndertiid allegearre bosk. Us Sake-omme wie dêr alris mei noch ien. Hy hat it my sels forteld en 't wie gjin man om to ligen. Sy hearden der ynienen in lawaei op 'e Bearnewyk, it wie ôfgryslik. Troch de hiele bosk, njonken har wienen oer in stripe fan twa, trije meter distânsje de beammen oan 'e groun ta bûgd.\nFolle letter hearde ik, dat dêr in spoarlyn komt. Dat gebeurt dus yn 'e takomst. It hat foartjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26066,"r":"CJ058610","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"One night a man could not sleep because there was so much noise and light outside. Later a national highway came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Bearn wenne yn Driemunt. Dy sei us op in moarn: \"Ik ha de hiele nacht net slept.\" Hy sei tsjin ús: \"Hwat wie't dêr allegear in leven en hwat in ljocht allegear. 't Gong de hiele nacht troch.\"\nDat wie op it plak, dêr't nou de rykswei is. Dat hat hy fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26088,"r":"CJ058805","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A woman once saw lots of little lights on the heath. Later a tram came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem seach us yn 'e Bisskop op 'e heide by joun allegear ljochtsjes. Letter kom de tram dêr lâns. Dat hawwe dy ljochtsjes doe west. Dat wie foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26221,"r":"CJ060002","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Behind the bog near the Wyldfjild, an old woman is sitting one day in the house without doors. Then she sees two beams of light coming straight at her and leaves the house. Later her house has to go to make way for the tramline that runs straight through it. She had seen the tram coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jierren lyn is it achter it Fean by 't Wyldfjild gebeurd dat der op in joun in âld-minske op it húske siet. Dy arbeiderswenten hienen froeger gjin doarren foar de húskes en wylst hja dêr siet, kommen der twa hiele greate gleone koppen lyk op har yn.\nHja wie hals oer de kop fan 't húske stoud.\nLetter moest it hûske dêr't sy yn wenne, derôf, hwant de trambaen gong krekt troch it hûs hinne.\nHja hat de tram doe by joun oankommen sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26783,"r":"CJ061102","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"One evening people see spinning lights. They belong to a tram that would come later. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik in jonkje wie, seagen se hjir draeiljochten by joun. Doe wie der noch gjin tram. Letter wienen 't de ljochten fan 'e tram. 't Hat foartsjirmerij west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26890,"r":"CJ061701","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Grandma once hears so much thundering and noise that the house shakes. She predicts that a tram or train will pass by in the future. That happens. It was a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us beppe kom op in nacht om in ûre of ien kjel út bêd wei. \n't Wie allegear gedinder en lûd, 't hûs hie der fan skodde.\nDe oare deis sei se: \"Nou komt hjir in tram of in trein lâns. Ik ha der klear de lûden fan heard.\nLetter is de tram dêr kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26893,"r":"CJ061704","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Jan de Haan has had a few drinks at Durk van Dellen's, and Durk walks him part of the way home. Jan continues alone and is suddenly pushed to the side of the road. A train passes him. Yet no train or tram ever came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jan de Haan en syn suster wienen beide ongetroud. Sy wennen yn Surhústerfean. Op in kear wienen se togearre to jounpraten nei Durk van Dellen, dy wenne ek yn Surhústerfean. Sy moesten in âlde sânreed del om dêr to kommen.\nDoe't it al acht ûre wie, doe wie 't noch hast dei. Doe hie Jan syn suster sein: \"Ik gean nei hûs ta, ik fiel my net sa lekker.\" Jan fortelde: \"Ik bleau dêr allinnich. Doe rekke ik oan 'e buorrel by Durk van Dellen.\nDe nachts om ien ûre sei 'k: 'Ik mat fuort'.\nDurk brocht my in ein op stap. Ik sei tsjin him: 'Dû mast mar net to fier mei, 't is hjir allegear djippe wettergatten oan wjerskanten'. Hy wie nochal hwat âlder as ik. Dat hy gong werom. Doe't ik sa'n twahondert meter allinne roan hie, woarde ik samar ynienen oan kant set fan 'e wei. Ik woarde der gewoan hinne set. En ik hearde in trein, dy brulde der oer. Dy stoude my foarby. Ik mat op 'e rails roan ha.\nMar der is letter noait in tram of in trein kom.\nKinne it ek de trekkers west ha?\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26931,"r":"CJ061907","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Fifty or sixty years ago, people from Kompenije and on the Folgerster laan saw lights beforehand and heard railway sounds. Later the tram came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sa'n fyftich à sechstich jier lyn seagen guon út 'e Kompenije fan tofoaren de ljochten en sy hearden de lûden fan 't spoar, dat dêr lâns komme soe. Ek oan 'e Folgerster loane ha guon it wol heard en sjoen. ('t Wie de tram)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27051,"r":"CJ063301","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Near Ingwierum someone hears the sound of a steamboat, which only comes later. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik sa'n jonge wie fan tolve jier gebeurde it dat se yn 'e buert fan Ingwierrum in lûd yn 'e loft hearden. Dat wie krekt it lûd as fan in stoomboat. Letter kommen de stoomboaten pas.\nDat lûd dat se doe heard ha, dat hat in 'foar gespeustel' west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27166,"r":"CJ063906","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"The wife of Piter Veenstra once saw in advance a tram that went through everything. It later came as well.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In âld minske, de frou fan Piter Veenstra, hat yndertiid de tram fan tofoaren sjoen. Se seach dat de tram troch de bosken en alles hinne gong. Dat is letter ek sa gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27195,"r":"CJ064101","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Father saw the tram on the Sumarreheide in advance. He sees the tram lights, and only a year later do they hear about a Belgian company that will build the tramline. Then the tram really comes.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit hat fantofoaren de tram op 'e Sumarreheide sjoen.\n\"Sjoch us,\" sei er, \"sokke gleone ljochten rinne dêr.\" Doe wie der fan in tram noch gjin sprake.\nIn jier letter hearden se earst oer in Belgyske maetskippij praten, dy't de tram oanlizze soe.\nLetter kom de tram der; doe seagen se deselde gleone ljochten by joun.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27213,"r":"CJ064201","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Jan van der Heide and Gjetsje van Eldring live in Drachtster Kompenije and before 1912 see lots of little lights on the Folgersterlaan. They think a waterway will come there and the lights are ships at night. But it is the tram, which comes in 1912.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jan van der Heide en Gjetsje van Eldring wienen heit syn âlden. Sy wennen to Drachtster Kompenije. Dy ha sjoen dat der de Folgerster loane allegear ljochtsjes del gongen.\nDat wie fóár 1912. Sy tochten: dêr komt in farwetter in dy ljochtsjes, dat binne de skippen by jountiid.\nMar yn 1912 is de tramlijn dêr kom. \"Dat hat it west\", seinen se doe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27326,"r":"CJ064910","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man once saw a whole row of little lights approaching. Later a tram came there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Olle Jelle fan 'e Bosweg zag voor lange tijd in hele rige lichtsjes aankoomn. 't Was bij oavend. Loater is doar de tram gekomen.\nHy het dat fan te foren sien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27344,"r":"CJ065101","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At the place where people used to see lights going past, a tram later came to run.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jierren foardat de tram kom seagen de minsken yn Grinzer Pein ljochten troch de lange Bosk gean. Sy wisten doe net hwat dat wie, mar doe't letter de tram kom, wisten se dat it foartjirmerij west hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27483,"r":"CJ066104","p":"Frieschepalen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man regularly saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) passing by. Later the tram came to run there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In omke fan myn mans kant wie skeper op Driemunt. Dêr wie 't doe yndertiid allegear noch heide.\nOp in kear sei er tsjin my: \"Ik ha justerjoun in wylde lantearne sjoen. Hy kom fan Mearum en gong de kant út nei Drachten.\"\nHy hat it letter noch faker sjoen. \"Der komt hwat to rinnen fan Mearum op Drachten yn\", sei er.\nIk sei: \"Merakels allegear.\"\nMar letter kom de tram nei Drachten dêr lâns.\n\"Sjochst wol?\" sei er.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27489,"r":"CJ066401","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man once saw lots of wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps). Later a tramline came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn omke Harm wie skieppehoeder. Dy hat yn 't fjild by Grinzer Pein wylde lantearnen sjoen. 't Wienen allegear ljochtsjes.\nMar in lyts skoftsje dêrnei, yn 1912 woarde der in nije tramlijn oanlein fan Grins nei Drachten. Dat wienen de ljochtsjes dy't hy sjoen hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27552,"r":"CJ066904","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Even before the railway was there, people heard the puffing of the train.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem kom fan Hurdegaryp. Mem fortelde, sy hienen dêr dúdlik it puffen fan 'e trein al heard, fier fantofoaren foardat hy der wie. Krekt deselde lûden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27684,"r":"CJ068303","p":"Noordwijk","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At a place where the tram later came, people had already seen little lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Fan 'e tram, dy't fan Drachten nei Burgum ried, seagen se yn Sumar fan tofoaren de ljochtsjes. In hiele rige achterelkoar, krekt op it plak, dêr't letter de trambaen wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27839,"r":"CJ069601","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People heard the sound of a tram at a certain spot. Later a tram really did come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In Opende is 't gebeurd dat mensen in de lucht een geluut als van een tram hoorden. Maar die was der toen nog niet. Korte tijd daarna kwàm die tram er.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28019,"r":"CJ071201","p":"Kornhorn","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People saw tram lights at a spot where there was nothing. Later a tram really did come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Te Mearum zagen ze van tevoren de lichtjes van de tram. Later waren ze er echt."},{"n":28036,"r":"CJ071301","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At a spot where people used to see all sorts of lights, a tram later came to run.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't der noch gjin tram ried oer de Folgerster loane ha forskeidene lju hjir fan tofoaren dêr allegearre ljochtsjes sjoen. Dat wienen de ljochtsjes fan 'e tram by joun, doe't dy der letter wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28051,"r":"CJ071403","p":"Kornhorn","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"For a long time people saw all sorts of lights. Later a goods train came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Toen ik jong was, sagen se allemoal lichten. Doar is de goederentrein loater komen. Ik heb die lichten self wel sien. Ik was drie en twintig joar, doe kwam die trein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28219,"r":"CJ072901","p":"Kornhorn","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People saw the lights of the tram beforehand. People had also seen wagons without horses.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der woaren mensen hier die hebben van tevoren de lichten gezien van de tram die van Groningen noar Drachten reed. Der woaren ook mensen, die soagen woagens riden zonder peerden. Loater kwam de tram bij Noordwyk langs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28253,"r":"CJ073111","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man could not sleep at night in his caravan because of the noise and all the lights he heard and saw. Later the national highway came. Several people had also seen the tram running beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Bearn van der Woude sei op in kear yn 't foarige: \"Ik koe fannacht net sliepe. (Hy wenne doe op Driemunt). Der komt fêst hwat. 't Wienen allegear ljochten en in leven dat der wie - der komt fêst hwat.\"\nNou is de greate Rykswei 43 der troch. Flak njonken it plak, dêr't hy mei syn woanwein stie.\nDer binne ek forskeidene dy't de tram fan tofoaren riden sjoen ha.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28353,"r":"CJ074111","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People heard a train going over the rails at a spot, but in reality there was nothing. Later a train really did come to run there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sa wie 't ek mei de trein fan Ljouwert nei Swolle. Sy hearden de trein oer de rails gliden. It kom altyd fan 'e kant fan Ljouwert út wei. Letter is de trein der kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28431,"r":"CJ074703","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Even before there was a railway line, people had heard a train running there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foardat it spoar hjir wie, ha de minsken it al riden heard, krekt like dúdlik as doe't it der letter wie, sei myn âlde omke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28668,"r":"CJ077506","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Father once saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns) that looked like a train and also heard the whistle. That was at the Readskuorre near Drogeham. He claims the train will come there later, but so far no train has come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit hat froeger wylde lantearnen sjoen krekt as in trein. Dat gong by Readskuorre lâns troch Droegeham op Koatstertille yn. Heit biwearde, hy hie de trein rinnen sjoen. Hy hat de trein ek fluitsjen heard.\n\"It duorret mar even,\" sei heit, \"dan komt dy trein hjir.\"\nMar heit is nou al twa en fyftich jier dea, en der is noch altyd gjin trein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28738,"r":"CJ078403","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Father is on his way from Harkema to Drachtster Compagnie and sees little lights on the Folgersterlaan in the evening. Later a tram comes at the same spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit roan ris in kear fan 'e Harkema nei Drachtster Kompenije. 't Wie op in joun. Hy kom de Folgerster loane del. Doe kommen dêr allegear ljochtsjes oan. Heit woarde kjel. Hy tocht: hwat wy nou bileve sille, wyt ik net. Mar even letter wienen dy ljochtsjes ek wer fuort.\nHeit fortelde 't oan oaren hwat er sjoen hie. In skoftsje letter kom dêr de tram lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28869,"r":"CJ079508","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"De Vries from Groninger Opeinde sees a row of little lights before the tram from Drachten to Groningen exists. He foresaw the tram in an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In sekere de Vries út Grinzer Pein seach in hiele rigele ljochtsjes yn 'e tiid krekt foardat de tram fan Drachten nei Grins ta der kom. Dêr hat dat foartjirmerij fan west, woed er biweare.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32806,"r":"CJ083802","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man hears a rumbling in the sky just before the train comes.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit fortelde, hja hearden froeger gebolder yn 'e loft, krekt foardat de trein kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33662,"r":"CJ092501","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At a place where a tram came to run, people had already seen the tram beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De tram dy't fan Drachten nei Mearum rydt, is fan to foaren sjoen woarn troch in bulte minsken dy't oan 'e Skieding, op 'e Skâns en Sakebuorren wennen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29474,"r":"CJ081715","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"On the heath people used to often see wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns). They were the harbingers of the later tram.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Sumarreheide seagen se froeger wylde lantearnen.\nBeppe hat se faek sjoen. Dat wienen de foarboaden fan 'e tram, dy't dêr letter lâns ried.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32663,"r":"CJ082304","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People hear the train from Leeuwarden to Groningen running before it even exists. It is a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon hearden de trein fan Ljouwert nei Grins fier fan to foaren al, foardat der noch sprake wie fan in trein, al to Sânbulten riden. Dat wie foartjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":128388,"r":"ENGELB_02_001","p":"Rossum","v":"Ov.","y":1970,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Seeing the lights of a train before there is a railway track.","i":"H.E.","o":"Mien grootmore was vrowe baakster en dee gung van hoes oet, van Wolcheman oet nao 't Straokal hen; doa was wat jôngs of doa zol wat jôngs kom'm en doe is ze ôp 'n Zek 'n mösdiek bie Buuks-Jenske, doe zäög ze ineans 'n trein loop'n owwe 'n Aotmöskediek hen en doe ze doa kotbie was, doe zäög ze an de laamp'n at 'n trein läöp en ok laamp'n braan'n vuur den trein en dat was dan zaogenaamd nen keal met iezer'n aong, want zie wus'n in dee tied van trein'n en kiepkaor'n niks of. Zie is doa hengaon en ennige joar'n later, doe bint de straot'n in Rossum anlegd en doe ze die doa anlen'n, doe hebt ze de stèèn'n bracht, die ze van 't knaal brach'n, woa nô Bèèntjes-Bennad zien hoes stèèt en doa hebt ze die toosmet'n en doe bint die straot'n anlegd en dat was ennige joar'n verlen'n en doe läöp de Punt oet Aotmöske, Diekhoes genaamd, dee hef de kipkeurkes doa langs 'n diek vuurd met dat ding der vuur en die har zee zein loop'n en doa zat'n meschien wa tweintig, viemtweintig van die kiepkaor'n achter, mè het kwam inderdaod oet, dat was met ennige joar'n, want zie zeg nog teng mien vare: ik belew 't nich, mè doe belews 't nog wa, Jans, met ennige joar'n zas doe 'n trein langs 'n Aotmöskediek zein loop'n, terwijl 'n hei en 'n pos nog an 'n diek wös, mè ik heb zölm as klène jông an 'n Aotmöskediek help'n wèèrk'n, de stèèn'n vôtwèèrk'n bie Bèèntjes-Bennad zien hoes en zie zint aolmaol owwe 'n Aotm","l":"Twents"},{"n":32792,"r":"CJ083701","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Certain little lights turn out to be a portent of the tram that will later run at that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Eren hellen wy de turf achter Trimunt wei. Dêr wennen minsken, dy seagen ljochtsjes oer de heide. Letter, yn 1913 kaem de trambaen dêr lâns. Doe seinen se: \"Sjoch, dat binne de ljochtsjes, dy't wy al lang sjoen ha.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32821,"r":"CJ084103","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man hears the sounds of cars and aeroplanes before those means of transport even exist. The same man also sees the lights of the tram before it runs.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Edze-om wie mem har jongste broer, dy is yn Limburch forstoarn. Dy hearde fan tofoaren al de lûden fan 'e auto's en de fleanmesines. Ek seach er ljochtsjes fan 'e tram. Dat is allegear neikom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32920,"r":"CJ084808","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man had seen the tram running across the heath before the tram was really there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Jelle Polderdyk hat yn Grinzer Pein wenne. Dêr is er ek stoarn, yn 't werkhûs. Dy Jelle fortelde heit dat er froeger de tram sjoen hie, dy ried oer de Mearumer heide. Dat wie noch fier foar de tiid dat de tram der echt wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33140,"r":"CJ087315","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Someone once saw a lot of wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps). Later a railway line came at that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Linse de Haan syn heit seach op it plak, dêr't letter de spoarlijn kom allerhande wylde lantearnen. Dat hat de foarboade west fan 'e trein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33251,"r":"CJ088202","p":"Schagerbrug","v":"N.-H.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man used to see wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) on the heath. Later the tramline came there. They were omens of the lit carriages.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit seach froeger wylde lantearnen oer de heide, op in rige. Letter wie dêr de trambaen. De ljochtsjes, dat wienen de forljochte coupé's.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33535,"r":"CJ091001","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People sometimes saw little lights at a certain spot. Later a tram came to run there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie noch gjin 25 jier doe kom ik to wenjen op 'e Skieding tusken Oerterp en Grinzerpein. Doe wienen dêr minsken dy seagen dêr ljochtsjes, sa nou en dan.\n\"Hjir komt hwat,\" seinen se, \"dat kin net útbliuwe.\" En it bleau ek net út.\nDe tram kom dêr lâns. 't Wie tjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33624,"r":"CJ091802","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"One night a man saw a great light pass by; he did not know what it was. Later cars came to drive there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Auke Siebenga fan Nyegeaster Pein hie nei Aldegea nei de faem ta west. Hy wie op 'e weromreis en roan de Aldegeaster dyk del. Hy wie noch net oan 't brechje ta. Der stienen trije rigen swiere ikebeammen oan wearskanten fan 'e wei. Doe kom der in ljocht oan, de kant fan Nyegea út wei. Auke sprong oan kant, hwant hy tocht: dat kin wolris in auto wêze. Hy hie noch noait in auto sjoen, mar der wol oer praten heard. Op it paedtsje tusken de beammen bleau er stean. It ljocht woarde al mar greater mei't it tichterby kom. Alles om him hinne woarde forljochte. Mar it wie allinne mar in ljocht, der siet neat achter oan.\nHwat kin soks nou west ha?\nLetter kommen dêr fansels de auto's lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34515,"r":"CJ091903","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) were the omens of the later bicycles and cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen woarden hjir yn 'e Harkema faek sjoen. Dat wienen de foarboaden fan 'e lettere fytsen en auto's, wurdt der gauris sein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34558,"r":"CJ093203","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People used to see wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps). Those were the omens of the later bicycles and cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem sei froeger: \"Sjoch, dêr binne wer wylde lantearnen.\" It wienen doe allegear noch modderpaden. Nou binne dy forhurde en dêr ride de auto's en de fytsen oer. De ljochten dêr fan, dat ha de froegere wylde lantearnen west, dy't klear to sjen wienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34559,"r":"CJ093204","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People once heard at a certain spot the sound of a train running on a track. But there was nothing to be seen. Later a train really came to run there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen yndertiid oan 'e Koopmanswei. Fan in trein wie doe noch gjin sprake. Mar doe hearden se op in kear klear de lûden, krekt as ried der in trein oer rails hinne. Doe binne se allegearre dêrhinne gong dêr't dat lûd weikom. Mar der wie neat. Letter ried dêr de trein lâns, krekt op itselde plak dêr't se 't lûd weikommen heard hiene.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34560,"r":"CJ093205","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People once heard a noise in the sky, but there was nothing to be seen. When they later heard that noise again, they saw an aeroplane.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mem en dy hawwe ek ris heard dat it sa bot rûsde yn 'e loft. Hja der út nei bûten ta. Mar der wie neat. Folle letter hearden se datselde rûzjen wer. Mar doe dienen de fliechmesines it. Doe't hja it de earste kear heard hienen wie dêr noch gjin sprake fan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33768,"r":"CJ094101","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People used to see wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) on the heath. Later a motorway came.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sa'n fjirtich jier lyn seagen wy wylde lantearnen op 'e Hege Wei. Dat wie doe in sânpaed, dêr kom omtrint neat lâns. Nou stiet it der noait stil, sûnt de wei forhurde en forbrede \nis.\nElk ogenblik snuorje der auto's lâns. De lettere autoljochten dêr, wolle se wol ha woarden troch dy wylde lantearnen oantsjut.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33848,"r":"CJ094701","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People sometimes heard the sound of iron on iron at a certain spot. Later a tram came to run there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit wenne froeger oan 'e Hearrewei ûnder Sumar.\nFaek hat er forteld dat se soms achter hûs lûden hearden; it wie krekt dat der izer oer izer hinne glied.\nAl gau dêrnei is de tram dêr kom. Dat ha de lûden doe west fan 'e tram dy't oer de rails glied.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":35910,"r":"CJ094901","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Little lights used to be seen on the heath: a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of cars on the national highway.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't wy noch op 'e Gariperheide wennen seagen wy dêr soms ljochtsjes op it plak dêr't nou de nije rykswei is. Guon wolle ha dat dat de ljochtsjes west ha fan 'e auto's dy't dêr nou lâns ride.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36026,"r":"CJ095902","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Old Tamme Hooijenga told that he was once near the old tramway, when no tram ran yet, and heard a whistle. That was the whistle of the steam tram built later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Tamme Hooijenga dat wie de heit fan Jelle Hooijenga. Dy wenne op Sumarreheide. Dy fortelde dat hy wie ris tichte by de âld tramwei west - mar der wie doe noch gjin tram - doe hearde hy klear in fluitsje. Dat wie it fluitsjen fan 'e lettere stoomtram.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":128412,"r":"ENGELB_04_001","p":"Rossum","v":"Ov.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"The narrator sees a row of little lights in front of him, which later vanish. The woman and the chaplain he tells say that a paved road will come later.","i":"H.E.","o":"Hamse: Ik weet nich, of ik dat zao verteln kan, mer prebearn dan. Ja dat is west in 1914, doe was d'r ne landbouwcursus hier in Rossum en dee cursus doerde - meester Helt gaf dee - en dee cursus doerde tot half tien.\nEngelbertink: Gaf meester Plegt dee dan nich?\nH: Meester Plegt deer dat ok wa, één aomd deer meester Plegt dat en twee aomn meester Helthoes, jao en dee cursus doerde dan tot half tien en de straot dee gung nog nich ôp Lemsel an.\nE: Dat was nog nen zaandweg.\nH: Jao, van Benneker oet lööp gennen pad langs 'n zaandweg, d'r lööp zon welkn tuske en doar lööp zon fietsnpedke, doar fietsn ik owwer, kwam ik an 'n Aotmöskediek en doar ineens gung d'r zao ne rie lechkes gungn d'r vuur mie hen richting ôp Aotmöske an en ik bleef stilstaon en ik was ok nich a'k bang was, ok nich, ik daenk effn wochn, 't was net of d'r ne trein veur mie henlööp en doe ok zao ineens is 't weg, doe ben ik wier Iop fiets gaon en fietsn ik naor hoes naor Derkman hen; ik kwam bie Derkman in hoes, de vrouw van Derkman, de vaar bie Derkman was a lang daod, dee vrouw dee zat in hoes, wochn zao lang, a'k in hoes kwam en doe vertöl ik dat en doe zeg dee vrouw:“Oh, dan koomp doar ne straot hen” en dat net zao.\nE: Doe later is dat ne straot wörn he?\nH: Nô is d'r ne straot, ja ik heb wa mear zukke speukerij had en zuk ding, doe vertöl ik dat ok an ne keplaon hier in 't gebouw, \"ja\", zeg he, \"die dingen bes","l":"Twents"},{"n":128414,"r":"ENGELB_04_003","p":"Rossum","v":"Ov.","y":1972,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"The narrator's parents foresee the coming of a tram line.","i":"H.E.","o":"Mien vare, den is dat vrower passeard, den is doe wier kömn oet de stad en ja, dat is n`io a zaowat 80 joar lenn, ik wet nich wannear precies den tram hier maakt is van Daenekaamp naor Rossum of owwer Rossum op stad an, mer mier vare den kwam doe 's aoms wier oet de stad - he har bosschôpn daon, he was doe hier ôp 't melkfabriek, machinist ôp 't melkfabriek, he kwam doar, woar ôngevear Hoemboer wount en doe zöt he doar ineens 'n paar lechkes, doe was dat aolmaol vaeld, doe was dat aolmaol woestenij, dat daenkt mie nog at 't aolmaol hei was en doe zöt he 'n paar lechkes en daenkt ok bie zichzölf, wat kan doar nô nog wenn, strööpers in 't vaeld har he dacht, jao en he geet naor hoes hen en vertaelt dat tengn mien more, more har doe voart zegd, zie zeit, at doar wat langs koump, d'r koump meschien nog ne straot langs en doe later is 't 'n tram wörn.\nE: 'n Tram is nô ok a wier vôt.\nH: 'n Tram is nô ok a wier vôt, mer dat was doe heel wat biezunders.","l":"Twents"},{"n":36221,"r":"CJ097405","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Polecat hunters often used to see lanterns at places where a road would later come. Piter Kloosterman could see the tram in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Murdejagers seagen froeger faek wylde lantearnen. Letter kom der op sokke plakken dan in wei.\nAlde Piter Kloosterman hie op 'e Sumarreheide de tram fantofoaren al sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36571,"r":"CJ098914","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People sometimes used to see lanterns, which they later said belonged to the future bicycles. Some people also saw the train before it was there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir waerden froeger gauris wylde lantearnen sjoen. Dat doelde op 'e lettere fytsen, seinen se letter.\nForskate lju ha hjir de trein fan tofoaren sjoen, foardat dy der noch wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36950,"r":"CJ101401","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Mother had once seen two lights across the heath between two places. Later the tram ran there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wennen by de Skieding ûnder Drachtster Kompenije.\nMem fortelde op in moarn. Nou haw ik justerjoun twa ljochtsjes oer de heide kommen sjoen, dy gongen fan Mearum nei Trimunt ta. Dat wie noch foardat de tram dêr lâns ried.\nLetter is dy dêr kaem. It wie foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36966,"r":"CJ101504","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People saw little lights floating over the field and carriages driving. Those were the portents of the tram that began running there in 1912.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Houtigehage seagen se oer 't Wyldfjild alle jounen in lantearne sweven.\nYn 1912 is de tram hjir kaem. Foar dy tiid seagen de minsken elke joun rydtugen riden. Dat wienen de foarboaden fan 'e tram. It is neikaem. Se neamden dy ljochtsjes wol wylde lantearnen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37163,"r":"CJ102901","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A boy once came running hard: did you see that wagon without horses? It was a portent of the trains.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Mem fortelde, dat har mem dy wenne to Feanwâldsterwâl.\nDêr wenne in jonge, fortelde beppe, dy kaem op in kear hurd ta 't hûs útrinnen, en dy rôp: Sjogge jimme 't net? Sjogge jimme 't net? Dêr komt in wein oanriden sûnder hynder.\" Dat wie it lettere spoar.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37211,"r":"CJ103201","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Some had heard the sounds of the train beforehand; some had also seen the lights beforehand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanmem kaem fan Feanwâldsterwâl. Hja hat faek forteld dat de minsken dêr de lûden fan 'e trein heard hienen foardat der noch sprake fan wie dat der in trein komme soe.\nEk guon hienen de ljochten fan 'e trein fantofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37365,"r":"CJ104034","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Before the train was there, people had already heard it puffing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e sechstiger jierren fan 'e foarige ieu, fortelde beppe ha de minsken yn Sweagerbosk de trein al puffen heard.\nDoe wie der noch fan gjin trein sprake.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37446,"r":"CJ104408","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1973,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Between Dokkum and Anjum people saw wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) as portents of the train.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Achter Dokkum wennen lju dy hienen in foargefoel fan 'e trein dy't der letter kaem is. De trein ried fan Dokkum nei Anjum. Dy minsken seagen dan wylde lantearnen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38172,"r":"CJ108201","p":"Feanwâldsterwâl","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Shortly before a railway line is built, the sound of a passing train is heard.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn mem kom fan Wâlterswâld. Yn 'e tiid doe't sy jong wie ried der noch gjin trein. Mar krekt fan tofoaren, doe't der sprake fan wie dat se 't spoar oanlizze soenen, hearden se, as se yn 'e hûs sieten, it lûd fan 'e ridende trein.\nDat wie foargedrûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38410,"r":"CJ109224","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Before any train runs, people hear the sound of trains.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebolder fan 'e trein ha se hjir fier fan tofoaren heard doe't der noch gjin trein wie.\nDoe't hy der letter wie, seinen se: \"Dat wie 't hwat wy doe heard ha.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38436,"r":"CJ109320","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People see a train running beforehand; they see the lights approaching and rushing past.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Feanwâldsterwâl wennen ek guon, dy ha by nacht de trein fan tofoaren riden sjoen. Se seagen de ljochten, dy't der oankamen en hurd foarbystouden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38584,"r":"CJ109839","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Some people saw the lights of the tram before the tram began to run.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't de tram noch net troch Feanwâlden ried wienen hjir al guon dy't de ljochten fan 'e tram sjoen ha.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29577,"r":"CJ110608","p":"Rottevalle","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Two old people hear a chugging sound and see lights. It is a portent: later the tram would run at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"'t Wie yn 'e tiid dat de tramlijn fan Grins nei Drachten noch net bistie. Twa âlde minsken fan Drachtster Kompenije hienen to jounpraten west nei Houtigehage. Doe't se by Luchtenveld kamen moesten se in âld reed yn. Doe hearden se dêr ynienen: Tuf-tuf-tuf-tuf. En hja seagen twa ljochten, dy kamen de hoeke om.\n't Wie op in hûndert meter fan har ôf. Doe wie 't ynienen fuort.\nGjin jier letter binne se mei de tramlijn bigoun.\n't Wie foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29634,"r":"CJ110909","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At a certain place people hear the sound of the train on the rails before the train even runs. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Sânbulten hearden de minsken al fier fan tofoaren de trein oer de rails hinne gliden, doe't der noch gjin sprake fan in trein wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29737,"r":"CJ111410","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Every evening a big light shines into a man's house. It is a portent: later the man has to leave his house because the train is going to run at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn omke wenne op 'e Oastersingel yn 'e Westerein. Alle jounen kaem der in great ljocht op him ta en dat gong dwars by him troch 't hûs hinne.\nIn skoft letter moest it hûs der ôf, doe kaem de trein dêr en dy kaem krekt to riden oer de froegere founeminten fan it hûs.\nDat hie dus dat greate ljocht west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":128457,"r":"ENGELB_08A_005","p":"Mander","v":"Ov.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Little lights are an omen of the coming of a railway.\nA quack claims that if the doctor dies, the narrator's grandfather will die too.\nProtection against witches.","i":"H.E.","o":"....... Mien grootvader, den was nog a völ kwakzalver, nich, den har dat book wiln owwernemn, den hef der 's nachts oet west ok wa, at der wat vuurvöl neumn ze dat vrower \"loopn\". At der hier of doar nog 'n lechke braanden, dan hadn ze a nen trein zejn loopn, nich. Hier was vrower bie de Wigger, doar was den groot met, dat was den Maanderschen dokter, doar was der een an 't kwakzalvern en den kwam oet Duutslaand, den was klook en den is ok nog gezeld en braandmearkt, zer mien moder aajt, doe he dat vertöl, hier van 'n Maanderschen dokter, dat we'j toch wa?\nIk: Ja den ken ik wa, ik wet 'm wa te wônn.\nB: at den Maanderschen dokter doad zôl goan, nich, dan zôl mien grootvader hengoan, nich, doar lachn ze dan mangs um, he was der hengoan, verschiedenn hadn nich doan, mer he har niks vernömn, niks doan.\n...... Doar hadn ze wa wat vuur de heksn, nich, dee hebt ze vrower wa had, nich, zee môsn wat in 'n tuk hebn had, dee heksn.\nIk: Dan môsn ze wat metnemn in 'n tuk en dan wördn ze nich bedreigd duur de heksen .....","l":"Twents"},{"n":131059,"r":"VODA_032_04","p":"Ommen","v":"Ov.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"On a building site people saw a great many farm carts racing along one after another, a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a train. There were plans for a railway line there, but it was not built at the time.\nThe narrator seems to want to show with this story how superstitious people used to be.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"En doa bunt wel ens meer van die dingen ’weast, det ik mich ’n beetje over verwonderd, vroeger toen ik jonk was, en dan zaten wie ’s oabens beej mekare, beej de kachel, en dan hed ik oabens beej ‘weast det ik ’s oabens niet meer noar ’n buut’n dors, zo bange waar ik, wat die olde minse vertelden.\n’t Was ook op ’n keer, vertelden ze ook [auto rijdt voorbij] en doar is nog nooit geen spore komt trouwens, maar toe heb’ ze ook ’n spoortrein, was ’n eh… ’n eh… grote bouwvlakte, en doar heb’ ze ’n hele koppel, ze’en ze, heleboel boerenwagens achter mekaar aan die steuven doar langs. Doar bun wel plannen ‘eweas, hebben die luie loat’n liggen, maar hij is ‘r nie gekom’n, die is naderhèr gekom’n.\nJa, zo kan je zie [baby op de achtergrond] hoe v… biegeleuvig dat vroeger ook de mensen waren. ‘n Ien had dit en ’n ander had dat.","l":"Sallands"},{"n":131147,"r":"VODA_032_09","p":"Ommen","v":"Ov.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"The shepherd of Beerze (a hamlet in the municipality of Ommen) had to move his sheep out of the way of a huge contraption that gave off smoke. A few years later a railway line came at that spot. The man had seen a voorspooksel or voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the train.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Weej ha’n straks al over die spoorlijn, doar hèf Ben van der Vecht van verteld, maar de Beerze scheper dean hadden wel joaren veurdet de lijn om Mijnbergen lag, kwaamp dean in huus en vertelde det-e zien schoapen veur ’n heel groot gevoarte woar ’t rook uut kwaam weg’halen had en det was van omnomijnbarige [?] reden. En enkele joaren later lag doar de lijn. De’s de ierste.","l":"Sallands"},{"n":31106,"r":"CJ115501","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At a certain place the tram is heard before it even runs. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn 'e Houtigehage ha forskeidene west, dy't froeger de tram fan 'e Folgersterloane heard ha, fier foardat dy der noch wie. Dat wie foartsjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31250,"r":"CJ116201","p":"Nietap","v":"Dr.","y":1977,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At a certain place people hear the train before it even runs. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Voordat de trein tussen Leeuwarden en Groningen er was hebben ze op Westerzand (bij Gaarkeuken) hem al horen rijden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31316,"r":"CJ116604","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A few people see the tram before it even runs. It is a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It barnende lân is fan it Sumarre tramstasjon oant Sumarreheide. Jouns 10 ûre ried dêr in ding lâns mei twa gleone eagen. Dat wie de foarboade fan de lettere tram. In soad lju ha him fantofoaren sjoen. Hy ried by de beamwâl lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31318,"r":"CJ116606","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"The portents of the tram are called wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns).","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De foarboaden fan 'e tram neamden se yn 'e Sumarreheide ek wol wylde lantearnen. Dy gongen by de wâl lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31418,"r":"CJ117511","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A woman claims to have heard the tram before it even ran.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Skoanmem hat faek sein dat se de tram fan Drachten fier fan tofoaren al heard hie en in bulte oare minsken ek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31480,"r":"CJ117901","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man sees the tram go by before it even runs. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit wie noch net troud, hy hie al forkearing mei mem. Op in joun wie er nei har ta, doe ried sa mar ynienen de tram by harren lâns, hoewol dêr hielendal gjin tram wie. Twa jier letter kaem de tram der lâns; hja hienen dat dus fan tofoaren al sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31503,"r":"CJ118008","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At a certain place wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns) can often be seen. It is a portent of the tram.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men seach faek wylde lantearnen oer Sumarreheide.\nLetter kaem de tram; doe wisten se hwat it bitsjut hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31572,"r":"CJ118601","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At a certain place a terrible noise can always be heard at ten o'clock in the evening. It is a portent: later the tram runs there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't de tram der noch net wie kaem Hedzer-om op in joun om in ûre of tsien fan Wergea werom op 'e Sumarreheide. \"Hark,\" sei er, \"hwat is dat?\" It wie in gerattel en gebolder fan jewelste. En dêr wie neat to sjen.\n\"Dat ha wy wol honderten kearen heard,\" sei heit, \"altyd om tsien ûre hinne.\" Letter ried de 10-ûre tram dêr oer de heide.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31573,"r":"CJ118602","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At a certain place a lot of noise is heard and steam is seen. It is a portent: later there is a station of the steam tram at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It Barnde Lân is it plak to Sumar dêr't letter it tramsjasjon kaem is. Alde pake Tamme kaem dêr faek lâns. Dêr wie dan in stik leven, sei er, noait liker as dat men dêr stoom fleane liet. Letter waerd dêr it stasjon boud en kaem de stoomtram dêr.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31583,"r":"CJ118612","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At a certain place a kind of pigsty with two lights is seen. It is a voorgezicht (a vision of the future): later the tram runs at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't de tram foar 't earst oer de Sumarreheide ried, tochten se dat it in bargehok wie mei twa gleone ljochten der oan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31624,"r":"CJ119107","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A group of people saw the tram before it even ran.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek in bult minsken út dizze streek ha de tram al lang fan tofoaren riden sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31641,"r":"CJ119217","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At a certain place a kind of pigsty with two lights can be seen in the evening. Strange sounds are also heard. It is a portent: later the tram runs at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Sumarreheide hearden se, foar dat de tram dêr kaem, de lûden al dy't er makke. En sy seagen jouns hwat foarbytuffen dat der útseach as in bargehok, fjouwerkant mei twa gleone ljochten der foar. Dat wie de lettere tram.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31802,"r":"CJ119714","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A group of people see the light of the tram on the heath and also hear the tram running, although the tram is not actually running yet. It is a portent.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In soad minsken fan 'e heide ha fan tofoaren de ljochten fan 'e tram sjoen en ek de lûden heard, doe't hy der noch net wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31939,"r":"CJ120901","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man sees a wilde lantaarn (wild lantern) floating. It is a portent: later the tram runs at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Bearn v.d. Woude wenne yn 'e Parken. Hy fortelde, dat hy seach dêr in ljocht, dat biweegde fan Oast nei West. 't Wie op in joun. Syn frou wie syklik, dy lei op bêd, dy rôp hy der ek by, doe seach dy it ek. 't Wie in wylde lantearne. Letter kaem de tram dêr lâns, dêr wie 't de foarboade fan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31960,"r":"CJ121001","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A boy sometimes sees a wilde lantaarn (wild lantern) floating at a certain place. It is a portent of, for example, the tram.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't wy op Gariperheide wennen, seagen wy wolris in wylde lantearne. As jonge wie ik dêr bang foar hwant it praet fan 'e greate minsken gong dêr gauris oer. It tsjutte op dingen dy't komme soenen, lyk as de tram en sa.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31984,"r":"CJ121103","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"One night a man sees a long wagon with lights. It is a portent: later the tram runs at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn swager wenne yn 'e Grinzer Pein. Op in nacht kaem er hwat let thús. Doe seach er dêr yn 'e Pein in lange wein mei ljochten. Hy wist net hwat it wie.\nLetter kaem de tram dêr. \"Dat is nou datselde hwat ik dy nachts sjoen ha\", sei er. Dat wie likernoch 1 jier nei tiid.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32015,"r":"CJ121506","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People saw and heard the tram before it even ran: an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Noch foardat de tram fan Grins nei Drachten der wie, ha gâns minsken by joun de ljochten al sjoen en guon hearden him ek wol oankommen yn de Pein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32061,"r":"CJ121905","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"A man hears a rattling sound and sees two glowing eyes. It is a portent: later the tram runs at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn pake wenne oan 'e Ielke Boonstrawei, yn in spitkeet.\nOp in kear sei er: \"Hjir gebeurt hwat.\" Hy hearde hwat hiel fluch foarby ratteljen. \"'t Giet hurd,\" sei er, \"en 't hie twa gleone egen.\"\n15 à 16 jier letter is de tram dêr kaem. Krekt yn 'e bocht hie pake 't sjoen. \"'k Seach him dúdlik oankommen\", sei er.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32063,"r":"CJ121907","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"People foresaw the coming of the tram and the building of a road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De wei oer de heide wie froeger in reed; de Jelke van der Meer-wei hyt er nou. Guon minsken ha dy wei fan tofoaren dêr al sjoen.\nSa ek de trambaen, dy ha guon ek fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32113,"r":"CJ122403","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"At a certain place wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns) can be seen. It is a portent: later the tram runs at that place.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr't letter de tramwei kaem seagen guon op 'e Gariperheide wylde lantearnen. \"Hjir komt hwat\", seinen se. Doe kaem de tram dêr.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":128637,"r":"ENGELB_19_006","p":"Weerselo","v":"Ov.","y":1983,"c":"SINSAG 0492","d":"Seeing carts without horses before cars and trams run.","i":"H.E.","o":"S: Vroeger toen zeadn ze, toen hadn ze zeen, dat bie oons deur n polder dat doar waagns langs gongn zoonder peerde, zonder peerde, dat wol ja gen meanske geleuvn en n tiedje later, toen gongn der waagns langs zonder peerde, want toen is nen tram komn van Dedemsvoart noar Slaghaarn, die is komn en doar in de polder kwam ne grote weg langs, doar gongn de auto's deur.\nE: Dat is den grootn autoweg van Zwolle op Coeverdn an?\nS: Ja, nee die gong binndeur op Hoogeveen an, op Hoogeveen an.\nE: Dat is van ouns oet de richtste weg noar Hoogeveen, dan goa'w owwer Slaghaarn.\nS: Ja, ja, ja,\nE: Den ken ik wa. Oh, den hadn ze ok a van te vuurtn zeen.\nS: Joa, den hadn ze a van te veurtn zeen.","l":"Twents"},{"n":21938,"r":"CJ030304","p":"Oosterwierum","v":"Fr.","y":1951,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"People see a ship come sailing across a dry plain.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e droechte kom in tsjalk op ús tasilen yn Makkum op 't Waed.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":130868,"r":"KEUNING001707","p":"Driezum","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"At a place where little lights are seen as if ships were sailing, a canal was later dug.","i":"S.K.","o":"foartsjirmerij\nDer wierne ek minsken, dy seagen jouns altyd op it selde plak ljochtsjes oer it lân gean, krekt as farden dêr skippen lâns.\nLetter is precies op dat selde plak in feart groeven.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131424,"r":"KEUNING008605","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"Ships and a bridge are seen at a place where a canal and bridge are later built.","i":"S.K.","o":"By Burgumerdaem is sa 'n sechstich jier lyn ris ien west, dy seach skippen farren. Ek seach hy in hiele hege brêge. En dêr wie doe noch neat fan soks. Letter is it Knillesdjip der kaem en nou leit der in hele hege brêge oerhinne.","l":"Fries"},{"n":45514,"r":"WEV003501","p":"Jipsinghuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"Hearing in advance the sounds that industry and machines make now; a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of sailing ships in a canal.","i":"F.W.","o":"Zal ik je eens zeggen, wat wij vroeger al gehoord hebben? Je kent het Weenderveld, hier vlakbij. Nu een stuk bouwland. Maar toen alles nog woest was, hoorden we reeds het kloppen van hamers, het dreunen van machines enz. Nu staan er gebouwen en ratelen er landbouwwerktuigen.\nIk zelf niet, maar anderen hebben grote doeken zien zweven met lichtjes er onder. Waar? Nou, waar nu een kanaal is. Later zeiden ze, zie je wel, daar gaat een schip met een groot zeil; het licht kwam uit het vooronder.\nBijgeloof? Misschien. De mensen zagen het dan toch maar."},{"n":45772,"r":"WEV004401","p":"Mussel","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"Seeing a ship with a sail pulled by a white horse at the place where a canal later comes. The first ship is said to have been pulled by a white horse.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop. \nDoar kan ’k joe wol wat van verteln. Zulm heb ’k niks zain. Mien schoonvoader wol. In 1915 is ’t nei-knoal hier komen - Mussel-A-kanaal - moar wied veur tied zee ’e tegen zien vrou:\n“Zugst doar niks?”\n“Woar?” zee ze.\n“Kiek, doar op Broambaarg, doar voart ’n schip; d’r is ’n groot zail op en d’r lop ain wit peerd veur.”\nMien schoonmoetje zag niks.\nNô ja, knoal is d’r komen en noar dat d’r verteld wordt, mout d’r veur ’t eerste schip, dat d’r deur komen is, ’n wit peerd west wezen.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":41146,"r":"WEV004803","p":"Sellingerbeetse","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"Seeing a ship in advance at the place where a canal later comes.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nToun ik nog in Drente woonde, heb ik de volgende gevallen van veurloop heurd.\nDei P., woar ’k ’t zonet over had, zag wied veurdat d’r ’n knoal was in Emmer-Erfscheidenveen, doar al ’n schip voaren mit zeil, peerd en aal.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":42992,"r":"WEV005004","p":"Ter Apelkanaal","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"Seeing a ship sail at the place where a canal later comes; do not walk in the middle of the road, or you may be pushed aside.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop was dir vanzölf ook. Op Ter Hoar was aine, dei 't nei-knoal (= Ruiten-A.-kanaal) zain heft. Schepen zag 'e voaren. Wied veurdat 't knoal groaven is. Liekstoaties zag 'e ook veurbie trekken, zo zee 'e teminste. \n't Heb hom wel es zeggen heurd:“Loop nooit midden op de weg, lu. Je hebben kans, dat ie biezied smeten worden.”  \nDan zol dir wat langs goan, snappen ie.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43288,"r":"WEV006101","p":"Kopstukken","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of the building of a bridge: hearing knocking on wooden posts.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nJoa lu, dat bestèèt.\nDat heb ik ja wol heurd van mensn, dai absoluut betrouwboar warn.\n\nOp Kopstukn zatn ais n poar oal mensn op boetn te prootn.\nt Was n zömmeroavend. Opains heurn ze geklop. Is naarns n mens in de buurt te zain, man t geluud van holtn poaln is goud dudelk.\nZai zeg dan:“Wat is dat toch?”\nEn de man zeg:“Dat binnen heipoaln”.\n“Man dr bint hier ja gain heipoaln bie ons.”\n“Nee, k wait t wol, man dr zal hier wol n keer wat bouwd worn.”\nHet hef nog zeker twintig joar duurd, en dou is n luddek eindje van dat hoes of n knoal groavn. En dou dr ook n brugge moakt is, hebben ze door heipoaln bie broekt.\nKanst verhoal veur woar aanneemn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43410,"r":"WEV006802","p":"Vriescheloo","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"Seeing in advance a ship with a sail and a white horse in the field where a canal was later dug.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik heb ook n vrou kend, dei spouk-kieken kon.\nZai zat es n keer teegn t hoes en toun zee ze:“Kiek es, door zai k n schip voarn; is n groot zail op en dr lopt n wit peerd veur.”\nZai keek gewoon over t veld, woor gans gain woater was.\nJoarn loater is door langs t knoal groavn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43581,"r":"WEV006907","p":"Vriescheloo","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"Before the canal is dug, a man sees a ship with a horse in front of it at that spot; he also hears a bell strike at the place where a house is later built.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nVan mien voader waik nog, dat e zee: “Dr mout nog es n knoal in de buurt komen; ik heb n schip zain mit n peerd dr veur.” \nd Oal man het gliek kreegn. \nOok luip e ais langs de weg en den blift e stoan.  “Nou, heur k nou n klokke sloagn; dat ken toch nait.” \nIs in de buurt niks te zain den land. \nToch wordt door loater n hoes zet. De bewoners hebben n oal grode kastklokke. Toun voader loater wel es bie dei mensn kwam, zee e; “Dat is den de klokke, dei k joarn terogge sloagn heurd heb.”","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44146,"r":"WEV007803","p":"Vledderhuizen","v":"Gr.","y":1964,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"At the place where he lives a man hears water flowing, a portent of the lock chamber in the canal that was dug later.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mien schoonvoader hef de sluuskolk heurd in t neiknoal.\nHai woonde ja, woor non t knoal is, man in dai doagen was t aal nog land. En toch hef d oal man t woater stroomm heurd.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":130226,"r":"BIJLSMA000904","p":"Oosterwierum","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"A farmer's cradle stood on a haystack during the flood of 1825. A haymaker warns of a three-master; the others see nothing. Later the land became water on which ships sail.","i":"T.B.","o":"By âlde Fitus Lolkema to Sânfurderyp - syn widze hie mei de wetterfloed yn 1825 boppe yn 'e golle op it hea stien - wie ris in ûngetider, dy't mear seach as sljocht hin en wer. Op in kear sieten se to skoftsjen yn it hailân. Doe sei er tsjin de oaren: \"Nou mannen, wy meije wol meitsje dat we hjir weikomme, der komt in greate trijmester rjocht op ús oansilen.\" Dat koe net, hwant it wie allegear lân om harren hinne. De oaren seagen neat en laken him út.\nLetter waerd it dêr allegear wetter en foeren der skippen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":11502,"r":"CJ000211","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"A woman sees ships sailing over the heath with lanterns in their masts. Years later two canals were dug there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 't foarige wie 't yn 'e Wierren (ûnder Nyegea) noch allegearre heide. Op in kear seach ús mem samar troch dy heide skippen farren mei de lantearne yn 'e mêst. Jierren letter waerden dêr twa fearten groeven. Ien dêrfan is de polderfeart, dy't yn Earnewâld útkomt. Dêr farden letter skippen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":44262,"r":"WEV008001","p":"Sellingen","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"Seeing a ship with a cloth on a pole on land is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a canal; something going along the road without a horse is a voorloop of the tram.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nDe volgende veurvaln binnen mie bekend.\nAin vrou in Jipsnghoezen hef t knoal zain, wol al vertig joar van te veurn. Ze zag n schip mit n groot douk aan n poale over t laand schoeven.\n“En wat hier nog n keer veur ons hoes langs komp, da wait k nich. t Roast dr over de weg en dr is hail gain peerd veur.”\nNoaderhand bleek dat de tram te wezen.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44548,"r":"WEV009005","p":"Holte","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"A grey cloth above the land is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of ships in a canal that is being dug. A flame above the canal is a voorloop of a child drowning.","i":"F.W.","o":"Veurloop.\nTuskn Onstwedde en Pekel zaggen we voak n grieze labbe over t land goan. As ie dan kiekn gungen, was er niks te zain.\nNoaderhand is door n knoal groavn en dou vuirn dr scheepn langs; dai labbe is t zeilvan t schip west, dat leuf k vaste.\n\nDou dai wieke dan kloar was, is t ais gebeurd, dat wie vuur boovn t woater zaggen. Nich altied, zo non endan.\nIs loater n kind verdronkn op dat stee; en t wonderlieke is, dat dai vuurvlam nooit weer zain is. Toch aigenoardig, wadde?","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45018,"r":"WEV009701","p":"Sleen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"Seeing bridges, a canal and a fire in advance.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik kan joe wel over iets verteln; maar dat was veur mien tied en ik zelf leuve er niet aan. Mien ollers en meer andere mensn namen wat ik je vertelle veur waar aan.\n\nMien moeder hef de bruggen en ook het kanaal van Nieuw-Amsterdam naar Coevorden gezien, wied veur die er waarn. De bruggen lagen op dezulfde plaatsen, die sie aanweezn hadde. Zo zee ze teminste, maar ik betwiefel dat.\n\nZij vertelde ook: \"Wie zaatn ies in de kamer en toen wier et iniens zo licht; er straalden een rode gloed deur de ramen naar binnen; en t was al donker, de zunne was onder.\"\nOver verloop van tied brandt er et huus van de buurn op en toen zagen ze weer de zulfde gloed in de kamer schienen.","l":"Drents"},{"n":43139,"r":"WEV010201","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"A man born with a caul sees funeral processions, and sees a ship sailing over land where a canal was later dug.","i":"F.W.","o":"Zo hail veul ken k nait verteln. Ik wait wel n beetje over veurgezicht, dat gain biegeleuf is, en wider is mie wel t ain en ander verteld woor ik schollers over ophoal.\n\nIk heb zulf n zeun had, dei veur zain kon. \nHai zee moar zo: \"Kiek, door komp n schip aan; ik zai hom over t land voarn.\" Liekstoaties kon hai ook zain, moar hai proade dr nooitover, door had e n hekel aan. \nWat hai zag, kwam wel uut. t Knoal is dr komen, scheepn voarn dr nou op dezulfde stee-n, woor hai ze zain het. \nHai was trouwens mit de helm geboorn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43519,"r":"WEV011401","p":"Rijsdam","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"A man born with a caul predicts the digging of a canal, the sailing of ships and the building of houses, sees white figures that disappear after he recites a psalm verse, sees a coffin standing on the road and predicts a funeral procession. He predicts that his wife is pregnant with a child that is not her husband's.","i":"F.W.","o":"Spookn en heksn, dat was non t underwaarp van ale doagn in mien jonge joarn. Ik bin wol al zo baange west, as ik as kind zat te lustern noar mien olle lu en de buurn. \nDoorum bin k dr non wat flauw van, man k wil joe wol t ain en ander verteln. Man schrief dr niks van op; ik wil nich in de kraande.\n\nIn de Riesdam woonde dan n man dai mit de helm geboorn was en zodounde In de Riesdam woonde dan n man, dai mit de helm geboorn was en zodounde t veurgezicht har. Hai kreeg wol ais gliek, dan kwammen zien veurspelsels oet: t nei-knoal hef hai zain, hai zag dat ze dr mit aan t groavn warn; luipn ook widde peerden veur de woagns. Scheepn zag e ook voarn. Hoezn, dai loater bouwd binnen, hef e stoan zain en goa zo man deur. Door was gain flauwekul bie.\nMan hai vertelde ook van widde wieven. \nZo mout hai dan n keer van de Riesdam noar Selng loopn weezn en dou kwam dr wat noast hum loopm. Twai widde wievn. t Zwait was hum oetbrookn. Zai deden hum wol niks, man t was zo angstig. \nIn t lest was hum wat in de zin schootn. Hai zai n regel van n psalmversie op. Dit was t: \"De Heer is bij mij, k zal niet vrezen\". En kiek, dou wazzen de widde gedoantn inains verdweenn.\n\nHai luip ook es n moal bie oavend over v zandloane mit de stok in de hand. Was nog aine bie hum. \"Wacht eevn\", zee hai, \"blief stoan, door steet wat.\" Hai pakde de stok en huif dr mit op n liekkiste, dai midden op t pad stun.\n\"Non","l":"Gronings"},{"n":12308,"r":"CJ001305","p":"Nijega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"Women see ships sailing over the land where a canal was later dug.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De mem en beppe fan myn skoanmem soenen op in jountiid nei de tramhalte ta yn Nyegea om harren man (en heit) ôf to heljen. Sy wisten noait hoe't er thúskomme soe, hwant hy brûkte wol us drank en dan wie 't net fortroud, dat er allinne roan. Doe seagen dy twa froulju ûnderweis yn 'e Wierren (ûnder Nyegea) skippen farren op it lân. Letter is dêr in feart groeven en doe farden der ek echt skippen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15708,"r":"CJ002805","p":"Oudega","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"Some people heard the sound of the tram long before the rails were laid, or saw its lights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der binne guon dy ha al fier fan tofoaren it lûd heard fan it lizzen fan 'e rails, doe't de tramwei fan Sumar oanlein woarde. Us mem hat de ljochtsjes fan 'e tram sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17009,"r":"CJ007607","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"The narrator's mother sees a bright lamp burning above the canal. Later a bridge was built there with a lamp above it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"\"Sjoch,\" sei ús mem alris, \"sa'n heldere lampe brânt dêr oer de Sweagerfeart. Doe kom dêr letter in brêge mei in lampe der boppe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26255,"r":"CJ060201","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"In Rotfalle lives a certain Kuipers, who can foresee things. He stood on the Alpen in Harkema and in 1880 saw seagoing ships sailing in the Knjillisdjip. The canal was later widened and seagoing ships regularly sail there. He can also order food from London without an air connection. Later this happened by means of aeroplanes.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Rotfalle wenne in mounder, in sekere Kuipers. Dy seach dingen foarút. Hy hie op 'e Alpen stien yn 'e Harkema en doe seach er séskippen farren yn 't Knjillisdjip. Dat wie om 1880 hinne.\nLetter is 't kanael forbrede en nou farre der geregeld séskippen lâns.\nEk sei er, dat se sûnder tried troch de loft iten bistelle koenen to Londen.\nDat is letter echt gebeurd troch middel fan fleanmesines.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":45793,"r":"WEV015602","p":"Veele","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"Seeing ships on the heath where a canal was later dug; seeing lights in the field, predicting that houses will be built somewhere. Someone always looks up in silence at a farm; later someone falls down there and dies.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik heb vrouger scheepn voarn zain over de heide. En is t knoal er non of nich? Ik heb löchtn zain in t veld en zee dan, dat er hoezn komen zoln, en zai bint dr toch? \nIk wait nog, dat dr eerder aine bie ain van de buurn voak aanloopn kwam en dan keek hai altied boovn noar t golf. \nHai zee niks. Loater begreepn wie, woorum e dat dee. Ieder bot, as dai man noar boovn keek, zag e al, wat dr loater gebeurd is. \nIs n jongkerel oet t golf vaaln; hai was dood. Man de kerel kön dat ja nich zegn? Waitn hef hai t.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":132063,"r":"VODA_037_01","p":"Vriezenveen","v":"Ov.","y":1968,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"A man sees a large sailing ship sailing over the land at a spot where a canal would later be dug.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Verteller: Vroeguh wat mie grootvader was […] dae proat'n ook gaer enne zo heet mie ook wel een met m’n vader, daen proat'n gaer en… en doe komt Ting? dea komp ……aan en noa de schuut’n ‘ewaes en he haed de schuut’n vol krieg’n.\nHij zegguh: “Johannes, ik heb vandaag wat gezien dat vergeet ik van mijn hele leven niet.”\nStem: Zo.\nVerteller: M’n grootvader zegt: “Ma wa hè je dan ‘ezeën?”\n“Ja da was daar omstreeks,” had er zegd, “dat noe der Wiek is.”\nStem: O.\nVerteller: Tussen de darde en de vierde zief.\nStem: I… è…\nVerteller: “n toen was d’r een schip van... van het westen kwam zeilen en dan was d’r zo veur ‘m langs ’egaone. En da was ‘t oosten innegoan. En ik ben op m’n ene knie gaan zitt’n, ik heb d’r naar gekeken. Dat schip met zeil en mast. Was ’m doar zo voorbie gegaon.”\nStem: Was dat dan...\nVerteller: Da was ‘t oosten inderdaad. Da was later…\nStem: Was dat dan zoveel biezonders?\nVerteller: Ja, maar doe was doar nog genen Wiek of niks.\nStem: Oh! Was da gene Wieke!\nVerteller: Nee niks!\nStem: Oh!\nVerteller: Niks, Eieveld.\nStem: Oh! Eiveld!\nVerteller: As hier d’n sloo… de schuurtjes loop’n.\nStem: Ja. Oh!\nVerteller: Ja… En hoe… en later doe ware de scheep’n d’al in da rooie veld, da bie Van Rooij’n?. Een schip had e ’zegd met zeil en mast.","l":"Zeeuws"},{"n":25936,"r":"CJ057901","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"In the past people saw ships sailing over a stretch of heath. Later a small side canal was dug there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem fortelde, skeef oer de Wierren nei de Sumarreheide seagen guon in skip silen oer de heide yn froeger tiid.\nLetter kom dêr in opfeartsje, fan Aldegea ôf. Dêr farden doe wol skippen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33252,"r":"CJ088203","p":"Schagerbrug","v":"N.-H.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"In the past people saw wild lanterns on the heath. Later a canal came there. The little lights were the future masts of the ships.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Susterweisfeart (dy't der doe noch net wie) seagen se yn 'e Sumarreheide froeger ek wylde lantearnen. Mar dy wienen folle heger as gewoane. Letter ha se dêr de feart groeven en dy ljochtsjes, dat wienen de mêsten fan 'e skippen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12978,"r":"YPFOE129","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"A man goes fishing in the evening. When his dog starts howling frighteningly, the fisherman takes it as a bad sign. Suddenly he sees a big black thing approaching over the water, with smoke coming off it. The fisherman gets scared and flees. A few years later a steamboat sails on that same water for the first time. The fisherman had foreseen it all.","i":"Y.P.","o":"Wat Tamme Wobbes efter de Eastermarre mûne seach\nIt spilet yn 'e twadde helte fan 'e foarige ieu, mar wannear kin ik net krekt sizze. Tamme Wobbes wie in âld skipper en hy mocht graach fiskje. Op in jûne yn it begjin fan augustus gong er efter de mûne \nsitten te poeren. It hie in waarme dei west, de sinne wie al lang weisakke efter de Burgumer tsjerke, de dauwe kaam opsetten út 'e sleatten en striek oer't lân. It fangen waard net folle, mar it wie in moaie, fredige jûn. Hark, dêr kamen noch in pear weiden hea de Sumarrewei del, grif boeren út'e Boerestreek, dy't blaugêrshea efter Garyp wei helle hienen.\nIt lûd stoar wei. Even letter begûn Jelle Imkes syn hûn te spoekgûlen. Dat hearde raar en dat mocht er net graach hearre, want it betsjutte net folle goeds. Hy siet te mimerjen, de ieltsjes woenen noch net bite. En dêr ynienen—dêr klonk gelûd oer de mar wei. Der kaam in grut swart ding oanskowen, skeanoer. Tsjokke reekwolken kamen der út, ûnder skynde fjoer te wêzen. It kaam sa tichte by, dat de baren sloegen tsjin syn boatsje oan. Hy waard sa benaud, dat hy sprong der út en kaam heal yn 't wetter en heal op 'e kant te lâne, en hy makke dat er fuortkaam.\nYn 'e herberch praten se der noch oer nei. Guon seinen, hy wie grif yn 'e sliep fallen en hie in drôge hân. Oaren seinen: 'Wy sille wol ris sjen'. Wat barde? In jiermennich letter kochien in pear Iju in stoomboat. Dy soe farre f","l":"Fries"},{"n":29626,"r":"CJ110901","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"A man sees ships sailing before the canal has even been dug. It is a vision of the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit dy fortelde fan in kanael, de Strobosker trekfeart. Doe't dat kanael der noch net wie, seach heit dêr de skippen al farren. Heit wenne yn Sânbulten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31399,"r":"CJ117403","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1978,"c":"SINSAG 0493","d":"A man out at night suddenly hears a dog howling eerily and becomes very frightened. Shortly afterwards he hears a strange sound and sees something black approaching over the water. When the thing then also moves over the land, the man quickly gets away. It is a portent: later a canal is dug at that place and the steamboat sails there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tamme Wobbes wenne to Eastemar, yn 'e buorren. Nachts gong er faek to pûren. Op in nacht wie dat wer it gefal. 't Wie oer tolven. Hy gong achter de feart nei de Lits ta. Doe bigoun dêr in houn to spûkgûlen. Der waerd er kjel fan. Hy stiet noch even to pûren en fangt noch in pear ielen.\nDan heart er ynienen in fremd lûd. Ut 'e Mar wei sjocht er in soarte fan ding oankommen earst oer 't wetter. Mar dan giet it oer 't lân, krekt op it plak, dêr't letter de Lits forgroeven is. Der kaem fjûr en reek út dat ding. 't Kaem op him ta. Hy sprong út 'e boat wei oan lân en is nei hûs ta flein, sa hurd er koe. Hy liet boat en iel achter.\nDit hat foartsjirmerij west fan 'e lettere Eastemarre stoomboat en fan 'e forgroeven Lits. It is al folle langer as hûndert jier lyn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":39192,"r":"ZEEUW280","p":"Wissekerke","v":"Zl.","y":1834,"c":null,"d":"The chronicles carefully record the appearance of comets as harbingers of terrible events. As examples, a poem and two incidents: on 29 August 1088 a star in the shape of a four-headed, fire-breathing dragon seemed to announce a plague epidemic, and in 1264 a star appeared for three consecutive months. It disappeared when Pope Urban died.","i":null,"o":"Wonderlijke teekenen.\n\nNauwkeurig vindt men in de kronieken de verschijning der kometen opgeteekend, als onheilspellende voorboden van verschrikkelijke gebeurtenissen.\n Een boec doet mi weten\n Als ene in enich lant schijnt,\n Dat lant wordt ghepijnt,\n Van ere plaghen; van drien\n Moet hem emmer dan gescien.\n Deerste es sterfte ghemeene,\n Van ouden, jonc, groot of clene.\n Dander hongher en tarde 1) mede,\n Manslacht van onvrede 2)\n Van lantshere onderlinghe.\n\nZoo werd er in het jaar 1088 op den negen en twintigsten Augustus in de lucht een \"vervaerlijke waensterre\" gezien, \"hebbende de gedaente van een vierige Draek, uyt wiens muylen alom schichten schoten.\" Daarop kwam de pest.\nIn 1264 verscheen een \"grouwsaeme waensterre\", drie achtereenvolgende maanden lang. Ze verdween in denzelfden nacht, dat paus Urbanus stierf.\n\n1. Duurte. 2. Oorlog."},{"n":39196,"r":"ZEEUW284","p":"Sluis","v":"Zl.","y":1859,"c":null,"d":"On the night of 22 March 1643 several people saw a terrible flash of lightning above Sluis, which ended over the town like musket and cannon shots in smoke and foul-smelling vapour. This is without doubt the wrath of the righteous God who rules over the whole land, and a harbinger of disaster, plague epidemics and bloody wars.\nThe church council orders a day of fasting and prayer on Wednesday, so that God's wrath might be averted through penitence and prayer.","i":null,"o":"Wonderlijke teekenen.\n\n\"Den 22 Martii 1643, Sondaeghs 's nachts van den thienen tot den elven is van verscheydene personen over dese stadt (Sluis) gesien een vreeselyck gelicht, namentlijck een doot verwig streckende van 't oosten, beginnende uyt een donckere wolcke, met blixem scherp, als een handvat breed, opgaende, ende in 't westen wederom scherp nedergaende als een roede, ende daer naer omtrent den twaelffen voortschietende vyervlammen gints ende weder over alle canten over de stadt, als musket ende kanonschoten in roock ende stinckenden damp desinerende; welcke buyten allen twyffel teyckenen syn, dat de rechtveerdige toorn Godts over ons geheele lant is ontsteecken, ende voorboden syn van toekomende oordeelen, van pestilentien ende bloedige oorloogen\".\nEenstemmig besloot toen de kerkenraad om een vast- en biddag te ordonneeren, op den komenden Woensdag, \"opdat by dese gemeynte, over welcke Godts toorn is ontsteecken, Godt door boetveerdicheyt, ende gebeden mocht tegemoet gegaen worden ende synen verschrickelycken toorn werde affgewent.\"","l":"17e-eeuws Nederlands"},{"n":39591,"r":"CBOEK439","p":"Zaandam","v":"N.-H.","y":1882,"c":"TM 4302","d":"Article about know-it-all attitudes and superstition in farming, things you should do with a waxing moon, remedies for toothache, omens, etc.","i":"G.R.","o":"Betweterij en bijgeloof, ook bij den landbouw\n\nDe hoogste wijsheid van den mensch bestaat niet daarin, dat hij erkent niets te weten, maar in de zekerheid, in het besef, dat hij niet alles kan weten en evenwel de roeping heeft om te jagen naar de hoogste wetenschap. De eerste tred op die ladder, waarvan in 't korte menschenleven slechts enkele sporten worden betreden, is zelfkennis. Voorzeker, zich zelven te kennen is de hoogste wijsheid! De gulden waarheid geldt voor iederen sterveling, ook voor den landbouwer. En voor hem, voor den landman, niet enkel als mensch, maar ook als drijfkracht, als de ziel der boerderij, past het deze waarheid te beleven. Daarvoor is noodig, dat de boer zijne zelfkennis niet beperkt tot zijne eigen boerderij - ook daar buiten moet hij een blik slaan om een duidelijk, algemeen begrip van den Nederlandschen landbouw te hebben. Onze landbouwers moesten meer onderzoeken, wat er zoo al omgaat bij onze landbouw; dikwijls is er zelfs in de naaste omgeving veel te leren.\n't Is vreemd, maar niettemin waar, dat onwetende lieden zeer veel achting voor de onkunde hebben. Hoe gaarne galmen zij 't niet uit, dat ze zoo weinig weten. Nu zou die belijdenis wel loffelijk mogen heeten, wanneer die onkunde een spoorslag tot onderzoek bleek te zijn, maar... men gaat den gang der dwazen, die alleen door eigen ondervinding leeren en dan meestal hoog leergeld moeten geven"},{"n":39346,"r":"CBOEK347","p":"Purmerend","v":"N.-H.","y":1892,"c":"TM 4001","d":"Some predictions concerning the weather.","i":"M.H.","o":"voorspellingen\n\nAls de hond of de kat op 't ijs komen, gaat 't zeker dooien.\nAls de hond gras eet, volgt er zeker regen.\nStaat de wind op 20 M[aa]rt in 't N[oorden], dan staat ze er dertien weken later nog."},{"n":39606,"r":"CBOEK452","p":"Bathmen","v":"Ov.","y":1892,"c":"TM 2901","d":"When a child is born with a caul, an honest midwife gives the child the caul to swallow, or buries it. A bad one sells it to sailors, because it protects them from shipwreck. There are many stories of people born with a caul who know in advance when someone will die, because a few days beforehand they had to get out of bed at night to open a gate through which the neighbours would have to carry the coffin, or because they had come into contact with that coffin in some other way.","i":"J.V.","o":"Als een kind met een helm geboren is, geeft een eerlijke baker het kind den helm weer in, of begraaft hem. Een slechte verkoopt hem aan de zeematrozen, omdat deze daardoor gevrijwaard worden van schipbreuk. Er zijn vele verhalen van menschen, die met een helm geboren zijn (bv. Alb. Brunswijker, bijg. Albertoom den Dekker), die vooruit weten, wanneer iemand sterven zal, omdat ze een paar dagen te voren 's nachts het bed uit moesten om een hek los te doen, waar de buren met de doodkist door moesten, of dat zij op een andere manier met die kist in aanraking waren geweest."},{"n":39679,"r":"CBOEK501","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1892,"c":"TM 4001","d":"All kinds of weather predictions (folk belief).","i":"H.B.","o":"Volksweervoorspellingen\n\nSneeuw op het slijk, Vorst aan den dijk.\nDondert het 's najaars op de kale boomen, hard' winter.\nVeel noten hard' winter.\nZoo de wind is, als de zon de linie passeert, waait hij drie weken.\nMorgenrood brengt water in de sloot; avondrood mooi weer aan boord.\nStaat de zon op stutten, regen.\nAlleen drijvende wolken (schapepensen), regen.\nKruipnevels, regen.\nSchuilen de kippen bij regen niet, dag regen.\nBij vorst worden de koeien, op stal staande, wel eens onrustig, verandering.\nZijn eenden en kippen rumoerig, zware wind, zelfs vliegende storm.\nStaat de maansikkel rechtop, druipmaan, ligt ze achterover, droogmaan.\nStaat er een sterretje (klapper of verklikker) dicht bij de maan, wind.\nBeharsen de bijen in den herfst den korf buitengewoon, hard' winter. \nMaandag nieuwe maan, ruw weer.\nGaan de rookwolken uit den schoorsteen der stoombooten \"over den kop\", ruw weer.\nSpringen de gebrande koffieboonen tegen het deksel van den blikken trommel, wind.\nBegint de koperen pompkraan te zweeten, regen.\nEikenhouten meubels kraken tegen wind.\nPadden en slakken laten zich tegen regen meer zien.\nKraaien vliegen tegen regen bij troepen.\nAls de zon onklaar ondergaat (in een nest kruipt), regen.\nVliegen de zwaluwen laag, regen.\nAls de smidse, de slooten en het privaat rieken, regen.\nValt het roet en wordt het zout nat, regen.\nBlijft de gemalen koffie hangen aan de wanden van h"},{"n":60749,"r":"DYKFRIES2136","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":null,"d":"In Nieuwebrug lived the fortune-teller Hinke, who was called Hinke Kaart (Hinke Cards). One evening two women visit her for advice. Sytske is housekeeper to a shopkeeper. For a long time she had a suitor, Japik, but when the shopkeeper's wife died and the shopkeeper told her he would like her to stay in his service, she thought she had a chance of marrying him and broke off with Japik. The shopkeeper, however, turns out to have no plans to marry, and Sytske tries to renew her ties with Japik. But Japik makes no move towards her. Sytske wants to know whether she can be even more open with Japik and so asks for advice. Her friend has come along because Sytske dreaded going to the fortune-teller alone. Hinke tells Sytske she will answer everything honestly and reads the cards. The cards are favourable and predict a good marriage between Sytske and Japik. Half a year later the couple are married.","i":"W.D.","o":"Op het Schavernek te Leeuwarden heeft, gelijktijdig en nog na Akke eene dergelijke vrouw geleefd en gewerkt. In het gehucht Nieuwebrug ten noorden van Heerenveen woont nog eene waarzegster, niet minder vermaard, zeker ook niet minder bekwaam, dan in haar tijd Akke van 't Vliet, en alzoo eene waardige opvolgster van deze. Zij wordt dan ook steeds Hinke Kaart genoemd, welken naam zij zich laat welgevallen, want zij is de vriendelijkheid zelve. Evenals Akke, en vooral als de vrouw op het Schavernek, ontvangt Hinke wel bezoek van aanzienlijken. Zij is gehuwd en haar man speelt, wanneer het soms te pas komt, wel de rol van handlanger. Haar eenvoudige doch knappe woning staat aan den grooten weg. Het is schemeravond. Twee meisjes, beide met het voorschoot om het hoofd geslagen, schijnbaar voor den tocht, maar werkelijk omdat zij zich wat schamen, sluipen de huisdeur in. Zoodra de bezoeksters het doel harer komst hebben te kennen gegeven, wordt het licht ontstoken. Alles in het vertrek ziet er, evenals de vrouw zelf, proper uit; zij is het beeld eener zindelijke arbeidersvrouw, maar ter dege bespraakt. Hinke gaat zitten bij de tafel en de meisjes worden verzocht tegenover haar plaats te nemen. Uit de tafellade haalt Hinke een spel kaarten van 32, en terwijl zij dit met verwonderlijke vlugheid schudt, verzoekt zij met ernstigen aandrang, dat op alles wat zij zal vragen naar waarheid wo"},{"n":69239,"r":"DYKFRIES2142","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":null,"d":"Apple pips have the power of prophecy. If you take a smoothed apple pip between thumb and finger and let it shoot away after saying the words:\n\n\"Little sprout, sprout!\nWhere does my sweetheart live?\"\n\nthe direction of the pip will tell you in which region your future beloved lives.","i":"W.D.","o":"Ook in appelpitjes zit voorspellende kracht. Neem een door vocht gladgemaakt appelpitje tusschen duim en vinger en doe het door sterke drukking wegspatten na het uitspreken der woorden: \n\n«Sprútsje sprút!\nHokker (naar welken kant) woont myn vrijer (of vrijster) út ?»\n\nDe richting die het pitje neemt wijst de kompasstreek aan, waarin de nog onbekende zoetelief verblijf houdt."},{"n":69878,"r":"DYKFRIES2257","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":null,"d":"Anyone who has a wild poppy in their mouth and falls will die. It is therefore advisable never to put such a flower in your mouth. Others say the same of the water lily, the flower of the pompebladen, which the Frisians call swanneblom (swan flower). And some believe that the unfortunate person who breaks such a flower while holding it in their hands will get the falling sickness and may die of it.","i":"W.D.","o":"Wie met een spokebloem (wilde papaver) in den mond komt te vallen, zal het besterven. Het is daarom raadzaam, nooit zulk eene bloem in den mond te nemen. Anderen vertellen hetzelfde van de waterlelie, de bloem der pompebladen, bij de Friezen swanneblom genoemd. En sommigen gelooven dat de onverlaat, die zulk een bloem in de handen houdende breekt, de vallende ziekte zal krijgen en er wellicht aan sterven."},{"n":69891,"r":"DYKFRIES2270","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":null,"d":"A list of various kinds of omens, both favourable and unfavourable, that can be read from an observed phenomenon.\n\nDreams and their meaning, especially in connection with a death or when a quarrel arises. Omens indicating (unexpected) visitors who will soon call. Itching limbs and what they mean. Omens to do with drinking tea. Omens that bring good luck or bad luck. The call of the bittern, said to predict the price of rye. Omens about marriage and love. White spots on the nails and what they mean. When someone is considered veeg (doomed to die). Animals and animal sounds that point to misfortune or deaths. Stopped clocks, other timepieces and the ringing of bells can announce an approaching death. Animals that stand for prosperity but must not be disturbed, or misfortune will follow. Omens about pregnant women, newborns and young children. Other omens.","i":"W.D.","o":"Waar men des avonds vóór het naar bed gaan het laatst aan denkt, daar droomt men des nachts van. \nEr zijn menschen, die, wanneer zij op de linkerzijde liggen te slapen, droomen van dingen, die tot het verleden behooren, maar op de rechterzijde liggende, van toekomende dingen of althans van iets, dat beteekenis heeft voor de toekomst en ook nakomt. \nDroomt iemand dat hem de tanden uitvallen, dan sterft er binnen kort een zijner kennissen. Zoo ook, wanneer hij droomt van visch of van schoon linnengoed.\nDroomt men van vette aal, dan komt er in den omtrek een sterfgeval. Anderen zeggen: dan moet een onzer nabestaanden sterven. Weêr anderen voorspellen alleen dat men ter begrafenis zal worden verzocht, en dit kan geschieden bij den dood van een kennis, zoowel als van een familielid. \nDroomt men van een bruiloft, dit beteekent eene aanstaande begrafenis in de familie, en omgekeerd beteekent het droomen van eene begrafenis, dat men eerlang eene bruiloft zal bijwonen. \nHet droomen over hondengeblaf beteekent sterven. Zoo ook het droomen over paarden. Dit kan ook de beteekenis hebben van groot nieuws, dat men te hooren zal krijgen en tevens dat men met valsche menschen omgaat. Dit laatste is altijd de beteekenis van droomen over katten. \nDroomt iemand dat hij vliegt, dan zal hij worden opgehangen. \nDroomen over geld is een voorteeken van twist. Ook kan het beteekenen, dat men iets zal v"},{"n":69966,"r":"DYKFRIES2331","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1896,"c":null,"d":"The first swallow seen in spring is called the zwaaltje-voorbode (herald swallow), because it seems to announce that its travelling companions will soon arrive.","i":"W.D."},{"n":8791,"r":"CBAK0176","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1901,"c":null,"d":"A sick, superstitious man sees a cow with flaming lights in his box bed, which he probably regards as a bad omen.","i":"C.B.","o":"Een oude heer die doodziek is, en hoogst waarschijnlijk sterven zal, en daarenboven erg bijgeloovig is, verzekerde mij dat hij in de bedstee eenige weken geleden een koe met vlammende lichten gezien had. Welke prognostante beteekenis dit had wou, of liever: kon hij mij niet zeggen, doch ik denk dat hij het als een kwaad voorteeken beschouwde."},{"n":39381,"r":"CBOEK360","p":"Dordrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1902,"c":"TM 4302","d":"Among other things: a remedy for convulsions in children; omens of deaths; omens of bad weather or a harsh winter.","i":"A.O.","o":"Voor een kind dat \"stòipkes\" heeft, is de aanwezigheid der moeder kwaad. Althans men vindt nog de meening, dat in zulk een geval de moeder zich van de wieg, liefst zelfs uit het huis moet verwijderen. Helpt dat niet, dan kan de vader zijn jas of \"oudervest\" voor de wieg hangen, dat geeft zeker verlichting.\nRingetjes in de ooren werd (wordt?) hier geacht gezond te zijn.\nHet knippen van het haar geschiedt het best met aangroeiende maan; tegelijk met de maan groeit ook het haar.\nZij het ook bij uitzondering, toch vindt men hier nog op sommige daken de sedum majus, die hier in plaats van huislook ook hòisloôp wordt genoemd. Van het geloof aan bliksemwerende kracht, die de plant zou bezitten, heb ik hier nooit iets gemerkt. De plant schijnt nu eerder gekweekt te worden, omdat zij als geneesmiddel wordt aangewend tegen het zuur bij kinderen.\nEierschalen mogen niet verbrand worden, anders houden de kippen op met leggen. Vgl. Sloet, De dieren in het germ. volksgeloof, blz. 261.\nHet blaffen van een hond des nachts wordt als een ongunstig voorteeken beschouwd, vooral echter het janken; meestal sterft er dan gauw een in de buurt. Ook het in 't slot springen van een deur 's avonds of 's nachts wordt beschouwd als een voorteeken van een sterfgeval.\nTe Heinenoord, Stougiesdijk (buurt onder Mijns Heerenland) betoont men bij het sterven van iem[and] uit de buurt rouw door het buitenluik, het v"},{"n":72541,"r":"MARKUS06","p":"Arnhem","v":"Gld.","y":1907,"c":null,"d":"Mie Sultan was a famous fortune-teller who could read the future in cards. By her own account she was a pupil of Madame Lenormand, the fortune-teller of the great Napoleon.\nStieneke Swarts was a fortune-teller who predicted the future with coffee grounds and by spinning an egg. Stieneke had a harelip and was therefore hard to understand. So if a prediction did not come true, she could say that people had not understood her properly.","i":"A.M.","o":"Hiertegenover stond het „fort van Swaan\", waar verscheidene families ingekwartierd waren, onder anderen ook „Mie Sultan\", eene beroemde waarzegster, die de kunst verstond, in de toekomst te lezen ; zij werkte voornamelijk met de kaart en was volgens haar zeggen ook eene leerlinge van madame Lenormand, de waarzegster van den grooten Napoleon, dien zij in den Franschen tijd had leeren kennen. \nZij zag dan ook uit de hoogte neer op “Stieneke Swarts” met den hazenmond, die in de Beijerpoort hetzelfde bedrijf uitoefende, en de toekomst voorspelde uit het koffiedik of uit het draaien van een ei; daar Stieneke gezegend was met eene hazenlip, was zij moeilijk te verstaan, welk gebrek haar echter heerlijk uit de verlegenheid redde, als eene zaak anders uitkwam dan zij had voorspeld. Men had haar dan niet begrepen."},{"n":9339,"r":"CBAK0481","p":"Zuiderwoude","v":"N.-H.","y":1911,"c":null,"d":"The foot-and-mouth disease now raging was foretold in the Bible.","i":"C.B.","o":"Hij gelooft ook dat het thans heerschende mond- en klauwzeer van het vee reeds voorspeld is, en wel in Openbaringen 16:10 of 16 in verband met Exodus 9:9-10A."},{"n":41766,"r":"COHEN021","p":"Zutphen","v":"Gld.","y":1918,"c":null,"d":"The knight Reynout van Valkenburg goes off to war, leaving behind his pregnant wife and his mother. He predicts that his fame will be sung by many singers. Their child is born. The knight returns wounded and dies just after arriving, in his mother's presence. His mother hides Reynout's death from his wife, because she has been ill in bed since the birth of her child. Three times the young woman wakes: from the tolling of the bells, the making of the coffin, and the funeral chant at his burial. Her mother-in-law says nothing is wrong. The fourth time the wife wakes, Reynout's mother can no longer hide the truth and tells her of Reynout's death. The lady grieves so deeply over her husband's death that the stones grant her plea to be joined with him. The castle rock splits open and the woman sinks into the chasm where her husband also lay. From the same rock an oak tree grew. From its top two birds, a dove and her mate, flew up together to heaven.","i":"L.d.B.","o":"Duif en Doffer\n\nReynout van Valkenburg ... u heeft uw vrouw meer liefgehad dan\nhaar kind.\n\nHij was uitgereden, de trotsche held.\n\n\"Vaarwel! vaarwel! Nog geen jaar en ik keer weder. Mijn plaats is,\nwaar mijn mannen en vrienden zijn. Als ik terug kom van den langen\nweg, luister dan naar het lied van den zanger, want mijn naam zal\nhij zingen ...: Reynout van Valkenburg. Vaarwel! En als het kind is\ngeboren, neem het in uwe armen, en wieg het bij dat lied. Vaarwel\nook, edele moeder! Geboren ben ik, om te strijden, want groot is\nmijn geslacht. Streel mijn armen onverwinbaar zijn ze van kracht, en\nwee den vijand. Om het edele goed en bloed en recht strijd ik--wees\ndaarom niet versaagd. Vaarwel!\"\n\nHij reed heen, en de vrouwen zagen hem verdwijnen als een stofwolk\nop den weg, opwarrelende en verwarrelende in den wind. Hij ging,\nwaar de strijd hem wachtte. Hij streed, waar het gevaar 't grootst was.\n\n\"Reynout van Valkenburg!\" klonk zijn stem, en de vijanden vloden. Zóó\nrukten hij en zijn vrienden van slag tot slag, steeds dieper dringend\nin het vreemde land. Het geschiedde, wat hij had gezegd: vele zangers\nzongen van zijn roem, hun liederen klonken over de landen, en tot in\nReynout's slot drongen zij door. Reynout's vrouw hoorde ze in hare\nkrankheid en ze fluisterde tot haar kind:\n\n\"O groot geluk, dat gij geboren zijt in deze dagen, nu zijn roem over\nde wereld schalt. Wanneer hij wederke"},{"n":41777,"r":"COHEN029","p":"Zutphen","v":"Gld.","y":1918,"c":null,"d":"A ship of the dead lies waiting. An invisible hand knocks on the window when someone is going to die. A sick boy is woken. At a man who begs to enjoy the world for one more year, the figure passes by. All the dead sail with the ship of the dead to England. After a year the ship returns. The figure takes the boy along. This year too the man begs for his life, and again the ship of the dead leaves without him. The dead feel a deep pain because one of them has not sailed with them. Years later the ship sets out again. The boy hears the thoughts of the man, who wants to ask death for another year's delay. But the boy knows the man has already asked for delay for the last time. That evening the figure comes to the man again and asks him for the third time whether he is willing to come to the land of the dead. Again the man refuses, this time saying he must care for his son. The next moment his son is struck by lightning and falls dead. Now the man is willing to go with the figure, but the figure says he will have to live another thirty years.","i":"L.d.B.","o":"Doodendroom\n\nIn den nacht lag het doodenschip voor 't eiland Walcheren. Op het dek\nstond de zwijgende schipper. Geluidloos werkte de bemanning, en de\nstuurman bij het roer zag peinzend vóór zich. Op alle gezichten was\n't licht der maan--maar buiten hen viel geen licht.\n\nEr was een onzichtbare hand, die, wanneer iemand dood zou gaan,\naan het venster klopte. Dan weder gleed de gedaante, wien de hand\nbehoorde, verder, één met den nacht, zonder een trilling, zonder een\nnevel. Overal, waar een mensch moest sterven, klopte zij, zoo zacht,\ndat 't stiller was dan het ritselen van een blad. Wie kan zeggen, wat\nhet voor geluid was? Een klanklooze klank, onweerstaanbaar voor hem,\ndie van 't leven scheidde. Zooals in den avond een uil wiekt door\nde stilte, of gelijk een luwte ondeelbaar-even vaagt en vervaagt,\nzoo moet 't zijn geweest, dat het voor den stervende klonk--klonk?\n\nEr was een jonge knaap, die lang ziek geweest was, en de hand\naarzelde nog even. Toen gleed ze langs 't venster, en zooals een\nander kind droomerig volgt 't blij geluid van trommel en fluit,\nwanneer 't zonnelicht schijnt, zoo stond de jonge knaap op, en\nvolgde de geluidloosheid, die hem voorafging. Het vreemde was,\ndat hij zijn weg wist. Telkens stond hij even stil, als de hand der\nschrijdende gestalte een venster beroerde--om dan weder te volgen,\nwat een vormlooze, kleurlooze, alleen maar voortgaande gedaante was."},{"n":39154,"r":"ZEEUW242","p":"Wissekerke","v":"Zl.","y":1918,"c":null,"d":"Emperor Charles once saw dragon ships sailing at great speed and wanted to seize the pirates, but they were too fast. Then he predicted that his descendants would still have much trouble from the blond menace.","i":"J.R.W.S./F.L.","o":"Keizer Karels Voorspelling. (De Noormannen)\n\nKeizer Karel vertoefde eens aan de zeekust, toen uit het grimmige Noorden de drakenschepen der Vikingen kwamen gevaren. Eenigen van zijn begeleiders meenden dat het vaartuigen waren van kooplieden uit het Zuiden, of birlinns van de Britsche eilanden. Anderen dachten dat het schepen der Zwarte Mooren waren. Maar Karel zag wel aan de snelheid van de schepen, dat het zeeroovers waren en wilde hen vervolgen, maar ze waren in korten tijd verdwenen op de hooge zee.\nToen ze dien avond aan de maaltijd zaten, stond de keizer op en trad aan het venster dat uitzag over de zee. Tranen stroomden over zijn wangen en toen zijn gevolg hem vroeg wat hem zoo hedroefde, zei hij: \"Ik denk er over hoe mijn nakomelingen door deze snelle roovers bitter zullen lijden, wanneer ze al tijdens mijn leven deze landen willen plunderen hoe zal het dan zijn na mijn dood.\"\nVan dien dag af liet hij alle kusten bewaken, bouwde wachttorens en versterkte zijn vloot.\nKarels voorspelling is uitgekomen. Menigmaal hebben de Blonde Bestiën moordend en brandend deze eilanden afgestroopt."},{"n":9420,"r":"CBAK0559","p":"Beets","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":null,"d":"Out of disbelief, a shipowner at first ignores his wife's advice to ask a fortune-teller why one of his ships has failed to return. After much urging from her he goes anyway, but the fortune-teller tells him at once that he did not come of his own accord. She predicts that from now on the ship will suffer damage and be wrecked. This comes true, and on inquiry it turns out the ship was wrecked on the day and at the hour he was with the fortune-teller.","i":"C.B.","o":"Een heer had schepen op zee. Achtereenvolgens kwamen allen behouden binnen, op één na. Dat was weg en bleef weg. Zijn vrouw ried hem aan om naar de waarzegster te gaan en daar te gaan hooren wat de oorzaak daarvan kon zijn. Hij had daar geen zin in, omdat hij niet aan de uitspraken van waarzegsters geloofde. Maar omdat het schip maar steeds weg bleef en zijn vrouw hem bovendien al maar aan zijn hoofd zeurde, gaf hij ten slotte toe en begaf zich naar het opgegeven adres. Zoodra hij de kamer bij haar binnenkwam zei het wijf:\n\"Jij komt ook niet uit je zelf, jij wordt gestuurd om eens te vernemen naar je laatste schip. Nou tot op dit oogenblik ging het er goed mee, maar van nu af zal het averij krijgen en vergaan, omdat jij niet in mijn kunst geloofde.\"\nInderdaad is het schip vergaan en bij navraag, aan later thuisgekomen, geredde manschappen, bleek hem, dat zijn schip vergaan was op den dag en het uur, dat hij naar de waarzegster geweest was.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.112-113)"},{"n":9422,"r":"CBAK0561","p":"Beets","v":"N.-H.","y":1922,"c":"TM 3102","d":"A woman can predict death, but can also make the sick well. For example, she cures someone bent over with rheumatism without his noticing, without touching or speaking to him.","i":"C.B.","o":"Almers G. uit de Beets (Noord-Holland). Behalve dat zij den dood kon voorspellen, verstond zij de kunst om zieken gezond te maken. Eens zag ze iemand aankomen, krom van de rheumatiek.\n\"Wie is dat?\" vroeg zij aan mijn zegsman.\n\"Wel N.N.,\" was zijn antwoord.\n\"Dat mag niet,\" zei G., en van af dat oogenblik zag mijn verteller N.N. rechter op gaan loopen. Zonder dat de patiënt wist wie hem beter maakte, zonder hem aan te raken of hem toe te spreken, verrichtte zij dit kunststuk.\n(C. Bakker: `Geesten- en heksengeloof in Noord-Holland boven het IJ', in: De Gids 1922, p.267.)"},{"n":35903,"r":"ZEEUW187","p":"Yerseke","v":"Zl.","y":1923,"c":"TM 2901","d":"An old miller could smell death; he had been born with a caul, and the wet nurse had thrown the membrane onto the dung pit instead of burning it.","i":"G.D.v.O.","o":"De Helm.\n\nDe oude mulder van Ierseke kon den dood ruiken. Als de arts nog geen gevaar voor sterven vermoedde, zei hij reeds dat het mis zou loopen. En dat kwam altijd uit.\nOok hij was met den helm geboren, en de minne had tegen het uitdrukkelijke bevel van den dokter, het vliesje op den mestput geworpen, in plaats van het te verbranden. Dat nu had het hem gelapt."},{"n":35904,"r":"ZEEUW188","p":"Yerseke","v":"Zl.","y":1923,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A woman born with a caul foresees the funeral procession of","i":"G.D.v.O.","o":"De Helm.\nAdriana Glerum leefde te Ierseke op kosten van ,,grotte voer\", of wel van het burgelijk armbestuur, en was gehuisvest in een tamelijk groot gebouw, dat echter zoo bevolkt was, dat twee huishoudens vaak een kamer bewoonden. Dat gaf vaak aanleiding tot twisten, dan moesten de armvaders tusschenbeiden komen, en met krijt werd op den vloer van roode plavuizen de grens van hun gebied getrokken. Gelukkig voor Adriana dat ze nog onder de eerste bewoners van het nieuwe gebouw Vredelust behoorde.\nDe minne had bij de geboorte verzuimd het vlies voor haar oogen weg te nemen. Als nu een van haar medeburgers ging sterven, had ze daar erg mee te tobben, moest het bed uit, naar buiten, en stond dan tegen de deur of het raam geleund, uit te zien naar den begrafenisstoet, die voorbij trok. Wie het was, kon ze wel niet zien, wel uit het aantal volgers in den stoet opmaken, of het een oud of een jong mensch was. Was de stoet voorbij dan ging ze afgetobd naar bed."},{"n":39195,"r":"ZEEUW283","p":"Wissekerke","v":"Zl.","y":1923,"c":null,"d":"A bright northern light was a sign of the \"fiery plague\". So too on 14 January 1192. The name Heerbrand (army fire) already points to a harbinger of wars, which people saw in the northern lights.","i":"J.R.W.S.","o":"Wonderlijke teekenen.\n\nEen helder noorderlicht was mede een voorteeken van de \"vierige pest\", zooals dat van den veertienden Januari 1192, toen geheel het noorden wel een openstaande vurige oven geleek.\nDe naam heerbrand wijst er reeds op, dat men in het noorderlicht, vooral de voorbode van toekomstige oorlogen ziet."},{"n":39222,"r":"ZEEUW310","p":"Wissekerke","v":"Zl.","y":1923,"c":"TM 2602","d":"Some nicknames for the inhabitants of Goes.\nAlso a four-line rhyme about the memorable year 1734, in which it had been predicted that the world would end. The people of Goes closed the town and took many precautions. Sometimes perhaps too many....","i":null,"o":"Spotsagen en Spotnamen b. De steden: Goes.\n\nOp Wolfaartsdijk noemt men de Goesenaars stadsche lucht en ook stadsche Stoepschieters.\nPotschieters is mede hun spotnaam, evenals Ganzekoppen en Ganzebekken.\nHet stadswapen vertoont een gans (oudnl. goes is gans).\n\nAls Joris Christ aan 't kruis zal slaan, \nMarkus uit 't graf hem op doen staan, \nEn Jan met hem uit wandelen gaan, \nZal 't eind der wereld komen aan\n\nIn het gedenkwaardige jaar 1734 viel inderdaad Goede Vrijdag op St. Joris, Paschen, het feest der opstanding, op St. Markus, en de H. Sacramentsdag op St. Jan. De wereld zou vergaan. Toen verspreidde zich het gerucht dat de Katholieken in alle landen als één man zouden opstaan en de Protestanten te vuur en te zwaard zouden verdelgen.\nDe Ganzekoppen van Goes namen de mare zoo ernstig op, dat ze de poorten van hun stad grendelden. De schutters kwamen in het geweer en hielden 's nachts wacht op de wallen, want de Roomsche boeren zouden in opstand komen, en van over de Schelde zouden de Vlamingen hun te hulpe snellen.\n't Is middernacht, daar hoort een der schildwachten gerucht in de gracht. Stellig willen de boeren in het heimelijk duister het water overzwemmen. Hij schreeuwt alarm; alles raakt in rep en roer, men snelt naar de bedreigde plek... daar komt een hond uit het water gekropen en schudt zich af aan de wallekant.\n't Was den volgenden dag markt, maar de boeren, die in gro"},{"n":42709,"r":"KEMP093","p":"Broek","v":"L.","y":1925,"c":null,"d":"A druid, a wise woman, predicts that the soldier Diocletian will become emperor when he kills the wild boar. Later, in 283, during a campaign against the Parthians, Emperor Carus is struck unconscious in his tent by a lightning bolt and then killed by his servants. His son Numerian, who was to succeed to the throne, was killed by his father-in-law Aper so that he would get the throne. But Diocletian kills Aper and is then proclaimed emperor of the Romans, he, the son of a slave, and reigns as such from 284 to 305.\nAnd so the druid's prediction came true, for 'Aper' means 'wild boar'.","i":"I.S.","o":"DIOCLETIAAN EN DE DRUïDE.\n\nHet was in het midden van de derde eeuw na Christus. In een herberg langs den weg van Tongeren naar Coriovallum zat een Romeinsch soldaat, afkomstig uit de Dalmatische stad Diokleia, de zoon van een slaaf; hij rustte er uit van vermoeienis. Toen kwam in die herberg een druïde, een wijze vrouw. Mogelijk kwam zij terug van een wandeling door bosch en heide, waar ze geneeskrachtige kruiden gezocht had; mogelijk had zij een bezoek gebracht aan ouden en zwakken en zieken in hun hutten. Nu trad zij de herberg binnen, om te zien of er voor haar geen winst te behalen was. Want de wijze druïde was met alles op de hoogte, wat voor anderen geheim bleef: ziekten genezen, droomen uitleggen, de toekomst voorspellen, enz.\nZe raakte spoedig met Diocletiaan, zoo heette de soldaat, in gesprek en die klaagde over zijn magere verdienste; arme boel, waar niets af kon. Maar de druïde diende hem van antwoord: ,,Neen, Diocletiaan, dat is het niet\", zeide ze, ,Maar je bent een gierig mensch, je kunt van je penningen niet scheiden. Diocletiaan lachte en zeide: \"Verkwistend zal ik worden, als ik keizer zal zijn!\" en hij dacht er natuurlijk bij: nooit. Maar toen stond de oude vrouw op en stak haar hand in de hoogte. ,,Diocletiaan!\" zei ze, ,,lach er niet mee: gij zult keizer worden, nadat ge het wilde zwijn zult hebben gedood!\" Diocletiaan onthield de woorden van de wijze vrouw."},{"n":42822,"r":"KEMP163","p":"Broek","v":"L.","y":1925,"c":null,"d":"On the Havenstraat in Maastricht a man appeared who could make himself as tall as he liked. He was seen as the harbinger of illness at the houses where he appeared. When one day a woman from the neighbourhood suddenly became rich and went to live off her income, it was said that she had driven the tall man away [?]. After that time the tall man, the terror of the neighbourhood, was indeed never seen again.","i":"I.S.","o":"DE LANGE MAN.\n\nOp de Havenstraat te Maastricht vertoonde zich des nachts een héél lange man, die zich zoo lang kon maken, als hij wilde. Hij kwam ergens uit een keldergat, richtte zich op in de straat, tot hij nog hooger werd dan de huizen, klopte overal op de ruiten, en poogde over of door de gordijnen heen te kijken.\nHij werd wel beschouwd als voorbode van ziekte in het huis, waarvoor hij zich vertoonde.\nToen op zekeren dag een vrouw uit de buurt plotseling rijk werd en van haar renten ging leven, werd er gezegd, dat zij den langen man had uitgehaald. Na dien tijd werd de lange man, de schrik van de buurt, inderdaad niet meer gezien."},{"n":42328,"r":"LAAN016c","p":"Lellens","v":"Gr.","y":1930,"c":"TM 2901","d":"To be able to foretell the future, you must be born with a caul. Some keep that membrane in a little box in the cupboard.","i":"E.F.","o":"Ieder is nait geschikt om veurlopen te zain; din mòie mit de helm geboren wezen. Paardij baargen dat vluuske op in 'n deuske in 't kamnet.\nDij mit 'n helm geboren is, dij zel 't mitlopen in de wereld. Mor zo ain het ook 'n veurgevuil van wat ter gaauw gebeuren zel.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":35866,"r":"VVUNL327","p":"Brunssum","v":"L.","y":1931,"c":null,"d":"A miner laughs at an old woman's prophecy and falls down that very same day, just as she had predicted.","i":"G.L.","o":"Profetie van 'n oude vrouw \n\nIn een der mijndorpen van Kerkrade moet een oude vrouw hebben gewoond (mij werd nadien ook medegedeeld: nog wonen!), die profetisch was. Op 'n avond had men 't erover in 'n café; 'n mijnwerker die 't hoorde, lachte erom: 'Iech bin es benuujd wat ver wongesch het va' miech sal sage,' gekscheerde hij. Waarop hij de oude vrouw geweldig begon door te halen. \nEnige dagen later trof het, dat hij in aanraking kwam met de bewuste 'oude' vrouw. En ze voorspelde hem à bout portant dat hij nog diezelfde dag van de mijnschacht naar beneden zou storten. Maar nog harder en spottender begon de mijnwerker te lachen; welgemoed nam hij z'n pungel en stapte hij naar de Domaniale, waar hij werkte, voor de middagschicht. \nDoch eer de dag om was, kwam van de mijn het bericht thuis dat de man was verongelukt: hij was van de schacht naar beneden gestort en men had hem onder in de soemp verpletterd gevonden."},{"n":48210,"r":"SINBRABSAG295","p":"Vorstenbosch","v":"N.-Br.","y":1933,"c":null,"d":"Ruth Antonius, a hermit (or ordinary farmer) near Vorstenbosch, makes a number of remarkable predictions concerning his death. To his neighbours' great astonishment, they all come true. From then on everyone believes in the predictions Ruth made during his life, and every one of them comes true too.","i":"F.C.","o":"No. 295. Over den laatsten slag vertelt een sage uit Vorstenbosch, een gehucht van Nistelrode.\n Achter de bergen leefde voor ongeveer 150 of 200 jaar de brave Ruth Antonius. Velen beweren dat hij een kluizenaar was, anderen zeggen een gewoon boertje, hoe het ook zij, hij bezat de gave der voorspelling.\n Hij profeteerde: \"Als ik zal sterven zal men mij niet door de voordeur uitdragen, maar door mijn stalletje, achter het huis.\" En alzoo gebeurde het. 's Morgens voor zijn begrafenis brak er een geweldige onweersbui los, en de zware linde, die zijn erf aan de voorkant beschutte, viel op het huisje, zoodat de voordeur versperd was en Ruth achterom werd gedragen. Maar daarenboven had hij nog gezegd: \"met een wit paard brengen ze mij naar het kerkhof.\" De buren lachten, uren in den omtrek bezat niemand een schimmel. Maar met de een of andere zware karwei ontwrichtte een paard zijn poot, juist het paard van den boer, waarop het lot was gevallen. Wat nu gedaan; een ieder had zijn paard dringend noodig, om ontwortelde boomen op te ruimen na dat zware weer en... de boer moest bij zijn broer, in het naaste dorp, een paard leenen, en jawel, die had een wit paard. Zoo kreeg Ruth voor den tweeden maal gelijk. Nu begon men alles wat hij gezegd had, te gelooven.\n Ruth zei dat er op Vorstenbosch een kerk zou komen, met de toren in een bepaalde richting, die kerk staat er nu ongeveer tachtig jaa"},{"n":46741,"r":"FRANKE010","p":"Zutphen","v":"Gld.","y":1934,"c":null,"d":"In Zeeuws-Vlaanderen there live people who were born with a caul. They can see into the future and know where death will knock next.","i":"I.M.","o":"De helm\n\nEr gebeuren meer wonderlijke dingen in Zeeuwsch-Vlaanderen.\nDat van de Vos Reynaerde is al erg genoeg maar dat is alles zoo lang geleden. Dat was vroeger, heel vroeger. Nu, en toen was het een wonderlijke tijd. In het grijze verleden ligt zooveel geheimzinnigs.\nMaar heden ten dage. Ja, de steen Del Mare staat er nog maar Reintje is er niet meer. Reintje is lang ter ziele, zoo slim en zoo geslepen hij dan ook was.\nWat er dan nog wel altijd gebeurt, in deze dagen nog?\nEr worden in Zeeuwsch-Vlaanderen nog altijd kinderen met de helm geboren. Echt, met de helm, en degeen waarmee dat gebeurt kan in de toekomst zien.\nEn meest ziet hij nare dingen. Of is het soms niet akelig, als je op klaarlichte dag een begrafenis ziet die er niet is?\nEn toch gebeurt dat.\nHij die met de helm geboren is ziet de dood komen. Hij weet waar hij de volgende keer aankloppen zal en wie hij weg zal halen.\nU dacht dat dit uit de tijd was nietwaar? Dat de helm volledig afgedaan had?\nMis man, mis. Ga naar Zeeuwsch-Vlaanderen en leg uw oor te luisteren.\nU zult er over hooren fluisteren door oude wijfjes met breed uitwaaierende kanten mutsen, of met veelhoekige witte, nauw om het hoofd sluitende kanten mutsen. 't Komt er niet op aan welke vorm de muts heeft. Er onder leeft het geloof aan de wonderkracht van de helm.\nProbeer niet het weg te redeneeren. Het zal u niet lukken.\nKomt het niet elke dag voor? L"},{"n":47668,"r":"FRANKE053","p":"Zutphen","v":"Gld.","y":1934,"c":null,"d":"A mermaid who was terribly thirsty rewarded the town that gave her what she asked for, a full bowl of fresh water, with the prediction that the town would exist forever.","i":"I.M.","o":"De zeemeermin van Bergen op Zoom\n\nEens is er een zeemeermin geweest die vreeselijke dorst had. Ach ja, ze had dagen achtereen gezwommen zonder een slok water. Ze versmachtte gewoon.\nZoo kwam ze dan, uitgeput van dorst en vermoeienis voor de haven van Zevenbergen.\nHet is te begrijpen dat dit bezoek nog al opzien baarde. De heele stad liep zoowat leeg om het zeewijf te zien. Jong en oud, arm en rijk stond aan de haven de zeemeermin aan te gapen.\nEn toen ze begon te praten steeg de verbazing ten top.\nHoor! Hoor! ze spreekt! Wat zegt ze? Ze vraagt wat, hoor! Ze vraagt om drinken!\nWel, laat ze zeewater drinken.\nMaar nee, dat was het niet wat de zeevrouw begeerde. Het was zoet water dat ze verlangde. Och, dat men haar toch een kom zoet water zou aanreiken! Eén kom maar. Ze zou er de burgerij van Zevenbergen eeuwig dankbaar voor blijven.\nMaar die van Zevenbergen lachten de arme zeemeermein in haar gezicht uit. Een kom water! Ha ha ha!\nMismoedig zwom de zeevrouw verder, naar de haven van Steenbergen. En herhaalde voor de saamgestroomde menschen haar verzoek.\nDie van Steenbergen waren minder hardvochtig.\nWater vraagt ze! Alla, geef haar een halve kom vol!\n't Was wat, maar niet volledig wat ze vroeg.\nVerder zwom de zeemeermin en eindelijk kwam ze voor Bergen op Zoom.\nEn zie, daar werd eindelijk aan haar verzoek voldaan. Men gaf haar een kom vol water, zoo groot dat ze kon drinken zoveel"},{"n":47798,"r":"FRANKE073","p":"Zutphen","v":"Gld.","y":1934,"c":null,"d":"Strange things sometimes happened in Zandvoort. Sometimes the sea there, only in Zandvoort, was suddenly very high, right up to the dunes. Whales also washed ashore now and then, which was said to be a bad omen. There was even a poet who wrote a poem about it.","i":"I.M.","o":"De wallevisch van Zandvoort\n\nEr gebeurden in Zandvoort soms vreemde dingen. Is het niet eens voorgekomen dat de zee ineens hoog werd? Zoo hoog dat de vloeden tegen de duinen klommen? Nu moet u niet zeggen, een springvloed. Nee, een springvloed was het niet. Hoe zou er een springvloed kunnen komen alleen te Zandvoort en op andere plaatsen niet?\nEn dat was toch het geval met deze wonderbaarlijke vloed. De zee steeg hoog, ineens, zonder eenig voorteeken, alleen bij Zandvoort en er vlak in de buurt. Nergens anders had men er iets van vernomen.\nWas dat niet een wonderlijke vloed?\nEr gebeurden meer dingen te Zandvoort. Er strandden schepen soms, natuurlijk, maar niet alleen schepen. Het kwam meermalen voor dat er walvisschen aan land spoelden.\nNu zou men van al die walvisschen niets meer weten en dat zou jammer wezen, als er niet een dichter geweest was die er tenminste één bezongen had. Het spek van die visschen is allang verkocht, er is allang traan van gekookt en wie zal zeggen, hoeveel visscherslaarzen en soldatenschoenen er mee ingesmeerd zijn. Nu zou men van al die gestrande walvisschen niets meer weten als er niet zoo'n dichter geweest was.\nMaar zoo'n dichter was er. Hij bezong zoo'n aan land gespoelde wallevisch. Luister maar:\n\n\"Wanneer ons 't vierde licht van 't nieuwe jaar kwam groeten\nIs hier dees wallevisch lang drie en zestig voeten\nNaar Noortwyk op de zee naar Zantfoort"},{"n":13498,"r":"LYST234","p":"Vught","v":"N.-Br.","y":1937,"c":"AT 0113A","d":"A man hears the gnomes whispering that they want to move the next day because their king has been murdered. He tells everyone what he has heard. A man born with a caul thinks he knows where the gnomes will go. Because he wants to know what the dwarfs look like and how many there are, he lies down under a little bridge on the route he predicted. All night long hundreds of gnomes walk over him. No gnomes were ever seen in that province again.","i":"A.W.H.v.H.","o":"Een man uit Veldhoven stond op een avond bij de gewezen hoef \"De Hesthok\" onder Meerveldhoven, naar een geraas te luisteren, dat door vele fijne stemmetjes werd voortgebracht. Hij hoorde zeggen: \"We trekken morgennacht van hier, omdat Kyrië dood is.\" Hij vertelde nu aan vele menschen wat hij gehoord had. Een Veldhovensche man, die met de helm geboren was, wist zeker, dat zij den weg naar Duizel zouden volgen. Hij hunkerde ernaar de dwergen te zien en te weten, hoe talrijk ze waren. Daarom ging hij in de Goorstraat te Veldhoven in een drooge sloot zitten. Te middernacht ontwaarde hij in den maneschijn een stofwolk. Spoedig verschool hij zich onder een brugje, al stond hij daar tot de knieën in het water. Tot den morgen toe trippelden honderden en honderden kabouters over hem heen. De boer ging bij de opkomst der zon naar huis en later werden in Noord-Brabant geen kabouters meer gezien."},{"n":47351,"r":"SINUTSAG046","p":"Amersfoort","v":"Utr.","y":1938,"c":null,"d":"In Amersfoort they once hanged an innocent man from a tree. He predicted that if he was innocent, the tree would die. Since then nobody has managed to keep the trees on the Galgenberg alive.","i":"M.H.","o":"De onschuldig veroordeelde. \n\nOp den Galgenberg of de Zeven Boompjes bij Amersfoort stond in vroeger tijden een boom, waaraan de misdadigers werden opgehangen. Iemand die onschuldig tot den strop veroordeeld was, heeft, staande voor dien boom, tot het allerlaatste oogenblik nog gezworen, dat hij onschuldig was, en hij voorspelde dat, ten bewijze van zijn onschuld, de boom zou sterven. Dat is ook geschied....en sedert dien is het niet gelukt zeven boomen tegelijk in het leven te houden: zoodra men een dooden boom door een levende vervangt, sterft weer een andere."},{"n":45472,"r":"BRUIJN0003","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1946,"c":"AT 0736A","d":"An immensely rich widow from Stavoren orders her skipper to find the most precious thing on earth and bring it to Stavoren, so that she might gain even more wealth and prestige. After a long search the skipper finally finds the most precious treasure on earth in Danzig: beautiful, glossy red-brown wheat. He has his ship loaded full and returns to Stavoren. But the Lady is not pleased. Wheat? She has no use for it. She orders the skipper to throw the wheat overboard, but is interrupted by an old beggar who asks whether she could not give the wheat to the poor instead. The Lady refuses and the wheat goes overboard. The beggar predicts that one day, like the people cheering the Lady on the quay, she too will go about as a beggar. At that the Lady throws a precious ring into the water, saying: \"This ring will sooner return from the sea to my hand than a single word of your prophecy come true!\" But the opposite happens: the ring returns and the Lady becomes a beggar. The place where the wheat was thrown into the sea grows into a sandbank that blocks the rich merchants' ships. Wheat grows on the sandbank, but it bears no grain. Within a few years the glory of the town of Stavoren has vanished.","i":"C.B.","o":"Het Vrouwtje van Stavoren\n\nVroeger was Stavoren een rijke stad, in vele landen bekend. De kooplieden dreven er handel tot ver over de zee en verdienden er schatten mee. Ze woonden in huizen groot en schoon. Er wordt gezegd, dat velen hun huisdeuren met goud hadden beslagen en dat hun erven met zilveren kettingen waren afgezet. Rijkdom maakt vaak trots, en trots waren ook de burgers van Stavoren. Van allen was één echter de hovaardigste: een weduwe, jong van jaren nog, maar de rijkste onder de rijken. Ze woonde in een huis als een paleis; prachtige tapijten bedekten de wanden en vloeren; het blonk er overal van goud, zilver en edelsteen. Ze bezat de meeste schepen, de meeste pakhuizen, de meeste waren. Haar schepen voeren de gehele, toen bekende wereld rond. Ze kwamen thuis met de kostbaarste schatten, ze voerden de kostbaarste schatten als koopwaar weer mee. Niemand wist, hoe rijk deze Vrouwe van Stavoren wel was, zij zelf wist het ook niet. Ieder vloog op haar wenken, haar wil was wet. Voor niets hadden de Staverse burgers meer ontzag dan voor rijkdom.\nRijk was de Vrouwe van Stavoren dus wel, doch tevreden was ze niet.\nDat gaat meer zo.\nDe kostbaarste schatten bezat zij, de kostbaarste schatten voerden haar schepen regelmatig voor haar aan, toch moesten er, dacht ze, nog mooiere en kostbaardere op de wereld wezen. En ze wou het allermooiste bezitten, dat er op deze aarde te ve"},{"n":35263,"r":"BRUIJN0016","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1946,"c":null,"d":"Westerschouwen was once a small town of great wealth and prosperity. After a while the people grew too big for their boots. They thought themselves, their town, their harbour and their ships marvellous. They were the best. If someone else was badly off, that was not their problem.\nOne day the fishermen catch a mermaid. They treat her with mockery and humiliation and hang her high in the mast. Not long after, a merman comes; he is the mermaid's husband. He asks the fishermen to set his wife free, but they refuse. When they reach the harbour he asks again, for otherwise his wife will die within the hour. Again the fishermen refuse and even throw stones. Then the merman lays a curse on the town: either they free his wife or Westerschouwen will perish. Again the fishermen refuse, and it happens as the merman predicted. The town perishes; only the tower still stands.","i":"C.B.","o":"DE ONDERGANG VAN WESTERSCHOUWEN\n\nRondom de stad Westerschouwen waren de lucht en de zee; de lucht wijd en hoog, de zee groot en machtig. Door de lucht voer de wind en joeg de golven op en blies de schepen voort. En de golven droegen de schepen naar de haven, en met de rijkbeladen vaartuigen kwam de welvaart naar de stad. De mensen waren er welgemoed en ijverig doende. \nDit ging zo jaren voort, de stad groeide, de mensen werden rijk. Toen kwam het ongeluk over Westerschouwen. De rijkdom maakte haar burgers zelfingenomen en trots. Er was geen betere stad dan Westerschouwen; er waren nergens snellere schepen; er was geen mooiere haven, op de hele wereld niet; er waren nergens zulke goede vissers. Zij hadden de stad groot gemaakt, ze hadden hun voorspoed en rijkdom dus verdiend; het was vanzelfsprekend, dat het hun goedging. Was er ergens anders armoede? Eigen schuld, hoor! Helpen? Waar denk je aan? Red je zelf maar, wij redden ons zelf ook! Een ieder moet zijn eigen boontjes maar doppen!\nTrots en hardvochtig werden de mensen van Westerschouwen, hun buidels raakten vol, maar hun hart raakte leeg. Dat was hun nood! Niemand redde hen daaruit, daaruit konden ze zichzelf slechts redden. Doch wie van deze nood tegen hen gesproken had, dien zouden ze uitgelachen hebben. Toen gebeurde het op een dag, dat er een van hun vissersboten een wonderlijke vangst werd gedaan. Het uitgeworpen net,"},{"n":20079,"r":"CJ016714","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":"TM 4302","d":"A farmer gets a remedy from the sorcerer Hinse for his sick cow, which is suffering from bloat. The animal does not recover right away, but Hinse predicts that the cow will be chewing the cud again by the time he gets home. That is exactly what happens.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In boer op it Wytfean hie in blastige koe. Hy gong nei it Swartfean, nei Hinse. Dy joech him guod mei, mar it bikom net. Doe gong de boer wèr nei 't Swartfean. Hinse sei: \"Op it stuit wjerkôget dyn koe noch net, mar astû aenst thús komste is er oan 't wjerkôgjen. En it kom krekt sa út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23665,"r":"CJ040804","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1950,"c":null,"d":"A man once saw a funeral procession pass by. It had to be for a woman who had died in childbed, because a white cloth lay over the coffin.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit hie in broer, dat wie Sytse Koster. Dy wenne yn 'e Hamsterheide, mar hy arbeide yn Eastemar by Wilko Werumeus Buning. Doe seach er op in kear op 'e Boskwei, dêr't er lâns moest in lykstaesje.\nIt wie in kreamfrou dy't der stoarn wie, hwant hja hie in wyt kleed oer de kiste hinne. De lykstaesje gong him foarby. 't Wie foartjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12549,"r":"CJ002208","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1954,"c":"TM 3109","d":"Someone is always ill. When his pillow is opened, a wreath is found inside. His grandfather takes it to a devil banisher, but the man never comes home again. This is also what the devil banisher predicts.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tsjoensters wienen der froeger plenty yn Stiensgea. Der binne rounom wol krânsen út 'e kessens helle woarn. Dêr siet naeijern, stopjern, lapkes en alsamear yn.\nHwa't hjir allegear net bitsjoend west ha - dêr ha je Fokke Alma. Dy sukkele. 't Kessen woarde iepentoarnd. Doe founen se in krâns. Pake gong foar him nei de duvelbander ta, mar hy is net mei de drank thúskom. Dat hie de duvelbander trouwens al foarspeld.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15510,"r":"CJ002219","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1954,"c":null,"d":"A girl in Readskuorre has supernatural gifts. She has power over animals and she can foretell the future. She predicted the death of her boyfriend.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wenne yn Readskuorre in fanke, dat koe pine stilje. Sy hie de magneet yn 'e hannen. Op in kear hie de boer trije hoklingen by harren yn 't lân en dy rekken alle trije yn 'e feart. Hy koe se der mei gjin mooglikheit wer útkrije. Doe gong er nei de pleats, dêr't it fanke wenne, en frege har mem of de manlju ek thús wienen. Dat wie 't gefal net, mar de dochter sei: \"Ik sil wol even mei.\" Sy rôp de hoklingen alle trije ien foar ien by de namme en sy kommen alle trije by har en se dienen har neat.\nSy woarde greater en âlder en sy krige forkearing.\nHar feint handele yn hynders. It soe de oare deis hynstemerk wêze. De feint sei: \"Dêr gean 'k hinne. Dêr kin 'k myn slach slaen.\"\nMar syn faem sei: \"Dêr soe 'k mar net hinne gean as ik dy wie.\"\nMar hy sei: \"Dêr gean 'k àl hinne, hwant dêr bin 'k alle jierren en ik fortsjinje dêr altyd goed.\"\nSy sei: \"Dan is ús forkearing út. Nou matstû it mar wite. Ik ha dy warskôge.\"\nHy sei: \"'t Sil wol hwat tafalle. Dêr ha 'k gjin noed mei.\" Hy die dus syn eigen sin en gong nei de hynstemerk. Lyk as altyd gong er achter de hynders lâns.\nHy liet de hynders bidrave. Op in oar plak gong er wer achter in hynder stean. Mar dat hynder joech him in klap, dat hy wie opslach dea.\nDer woarde biricht brocht by syn folk thús.\nDoe moest syn faem ek biricht ha. Ien fan 'e famylje gong skriemend nei har ta.\nSe sei tsjin har: \"It stiet der net bêst foar. Ik màt it s","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":15759,"r":"CJ003009","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1955,"c":null,"d":"Two men see a third man walk onto the farmyard in the evening, and predict that the horses will rear and kick. That is what happened.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By in plaets yn Koatstertille seagen twa man us ien by joun it hiem opgean. It wie deun by it Knjillisdjip en dyselde hie in glêdde jas oan. De beide mannen seinen tsjin elkoar: Even wachtsje, hwant aenst bigjinne de hynders to slaen en to bûtsen. En dat gebeurde èk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":13402,"r":"LYST151","p":"Oldehove","v":"Gr.","y":1957,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A farmer visits another farmer. This farmer, who was born with a caul, says he has just seen visitors in a black carriage at the first farmer's house. When the farmer gets home, his wife has died.","i":"J.J.B.","o":"Veurlopen\nEen boer op \"Hoogheem\" ging eens een bezoek brengen bij zijn buurman op 10 minuten afstand, wonende op \"Barnwerd\". Bij zijn aankomst vertelde de Barnwerdse boer (die blijkbaar ook met de helm geboren was) dat hij juist gezien had, dat er op \"Hoogheem\" bezoek gekomen was van iemand in een zwarte wagen. De Hoogheemster haastte zich toen naar zijn boerderij terug. Bij zijn aankomst bleek, dat zijn vrouw was overleden. \nNu moet er bij verteld worden, dat die vrouw reeds lang ziekelijk was."},{"n":13469,"r":"LYST205","p":"Meerkerk","v":"Utr.","y":1957,"c":null,"d":"Seeing a white figure in the churchyard digging a grave means that someone will soon die.","i":"A.d.B.","o":"Ook geloofde men wel aan de \"blinde belie\", een witte gedaante, die 's avonds bij maanlicht op 't kerkhof gezien werd, bezig met 't graven van een graf, als voorbode van een sterfgeval in het dorp. \nOf dit samenhangt met \"beeldwit\", weet ik niet. Wel is bekend de uitdrukking: \"zo wit als een beeld\" (bijgedachte: een wit beeldhouwwerk) en ook: \"Hij doet zo gek als een blinde belie\"."},{"n":23675,"r":"CJ040910","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1960,"c":null,"d":"At night you can come across a funeral procession. A young man in Harkema does not dare to cycle in the middle of the road.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men kin yn 'e nacht lykstaesjes tsjinkomme. Hjoed-de-dei is der in jongfeint yn 'e Harkema, dy doart net midden op 'e wei to fytsen (1953).","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":43468,"r":"AMPT000507","p":"Hasselt","v":"Ov.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2902","d":"People are afraid of gypsies, who are seen as child snatchers and who can also predict the future.","i":"M.J.A.","o":"Zigeuners daar waren we altijd bang voor, het waren kinderrovers, ook konden ze de toekomst voorspellen."},{"n":21244,"r":"CJ025109","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"Hindrik Pijl once stroked a man's goat with his hand and said it was a fine animal. The man predicted that the goat would be dead the next day, and that was indeed the case.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By Durk Mozes die er krekt allyk. Mar dêr wie it in geit. Hy striek de geit oer de hûd.\n\"Hwat in moaije geit\", sei er.\nDoe sei Durk: \"Moarn is er dea.\" En hy wie dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":210422,"r":"ENGELS001009","p":"Helden","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man born with a caul can heal and take pain away.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Mensen, met de helm geboren:\nVan Wullem Swinkels, een boertje, wonende op den Houwenberg bij Grashoek, werd verteld, dat hij met de helm geboren was. Hij ging voor sommige mensen door als een (kleine) wonderdoener. Hij kon, door gebeden of bezweringen iemand van nabij, of zelfs van veraf, genezen of de pijn wegnemen! Een zoon van mij draaide zich in de werkplaats een vinger af. Nadat hij door de dokter verbonden was, kreeg hij ondragelijke pijn. Ten einde raad belde mijn vrouw Swinkels. Deze deed, zonder over te komen, de pijn op korte termijn weg!\nIk heb ook horen vertellen, dat hij de vrouw van een kennis, die met een borstontsteking in het ziekenhuis in Venlo lag, van huis uit genas. De man is enkele jaren dood.\n\nVerslag 57, Omzetting vanuit de Ned. taal in Heldens dialect van de verhalen, opgenomen onder no. L291-10 van verteller Frans Dorssers, Helden. Helden, 5-2-1970.\nWöllem Swinkels, van d’n Houwenberg gaaf zich oet vör e soort wonderdoener, en koos minse genèzen en van pien vrei make. Hè zoo “mèt d’n helm gebore zien”, en daoröm. Hè koos tét wél op groeëten aafsjtand. Enne zoon van mich verloor inde werkplats enne vinger. Hè woord nao behandeling oet ’t zeekenhoes nao hoes gesjteurd, mér kreeg d’r s’jnaochts veul pien aan. We belde Wöllem Swinkels op. Dèè kwaam hei neet over de floer, mér dieë vandao oet dor bèèën (de pien wèg), en mèt suksés. \nIch weit, dét ‘n ’n vrou"},{"n":210430,"r":"ENGELS001017","p":"Helden","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A fortune teller's prediction that a man will be taken away comes true.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Waarzeggers:\nEven vóór de laatste oorlog kwam er eens een zigeunerin bij hotel Ueberbach in Panningen, die aan waarzeggen deed. Mijn broer Mathieu liet zich voor de grap de toekomst voorspellen. Onder anderen voorspelde de vrouw, dat hij nog eens van huis en haard weggevoerd zou worden. Dit kwam uit, want hij werd in de oorlog, (evenals 800 andere mannen uit Helden!) naar Duitsland gedeporteerd.\n\nVerslag 57, Omzetting vanuit de Ned. taal in Heldens dialect van de verhalen, opgenomen onder no. L291-10 van verteller Frans Dorssers, Helden. Helden, 5-2-1970.\nMien broor Tjeu, bezig mèt Kèrmes haoën; - ’t waas vör d’n oorlog, - kwaam an Kapél in hotel Ueberbach. Dao kwaam ’n szigeunerin, die de toukomst vorsjpélde. Vör de gekke jen leet Tjeu zich aug behandele. Ze vörsjpélden öm, det ’n nag èns van hoes en hèèrd wèg zo kome. Dét kwaam in dèè zin oet, tét te mèt 800 anger Heldjesen op 18 nov. 1944 nao de wèrkkampen in Pruusses woord gedeporteerd."},{"n":210514,"r":"ENGELS001605","p":"Helden","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A fortune teller's prediction comes true.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Waarzeggers:\nOp de kermis in Helden kwamen indertijd, omstreeks 1938, een troep zigeuners, waarbij een vrouw aan waarzeggen deed. Men kon haar tegen betaling raadplegen. Het werd door alleman als een grapje beschouwd, doch alleen brutale jongens durfden er aan. Een buurjongen was met zijn meisje vlot uitgeweest. Met een stuk in de kraag ging zijn meisje naar de waarzegster. Onder anderen voorspelde de waarzegster, dat ze vier kinderen zou krijgen. Dit kwam toevallig ook nog uit!\n\nVerslag 49, Omzetting in Heldens dialect van de verhalen, verteld door: Willem Engels, Helden, en wel onder no. L291-16. Helden, 18-2-1969. Aanvulling Helden, 1-3-1969\nIn 1938 kwaam op Heljese kèrmes ennen troep zigeuners. Dao waas ’n vrouw bei, die in ’n tentje an waorzegken dieë. Me besjouwden ’t as e grépke. Toch gingen allein opgesjote jonges, die d’r einen teveul oet heien, op bezeuk. ’t Mèèdje van enne nabberjong, dét aug gét veul gedronken hei, leet zich aug waorzegke. De vrouw beloofde eur 4 kinjer. Dét ès toevallig aug nag oetgekome."},{"n":209485,"r":"HOL000111","p":"Ingen","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul are bulletproof, foresee everything, and have to get up for every death.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen, die met de helm geboren waren, waren kogelvrij, zij konden van alles zien, werden voor alle sterfgevallen geklopt, moesten dan hun bed uit."},{"n":209505,"r":"HOL000203","p":"Ingen","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul have to get up the night before a death to open the churchyard gate.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Vroeger werd er ook verteld, dat mensen, die met de helm geboren waren wakker geklopt werden de nacht voor het overlijden, om het \"hekke\" van het kerkhof open te gaan zetten."},{"n":209522,"r":"HOL000311","p":"Ingen","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who can see into the future were born with a caul; cauls are sold to soldiers, who then become bulletproof.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Met de helm geboren. Mensen, die in de toekomst kunnen zien, zijn met de helm geboren. Zij moeten er \"'s nachts uit\" (zie hierboven). De \"juffers\" (vroedvrouwen) hielden de helm voor zichzelf. Ze verkochten ze aan \"de hoge van onder diens\". Deze waren dan kogelvrij, naar ik vermoed. \nAndere \"juffers\" gooiden de helm in de kachel."},{"n":209550,"r":"HOL000416","p":"Ingen","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Those born with a caul can see everything and are bulletproof.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen, die met de helm geboren waren, konden \"alles\" zien. Zij konden niet door een kogel geraakt worden."},{"n":209561,"r":"HOL000427","p":"Ingen","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"When a man who can see into the future visits, a girl asks whether she is going to die now.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"De dochter vertelt dat Gart Jan de Kat eens bij haar kwam, toen zij (een kind nog) een zweer aan haar been had. Hij zat haar maar strak aan te kijken en zij herinnert zich nog, dat zij aan grötje (grootmoeder) vroeg: \"Gao ik nou dood, GJ de K keek me mar aon\". Grötje trachtte haar gerust te stellen."},{"n":209563,"r":"HOL000429","p":"Ingen","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A woman predicts that a man who carried 99 dead to their graves will be the hundredth dead himself.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Iemand, een meisje, kon de toekomst voorspellen. Zij vertelde aan een man, wat hem overkomen zou. \"De 99e hedde weggebroch en de honderdste zijde zelf\" zei ze en dat kwam uit"},{"n":209564,"r":"HOL000430","p":"Ingen","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"After a refusal to have the future foretold, a foal drowns.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Op de Poel waar de dochter van Van Eck \"diende\", was eens een vrouw met \"negotie\" gekomen. Ze wilde de boerin de toekomst voorspellen. Deze voelde daar niet voor. \"Je hebt een prachtig veulen\", zei de vrouw. De volgende dag was het veulen \"verzope\""},{"n":209582,"r":"HOL000515","p":"Ommeren","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A prediction that a child will die is fulfilled when the predictor's wife gives birth to a stillborn child.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"G.J. de Kat had eens tegen de moeder van Van Ommeren, die zwanger was, gezegd: \"da keint behaude nie\". Zijn eigen vrouw beviel van een dood kind en daarmee was aan de voorspelling voldaan."},{"n":209593,"r":"HOL000526","p":"Ommeren","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A sorcerer's prediction that a horse will not die comes true.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Bart had een vooruitziende blik, want toen eens een paard van Dirk de Haas in de sloot gezeten had en op een slee naar huis moest worden gereden, lopen kon het dier niet meer, zei Bart: \"Hij gao nie dood\" En het beest knapte weer op. (Een paard in de sloot was een ernstig geval, want het dier, dat zijn best deed er uit te komen, zakte steeds dieper weg in de modder. Met man en macht, soms met behulp van een katrol, maar in ieder geval met behulp van touwen, werd het dier er uitgetrokken)."},{"n":209661,"r":"HOL000809","p":"Lienden","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Children born with a caul must be cared for to prevent an unhappy life; cauls are sold to soldiers, who are then bulletproof.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Kinderen, die \"met de helm geboren\" werden moesten goed verzorgd worden. Gebeurde dit niet, dan zouden het ongelukkige schepsels worden, die later 's nachts uit hun bed moesten om de hekken van het kerkhof open te zetten voor een begrafenisstoet, die daar spoedig zou binnengaan. Vroedvrouwen verkochten soms die helm \"aan mensen die geld hadden\", vooral aan soldaten, want het bij zich dragen van die helm maakte kogelvrij"},{"n":209662,"r":"HOL000810","p":"Lienden","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A clairvoyant predicts someone's death, which comes true.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Zegslieden hadden wel eens horen praten over helderzienden. Iemand had eens tegen zijn buurlui gezegd, dat een bepaald persoon binnen korte tijd zou sterven en dit was ook gebeurd."},{"n":209679,"r":"HOL000827","p":"Lienden","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"TM 4001","d":"The arrival of a hunchback is an omen of rain.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Zag men een persoon met een bult aankomen, dan werd er gezegd: \"We krijge règon\""},{"n":209722,"r":"HOL001014","p":"Opheusden","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Those born with a caul are clairvoyant; owning a caul makes one bulletproof; midwives trade in cauls.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen, die met de helm geboren waren, waren helderziend. Vroedvrouwen dreven er handel in. Wie zo 'n vliesje in zijn bezit had, was kogelvrij."},{"n":209723,"r":"HOL001015","p":"Opheusden","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"Convinced that clairvoyants exist, but no examples of clairvoyance.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Helderzienden bestaan er wel was de overtuiging, maar men wist geen voorbeelden te geven van hun helderziendheid."},{"n":130768,"r":"KEUNING000507","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"When a child is born with a caul, it must be pulled off the head from back to front to prevent damage.","i":"S.K.","o":"As in bern mei de helm geboren waerd, moast dy fan efteren nei foaren ôflutsen wurde, oars waerd de holle (it antlit) skeind.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130828,"r":"KEUNING001304","p":"Noardburgum","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A fortune teller reading coffee grounds predicts that a girl's courtship will end and that she will then go courting with someone who will soon die; this comes true.","i":"S.K.","o":"In âld minske by úzes roun mei pakjes sûkerij. Foar in botsen in pakje. Faek waerd hja yn 'e hûs kloppe. Hwant hja koe ek wiersizze. Myn wiif hat it ek es dien, doe 't hja noch in jongfaem wier. Hja krige dan in kop kofje. Der riedde hja dan hwat yn en geat de kofje der foarsichtich ôf, dat it kofjedik yn it kopke stean bleauw. En doe sei hja:\n\"Dou hast nou noch sterke forkearing nou? Mar dat sil útreitsje. Mar dan krigest forkearing mei in oare feint. Mar dat is slim. Dy jonge sil gau stjerre.\"\nIt kaem ek sa út.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130875,"r":"KEUNING001802","p":"Wâlterswâld","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A prediction made after reading a hand comes true.","i":"S.K.","o":"Doe 't ik noch in bern wier, ha ik ris sizzen heard, dat hjir ien wier, dy sei tsjin in jonge man, dy 't krekt troud wier:\n\"Lit my dyn hân ris sjen.\" Hy seach yn de hân en sei:\n\"Dû krigest fiif bern.\"\nEn it is ek út kaem.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130927,"r":"KEUNING002701","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A woman foretells the future from coffee grounds.","i":"S.K.","o":"In eintsje hjirôf wenne in âld minske. Dy neamden wy de kopkekiker. Hja koe út it kofjedik de takomst foarspelle.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130939,"r":"KEUNING002809","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"TM 3101","d":"A quack healer's prediction that a man will not get home with the medicine comes true. The first woman the man meets with the new bottle is the guilty one.","i":"S.K.","o":"In man helle ris guod foar in siik skiep by Greate Wopke. \"Ik wol it dy wol mei jaen,\" sei W., \"mar dou komst der net mei thús.\"\nDe man lake der om, mar de oare moarns stie hy al wer by W. foar de doar, om nij guod. Hy wier hast thús, doe wier de flesse yn grús fallen. \"Hoe kaem dat nou,\" frege hy W. \"Dat hat it selde frommes dien, datstou aenst it earst tomjitte komme silste,\" sei W.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131139,"r":"KEUNING004902","p":"Drachten","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A fortune teller's prediction that the much younger wife will not be the one to live longer comes true.","i":"S.K.","o":"Yn Nijbrêge wenne de wiersister Hinke Kaert. Ús heit is pas troud, doe hy 53 jier wie. Mem wie noch mar 26 jier. Heit en mem koene net sa bêst meielkoar. Mem is ris nei Hinke ta west. Hja frege, hwa earst stjerre soe, heit of sy sels. Hinke sei: \"Jo tinke, dat jo it langst libje sille. omt jo safolle jonger binne. Mar sa is it net. Jo man libbet it langst.\" En sa barde it ek.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131140,"r":"KEUNING004903","p":"Drachten","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A card reader's prediction that people are walking around in clothes made from a stolen cover cloth comes true.","i":"S.K.","o":"In mounder brocht ris mei syn moalwein moal by in boer. Wylst hy in sek moal yn de skuorre brocht, waerd it nije weinkleed stellen. Hy gong nei Hinke ta, om to hearen, of dy ek wist, hwa it dien hie. Foar hy hwat sein hie, sei Hinke al, hwat syn boadskip wie. Hja miende, dat it oer stellene klean gie. Mar hja sei der by: \"It is in nij blau kleed. En der stean letters op. Guon net sa fier ôf rinne yn it koart yn kilen fan de selde kleur. Tink dêr mar om, dan wite jo genôch.\" En it kaem ek út.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131141,"r":"KEUNING004904","p":"Drachten","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A prediction that a gold watch a man has lost is at a goldsmith's comes true.","i":"S.K.","o":"Gekke K. hie aerdich hwat sinten. Dêrtroch kaem it fêst, dat hy altyd wol maten krije koe, om mei út to gean. Op in kear, dat hja wer ris nei in feestje wiene, rekke hy syn gouden horloge kwyt. Hy ek nei Hinke Kaert. Dy sei: \"Jo geane mar nei Snits, nei in goudsmid, dy 't yn dy en dy strjitte wennet. Dêr sille jo jou heloazje wer fine.\" En wer wie it sa.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131195,"r":"KEUNING005706","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A fortune teller's prediction that someone will earn a lot of money comes true.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ik wie noch feint, doe krige ik yn de holle, om my as môlkfeint yn Dútsklân to forhieren. Min gong dan nei ien fan de minsken yn Dútslân, dy adfortinsjes yn Hepkema hienen, hwer môlkfeinten yn frege waerden. Ik reizge doe nei Wezel. Underweis mette ik noch ien mei sa 'n blaupûde by him.\nNou ha ik noch forgetten to sizzen, dat ik foar de tiid nei Hinke Kaert west bin. Foar dat ik noch hwat sein hie, sei hja al: \"Soa, jo sille ek mar in protte jild fortsjinje hè.\" Nou, dêr prakkesearde ik net oer. As ik mei net to folle muoite mar safolle fortsjinne, dat ik der fleurich fan libje koe, wie it my moai genôch.\nDoe wy togearre yn it kantoar yn Wezel stiene, hearden wy, dat der mar ien frege waerd. Foar in stâl fan 17 kei. Fiifenfyftich mark yn de moanne. Wy lotten der om en myn maet krige it. Ik hingele dêr in pear dagen om en doe gong ik der ris wer hinne. En nou waerd der wer ien frege. Ek mar in lytse stâl en sechstich mark yn 'e moanne. Der wie, ljeau ik noch nea safolle yn Dútsklân fortsjinne. Hoe koe Hinke Kaert dat dochs wite?","l":"Fries"},{"n":131394,"r":"KEUNING008205","p":"Wierum","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"TM 3101","d":"A devil banisher's prediction that a man who visits him about a sick child will be attacked by a flock of birds comes true.","i":"S.K.","o":"Heit is ek ris nei G.W. west. In broerke fan my wie siik. Hoe dat fjirder gien is, wyt ik net, mar wol wyt ik, dat W. tsjin heit sei: \"Do komst aenst troch in stik lân, dêr binne in protte fûgels en dy kinne net fan dy ôf bliuwe.\"\nEn it wie ek sa. Underweis roun heit troch in stik greide, dêr sloech hy mei de hannen en mei de pet, hwat hy koe, om de fûgels fan him ôf to hâlden.","l":"Fries"},{"n":43809,"r":"KOOIJMAN0011","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"Because of a dangerous approaching thunderstorm, a priest advises people not to go into cafés along the way: whoever drinks anything will die. They were allowed to go to only one café, and if they dug three spadefuls of earth there, blue flames would shoot out of the ground.","i":"H.K.","o":"Er waren bij ons kerels, die dronken en zo. In ieder café gingen ze opsteken. Op een keer zei de pater in de kerk: \"Ga meteen naar huis. Er is hevig onweer op komst. Die onderweg iets gebruikt, zal niet levend thuiskomen. Bij één café mag je aangaan, bij café De Wit\". Dat was halverwege Bergschenhoek-Bleiswijk. Die pater zei: \"Als je daar drie spitten in de grond doet, slaan de blauwe vlammen eruit\". Ze deden drie spitten in de grond en er kwamen vlammen uit. Later hebben ze daar aardgas gevonden, zo men zegt."},{"n":50575,"r":"KOOIJMAN0029","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A farmer was afraid to have his thatched roof repaired because he saw mice in his barn loft and nowhere else. He believed this was an omen: if he repaired the roof he would fall ill and die.","i":"H.K.","o":"Een boer (1) klimt op een leer naar de schuurzolder. Hij steekt zijn kop boven de zolder uit en hij ziet muizen lopen. Die muizen vluchten weg naar alle kanten, Hij ziet ook een gat in het rietdak. Je weet, hoe een boer is: hij wil een gat gedicht hebben. Toch heeft hij het niet gedaan. Hij was bang, dat hij een ziekte kreeg. Die boer heeft zo'n antipathie tegen dat riet, hij durft het nog niet met een stijlbezem aan te raken. Dat dak vervalt. Iedere keer ligt er weer riet op de zolder. Z'n vrouw zegt: \"Laat het dak toch eens repareren. Voor die vijftig gulden\". Maar die boer zegt: \"Het gaat niet om die vijftig gulden\". Hij wil het voor een ander niet weten. Die boer klimt weer op die ladder. Ziet weer die muizen gaan. Zoek het hele huis maar na, je vindt de muizen niet. Sloop de muren maar, je vindt de muizen niet. Ze zitten in het dak. Maar hij doet het niet (2). Hij zag in die muizen een voorbode. Hij denkt: \"Als ik het doe, ben ik dood\". Dat was een betoverde zolder.\n\n(1) uit Gouderak \n(2) d.w.z. het dak laten maken"},{"n":50652,"r":"KOOIJMAN0112","p":"Ameide","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul can do anything.","i":"H.K.","o":"VOLKSGELOOF IN AMEIDE\nMensen die met de helm op geboren waren, konden alles. In de regel waren het wel bijzondere figuren."},{"n":50679,"r":"KOOIJMAN0139","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"In Oudewater there used to be someone who was born with a caul. That person was put out of the house.","i":"H.K.","o":"Ja, in Ouwater had je vroeger ok iemand, die met de helm was geboren. Hij kon 't in huis niet houwe! Hij mos d'r uit!"},{"n":50902,"r":"KOOIJMAN0203","p":"Benschop","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"If a child was born with a caul and the caul was buried, the child would have a happy and prosperous life. But if the caul was not buried, the child would remain blind, wander over the churchyard at night and foretell funerals.\nParents were often afraid that the doctor would secretly sell the child's caul, since it could protect others against bullets or drowning.","i":"H.K.","o":"Als een kind met de blinde belie geboren was, waren ze vroeger in Benschop bang dat de dokter de helm meenam, stiekum en die verkocht aan iemand die naar Indië ging. Die persoon droeg hem op z'n hart en hij was kogelvrij. Zo'n kind werd dan een blinde baby, omdat die blinde belie niet begraven was. Hij wandelde 's nachts over het kerkhof. Hij zag ook een begrafenis van tevoren. Die met de blinde belie geboren was, was een gelukkig kind. Kreeg voorspoed in z'n leven. Als de helm tenminste begraven wier."},{"n":50913,"r":"KOOIJMAN0214","p":"Benschop","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"TM 4001","d":"Stockings slipping down are an omen of rain.","i":"H.K."},{"n":50914,"r":"KOOIJMAN0215","p":"Benschop","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"TM 4001","d":"If someone with a hunchback comes past the door, it foretells rain.","i":"H.K.","o":"Als er iemand met een bult aan de deur komt, krijg je ook regen."},{"n":51004,"r":"KOOIJMAN0303","p":"IJsselstein","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A girl who wakes up screaming at midnight is said to seem as if she was born with a caul.","i":"H.K.","o":"MET DE HELM GEBOREN\n\nG. van ons die begon altijd 's-nachts om twaalf uur te huile en te gille....Dan zee moeder:\n-'t Lijkent wel, of ze met de helm is gebore! Want die doen dat ok. \nNou, G. was niet met de helm gebore. Maar we hebbe zat met d'r meegemaakt."},{"n":51024,"r":"KOOIJMAN0317","p":"Brandwijk","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"There used to be the Zwarte Jannegies faith, a sect founded by Jannetje Hoodsen. She had many followers and held services full of singing and dancing. These services were sometimes disrupted by opponents. After her death she was venerated as a saint. A ritual with a sheet was said to foretell whether one would be saved or lost in the hereafter.","i":"H.K.","o":"Vroeger had je hier' in Brandwijk 't Zwarte Jannegies* geloof. Zwart Jannegie was een vrouw uit Veenendaal, die had hier een soort geloof opgebouwd. Ok had ze een aanhang. Dan wier d'r een lake gespanne onder de zolder, je most door het luik stappe. Bleef het lake heel, dan kwam je in 't hiernamaals goed terecht. Viel je d'r doorheen, dan was je verlore. Dan kwam d'r een gat in 't lake. Ik denk maar zo, dat het de ene keer een goed laken geweest is en de andere keer een slecht laken.\n\n*Zwart Jannegie, zo noemde men in de streek Jannetje Hoodsen, die een zeer merkwaardige religieuze secte in het leven had geroepen. Het centrum van haar activiteit lag in Polsbroek, vooral daar had ze een grote aanhang. Tijdens de bijeenkomsten ten huize van voorheen nederlands-hervormde of gereformeerde boeren werd er gezongen en gedanst. Het kwam wel voor, dat zulke bijeenkomsten door anders denkenden op ruwe wijze werden verstoord. Jannetje zelf kwam uit Veenendaal. Haar optreden viel omstreeks het eind van de negentiende eeuw. Ze werd als een heilige vereerd, vooral in Polsbroek en omgeving."},{"n":70002,"r":"KOOIJMAN0499","p":"Goudriaan","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"The seventh son was born with a caul and had special powers. He could strijken (heal by stroking).","i":"H.K.","o":"De zevende zoon werd met de helm gebore, hij had bijzondere begaafdhedes. Hij kon strijke."},{"n":70009,"r":"KOOIJMAN0504","p":"Bergambacht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Through the centuries children have been born with a caul. Such children have a membrane over the head at birth, which is removed after birth. According to old superstition the child was normal if the membrane was burned. But if it was stolen by the doctor, the midwife or the maternity nurse, the child had second sight, or had a special abnormality or gift. The membrane was also dried and sold for a high price. According to folk belief, carrying a caul made one bulletproof.","i":"H.K."},{"n":70015,"r":"KOOIJMAN0510","p":"Bergambacht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"An owl screeching in the night means a death. Some people are still frightened by it.","i":"H.K.","o":"Een uil die krast in de nacht betekent een sterfgeval. Daar maken sommige mensen zich nog angstig over."},{"n":70075,"r":"KOOIJMAN0537","p":"Hekendorp","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"If someone was born with a caul, you had to bury the caul.","i":"H.K.","o":"Als iemand met de helm geboren was, moest je de helm begraven."},{"n":70081,"r":"KOOIJMAN0542","p":"Hoogblokland","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"The seventh son was lucky. He was born with a caul.","i":"H.K."},{"n":70086,"r":"KOOIJMAN0545","p":"Hoogblokland","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"Black cats on the road in the evening foretell disaster.","i":"H.K."},{"n":70092,"r":"KOOIJMAN0550","p":"Hoogblokland","v":"Z.-H.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"The seventh son is born with a caul, they used to say in Meerkerk. The caul was then sewn into his shirt or undervest.","i":"H.K.","o":"\"De zevende zoon is met de helm gebore\", zeje ze vroeger in Meerkerk. Die helm wier in d'r hemd of borstrok genaaid."},{"n":70108,"r":"KOOIJMAN0564","p":"Lexmond","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A little brother was born with a caul. The grandmother made sure the caul was buried with the afterbirth. Will-o'-the-wisps are a consequence of children born with a caul. Also, with that caul you were bulletproof in the war. A child born with a caul was called a blinde belie.","i":"H.K.","o":"Een broertie van me is met de helm gebore. Me grootmoeder heb d'r toen voor gezorgd dat 't met de nageboorte begrave werd. Dwaallichies, zee m'n grootmoeder, dat was een gevolg van kindere die met de helm gebore ware. As de dokter de helm gestole had, dan moste die kindere gaan lope in de gedaante van dwaallichies. As d'r een soortgenoot zak maar zegge van zo een begrave werd, dan moste ze hem een dag eerder in de geest begrave. Dan moest je aan de rechter- of an de linkerkant van de weg lope. Dan had je geen last. Anders werd je opzij gezet. Met. die helm was je kogelvrij in den oorlog. Je kon ze ok verkope, maar dat was ten nadele van het kind. Zo een, die met de helm gebore was, die noemde ze een blinde belie."},{"n":70142,"r":"KOOIJMAN0588","p":"Zegveld","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul was said to be a special child.","i":"H.K.","o":"Die met de helm geboren was, dat scheen een bijzonder kind te zijn*."},{"n":70157,"r":"KOOIJMAN0599","p":"Utrecht","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"When a child was born with a caul, people were always afraid that the doctor would take it away. But then the child would lose its mind.","i":"H.K.","o":"As een kind met de helm gebore is, dan ware ze altijd bang, dat de dokter dat zou meeneme. Maar het kind was dan z'n verstand kwijt."},{"n":70294,"r":"KOOIJMAN0725","p":"Polsbroek","v":"Utr.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Those born with a caul can do more than others; they can see a funeral in advance.","i":"H.K.","o":"MET DE HELM GEBOREN\n\nMense, die mit de helm gebore zijn, die kinne meer dan een ander. Die konde van tevore een begrafenis zien, die moeste d'r voor opzij gaan. (Vlist).","l":"Zuid-Hollands"},{"n":129098,"r":"KROSENBRINK00107","p":"Rekken","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"Olde Menert had foretold that Bearnt Winkelhorst's farm would burn down. On 3 May 1943 the farm burned down. The fire was put out with difficulty, but they could not save the horse. At first Winkelhorst would not believe the prediction, but now he did.","i":"G.J.H.K.","o":"Van de boerderi’je van Bearnt Winkelhorst was veurspeld, dat ze zol verbrannen. Twee jaor veur dee tied was ut al veurspeld deur ne Duutsen boer, Olde Menert, den net ovver de grenze wonnen. Den had ut al ezene. Op 3 mei 1943, ton Winkelhorst op ut veane was brannen ut spil af. Ut brannen onwies hard en met möjte konnen ze den hoesraod redden. Maor ut peard verbrannen in den stal, want ze mennen, dat de baas dat met hadde naor ut veane. Winkelhorst had de veurspellinge neet willen gleuven, maor noo wal.","l":"Gelders"},{"n":129102,"r":"KROSENBRINK00202","p":"Neede","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A boy always went to fetch bread on Sunday evening. People thought he could just as well do it on another day. One Sunday he went again, but it had been foretold that he would not reach the bakery. On the way a little man jumped onto his neck and said: 'If you can carry a loaf, you can carry me too.' The boy never reached the bakery and lay ill in bed for six weeks. After that he was startled by everything. One day a child's shirt fell on his back and he ran off. When he ran faster, the shadow of the shirt moved along with him. When he reached a house, the occupants told him it was only a child's shirt.","i":"G.J.H.K.","o":"Ne jonge ging altied op zondagaovend hen brood halen. De leu stotten zich daor an. Hee kon joo wal op ne andern dag gaon. Op ne zondag ging e der wear hen en um was al veurspeld, dat e neet in de bakkeri’je zol kommen. Maor hee ging toch. Onderweggens sprong um zon klein menneken op den nakke en kek um stief in de ogene. Hee kon haoste neet mear veuroet kommen. Ut menneken zea teggen um: Zowaor a’j un brood könt dreagen, dan kö’j mi’j ok dreagen. Den jonge kwam neet in de bakkeri’je en mos zes weake zeek in bedde blieven liggen. \nHee was der zo bange van ewordene, dat e noo veur alles schrok. Op ne keare leep e onder ne dreugedraod hen en ton veel der net un kinderhemd af op ziene rugge. Hee veulen wat achter zich, want ut bleef haöken an ene van de haöken van ziene bokse. En den jonge ging an ut lopen. Hee zoog de schemme achter zich en hoo harder as hee leep, eaven hard leep de schemme van ut hemd met. Drievenat kwam e bi’j un hoes an, waor ze um vrogen, wat of e toch hadde. En daor vertellen ze um, dat e veur un kinderhemd op den löppe was egaone.","l":"Gelders"},{"n":129154,"r":"KROSENBRINK00510","p":"Bredevoort","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"Dore Leutjes could foretell fires in houses. A house on the market in Winterswijk would burn down, and a café on the Kottenseweg. And later she said that seven houses on the Hoogstraat in Aalten would burn down.","i":"G.J.H.K.","o":"Dore Leutjes kon veuroet zeen of der un hoes in brand kwam. Zee veurspellen, dat in Wenters an de markt un hoes af zol brannen en ok un cafe an de Kottenseweg. En later zea ze utzelfde van Aalten, waor an de Hogestraote zövven huze verbrannen.","l":"Gelders"},{"n":129227,"r":"KROSENBRINK00512","p":"Bredevoort","v":"Gld.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A miller's hand once came to the mill near Silvolde. The old hand predicted he would not stay long. The first night, while the new hand was milling, a cat came and stood by him, and he hit it with a flour sack. The cat suddenly began to talk, so he took his knife and chopped off the cat's paw. The cat fled and he put the paw in his bag. The next morning he found the grandmother in bed in the miller's house. She had cut off her finger. The hand gave the paw to the miller, for it was the grandmother who had come to him at night as a cat.","i":"G.J.H.K.","o":"Op ne mölle bi’j Silvolde kwam ne ni’jen möldersknech. Den olden knech veurspellen al wal, dat e daor neet lange zol blieven. Ut zal mi’j is ni’jen of i’j ut daor lange volholdt. Maor den knech was neet bange. Den earsten den besten nach, ton e drok an ut malen was, kwam der ne katte bi’j um. Den knech nam ne mealzak en flearn der de katte met umme den kop. De katte begon opins te praoten en zea: At straks ut olde griezeken maor is kump, dee zal ow wal. Den knech maken zich hellug en nam zien mes, heeuw der met van zich af en sloog de katte ne poot af. De katte schreeuwen en vloog weg. Den poot stok de knech in ziene tasse. Den andern morgen ton e op ut möldershoes kwam, lag de grotmoder in bedde. Tone vroog, wat of eur fealen, zea’n ze dat ze zich slim in de hand esneane had. Ne vinger der knats af. Ton gaf den knech den poot an de mölder, ant ut was de grotmoder ewes, dee ‘snachens bi’j um op de mölle was ekom’ne.","l":"Gelders"},{"n":44118,"r":"KUSTERS000302","p":"Someren","v":"N.-Br.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A fortune teller makes predictions that come true.","i":"C.K.","o":"In Breda dur wónt er een die kan de toekomst vurspelle. Dur heb ik toch ók wel wa aarigs van óndervónne. Ik waar toe voerman op Eindhoven en toe 'k ne keer mi de kaar thuis kwam miste ik ne pak lijne van f85-. De mense mooste die pak hebbe mer je ik ha um nie. Ik ha 't zó nooi en ik weest ók nie wa 'k deran koost doew. Toe zittur ene: \"Naarus\", zeetie, ge moost us nu 'n waarzegster gò\" Ik did evèl nie gèr en ik zi 't tege niemus wont de gistelijke wòu dè nie hebbe\nIk dee nu den Bos en ik weest gin waarzegster woone en 'k durfde 't irst ook an niemuze te vròge. Mèr toe zag ik d'r zo inne stò en die gaf ik e kwartje en ik vroeg of ie 'n waarzegster weest. Je hij weest er een en ie wis me de weg. Ik moost dur veul stròte en kwamp toe bij 'n vrouw die d'r zaat mi 'n dochter. Die dòchter móst irst weg en toe viejt ze de kaart. \"Ge het 'n zwarte vrouw\" zee ze en ik verschoot wont ha gelijk. Min vrouw dè waar toch zo'n zwarte. Ze zag wel dek verschoot en ze zee: \"ge zeet ongerust mer 't kumt allemol goe. Ge zalt alles terugvijne en ge zalt 'n erfenis kriejge. Mer vandaag gó de ge nog nivven 'n lopend watter en ge zalt 't ovend zat thuis komme\". Ik dacht bij m'n eige: \"zat thuis komme dè zal dan toch nie gebeure\" En d'n hillen tijd onderweege ging ik nergens an. Ik kwam langs 't kanaal (dè waar dè loopend watter) en vur Sluis XI ha 'k ne voerman bij me en die moost an bij schipper Lamm","l":"Brabants"},{"n":44831,"r":"KUSTERS000311","p":"Someren","v":"N.-Br.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A prediction that people will fly through the air.","i":"C.K."},{"n":44968,"r":"KUSTERS000408","p":"Someren","v":"N.-Br.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul become geniuses.","i":"C.K."},{"n":46187,"r":"KUSTERS001401","p":"Neerkant","v":"N.-Br.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A prediction comes true that women will one day wear men's clothing and men women's clothes.","i":"C.K.","o":"De profecei zi, dat ur n'n tijd zal komme, det vrouwvolk maanskleer zal draage en 't maansvolk vrouwekleer. En kie, tiggeworrig eest al bekant zoweit. Zo'n profeceien komme uit 't boek van Joannes.","l":"Brabants"},{"n":46328,"r":"KUSTERS001503","p":"Leende","v":"N.-Br.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Whoever is born with a caul is clairvoyant.","i":"C.K."},{"n":46380,"r":"KUSTERS001716","p":"Nederweert","v":"L.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A prediction by someone born with a caul comes true, that a priest will be fetched with a white horse.","i":"C.K.","o":"Wie met den helm op geboren is, ziet in de toekomst. Zo iemand voorspelde eens, dat er spoedig een stervende in de buurt zou zijn, waarvoor men 's nachts 'n priester zou moeten halen. 't Zou niet kunnen, dacht men, want er was niet eens 'n wit paard in de buurt. Toch gebeurde het: een boer verkocht z'n paard in ruil voor 'n witte schimmel. Kort daarop moest men 's nachts een priester halen voor 'n bediening.\n Voor een nachtelijke bediening moesten twee mannen met 'n los paard (wit) naar de kerk. \n Daar stond de sjees waarmee de priester naar de zieke ging. Een der mannen leidde dan het paard op de terugweg; de andere luidde met de bel."},{"n":206948,"r":"KUSTERS003301","p":"Asten","v":"N.-Br.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A witch predicts that a woman will stop laughing.","i":"C.K.","o":"'n Vrouw die met de korf rondging, vroeg aan 'n tante: \"Hi Annemiej niks nodig?\" Vertelster lachte. De vrouw (heks) antwoordde: Nauw laagte ge, mer latter zal d'n tol betald worre\"."},{"n":43082,"r":"WEV000901","p":"Ter Apel","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A man who has to go out at night to see funeral processions sees funerals in advance.","i":"F.W.","o":"Hier laten we de heer Roede aan 't woord.\n\nIk heb al veel meegemaakt.\n'k Heb ook gezworven hier en daar.\nEr is veel fantasie en bangmakerij in de wereld.\nMaar er is meer dan je denkt.\nLuister.\nMijn vader werd geboren te Rolde.\nIn Drente wonen eerlijke mensen.\nWat hij me dan ook verteld heeft, is de volle waarheid.\nAls jongen kwam hij te werken in het veen te Roswinkel, bij de oude Pachter.\nDat was een beste man. Hij had echter iets. Hij kon wat zien.\nDat was erg vervelend, want dan moest hij er 's nachts soms uit.\nHet gaf niet, welke tijd het was; als hij naar iets heen getrokken werd, dan moest hij gaan.\nWaar hij heen ging en wat hij zag, zei hij tegen niemand.\nMijn vader vroeg eens, of hij mee mocht.\n\"'k Zol' t nait doun, mien jong,\" zei de oude, \"huist er nait noar verlangen, das 't ook wat zugst.\"\nMijn vader, die niet bang was, bleef er evenwel op staan.\nEn zo gebeurde het, dat Pachter hem op een nacht wakker maakte.\nDaar gingen ze door de duisternis.\nOp eens zei Pachter:\n\"Daor komen ze aon.\"\n\"Wat komp 'ter aon?\" vroeg m'n vader.\n\"Zugst nait dei liekstoatie? Dei vrouw wordt begroaven. Kiek, dei en dei lopen d'r achter.\"\nMijn vader zei: \"Ik zai niks.\"\n\"Magst bliede um wezen, mien jong. Moar kom 'n beetje aan de kaande, anders wordst van de weg smeet'n.\"\n\nDrie weken later ging de lijkwagen met de genoemde personen langs dezelfde weg."},{"n":45360,"r":"WEV002602","p":"Nieuwe Pekela","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A card reader foretells the future, mainly for unmarried girls. She does not look after her husband. After he complains of a sore leg, someone else sees that there are maggots in the swelling.","i":"F.W.","o":"In ’t veen woonde oude Bedde-Wik, een “wikwief.” Ze kon de toekomst voorspellen door middel van kaarten. Het kostte zeven stuivers. Het meest kwamen vrijgezelle meisjes, die de huwbare leeftijd hadden, maar niet aan de man konden komen.\nHaar man had een slecht leven. \n’t Is toch eens gebeurd, dat er een buurman kwam. De oude baas lag op bed en kreunde: “O, mien bain, mien bain.”\n“Wat scheelt je been?”\n“O, ’t dut zo zeer!”\nNu, buurman heeft eens geholpen en ontdekte een grote verdikking vol met maden. Hij viel meteen flauw.\nJa, in ’t veen ging het raar toe.","l":"Gronings; Standaardnederlands"},{"n":45377,"r":"WEV002903","p":"Vlagtwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"Do not walk through the wheel tracks of a funeral procession that has passed, for then you will see the dead person again.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wanneer er een lijkstoet gepasseerd was, dan moest men niet door het wagenspoor lopen. Want dan zou men de gestorvene weer zien. Als kind meed men die sporen dan ook."},{"n":50518,"r":"WOUDA001501","p":"Heeg","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man born with a caul can foretell who will die soon.","i":"E.W.","o":"Yn Heech wenne in man, Sibbele Attes, dy mei de helm geboren wie. Jouns hinge der faek oer de ûnderdoar to praten mei de buorren. Hy koe krekt fortelle, hwa 't dy wyks stjerre soe. Sa wie der ris in man stoarn. Se praetten der oer. Sibbele Attes seach ris yn 't waer sen sei:“Moarn noch twa!”\nEn it kaem ek sa út!","l":"Fries"},{"n":129833,"r":"WOUDA002206","p":"Workum","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":"TM 3102","d":"A sick woman has been given up by the doctors. A charmer's prediction that the woman will recover and her husband will die comes true.","i":"E.W.","o":"It greatste wûnder, dat ik meimakke ha, wie mei Jantsje Vrolijk. Dy wie yn desimber siik wurden. Se rekke yn Ljouwert yn 't sikenhús. Dêr waerd se opereard. Der waerd spul opstjûrd nei Utrecht foar ûndersyk. De dokters joegen har noch gjin jier, hwant it like net bêst. “It komt hwerom” seine se tsjin de famylje. En it gong lyk as de dokters seinen, al mar achterút. In maert is se al frij min. Doe komt Wopke by ús op in kear; ik leau by in kou. Ik sei tsjin Wopke: “Hoe giet it yn Woarkum?” Hy sei:“ Nou, mei Jantsje sil wol gean, mar Frans!” (Frans wie har man) Dy wie soune mienden wy. Wopke gong wer fut en ik sei tsjin de frou: “Dy man is nou dochs ek wol goed mis.” Mar fjouwer wike letter wie Frans siik en noch fjouwer wike letter nei 't sikenhûs foar ûndersyk. Dêr opereard, of leaver: iepen hawn. Kanker! Yn april, maeije, ha se hjir to gearre lein, elk op in bêd. Wopke kaem stees by Jantsje. De dokter en de famylje seine: “Hwa sil earst gean?” Yn augustus is Frans oerleden en Jantsje is genezen, nettsjinsteande se troch alle dokters opjown wie! Se libbet noch en it is al jierren lyn.","l":"Fries"},{"n":129916,"r":"WOUDA024003","p":"Haskerdijken","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A fortune teller predicts that the village will grow, which has come true.","i":"E.W.","o":"Hinke sei:“Stobbegat (it tsjintwurdige Vegelinsoard) wurdt in greate plaets. Der ride weinen sûnder hynders en der komme greate diken (wegen) mei beammen der lâns. En it wie, doe Hinke it sei, in ûnherberchsum lân, mei petgatten en trekgatten en reidkragen. Der stiene in pear earme turfmakkershûskes. Nou lizze der twa greate wegen, de petgatten bin ynpoldere en it wurdt al in heel doarp.","l":"Fries"},{"n":129918,"r":"WOUDA024008","p":"Haskerdijken","v":"Fr.","y":1962,"c":null,"d":"A card reader was born with a caul, but is cheerful and helps the poor.","i":"E.W.","o":"Hinke wie mei de helm geboren. Se hie it twadde gesicht. Mar se hie altyd wille en die by de earme minsken om har hinne in bulte goed. Har man hjitte Pieter Hamburg.","l":"Fries"},{"n":32447,"r":"CJ126101","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"TM 3109","d":"Piter Poes discovers a witch's wreath in the pillow of someone who is bewitched. Piter predicts that the first person to come to the door is guilty of the witchcraft. Piter advises throwing a bucket of water over the culprit's head. Just as Piter is on his way again, he realises he has forgotten something and returns to the house. At the house he promptly gets a bucket of water thrown over him.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wolter Veenstra wenne by Hústerheide. Der wie by him gauris tsjoenderije. Dan woarde Piter Poes fan Sumarreheide helle. Dy kom op 'e hounekarre.\nOp in kear wie der ek wer ien bitsjoend. Piter Poes hie de kessens neisjoen. Der siet in krânse yn.\nPiter sei: \"De earste dy't hjir oer de drompel komt, hat it dien. Dy mat in ammerfol wetter oer de hûd ha.\"\nDoe rekke Piter Poes fuort.\nMar doe trof it sa raer. Piter Poes hie hwat forgetten en kearde werom mei de hounekarre. Hy kom by de doar.\nDoe krige er sels it ammerfol wetter, dat klear stie, oer de hûd.\nEk in kear hat myn omke fan Feanwâldsterwâl Piter Poes ophelle en doe wipte ûnderweis de hounekarre om. Piter Poes rekke der ûnder.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":210580,"r":"ENGELS002005","p":"Baarlo","v":"L.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A differing opinion on the meaning of being born with a caul.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Met de helm geboren:\nHet begrip “met de helm geboren” wordt soms als natuurlijk geval beschouwd; n.l. dat een kind de nageboorte over het hoofd heeft zitten bij zijn komst. Ik deel die mening niet, en meen, er onder te moeten verstaan, mannelijke personen, waarbij de huis van het geslachtsdeel los zit, en opgestroopt kan worden. Dergelijke mensen zouden beschikken over bijzondere verstandelijke vermogens en hoedanigheden. Ze zouden dus meer verstand hebben als normaal.\n\nGeen omzetting in dialect van het verhaal door Engels."},{"n":210610,"r":"ENGELS002209","p":"Meijel","v":"L.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"A clairvoyant tells in advance what is wrong with a woman, but cannot cure her.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Helderzienden:\nEen dochter van me, die onderwijzeres is, had in haar jeugd veel last met haar maandstonden, en was dan telkens voor enige dagen niet in staat, haar werk te verrichten. De dokter kon haar niet helpen. Ten einde raad ging ze, op veler advies, er mee naar Mevr. Lefèbre in Breda, een helderziende, die zich met genezing bezig hield. Deze vrouw vertelde haar vooraf van A tot Z wie ze was; waar ze woonde, en wat haar mankeerde. Ze gaf haar een kruidenthee om haar te cureren. Het hielp echter geen steek.\n\nGeen omzetting in dialect van het verhaal door Engels."},{"n":209750,"r":"HOL001108","p":"Eck en Wiel","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Those born with a caul are clairvoyant; midwives sell the caul.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen, die met de helm geboren zijn, kunnen in de toekomst zien. Bij Geurt van Kesteren was ook één van de kinderen met dat vlies geboren. Zo'n \"helm\" was een begeerd voorwerp. Vroedvrouwen verkochten het."},{"n":209775,"r":"HOL001208","p":"Eck en Wiel","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Trade in cauls, because people born with a caul cannot be hit in a war.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen, die met de helm geboren zijn, kunnen niet getroffen worden in de oorlog. Daarom was er vroeger een levendige handel in. De bakers verkochten ze voor wel f 300, toen een geweldig bedrag."},{"n":209801,"r":"HOL001314","p":"Eck en Wiel","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"A clairvoyant reveals where lost wedding rings are.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"J v.d. Waal-Kuipers was beide trouwringen (die van haar en haar overleden man) kwijt. Een helderziende in Nijmegen zei precies, waar ze lagen. En daar vond juffr. V.d. Waal ze ook."},{"n":209827,"r":"HOL001411","p":"Kesteren","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul is said to be clairvoyant.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Een lid van de politie vertelde vol trots, dat zijn zoon met de helm geboren was. Zo iemand was helderziende volgens zijn vader. Deze zoon is echter geen bijzonder persoon geworden, verschillende keren is hij met de justitie in aanraking gekomen."},{"n":209849,"r":"HOL001508","p":"Kapel-Avezaath","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul are clairvoyant; whoever owns a caul is bulletproof.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen, die met de helm geboren waren, werden gehouden voor helderzienden. Er werd handel gedreven in die helm, omdat de bezitter er van, niet getroffen kon worden door een kogel. Een soldaat lag eens ergens op een muur te schieten. De kogels vlogen om hem heen, doch hij werd niet geraakt, hij was kogelvrij werd gedacht."},{"n":209879,"r":"HOL001614","p":"Opheusden","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Those born with a caul are clairvoyant; cauls are sold because their owners are bulletproof.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen, die met de helm geboren zijn, zijn helderzienden. Dokters en vroedvrouwen waren er fel op. De helm werd verkocht aan \"hogen\" van onder dienst, want de bezitter er van, was kogelvrij."},{"n":209895,"r":"HOL001629","p":"Opheusden","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Those born with a caul must get up at night to open the churchyard gate for a funeral procession.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Die met de helm geboren waren, moesten soms 's nachts hun bed uit om de hekken van het kerkhof open te zetten voor een begrafenis, die daar moest aankomen."},{"n":209925,"r":"HOL001721","p":"Kesteren","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul can see into the future; taking the caul away makes the child unhappy.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen, die met de helm geboren waren, konden in de toekomst zien. Bakers waren er fel op. Het kind werd ongelukkig, als de helm meegenomen werd. Die er in het bezit van waren, werden helderziend."},{"n":210002,"r":"HOL002013","p":"Maurik","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul sense a death in advance and are bulletproof.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen, die “metom helm” geboren zijn, zijn onrustig, als er iemand op sterven ligt. Deze mensen werden geacht kogelvrij te zijn"},{"n":210004,"r":"HOL002015","p":"Maurik","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"A clairvoyant sees more than ordinary people.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Helderzienden kunnen verschillende dingen zien, die gewone mensen niet zien. Daarom gaat men, als men bv. een proces voert naar een helderziende. Deze wijst de dader aan, zegt, waar buit verborgen is enz."},{"n":210027,"r":"HOL002109","p":"Maurik","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Those born with a caul foresee funerals, are bulletproof and clairvoyant; the caul must be buried, not sold.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Hent de Droetel was \"meten helem\" geboren. Hij moest de hekken van het kerkhof open gaan zetten de nacht voor een begrafenis. Van personen, die met de helm geboren waren, konden sommige in de toekomst zien, niet alle. Iemand, die zo’n \"helm\" had, was kogelvrij. Die vliesjes werden dan ook gekocht voor \"vø.l gelt\". Als de helm van een pas geborene verkocht werd, was het kind ongelukkig. Zo'n helm moest begraven worden."},{"n":210040,"r":"HOL002122","p":"Maurik","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"A clairvoyant foresees fires and deaths and must open the churchyard gates.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Op Valentijn (toponiem) waren een paar personen aan het aardappel rooien: Dorus den Buter, de gebr. Prijs, Hentje Pikman (scheldnaam). Hentje Pikman, die helderziende was, keek, toen de koffie op was, in het kommetje van Dorus in het achtergebleven koffie \"drab\". Hij zei tegen Dorus, dat hij gauw in het vuur zou kijken. En ja: de volgende nacht brandde het ouderlijk huis van Dorus af. Heintje wist, wanneer er iemand sterven zou, hij moest de hekken van het kerkhof open gaan zetten voor een begrafenis."},{"n":210073,"r":"HOL002216","p":"Ochten","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Those born with a caul are clairvoyant; taking the caul away brings unhappiness; owning a caul makes one bulletproof.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Met de helm geboren. Mensen, die met de helm geboren waren, konden in de toekomst zien. Werd die \"helm\" aan het kind ontnomen, dan werd dit ongelukkig. Vroedvrouwen enz. waren er echter gek op. Hoewel dat vlies niet verkocht mocht worden, deden ze het toch. De kopers waren kogelvrij, vandaar dat er veel animo voor bestond."},{"n":131672,"r":"KEUNING012908","p":"Blije","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"TM 3106","d":"A healer's prediction that a sick ox will recover comes true.","i":"S.K.","o":"By de kei, dy in boer hjir op stâl hie, wie ien in greate lijer. It wie in okse. De féarts hie al sein:\n\"Meitsje him mar ôf. Dat wurdt doch neat.\" Nou, wy woenen der wol oan, hwant it bist stonk ôfgryslik.\nMar de boer helle W. der ris by. Dy biharke it bist ris effen en saei: \"It bist is fan 't simmer forklûme.\" Nou, dat koe. Doe sy der in okse fan makken, hie it bist tsjinspartele en wie yn 'e sleat rekke.\n\"Mar jim hoeve der neat oan to dwaen,\" sei W. \"Ankum maeitiid knapt hy hurd op.\" It is in prachtbist wurden.","l":"Fries"},{"n":131724,"r":"KEUNING013802","p":"Koarnjum","v":"Fr.","y":1963,"c":"TM 3109","d":"Belief in witchcraft, wreaths in pillows, people born with a caul.","i":"S.K.","o":"Ja, hjir wienen froeger ek wol bygelovige minsken. Jan Skipper leaude fêst oan tsjoenderij. Dan hienen sy it oer krânsen yn it kessen. En oer minsken, dy mei de helm op berne wienen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":70479,"r":"KOOIJMAN0838","p":"Reeuwijk","v":"Z.-H.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul are clairvoyant.","i":"H.K.","o":"MET DE HELM GEBOREN\n\nMense, die met de helm gebore zijn, die benne helderziend. \nTenminste, dat werd vroeger gezegd.","l":"Zuid-Hollands"},{"n":72514,"r":"KOOIJMAN1073","p":"Nieuwerkerk aan den IJssel","v":"Z.-H.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Those born with a caul are clairvoyant and bulletproof; cauls are stolen to be sold.","i":"H.K.","o":"MET DE HELM GEBOREN\n\nAs je met de helm was gebore, dan had je iets aparts, ik zal maar zegge, ze ware helderziend. Iemand die met de helm gebore was, die kon kijke door een muur zonder gat...ze ware kogelvrij. De helme wiere gestole door de baaksters. Ze wiere duur verkocht!","l":"Zuid-Hollands"},{"n":72606,"r":"KOOIJMAN1118","p":"Zevenhuizen","v":"Z.-H.","y":1963,"c":"TM 4001","d":"When the snails came out crawling, rain was predicted.","i":"H.K."},{"n":72607,"r":"KOOIJMAN1119","p":"Zevenhuizen","v":"Z.-H.","y":1963,"c":"TM 4001","d":"When there was a sun dog in the sky, rain was predicted.","i":"H.K."},{"n":72634,"r":"KOOIJMAN1143","p":"Haastrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul have a little net on their head. In the old days they said the doctor would take it with him because it was worth money. Those born with a caul are bulletproof.","i":"H.K.","o":"Mense die mit de helm gebare binne, die hebbe een netjie op d'r hoofd. Vroeger zeje ze: dat neemt de dokter mee, die probeert d'r munt uit te slaan. Die een helm hebbe, bin kogelvrij.","l":"Zuid-Hollands"},{"n":72650,"r":"KOOIJMAN1156","p":"Oudewater","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"That day labourer also told me that the seventh son has something special. He is born with a caul.","i":"H.K.","o":"Die daggelder heb mijn ok is verteld, dat de zevende zoon, die heb iets aparts, die is met de helm geboren.","l":"Utrechts"},{"n":72658,"r":"KOOIJMAN1164","p":"Oudewater","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Whoever is born with a caul is bulletproof. And if people knew a child had been born with a caul, they tried to steal it.","i":"H.K.","o":"Die met de helm gebore is, die is kogelvrij. As ze wiste, dat 't keind met de helm gebore was, dan probeerde ze die te stele.","l":"Utrechts"},{"n":72688,"r":"KOOIJMAN1191","p":"Blokland","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"There was once a woman who was born with a caul. Some people went to her house in the evening to look under the door. The woman foretold the churchyard for some of them.","i":"H.K.","o":"Je had hier vroeger een vrouw, die was met de helm gebore. D'r ware nieuwsgierige mense, die ginge 's aves naar d'r huissie en die keke dan onder de deur door. Die vrouw voorspelde sommige van hun dan het kerkhof.","l":"Utrechts"},{"n":72704,"r":"KOOIJMAN1205","p":"Blokland","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"My mother once heard noise in the attic and thought it was an omen. We didn't believe it and said it was just the rats. But it came true, for shortly afterwards my sister died.","i":"H.K.","o":"M'n moeder heb me wel is verteld, op een keer hoort ze een lawaai op zolder. M'n moeder dacht: \"Dat is een voorteken\". Wij zeje: \"Ach mens, dat zijn de ratte maar\" . Maar 't kwam toch uit wat m'n moeder dacht. Want kort daarop kwam m'n zuster te sterve."},{"n":72729,"r":"KOOIJMAN1227","p":"Hooge Vaart","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul went roaming at night. If they thought someone was going to die, they would already walk there beforehand.","i":"H.K.","o":"Die ginge 's nachts kuiere die mee diejen helm gebore ware. En as ze nou dochte dat d'r iemand ging sterve, ginge ze al nachts van tevore daor wandele.","l":"Noord-Brabants"},{"n":72738,"r":"KOOIJMAN1235","p":"Drongelen","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"In Drongelen children were also born with a caul. Someone had foreseen the whole funeral in advance. They always have to go outside at night, it is terrible.","i":"H.K.","o":"Mee den helm gebore, ja das in Drongele ok gebeurd. Iemand ha heel.de begrafenis al vooruitgezien. Ze moete d'r 's nachts altijd uit. Dan moete ze naar buite. Das iets verschrikkelijks.","l":"Noord-Brabants"},{"n":72801,"r":"KOOIJMAN1289","p":"Zijderveld","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Whoever was born with a caul was a child of fortune.","i":"H.K."},{"n":72820,"r":"KOOIJMAN1306","p":"Woudrichem","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Those born with a caul have a little hole in their neck by which you can recognise them. And they were bulletproof. If the maternity nurse took the caul away, they were unhappy forever. But if the caul stayed with the person, nothing was wrong.","i":"H.K.","o":"Met den helm gebore, die hadden een gaatje in d'r nek. Daaraan kon je 't zien. As de baakster een helm meenam dan ware ze levenslang ongelukkig. De mensen schuwden 'm. De baakster probeerde de helm te verdonkeremane. Je was kogelvrij. As de helm bij de mens zelf bleef, was er niks an de hand.","l":"Noord-Brabants"},{"n":72846,"r":"KOOIJMAN1329","p":"Rijswijk","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 4001","d":"Very occasionally a weather loach was caught and put in a bottle of water. If it then thrashed about, that foretold bad weather.","i":"H.K.","o":"Vroeger werd de weeraal gevonge. Da was maor heel zelde. Die werde in een fles waoter gedaan. As die weeraol tekeerging, da voorspelde slecht weer.","l":"Noord-Brabants"},{"n":72847,"r":"KOOIJMAN1330","p":"Rijswijk","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 4001","d":"Dew hanging above the ditch, toads crossing the road, or a drop hanging on an arum lily are all signs that rain is coming.","i":"H.K.","o":"As d'r dauw bove de slote hangt, dan krijg je den anderen dag regen. Padden over de weg: regen. Een druppel aan een aronskelk: ook regen."},{"n":72854,"r":"KOOIJMAN1335","p":"Giessen","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"The caul of people born with a caul is always taken away by the doctor.","i":"H.K.","o":"Mense met den helm gebare, die werd door de dokters meegenomen.","l":"Noord-Brabants"},{"n":72865,"r":"KOOIJMAN1345","p":"Moordrecht","v":"Z.-H.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul had a little magic power. They could heal sick people.","i":"H.K.","o":"Mensen, die met de helm zijn geboren, die hebbe een vlies over d'r hoofd. Ze hadde een bietjie tovermacht. Ze konde zieke mense' geneze."},{"n":72878,"r":"KOOIJMAN1357","p":"Sleeuwijk","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 4001","d":"Rain birds predict rain. Rain also comes when the owl calls.","i":"H.K."},{"n":72893,"r":"KOOIJMAN1371","p":"Hagestein","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul could do something special. So could the seventh son.","i":"H.K.","o":"Mense die met de helm zijn gebore, die konde iets bijzonders. De zevende zoon ok."},{"n":72915,"r":"KOOIJMAN1389","p":"Andel","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"Many people were murdered and someone predicted that the murderers would not die a natural death. That all came true: the first was shot dead and another fell out of a tree and drowned.","i":"H.K.","o":"Dat heb een vrouwken uit Veen me wel is verteld. D'r werde ouwe mensen vermoord. En d'r was.een mens, die had een gezicht gekrege en die zee: ,,Deze mense zullen geen natuurlijke dood sterven\". Dat is ok uitgekommen. De eerste is in een ruzie doodgeschote, de tweede is weer op een andere manier gestorve en de derde is uit een boom gevalle en verdronke. Die man had dat allemaal precies voorspeld, bijvoorbeeld: ,,Den diejen en diejen mens zal uit de boom valle\". Volgens da vrouwke is dat waar gebeurd."},{"n":72926,"r":"KOOIJMAN1400","p":"Andel","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 4001","d":"Toads on the road meant that rain was predicted.","i":"H.K."},{"n":125522,"r":"KOOIJMAN1408","p":"Uitwijk","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul are bulletproof.","i":"H.K."},{"n":125593,"r":"KOOIJMAN1471","p":"Poederoijen","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who are born with a caul are bulletproof.","i":"H.K."},{"n":125603,"r":"KOOIJMAN1480","p":"Brakel","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul were bulletproof. The caul had to be destroyed.","i":"H.K.","o":"De dokters waren fel op de helm. Die helm moest vernietigd worden. Ze waren kogelvrij."},{"n":125639,"r":"KOOIJMAN1504","p":"Herwijnen","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Whoever is born with a caul is invulnerable.","i":"H.K.","o":"Wie met de helm geboren is, is onkwetsbaar. De helm moest begraven worden."},{"n":125670,"r":"KOOIJMAN1524","p":"Poederoijen","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul were bulletproof and had the gift of prophecy.","i":"H.K.","o":"Mensen die met de helm gebore waren, die waren kogelvrij. Die ginge 's nachts als iemand gestorven was, de hekken openzetten."},{"n":125706,"r":"KOOIJMAN1538","p":"Haaften","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"When there was shooting during fishing in the old days, those born with a caul were not bothered, because the bullets had no effect on them.","i":"H.K.","o":"Vroeger dan gingen die vissers de Maas op en dan had je van die echte rasstropers en dan werd d'r geschote. Maar die met de helm gebore ware, daar hadde de geweerkogels geen invloed op."},{"n":125707,"r":"KOOIJMAN1539","p":"Haaften","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"If someone was born with a caul, the caul had to be put away. If someone took it out, it could be used to do supernatural things.","i":"H.K.","o":"Vroeger dan werd d'r gezegd, met de helm geboren. De helm werd hier of daar weggestopt. As ze n'm tevoorschijn brachte dan konde ze daar bovenaardse machte mee doen."},{"n":125752,"r":"KOOIJMAN1564","p":"Culemborg","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who were born with a caul could predict a funeral.","i":"H.K.","o":"Dat hoorde je vroeger, je mocht niet op 't wagespoor komme. Dat ware de bleinde belies, die liepe zelf op 't wagespoor. Dat ware mense die ware met de helm gebore, wie de helm was ontstole. As d'r dan iemand slecht was, dan liepe die mense een dag of anderhalve dag vooruit al naar 't kerkhof. Die bleinde belies ginge die mense begrave."},{"n":125753,"r":"KOOIJMAN1565","p":"Culemborg","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"As long as someone had not been buried, the doors could not be shut. It was also the custom after a death to turn the mirror around and stop the clock.","i":"H.K.","o":"Dat heb ik wel is gehoord, dat er iemand in de Betuwe was gestorven en dat er werd gezegd, zolang de dode boven de aarde stond, kon je geen ene deur sluiten. As jonge zijnde in Kuilenburg was het bij een sterfgeval de gewoonte de spiegel om te draaien en de klok stil te zetten."},{"n":125766,"r":"KOOIJMAN1576","p":"Hank","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who were born with a caul had something special about them. They could also heal by laying on hands.","i":"H.K.","o":"[Met de helm geboren:] Da was iets bijzonders, een beetje gelukskind, die deje dan strijke."},{"n":125769,"r":"KOOIJMAN1579","p":"Hank","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 4001","d":"Snails with a lump of mud on their tail meant it was going to rain. The knife grinder also foretold rain.","i":"H.K.","o":"Slakken met een kluitje slik op d'r staart: regen.\nDe scharesliep langs de deur: regen."},{"n":125958,"r":"KOOIJMAN1620","p":"Dalem","v":"Z.-H.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who are born with a caul are lucky.","i":"H.K."},{"n":127467,"r":"KOOIJMAN2123","p":"Moerdijk","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Children who were born with a caul were exceptionally wise.","i":"H.K.","o":"Met de helm geboren: Ingeval dat gebeurd was, dan waren de kinderen bijzonder wijs."},{"n":127515,"r":"KOOIJMAN2147","p":"Drunen","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Napoleon was born with a caul. Until Elba he was always lucky.","i":"H.K.","o":"Mensen met de helm geboren dat waren mensen die het geluk altijd bij zich hadden. Dat was zo algemeen bekend, dat Napoleon met de helm is geboren, maar of hij hem op Elba nog had, dat weet ik niet."},{"n":127544,"r":"KOOIJMAN2162","p":"Doeveren","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"When the cock crows before three in the morning, it is a bad omen for the family where this happens.","i":"H.K."},{"n":127478,"r":"KOOIJMAN2210","p":"Hurwenen","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who are born with a caul see into the dark. They know when someone is going to die. They are children of fortune. The caul had to be buried.","i":"H.K.","o":"Mensen met de helm geboren, die kijken in het duister. Ze weten wanneer iemand sterft. 't Zijn gelukskinderen. De helm moest begraven worden."},{"n":127536,"r":"KOOIJMAN2231","p":"Hurwenen","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Where we lived there was an old man, B. de N. Whenever he stood on a street corner somewhere, the rumour soon went round: within three days there will be a death in the street. For De N. had been born with a caul, and it had been stolen by the maternity nurse, and so now he had to open the gate at night. And then there would be a funeral procession, and anyone who got in the way was pushed aside.","i":"H.K.","o":"Bij ons was er een ouwe man, B. de N., als die ergens op een hoek van de straat stond, dan ging al gauw het gerucht: binnen drie dagen een dode in de straat. Want De N. was met den helm geboren en die was door de baakster gestolen en nou moest hij 's nachts het hek openmaken. En dan was er een lijkstaatstie en die in de weg kwam die werd op zij gezet."},{"n":127581,"r":"KOOIJMAN2238","p":"Wagenberg","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"Once, when three of us soldiers were on patrol at the border, we came into a small café. A woman could predict with a wedding ring when we would get married. One of us was already married and she knew it at once. I would marry when I was twenty-nine, and that came true too. And the other one would marry at twenty-seven, but whether that came true I don't know, because I never saw him again.","i":"H.K."},{"n":127603,"r":"KOOIJMAN2248","p":"Drunen","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"If you are born with a caul, you are fortunate.","i":"H.K."},{"n":127623,"r":"KOOIJMAN2259","p":"Acquoy","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"I experienced that too. I was at a fair in Leerdam. I was seventeen or eighteen. There was a fortune-teller's tent, and there was someone there who could predict everything, from the year on the ten-guilder coin in your pocket to other things like that.","i":"H.K."},{"n":127624,"r":"KOOIJMAN2260","p":"Acquoy","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone who was born with a caul had to go and bury someone three days in advance. He had to get out of bed. They could tie him down, but then he would die.","i":"H.K."},{"n":127630,"r":"KOOIJMAN2265","p":"Heesselt","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul knew the black arts. They were bulletproof. The caul was sold during the war.","i":"H.K."},{"n":127702,"r":"KOOIJMAN2308","p":"Maren","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"When passing the old woman's house, you had to get off the cart and lead the horse by the head. She was born with a caul.","i":"H.K.","o":"Vroeger waren ze daar erg bang van. Als ze langs een boske moesten, dan dacht~n ze dat er een toverheks in zat. Bij ons had je ook zo'n ouwe vrouw langs de weg. Vader zei altijd: Als je daar langskwam, dan was 't zeker, dan gingen ze van de weg af. De mensen die daar langs moesten, die gingen van de kar en ze leidden 't paard bij de' kop, tot ze 't huis voorbij waren. De kinderen mochten niks van zo iemand aannemen. Zulke mensen waren met de helm geboren."},{"n":127735,"r":"KOOIJMAN2338","p":"Kedichem","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone who was born with a caul was very lucky.","i":"H.K.","o":"Dat was zo, als iemand aan een groot gevaar ontsnapt was, of hij had een groot geluk, dan werd dikwijls gezegd: \"Hij is met de helm geboren\"."},{"n":127737,"r":"KOOIJMAN2340","p":"Kedichem","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":"TM 4001","d":"The regenfluiter (rain whistler, a bird) was considered the herald of rain.","i":"H.K.","o":"Hier huist een soort vogel, die noemen ze de regenfluiter. Hoe die vogel werkelijk heet, weet ik niet. Maar met een dichte lucht en krimpende wind kan je hem vaak horen fluiten, een soort eentonig gefluit. Hij werd beschouwd als de aankondiger van regen."},{"n":127742,"r":"KOOIJMAN2344","p":"Tull","v":"Utr.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who were born with a caul had firm faith in it.","i":"H.K.","o":"Je had mensen die met de helm waren geboren. Die stelden daar zo'n vast vertrouwen in, de mensen van vroeger. Kijk eens hier, ik had een broer van mijn moeder en die was ook met de helm geboren. Dat waren aparte mensen."},{"n":127750,"r":"KOOIJMAN2351","p":"Alem","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 4001","d":"When it had been dry for a long time, we were glad to see the knife grinder come by the door. That foretold rain.","i":"H.K."},{"n":127791,"r":"KOOIJMAN2381","p":"Zevenbergschen Hoek","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"If someone is lucky, they were born with a caul. Also bulletproof in the war.","i":"H.K.","o":"Als iemand gelukkig is, die is met den helm geboren. Voorts kogelvrij in de oorlog."},{"n":127799,"r":"KOOIJMAN2384","p":"Raamsdonk","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"When someone was lucky: he was born with a caul.","i":"H.K."},{"n":128053,"r":"KOOIJMAN2388","p":"Lith","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul are lucky.","i":"H.K."},{"n":127818,"r":"KOOIJMAN2450","p":"Brakel","v":"Gld.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Whoever is born with a caul has foresight, is lucky and is bulletproof.","i":"H.K."},{"n":127826,"r":"KOOIJMAN2458","p":"De Moer","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who are born with a caul have foresight, are bulletproof, and are very gifted and intelligent.","i":"H.K."},{"n":128083,"r":"KOOIJMAN2536","p":"Lith","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Whoever is born with a caul is lucky and bulletproof.","i":"H.K."},{"n":128096,"r":"KOOIJMAN2548","p":"Lith","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who are born with a caul are lucky and have foresight.","i":"H.K."},{"n":47497,"r":"KUSTERS004016","p":"Helmond","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"Saying based on a prediction at the arrival of the first train.","i":"C.K.","o":"In 1866 kwam de eerste trein. 't Stationsplein stond vol volk te wachten. Stabel had er een herberg en voorspelde: \"'t zal laat worre\" Inderdaad kwam de trein uren over tijd. Nog zegt men in Helmond:\"'t zal laat worre zee Stabeltje.\""},{"n":207754,"r":"KUSTERS004703","p":"Milheeze","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"Predictions of the construction of a canal and a railway.","i":"C.K.","o":"De profecei zee: dat er water zal komen op de grens tussen Brabant en Limburg; in de laatste oorlog is daar 'n kanaal gegraven. Ook dat de rijtuigen vooruit zouden kunnen zonder paard maar met behulp van vuur. 'n Boer redeneerde:\"dè wil ik wel us ziej, dè m'n kaar vuruit zal gò as ik er u vuurke onder stook\" Toch gebeurde het want de spoorlijn Eindhoven-Venlo werd aangelegd en die rijtuigen gingen vooruit zonder paard"},{"n":207779,"r":"KUSTERS005211","p":"Aarle-Rixtel","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 4001","d":"Toads become frogs and predict rain.","i":"C.K."},{"n":206994,"r":"KUSTERS005601","p":"Mierlo","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"Prediction of carriages that run without horses.","i":"C.K.","o":"Aan de openbare school was 'n hoofd en 'n onderwijzer. Alle jongens gingen er naar school en ook enkele niet-katholieke meisjes. 't Hoofd vertelde: Er zal 'n tijd komen, dat de rijtuigen zonder paard over de straat gaan. Er zal wél 'n koetsier bij zijn, die de rijtuigen kan laten lopen zoals hij wil. Onder den bok van de rijtuigen zal 'n bak zijn vol flessen en door de kracht van die flessen gaan de rijtuigen vooruit."},{"n":206995,"r":"KUSTERS005602","p":"Mierlo","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"A pope's prediction, which came true, that the weapons would fall from the hands of Napoleon's soldiers.","i":"C.K.","o":"Rond 1884 was Verteller op kostschool op St. Louis in Weert. Iedere week was er 'n wandeling en iedere maand 'n grote wandeling. Voor onderweg kreeg iedere jongen dan 2 sigaren. \nBij zo'n wandeling had Verteller in Ell bij Weert 'n oude man ontmoet, die de tocht van Napoleon naar Moskou had meegemaakt. Die oud-soldaat had gewezen op de voorspelling van de Paus, dat de wapens van Napoleons soldaten uit hun handen zouden vallen. Dat was letterlijk gebeurd. Vervolgd door de Russen waren veel soldaten van Napoleon in de Berezina verdronken; door de barre kou en door bevriezing van ledematen kon niemand nog de wapens hanteren."},{"n":207006,"r":"KUSTERS005701","p":"Mierlo","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"Prediction of flying wagons and flying horses through the air.","i":"C.K.","o":"Er werd voorspeld: er zullen vliegende wagens en vliegende paarden door de lucht gaan."},{"n":207015,"r":"KUSTERS005803","p":"Mierlo","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"Predicting that there will be carriages without horses.","i":"C.K.","o":"'n Oude voorspelling zei: er zullen rijtuigen zonder paard over de wegen gaan."},{"n":207023,"r":"KUSTERS005907","p":"Mierlo","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 3102","d":"Clairvoyants heal burns and bleeding, among other things.","i":"C.K.","o":"In Geldrop zijn helderzienden. Die kunnen genezen van brandwonden, bloedingen enz."},{"n":207044,"r":"KUSTERS006011","p":"Mierlo","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"Prediction of flying machines, and that boys and girls would wear the same clothes.","i":"C.K.","o":"Vroeger werd voorspeld: \"er zalle vliegmesiene dur de locht vliejge\" en nu zeggen ze, dat er 'n weg wordt aangelegd naar de maan\nEr zal 'n tijd komen, dat jongens en meisjes niet meer uit elkaar zijn te kennen en nu is 't al zo, want de meisjes zijn net eender gekleed als de jongens."},{"n":207090,"r":"KUSTERS006613","p":"Mierlo","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone who is born with a caul becomes powerful.","i":"C.K."},{"n":207092,"r":"KUSTERS006615","p":"Mierlo","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"Experiences with a clairvoyant and a healer that undermine belief in their gift.","i":"C.K.","o":"De 1° vrouw van Verteller had kanker en lag daarvoor in Eindhoven in het ziekenhuis. Met haar foto ging hij toen naar Mevr. Héberlée (helderziende) in Breda. Ze ontving hem niet omdat hij tevoren niet had aangevraagd. Daarna bezocht hij 'n genezer in de Peperstraat in Woensel (Eindhoven). Die bekeek de foto, zei, dat de vrouw ernstig ziek was maar nooit in het ziekenhuis zou komen. Toen geloofde hij er niet meer in."},{"n":207225,"r":"KUSTERS007811","p":"Heeze","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"Prediction that wagons will travel through the air and wagons will run without horses.","i":"C.K.","o":"De profecei zee: \"er zalle wagens dur de locht rijen en er zalle wagens zonder perd over de weg vare.\"","l":"Brabants"},{"n":207234,"r":"KUSTERS007905","p":"Heeze","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"Trust in a clairvoyant with a healing gift.","i":"C.K.","o":"Vertelster had veel vertrouwen in de helderziende Mevr. Héberlée uit Breda, die nu 'n paar jaar dood is. Lang geleden heeft die dame haar precies verteld, wat ze mankeerde en wat haar pijnen betekenden en sindsdien heeft ze nergens meer last van gehad"},{"n":207238,"r":"KUSTERS008003","p":"Heeze","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"Prediction that people will travel through the air in carts.","i":"C.K.","o":"Johannes van Leliëndaal voorspelde: \"er zullen mensen met wagens door de lucht gaan\" (vliegtuigen)"},{"n":207288,"r":"KUSTERS008410","p":"Geldrop","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Whoever is born with a caul will have good fortune.","i":"C.K."},{"n":207301,"r":"KUSTERS008421","p":"Geldrop","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"Prediction of the car, the train and the aeroplane.","i":"C.K.","o":"De profecei zee, dat er wagens zouden komen zonder paard en dat de mensen door de lucht zouden vliegen."},{"n":207359,"r":"KUSTERS008910","p":"Geldrop","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":"TM 3109","d":"A heksenkrans (witch's wreath, a clump of feathers) in a pillow is a bad omen.","i":"C.K.","o":"Soms vond men 'n krans in bed. Dat was 'n slecht voorteken van onheil door toedoen van 'n heks."},{"n":47596,"r":"KUSTERS04103","p":"Milheeze","v":"N.-Br.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"Stina was clairvoyant. She was also a cunning thief: by a trick she stole half a pound of coffee beans.","i":"C.K.","o":"Stina was ook helderziend. Eens was Stina in een winkel en vroeg een half pond koffiebonen. Ze liet ze in ’n bus schudden, die ze “in de slip” hield. Ze ontdekte dat ze geen geld bij zich had, deponeerde de bus op de toonbank en zou straks terugkomen. ’t Werd avond maar Stina kwam niet. De bus op de toonbank bleek leeg, ze had geen bodem dus Stina had d’r koffiebonen rustig in d’r slip (schort) meegenomen."},{"n":208486,"r":"LINSSEN004412","p":"Nunhem","v":"L.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A person born with a caul predicts the next death and a disaster.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"XII. Wie met de helm geboren was, zou in de toekomst kunnen zien. \nEen vriend van de grootvader wist te vertellen wie de volgende overledene zou zijn in het dorp. Een spoorman uit Weert zou de watersnood van 1953 hebben voorspeld."},{"n":45644,"r":"WEV004006","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"A man frightens others by asking them to take over his made-up gift of seeing lijkstaties (phantom funeral processions).","i":"F.W.","o":"Nu zal ik je vertellen, dat er vroeger ook veel verteld werd om anderen bang te maken. De verteller zelf was dan niet bijgelovig, maar de hoorder wel.\nLuister maar eens.\nZelf ben ik als kwajongen echt benauwd geweest. In Sellingerbeetse woonde Harm Hinnerk. Hij vertelde me:\n“Ik gung lestdoags hail vrou in ’t veen in de Valterblokken. Op de dreve kwam ’k ’n vrou tegen. Zai reerde. Ik zee, wat is d’r mens, hindert joe wat of hebben ie schele?\nOch man, zee ze, ik mout d’r voak oet ’s mörgens, dan zai ’k liekwoagens en zo; ’k heb ’t al joaren könd en nôn wil ’t er aigenliek wol geern of.\nOch jong, ik kreeg zo mit ’t mens te doun. Dou heb ’k man zegd; ik wil ’t wol van joe overnemen, kan dat?\nJoa, zee ’t wief; ik goa op ain knai liggen, ie goan achter mie stoan en kieken dan tussen mien vingers deur.\nIk dee dat en wat zag ik dou ? Ain wit hondje. En van dat ogenblik of kan ik nou van alles zain.\nMoar ja jong, ik bin ook al weer old en ’k wil d’r geern weer of. Wost doe ’t van mie overnemen? Dan moust ook even over mien scholler deur de vingers kieken. Wolt dat?”\nIk was zo bang geworden, dat ik gauw zei: “Voor geen honderd gulden.”\nLater hoorde ik, dat oale Harm Hinnerk het verhaal verzonnen had, maar er meer dan een de schrik mee op ’t lijf had gejaagd. Voel je wel, de hoorders dachten toch innerlijk, dat het kon.\nOok wel volwassen mensen waagden het niet Harm Hinnerk van zijn z.g."},{"n":45647,"r":"WEV004007","p":"Jipsingboertange","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":null,"d":"Fear in a man who is asked to become the successor of someone who can see lijkstaties (phantom funeral processions) and can bewitch cattle.","i":"F.W.","o":"Dat is al lang geleden, maar nu iets over bijgeloof van jongere datum. \nMijn broer is ook een grappenmaker. Graag neemt hij de mensen er tussen. Nog dit jaar kreeg hij het twee keer klaar door spannend te vertellen grote volwassen kerels bijgelovig te krijgen. \nOp een feestavond hier in Jipsingboertange vertelde hij: “Oal Jan Oarends mout d’r ’s nachts voak oet. Dan lop hai deur de Beetse en zug doden en liekwoagens. Dan komen d’r mensken bie hum, of hai ’t vai bezetten wil. Man Jan is zo old, hai wil geern, dat ’t ain ander ’t overnemt. Hai hef mie ’t al vroagd, man ’k duur d’r nich op aan. Zol ’t nich wat veur die wezen, Wilm?”\nDit vroeg hij aan de gastheer.\nMaar deze werd wit om de neus en zei: “’k Wil d’r niks mit te moaken hebben.”\nDe man durfde beslist niet."},{"n":41136,"r":"WEV004701","p":"Blekslage","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Opinion that there is a lot of nonsense among the stories, but that more exists than people think. Voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of a death when a man born with a caul walks past a house at night.","i":"F.W.","o":"Wat is nô biegeleuf? Vrouger was t’r meer dan nô, dat is wol zeker. En toch bestèèt d’r meer dan hail wat mensken denkt. Ik heb in de Beetse woond en mien vrou komp oet Onstwedde; wie hebt dus al veul verhoalen heurd. D’r zal wol ’n bult onzin bie west wezen, man ie mouten nich alles biegeleuf nuimen. Door hè-je beveurbeld veurloop. \nWel mit de helm geboorn is, kan veuroet kieken. Door hè-jè dai rooie S. in Onstwedde. \nMien schoonmoeke har glad ’n hekel aan ’t kerel, as ’e veur ’t hoes langs gung. Bie nacht dan, goud verstoan. Ie können d’r wiz op aan, dat d’r ’n staarfgeval kwam. Dat is nô gain flauwekul. De man har d’r zölf vreselk last van. Asmits welterde e zuk deur ’t gres. \nAs ze de helm man opbaargd hadden, was ’t wol goud goan, man mensken zegt, as dai helm votsmeet’n wordt, dan wordt ze spoukkieker. Of ’t woar is? ’k Leuf ’t aal.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":43283,"r":"WEV006004","p":"Smeerling","v":"Gr.","y":1963,"c":"TM 4302","d":"A hare in the wheel track in the morning is an omen of a bad day. Remedies for measles, gout, sores and swollen breasts.","i":"F.W.","o":"Biegeleuf\nJoa, dat bestön; zeg man zo umstreeks 1900 nog. \nDoar ha-je oal Theodoor; hai zag ja letterlijk altied en overal spookn. As e s mörns mit peerd en woagen vot gung noar t land en hai zag n hoase in d woagnspoor loopn, dan gung e beslist weer noar hoes. Want dan wördt n slechte dag.\nTeegn mezzels -mazelen- namen d olle vroulu n puutje schoabekeudels. Dai wörn in hait woater oetkookt en t nat dronkn kinder op\nWel last van jicht har, luip mit n kastanje in de buutse. Ik denk, dat dr nog wol zuks binnen.\nOp n zwele -zweer- möz n leevndige kikker legd worn.\nOp zwelnde borstn bie n vrou möz n smeersel van vet en nog wat.\nIn aal geval möz dr wat bie weezn oet n snoukekop.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":210098,"r":"HOL002311","p":"Kapel-Avezaath","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul are clairvoyant; those who possess a caul are bulletproof.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen die met \"de helm\" waren geboren, waren helderzienden, als ze de helm behouden hadden. Had men hun die helm ontnomen, dan werden ze ongelukkig. Het gevaar, dat hun die ontnomen werd, was groot, daar er veel vraag naar was en dus de prijzen er voor hoog waren. Vroedvrouwen, bakers verkochten die voor veel geld aan officieren; hadden die zo 'n vliesje bij zich, dan waren ze kogelvrij."},{"n":210099,"r":"HOL002312","p":"Kapel-Avezaath","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":null,"d":"A clairvoyant foresees the bombing of Rotterdam.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Helderzienden zien dingen, die nog moeten plaats hebben. Een meisje in Rotterdam had het bombardement al van te voren gezien, maar zij had niet over haar \"gezicht\" gesproken. Dit doen helderzienden nooit. Of zij het niet \"magge zegge\"?"},{"n":210120,"r":"HOL002413","p":"Opheusden","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul see everything.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen, die met de helm geboren waren, konden \"alles\" zien. (Meer werd er niet van gezegd)"},{"n":210176,"r":"HOL002617","p":"Tiel","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"TM 2901","d":"What happens to children born with a caul; possessing a caul makes one bulletproof.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Een kind, dat met de helm geboren was, kon in de toekomst zien. Werd de helm verkocht, dan werd het kind ongelukkig. En er was veel ambitie voor deze helmen, want wie er één in zijn bezit had, was kogelvrij. Zij waren hoog in prijs en als de vroedvrouwen er kans toe zagen, verkochten zij die vliesjes."},{"n":210189,"r":"HOL002630","p":"Tiel","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"TM 4001","d":"Seeing a hunchback is an omen of rain.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Bultenaars hoorden tot de van God getekenden. Als men een bultenaar zag, voorspelde dit slecht weer."},{"n":210205,"r":"HOL002714","p":"Ochten","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"TM 2901","d":"The owner of a caul is bulletproof; whoever is born with a caul is clairvoyant.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Dirkje den Hartog moet met de helm geboren zijn. Bakers waren gek op die vliesjes. De dokter haalde de helm er af en liet die begraven, maar bakers verkochten hem. Wie zo'n helm in zijn bezit had, was kogelvrij, daarom waren soldaten er gek op. Mensen, die er mee geboren waren, waren helderzienden, konden dus zien, wat er in de toekomst zou gebeuren."},{"n":210224,"r":"HOL002733","p":"Ochten","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":null,"d":"Prediction on seeing the first stork.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Zag men de eerste ooievaar in de lente vliegen, dan zou men dat jaar vlug zijn. Zag men die zitten dan lui."},{"n":210229,"r":"HOL002802","p":"Varik","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"TM 4905","d":"Dancing will-o'-the-wisps are an omen of bad weather.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"dwa.lixtr werden wel gezien op het stuk land tussen Dick Warners en Wildemans, aan het begin van Varik gelegen. Zag men deze dwa.lixtr dan meende men, dat er slecht weer op til was. De lichtjes dansten op en neer en gingen heen en weer. Van meelokken etc. wist men niets."},{"n":210251,"r":"HOL002907","p":"Varik","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul are clairvoyant; possessing a caul makes one bulletproof.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen die met de helm geboren waren (medom helmkr), konden in de toekomst zien. De helmen werden verkocht aan soldaten, want wie zo'n helm in zijn bezit had, was kogelvrij, maar de kinderen, aan wie ze ontnomen werden, werden ongelukkig."},{"n":210318,"r":"HOL0032012","p":"Dodewaard","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Removing the caul from a newborn means removing its clairvoyance; a person born with a caul foresees events.","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Als de helm aan een pasgeborene, die er mee ter wereld was gekomen, werd ontnomen, dan werd hem daardoor de helderziendheid ontnomen.\n[Na 23] (Toevoegen bij 12) Martinus van Ingen was met de helm geboren. Hij kon van te voren alles zien\". Zelf had hij op deze bijzondere gave van hem geen acht geslagen, maar iemand uit zijn omgeving had deze wel opgemerkt. Deze maakte er Van Ingen op attent"},{"n":210317,"r":"HOL003210","p":"Dodewaard","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Those born with a caul are clairvoyant and see lijkstaties (phantom funeral processions).","i":"A.R.H.","o":"Mensen, die met de helm geboren waren, waren helderzienden. Zij zagen ook de \"lijkstaties\" soms trekken in de donkere avond. Zij zagen, wie er achter de lijkwagen gingen, van welke kant die kwam, van wie de paarden waren, die er voor liepen en zij hoorden ook het getrappel van de paarden."},{"n":128103,"r":"KOOIJMAN2565","p":"Dongen","v":"N.-Br.","y":1964,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul have foresight, are lucky and are bulletproof.","i":"H.K."},{"n":207390,"r":"KUSTERS009203","p":"Nederweert","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":"TM 3109","d":"A child will die if the wreath in its pillow grows closed.","i":"C.K.","o":"Als er 'n krans in 't kussen zit en die groeit dicht, dan gaat het kind dood."},{"n":207398,"r":"KUSTERS009301","p":"Nederweert","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":null,"d":"Making a cross with water from a pit, and the prediction that a church will come there.","i":"C.K.","o":"Waar nu de kerk staat, was tevoren 'n stuk land met bulten en kuilen. Dikwijls stond er water in die kuilen. 'n Gek, die er dichtbij woonde ging er dan heen, maakte 'n kruis met water uit zo'n kuil en voorspelde: \"Hier zal iets heiligs komen\""},{"n":208737,"r":"LINSSEN006911","p":"Ell","v":"L.","y":1964,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Those born with a caul are lucky in everything.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Van kinderen, die met de helm geboren waren, werd verteld, dat zij in alles geluk zouden hebben."},{"n":22508,"r":"TINNEV162","p":"Didam","v":"Gld.","y":1964,"c":null,"d":"Conversation between G. Bisseling, M. Hendriksen and W. van der Heyden. The Slakweg from ten Benzel to the church is called that because it was made of iron slag. The Zonderweg was supposedly once called Zondaarsweg (Sinners' Road), because sinners were taken along it to the Smachmigoor to the stake. Aant van der Heyden, the narrator's father, had second sight: he foresaw the school at Loerbeek before it was built, as well as the house on the Kerkdijk where Harmsen lives.","i":"A.T.","o":"18 november 1964.\nG. Bisseling: Ik bun hier gebore. Wi'j harren een heel olderwets huus, waorien veur ien de kamer nog een gebint stong geliek as bi'j de boeren achter ien huus steet; ien de schuren en zo. Wi'j harren ook nog allemaol bedstèje. Deze plaats hiette de Köölse Stèèj; de vrachri'jers reje van Köle tot Amsterdam. Gi'j konnen hier oaveral iesderslak vinne. Daor hemme ze de weg van ten Benzel nao de kerk van gemaak; die nume ze toe de Slakweg.\nIen Bèèk hék bi'j den Benzel 't male geleerd; toe buk wiejer 't land ien gegaon. Ik geleuf dak de eerste fiets ien Bèèk het gehad; zon höltere; ik kwam duk op de kop ien de graaf terech. Wi'j waren der arg op um der op te rammele; mao dat ging nog zo gemakkelijk niet.\nIk hét al dukker geheurd dat de Sonderkolk dreug is komme te staon toe der een put is gegrave bi'j 't bouwe van 't tolhuus.\nM. Hendriksen: Peter Meisters zei dat de Zonderweg eigenlijk de Zondaarsweg hiette. Oaver de Zondaarsweg brochte ze met twee begeleiders een zondaar nao de Smachmigoor, nao de brandstabel of zukke dinge. De grave van Bergh harre vroeger die rechte gehad. Wi'j hemme nog een schedel van de Smachmigoor ien de kas staon; die hét Meisters daor gevonde.\nW. van der Heyden: Mien vader, Aant van der Heyden, zag van alles; hij wis van alles. Hi'j het toe ook gezien dat ien Loerbèèk een school kwam. Hi'j was helderziende.\nM. Hendriksen: Bu gi'j der niet b","l":"Liemers"},{"n":130248,"r":"BIJLSMA001012","p":"Scharsterbrug","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":null,"d":"Predictions by a fortune teller that come true.","i":"T.B.","o":"Op 'e Gerdyk lei alear in skipke, dêr't \"lytse Knille\" yn wenne. Hja hjitte Kornelia Modderman, en koe wiersizze. Hja sei Oord syn beppe oan dat der in feest by harres komme soe, hja seach dat de minsken de doarren út stiene. In skoftsje letter stoar beppe en dêr kaem gâns folk op tasetten.\nTsjin Oord syn mem sei lytse Knille, dat hja deis thús bliuwe moast. Hja moast in pûdtsje mei kamfer ûnder de drompel lizze, dan koene de dieven der net ynkomme. It wie de famylje Hylkema, dy't dêr wolris oer de flier kaem, en dy hiene earne oars ek wolris ynbrutsen. Hja stielen ek wol koalen út 'e tún.\nJehannes hylkema wenne dêr tichte by. Hja kamen net wer.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130253,"r":"BIJLSMA001103","p":"Joure","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":null,"d":"Prediction of the end of the world when women wear men's clothing and carts drive without horses.","i":"T.B.","o":"Foar in sâwntich jier sei Roel Moedt, âld arbeider by de Hooghiemstras, \"as de froulju manlju's klean oandogge en de weinen sûnder hynders ride, dan rint de wrâld nei de ein\".","l":"Fries"},{"n":130360,"r":"BIJLSMA002509","p":"Bakhuizen","v":"Fr.","y":1965,"c":null,"d":"A rumour that the priest is the father of a pregnant unmarried woman's child is strengthened by his sermon about the mote and the beam. Three men accuse him and the priest is transferred. At his farewell he predicts consequences for the men during their lives. Each of the three men meets with misfortune. Later it turns out the child was fathered by a married man.","i":"T.B.","o":"It sil sa'n foech 85 jier lyn wêze, dat der to Bakhuzen twa âld fammen wennen. It wiene huodtsjemaksters. Op in kear die it bliken dat de iene bifalle moast. De pastoar Steenhof, dy't der noch al ris oer de flier kaem, waerd foar de takomstige heit oansjoen. \nYn dy snuorje preke de pastoar oer de splinter en de balke - tige tafallich mûlk -, itjinge it praet bisterke.\nDe pastoar waerd troch trije mannen oanklage, en it einbislút wie, dat er oerpleatst waerd. By syn ôfskie sei er dat it de lju der nei gean soe. Dêrby tsjutte er net op it hjirneimiels, de hel of sokssahwat, mar hie it oer it ierdske libben. It kaem ek sa út. De iene krige by in ûngemak in stik fan de tonge, de twadde rekke by joun yn in sleatsje, in groppe wie it eins mar, en fordronk, de trêdde krige in biroerte en stoar.\nLetter kaem it út, dat in âld boer de heit fan it bern fan de huodtsjemakster wie. Dy boer hie by syn frou in bern, dat alhiel gjin forstân hie. It wie in jonge, dy't yn in apart hokje efter traljes hâlden waerd.","l":"Fries"},{"n":210801,"r":"ENGELS003708","p":"Blerick","v":"L.","y":1965,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who are lucky are said to have been born with a caul.","i":"G.G.E.","o":"Met de helm geboren:\nZo noemde men vroeger iemand, die altijd geluk in het leven had; of ook wel iemand, die een buitenkansje kreeg.\n\nGeen omzetting in dialect van het verhaal door Engels."},{"n":49664,"r":"GENDT034","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"AT 0671D","d":"On Christmas Night animals can talk. A farmhand who does not believe this keeps watch above the stable on Christmas Night. At midnight he hears the horse say that the farmhand will soon die. To prevent this, the farmhand goes to work for a farmer in a village further on. When he has to take an animal to his old master for this farmer, he falls from the cart and breaks his neck.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Da alle diere ien de kersnach ien de stal opstoan en da ze ieder iend’r eigen toal dan God love, heggellie duk zat gehörd. De koeie bulke [loeien], de scheup blère, de geite blentere, de pèrd hinneke, de vogels zinge en ieder gebruuk zien eige toal. Mar, wa ’k oe nou vertel, zuj nog wel nooit gehörd hemme. Ik heb ’t van mien moeder. Ze het vroeger es gediend bé’j ’n boer veuron ien Duitsland. Dor proate ze hos net ender es ien Gendt. Op ’n kersoavend zèj den boer: “Vannach um twoalf uur zullen de beeste ien de stal wer gon proate”. Mar den bouwmeister* gleufdenet nie. Hé’j doch: “Ik zal vanoavend loat op de zolder boven de pèrd de wach houe”. Dor sloeg de klok twoalf uur. Hé’j luusterde schèrp. Ja heur, de pèrd stonnen op. Hé’j hörde ze stampe op de vloer. En ’t ene pjed zèj duidelijk tegen ’t aandere :“Wé’j bringe onzen bouwmeister ok gaauw nor ’t kerkhof”. Den bouwmeister schrok hèvig. Hé’j wier bar bang. En smiddags on toffel zèj hé’j tegen den boer: “Ik wou wel es veraand’re van den diens. Ik het hier al ’n helen hort gewes. Ik wou ok wel es bé’j ’n aander gon kieke”. “Mar kjel”, zèj den boer, “wa kumtat onverwachs. Ge beval meen goed. Wurrum zoj goan? We kunne toch bes opschiete. En ik heb er ok nooit iets van gehörd, dat ’t ou hier nie nor de zin zou zien”. “Ja, da ’s wel woar. Mar ’n mins wel es wadaanders. Ik wou toch mar es uutkieke”. Wurrum dattie eigelijk weg wou, zè","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":49713,"r":"GENDT079","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"AT 0671D","d":"It used to be said that horses could talk at twelve o'clock on Christmas Night. Two farmhands want to play a joke on another farmhand and tell him the horses will talk. This farmhand sits with the horses at night, where the other two also hide. At midnight the farmhands pretend to be the talking horses and predict the other farmhand's death. He is terribly frightened. The next day at breakfast the farmhands tell him it was a joke.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Ze zèje vroeger: “Ien de kersnach um twoalf ure proate de pèrd”. D’r ware op ’n boerderé’j drie knechs. De kleine knech was ’n grappemaker, die de grote knech er wel es tusse noom. Op ’n kersoavend zèj tège den bouwmeister: “Nou moj toch es heure. Vannach zulle de pèrd wer gon proate”. Den bouwmeister doch: “Dor mot ik toch es meer van wete”. En hi–j gieng ien de kortkis onder den bak van de pèrd ligge. De twee aander knechs hadde da gezien en gienge ien de stal achter de perd zitte, ien ’t duuster. Midden ien de nach, toe ’t twoalf uur sloeg, zèj de kleine knech tege d’n aandre: “We hemme nou twee zondage, eerste en tweede kerstdag, en dan zal den bouwmeister wel begrave worre”. “Ja”, zei d’n aandre, “da zal er wel van komme”. Den bouwmeister ien de kis hörde da en doch datte pèrd on ’t proate ware en hé’j wier zo bang, dattie uut de kortkis sprong en gieng lope. ’s Mèrs bé’j de boteram hemme de twee grappemakers mar verteld, da zé’j de sprèkende pèrd ware. En ze hemme er lotter same nog duk schik over gehad.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":50196,"r":"GENDT172","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1965,"c":"TM 4001","d":"Custom of sprinkling salt on Christmas Night into twelve onion skins, one for each month of the year, and checking on Christmas Day which were dry and which wet, as a weather forecast.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Opte Polder hadde vroeger inkele ouwe minse nog ’n aander gebruuk ien de kersnach. Ze nome twoalf lookdöpkes [rokken van uien] en zette die soaves loat, vör middernach, op toffel. Die döpkes mosse de twoalf monde van ’t joar ondujje. Van links nor rechts vör januari tot december. Ekkes vör of um twoalf uur wier d’r ien ielk döpke ’n bietje zout gedoan. Opten erste kerstdag smèrs wier dan noagegoan, welke döpkes dreug ware. Doaruut kosse ze zien, ien welke monde van ’t né’je joar ’t nat of dreug zou zien, dus ok of we bijvoorbeeld ’n natte of ’n dreuge zommer zoue kriege.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":207545,"r":"KUSTERS011005","p":"Asten","v":"N.-Br.","y":1965,"c":"TM 2902","d":"Gypsies can predict the future.","i":"C.K.","o":"Als zigeuners op 'n uithoek kwamen, waarschuwden de boeren elkaar; men hield dan alle deuren gesloten. Ze konden de toekomst voorspellen maar men gaf ze weinig kans."},{"n":207629,"r":"KUSTERS011707","p":"Asten","v":"N.-Br.","y":1965,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Being born with a caul brings luck.","i":"C.K."},{"n":207630,"r":"KUSTERS011708","p":"Asten","v":"N.-Br.","y":1965,"c":null,"d":"Elderly people talk about omens and prophecy.","i":"C.K.","o":"Oude mannen praatten ooit langdradig over \"vurteekes\" en over \"de prófecy\".","l":"Brabants; Standaardnederlands"},{"n":209011,"r":"LINSSEN009807","p":"Koningsbosch","v":"L.","y":1965,"c":"TM 2902","d":"A gypsy woman predicts who will and who will not become someone's wife.","i":"G.H.L.","o":"Zigeuners hielden zich vroeger nog al eens op in afgelegen oorden, zoals Koningsbosch. Het was in de droge zomer van 1911, dat verteller in aanraking kwam met een zigeunerin, die hem de toekomst voorspelde. Hij was toen nog niet getrouwd, maar de zigeunerin wist hem te vertellen, althans te omschrijven, met welk meisje hij zou trouwen, het-geen volgens hem ook later gebeurd was. Zij gaf ook de omschrijving van een ander meisje, op wie hij destijds ook een oogje had, maar met wie hij niet zou trouwen."},{"n":35612,"r":"VVUNL073","p":"Keent","v":"L.","y":1965,"c":null,"d":"A woman predicts that the barn her husband is building against her wishes will never be finished, and one night it collapses.","i":null,"o":"Heks doet schuur, door haar man gebouwd, invallen \n\nTrui van Waterschot kon het niet goed verdragen dat haar man een schuur bijbouwde achter hun boerderij. Tegen iedereen zei ze dat die schuur nooit zou afkomen. En inderdaad, toen ze bijna af was, viel ze op een nacht in en ze is nooit meer terug opgebouwd."},{"n":35648,"r":"VVUNL109","p":"Keent","v":"L.","y":1965,"c":null,"d":"My sister-in-law predicted that I would break my leg. Because I knew she could predict the future, I kept still, but at night I fell out of bed and broke my leg.","i":null,"o":"Waarzegster voorspelt iemand dat hij zijn been zal breken\n\nMijn schoonzuster kon ook de toekomst voorspellen. Ik moet zeggen dat alles wat ze zei altijd uitkwam. Ze zei eens tegen mij dat ik spoedig mijn been zou breken. Ik was dan ook erg voorzichtig, want ik wist dat ze kon voorspellen. 's Avonds echter viel ik uit mijn bed en had ik mijn been gebroken en het is nooit meer volledig genezen."},{"n":35805,"r":"VVUNL266","p":"Stramproy","v":"L.","y":1965,"c":null,"d":"A woman predicts that the plague of rats will soon be over, and the next day they lie dead in the brook.","i":null,"o":"Heks doodt ratten in een beek \n\nZe vertellen van de heksen allerlei kwaad, maar de mensen vergeten dat ze soms toch ook veel goed gedaan hebben. Zo zat de beek bij ons achter de tuin vol ratten en het stonk verschrikkelijk. Bij ons kwam er een vrouw die men overal de heks noemde en toen ik haar over de beek sprak, zei ze dat het spoedig over zou gaan. En inderdaad, de volgende dag lagen de ratten dood in de beek. We hebben de beek toen zuiver gemaakt en we hebben nooit geen last van ratten meer gehad."},{"n":44282,"r":"WEV008405","p":"Nieuw-Weerdinge","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":null,"d":"A skipper hears knocking in the hold where his wife's coffin stands. When the coffin is opened, she turns out to be still alive.","i":"F.W.","o":"Ik zel joe aigen belevenissen vertellen; alles is woar.\n\nLag ’n moal ’n schip bie ons veur ’t huus. Toun sturf de vrou van de schipper. De kiste wör onder in ’t schip hen zet.\nOp ’n oavend heurt ’t schipper klopn, doar onder. Hai duurt nait kiekn, moar woarschouwt de mensen aan de wale.\nDei goan noar de kiste, moaken dei open en zain den, dat de vrou leeft. Echt woar gebeurd, want schipper en de vrou hebben nog joaren veur ons voarn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":44560,"r":"WEV009205","p":"Onstwedde","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Whoever is born with a caul can see the future. If the caul is buried at once, nothing is wrong.\nA woman keeps six cauls of children who died.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mit helm geboorn.\nKiek, wel mit helm geboorn is, kan veuroet zain; hai wordt spuikkieker. As de helm onmiddelk in de grond stopt wordt, is dr niks an de hand, man anders worden t bezundere mensn.\nEn leuft ais, dat dat nich zo mooi is.\nDou k in dainst was, kwam ik wol ais bie n vrouw in hoes, dai zes helms in de kaaste lign har. Dai wazzen van zes kinder, dai allemoal overleden warn; man de helms har t oal mens opbaargt. Zai wol ze mie wol ais zain loatn, man door har ik ja gain belang bie.\nt Wazzen dreuge vliezn. In de vörm van n haalve bolle.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":45034,"r":"WEV009809","p":"Emmen","v":"Dr.","y":1965,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Whoever is born with a caul can see the future; knows the outcome of war; later the idea arose that they can also predict other events.","i":"F.W.","o":"Helm.\nWie met een helm geboren was, verstond de kunst om vooruit te kunnen zien. Het werdzo verklaard; dat woordje helm.\nWie zo n helm bezat, wist in geval van oorlog de afloop van een veldslag: winnen of verliezen. En soldaten dragen immers helmen; later zei men, dat de bewuste personen ook andere zaken wisten te voorspellen."},{"n":43504,"r":"WEV011104","p":"Sellingen","v":"Gr.","y":1965,"c":"TM 4001","d":"Roosters that crow at nine o'clock in the evening or later predict rain and wind.","i":"F.W.","o":"As de hoanen s oavends om n uur of negen of loater nog kraaien, den kriegn ie gauw regen en wind.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":130392,"r":"BIJLSMA002903","p":"Ouwsterhaule","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"A man knows when he will die; it has been foretold to him.","i":"T.B.","o":"Der wenne alear in âld man to Oldeouwer - Ten Hoeve hjitte er - dy wist hwannear er stjerre soe. Dat wie him oansein.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130393,"r":"BIJLSMA002904","p":"Ouwsterhaule","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"A warning not to walk in the middle of the road in the evening, because one may meet a funeral procession.","i":"T.B.","o":"Idzenga syn beppe sei, jouns net midden op 'e dyk rinne. Der kin jin in lykstaesje tsjin komme.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130507,"r":"BIJLSMA004704","p":"Luinjeberd","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"People who have lost something go to the fortune-teller. A fortune-teller's warning and prediction comes true: she told a fisherman to put a good lock on the fish well, because someone who is not a fisherman would offer a batch of fish to the fish buyer.","i":"T.B.","o":"Hinke Kaert fan Nijbrêge wie in bikend wiersizster. As de lju dêrre hwat misten, dan mar even nei Hinke. Op in moarn soe Noppert syn heit to fiskjen, dat wie syn fak, doe 't Hinke sei: \"Sille wy earst even yn it kofjetsjok sjen, Piter\". Dat gie oan en Hinke sei: \"Dou meist wol in goed slot op 'e kear dwaen, immen, dy't net fisket, hat mear mûdhoun as dou\".\nHeit gie mei fisk nei de keapman op it Fean, en dêr bliek, dat syn sweager gâns mûdhoun brocht hie, wylst dy net iens fiske.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130508,"r":"BIJLSMA004705","p":"Luinjeberd","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"A fortune-teller's prediction comes true that a maidservant did not steal a missing silver milk spoon, and that the spoon will be found again.","i":"T.B.","o":"By de forfeander Durk Knol wiene se in sulveren molkleppel kwyt, nearne to finen. Men hâldde de faem derfoar. Hinke sei, dêr is neat fan oan, de faem is sa earlik as goud. Dan en dan sille Jim de leppel werfine. It wie ek sa; mei it húshimmeljen kaem er wer boppe wetter.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130509,"r":"BIJLSMA004706","p":"Luinjeberd","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"A fortune-teller's prediction comes true that a farmer will find his stolen goods with someone from whom he buys cattle.","i":"T.B.","o":"By Durk Hogenberg, boer to Nijbrêge wiene ris twa fuorken en in harke út it lân stellen. Hinke waerd rieplachte en dy sei, dat Durk by immen komme soe om fé to keapjen en dêr soed er syn ark werfine. Folle letter soed er by immen yn it Skar in pear kninen keapje. Yn it hok seach er syn ark stean.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130510,"r":"BIJLSMA004707","p":"Luinjeberd","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"A fortune-teller's prediction comes true that the figure one meets on the way is harmless.","i":"T.B.","o":"Noppert syn beppe hat ek ris by Hinke Kaert west. Hinke sei: as jimme nei hûs gean (Lúnbert) dan sil jim op 'e Spitsendyk hwat tsjinkomme, mar dêr hoege jim net bang foar to wêzen\".\nIt kaem ek sa út; op 'e Spitsen dyk (dyk fan Nijbrêge nei Lúnbert) seagen se hwat oankommen. Doe 't it tichterby kaem, bliek it in geit to wêzen.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130606,"r":"BIJLSMA006304","p":"Goingarijp","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"A woman with cat's eyes can see in advance who will die.","i":"T.B.","o":"To Eagmaryp wenne destiids in minske, dy hie katte-eagen. Hja koe foarútsjen en sei yn it foar as der ien stjerre soe.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130608,"r":"BIJLSMA006306","p":"Goingarijp","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"TM 4001","d":"Weather predictions for rain and for dry weather.","i":"T.B.","o":"As de mol wrot, komt der wetter. As it koper blinkt, kin men droech en helder waer forwachtsje.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130615,"r":"BIJLSMA006503","p":"Raerd","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"A prediction comes true of what the lot that exempts one from military service will look like.","i":"T.B.","o":"Stellingwerf syn heit hat boer west to Raerd, Tersoal en Easterwjirrum. Hja ha ris in mier hawn út Nijehoarne. Doe 't Teake Stellingwerf lotsje moast foar de militaire tsjinst, sei dy mier tsjin him: \"Astû in lot nimst, dêr ’t it rinkje yn it midden omhinne sit, dan bist frij. Krijst ien dêr ’t it oan in ein sit, dan bist oanlotte.\"\nHy hie der rekken mei hâlden en wie frij lotte.","l":"Fries"},{"n":130642,"r":"BIJLSMA007102","p":"Beetsterzwaag","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"Noise made by birds is an omen of an event.","i":"T.B.","o":"Op 'e hoeke to Langwar koenen de fûgels soms heislik to kear gean. Men sei dan wol, dat der it ien of oare barre soe.","l":"Fries"},{"n":12248,"r":"CJ000912","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"A woman can predict the future with cards.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tjille Kaert wenne op 'e Gerdyk yn in lyts skipke. Sy koe kaertlizze. Wibe hat der ris hinne west. Syn nicht Pytsje wie by him.\nWibe wie hwat oansketten en sei: Dit is myn faem. In kreas frommes, net? (Mar dêr wie neat fan oan) Tjille sei: Dat is jou faem net en likemin jou frou. Ik wol jo de kaert net lizze, jo meitsje my hwat wiis. Sy hie it dus wol goed sjoen.\nTsjin Pytsje sei se: Jimme hûs stiet fol brulloften. Pytsje sei: Wy trouwe noch lang net. Mar Tjille krige gelyk.\nDoe ha ik en Doutsen nei har ta west. Sy sei tsjin my: Der wennet in lange frou njonken jo. Dy is altyd jaloersk op jo en wol jo tsjinwurkje. Mar jo matte net bang foar har wêze, hear. (Dat kom út, sa'n ien wenne der njonken ús)\nTsjin Doutsen sei se: Jimme matte dy beam by jimme hûs útroegje. Under dy beam sit in protte jild. (Mar dat ha se noait dien)\nDoe't wy fuort gongen, sei se noch tsjin Doutsen: Jo matte oppasse. Jo krije in skuor yn 'e rok. Wy wisten net hwat se dêr mei bidoelde. Mar koarte tiid dêrnei moest Doutsen trouwe. Dat hat dy skuor yn 'e rok west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12281,"r":"CJ001117","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"A card reader sees in the cards who will and who will not become his wife. That comes true, as does the prediction that he will soon be home.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw ris by in kaertlizter yn Dútslân west. Sy lei seis kaerten op 'e tafel en dêr luts se ien út.\nDoe sei se: Dû hast kunde oan dy en dy faem. Mar dy krijstû net. Doe hast ek noch kunde oan in oare faem, dy is sa en sa. Dy krijst ek net. It wiif datstû krijste sjocht der sa en sa út. Dû bist net in lang skoft mear fan hûs ôf, dû bist gau thús.\nDat mei dy fammen, dat kloppe, mar dat lêste dêr hie se it mis mei, tochte ik. Ommers Fryslân lei in hiel ein fan Dútslân en ik wie noch lang net fan doel om nei hûs ta. Mar it kom wol sa't se sein hie.\n14 dagen letter bin 'k thús kaem. Troch ûnforwachte omstannichheden moest ik nei hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12482,"r":"CJ001804","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"It has been predicted that someone will one day drown in a certain lake.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Liuwepoel (yn 'e Harkema) mat noch ien fordrinke. Dêr wurdt altyd foar warskôge. 't Is in kear sein woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12483,"r":"CJ001805","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"It has been predicted that someone will drown at a certain spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foar sa'n 60 jier seinen se dat der by Hoogkerk-Vierverlaten ek ien forsûpe moest. Dêr woarde doe ek altyd foar warskôge.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":12522,"r":"CJ002009","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"Lanterns stand somewhere. That is a prediction of what will later come there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Skieding, yn 'e buert fan 'e Wilhelmina-hoeve, wienen wylde lantearnen. Dat tsjutte op hwat dat letter gebeure soe. Foartjirmerije. Mar hwat, dat wyt ik net mear.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16133,"r":"CJ004618","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"When Sytse van der Hoek had died, the narrator's mother sewed the little pillowcase he was given in his coffin. Because she had no scissors at hand, her mother bit off the thread. The neighbour woman predicted that she would now lose all her teeth. That came true.\nHer mother also combed the hair of the dead, but the comb always went into the coffin. For if someone later combed his hair with that comb, it would all fall out.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't Sytse van der Hoek stoarn wie, naeide mem oan it kessensloopke, dat er meikrige yn 'e kiste. Omt der net in skjirre by de hân wie, biet mem de tried ôf. Doe sei de buorfrou: \"Dit is net bêst, al dyn tosken rekkest kwyt.\" It is ek útkaem. Stadichoan rekke se tosken kwyt en in pine yn 'e mûle, dat se útstien hat! Letter hat se it restant der útskuorre litten.\nMem die sok wurk faek as der guon forstoarn wienen.\nSy kamde de liken ek it hier út. Mar dy kaem kom mei yn 'e kiste. Hwant as letter ien syn hier mei dy kaem útkamde, foel it hier allegear út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16265,"r":"CJ004913","p":"Noardburgum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Jan Jager was born with a caul. He always slaughtered a lot and then went salting in the evening. A funeral procession sometimes passed him then.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jan Jager is mei de helm geboaren. Dy slachte altyd in bult. Hy gong dan jouns wol to sâltsjen. En doe is him wolris in lykstaesje passeard.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16266,"r":"CJ004914","p":"Noardburgum","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Whoever is born with a caul is bulletproof.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":16830,"r":"CJ006217","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who are born with a caul are bulletproof.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":16935,"r":"CJ007111","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"A man is bulletproof because he is so pious. During the war a mate asked him one evening whether they were still bulletproof. He then predicted that his mate would die the next day and he would survive. That came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Karst Westra wie kûgelfrij. Dat kom trochdat er sa froom wie. Hy wie yn 'e oarloch, dat is wol hûndert jier lyn. Op in joun sei syn maet tsjin him: \"Soenen wy noch wol kûgelfrij wêze, Karst?\" Doe sei Karst: \"Dû leiste moarn tsien ûre.\nMar ik stean hjir yn 'e namme des Hearen Heare.\"\nHy seach it yn in fisioen. 't Kom ek sa út. De oare moarns tsien ûre sneuvele syn maet. Alles om him hinne woarde deasketten. Mar hy is levend wer thús kom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16992,"r":"CJ007503","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"A card reader once tells the future of the narrator and his two friends, when all three have a girl: for the narrator the girl is only a passing fling, the others will marry their girls. That is how it turned out. She also predicted that another friend would marry a widow. That came true as well.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Japiks Fokje koe kaertlizze. Hja wie ôfkomstich fan 'e Harkema. Manlju kinne tsjoene, plichte se to sizzen, froulju net.\nIk haw ris nei har ta west mei twa kammeraten. Wy hienen alle trije in faem. Sy sei tsjin my: 't Is mei dy mar in skarreltsje, mar de oare beiden sille mei har fammen trouwe. De kaerten wiisden dat út. It is sa ek útkaem. Ik ha dy faem mar even hawn. Myn maten trouden mei de fammen dy't se doe hienen.\nTsjin in oare kammeraet fan my sei se ris: Dû krigest ien mei in lape op 'e rôk. Hy is mei in widdou troud (Boorsma hyt er; hy wennet yn 'e Westerein).","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":16993,"r":"CJ007504","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"A card reader once predicts that someone will knock at the narrator's home. That night a woman does indeed knock. Her husband has gone mad and has to be tied up. When the cards are black, the card reader predicts that a death will come. She also sees that the family will soon receive money and that the narrator will get a house with poplars around it. Everything came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Thomas Klare koe ek kaertlizze. Sy wenne by 't spoar. Earder hie se yn Houtigehage wenne. Op in kear kaem se by ús. Sy sei: Hjir is kloppe of hjir wurdt aenst kloppe.\nDoe kloppen se yn 'e nacht by ús. In suster fan Griet har man hie 't yn 'e holle krigen. Dy moest fêstboun wurde.\nKlare sei ek noch, wylst se de kaerten skodde: It binne allegear swarte kaerten. Is der hwat by jimme? It is allegear rouwe. Der stjert skielk ien.\nDat is ek gebeurd.\nDoe sei se: Omfierrens wennet ien, dêr matte jimme sinten fan ha. Dy sinten krije jimme skielk. Dat kaem èk út.\nDoe sei se noch tsjin my: Jo krije in eigen hûs en dêr stean hege beammen om hinne. En dat duorret net sa lang mear. Dat kloppe ek. Dat is dit hûs woarn, dêr ha popelieren om hinne stien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17007,"r":"CJ007605","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"Two men hear a loud sound of shooting near a farm. When they go to look, there is nothing to be seen. Later the Germans held exercises at that spot. It was a foreshadowing.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek in kear, 't wie noch foar de oarloch doe kaem ik mei noch ien de wei del. Wy roannen achter de pleats fan Piter Zuidema oan 'e Wâlddyk. Doe hearden wy ynienen sjitten. Dat knettere en rikketikke krekt as woarden der fyftich mitrailleurs ôfsketten. \"Duvel, hwat woarde ik dêr kjel,\" sei 'k. \"De bonken binne der my dôf fan. It komt fan 'e pleats.\"\nWy gongen der hinne, mar der wie neat to sjen. Letter ha de Dútsers dêr oefene. 't Wie foartsjirmerij. (Ik ha om 'e hiele pleats hinne west, de doarren sieten fêst. Ik sei: \"Hjir is neat.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17085,"r":"CJ008013","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"Four of the narrator's mother-in-law's children died. Each time, beforehand, a magpie came to sit chattering on the windowsill. That was the announcement of death.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"By myn skoanmem binne fjouwer bern stoarn. Elke kear fan tofoaren kaem der in ekster yn 't finsterbank dy bigoun to skatterjen. Dat wie de tiding fan 'e dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17111,"r":"CJ008303","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Taeke Syngsang in Garijp was born with a caul.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":17116,"r":"CJ008308","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"TM 3106","d":"In Suameerderheide people go to Wopke the exorcist in Kûkherne and not to Piter Poes on the Heide. Once the narrator's mother and another woman are given a potion to take home. Wopke predicts that the bottle will break on the way. That happens. According to Wopke, the new potion will arrive intact. That happens too.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As men yn Sumarreheide nei in duvelbander moest gong men nei Kûkherne, net nei Piter Poes, hoewol dy op 'e Heide wenne.\nMem en noch in minske ha us nei Wopke ta west om in drankje. Wopke sei: \"Hjir ha jim in drankje, mar ik tink net dat it hiel toplak komt.\"\nUnderweis bruts it fleske.\nDoe gongen se wer nei Wopke ta. Sy krigen wer in drankje. Wopke sei: \"Nou komt der jim niks oer, pak op.\"\nSy kommen feilich mei it drankje thús.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17321,"r":"CJ008509","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"If someone has stabbed another with a knife and the blood stays in his clothes, he will die.\nFokke Pander stabbed someone. His wife cannot get the blood out of his clothes. She predicts that he will die. That happens too.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As se ien stekke mei 't mes en 't bloed giet net út dyselde syn klean wei, dan giet er dea. Fokke Pander hat us ien stutsen. De frou wosk syn klean. Mar it bloed woe der net út. Doe sei se: \"Hy giet dea.\" Hy is ek dea gong.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17462,"r":"CJ009309","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"TM 3101","d":"A man has a sick child. He goes to an exorcist to fetch a remedy, because the child is bewitched. On the way the potion grows hotter and hotter. On the way the man meets the apparition of his mother, who tries to take the potion from him. The exorcist had predicted this; it is part of the witchcraft, so that the remedy would not reach the child.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wenne hjir op 'e heide in man, dy hie in siik bern. Hy gong nei Wopke ta fan Kûkherne. Dy joech him guod. Wopke sei: \"Dat guod wurdt hoe langer hoe hiter ûnderweis. Tink derom en biwarje it goed. Der sil dy wol ien tomjitte komme, hwant jimme bern is bitsjoend. De flesse woardde sa hyt, dat hy koe him op 't lêst hast net langer daeije. Doe wied er al op 'e Langewyk. En doe kom syn eigen mem him tomjitte.\n\"Jonge, bistû hjir?\" sei se.\n\"Ja,\" sei de soan, \"ik bin hjir. Mar men moest hinne gean en neuk dy yn 'e Langewyk. Ast myn mem net wieste...\"\n\"Och jonge,\" sei se, \"ik doch dy neat.\"\nMar hja koe hast net fan 't drankje ôfbliuwe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":17659,"r":"CJ010617","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Some children are born with a caul on. If it is pulled downwards, the child never sees anything. But if it is pulled upwards, they have to see everything. No wonder those cauls are so heavy. The caul makes you bulletproof. Even if 25 men shoot at you with their rifles, they cannot shoot you dead.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der binne wol bern, dy wurde mei de helm geboaren. Ik bin der sels ien fan en ús heit ek. As se de helm nei ûnderen lûke, krije dy bern noait hwat to sjen, mar lûke se him nei boven, dan matte se alles sjen. Dy helms binne ôfgryslike djûr. En dat is neat gjin wûnder. Hwant as steane der fiif en twintich man tsjin jin oer mei in laden gewear en dy wolle jin deasjitte, as men sa'n helm yn 'e bûse hat, dan is men kûgelfrij, dan kinne se jin noait sjitte.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19422,"r":"CJ012903","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"A woman could always predict that she would get visitors.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik slepte as bern wol us by minsken yn Twizelerheide. Dy frou wist de dingen altyd fan tofoaren. \"Der komt aenst ek ien\", sei se. Dan hie se de doar al in skoftsje fan tofoaren heard. Soks kaem altyd nei.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":19425,"r":"CJ012906","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"A man predicted the death of a healthy, very strong relative. Three weeks later that man died. The same person then predicted that when everyone gathered after the funeral, someone would stand by the chimney. And when the minister was speaking, he would hold on to the mantelpiece. That came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn heit hat nou fjouwerensawntich jier wei west. Ik wie goed alwe jier doe't er stoar. Trije wiken foar syn dea sei Knjillis Veenstra tsjin ús mem: \"Dû hâldst Fokke net lang mear.\" En doe wie heit doch noch sa soun as in fisk. Hy krige krampkolyk en hy wie sa soun en sa dea. It wie in keardel as in beam en izersterk. Hy wie noch gjin seisenfjirtich jier âld.\nDoe't er stoarn wie, sei Knjillis-om: \"Hwannear't er op 't hôf komt en it folk forieniget him by jimmes yn 'e keamer, dan giet der ien by de skoarstienmantel stean, dy hâldt him dêr sa lang oan fêst as dûmny oan 't wurd is.\"\nDat is krekt sa útkaem. Hy hie dat fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20151,"r":"CJ017304","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"TM 3103","d":"Two men visit a card reader, but they do not believe the predictions at all. They are blindfolded and may take a coin, but the men refuse. They are then given a magic note that they cannot get rid of; burning or burying it does not help. The note keeps coming back. Only throwing it into the rye helps, because rye is holy.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wienen twa man by in kaertlizter. Mar se leauden net hwat it minske sei. Se seinen: \"Dit is hjir neat wurdich.\" Doe blyndoeke it minske de beiden en brocht se yn in oare keamer. Dêr leinen allerhande wikseldaelders op 'e tafel. Dêr koenen se elk ien fan meinimme. Mar de beide maten wegeren. Doe krigen se elk in briefke mei. Mar dat briefke koenen se noait kwyt wurde. Smieten se it yn it fjûr, it lei in setsje letter wer op 'e skoarstienmantel. Bidobben se it yn 'e groun, it kom wer foar 't ljocht. Mar doe treau ien fan 'e twa it yn it brea, doe wie it foargoed fuort. Hwant brea is heilich.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20673,"r":"CJ020715","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man who was born with a caul often had to get up at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Skoanheit wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest der wol gau us ôf as er op bêd lei. 't Wie hast altyd yn 'e nacht. Dan moest er sjen. Hindrik Pitstra hiet er. Hy wenne oan 'e Langewyk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27419,"r":"CJ065413","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1966,"c":null,"d":"The day after giving birth to a stillborn baby, the mother predicted that she would die too. That same night she died. The baby was buried with her in her coffin. A white cloth was laid over the coffin.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oardel jier en in wike neidat ús Gees geboaren is, soenen wy nei ús wurk ta. Doe't wy fuort gongen, sei ús mem: \"Nou is 't myn tiid ek.\"\nDeselde deis stoar se. De nachts fan tofoaren hie se in lyts dea popke krigen. Sy woarde mei 't bern bigroeven, togearre yn ien kiste. Der kom in wite pakdoek oerhoeks oer de kiste to lizzen. Sa stie dy op 'e boerewein. It gebeurde yn septimber 1903. Hja wie doe fjouwer en tritich jier âld.\nHja hie der in foargefoel fan hawn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":41527,"r":"OIRSCHOT000602","p":"Heeze","v":"N.-Br.","y":1966,"c":"TM 2902","d":"A gypsy who can predict the future cannot do so if one stays a few metres away from him.","i":"A.v.O.","o":"ZIGEUNER \n't Is in café de Zwaon geburd. 'n Kameraod en ik kwame 'ne heer tege, zonne rondzwerver, zoiets as 'n zigeuner, die kos over de hele levensloop voorspelle. Hij vruug ons: zak jouwe levensleup veurspelle? Da kunde gij nie, zin ik, ik wit zeker da ge 't nie kaant. Hij begos te praote. Ik zee: daor is gin woord van waor. Daor begos ie tege m'n kameraod ook, over de liefde en al. We komme in 't café, 'n potje bier vatte; en hij begos hier ok te veurspelle. Toen zei ene tege mij: Dan moette jouwe levensloop ok us laote verklaore. Toen zei de zigeuner of zoiets was ie, de rondzwerver,: tege hem begin ik nie. Ge moet er ok altij 'n paor meter van af blijve staon; dan kunne ze 't nie.","l":"Noord-Brabants"},{"n":130054,"r":"VERHOEFF000504","p":"Strijen","v":"Z.-H.","y":1966,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who were born with a caul, or who possess one, are bulletproof.","i":"J.V.","o":"Als je met de helm geboren was, was je kogelvrij, maar dan moest je die helm zelf hebben. De bakers probeerden zo’n helm te pakken te krijgen, want die kon je voor veel geld verkopen aan legerofficieren."},{"n":43704,"r":"WEV012005","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1966,"c":"TM 3108","d":"Nightmares and how tangles form in horses' manes; an omen of marrying someone; meeting black cats and donkeys means bad luck.","i":"F.W.","o":"Mit de peerden was ook wel es wat. Dat hef mien voar zulf nait mitmoakt, moar weer heurd van ollere mensn; dat is nou al over honderd joar leden. Dei hail olle mensn zeden, dat er nachtmerries bestunden. Dei kroopn s nachts deur sleudelgoatn of glievn en klommen op de peerden. Zai klattern bie de maonen omhoog, woordeur de daiern den vlöchtn in de moanen kreegn.\nHai geleufde zuk soort dingen nait.\n\nWel geleufde hai weer aan andere dingen. \nZo, en hai mainde t, zee hai: \"As ie aine in t woater drievn zain in joen verbeeln, dus nait echt, den goan ie loater mit zo'n persoon trouwn.\"\n En t zel wel zo weezn, want hai hef mien mouder in t woater zain, zunder dat ze dr werkliek in lag.\n\nHai woarschouwde veur zwaarde katn en ezels. \nAs ie op pad wazzen en ie kwamen ain van dei daiern inteegn, den konden ie rustig weer noar huus goan, want anders zol t slechte dag worn. Ezels kwammen in dei tied nog wel es veur, net zo goud as ossen veur de ploug of de wupkoare.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":18092,"r":"CJ011414","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":null,"d":"A woman once predicted that a child of the neighbours would soon be in the churchyard. A short time later a neighbour girl fell ill, and she died in hospital.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear sei skoanmem tsjin my: \"Der komt yn 't koart in bern fan ús buorlju op 't hôf. Ik ha 't al sjoen.\"\nKoarte tiid dêrnei woarde ien fan 'e famkes siik. Sy rekke nei 't sikenhûs ta. It bern kom dea wer thús.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20109,"r":"CJ016908","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"When a child is born with a caul, the caul is quickly hidden away from greedy doctors. A caul is worth money, and doctors are keen to sell it on.\nA soldier born with a caul can never be shot dead: he is bulletproof.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De dokters binne gleon op 'e helms. As der ien mei de helm geboaren wurdt, dan moffelje se dy helm gau wei. Hwant dy helms binne jild wurdich. Dy kinne se djûr forkeapje.\nIn soldaet, dy't in helm by him draecht, dy kinne se noait deasjitte. Dy is kûgelfrij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20218,"r":"CJ017905","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":null,"d":"A woman sees a funeral procession passing by and pulls someone aside to make way for it. A short time later her husband dies.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik bin us mei in frommes oproan yn 'e Harkema.\nDoe seach dat frommes in lykstaesje, mar ik seach neat. Sy skuorde my rimpen fan 'e wei. Oars, sei se, wie 'k oan kant smiten woarn.\nKoarte tiid dêrnei is har man stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20256,"r":"CJ018102","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul can often foresee and predict things.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Japik Douwe wie timmerman yn Burgumerheide. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren. Syn âld wyfke plichte wol faek by ús mem to kommen. Hja gong dan oan 'e ein fan 'e tafel op knibbels lizzen en dan fortelde se hwat Japik wer sjoen hie. Ik hearde as jonkje dy forhalen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20272,"r":"CJ018118","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Bulletproof people were born with a caul or carry a caul with them.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":20516,"r":"CJ019716","p":"Sweagerbosk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul is bulletproof. Anyone who owns a caul is bulletproof too. That is why you must always watch out for greedy midwives who secretly keep cauls at births.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei de helm geboaren wie, wie kûgelfrij. Ek deselden dy't sa'n helm yn bisit hienen, wienen kûgelfrij. De froedfrou wie altyd och sa hyt op sa'n helm. Dy knoffele se meast achterút.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20611,"r":"CJ020409","p":"Tzummarum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man who was born with a caul stopped briefly in front of a house three days in a row. Not long afterwards the girl who lived in the house drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn Tsjummearum hat in man wenne, dy wie mei de helm geboaren.\nSahwat yn 1902 is hjir in fanke stoarn, dat hiet fan Anne. Hja moast omke tsjin my sizze.\nDy man dy't mei de helm geboaren wie gong op in dei by harren foar de ruten lâns. Doe stie er even stil en gyng doe wer fuort. Soks die er oars noait.\nDe twadde deis die er itselde wer.\nDe trêdde deis kaem er wer. Doe seach er Anne. Hy bleau even stean om nei har to sjen. In skoftsje letter is Anne fordronken.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20612,"r":"CJ020410","p":"Tzummarum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man had been restless all afternoon, but he would not say why. Later he and his work crew met another work crew. While they were still very far away, the man already said that one of the others had drowned. He had been born with a caul.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dyselde man wurke yn in ploech yn 'e Mieden.\nOp in dei wie Anne Gryt (Bylsma) har heit fordronken. Dy wurke yn in oare ploech.\nDe man mei de helm wie de hiele middei ûnrêstich.\nSy seinen tsjin him: \"Hwat is der, man?\" Mar hy woe it net sizze.\nDe jouns nei seizen kaem de hiele ploech de buorren ynrinnen.\nFan 'e oare kant kaem èk in ploechje fan it wurk. Mar dy hienen in ljedder by har en dêr droegen se it lyk fan Piet Louw op, dy't fordronken wie.\nDe beide ploegen moeten inoar. Mar hja wienen noch lang net oan inoar ta, doe sei de man mei de helm: \"'t Is Piet Louw, dy is fordronken.\"\nDat hied er sjoen. Dêr hied er sa ûnrêstich fan west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20620,"r":"CJ020501","p":"Tzummarum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"When a man who was born with a caul stopped briefly in front of a house, someone in that house died within a short time.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Tsjummearum hat in man wenne, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy kaem wolris op in plak, dêr't er oars noait kaem. Dan seach er dêr by 't hûs op, hy bleau even stean en gong wer fuort. In dei of hwat letter stoar der dan ien yn dat hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20621,"r":"CJ020502","p":"Tzummarum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man who was born with a caul stopped briefly by a child. That same evening the child died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy hawwe in jonkje forlern dat yn 1919 geboaren is.\nIt wie yn 'e simmer fan '20. Skoanmem wenne by ús yn. Sy wie oan 't wurk. Ik wie op 'e tún en de frou wie om boadskippen.\nDoe seach skoanmem dy âld man, dy't mei de helm geboaren wie, om 'e hoeke kommen. 't Wie om Maeije hinne. Hy bleau even stean. De lytse jonge lei to sliepen. 't Wie sahwat fiif ûre yn 'e middei.\nIt jonkje woarde net lekker, it rekke siik.\nDe sneon-to-middeis is it stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":20797,"r":"CJ021308","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":null,"d":"Everything a fortune teller predicted to a man in his youth later came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Nijebrêge wenne Hinke Kaert, dat wie in bikend wiersizter. Myn broer en ik en noch ien ha der us mei ús trijen hinne west.\nMyn broer wenne yn Dútslân. Ik soe der ek hinne foar de simmermaenden.\nIk gong it earst nei Hinke ta fan 'e trije.\nHinke telde de kaerten.\n\"Jo ha der ek al jong by west\", sei se.\n\"Hoesa?\" frege ik.\n\"Jo ha al yn 't bûtenlân west.\" Fierder sei se, myn âlden leefden noch. Ik soe let trouwe. 'k Wie sear kieskeurich yn 'e froulju. Ik soe in arbeidersdochter ha, dy't nou boerefaem wie. It wie in goede faem. Mar wy soenen net lang by elkoar bliuwe. Wy soenen hielendal by inoar wei.\n\"Hoe lang dan?\" frege ik.\n\"Sahwat seis à sawn jier\", sei se. \"En jim sille twa bern ha. Jo sille noch wol krapte meimeitsje. Mar jo krije in bêste âlde dei.\"\nIt is allegear wurd foar wurd krekt sa útkaem.\nNei sawn jier woarde myn frou kranksinnich en moast se nei in gesticht. En ik ha 't froeger tige krap hawn.\nDoe kaem Jan oan 'e beurt, dy't by ús wie. Mar dy krige net folle goeds to hearren.\n\"Moat ik jo de warheit fortelle?\" sei se. \"Jo binne nochal driftich en jo kinne wolris lulk op my wurde.\" mar Jan woe 't witte.\nDoe sei se: \"Jo binne in echte stokelder. Jo dogge neat leaver as rúzje meitsje. Dêrby binne jo sa lui as in stok. En jo litte in oar de kastanjes út it fjûr helje. Jo tinke allinne mar oan josels. Jou frou kriget in swier lot by jo.\"\n(Ek dit kloppe as in bus)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21016,"r":"CJ023103","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Egbert de Jong was born with a caul. One must be careful how the caul is pulled off newborn children.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Egbert de Jong yn 'e Himrik wie mei de helm geboaren. Men mat oppasse hoe't men de helm der ôflûkt by in pasgeboaren bern.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21019,"r":"CJ023106","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man was born with a caul and often had to get up at night to go to the churchyard. He lived in a caravan. One night a funeral procession came by that could not get past. The man had to move the caravan. The hearse stopped in front of a house. The next day someone living in that house died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Himrik stie in woanwein, dêr wenne in man yn, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Alle nachten moest hy der ôf en nei 't tsjerkhôf ta. Der waerd dan op 'e wein kloppe en dan sei er 'ja'.\nOp in kear kom der in lykstaesje lâns by nacht. Dy koe net passeare. Hy moast mei de wein fan 't sté. Dat die er dyselde nachts.\nDe oare deis forstoar der ien. 't wie famylje fan 'e smid. Dy kaem in dei of hwat letter op 't hôf. Foar 't hûs fan 'e smid hâldde de wein stil, krekt op it plak dêr't oars de woanwein stie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21045,"r":"CJ023602","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":null,"d":"Two couples once went to a fortune teller. She saw at once that each boy had sat down next to the other's girl. She told one of the girls that within two weeks she would lose something shiny and round. A few days later she had indeed lost her hand pump. She would have three children. She and her husband would earn a good living, but they would have to work hard for it. And her husband would work with sharp things. All of it came true. Her husband went to work with the spade and the fork.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In neef fan my en syn faem en ik mei myn feint ha ris mei ús fjouweren nei de wiersizter ta west. Dy wenne to Ljouwert, achter oan 'e Nijstêd.\nWy hienen bisluten it minske to grazen to nimmen. Myn neef gong njonken my sitten en myn feint by de faem fan myn neef.\nMar it earste dat it minske sei, wie: \"Jimme hearre sa net to sitten. Jo hearre dêr by en jo hearre dêr by\", sei se tsjin 'e manlju.\nIk hie yn dy tiid krekt in fyts krigen. Sy sei tsjin my: \"Jo slepe in ding wei binnen de fjirtsjin dagen. Dat blinkt as sulver en 't is roun.\" Ik tocht: \"O heden, dat is myn sulveren doekspjelde\", en ik taestte der al nei, mar sy skodde mei de holle.\nNei in dei of hwat sleepte ik yn 'e heide by Haulerwyk yn 't fjild myn hânpomp wei. Mar ik krige him wer. Dat hie se dus goed sjoen.\nIk soe trije bern krije. Dat is ek neikaem.\nMyn man en ik soenen goed ús brea ha, mar wy moasten der in bulte swier wurk foar dwaen. Ek dàt wie wier. En myn man, sei se, gong mei in bult skerp om. Dat is ek útkaem: dat wienen de skeppe en de furke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21050,"r":"CJ023607","p":"Haulerwijk","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A caul is a triangular piece of skin that must be pulled off a newborn child the right way, namely upwards. But often this is done sideways and it passes over the eyes. Then the child is troubled by it later and has to see all sorts of things in advance.\nSomeone born with a caul is bulletproof. Some also believe that whoever has bought a caul and keeps it is bulletproof.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei de helm geboaren is, is kûgelfrij. Der wurdt ek wol sein, dy't in helm kocht hat en yn syn bisit hat, dy is kûgelfrij. Yn de regel wurdt de helm forkeard ôflutsen. De helm is in lyts trijehoekich stikje fel. It mat nei boven ta lutsen wurde. Dan krijt it bern gjin lêst en hoeft er letter neat to sjen. Mar gewoanlik lûke se it nei oerdwars ta ôf. Dan falle de egen der oer. Dan krije sokke bern letter lêst en matte se allerhande dingen foarút sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21114,"r":"CJ024202","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A few boys were walking about when one of them said they had to step aside because a hearse had to pass. This boy was born with a caul, which is why he saw it. Indeed, a few days later someone died, and his body was driven past there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sibe Boomsma wenne op 'e Boelensloane. Hy hie in soan, dy wie mei de helm geboaren.\nOp in kear kuijere er mei 't jongfolk op 'e wei. Dêr wie ik ek by. Doe sei er ynienen: \"Gean even oan kant, hwant der mat in lykwein passeare.\"\nWy gongen allegear oan kant, mar wy seagen neat. Mar wrachtich, in pear dagen letter stoar der ien en it lyk woarde dêr lâns riden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21286,"r":"CJ025501","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Knjillis Veenstra often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. He was born with a caul. People were afraid when they saw him walking towards them, especially if someone in the family was ill. He foresaw that his own daughter would drown.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Knjillis Veenstra wenne yn 'e Westerein by 't spoar. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren en moest faek yn 'e nacht út bêd wei om hwat to sjen. Hy hat him der wol hiel bot tsjin forset, dan wòed er lizzen bliuwe, mar 't joech neat, der wie in macht dy't him dreau.\nHy hat fan tofoaren sjoen, dat syn eigen dochter fordronk. Hy doarst it net tsjin 't âld-minske to sizzen.\nAs de minsken Knjillis rinnen seagen, wienen se deabinaud. Hwant dan tochten se: \"Hy komt dizze kant út. Kin der ek hwat yn ús húshâlding gebeure?\"\nFoaral as der siken wienen wie de frees great.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21376,"r":"CJ026307","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":null,"d":"People said that wilde lantaarns (wild lanterns, will-o'-the-wisps) were omens.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":21448,"r":"CJ026715","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":null,"d":"A woman predicted to her son that his fourth child would also be a boy. When the child was born, the son came to tell her it was a girl. The woman said he was lying, and he admitted he was joking.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn soan hie trije jonges. Sy woenen sa graech in famke ha. Doe wie syn frou wer yn forwachting.\n\"It wurdt wer in jonge\", sei 'k.\nDoe't it bern der wie, kom myn soan by my en sei: \"'t Is in famke!\"\n\"Dû liichst it\", sei 'k. En 't wie ek sa. Hy makke gekheit. 't Wie wer in jonge.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21667,"r":"CJ028009","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":null,"d":"A braggart is convinced he will win an important contest. When someone predicts that he will not even take part in it, the braggart goes home disappointed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ek in kear doe kom hjir in jongkeardel, dy soe de oare deis oan in wedstriid meidwaen. Hy swetste sa bot, dat hy soe it winne, dat ik hie der op 't lêst skjin myn nocht fan. Ik sei tsjin him: \"Sil ik dy us hwat sizze? Dû silst net iens oan 'e wedstriid meidwaen.\"\nDoe gong er fuort. Hy wie sa mismoedich, dat hy hat it opsein en hat net oan 'e wedstriid meidien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":21966,"r":"CJ030716","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 3101","d":"Children who are lagging in growth turn out to be bewitched. Wopke the exorcist gives the father a potion, but gloomily predicts that he will not get the bottle home intact. The father will come back for a new bottle the next day, Wopke says. It happens exactly as Wopke predicted.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De bern fan Jelle Huisman fan 'e Wygeast woenen net groeije. Hwat de âlders der ek oan dienen, it bleauwen tjirmers. Op it lêst kommen Jelle en 't wiif der achter dat de bern bitsjoend wienen. Der siet kweafolk achter. Jelle wie gau út 'e rie. Hy stapte nei greate Wopke ta. Wopke joech him in drank mei, mar sei der by: \"Ik jow dy wol in drank, mar dû komst der net mei thús. De flesse rekket ûnderweis stikken.\"\nJelle lake hwat en sei: \"Dat sil wol hwat tafalle.\"\nWopke sei: \"Dû silst wol sjen, mar kom moarn mar om in nijen-ien. Dy krigest hiel thús.\"\nJelle stapte nei hûs ta mei de drank yn 'e binnenbûse fan 'e jas. Doe't er op 'e brêge by hûs wie, foel de drank der út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23416,"r":"CJ039103","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":null,"d":"A man often saw things before they happened. Once he predicted that the canal de Zwemmer would be widened and that it would flow with dead people. A terrible war would come. The first has come true; the rest remains to be seen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tusken Skûlenburch en Jistrum matte trije hûskes stien ha, yn 't iene dêrfan matte pake en dy wenne ha: heit syn âlden. Dêrnjonken wenne in man, dy moest alles sjen. Jouns kom er wol us by pake en beppe. Op in kear hie hy der wer op út west, sa fortelde er. Alhiel oer Eastemar, Sumar en sa nei Swartkrús.\n\"Ik bin der noch raer fan fan hwat ik dêr sjoen ha\", sei er. \"'t Kanael woarde forbrede (de Swemmer). 't Is net bêst,\" sei er, \"hwant 't sil strome fan deade minsken en 't is allegearre bloed. Wy krije noch in slimme oarloch.\" (Yntje Jans?)\nHeit hat dit faek forteld. Hy wie doe noch in bern, doe't er it hearde.\nIen ding is al neikommen, it forbreedzjen fan 'e Swemmer. It oare mat ôfwachte wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33222,"r":"CJ088004","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1967,"c":null,"d":"A fortune teller predicted to a man that he would become an innkeeper. The man bought an inn twice.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Lytse Kjille wie wiersizter to Drachten yn 'e Hounestege. Se hiet eins Cornelia Modderman.\nSy hat my de kaert ek al ris lêzen. Myn kammeraet en ik, elk mei de faem ha ris by har west.\nKjille reizge mei in tromp mei bân, sjippe en lint by de minsken lâns. Joech men har in stûr ekstra, dan lei se de kaert. Se sei fan my, ik soe kastlein wurde.\nMyn oansteande frou sei: \"Dat sil er net wurde.\"\n\"Hy wurdt it dochs\", sei se.\nHja hat der wol hwat fan sjoen. Twa kear ha 'k in herberch kocht. Ik ha de Phoenix kocht foar ƒ16000.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":50358,"r":"GENDT268","p":"Gendt","v":"Gld.","y":1967,"c":null,"d":"A man can predict the sex of a child.","i":"M.H.D.","o":"Bart van Vorssele zien vrouw was ien verwachting. Kees kos vörspelle of ’t ’n jonge of ’n meisje zou zien. “Wedde um ’n halve liter jenever, dat ’t ’n djernje wur?”, zei Kees. En ’t kwam uut. Mien vrouw verwachtte ok ’n kienje. We hadde droe jonges en een djern. Kees vroeg: “Eef, wa zou gé’j ’t liefst hemme: ’n jonge of ’n meisje?” “Nou naturlijk ’n djernje”, zei ik. “Mar ’t wurdt ’n jong”, zei Kees. En wer had ie geliek.\n\nIk kreeg in de gaten, dat Eef zijn eigen richting in wilde. Natuurlijk ging ik daar op in. Hij wilde me raadsels opgeven.","l":"Gendts (Achterhoeks)"},{"n":130102,"r":"VERHOEFF000906","p":"Zinkweg","v":"Z.-H.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A woman born with a caul has to look out at midnight and see a funeral. Whoever looks over her left shoulder can see the funeral too.","i":"L.V.","o":"Stijntje Oosterman, die was getrouwd mit Lou Blaak, die was mit d’n helm gebore. Snachs om twaalf ure gong de bovedeur ope en dan moes-ze naar boite kijke en dan zag ze een begrafenis. Als je over d’r linkerschoer meekeek, kon je ’t ook zien, wie d’r binnekort begrave zou worde, maar dat ware d’r maar weinig die dat durfde. Snachs durfde d’r niemand voorbij te gaan, want dan zou ’t wel ‘es kenne, datze je zag as de kommende begrafenis.","l":"Oud-Beijerlands"},{"n":46217,"r":"WEV016808","p":"Schaaphok","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul can see the future; cauls are sought after by midwives and doctors; eating the caul so as not to have to see evil; someone born with a caul can be recognised by a dimple at the temples.","i":"F.W.","o":"In dizze omgeevn wazzen netuurlijk ook gounend, dei mit de helm geboorn warn. Zokke mensn konden veuruut kiekn. Nou wazzen boakersen dokters slim wies mit de helms; zai namen ze den voak mit. Anders mos men dei dingen deur t eetn mengen en wel den mit dat ding geboorn was, mos de helm op eetn. Den zol hai gain lasst hebben van kwoad zain laoter.\nAin dei mit de helm geboorn is, kennen ie aan n koeltje bie de sloapn aan baide kanten van de kop.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46240,"r":"WEV017307","p":"Overschild","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":null,"d":"Predicting the future by laying down a cross-shaped key, turning a Bible and reciting a formula.","i":"F.W.","o":"Toukomst veurspeln.\nWazzen vrouger mensn, dei et zo deden.\nZai pakten ain biebel en n kruus-sleutel.\nDe sleutel wur hen legd en de biebel luitn ze ronddraaien aan n droad. Doorbie zeden ze: “Ik ben de alpha en de omega”.\nPrecies wait ik etnait; as ik mien grootmoe wieder vruig, huil ze dr over op; moar zonder kruus-sleutel kon t nait.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46246,"r":"WEV017403","p":"Bourtange","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A girl born with a caul only finds peace when she is given the caul at her marriage. Midwives often take the caul away to sell it to the parents when the child runs into trouble.","i":"F.W.","o":"Helm.\nMien zuster is door mit geboorn. Zo’n helm mout in t bezit van de aigenoar blieven, anders krig e loater last. Moeke het hum opbaargt in t kamnet. Nou har mien zuster de aignoarighaid, dat ze bie gain mens laank weezn kon. As ze eevn bie n ander daind har, mos ze weer noar hoes. Dou ze trouwd is, het moeke heur de helm mitgeevn. Dou was t goud.\nDe boakerskes vrouger namen ze voak stiekum mmit. Zai woln er geld oetsloagn; as t kind noaderhand last kreeg, gungen ze de helm weer aan de aoln verkoopn.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46261,"r":"WEV017501","p":"Weite","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A son was born with a caul, which brings him luck.","i":"F.W.","o":"De helm.\nMien zeun is mit de [toevoeging met balpen: helm] geboorn. Dat brengt hom altied geluk. \nAs hai vandoage gain cent meer het, kennen ie dr op aan, dat e mörn weer goud verdaint. Schatriek har e weezn kend, moar hai bezit nait veul. Wat e mit ain hand verdaint, geft hai mit twei-e uut. (Inderdaad, deze knaap is wijd en zijd bekend: F.W.).","l":"Gronings"},{"n":46275,"r":"WEV017606","p":"Muntendam","v":"Gr.","y":1967,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Various things can happen to a person born with a caul, such as seeing evil or becoming unhappy without the caul. Midwives take the caul away to sell to skippers, who will then have a prosperous voyage.","i":"F.W.","o":"Helm.\nAs aine mit de helm geboorn wordt, dan kennen door verschilnde dingen mit gebeurn.\nLoater ken hai misschien kwoad zain.\nVrouger nammen de boakers ze mit en verkochden ze aan de schipppers. Dei harn den n goi-e voart.\nMoar zo’n kind, dei de helm ofstooln wur, was loater ongelukkig.","l":"Gronings"},{"n":21770,"r":"CJ0286A13","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 3101","d":"A father is on his way home with a potion for his bewitched child when something - the narrator does not know exactly what - tries to take the potion from him. Because the bottle falls and breaks, Wopke the exorcist has to give the father a new one. Wopke had foreseen this and predicts that the father will now get the potion home intact.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't ik noch in bern wie, wie der ien fan ús al us in kear bitsjoend. Doe gong ús heit mei it wetter fan it bern nei greate Wopke ta.\nWopke joech heit in drankje en dêr gong heit mei werom op hûs ta.\nMar ûnderweis wie der ynienen hwat by him opsprong. Hwat it krekt west hie, wist er net, mar it drankje, dat er yn 'e bûse hie, rekke dêrtroch stikken, en hy moest werom nei Wopke ta.\n\"Kom, bist dêr al wer,\" hie Wopke sein, \"dat hie 'k al forwachte. Hjir is in nij drankje en nou komt der dy ûnderweis neat oer.\"\nEn sa wie 't ek.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22161,"r":"CJ033401","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 3101","d":"Wopke the exorcist foretells that a child has been bewitched by an old woman, a witch. Out for revenge, the father of the bewitched child decides to burn the old woman and waits for her with a big fire. When the witch arrives at the house, she becomes very frightened and explains how the child can be cured. The father follows her advice: he and his child sit under a sheet with their heads over the steam of boiling cow's milk. At once a snake comes out of the child's throat. This is just as the witch had predicted: the father must not kill the snake, or the witch will die too.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en dy wennen op 'e Fjouwer Roeden. Sy hienen in jonkje, dat woarde siik. Sy woenen nei Greate Wopke ta to Kûkherne. Mar sy koenen it wetter fan it bern net meinimme, dêr wie 't noch to lyts ta. Doe nom heit it himdtsje fan 't jonkje mei.\n\"Wite jo ried?\" sei heit tsjin Wopke. Hy liet Wopke 't himdtsje sjen.\nWopke biseach it en sei: \"Der komt wolris in âld wiif by jimmes, hè?\"\n\"Ja\", sei heit.\n\"Hwat seit se?\"\n\"Hoe is 't mei de lytse jonge?\"\n\"En hwat sizze jo dan?\"\n\"Gelyk, hè?\" siz ik dan.\n\"Jo matte dat wiif yn 'e rekken hâlde\", sei Wopke. \"Dy hat it bern bitsjoend.\"\nHeit wie foar de duvel net bang. \"As dat âld wiif komt, forbrân ik har\", sei er.\nWopke joech him guod mei.\nDoe't heit thús wie lei er in hiel great fjûr oan yn 'e fjûrpot. En doe wachte er op 't âld wiif.\nAl gauwachtich kom se der oan.\n\"Binne jo al wer thús, Lútsen?\" sei se.\n\"Ja\", sei heit en hy krige har by de earm beet. \"Dit fjûr is foar dy. Dû silst opslach it bern better meitsje en oars forbrân ik dy levend.\" (Heit hie 't ek dien, hwant dy stie nergens foar.)\nMar doe woarde 't âld wiif binaud.\nSy sei: \"Ik sil 't dy wol sizze. Dû mast fiif mingels feare koemolke siede. As it goed siedt mastû der mei 't bern boppe sitten gean mei de holle. De damp fan 'e molke mat nei jimme gesichten gean. Jimme matte togearre ûnder in lekken sitte.\nDan sil 't bern in ding ta de hals útkomme. Mar dû mast dat ding net dea dwaen,","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22190,"r":"CJ033605","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 3101","d":"Wopke the exorcist gives a father a potion for his bewitched child. Wopke forbids him to let strange eyes see the potion and advises him to keep it carefully under his coat. Several cats will try to take the potion from him to prevent the cure, Wopke says. Wopke's prediction comes true: the cats jump up at him, but the father manages to get the potion home intact.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit syn heit mat as jonkje bitsjoend west ha.\n't Bern seach der raer út. Doe gong syn heit nei Kûkherne ta, nei de duvelbander.\nWopke sei: \"Ja, jonge, dû bist krekt op 'e tiid. Even letter, en dan hie 't jonkje wei west.\"\n\"Hwat mankeart it bern dan?\" frege Pake.\n\"Dat siz ik net,\" antwurde Wopke, \"mar ik sil dy in drank klear meitsje. Mar dû mast oppasse. De drank ûnder 'e klean hâlde. Der meije gjin fremde egen oer gean. Tink der om en hâld dy dêr oan. By de earste draei, dêrst' oer mast, sil in kat wêze. Dy hat it op it drankje forsjoen. By de twadde draei sille miskien wol tsien katten wêze. Hâld it drankje ûnder 'e jas. Lit gjin fremde egen oer de drank gean. Ast' thús komste mast it bern der opslach hwat fan yn jaen.\"\nUnderweis wienen de katten by him opsprong. Mar pake hâldde it guod stiif ûnder 'e jas, dat der gjin oare egen oer foelen.\nHy kom der bihâlden mei thús en 't jonkje is wer better woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22220,"r":"CJ033804","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 3101","d":"Wopke the exorcist gives a father a potion for his bewitched child. Wopke predicts that the first person the father meets the next morning will say 'Where have you been?' That person has bewitched the child. It turns out exactly so.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Bulten wie in bern bitsjoend. De heit gong nei de duvelbander greate Wopke ta. Wopke joech in drankje mei. Hy sei: \"De earste dyst moarnmoarne tsjinkomste sil dy freegje: - Hwer hast hinne west? - dy hat it bern bitsjoend.\"\nIt wie Alle Tet (de frou fan Alle Wagenaar, dy't him de oare moarns it earst dêr nei frege).","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22740,"r":"CJ035210","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"A folk healer can make predictions from urine.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us heit reizge froeger altyd mei de wetters fan sike minsken nei Knjillis Wytses ta. Knjillis Wytses wie wûnderdokter yn Sumar. Hy koe mear as in oar.\nOp in kear gong heit nei him ta mei it wetter fan twa mannen. Dy hienen beide bloed spuid. Doe't er it wetter bisjoen hie, sei er: \"De iene kin 'k mei Gods help geneze, mar de oare binne gjin krûden foar woechsen.\"\nDe iene hie maechbloeding hawn, de oare hie kanker.\nDe iene is wer better woarn, de oare stoar.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":22761,"r":"CJ035312","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 3101","d":"The father of a bewitched child consults Wopke the exorcist. Wopke gives him a potion but warns him about a cat that will try to take the medicine from him to prevent the cure. Wopke's prediction comes true: a cat breaks the bottle. When the father goes back to Wopke for a new potion, Wopke says an old woman will come to the door asking how the sick child is. The old woman is the witch, Wopke says. The father closes up every opening of the house to keep the witch from entering. Heksenkransen (witches' wreaths, clumps of feathers) are found in the child's pillows. When they burn the wreaths in the fire, the witch's cat leaps against the window.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Jan Bearns van der Veen wenne yn 'e Mieden by de Bûtenpostumer feart. Hy hie in bern, dat wie net goed. Doe gong er nei greate Wopke ta. Dy wenne yn Kûkherne. Wopke joech him in drank. Hy sei: \"Tink der om, dû mast aenst om in peal hinne. Dan komt der in kot by dy en dy wol by dy opspringe. Dû mast om 't fleske tinke.\"\nSûnder dat Jan der erch yn hie kom er by de peal. Dêr wie de kat en dy sprong by him op. De flesse stikken en de drank wei.\nDoe gong Jan wèr nei Wopke ta.\nWopke sei: \"Bist dêr al wer?\"\n\"Ja,\" sei Jan, \"de kat sprong tsjin my oan.\"\n\"Dû mast nou better oppasse\", sei Wopke, en hy joech him wèr in drank. \"Astû thús komste, komt der dalik in âld-wiif by de doar. Dy hat jimme bern bitsjoend. It kom krekt sa út.\nDoe't Jan krekt thús wie, kom der in âld-minske by de doar, dy't frege hoe't it mei it bern wie.\nMar sy lieten har der net yn.\nAlle iepeningen yn 'e hûs woarden tichtdien. De skoarstien en de kaeisgatten, ja alles.\nDoe toarnden se de kessens iepen. Dêr sieten krânsen yn, dy forbrânden se yn 't fjûr. Wylst se dat dienen sprong deselde kat, dy't it drankje stikken makke hie, foar de glêzen om.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23022,"r":"CJ037212","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"If the caul of a newborn baby is pulled off upwards, the child will later be able to see into the future. If the caul is pulled off downwards, he sees nothing. Sunday's children are zwachtelbinders (swaddle-binders, people with second sight). People born with a caul and on a Sunday are fortune tellers. If there is a caul on board a ship, the ship will never sink.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As jy de helm by in pasgeboaren bern nei boppe ta ôflûke, dan kin dat bern letter yn 'e takomst sjen.\nLûkt men de helm nei ûnderen ta ôf, dan sjocht er net hwat.\nDy't op snein geboaren wurde binne knoffelbân-biners; ek wiersizers (dan matte se ek mei de helm geboaren wêze).\nAs in helm op in skip is, dan forgiet it skip noait en to nimmer.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23023,"r":"CJ037213","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul is bulletproof in war.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't in helm hat en dy giet yn 'e oarloch, dy bliuwt kûgelfrij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23045,"r":"CJ037407","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul is bulletproof. He has to get up at night to see funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ien dy't mei de helm geboaren is, is kûgelfrij. Hy mat der nachts wol us út om lykstaesjes to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23061,"r":"CJ037605","p":"Ikkerwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"With a man who had been born with a caul, there was always a knocking on the window at night. Then he had to get out of bed.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Ritske Vellinga wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest der nachts út. Ik ha 't wol us troffen, dat er om tolve ûre yn 'e nacht by de doar stie. Sy kloppen dan fan tofoaren by him op 't rút. Dan gong hy der út. Dan koed er net langer yn 'e hûs bliuwe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23087,"r":"CJ037802","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man who had been born with a caul saw funerals in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op Kollumersweach wenne in man, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy seach fan tofoaren bigraffenissen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23132,"r":"CJ038303","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"A couple once told the woman's father that they had seen a very large light. The father said it was three omens: a new house would be built on that spot, a new road would come, and there would be a death. The new house and the new road did indeed come. And not long after, the father died, after being ill in bed for two days.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It wie yn Grinzer Pein. Ik en myn earste man kommen op in jountiid út it tsjerkje. Wy kommen fan 'e sangforieniging. 't Wie tsjuster. Ynienen stienen wy yn 't folle ljocht.\nWy gongen nei heit en dy ta. Dêr fortelde ik hwat wy sjoen hienen. \"Hwat soe soks nou bitsjutte?\" frege ik.\nDoe sei heit: \"Moarn sil ik jimme fortelle hwat jim sjoen ha.\"\nDe oare moarns sei 'k tsjin heit: \"Hwat wie 't nou, heit?\"\n\"Jimme ha trije dingen sjoen\", sei er. \"Jimme ha in nij hûs sjoen. Jimme ha in nije wei sjoen en jimme ha in sterfgefal sjoen. Tink mar us om myn wurden.\" It is alle trije útkom. Koarte tiid dêrnei kom der op dat plak in nij hûs to stean. En ek al gau dêrnei kom dêr in nije wei lâns, dwars troch heit syn lân hinne. En ús heit kom samar nei twa dagen sykte alhiel ûnforwacht to forstjerren. 't Is alle trije neikom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23153,"r":"CJ038403","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"During the war, two men once saw a glowing object fly through the air. Later a road was built on that spot, so it had been an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie twa omkesizzers, beide âld-feinten. 't Wienen Sipke en Taeke de Vries. Sipke is dea. Taeke wennet oan 'e âlde tramwei, dy buorket dêr hwat allinnich.\n't Wie yn 'e lêste oarloch, doe wienen se togearre by de polderdyk. 't Wie op in saterdeijoune. Sy hienen dêr in skiep rinnen mei twa lammen.\n't Woarde donker. Taeke sei tsjin Sipke: \"Mast dêr us sjen.\"\nDoe kom dêr in stik fjûr yn 'e loft, dat hie de foarm fan in bynstok. Dy wie boven oer har hinne gong, skean achter Garyp troch. By de polderdyk gong it ding skean troch de Wierren, op in nije plaets oan.\n\"Hwat wie dat nou?\" sei Taeke, doe't er 't my fortelde. Ik sei: \"As wy it leve, dan komme wy dat wol to sjen.\" En nou wite wy it: Der komt nou in wei lâns, krekt deselde plakken lâns dêr't dy gleone bynstok fan kleare fjûr doe lâns gong is.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23381,"r":"CJ038809","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"Three young men once came to Hinke Kaert. Of the first she knew that his wife sometimes collapsed for no reason. Of the second she knew that he was already married, and that one day he would walk around in a cap with a red band. That was right, because he became a road worker. To the third she predicted that he would very soon have an accident. On the way back his bicycle got caught in the tram rails and he fell.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha ris mei ús trijen op 'e fyts nei Hinke Kaert west. Dy wenne op Nijebrêge. Ik en myn broer en Jan.\nMyn broer wie de âldste, dy kom it earst oan 'e beurt.\n\"Hwat binne jo ûngelokkich\", sei se tsjin him.\n\"Ja?\" sei myn broer.\n\"Ja,\" sei se, \"jou frou falt der soms samar hinne.\"\nDat kloppe.\nDoe kom ik oan 'e beurt. Ik sei út 'e gek: \"'t Sil my binije hwat frou ik krij.\"\n\"Nou, nou,\" sei se, \"jo binne al troud.\" (dat wie ek sa) \"Jo krije noch us in pet op mei in reade bân der om.\"\nIt klopte. Ik woarde wegwerker nei forrin fan tiid. \nTsjin Jan sei se: \"Jo matte aenst oppasse. Jo krije aenst in ûngelok.\" Dat is ek gebeurd. Hy foel mei de fyts doe't hy yn 'e Gerdyk mei de fyts yn 'e tramrail rekke op 'e weromreis.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23387,"r":"CJ038904","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"A card reader advised a newly married young man to buy the stretch of heath next to his house. She predicted that he would have an odd number of children, and that there would still be carpentry done in his house. All of that came true, but he did not buy the stretch of heath.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw ris by lytse Kjille west, dy wie kaertlizter op 'e Gerdyk. Ik wie doe krekt troud en sahwat twintich jier. Ik gong der foar aerdichheit hinne.\n\"O heden,\" sei se, \"jou takomst liket goed. As jo hwat wolle, der leit heide njonken jou hûs. Dat matte jo altyd keapje.\"\nIk sei: \"Dan mat ik jild ha.\"\nDoe sei se: \"Dat leit foar jo klear.\"\nWy hienen noch gjin bern. Ik frege har: \"Krije wy ek bern?\"\n\"Ja,\" sei se, \"mar ûneven.\" Dat is ek útkom.\n\"Dêr't jo komme to wenjen,\" sei se, \"yn dat hûs sil ek noch timmere wurde.\" Dat is ek gebeurd.\nMar ik ha dy heide net kocht. Mar sy hat ek net sein dat ik dat dwaen soe. Sy hat it my allinne mar oanret.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23607,"r":"CJ040304","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Jan Ketelaar from Burgum was born with a caul.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":23625,"r":"CJ040403","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"VDK 1676F","d":"An eldest farmhand was once told that he would have a terrible accident, but he did not believe it. One evening the youngest farmhand had to go out into the fields to do something. The eldest farmhand decided to give him a good scare. He waited for him with a white sheet over himself. When the youngest farmhand came home, he stammered out that he had hit something white on the head. They went to look and found the dead body of the eldest farmhand.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie in greatfeint, dy wenne by de boer yn Boarn. Op in kear gong er nei Hinke ta. Hy woe de takomst wite. Hinke sei, der soe him in great ûngelok oerkomme. De greatfeint leaude it net.\nDer wie ek in lytsfeint by har op 'e plaets. Dy wie deabinaud yn 't tsjuster. Doe moest der us in kear in stik ark helle wurde. Dêr moesten se twa, trije stikken lân foar delrinne. 't Wie al tsjuster. De lytsfeint woarde der op útstjûrd om dat stik ark to heljen, hwant sy moesten it brûke.\nDoe tocht de greatfeint: \"Nou sil ik him bang meitsje.\" Hy gong op healwei by in hekke stean mei in lekken oer de kop en dêr wachte er de lytsfeint op.\nDe lytsfeint kom in skoft letter hymjend en blazend thús.\n\"Hwat is der nou oan?\" fregen se him.\nDoe sei de lytsfeint: \"Der wie hwat by de hekke. Hwat it wie, dat wyt ik net, mar 't wie wyt en ik ha 't op 'e kop slein.\"\nDoe't se der hinne gongen, die bliken, dat de greatfeint, dy wie deaslein.\nDit is sa'n sechstich jier lyn gebeurd.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23627,"r":"CJ040405","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Some people are born with a caul. If they keep the caul, such a person has to get up at night to see funerals. If the caul is burned, this is not the case.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon wurde mei de helm geboaren. As se dy helm biwarje, mat sa'n persoan der nachts út om bigraffenissen to sjen. As se de helm opbrânne is dat net it gefal.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23703,"r":"CJ041105","p":"Peize","v":"Dr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who had been born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funerals.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon hjirre wienen mei de helm geboaren. Dy seagen dan bigraffenissen fantofoaren. Sy moèsten it sjen, sy gongen der yn 'e nacht ôf.\nMyn neef hie forkearing mei in dochter fan âlde Ritske Vellinga. Ritske wie soms de hiele nacht der op út, dat hat myn neef my sels wol forteld. Ritske wie mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23779,"r":"CJ042003","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A grandfather told his son and daughter-in-law that their newborn little son would not live long. He had already seen it in advance; he had been born with a caul.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn jonge is troud mei in dochter fan Piter Mook (= P. de Graaf). Sy krigen in berntsje. Doe kom Piter by harren en sei: \"Jimme ha dit jonkje al, mar jimme hâlde it net.\"\n\"Hwat wyt heit dêr fan?\" sei ús jonge.\n\"Tink mar om myn wurden\", sei Piter.\nHy krige gelyk. 't Bern rekke wei. (Piter Mook wie mei de helm geboaren)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23806,"r":"CJ042107","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"Hinke Kaert predicted to a girl that her sweetheart would get another girlfriend. On the way back she would also lose something shiny and tear her dress. It all came true; it was a ring that she lost.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In skoftsje letter bin 'k nei Hinke ta west mei 't fanke, dêr't ik doe hwat gedoente mei hie. It wie ûngeregelde forkearing, 't gong sa'n bytsje fan 'e hak op 'e tak. Hinke sei tsjin har: \"Nou bistû hjir èk. Dû mienste datstû him krijste, mar né, hy krijt in fanke hjir fandinne súd en west.\"\nDat is ek gebeurd. 't Kom krekt út.\nDe jouns wie 't sa tûk. Wy woenen de jouns nei Akkrumer merke. Wy geane by Hinke wei. Doe sei Hinke tsjin myn faem: \"Tink der om, fanke, dû hast in moai nij jurkje oan, mar och - dû forliest hwat blinkends en dû krigest in skuor yn 'e jurk.\"\nWy smieten to Akkrum ús fytsen by Prinsen yn 'e hynstestâl en doe yn 'e skommel. Doe't wy út 'e luchtskommel weistapten, wie myn faem har rinkje kwyt en sy hie in skuor yn 'e jurk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23809,"r":"CJ042110","p":"Ureterp","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"A bargeman's little child was once safely tied to a line in the water. But then a big dog came and shook itself. The child choked on the water the dog shook off. A card reader had already predicted to the mother that this would happen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dit gefal ha 'k ris fan in frou heard. Ik en myn arbeider wienen op in stik lân oan 't dongjen, dat wie ûnder Boarn. Doe wie 't tiid fan kofje. Dat dronken wy by de helling op.\nDoe wie dêr in skipperswyfke en dy snokte. Hja hie fortriet, dat wie skoan to fornimmen.\n\"Hwat skeelt der oan?\" frege ik.\nDoe sei se: \"O, it is hjir krekt itselde. Ik haw in jonkje forlern yn Terwispel troch 't wetter. Ik wie fan tofoaren warskôge. In kaertlizter hat al us sein, dat it gebeure soe. Hwat blykt? In greate, swarte wetterhoun hat it dien. It berntsje siet fêst oan 'e line by 't âld skipke. Der komt in houn út it wetter, dy skoddet him út en it berntsje stikt yn it wetter dat dy houn útskoddet.\"\nDêr't dat berntsje fordronken wie, wie 't krekt sa as yn Boarn by de helling.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23826,"r":"CJ042209","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"A man claimed it had been revealed to him that he would live to be a hundred. He had been in prison, from where he could not go out to see funeral processions. Then Jesus came to him through the bars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining biweart dat er hûndert jier âld wurde sil. Dat is him iepenbiere, seit er.\nHy hat in jier yn 'e gefangenis sitten. Doe koe hy der net út om lykstaesjes to sjen. Doe is Jezus by him kaem troch de traeljes hinne, sei er.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23869,"r":"CJ042604","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"Two women were once walking along the road around midnight when they were suddenly lifted up and set down in a completely different place. They thought it had been a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jehannes Bos syn wiif Sjouk en Ielke syn wiif dy gongen us op in nacht tusken tolven en ienen de wei del. Doe woarden se samar oplicht en kommen op in hiel oar plak wer del. 't Gebeurde yn Drachtster Kompenije.\nSe tinke, dat dêr in lykstaesje west hat.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23871,"r":"CJ042606","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Some children are born with a caul. If the caul is peeled off downwards, all is well. But if the caul is pulled upwards, that person will see all kinds of things. A horse can also be born this way. If the caul is peeled off backwards, it carries its head high. But if it is done downwards, it walks with its head hanging forward.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer is mei de helm geboaren. Wurdt de helm nei ûnderen strûpt, dan is it goed, gebeurt it oarsom, dan mat er alles sjen.\nIn hynder wurdt ek sa geboaren. Strûpt men de helm achterstofoar ôf, dan draecht er de kop omheech, docht men it nei ûnderen ta, dan rint er mei de kop foardel.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23900,"r":"CJ042804","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man who had been born with a caul often had to get up at night to see something. Sometimes after only half an hour.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Keeke hie it net maklik. Soms hied er noch mar in healûre op bêd lein, dan moest hy der út om hwat to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":23921,"r":"CJ042914","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"A woman foretold the future by reading coffee grounds.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem seach yn kofjedik, sa lei se de takomst út.\nMyn muoike koe kaertlizze. Dat wie Fokje v.d. Heide - v.d. Meer.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24044,"r":"CJ044006","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"A man always saw funeral processions. In his younger years he had sworn a lot and cursed everything. Perhaps it was his punishment that later he had to foresee everything.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Knjillis Veenstra seach lykstaesjes. Hy wie yn syn jonge jierren in man dy't altyd flokte en alles forwinske. Miskien wie 't syn straf wol, dat er letter alles sjen moest.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24072,"r":"CJ044113","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man who had been born with a caul often saw funerals in advance. He was then driven to the churchyard at night. He also saw the funeral of his own daughter.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Keeke (= Knjillis Veenstra) wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy seach de bigraffenissen foarút. Hy gong dan yn 'e nacht nei 't tsjerkhôf ta, dêr woarde er hinne dreaun. Hy hat fan to foaren de bigraffenis fan syn eigen dochter sjoen, dy't fordronken is.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24083,"r":"CJ044124","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2900","d":"Freemasons never lack money. They are bulletproof, just like people born with a caul. Every now and then one of them has to die. If they want to leave the Freemasons, they have to die. They have to sign a contract in blood. They have to lie in a coffin all night, and they do all sorts of things with it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Frijmitselders hawwe noait forlet fan jild. Se binne kûgelfrij, krekt as deselden dy't mei de helm geboaren binne.\nSa nou en dan mat der ien fan har deamakke wurde. Se komme der noait wer by wei of sy matte stjerre. Sy matte in kontrakt mei bloed ûndertekenje. Sy matte in hiele nacht yn in deadskiste lizze en dêr helje se dan fan alles mei út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24113,"r":"CJ044230","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"A fortune teller predicted to a man that he would soon get a dog that would bite four of his animals to death. Besides that, he would like to have a wife again, but that would never happen. Three women were already in love with him, and that week a fourth would fall in love with him. Everything came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha wol us nei lytse Kjille west, de wiersizter fan 'e Gerdyk. 't Kom allegear út hwat se sei.\n\"Krijst aenst in houn\", sei se. \"Dy byt dy fjouwer piken dea.\"\n't Wie ek sa.\n\"Wolst ek wol wer in frou ha,\" sei se, \"mar dû krigest noait ien wer. Der binne oars fjouwer op dy forleafd.\"\n\"Trije\", sei 'k.\n\"Ja,\" sei se, \"mar de fjirde komt fan 'e wike.\"\n't Wie ek sa.\n\"Mar dû wolst der net ien fan ha\", sei se.\nIt kloppe allegear.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24134,"r":"CJ044321","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"P. de Graaf is known for having been born with a caul.\nIn Houtigehage, among other places, several cases are known of people whose funeral he saw before they had even died. Some people are afraid of him. He does have a strange look.\nAccording to the directress I would not get anywhere with him, but his answers were clear and well thought out. He is, however, very deaf.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":24173,"r":"CJ044511","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul is bulletproof. Anyone who owns a caul is also bulletproof. That is why they are so expensive. Doctors secretly take them away; they are crazy about them.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei de helm geboaren is, is kûgelfrij. Ek deselden dy't sa'n helm yn besit ha. Dêrtroch binne dy helms sa djûr. De dokters knoffelje se achterút, dy binne der gleon op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24206,"r":"CJ044903","p":"Harlingen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Whoever is born with a caul sees evil coming in advance.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":24209,"r":"CJ044906","p":"Harlingen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"In the past people were never allowed to walk in the middle of the road, because of the funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wij mochten nooit midden op de weg loopn. Vanwege een lijkstaasje."},{"n":24334,"r":"CJ045807","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"If a child is born with a caul, you must quickly remove the caul, which covers the whole face, to prevent the child from suffocating.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In helm dat is in wyt floers, dat it bern hielendal oer 't gesicht hinne hat, as it geboaren wurdt. Men mat der fluch by wêze, om 't der ôf to heljen, oars smoart it bern. Mem wie kreamheinster. Hja sei, Fokke Witteveen (nou yn Kanada) hie twa bern krigen, dy't allebeide mei de helm geboaren wienen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24420,"r":"CJ046308","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 3101","d":"Bewitched people consult the exorcist Frânse Hinke. Frânse predicts that a cat or a dog will come towards the people to snatch away a healing potion.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der by ús folk ien bitsjoend wie gongen wy nei Frânse Hinke ta yn 'e Rottefalle.\nHja sei dan: Der komt jim in kat tomjitte, ek wol in houn, dy't tsjin jim opspringt dêr en dêr. Dy wol it drankje kapot meitsje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24585,"r":"CJ047616","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Soldiers born with a caul are bulletproof. At sea, too, someone with a caul is safe. Cauls are sometimes sold on.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Soldaten dy't mei de helm geboaren binne, binne kûgelfrij. Ien dy't mei de helm geboaren is, is op sé ek feilich.\nDe helms wurde soms djûr forkocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24711,"r":"CJ049407","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 3101","d":"A sick child turns out to be bewitched. Wopke the exorcist gives the child's father a potion, but urges him to protect the bottle well against breaking. Wopke predicts that the child's father might well run into someone on the gangplank. The father manages to get the potion home safely. The little boy soon recovers. Later the mother discovers three feather wreaths in the bewitched boy's pillow.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"It gebeurde ris dat der in bern van my bitsjoend rekke. Doe wenne ik hjir al. Doe ik nei Wopke ta to Kûkherne. Wopke joech my in fleske mei guod. 'k Moest der goed op passe dat it fleske net stikken rekke, sei er, hwant dat koe gebeure. As it iene of oare my tsjin 'e jas oan stompte dan gong 't fleske stikken.\nHealwei de Swâdde yn Twizelerheide moest ik oer in planke. Dêr warskôge er my foar, dêr koe my wolris ien moetsje.\n\"As ien my moetet en dy komt my nei,\" sei 'k, \"dan traepje 'k him fuort yn 'e Swâdde.\" 'k Wie froeger net sa mak.\nIk seach by de planke in wiif. Ik tocht: \"Dû mast oppasse fanke, hwant dû hast net mei in makken-ien to dwaen!\" Mar ik wie earder by de planke as hja.\nIk kaem bihâlden mei de drank thús.\nDe jonge krige fan it guod út it fleske en wie al moai-gau wer better.\nIt wiif hat syn kessen leech helle. Der sieten trije krânsen yn fan fear. 't Wienen roune dingen, krekt as in bûterkoeke. Ien wie klear, ien krapoan en de trêdde wie in bigjin mei makke. Dy krânsen ha 'k weismiten. It wienen dingen dy koenen net troch minskehannen makke wurde.\nSe wienen sahwat in finger dik, de fearkes leinen allegear ien kant út en der siet fan alles yn. Allegear fodsjes en flardtsjes sieten der trochhinne. Ek jern.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":24877,"r":"CJ050007","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People with a caul are bulletproof. A father burns his newborn son's caul. Greedy doctors often spirit the cauls away at birth to sell them for a lot of money to army officers. If the caul is pulled upwards off the head, the newborn will have visions of the future all his life. If the caul is pulled downwards, he will not. The caul is sacred.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn heit fortelde, dy't mei de helm geboaren wie, wie kûgelfrij. Myn broer Hindrik is mei de helm geboaren. heit seach it, by de bifalling. Heit die him der gau ôf. Hy loek him nei ûnderen ta.\nHy hat him forbrând.\nDokters knoffelen de helms froeger faek achterút. Dan forkochten se dy oan ofsieren yn 't leger.\nWurdt de helm by 't ôfnimmen omheechlutsen, dan mat it bern letter alles sjen. Nei ûnderen ta dan wurde de egen ticht strutsen.\nDe helm is heilich.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25164,"r":"CJ051911","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1968,"c":"AT 0990","d":"At night a merchant sees activity in the churchyard: a grave is being filled in. It is a vision of the future: later a farmer dies. The next morning the farmer turns out to be lying alive in his coffin: he had only seemed dead. The grave prepared in the churchyard is quickly filled in.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dyselde man fan Meppel fortelde ek:\nDer wie in man, dy handele altyd. Hy slepte faek by in boer. Op in kear wied er op in joune let by dyselde boer oankom.\nTichte by de plaets fan dy boer wie in tsjerkhôf. Dêr wie dy koopman lâns kom. Doe hied er tocht: \"It is nacht, hwat fremd, der binne noch in pear minsken op 't tsjerkhôf.\"\nIt like him ta dat dy in graef tichtsmieten.\nDoe't er op it spul oankom wie, dêr't de boer wenne, seinen se dêr tsjin him: \"De boer is stoarn.\" Hy koe dêr nou better net sliepe, hwant de boer lei yn 'e kiste en dy stie dêr yn 'e hûs. Mar hy koe wol ûnderdak krije by in buorman, dy koe him wol goed.\nDe oare moarns wienen de minsken by de kiste kom, dêr't de boer yn lei en doe hie dy boer net dea west. Hy hie skyndea west.\nHja hienen krekt in graef makke op it tsjerkhôf. Mar doe't der biricht kom dat de boer noch net dea wie, makken se it gau wer ticht.\nDe koopman hie dat de nachts fan tofoaren al sjoen.\nDat wie foartjirmerije.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":206912,"r":"OIRSCHOT002905","p":"Helvoirt","v":"N.-Br.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"Strange man predicts death when he gets nothing while begging; searches for treasure.","i":"A.v.O.","o":"Dood voorspellen\nNou hadde hier in Helvert vruuger ok iemand, die oew dood veurspelde. Da was 'n mooi tiepke, Pietje de Bont hiettenie. Mun taante wonde bij de burregemister, bij Pirke Verster dan; die wonde daor veur meid. Riggelmaotig kwaam Pietje de Bont daor aonbelle en dan zit ie \"ik pejaor\". Dur waore nogal veul van die tiepkes, hij hé gewond tusse Bart Braok en Schaopedonk. Daor wonde Driekse Elings ok, en Tonna zun vrouw. Pietje zee altij: Tonna, mar nie teveul praot maoke tege de bure; da doek zelluf wel. Hij ging dan bij de miense aon en dan zeetie \"Zeg mar dak wel un kachel heb, mar gin kole\", en as ie dan niks krig, veurspeldenie da ge dood ging, en dan zin ie durbij: \"ik ha honger en gij het me nie gespijzigd\" En warempul, ze ginge dood. Iederin dacht datie erm was, mar toen ie zelluf dood was hek minstuns vèfentwintig fundasie geheurd in de kerruk. 't Was un mooi menneke mee van die siep oogskus. En dan ging ie ok in de hai spaoie, op zoek nar schatte, en dan zittie: \"Dan komt klomp mee unne ijzere pin en tis nooit nie diep genog\". In ut oog was 't un godsvruchtig miens. Nou hadde hier twee misse; ik zat altij in de leste; daor kwaamp ie altij, en dan zat ie achtur in de kerruk, mar as ut afgelope was gong ie spesiaal in de vurste bank zitte, da ze allemaol gezien hadde dattie dur was. Mar ge moes zorruge da ge um iets gaaft","l":"Brabants"},{"n":41717,"r":"OIRSCHOT003003","p":"Haaren","v":"N.-Br.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"Castle owner predicts that a boy will get the job of level-crossing keeper.","i":"A.v.O.","o":"Voorspellen\nDe jonker moet un aorige gewist zèn; dun blinde jonkur, zinne ze op t lest, mar hij kon toch aorige dinge veurspelle. Daor moes unne kir op de overwegt unne nuwe wachter komme; das waor nou kIs Mai wont; Wagemans ha dar nog un kafee gehouwe; en daor was unne jonge, en die viette dan zun petje af as ie de jonker tegekwaam; Op unne kir ha de jonker um mee un meske zien lope. En dun vollegunde kir datie um wir tegekwaam, hiel ie um aon; zeg kunde gij us efkus hier, zin de jonker, en de jonge zunne pet aaf. Zuukte onderhaand te trouwe?, vruug de jonker. Jao, da wil ik wel, zee de jonge, mar ik hè gin werruk; Zoude nie wachter wille worre? vruug de jonker. Jao, zeede jonge; da zouk wel wille, mar das verkeke; daor is al iemund benoemd, die hek zelluf gesproke. \nDa zulle me nog us zien, zee de jonker. Mar wilde dur wone? Da zou die jonge graag wille. Dan wordut, zee de jonkur, en al was de nuwe wachter dan ok al benoemd, de jonker hee gelijk gekrege. De jonge wier daor wachter op de lijn. Hij kos mir veurspelle.","l":"Brabants"},{"n":41718,"r":"OIRSCHOT003004","p":"Haaren","v":"N.-Br.","y":1968,"c":null,"d":"Castle owner predicts who will not become mayor.","i":"A.v.O.","o":"(voorspellen 2)\nDe jonker heet nog us unne kir Un grap meegemaokt mee de burregemistersbenoeming in Haore. Dun overgrotvaoder van deze Van den Oevers was hier burregemister, en daor moes toen unne nieuwe komme, en toen wouwe ze eigeluk zunne zoon, van Van den Oever, burregemister maoke, gedippetirde staote dan, en da was zowa in kanne en kruike, mar de jonker zee, toen ie da hurde: da geburt nie, mee de dieje hebbe we al zoveul ongemakke gehad, da geburt nie; en daorum hebbe ze in Haore un plaotsvervanger gehad van Bokstul, ik wit nie mir hoe die hiet. De jonker zee allenig mar: wie ut wordt wit ik al, en da wies toen nog niemand, en hij liet iemand um halluf jaor teveure bij um komme, en da was un zekere Schijvuns; ze hebbe hier wel vier of vèf jaore un plaotsvervanger gehad, mar ut is utgekomme wa de jonker ha gezeet, en zo zèn ur nog zoveul dinge. \nWie da ok wir gewist is tusse burregemister Van den Oever en Schijvens in wit ik nie mir, mar da da waor is moet te vinde zèn; al lang teveure wies hij al wie ut zou worre, op ut gemintehuis moet da nog wel te vinde zèn wie ut was. \nDe Van den Oevers hadde ut bij de jonker bedurreve mee unne weg legge. De jonker wouw de harde weg over dun dreef hebbe en Van den Oever wouw um langs zèn huis hebbe, en da kon ie nie kére, dun jonker, want dun harde weg kwaam daor.","l":"Brabants"},{"n":130141,"r":"VELDHUYZEN000109","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A person born with a caul, called in because of a missing girl, predicts that she is lying in the yard, and this comes true. The girl is found in a well.","i":"J.V.","o":"Dit verhaal ken je alle mensen vragen, ze weten dan direct over wie het gaat.\n Ik heb vroeger privé-les gehad van Sjors Heering. Die was de oprichter van hotel Spaander. Die was getrouwd en had een dochtertje van een jaar of vijf, zes. Toen overleed zijn vrouw. Na een tijdje is t’ie met een Poolse vrouw getrouwd. Lutemitski heette zij. Op de kermis kwamen veel duitse en poolse kermisgasten, die dan wel de winter overbleven. \nOp een keer was zijn dochtertje zoek, ze konden ze nergens vinden. Toen hebben ze er een telepaat bij gehaald, iemand die dus met de helm geboren is. Die zei dat ze nog op het erf moest zijn. Ze hebben ze toen in de put gevonden. Die vrouw hebben ze toen gearresteerd."},{"n":130144,"r":"VELDHUYZEN000112","p":"Amsterdam","v":"N.-H.","y":1968,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Because his family refuses to sell the caul of a man born with a caul, he died young.","i":"J.V.","o":"Er kwam wel eens een kapitein van een koopvaarder, die veel geld over had voor een vluus. Hadden ze hem maar van oom Jan verkocht, dan had ie nog wel geleefd. Maar dat wilden ze toen niet."},{"n":25579,"r":"CJ055502","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":null,"d":"Two friends once went to a card reader. She predicted that they would soon have work at the sugar factory. For one of them it came true, for the other it did not.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der binne guon, dy kinne wiersizze.\nIk wyt dìt der fan.\n't Wie yn 'e krisisjierren. It wie in minne en nuvere tiid. Us heit wie op 't sûkerfabryk, dy hie wurk.\nKlaes wie in maet fan my. Dy woe wol mollefange, mar hy hie net in houn. Myn broer sei: \"Kinst wol sinten fan my krije foar in houn\", mar dat woe Klaes net.\nHy sei: \"Ik wol de sinten sels fortsjinje. Earst mar ris nei 't sûkerfabryk.\"\nMar né, dêr wie gjin wurk foar him. Op it strûpfabryk èk net. Foar my wie dêr ek gjin wurk.\nKlae sei tsjin my: \"Sille wy us nei in kaertlizter?\"\nDat gong oan.\nDy kaertlizter sei tsjin Klaes: \"Jim ha der op út west. Jim ha dêr en dêr hinne west. Mar dat is mislearre.\nMar der binne jo sinten oanbean. Dêr matte jo mei dwaen hwat jou doel is.\"\nDoe kom ik foar.\n\"Jo binne mei 't selde doel fuortgong\", sei se. \"Mar 't wie mis, hè? Mar jo komme der àl.\"\n\"Kom ik àl op 't sûkerfabryk?\" sei 'k.\n\"Ja\", sei se.\nDoe sei se tsjin my: \"Nou matte jo oan hwat tinke; dan sil ik sizze, hwat dat is.\"\nDoe tocht ik: Dan wol 'k fan 'e wike op in joun mei dat fanke.\nSy sei: \"Hwat jo tinke, dat kinne jo wol dwaen, hear.\"\n\"Hwat is dat dan?\" frege ik.\n\"Hwat jo tinke fan dat fanke, dat kin wol\", sei se.\nDy wiersizter wenne yn Grins.\nTwa dagen letter stjûrde heit in telegram: ik moest op 't Sûkerfabryk komme.\n(Klaes hat der noait west.)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25580,"r":"CJ055503","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":null,"d":"A card reader predicted that his girlfriend would not live much longer. He would meet someone else on a road some distance from here. That is how it happened.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha forkearing hawn, ik bin net mei har troud, mar ik ha in soan by har woan. Sy is fuort dêrnei stoarn.\nDoe't se noch leefde, kom ik by in kaertlizter. Dy sei: ik hie har net lang mear. Mar ik soe in oaren ien treffe op in rûm ein wei.\nDat is allegear útkom. 't Hie hurdsilen west yn Grou, doe trof ik dêr op 'e wei ien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25688,"r":"CJ056221","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":null,"d":"Two couples once came to Hinke Kaert to have their fortunes told. They wanted to fool her by each sitting next to the other's partner. But she saw through it at once.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der kommen ris twa pearkes by Hinke Kaert. Dy woenen de takomst wol wite. Mar sy hienen ôfpraet, sy soenen Hinke der tusken nimme en wienen forkeard by elkoar sitten gong: de iene siet by de oare syn faem. Sy hienen fan fannen forwiksele.\nMar Hinke fornaem it dalik. \"Jo hearre by dizze,\" sei se, \"en jo by dy.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25778,"r":"CJ056819","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man who was born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Willem Bos fan 'e Harkema wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest altyd alles sjen. Nachts moest hy der út. Dan bleau er op 't eigen hiem stean. Dêr seach er de bigraffenis passearen.\nHy hat de bigraffenis fan myn mem sa ek fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25836,"r":"CJ057214","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A girl was born with a caul, so she always saw everything before it happened. She always went out at night. She always knew who was going to die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn omke hie in foardochter. Dat wie Romkje. Dy moest nachts alles sjen. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Nachts gong se der op út. Sy wist altyd hwa't der stjerre soenen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25898,"r":"CJ057610","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man who was born with a caul heard wailing coming from the water at a certain spot. He predicted that someone would drown there one day. But now it has become a road, so some other accident will probably happen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hier is een weg, dat is de Bosweg. Froeger noemden se dat de Klontjebuurt. 't Was toen in olle reed met woater.\nDouwe het doar is gejammer hoard. Se dochten altyd, dat doar noch us een fordrinken moest, moar nou it in weg is kan 't ook wel een ander ongeluk wordn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25907,"r":"CJ057708","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A woman who was born with a caul knew everything in advance. In the evenings she stood by the road watching.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Petten wenne Jille Antsje (J. Hamstra syn wiif). Dat minske wie mei de helm geboaren, seinen se. Dy wist alles foarút. Hja wenne dêr hiel iensum, mar hja wist krekt hwa't der by har lâns komme soenen. Ik en myn wiif binne der is op in nacht om twa ûre lâns kom. Doe stie hja op 'e daem; krekt as wachte se ús op.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25932,"r":"CJ057811","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":null,"d":"Tryn Snipel was a card reader. She once predicted to a woman that she would not live to be old. The woman died when she was 47.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Tryn Snipel, syn wiif, kom us by ús mem, doe gong ús heit krekt fuort. Doe sei se: \"O, o, dy wurdt net âld.\"\nMar dêr hat se ús mem mei bidoeld, dy is mar sawn en fjirtich jier woarn.\nDer kom altyd in protte jongfolk by Tryn Snipel. Sy lei har de kaert.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25933,"r":"CJ057812","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":null,"d":"A card reader predicted to a young woman that one day she would go across the water and not come back. The woman went into service with a divorced minister and married him. But after some years he wanted to be rid of her and took her to Ameland. There he drowned her in the sea.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jits Spoelstra wenne op 'e Houtigehage. Sy gong us op in kear nei lytse Kjille op 'e Gordyk. Dat wie in kaertlizter. Jits wie doe noch net troud.\nKjille sei tsjin har: \"Dû silst in kear oer 't wetter hinne gean, mar ik wit net ast wol werom komste.\"\nJits wie letter by in dûmny as húshâldster. Hy wie by de earste frou wei en troude letter mei Jits. Mar doe woed er ek wol wer fan Jits ôf. Hy nom har mei nei 't Amelân en dêr hat er har forsûpt yn 'e sé.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":25934,"r":"CJ057813","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":null,"d":"A card reader once predicted to a young woman that she would go into service across the water and would fall down the stairs there. That came true. She went to work as a maid in Velzen and fell down the stairs there with a bucket of water.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik ha sels ek al ris in kear by Kjille west. Sy sei tsjin my: \"Dû giest fuort to tsjinjen oer 't wetter en dan silstû fan 'e trap falle.\" 't Is útkom. Ik haw in skoftsje as faem yn Velzen west en dêr bin 'k mei in amer wetter fan 'e trap fallen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26072,"r":"CJ058703","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":null,"d":"A doctor in Akkrum invented a steam engine. He wanted to call it the 'walk-alone'. The notary predicted it would come to nothing. When the machine was finished, the doctor could not control it, and it smashed everything to pieces.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Akkrum wenne in dokter, dy foun in mesine út. 't Wie in stoommesine. As er klear wie soe er hite de rin-allinne.\nDe notaris sei: \"'t Wurdt neat.\"\nDoe't de dokter de mesine klear hie, koed er him net bistjûre. Hy jage alles oan fodden en flarden. Alles hwat fóár him kom, gong kapot. De notaris krige wol gelyk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26115,"r":"CJ059007","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man who was born with a caul always saw funeral processions in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Boardzer Bruining fan 'e Boelensloane koe nachts alle lykstaesjes sjen. As der ien wie moest hy der nachts út. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren. As er mei ien oproan, sei er wol gauris: \"Gean even oan kant.\" Dan seagen dy minsken neat, mar hy wòl.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26325,"r":"CJ060819","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"If you are born with a caul or buy one, you are bulletproof. Doctors sometimes secretly take these cauls and sell them on to bigwigs. Officers and commanders also carry cauls.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei de helm geboaren is, is kûgelfrij. Ek deselde dy't sa'n helm keapet. Dokters nimme wol helms mei sûnder dat de âlders fan 't bern it witte. Hege omes jowe der tûzenen foar. Ofsieren en oversten ha helms by har.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26918,"r":"CJ061810","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"SINLEG 0023","d":"On the way, my brother-in-law and I rest for a moment at a spot where father will later have his house. At this spot we see a little red light. Later we learn that the red light is a little curtain hanging in front of the window. It was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn swager en ik gongen us om in sekfol baelders út.\nDoe rêstten wy even ûnderweis. 't Wie op in joun en al \nmoai-let. Wy sieten op in plak, dêr't tichte by ús heit letter syn wentsje krigen hat. Mar dat wisten wy doe noch net. Mar doe seagen wy der in read ljochtsje.\nKrekt op datselde plak kom letter heit syn wentsje to stean. Der siet in rútsje yn mei in read gordyntsje der foar. Dat hie dat reade ljochtsje west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26975,"r":"CJ062401","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul is bulletproof in war. Doctor Andriessen once burned a caul just after the birth, because otherwise the child would be unhappy all its life. Such a caul is worth a lot of money.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't in helm hat is kûgelfrij yn 'e oarloch. Dokter Andriessen fan Grootegast hat der weest bij de geboorte van een kiend bij minsken hier. Hy het seit: \"Ik kan dat ding duur ferkoopn, moar ik wil 't kiend niet ongelukkig moakn.\" Hy het it opbrând. So'n helm is tweehonderd gulden weerd.\nHij moet onmiddellijk fernietigd worden, anders is 't kiend levenslang ongelukkig.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":26983,"r":"CJ062409","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":null,"d":"Gurbe lives with a girl in Skieding, and a fortune-teller predicts that the girl will die when she is twenty-one. Although other people dismiss it as nonsense, it keeps gnawing at her. She has his child at her family's home, and on the thirteenth day she gets peritonitis and dies. She has just turned twenty-one, so the fortune-teller was right.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doar woonde froeger een feintje bij de Skieding, die huisde doar met een meisje. 't Was Gurbe Steensma. Hij woont nu in Drachten in Rustoord. 't Meiske ging noar de koartlegger. Die sei, 't meiske sou overlijden as se een en twintig joar old was.\nDe minsken seiden teugen hoar: Loof doar niet in, moar 't sat heur altijd dwars. Se moest der altijd an denken.\nToen moest se in kiend hebbn fan Gurbe. Se is bij de familie fan heur befallen. 't Was in jonkje. Die is nu al lang groot. Gurbe was in die tijd bij syn moeke.\nDe dertiende dag kreeg sij buikfliesontsteking en toen was se so moar dood. Krekt een en twintig joar.\nDe woarsegger had wel gelyk.","l":""},{"n":27118,"r":"CJ063624","p":"Soesterberg","v":"Utr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who are born with a caul are also bulletproof.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":27242,"r":"CJ064315","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"SINLEG 0023","d":"Father once sees a whole row of wild lanterns giving off light. He predicts that houses will soon be built on that spot, and later the Warmoldsstraat is built there.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Heit en dy seagen froeger ris in hiele rige wylde lantearnen.\nIt wienen allegear ljochtsjes. Hwat hjir nochris gebeure sil, seinen heit en dy, it wurde hjir skielk allegear huzen. En dat is útkom. It wie de Warmoldsstrjitte, dêr't dy ljochtsjes wienen; der stie doe net in hûs. Nou bin 't allegear huzen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27254,"r":"CJ064327","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"One night Wibe Alma and Knjillis Hit are in Jille Antsje's yard to steal kale. Knjillis then says that Jille was born with a caul and sees everything. Jille is indeed standing at the window, and they run off fast.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn skoanheit Wibe Alma en syn omke Knjillis Hut wienen us op in kear op in nacht op it hiem fan Jille Antsje om moes (= boerekoal) to stellen. Doe sei skoanheit tsjin Knjillis sa:\n\"Dat âld wiif is mei de helm geboaren. Dy sjocht alles.\"\n\"Soe 't sa wêze?\" sei Knjillis. En sy seagen beide tagelyk nei 't hûs. En dêr seagen se Antsje foar 't glês stean.\nDêr hienen jy it al. Sy binne hurd útnaeid.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27351,"r":"CJ065108","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul sees funerals in advance. They have to get out of bed to see them, and so know in advance who will die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei de helm geboaren is sjocht bigraffenissen foarút.\nSokken matte út bêd wei om se to sjen. Likele Kuipers wie ek sa'n man. Dy wist fan tofoaren as der ien stoar, seinen se. Hy wenne to Grinzer Pein oan 'e Skieding.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27375,"r":"CJ065203","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":null,"d":"A group of boys once called names at an old woman who was said to be a witch. The woman made as if to jump across the four-metre ditch, and the boys ran off as fast as they could. She often had to get up at night to see funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wenne yn Twizelerheide in âld minske, dat wie Minne Ael, dy gong foar in tsjoenster troch. Hja wie nachts faek warber. Hja wenne oan 'e Swâdde. Dy wie sa'n fjouwer meter breed.\nOp in kear skelden in pear jonges har út, dy wienen oan 'e oare kant fan 'e Swâdde. Doe die se in pear stappen achterút en sei: \"Ik sil jim krije\", krekt as soe se in oanloop nimme.\nDoe naeiden dy jonges hurd út.\nHja moest der nachts út as der in lykstaesje ûnderweis wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27478,"r":"CJ066004","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":null,"d":"A woman once went to a card reader. The card reader predicted many things for her, all of which came true. She would divorce and remarry. She would move house. Her son would get a permanent job as a driver within four weeks. She would win something in the lottery. She would lose her purse. Her daughter's husband would get cancer, and so on.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn wiif is sauntsjin jier jonger as ik. Sy is fan har earste man skeiden. Sy hat ris in kear nei in kaertlizter yn Grins west.\nHja sei tsjin dy kaertlizter: \"Ik woe graech de takomst wite fan 't leven.\"\nDe kaertlizter hie tsien kaerten op in rige lizzen. Dêr moest myn wiif trije trijetallen fan opnimme. De tsiende bleau lizzen.\nDe kaertlizter kearde de kaerten om. Doe sei se: \"Jo binne geskeiden. Jo binne nou by in hiel goeije man (!) Doe sei se: \"Jo komme tusken 't Fean en Drachten to wenjen.\" (Dat is allegear neikom) Doe sei se: \"Der komt binnenkoart in sterfgefal by jo yn 'e famylje.\" Dat kloppe ek. Har broer Marten fan Aldegea stoar.\nDoe frege myn wiif nei har soan. Dy hie op dat stuit gjin wurk. Sy woe graech wite of er ek gau wurk krije soe.\nDoe sei se: \"Binnen fjouwer wike tiid hat jou soan fêst wurk.\"\nEn doe makke se de biwegings fan ien dy't achter 't stjûr fan in auto sit (mei de earms). Dat kom nei. Hy kom op in greate auto to riden fan 'e Mearumer molkfabryk.\nDoe sei se, myn wiif moest op har beurs passe, dy rekke se kwyt.\nLetter sleepte se har beurs wei mei fyftich goune der yn.\nSy sei ek noch, myn wiif moest lotten keapje. Dan soe se hwat winne. Dat is ek gebeurd. Myn wiif hat inkelde kearen hwat woan, ûnder mear in wollene tekken.\nDoe sei se, wy soenen nòch ris forhúzje, fan Grinzer Pein ôf.\nDat is ek gebeurd. Yn 1966 binne wy hjir yn Mearum kom.\nSe sei, myn wii","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27499,"r":"CJ066411","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul is bulletproof. Paul Krüger was born with a caul and therefore bulletproof. He saw all sorts of things. At night he had to get up to see funerals. He was clairvoyant.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ien dy't mei de helm geboaren wie, wie kûgelfrij. Paul Krüger wie ek kûgelfrij. Hy wie ek mei de helm geboaren en moest alles sjen. Nachts moest hy der út. Dan seach er bigraffenissen.\nHy wie heldersjende.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27551,"r":"CJ066903","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man who was born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funeral processions, whether he wanted to or not.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As heit it oer sokke dingen hie sei mem: \"Dû mast dy dêr stil oer hâlde. Dêr meije wy net oer prate.\" Mem hie der in hekel oan.\nAs hy der yn 'e nacht op út west hie, sei mem: \"Hè, hwerom hast der nou wer út west?\" Mar hy koe net oars, hy moest it sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27649,"r":"CJ067908","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Sunday's children are swaddling-binders. Someone born with a caul sees funerals in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ien dy't op in snein geboaren is, dy kin knoffelbannen lizze.\nDy't mei de helm geboaren is sjocht bigraffenissen fantofoaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27687,"r":"CJ068306","p":"Noordwijk","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul sees things in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ien dy't mei de helm geboaren is sjocht de dingen foarút. Froeger lieten se de helm sitte. Nou komt dat hast net mear foar.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38681,"r":"CJ069503","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Whoever is born with a caul sees funerals in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon wurde mei de helm geboaren. Sokken sjogge fantofoaren bigraffenissen. Dan stjert der gauachtich ien. Sokke minsken wurde twongen om it to sjen. Sy kinne dan net op bêd bliuwe.\nMinsken matte jouns noait midden op 'e wei rinne. Hwant soms komt der in lykstaesje oan. Dan kinne se sa gau net fan 'e wei ôf komme. Dan geane se foar by de lykwein op, rjocht oer de kiste hinne en achter tûmelje se der by del.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27844,"r":"CJ069606","p":"Marum","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":null,"d":"In the old days there were people who went outside at night to see a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In Opende waren mensen die gingen 's nachts lopen om een lijkstatie te zien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27850,"r":"CJ069802","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A woman was born with a caul. She often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. The next day she always had a terrible headache.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ulbe Akke fan Moddergat wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest der nachts út. Hja woarde wekker en wie dan alhiel oerstjûr. Dan seach se in lykstaesje. Hja hat ek de lykstaesje sjoen fan 'e buorfrou dy't tsjin har oer wenne.\nAs hja wer in lykstaesje sjoen hie, wie se de oare deis mâl fan 'e pine yn 'e holle.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27981,"r":"CJ070904","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":null,"d":"One should never walk in the middle of the road at night, or one runs the risk of running into a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne, wol men net it gefaer rinne tsjin in lykstaesje op to rinnen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27982,"r":"CJ070905","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Some people born with a caul have to go out at night to see funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon dy't mei de helm geboaren binne, matte nachts út bêd wei. Dan matte se der op út om lykstaesjes to sjen. Dat soart minsken hienen je froeger oeral wol.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":27993,"r":"CJ071002","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Douwe Stavasius was born with a caul. He always knew in advance who would die. Sometimes sick people went to him to ask whether they would die or get better. If Douwe then said: \"Just go home calmly,\" they knew they would get better.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn 'e Pein wenne in man, dy wie mei de helm geboaren.\nDat wie Douwe Stavasius. As der ien slim siik wie gong men wol nei him ta. Dan fregen se him of er ek hwat sjoen hie. Dan kommen se to witen as de dea neiby wie of net. Hwant hy liet altyd wol hwat út. Sei er: \"Gean mar rêstich nei hûs\", dan bitsjutte dat [dat] der foarlopich gjin gefaer wie en hy neat sjoen hie.\nHeit hat ris in kear nei him ta west foar ien dy't slim siik wie. 't Wie in famke. Sy leeft nou noch.\n\"Gean mar wer rêstich nei hûs\", sei Douwe. Dat wie in teken, dat der gjin gefaer by wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28012,"r":"CJ071112","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Knjillis Veenstra was born with a caul. Because of this he often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. He also saw in advance how his daughter drowned and how his son hanged himself from an apple tree. Of his other son he knew in advance that he would marry another, much younger woman, who would die in childbirth.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Twizelerheide wenne in sekere Knjillis Veenstra. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy gong der nachts faek út. Dan moest er lykstaesjes sjen. Hy woarde dreaun. Hy moest soms sa hurd, dan hied er net iens tiid om him fatsoenlik oan to klaeijen. Dan hied er mar gau hwat bêddeguod om him hinne goaid, lyk as in lekken ensa. Hy roan soms oan 't spoar ta. Hy hat sjoen fan tofoaren dat syn eigen dochter har foar syn hûs fordronk.\nHy hie in soan, dy wie troud, dy wenne dat nei Westergeast út. Hy seach fan tofoaren, dat dy soan him ophong yn 'e apelbeam.\nKees wie in rare, botte keardel. 'Keke' seinen se tsjin him.\nKnjillis hie ek in soan, dy wie molkrider. Dy wie troud; syn frou kom út 'e Twizeler Mieden.\nHy sei tsjin syn soan: \"It giet strak raer mei jim.\"\n\"Hoe sa\", sei de soan. Hy sei: \"Dû rekkest aenst by 't wiif wei en dû troust wer mei in oar frommes, dat folle jonger is as dû. En dy stjert yn 'e kream.\"\nDat kom allegear út. De man troude mei in jonger frommes. Hja forstoar yn 'e kream. Hja wie de earste dy't op 't nije tsjerkhôf to Twizel biïerdige woarde. Hja hie in wite doek oerhoeks oer de kiste lizzen. Dat hie Knjillis allegear fan tofoaren sjoen.\nHy hoefde der net àlle nachten út. En doe't er âlder woarde hoefde er sa fier net mear to rinnen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28037,"r":"CJ071302","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Some people are born with a caul. If the caul is first pulled up from the front and removed that way, those people quite often see things. Doctors sometimes sold these cauls for a lot of money, because someone with such a caul was protected, and some are even bulletproof.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der binne minsken dy wurde mei de helm geboaren. As se dy helm fan tofoaren omheech lûke en sa ôfnimme, dan sjogge sokke minsken hwat. Dy helms woarden froeger troch de dokters foar in protte jild forkocht. Guon dy't sa'n helm hienen wienen kûgelfrij. Elkenien dy't sa'n helm hat, wurdt biskerme.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28114,"r":"CJ071821","p":"Moddergat","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A woman was born with a caul. She often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. Because of this she always knew who was going to die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Moddergat wenne in frou, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy wist altyd hwa't der stjerre soe. Nachts gong se fan bêd ôf om de lykstaesjes to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28160,"r":"CJ072107","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":null,"d":"A woman once took a bite of an apple she had been given by a witch. Someone who was born with a caul told her she should not have done that. She might just as well have bitten into a toad, and then she would have been poisoned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us mem fortelde, hja hie us in apel krige fan Alle Tet. Mem biet der yn. Doe sei Hindriks Janke (dy't mei de helm geboaren wie) tsjin har: \"Saek, Saek, dat mast noait wèr dwaen. Hiest ek wol yn in pod bite kind!\" Dan hie mem forgiftige west en yn 'e macht fan 'e tsjoenster.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28205,"r":"CJ072712","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul is bulletproof. People sometimes get a lot of money for such a caul, because it protects people from accidents.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei de helm geboaren wurde binne skotfrij. De helms woarden froeger wol djûr forkocht, hwant dy biskermen de minsken tsjin ûngelokken, seinen se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28226,"r":"CJ072908","p":"Kornhorn","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man was born with a caul. He often had to get up at night to see funerals.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Een zekere Zwart was met de helm geboaren. Die kwam achter Grotegast weg. Die ging 's nachts op stap om begrafenissen te zien. Hij kon van tevoren zeggen woar een begrafenis zou komen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28236,"r":"CJ072918","p":"Kornhorn","v":"Gr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"If a seer's caul is not burned, he has to see all misfortunes, such as funeral processions and the like.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wanneeer de helm van een ziener niet verbrand wordt, moet hij alle ongemakken zien, zoals lijkstaatsies en dergelijke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28260,"r":"CJ073204","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"If someone was born with a caul, he saw funeral processions in advance. He would then warn others to step aside for a moment.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn âlden fortelden, it gebeurde froeger wol gauris, dat guon lykstaesjes fantofoaren seagen. Hied er ien by him, dan sei er: \"Gean even oan kant, der komt in lykstaesje oan.\" Sa'n ien wie mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28357,"r":"CJ074115","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":null,"d":"A man always saw funeral processions at night. A farmhand refused to believe it and went with him one night. He saw nothing, but when he looked over the man's left shoulder, he too saw one coming. From then on the man no longer saw them, but the farmhand did.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hindrik de Groot wenne yn Skoat. Hy seach altyd lykstaesjes fan tofoaren. Der wie in boerefeint dy woe dat net leauwe.\n\"Kom dan mar ris mei,\" sei Hindrik, \"dan silstû it èk sjen.\"\nDoe gongen se der op in nacht togearre op út.\nDoe sei Hindrik: \"Dêr komt wer in lykstaesje oan.\"\n\"Ik sjoch neat\", sei de feint.\n\"Sjoch dan mar oer myn linker skouder hinne\", sei Hindrik.\nDat die dy feint en doe seach er de lykstaesje èk.\nMar doe seach Hindrik de Groot it nèt mear. Dy wie it tonei kwyt. De feint moest it nou altyd sjen. It wie op him oergien.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28364,"r":"CJ074122","p":"Oranjewoud","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 3109","d":"Witches make wreaths in pillows. Whoever sleeps on such a pillow will die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tsjoensters makken krânsen yn 'e kessens. As der in krâns dien wie gong deselde dy't der op slepte dea.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28367,"r":"CJ074201","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":null,"d":"A woman often made predictions. She could also read coffee grounds. It always came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde frou Reitsma (Wybenga) fan 'e Koaten is de skoanmem fan myn suster Roas. Roas hat it wol gauris oer har. Sy kin kaertlizze en sy kin yn 't kofjedik sjen. Dêr kin se de takomst út gewaer wurde. En 't komt altyd út. Ik bin eins mar in bytsje bang foar har. Op in kear sei se: \"Ik krij hjoed in roun ding mei in stâlle.\" Dyselde jouns brocht har dochter har in koekpanne mei.\nTsjin har soan sei se: \"Forkeapje noait in koe op 'e trettsjinde fan 'e maend.\"\nHja bigjint ek noait op 'e 13e mei in nije sok to breidzjen. Hwant dan komt der in ûngelok.\nHar dochter yn Westergeest wie al wit hoe lang troud en hie noch gjin bern. Hja sei: \"Dû hoechst dy net ûngerust to meitsjen, fanke, hwant dû krijst in poppe, hear. Ik ha 't sjoen.\" Letter krige se in famke.\nUs mem wie op in kear by myn suster Roas to praten.\nDoe't se fuort wie, kom frou Reitsma dêr. Tafallich krige se it kopke yn hannen, dêr't ús mem út dronken hie. Dêr sieten noch in pear théblêdden yn. Hja seach der yn en doe sei se: \"Dy't dêr út dronken hat, dy stiet noch wol hwat to wachtsjen.\" Us mem krige datselde jiers kanker oan 'e slokdarm, dêr't se oan stoarn is.\nOp in kear sei se: \"Hark ris, sa nuver let de klok. Der sil him hjir tichteby yn 't koart ien ophingje.\" It duorre mar even doe fortelden se dat der hie to Jistrum in frommeske har ophong. De klok hie klipt, sei se.\nEk us in kear doe sei se: \"Nou sil der hjir flakby in","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28437,"r":"CJ074709","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A woman was born with a caul. At night she often had to get up to see something.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Twizelerheide wennet in frommeske, dat is mei de helm geboaren. Nachts mat se der ôf. Dan wurdt der kloppe. Dan mat se wer hwat sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28438,"r":"CJ074710","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man was born with a caul. He saw all sorts of things in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Lytse Roel van Kammen wennet yn Kollumersweach, yn in hok oan 't spoar. Dy is ek mei de helm geboaren. 't Is in swalker, hy sjocht fan alles fan tofoaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28475,"r":"CJ075305","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 2901","d":"If you are born with a caul, you are bulletproof, just like Freemasons. Doctors are mad about such a caul and spirit it away. Then in wartime they are bulletproof.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Deselden dy't mei de helm geboaren wurde binne kûgelfrij.\nFrijmetselers binne ek kûgelfrij.\nDe dokters wienen earen fûl op sa'n helm. Dy helm knoffelen se achterút. Yn tiden fan oarloch droegen se dy helm by har, dan wienen se kûgelfrij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":28625,"r":"CJ076709","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1969,"c":"TM 3101","d":"Janke has a baby and an old neighbour woman comes to swaddle it. Then Janke falls ill and her husband goes to fetch Hinke Kaert from Nijebrug. She finds that Janke is bewitched and takes a blue stone out of the road. She puts something under it and lays the stone back in front of the door. She predicts that the neighbour will not come in but will ask how Janke is doing. That indeed happens, and the husband gives the little woman a sound beating. In the pillow they find feather wreaths. The little woman stayed away.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn wiif har pake en beppe wennen yn Beets. Njonken harren wenne in âld-wyfke, dat kom dêr folle oer 'e flier.\nAs der in bern geboaren waerd, dan kaem hja dêr to bakerjen.\nMar op in kear doe waerd beppe Janke siik.\nDoe gong pake nei Nijebrêge nei Hinke Kaert. Hinke gong mei nei Beets ta.\nHinke sei: \"Hjir is hwat oan 'e gong. Jo binne bitsjoend, Janke. Mar ik sil jo helpe.\"\nHinke helle in stien út 'e groun wei foar de middeldoar. 't Wie in blauwe stien. Doe die se hwat yn it gat en doe de stien der wer oerhinne.\nSy sei: \"Nou sil de buorfrou moarn komme om to freegjen hoe't it mei Janke giet, mar sy komt net oer de drompel. Sy bliuwt by de doar stean en dan freget se wol hoe't it mei jo is.\"\nSa gebeurde 't ek.\nDe oare deis bleau 't âld-wiif by de doar stean, ynpleats dat sy der yn kaem. En sy frege: \"Hoe is 't mei Janke?\"\nPake sei: \"Dat sil 'k dy fortelle, hoe 't mei Janke is.\" En doe krige er de strykstok (= strikel) en dêr joech er it âld-minske in pear flinke meppen mei. Hja wie woest.\n(Beppe is it to witten kaem, dat se bitsjoend wie, doe't se it kessen iepenmakke. Dêr sieten krânsen fan fear yn. Allerhande kleuren wienen dêr yn forwurke. De allermoaiste fearren en alle soarten fan lapkes. In wûnder, sa moai.)\n't Ald-minske hat noait wer binnendoar west.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29324,"r":"CJ080520","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul is bulletproof.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":29342,"r":"CJ080617","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who were born with a caul saw funerals in advance. Because of this they always knew exactly who would die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn 'e Harkema wennen froeger guon dy koenen altyd krekt fantofoaren fortelle as der wer ien stjerre soe.\nDy seagen de bigraffenis al fan tofoaren. Sokken wienen mei de helm geboaren.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29359,"r":"CJ080713","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man was born with a caul. At night he often had to get up to see funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy wienen ris to Úthuzermeden foar in boer oan 't flaechsteppen.\nAlde Willem Bos (fan 'e Harkema) wie by ús. Op in moarn sei er tsjin heit: \"Ik moest der fannacht út.\" Hy hie hwat sjoen. Willem Bos woarde dan altyd yn 'e nacht warskôge. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren, seinen se. Hy seach altyd lykstaesjes.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29371,"r":"CJ080809","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":null,"d":"A woman could predict the future with playing cards.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Thomas Klare fan Houtigehage koe de takomst forspelle.\nSy die dat mei spylkaerten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29397,"r":"CJ081016","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"TM 2901","d":"When a child was born with a caul, it was removed straight away. The caul was then not burned, but glowing ashes were put on it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Woarde der in bern mei in helm geboaren, dan woarde dy helm fuort forwidere. Hy woarde net forbrând, mar der woarde gleone jiske op dien. Forbrânne mocht net.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29399,"r":"CJ081018","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":null,"d":"In the past some women read cards and predicted the future with them.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Thomas Clare fan 'e Houtigehage hat foar hûnderten de kaert útlein. Mar 't kloppe altyd net hwat se sei.\nHar muoike Tryn Snipel wenne oan 'e Spekloane. Dy koe ek kaertlizze en dat kom yn de regel wol aerdich út.\nAs ien hwat los wie en graech in buorrel mocht, dan sei Clare: \"Jo matte de portemonnaie yn 'e linker bûse dwaen.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29416,"r":"CJ081306","p":"Houtigehage","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man was born with a caul. He always knew in advance who would die soon.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Piter de Graaf wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy wist altyd to sizzen hwer't mei koarten ien stjerre soe. Hy hat wenne oan 'e Dwarsfeart to Drachten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29478,"r":"CJ081719","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Some children are born with a caul. If the caul is burned right at birth, such a person does not have to get up at night later on. Otherwise they have to foresee everything.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon bern wurde mei de helm geboaren. As dy helm fuort by de geboarte forbrând wurdt, hoeve sokke lju der letter nachts net ôf. Oars matte se alles sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":32650,"r":"CJ082112","p":"De Tike","v":"Fr.","y":1970,"c":"TM 4902","d":"If you step on a toad, thunder comes. When it is going to rain, toads come into the house. They are omens.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Trapet men op in pod, dan komt der tonger.\nAs 't reine wol, komme de podden yn 'e hûs.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":207905,"r":"EGGEN002202","p":"Bemelen","v":"L.","y":1970,"c":"TM 3102","d":"Woman heals people and animals, predicts how long the war will last.","i":"C.E.","o":"Onderwerp : helderziendheid.\nTijd : 1914\nPlaats : Gasthuis-Bemelen. \n\nWat ich zellef ins höb mitgemaak: \nbie òs oppe boerderie woort mèt e paar kiër op e jaor gewesje, de grwoate wesj. \nDan waor ummer 'n auw widdevrouw die òs holp. Dat waor e good minsj, die kant van die kunskes. Es ins eine tandpein hauw, of get versjtoēk, of dao waor get mèt e peerd of 'n koo, dan deeg die dat weg. \nNoe weit ich nog good, ’t waor augustus van viërtjiën, d'n oorlog waor sjus aan de gang.\nDoe inderins zaet zie: \"Daen oorlog doert veer jaor en veer maond!\". \nEn 'r haet auch werkelik zwoalang gedoerd!\nDèh, wie kint noe zwoaget?!","l":"Limburgs"},{"n":33145,"r":"CJ087320","p":"Opeinde","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul has to see everything. He is bulletproof.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei de helm geboaren is mat alles sjen. Hy is kûgelfrij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33157,"r":"CJ087503","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A woman was born with a caul and often had to get up at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Aldeboarn wenne in frou dy wie mei de helm geboaren. As der hwat to sjen wie moest sy der nachts altyd ôf. It hindere har bot en sy klage der faek oer.\nDe lju seinen tsjin har: \"Bliuw lizzen, minske.\"\nMar hja sei: \"Dat kin ik net.\"\n\"Och\", seinen se, en sy woenen it net leauwe.\nDoe sei se: \"Jimme matte 't jim foarstelle as dat jim noadich pisje matte. Dan geane jim der èk ôf. Sa mat ik èk sjen.\"\nMar hja fortelde noait hwat se seach.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33193,"r":"CJ087716","p":"Drogeham","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":null,"d":"At night one should never walk in the middle of the road. One can then be driven to the side by a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Nachts mat men noait midden op 'e wei rinne. Men wurdt dan samar oan kant skoud troch in lykstaesje.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33204,"r":"CJ087804","p":"Dokkum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":null,"d":"One should never walk in the middle of the road at night, or else you may run into an invisible funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat noait yn 'e nacht midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant dan kinne jo tsjin in lykstaesje oanrinne, dy't jo net sjogge.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33210,"r":"CJ087810","p":"Dokkum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul is bulletproof.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":33276,"r":"CJ088307","p":"Schagerbrug","v":"N.-H.","y":1971,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funeral processions. After the man had committed a murder, he never found peace again.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sjoerd van der Heide wenne to Aldegea. Dy wie ek mei de helm geboaren. Dy gong der nachts ek ôf om nei bigraffenissen to sjen. Hy hat ris in moart dien, dêr hied er letter in soad lêst fan, hy wie altyd ûnrêstich.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33282,"r":"CJ088313","p":"Schagerbrug","v":"N.-H.","y":1971,"c":null,"d":"A fortune teller once knew the exact birthday of a young man. She predicted that he would go over the water. A year later the man went across the Afsluitdijk to Holland.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw ris in kear op Wergeaster merke west. Dêr wie 'k mei myn kammeraet Ljibbe hinne. Dêr wie ek in wiersizter.\nDêr gongen wy hinne. Dat minske sei presys myn leeftyd op 'e dei ôf. Hja sei: \"Yn dizze hoeke sille jo net lang mear forkeare. Jo geane oer 't wetter.\"\n't Oare jiers gong ik nei Hollân ta. Oer de ôfslútdyk.\n't Kloppe allegear as in bus. Hja die 't mei kaerten.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33297,"r":"CJ088415","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"TM 2901","d":"When children are born with the membrane still over their heads, they are born with a caul. If the membrane is pulled backwards, they will have to see everything later. If it is pulled off forwards, they will not.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der binne bern dy wurde geboaren mei in flues om 'e holle.\nSokken, seit men, binne mei de helm geboaren. As se dat flues achteroer lûke matte sokke bern letter alles sjen.\nAs se it foaroer lûke, dan net. By de Petten yn 'e Harkema hat in frommes wenne dat mei de helm geboaren wie. Dy moest der nachts ôf as der letter in sterfgefal wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33317,"r":"CJ088803","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man born with a caul often had to get up at night to see funerals.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Piter de Graaf wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy wenne op 'e Suderdwarsfeart by de âlde sûkerfabryk. Nachts gong hy der faek op út om bigraffenissen to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33422,"r":"CJ090002","p":"Dokkum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":null,"d":"Hinke Kaert made predictions for two girls. All the predictions later came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hinke Kaert, dy't letter to Nijebrêge wenne, is ôfkomstich fan Wergea. Se seinen dêr yn Wergea altyd Hinke fan Rutsje. Hja hat twakear troud west. Hja hie fjouwer soannen. De fjirde soan wie in oerwinneling.\nIn frou fan Wergea fortelde my ris: ik haw mei in freondin as greatfanke nei Nijebrêge ta west. Hja sei tsjin my: \"Jo sille noch tsien jier faem bliuwe. Dan sille jo trouwe en fier fuort gean. Jimme sille it goed dwaen en dan weromkomme.\"\nTsjin myn freondinne sei se: \"Jo komme, al ridlik gau, nei oan 'e wei yn in húske to wenjen.\"\nHwat hja dêr foarspeld hat is krekt sa neikom.\nIk bin nei tsien jier troud. Doe binne wy nei Amerika tein. Wy ha dêr bêst buorke. En doe binne wy hjir werkom.\nMyn freondinne krige in healjier letter de tarring. Al gau dêrnei woarde se bigroeven tichte by de dyk yn Wergea. Dat lytse houten hûske wie de deakiste.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33452,"r":"CJ090315","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":null,"d":"A card reader made predictions for a young man. They all came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Fedde Klare (earder Thomas Klare) yn Twizelerheide koe kaertlizze. Ik haw der wol west; it jongfolk gong der wol faek hinne. Sy sei tsjin my: \"Dû krijst glêdde knopen oan 'e jas en dû silst in reis meitsje oer de sé.\"\nDat is beide útkom. Ik haw ûnder tsjinst west - dat wie doe noch net bikend - en dêr krige ik glêdde knopen oan 'e jas. En ik haw in kear oer de Sudersé oer Staveren en Inkhuzen nei Amsterdam ta west.\nKlare skodde de kaerten troch elkoar. Der siet altyd in megere kat by har op 'e tafel. Sy lei de kaerten yn trije hoopkes del. En dan sei se: \"Dit acht je niet. Dit verwacht je niet. Maar dit komt je gewis.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33512,"r":"CJ090501","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A woman predicted to her sister that on coming home she would hear bad news about a relative. That was indeed the case. The woman was born with a caul.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn suster Hiltsje, dy't oan 'e Grinzer Strjitwei wennet by Koaten wyt mear as sljochtwei. Sy woarde mei de helm geboaren. Sterfgefallen en al sokke dingen mear wyt hja fan tofoaren. Ik bin der wolris bang foar west.\nOp in kear wie 'k by har to praten. Doe sei se: \"Astû aenst thús komste dan fornimste dat der ien út jim famylje tige siik is. Dy sil ek wol stjerre. Mar 't is net sa nei yn 'e famylje.\"\nIk kom de jouns thús, doe sei Kij: \"Tryntsjemuoi is ek tige min.\" \n\"O ja\", sei 'k.\nSy is doe ek stoarn. Har man wie in broer fan myn man syn heit.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33513,"r":"CJ090502","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":null,"d":"A woman once predicted to another woman that she would get a flower. She saw it in the coffee grounds. It came true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Myn man Kij syn beppe koe wiersizze. Sy foarspelde ien samar de takomst. Hja hat it o sa krap hawn. Har dochter Antsje sukkele altyd. Sy krige twa dûbeltsjes fan 'e earmfâlden. Op in kear doe wie se by ús en doe seach se wer yn 't kofjedik. \"Hea,\" sei se, \"noait liker as krijstû in blom.\"\nMem sei: \"Hoe komt mem der by. Hwer soe ik in blom wei krije. Hjir komt noait ien mei blommen.\"\n\"Nou,\" sei 't âld-minske, \"tink der mar ris om. It is klear to sjen, dû krijst in blom.\"\nKoarte tiid dêrnei kom der in famke by ús. \"Sjoch,\" sei se, \"hjir ha 'k in loat fan in blom. It is sa'n moaijen ien, dat mem sei, dêr moest ik jo in loat fan bringe.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34481,"r":"CJ090606","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1971,"c":null,"d":"While predicting, a card reader always said: \"This you do not heed. This you do not expect. This will surely come to you.\"","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Fedde Klare (froeger Thomas Klare), de mem fan Tsearde Antsje koe kaertlizze. As jongfolk gongen wy dêr gauris hinne. It duorre sahwat in ûre, dan wie se mei ús klear. Sy bigong altyd sa mei de kaerten:\nDit acht je niet.\nDit verwacht je niet.\nDit komt je gewis.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34501,"r":"CJ090715","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":null,"d":"When the butter would not come, people believed the churn was bewitched. The churning mill sometimes began to turn by itself at night. That was an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As 't net bûterje woe, dan wie de tsjerne bitsjoend, seinen se. De tsjernmoune bigong soms nachts samar út himsels to draeijen. Dat wie foartsjirmerij.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33524,"r":"CJ090908","p":"Twijzel","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"TM 2901","d":"In the past some people were born with a caul. They often had to get up at night to see funerals.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wienen guon, dy wienen mei de helm geboaren. Dy moesten fan to foaren bigraffenissen sjen. De needsaek twong har ta 't bêd út. Sa'n man wie Knjillis Veenstra fan Twizelerheide. Hy wenne by 't spoar.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33538,"r":"CJ091004","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"TM 2901","d":"In the past people were sometimes born with a caul. They were said to see all sorts of things.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Foarhinne wienen der minsken, dy woarden mei de helm geboaren. Dy moesten alles sjen. 't Wienen meast manlju. Men heart der nou net mear fan.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34520,"r":"CJ091908","p":"Harkema","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man was born with a caul. He often had to get up at night to see funerals. Because of this he always knew in advance who would die, but he never wanted to talk about it.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir op 'e buert hat in man wenne, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest altyd bigraffenissen fan tofoaren sjen. Dat gebeurde faek by nacht. Hy hat it wol forteld. Dan lei er op bêd, dan woe er wol lizzen bliuwe, mar dat wie in ûnmooglike saek.'t Wie in geheime driuw. Hy mòest der út en sjen. Hie er 't sjoen dan koe er wer nei hûs ta gean.\nHy wist altyd wol hwa't der stjerre soenen, mar dêr woed er net oer prate.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34527,"r":"CJ092202","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man was born with a caul. At night he often had to get up to see funeral processions in advance. When his son was going to have a baby, he also knew in advance that the baby would be stillborn.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Surhústerfean wenne froeger âlde Sytse Wijma. Sytse wie mei de helm geboaren; hy seach alle bigraffenissen út 'e omkriten fan 't Fean foarút. It kom altyd nei hwat hy fortelde.\nNachts moest hy der faek ôf om lykstaesjes to sjen. It gebeurde wol dat er seach dat se in kiste ûnder 't finster op skouden, dan koe de kiste net troch de doar.\nHy hie in soan, dy hiet Rapke. Dy syn frou forwachte in poppe. Fan tofoaren makke hja dêr allegear guod foar. Doe sei Sytse op in kear tsjin har: \"Fanke, dû hoechst dêr net folle drokte fan to meitsjen, hwant it bern giet dochs dea.\"\nHy krige gelyk. It woarde in dead popke.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34533,"r":"CJ092208","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":null,"d":"A woman never dared to walk in the middle of the road, for fear of running into a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In muoike fan my wenne yn Koartwâld, mar sy hie har wurk yn Stiensgea. Hja roan altyd op 'e berm lâns.\n\"Ik doar net op 'e wei to rinnen,\" sei se, \"hwant dan kin 'k wol ris by in lykstaesje op rinne.\"\n\n.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34549,"r":"CJ092807","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":null,"d":"A man taught his son not to walk in the middle of the road. Otherwise he might run into a funeral procession. The man always saw funeral processions in advance, but did not always know who would die.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wyt noch bêst dat heit my ris op in joune let ophelle hat, doe wie mem siik. Ik roan gewoan de wei lâns, doe sei er tsjin my: \"Dû meist net midden op 'e wei rinne. Dat heart sa net. Der kin ris in lykstaesje oankomme, dan wurdst oan kant reage.\"\nHeit seach de lykstaesjes wol fan tofoaren, mar hy wist net altyd hwa't der stjerre soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33708,"r":"CJ093013","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":null,"d":"Two people had predicted to Hitler how the war would go, and it came true. So Hitler already knew.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Doe't Hitler oan 'e macht kaem, wenne der yn Frankryk in minske, in sikere Madame, dy koe alles foarút sjen. Dêr stjûrde Hitler ien hinne om presys gewaer to wurden hoe't it forrin wêze soe fan syn polityk. It minske hat alles haarfijn forteld. It is krekt sa gong oant yn 'e lytste bysûnderheden ta.\nTrouwens in diplomaet Dimitrow hat him ek foarspeld hoe't it forrin fan 'e oarloch wêze soe. Dat is ek útkom. Dat Hitler wie op 'e hichte.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34601,"r":"CJ093711","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":null,"d":"When a dog howls, our mother says something is going to happen. When black crows walk across the yard, something is about to happen. If the crows let their wings droop, it foretells sorrow and mourning, and if they strut about jauntily, it points to something cheerful. Auntie Hiltsje can always tell from the magpies what kind of clothes people will put on, for mourning or for celebration.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As in houn bigoun to spûkgûlen, sei ús mem: \"Der komt hwat!\"\nAs hjir greate swarte roeken op 't hiem omstapten, sei mem: \"Der komt aenst ek wer hwat. Dat binne leedsizzers.\"\nDat koe se oan 'e roeken sjen. Dy roeken lieten dan de fleugels sakje. Stapten se parmantich dan tsjutte dat op feestlikheit.\nLieten se de fleugels sakje, dan bitsjutte dat fortriet en rou. Us Hiltsjemuoi kin noch altyd oan 'e eksters sjen hwat foar klean de minsken oan krije, dy't komme. Rou of fleur.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":34631,"r":"CJ093924","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"TM 2901","d":"He was born with a caul. If they take the caul off from back to front, he will have to see everything later. But if they pull the caul upwards, he does not have to see.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon wurde mei de helm geboaren. Dy moat der ôf lutsen wurde. As se dy helm fan achteren nei foaren ôflûke, dus fan boppen nei ûnderen, matte se letter alles sjen. Lûke se de helm by 't kin wei omheech, dus nei boppen ta, dan hoeve se neat to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33859,"r":"CJ094802","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":null,"d":"A man always made predictions with the coloured ribbons on his stick. That is how he also predicted that war would come.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir wie in man, dy neamden se Sipke Moaiwaer. 't Wie yn myn jonge jierren al in âld man. Hy hie in stok yn 'e hân, dêr sieten allegear kleurde linten oan. Hy seach altyd yn 'e loft. As de bern him fregen nei 't waer en 't soe moai wurde, dan nom er it blauwe lint yn 'e hân.\nMar hy hat ek foarspeld dat der oarloch komme soe. Dat wie fóár 1914 doe't er dat tsjin 'e bern sei. Doe krige er 't reade lint yn 'e hân. Hy sei: \"Ja berntsjes, jim bileve aenst rare tiden, hwant der komt oarloch.\" Dat is útkom.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":33861,"r":"CJ094804","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":null,"d":"A card reader once could not predict anything, because a boy was laughing terribly.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wy ha ris mei in ploechje jongfolk nei âlde Clara ta west. Dy soe ús de kaert lizze. Mar der wie ien jonge by, dy lake hyltyd. Hy hie mei alles de gek. Doe koe Clara it net dwaen, omdat dy jonge sa lake.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":35915,"r":"CJ094906","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"TM 3401","d":"A gate keeps opening, because a funeral procession has to pass through.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"To Hurdegaryp is in homeije, dy kinne se net ticht hâlde. Se ha dy hekke wol mei dikke kettings fêst makke, it joech neat. De oare moarns wie er wer iepen. Hy stiet noch altyd iepen. Dit komt, dêr mat in lykstaesje lâns. Der stie froeger in kastiel by: Bennemastate. In lykstaesje mei net stopje. Dêr mat alles foar út 'e wei. Dêrtroch giet dy homeije iepen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":35930,"r":"CJ095008","p":"Eastermar","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul is bound to see funeral processions. Do not ride in the middle of the road at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon wurde mei de helm geboaren. Dy sjogge de lykstaesjes foarút. Ik haw sa'n ien noait kend. \"Sy matte it bislist sjen\", sizze se. Us mem sei altyd: \"Rin by nacht noait midden op in paed.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36079,"r":"CJ096225","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1972,"c":null,"d":"Minse Griper could read cards. Many young people always came to him. His predictions were usually right.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Minse Griper fan Boelensloane koe kaertlizze. Dêr gongen wy wolris hinne. Dêr kaem in soad jongfolk altyd. It kloppe wol aerdich hwat er jin fortelde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":35994,"r":"CJ095604","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 3401","d":"There are people who are bound to see everything. They were born with a caul. Often they have to get out of bed at night and walk who knows how far to see the funeral procession. Then the gates are flung open for them.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der binne guon dy màtte alles sjen. Sokken binne mei de helm geboaren. Faek matte se der nachts om út bêd wei komme.\nDan wolle se der net út, mar sy matte. Sa'n ien hat der wenne yn Twizelerheide. 't Wie Knjillis Veenstra.\nSoms moest er wit hoe fier rinne yn 'e nacht om de lykstaesje to sjen, wolris oan Kollumersweach ta. Dan woarden de hekken samar foar him iepensmiten, om it him makliker to meitsjen en dat er op tiid komme soe.\nHy moest soms wit hoe hurd rinne om der to kommen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":35998,"r":"CJ095608","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"A card reader predicts that one lad will marry sooner than the other, and that same year the latter died.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw ienkear yn myn feintejierren by in wiersizter west yn Ljouwert. Myn kammeraet wie by my. De kaertlizter siet by ús en lei de kaerten út inoar. Doe siet se in skoft foar har út to sjen neidat wy in kaert lutsen hienen. Op 't lêst sei se tsjin my: \"Jo trouwe earder as jou kammeraet.\"\nMear woe se net sizze. Wy koenen neat mear út har krije. \nMar datselde jiers noch is myn kammeraet stoarn.\nAs hja dat doe sjoen hat en net fortelle woe?","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36081,"r":"CJ096302","p":"Kollum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"In Sweagerbosk lived an old man who was born with a caul. He always had one sock on and one sock off and was always running about. He also saw funeral processions. At night he often had to get out of bed, and then he ran to arrive in time. The gates opened by themselves. Once he stopped by the railway at Sanbulten and already saw there the dead man who would only fall (from the train) the next day.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Sweagerbosk wenne in âld man, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy hie ien sok oan en ien sok út en roan altyd om. Wy wienen der bang foar, hwant hy seach altyd lykstaesjes. De lju tochten: o hea, as er hjir mar net by ús komt, hwant dan gebeurt der hwat. Meastal wie hy der yn 'e nacht op út. Hy wenne by in poel, oan 't spoar ûnder Twizelerheide. Hy rekke soms raer út bêd wei, hwant hy wòe soms net. Mar hy moest. Hy woarde dreaun, krekt as sieten se him achter. Dan switte hy der soms oer. Soms moest er hiel hurd rinne om op tiid to kommen. Dan gongen de hekken fansels foar him iepen, seinen se.\nEk ris in kear doe fleach er nei 't spoar ta yn Sânbulten. Dêr bleau er stean. Hy stie dêr mar to sjen nei in bipaeld plak. De oare deis foel dêr ien út 'e trein, dy wie opslach dea. Wylst hy dêr stie seach er dy deade dêr al fan tofoaren lizzen.\nSokke dingen wist er altyd foarút. Hwat is nou soks?","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36192,"r":"CJ097111","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 4902","d":"A toad announces thunder. Mud on a snail's tail means rain.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Sjocht men in pod, dan komt der tonger.\nSjocht men modder op 'e sturt fan in slak, dan sil 't reine.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36201,"r":"CJ097207","p":"Boelenslaan","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 3105","d":"The youngest of seven daughters is a nightmare, and the youngest of seven sons is born with a caul [possessing supernatural gifts]. Boomsma was such a seventh son, and he could foretell deaths.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Fan sawn dochters is de jongste in nachtmerje.\nAs der sawn jonges binne sit der yn 'e sawnde hwat mear as yn 'e oaren. De sawnde is mei de helm geboaren.\nBoomsma fan 'e Boelensloane wie sa'n ien. Hy hat ús sels wol forteld dat er oan 't tikjen fan 'e klok hearde dat der binne safolle dagen ien nei 't hôf ta brocht wurde soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36268,"r":"CJ097531","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"Kjille was a card reader. When Piter Veenstra came to her, she made very strange predictions. It seemed as if she was holding something back. A short time later Piter was murdered.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Lytse Kjille wenne op 'e Gerdyk. Hja wie kaertlizter. Heit en Piter-om ha ris nei har ta west. Hwat se heit fortelde is allegear neikom. Mar hwat se fan Piter-om sei, dat wienen allegear nuvere forhaeltsjes. It wie krekt, sei heit, as woe se net sizze hwat se sizze moest. Tuskentiden wie se hyltyd stil. Koarte tiid dêrnei woarde Piter-om formoarde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36306,"r":"CJ097711","p":"Buitenpost","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"The storyteller's mother could predict that a man who lived in Holland would never go back there. Shortly afterwards he jumped from a bridge railing and drowned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Wigers Gjertsje hie in soan Theunis, dy wenne yn Hollân. Nou en dan kom er thús by syn mem . Op in kear wie dat wer it gefal. Doe sei ús mem: \"Hy giet net wer nei Hollân ta.\"\nHy is even letter fan 'e brêgeleuning yn 't kanael sprong en forsûpt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36533,"r":"CJ098822","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Some children are born with a caul. That caul must be removed from top to bottom, and not pulled over the forehead: otherwise the child will later be bound to see everything.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der binne bern dy wurde mei de helm geboaren. Men mat der goed om tinke dat dy helm nei ûnderen ta ôflûkt wurdt. Wurdt er nei boven ta ôflûkt, oer de foarholle hinne, dan mat sa'n bern letter alles sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36670,"r":"CJ099506","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People who were born with a caul later saw funeral processions. They often got out of bed at night to look. In the old days we always had to take care not to walk in the middle of the road, because then you could suddenly be thrown into the ditch.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon wurde mei de helm geboaren, dy sjogge letter altyd lykstaesjes. Hja geane nachts faek út bêd wei om der nei to sjen. Tink der om, seinen se froeger tsjin ús, net midden op 'e wei rinne. Oars kinne jim yn 'e sleat smiten wurde.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36681,"r":"CJ099608","p":"Surhuizum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Romkes Ages was born with a caul. He got out of bed at night and ran past the dairy factory to the little bridge. From there he saw all sorts of things that would happen later.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Romke Ages wenne yn Surhuzum. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Nachts gong er faek fan 't bêd en der út. Dan roun er by 't molkfabryk lâns nei 't brechje ta. Dêr gong er op stean en dan seach er fan alles. Dêrtroch wist er altyd fan tofoaren hwat der gebeure soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36704,"r":"CJ099907","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Hindrik was born with a caul. At night he had to get up to see funeral processions. Then he already knew who would die. He also warned people to step aside when he saw such a procession. If they did not, they had an accident or were shoved.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der binne guon, dy wurde mei de helm geboaren. Dy matte lykstaesjes fan tofoaren sjen. Sa'n man ha 'k ek kend to Boarnburgum. Dat wie Hindrik Wybenga. Dy moest der nou en dan nachts út. Dan seach er alle minsken dy't achter 't lyk oan roannen. Dy koed er meast allegear wol en dan wist er meastal èk wol hwa't der stjerre soe. As de lykstaesje der oan kaem gong er oan kant stean. Hy sei ek wolris tsjin 'e minsken: \"Gean even oan kant stean, hwant der komt in lykstaesje oan.\" Dy oare minsken seagen neat. Mar as se net oan kant stean gongen en gjin rûmte joegen, dan krigen se in ûngelok. Dan waerden se stompt.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36754,"r":"CJ100119","p":"Kootstertille","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Some children are born with a caul. They later saw everything. They could foresee death, like my uncle, who had already seen the deaths of all seven of his children in the form of little coffins on the floor.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der binne bern dy wurde mei de helm geboaren. As se dy helm nei boven ta fan 't gesicht lûke, sjogge se letter alles.\nIk haw in skoansuster to Westergeast to wenjen. Dêr njonken wennet in frou dy is mei de helm geboaren.\nIn omke fan my sjocht de dea ek foarút. 't Is in Wybenga.\nSawn kear hat er in bern forlern en alle sawn kearen hat er fan tofoaren de kiste oer de flier stean sjoen. 't Is in broer fan mem. Hy wennet yn 'e Westerein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36785,"r":"CJ100210","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"The same man was once in Amsterdam when there was a funeral. When the funeral procession passed, the man in the coffin began to shout: I want to get out! The bearers were so frightened that they dropped the coffin and ran off.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dyselde man wie ris in kear yn Amsterdam. Doe wie dêr krekt in bigraffenis. Doe't er de lykstaesje foarbykaem bigoun deselde yn 'e kiste to roppen: \"Ik wol derút! Ik wol der út!\" De dragers waerden sa binaud dat hja lieten de kiste donderje en naeiden hurd út.\nIt wie deselde Hearrefeanster dy't dit lapt hie. Hy koe bûksprekke. (Beide teltsjes binne wier bard).","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36818,"r":"CJ100602","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Whoever is born with a caul can foresee who will die. Such a person sees the funeral beforehand. Caul-bearers often have to get up at night.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Us beppe wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy wist altyd krekt as der ien deagean soe. Dan seach se de bigraffenis al fan tofoaren. Dy't mei de helm geboaren binne matte der nachts út.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36830,"r":"CJ100614","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"If a boy wet the bed, he had to urinate on the path on the same day a funeral procession passed, in the same direction the procession was going. Then the bedwetting was over.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der in jonge op bêd pisse (in bêdmiger) dan moest sa'n jonkje deselde deis as der in lykstaesje foarby gong op it paed pisje, deselde kant út mei de strael, dêr't de lykstaesje hinnegong. Dan wie 't bêdpisjen oer.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36839,"r":"CJ100701","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Bontsje Keke was born with a caul. He often had to get up at night to see funeral processions, whether he wanted to or not. The gates opened by themselves for him. He also foresaw the funeral of his own daughter.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Keke wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy wenne yn Twizeler Heide. Nachts moest hy der út as der lykstaesjes wienen.\nSoms woed er net. Mar hy moest. Dan waerd er twongen.\nSoms yn 'e ûnderbroek en op bleate fuotten der op út yn 'e nacht. Sa hurd moest er dan. Dan gongen de hekken foar him iepen. Hwant hy moest op tiid wêze.\nHy hat ek de bigraffenis fan syn eigen dochter fan tofoaren sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36856,"r":"CJ100801","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINLEG 0023","d":"In the old days people often saw lights in the sky. Those were the forerunners of the later aeroplanes.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Froeger waerden hjir ljochtsjes yn 'e loft sjoen. Dat wienen de lettere fliegmesines. Omke hat se faek sjoen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36868,"r":"CJ100813","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 3105","d":"Of seven daughters, one is a nightmare. Nightmares come through the keyhole at night. If you lie on your side they do not bother you, but on your back they do. They come to the foot of the bed and then slowly crawl up to your throat. If you put your slippers upside down in front of the bed, they cannot step into them. Some children are born with a caul. If it is pulled off backwards, nothing is wrong. Otherwise the child will later be clairvoyant.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wienen der sawn famkes yn in gesin dan wie der in nachtmerje by. As men nachts op 'e rêch lei wie der kâns dat de nachtmerje by jin kaem. By 't fuottenein kaem se by jin, stadichoan kaem se heger, op 't lêst wie se oan 'e kiel ta. Lei men op 'e side, dan krige men der gjin lêst fan.\nIn nachtmerje kaem troch 't kaeisgat. Set men de toffels omkeard foar 't bêd, dan kin se dêr net ynstappe. Dan komt se net.\nDer binne bern dy ha in helm op mei de geboarte. As dy helm achteroer lutsen wurdt is it goed. Lûkt men de helm der foaroer ôf, dan mat sa'n bern letter alles sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36881,"r":"CJ100826","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Whoever is born with a caul is bulletproof. The same goes for the owner of a caul. Midwives used to be mad about cauls. They tried to pocket them on the sly and then sell them at a high price. Doctors did so too.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't mei in helm geboaren is is kûgelfrij. Ek deselde dy't in helm yn syn bisit hat is kûgelfrij. De froedfroulju wienen froeger gleon op 'e helmen. Dy knoffelen se achterút en se waerden djûr forkocht. Ek de dokters forkochten se wol.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36916,"r":"CJ101217","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"Once I saw through the window water, a ship, seabirds, and live shellfish on the ship. The prediction has not yet come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in kear seach ik hjir ta 't finster út. Doe seach ik in great wetter, skean troch de finne hinne. Dêr farde in skip oer lâns. Séfûgels fleagen dêr boppe. Yn it skip wienen núnders, dy pipen der oer. Dy beesten wienen noch levend.\n- Dat mat allegear noch neikomme (as it neikomt)","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36923,"r":"CJ101224","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man was born with a caul. He always had to get up at night to see funeral processions. If he did not, he lay there trembling.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 'e Noarderdwarsfeart wenne in man, dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Dy moest der út as der in lykstaesje to sjen wie by nacht. Die er it net dan lei er to triljen. Hy roan soms hiele einen de mieden yn. Hy woarde dreaun.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":36970,"r":"CJ101508","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Caul-bearers always had to get out of bed to see funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon waerden mei de helm geboaren, dy moesten letter lykstaesjes sjen. Hjir hat in sekere Piter de Graaf wenne dy moest altyd út bêd wei om dêr nei to sjen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37093,"r":"CJ101908","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"Never run in the middle of the road at night, because of possible funeral processions.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Noait midden op 'e wei rinne by nacht, fanwege de lykstaesjes, dy't men net sjen kin.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37118,"r":"CJ102301","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"SINLEG 0023","d":"Where there is now a ring road, people used to see lights glowing. Those were the forerunners of the later car headlights.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dêr't nou de rondwei oer de Noarderdwarsfeart hinnegiet seach ús heit froeger oan beide kanten gleone ljochten. Dan sei er: \"Dêr komt nochris hwat.\" Hwant dy gleone ljochten, dat wienen de lettere auto's by joun en by nacht.\nDe man hat gelyk krigen. De rondwei is der kaem en it rydt dêr altyd troch.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37142,"r":"CJ102503","p":"Boornbergum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Joeke Spukguler was born with a caul and had foreseen his death exactly: how he was carried in his coffin out under the window because the coffin would not fit through the hallway.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op 'e Suderdwarsfeart to Drachten wenne Joeke Spûkgûler yn 't sûkerijfabryk. Dy seach dêr dat syn eigen lykkiste ûnder 't glês troch skoud waerd. Se koenen de swaei net krije troch de gong, dêrom moest er ûnder 't glês troch.\nJoeke wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy fortelde dit gefal oan guon. It is krekt sa neikaem.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37160,"r":"CJ102801","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Hantsje was born with a caul. He could see funerals coming in advance.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Yn Tersoal wenne Hantsje Hoekstra. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy hat forskeidene bigraffenissen foarút sjoen. Hy fortelde it de minsken wolris. 't Kaem altyd nei hwat er seach.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37221,"r":"CJ103211","p":"Jistrum","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Jehannes was born with a caul. He had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions, and he had to step aside for them.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Jehannes Tsyske wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy seach bigraffenissen fan tofoaren. Hy kaem der nachts foar út bêd wei. Dan kaem er de lykstaesje tsjin. Hy moest dan oan kant gean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37332,"r":"CJ104001","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Knjillis was born with a caul. He could see people's deaths coming. Caul-bearers are clairvoyant, unless the caul is burned.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir hat wenne oan 't spoar in sekere Knjillis Veenstra, dy't se Bontsje Knjillis en ek wol Keke neamden.\nAs der ien siik wie en dy wie min, dan wist Keke fan tofoaren of dy persoan stjerre soe. Hy moest der dan nachts út, dan seach er de bigraffenis fan dy persoan.\nDy en dy stjert ek, sei er dan, en dat kaem altyd út.\nHy wie mei de helm geboaren.\nIen dy't mei de helm geboaren is mat alles sjen, behalve as se de helm forbrânne.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37336,"r":"CJ104005","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"One should never walk in the middle of the road at night, because of an invisible funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Men mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne by nacht, hwant dan kin men tsjin in lykstaesje oprinne dy't men net sjocht.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37340,"r":"CJ104009","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"Fokje was a card reader. When we were expecting a child, she predicted that our child would die and be buried in a little white coffin. When her husband died, she said that he had still knocked from inside his coffin.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Alde Japiks Fokje hat hjir wenne, dy hat ek yn 'e Koaten wenne. Dat wie in kaertlizter. Sa'n fyftich jier lyn gongen de jonge bazen dêrhinne.\nWy forwachten in berntsje, doe gong ik nei Fokje ta om 'e kaert útlein to krijen.\nMyn frou rekke yn 't sikenhûs, doe't hja yn forwachting wie.\nFokje sei: \"Dat bern krije jim net thús. Ik ha 't bern fannacht yn 't wite kistje lizzen sjoen.\"\n't Is echt gebeurd. It bern kaem yn in wyt kistje to lizzen, sûnder dat ik dêr permisje ta jown hie.\nLetter stoar har man Japik. Ik sei: ik mat der mar even hinne. Ik gong der hinne mei in stik woarst.\nIk sei: \"Japik is stoarn, hè.\" (hy lei yn 'e kiste)\n\"Ja,\" sei se, \"mar hy hat hjoed noch kloppe, wylst er yn 'e kiste lei.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37395,"r":"CJ104103","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"Two sisters once heard the sound of a car engine without seeing anything. That was the omen of the later cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Twa susters fan myn skoanheit wennen yn Surhústerfean.\nHja wienen op in joun oan 't kuijerjen, doe hearden se yn 'e fierte in lûd, krekt sa't nou de motor fan in auto jowt.\nHja hearden in ding oer de wei snuorjen, sûnder dat se it seagen. Dat hat neffens har de oankundiging fan 'e auto's west, dy't der pas folle letter kamen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37406,"r":"CJ104210","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"A man tells that he dreamed that night that he was selling fish with the dog cart. His wife said that was an omen of a death in the family. The man did not believe it, but that is indeed what happened.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Knjillis Kalsbeek fortelde syn frou op in moarn: 'k Ha fannacht droomd dat ik stie yn 'e buorren mei de hounekarre en ik forkocht fisk.\nDoe sei syn frou: \"Oe, dan komt der in deaden yn 'e famylje!\"\n\"Och,\" sei Knjillis, \"praetsjes fan neat. Der stienen allegear froulju om dy hounekarre hinne\", sei er.\n\"Oe,\" sei 't minske, \"wie ik der ek by?\"\n\"Né,\" sei er, \"dû wiest der net by.\"\nKoarte tiid dêrnei is hja stoarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37412,"r":"CJ104216","p":"Augustinusga","v":"Fr.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"On the way, Jan Hepkes met a father and son going to the little farmer for advice, because the old mother was very ill. The little farmer had died that very morning. Jan examined the sick old woman's urine and predicted that she would die within a week anyway. Later he heard that this had indeed come true.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik wie froeger slachtersfeint by Rusticus yn Bûtenpost. Op in kear moest ik nei de slachter yn Burum. Dêr trof ik Jan Hepkes. Doe sei er: \"Dêr hie 'k nyskes in nuver gefal.\"\n\"Hwat dan?\" frege ik.\n\"Ik trof in heit mei in soan op 'e wei. Dy woenen nei 't boerke ta fan Warfstermoune. Ik sei: - Hwat dêr -? - Hja fregen my hwer't it boerke wenne. Ik sei: - Dêr kinne jim wol hinne gean, mar de man lei fan 'e moarn dea op bêd.\"\n\"Och heden,\" seinen se, \"dat is hwat.\"\nIk sei: Skeelt der by jimmes thús hwat oan?\n\"Ja,\" sei de man, \"myn âld minske is lang net goed en nou woenen wy even nei 't boerke ta om ried.\"\nIk sei: \"Ha jim 't wetter by jimme?\"\n\"Ja\", seinen se.\nIk sei: \"Mei 'k it even sjen?\"\nDoe helle de âld man in flesse ta de bûse út yn krantepapier. Dat die'k der ôf en ik skodde de flesse even. En doe hâldde ik him foar de sinne.\nEn doe sei 'k: \"It is miskien slim sein, mar mei 7, 8 dagen is 't minske dea.\"\n\"Och heden\", seinen se.\nHy gong fuort, en dy minsken ek.\nIn jier letter trof ik Jan Hepkes wer. Ik sei: \"Hoe is dat doe ôfroun mei dat minske?\"\nJan sei: \"Ik ried juster troch Bûtenpost. En doe stapt dêr in feint fan 'e fyts. Dy seit tsjin my: 'Ho ris even!'\"\nIk fan 'e fyts en ik sei: \"Hwat wie der, boeke?\"\n\"Nou,\" sei er, \"it is wol op jou sizzen útkaem mei ús mem. Nei acht dagen wie se dea.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37442,"r":"CJ104404","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"The evening before IJe shot four policemen dead, the sky already turned red, as a foreshadowing of the blood.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"De jouns fan tofoaren foardat de fjouwer plysjes troch IJe Wykstra fan Greategast deasketten waerden wie de loft alhiel read. Dit hat in foarboade west fan it bloedbad.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37444,"r":"CJ104406","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1973,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A caul-bearer saw funeral processions and always predicted when a funeral was coming.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"In broer fan heit wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy seach de lykstaesjes al fan tofoaren en wist altyd as der in bigraffenis op til wie. Hy wie frijgesel en wenne yn Hantum.\n't Kaem altyd nei hwat er seach.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":37445,"r":"CJ104407","p":"Opende","v":"Gr.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"Tryn was a card reader and her predictions came true. To one she predicted mourning, and to another that he would live happily by the water. That is exactly how it went.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Tryn Snipel wenne yn Houtigehage. It wie in kaertlizter.\nWy wienen der ris mei ús fjouweren hinne, wy woenen de kaert útlein ha. Hja wenne tichte by de Blaudobbe.\nTsjerk wie ek by ús, dy lake hiel bot. Doe sei Tryn:\n\"Ja leave, sa't de duvel der yn komt giet hy der ek wer út.\"\nDoe wie 't laitsjen fan Tsjerk oer.\nEarst krigen wy alle fjouwer in buorrel fan Tryn. Doe naem se de kaert. Doe sei se tsjin Tsjerk: \"Ja, Tsjerk, nou mast ris even sjen. De iene giet de oare nei. Hwat in rou yn 'e kaerten.\"\nTsjin ús sei se: \"Jimme binne oan 't wetter kom to wenjen en sille gelokkich wurde.\"\nWy hà trije jier oan 't wetter wenne doe't wy krekt troud wienen yn Kommersyl!\nFan dy rouwe yn Tsjerk syn kaerten is it ek útkaem.\nJanke, in suster fan Tsjerk, dy't yn 'e Boelensloane wenne, hat har sels de hals útsnien en Tsjerk hat him ophong.\nHy wie oars sa'n fleurige jonge, dy't altyd mei ús op en út gong. Wy koenen it ús net bigripe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":128426,"r":"ENGELB_06_002","p":"Volthe","v":"Ov.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"Two nuns agree that whoever dies first will send a message from heaven. The surviving nun hears knocking under the floor; others hear nothing. When she asks who is knocking, the dead nun makes herself known and says never to make such agreements again, for the road from heaven to earth is hard.","i":"H.E.","o":"D'r har 'n klaoster west, in 't Deurninger klaoster en door hadn twee zusters west en dee hadn gewoon west net as twee zusters en doe hadn zich an 't lest belowd wel 't eerst stäörf, den zôl ne bosschôp oet 'n hemmel stuurn, boe 't door was en woor he terecht was kömn. En dat ene dat staerft, mer d'r koomp niks, mer toe 'n maol, doe heur de zuster dee d'r owwerblewn was, dee heurde wat klopn ônder de vloor - zee was an 't dweiln - en dat har a 'n paar daag gaon en doe vertaelde ze dat an de overste en dee gung met en lôstern, mer dee kôn niks heurn, alleen dee zuster, dee heurde dat en doe wör de parochiegeestelijkheid in kennis staeld en dee komt ok, heurt ok niks, zee hadn dan zao maakt, zee zôl vraongn, wel of dat was en dat har ze ok doe ok daon, zee zôl zik bekaend maakn. Zee har zegd, dat zee 't was, zee was weer kömn um dee belofte te volbrengn, mer zee zôl toch nooit gen ofspraakn meer maakn, want de weg van de hemmel naor de eerde hen, dee was heel moeilijk.","l":"Twents"},{"n":128446,"r":"ENGELB_08_001","p":"Volthe","v":"Ov.","y":1973,"c":"TM 3116","d":"A parish priest predicts that a certain house will not burn down.","i":"H.E.","o":"Beierink: Kiek es, ik wet nich, of het woor is van van den Bosch (= een pastoor in Denekamp), ôp 'n breink, door is nen braand west, door is 'n hoes, is door in braand kömn en nô ja de hele Breinkstraot is practisch verbraand, hen, mer of ze nô pastoor van den Bosch hebt haald, ik wet 't ok nich, mer dat geläöw ik wa, hen, en doe har he zegd: \"Dat hoes, dat verbraandt nich\", en door was ok 'n braand owwersprungn en 'n volgende doorôp har wa wier braand.","l":"Twents"},{"n":209124,"r":"VODA_043_09","p":"Geleen","v":"L.","y":1973,"c":null,"d":"Work in the coal mines demanded a lot of independence and inventiveness from the miners. You work underground, the forces of nature are unpredictable and the situation is different every day. For many miners, switching to factory work on the assembly line, where initiative was not valued, was therefore not easy.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"Een enorm zelfstandig werk. Je kunt zeggen van, goed, het was toch ofwel iedere dag eh.. zoveel kubieke meter kool losmaken of iedere dag eh.. een meter galerij verder drijven. Maar uiteindelijk is mijnwerk iets dat niet in een fabriek gebeurt, maar onder de grond. Dat betekent eh.. iedere dag opnieuw strijd tegen de natuur. Een natuur die je niet kent, die iedere dag anders is. Drukverhoudingen, eh.. hardheid van de kool, ehm.. alle andere oorzaken die meespelen, bepaalden iedere dag opnieuw dat je moet zoeken naar wat is de handigste, de beste manier van werken. Dat kweekt dus een enorm stuk zelfstandigheid bij die mensen. En ik kan me heel goed voorstellen dat mensen die dan uit de mijn aan ander werk moeten komen, in de fabriek aan de lopende band of zo, dat die verduveld moeilijk daaraan kunnen wennen, omdat daar ieder eigen initiatief, als het ware, aan de kant gezet wordt. Je moet volgens uitgekiende handelingen het zo en zo doen, punt uit. En ehm.. dat was ondergronds, ja, een punt waar.. waar iedereen toch.. toch z’n eigen ik in kon terugvinden, ook zijn eigen inventieve vermogen, om zich met hele simpele dingen hulpmiddelen te verschaffen om makkelijker te werken. Bepaalde moeilijkheid, nou, een stuk ijzer, werden een paar gaten in geboord, ehm.. in gestoken beter gezegd, met een afbouwhamer, daar werd een ketting door en dan hing daar ergens een.. een laadpunt waardo"},{"n":37983,"r":"CJ107209","p":"Surhuisterveen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born on a Sunday were born with a caul. Such a person saw more, for example funeral processions. When people met a funeral procession at night they were pushed aside. Afterwards they no longer dared to pass that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Dy't op snein geboaren wie, wie mei de helm geboaren. Sa'n ien koe mear as in oar. Sokken seagen lykstaesjes fan tofoaren.\nBoardzer Bruining fan Houtigehage wie sa'n man.\nAs minsken nachts in lykstaesje metten, woarden se oan kant set. As har dat oerkom wie, doarsten se dêr letter net wer lâns.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38199,"r":"CJ108401","p":"Feanwâldsterwâl","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A niece by marriage was born with a caul. She sees everything in advance, such as funerals and accidents.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik haw in oantroude nicht hawn dy wenne op Koatstermoune. It wie de widdou fan Bartele Reitsma. Hja wie mei de helm geboaren. Alle bigraffenissen om har hinne seach se foarút, ek de ûngelokken dy't der gebeure soenen, ja, alles wist se foarút. Hiltsje hiet se.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38286,"r":"CJ108736","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul are compelled to see everything. People should not walk in the middle of the road at night, because they might run into a funeral procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon wurde mei de helm geboaren. Dy matte letter alles sjen.\nNachts mat in minske net midden op it paed rinne, hwant dan kin er tsjin in lykstaesje oanstjitte.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38333,"r":"CJ108922","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man born with a caul has to get up at night to see a funeral procession. He sees in advance that his daughter will drown herself.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Keke wenne yn Twizelerheide. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren. Nachts moest hy der altyd ôf om to sjen. Hy roan hiele einen om by in lykstaesje to kommen.\nHy woarde prest, hy koe net lizzen bliuwe.\nHy hat fan tofoaren sjoen dat syn eigen dochter har forsûpte.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38409,"r":"CJ109223","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"TM 4905","d":"Wild lanterns were the forewarnings of bicycles with lights and of cars.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wylde lantearnen seagen se hjir froeger hiel faek. Dat wienen de lettere fytsen mei de ljochten op en de auto's.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38566,"r":"CJ109821","p":"Feanwâlden","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"TM 2901","d":"People born with a caul sometimes have to get up at night. Usually they see funerals.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Minsken dy't mei de helm geboaren binne, matte der soms ôf om hwat to sjen. Hja sjogge yn 'e regel bigraffenissen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38610,"r":"CJ109903","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man was born with a caul, so he sees everything in advance. If the caul is pulled off from back to front, the person will later be compelled to see everything. The man walks far to see funeral processions, and all gates open for him by themselves.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Knjillis Veenstra fan Kollumersweach seach alles foarút. Hy hat foarút sjoen dat syn eigen dochter forsûpte. Har lykstaesje seach er ek. Hy wie mei de helm geboaren.\nAs se dy helm fan foaren nei achteren ôflûke, gebeurt der neat. Mar lûke se him fan achteren nei foaren ôf, dan mat sa'n ien letter alles sjen.\nAs der foar him in lykstaesje to sjen wie, siet er altyd achter in hekke fan in stik lân.\nHy roan lange einen om by sa'n lykstaesje to kommen.\nDe hekken gongen fansels foar him iepen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":38627,"r":"CJ110005","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man born with a caul has to get up at night to see funeral processions. He sees someone's funeral in advance. Gates open for him, and he walks through hedges and ditches.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Guon minsken seagen lykstaesjes fan tofoaren. Letter stoar der dan ien, dêr't hja de bigraffenis al fan sjoen hienen.\nIen fan 'e bikendsten hjir wie Bontsje Knjillis. Dy wie mei de helm geboaren. Hy wenne by 't spoar.\nHy woarde nachts opjage. Dan moest hy der út. Dan moest er in lykstaesje sjen. Dan roan er soms om 't leven. Dan sieten se him achter. Dan gongen alle hekken foar him iepen, sa'n haest wie der by.\nDan kaem er moarns wer thús. Dan koe men sjen dat er troch hagen en sleatten en alles hinnegong wie. Dan siet it einekroas him soms noch yn 't hier en syn klean wienen soms skuord.\nDe geest dreau him fuort, út it bêd wei.\nHy moest faek hiele lange einen rinne, hwer't mar in lykstaesje to sjen wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":10687,"r":"CJ110113","p":"Twijzelerheide","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"TM 3101","d":"Wopke the exorcist gives a potion for a bewitched person but warns that someone who wants to prevent the cure will try to take it away. Someone will strike the bottle up to three times to make it fall and break, Wopke says. The prediction comes true: a cat lashes out at the bottle, but it stays whole. The next day the witch in question has her body full of needles and pins because, as a cat, she could not break the potion.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie ien bitsjoend, dy wenne tusken Twizelerheide en de Westerein yn. Doe gongen se nei Wopke fan Kûkherne ta, de duvelbander. Dy joech dy lju in drankje mei en sei:\n\"As der jim nou aenst ien tomjitte komt, tink der dan om, dat dyselde net by de flesse komme kin. Hwant hy docht trije kear in raem op 'e flesse. Dy wol er kapot ha.\"\nDoe kaem der in kat, en dy is trije kearen by deselde opsprong dy't de flesse yn 'e bûs hie. Mar de flesse bleau hiel. De tsjoenster hie de oare deis it lichum fol nuddels en spjelden. Dat kaem trochdat se it drankje net stikken krije kind hie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29510,"r":"CJ110408","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":null,"d":"The narrator talks about his strange neighbour Bontsje Keke: almost everyone was afraid of him. (He was a clairvoyant.)","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Keke (= Knjillis Veenstra) wenne njonken it hûs, dêr't wy nou yn wenje. Ik haw him wol kend. Hy wie middelmatich-great en foars fan foarkommen. It wie in apart man. Hy woe wol prate, mar de measte minsken wienen bang foar him, wy èk.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29516,"r":"CJ110414","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":null,"d":"A clairvoyant man sees a coffin standing in his own room and predicts that he himself will soon die. But it is his son who dies: shortly afterwards the son hangs himself from an apple tree.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Keke hat hjir njonken wenne. Hy hie in soan yn Grinslân to wenjen. Doe hat Keke op in kear in lykkiste by him thús yn 'e keamer sjoen. Doe hie er tocht: \"Dat bin ik sels.\" Mar dat wie 't gefal net. De soan is ris in kear - dat wie letter - út Grinslân wei thús kaem en hat him hjir by him yn 't apelhôf oan in beam ophong. Sadwaende kaem dy kiste by Keke yn 'e keamer to stean. Doe't Keke dy kiste fan tofoaren stean sjoen hie, wist er net hwa't it wie.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29782,"r":"CJ111520","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"TM 3101","d":"The mother of a bewitched child consults Wopke the exorcist. Wopke gives her a potion but urges her to guard the medicine well. Someone will try to throw her into the water to take the bottle from her, Wopke says. He also impresses on her not to show the potion to that person. Wopke's prediction comes true: as the woman crosses the bridge, an old woman - the witch - comes towards her. The woman manages to get the potion home intact and the child recovers.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As der ien bitsjoend wie, gongen se faek nei in duvelbanner ta. Dat wie meastal Wopke fan Kûkherne.\nDêr wie in frou, dy har bern wie bitsjoend. Hja wenne hjir tichte by yn 'e Westerein. In âld minske hat it ús wol forteld.\nDat minske gong nei Wopke ta. Hja krige in drankje mei. Wopke sei tsjin har: \"Nou matte jo aenst op jou iepenst wêze. Aenst op 'e brêge komt der jo ien tomjitte, en dy wol om jo hinne kringe om jo yn 't wetter to krijen. Jo matte goed op it fleske passe, dat jo by jo ha.\nTink der om, dyselde dy't jo yn 't wetter kringe wol, dy mei dat fleske net sjen. En jo matte der op passe dat it net stikken rekket.\nDoe't it minske op 'e brêge kaem, hie dêr in âld wiif west, dat wie noch in âld-muoike fan my. En dat âlde wiif, dat hie mar om har hinne roun en mar om har hinne roun om har yn 't wetter to krijen. Mar sy koe 't net rêdde, 't minske hâldde 't op fuotten.\nIt drankje bleau hiel en it bern waerd wer better.\nMar dat âld wiif dêr op 'e brêge, dy âld-muoike fan my, dat wie de tsjoenster.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29787,"r":"CJ111525","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"TM 4902","d":"If you step on a toad, thunder will come. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J."},{"n":29826,"r":"CJ111711","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"TM 4902","d":"If you step on a toad or a snail, thunder will come. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Op in pod trapen wy noait, op in slak like min, hwant dan soe der tonger komme, mienden wy.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29924,"r":"CJ111713","p":"Kollumersweach","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"TM 2901","d":"The seventh of seven sons is born with a double caul. At night he is often driven out of bed to corpse roads to foresee deaths in passing funeral processions. The clairvoyant sometimes has to hurry to be on the spot when the vision appears. Because he was born with two cauls, he sees much more than others born with a caul. He is not a welcome guest, since everyone fears something is about to happen when he turns up.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bontsje Keke syn heit wie èk de sawnde fan sawn. Sadwaende wie hy sèls mei de dûbelde helm geboaren. Fan Twizel nei de Swâdde roun in lykpaed. En der roun ek in lykpaed fan Kollumersweach nei de Swâdde. Dy beide lykpaden kamen sahwat op itselde plak by de Swâdde út. Op dy lykpaden wie Bontsje Keke nachts wit hoe faek to finen. Dêr seach er de lykstaesjes. Dy moesten dêr lâns. En as der wer sa'n lykstaesje op komst wie, dan moest Keke ta 't bêd út. Dan koed er onmooglik lizzen bliuwe, ek al woe er noch sa graech. Krekt as sieten se him dan achter. Soms seach er twa, trije lykstaesjes op ien nacht. Hy wie deawarch, as er wer thúskaem. Hwant hy moest soms hurd rinne om se op tiid to sjen. Dan gongen de hekken samar út harsels foar him iepen.\nHy fortelde it wol gauris as er wer in hiele nacht yn 'e wapens west hie. Dan sei er: \"Nije wike wurdt hjir ien bigroeven. 'k Ha de lykstaesje sjoen.\"\nSoms sei er: \"Der stjert ek wer in popke nije wike. 'k Ha in lyts kistje sjoen, dêr't se achteroan roannen.\" Ek wol sei er: \"Nou stjert der oer in pear dagen in kreamfrou. 'k Seach de lykstaesje. Der lei in wyt ruft oer de kiste hinne.\"\nDêr roan ek in lykpaed nei Westergeast, dêr wie er ek faek, dêr seach er ek lykstaesjes. De boaze siet him altyd achter. Hy hie twa helms, dêrtroch seach er folle mear as oaren dy't mei de helm geboaren wienen.\nSyn dochter forsûpte har yn 'e dobbe. Dêr hat er de","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":29962,"r":"CJ111812","p":"De Westereen","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"TM 3101","d":"A sick child turns out to be bewitched. Witches' wreaths in the child's pillow turn out to contain threads and scraps from the clothes of the other family members. Wopke the exorcist gives a potion but warns of someone who is after the medicine. That person must not pass on the side where the bottle is carried, Wopke says. His prediction comes true: a woman - the witch - walks past the potion and the bottle breaks. Wopke gives a new potion. The bewitched child then passes a mouse in its stool and is cured afterwards. The witch in question can also turn herself into a tripe stomach.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Hjir yn 'e Westerein wie in bern, dat rekke bitsjoend. Doe gongen se nei Wopke fan Kûkherne ta. Dat wie de duvelbanner. It bern hie krânsen yn 't kessen en dêr sieten allegear triedden en lapkes yn dy krânsen bifrissele, dy wienen út 'e klean dy't dêr yn dat hûs troch de húsgenoaten fan dat bern droegen woarden. Wopke joech in drankje en sei: \"Tink der om, ûnderweis wol jo ien passeare en dy wol oan dy kant by jo lâns, dêr't jo it drankje drage. Mar jo matte der foar soargje dat dat net gebeurt.\"\nDoe wie der dat minske ûnderweis in frommes foarby kaem, dy prebearre har oan kant to triuwen. Hja woe oan dy kant lâns, dêr't it drankje wie. Doe rekke it drankje stikken.\nDoe moest dat minske opnij nei Wopke ta. En doe krige se wer in drankje mei.\nDeselde dy't har tomjitte kaem wie en 't drankje stikken makke hie, wie de tsjoenster, dy't it bern bitsjoend hie. \nIt bern krige fan 't drankje yn en doe't dat bern hwat yn 'e pot dwaen moest, siet dêr in mûs yn. Dy wie 't bern út de terms kom. Mar doe wie 't genezen. \nDat minske, dat him bitsjoend hie, foroare har nou en dan yn in pânse.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30409,"r":"CJ113041","p":"Broeksterwâld","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":null,"d":"A farmhand who was promised work starts a lawsuit when the farmer refuses to take him on. A fortune teller had earlier predicted that he would soon stand before 'great lords'. If he chose his words carefully, all would be well, the fortune teller said. The predictions come true: the man is assigned two good lawyers who will argue his case before the judge. The labourer cannot pay them, but holds out the prospect of huge sums of money from the farmer concerned. The lawyers win the case.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Ik hie ris in kear aksje mei in boer. Ik hie in simmer by him wurke en doe hienen wy ôfpraet, de oare simmers soe 'k wer komme. Dêr rekkene ik op. Mar doe't ik dan by him kaem, koed er my net brûke. Dat liet ik der net by sitte. 'k Hie getugen by my dy 't bifestigje koenen dat ik gelyk hie. Doe waerd dat in rjochtsaek. Ik gong earst nei in wiersizter ta. Ik woe wite hoe't it biteare soe. Ik fortelde har neat.\nHja sei: \"Jo sille binnenkoart foar greate hearen stean. Mar dan matte jo oppasse hwat jo sizze. Dan komt it wol goed.\"\nIt minske krige gelyk. Ik hie twa perfekte advokaten: Tysma en Okma. Ik sei tsjin harren: ik kin jim neat bitelje, mar as jimme foar my it proses winne, kinne jim dy boer safolle ôfsette as jim wolle. Nou, sa is it ek gien. Dy advokaten ha foar my sprutsen en de saek woun.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30549,"r":"CJ113606","p":"Mûnein","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":"TM 4902","d":"If you tread a toad to death, thunder will come. It is an omen.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"As men in pod deatrapet, dan komt der tonger, waerd ús froeger sein.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":30617,"r":"CJ113815","p":"Hurdegaryp","v":"Fr.","y":1974,"c":null,"d":"A card reader makes many predictions about the future.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oan 'e Achterwei yn/by Burgum wenne Jehannes Mike. Dy syn frou dat wie Albertsje Brjit. Dy koe kaertlizze. Hja wie wiid en siid bikend. In protte lju reizgen dêr hinne, sa yn 'e njoggentiger jierren en om 1900 hinne, fral jonge fammen.\nIk wit noch dat se tsjin sa'n faem sei: \"Dû krijst in keardel mei in rossige snor. It hûs dêrstû mei him komst to wenjen, steane beammen foar en it leit oan 't wetter. Mar jimme sille dêr net lang wenje. Dan komme jimme yn in oar hûs. Dat stiet ek oan 't wetter en dêr binne ek wer beammen foar.\"","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":210900,"r":"VODA_046_08","p":"Beverwijk","v":"N.-H.","y":1974,"c":"TM 2901","d":"The narrator was born with a caul. Grandpa buried the caul with the afterbirth in the ground to keep it from falling into the wrong hands, which would make the child unhappy all its life.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"V: verteller\nI: interviewer (Jaap Brand?)\n\n[Fluitend vogeltje op de achtergrond]\nV: Eh.. ik ben met de helm geboren. En ik zeg... bij wijze van spreken bepaalde dingen wat ik niet weet en toch waarheid is. Mijn grootvader, die heeft de helm weggedaan. En mijn moeder... \nI: Weggedaan? Hoe weggedaan? \nV: O, in de grond gespit met nageboorte en alles bij. \nI: Met wat d’r bij? \nV: Met de nageboorte en alles...\nI: Alles d’r bij, ah.\nV: ...in de grond gedaan. Want mijn opa die was heel erg bijgelovig, die zei: “Want als het hier in verkeerde handen terechtkom, dan ben je je hele leven ongelukkig.”"},{"n":210902,"r":"VODA_046_10","p":"Beverwijk","v":"N.-H.","y":1974,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Born with a caul. Selling the caul (amniotic membrane) could fetch a lot of money. The midwife's first question was whether there was a caul.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"[fluitend vogeltje op de achtergrond]\nWant m’n opa zeg: “Ik heb schatrijk kennen worden als ik die helm van jou bewaard had en verkocht had.” Ik weet wel eh.. [verkeer op de achtergrond] dat m’n dochter geboren werd, was ’t eerste wat de vroedvrouw vroeg of d’r een helm bij was."},{"n":131976,"r":"VODA_036_02","p":"Terneuzen","v":"Zl.","y":1975,"c":"TM 5004","d":"Shortly before Christmas the master, mistress and farmhand sit together. The farmhand tells his master never to go to the horse stable at midnight on Christmas Eve. Despite the warning, the farmer goes anyway. He hears the horse predict that the master will soon die. In no time the farmer was dead.","i":"H.E./J.B.","o":"“Jao”, hij zegt: “Da zou’k ou toch nog ‘s vertellen.” Hij zegt: “Da was… in Groenendijk, gemeente Hontenis, woonden d’n boer die’k goed gekend heb. ’n Goeien boer, met zijn vrouw en… ’n paor kindern.”\nEn het was zo kort voor Kertsmis, zitten op de laten avond, de kinderen zijn naor bed, zitten den baos en de bazin, want da dee ze in het land van Hulst, de baozin en Sjef, d’n jongen inwonenden knecht, die zitten rond d’n openhaord. En waor dan de… houtblokken nu flink loeiend vuur opleven… zegt Sjef tegen d’n baos: “Boas… weeteh gij wel da ge in de nacht, in de Kerstnacht, precies de twaalef uurn nooit in de pèrdestal mag kommn?” “Oh ja jongen… Ah la jongen,” zegt d’n boer, “waorom dan nie?” “Nee boas,” zegt Sjef, “Da meugde nooit doen, want wee degene die dat doet, hem zal ’t ongeluk treffen.” “Ghogho,” zegt d’n boer, “Sjef, Sjef, ge hèd lelijk te pakkn mijn jongen, gij leest te veel boeken!” De knecht zegt niks meer. Moar ja, menselijke eigenschap, die zit ook bij de boer, en die kan toch nie laten, die zegt tegen z’n vrouw: “Hoor ‘s, ik gao toch op de kerstnacht om twaalf uren gao ik de stal ’s in.” “Oei,” zegt z’n vrouw, “Doet da nie, wij kunnen wij beter naor de nachtmis gaon.” Maor den boer is d’r nie af te helpn en vijf voor twaaleven op zijn kousen, gaot ie de stal en verbergt zich achter de ruiven. De klok van Groenendijk laot zijn twaalf slagen horen en dan opeens hoor","l":"Zeeuws"},{"n":11468,"r":"YPFOE045","p":"Goutum","v":"Fr.","y":1976,"c":null,"d":"A girl is sent to the shop by her mother. On the way she meets someone who tells her she will die in December. At home she asks her mother and father if this is true. Her parents know nothing of it; the minister thinks the girl has imagined it. Her father grows somewhat tired of her going on about it and sends her to the shoemaker, who knows the Bible well. The shoemaker tells her the creation story. After that she visits him regularly and hears other Bible stories. When December comes, the girl falls ill. She dies. The shocking event leads many people to convert.","i":"Y.P.","o":"Yn desimber silstu stierre\nMynhear Koelstra, de evangelist fan Twizelerheide hat my al ris in ferhaal ferteld, dat hat him ôfspile dy kant nei Lúnbert ta. Dêr wie ris in frou, dy sei tsjin har famke: 'Dû moatst even nei de winkel — dát ophelje!' It fanke wie ûnderweis nei de winkel en doe kaam har ien temjitte, dy sei: 'Yn desimber silstû stjerre'.\nIt famke hie de boadskippen dien en doe sei se tsjin har mem: 'Ik ha mei in man praat en dy sei tsjin my, ik soe yn desimber stjerre — wit mem dêr ek wat fan?' 'Ei nee, ju', sei de mem, 'ei, dat kin net!' It famke sei it ek tsjin har heit en de heit sei: 'Leau dêr mar neat fan'.\nMar it wie dat famke net ôf te praten. Hyltyd begûn se der wer oer, dat dy man dat sein hie. Doe gongen se mei har nei dominy. 'Ah', sei dominy, 'daar is niets van waar, hoor! Daar moet je niet over nadenken. Dat zijn maar praatjes, dat verbeeld je je maar'. 'Nee', sei it famke, 'ik ferbeeld it my net'. Se wie der net ôf te bringen. Altyd dat geseur, tocht de heit, en op 't lêst sei er: 'No, gean dan mar ris nei dy skuonmakker. Dat is ien fan 'e oare tsjerke. Miskien wit dy der wat fan'.\nEn dat famke dêrhinne. Dy skuonmakker wie tige thús yn 'e bibel, en it famke wist neat fan 'e bibel ôf. En de skuonmakker har dêr fertelle oer de bibel, oer it ûntstean fan 'e skepping en allegearre. Hy liet dat famke hyltyd mar wer by him komme en dan fertelde er har fierder","l":"Fries"},{"n":129748,"r":"Voda_022_15","p":"Eindhoven","v":"N.-Br.","y":1977,"c":"TM 2901","d":"A man predicts the death of someone else in the neighbourhood. A woman may not know who, because it later turns out to be her mother-in-law.","i":"H.E.","o":"Maar diezelfde man, die liep enige weken later, of diezelfde man voorspelde enige weken later, weer de dood van iemand uit de buurt. Nu wilde men wel over zijn linker schouder kijken. Een in de buurt wonende vrouw vroeg het zelfs aan de man die met de helm geboren was, maar de man weigerde het haar. En inderdaad stierf enkele dagen later iemand uit de buurt. En nu wist men tevens waarom de vrouw niet over de linkerschouder van de man had mogen kijken, want de overledene was de schoonmoeder van de vrouw."},{"n":12980,"r":"YPFOE131","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1977,"c":null,"d":"A soothsayer predicts that a man will meet his end by the blow of a windmill sail. The man is a miller, and from then on resolves never to stand near the sails of his mill. One day the sails stop turning. He stands by the mill watching, until the sails suddenly start turning again. He is struck by a sail and dies.","i":"Y.P.","o":"De moleroede\nIk haw ris in ferhaal heard fan in man, dy hie it oer in kunde fan him. Dy kunde hie op Boalserter merke, of op Snitser merke, by in wiersizzer west en dy hie him foarsein, dat hy soe troch de slach fan in moleroede oan syn ein komme.\nHy wie boer en hy hie in mole, mar hy paste sûnt dy tiid altyd tige op; hy kaam der noait by as de mole yn 't wurk stie. Mar op in kear, it wie al in hiel skoft letter, wie er by de mole en dy stie ynslein. Mar op in stuit foel de wyn en de mole draaide net mear. Der soe mear seil by moatte. Hy rûn der sa op ta en stie der by te sjen, en doe ynienen begûn de mole wer te draaien en is er troch in roede deaslein.","l":"Fries"},{"n":12979,"r":"YPFOE130","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1978,"c":null,"d":"A farmer warns his farmhand and the farmhand's girlfriend that they had better not go skating, because he foresees it will be their last trip. The farmhand and the girl laugh about it and go anyway. On the way back they skate into a hole in the ice and drown. They are brought back to the farm frozen solid. Everything happened exactly as the farmer had already seen it.","i":"Y.P.","o":"Dit wurdt jim lêste reis\nWy mochten graach ride en wy sieten yn 't wetterlân. Mar heit warskouwe altiten:\n'Tink der om mei de marren, dat jim dêr noait jûns let oer geane'. En dan kaam in ferhaal op 'e lappen, dat hie er fan beppe. Ik wit net goed, wêr't it bard is, op 'e Groustermar of op 'e Burgumermar, ik wit wol, dat der in feint en in faam yn in kistewek ferdronken binne. Foaral de Burgumer lei foarhinne wol gauris kiste-ark yn. Dan is der iis byinoar op skood. Oerdei sjocht men dat wol, mar by skimerjûn of by tsjuster kin men der sa op ride. It is bomiis en dan falt it yn en dat is tige gefaarlik.\nDer wienen in feint en in faam, dy soenen tegearre te riden, mar de boer sei: 'Jim moatte dêrom tinke—dit wurdt jim lêste reis'. 'No, it moat net mâlder', sei de faam, 'wy komme strak wer thús'. De boer sei noch ris: 'Dat fertrou ik net'. Hy hie tefoaren har liken sjoen, seit it ferhaal. Mar sy gniisden der wat om. De hinnereis rieden se oer de mar en doe wie der neat te rêden, mar de weromreis doe lei der in kiste-ark en dêr rieden se beide yn en doe ferdronken se. Stiif befêrzen waarden se op 'e pleats binnen brocht, krekt sa't de boer se sjoen hie.","l":"Fries"},{"n":13718,"r":"YPFOE190a","p":"Leeuwarden","v":"Fr.","y":1978,"c":null,"d":"In the Wijd of Wartena, it is said, lies a sunken city. In fine, calm weather the old church bells can still be heard. Anyone sailing across the Wijd also risks getting his punting pole stuck in the roofs or tower of the sunken city. Objects are also fished up that are said to belong to people from the city. The city was founded by Redbad. He predicted that Wartena would become a fine, large city, but would also soon perish in a great flood.","i":"Y.P.","o":"De fersonken stêd Warten\n\nEn spoarleas gyng it nei de grûn \nMei minske, hûs en toer; \nEn neat fan alles is der bleaun, \nSa stiet yn d'âld kronyk beskreaun; \nNo streamt er't wetter oer.\n\nSikke Koldyk\n\n'Ik ha oars net heard, as dy fersonken stêd lei yn 't Wartenster Wiid. Se sizze ek altiten: as it hiel moai waar is en tige, tige stil, dan kin men de âlde klokkon noch hearre yn 't Wartenster Wiid. It hat ek sa west, as it tige stil waar wie, dan hoegde men dêr net oer te farren, want de kloet rekke fêst op ien fan 'e dakken fan 'e fersonken stod. As it blakstil wie, koenen de skippen wol lizzen bliuwe. Der is ek it ferhaal fan 'e skipper, waans kloet yn 'e toer fêst siet. Ik ha ek wol heard, dat men yn pleats fan by stil waar de klokken hearre koe, wannear't it tige stoarme. Mar ja, dan hat men safolle lûden yn 'e wrâld.\nIt hjitte altyd, dat se dêr no en dan it iene en it oare opfisken. Omke Jelle sei altyd: No, it is wier, ik ha 't sels sjoen. Der wie in boer oan 't hekkeljen en dy helle in piip op út it Wiid. Dat wie de piip fan ien fan 'e mannen dy't dêr mei de stêd fergongen wie.\nSjoch, dy stêd is ûntstien troch Redbad. Hy moat sein ha, Warten sil ien kear in stêd wêze, moaier as Rome en grutter as Utert. Der is ek profetearre, hy soe like hurd wer ferneatige wurde as er kommen wie. Ik wit wol, dat dy stêd fergongen is mei in grutte floed, doe't heal Fryslân der ûnder strûpt","l":"Fries"},{"n":31504,"r":"CJ118009","p":"Garyp","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":null,"d":"In the old days people often heard sounds of carpentry when no one was actually doing any. It was a portent: later a new house was built on that spot.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Faek hearden se hjir froeger timmerjen, sûnder dat der yn werklikheit timmere waerd. Op sa'n plak kaem dan letter in hûs to stean.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31584,"r":"CJ118613","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"TM 3106","d":"Because a farmer has two sick horses, he sends his labourer to Wopke the exorcist. The farmer gives his farmhand hay from the two sick horses, but also some hay from a healthy horse. Wopke is not fooled and soon sees that one of the horses is perfectly healthy. So he gives the farmhand two bottles of medicine and a pot of hay. Wopke warns the farmhand, who came on skates, not to go back over the ice because he might fall. The farmhand obeys and sets off home on foot. When he tires of walking, he ignores Wopke's warnings and straps on his skates. After skating for a while he falls and the bottles break, exactly as Wopke predicted. The farmhand returns to Wopke for new potions. The labourer tells the farmer that 'that devil of an exorcist' made him fall.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Oege wie arbeider by in boer. Dy boer hie twa sike hynders, dêrom stjûrde er Oege nei greate Wopke fan Kûkherne, de wûnderdokter en duvelbander. Hy joech Oege hier mei fan 'e sike hynders, mar ek hier fan in oar hynder, dat net siik wie. 't Wie yn 'e winter en 't iis dat hâldde, dat Oege ried op redens nei Kûkherne. Wopke biseach de trije soarten hier en joech Oege twa dranken mei yn fleskes en in pûdtsje mei hwat der yn. (Dêr bliek hjouwer yn to sitten, dat wie foar 't soune hynder. Se forrifelen Wopke net gau).\n\"Tink der om,\" sei Wopke, \"en gean net wer op redens werom, hwant astû komst to fallen, kinne de flessen wolris stikken wêze.\"\nOege roun earst in ein, mar doe tocht er: Hwat birin ik eins? Ik ha redens by my. Dy byn ik ûnder. It gong in hiel set goed. Mar doe't er yn Nyegea wie kaem er to fallen. De drankflessen stikken en alle drank fuort.\nOege werom nei Kûkherne.\n\"Soa,\" sei Wopke, \"wiest dêr al wer? Ik hie dy warskôge.\"\nHy krige twa nije drankjes mei en roun doe it hiele ein.\n\"Dy duvelse keardel hat my dêr falle litten\", sei er tsjin 'e boer. Hwant hy wist wol dat Wopke ek in duvelbanner wie.\nOege Pebesma wie dy arbeider. Hy wie fan Sumar ôfkomstich.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31604,"r":"CJ118907","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":null,"d":"A minister sees a leaf from a tree stick to the window of the parsonage. From the leaf he reads that he will die within ten days.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Der wie in dûmny dy seach op in kear in blêd tsjin it glês oan by him yn 'e pasterije. 't Wie it blêd fan in beam. Hy lies dêr út, dat syn libbensrin binnen tsien dagen ôfroun wêze soe.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31636,"r":"CJ119212","p":"Sumar","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"TM 2901","d":"Someone born with a caul, or who owns such a caul, is bulletproof. High-ranking army officers used to be keen to get hold of such cauls.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Deselde dy't yn 't bisit is fan sa'n helm, is kûgelfrij. Dêrom hienen de hege militairen yn 't leger froeger sa'n helm dy't se kocht hienen en by har droegen.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31952,"r":"CJ120914","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":null,"d":"A beekeeper makes all kinds of predictions based on the behaviour of his bees.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Piter van Velden wie bijker. Hy koe fan alles oan 'e bijen sjen. Hy wist altyd hok waer as der komme soe. En hy seach ek oan 'e bijen of der in stringe winter komme soe.\n\"As ik stjer,\" sei er, \"en 't wurdt de bijen net oansein, dan wurde se moedeloas. Dan binne se neat mear wurdich.\"\n\"Hoe mat dat dan?\" frege men him.\n\"Tikje even tsjin 'e kuorren oan en bring de tiding oer\", sei er.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31959,"r":"CJ120921","p":"Drachtstercompagnie","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":null,"d":"A man urges a companion to step aside for an approaching funeral procession. The companion cannot see the procession.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Bearn van der Woude fortelde: Op in nacht kaem ik mei in kameraed de Skieding del. Doe seach ik in lykstaesje oankommen, myn maet seach it net. Ik luts him gau oan kant, dat de lykstaesje passeare koe. Oars wie er oan kant stompt woarn.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":31968,"r":"CJ121009","p":"Burgum","v":"Fr.","y":1979,"c":"TM 3106","d":"An exorcist advises a man who has come for a potion for a sick horse not to go back the same way on skates, since the medicine might then be lost. The man ignores the warnings and skates back anyway. The exorcist's prediction comes true: shortly afterwards the bottle breaks.","i":"A.A.J.","o":"Wierd Harms Hoogstins wenne oan 'e âld trambaen (dat wie doe noch gjin trambaen). Hy gong foar in siik hynder nei Hinse Jehannes de Boer op it Swartfean. Dat wie in soart féarts, mar hy wie ek duvelbanner. 't Wie yn 'e winter en dêr lei in dikke laech iis op it wetter.\nHinse joech Wierd in drank mei. Wierd wie dêr op redens kaem, mar doe warskôge Hinse him. \"Tink derom,\" sei er, \"nou mast it selde paed net wer nimme as hinne, hwant dan kinst de drank wolris knoffelje. En gjin redens wer ûnderbine.\"\nMar Wierd sloech die ried yn 'e wyn. Hy stie al gau wer op 'e redens, mar doe't er oan Nyegeasterhoek ta wie, foel er en de drankflesse rekke stikken. Dat doe opnij nei Hinse ta.\nDoe krige er dan wèr in drank mei en dêr is er hiel mei thús kaem, hwant doe hied er net reedriden.","l":"Fries (Woudfries)"},{"n":128571,"r":"ENGELB_15_008","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1979,"c":"TM 3102","d":"Foretellers of the future and healers.","i":"H.E.","o":"H.E.: Nee, t verhaal op zikzölf is mooi. ll He’j hier in Geester nog leu had dee de tookomst kon vuurspeln?\nF.Ve.: Joawa, dee bint der nog wa\nJ.Ve.: Dee hebt hier wa west.\nVr. Met ne fancy-fair. Nem doar an de Tubbige weg Lucas of an de Vasser weg, den slager\nJ.Ve.: Beernink.\nVr.: Den kan veuln.\nJ.Ve.: Joa, den kan ok striekn.\nVr.: Dat kan ik ok wa ... hebt der hen west. Mörsink-Leen hef der hen west Lenie is a opereerd en hef ne neie hup kregn en koomp moandag a wier. Dat is good oetvöln, den hef geluk had.","l":"Twents"},{"n":128579,"r":"ENGELB_15_016","p":"Geesteren","v":"Ov.","y":1979,"c":"TM 3116","d":"A parish priest predicts which houses will burn down during a fire and which will not.","i":"H.E.","o":"H.E.: Of pasteurs, dee een of ander braand kondn bedwingn?\nVr. [Wolberink, Jan]: De grote braand in Vriezenveen. Vriezenveen is hoofdzakelijk protestant en dat hef noa n eerstn wereldoorlog west. Jan, wet ie dee joartaln nich, ik wet ze nich. Heel Vreeznven hebt ze antlestn ontruumd, want ze stoat ja al op n rijtje an weerskaantn langs de stroat hen. En umdat t al protestant is en de kaploan, den lop tusschen dee wonningn duur en doe pakt ze als oet en he zeg “Den mö’j ontruumn en den loa mer zitn, den braandt nich of” De leu hebt hem wa leug pakt, want dee leu löavn hem nich\nToen was de cassette afgelopen.","l":"Twents"},{"n":128587,"r":"ENGELB_16_003","p":"Oldenzaal","v":"Ov.","y":1979,"c":"TM 4001","d":"Croaking of frogs as a weather forecast; no knowledge of fortune tellers; origin of the names Hunenborg and hunebedden (megalithic tombs).","i":"H.E.","o":"Eng.: Ja, dee stroalingn en zoa, he? ... Ik mean, at t aans um was, at ze roopt dan.\nBr.: Dan krieg’j good weer.\nSp.: Nee, wie ’s oavnds wa es boetn stoan, met de oolde leu, dan, dee kikvörske, eenn begun der op hoge toon en n aander op leag, en dan kwam t hele koor, en dee veurspeln, doe ze t zedn goed weer, danmooi, mooi, mooi orkest maakn ze der van, en at n een oetschui kwam, kwak, kwak he begun ne leagere toon en ne aander nen hogern en efkes dan deed t hele koor dan gung t, en dee veurspeln goed weer, kikvöske en loakvörske, dee meen ik, a’w dee heurn roopn op n blad ... nen meter van de groond of op n blad zitn, at dee deadn tegn dreug weer.\nEng.: dan deadn ze t zölfde as gewone kikvörske, dus dan gaf t ok mooi weer.\nSp.: Dee zatn op n greun blad.\nEng.: Ko’j hoast nich zein.\nSp.: Nee dat völ nich op, ie mosn op t geluud of goan en dan mo’j ze vindn könn.\nEng.: Bint der nich meer? Loakvörsche.\nSp.: Nee, dee heik in gen joaren meer zeen.\nEng.: nee ok almoal oetstöarvn.\nSp.: Verrek, of was t no net andersum, dat ze tegn te water deedn, dat weet ik nich meer, of no nen loakvörsche tegn te water dee of tegn dreugte, kan ok weazn, at dee reupn um water, at ze op t blad zatn, dat we’k nich. dat möt oma wetn.\nEng.: Dee kö’j nich meer vroagn.\nSp.: Dat zo’k nich meer weetn meer, wat dat is.\nEng.: En leu met spölkaartn he’j ok nooit wat metmaakt?\nSp.: Nee.\nEng.: Of leu, dee in zo’n","l":"Twents"},{"n":128650,"r":"ENGELB_19_019","p":"Weerselo","v":"Ov.","y":1983,"c":null,"d":"A priest's prediction that nothing would happen in the parish during the war comes true.","i":"H.E.","o":"S: En toen die Aarhuus [Hendrikus Johannes Haarhuis, 1874-1951] hier, dezölfde Aarhuus dan, die hef hier later pastoor west, Toen n oorlog uutbrak, toen zeg he: Wees maar rustig, wees maar rustig, in Weerselo gebeurt niks. In miene parochie gebeurt niks. En zoowied as de parochie gong nooit, nooit gen vliegmachine valn, ok gen bom, niks, niks. Drect in Rossum wa, bie de keark hef wa wat leegn, biej Hersmeul hef wa wat leegn en bie ten Dam in Voalt hef wa wat leegn.\nE: In Weersel niks.\nS: In Weersel niks, in Soasel ook wa, biej Betsken Teun, hé vliegmachin op t hoes, en overal wa, mar in Weersel is niks, niks, niks valn.\nE: Dan hef t wa van te vuurtn könn bekiekn.\nS: He kon t van te veurtn bekiekn. He kon t van te veurtn bekiekn.","l":"Twents"}]);
